window.LH_GRADE_BUNDLES=window.LH_GRADE_BUNDLES||{};window.LH_GRADE_BUNDLES[5]={"subjects":{"afrikaans":{"id":"afrikaans","grade":5,"name":{"af":"Afrikaans Huistaal","en":"Afrikaans Home Language"},"short":{"af":"Afr","en":"Afr"},"icon":"📖","color":"#0d9488","intro":{"af":"Afrikaans Huistaal in Graad 5 bou jou vaardighede in luister en praat, lees en kyk, skryf en aanbied, en taalstrukture: woordsoorte, tye, woordorde (STOMPI), ontkenning, direkte en indirekte rede, spelling, idiome en beeldspraak. Jy lees verhale, gedigte, strokiesprente en advertensies en skryf self opstelle, briewe en opsommings. Die Novembereksamen toets gewoonlik leesbegrip, ’n visuele teks en taalstrukture, en jy skryf ook ’n opstel of kort skryfstuk – soms in ’n aparte vraestel.","en":"Afrikaans Home Language in Grade 5 builds your skills in listening and speaking, reading and viewing, writing and presenting, and language structures: parts of speech, tenses, word order (STOMPI), negation, direct and indirect speech, spelling, idioms and figures of speech. You read stories, poems, comic strips and advertisements and write your own essays, letters and summaries. The November exam usually tests reading comprehension, a visual text and language structures, and you also write an essay or short piece of writing – sometimes in a separate paper."},"examTips":[{"af":"Lees die leesstuk eers vinnig vir die hoofgedagte. Lees dan die vrae, en lees die teks ’n tweede keer stadig, sodat jy weet waarna jy soek.","en":"First read the passage quickly for the main idea. Then read the questions, and read the text a second time slowly, so that you know what you are looking for."},{"af":"Antwoord in volsinne en in jou eie woorde, tensy die vraag sê *haal aan*. Kyk na die punte: [2] beteken gewoonlik twee feite.","en":"Answer in full sentences and in your own words, unless the question says *haal aan* (quote). Look at the marks: [2] usually means two facts."},{"af":"Ken die vaste taalreëls uit jou kop: STOMPI, die dubbele ontkenning (*nie … nie*), werkwoorde sonder *ge-*, meervoude, verkleinwoorde en indirekte rede.","en":"Know the fixed language rules by heart: STOMPI, double negation (*nie … nie*), verbs without *ge-*, plurals, diminutives and indirect speech."},{"af":"Doen presies wat die taalvraag vra. *Skryf oor in die verlede tyd* beteken jy skryf die hele sin oor, nie net die werkwoord nie.","en":"Do exactly what the language question asks. *Skryf oor in die verlede tyd* (rewrite in the past tense) means you rewrite the whole sentence, not just the verb."},{"af":"Beplan jou opstel eers met ’n woordweb, skryf in paragrawe en hou ’n paar minute oor om spelling, hoofletters en leestekens na te gaan.","en":"Plan your essay first with a mind map, write in paragraphs and keep a few minutes to check spelling, capital letters and punctuation."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"DBE Reënboog-werkboeke (Graad 5)","en":"DBE Rainbow Workbooks (Grade 5)"},"url":"https://www.education.gov.za/Curriculum/Workbooks.aspx","note":{"af":"Gratis amptelike CAPS-werkboeke, ook vir Afrikaans Huistaal, in Afrikaans en Engels.","en":"Free official CAPS workbooks, including Afrikaans Home Language, in Afrikaans and English."}},{"title":{"af":"Siyavula: oop handboeke en oefening","en":"Siyavula: open textbooks and practice"},"url":"https://www.siyavula.com","note":{"af":"Gratis oop handboeke en oefenvrae vir verskeie vakke, aanlyn beskikbaar.","en":"Free open textbooks and practice questions for several subjects, available online."}}],"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Lees en woordsoorte","en":"Reading and parts of speech"},"topics":[{"id":"afr5-t1-leesbegrip","title":{"af":"Leesbegrip","en":"Reading comprehension"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal ’n teks slim kan lees, die hoofgedagte kan vind, feite van menings kan onderskei en letterlike en afleidingsvrae in volsinne kan beantwoord.","en":"You will be able to read a text smartly, find the main idea, tell facts from opinions and answer literal and inferential questions in full sentences."},"summary":{"af":"## Voor jy lees: vooruitskou\n\nBegin nie sommer by die eerste sin nie. Kyk eers na die **titel**, die **prente** en die **opskrifte**, en vra jouself: *Waaroor gaan hierdie teks?* Dit heet **vooruitskou**. So berei jy jou brein voor op die onderwerp, en jy verstaan makliker wat jy lees.\n\nLees die teks dan **twee keer**:\n\n1. **Vluglees:** lees vinnig deur om die **hoofgedagte** te kry – waaroor die hele teks gaan.\n2. **Lees noukeurig:** lees stadig en let op die besonderhede.\n\nSoek jy later ’n spesifieke feit, soos ’n naam, getal of bedrag? Dan **skandeer** jy: jou oë gly oor die teks totdat jy die woord raakloop. Jy hoef nie weer alles te lees nie.\n\n## Lees die teks\n\n> **Die tuin agter die saal**\n>\n> Verlede jaar was die stuk grond agter die skoolsaal net klippe en onkruid. Toe besluit die Graad 5-klas om ’n groentetuin te maak. Elke leerder het ’n leë melkbottel van die huis af gebring, en die kinders het die bottels as gieters gebruik.\n>\n> Eers moes hulle die klippe uithaal en die grond omspit. Dit was harde werk, en Pieter se hande was vol blase. Daarna het hulle spinasie, wortels en uie geplant. Elke oggend voor skool het twee leerders die beddings natgegooi.\n>\n> Ná ses weke was die spinasie groot genoeg om te oes. Die kinders het bossies spinasie vir R10 elk by die skoolhek verkoop. Met die geld het hulle nuwe saad en ’n tuinslang gekoop. Nou is die tuin die trots van die hele skool.\n>\n> “Spinasie is die lekkerste groente in die wêreld!” het Lerato gesê. Pieter het net gelag. Hy het nog altyd wortels verkies.\n\n## Soorte vrae\n\n| Soort vraag | Waar kry jy die antwoord? | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Letterlike vraag** | Dit staan reg daar in die teks. | *Wat het die kinders geplant?* |\n| **Afleidingsvraag** | Jy sit leidrade uit die teks en wat jy self weet bymekaar. | *Hoe het Pieter ná die eerste dag gevoel?* |\n| **Woord in konteks** | Lees die sinne voor en ná die woord. | *Wat beteken “oes” in paragraaf 3?* |\n| **Feit of mening** | Vra: kan ek dit bewys? | *Is Lerato se woorde ’n feit of ’n mening?* |\n\n> **Onthou:** By ’n afleidingsvraag staan die antwoord nie woord vir woord in die teks nie. Jy “lees tussen die reëls”. Pieter se hande was vol blase, so ons kan **aflei** dat die werk baie swaar was.\n\n## Feit of mening?\n\n- ’n **Feit** is waar en kan **bewys** of nagegaan word: *Die kinders het nuwe saad gekoop.*\n- ’n **Mening** is wat iemand **dink of voel**. Ander mense kan verskil: *Spinasie is die lekkerste groente in die wêreld.*\n\nWoorde soos *lekkerste, mooiste, beste, ek dink* en *ek voel* wys dikwels dat iets ’n mening is. Kyk hoe Pieter net lag: hy stem nie saam nie, want hy verkies wortels. Dit bewys dat Lerato se woorde ’n mening is.\n\n## Hoe om goeie antwoorde te skryf\n\n- Antwoord in ’n **volsin** en gebruik woorde uit die vraag. Vraag: *Wat het die kinders met die geld gekoop?* Antwoord: *Die kinders het nuwe saad en ’n tuinslang gekoop.*\n- Gebruik **jou eie woorde**, tensy die vraag sê **haal aan**. Dan skryf jy die presiese woorde uit die teks tussen aanhalingstekens.\n- Kyk na die **punte**: [2] beteken gewoonlik dat jy twee dinge moet noem.\n- By ’n **waarom-vraag** gee jy altyd ’n **rede**, met *omdat* of *want*.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om net *Ja* of *Nee* te skryf, of om ’n hele paragraaf uit die teks oor te skryf. Beantwoord presies wat gevra word – kort, volledig en in ’n volsin.","en":"## Before you read: previewing (*vooruitskou*)\n\nDon’t just start at the first sentence. First look at the **title**, the **pictures** and the **headings**, and ask yourself: *What is this text about?* This is called **previewing** (*vooruitskou*). Your brain gets ready for the topic, and you understand more easily.\n\nThen read the text **twice**:\n\n1. **Skimming** (*vluglees*): read quickly to get the **main idea** (*hoofgedagte*) – what the whole text is about.\n2. **Careful reading:** read slowly and notice the details.\n\nLooking for one specific fact later, such as a name, number or amount? Then you **scan** (*skandeer*): your eyes slide over the text until you find the word. You don’t have to read everything again.\n\n## Read the text\n\n> **Die tuin agter die saal**\n>\n> Verlede jaar was die stuk grond agter die skoolsaal net klippe en onkruid. Toe besluit die Graad 5-klas om ’n groentetuin te maak. Elke leerder het ’n leë melkbottel van die huis af gebring, en die kinders het die bottels as gieters gebruik.\n>\n> Eers moes hulle die klippe uithaal en die grond omspit. Dit was harde werk, en Pieter se hande was vol blase. Daarna het hulle spinasie, wortels en uie geplant. Elke oggend voor skool het twee leerders die beddings natgegooi.\n>\n> Ná ses weke was die spinasie groot genoeg om te oes. Die kinders het bossies spinasie vir R10 elk by die skoolhek verkoop. Met die geld het hulle nuwe saad en ’n tuinslang gekoop. Nou is die tuin die trots van die hele skool.\n>\n> “Spinasie is die lekkerste groente in die wêreld!” het Lerato gesê. Pieter het net gelag. Hy het nog altyd wortels verkies.\n\nUseful words: *onkruid* (weeds), *gieters* (watering cans), *omspit* (dig over), *beddings* (garden beds), *tuinslang* (hosepipe), *verkies* (prefer).\n\n## Kinds of questions\n\n| Kind of question | Where do you find the answer? | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Literal question** (*letterlike vraag*) | It is right there in the text. | *Wat het die kinders geplant?* (What did the children plant?) |\n| **Inferential question** (*afleidingsvraag*) | You combine clues from the text with what you already know. | *Hoe het Pieter ná die eerste dag gevoel?* (How did Pieter feel after the first day?) |\n| **Word in context** | Read the sentences before and after the word. | *Wat beteken “oes” in paragraaf 3?* |\n| **Fact or opinion** | Ask: can I prove it? | *Is Lerato se woorde ’n feit of ’n mening?* |\n\n> **Remember:** In an inferential question the answer is not written word for word in the text. You “read between the lines”. Pieter’s hands were full of *blase*, so we can **infer** that the work was very hard.\n\n## Fact or opinion?\n\n- A **fact** (*feit*) is true and can be **proved** or checked: *Die kinders het nuwe saad gekoop.* (The children bought new seed.)\n- An **opinion** (*mening*) is what someone **thinks or feels**. Other people may disagree: *Spinasie is die lekkerste groente in die wêreld.* (Spinach is the tastiest vegetable in the world.)\n\nWords like *lekkerste* (tastiest), *mooiste* (prettiest), *beste* (best), *ek dink* (I think) and *ek voel* (I feel) often show an opinion. Notice that Pieter just laughs: he doesn’t agree, because he prefers carrots. That proves Lerato’s words are an opinion.\n\n## How to write good answers\n\n- Answer in a **full sentence** (*volsin*) and use words from the question. Question: *Wat het die kinders met die geld gekoop?* Answer: *Die kinders het nuwe saad en ’n tuinslang gekoop.*\n- Use **your own words**, unless the question says **haal aan** (quote). Then you copy the exact words from the text between quotation marks.\n- Look at the **marks**: [2] usually means you must give two things.\n- For a **why question** always give a **reason**, using *omdat* or *want* (because).\n\n> **Common mistake:** Writing only *Ja* or *Nee*, or copying a whole paragraph from the text. Answer exactly what is asked – short, complete and in a full sentence."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Vooruitskou","en":"Previewing (vooruitskou)"},"def":{"af":"Om voor jy lees na die titel, prente en opskrifte te kyk en te voorspel waaroor die teks gaan.","en":"Looking at the title, pictures and headings before you read to predict what the text is about."}},{"term":{"af":"Vluglees","en":"Skimming (vluglees)"},"def":{"af":"Om ’n teks vinnig deur te lees net om die hoofgedagte te kry.","en":"Reading a text quickly just to get the main idea."}},{"term":{"af":"Skandeer","en":"Scanning (skandeer)"},"def":{"af":"Om jou oë vinnig oor ’n teks te laat gly om een spesifieke feit, soos ’n naam of getal, te vind.","en":"Letting your eyes move quickly over a text to find one specific fact, such as a name or number."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoofgedagte","en":"Main idea (hoofgedagte)"},"def":{"af":"Die belangrikste ding waaroor ’n hele teks of paragraaf gaan.","en":"The most important thing a whole text or paragraph is about."}},{"term":{"af":"Feit","en":"Fact (feit)"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat waar is en wat jy kan bewys of nagaan.","en":"Something that is true and that you can prove or check."}},{"term":{"af":"Mening","en":"Opinion (mening)"},"def":{"af":"Wat iemand dink of voel; ander mense kan daarmee verskil.","en":"What someone thinks or feels; other people may disagree with it."}},{"term":{"af":"Letterlike vraag","en":"Literal question (letterlike vraag)"},"def":{"af":"’n Vraag waarvan die antwoord reg daar in die teks staan.","en":"A question whose answer is written right there in the text."}},{"term":{"af":"Afleidingsvraag","en":"Inferential question (afleidingsvraag)"},"def":{"af":"’n Vraag waar jy leidrade uit die teks en jou eie kennis gebruik om die antwoord uit te werk.","en":"A question where you use clues from the text and your own knowledge to work out the answer."}},{"term":{"af":"Konteks","en":"Context (konteks)"},"def":{"af":"Die woorde en sinne rondom ’n woord wat jou help om sy betekenis te verstaan.","en":"The words and sentences around a word that help you understand its meaning."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanhaal","en":"Quote (aanhaal)"},"def":{"af":"Om die presiese woorde uit die teks tussen aanhalingstekens oor te skryf.","en":"To copy the exact words from the text between quotation marks."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"’n Letterlike vraag","en":"A literal question"},"problem":{"af":"Lees *Die tuin agter die saal*. Noem **twee** groentes wat die kinders geplant het. [2]","en":"Read *Die tuin agter die saal*. Name **two** vegetables that the children planted. [2]"},"steps":[{"af":"Die vraag sê *noem*, en die antwoord staan in die teks. Dit is ’n letterlike vraag.","en":"The question says *noem* (name), and the answer is in the text. It is a literal question."},{"af":"Skandeer vir woorde oor plant. Paragraaf 2 sê: *Daarna het hulle spinasie, wortels en uie geplant.*","en":"Scan for words about planting. Paragraph 2 says: *Daarna het hulle spinasie, wortels en uie geplant.* (Then they planted spinach, carrots and onions.)"},{"af":"Die vraag tel [2] punte, so noem twee groentes. Antwoord in ’n volsin met woorde uit die vraag.","en":"The question is worth [2] marks, so name two vegetables. Answer in a full sentence using words from the question."}],"answer":{"af":"Die kinders het spinasie en wortels geplant. (Uie is ook reg.)","en":"*Die kinders het spinasie en wortels geplant.* (The children planted spinach and carrots. Onions are also correct.)"}},{"title":{"af":"’n Afleidingsvraag","en":"An inferential question"},"problem":{"af":"Waarom dink jy het die kinders ’n tuinslang gekoop? [2]","en":"*Waarom dink jy het die kinders ’n tuinslang gekoop?* (Why do you think the children bought a hosepipe?) [2]"},"steps":[{"af":"Die teks sê nie direk hoekom nie, so dit is ’n afleidingsvraag. Soek leidrade.","en":"The text does not say why directly, so it is an inferential question. Look for clues."},{"af":"Leidraad uit die teks: die kinders het die beddings elke oggend met **melkbottels** natgegooi.","en":"Clue from the text: every morning the children watered the beds with **milk bottles**."},{"af":"Wat jy self weet: ’n bottel hou min water, en om heen en weer te loop om dit vol te maak, is stadig.","en":"What you already know: a bottle holds little water, and walking back and forth to fill it is slow."},{"af":"Sit die leidrade bymekaar en gee ’n rede met *omdat*.","en":"Put the clues together and give a reason with *omdat* (because)."}],"answer":{"af":"Ek dink hulle het ’n tuinslang gekoop omdat dit vinniger en makliker is om die tuin met ’n tuinslang nat te gooi as met melkbottels.","en":"*Ek dink hulle het ’n tuinslang gekoop omdat dit vinniger en makliker is om die tuin met ’n tuinslang nat te gooi as met melkbottels.* (I think they bought a hosepipe because it is quicker and easier to water the garden with a hosepipe than with milk bottles.)"}},{"title":{"af":"Feit of mening?","en":"Fact or opinion?"},"problem":{"af":"Is die volgende ’n feit of ’n mening? Gee ’n rede. (a) *Die kinders het bossies spinasie vir R10 elk verkoop.* (b) *Spinasie is die lekkerste groente in die wêreld.*","en":"Is each of these a fact or an opinion? Give a reason. (a) *Die kinders het bossies spinasie vir R10 elk verkoop.* (The children sold bunches of spinach for R10 each.) (b) *Spinasie is die lekkerste groente in die wêreld.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Dit kan nagegaan word: ’n mens kan die kinders vra of kyk hoeveel geld hulle gekry het.","en":"(a) It can be checked: you could ask the children or see how much money they received."},{"af":"(b) Die woord *lekkerste* wys wat Lerato voel. Pieter verskil van haar, want hy verkies wortels.","en":"(b) The word *lekkerste* (tastiest) shows what Lerato feels. Pieter disagrees with her, because he prefers carrots."},{"af":"Iets wat jy kan bewys, is ’n feit. Iets waaroor mense kan verskil, is ’n mening.","en":"Something you can prove is a fact. Something people can disagree about is an opinion."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Feit – dit kan bewys word. (b) Mening – dit is Lerato se gevoel, en ander mense, soos Pieter, dink anders.","en":"(a) Fact – it can be proved. (b) Opinion – it is Lerato’s feeling, and other people, like Pieter, think differently."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Woord in konteks","en":"A word in context"},"problem":{"af":"Wat beteken *oes* in die sin: *Ná ses weke was die spinasie groot genoeg om te oes.*?","en":"What does *oes* mean in the sentence: *Ná ses weke was die spinasie groot genoeg om te oes.*?"},"steps":[{"af":"Lees die sin en die sin daarna: die spinasie was **groot genoeg**, en toe het die kinders **bossies spinasie verkoop**.","en":"Read the sentence and the one after it: the spinach was **big enough**, and then the children **sold bunches of spinach**."},{"af":"Om spinasie te verkoop, moes hulle dit eers in die tuin afsny of pluk.","en":"To sell the spinach, they first had to cut or pick it in the garden."},{"af":"Toets jou antwoord: sit dit in die plek van *oes*: *groot genoeg om te pluk*. Dit maak sin.","en":"Test your answer: put it in place of *oes*: *groot genoeg om te pluk* (big enough to pick). It makes sense."}],"answer":{"af":"*Oes* beteken om plante of vrugte wat gereed is, te pluk of af te sny sodat jy dit kan gebruik.","en":"*Oes* means to harvest: to pick or cut plants or fruit that are ready so that you can use them."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat was agter die skoolsaal voordat die kinders die tuin gemaak het?","en":"What was behind the school hall before the children made the garden?"},"options":[{"af":"’n ou tuinslang","en":"an old hosepipe"},{"af":"klippe en onkruid","en":"stones and weeds"},{"af":"spinasie en wortels","en":"spinach and carrots"},{"af":"leë melkbottels","en":"empty milk bottles"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die eerste sin sê: *Verlede jaar was die stuk grond agter die skoolsaal net klippe en onkruid.* Die ander dinge kom eers later in die storie.","en":"The first sentence says: *Verlede jaar was die stuk grond agter die skoolsaal net klippe en onkruid.* (Last year the piece of ground behind the hall was just stones and weeds.) The other things only appear later in the story."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter vraag is ’n **afleidingsvraag**?","en":"Which question is an **inferential question**?"},"options":[{"af":"Wat het die kinders geplant?","en":"Wat het die kinders geplant?"},{"af":"Hoeveel het ’n bossie spinasie gekos?","en":"Hoeveel het ’n bossie spinasie gekos?"},{"af":"Hoe het Pieter waarskynlik ná die eerste dag gevoel?","en":"Hoe het Pieter waarskynlik ná die eerste dag gevoel?"},{"af":"Wat het die kinders met die geld gekoop?","en":"Wat het die kinders met die geld gekoop?"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die teks sê nêrens hoe Pieter gevoel het nie. Jy moet dit aflei uit die leidraad dat sy hande vol blase was. Die antwoorde op die ander vrae staan reg in die teks.","en":"The text never says how Pieter felt. You must infer it from the clue that his hands were full of blisters. The answers to the other questions (what they planted, the price, what they bought) are written right in the text."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die sin *Spinasie is die lekkerste groente in die wêreld* is ’n feit.","en":"The sentence *Spinasie is die lekkerste groente in die wêreld* is a fact."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Dit is Lerato se **mening**. *Lekkerste* wys ’n gevoel, en Pieter stem nie saam nie – hy verkies wortels.","en":"False. It is Lerato’s **opinion**. *Lekkerste* (tastiest) shows a feeling, and Pieter does not agree – he prefers carrots."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die kinders het elke bossie spinasie vir ___ verkoop.","en":"The children sold each bunch of spinach for ___."},"answers":{"af":["R10","R 10","R10,00","R10.00"],"en":["R10","R 10","R10,00","R10.00"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["R5","R20","R6"],"en":["R5","R20","R6"]}},"explain":{"af":"Skandeer vir die bedrag: *Die kinders het bossies spinasie vir R10 elk … verkoop.* Die getal ses in die teks gaan oor die ses weke, nie oor geld nie.","en":"Scan for the amount: *Die kinders het bossies spinasie vir R10 elk … verkoop.* The number six in the text is about the six weeks, not about money."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken *blase* in die sin *Pieter se hande was vol blase*?","en":"What does *blase* mean in the sentence *Pieter se hande was vol blase*?"},"options":[{"af":"seer, opgeswelde kolle van harde werk","en":"sore, swollen spots from hard work"},{"af":"klein gaatjies wat hy in die grond gemaak het","en":"small holes he made in the ground"},{"af":"seepborrels van die tuinslang","en":"soap bubbles from the hosepipe"},{"af":"vuil, modderige kolle op sy vingers","en":"dirty, muddy marks on his fingers"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die vorige sin sê *Dit was harde werk*. As jy lank met ’n graaf werk, kry jy seer, opgeswelde kolle (blase) op jou hande. Die konteks wys dus dat dit nie borrels of modder is nie.","en":"The sentence before says *Dit was harde werk* (It was hard work). If you dig with a spade for a long time, you get sore, swollen spots (blisters) on your hands. The context shows it is not bubbles or mud."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **hoofgedagte** van die teks?","en":"What is the **main idea** of the text?"},"options":[{"af":"Pieter hou meer van wortels as van spinasie.","en":"Pieter likes carrots more than spinach."},{"af":"Melkbottels is goeie gieters vir ’n tuin.","en":"Milk bottles make good watering cans for a garden."},{"af":"Spinasie kan ná ses weke geoes word.","en":"Spinach can be harvested after six weeks."},{"af":"’n Klas het saam ’n groentetuin gemaak en daarmee geld ingesamel.","en":"A class made a vegetable garden together and raised money with it."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die hoofgedagte vertel waaroor die **hele** teks gaan. Die ander drie is net klein besonderhede wat in een sin of twee voorkom.","en":"The main idea tells what the **whole** text is about. The other three are only small details that appear in a sentence or two."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke leesvaardigheid by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each reading skill to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"vooruitskou","en":"previewing (*vooruitskou*)"},"r":{"af":"kyk na die titel en prente voor jy lees","en":"look at the title and pictures before you read"}},{"l":{"af":"vluglees","en":"skimming (*vluglees*)"},"r":{"af":"lees vinnig vir die hoofgedagte","en":"read quickly for the main idea"}},{"l":{"af":"skandeer","en":"scanning (*skandeer*)"},"r":{"af":"soek vinnig na een spesifieke feit","en":"search quickly for one specific fact"}},{"l":{"af":"aflei","en":"inferring (*aflei*)"},"r":{"af":"lees tussen die reëls met leidrade","en":"read between the lines using clues"}},{"l":{"af":"aanhaal","en":"quoting (*aanhaal*)"},"r":{"af":"skryf die presiese woorde uit die teks oor","en":"copy the exact words from the text"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke vaardigheid het ’n ander doel: vooruitskou voor jy lees, vluglees vir die groot prentjie, skandeer vir een feit, aflei vir wat nie direk gesê word nie, en aanhaal wanneer die vraag die presiese woorde wil hê.","en":"Each skill has a different purpose: preview before you read, skim for the big picture, scan for one fact, infer what is not said directly, and quote when the question wants the exact words."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom het Pieter “net gelag” toe Lerato sê spinasie is die lekkerste groente?","en":"Why did Pieter “just laugh” when Lerato said spinach is the tastiest vegetable?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy was te moeg ná die harde werk om te praat.","en":"He was too tired after the hard work to talk."},{"af":"Hy het nie saamgestem nie, want hy verkies wortels.","en":"He did not agree, because he prefers carrots."},{"af":"Hy het gedink Lerato maak ’n grap oor die geld.","en":"He thought Lerato was making a joke about the money."},{"af":"Hy was bly dat al die spinasie verkoop is.","en":"He was glad that all the spinach was sold."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die volgende sin gee die leidraad: *Hy het nog altyd wortels verkies.* Hy het dus nie met Lerato saamgestem nie, maar wou nie stry nie.","en":"The next sentence gives the clue: *Hy het nog altyd wortels verkies.* (He has always preferred carrots.) So he did not agree with Lerato, but did not want to argue."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n ___ is wat iemand dink of voel, en jy kan dit nie bewys nie.","en":"An ___ is what someone thinks or feels, and you cannot prove it."},"answers":{"af":["mening"],"en":["opinion","mening"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["feit","hoofgedagte","opsomming"],"en":["fact","main idea","summary"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n **Mening** is ’n persoonlike gevoel of gedagte. ’n **Feit** kan wel bewys word.","en":"An **opinion** (*mening*) is a personal feeling or thought. A **fact** (*feit*) can be proved."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Wanneer jy **skandeer**, soek jy vinnig na spesifieke inligting soos ’n naam of ’n getal.","en":"When you **scan** (*skandeer*), you search quickly for specific information such as a name or a number."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Skandeer is om jou oë oor die teks te laat gly totdat jy die woord of getal kry wat jy soek, sonder om alles weer te lees.","en":"True. Scanning means letting your eyes slide over the text until you find the word or number you need, without reading everything again."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vraag: *Waarom het die kinders melkbottels gebring?* Watter antwoord is die **beste**?","en":"Question: *Waarom het die kinders melkbottels gebring?* (Why did the children bring milk bottles?) Which answer is the **best**?"},"options":[{"af":"Gieters.","en":"Gieters."},{"af":"Elke leerder het ’n leë melkbottel van die huis af gebring.","en":"Elke leerder het ’n leë melkbottel van die huis af gebring."},{"af":"Hulle het die bottels as gieters gebruik om die beddings nat te gooi.","en":"Hulle het die bottels as gieters gebruik om die beddings nat te gooi."},{"af":"Want hulle wou melk drink.","en":"Want hulle wou melk drink."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die beste antwoord is ’n volsin wat die vraag regtig beantwoord. *Gieters* is nie ’n volsin nie, die tweede antwoord is net uit die teks oorgeskryf en sê nie **waarom** nie, en die laaste een is nie waar nie.","en":"The best answer is a full sentence that really answers the question. *Gieters* is not a full sentence, the second answer is just copied from the text and does not say **why**, and the last one is not true."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is ’n **feit**?","en":"Which sentence is a **fact**?"},"options":[{"af":"Die tuin is die mooiste plek by die skool.","en":"Die tuin is die mooiste plek by die skool."},{"af":"Wortels smaak beter as uie.","en":"Wortels smaak beter as uie."},{"af":"Tuinmaak is die lekkerste stokperdjie.","en":"Tuinmaak is die lekkerste stokperdjie."},{"af":"Die kinders het nuwe saad gekoop.","en":"Die kinders het nuwe saad gekoop."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Dat die kinders saad gekoop het, kan nagegaan word, so dit is ’n feit. *Mooiste, beter* en *lekkerste* wys menings waaroor mense kan verskil.","en":"That the children bought seed can be checked, so it is a fact. *Mooiste* (prettiest), *beter* (better) and *lekkerste* (nicest) show opinions people can disagree about."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voor jy ’n teks lees, kyk jy na die titel en die prente. Dit heet ___.","en":"Before you read a text, you look at the title and the pictures. This is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["vooruitskou"],"en":["previewing","preview","vooruitskou"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["skandeer","opsomming","vluglees"],"en":["scanning","summarising","skimming"]}},"explain":{"af":"**Vooruitskou** gebeur **voor** jy lees: jy voorspel waaroor die teks gaan. Vluglees en skandeer doen jy terwyl jy die teks self lees.","en":"**Previewing** (*vooruitskou*) happens **before** you read: you predict what the text is about. Skimming and scanning are done while reading the text itself."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat moes die kinders doen **voordat** hulle kon plant?","en":"What did the children have to do **before** they could plant?"},"options":[{"af":"die klippe uithaal en die grond omspit","en":"take out the stones and dig over the soil"},{"af":"die spinasie oes en verkoop","en":"harvest and sell the spinach"},{"af":"’n tuinslang en nuwe saad koop","en":"buy a hosepipe and new seed"},{"af":"die beddings elke oggend natgooi","en":"water the beds every morning"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Let op die volgorde-woorde: *Eers moes hulle die klippe uithaal en die grond omspit … Daarna het hulle … geplant.* Die ander dinge het eers ná die plant gebeur.","en":"Notice the order words: *Eers* (first) they had to remove the stones and dig over the soil … *Daarna* (after that) they planted. The other things only happened after planting."}}]},{"id":"afr5-t1-selfstandige-naamwoorde","title":{"af":"Selfstandige naamwoorde, meervoude en verkleinwoorde","en":"Nouns, plurals and diminutives"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die soorte selfstandige naamwoorde kan herken en die regte meervoud, verkleinwoord en manlike of vroulike vorm van woorde kan skryf.","en":"You will be able to recognise the kinds of nouns and write the correct plural, diminutive and masculine or feminine form of Afrikaans words."},"summary":{"af":"## Soorte selfstandige naamwoorde\n\n’n **Selfstandige naamwoord** is ’n naam vir ’n mens, dier, plek, ding of idee.\n\n| Soort | Wat is dit? | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Soortnaam** | ’n gewone naam vir enige een van ’n soort | *seun, hond, stad, boom* |\n| **Eienaam** | die naam van een spesifieke mens, dier of plek; altyd ’n **hoofletter** | *Sipho, Bloemfontein, die Oranjerivier* |\n| **Versamelnaam** | een woord vir ’n hele groep | *’n trop beeste, ’n swerm bye, ’n span spelers* |\n| **Abstrakte naamwoord** | iets wat jy nie kan sien of vashou nie, soos ’n gevoel of idee | *liefde, vreugde, moed, vriendskap* |\n\nBaie abstrakte naamwoorde eindig op **-heid, -skap** of **-te**: *goedheid, vriendskap, lengte*.\n\n## Meervoude\n\n**Enkelvoud** beteken een; **meervoud** beteken meer as een. Die meeste woorde kry **-e** of **-s**.\n\n- **-e:** *hond → honde, boek → boeke*\n- **Lang klank – twee klinkers word een:** *boom → bome, skaap → skape, muur → mure*\n- **Kort klank – die medeklinker verdubbel:** *kat → katte, bus → busse, pen → penne*\n- **f word w:** *brief → briewe, duif → duiwe*\n- **-s** by woorde op **-el, -er, -em, -en, -ie**: *tafel → tafels, besem → besems, koppie → koppies*\n- **’s** by woorde op ’n enkele klinker: *ma → ma’s, foto → foto’s*\n- **-ers:** *kind → kinders, ei → eiers, kalf → kalwers*\n- **-ens:** *bed → beddens*\n\nWaarom een *o* in *bome* maar twee *t*’s in *katte*? In *bo-me* eindig die lettergreep op die klinker, en dan klink een *o* klaar lank. In *kat-te* hou die dubbele *t* die *a* kort.\n\n**Onreëlmatige meervoude** volg nie die reëls nie. Leer hulle uit jou kop:\n\n| Enkelvoud | Meervoud |\n|---|---|\n| skip | skepe |\n| stad | stede |\n| dag | dae |\n| pad | paaie |\n| oog | oë |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *boome* en *kate* is verkeerd. Sê die woord hardop: ’n **lang** klank kry een klinker (*bome*), ’n **kort** klank kry ’n dubbele medeklinker (*katte*).\n\n## Verkleinwoorde\n\n’n **Verkleinwoord** noem iets kleins: *’n hondjie, ’n boompie*. Kyk na die **laaste klank** van die woord:\n\n| Woord eindig op … | Uitgang | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| -d, -t | **-jie** | *hond → hondjie, kat → katjie* |\n| -m ná ’n lang klank of medeklinker | **-pie** | *boom → boompie, arm → armpie* |\n| ’n klinker, of -l, -n, -r ná ’n lang klank | **-tjie** | *koei → koeitjie, stoel → stoeltjie, deur → deurtjie* |\n| -k, -p, -s, -f, -g | **-ie** | *boek → boekie, huis → huisie* |\n| kort klank + -l, -m, -n, -r, -ng | **-etjie** | *bal → balletjie, son → sonnetjie, ring → ringetjie* |\n| -ing of -ang aan die einde van ’n langer woord | **-kie** (*ng* word *nk*) | *koning → koninkie, piesang → piesankie* |\n\nNá ’n kort klank verdubbel die medeklinker ook voor *-ie*: *kop → koppie, vis → vissie*. Die meervoud van ’n verkleinwoord kry altyd **-s**: *hondjies, boompies*.\n\n## Manlik en vroulik\n\nParty woorde het ’n aparte **manlike** en **vroulike** vorm:\n\n- **’n Heeltemal ander woord:** *seun – dogter, pa – ma, oom – tante, haan – hen, bul – koei, ram – ooi*\n- **-in:** *koning – koningin, vriend – vriendin, leeu – leeuin*\n- **-es:** *onderwyser – onderwyseres, prins – prinses, sanger – sangeres*\n\n> **Onthou:** As jy die vroulike vorm gebruik, verander die voornaamwoord ook: *die koning en **sy** kroon* → *die koningin en **haar** kroon*.","en":"## Kinds of nouns\n\nA **noun** (*selfstandige naamwoord*) is a name for a person, animal, place, thing or idea.\n\n| Kind | What is it? | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Common noun** (*soortnaam*) | an ordinary name for any one of a kind | *seun* (boy), *hond* (dog), *stad* (city), *boom* (tree) |\n| **Proper noun** (*eienaam*) | the name of one particular person, animal or place; always a **capital letter** | *Sipho, Bloemfontein, die Oranjerivier* |\n| **Collective noun** (*versamelnaam*) | one word for a whole group | *’n trop beeste* (a herd of cattle), *’n swerm bye* (a swarm of bees), *’n span spelers* (a team of players) |\n| **Abstract noun** (*abstrakte naamwoord*) | something you cannot see or hold, such as a feeling or idea | *liefde* (love), *vreugde* (joy), *moed* (courage), *vriendskap* (friendship) |\n\nMany abstract nouns end in **-heid, -skap** or **-te**: *goedheid* (goodness), *vriendskap* (friendship), *lengte* (length).\n\n## Plurals (*meervoude*)\n\n**Singular** (*enkelvoud*) means one; **plural** (*meervoud*) means more than one. Most words add **-e** or **-s**.\n\n- **-e:** *hond → honde, boek → boeke*\n- **Long sound – two vowels become one:** *boom → bome* (tree), *skaap → skape* (sheep), *muur → mure* (wall)\n- **Short sound – the consonant doubles:** *kat → katte, bus → busse, pen → penne*\n- **f becomes w:** *brief → briewe* (letter), *duif → duiwe* (pigeon)\n- **-s** for words ending in **-el, -er, -em, -en, -ie**: *tafel → tafels, besem → besems* (broom), *koppie → koppies* (cup)\n- **’s** for words ending in a single vowel: *ma → ma’s, foto → foto’s*\n- **-ers:** *kind → kinders* (child), *ei → eiers* (egg), *kalf → kalwers* (calf)\n- **-ens:** *bed → beddens*\n\nWhy one *o* in *bome* but two *t*’s in *katte*? In *bo-me* the syllable ends in the vowel, so one *o* already sounds long. In *kat-te* the double *t* keeps the *a* short.\n\n**Irregular plurals** do not follow the rules. Learn them by heart:\n\n| Singular | Plural |\n|---|---|\n| *skip* (ship) | *skepe* |\n| *stad* (city) | *stede* |\n| *dag* (day) | *dae* |\n| *pad* (road) | *paaie* |\n| *oog* (eye) | *oë* |\n\n> **Common mistake:** *boome* and *kate* are wrong. Say the word aloud: a **long** sound gets one vowel (*bome*), a **short** sound gets a double consonant (*katte*).\n\n## Diminutives (*verkleinwoorde*)\n\nA **diminutive** names something small: *’n hondjie* (a little dog), *’n boompie* (a little tree). Look at the **last sound** of the word:\n\n| Word ends in … | Ending | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| -d, -t | **-jie** | *hond → hondjie, kat → katjie* |\n| -m after a long sound or a consonant | **-pie** | *boom → boompie, arm → armpie* |\n| a vowel, or -l, -n, -r after a long sound | **-tjie** | *koei → koeitjie* (cow), *stoel → stoeltjie* (chair), *deur → deurtjie* (door) |\n| -k, -p, -s, -f, -g | **-ie** | *boek → boekie, huis → huisie* |\n| short sound + -l, -m, -n, -r, -ng | **-etjie** | *bal → balletjie, son → sonnetjie* (sun), *ring → ringetjie* |\n| -ing or -ang at the end of a longer word | **-kie** (*ng* becomes *nk*) | *koning → koninkie* (king), *piesang → piesankie* (banana) |\n\nAfter a short sound the consonant also doubles before *-ie*: *kop → koppie, vis → vissie*. The plural of a diminutive always adds **-s**: *hondjies, boompies*.\n\n## Masculine and feminine (*manlik en vroulik*)\n\nSome words have a separate **masculine** and **feminine** form:\n\n- **A completely different word:** *seun – dogter* (son – daughter), *pa – ma, oom – tante* (uncle – aunt), *haan – hen* (rooster – hen), *bul – koei* (bull – cow), *ram – ooi* (ram – ewe)\n- **-in:** *koning – koningin* (king – queen), *vriend – vriendin* (friend), *leeu – leeuin* (lion – lioness)\n- **-es:** *onderwyser – onderwyseres* (teacher), *prins – prinses* (prince – princess), *sanger – sangeres* (singer)\n\n> **Remember:** When you use the feminine form, the pronoun changes too: *die koning en **sy** kroon* (the king and his crown) → *die koningin en **haar** kroon* (the queen and her crown)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Selfstandige naamwoord","en":"Noun (selfstandige naamwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Naam vir ’n mens, dier, plek, ding of idee, soos ‘seun’ of ‘vreugde’.","en":"A name for a person, animal, place, thing or idea, e.g. ‘seun’ (boy) or ‘vreugde’ (joy)."}},{"term":{"af":"Soortnaam","en":"Common noun (soortnaam)"},"def":{"af":"’n Gewone naam vir enige mens of ding van ’n soort; dit begin met ’n kleinletter.","en":"An ordinary name for any person or thing of a kind; it starts with a small letter."}},{"term":{"af":"Eienaam","en":"Proper noun (eienaam)"},"def":{"af":"Die naam van een spesifieke mens, dier of plek, wat altyd met ’n hoofletter begin.","en":"The name of one particular person, animal or place, which always starts with a capital letter."}},{"term":{"af":"Versamelnaam","en":"Collective noun (versamelnaam)"},"def":{"af":"Een woord vir ’n hele groep, soos ‘trop’ of ‘swerm’.","en":"One word for a whole group, such as ‘trop’ (herd) or ‘swerm’ (swarm)."}},{"term":{"af":"Abstrakte selfstandige naamwoord","en":"Abstract noun (abstrakte selfstandige naamwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Naam vir iets wat jy nie kan sien of aanraak nie, soos ‘liefde’ of ‘moed’.","en":"A name for something you cannot see or touch, such as ‘liefde’ (love) or ‘moed’ (courage)."}},{"term":{"af":"Enkelvoud","en":"Singular (enkelvoud)"},"def":{"af":"Die vorm van ’n woord vir net een: ‘boom’.","en":"The form of a word for only one: ‘boom’ (tree)."}},{"term":{"af":"Meervoud","en":"Plural (meervoud)"},"def":{"af":"Die vorm van ’n woord vir meer as een: ‘bome, katte, tafels’.","en":"The form of a word for more than one: ‘bome, katte, tafels’."}},{"term":{"af":"Onreëlmatige meervoud","en":"Irregular plural (onreëlmatige meervoud)"},"def":{"af":"’n Meervoud wat nie die gewone reëls volg nie, soos ‘skip → skepe’ en ‘stad → stede’.","en":"A plural that does not follow the normal rules, such as ‘skip → skepe’ (ships) and ‘stad → stede’ (cities)."}},{"term":{"af":"Verkleinwoord","en":"Diminutive (verkleinwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord vir ’n klein ding, gemaak met ’n uitgang soos ‘-jie, -pie, -tjie, -ie, -etjie’ of ‘-kie’.","en":"A word for a small thing, made with an ending such as ‘-jie, -pie, -tjie, -ie, -etjie’ or ‘-kie’."}},{"term":{"af":"Manlik en vroulik","en":"Masculine and feminine (manlik en vroulik)"},"def":{"af":"Die vorm van ’n woord vir ’n manlike of ’n vroulike mens of dier, soos ‘haan’ en ‘hen’.","en":"The form of a word for a male or a female person or animal, such as ‘haan’ (rooster) and ‘hen’."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Meervoude volgens die reëls","en":"Plurals by the rules"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die meervoud van *skaap, bus, besem* en *kalf*.","en":"Write the plural of *skaap* (sheep), *bus, besem* (broom) and *kalf* (calf)."},"steps":[{"af":"*skaap* het ’n lang klank met twee a’s. Een a val weg en dit kry -e: *skape*.","en":"*skaap* has a long sound written with two a’s. One a falls away and it adds -e: *skape*."},{"af":"*bus* het ’n kort klank, so die s verdubbel voor die -e: *busse*.","en":"*bus* has a short sound, so the s doubles before the -e: *busse*."},{"af":"*besem* eindig op -em, so dit kry net -s: *besems*.","en":"*besem* ends in -em, so it just adds -s: *besems*."},{"af":"*kalf* kry -ers, en die f word w: *kalwers*.","en":"*kalf* adds -ers, and the f becomes w: *kalwers*."}],"answer":{"af":"skape, busse, besems, kalwers","en":"*skape, busse, besems, kalwers*"}},{"title":{"af":"Verkleinwoorde","en":"Diminutives"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die verkleinwoord van *kat, boom, son* en *boek*.","en":"Write the diminutive of *kat* (cat), *boom* (tree), *son* (sun) and *boek* (book)."},"steps":[{"af":"*kat* eindig op -t, so dit kry -jie: *katjie*.","en":"*kat* ends in -t, so it takes -jie: *katjie*."},{"af":"*boom* eindig op -m ná ’n lang klank, so dit kry -pie: *boompie*.","en":"*boom* ends in -m after a long sound, so it takes -pie: *boompie*."},{"af":"*son* het ’n kort klank en eindig op -n. Die n verdubbel en dit kry -etjie: *sonnetjie*.","en":"*son* has a short sound and ends in -n. The n doubles and it takes -etjie: *sonnetjie*."},{"af":"*boek* eindig op -k, so dit kry -ie: *boekie*.","en":"*boek* ends in -k, so it takes -ie: *boekie*."}],"answer":{"af":"katjie, boompie, sonnetjie, boekie","en":"*katjie, boompie, sonnetjie, boekie*"}},{"title":{"af":"Maak die sin vroulik","en":"Make the sentence feminine"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die sin oor en gebruik die vroulike vorme: *Die koning en sy vriend het die prins gegroet.*","en":"Rewrite the sentence using the feminine forms: *Die koning en sy vriend het die prins gegroet.* (The king and his friend greeted the prince.)"},"steps":[{"af":"*koning* kry -in: *koningin*. *vriend* kry ook -in: *vriendin*.","en":"*koning* adds -in: *koningin* (queen). *vriend* also adds -in: *vriendin*."},{"af":"*prins* kry -es: *prinses*.","en":"*prins* adds -es: *prinses* (princess)."},{"af":"Die voornaamwoord *sy* (manlik) word *haar* (vroulik).","en":"The pronoun *sy* (his) becomes *haar* (her)."}],"answer":{"af":"Die koningin en haar vriendin het die prinses gegroet.","en":"*Die koningin en haar vriendin het die prinses gegroet.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Soorte naamwoorde in ’n sin","en":"Kinds of nouns in a sentence"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die sin: *Die span van Pretoria het met groot moed gespeel.* Noem die eienaam, die versamelnaam en die abstrakte naamwoord.","en":"Read the sentence: *Die span van Pretoria het met groot moed gespeel.* (The team from Pretoria played with great courage.) Name the proper noun, the collective noun and the abstract noun."},"steps":[{"af":"*Pretoria* is die naam van een spesifieke stad en het ’n hoofletter: eienaam.","en":"*Pretoria* is the name of one particular city and has a capital letter: proper noun."},{"af":"*span* is een woord vir ’n groep spelers: versamelnaam.","en":"*span* (team) is one word for a group of players: collective noun."},{"af":"*moed* kan jy nie sien of vashou nie; dit is ’n eienskap: abstrakte naamwoord.","en":"*moed* (courage) is something you cannot see or hold; it is a quality: abstract noun."}],"answer":{"af":"Eienaam: Pretoria. Versamelnaam: span. Abstrakte naamwoord: moed.","en":"Proper noun: *Pretoria*. Collective noun: *span*. Abstract noun: *moed*."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is ’n **abstrakte** selfstandige naamwoord?","en":"Which word is an **abstract** noun?"},"options":[{"af":"tafel","en":"tafel"},{"af":"vreugde","en":"vreugde"},{"af":"Lerato","en":"Lerato"},{"af":"trop","en":"trop"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Vreugde* is ’n gevoel; jy kan dit nie sien of vashou nie. *Tafel* is ’n soortnaam, *Lerato* ’n eienaam en *trop* ’n versamelnaam.","en":"*Vreugde* (joy) is a feeling; you cannot see or hold it. *Tafel* (table) is a common noun, *Lerato* a proper noun and *trop* (herd) a collective noun."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die meervoud van *skip*?","en":"What is the plural of *skip* (ship)?"},"options":[{"af":"skepe","en":"skepe"},{"af":"skippe","en":"skippe"},{"af":"skips","en":"skips"},{"af":"skipe","en":"skipe"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*skip → skepe* is ’n onreëlmatige meervoud: die i word e. Jy moet dit uit jou kop leer.","en":"*skip → skepe* is an irregular plural: the i becomes e. You have to learn it by heart."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: een bed, twee ___","en":"Complete: *een bed, twee* ___ (one bed, two beds)"},"answers":{"af":["beddens"],"en":["beddens"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["bedde","beds","bedders"],"en":["bedde","beds","bedders"]}},"explain":{"af":"*bed* kry die uitgang -ens, en die d verdubbel ná die kort klank: *beddens*.","en":"*bed* takes the ending -ens, and the d doubles after the short sound: *beddens*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die verkleinwoord van *son*?","en":"What is the diminutive of *son* (sun)?"},"options":[{"af":"sontjie","en":"sontjie"},{"af":"sonnie","en":"sonnie"},{"af":"sonjie","en":"sonjie"},{"af":"sonnetjie","en":"sonnetjie"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*son* het ’n kort klank en eindig op -n. Die n verdubbel en dit kry -etjie: *sonnetjie*.","en":"*son* has a short sound and ends in -n. The n doubles and it takes -etjie: *sonnetjie*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die vroulike vorm van *haan* is *hen*.","en":"The feminine form of *haan* (rooster) is *hen*."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. *Haan* en *hen* is twee heeltemal verskillende woorde vir die mannetjie en die wyfie.","en":"True. *Haan* and *hen* are two completely different words for the male and the female bird."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter sin is daar ’n **versamelnaam**?","en":"Which sentence contains a **collective noun**?"},"options":[{"af":"Die bye vlieg om die blomme.","en":"Die bye vlieg om die blomme."},{"af":"Die by sit op die rooi blom.","en":"Die by sit op die rooi blom."},{"af":"’n Swerm bye vlieg om die blomme.","en":"’n Swerm bye vlieg om die blomme."},{"af":"Die blomme in die tuin is mooi.","en":"Die blomme in die tuin is mooi."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Swerm* is een woord vir ’n hele groep bye, so dit is ’n versamelnaam. In die ander sinne is *bye, by* en *blomme* gewone soortname.","en":"*Swerm* (swarm) is one word for a whole group of bees, so it is a collective noun. In the other sentences *bye, by* and *blomme* (bees, bee, flowers) are ordinary common nouns."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke manlike woord by sy vroulike vorm.","en":"Match each masculine word to its feminine form."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"seun","en":"seun"},"r":{"af":"dogter","en":"dogter"}},{"l":{"af":"bul","en":"bul"},"r":{"af":"koei","en":"koei"}},{"l":{"af":"ram","en":"ram"},"r":{"af":"ooi","en":"ooi"}},{"l":{"af":"prins","en":"prins"},"r":{"af":"prinses","en":"prinses"}},{"l":{"af":"leeu","en":"leeu"},"r":{"af":"leeuin","en":"leeuin"}}],"explain":{"af":"*seun – dogter, bul – koei* en *ram – ooi* is heeltemal ander woorde. *Prins* kry -es (*prinses*) en *leeu* kry -in (*leeuin*).","en":"*seun – dogter* (son – daughter), *bul – koei* (bull – cow) and *ram – ooi* (ram – ewe) are completely different words. *Prins* adds -es (*prinses*) and *leeu* adds -in (*leeuin*, lioness)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die meervoud van *kalf*?","en":"What is the plural of *kalf* (calf)?"},"options":[{"af":"kalwers","en":"kalwers"},{"af":"kalwe","en":"kalwe"},{"af":"kalfs","en":"kalfs"},{"af":"kalwes","en":"kalwes"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*kalf* kry -ers, en die f word w: *kalwers*. Dit is net soos *kind → kinders* en *ei → eiers*.","en":"*kalf* adds -ers, and the f becomes w: *kalwers*. It works like *kind → kinders* and *ei → eiers*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die vroulike vorm van *onderwyser* is ___.","en":"The feminine form of *onderwyser* (teacher) is ___."},"answers":{"af":["onderwyseres"],"en":["onderwyseres"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["onderwyserin","onderwyservrou","onderwyseresse"],"en":["onderwyserin","onderwyservrou","onderwyseresse"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Onderwyser* kry -es: *onderwyseres*, net soos *sanger → sangeres*. *Onderwyseresse* is die meervoud, nie die vroulike vorm nie.","en":"*Onderwyser* adds -es: *onderwyseres*, just like *sanger → sangeres*. *Onderwyseresse* is the plural, not the feminine form."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die meervoud van *muur*?","en":"What is the plural of *muur* (wall)?"},"options":[{"af":"muure","en":"muure"},{"af":"murre","en":"murre"},{"af":"muurs","en":"muurs"},{"af":"mure","en":"mure"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*muur* het ’n lang klank met twee u’s. Een u val weg en dit kry -e: *mure*. In *mu-re* klink een u klaar lank.","en":"*muur* has a long sound written with two u’s. One u falls away and it adds -e: *mure*. In *mu-re* one u already sounds long."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Eienaam begin altyd met ’n kleinletter.","en":"A proper noun always starts with a small letter."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Eienaam, soos *Sipho* of *Bloemfontein*, begin altyd met ’n **hoofletter**. Soortname begin met ’n kleinletter.","en":"False. A proper noun, such as *Sipho* or *Bloemfontein*, always starts with a **capital letter**. Common nouns start with a small letter."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die verkleinwoord van *piesang*?","en":"What is the diminutive of *piesang* (banana)?"},"options":[{"af":"piesangetjie","en":"piesangetjie"},{"af":"piesankie","en":"piesankie"},{"af":"piesangie","en":"piesangie"},{"af":"piesangtjie","en":"piesangtjie"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*piesang* eindig op -ang aan die einde van ’n langer woord. Die *ng* word *nk* en dit kry -ie: *piesankie*, net soos *koning → koninkie*.","en":"*piesang* ends in -ang at the end of a longer word. The *ng* becomes *nk* and it takes -ie: *piesankie*, just like *koning → koninkie*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die verkleinwoord: boom → ___","en":"Write the diminutive: *boom* (tree) → ___"},"answers":{"af":["boompie"],"en":["boompie"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["boomtjie","boomie","bommetjie"],"en":["boomtjie","boomie","bommetjie"]}},"explain":{"af":"*boom* eindig op -m ná ’n lang klank, so dit kry -pie: *boompie*.","en":"*boom* ends in -m after a long sound, so it takes -pie: *boompie*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter sin is die meervoud **verkeerd**?","en":"In which sentence is the plural **wrong**?"},"options":[{"af":"Die kinders het eiers gekoop.","en":"Die kinders het eiers gekoop."},{"af":"Ons het drie dae lank gestap.","en":"Ons het drie dae lank gestap."},{"af":"Die skippe het in die hawe gelê.","en":"Die skippe het in die hawe gelê."},{"af":"Die boere het hul skape getel.","en":"Die boere het hul skape getel."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die meervoud van *skip* is *skepe*, nie *skippe* nie. *Kinders, eiers, dae* en *skape* is almal korrek.","en":"The plural of *skip* (ship) is *skepe*, not *skippe*. *Kinders, eiers, dae* and *skape* are all correct."}}]},{"id":"afr5-t1-lidwoorde-voornaamwoorde","title":{"af":"Lidwoorde en voornaamwoorde","en":"Articles and pronouns"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal *die* en *’n* reg kan gebruik en die regte persoonlike, besitlike, aanwysende en vraende voornaamwoord in ’n sin kan kies.","en":"You will be able to use *die* and *’n* correctly and choose the right personal, possessive, demonstrative and interrogative pronoun in a sentence."},"summary":{"af":"## Lidwoorde: *die* en *’n*\n\n’n **Lidwoord** staan voor ’n selfstandige naamwoord. Afrikaans het net twee:\n\n- **Bepaalde lidwoord – *die*:** vir ’n spesifieke ding wat ons reeds ken. Dit werk vir enkelvoud én meervoud: *die hond, die honde*.\n- **Onbepaalde lidwoord – *’n*:** vir enige een, nie ’n spesifieke een nie. Dit staan **net voor ’n enkelvoud**: *’n hond*. In die meervoud laat jy dit weg: *Daar speel honde in die park.*\n\nVergelyk: *Ek wil ’n appel hê* (enige appel) en *Ek wil die appel hê* (daardie een spesifieke appel). As ons iets vir die eerste keer noem, gebruik ons gewoonlik *’n*; daarna weet die leser watter een, en dan word dit *die*.\n\n> **Onthou:** *’n* kry nooit ’n hoofletter nie. Aan die begin van ’n sin kry die **volgende woord** die hoofletter: *’n Seekoei swem in die rivier.* Die afkappingsteken (’) wys dat letters weggelaat is – *’n* kom van *een*.\n\n## Persoonlike voornaamwoorde\n\n’n **Voornaamwoord** staan in die plek van ’n naamwoord, sodat ons nie dieselfde naam oor en oor herhaal nie: *Thabo is honger. **Hy** eet.*\n\nDie vorm hang daarvan af of die woord die **onderwerp** is (wie iets doen) of die **voorwerp** (aan wie dit gedoen word):\n\n| Persoon | Onderwerp | Voorwerp |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1ste persoon enkelvoud | ek | my |\n| 2de persoon enkelvoud | jy | jou |\n| 3de persoon manlik | hy | hom |\n| 3de persoon vroulik | sy | haar |\n| 3de persoon (ding) | dit | dit |\n| 1ste persoon meervoud | ons | ons |\n| 2de persoon meervoud | julle | julle |\n| 3de persoon meervoud | hulle | hulle |\n\n***Hy** sien **haar**. **Sy** sien **hom**.* Ná woorde soos *vir, met, by* en *van* gebruik jy die voorwerpsvorm: *vir hom, met haar, by my*. Vir ’n ouer persoon kan jy beleefd **u** sê: *Kan u my help, Oom?*\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *Ek het vir hy gesê* is verkeerd. Ná *vir* kom die voorwerpsvorm: *Ek het vir **hom** gesê.* Aan die begin van die sin staan die onderwerpsvorm: ***Hy** en ek gaan swem* (nie *Hom en my* nie).\n\n## Besitlike voornaamwoorde\n\n’n **Besitlike voornaamwoord** wys aan wie iets behoort.\n\n| Voor die naamwoord | Alleen, sonder naamwoord |\n|---|---|\n| my boek | Die boek is **myne**. |\n| jou pen | Die pen is **joune**. |\n| sy bal | Die bal is **syne**. |\n| haar tas | Die tas is **hare**. |\n| ons huis | Die huis is **ons s’n**. |\n| julle hond | Die hond is **julle s’n**. |\n| hulle motor | Die motor is **hulle s’n**. |\n\nBy ’n naam of ’n ander naamwoord gebruik jy **se**: *Thabo se fiets, die hond se bak*. Alleen word dit **s’n**: *Die fiets is Thabo s’n.* In gesprekke hoor jy dikwels *hulle se huis* of *ons se huis*, maar in jou skryfwerk is *hulle huis* en *ons huis* beter.\n\n## Aanwysende en vraende voornaamwoorde\n\n**Aanwysende voornaamwoorde** wys iets aan:\n\n- **hierdie** – vir iets naby jou: *Hierdie boek in my hand is myne.*\n- **daardie** – vir iets verder weg: *Daardie boek op die rak is joune.*\n\n**Vraende voornaamwoorde** vra ’n vraag:\n\n- **wie** – vir mense: *Wie klop aan die deur?*\n- **wat** – vir dinge: *Wat eet jy?*\n- **watter** – as jy uit ’n groep kies; dit staan voor ’n naamwoord: *Watter trui is joune?*\n- **wie se** – om te vra aan wie iets behoort: *Wie se tas is dit?*","en":"## Articles: *die* and *’n*\n\nAn **article** (*lidwoord*) stands before a noun. Afrikaans has only two:\n\n- **Definite article – *die*** (the): for a particular thing we already know. It works for singular and plural: *die hond, die honde* (the dog, the dogs).\n- **Indefinite article – *’n*** (a/an): for any one, not a particular one. It stands **only before a singular**: *’n hond* (a dog). In the plural you leave it out: *Daar speel honde in die park.* (Dogs are playing in the park.)\n\nCompare: *Ek wil ’n appel hê* (I want an apple – any apple) and *Ek wil die appel hê* (I want the apple – that particular one). When we mention something for the first time, we usually use *’n*; after that the reader knows which one, so it becomes *die*.\n\n> **Remember:** *’n* never gets a capital letter. At the start of a sentence the **next word** gets the capital: *’n Seekoei swem in die rivier.* (A hippo swims in the river.) The apostrophe (’) shows that letters were left out – *’n* comes from *een* (one).\n\n## Personal pronouns (*persoonlike voornaamwoorde*)\n\nA **pronoun** (*voornaamwoord*) takes the place of a noun, so that we don’t repeat the same name over and over: *Thabo is honger. **Hy** eet.* (Thabo is hungry. He eats.)\n\nThe form depends on whether the word is the **subject** (*onderwerp* – who does something) or the **object** (*voorwerp* – to whom it is done):\n\n| Person | Subject | Object |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1st person singular | *ek* (I) | *my* (me) |\n| 2nd person singular | *jy* (you) | *jou* (you) |\n| 3rd person masculine | *hy* (he) | *hom* (him) |\n| 3rd person feminine | *sy* (she) | *haar* (her) |\n| 3rd person (thing) | *dit* (it) | *dit* (it) |\n| 1st person plural | *ons* (we) | *ons* (us) |\n| 2nd person plural | *julle* (you) | *julle* (you) |\n| 3rd person plural | *hulle* (they) | *hulle* (them) |\n\n***Hy** sien **haar**. **Sy** sien **hom**.* (He sees her. She sees him.) After words like *vir, met, by* and *van* you use the object form: *vir hom, met haar, by my*. To an older person you can politely say **u**: *Kan u my help, Oom?* (Can you help me, Uncle?)\n\n> **Common mistake:** *Ek het vir hy gesê* is wrong. After *vir* comes the object form: *Ek het vir **hom** gesê.* (I told him.) At the start of the sentence you use the subject form: ***Hy** en ek gaan swem* (not *Hom en my*).\n\n## Possessive pronouns (*besitlike voornaamwoorde*)\n\nA **possessive pronoun** shows who something belongs to.\n\n| Before the noun | On its own, without a noun |\n|---|---|\n| *my boek* (my book) | *Die boek is **myne**.* (mine) |\n| *jou pen* (your pen) | *Die pen is **joune**.* (yours) |\n| *sy bal* (his ball) | *Die bal is **syne**.* (his) |\n| *haar tas* (her bag) | *Die tas is **hare**.* (hers) |\n| *ons huis* (our house) | *Die huis is **ons s’n**.* (ours) |\n| *julle hond* (your dog) | *Die hond is **julle s’n**.* (yours) |\n| *hulle motor* (their car) | *Die motor is **hulle s’n**.* (theirs) |\n\nWith a name or another noun you use **se** (’s): *Thabo se fiets* (Thabo’s bicycle), *die hond se bak* (the dog’s bowl). On its own it becomes **s’n**: *Die fiets is Thabo s’n.* (The bicycle is Thabo’s.) In conversation you often hear *hulle se huis* or *ons se huis*, but in your written work *hulle huis* and *ons huis* are better.\n\n## Demonstrative and interrogative pronouns\n\n**Demonstrative pronouns** (*aanwysende voornaamwoorde*) point something out:\n\n- **hierdie** (this) – for something near you: *Hierdie boek in my hand is myne.*\n- **daardie** (that) – for something further away: *Daardie boek op die rak is joune.*\n\n**Interrogative pronouns** (*vraende voornaamwoorde*) ask a question:\n\n- **wie** (who) – for people: *Wie klop aan die deur?*\n- **wat** (what) – for things: *Wat eet jy?*\n- **watter** (which) – when you choose from a group; it stands before a noun: *Watter trui is joune?*\n- **wie se** (whose) – to ask who something belongs to: *Wie se tas is dit?*"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Lidwoord","en":"Article (lidwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woordjie voor ’n selfstandige naamwoord: ‘die’ of ‘’n’.","en":"A small word before a noun: ‘die’ (the) or ‘’n’ (a/an)."}},{"term":{"af":"Bepaalde lidwoord","en":"Definite article (bepaalde lidwoord)"},"def":{"af":"Die lidwoord ‘die’, wat ’n spesifieke ding aandui wat ons reeds ken.","en":"The article ‘die’ (the), which points to a particular thing we already know."}},{"term":{"af":"Onbepaalde lidwoord","en":"Indefinite article (onbepaalde lidwoord)"},"def":{"af":"Die lidwoord ‘’n’, wat enige een aandui en net voor ’n enkelvoud staan.","en":"The article ‘’n’ (a/an), which means any one and stands only before a singular."}},{"term":{"af":"Voornaamwoord","en":"Pronoun (voornaamwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat in die plek van ’n selfstandige naamwoord staan, soos ‘hy’ of ‘dit’.","en":"A word that takes the place of a noun, such as ‘hy’ (he) or ‘dit’ (it)."}},{"term":{"af":"Persoonlike voornaamwoord","en":"Personal pronoun (persoonlike voornaamwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Voornaamwoord vir ’n persoon of ding, soos ‘ek, jy, hy, sy, ons, hulle’.","en":"A pronoun for a person or thing, such as ‘ek, jy, hy, sy, ons, hulle’ (I, you, he, she, we, they)."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderwerp","en":"Subject (onderwerp)"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon of ding wat in die sin iets doen, soos ‘hy’ in ‘Hy skop die bal’.","en":"The person or thing that does something in the sentence, like ‘hy’ in ‘Hy skop die bal’ (He kicks the ball)."}},{"term":{"af":"Voorwerp","en":"Object (voorwerp)"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon of ding aan wie iets gedoen word, soos ‘hom’ in ‘Ek sien hom’.","en":"The person or thing something is done to, like ‘hom’ in ‘Ek sien hom’ (I see him)."}},{"term":{"af":"Besitlike voornaamwoord","en":"Possessive pronoun (besitlike voornaamwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Voornaamwoord wat wys aan wie iets behoort, soos ‘my, haar, myne, joune’.","en":"A pronoun that shows who something belongs to, such as ‘my, haar, myne, joune’ (my, her, mine, yours)."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanwysende voornaamwoord","en":"Demonstrative pronoun (aanwysende voornaamwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Voornaamwoord wat iets aanwys: ‘hierdie’ (naby) of ‘daardie’ (ver).","en":"A pronoun that points something out: ‘hierdie’ (this – near) or ‘daardie’ (that – far)."}},{"term":{"af":"Vraende voornaamwoord","en":"Interrogative pronoun (vraende voornaamwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Voornaamwoord waarmee jy ’n vraag vra: ‘wie, wat, watter’.","en":"A pronoun you use to ask a question: ‘wie, wat, watter’ (who, what, which)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"*Die* of *’n*?","en":"*Die* or *’n*?"},"problem":{"af":"Vul *die* of *’n* in en let op die hoofletters: *___ olifant het by ons kamp verbygestap. ___ olifant was baie groot.*","en":"Fill in *die* or *’n* and watch the capital letters: *___ olifant het by ons kamp verbygestap. ___ olifant was baie groot.* (An elephant walked past our camp. The elephant was very big.)"},"steps":[{"af":"In die eerste sin noem ons die olifant vir die eerste keer – enige olifant. Dus: *’n*.","en":"In the first sentence we mention the elephant for the first time – any elephant. So: *’n*."},{"af":"*’n* kry nie ’n hoofletter nie, so die **O** van *olifant* kry die hoofletter: *’n Olifant*.","en":"*’n* does not take a capital letter, so the **O** of *olifant* gets the capital: *’n Olifant*."},{"af":"In die tweede sin weet ons reeds watter olifant dit is, so ons gebruik *die*. Dit begin die sin, so dit kry ’n hoofletter: *Die*.","en":"In the second sentence we already know which elephant it is, so we use *die*. It starts the sentence, so it gets a capital: *Die*."}],"answer":{"af":"’n Olifant het by ons kamp verbygestap. Die olifant was baie groot.","en":"*’n Olifant het by ons kamp verbygestap. Die olifant was baie groot.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Vervang met voornaamwoorde","en":"Replace with pronouns"},"problem":{"af":"Vervang die name en die naamwoord met voornaamwoorde: *Sipho het die bal vir Zanele gegee.*","en":"Replace the names and the noun with pronouns: *Sipho het die bal vir Zanele gegee.* (Sipho gave the ball to Zanele.)"},"steps":[{"af":"*Sipho* is ’n seun en die onderwerp (hy doen die gee): *Hy*.","en":"*Sipho* is a boy and the subject (he does the giving): *Hy* (he)."},{"af":"*die bal* is ’n ding: *dit*.","en":"*die bal* (the ball) is a thing: *dit* (it)."},{"af":"*Zanele* is ’n meisie en staan ná *vir*, so ons gebruik die voorwerpsvorm: *haar*.","en":"*Zanele* is a girl and comes after *vir*, so we use the object form: *haar* (her)."}],"answer":{"af":"Hy het dit vir haar gegee.","en":"*Hy het dit vir haar gegee.* (He gave it to her.)"}},{"title":{"af":"Besitlike voornaamwoorde wat alleen staan","en":"Possessive pronouns on their own"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf oor sodat die besitlike voornaamwoord alleen staan: (a) *Dit is my tas.* (b) *Dit is Lerato se fiets.* (c) *Dit is ons huis.*","en":"Rewrite so that the possessive pronoun stands on its own: (a) *Dit is my tas.* (b) *Dit is Lerato se fiets.* (c) *Dit is ons huis.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *my* word alleen *myne*: *Die tas is myne.*","en":"(a) *my* on its own becomes *myne* (mine): *Die tas is myne.*"},{"af":"(b) Lerato is ’n meisie, so *haar* word alleen *hare*. Jy kan ook *Lerato s’n* sê.","en":"(b) Lerato is a girl, so *haar* on its own becomes *hare* (hers). You can also say *Lerato s’n* (Lerato’s)."},{"af":"(c) *ons* word alleen *ons s’n*: *Die huis is ons s’n.*","en":"(c) *ons* on its own becomes *ons s’n* (ours): *Die huis is ons s’n.*"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Die tas is myne. (b) Die fiets is hare / Lerato s’n. (c) Die huis is ons s’n.","en":"(a) *Die tas is myne.* (b) *Die fiets is hare / Lerato s’n.* (c) *Die huis is ons s’n.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Vrae met vraende voornaamwoorde","en":"Questions with interrogative pronouns"},"problem":{"af":"Vra ’n vraag waarvan die vetgedrukte deel die antwoord is: (a) ***Fatima** het die prys gewen.* (b) *Ek wil die **rooi** appel hê.* (c) *Dit is **Ravi se** tas.*","en":"Ask a question to which the bold part is the answer: (a) ***Fatima** het die prys gewen.* (Fatima won the prize.) (b) *Ek wil die **rooi** appel hê.* (I want the red apple.) (c) *Dit is **Ravi se** tas.* (It is Ravi’s bag.)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die antwoord is ’n persoon, so ons gebruik *wie*: *Wie het die prys gewen?*","en":"(a) The answer is a person, so we use *wie* (who): *Wie het die prys gewen?*"},{"af":"(b) Die antwoord kies een appel uit ’n groep, so ons gebruik *watter* voor die naamwoord: *Watter appel wil jy hê?*","en":"(b) The answer chooses one apple from a group, so we use *watter* (which) before the noun: *Watter appel wil jy hê?*"},{"af":"(c) Die antwoord sê aan wie die tas behoort, so ons gebruik *wie se*: *Wie se tas is dit?*","en":"(c) The answer says who the bag belongs to, so we use *wie se* (whose): *Wie se tas is dit?*"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Wie het die prys gewen? (b) Watter appel wil jy hê? (c) Wie se tas is dit?","en":"(a) *Wie het die prys gewen?* (b) *Watter appel wil jy hê?* (c) *Wie se tas is dit?*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter sin is die lidwoorde korrek gebruik?","en":"In which sentence are the articles used correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Daar wei ’n koei en twee kalwers in die veld.","en":"Daar wei ’n koei en twee kalwers in die veld."},{"af":"Daar wei ’n koei en ’n twee kalwers in die veld.","en":"Daar wei ’n koei en ’n twee kalwers in die veld."},{"af":"Daar wei ’n koeie en twee kalwers in die veld.","en":"Daar wei ’n koeie en twee kalwers in die veld."},{"af":"Daar wei die ’n koei en twee kalwers in die veld.","en":"Daar wei die ’n koei en twee kalwers in die veld."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*’n* staan net voor ’n enkelvoud (*’n koei*). Voor ’n meervoud soos *kalwers* of *koeie* val dit weg, en *die* en *’n* staan nooit saam nie.","en":"*’n* stands only before a singular (*’n koei* – a cow). Before a plural like *kalwers* (calves) or *koeie* (cows) it falls away, and *die* and *’n* never stand together."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Ma het ___ gevra om die skottelgoed te was.* (Johan)","en":"Complete: *Ma het ___ gevra om die skottelgoed te was.* (Mom asked ___ to wash the dishes.) (Johan)"},"options":[{"af":"hy","en":"hy"},{"af":"sy","en":"sy"},{"af":"hom","en":"hom"},{"af":"hulle","en":"hulle"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Johan is ’n seun en hier is hy die **voorwerp** (Ma vra hom), so ons gebruik *hom*, nie *hy* nie.","en":"Johan is a boy and here he is the **object** (Mom asks him), so we use *hom* (him), not *hy* (he)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Ek en my broer speel saam. ___ speel buite in die son.","en":"*Ek en my broer speel saam.* (My brother and I play together.) ___ *speel buite in die son.* (___ play outside in the sun.)"},"answers":{"af":["Ons"],"en":["Ons"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Hulle","Julle","Ek"],"en":["Hulle","Julle","Ek"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Ek en my broer* sluit jouself in, so dit is die 1ste persoon meervoud: *Ons*.","en":"*Ek en my broer* (my brother and I) includes yourself, so it is the 1st person plural: *Ons* (we)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Ons gebruik *daardie* vir iets wat naby ons is.","en":"We use *daardie* for something that is near us."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. *Hierdie* is vir iets naby jou; *daardie* is vir iets verder weg.","en":"False. *Hierdie* (this) is for something near you; *daardie* (that) is for something further away."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Is hierdie potlood ___, Liam?*","en":"Complete: *Is hierdie potlood ___, Liam?* (Is this pencil ___, Liam?)"},"options":[{"af":"jou","en":"jou"},{"af":"jy","en":"jy"},{"af":"jouse","en":"jouse"},{"af":"joune","en":"joune"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Daar kom nie ’n naamwoord ná die besitlike voornaamwoord nie; dit staan alleen. Dan word *jou* in sy plek *joune*.","en":"No noun follows the possessive pronoun; it stands on its own. Then *jou* (your) becomes *joune* (yours)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *___ van die twee rokke gaan jy na die partytjie dra?*","en":"Complete: *___ van die twee rokke gaan jy na die partytjie dra?* (___ of the two dresses are you going to wear to the party?)"},"options":[{"af":"Wie","en":"Wie"},{"af":"Watter","en":"Watter"},{"af":"Wat","en":"Wat"},{"af":"Waar","en":"Waar"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Jy kies een rok uit ’n groep van twee, so jy gebruik *watter*. *Wie* is vir mense en *waar* vra na ’n plek.","en":"You choose one dress from a group of two, so you use *watter* (which). *Wie* (who) is for people and *waar* (where) asks about a place."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die kinders het ’n hut gebou. Die hut is ___ s’n.","en":"*Die kinders het ’n hut gebou.* (The children built a hut.) *Die hut is ___ s’n.* (The hut is ___.)"},"answers":{"af":["hulle","hul"],"en":["hulle","hul"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["hom","haar","julle"],"en":["hom","haar","julle"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Die kinders* is meer as een persoon en ons praat oor hulle (3de persoon meervoud): *hulle s’n*.","en":"*Die kinders* (the children) are more than one person and we are talking about them (3rd person plural): *hulle s’n* (theirs)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke soort woord by die regte voorbeeld.","en":"Match each kind of word to the correct example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"bepaalde lidwoord","en":"definite article"},"r":{"af":"die","en":"die"}},{"l":{"af":"onbepaalde lidwoord","en":"indefinite article"},"r":{"af":"’n","en":"’n"}},{"l":{"af":"besitlike voornaamwoord","en":"possessive pronoun"},"r":{"af":"myne","en":"myne"}},{"l":{"af":"aanwysende voornaamwoord","en":"demonstrative pronoun"},"r":{"af":"daardie","en":"daardie"}},{"l":{"af":"vraende voornaamwoord","en":"interrogative pronoun"},"r":{"af":"watter","en":"watter"}}],"explain":{"af":"*Die* en *’n* is die twee lidwoorde. *Myne* wys besit, *daardie* wys iets aan en *watter* vra ’n vraag.","en":"*Die* (the) and *’n* (a) are the two articles. *Myne* (mine) shows possession, *daardie* (that) points something out and *watter* (which) asks a question."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Die meisies het ___ eie kos skool toe gebring.*","en":"Complete: *Die meisies het ___ eie kos skool toe gebring.* (The girls brought ___ own food to school.)"},"options":[{"af":"haar","en":"haar"},{"af":"julle","en":"julle"},{"af":"hulle","en":"hulle"},{"af":"sy","en":"sy"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Die meisies* is meervoud, so die besitlike voornaamwoord is *hulle* (hulle eie kos). *Haar* en *sy* is enkelvoud.","en":"*Die meisies* (the girls) is plural, so the possessive pronoun is *hulle* (their own food). *Haar* and *sy* are singular."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die lidwoord *’n* gebruik ons net voor ’n enkelvoudige selfstandige naamwoord.","en":"We use the article *’n* only before a singular noun."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Ons sê *’n hond*, maar in die meervoud val *’n* weg: *honde*, nie *’n honde* nie.","en":"True. We say *’n hond* (a dog), but in the plural *’n* falls away: *honde* (dogs), not *’n honde*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is korrek?","en":"Which sentence is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Hom en ek gaan môre swem.","en":"Hom en ek gaan môre swem."},{"af":"Hy en ek gaan môre swem.","en":"Hy en ek gaan môre swem."},{"af":"Hy en my gaan môre swem.","en":"Hy en my gaan môre swem."},{"af":"Hom en my gaan môre swem.","en":"Hom en my gaan môre swem."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Hy en ek* is saam die **onderwerp** van die sin, so albei moet in die onderwerpsvorm wees: *hy* en *ek*.","en":"*Hy en ek* (he and I) together are the **subject** of the sentence, so both must be in the subject form: *hy* and *ek*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *___ boek hier in my hand is baie oud.*","en":"Complete: *___ boek hier in my hand is baie oud.* (___ book here in my hand is very old.)"},"options":[{"af":"Hierdie","en":"Hierdie"},{"af":"Daardie","en":"Daardie"},{"af":"Watter","en":"Watter"},{"af":"Wie se","en":"Wie se"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die boek is naby (*hier in my hand*), so ons gebruik *hierdie*. *Daardie* is vir iets wat ver is.","en":"The book is near (*hier in my hand*), so we use *hierdie* (this). *Daardie* (that) is for something far away."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vul die vraende voornaamwoord in: ___ se tas lê op die vloer?","en":"Fill in the interrogative pronoun: ___ *se tas lê op die vloer?* (___ bag is lying on the floor?)"},"answers":{"af":["Wie"],"en":["Wie"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Wat","Watter","Hoe"],"en":["Wat","Watter","Hoe"]}},"explain":{"af":"Om te vra aan wie iets behoort, gebruik ons *wie se*: *Wie se tas lê op die vloer?*","en":"To ask who something belongs to, we use *wie se* (whose): *Wie se tas lê op die vloer?*"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord in die sin is ’n **besitlike** voornaamwoord? *Sy het haar fiets by die skool gelos.*","en":"Which word in the sentence is a **possessive** pronoun? *Sy het haar fiets by die skool gelos.* (She left her bicycle at school.)"},"options":[{"af":"Sy","en":"Sy"},{"af":"die","en":"die"},{"af":"fiets","en":"fiets"},{"af":"haar","en":"haar"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Haar* wys aan wie die fiets behoort, so dit is besitlik. *Sy* is ’n persoonlike voornaamwoord (die onderwerp), *die* is ’n lidwoord en *fiets* is ’n naamwoord.","en":"*Haar* (her) shows who the bicycle belongs to, so it is possessive. *Sy* (she) is a personal pronoun (the subject), *die* is an article and *fiets* (bicycle) is a noun."}}]},{"id":"afr5-t1-werkwoorde-tye","title":{"af":"Werkwoorde en tye","en":"Verbs and tenses"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal hoof- en hulpwerkwoorde kan herken en sinne korrek in die teenwoordige, verlede en toekomende tyd kan skryf, ook met werkwoorde sonder *ge-*.","en":"You will be able to recognise main and auxiliary verbs and write sentences correctly in the present, past and future tense, including verbs without *ge-*."},"summary":{"af":"## Hoofwerkwoorde en hulpwerkwoorde\n\n’n **Werkwoord** sê wat iemand **doen** of wat **gebeur**: *hardloop, eet, skryf, reën*. Dit kan ook sê hoe iets **is**: *Die sop is warm.*\n\n- Die **hoofwerkwoord** dra die belangrikste betekenis: *Ek **skryf** ’n brief.*\n- ’n **Hulpwerkwoord** help die hoofwerkwoord. Dit sê iets oor die **tyd** of oor *moet, kan* of *wil*: ***het, sal, kan, moet, wil, mag***. *Ek **sal** môre ’n brief **skryf**.*\n\n’n Afrikaanse werkwoord bly dieselfde vir elke persoon: *ek loop, jy loop, hy loop, hulle loop*.\n\n## Die drie tye\n\n| Tyd | Hoe maak jy dit? | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Teenwoordige tyd** (nou) | werkwoord op die 2de plek | *Thabo **skop** die bal.* |\n| **Verlede tyd** (klaar gebeur) | **het** op die 2de plek + **ge-**werkwoord aan die einde | *Thabo **het** die bal **geskop**.* |\n| **Toekomende tyd** (gaan nog gebeur) | **sal** op die 2de plek + werkwoord aan die einde | *Thabo **sal** die bal **skop**.* |\n\nWoorde soos *gister* en *verlede week* wys na die verlede; *môre* en *volgende jaar* wys na die toekoms. As die sin met so ’n woord begin, bly *het* of *sal* op die 2de plek: ***Gister het** Thabo die bal geskop.*\n\nBegin die werkwoord met ’n *e*? Dan kry die *e* ná *ge-* ’n **deelteken**, sodat jy die klanke apart sê: *eet → geëet, eindig → geëindig*.\n\n> **Onthou:** Die verlede tyd het **twee dele** nodig: *het* + die *ge-*werkwoord. Skryf *Ek **het** gesing* – nie *Ek gesing* of *Ek het sing* nie.\n\n## Werkwoorde sonder ge-\n\nWerkwoorde wat met **be-, ge-, her-, ont-, ver-** of **er-** begin, kry **nie** *ge-* in die verlede tyd nie. Sê hulle hardop: *be-TAAL, ver-TEL*. Die klem val nie op die eerste lettergreep nie, net soos by *ge-*, daarom kry hulle nie nog ’n *ge-* nie.\n\n| Voorvoegsel | Teenwoordige tyd | Verlede tyd |\n|---|---|---|\n| be- | Ek betaal. | Ek het betaal. |\n| ge- | Ons gebruik dit. | Ons het dit gebruik. |\n| her- | Sy herhaal die vraag. | Sy het die vraag herhaal. |\n| ont- | Hy ontmoet sy oom. | Hy het sy oom ontmoet. |\n| ver- | Hulle vertel ’n storie. | Hulle het ’n storie vertel. |\n| er- | Ek erken my fout. | Ek het my fout erken. |\n\nPasop vir woorde soos *verf* en *erf*: hulle begin net toevallig met dieselfde letters, maar dit is nie ’n voorvoegsel nie. Hulle kry wel *ge-*: *het geverf, het geërf*.\n\n**Skeibare werkwoorde** soos *opstaan, aantrek* en *wegloop* kry *ge-* in die **middel**: *Ek het vroeg **opgestaan**. Sy het haar trui **aangetrek**.*\n\n## Spesiale vorme in die verlede tyd\n\n’n Paar belangrike werkwoorde het ’n eie vorm vir die verlede tyd:\n\n| Teenwoordige tyd | Verlede tyd |\n|---|---|\n| Ek **is** moeg. | Ek **was** moeg. |\n| Ons **het** ’n hond. | Ons **het** ’n hond **gehad**. |\n| Hy **kan** swem. | Hy **kon** swem. |\n| Sy **wil** gaan speel. | Sy **wou** gaan speel. |\n| Julle **moet** leer. | Julle **moes** leer. |\n\nDie tweede werkwoord bly aan die einde: *Ek **kon** nie **kom** nie. Ons **moes** vroeg **opstaan**.*\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie *ge-* by hierdie spesiale vorme of by *be-, ver-*-woorde sit nie. Skryf *Ons **moes** werk* (nie *Ons het gemoet werk* nie) en *Ek het my pen **verloor*** (nie *geverloor* nie).","en":"## Main verbs and auxiliary verbs\n\nA **verb** (*werkwoord*) says what someone **does** or what **happens**: *hardloop* (run), *eet* (eat), *skryf* (write), *reën* (rain). It can also say how something **is**: *Die sop is warm.* (The soup is hot.)\n\n- The **main verb** (*hoofwerkwoord*) carries the most important meaning: *Ek **skryf** ’n brief.* (I write a letter.)\n- An **auxiliary verb** (*hulpwerkwoord*) helps the main verb. It says something about **time** or about must, can or want: ***het, sal, kan, moet, wil, mag***. *Ek **sal** môre ’n brief **skryf**.* (I will write a letter tomorrow.)\n\nAn Afrikaans verb stays the same for every person: *ek loop, jy loop, hy loop, hulle loop* (I walk, you walk, he walks, they walk).\n\n## The three tenses (*tye*)\n\n| Tense | How do you make it? | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Present tense** (*teenwoordige tyd* – now) | verb in 2nd place | *Thabo **skop** die bal.* (Thabo kicks the ball.) |\n| **Past tense** (*verlede tyd* – already happened) | **het** in 2nd place + **ge-** verb at the end | *Thabo **het** die bal **geskop**.* (Thabo kicked the ball.) |\n| **Future tense** (*toekomende tyd* – still to happen) | **sal** in 2nd place + verb at the end | *Thabo **sal** die bal **skop**.* (Thabo will kick the ball.) |\n\nWords like *gister* (yesterday) and *verlede week* (last week) point to the past; *môre* (tomorrow) and *volgende jaar* (next year) point to the future. If the sentence starts with such a word, *het* or *sal* stays in 2nd place: ***Gister het** Thabo die bal geskop.*\n\nDoes the verb begin with an *e*? Then the *e* after *ge-* gets a **diaeresis** (*deelteken*), so that you say the sounds separately: *eet → geëet* (eat → ate), *eindig → geëindig* (end → ended).\n\n> **Remember:** The past tense needs **two parts**: *het* + the *ge-* verb. Write *Ek **het** gesing* (I sang) – not *Ek gesing* or *Ek het sing*.\n\n## Verbs without ge-\n\nVerbs that begin with **be-, ge-, her-, ont-, ver-** or **er-** do **not** take *ge-* in the past tense. Say them aloud: *be-TAAL, ver-TEL*. The stress does not fall on the first syllable, just as with *ge-*, so they don’t get another *ge-*.\n\n| Prefix | Present tense | Past tense |\n|---|---|---|\n| be- | *Ek betaal.* (I pay.) | *Ek het betaal.* |\n| ge- | *Ons gebruik dit.* (We use it.) | *Ons het dit gebruik.* |\n| her- | *Sy herhaal die vraag.* (She repeats the question.) | *Sy het die vraag herhaal.* |\n| ont- | *Hy ontmoet sy oom.* (He meets his uncle.) | *Hy het sy oom ontmoet.* |\n| ver- | *Hulle vertel ’n storie.* (They tell a story.) | *Hulle het ’n storie vertel.* |\n| er- | *Ek erken my fout.* (I admit my mistake.) | *Ek het my fout erken.* |\n\nWatch out for words like *verf* (paint) and *erf* (inherit): they just happen to start with the same letters, but it is not a prefix. They do take *ge-*: *het geverf, het geërf*.\n\n**Separable verbs** (*skeibare werkwoorde*) such as *opstaan* (get up), *aantrek* (put on) and *wegloop* (run away) take *ge-* in the **middle**: *Ek het vroeg **opgestaan**. Sy het haar trui **aangetrek**.*\n\n## Special past tense forms\n\nA few important verbs have their own past tense form:\n\n| Present tense | Past tense |\n|---|---|\n| *Ek **is** moeg.* (I am tired.) | *Ek **was** moeg.* (I was tired.) |\n| *Ons **het** ’n hond.* (We have a dog.) | *Ons **het** ’n hond **gehad**.* (We had a dog.) |\n| *Hy **kan** swem.* (He can swim.) | *Hy **kon** swem.* (He could swim.) |\n| *Sy **wil** gaan speel.* (She wants to go and play.) | *Sy **wou** gaan speel.* (She wanted to …) |\n| *Julle **moet** leer.* (You must study.) | *Julle **moes** leer.* (You had to study.) |\n\nThe second verb stays at the end: *Ek **kon** nie **kom** nie.* (I could not come.) *Ons **moes** vroeg **opstaan**.* (We had to get up early.)\n\n> **Common mistake:** Don’t add *ge-* to these special forms or to *be-, ver-* words. Write *Ons **moes** werk* (not *Ons het gemoet werk*) and *Ek het my pen **verloor*** (not *geverloor*)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Werkwoord","en":"Verb (werkwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat sê wat iemand doen of wat gebeur, soos ‘hardloop’ of ‘reën’.","en":"A word that says what someone does or what happens, such as ‘hardloop’ (run) or ‘reën’ (rain)."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoofwerkwoord","en":"Main verb (hoofwerkwoord)"},"def":{"af":"Die werkwoord wat die belangrikste betekenis in die sin dra, soos ‘skryf’ in ‘Ek sal skryf’.","en":"The verb that carries the main meaning in the sentence, like ‘skryf’ (write) in ‘Ek sal skryf’."}},{"term":{"af":"Hulpwerkwoord","en":"Auxiliary verb (hulpwerkwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Werkwoord wat die hoofwerkwoord help, soos ‘het, sal, kan, moet’ en ‘wil’.","en":"A verb that helps the main verb, such as ‘het, sal, kan, moet’ and ‘wil’."}},{"term":{"af":"Teenwoordige tyd","en":"Present tense (teenwoordige tyd)"},"def":{"af":"Die vorm van die sin vir iets wat nou gebeur: ‘Sy lees.’","en":"The form of the sentence for something happening now: ‘Sy lees.’ (She reads.)"}},{"term":{"af":"Verlede tyd","en":"Past tense (verlede tyd)"},"def":{"af":"Die vorm vir iets wat klaar gebeur het, gewoonlik met ‘het’ en ’n ‘ge-’-werkwoord: ‘Sy het gelees.’","en":"The form for something that already happened, usually with ‘het’ and a ‘ge-’ verb: ‘Sy het gelees.’ (She read.)"}},{"term":{"af":"Toekomende tyd","en":"Future tense (toekomende tyd)"},"def":{"af":"Die vorm vir iets wat nog gaan gebeur, met ‘sal’ en die werkwoord aan die einde: ‘Sy sal lees.’","en":"The form for something still to happen, with ‘sal’ and the verb at the end: ‘Sy sal lees.’ (She will read.)"}},{"term":{"af":"Voorvoegsel","en":"Prefix (voorvoegsel)"},"def":{"af":"’n Deeltjie voor aan ’n woord, soos ‘be-’ in ‘betaal’ of ‘ver-’ in ‘vertel’.","en":"A part added to the front of a word, like ‘be-’ in ‘betaal’ (pay) or ‘ver-’ in ‘vertel’ (tell)."}},{"term":{"af":"Skeibare werkwoord","en":"Separable verb (skeibare werkwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Werkwoord wat uit twee dele bestaan wat kan skei, soos ‘opstaan’: ‘Ek staan op’ en ‘Ek het opgestaan’.","en":"A verb made of two parts that can separate, like ‘opstaan’ (get up): ‘Ek staan op’ and ‘Ek het opgestaan’."}},{"term":{"af":"Deelteken","en":"Diaeresis (deelteken)"},"def":{"af":"Die twee puntjies (¨) op ’n klinker wat wys dat ’n nuwe lettergreep daar begin, soos in ‘geëet’.","en":"The two dots (¨) on a vowel showing that a new syllable starts there, as in ‘geëet’ (eaten)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Van teenwoordig na verlede tyd","en":"From present to past tense"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf in die verlede tyd: *Thabo skop die bal oor die heining.*","en":"Write in the past tense: *Thabo skop die bal oor die heining.* (Thabo kicks the ball over the fence.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Vind die werkwoord: *skop*. Dit staan op die 2de plek.","en":"Find the verb: *skop* (kick). It is in 2nd place."},{"af":"Sit *het* op die 2de plek, waar *skop* was: *Thabo het …*","en":"Put *het* in 2nd place, where *skop* was: *Thabo het …*"},{"af":"Sit *ge-* voor die werkwoord en skuif dit na die einde: *geskop*.","en":"Put *ge-* in front of the verb and move it to the end: *geskop*."}],"answer":{"af":"Thabo het die bal oor die heining geskop.","en":"*Thabo het die bal oor die heining geskop.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Werkwoorde sonder ge-","en":"Verbs without ge-"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf in die verlede tyd: *Ma betaal die rekening. Sy vertel ons van die vakansie.*","en":"Write in the past tense: *Ma betaal die rekening. Sy vertel ons van die vakansie.* (Mom pays the bill. She tells us about the holiday.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Die werkwoorde is *betaal* en *vertel*. Hulle begin met *be-* en *ver-*.","en":"The verbs are *betaal* (pay) and *vertel* (tell). They begin with *be-* and *ver-*."},{"af":"Werkwoorde met *be-* en *ver-* kry nie *ge-* nie.","en":"Verbs with *be-* and *ver-* do not take *ge-*."},{"af":"Sit *het* op die 2de plek en die werkwoord, sonder *ge-*, aan die einde.","en":"Put *het* in 2nd place and the verb, without *ge-*, at the end."}],"answer":{"af":"Ma het die rekening betaal. Sy het ons van die vakansie vertel.","en":"*Ma het die rekening betaal. Sy het ons van die vakansie vertel.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Spesiale verledetydsvorme","en":"Special past tense forms"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf in die verlede tyd: *Ek is moeg, want ek moet vroeg opstaan.*","en":"Write in the past tense: *Ek is moeg, want ek moet vroeg opstaan.* (I am tired, because I must get up early.)"},"steps":[{"af":"*is* het ’n eie verledetydsvorm: *was*.","en":"*is* has its own past form: *was*."},{"af":"*moet* word *moes*.","en":"*moet* becomes *moes*."},{"af":"*opstaan* bly as tweede werkwoord aan die einde, sonder *ge-*, want *moes* wys reeds die verlede tyd.","en":"*opstaan* stays at the end as the second verb, without *ge-*, because *moes* already shows the past tense."}],"answer":{"af":"Ek was moeg, want ek moes vroeg opstaan.","en":"*Ek was moeg, want ek moes vroeg opstaan.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Toekomende tyd","en":"Future tense"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf in die toekomende tyd en begin dan die sin met *Môre*: *Ons speel netbal in die park.*","en":"Write in the future tense, then start the sentence with *Môre* (tomorrow): *Ons speel netbal in die park.* (We play netball in the park.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Sit *sal* op die 2de plek en skuif *speel* na die einde: *Ons sal netbal in die park speel.*","en":"Put *sal* in 2nd place and move *speel* to the end: *Ons sal netbal in die park speel.*"},{"af":"Begin nou met *Môre*. *Sal* moet op die 2de plek bly, so *ons* skuif ná *sal*.","en":"Now start with *Môre*. *Sal* must stay in 2nd place, so *ons* moves after *sal*."}],"answer":{"af":"Ons sal netbal in die park speel. / Môre sal ons netbal in die park speel.","en":"*Ons sal netbal in die park speel.* / *Môre sal ons netbal in die park speel.*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Skryf in die verlede tyd: *Sy sing ’n liedjie.*","en":"Write in the past tense: *Sy sing ’n liedjie.* (She sings a song.)"},"options":[{"af":"Sy het ’n liedjie gesing.","en":"Sy het ’n liedjie gesing."},{"af":"Sy het ’n liedjie sing.","en":"Sy het ’n liedjie sing."},{"af":"Sy het gesing ’n liedjie.","en":"Sy het gesing ’n liedjie."},{"af":"Sy was ’n liedjie gesing.","en":"Sy was ’n liedjie gesing."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die verlede tyd het *het* op die 2de plek en die *ge-*werkwoord aan die einde nodig: *Sy het ’n liedjie gesing.*","en":"The past tense needs *het* in 2nd place and the *ge-* verb at the end: *Sy het ’n liedjie gesing.*"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter werkwoord kry **nie** *ge-* in die verlede tyd nie?","en":"Which verb does **not** take *ge-* in the past tense?"},"options":[{"af":"speel","en":"speel"},{"af":"loop","en":"loop"},{"af":"vertel","en":"vertel"},{"af":"skryf","en":"skryf"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Vertel* begin met die voorvoegsel *ver-*, so dit word *het vertel*. Die ander word *het gespeel, het geloop* en *het geskryf*.","en":"*Vertel* (tell) begins with the prefix *ver-*, so it becomes *het vertel*. The others become *het gespeel, het geloop* and *het geskryf*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Ek het gister my ouma ___. (besoek)","en":"*Ek het gister my ouma* ___. (*besoek* – visit)"},"answers":{"af":["besoek"],"en":["besoek"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["gebesoek","besoekte","sal besoek"],"en":["gebesoek","besoekte","sal besoek"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Besoek* begin met *be-*, so dit kry nie *ge-* nie: *Ek het gister my ouma besoek.*","en":"*Besoek* begins with *be-*, so it does not take *ge-*: *Ek het gister my ouma besoek.* (I visited my granny yesterday.)"}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In die toekomende tyd gebruik ons *sal*, en die hoofwerkwoord staan aan die einde van die sin.","en":"In the future tense we use *sal*, and the main verb stands at the end of the sentence."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. *Sal* staan op die 2de plek en die hoofwerkwoord aan die einde: *Ek sal môre my kamer opruim.*","en":"True. *Sal* stands in 2nd place and the main verb at the end: *Ek sal môre my kamer opruim.* (I will tidy my room tomorrow.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Ek ___ gister nie skool toe gaan nie, want ek was siek.*","en":"Complete: *Ek ___ gister nie skool toe gaan nie, want ek was siek.* (I ___ go to school yesterday, because I was sick.)"},"options":[{"af":"kan","en":"kan"},{"af":"kon","en":"kon"},{"af":"kom","en":"kom"},{"af":"sal","en":"sal"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Gister* en *was* wys die verlede tyd, so *kan* word *kon*.","en":"*Gister* (yesterday) and *was* show the past tense, so *kan* (can) becomes *kon* (could)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke teenwoordige vorm by sy verlede vorm.","en":"Match each present form to its past form."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"is","en":"is"},"r":{"af":"was","en":"was"}},{"l":{"af":"het","en":"het"},"r":{"af":"het gehad","en":"het gehad"}},{"l":{"af":"kan","en":"kan"},"r":{"af":"kon","en":"kon"}},{"l":{"af":"wil","en":"wil"},"r":{"af":"wou","en":"wou"}},{"l":{"af":"moet","en":"moet"},"r":{"af":"moes","en":"moes"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hierdie vyf werkwoorde het ’n eie verledetydsvorm wat jy moet ken: *is → was, het → het gehad, kan → kon, wil → wou, moet → moes*.","en":"These five verbs have their own past form that you must know: *is → was, het → het gehad, kan → kon, wil → wou, moet → moes*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is die **hulpwerkwoord** in die sin? *Die kinders sal môre ’n toets skryf.*","en":"Which word is the **auxiliary verb** in the sentence? *Die kinders sal môre ’n toets skryf.* (The children will write a test tomorrow.)"},"options":[{"af":"skryf","en":"skryf"},{"af":"toets","en":"toets"},{"af":"môre","en":"môre"},{"af":"sal","en":"sal"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Sal* help die hoofwerkwoord *skryf* en wys dat dit in die toekoms gebeur. *Toets* is ’n naamwoord en *môre* sê wanneer.","en":"*Sal* (will) helps the main verb *skryf* (write) and shows that it happens in the future. *Toets* (test) is a noun and *môre* (tomorrow) says when."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gister het ek ’n groot appel ___. (eet)","en":"*Gister het ek ’n groot appel* ___. (*eet* – eat)"},"answers":{"af":["geëet"],"en":["geëet"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["geeet","geët","eet"],"en":["geeet","geët","eet"]}},"explain":{"af":"*ge-* + *eet* gee drie e’s langs mekaar. Die deelteken op die eerste e van *eet* wys dat jy *ge* en *eet* apart sê: *geëet*.","en":"*ge-* + *eet* gives three e’s in a row. The diaeresis on the first e of *eet* shows that you say *ge* and *eet* separately: *geëet*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is in die **toekomende tyd**?","en":"Which sentence is in the **future tense**?"},"options":[{"af":"Lerato sal die hond môre bad.","en":"Lerato sal die hond môre bad."},{"af":"Lerato het die hond gebad.","en":"Lerato het die hond gebad."},{"af":"Lerato bad die hond nou.","en":"Lerato bad die hond nou."},{"af":"Lerato moes die hond bad.","en":"Lerato moes die hond bad."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Sal* wys dat iets nog gaan gebeur. *Het gebad* en *moes* is verlede tyd, en *bad … nou* is teenwoordige tyd.","en":"*Sal* shows that something is still going to happen. *Het gebad* and *moes* are past tense, and *bad … nou* is present tense."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Werkwoorde wat met *ver-* begin, kry *ge-* in die verlede tyd, soos *Ek het my pen geverloor*.","en":"Verbs that begin with *ver-* take *ge-* in the past tense, as in *Ek het my pen geverloor*."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Werkwoorde met *ver-* kry nie *ge-* nie: *Ek het my pen verloor.*","en":"False. Verbs with *ver-* do not take *ge-*: *Ek het my pen verloor.* (I lost my pen.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Skryf in die verlede tyd: *Die span verloor die wedstryd.*","en":"Write in the past tense: *Die span verloor die wedstryd.* (The team loses the match.)"},"options":[{"af":"Die span het die wedstryd geverloor.","en":"Die span het die wedstryd geverloor."},{"af":"Die span het die wedstryd verloor.","en":"Die span het die wedstryd verloor."},{"af":"Die span het verloor die wedstryd.","en":"Die span het verloor die wedstryd."},{"af":"Die span verloor het die wedstryd.","en":"Die span verloor het die wedstryd."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Verloor* begin met *ver-*, so dit kry nie *ge-* nie. *Het* staan op die 2de plek en *verloor* aan die einde.","en":"*Verloor* (lose) begins with *ver-*, so it does not take *ge-*. *Het* stands in 2nd place and *verloor* at the end."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Skryf in die verlede tyd: *Ek staan elke oggend om sesuur op.*","en":"Write in the past tense: *Ek staan elke oggend om sesuur op.* (I get up at six o’clock every morning.)"},"options":[{"af":"Ek het elke oggend om sesuur geopstaan.","en":"Ek het elke oggend om sesuur geopstaan."},{"af":"Ek het elke oggend om sesuur gestaan op.","en":"Ek het elke oggend om sesuur gestaan op."},{"af":"Ek het elke oggend om sesuur op gestaan.","en":"Ek het elke oggend om sesuur op gestaan."},{"af":"Ek het elke oggend om sesuur opgestaan.","en":"Ek het elke oggend om sesuur opgestaan."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Opstaan* is ’n skeibare werkwoord. In die verlede tyd kom *ge-* in die middel en dit word een woord: *opgestaan*.","en":"*Opstaan* (get up) is a separable verb. In the past tense *ge-* goes in the middle and it is written as one word: *opgestaan*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf in die toekomende tyd: Môre ___ ons by Oupa gaan kuier.","en":"Write in the future tense: *Môre ___ ons by Oupa gaan kuier.* (Tomorrow we ___ visit Grandpa.)"},"answers":{"af":["sal"],"en":["sal"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["het","was","is"],"en":["het","was","is"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die toekomende tyd gebruik *sal* op die 2de plek. *Het* en *was* is verlede tyd, en *is* pas nie hier nie.","en":"The future tense uses *sal* (will) in 2nd place. *Het* and *was* are past tense, and *is* does not fit here."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is die **hoofwerkwoord** in die sin? *Pieter moet sy kamer opruim.*","en":"Which word is the **main verb** in the sentence? *Pieter moet sy kamer opruim.* (Pieter must tidy his room.)"},"options":[{"af":"moet","en":"moet"},{"af":"opruim","en":"opruim"},{"af":"kamer","en":"kamer"},{"af":"sy","en":"sy"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Opruim* sê wat Pieter doen, so dit is die hoofwerkwoord. *Moet* is die hulpwerkwoord wat dit help.","en":"*Opruim* (tidy up) says what Pieter does, so it is the main verb. *Moet* (must) is the auxiliary verb that helps it."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Sinne bou en beskryf","en":"Building and describing sentences"},"topics":[{"id":"afr5-t2-byvoeglike-naamwoorde","title":{"af":"Byvoeglike naamwoorde en trappe van vergelyking","en":"Adjectives and degrees of comparison"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal byvoeglike naamwoorde voor en ná die naamwoord korrek kan skryf en die trappe van vergelyking, ook die onreëlmatige, reg kan gebruik.","en":"You will be able to write adjectives correctly before and after the noun and use the degrees of comparison, including the irregular ones."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat doen ’n byvoeglike naamwoord?\n\n’n **Byvoeglike naamwoord** beskryf ’n selfstandige naamwoord. Dit sê **hoe** iets lyk, voel, klink of is: *’n **rooi** bal, ’n **sagte** kussing, die **lang** pad*.\n\nDit kan op twee plekke staan:\n\n- **Attributief** – **voor** die naamwoord: *die **groot** huis, ’n **koue** dag*\n- **Predikatief** – **ná** die naamwoord, gewoonlik ná *is, was, word* of *lyk*: *Die huis is **groot**. Die dag is **koud**.*\n\n> **Onthou:** ’n Predikatiewe byvoeglike naamwoord kry **nooit** ’n *-e* nie: *Die kussing is sag* (nie *sagte* nie).\n\n## Wanneer kry dit ’n -e?\n\nVoor die naamwoord bly party byvoeglike naamwoorde dieselfde, maar ander kry ’n **-e** of verander hul spelling. Dit maak nie saak of *die* of *’n* voor staan nie.\n\n| Predikatief | Attributief | Wat gebeur? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Die huis is groot. | ’n groot huis | bly dieselfde |\n| Die rok is mooi. | die mooi rok | bly dieselfde |\n| Die kussing is sag. | ’n sagte kussing | kry -e |\n| Die perd is vinnig. | die vinnige perd | -ig kry -e |\n| Die man is vriendelik. | ’n vriendelike man | -lik kry -e |\n| Die koffie is koud. | koue koffie | d val weg, kry -e |\n| Die kos is goed. | goeie kos | word *goeie* |\n| Die berg is hoog. | die hoë berg | g val weg, kry ë |\n| Die pad is lank. | die lang pad | k word g |\n| Die skoene is nuut. | nuwe skoene | t word w, kry -e |\n\nKort woorde soos *groot, klein, mooi, rooi, wit, swart, slim* en *warm* bly gewoonlik dieselfde. Woorde wat op **-ig** of **-lik** eindig, kry altyd **-e**. As jy twyfel, sê dit hardop: *’n sagte kussing* klink reg, maar *’n sag kussing* klink vreemd.\n\n## Trappe van vergelyking\n\nAs ons dinge **vergelyk**, gebruik ons drie **trappe**:\n\n| Stellende trap | Vergrotende trap (-er) | Oortreffende trap (-ste) |\n|---|---|---|\n| klein | kleiner | kleinste |\n| dik | dikker | dikste |\n| groot | groter | grootste |\n| lank | langer | langste |\n| hoog | hoër | hoogste |\n| duur | duurder | duurste |\n| vinnig | vinniger | vinnigste |\n\n- Ná ’n **kort klank** verdubbel die medeklinker: *dik → dikker, nat → natter*.\n- Woorde wat op **-r** eindig, kry **-der**: *duur → duurder, swaar → swaarder*.\n- Ons vergelyk twee dinge met **as**: *Thabo is **langer as** Sipho.* Is hulle ewe lank, sê ons **so … soos**: *Thabo is so lank soos Sipho.*\n- Die oortreffende trap kry gewoonlik **die**: *Zanele is **die langste** in die klas.*\n- By party lang woorde gebruik ons **meer** en **mees**: *opgewonde → meer opgewonde → mees opgewonde*.\n\n## Onreëlmatige trappe\n\nHierdie trappe volg nie die reëls nie. Leer hulle uit jou kop:\n\n| Stellend | Vergrotend | Oortreffend |\n|---|---|---|\n| goed | beter | beste |\n| veel / baie | meer | meeste |\n| min | minder | minste |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie twee trappe saam gebruik nie: *meer groter* en *mees mooiste* is verkeerd. Skryf net *groter* of *mooiste*. Vergelyk ook met **as**, nie met *dan* nie: *groter as die renoster*.","en":"## What does an adjective do?\n\nAn **adjective** (*byvoeglike naamwoord*) describes a noun. It says **how** something looks, feels, sounds or is: *’n **rooi** bal* (a red ball), *’n **sagte** kussing* (a soft cushion), *die **lang** pad* (the long road).\n\nIt can stand in two places:\n\n- **Attributive** (*attributief*) – **before** the noun: *die **groot** huis* (the big house), *’n **koue** dag* (a cold day)\n- **Predicative** (*predikatief*) – **after** the noun, usually after *is, was, word* or *lyk* (looks): *Die huis is **groot**. Die dag is **koud**.*\n\n> **Remember:** A predicative adjective **never** takes an *-e*: *Die kussing is sag* (not *sagte*).\n\n## When does it take an -e?\n\nBefore the noun some adjectives stay the same, but others add an **-e** or change their spelling. It makes no difference whether *die* or *’n* comes first.\n\n| Predicative | Attributive | What happens? |\n|---|---|---|\n| *Die huis is groot.* (big) | *’n groot huis* | stays the same |\n| *Die rok is mooi.* (pretty) | *die mooi rok* | stays the same |\n| *Die kussing is sag.* (soft) | *’n sagte kussing* | adds -e |\n| *Die perd is vinnig.* (fast) | *die vinnige perd* | -ig adds -e |\n| *Die man is vriendelik.* (friendly) | *’n vriendelike man* | -lik adds -e |\n| *Die koffie is koud.* (cold) | *koue koffie* | d drops, adds -e |\n| *Die kos is goed.* (good) | *goeie kos* | becomes *goeie* |\n| *Die berg is hoog.* (high) | *die hoë berg* | g drops, adds ë |\n| *Die pad is lank.* (long) | *die lang pad* | k becomes g |\n| *Die skoene is nuut.* (new) | *nuwe skoene* | t becomes w, adds -e |\n\nShort words such as *groot, klein, mooi, rooi, wit, swart, slim* and *warm* usually stay the same. Words ending in **-ig** or **-lik** always add **-e**. If you are unsure, say it aloud: *’n sagte kussing* sounds right, but *’n sag kussing* sounds strange.\n\n## Degrees of comparison (*trappe van vergelyking*)\n\nWhen we **compare** things, we use three **degrees**:\n\n| Positive (*stellend*) | Comparative (*vergrotend*, -er) | Superlative (*oortreffend*, -ste) |\n|---|---|---|\n| *klein* (small) | *kleiner* | *kleinste* |\n| *dik* (thick) | *dikker* | *dikste* |\n| *groot* (big) | *groter* | *grootste* |\n| *lank* (tall/long) | *langer* | *langste* |\n| *hoog* (high) | *hoër* | *hoogste* |\n| *duur* (expensive) | *duurder* | *duurste* |\n| *vinnig* (fast) | *vinniger* | *vinnigste* |\n\n- After a **short sound** the consonant doubles: *dik → dikker, nat → natter* (wet).\n- Words ending in **-r** add **-der**: *duur → duurder, swaar → swaarder* (heavy).\n- We compare two things with **as** (than): *Thabo is **langer as** Sipho.* (Thabo is taller than Sipho.) If they are equally tall, we say **so … soos** (as … as): *Thabo is so lank soos Sipho.*\n- The superlative usually takes **die**: *Zanele is **die langste** in die klas.* (Zanele is the tallest in the class.)\n- With some long words we use **meer** and **mees** (more, most): *opgewonde → meer opgewonde → mees opgewonde* (excited).\n\n## Irregular degrees\n\nThese degrees don’t follow the rules. Learn them by heart:\n\n| Positive | Comparative | Superlative |\n|---|---|---|\n| *goed* (good) | *beter* | *beste* |\n| *veel / baie* (much/many) | *meer* | *meeste* |\n| *min* (little/few) | *minder* | *minste* |\n\n> **Common mistake:** Don’t use two degrees together: *meer groter* and *mees mooiste* are wrong. Write only *groter* or *mooiste*. Also compare with **as**, not with *dan*: *groter as die renoster* (bigger than the rhino)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Byvoeglike naamwoord","en":"Adjective (byvoeglike naamwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat ’n selfstandige naamwoord beskryf, soos ‘rooi’ of ‘sagte’.","en":"A word that describes a noun, such as ‘rooi’ (red) or ‘sagte’ (soft)."}},{"term":{"af":"Attributief","en":"Attributive (attributief)"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer die byvoeglike naamwoord voor die naamwoord staan: ‘die hoë berg’.","en":"When the adjective stands before the noun: ‘die hoë berg’ (the high mountain)."}},{"term":{"af":"Predikatief","en":"Predicative (predikatief)"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer die byvoeglike naamwoord ná die naamwoord staan, gewoonlik ná ‘is’: ‘Die berg is hoog.’","en":"When the adjective stands after the noun, usually after ‘is’: ‘Die berg is hoog.’ (The mountain is high.)"}},{"term":{"af":"Verbuiging","en":"Inflection (verbuiging)"},"def":{"af":"Die verandering van ’n byvoeglike naamwoord voor ’n naamwoord, soos ‘sag’ wat ‘sagte’ word.","en":"The change to an adjective before a noun, like ‘sag’ becoming ‘sagte’."}},{"term":{"af":"Trappe van vergelyking","en":"Degrees of comparison (trappe van vergelyking)"},"def":{"af":"Die drie vorme van ’n byvoeglike naamwoord wat ons gebruik om dinge te vergelyk: ‘klein, kleiner, kleinste’.","en":"The three forms of an adjective we use to compare things: ‘klein, kleiner, kleinste’ (small, smaller, smallest)."}},{"term":{"af":"Stellende trap","en":"Positive degree (stellende trap)"},"def":{"af":"Die gewone vorm van die byvoeglike naamwoord, sonder vergelyking: ‘klein’.","en":"The ordinary form of the adjective, without comparing: ‘klein’ (small)."}},{"term":{"af":"Vergrotende trap","en":"Comparative degree (vergrotende trap)"},"def":{"af":"Die vorm met ‘-er’ of ‘meer’ wat twee dinge vergelyk: ‘kleiner as’.","en":"The form with ‘-er’ or ‘meer’ that compares two things: ‘kleiner as’ (smaller than)."}},{"term":{"af":"Oortreffende trap","en":"Superlative degree (oortreffende trap)"},"def":{"af":"Die vorm met ‘-ste’ of ‘mees’ vir die heel meeste van almal: ‘die kleinste’.","en":"The form with ‘-ste’ or ‘mees’ for the very most of all: ‘die kleinste’ (the smallest)."}},{"term":{"af":"Onreëlmatige trappe","en":"Irregular degrees (onreëlmatige trappe)"},"def":{"af":"Trappe wat nie die gewone reëls volg nie, soos ‘goed, beter, beste’.","en":"Degrees that don’t follow the normal rules, such as ‘goed, beter, beste’ (good, better, best)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Van predikatief na attributief","en":"From predicative to attributive"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die byvoeglike naamwoord voor die naamwoord: (a) *Die kussing is sag.* (b) *Die berg is hoog.* (c) *Die rok is mooi.*","en":"Put the adjective before the noun: (a) *Die kussing is sag.* (The cushion is soft.) (b) *Die berg is hoog.* (The mountain is high.) (c) *Die rok is mooi.* (The dress is pretty.)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *sag* kry ’n -e voor die naamwoord: *’n sagte kussing*.","en":"(a) *sag* adds an -e before the noun: *’n sagte kussing*."},{"af":"(b) By *hoog* val die g weg, en die -e kry ’n deelteken sodat jy *ho-ë* sê: *die hoë berg*.","en":"(b) In *hoog* the g drops, and the -e gets a diaeresis so that you say *ho-ë*: *die hoë berg*."},{"af":"(c) *mooi* bly dieselfde: *die mooi rok*.","en":"(c) *mooi* stays the same: *die mooi rok*."}],"answer":{"af":"’n sagte kussing; die hoë berg; die mooi rok","en":"*’n sagte kussing; die hoë berg; die mooi rok*"}},{"title":{"af":"Die drie trappe","en":"The three degrees"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die vergrotende en oortreffende trap van *dik, groot* en *duur*.","en":"Write the comparative and superlative of *dik* (thick), *groot* (big) and *duur* (expensive)."},"steps":[{"af":"*dik* het ’n kort klank, so die k verdubbel voor -er: *dikker*, en dan *dikste*.","en":"*dik* has a short sound, so the k doubles before -er: *dikker*, and then *dikste*."},{"af":"*groot* het ’n lang klank. Voor -er is een o genoeg: *groter*. Voor -ste bly albei o’s: *grootste*.","en":"*groot* has a long sound. Before -er one o is enough: *groter*. Before -ste both o’s stay: *grootste*."},{"af":"*duur* eindig op -r, so dit kry -der: *duurder*, en dan *duurste*.","en":"*duur* ends in -r, so it adds -der: *duurder*, and then *duurste*."}],"answer":{"af":"dik – dikker – dikste; groot – groter – grootste; duur – duurder – duurste","en":"*dik – dikker – dikste; groot – groter – grootste; duur – duurder – duurste*"}},{"title":{"af":"Onreëlmatige trappe in ’n sin","en":"Irregular degrees in a sentence"},"problem":{"af":"Voltooi met die regte trap van *goed*: *Ravi se tekening is goed, maar Aisha s’n is ___ en Nomsa s’n is die ___ van almal.*","en":"Complete with the correct degree of *goed* (good): *Ravi se tekening is goed, maar Aisha s’n is ___ en Nomsa s’n is die ___ van almal.* (Ravi’s drawing is good, but Aisha’s is ___ and Nomsa’s is the ___ of all.)"},"steps":[{"af":"*goed* is onreëlmatig: *goed – beter – beste*.","en":"*goed* is irregular: *goed – beter – beste*."},{"af":"Aisha se tekening word met Ravi s’n vergelyk (twee tekeninge): vergrotende trap, *beter*.","en":"Aisha’s drawing is compared with Ravi’s (two drawings): comparative, *beter*."},{"af":"Nomsa s’n is die beste *van almal*: oortreffende trap, *beste*.","en":"Nomsa’s is the best *of all*: superlative, *beste*."}],"answer":{"af":"Ravi se tekening is goed, maar Aisha s’n is beter en Nomsa s’n is die beste van almal.","en":"*Ravi se tekening is goed, maar Aisha s’n is beter en Nomsa s’n is die beste van almal.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Verbeter die foute","en":"Correct the mistakes"},"problem":{"af":"Verbeter die sin: *Die olifant is meer groter dan die renoster.*","en":"Correct the sentence: *Die olifant is meer groter dan die renoster.* (The elephant is more bigger than the rhino.)"},"steps":[{"af":"*meer groter* gebruik twee trappe saam. *Groter* is klaar die vergrotende trap, so *meer* moet weg.","en":"*meer groter* uses two degrees together. *Groter* is already the comparative, so *meer* must go."},{"af":"In Afrikaans vergelyk ons met *as*, nie met *dan* nie.","en":"In Afrikaans we compare with *as* (than), not with *dan*."}],"answer":{"af":"Die olifant is groter as die renoster.","en":"*Die olifant is groter as die renoster.*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter sin is die byvoeglike naamwoord **predikatief**?","en":"In which sentence is the adjective **predicative**?"},"options":[{"af":"Die water in die dam is koud.","en":"Die water in die dam is koud."},{"af":"Ons swem in die koue water.","en":"Ons swem in die koue water."},{"af":"’n Koue wind waai vandag.","en":"’n Koue wind waai vandag."},{"af":"Ma maak vir ons koue tee.","en":"Ma maak vir ons koue tee."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"In *Die water … is koud* staan *koud* ná die naamwoord, ná *is*: predikatief, sonder -e. In die ander sinne staan *koue* voor die naamwoord.","en":"In *Die water … is koud* the word *koud* stands after the noun, after *is*: predicative, without -e. In the other sentences *koue* stands before the noun."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte vorm: *Lerato is ’n ___ vriendin.* (goed)","en":"Choose the correct form: *Lerato is ’n ___ vriendin.* (Lerato is a ___ friend.) (*goed*)"},"options":[{"af":"goed","en":"goed"},{"af":"goede","en":"goede"},{"af":"goeie","en":"goeie"},{"af":"goei","en":"goei"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Voor die naamwoord word *goed* altyd *goeie*: *’n goeie vriendin*.","en":"Before the noun *goed* always becomes *goeie*: *’n goeie vriendin* (a good friend)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die Drakensberg is ’n ___ bergreeks. (hoog)","en":"*Die Drakensberg is ’n ___ bergreeks.* (The Drakensberg is a ___ mountain range.) (*hoog*)"},"answers":{"af":["hoë"],"en":["hoë"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["hoog","hoge","hoeë"],"en":["hoog","hoge","hoeë"]}},"explain":{"af":"Voor die naamwoord val die g van *hoog* weg en dit kry ’n -ë: *’n hoë bergreeks*.","en":"Before the noun the g of *hoog* drops and it gets an -ë: *’n hoë bergreeks* (a high mountain range)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Byvoeglike naamwoord wat ná die naamwoord staan (predikatief), kry nooit ’n -e nie.","en":"An adjective that stands after the noun (predicative) never takes an -e."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Ons sê *Die kussing is sag*, nie *Die kussing is sagte* nie. Net voor die naamwoord kan ’n -e bykom.","en":"True. We say *Die kussing is sag*, not *Die kussing is sagte*. An -e can only be added before the noun."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **vergrotende trap** van *dik*?","en":"What is the **comparative** of *dik* (thick)?"},"options":[{"af":"diker","en":"diker"},{"af":"dikker","en":"dikker"},{"af":"meer dik","en":"meer dik"},{"af":"dikste","en":"dikste"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*dik* het ’n kort klank, so die k verdubbel voor -er: *dikker*. *Dikste* is die oortreffende trap.","en":"*dik* has a short sound, so the k doubles before -er: *dikker*. *Dikste* is the superlative."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi met die **oortreffende trap**: *Ons ry met die ___ trein in die land.* (vinnig)","en":"Complete with the **superlative**: *Ons ry met die ___ trein in die land.* (We ride on the ___ train in the country.) (*vinnig*)"},"options":[{"af":"vinniger","en":"vinniger"},{"af":"mees vinniger","en":"mees vinniger"},{"af":"vinnigstes","en":"vinnigstes"},{"af":"vinnigste","en":"vinnigste"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die oortreffende trap van *vinnig* is *vinnigste* – die heel vinnigste van almal. *Vinniger* is die vergrotende trap.","en":"The superlative of *vinnig* (fast) is *vinnigste* (fastest) – the very fastest of all. *Vinniger* is the comparative."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke stellende trap by sy vergrotende trap.","en":"Match each positive degree to its comparative."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"goed","en":"goed"},"r":{"af":"beter","en":"beter"}},{"l":{"af":"veel","en":"veel"},"r":{"af":"meer","en":"meer"}},{"l":{"af":"min","en":"min"},"r":{"af":"minder","en":"minder"}},{"l":{"af":"hoog","en":"hoog"},"r":{"af":"hoër","en":"hoër"}},{"l":{"af":"duur","en":"duur"},"r":{"af":"duurder","en":"duurder"}}],"explain":{"af":"*goed → beter, veel → meer* en *min → minder* is onreëlmatig. *hoog → hoër* verloor die g, en *duur → duurder* kry -der omdat dit op -r eindig.","en":"*goed → beter, veel → meer* and *min → minder* are irregular. *hoog → hoër* loses the g, and *duur → duurder* adds -der because it ends in -r."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is korrek?","en":"Which sentence is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Sipho is langer dan sy broer.","en":"Sipho is langer dan sy broer."},{"af":"Sipho is meer langer as sy broer.","en":"Sipho is meer langer as sy broer."},{"af":"Sipho is langer as sy broer.","en":"Sipho is langer as sy broer."},{"af":"Sipho is langste as sy broer.","en":"Sipho is langste as sy broer."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Ons vergelyk twee mense met die vergrotende trap en **as**: *langer as*. *Dan* is verkeerd, *meer langer* gebruik twee trappe, en *langste* is vir die meeste van almal.","en":"We compare two people with the comparative and **as** (than): *langer as*. *Dan* is wrong, *meer langer* uses two degrees, and *langste* is for the most of all."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hierdie tas is swaar, maar daardie een is nog ___.","en":"*Hierdie tas is swaar, maar daardie een is nog ___.* (This bag is heavy, but that one is even ___.)"},"answers":{"af":["swaarder"],"en":["swaarder"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["swaarer","swaarste","swarer"],"en":["swaarer","swaarste","swarer"]}},"explain":{"af":"*swaar* eindig op -r, so die vergrotende trap kry -der: *swaarder*.","en":"*swaar* (heavy) ends in -r, so the comparative adds -der: *swaarder* (heavier)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die oortreffende trap van *goed* is *goedste*.","en":"The superlative of *goed* is *goedste*."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. *goed* is onreëlmatig: *goed – beter – beste*.","en":"False. *goed* (good) is irregular: *goed – beter – beste* (good – better – best)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter twee woorde is byvoeglike naamwoorde? *Die klein katjie slaap op die sagte kombers.*","en":"Which two words are adjectives? *Die klein katjie slaap op die sagte kombers.* (The small kitten sleeps on the soft blanket.)"},"options":[{"af":"klein, sagte","en":"klein, sagte"},{"af":"katjie, kombers","en":"katjie, kombers"},{"af":"slaap, sagte","en":"slaap, sagte"},{"af":"klein, slaap","en":"klein, slaap"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*klein* beskryf die katjie en *sagte* beskryf die kombers. *Katjie* en *kombers* is naamwoorde en *slaap* is ’n werkwoord.","en":"*klein* (small) describes the kitten and *sagte* (soft) describes the blanket. *Katjie* and *kombers* are nouns and *slaap* (sleeps) is a verb."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Zanele was die ___ kind in die klas toe die vakansie begin het.*","en":"Complete: *Zanele was die ___ kind in die klas toe die vakansie begin het.* (Zanele was the ___ child in the class when the holiday started.)"},"options":[{"af":"meeste opgewonde","en":"meeste opgewonde"},{"af":"mees opgewonde","en":"mees opgewonde"},{"af":"mees opgewondste","en":"mees opgewondste"},{"af":"meer opgewondste","en":"meer opgewondste"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"By ’n lang woord soos *opgewonde* gebruik ons *mees* vir die oortreffende trap: *die mees opgewonde kind*. Moenie *mees* en -ste saam gebruik nie.","en":"With a long word like *opgewonde* (excited) we use *mees* for the superlative: *die mees opgewonde kind* (the most excited child). Don’t use *mees* and -ste together."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Ek het min geld, maar my broer het nog ___ geld as ek.","en":"*Ek het min geld, maar my broer het nog ___ geld as ek.* (I have little money, but my brother has even ___ money than me.)"},"answers":{"af":["minder"],"en":["minder"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["minner","minste","mindere"],"en":["minner","minste","mindere"]}},"explain":{"af":"*min* is onreëlmatig: *min – minder – minste*. Ons vergelyk twee mense (*as ek*), so ons gebruik die vergrotende trap: *minder*.","en":"*min* is irregular: *min – minder – minste*. We compare two people (*as ek* – than me), so we use the comparative: *minder* (less)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter sin is die byvoeglike naamwoord korrek gebruik?","en":"In which sentence is the adjective used correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Die vriendelik juffrou het ons gehelp.","en":"Die vriendelik juffrou het ons gehelp."},{"af":"Die juffrou is baie vriendelike.","en":"Die juffrou is baie vriendelike."},{"af":"’n Vriendelikke juffrou het ons gehelp.","en":"’n Vriendelikke juffrou het ons gehelp."},{"af":"Die vriendelike juffrou het ons gehelp.","en":"Die vriendelike juffrou het ons gehelp."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Woorde op -lik kry -e voor die naamwoord: *die vriendelike juffrou*. Ná *is* kry dit nie -e nie (*is vriendelik*), en die k word nie verdubbel nie.","en":"Words ending in -lik add -e before the noun: *die vriendelike juffrou* (the friendly teacher). After *is* there is no -e (*is vriendelik*), and the k is not doubled."}}]},{"id":"afr5-t2-bywoorde-voorsetsels","title":{"af":"Bywoorde en voorsetsels","en":"Adverbs and prepositions"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal bywoorde van tyd, plek en wyse kan herken, die regte voorsetsel in ’n sin kan kies en vaste uitdrukkings soos *trots op* en *bang vir* korrek kan gebruik.","en":"You will be able to recognise adverbs of time, place and manner, choose the right preposition in a sentence and use fixed expressions such as *trots op* and *bang vir* correctly."},"summary":{"af":"## Bywoorde\n\n’n **Bywoord** sê meer oor die **werkwoord**: **wanneer**, **waar** of **hoe** iets gebeur.\n\n| Soort bywoord | Vraag | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Tyd** | Wanneer? | *gister, vandag, môre, nou, later, altyd, dikwels* |\n| **Plek** | Waar? | *hier, daar, buite, binne, oral, bo, onder* |\n| **Wyse** (manier) | Hoe? | *vinnig, stadig, hard, saggies, versigtig, netjies* |\n\n*Gister het Nomsa vinnig buite gehardloop.* Hier is *gister* ’n bywoord van tyd, *vinnig* van wyse en *buite* van plek.\n\nBywoorde van **graad** sê hoe erg of hoeveel: *baie, so, te, nogal*. *Die water is **baie** koud.*\n\n> **Onthou:** As ’n bywoord van tyd die sin begin, bly die werkwoord op die tweede plek: ***Môre gaan** ons see toe.*\n\n## Byvoeglike naamwoord of bywoord?\n\nIn Afrikaans lyk die twee dikwels presies dieselfde! Kyk **wat** die woord beskryf:\n\n- *Die **vinnige** perd …* – *vinnige* beskryf die **perd** (’n naamwoord). Dit is ’n **byvoeglike naamwoord**.\n- *Die perd hardloop **vinnig**.* – *vinnig* sê **hoe** die perd hardloop (die werkwoord). Dit is ’n **bywoord**, en ’n bywoord kry nooit ’n -e nie.\n\n**Toets:** Vra *Hoe?* ná die werkwoord: *Hoe hardloop die perd?* – *Vinnig.* As die woord die antwoord gee, is dit ’n bywoord.\n\n## Voorsetsels\n\n’n **Voorsetsel** staan voor ’n naamwoord of voornaamwoord en wys hoe dinge met mekaar verband hou – dikwels **waar** iets is.\n\n| Voorsetsel | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|\n| op | Die kat lê **op** die bed. |\n| in | Die melk is **in** die yskas. |\n| onder | Die skoene staan **onder** die bed. |\n| langs | Lerato sit **langs** haar maat. |\n| agter / voor | Die tuin is **agter** die huis en die motor staan **voor** die huis. |\n| tussen | Die B staan **tussen** die A en die C. |\n| oor | Die voël vlieg **oor** die dak. |\n| uit | Pa haal die koekie **uit** die blik. |\n| na | Ons ry **na** Durban. (Of: Ons ry Durban **toe**.) |\n| met / sonder | Sy skryf **met** ’n pen. Hy gaan uit **sonder** sy baadjie. |\n| vir | Die geskenk is **vir** Ma. |\n\nVir **tyd** gebruik ons: **om** ’n uur (*om drie-uur*), **op** ’n dag (*op Maandag*) en **in** ’n maand of seisoen (*in Desember, in die winter*).\n\n## Vaste uitdrukkings\n\nParty woorde gaan altyd saam met ’n **vaste voorsetsel**. Leer hulle as ’n paar, want jy kan nie die voorsetsel raai nie. Skryf elke nuwe een saam met ’n voorbeeldsin in jou taalboek neer:\n\n| Uitdrukking | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|\n| bang **vir** | Sipho is bang **vir** slange. |\n| lief **vir** | Ek is lief **vir** my ouma. |\n| trots **op** | Ons is trots **op** ons span. |\n| wag **vir** | Ons wag **vir** die bus. |\n| kwaad **vir** | Moenie kwaad wees **vir** jou broer nie. |\n| luister **na** | Luister mooi **na** die vraag. |\n| dink **aan** | Ek dink baie **aan** my oupa. |\n| hou **van** | Ek hou **van** pannekoek. |\n| glo **in** | Hy glo **in** homself. |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie Engels woord vir woord vertaal nie. *Proud of* is ***trots op*** (nie *trots van* nie), en *afraid of* is ***bang vir*** (nie *bang van* nie).","en":"## Adverbs (*bywoorde*)\n\nAn **adverb** tells us more about the **verb**: **when**, **where** or **how** something happens.\n\n| Kind of adverb | Question | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Time** (*tyd*) | *Wanneer?* (When?) | *gister* (yesterday), *vandag* (today), *môre* (tomorrow), *nou* (now), *later, altyd* (always), *dikwels* (often) |\n| **Place** (*plek*) | *Waar?* (Where?) | *hier* (here), *daar* (there), *buite* (outside), *binne* (inside), *oral* (everywhere), *bo* (above), *onder* (below) |\n| **Manner** (*wyse*) | *Hoe?* (How?) | *vinnig* (fast), *stadig* (slowly), *hard* (loudly/hard), *saggies* (softly), *versigtig* (carefully), *netjies* (neatly) |\n\n*Gister het Nomsa vinnig buite gehardloop.* (Yesterday Nomsa ran fast outside.) Here *gister* is an adverb of time, *vinnig* of manner and *buite* of place.\n\nAdverbs of **degree** say how much: *baie* (very), *so, te* (too), *nogal* (quite). *Die water is **baie** koud.* (The water is very cold.)\n\n> **Remember:** If an adverb of time starts the sentence, the verb stays in second place: ***Môre gaan** ons see toe.* (Tomorrow we are going to the sea.)\n\n## Adjective or adverb?\n\nIn Afrikaans the two often look exactly the same! Look at **what** the word describes:\n\n- *Die **vinnige** perd …* (the fast horse) – *vinnige* describes the **horse** (a noun). It is an **adjective**.\n- *Die perd hardloop **vinnig**.* (The horse runs fast.) – *vinnig* says **how** the horse runs (the verb). It is an **adverb**, and an adverb never takes an -e. (English often adds -ly; Afrikaans does not.)\n\n**Test:** Ask *Hoe?* (How?) after the verb: *Hoe hardloop die perd?* – *Vinnig.* If the word gives the answer, it is an adverb.\n\n## Prepositions (*voorsetsels*)\n\nA **preposition** stands before a noun or pronoun and shows how things are related – often **where** something is.\n\n| Preposition | Example |\n|---|---|\n| *op* (on) | *Die kat lê **op** die bed.* |\n| *in* (in) | *Die melk is **in** die yskas.* (fridge) |\n| *onder* (under) | *Die skoene staan **onder** die bed.* |\n| *langs* (next to) | *Lerato sit **langs** haar maat.* |\n| *agter / voor* (behind / in front of) | *Die tuin is **agter** die huis en die motor staan **voor** die huis.* |\n| *tussen* (between) | *Die B staan **tussen** die A en die C.* |\n| *oor* (over) | *Die voël vlieg **oor** die dak.* |\n| *uit* (out of) | *Pa haal die koekie **uit** die blik.* (tin) |\n| *na* (to) | *Ons ry **na** Durban.* (Or: *Ons ry Durban **toe**.*) |\n| *met / sonder* (with / without) | *Sy skryf **met** ’n pen. Hy gaan uit **sonder** sy baadjie.* |\n| *vir* (for) | *Die geskenk is **vir** Ma.* |\n\nFor **time** we use: **om** for a clock time (*om drie-uur* – at three o’clock), **op** for a day (*op Maandag* – on Monday) and **in** for a month or season (*in Desember, in die winter*).\n\n## Fixed expressions (*vaste uitdrukkings*)\n\nSome words always go with a **fixed preposition**. Learn them as a pair, because you can’t guess the preposition – and it is often not the one English uses. Write each new one down in your language book with an example sentence:\n\n| Expression | Example |\n|---|---|\n| *bang **vir*** (afraid of) | *Sipho is bang **vir** slange.* (snakes) |\n| *lief **vir*** (fond of, love) | *Ek is lief **vir** my ouma.* |\n| *trots **op*** (proud of) | *Ons is trots **op** ons span.* |\n| *wag **vir*** (wait for) | *Ons wag **vir** die bus.* |\n| *kwaad **vir*** (angry with) | *Moenie kwaad wees **vir** jou broer nie.* |\n| *luister **na*** (listen to) | *Luister mooi **na** die vraag.* |\n| *dink **aan*** (think of) | *Ek dink baie **aan** my oupa.* |\n| *hou **van*** (like) | *Ek hou **van** pannekoek.* |\n| *glo **in*** (believe in) | *Hy glo **in** homself.* |\n\n> **Common mistake:** Don’t translate English word for word. *Proud of* is ***trots op*** (not *trots van*), and *afraid of* is ***bang vir*** (not *bang van*)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Bywoord","en":"Adverb (bywoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat meer sê oor die werkwoord: wanneer, waar of hoe iets gebeur.","en":"A word that tells more about the verb: when, where or how something happens."}},{"term":{"af":"Bywoord van tyd","en":"Adverb of time (bywoord van tyd)"},"def":{"af":"’n Bywoord wat die vraag ‘Wanneer?’ beantwoord, soos ‘gister’ of ‘môre’.","en":"An adverb that answers the question ‘Wanneer?’ (When?), such as ‘gister’ (yesterday) or ‘môre’ (tomorrow)."}},{"term":{"af":"Bywoord van plek","en":"Adverb of place (bywoord van plek)"},"def":{"af":"’n Bywoord wat die vraag ‘Waar?’ beantwoord, soos ‘hier’ of ‘buite’.","en":"An adverb that answers the question ‘Waar?’ (Where?), such as ‘hier’ (here) or ‘buite’ (outside)."}},{"term":{"af":"Bywoord van wyse","en":"Adverb of manner (bywoord van wyse)"},"def":{"af":"’n Bywoord wat die vraag ‘Hoe?’ beantwoord, soos ‘vinnig’ of ‘versigtig’.","en":"An adverb that answers the question ‘Hoe?’ (How?), such as ‘vinnig’ (fast) or ‘versigtig’ (carefully)."}},{"term":{"af":"Bywoord van graad","en":"Adverb of degree (bywoord van graad)"},"def":{"af":"’n Bywoord wat sê hoe erg of hoeveel, soos ‘baie’ in ‘baie koud’.","en":"An adverb that says how much, like ‘baie’ (very) in ‘baie koud’ (very cold)."}},{"term":{"af":"Voorsetsel","en":"Preposition (voorsetsel)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woordjie voor ’n naamwoord wat wys hoe dinge verband hou, soos ‘op, onder’ of ‘tussen’.","en":"A small word before a noun that shows how things are related, such as ‘op’ (on), ‘onder’ (under) or ‘tussen’ (between)."}},{"term":{"af":"Vaste uitdrukking","en":"Fixed expression (vaste uitdrukking)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat altyd met dieselfde voorsetsel saamgaan, soos ‘trots op’ of ‘bang vir’.","en":"A word that always goes with the same preposition, such as ‘trots op’ (proud of) or ‘bang vir’ (afraid of)."}},{"term":{"af":"Anglisisme","en":"Anglicism (anglisisme)"},"def":{"af":"’n Fout wat ontstaan as jy Engels woord vir woord in Afrikaans vertaal, soos ‘trots van’.","en":"A mistake that happens when you translate English word for word into Afrikaans, such as ‘trots van’."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Soorte bywoorde","en":"Kinds of adverbs"},"problem":{"af":"Noem die bywoorde en sê watter soort elkeen is: *Gister het Nomsa vinnig buite gehardloop.*","en":"Find the adverbs and say what kind each one is: *Gister het Nomsa vinnig buite gehardloop.* (Yesterday Nomsa ran fast outside.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Vra *Wanneer het sy gehardloop?* – *gister*: bywoord van tyd.","en":"Ask *Wanneer?* (When did she run?) – *gister*: adverb of time."},{"af":"Vra *Hoe het sy gehardloop?* – *vinnig*: bywoord van wyse.","en":"Ask *Hoe?* (How did she run?) – *vinnig*: adverb of manner."},{"af":"Vra *Waar het sy gehardloop?* – *buite*: bywoord van plek.","en":"Ask *Waar?* (Where did she run?) – *buite*: adverb of place."}],"answer":{"af":"gister – tyd; vinnig – wyse; buite – plek","en":"*gister* – time; *vinnig* – manner; *buite* – place"}},{"title":{"af":"Voorsetsels uit ’n prent","en":"Prepositions from a picture"},"problem":{"af":"’n Prent wys ’n slaapkamer: ’n kat slaap bo-op die bed, ’n paar skoene staan op die vloer onder die bed, en ’n bal lê tussen die bed en die kas. Voltooi: *Die kat slaap ___ die bed. Die skoene staan ___ die bed. Die bal lê ___ die bed en die kas.*","en":"A picture shows a bedroom: a cat sleeps on top of the bed, a pair of shoes stands on the floor under the bed, and a ball lies between the bed and the cupboard. Complete: *Die kat slaap ___ die bed. Die skoene staan ___ die bed. Die bal lê ___ die bed en die kas.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Die kat is bo-op die bed: *op*.","en":"The cat is on top of the bed: *op* (on)."},{"af":"Die skoene is laer as die bed, daaronder: *onder*.","en":"The shoes are lower than the bed, beneath it: *onder* (under)."},{"af":"Die bal het die bed aan die een kant en die kas aan die ander kant: *tussen*.","en":"The ball has the bed on one side and the cupboard on the other: *tussen* (between)."}],"answer":{"af":"Die kat slaap op die bed. Die skoene staan onder die bed. Die bal lê tussen die bed en die kas.","en":"*Die kat slaap op die bed. Die skoene staan onder die bed. Die bal lê tussen die bed en die kas.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Verbeter die vaste uitdrukkings","en":"Correct the fixed expressions"},"problem":{"af":"Verbeter die sin: *Ek is trots van my suster, want sy is nie bang van die donker nie.*","en":"Correct the sentence: *Ek is trots van my suster, want sy is nie bang van die donker nie.* (I am proud of my sister, because she is not afraid of the dark.)"},"steps":[{"af":"*trots van* is ’n anglisisme (Engels *proud of*). Die vaste uitdrukking is *trots op*.","en":"*trots van* is an anglicism (English *proud of*). The fixed expression is *trots op*."},{"af":"*bang van* is ook uit Engels vertaal (*afraid of*). Die vaste uitdrukking is *bang vir*.","en":"*bang van* is also translated from English (*afraid of*). The fixed expression is *bang vir*."}],"answer":{"af":"Ek is trots op my suster, want sy is nie bang vir die donker nie.","en":"*Ek is trots op my suster, want sy is nie bang vir die donker nie.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Byvoeglike naamwoord of bywoord?","en":"Adjective or adverb?"},"problem":{"af":"Is die vetgedrukte woorde byvoeglike naamwoorde of bywoorde? *Die **vinnige** perd hardloop **vinnig** om die baan.*","en":"Are the bold words adjectives or adverbs? *Die **vinnige** perd hardloop **vinnig** om die baan.* (The fast horse runs fast around the track.)"},"steps":[{"af":"*vinnige* staan voor *perd* en beskryf die perd, ’n naamwoord. Dit het ook ’n -e. Dus: byvoeglike naamwoord.","en":"*vinnige* stands before *perd* (horse) and describes the horse, a noun. It also has an -e. So: adjective."},{"af":"*vinnig* sê hoe die perd *hardloop* – dit beskryf die werkwoord. Dus: bywoord van wyse.","en":"*vinnig* says how the horse *hardloop* (runs) – it describes the verb. So: adverb of manner."}],"answer":{"af":"*vinnige* = byvoeglike naamwoord; *vinnig* = bywoord van wyse","en":"*vinnige* = adjective; *vinnig* = adverb of manner"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is ’n **bywoord van tyd**?","en":"Which word is an **adverb of time**?"},"options":[{"af":"gister","en":"gister"},{"af":"hier","en":"hier"},{"af":"vinnig","en":"vinnig"},{"af":"buite","en":"buite"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Gister* beantwoord die vraag *Wanneer?* *Hier* en *buite* is bywoorde van plek, en *vinnig* is ’n bywoord van wyse.","en":"*Gister* (yesterday) answers the question *Wanneer?* (When?). *Hier* and *buite* are adverbs of place, and *vinnig* is an adverb of manner."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Die hond kruip ___ die tafel weg, want hy is bang vir die donderweer.*","en":"Complete: *Die hond kruip ___ die tafel weg, want hy is bang vir die donderweer.* (The dog hides ___ the table, because it is afraid of the thunder.)"},"options":[{"af":"op","en":"op"},{"af":"oor","en":"oor"},{"af":"onder","en":"onder"},{"af":"sonder","en":"sonder"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Om weg te kruip, gaan die hond **onder** die tafel in. *Op* en *oor* sou hom bo-op of bo-oor die tafel sit, en *sonder* maak nie sin nie.","en":"To hide, the dog goes **under** (*onder*) the table. *Op* (on) and *oor* (over) would put it on top of or above the table, and *sonder* (without) makes no sense."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Ek is baie lief ___ my ouma.","en":"*Ek is baie lief ___ my ouma.* (I love my granny very much.)"},"answers":{"af":["vir"],"en":["vir"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["van","op","met"],"en":["van","op","met"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Lief vir* is ’n vaste uitdrukking: *Ek is lief vir my ouma.*","en":"*Lief vir* is a fixed expression: *Ek is lief vir my ouma.*"}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In die sin *Lerato skryf netjies* is *netjies* ’n bywoord van wyse.","en":"In the sentence *Lerato skryf netjies* (Lerato writes neatly), *netjies* is an adverb of manner."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. *Netjies* sê **hoe** Lerato skryf, so dit is ’n bywoord van wyse.","en":"True. *Netjies* (neatly) says **how** Lerato writes, so it is an adverb of manner."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Hierdie geskenk is ___ jou, want dit is jou verjaarsdag!*","en":"Complete: *Hierdie geskenk is ___ jou, want dit is jou verjaarsdag!* (This present is ___ you, because it is your birthday!)"},"options":[{"af":"van","en":"van"},{"af":"vir","en":"vir"},{"af":"met","en":"met"},{"af":"uit","en":"uit"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Geskenk wat iemand kry, is **vir** daardie persoon. *Van jou* sou beteken dat jy dit gegee het.","en":"A present someone receives is **for** (*vir*) that person. *Van jou* would mean that you gave it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter vraag beantwoord ’n **bywoord van plek**?","en":"Which question does an **adverb of place** answer?"},"options":[{"af":"Wanneer?","en":"Wanneer?"},{"af":"Hoe?","en":"Hoe?"},{"af":"Wie?","en":"Wie?"},{"af":"Waar?","en":"Waar?"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Bywoord van plek sê **waar** iets gebeur, soos *hier, daar* of *buite*. *Wanneer?* is vir tyd en *Hoe?* vir wyse.","en":"An adverb of place says **where** something happens, such as *hier, daar* or *buite*. *Wanneer?* (When?) is for time and *Hoe?* (How?) for manner."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke woord by sy vaste voorsetsel.","en":"Match each word to its fixed preposition."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"trots","en":"trots"},"r":{"af":"op","en":"op"}},{"l":{"af":"luister","en":"luister"},"r":{"af":"na","en":"na"}},{"l":{"af":"dink","en":"dink"},"r":{"af":"aan","en":"aan"}},{"l":{"af":"hou","en":"hou"},"r":{"af":"van","en":"van"}},{"l":{"af":"glo","en":"glo"},"r":{"af":"in","en":"in"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hierdie pare moet jy leer: *trots op, luister na, dink aan, hou van* en *glo in*.","en":"You have to learn these pairs: *trots op* (proud of), *luister na* (listen to), *dink aan* (think of), *hou van* (like) and *glo in* (believe in)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *In die alfabet staan die letter B ___ die A en die C.*","en":"Complete: *In die alfabet staan die letter B ___ die A en die C.* (In the alphabet the letter B stands ___ the A and the C.)"},"options":[{"af":"agter","en":"agter"},{"af":"onder","en":"onder"},{"af":"tussen","en":"tussen"},{"af":"sonder","en":"sonder"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die B het die A aan die een kant en die C aan die ander kant, so dit staan **tussen** hulle.","en":"The B has the A on one side and the C on the other, so it stands **between** (*tussen*) them."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die skool begin elke dag ___ halfagt.","en":"*Die skool begin elke dag ___ halfagt.* (School starts every day ___ half past seven.)"},"answers":{"af":["om"],"en":["om"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["op","in","by"],"en":["op","in","by"]}},"explain":{"af":"Vir ’n tyd op die horlosie gebruik ons **om**: *om halfagt, om drie-uur*. *Op* is vir ’n dag en *in* vir ’n maand.","en":"For a clock time we use **om** (at): *om halfagt, om drie-uur*. *Op* is for a day and *in* for a month."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In die sin *Die vinnige hasie hardloop weg* is *vinnige* ’n bywoord.","en":"In the sentence *Die vinnige hasie hardloop weg* (The fast little hare runs away), *vinnige* is an adverb."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. *Vinnige* beskryf die **hasie**, ’n naamwoord, so dit is ’n byvoeglike naamwoord. ’n Bywoord sou die werkwoord beskryf en kry nie ’n -e nie.","en":"False. *Vinnige* describes the **hare** (*hasie*), a noun, so it is an adjective. An adverb would describe the verb and does not take an -e."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin gebruik die vaste uitdrukking **korrek**?","en":"Which sentence uses the fixed expression **correctly**?"},"options":[{"af":"Ons wag al ’n uur vir die bus.","en":"Ons wag al ’n uur vir die bus."},{"af":"Ons wag al ’n uur van die bus.","en":"Ons wag al ’n uur van die bus."},{"af":"Ons wag al ’n uur aan die bus.","en":"Ons wag al ’n uur aan die bus."},{"af":"Ons wag al ’n uur uit die bus.","en":"Ons wag al ’n uur uit die bus."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die vaste uitdrukking is *wag vir*: *Ons wag al ’n uur vir die bus.*","en":"The fixed expression is *wag vir* (wait for): *Ons wag al ’n uur vir die bus.* (We have been waiting for the bus for an hour.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Moenie ___ jou hoed in die son speel nie!*","en":"Complete: *Moenie ___ jou hoed in die son speel nie!* (Don’t play in the sun ___ your hat!)"},"options":[{"af":"met","en":"met"},{"af":"vir","en":"vir"},{"af":"onder","en":"onder"},{"af":"sonder","en":"sonder"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die raad is dat jy jou hoed moet dra, so jy moet nie **sonder** jou hoed speel nie.","en":"The advice is that you should wear your hat, so you must not play **without** (*sonder*) your hat."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Pa haal die laaste koekie ___ die blik.","en":"*Pa haal die laaste koekie ___ die blik.* (Dad takes the last biscuit ___ the tin.)"},"answers":{"af":["uit"],"en":["uit"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["in","op","onder"],"en":["in","op","onder"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die koekie was in die blik en Pa haal dit daar weg, so dit kom **uit** die blik.","en":"The biscuit was in the tin and Dad takes it away from there, so it comes **out of** (*uit*) the tin."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **bywoord van plek** in die sin? *Ons het gister lekker by die see gespeel.*","en":"What is the **adverb of place** in the sentence? *Ons het gister lekker by die see gespeel.* (We played nicely at the sea yesterday.)"},"options":[{"af":"gister","en":"gister"},{"af":"by die see","en":"by die see"},{"af":"lekker","en":"lekker"},{"af":"gespeel","en":"gespeel"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*By die see* sê **waar** ons gespeel het. *Gister* sê wanneer (tyd), *lekker* sê hoe (wyse) en *gespeel* is die werkwoord.","en":"*By die see* (at the sea) says **where** we played. *Gister* says when (time), *lekker* says how (manner) and *gespeel* is the verb."}}]},{"id":"afr5-t2-voegwoorde-woordorde","title":{"af":"Voegwoorde en woordorde (STOMPI)","en":"Conjunctions and word order (STOMPI)"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal sinne in die regte STOMPI-volgorde kan skryf en twee sinne met voegwoorde soos *want, dus* en *omdat* korrek kan saamvoeg.","en":"You will be able to write sentences in the correct STOMPI order and join two sentences correctly with conjunctions such as *want, dus* and *omdat*."},"summary":{"af":"## Die werkwoord staan op die tweede plek\n\nIn ’n gewone Afrikaanse stelsin staan die **eerste werkwoord** altyd op die **tweede plek**:\n\n*Ons **ry** elke dag met die bus skool toe.*\n\n“Plek” beteken ’n sinsdeel, nie een woord nie. As die sin met iets anders as die onderwerp begin, bly die werkwoord op die tweede plek en die **onderwerp skuif ná die werkwoord**. Dit heet **inversie**:\n\n*Elke dag **ry ons** met die bus skool toe.*\n\n## STOMPI\n\nDie res van die sin volg ’n vaste volgorde. Onthou dit met die woord **STOMPI**:\n\n| Letter | Sinsdeel | Vra | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **S** | Onderwerp (subjek) + werkwoord | Wie? | *Ek sal* |\n| **T** | Tyd | Wanneer? | *môre* |\n| **O** | Voorwerp (objek) | Wat? | *die koek* |\n| **M** | Manier | Hoe? | *versigtig* |\n| **P** | Plek | Waar of waarheen? | *na Ouma toe* |\n| **I** | Infinitief of 2de werkwoord | Watter werkwoord nog? | *neem* |\n\n*Ek **sal** môre die koek versigtig na Ouma toe **neem**.*\n\nNie elke sin het al die dele nie. Laat weg wat nie daar is nie, maar hou die volgorde: *Ons **gaan** Saterdag met die trein Kaapstad toe.* (S, T, M, P)\n\n> **Onthou:** Die **2de werkwoord** (ná *sal, kan, moet, wil* of *het*) staan heel aan die **einde**: *Ek **kan** goed **swem**. Sy **het** die bal **gevang**.*\n\n## Voegwoorde en woordorde\n\n’n **Voegwoord** las twee sinne aanmekaar. Die voegwoord bepaal wat met die woordorde gebeur. Kom ons voeg *Dit reën* en *Ons speel binne* saam:\n\n**Groep 1 – die woordorde bly dieselfde:** *en, maar, of, want*\n\n- *Dit reën **en** ons speel binne.*\n- *Ons speel binne, **want** dit reën buite.*\n\n**Groep 2 – die werkwoord kom reg ná die voegwoord:** *dus, daarom*\n\n- *Dit reën, **dus speel** ons binne.*\n\n**Groep 3 – die werkwoord gaan na die einde:** *omdat, dat, toe, as, wanneer, terwyl, sodat, voordat, nadat*\n\n- *Ons speel binne, **omdat** dit buite **reën**.*\n- *Ek weet **dat** jy môre **kom**.*\n- *Ons het geswem **toe** dit warm **was**.*\n- *Lees ’n boek **terwyl** jy **wag**.*\n- *Ma het ons geroep **nadat** sy die kos **gemaak het**.*\n\nLet op die laaste sin: as daar twee werkwoorde aan die einde is, kom *het* ná die *ge-*woord: *gemaak het*.\n\nKies die voegwoord volgens wat jy wil sê:\n\n- iets **byvoeg**: *en* · ’n **teenstelling**: *maar* · ’n **keuse**: *of*\n- ’n **rede**: *want, omdat* · ’n **gevolg**: *dus, daarom* · ’n **doel**: *sodat*\n- **tyd**: *toe, wanneer, terwyl, voordat, nadat* · ’n **voorwaarde**: *as*\n\n## Begin met die voegwoord\n\n’n Groep 3-voegwoord kan ook die sin **begin**. Dan kom daar ’n **komma** ná die eerste deel, en die tweede deel begin met die **werkwoord**:\n\n- ***Wanneer** die klok **lui**, **gaan** ons klas toe.*\n- ***Voordat** jy **eet**, **was** jy jou hande.*\n\nOnthou dit as **werkwoord – komma – werkwoord**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *want* en *omdat* beteken amper dieselfde, maar hulle werk anders! *…, want dit **reën** buite* (werkwoord bly op die 2de plek), maar *…, omdat dit buite **reën*** (werkwoord aan die einde). Moet hulle nie meng nie.","en":"## The verb stands in second place\n\nIn an ordinary Afrikaans statement the **first verb** always stands in **second place**:\n\n*Ons **ry** elke dag met die bus skool toe.* (We ride to school by bus every day.)\n\n“Place” means a part of the sentence, not one word. If the sentence starts with something other than the subject, the verb stays in second place and the **subject moves after the verb**. This is called **inversion** (*inversie*):\n\n*Elke dag **ry ons** met die bus skool toe.* (Every day we ride to school by bus.)\n\n## STOMPI\n\nThe rest of the sentence follows a fixed order. Remember it with the word **STOMPI**:\n\n| Letter | Sentence part | Ask | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **S** | Subject (*onderwerp*) + verb | Who? | *Ek sal* (I will) |\n| **T** | Time (*tyd*) | When? | *môre* (tomorrow) |\n| **O** | Object (*voorwerp*) | What? | *die koek* (the cake) |\n| **M** | Manner (*manier*) | How? | *versigtig* (carefully) |\n| **P** | Place (*plek*) | Where (to)? | *na Ouma toe* (to Granny) |\n| **I** | Infinitive or 2nd verb | Which other verb? | *neem* (take) |\n\n*Ek **sal** môre die koek versigtig na Ouma toe **neem**.* (I will carefully take the cake to Granny tomorrow.)\n\nNot every sentence has all the parts. Leave out what isn’t there, but keep the order: *Ons **gaan** Saterdag met die trein Kaapstad toe.* (We are going to Cape Town by train on Saturday.) (S, T, M, P)\n\n> **Remember:** The **2nd verb** (after *sal, kan, moet, wil* or *het*) goes right at the **end**: *Ek **kan** goed **swem**.* (I can swim well.) *Sy **het** die bal **gevang**.* (She caught the ball.)\n\n## Conjunctions (*voegwoorde*) and word order\n\nA **conjunction** joins two sentences. The conjunction decides what happens to the word order. Let’s join *Dit reën* (It is raining) and *Ons speel binne* (We play inside):\n\n**Group 1 – the word order stays the same:** *en* (and), *maar* (but), *of* (or), *want* (because)\n\n- *Dit reën **en** ons speel binne.*\n- *Ons speel binne, **want** dit reën buite.*\n\n**Group 2 – the verb comes straight after the conjunction:** *dus, daarom* (so, therefore)\n\n- *Dit reën, **dus speel** ons binne.*\n\n**Group 3 – the verb goes to the end:** *omdat* (because), *dat* (that), *toe* (when – past), *as* (if/when), *wanneer* (when), *terwyl* (while), *sodat* (so that), *voordat* (before), *nadat* (after)\n\n- *Ons speel binne, **omdat** dit buite **reën**.*\n- *Ek weet **dat** jy môre **kom**.* (I know that you are coming tomorrow.)\n- *Ons het geswem **toe** dit warm **was**.* (We swam when it was hot.)\n- *Lees ’n boek **terwyl** jy **wag**.* (Read a book while you wait.)\n- *Ma het ons geroep **nadat** sy die kos **gemaak het**.* (Mom called us after she had made the food.)\n\nLook at the last sentence: when there are two verbs at the end, *het* comes after the *ge-* word: *gemaak het*.\n\nChoose the conjunction by what you want to say:\n\n- **adding** something: *en* · a **contrast**: *maar* · a **choice**: *of*\n- a **reason**: *want, omdat* · a **result**: *dus, daarom* · a **purpose**: *sodat*\n- **time**: *toe, wanneer, terwyl, voordat, nadat* · a **condition**: *as* (if)\n\n## Starting with the conjunction\n\nA Group 3 conjunction can also **start** the sentence. Then there is a **comma** after the first part, and the second part starts with the **verb**:\n\n- ***Wanneer** die klok **lui**, **gaan** ons klas toe.* (When the bell rings, we go to class.)\n- ***Voordat** jy **eet**, **was** jy jou hande.* (Before you eat, you wash your hands.)\n\nRemember it as **verb – comma – verb**.\n\n> **Common mistake:** *want* and *omdat* both mean “because”, but they work differently! *…, want dit **reën** buite* (verb stays in 2nd place), but *…, omdat dit buite **reën*** (verb at the end). Don’t mix them up."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Woordorde","en":"Word order (woordorde)"},"def":{"af":"Die volgorde waarin die woorde en sinsdele in ’n sin staan.","en":"The order in which the words and sentence parts stand in a sentence."}},{"term":{"af":"STOMPI","en":"STOMPI"},"def":{"af":"’n Geheuewoord vir die volgorde van sinsdele: Onderwerp, Tyd, Voorwerp, Manier, Plek, Infinitief.","en":"A memory word for the order of sentence parts: Subject, Time, Object, Manner, Place, Infinitive."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderwerp","en":"Subject (onderwerp)"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon of ding wat in die sin iets doen: ‘Ons’ in ‘Ons ry skool toe’.","en":"The person or thing that does something in the sentence: ‘Ons’ (we) in ‘Ons ry skool toe’."}},{"term":{"af":"Voorwerp","en":"Object (voorwerp)"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon of ding waaraan iets gedoen word: ‘die koek’ in ‘Ek neem die koek’.","en":"The person or thing something is done to: ‘die koek’ (the cake) in ‘Ek neem die koek’."}},{"term":{"af":"Infinitief","en":"Infinitive (infinitief)"},"def":{"af":"Die 2de werkwoord wat aan die einde van die sin staan, soos ‘swem’ in ‘Ek kan swem’.","en":"The 2nd verb that stands at the end of the sentence, like ‘swem’ in ‘Ek kan swem’ (I can swim)."}},{"term":{"af":"Inversie","en":"Inversion (inversie)"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer die werkwoord voor die onderwerp staan omdat die sin met iets anders begin: ‘Môre gaan ons’.","en":"When the verb comes before the subject because the sentence starts with something else: ‘Môre gaan ons’ (Tomorrow we go)."}},{"term":{"af":"Voegwoord","en":"Conjunction (voegwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat twee sinne of sinsdele aanmekaar las, soos ‘en, want, omdat’.","en":"A word that joins two sentences or parts of sentences, such as ‘en, want, omdat’ (and, because)."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoofsin","en":"Main clause (hoofsin)"},"def":{"af":"’n Sin wat op sy eie kan staan en sin maak: ‘Ons speel binne.’","en":"A sentence that can stand on its own and make sense: ‘Ons speel binne.’ (We play inside.)"}},{"term":{"af":"Bysin","en":"Subordinate clause (bysin)"},"def":{"af":"’n Sinsdeel wat met ’n voegwoord soos ‘omdat’ begin en nie alleen kan staan nie; die werkwoord staan aan die einde.","en":"A part of a sentence that starts with a conjunction such as ‘omdat’ and cannot stand alone; its verb stands at the end."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Rangskik volgens STOMPI","en":"Arrange according to STOMPI"},"problem":{"af":"Rangskik die sinsdele in die regte volgorde: *na die strand / gaan / ons / Saterdag / met die trein*","en":"Put the sentence parts in the correct order: *na die strand / gaan / ons / Saterdag / met die trein* (to the beach / go / we / Saturday / by train)"},"steps":[{"af":"S + werkwoord: wie gaan? *Ons gaan*.","en":"S + verb: who is going? *Ons gaan*."},{"af":"T – wanneer? *Saterdag*. Daar is geen voorwerp (O) nie.","en":"T – when? *Saterdag*. There is no object (O)."},{"af":"M – hoe? *met die trein*. P – waarheen? *na die strand*.","en":"M – how? *met die trein* (by train). P – where to? *na die strand* (to the beach)."},{"af":"Daar is geen 2de werkwoord (I) nie, so die sin is klaar.","en":"There is no 2nd verb (I), so the sentence is complete."}],"answer":{"af":"Ons gaan Saterdag met die trein na die strand.","en":"*Ons gaan Saterdag met die trein na die strand.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Begin met die tyd (inversie)","en":"Start with the time (inversion)"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die sin oor en begin met *Saterdag*: *Ons gaan Saterdag met die trein na die strand.*","en":"Rewrite the sentence starting with *Saterdag*: *Ons gaan Saterdag met die trein na die strand.*"},"steps":[{"af":"*Saterdag* staan nou op die eerste plek.","en":"*Saterdag* now takes the first place."},{"af":"Die werkwoord *gaan* moet op die tweede plek bly.","en":"The verb *gaan* must stay in second place."},{"af":"Die onderwerp *ons* kom nou ná die werkwoord. Die res bly in STOMPI-volgorde.","en":"The subject *ons* moves to after the verb. The rest stays in STOMPI order."}],"answer":{"af":"Saterdag gaan ons met die trein na die strand.","en":"*Saterdag gaan ons met die trein na die strand.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Voeg saam met *want* en met *omdat*","en":"Join with *want* and with *omdat*"},"problem":{"af":"Voeg die twee sinne saam, eers met *want* en dan met *omdat*: *Zanele is moeg. Sy het baie hard gewerk.*","en":"Join the two sentences, first with *want* and then with *omdat*: *Zanele is moeg. Sy het baie hard gewerk.* (Zanele is tired. She worked very hard.)"},"steps":[{"af":"*Want* is Groep 1: die woordorde bly dieselfde. *Zanele is moeg, want sy het baie hard gewerk.*","en":"*Want* is Group 1: the word order stays the same. *Zanele is moeg, want sy het baie hard gewerk.*"},{"af":"*Omdat* is Groep 3: die werkwoord *het* gaan na die einde.","en":"*Omdat* is Group 3: the verb *het* goes to the end."},{"af":"Aan die einde kom *het* ná *gewerk*: *… omdat sy baie hard gewerk het.*","en":"At the end *het* comes after *gewerk*: *… omdat sy baie hard gewerk het.*"}],"answer":{"af":"Zanele is moeg, want sy het baie hard gewerk. / Zanele is moeg, omdat sy baie hard gewerk het.","en":"*Zanele is moeg, want sy het baie hard gewerk.* / *Zanele is moeg, omdat sy baie hard gewerk het.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Begin met *Wanneer*","en":"Start with *Wanneer*"},"problem":{"af":"Voeg saam en begin met *Wanneer*: *Die klok lui. Ons gaan klas toe.*","en":"Join the sentences and start with *Wanneer* (when): *Die klok lui. Ons gaan klas toe.* (The bell rings. We go to class.)"},"steps":[{"af":"*Wanneer* is Groep 3, so in die eerste deel gaan die werkwoord na die einde: *Wanneer die klok lui*.","en":"*Wanneer* is Group 3, so in the first part the verb goes to the end: *Wanneer die klok lui*."},{"af":"Sit ’n komma ná die eerste deel.","en":"Put a comma after the first part."},{"af":"Die tweede deel begin met die werkwoord: *gaan ons klas toe* (werkwoord – komma – werkwoord).","en":"The second part starts with the verb: *gaan ons klas toe* (verb – comma – verb)."}],"answer":{"af":"Wanneer die klok lui, gaan ons klas toe.","en":"*Wanneer die klok lui, gaan ons klas toe.*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin het die korrekte woordorde?","en":"Which sentence has the correct word order?"},"options":[{"af":"Elke oggend ons ry met die bus skool toe.","en":"Elke oggend ons ry met die bus skool toe."},{"af":"Ons ry elke oggend met die bus skool toe.","en":"Ons ry elke oggend met die bus skool toe."},{"af":"Ons elke oggend ry met die bus skool toe.","en":"Ons elke oggend ry met die bus skool toe."},{"af":"Ons ry skool toe elke oggend met die bus.","en":"Ons ry skool toe elke oggend met die bus."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die werkwoord *ry* staan op die 2de plek, gevolg deur tyd (*elke oggend*), manier (*met die bus*) en plek (*skool toe*): STOMPI.","en":"The verb *ry* stands in 2nd place, followed by time (*elke oggend*), manner (*met die bus*) and place (*skool toe*): STOMPI."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin wat met *Gister* begin, is korrek?","en":"Which sentence starting with *Gister* (yesterday) is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Gister het ons by die see geswem.","en":"Gister het ons by die see geswem."},{"af":"Gister ons het by die see geswem.","en":"Gister ons het by die see geswem."},{"af":"Gister ons het geswem by die see.","en":"Gister ons het geswem by die see."},{"af":"Gister het geswem ons by die see.","en":"Gister het geswem ons by die see."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Gister* is die eerste sinsdeel, so *het* moet op die 2de plek kom en *ons* skuif ná *het* (inversie). *Geswem* bly aan die einde.","en":"*Gister* is the first sentence part, so *het* must come in 2nd place and *ons* moves after *het* (inversion). *Geswem* stays at the end."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Ek weet ___ jy die toets sal slaag.","en":"*Ek weet ___ jy die toets sal slaag.* (I know ___ you will pass the test.)"},"answers":{"af":["dat"],"en":["dat"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["want","maar","dus"],"en":["want","maar","dus"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Dat* las ’n sin aan *Ek weet* en stuur die werkwoorde (*sal slaag*) na die einde.","en":"*Dat* (that) joins a sentence to *Ek weet* (I know) and sends the verbs (*sal slaag*) to the end."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Ná die voegwoord *want* skuif die werkwoord na die einde van die sin.","en":"After the conjunction *want* the verb moves to the end of the sentence."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. *Want* is ’n Groep 1-voegwoord: die woordorde bly dieselfde. *Ek eet, want ek is honger.* Dit is *omdat* wat die werkwoord na die einde stuur.","en":"False. *Want* is a Group 1 conjunction: the word order stays the same. *Ek eet, want ek is honger.* (I eat, because I am hungry.) It is *omdat* that sends the verb to the end."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voeg saam met *omdat*: *Lerato lag. Die grap is snaaks.*","en":"Join with *omdat*: *Lerato lag. Die grap is snaaks.* (Lerato laughs. The joke is funny.)"},"options":[{"af":"Lerato lag, omdat die grap is snaaks.","en":"Lerato lag, omdat die grap is snaaks."},{"af":"Lerato lag, omdat is die grap snaaks.","en":"Lerato lag, omdat is die grap snaaks."},{"af":"Lerato lag, omdat die grap snaaks is.","en":"Lerato lag, omdat die grap snaaks is."},{"af":"Lerato lag omdat, die grap snaaks is.","en":"Lerato lag omdat, die grap snaaks is."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Omdat* is ’n Groep 3-voegwoord: die werkwoord *is* gaan na die einde: *omdat die grap snaaks is*.","en":"*Omdat* is a Group 3 conjunction: the verb *is* goes to the end: *omdat die grap snaaks is*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voegwoord verander die woordorde **nie**?","en":"Which conjunction does **not** change the word order?"},"options":[{"af":"omdat","en":"omdat"},{"af":"terwyl","en":"terwyl"},{"af":"nadat","en":"nadat"},{"af":"maar","en":"maar"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Maar* is ’n Groep 1-voegwoord, saam met *en, of* en *want*. *Omdat, terwyl* en *nadat* stuur die werkwoord na die einde.","en":"*Maar* (but) is a Group 1 conjunction, together with *en, of* and *want*. *Omdat, terwyl* and *nadat* send the verb to the end."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke STOMPI-letter by sy sinsdeel.","en":"Match each STOMPI letter to its sentence part."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"S","en":"S"},"r":{"af":"onderwerp – wie?","en":"subject – who?"}},{"l":{"af":"T","en":"T"},"r":{"af":"tyd – wanneer?","en":"time – when?"}},{"l":{"af":"M","en":"M"},"r":{"af":"manier – hoe?","en":"manner – how?"}},{"l":{"af":"P","en":"P"},"r":{"af":"plek – waar?","en":"place – where?"}},{"l":{"af":"I","en":"I"},"r":{"af":"infinitief – 2de werkwoord","en":"infinitive – 2nd verb"}}],"explain":{"af":"STOMPI: **S**ubjek (onderwerp), **T**yd, **O**bjek (voorwerp), **M**anier, **P**lek en **I**nfinitief, wat aan die einde staan.","en":"STOMPI: **S**ubject, **T**ime, **O**bject, **M**anner, **P**lace and **I**nfinitive, which stands at the end."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Nadat ons ___, het ons die skottelgoed gewas.*","en":"Complete: *Nadat ons ___, het ons die skottelgoed gewas.* (After we ___, we washed the dishes.)"},"options":[{"af":"het geëet","en":"het geëet"},{"af":"geëet het","en":"geëet het"},{"af":"eet het","en":"eet het"},{"af":"geëet","en":"geëet"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Nadat* stuur die werkwoorde na die einde, en daar kom *het* ná die *ge-*woord: *Nadat ons geëet het*.","en":"*Nadat* (after) sends the verbs to the end, and *het* comes after the *ge-* word: *Nadat ons geëet het*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In ’n gewone Afrikaanse stelsin staan die eerste werkwoord altyd op die ___ plek.","en":"In an ordinary Afrikaans statement the first verb always stands in the ___ place."},"answers":{"af":["tweede","2de","2"],"en":["second","2nd","2"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["eerste","laaste","derde"],"en":["first","last","third"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die werkwoord staan op die **tweede** plek, al begin die sin met iets anders as die onderwerp: *Môre **gaan** ons see toe.*","en":"The verb stands in the **second** place, even when the sentence starts with something other than the subject: *Môre **gaan** ons see toe.*"}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In die sin *Môre gaan ons Kaapstad toe* staan die werkwoord voor die onderwerp, omdat die sin met ’n tydwoord begin.","en":"In the sentence *Môre gaan ons Kaapstad toe* the verb stands before the subject, because the sentence starts with a time word."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Dit is inversie: *Môre* neem die eerste plek, *gaan* bly op die tweede plek en *ons* skuif ná die werkwoord.","en":"True. This is inversion: *Môre* (tomorrow) takes first place, *gaan* stays in second place and *ons* moves after the verb."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin met *dus* is korrek?","en":"Which sentence with *dus* (so) is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is koud, dus trek ek my baadjie aan.","en":"Dit is koud, dus trek ek my baadjie aan."},{"af":"Dit is koud, dus ek trek my baadjie aan.","en":"Dit is koud, dus ek trek my baadjie aan."},{"af":"Dit is koud, dus ek my baadjie aantrek.","en":"Dit is koud, dus ek my baadjie aantrek."},{"af":"Dit is koud, dus aan trek ek my baadjie.","en":"Dit is koud, dus aan trek ek my baadjie."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Dus* is ’n Groep 2-voegwoord: die werkwoord kom reg ná *dus*, en dan die onderwerp: *dus trek ek*.","en":"*Dus* is a Group 2 conjunction: the verb comes straight after *dus*, and then the subject: *dus trek ek*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin met *Toe* is korrek?","en":"Which sentence with *Toe* (when) is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Toe die reën ophou, ons het buite gespeel.","en":"Toe die reën ophou, ons het buite gespeel."},{"af":"Toe hou die reën op, ons het buite gespeel.","en":"Toe hou die reën op, ons het buite gespeel."},{"af":"Toe die reën hou op, het ons buite gespeel.","en":"Toe die reën hou op, het ons buite gespeel."},{"af":"Toe die reën ophou, het ons buite gespeel.","en":"Toe die reën ophou, het ons buite gespeel."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Toe* is hier Groep 3: *ophou* gaan na die einde van die eerste deel. Ná die komma begin die tweede deel met die werkwoord *het*: werkwoord – komma – werkwoord.","en":"Here *toe* is Group 3: *ophou* (stop) goes to the end of the first part. After the comma the second part starts with the verb *het*: verb – comma – verb."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Pa gee vir Ma ’n sambreel, ___ sy nie nat word nie.","en":"*Pa gee vir Ma ’n sambreel, ___ sy nie nat word nie.* (Dad gives Mom an umbrella, ___ she does not get wet.)"},"answers":{"af":["sodat"],"en":["sodat"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["want","maar","dus"],"en":["want","maar","dus"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Sodat* wys die doel (waarom Pa dit doen) en stuur die werkwoord *word* na die einde. Ná *want* of *maar* sou dit *sy word nie nat nie* wees.","en":"*Sodat* (so that) shows the purpose (why Dad does it) and sends the verb *word* to the end. After *want* or *maar* it would be *sy word nie nat nie*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **infinitief** (2de werkwoord) in die sin? *Ek sal môre my kamer netjies opruim.*","en":"What is the **infinitive** (2nd verb) in the sentence? *Ek sal môre my kamer netjies opruim.* (I will tidy my room neatly tomorrow.)"},"options":[{"af":"sal","en":"sal"},{"af":"môre","en":"môre"},{"af":"opruim","en":"opruim"},{"af":"netjies","en":"netjies"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Sal* is die eerste werkwoord op die 2de plek. *Opruim* is die 2de werkwoord en staan aan die einde (die I van STOMPI).","en":"*Sal* is the first verb in 2nd place. *Opruim* (tidy up) is the 2nd verb and stands at the end (the I of STOMPI)."}}]},{"id":"afr5-t2-ontkenning-sinsoorte","title":{"af":"Ontkenning, vraagsinne en sinsoorte","en":"Negation, questions and sentence types"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal sinne korrek met *nie … nie* en ontkennende woorde negatief kan maak, vrae kan vorm en die vier sinsoorte met die regte leesteken kan skryf.","en":"You will be able to make sentences negative correctly with *nie … nie* and negative words, form questions and write the four sentence types with the correct punctuation."},"summary":{"af":"## Dubbele ontkenning: nie … nie\n\nIn Afrikaans maak ons ’n sin ontkennend (negatief) met **twee keer *nie***:\n\n- Die **eerste *nie*** staan reg ná die werkwoord (of ná ’n voornaamwoord soos *hom* of *dit*).\n- Die **tweede *nie*** staan heel aan die **einde** van die sin.\n\n| Positief | Negatief |\n|---|---|\n| Ek hou van spinasie. | Ek hou **nie** van spinasie **nie**. |\n| Sy het die toets geslaag. | Sy het **nie** die toets geslaag **nie**. |\n| Ons sal die deur oopmaak. | Ons sal **nie** die deur oopmaak **nie**. |\n\nDink aan die twee *nie*’s soos **hakies**: die eerste maak die ontkenning oop, en die tweede maak dit aan die einde weer toe. Alles tussenin is deel van wat nie gebeur nie.\n\n**Een *nie* is genoeg** as die sin ná die eerste *nie* klaar is: *Die baba slaap **nie**. Ek weet **nie**. Ek ken hom **nie**.*\n\n> **Onthou:** Kyk wat ná die eerste *nie* kom. Is daar nog woorde? Sit ’n tweede *nie* aan die einde. Is daar niks? Dan is een *nie* genoeg.\n\n## Ontkennende woorde\n\nHierdie woorde maak ’n sin ook negatief. Hulle kry ook ’n *nie* aan die einde van die sin:\n\n| Positief | Negatief | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| iets | **niks** | *Ek het **niks** gekoop **nie**.* |\n| iemand | **niemand** | ***Niemand** het my gehelp **nie**.* |\n| altyd | **nooit** | *Hy is **nooit** laat **nie**.* |\n| oral | **nêrens** | *Ek kan my pen **nêrens** kry **nie**.* |\n| ’n | **geen** | *Daar is **geen** melk in die yskas **nie**.* |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Gebruik net **een** ontkennende woord voor in die sin. *Ek het nie niks gekry nie* is verkeerd; skryf *Ek het **niks** gekry **nie***. Die *nie* aan die einde mag jy ook nie vergeet nie.\n\n## Vraagsinne\n\nDaar is twee maniere om ’n vraag te maak:\n\n1. **Ja/nee-vraag:** sit die **werkwoord vooraan**. *Jy speel sokker.* → ***Speel** jy sokker?* *Sy het geëet.* → ***Het** sy geëet?*\n2. **Vraagwoord-vraag:** begin met ’n **vraagwoord**, dan die werkwoord, dan die onderwerp: *Waar **woon** jy?*\n\n| Vraagwoord | Vra na … | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| wie | ’n persoon | *Wie het gebel?* |\n| wat | ’n ding | *Wat eet jy?* |\n| waar | ’n plek | *Waar woon jy?* |\n| wanneer | ’n tyd | *Wanneer begin die vakansie?* |\n| hoekom | ’n rede | *Hoekom huil die baba?* |\n| hoe | ’n manier | *Hoe maak jy pannekoek?* |\n| hoeveel | ’n getal | *Hoeveel broers het jy?* |\n\n’n Vraag eindig altyd met ’n **vraagteken (?)**. Ook ’n vraag kan negatief wees: *Kom jy **nie**? Het jy **nie** jou huiswerk gedoen **nie**?*\n\n## Sinsoorte en leestekens\n\n| Sinsoort | Wat doen dit? | Leesteken | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Stelsin** | vertel of sê iets | punt (.) | *Die son skyn.* |\n| **Vraagsin** | vra iets | vraagteken (?) | *Skyn die son?* |\n| **Bevelsin** | gee ’n opdrag; begin met die werkwoord | punt of uitroepteken | *Maak die deur toe.* *Kom hier!* |\n| **Uitroepsin** | wys ’n sterk gevoel | uitroepteken (!) | *Wat ’n pragtige dag!* |\n\n’n Negatiewe bevel begin met **moenie** en eindig met **nie**: ***Moenie** in die gang hardloop **nie**!*","en":"## Double negation: *nie … nie*\n\nIn Afrikaans we make a sentence negative with **two *nie*’s** (not):\n\n- The **first *nie*** comes straight after the verb (or after a pronoun such as *hom* or *dit*).\n- The **second *nie*** comes right at the **end** of the sentence.\n\n| Positive | Negative |\n|---|---|\n| *Ek hou van spinasie.* (I like spinach.) | *Ek hou **nie** van spinasie **nie**.* (I don’t like spinach.) |\n| *Sy het die toets geslaag.* (She passed the test.) | *Sy het **nie** die toets geslaag **nie**.* |\n| *Ons sal die deur oopmaak.* (We will open the door.) | *Ons sal **nie** die deur oopmaak **nie**.* |\n\nThink of the two *nie*’s as **brackets**: the first one opens the negation, and the second one closes it again at the end. Everything in between is part of what does not happen.\n\n**One *nie* is enough** if the sentence is finished after the first *nie*: *Die baba slaap **nie**.* (The baby is not sleeping.) *Ek weet **nie**.* (I don’t know.) *Ek ken hom **nie**.* (I don’t know him.)\n\n> **Remember:** Look at what comes after the first *nie*. Are there more words? Put a second *nie* at the end. Is there nothing? Then one *nie* is enough.\n\n## Negative words (*ontkennende woorde*)\n\nThese words also make a sentence negative. They also take a *nie* at the end of the sentence:\n\n| Positive | Negative | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| *iets* (something) | ***niks*** (nothing) | *Ek het **niks** gekoop **nie**.* (I bought nothing.) |\n| *iemand* (someone) | ***niemand*** (nobody) | ***Niemand** het my gehelp **nie**.* (Nobody helped me.) |\n| *altyd* (always) | ***nooit*** (never) | *Hy is **nooit** laat **nie**.* (He is never late.) |\n| *oral* (everywhere) | ***nêrens*** (nowhere) | *Ek kan my pen **nêrens** kry **nie**.* (I can’t find my pen anywhere.) |\n| *’n* (a) | ***geen*** (no) | *Daar is **geen** melk in die yskas **nie**.* (There is no milk in the fridge.) |\n\n> **Common mistake:** Use only **one** negative word early in the sentence. *Ek het nie niks gekry nie* is wrong; write *Ek het **niks** gekry **nie*** (I got nothing). And don’t forget the *nie* at the end.\n\n## Questions (*vraagsinne*)\n\nThere are two ways to make a question:\n\n1. **Yes/no question:** put the **verb first**. *Jy speel sokker.* → ***Speel** jy sokker?* (Do you play soccer?) *Sy het geëet.* → ***Het** sy geëet?* (Has she eaten?)\n2. **Question-word question:** start with a **question word**, then the verb, then the subject: *Waar **woon** jy?* (Where do you live?)\n\n| Question word | Asks about … | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| *wie* (who) | a person | *Wie het gebel?* (Who phoned?) |\n| *wat* (what) | a thing | *Wat eet jy?* (What are you eating?) |\n| *waar* (where) | a place | *Waar woon jy?* |\n| *wanneer* (when) | a time | *Wanneer begin die vakansie?* (When does the holiday start?) |\n| *hoekom* (why) | a reason | *Hoekom huil die baba?* (Why is the baby crying?) |\n| *hoe* (how) | a way | *Hoe maak jy pannekoek?* (How do you make pancakes?) |\n| *hoeveel* (how many/much) | a number | *Hoeveel broers het jy?* (How many brothers do you have?) |\n\nA question always ends with a **question mark (?)**. A question can be negative too: *Kom jy **nie**?* (Aren’t you coming?) *Het jy **nie** jou huiswerk gedoen **nie**?* (Didn’t you do your homework?)\n\n## Sentence types and punctuation\n\n| Sentence type | What does it do? | Punctuation | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Statement** (*stelsin*) | tells or says something | full stop (.) | *Die son skyn.* (The sun is shining.) |\n| **Question** (*vraagsin*) | asks something | question mark (?) | *Skyn die son?* |\n| **Command** (*bevelsin*) | gives an instruction; starts with the verb | full stop or exclamation mark | *Maak die deur toe.* (Close the door.) *Kom hier!* |\n| **Exclamation** (*uitroepsin*) | shows a strong feeling | exclamation mark (!) | *Wat ’n pragtige dag!* (What a beautiful day!) |\n\nA negative command starts with **moenie** (don’t) and ends with **nie**: ***Moenie** in die gang hardloop **nie**!* (Don’t run in the passage!)"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Ontkenning","en":"Negation (ontkenning)"},"def":{"af":"Om ’n sin negatief te maak, sodat dit sê dat iets nie so is nie.","en":"Making a sentence negative, so that it says something is not so."}},{"term":{"af":"Dubbele ontkenning","en":"Double negation (dubbele ontkenning)"},"def":{"af":"Die Afrikaanse reël dat ’n negatiewe sin twee keer ‘nie’ kry: ‘Ek hou nie van tamaties nie.’","en":"The Afrikaans rule that a negative sentence gets ‘nie’ twice: ‘Ek hou nie van tamaties nie.’ (I don’t like tomatoes.)"}},{"term":{"af":"Ontkennende woord","en":"Negative word (ontkennende woord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat self negatief is, soos ‘niks, niemand, nooit, nêrens’ en ‘geen’.","en":"A word that is negative in itself, such as ‘niks, niemand, nooit, nêrens’ and ‘geen’ (nothing, nobody, never, nowhere, no)."}},{"term":{"af":"Stelsin","en":"Statement (stelsin)"},"def":{"af":"’n Sin wat iets vertel en met ’n punt eindig.","en":"A sentence that tells something and ends with a full stop."}},{"term":{"af":"Vraagsin","en":"Question (vraagsin)"},"def":{"af":"’n Sin wat iets vra en met ’n vraagteken eindig.","en":"A sentence that asks something and ends with a question mark."}},{"term":{"af":"Vraagwoord","en":"Question word (vraagwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord waarmee ’n vraag begin, soos ‘wie, waar, wanneer, hoekom’ of ‘hoeveel’.","en":"A word that starts a question, such as ‘wie, waar, wanneer, hoekom’ or ‘hoeveel’ (who, where, when, why, how many)."}},{"term":{"af":"Bevelsin","en":"Command (bevelsin)"},"def":{"af":"’n Sin wat ’n opdrag gee en met die werkwoord begin: ‘Sit asseblief.’","en":"A sentence that gives an instruction and starts with the verb: ‘Sit asseblief.’ (Please sit.)"}},{"term":{"af":"Uitroepsin","en":"Exclamation (uitroepsin)"},"def":{"af":"’n Sin wat ’n sterk gevoel wys en met ’n uitroepteken eindig: ‘Hoera, ons het gewen!’","en":"A sentence that shows a strong feeling and ends with an exclamation mark: ‘Hoera, ons het gewen!’ (Hooray, we won!)"}},{"term":{"af":"Leesteken","en":"Punctuation mark (leesteken)"},"def":{"af":"’n Teken soos ’n punt, komma, vraagteken of uitroepteken wat help om ’n sin reg te lees.","en":"A mark such as a full stop, comma, question mark or exclamation mark that helps you read a sentence correctly."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Maak die sinne negatief","en":"Make the sentences negative"},"problem":{"af":"Maak negatief: (a) *Thabo eet sy groente.* (b) *Die baba slaap.*","en":"Make negative: (a) *Thabo eet sy groente.* (Thabo eats his vegetables.) (b) *Die baba slaap.* (The baby is sleeping.)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Sit die eerste *nie* ná die werkwoord *eet*: *Thabo eet nie …*","en":"(a) Put the first *nie* after the verb *eet*: *Thabo eet nie …*"},{"af":"Ná die eerste *nie* kom nog woorde (*sy groente*), so sit ’n tweede *nie* aan die einde.","en":"After the first *nie* there are more words (*sy groente*), so put a second *nie* at the end."},{"af":"(b) Ná *slaap nie* kom niks meer nie, so een *nie* is genoeg.","en":"(b) After *slaap nie* nothing more follows, so one *nie* is enough."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Thabo eet nie sy groente nie. (b) Die baba slaap nie.","en":"(a) *Thabo eet nie sy groente nie.* (b) *Die baba slaap nie.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Gebruik ontkennende woorde","en":"Use negative words"},"problem":{"af":"Maak negatief deur die vetgedrukte woord te verander: (a) *Ek het **iets** in my tas.* (b) *Ons gaan **altyd** Saterdae swem.*","en":"Make negative by changing the bold word: (a) *Ek het **iets** in my tas.* (I have something in my bag.) (b) *Ons gaan **altyd** Saterdae swem.* (We always go swimming on Saturdays.)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die teenoorgestelde van *iets* is *niks*: *Ek het niks in my tas …*","en":"(a) The opposite of *iets* (something) is *niks* (nothing): *Ek het niks in my tas …*"},{"af":"Daar kom woorde ná *niks*, so die sin kry ’n *nie* aan die einde.","en":"Words come after *niks*, so the sentence gets a *nie* at the end."},{"af":"(b) Die teenoorgestelde van *altyd* is *nooit*, en die sin kry weer ’n *nie* aan die einde.","en":"(b) The opposite of *altyd* (always) is *nooit* (never), and the sentence again gets a *nie* at the end."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Ek het niks in my tas nie. (b) Ons gaan nooit Saterdae swem nie.","en":"(a) *Ek het niks in my tas nie.* (b) *Ons gaan nooit Saterdae swem nie.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Maak vrae","en":"Make questions"},"problem":{"af":"Maak twee vrae van die sin *Fatima woon in Kimberley*: (a) ’n ja/nee-vraag en (b) ’n vraag met *waar*.","en":"Make two questions from the sentence *Fatima woon in Kimberley* (Fatima lives in Kimberley): (a) a yes/no question and (b) a question with *waar* (where)."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Skuif die werkwoord *woon* na vore: *Woon Fatima in Kimberley?*","en":"(a) Move the verb *woon* to the front: *Woon Fatima in Kimberley?*"},{"af":"(b) *In Kimberley* is ’n plek, so die vraagwoord *waar* vervang dit en begin die vraag.","en":"(b) *In Kimberley* is a place, so the question word *waar* replaces it and starts the question."},{"af":"Ná *Waar* kom die werkwoord en dan die onderwerp, en die vraag kry ’n vraagteken.","en":"After *Waar* comes the verb and then the subject, and the question gets a question mark."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Woon Fatima in Kimberley? (b) Waar woon Fatima?","en":"(a) *Woon Fatima in Kimberley?* (b) *Waar woon Fatima?*"}},{"title":{"af":"Sinsoorte en leestekens","en":"Sentence types and punctuation"},"problem":{"af":"Watter soort sin is elkeen? Skryf dit oor met ’n hoofletter en die regte leesteken: (a) *maak jou boek oop* (b) *wat ’n groot olifant* (c) *hoe laat is dit*","en":"What type of sentence is each one? Rewrite it with a capital letter and the correct punctuation: (a) *maak jou boek oop* (open your book) (b) *wat ’n groot olifant* (what a big elephant) (c) *hoe laat is dit* (what time is it)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Dit begin met die werkwoord en gee ’n opdrag: bevelsin, met ’n punt.","en":"(a) It starts with the verb and gives an instruction: command, with a full stop."},{"af":"(b) Dit wys verbasing, ’n sterk gevoel: uitroepsin, met ’n uitroepteken.","en":"(b) It shows surprise, a strong feeling: exclamation, with an exclamation mark."},{"af":"(c) Dit begin met die vraagwoord *hoe* en vra iets: vraagsin, met ’n vraagteken.","en":"(c) It starts with the question word *hoe* and asks something: question, with a question mark."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Maak jou boek oop. (bevelsin) (b) Wat ’n groot olifant! (uitroepsin) (c) Hoe laat is dit? (vraagsin)","en":"(a) *Maak jou boek oop.* (command) (b) *Wat ’n groot olifant!* (exclamation) (c) *Hoe laat is dit?* (question)"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Maak negatief: *Ek hou van spinasie.*","en":"Make negative: *Ek hou van spinasie.* (I like spinach.)"},"options":[{"af":"Ek hou nie van spinasie nie.","en":"Ek hou nie van spinasie nie."},{"af":"Ek hou nie van spinasie.","en":"Ek hou nie van spinasie."},{"af":"Ek nie hou van spinasie nie.","en":"Ek nie hou van spinasie nie."},{"af":"Ek hou van spinasie nie nie.","en":"Ek hou van spinasie nie nie."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die eerste *nie* kom ná die werkwoord *hou*, en omdat daar nog woorde volg, kom die tweede *nie* aan die einde.","en":"The first *nie* comes after the verb *hou*, and because more words follow, the second *nie* comes at the end."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Maak negatief: *Die hond blaf.*","en":"Make negative: *Die hond blaf.* (The dog barks.)"},"options":[{"af":"Die hond blaf nie nie.","en":"Die hond blaf nie nie."},{"af":"Die hond nie blaf nie.","en":"Die hond nie blaf nie."},{"af":"Die hond blaf niks nie.","en":"Die hond blaf niks nie."},{"af":"Die hond blaf nie.","en":"Die hond blaf nie."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ná *blaf nie* kom niks meer nie, so een *nie* is genoeg: *Die hond blaf nie.*","en":"After *blaf nie* nothing more follows, so one *nie* is enough: *Die hond blaf nie.*"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Ek het my sleutels oral gesoek, maar ek kon hulle ___ kry nie.","en":"*Ek het my sleutels oral gesoek, maar ek kon hulle ___ kry nie.* (I looked for my keys everywhere, but I could not find them anywhere.)"},"answers":{"af":["nêrens"],"en":["nêrens"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["niks","niemand","geen"],"en":["niks","niemand","geen"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die teenoorgestelde van *oral* (alle plekke) is *nêrens* (geen plek nie). Let op die kappie op die ê.","en":"The opposite of *oral* (everywhere) is *nêrens* (nowhere). Note the circumflex on the ê."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Bevelsin begin gewoonlik met ’n werkwoord, soos *Sit jou skoene in die kas.*","en":"A command usually starts with a verb, as in *Sit jou skoene in die kas.* (Put your shoes in the cupboard.)"},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Bevelsin gee ’n opdrag en begin met die werkwoord (*Sit*); daar is gewoonlik geen onderwerp nie.","en":"True. A command gives an instruction and starts with the verb (*Sit* – put); there is usually no subject."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter vraag is korrek?","en":"Which question is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Waar jy het jou tas gelos?","en":"Waar jy het jou tas gelos?"},{"af":"Waar het jy jou tas gelos?","en":"Waar het jy jou tas gelos?"},{"af":"Jy het waar jou tas gelos?","en":"Jy het waar jou tas gelos?"},{"af":"Waar het jy gelos jou tas?","en":"Waar het jy gelos jou tas?"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Ná die vraagwoord *Waar* kom die werkwoord *het*, dan die onderwerp *jy*, en die *ge-*woord *gelos* bly aan die einde.","en":"After the question word *Waar* comes the verb *het*, then the subject *jy*, and the *ge-* word *gelos* stays at the end."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter leesteken hoort aan die einde? *Wat ’n pragtige sonsondergang*","en":"Which punctuation mark belongs at the end? *Wat ’n pragtige sonsondergang* (What a beautiful sunset)"},"options":[{"af":"punt (.)","en":"full stop (.)"},{"af":"vraagteken (?)","en":"question mark (?)"},{"af":"uitroepteken (!)","en":"exclamation mark (!)"},{"af":"komma (,)","en":"comma (,)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die sin wys bewondering – ’n sterk gevoel – so dit is ’n uitroepsin met ’n uitroepteken. Al begin dit met *Wat*, vra dit niks nie.","en":"The sentence shows admiration – a strong feeling – so it is an exclamation with an exclamation mark. Even though it starts with *Wat*, it does not ask anything."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke positiewe woord by sy negatiewe woord.","en":"Match each positive word to its negative word."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"iets","en":"iets"},"r":{"af":"niks","en":"niks"}},{"l":{"af":"iemand","en":"iemand"},"r":{"af":"niemand","en":"niemand"}},{"l":{"af":"altyd","en":"altyd"},"r":{"af":"nooit","en":"nooit"}},{"l":{"af":"oral","en":"oral"},"r":{"af":"nêrens","en":"nêrens"}},{"l":{"af":"’n","en":"’n"},"r":{"af":"geen","en":"geen"}}],"explain":{"af":"*iets → niks, iemand → niemand, altyd → nooit, oral → nêrens* en *’n → geen*. Onthou: al hierdie negatiewe woorde kry ’n *nie* aan die einde van die sin.","en":"*iets → niks* (something → nothing), *iemand → niemand* (someone → nobody), *altyd → nooit* (always → never), *oral → nêrens* (everywhere → nowhere) and *’n → geen* (a → no). Remember: all these negative words take a *nie* at the end of the sentence."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Ons het ___ brood in die huis nie.*","en":"Complete: *Ons het ___ brood in die huis nie.* (We have ___ bread in the house.)"},"options":[{"af":"geen","en":"geen"},{"af":"niks","en":"niks"},{"af":"niemand","en":"niemand"},{"af":"nêrens","en":"nêrens"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Geen* staan voor ’n naamwoord (*brood*) en beteken *nie enige nie*. *Niemand* is vir mense en *nêrens* vir plekke.","en":"*Geen* (no) stands before a noun (*brood* – bread) and means *not any*. *Niemand* (nobody) is for people and *nêrens* (nowhere) for places."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"___ appels het jy gekoop? – Ek het ses appels gekoop.","en":"___ *appels het jy gekoop?* – *Ek het ses appels gekoop.* (___ apples did you buy? – I bought six apples.)"},"answers":{"af":["Hoeveel"],"en":["Hoeveel"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Wanneer","Hoekom","Wie"],"en":["Wanneer","Hoekom","Wie"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die antwoord is ’n getal (*ses*), so die vraagwoord is *Hoeveel*.","en":"The answer is a number (*ses* – six), so the question word is *Hoeveel* (how many)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die sin *Niemand het die kat gesien nie* is verkeerd, want dit het twee ontkenningswoorde.","en":"The sentence *Niemand het die kat gesien nie* (Nobody saw the cat) is wrong, because it has two negative words."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die sin is korrek: ’n ontkennende woord soos *niemand* kry altyd ’n *nie* aan die einde. Dit is die dubbele ontkenning van Afrikaans.","en":"False. The sentence is correct: a negative word such as *niemand* always takes a *nie* at the end. This is Afrikaans double negation."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is ’n **stelsin**?","en":"Which sentence is a **statement**?"},"options":[{"af":"Vertrek die trein om agtuur?","en":"Vertrek die trein om agtuur?"},{"af":"Klim gou op die trein!","en":"Klim gou op die trein!"},{"af":"Sjoe, die trein is vinnig!","en":"Sjoe, die trein is vinnig!"},{"af":"Die trein vertrek om agtuur.","en":"Die trein vertrek om agtuur."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Stelsin vertel net iets en eindig met ’n punt. Die ander is ’n vraagsin, ’n bevelsin en ’n uitroepsin.","en":"A statement just tells something and ends with a full stop. The others are a question, a command and an exclamation."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter negatiewe bevel is korrek?","en":"Which negative command is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Moenie op die gras loop.","en":"Moenie op die gras loop."},{"af":"Moenie op die gras loop nie.","en":"Moenie op die gras loop nie."},{"af":"Nie op die gras loop nie.","en":"Nie op die gras loop nie."},{"af":"Moenie nie op die gras loop nie.","en":"Moenie nie op die gras loop nie."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Negatiewe bevel begin met *Moenie* en eindig met *nie*: *Moenie op die gras loop nie.*","en":"A negative command starts with *Moenie* (don’t) and ends with *nie*: *Moenie op die gras loop nie.* (Don’t walk on the grass.)"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"*Het jy al geëet?* is ’n ja/nee-vraag, want die ___ staan voor in die sin.","en":"*Het jy al geëet?* (Have you eaten yet?) is a yes/no question, because the ___ stands at the front of the sentence."},"answers":{"af":["werkwoord"],"en":["verb","werkwoord"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["onderwerp","vraagwoord","voorwerp"],"en":["subject","question word","object"]}},"explain":{"af":"By ’n ja/nee-vraag skuif die werkwoord (*Het*) na vore. Daar is geen vraagwoord nie.","en":"In a yes/no question the verb (*Het*) moves to the front. There is no question word."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Maak negatief: *Die kinders het iets gehoor.*","en":"Make negative: *Die kinders het iets gehoor.* (The children heard something.)"},"options":[{"af":"Die kinders het nie niks gehoor nie.","en":"Die kinders het nie niks gehoor nie."},{"af":"Die kinders het niks gehoor.","en":"Die kinders het niks gehoor."},{"af":"Die kinders het niks gehoor nie.","en":"Die kinders het niks gehoor nie."},{"af":"Die kinders niks het gehoor nie.","en":"Die kinders niks het gehoor nie."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*iets* word *niks*, en omdat *gehoor* ná *niks* kom, kry die sin ’n *nie* aan die einde. *Nie niks* gebruik twee ontkenningswoorde voor in die sin – dit is verkeerd.","en":"*iets* becomes *niks*, and because *gehoor* comes after *niks*, the sentence gets a *nie* at the end. *Nie niks* uses two negative words early in the sentence – that is wrong."}}]},{"id":"afr5-t2-direkte-indirekte-rede","title":{"af":"Direkte en indirekte rede","en":"Direct and indirect speech"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal direkte rede met die regte leestekens kan skryf en stelsinne, vrae en bevele korrek na indirekte rede kan omskakel.","en":"You will be able to write direct speech with the correct punctuation and change statements, questions and commands correctly into indirect speech."},"summary":{"af":"## Direkte rede\n\n**Direkte rede** gee die **presiese woorde** van die spreker, tussen **aanhalingstekens** (“ ”).\n\n- **Spreker eerste:** dan ’n **dubbelpunt**, en die aanhaling begin met ’n **hoofletter**: *Thabo sê: “Ek is honger.”*\n- **Spreker laaste:** ’n **komma** binne die aanhalingstekens, en die werkwoord staan voor die spreker: *“Ek is honger,” sê Thabo.*\n- ’n Vraag of uitroep hou sy eie leesteken binne die aanhalingstekens: *“Is jy honger?” vra Ma. “Pasop!” skree Pa.*\n- Elke keer as ’n ander persoon praat, begin jy op ’n **nuwe reël**.\n\nKyk hoe elke spreker op ’n nuwe reël begin:\n\n*“Waar is my kryte?” vra Anika.*\n\n*“Hulle lê op die tafel,” antwoord Ravi.*\n\n*Anika glimlag en sê: “Baie dankie, Ravi!”*\n\nIn plaas van *sê* kan jy ook ander werkwoorde gebruik wat wys **hoe** iemand praat: *vra, antwoord, skree, fluister, roep*.\n\n> **Onthou:** Die punt, komma, vraagteken of uitroepteken van die gesegde woorde staan **binne** die aanhalingstekens.\n\n## Indirekte rede: stelsinne\n\nIn **indirekte rede** vertel jy **wat** iemand gesê het, sonder sy presiese woorde en sonder aanhalingstekens. Volg hierdie stappe:\n\n1. Laat die dubbelpunt en aanhalingstekens weg. *sê* word ***het gesê***.\n2. Voeg die voegwoord **dat** in.\n3. Verander die **voornaamwoorde**: *ek → hy/sy, my → sy/haar, ons → hulle*.\n4. Verander die **tyd** na die **verlede tyd**: *is → was, kan → kon, sal → sou, speel → gespeel het*.\n5. Verander woorde van **tyd en plek** (sien die tabel).\n6. Ná *dat* gaan die werkwoord na die **einde**.\n\n*Lerato sê: “Ek speel vandag netbal.”* → *Lerato het gesê **dat sy daardie dag** netbal **gespeel het**.*\n\n| Direkte rede | Indirekte rede |\n|---|---|\n| hier | daar |\n| vandag | daardie dag |\n| môre | die volgende dag |\n| gister | die vorige dag |\n| nou | toe |\n| hierdie | daardie |\n\nVerlede tyd bly verlede tyd: *Sipho sê: “Ek het geëet.”* → *Sipho het gesê dat hy **geëet het**.*\n\n## Vrae in indirekte rede\n\n- **Ja/nee-vraag** → gebruik **of**: *Pa vra vir Sipho: “Het jy jou huiswerk gedoen?”* → *Pa het vir Sipho gevra **of** hy sy huiswerk gedoen het.*\n- **Vraagwoord-vraag** → die **vraagwoord** bly en werk soos *dat*: *Nomsa vra: “Waar is my skoene?”* → *Nomsa het gevra **waar** haar skoene **was**.*\n\nNá *of* en ná die vraagwoord gaan die werkwoord ook na die **einde**, net soos ná *dat*. *vra* word ***het gevra***, en die vraagteken val weg, want die nuwe sin is ’n stelsin.\n\n## Bevele in indirekte rede\n\n’n **Bevel** kry **moet**: *Ma sê vir Liam: “Maak jou kamer skoon.”* → *Ma het vir Liam gesê dat hy sy kamer **moet skoonmaak**.*\n\n’n Negatiewe bevel met *moenie* word **nie … moet … nie**: *Die juffrou sê vir die kinders: “Moenie raas nie!”* → *Die juffrou het vir die kinders gesê dat hulle **nie moet raas nie**.*\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om die voornaamwoord te vergeet. *Zanele sê: “Ek is moeg.”* word *Zanele het gesê dat **sy** moeg was* – nie *dat ek moeg was* nie, want jy is nie Zanele nie.","en":"## Direct speech (*direkte rede*)\n\n**Direct speech** gives the speaker’s **exact words**, between **quotation marks** (“ ”).\n\n- **Speaker first:** then a **colon**, and the quote starts with a **capital letter**: *Thabo sê: “Ek is honger.”* (Thabo says: “I am hungry.”)\n- **Speaker last:** a **comma** inside the quotation marks, and the verb comes before the speaker: *“Ek is honger,” sê Thabo.*\n- A question or exclamation keeps its own punctuation mark inside the quotation marks: *“Is jy honger?” vra Ma.* (“Are you hungry?” asks Mom.) *“Pasop!” skree Pa.* (“Watch out!” shouts Dad.)\n- Every time a different person speaks, you start on a **new line**.\n\nSee how each speaker starts on a new line:\n\n*“Waar is my kryte?” vra Anika.* (“Where are my crayons?” asks Anika.)\n\n*“Hulle lê op die tafel,” antwoord Ravi.* (“They are lying on the table,” answers Ravi.)\n\n*Anika glimlag en sê: “Baie dankie, Ravi!”* (Anika smiles and says: “Thank you very much, Ravi!”)\n\nInstead of *sê* (says) you can also use other verbs that show **how** someone speaks: *vra* (asks), *antwoord* (answers), *skree* (shouts), *fluister* (whispers), *roep* (calls).\n\n> **Remember:** The full stop, comma, question mark or exclamation mark of the spoken words goes **inside** the quotation marks.\n\n## Indirect speech (*indirekte rede*): statements\n\nIn **indirect speech** you report **what** someone said, without their exact words and without quotation marks. Follow these steps:\n\n1. Leave out the colon and quotation marks. *sê* (says) becomes ***het gesê*** (said).\n2. Add the conjunction **dat** (that).\n3. Change the **pronouns**: *ek → hy/sy* (I → he/she), *my → sy/haar* (my → his/her), *ons → hulle* (we → they).\n4. Change the **tense** to the **past tense**: *is → was, kan → kon, sal → sou, speel → gespeel het*.\n5. Change words of **time and place** (see the table).\n6. After *dat* the verb goes to the **end**.\n\n*Lerato sê: “Ek speel vandag netbal.”* (Lerato says: “I am playing netball today.”) → *Lerato het gesê **dat sy daardie dag** netbal **gespeel het**.* (Lerato said that she played netball that day.)\n\n| Direct speech | Indirect speech |\n|---|---|\n| *hier* (here) | *daar* (there) |\n| *vandag* (today) | *daardie dag* (that day) |\n| *môre* (tomorrow) | *die volgende dag* (the next day) |\n| *gister* (yesterday) | *die vorige dag* (the day before) |\n| *nou* (now) | *toe* (then) |\n| *hierdie* (this) | *daardie* (that) |\n\nPast tense stays past tense: *Sipho sê: “Ek het geëet.”* (I have eaten.) → *Sipho het gesê dat hy **geëet het**.*\n\n## Questions in indirect speech\n\n- **Yes/no question** → use **of** (whether/if): *Pa vra vir Sipho: “Het jy jou huiswerk gedoen?”* → *Pa het vir Sipho gevra **of** hy sy huiswerk gedoen het.* (Dad asked Sipho whether he had done his homework.)\n- **Question-word question** → the **question word** stays and works like *dat*: *Nomsa vra: “Waar is my skoene?”* (Where are my shoes?) → *Nomsa het gevra **waar** haar skoene **was**.*\n\nAfter *of* and after the question word the verb also goes to the **end**, just as after *dat*. *vra* (asks) becomes ***het gevra*** (asked), and the question mark falls away, because the new sentence is a statement.\n\n## Commands in indirect speech\n\nA **command** gets **moet** (must): *Ma sê vir Liam: “Maak jou kamer skoon.”* (Clean your room.) → *Ma het vir Liam gesê dat hy sy kamer **moet skoonmaak**.*\n\nA negative command with *moenie* becomes **nie … moet … nie**: *Die juffrou sê vir die kinders: “Moenie raas nie!”* (Don’t make a noise!) → *Die juffrou het vir die kinders gesê dat hulle **nie moet raas nie**.*\n\n> **Common mistake:** Forgetting to change the pronoun. *Zanele sê: “Ek is moeg.”* becomes *Zanele het gesê dat **sy** moeg was* – not *dat ek moeg was*, because you are not Zanele."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Direkte rede","en":"Direct speech (direkte rede)"},"def":{"af":"Die presiese woorde wat iemand sê, tussen aanhalingstekens: Thabo sê: “Ek is honger.”","en":"The exact words someone says, between quotation marks: Thabo sê: “Ek is honger.”"}},{"term":{"af":"Indirekte rede","en":"Indirect speech (indirekte rede)"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer jy oorvertel wat iemand gesê het, sonder aanhalingstekens: Thabo het gesê dat hy honger was.","en":"When you report what someone said, without quotation marks: Thabo het gesê dat hy honger was (Thabo said that he was hungry)."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanhalingstekens","en":"Quotation marks (aanhalingstekens)"},"def":{"af":"Die tekens “ ” wat om die presiese woorde van ’n spreker staan.","en":"The marks “ ” that go around a speaker’s exact words."}},{"term":{"af":"Dubbelpunt","en":"Colon (dubbelpunt)"},"def":{"af":"Die leesteken (:) wat ná die spreker en voor die aanhaling staan: Ma sê: “…”","en":"The punctuation mark (:) that comes after the speaker and before the quote: Ma sê: “…”"}},{"term":{"af":"Spreker","en":"Speaker (spreker)"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon wat die woorde sê.","en":"The person who says the words."}},{"term":{"af":"Voegwoord *dat*","en":"The conjunction *dat*"},"def":{"af":"Die woord wat ’n stelsin in indirekte rede inlei en die werkwoord na die einde stuur.","en":"The word (meaning ‘that’) that introduces a statement in indirect speech and sends the verb to the end."}},{"term":{"af":"Voegwoord *of* in vrae","en":"The conjunction *of* in questions"},"def":{"af":"Die woord wat ’n ja/nee-vraag in indirekte rede inlei: Ma het gevra of ek honger was.","en":"The word (meaning ‘whether’) that introduces a yes/no question in indirect speech: Ma het gevra of ek honger was."}},{"term":{"af":"Bevel","en":"Command (bevel)"},"def":{"af":"’n Opdrag; in indirekte rede kry dit ‘moet’: Ma het gesê dat ek moet slaap.","en":"An instruction; in indirect speech it gets ‘moet’ (must): Ma het gesê dat ek moet slaap."}},{"term":{"af":"Tydsverandering","en":"Change of tense (tydsverandering)"},"def":{"af":"Die verandering na die verlede tyd in indirekte rede, soos ‘sê → het gesê’ en ‘is → was’.","en":"The change to the past tense in indirect speech, such as ‘sê → het gesê’ (says → said) and ‘is → was’."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Leestekens in direkte rede","en":"Punctuation in direct speech"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf met die regte leestekens en hoofletters: *ek gaan saam sê sipho*","en":"Write with the correct punctuation and capital letters: *ek gaan saam sê sipho* (I am coming along, says Sipho)"},"steps":[{"af":"Sipho se presiese woorde is *ek gaan saam*. Sit dit tussen aanhalingstekens en begin met ’n hoofletter: “Ek gaan saam …","en":"Sipho’s exact words are *ek gaan saam*. Put them between quotation marks and start with a capital letter: “Ek gaan saam …"},{"af":"Die spreker kom ná die woorde, so sit ’n komma binne die aanhalingstekens.","en":"The speaker comes after the words, so put a comma inside the quotation marks."},{"af":"*Sipho* is ’n eienaam en kry ’n hoofletter; *sê* bly klein en die sin eindig met ’n punt.","en":"*Sipho* is a proper noun and gets a capital letter; *sê* stays small and the sentence ends with a full stop."}],"answer":{"af":"“Ek gaan saam,” sê Sipho.","en":"*“Ek gaan saam,” sê Sipho.*"}},{"title":{"af":"’n Stelsin in indirekte rede","en":"A statement in indirect speech"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf in indirekte rede: *Lerato sê: “Ek is baie bly vandag.”*","en":"Write in indirect speech: *Lerato sê: “Ek is baie bly vandag.”* (Lerato says: “I am very happy today.”)"},"steps":[{"af":"Laat die dubbelpunt en aanhalingstekens weg; *sê* word *het gesê*, en voeg *dat* in.","en":"Leave out the colon and quotation marks; *sê* becomes *het gesê*, and add *dat*."},{"af":"*Ek* is Lerato, ’n meisie, so *ek* word *sy*.","en":"*Ek* is Lerato, a girl, so *ek* becomes *sy* (she)."},{"af":"*is* word *was*, en *vandag* word *daardie dag*.","en":"*is* becomes *was*, and *vandag* becomes *daardie dag*."},{"af":"Ná *dat* gaan die werkwoord *was* na die einde.","en":"After *dat* the verb *was* goes to the end."}],"answer":{"af":"Lerato het gesê dat sy daardie dag baie bly was.","en":"*Lerato het gesê dat sy daardie dag baie bly was.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Vrae in indirekte rede","en":"Questions in indirect speech"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf in indirekte rede: (a) *Oupa vra vir Pieter: “Kan jy my help?”* (b) *Die juffrou vra: “Wie het hierdie prent geteken?”*","en":"Write in indirect speech: (a) *Oupa vra vir Pieter: “Kan jy my help?”* (Grandpa asks Pieter: “Can you help me?”) (b) *Die juffrou vra: “Wie het hierdie prent geteken?”* (The teacher asks: “Who drew this picture?”)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Dit is ’n ja/nee-vraag, so gebruik *of*. *jy* (Pieter) word *hy*, *my* (Oupa) word *hom*, en *kan* word *kon*.","en":"(a) It is a yes/no question, so use *of*. *jy* (Pieter) becomes *hy*, *my* (Grandpa) becomes *hom*, and *kan* becomes *kon*."},{"af":"(b) Dit begin met die vraagwoord *wie*, so *wie* bly. *hierdie* word *daardie*.","en":"(b) It starts with the question word *wie*, so *wie* stays. *hierdie* becomes *daardie*."},{"af":"*Het geteken* is klaar verlede tyd en bly so, maar *het* skuif na die einde: *geteken het*. *Vra* word *het gevra* en die vraagteken val weg.","en":"*Het geteken* is already past tense and stays so, but *het* moves to the end: *geteken het*. *Vra* becomes *het gevra* and the question mark falls away."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Oupa het vir Pieter gevra of hy hom kon help. (b) Die juffrou het gevra wie daardie prent geteken het.","en":"(a) *Oupa het vir Pieter gevra of hy hom kon help.* (b) *Die juffrou het gevra wie daardie prent geteken het.*"}},{"title":{"af":"’n Bevel in indirekte rede","en":"A command in indirect speech"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf in indirekte rede: *Die afrigter sê vir die span: “Hardloop vinniger!”*","en":"Write in indirect speech: *Die afrigter sê vir die span: “Hardloop vinniger!”* (The coach says to the team: “Run faster!”)"},"steps":[{"af":"*sê* word *het gesê*; voeg *dat* in.","en":"*sê* becomes *het gesê*; add *dat*."},{"af":"Die bevel is vir die span, so die onderwerp word *hulle*.","en":"The command is for the team, so the subject becomes *hulle* (they)."},{"af":"’n Bevel kry *moet*, en die werkwoorde gaan na die einde: *moet hardloop*. Die uitroepteken val weg.","en":"A command gets *moet*, and the verbs go to the end: *moet hardloop*. The exclamation mark falls away."}],"answer":{"af":"Die afrigter het vir die span gesê dat hulle vinniger moet hardloop.","en":"*Die afrigter het vir die span gesê dat hulle vinniger moet hardloop.*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin het die korrekte leestekens?","en":"Which sentence has the correct punctuation?"},"options":[{"af":"Thabo sê: “Ek gaan saam.”","en":"Thabo sê: “Ek gaan saam.”"},{"af":"Thabo sê “ek gaan saam.”","en":"Thabo sê “ek gaan saam.”"},{"af":"Thabo sê: “Ek gaan saam”.","en":"Thabo sê: “Ek gaan saam”."},{"af":"Thabo sê: Ek gaan saam.","en":"Thabo sê: Ek gaan saam."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Ná die spreker kom ’n dubbelpunt, die aanhaling begin met ’n hoofletter en die punt staan binne die aanhalingstekens.","en":"After the speaker comes a colon, the quote starts with a capital letter and the full stop goes inside the quotation marks."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Skryf in indirekte rede: *Zanele sê: “Ek is honger.”*","en":"Write in indirect speech: *Zanele sê: “Ek is honger.”* (Zanele says: “I am hungry.”)"},"options":[{"af":"Zanele het gesê dat ek honger was.","en":"Zanele het gesê dat ek honger was."},{"af":"Zanele het gesê dat sy was honger.","en":"Zanele het gesê dat sy was honger."},{"af":"Zanele het gesê dat sy honger was.","en":"Zanele het gesê dat sy honger was."},{"af":"Zanele het gesê dat haar honger was.","en":"Zanele het gesê dat haar honger was."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Ek* (Zanele) word *sy*, *is* word *was*, en ná *dat* staan die werkwoord *was* aan die einde.","en":"*Ek* (Zanele) becomes *sy* (she), *is* becomes *was*, and after *dat* the verb *was* stands at the end."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Sipho vra: “Is die winkel oop?” → Sipho het gevra ___ die winkel oop was.","en":"*Sipho vra: “Is die winkel oop?”* (Is the shop open?) → *Sipho het gevra ___ die winkel oop was.*"},"answers":{"af":["of"],"en":["of"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["dat","wat","as"],"en":["dat","wat","as"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Ja/nee-vraag word in indirekte rede met *of* ingelei: *Sipho het gevra of die winkel oop was.*","en":"A yes/no question is introduced with *of* (whether) in indirect speech: *Sipho het gevra of die winkel oop was.*"}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In indirekte rede gebruik ons nie aanhalingstekens nie.","en":"In indirect speech we do not use quotation marks."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Indirekte rede vertel net wat gesê is, nie die presiese woorde nie, so daar is geen aanhalingstekens nie.","en":"True. Indirect speech only reports what was said, not the exact words, so there are no quotation marks."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Skryf in indirekte rede: *Pa sê: “Ek werk vandag hier.”*","en":"Write in indirect speech: *Pa sê: “Ek werk vandag hier.”* (Dad says: “I am working here today.”)"},"options":[{"af":"Pa het gesê dat hy vandag hier gewerk het.","en":"Pa het gesê dat hy vandag hier gewerk het."},{"af":"Pa het gesê dat ek daardie dag daar gewerk het.","en":"Pa het gesê dat ek daardie dag daar gewerk het."},{"af":"Pa het gesê dat hy daardie dag daar werk het.","en":"Pa het gesê dat hy daardie dag daar werk het."},{"af":"Pa het gesê dat hy daardie dag daar gewerk het.","en":"Pa het gesê dat hy daardie dag daar gewerk het."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*ek → hy, vandag → daardie dag, hier → daar*, en *werk* word *gewerk het* aan die einde. Die ander opsies vergeet een van hierdie veranderinge.","en":"*ek → hy, vandag → daardie dag, hier → daar*, and *werk* becomes *gewerk het* at the end. The other options forget one of these changes."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord vervang *hier* in indirekte rede?","en":"Which word replaces *hier* (here) in indirect speech?"},"options":[{"af":"hierdie","en":"hierdie"},{"af":"daar","en":"daar"},{"af":"daardie dag","en":"daardie dag"},{"af":"toe","en":"toe"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Hier* word *daar*, want die persoon wat oorvertel, is gewoonlik nie meer op dieselfde plek nie. *Daardie dag* vervang *vandag* en *toe* vervang *nou*.","en":"*Hier* (here) becomes *daar* (there), because the person reporting is usually no longer in the same place. *Daardie dag* replaces *vandag* and *toe* replaces *nou*."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke woord in direkte rede by die woord in indirekte rede.","en":"Match each word in direct speech to the word in indirect speech."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"hier","en":"hier"},"r":{"af":"daar","en":"daar"}},{"l":{"af":"vandag","en":"vandag"},"r":{"af":"daardie dag","en":"daardie dag"}},{"l":{"af":"môre","en":"môre"},"r":{"af":"die volgende dag","en":"die volgende dag"}},{"l":{"af":"gister","en":"gister"},"r":{"af":"die vorige dag","en":"die vorige dag"}},{"l":{"af":"nou","en":"nou"},"r":{"af":"toe","en":"toe"}}],"explain":{"af":"In indirekte rede vertel jy later en van ’n ander plek af, so woorde van tyd en plek verander: *hier → daar, vandag → daardie dag, môre → die volgende dag, gister → die vorige dag, nou → toe*.","en":"In indirect speech you report later and from somewhere else, so words of time and place change: *hier → daar* (here → there), *vandag → daardie dag* (today → that day), *môre → die volgende dag* (tomorrow → the next day), *gister → die vorige dag* (yesterday → the day before), *nou → toe* (now → then)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Skryf in indirekte rede: *Ma sê vir Aisha: “Was jou hande.”*","en":"Write in indirect speech: *Ma sê vir Aisha: “Was jou hande.”* (Mom says to Aisha: “Wash your hands.”)"},"options":[{"af":"Ma het vir Aisha gesê dat sy haar hande moet was.","en":"Ma het vir Aisha gesê dat sy haar hande moet was."},{"af":"Ma het vir Aisha gesê dat jy jou hande moet was.","en":"Ma het vir Aisha gesê dat jy jou hande moet was."},{"af":"Ma het vir Aisha gesê dat sy haar hande was.","en":"Ma het vir Aisha gesê dat sy haar hande was."},{"af":"Ma het vir Aisha gesê was jou hande.","en":"Ma het vir Aisha gesê was jou hande."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Bevel kry *moet*, en *jou* (Aisha) word *haar*: *dat sy haar hande moet was*. Sonder *moet* is dit nie meer ’n bevel nie.","en":"A command gets *moet*, and *jou* (Aisha) becomes *haar*: *dat sy haar hande moet was*. Without *moet* it is no longer a command."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die juffrou vra: “Wie het die venster oopgemaak?” → Die juffrou het gevra ___ die venster oopgemaak het.","en":"*Die juffrou vra: “Wie het die venster oopgemaak?”* (Who opened the window?) → *Die juffrou het gevra ___ die venster oopgemaak het.*"},"answers":{"af":["wie"],"en":["wie"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["of","dat","wat"],"en":["of","dat","wat"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die vraag begin met die vraagwoord *wie*, en in indirekte rede bly die vraagwoord: *gevra wie die venster oopgemaak het*.","en":"The question starts with the question word *wie* (who), and in indirect speech the question word stays: *gevra wie die venster oopgemaak het*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy ’n vraag soos *“Is jy siek?”* in indirekte rede skryf, gebruik jy die voegwoord *dat*.","en":"When you write a question like *“Is jy siek?”* (Are you sick?) in indirect speech, you use the conjunction *dat*."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Ja/nee-vraag kry *of*: *Ma het gevra of ek siek was.* *Dat* is vir stelsinne.","en":"False. A yes/no question gets *of*: *Ma het gevra of ek siek was.* *Dat* is for statements."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is korrek gepunktueer?","en":"Which sentence is punctuated correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"“Waar is jou tas”? vra Liam.","en":"“Waar is jou tas”? vra Liam."},{"af":"“Waar is jou tas,” vra Liam?","en":"“Waar is jou tas,” vra Liam?"},{"af":"“Waar is jou tas.” vra Liam?","en":"“Waar is jou tas.” vra Liam?"},{"af":"“Waar is jou tas?” vra Liam.","en":"“Waar is jou tas?” vra Liam."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die vraagteken hoort by Liam se woorde, so dit staan binne die aanhalingstekens. Die hele sin eindig met ’n punt ná *Liam*.","en":"The question mark belongs to Liam’s words, so it goes inside the quotation marks. The whole sentence ends with a full stop after *Liam*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Skryf in indirekte rede: *Johan sê: “My hond kan baie vinnig hardloop.”*","en":"Write in indirect speech: *Johan sê: “My hond kan baie vinnig hardloop.”* (Johan says: “My dog can run very fast.”)"},"options":[{"af":"Johan het gesê dat my hond baie vinnig kon hardloop.","en":"Johan het gesê dat my hond baie vinnig kon hardloop."},{"af":"Johan het gesê dat sy hond baie vinnig kon hardloop.","en":"Johan het gesê dat sy hond baie vinnig kon hardloop."},{"af":"Johan het gesê dat sy hond baie vinnig kan hardloop het.","en":"Johan het gesê dat sy hond baie vinnig kan hardloop het."},{"af":"Johan het gesê dat sy hond kon baie vinnig hardloop.","en":"Johan het gesê dat sy hond kon baie vinnig hardloop."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*My* (Johan) word *sy*, *kan* word *kon*, en ná *dat* staan die werkwoorde aan die einde: *kon hardloop*.","en":"*My* (Johan’s) becomes *sy* (his), *kan* becomes *kon*, and after *dat* the verbs stand at the end: *kon hardloop*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Ravi sê: “Ek sal jou help.” → Ravi het gesê dat hy my ___ help.","en":"*Ravi sê: “Ek sal jou help.”* (I will help you.) → *Ravi het gesê dat hy my ___ help.*"},"answers":{"af":["sou"],"en":["sou"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["sal","wou","het"],"en":["sal","wou","het"]}},"explain":{"af":"In indirekte rede word *sal* die verledetydsvorm *sou*. *Wou* is die verlede tyd van *wil* en verander die betekenis.","en":"In indirect speech *sal* (will) becomes its past form *sou* (would). *Wou* is the past of *wil* (want) and changes the meaning."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Skryf hierdie indirekte rede as direkte rede: *Lerato het gesê dat sy daardie dag moeg was.*","en":"Write this indirect speech as direct speech: *Lerato het gesê dat sy daardie dag moeg was.* (Lerato said that she was tired that day.)"},"options":[{"af":"Lerato sê: “Sy is vandag moeg.”","en":"Lerato sê: “Sy is vandag moeg.”"},{"af":"Lerato sê: “Ek was daardie dag moeg.”","en":"Lerato sê: “Ek was daardie dag moeg.”"},{"af":"Lerato sê: “Ek is vandag moeg.”","en":"Lerato sê: “Ek is vandag moeg.”"},{"af":"Lerato sê: Ek is vandag moeg.","en":"Lerato sê: Ek is vandag moeg."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Werk terug: *sy → ek, daardie dag → vandag, was → is*, en sit Lerato se presiese woorde tussen aanhalingstekens ná ’n dubbelpunt.","en":"Work backwards: *sy → ek, daardie dag → vandag, was → is*, and put Lerato’s exact words between quotation marks after a colon."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Woorde, klanke en beelde","en":"Words, sounds and images"},"topics":[{"id":"afr5-t3-leestekens-spelling","title":{"af":"Leestekens en spelling","en":"Punctuation and spelling"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal hoofletters en leestekens reg kan gebruik, weet wanneer ’n woord ’n deelteken of kappie kry, woorde in lettergrepe kan verdeel en vinnig in ’n woordeboek kan soek.","en":"You will be able to use capital letters and punctuation marks correctly, know when a word takes a diaeresis or a circumflex, divide words into syllables and look up words quickly in a dictionary."},"summary":{"af":"## Hoofletters en eindtekens\n\nLeestekens is soos padtekens vir die leser: hulle wys waar om te stop, te wag of ’n vraag te vra.\n\nGebruik ’n **hoofletter**:\n- aan die begin van elke sin;\n- vir **eiename**: mense, plekke, dae, maande en feesdae (*Sipho, Durban, Maandag, Desember, Kersfees*);\n- vir tale (*Afrikaans, Engels*).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die woord *ek* kry net aan die begin van ’n sin ’n hoofletter: *Thabo en ek speel sokker.* As ’n sin met *’n* begin, kry die **volgende woord** die hoofletter: *’n Hond blaf by die hek.*\n\nElke sin eindig met ’n **eindteken**:\n- **punt (.)** ná ’n stelsin: *Ons speel buite.*\n- **vraagteken (?)** ná ’n vraag: *Waar is my tas?*\n- **uitroepteken (!)** ná ’n bevel of sterk gevoel: *Pasop vir die slang!*\n\n## Komma en aanhalingstekens\n\nDie **komma (,)** is ’n kort ruskans in die sin.\n- In ’n **lys** skei kommas die items. Voor *en* kom daar nie ’n komma nie: *Ek koop brood, melk, eiers en botter.*\n- By die **aanspreekvorm**, as jy iemand se naam noem terwyl jy met hom of haar praat: *Zanele, kom eet!* of *Dankie, Liam.*\n- Ná ’n sinsdeel wat voor in die sin staan: *As dit reën, bly ons binne.*\n\n**Aanhalingstekens (“ ”)** staan om die presiese woorde wat iemand sê: *Ma sê: “Was jou hande.”* Die punt, vraagteken of uitroepteken van die gesegde staan **binne** die aanhalingstekens.\n\n## Die afkappingsteken (’)\n\nDie afkappingsteken wys dat ’n letter weggelaat is, of help jou om die woord reg te lees:\n- in die lidwoord **’n** (kort vir *een*);\n- in die meervoud van woorde wat op ’n **enkele klinker** eindig: *ma’s, ouma’s, foto’s, taxi’s*;\n- in *’s oggends, ’s middags* en *’s aands*.\n\n> **Onthou:** Afrikaans wys besit met **se**, nie met ’n afkappingsteken nie: *Thabo se fiets*, nooit *Thabo’s fiets* nie.\n\n## Deelteken en kappie\n\nDie **deelteken (¨)** wys dat die klinker ’n **nuwe lettergreep** begin. Sonder die deelteken sal jy die woord verkeerd lees.\n\n| Woord | Lettergrepe | Sonder deelteken lees jy … |\n|---|---|---|\n| *reën* | re-ën | *reen* (soos *been*) |\n| *oë* | o-ë | *oe* (soos in *boek*) |\n| *geëet* | ge-eet | *geeet* (onduidelik) |\n| *geïnteresseerd* | ge-ïn-te-res-seerd | *ei* (soos in *trein*) |\n\nDie **kappie (^)** op *ê, ô* en *û* wys ’n spesiale klank: *sê, wêreld, môre, brûe* (meervoud van *brug*). Die kappie kan die betekenis verander: *Ma **se** boek* (besit), maar *Ma **sê** ons moet slaap* (praat).\n\n## Klinkers, tweeklanke en lettergrepe\n\nDie **klinkers** is *a, e, i, o, u* (en *y*). Al die ander letters is **medeklinkers**. Soms maak twee klinkerletters saam **een klank**: *ei* (trein), *ui* (huis), *ou* (koud), *oe* (boek), *ie* (vier), *eu* (deur). Hierdie **tweeklanke** bly altyd saam in een lettergreep.\n\n’n **Lettergreep** is ’n deel van ’n woord wat jy in een klap sê. Elke lettergreep het een klinkerklank: *ta-fel, kom-kom-mer, ver-jaars-dag*. Klap saam terwyl jy die woord sê om die lettergrepe te tel.\n\n## Alfabetiese volgorde en die woordeboek\n\nWoorde in ’n **woordeboek** staan in **alfabetiese volgorde**. As die eerste letters dieselfde is, kyk na die tweede letter, dan na die derde: *bal, berg, blom, boom*.\n- Die **gidswoorde** bo-aan die bladsy is die eerste en die laaste woord op daardie bladsy. Hulle help jou om vinnig te soek.\n- Die **trefwoord** is die vetgedrukte woord wat verduidelik word.\n- Die woordeboek gee ook die **woordsoort**, die meervoud en een of meer **betekenisse**.","en":"## Capital letters and end marks\n\nPunctuation marks are like road signs for the reader: they show where to stop, pause or ask a question.\n\nUse a **capital letter** (*hoofletter*):\n- at the start of every sentence;\n- for **proper nouns** (*eiename*): people, places, days, months and holidays (*Sipho, Durban, Maandag, Desember, Kersfees*);\n- for languages (*Afrikaans, Engels*).\n\n> **Common mistake:** Unlike English *I*, the Afrikaans word *ek* only takes a capital at the start of a sentence: *Thabo en ek speel sokker.* (Thabo and I play soccer.) If a sentence starts with *’n*, the **next word** gets the capital: *’n Hond blaf by die hek.* (A dog barks at the gate.)\n\nEvery sentence ends with an **end mark**:\n- **full stop (.)** (*punt*) after a statement: *Ons speel buite.* (We play outside.)\n- **question mark (?)** (*vraagteken*) after a question: *Waar is my tas?* (Where is my bag?)\n- **exclamation mark (!)** (*uitroepteken*) after a command or strong feeling: *Pasop vir die slang!* (Watch out for the snake!)\n\n## The comma and quotation marks\n\nThe **comma (,)** (*komma*) is a short pause in the sentence.\n- In a **list**, commas separate the items. There is no comma before *en* (and): *Ek koop brood, melk, eiers en botter.*\n- With the **form of address** (*aanspreekvorm*), when you say someone’s name while talking to them: *Zanele, kom eet!* (Zanele, come and eat!) or *Dankie, Liam.*\n- After a part of the sentence that stands in front: *As dit reën, bly ons binne.* (If it rains, we stay inside.)\n\n**Quotation marks (“ ”)** (*aanhalingstekens*) go around the exact words someone says: *Ma sê: “Was jou hande.”* (Mom says: “Wash your hands.”) The full stop, question mark or exclamation mark of the spoken words goes **inside** the quotation marks.\n\n## The apostrophe (’)\n\nThe apostrophe (*afkappingsteken*) shows that a letter has been left out, or helps you read the word correctly:\n- in the article **’n** (short for *een*; a/an);\n- in the plural of words ending in a **single vowel**: *ma’s, ouma’s, foto’s, taxi’s*;\n- in *’s oggends, ’s middags* and *’s aands* (in the morning, afternoon, evening).\n\n> **Remember:** Afrikaans shows ownership with **se**, not with an apostrophe: *Thabo se fiets* (Thabo’s bicycle), never *Thabo’s fiets*.\n\n## Diaeresis and circumflex\n\nThe **diaeresis (¨)** (*deelteken*) shows that the vowel starts a **new syllable**. Without it you would read the word wrongly.\n\n| Word | Syllables | Without the diaeresis you would read … |\n|---|---|---|\n| *reën* (rain) | re-ën | *reen* (like *been*) |\n| *oë* (eyes) | o-ë | *oe* (as in *boek*) |\n| *geëet* (eaten) | ge-eet | *geeet* (unclear) |\n| *geïnteresseerd* (interested) | ge-ïn-te-res-seerd | *ei* (as in *trein*) |\n\nThe **circumflex (^)** (*kappie*) on *ê, ô* and *û* shows a special sound: *sê* (say), *wêreld* (world), *môre* (tomorrow), *brûe* (bridges, plural of *brug*). It can change the meaning: *Ma **se** boek* (Mom’s book – ownership), but *Ma **sê** ons moet slaap* (Mom says we must sleep).\n\n## Vowels, vowel pairs and syllables\n\nThe **vowels** (*klinkers*) are *a, e, i, o, u* (and *y*). All the other letters are **consonants** (*medeklinkers*). Sometimes two vowel letters together make **one sound**: *ei* (trein), *ui* (huis), *ou* (koud), *oe* (boek), *ie* (vier), *eu* (deur). These vowel pairs (*tweeklanke*) always stay together in one syllable.\n\nA **syllable** (*lettergreep*) is a part of a word that you say in one clap. Every syllable has one vowel sound: *ta-fel, kom-kom-mer, ver-jaars-dag*. Clap while you say the word to count the syllables.\n\n## Alphabetical order and the dictionary\n\nWords in a **dictionary** (*woordeboek*) are in **alphabetical order**. If the first letters are the same, look at the second letter, then the third: *bal, berg, blom, boom*.\n- The **guide words** (*gidswoorde*) at the top of the page are the first and last words on that page. They help you search quickly.\n- The **headword** (*trefwoord*) is the word in bold that is explained.\n- The dictionary also gives the **part of speech** (*woordsoort*), the plural and one or more **meanings**."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Leesteken","en":"Punctuation mark (leesteken)"},"def":{"af":"’n Teken soos ’n punt, komma of vraagteken wat die leser help om die sin reg te lees.","en":"A mark such as a full stop, comma or question mark that helps the reader read the sentence correctly."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanspreekvorm","en":"Form of address (aanspreekvorm)"},"def":{"af":"Die naam waarmee jy iemand direk aanspreek; ’n komma skei dit van die res van die sin: *Sipho, kom hier.*","en":"The name you use to speak to someone directly; a comma separates it from the rest of the sentence: *Sipho, kom hier.* (Sipho, come here.)"}},{"term":{"af":"Aanhalingstekens","en":"Quotation marks (aanhalingstekens)"},"def":{"af":"Die tekens (“ ”) wat om die presiese woorde staan wat iemand sê.","en":"The marks (“ ”) that go around the exact words someone says."}},{"term":{"af":"Afkappingsteken","en":"Apostrophe (afkappingsteken)"},"def":{"af":"Die teken (’) wat wys dat ’n letter weggelaat is of wat ’n meervoud help lees, soos in *’n* en *foto’s*.","en":"The mark (’) that shows a letter has been left out or helps you read a plural, as in *’n* and *foto’s*."}},{"term":{"af":"Deelteken","en":"Diaeresis (deelteken)"},"def":{"af":"Die twee kolletjies (¨) op ’n klinker wat wys dat dit ’n nuwe lettergreep begin, soos in *reën* en *oë*.","en":"The two dots (¨) on a vowel showing that it starts a new syllable, as in *reën* (rain) and *oë* (eyes)."}},{"term":{"af":"Kappie","en":"Circumflex (kappie)"},"def":{"af":"Die dakkie (^) op *ê, ô* of *û* wat ’n spesiale klank wys, soos in *sê* en *môre*.","en":"The little roof (^) on *ê, ô* or *û* that shows a special sound, as in *sê* (say) and *môre* (tomorrow)."}},{"term":{"af":"Tweeklank","en":"Vowel pair (tweeklank)"},"def":{"af":"Twee klinkerletters wat saam een klank maak, soos *ui* in *huis* of *ei* in *trein*.","en":"Two vowel letters that make one sound together, such as *ui* in *huis* (house) or *ei* in *trein* (train)."}},{"term":{"af":"Lettergreep","en":"Syllable (lettergreep)"},"def":{"af":"’n Deel van ’n woord wat jy in een klap sê, met een klinkerklank: *ta-fel*.","en":"A part of a word that you say in one clap, with one vowel sound: *ta-fel* (table)."}},{"term":{"af":"Alfabetiese volgorde","en":"Alphabetical order (alfabetiese volgorde)"},"def":{"af":"Die volgorde van die alfabet; jy vergelyk woorde letter vir letter van voor af.","en":"The order of the alphabet; you compare words letter by letter from the front."}},{"term":{"af":"Gidswoorde","en":"Guide words (gidswoorde)"},"def":{"af":"Die twee woorde bo-aan ’n woordeboekbladsy: die eerste en die laaste woord op daardie bladsy.","en":"The two words at the top of a dictionary page: the first and the last word on that page."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Hoofletters en leestekens invoeg","en":"Adding capitals and punctuation"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die sin oor met die regte hoofletters en leestekens: *sipho het brood melk en eiers by die winkel in durban gekoop*","en":"Rewrite the sentence with the correct capital letters and punctuation: *sipho het brood melk en eiers by die winkel in durban gekoop* (Sipho bought bread, milk and eggs at the shop in Durban)"},"steps":[{"af":"Die sin begin met *sipho*. Dit is die eerste woord én ’n eienaam, so dit kry ’n hoofletter: *Sipho*.","en":"The sentence starts with *sipho*. It is the first word and a proper noun, so it gets a capital: *Sipho*."},{"af":"*durban* is die naam van ’n stad, ’n eienaam: *Durban*.","en":"*durban* is the name of a city, a proper noun: *Durban*."},{"af":"*brood melk en eiers* is ’n lys. Sit ’n komma ná *brood*, maar nie voor *en* nie.","en":"*brood melk en eiers* is a list. Put a comma after *brood*, but not before *en*."},{"af":"Dit is ’n stelsin (dit vertel iets), so dit eindig met ’n punt.","en":"It is a statement (it tells something), so it ends with a full stop."}],"answer":{"af":"Sipho het brood, melk en eiers by die winkel in Durban gekoop.","en":"*Sipho het brood, melk en eiers by die winkel in Durban gekoop.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Deelteken en kappie","en":"Diaeresis and circumflex"},"problem":{"af":"Verbeter die spelling: *Ma se dat die reen more na die berge sal kom.*","en":"Correct the spelling: *Ma se dat die reen more na die berge sal kom.* (Mom says that the rain will come to the mountains tomorrow.)"},"steps":[{"af":"*se* is hier die werkwoord (Ma praat), nie besit nie. Die werkwoord kry ’n kappie: *sê*.","en":"*se* is the verb here (Mom is speaking), not ownership. The verb takes a circumflex: *sê*."},{"af":"*reen* sê jy re-ën: die tweede *e* begin ’n nuwe lettergreep. Dit kry ’n deelteken: *reën*.","en":"You say *reen* as re-ën: the second *e* starts a new syllable. It takes a diaeresis: *reën*."},{"af":"Die woord vir die volgende dag word met ’n kappie geskryf: *môre*.","en":"The word for the next day is written with a circumflex: *môre*."}],"answer":{"af":"Ma sê dat die reën môre na die berge sal kom.","en":"*Ma sê dat die reën môre na die berge sal kom.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Alfabetiese volgorde","en":"Alphabetical order"},"problem":{"af":"Rangskik in alfabetiese volgorde: *skool, sap, slang, son, sak*","en":"Arrange in alphabetical order: *skool, sap, slang, son, sak*"},"steps":[{"af":"Al die woorde begin met *s*, so kyk na die tweede letter: *a* (sap, sak), *k* (skool), *l* (slang), *o* (son). In die alfabet kom a, k, l, o in dié volgorde.","en":"All the words start with *s*, so look at the second letter: *a* (sap, sak), *k* (skool), *l* (slang), *o* (son). In the alphabet a, k, l, o come in this order."},{"af":"*sap* en *sak* begin albei met *sa-*, so kyk na die derde letter: *k* kom voor *p*. Dus kom *sak* voor *sap*.","en":"*sap* and *sak* both start with *sa-*, so look at the third letter: *k* comes before *p*. So *sak* comes before *sap*."}],"answer":{"af":"sak, sap, skool, slang, son","en":"*sak, sap, skool, slang, son*"}},{"title":{"af":"Lettergrepe","en":"Syllables"},"problem":{"af":"Verdeel in lettergrepe en tel hulle: *verjaarsdag, komkommer, reën, huise*","en":"Divide into syllables and count them: *verjaarsdag* (birthday), *komkommer* (cucumber), *reën* (rain), *huise* (houses)"},"steps":[{"af":"Klap elke woord: *ver-jaars-dag* het 3 klappe.","en":"Clap each word: *ver-jaars-dag* has 3 claps."},{"af":"Tussen twee dieselfde medeklinkers verdeel jy die woord: *kom-kom-mer* (3).","en":"Between two of the same consonants you split the word: *kom-kom-mer* (3)."},{"af":"Die deelteken wys ’n nuwe lettergreep: *re-ën* (2).","en":"The diaeresis shows a new syllable: *re-ën* (2)."},{"af":"Die tweeklank *ui* bly saam, en die enkel medeklinker gaan na die volgende lettergreep: *hui-se* (2).","en":"The vowel pair *ui* stays together, and the single consonant goes to the next syllable: *hui-se* (2)."}],"answer":{"af":"ver-jaars-dag (3), kom-kom-mer (3), re-ën (2), hui-se (2)","en":"*ver-jaars-dag* (3), *kom-kom-mer* (3), *re-ën* (2), *hui-se* (2)"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin het die komma op die regte plek?","en":"Which sentence has the comma in the right place?"},"options":[{"af":"Zanele, kom help my asseblief.","en":"Zanele, kom help my asseblief."},{"af":"Zanele kom help my asseblief.","en":"Zanele kom help my asseblief."},{"af":"Zanele kom, help my asseblief.","en":"Zanele kom, help my asseblief."},{"af":"Zanele kom help, my asseblief.","en":"Zanele kom help, my asseblief."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Zanele is die **aanspreekvorm**: jy praat met haar en noem haar naam. Die komma skei haar naam van die res van die sin.","en":"*Zanele* is the **form of address**: you are talking to her and say her name. The comma separates her name from the rest of the sentence."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die woord *ek* kry altyd ’n hoofletter, net soos *I* in Engels.","en":"The word *ek* always takes a capital letter, just like *I* in English."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. *ek* kry net aan die begin van ’n sin ’n hoofletter. In die middel van ’n sin skryf jy *ek*: *Thabo en ek speel.*","en":"False. *ek* only takes a capital at the start of a sentence. In the middle of a sentence you write *ek*: *Thabo en ek speel.* (Thabo and I play.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord moet die hoofletter kry as jy hierdie sin reg skryf? *’n hond blaf by die hek.*","en":"Which word must get the capital letter when you write this sentence correctly? *’n hond blaf by die hek.* (A dog barks at the gate.)"},"options":[{"af":"’n","en":"’n"},{"af":"blaf","en":"blaf"},{"af":"hond","en":"hond"},{"af":"hek","en":"hek"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"As ’n sin met *’n* begin, bly *’n* klein en kry die **volgende woord** die hoofletter: *’n Hond*. *hek* is ’n soortnaam en kry nie ’n hoofletter nie.","en":"If a sentence starts with *’n*, the *’n* stays small and the **next word** gets the capital: *’n Hond*. *hek* (gate) is a common noun and takes no capital."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Kies die regte woord: *Ma ___ ons moet vroeg gaan slaap.*","en":"Choose the correct word: *Ma ___ ons moet vroeg gaan slaap.* (Mom ___ we must go to bed early.)"},"answers":{"af":["sê"],"en":["sê"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["se","sè","seë"],"en":["se","sè","seë"]}},"explain":{"af":"Hier praat Ma, so jy gebruik die werkwoord *sê* met ’n kappie. *se* (sonder kappie) wys besit: *Ma se boek*.","en":"Here Mom is speaking, so you use the verb *sê* (says) with a circumflex. *se* (without the circumflex) shows ownership: *Ma se boek* (Mom’s book)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die gidswoorde bo-aan ’n woordeboekbladsy is *mier* en *mol*. Watter woord sal jy op dié bladsy kry?","en":"The guide words at the top of a dictionary page are *mier* and *mol*. Which word will you find on that page?"},"options":[{"af":"maan","en":"maan"},{"af":"mis","en":"mis"},{"af":"mou","en":"mou"},{"af":"muis","en":"muis"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*mis* kom ná *mier*, want by die derde letter kom *s* ná *e*. Dit kom voor *mol*, want *i* kom voor *o*. *maan* kom voor *mier*, en *mou* en *muis* kom ná *mol*.","en":"*mis* comes after *mier*, because at the third letter *s* comes after *e*. It comes before *mol*, because *i* comes before *o*. *maan* comes before *mier*, and *mou* and *muis* come after *mol*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter lys is in alfabetiese volgorde?","en":"Which list is in alphabetical order?"},"options":[{"af":"bal, blom, berg, boom","en":"bal, blom, berg, boom"},{"af":"berg, bal, blom, boom","en":"berg, bal, blom, boom"},{"af":"bal, berg, boom, blom","en":"bal, berg, boom, blom"},{"af":"bal, berg, blom, boom","en":"bal, berg, blom, boom"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Al die woorde begin met *b*, so kyk na die tweede letter: *a* (bal), *e* (berg), *l* (blom), *o* (boom). In die alfabet kom a, e, l, o in dié volgorde.","en":"All the words start with *b*, so look at the second letter: *a* (bal), *e* (berg), *l* (blom), *o* (boom). In the alphabet a, e, l, o come in this order."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die meervoud: een ouma, twee ___","en":"Write the plural: *een ouma, twee* ___ (one granny, two grannies)"},"answers":{"af":["ouma’s","ouma's"],"en":["ouma’s","ouma's"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["oumas","oumae","ouma’e"],"en":["oumas","oumae","ouma’e"]}},"explain":{"af":"*ouma* eindig op ’n enkele klinker (*a*), so die meervoud kry ’n afkappingsteken en *s*: *ouma’s*.","en":"*ouma* ends in a single vowel (*a*), so the plural takes an apostrophe and *s*: *ouma’s*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is korrek?","en":"Which sentence is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Thabo’s fiets is rooi.","en":"Thabo’s fiets is rooi."},{"af":"Thabos fiets is rooi.","en":"Thabos fiets is rooi."},{"af":"Thabo se fiets is rooi.","en":"Thabo se fiets is rooi."},{"af":"Thabo sê fiets is rooi.","en":"Thabo sê fiets is rooi."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Afrikaans wys besit met **se** (sonder kappie): *Thabo se fiets*. ’n Afkappingsteken soos in Engels is fout, en *sê* met ’n kappie beteken ‘praat’.","en":"Afrikaans shows ownership with **se** (no circumflex): *Thabo se fiets* (Thabo’s bicycle). An apostrophe as in English is wrong, and *sê* with a circumflex means ‘say’."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke leesteken by sy gebruik.","en":"Match each punctuation mark to its use."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"punt ( . )","en":"full stop ( . )"},"r":{"af":"aan die einde van ’n stelsin","en":"at the end of a statement"}},{"l":{"af":"vraagteken ( ? )","en":"question mark ( ? )"},"r":{"af":"aan die einde van ’n vraag","en":"at the end of a question"}},{"l":{"af":"uitroepteken ( ! )","en":"exclamation mark ( ! )"},"r":{"af":"ná ’n bevel of ’n sterk gevoel","en":"after a command or a strong feeling"}},{"l":{"af":"komma ( , )","en":"comma ( , )"},"r":{"af":"skei die items in ’n lys","en":"separates the items in a list"}},{"l":{"af":"aanhalingstekens ( “ ” )","en":"quotation marks ( “ ” )"},"r":{"af":"om die presiese woorde wat iemand sê","en":"around the exact words someone says"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke leesteken het ’n eie taak. Die punt, vraagteken en uitroepteken sluit sinne af; die komma gee ’n kort ruskans; aanhalingstekens wys direkte woorde.","en":"Each punctuation mark has its own job. The full stop, question mark and exclamation mark end sentences; the comma gives a short pause; quotation marks show someone’s exact words."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe verdeel jy *sonneblom* in lettergrepe?","en":"How do you divide *sonneblom* (sunflower) into syllables?"},"options":[{"af":"son-ne-blom","en":"son-ne-blom"},{"af":"so-nne-blom","en":"so-nne-blom"},{"af":"sonn-e-blom","en":"sonn-e-blom"},{"af":"son-neb-lom","en":"son-neb-lom"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Klap die woord: *son-ne-blom* (3). Tussen die twee *n*’e verdeel jy die woord, en *blom* bly heel, want dit is ’n woord op sy eie.","en":"Clap the word: *son-ne-blom* (3). You split between the two *n*’s, and *blom* (flower) stays whole because it is a word on its own."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die deelteken in *oë* wys dat jy die *o* en die *e* apart moet uitspreek.","en":"The diaeresis in *oë* (eyes) shows that you must pronounce the *o* and the *e* separately."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Sonder die deelteken sou jy *oe* lees soos in *boek*. Met die deelteken sê jy *o-ë*: twee lettergrepe.","en":"True. Without the diaeresis you would read *oe* as in *boek*. With it you say *o-ë*: two syllables."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is heeltemal reg gespel?","en":"Which sentence is spelt completely correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Ek se dit gaan môre reën.","en":"Ek se dit gaan môre reën."},{"af":"Ek sê dit gaan môre reen.","en":"Ek sê dit gaan môre reen."},{"af":"Ek sê dit gaan mòre reën.","en":"Ek sê dit gaan mòre reën."},{"af":"Ek sê dit gaan môre reën.","en":"Ek sê dit gaan môre reën."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*sê* (praat) en *môre* kry ’n kappie, en *reën* kry ’n deelteken. Elke ander sin het een spelfout.","en":"*sê* (say) and *môre* (tomorrow) take a circumflex, and *reën* (rain) takes a diaeresis. Each of the other sentences has one spelling mistake."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Watter tweeklank ontbreek? *h___s* (die gebou waarin jy woon)","en":"Which vowel pair is missing? *h___s* (the building you live in)"},"answers":{"af":["ui"],"en":["ui"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["ei","ou","eu"],"en":["ei","ou","eu"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die woord is *huis*. Die tweeklank *ui* maak een klank en bly saam in die woord.","en":"The word is *huis* (house). The vowel pair *ui* makes one sound and stays together in the word."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin het die kommas reg?","en":"Which sentence has the commas right?"},"options":[{"af":"Ek het brood, melk, eiers, en botter gekoop.","en":"Ek het brood, melk, eiers, en botter gekoop."},{"af":"Ek het brood, melk, eiers en botter gekoop.","en":"Ek het brood, melk, eiers en botter gekoop."},{"af":"Ek het, brood, melk, eiers en botter gekoop.","en":"Ek het, brood, melk, eiers en botter gekoop."},{"af":"Ek het brood melk, eiers en botter gekoop.","en":"Ek het brood melk, eiers en botter gekoop."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In ’n lys kom ’n komma tussen die items, maar **nie** voor *en* nie. Daar kom ook nie ’n komma voor die eerste item nie.","en":"In a list a comma goes between the items, but **not** before *en* (and). There is also no comma before the first item."}}]},{"id":"afr5-t3-woordeskat-woordbou","title":{"af":"Woordeskat en woordbou","en":"Vocabulary and word building"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal sinonieme, antonieme, homonieme en homofone kan herken, nuwe woorde met samestellings en voor- en agtervoegsels kan bou en die betekenis van ’n onbekende woord uit die sin kan aflei.","en":"You will be able to recognise synonyms, antonyms, homonyms and homophones, build new words with compounds, prefixes and suffixes, and work out the meaning of an unknown word from the sentence."},"summary":{"af":"## Sinonieme en antonieme\n\nHoe meer woorde jy ken, hoe beter kan jy lees, praat en skryf. Woorde hang op baie maniere met mekaar saam.\n\n**Sinonieme** is woorde met (amper) **dieselfde betekenis**. Hulle help jou om nie heeltyd dieselfde woord te herhaal nie: *vinnig – gou, mooi – pragtig, bly – gelukkig, dapper – moedig, praat – gesels*.\n\n**Antonieme** is woorde met die **teenoorgestelde betekenis**: *warm – koud, hoog – laag, wen – verloor, lig – donker*. Baie antonieme maak jy met die voorvoegsel **on-**: *gelukkig – ongelukkig, eerlik – oneerlik, bekend – onbekend, moontlik – onmoontlik*.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Nie elke woord kry *on-* nie. Die teenoorgestelde van *groot* is *klein*, nie *ongroot* nie.\n\n## Homonieme en homofone\n\n**Homonieme** word **dieselfde gespel en uitgespreek**, maar het **verskillende betekenisse**. Die res van die sin wys watter betekenis bedoel word:\n- *Die **by** sit **by** die blom.* (’n insek; naby)\n- *Die stoel is te **laag**. Ma smeer ’n dik **laag** konfyt op.* (nie hoog nie; ’n lagie)\n- *Ek drink tee uit ’n **koppie**. Ons klim teen die **koppie** uit.* (’n beker; ’n klein heuwel)\n\n**Homofone** **klink dieselfde**, maar word **anders gespel** en beteken iets anders:\n- *reis* (’n tog) – *rys* (kos)\n- *hart* (in jou bors) – *hard* (nie sag nie)\n- *ys* (bevrore water) – *eis* (vra dat iets moet gebeur)\n\n## Samestellings\n\n’n **Samestelling** is ’n nuwe woord wat uit **twee of meer woorde** bestaan. Jy skryf dit as **een woord**: *skool + tas = skooltas, voet + bal = voetbal, see + skulp = seeskulp*. Die **laaste deel** sê wat dit is: ’n *voetbal* is ’n soort bal en ’n *seeskulp* is ’n soort skulp.\n\nSoms kom daar ’n **verbindingsklank** (*-s-* of *-e-*) tussen die woorde: *dorp + s + plein = dorpsplein, perd + e + by = perdeby*.\n\n## Afleidings met voor- en agtervoegsels\n\n’n **Afleiding** maak jy deur ’n stukkie **voor** (voorvoegsel) of **agter** (agtervoegsel) ’n woord te sit. So ’n stukkie kan nie alleen as woord staan nie.\n\n| Voegsel | Wat dit doen | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| **on-** | maak die teenoorgestelde | *eerlik → oneerlik, vriendelik → onvriendelik* |\n| **ver-** | maak ’n werkwoord, dikwels vir ’n verandering | *beter → verbeter, kleur → verkleur* |\n| **-heid** | maak ’n selfstandige naamwoord | *waar → waarheid, vry → vryheid* |\n| **-loos** | beteken *sonder* | *kleur → kleurloos, dak → dakloos* |\n| **-lik** | maak ’n byvoeglike naamwoord | *eer → eerlik, vriend → vriendelik* |\n| **-ing** | maak ’n selfstandige naamwoord van ’n werkwoord | *oefen → oefening, teken → tekening* |\n\n> **Onthou:** Samestelling = **woord + woord** (*voetbal*). Afleiding = **woord + voegsel** (*vryheid, onbekend*).\n\n## Woordfamilies en betekenis uit konteks\n\n’n **Woordfamilie** is ’n groep woorde wat van dieselfde **stamwoord** kom: *speel → speler, speelgoed, speelgrond, speletjie*. As jy die stamwoord ken, kan jy die betekenis van die ander woorde raai.\n\nKry jy ’n **onbekende woord**? Moenie ophou lees nie:\n1. Lees die hele sin en die sin daarna.\n2. Soek **leidrade**: ’n sinoniem, ’n teenoorgestelde of ’n voorbeeld naby die woord.\n3. Kyk of jy ’n bekende stamwoord of voegsel in die woord herken.\n4. Sit jou raaiskoot in die plek van die woord en kyk of die sin nog logies is.\n\n*Die hond was so **gulsig** dat hy sy hele bak kos in een oomblik opgeslurp het.* Die leidraad *hele bak in een oomblik* wys dat *gulsig* beteken: hy eet baie en vinnig.","en":"## Synonyms and antonyms\n\nThe more words you know, the better you can read, speak and write. Words are linked to each other in many ways.\n\n**Synonyms** (*sinonieme*) are words with (almost) **the same meaning**. They help you not to repeat the same word all the time: *vinnig – gou* (fast – quick), *mooi – pragtig* (pretty – beautiful), *bly – gelukkig* (glad – happy), *dapper – moedig* (brave – courageous), *praat – gesels* (talk – chat).\n\n**Antonyms** (*antonieme*) are words with the **opposite meaning**: *warm – koud* (hot – cold), *hoog – laag* (high – low), *wen – verloor* (win – lose), *lig – donker* (light – dark). Many antonyms are made with the prefix **on-** (un-/dis-): *gelukkig – ongelukkig* (happy – unhappy), *eerlik – oneerlik* (honest – dishonest), *bekend – onbekend* (known – unknown), *moontlik – onmoontlik* (possible – impossible).\n\n> **Common mistake:** Not every word takes *on-*. The opposite of *groot* (big) is *klein* (small), not *ongroot*.\n\n## Homonyms and homophones\n\n**Homonyms** (*homonieme*) are **spelt and pronounced the same** but have **different meanings**. The rest of the sentence shows which meaning is meant:\n- *Die **by** sit **by** die blom.* (The **bee** sits **near** the flower.)\n- *Die stoel is te **laag**. Ma smeer ’n dik **laag** konfyt op.* (The chair is too **low**. Mom spreads on a thick **layer** of jam.)\n- *Ek drink tee uit ’n **koppie**. Ons klim teen die **koppie** uit.* (I drink tea from a **cup**. We climb up the **small hill**.)\n\n**Homophones** (*homofone*) **sound the same** but are **spelt differently** and mean different things:\n- *reis* (a journey) – *rys* (rice)\n- *hart* (heart) – *hard* (hard, not soft)\n- *ys* (ice) – *eis* (to demand)\n\n## Compounds\n\nA **compound** (*samestelling*) is a new word made of **two or more words**. You write it as **one word**: *skool + tas = skooltas* (school bag), *voet + bal = voetbal* (football), *see + skulp = seeskulp* (seashell). The **last part** tells you what it is: a *voetbal* is a kind of *bal* and a *seeskulp* is a kind of *skulp* (shell).\n\nSometimes a **linking sound** (*verbindingsklank*: *-s-* or *-e-*) comes between the words: *dorp + s + plein = dorpsplein* (town square), *perd + e + by = perdeby* (wasp).\n\n## Derivatives with prefixes and suffixes\n\nYou make a **derivative** (*afleiding*) by putting a small part **in front of** (prefix, *voorvoegsel*) or **after** (suffix, *agtervoegsel*) a word. Such a part cannot stand alone as a word.\n\n| Affix | What it does | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| **on-** | makes the opposite | *eerlik → oneerlik, vriendelik → onvriendelik* (friendly → unfriendly) |\n| **ver-** | makes a verb, often for a change | *beter → verbeter* (improve), *kleur → verkleur* (change colour) |\n| **-heid** | makes a noun | *waar → waarheid* (truth), *vry → vryheid* (freedom) |\n| **-loos** | means *without* (like -less) | *kleur → kleurloos* (colourless), *dak → dakloos* (homeless) |\n| **-lik** | makes an adjective | *eer → eerlik* (honest), *vriend → vriendelik* (friendly) |\n| **-ing** | makes a noun from a verb | *oefen → oefening* (exercise), *teken → tekening* (drawing) |\n\n> **Remember:** Compound = **word + word** (*voetbal*). Derivative = **word + affix** (*vryheid, onbekend*).\n\n## Word families and meaning from context\n\nA **word family** (*woordfamilie*) is a group of words that come from the same **root word** (*stamwoord*): *speel* (play) → *speler* (player), *speelgoed* (toys), *speelgrond* (playground), *speletjie* (game). If you know the root word, you can guess the meaning of the others.\n\nDo you find an **unknown word**? Don’t stop reading:\n1. Read the whole sentence and the next one.\n2. Look for **clues**: a synonym, an opposite or an example near the word.\n3. See if you recognise a known root word or affix in the word.\n4. Put your guess in the place of the word and check that the sentence still makes sense.\n\n*Die hond was so **gulsig** dat hy sy hele bak kos in een oomblik opgeslurp het.* (The dog was so **greedy** that he gobbled up his whole bowl of food in one moment.) The clue *hele bak in een oomblik* (whole bowl in one moment) shows that *gulsig* means he eats a lot and fast."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Sinoniem","en":"Synonym (sinoniem)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord met (amper) dieselfde betekenis as ’n ander woord: *vinnig – gou*.","en":"A word with (almost) the same meaning as another word: *vinnig – gou* (fast – quick)."}},{"term":{"af":"Antoniem","en":"Antonym (antoniem)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord met die teenoorgestelde betekenis: *warm – koud*.","en":"A word with the opposite meaning: *warm – koud* (hot – cold)."}},{"term":{"af":"Homoniem","en":"Homonym (homoniem)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat dieselfde gespel en uitgespreek word as ’n ander woord, maar iets anders beteken: *by* (insek) en *by* (naby).","en":"A word that is spelt and pronounced like another word but means something else: *by* (bee) and *by* (near)."}},{"term":{"af":"Homofoon","en":"Homophone (homofoon)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat dieselfde klink as ’n ander woord, maar anders gespel word en iets anders beteken: *reis – rys*.","en":"A word that sounds like another word but is spelt differently and means something else: *reis – rys* (journey – rice)."}},{"term":{"af":"Samestelling","en":"Compound (samestelling)"},"def":{"af":"’n Nuwe woord wat uit twee of meer woorde bestaan: *skool + tas = skooltas*.","en":"A new word made of two or more words: *skool + tas = skooltas* (school bag)."}},{"term":{"af":"Afleiding","en":"Derivative (afleiding)"},"def":{"af":"’n Nuwe woord wat jy maak deur ’n voorvoegsel of agtervoegsel by ’n woord te voeg: *oneerlik, vryheid*.","en":"A new word you make by adding a prefix or suffix to a word: *oneerlik* (dishonest), *vryheid* (freedom)."}},{"term":{"af":"Voorvoegsel","en":"Prefix (voorvoegsel)"},"def":{"af":"’n Stukkie voor aan ’n woord wat die betekenis verander, soos *on-* in *ongelukkig*.","en":"A small part at the front of a word that changes its meaning, like *on-* in *ongelukkig* (unhappy)."}},{"term":{"af":"Agtervoegsel","en":"Suffix (agtervoegsel)"},"def":{"af":"’n Stukkie agter aan ’n woord wat ’n nuwe woord maak, soos *-heid* in *waarheid*.","en":"A small part at the end of a word that makes a new word, like *-heid* in *waarheid* (truth)."}},{"term":{"af":"Woordfamilie","en":"Word family (woordfamilie)"},"def":{"af":"’n Groep woorde wat van dieselfde stamwoord kom: *speel, speler, speelgoed*.","en":"A group of words that come from the same root word: *speel, speler, speelgoed* (play, player, toys)."}},{"term":{"af":"Konteks","en":"Context (konteks)"},"def":{"af":"Die woorde en sinne rondom ’n woord wat jou help om sy betekenis te verstaan.","en":"The words and sentences around a word that help you understand its meaning."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Antonieme vorm","en":"Forming antonyms"},"problem":{"af":"Gee die antoniem van: *eerlik, bekend, hoog, wen*.","en":"Give the antonym of: *eerlik* (honest), *bekend* (known), *hoog* (high), *wen* (win)."},"steps":[{"af":"*eerlik* en *bekend* kan die voorvoegsel **on-** kry: *oneerlik, onbekend*.","en":"*eerlik* and *bekend* can take the prefix **on-**: *oneerlik, onbekend*."},{"af":"*hoog* en *wen* kry nie *on-* nie. Jy moet ’n heel ander woord kies: *laag* en *verloor*.","en":"*hoog* and *wen* do not take *on-*. You must choose a completely different word: *laag* (low) and *verloor* (lose)."},{"af":"Toets elke paar in ’n sin: *Die muur is hoog, maar die heining is laag.*","en":"Test each pair in a sentence: *Die muur is hoog, maar die heining is laag.* (The wall is high, but the fence is low.)"}],"answer":{"af":"oneerlik, onbekend, laag, verloor","en":"*oneerlik, onbekend, laag, verloor*"}},{"title":{"af":"Samestelling of afleiding?","en":"Compound or derivative?"},"problem":{"af":"Sê of elke woord ’n samestelling of ’n afleiding is: *skooltas, vryheid, onbekend, perdeby*.","en":"Say whether each word is a compound or a derivative: *skooltas, vryheid, onbekend, perdeby*."},"steps":[{"af":"*skooltas* = *skool* + *tas*: twee woorde, dus ’n **samestelling**.","en":"*skooltas* = *skool* + *tas*: two words, so a **compound**."},{"af":"*vryheid* = *vry* + *-heid*: ’n woord plus ’n agtervoegsel, dus ’n **afleiding**.","en":"*vryheid* = *vry* + *-heid*: a word plus a suffix, so a **derivative**."},{"af":"*onbekend* = *on-* + *bekend*: ’n voorvoegsel plus ’n woord, dus ’n **afleiding**.","en":"*onbekend* = *on-* + *bekend*: a prefix plus a word, so a **derivative**."},{"af":"*perdeby* = *perd* + *-e-* + *by*: twee woorde met ’n verbindingsklank, dus ’n **samestelling**.","en":"*perdeby* = *perd* + *-e-* + *by*: two words with a linking sound, so a **compound**."}],"answer":{"af":"Samestellings: skooltas, perdeby. Afleidings: vryheid, onbekend.","en":"Compounds: *skooltas, perdeby*. Derivatives: *vryheid, onbekend*."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Homoniem in ’n sin","en":"A homonym in a sentence"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik die twee betekenisse van *koppie* in: *Ouma drink tee uit haar blou koppie terwyl sy na die koppie agter die plaas kyk.*","en":"Explain the two meanings of *koppie* in: *Ouma drink tee uit haar blou koppie terwyl sy na die koppie agter die plaas kyk.* (Granny drinks tea from her blue koppie while she looks at the koppie behind the farm.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Die eerste *koppie* is iets waaruit jy tee drink: ’n **beker**.","en":"The first *koppie* is something you drink tea from: a **cup**."},{"af":"Die tweede *koppie* is iets waarna jy kyk, agter die plaas: ’n **klein heuwel**.","en":"The second *koppie* is something you look at, behind the farm: a **small hill**."},{"af":"Dieselfde spelling en klank, maar ’n ander betekenis: *koppie* is ’n **homoniem**.","en":"Same spelling and sound, but a different meaning: *koppie* is a **homonym**."}],"answer":{"af":"koppie 1 = ’n beker vir tee; koppie 2 = ’n klein heuwel","en":"*koppie* 1 = a cup for tea; *koppie* 2 = a small hill"}},{"title":{"af":"Betekenis uit konteks","en":"Meaning from context"},"problem":{"af":"Wat beteken *vermorsing* in: *Die kraan het die hele nag gedrup, en die vermorsing van soveel water het Pa kwaad gemaak.*","en":"What does *vermorsing* mean in: *Die kraan het die hele nag gedrup, en die vermorsing van soveel water het Pa kwaad gemaak.* (The tap dripped all night, and the vermorsing of so much water made Dad angry.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Lees die hele sin: die kraan het die hele nag gedrup, so baie water het verniet weggeloop.","en":"Read the whole sentence: the tap dripped all night, so a lot of water ran away for nothing."},{"af":"Nog ’n leidraad: Pa is **kwaad**, so iets slegs het met die water gebeur.","en":"Another clue: Dad is **angry**, so something bad happened to the water."},{"af":"*-ing* wys dat dit ’n selfstandige naamwoord is. Toets jou raaiskoot: *die onnodige verlies van soveel water* – die sin is logies.","en":"*-ing* shows that it is a noun. Test your guess: *the needless loss of so much water* – the sentence makes sense."}],"answer":{"af":"*Vermorsing* beteken dat iets (hier water) onnodig verlore gaan.","en":"*Vermorsing* means that something (here water) is wasted or lost for no good reason."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is ’n **sinoniem** van *vinnig*?","en":"Which word is a **synonym** of *vinnig* (fast)?"},"options":[{"af":"stadig","en":"stadig"},{"af":"gou","en":"gou"},{"af":"vroeg","en":"vroeg"},{"af":"lui","en":"lui"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*gou* beteken ook dat iets nie lank neem nie, net soos *vinnig*. *stadig* is die antoniem, en *vroeg* gaan oor tyd, nie spoed nie.","en":"*gou* (quick) also means that something does not take long, just like *vinnig*. *stadig* (slow) is the antonym, and *vroeg* (early) is about time, not speed."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord behoort **nie** aan die woordfamilie van *speel* nie?","en":"Which word does **not** belong to the word family of *speel* (play)?"},"options":[{"af":"speler","en":"speler"},{"af":"speelgoed","en":"speelgoed"},{"af":"speletjie","en":"speletjie"},{"af":"spieël","en":"spieël"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*speler, speelgoed* en *speletjie* kom almal van die stamwoord *speel*. *spieël* (waarin jy jouself sien) lyk amper so, maar het niks met speel te doen nie.","en":"*speler* (player), *speelgoed* (toys) and *speletjie* (game) all come from the root word *speel*. *spieël* (mirror) looks similar, but has nothing to do with playing."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*Hart* en *hard* is homofone: hulle klink dieselfde, maar word anders gespel en beteken iets anders.","en":"*Hart* and *hard* are homophones: they sound the same but are spelt differently and mean different things."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die *d* aan die einde van *hard* klink soos ’n *t*, so die woorde klink dieselfde. *Hart* is die orgaan in jou bors; *hard* is die teenoorgestelde van *sag*.","en":"True. The *d* at the end of *hard* sounds like a *t*, so the words sound the same. *Hart* is the organ in your chest (heart); *hard* is the opposite of *sag* (soft)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Maak ’n selfstandige naamwoord met *-heid*: *Moenie jok nie; sê altyd die ___.* (waar)","en":"Make a noun with *-heid*: *Moenie jok nie; sê altyd die ___.* (Don’t lie; always tell the ___.) (*waar*)"},"answers":{"af":["waarheid"],"en":["waarheid"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["waarlik","waarte","waarloos"],"en":["waarlik","waarte","waarloos"]}},"explain":{"af":"*waar* + *-heid* = *waarheid*. Die agtervoegsel *-heid* maak ’n selfstandige naamwoord van die byvoeglike naamwoord *waar*.","en":"*waar* + *-heid* = *waarheid* (truth). The suffix *-heid* turns the adjective *waar* (true) into a noun."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is ’n **samestelling**?","en":"Which word is a **compound**?"},"options":[{"af":"voetbal","en":"voetbal"},{"af":"vriendelik","en":"vriendelik"},{"af":"onbekend","en":"onbekend"},{"af":"vryheid","en":"vryheid"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*voetbal* = *voet* + *bal*: twee woorde. Die ander is afleidings: *vriend + -lik*, *on- + bekend*, *vry + -heid*.","en":"*voetbal* = *voet* + *bal*: two words. The others are derivatives: *vriend + -lik*, *on- + bekend*, *vry + -heid*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter sin beteken *laag* ‘’n lagie’?","en":"In which sentence does *laag* mean ‘a layer’?"},"options":[{"af":"Die tafel is te laag vir Pa.","en":"Die tafel is te laag vir Pa."},{"af":"Die voël vlieg laag oor die dam.","en":"Die voël vlieg laag oor die dam."},{"af":"Ma smeer ’n dik laag konfyt op die brood.","en":"Ma smeer ’n dik laag konfyt op die brood."},{"af":"Die rivier is laag ná die droogte.","en":"Die rivier is laag ná die droogte."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*’n Dik laag konfyt* is ’n lagie konfyt bo-op die brood. In die ander sinne beteken *laag* ‘nie hoog nie’. *Laag* is ’n homoniem.","en":"*’n Dik laag konfyt* is a layer of jam on the bread. In the other sentences *laag* means ‘not high’ (low). *Laag* is a homonym."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke woord by sy antoniem.","en":"Match each word to its antonym."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"wen","en":"wen"},"r":{"af":"verloor","en":"verloor"}},{"l":{"af":"hoog","en":"hoog"},"r":{"af":"laag","en":"laag"}},{"l":{"af":"dapper","en":"dapper"},"r":{"af":"bang","en":"bang"}},{"l":{"af":"begin","en":"begin"},"r":{"af":"eindig","en":"eindig"}},{"l":{"af":"eerlik","en":"eerlik"},"r":{"af":"oneerlik","en":"oneerlik"}}],"explain":{"af":"Antonieme het teenoorgestelde betekenisse. Net *eerlik* vorm sy antoniem met *on-*; die ander het ’n heel ander woord nodig.","en":"Antonyms have opposite meanings: *wen – verloor* (win – lose), *hoog – laag* (high – low), *dapper – bang* (brave – scared), *begin – eindig* (begin – end). Only *eerlik* forms its antonym with *on-*; the others need a completely different word."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees: *Ná die lang stap teen die berg op was Ravi so uitgeput dat hy op die bank aan die slaap geraak het.* Wat beteken *uitgeput*?","en":"Read: *Ná die lang stap teen die berg op was Ravi so uitgeput dat hy op die bank aan die slaap geraak het.* (After the long walk up the mountain Ravi was so uitgeput that he fell asleep on the couch.) What does *uitgeput* mean?"},"options":[{"af":"baie honger","en":"very hungry"},{"af":"baie bang","en":"very scared"},{"af":"baie moeg","en":"very tired"},{"af":"baie kwaad","en":"very angry"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die leidrade is *die lang stap teen die berg op* en *aan die slaap geraak*. Iemand wat ná ’n lang stap dadelik aan die slaap raak, is baie moeg.","en":"The clues are *die lang stap teen die berg op* (the long walk up the mountain) and *aan die slaap geraak* (fell asleep). Someone who falls asleep straight after a long walk is very tired."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die antoniem met *on-*: bekend → ___","en":"Write the antonym with *on-*: *bekend* (known) → ___"},"answers":{"af":["onbekend"],"en":["onbekend"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["ombekend","ontbekend","verbekend"],"en":["ombekend","ontbekend","verbekend"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die voorvoegsel *on-* maak die teenoorgestelde: *onbekend*. Die *n* bly ’n *n*, al klink dit amper soos *m* voor die *b*.","en":"The prefix *on-* makes the opposite: *onbekend* (unknown). The *n* stays an *n*, even though it sounds almost like *m* before the *b*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is ’n afleiding met ’n **agtervoegsel**?","en":"Which word is a derivative with a **suffix**?"},"options":[{"af":"tekening","en":"tekening"},{"af":"voetbal","en":"voetbal"},{"af":"onwaar","en":"onwaar"},{"af":"skooltas","en":"skooltas"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*tekening* = *teken* + *-ing*: die stukkie kom agter die woord. *onwaar* het ’n voorvoegsel, en *voetbal* en *skooltas* is samestellings.","en":"*tekening* (drawing) = *teken* + *-ing*: the part comes after the word. *onwaar* (untrue) has a prefix, and *voetbal* and *skooltas* are compounds."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*Dakloos* beteken dat iemand ’n mooi dak oor sy kop het.","en":"*Dakloos* means that someone has a nice roof over their head."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die agtervoegsel *-loos* beteken *sonder*. *Dakloos* beteken dat iemand **sonder** ’n huis of dak is.","en":"False. The suffix *-loos* means *without*. *Dakloos* (homeless) means that someone is **without** a home or roof."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken *kleurloos*?","en":"What does *kleurloos* mean?"},"options":[{"af":"vol kleur","en":"full of colour"},{"af":"met net een kleur","en":"with only one colour"},{"af":"met ’n mooi kleur","en":"with a pretty colour"},{"af":"sonder kleur","en":"without colour"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*-loos* beteken *sonder*, so *kleurloos* is iets sonder kleur, soos skoon water.","en":"*-loos* means *without*, so *kleurloos* (colourless) is something without colour, like clean water."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Kies die regte homofoon: *Ons eet ___ en kerrie.*","en":"Choose the correct homophone: *Ons eet ___ en kerrie.* (We eat ___ and curry.)"},"answers":{"af":["rys"],"en":["rys"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["reis","ruis","rits"],"en":["reis","ruis","rits"]}},"explain":{"af":"*rys* (met *y*) is die kos. *reis* (met *ei*) klink dieselfde, maar beteken ’n tog of rit.","en":"*rys* (with *y*) is the food (rice). *reis* (with *ei*) sounds the same, but means a journey or trip."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **antoniem** van *vriendelik*?","en":"What is the **antonym** of *vriendelik* (friendly)?"},"options":[{"af":"vriendloos","en":"vriendloos"},{"af":"onvriendelik","en":"onvriendelik"},{"af":"ontvriendelik","en":"ontvriendelik"},{"af":"vriendskaplik","en":"vriendskaplik"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die voorvoegsel *on-* maak die teenoorgestelde: *onvriendelik*. *vriendloos* beteken ‘sonder vriende’ en *vriendskaplik* beteken amper dieselfde as *vriendelik*.","en":"The prefix *on-* makes the opposite: *onvriendelik* (unfriendly). *vriendloos* means ‘without friends’ and *vriendskaplik* means almost the same as *vriendelik*."}}]},{"id":"afr5-t3-idiome-spreekwoorde","title":{"af":"Idiome, spreekwoorde en vergelykings","en":"Idioms, proverbs and similes"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal bekende Afrikaanse idiome, spreekwoorde en vaste vergelykings verstaan, die letterlike en figuurlike betekenis kan onderskei en hulle reg in sinne kan gebruik.","en":"You will be able to understand well-known Afrikaans idioms, proverbs and fixed similes, tell the literal and figurative meaning apart and use them correctly in sentences."},"summary":{"af":"## Letterlik en figuurlik\n\nAfrikaans het baie kleurvolle uitdrukkings. As iemand sê jy het *’n gat in die dag geslaap*, het niemand regtig ’n gat gegrawe nie! Om sulke uitdrukkings te verstaan, moet jy twee soorte betekenis ken:\n- Die **letterlike betekenis** is presies wat die woorde sê.\n- Die **figuurlike betekenis** is wat die uitdrukking eintlik beteken.\n\n*Pa het sy hande vol.* Letterlik: Pa hou baie goed in sy hande vas. Figuurlik: Pa is **baie besig**. Die **konteks** (die res van die sin) wys watter betekenis bedoel word.\n\nHoekom gebruik mense sulke uitdrukkings? Hulle maak jou taal **kleurvol** en sê baie in min woorde. ’n Goeie uitdrukking in jou opstel wys dat jy jou taal goed ken.\n\n## Idiome\n\n’n **Idioom** is ’n **vaste groep woorde** met ’n figuurlike betekenis. Jy gebruik dit as **deel van ’n sin**, en jy kan die werkwoord in ’n ander tyd sit: *Sipho het Saterdag ’n gat in die dag geslaap.*\n\n| Idioom | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| ’n gat in die dag slaap | tot baie laat slaap |\n| met die deur in die huis val | iets dadelik en reguit sê, sonder ’n inleiding |\n| sy hande vol hê | baie besig wees |\n| die aap uit die mou laat | ’n geheim verklap |\n| koue voete kry | bang word en iets nie meer wil doen nie |\n| die kat uit die boom kyk | eers afwag en kyk wat gebeur |\n| twee vlieë met een klap slaan | twee dinge tegelyk regkry |\n| met die hoenders gaan slaap | baie vroeg gaan slaap |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie die woorde van ’n idioom verander nie. Dit is *die aap uit die mou laat*, nie *die aap uit die sak laat* nie. Jy mag wel die voornaamwoord aanpas: *Ma het **haar** hande vol.*\n\n## Spreekwoorde\n\n’n **Spreekwoord** is ’n **volledige sin** wat ’n **les** of **wysheid** oor die lewe leer. Die woorde van ’n spreekwoord verander nie.\n\n| Spreekwoord | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| Alle baat help. | Elke klein bietjie help. |\n| Oefening baar kuns. | As jy oefen, word jy goed in iets. |\n| Stille waters, diepe grond. | ’n Stil mens weet en dink dikwels meer as wat jy verwag. |\n| Haastige hond verbrand sy mond. | As jy te gou maak, maak jy foute. |\n| Eendrag maak mag. | Saam is ons sterk. |\n| Die appel val nie ver van die boom nie. | Kinders is dikwels net soos hulle ouers. |\n\nAnika oefen elke dag klavier en speel nou pragtig: *Oefening baar kuns.*\n\n## Vaste vergelykings\n\n’n **Vaste vergelyking** vergelyk twee dinge met **so … soos**. Die woorde is vas, en almal ken die vergelyking:\n- *so sterk soos ’n os*\n- *so koud soos ys*\n- *so bang soos ’n muis*\n- *so lig soos ’n veer*\n- *so wit soos sneeu*\n- *so stadig soos ’n skilpad*\n- *so hard soos klip*\n\n> **Onthou:** ’n **Idioom** is deel van ’n sin. ’n **Spreekwoord** is ’n hele sin met ’n les. ’n **Vaste vergelyking** het *so … soos*.\n\n## Gebruik dit reg in sinne\n\n1. Lees die situasie en dink wat eintlik gebeur.\n2. Kies die uitdrukking met die regte **figuurlike** betekenis.\n3. Pas die tyd en die voornaamwoord by jou sin aan, maar hou die res van die uitdrukking presies dieselfde: *Die onderwyseres het haar hande vol gehad met die nuwe klas.*","en":"## Literal and figurative\n\nAfrikaans has many colourful expressions. If someone says you *slept a hole in the day* (*’n gat in die dag geslaap*), nobody really dug a hole! To understand such expressions, you need to know two kinds of meaning:\n- The **literal meaning** (*letterlike betekenis*) is exactly what the words say.\n- The **figurative meaning** (*figuurlike betekenis*) is what the expression really means.\n\n*Pa het sy hande vol.* (Dad has his hands full.) Literally: Dad is holding lots of things in his hands. Figuratively: Dad is **very busy**. The **context** (the rest of the sentence) shows which meaning is meant.\n\nWhy do people use such expressions? They make your language **colourful** and say a lot in few words. A good expression in your essay shows that you know your language well.\n\n## Idioms\n\nAn **idiom** (*idioom*) is a **fixed group of words** with a figurative meaning. You use it as **part of a sentence**, and you may put the verb in another tense: *Sipho het Saterdag ’n gat in die dag geslaap.* (Sipho slept very late on Saturday.)\n\n| Idiom | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| *’n gat in die dag slaap* (sleep a hole in the day) | sleep until very late |\n| *met die deur in die huis val* (fall into the house with the door) | say something straight away, without an introduction |\n| *sy hande vol hê* (have his hands full) | be very busy |\n| *die aap uit die mou laat* (let the monkey out of the sleeve) | give away a secret |\n| *koue voete kry* (get cold feet) | become scared and not want to do something any more |\n| *die kat uit die boom kyk* (watch the cat out of the tree) | first wait and see what happens |\n| *twee vlieë met een klap slaan* (hit two flies with one swat) | get two things done at once |\n| *met die hoenders gaan slaap* (go to sleep with the chickens) | go to bed very early |\n\n> **Common mistake:** Don’t change the words of an idiom. It is *die aap uit die mou laat*, not *die aap uit die sak laat*. You may adjust the pronoun, though: *Ma het **haar** hande vol.* (Mom has **her** hands full.)\n\n## Proverbs\n\nA **proverb** (*spreekwoord*) is a **complete sentence** that teaches a **lesson** or **wisdom** about life. The words of a proverb do not change.\n\n| Proverb | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| *Alle baat help.* | Every little bit helps. |\n| *Oefening baar kuns.* | If you practise, you become good at something. |\n| *Stille waters, diepe grond.* | A quiet person often knows and thinks more than you expect. |\n| *Haastige hond verbrand sy mond.* | If you rush, you make mistakes. |\n| *Eendrag maak mag.* | Together we are strong. |\n| *Die appel val nie ver van die boom nie.* | Children are often just like their parents. |\n\nAnika practises the piano every day and now plays beautifully: *Oefening baar kuns.*\n\n## Fixed similes\n\nA **fixed simile** (*vaste vergelyking*) compares two things with **so … soos** (as … as). The words are fixed and everyone knows the simile:\n- *so sterk soos ’n os* (as strong as an ox)\n- *so koud soos ys* (as cold as ice)\n- *so bang soos ’n muis* (as scared as a mouse)\n- *so lig soos ’n veer* (as light as a feather)\n- *so wit soos sneeu* (as white as snow)\n- *so stadig soos ’n skilpad* (as slow as a tortoise)\n- *so hard soos klip* (as hard as stone)\n\n> **Remember:** An **idiom** is part of a sentence. A **proverb** is a whole sentence with a lesson. A **fixed simile** has *so … soos*.\n\n## Using them correctly in sentences\n\n1. Read the situation and think about what is really happening.\n2. Choose the expression with the right **figurative** meaning.\n3. Adjust the tense and the pronoun to your sentence, but keep the rest of the expression exactly the same: *Die onderwyseres het haar hande vol gehad met die nuwe klas.* (The teacher had her hands full with the new class.)"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Uitdrukking","en":"Expression (uitdrukking)"},"def":{"af":"’n Groep woorde wat saam ’n spesiale betekenis het, soos ’n idioom of spreekwoord.","en":"A group of words that together have a special meaning, such as an idiom or proverb."}},{"term":{"af":"Letterlike betekenis","en":"Literal meaning (letterlike betekenis)"},"def":{"af":"Die betekenis presies soos die woorde dit sê.","en":"The meaning exactly as the words say it."}},{"term":{"af":"Figuurlike betekenis","en":"Figurative meaning (figuurlike betekenis)"},"def":{"af":"Die eintlike betekenis van ’n uitdrukking, wat anders is as wat die woorde letterlik sê.","en":"The real meaning of an expression, which is different from what the words literally say."}},{"term":{"af":"Idioom","en":"Idiom (idioom)"},"def":{"af":"’n Vaste groep woorde met ’n figuurlike betekenis wat jy as deel van ’n sin gebruik: *sy hande vol hê*.","en":"A fixed group of words with a figurative meaning that you use as part of a sentence: *sy hande vol hê* (be very busy)."}},{"term":{"af":"Spreekwoord","en":"Proverb (spreekwoord)"},"def":{"af":"’n Volledige, vaste sin wat ’n les of wysheid leer: *Oefening baar kuns.*","en":"A complete, fixed sentence that teaches a lesson or wisdom: *Oefening baar kuns.* (Practice makes perfect.)"}},{"term":{"af":"Vaste vergelyking","en":"Fixed simile (vaste vergelyking)"},"def":{"af":"’n Bekende vergelyking met *so … soos* waarvan die woorde nie verander nie: *so koud soos ys*.","en":"A well-known comparison with *so … soos* (as … as) whose words do not change: *so koud soos ys* (as cold as ice)."}},{"term":{"af":"Konteks","en":"Context (konteks)"},"def":{"af":"Die res van die sin of situasie, wat wys watter betekenis bedoel word.","en":"The rest of the sentence or situation, which shows which meaning is meant."}},{"term":{"af":"Wysheid","en":"Wisdom (wysheid)"},"def":{"af":"Goeie raad oor die lewe wat mense oor baie jare geleer het.","en":"Good advice about life that people have learnt over many years."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Letterlik en figuurlik","en":"Literal and figurative"},"problem":{"af":"Gee die letterlike en die figuurlike betekenis van: *Die onderwyseres het haar hande vol met die nuwe klas.*","en":"Give the literal and the figurative meaning of: *Die onderwyseres het haar hande vol met die nuwe klas.* (The teacher has her hands full with the new class.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Letterlik: haar hande is vol – sy dra baie goed.","en":"Literally: her hands are full – she is carrying lots of things."},{"af":"Figuurlik: die klas gee vir haar baie werk, so sy is baie besig.","en":"Figuratively: the class gives her a lot of work, so she is very busy."},{"af":"Die konteks (*met die nuwe klas*) wys dat die figuurlike betekenis bedoel word, want ’n klas kan jy nie in jou hande dra nie.","en":"The context (*met die nuwe klas*, with the new class) shows that the figurative meaning is meant, because you cannot carry a class in your hands."}],"answer":{"af":"Letterlik: haar hande is vol. Figuurlik: sy is baie besig.","en":"Literally: her hands are full. Figuratively: she is very busy."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Idioom in die verlede tyd","en":"An idiom in the past tense"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf ’n sin in die verlede tyd met *’n gat in die dag slaap* oor Sipho, wat Saterdag eers om elfuur opgestaan het.","en":"Write a sentence in the past tense with *’n gat in die dag slaap* about Sipho, who only got up at eleven o’clock on Saturday."},"steps":[{"af":"Die idioom beteken ‘tot baie laat slaap’ – dit pas by Sipho.","en":"The idiom means ‘sleep until very late’ – it fits Sipho."},{"af":"Verlede tyd: *slaap* word *het … geslaap*.","en":"Past tense: *slaap* becomes *het … geslaap*."},{"af":"Die res van die idioom bly presies dieselfde: *’n gat in die dag*.","en":"The rest of the idiom stays exactly the same: *’n gat in die dag*."}],"answer":{"af":"Sipho het Saterdag ’n gat in die dag geslaap.","en":"*Sipho het Saterdag ’n gat in die dag geslaap.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Kies die regte spreekwoord","en":"Choose the right proverb"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato, Johan en Aisha kan nie die swaar kas alleen skuif nie. Toe hulle al drie saam stoot, skuif dit maklik. Watter spreekwoord pas?","en":"Lerato, Johan and Aisha cannot move the heavy cupboard on their own. When all three push together, it moves easily. Which proverb fits?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die les is dat mense saam sterker is as alleen.","en":"The lesson is that people are stronger together than alone."},{"af":"*Eendrag maak mag* beteken presies dit: saam is ons sterk.","en":"*Eendrag maak mag* means exactly that: together we are strong."},{"af":"*Alle baat help* gaan oor klein bietjies wat optel, en *Oefening baar kuns* oor oefen – hulle pas nie so goed nie.","en":"*Alle baat help* is about small bits adding up, and *Oefening baar kuns* is about practising – they do not fit as well."}],"answer":{"af":"Eendrag maak mag.","en":"*Eendrag maak mag.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Voltooi die vergelykings","en":"Complete the similes"},"problem":{"af":"Voltooi: *so koud soos …, so lig soos ’n …, so sterk soos ’n …*","en":"Complete: *so koud soos …* (as cold as …), *so lig soos ’n …* (as light as a …), *so sterk soos ’n …* (as strong as an …)"},"steps":[{"af":"Dink aan iets wat bekend is vir daardie eienskap: ys is baie koud.","en":"Think of something that is known for that quality: ice is very cold."},{"af":"’n Veer weeg amper niks nie, en ’n os kan swaar vragte trek.","en":"A feather weighs almost nothing, and an ox can pull heavy loads."}],"answer":{"af":"so koud soos ys, so lig soos ’n veer, so sterk soos ’n os","en":"*so koud soos ys, so lig soos ’n veer, so sterk soos ’n os*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken *’n gat in die dag slaap*?","en":"What does *’n gat in die dag slaap* mean?"},"options":[{"af":"’n kort middagslapie vat","en":"take a short afternoon nap"},{"af":"in ’n gat in die grond slaap","en":"sleep in a hole in the ground"},{"af":"die hele nag wakker lê","en":"lie awake all night"},{"af":"tot baie laat slaap","en":"sleep until very late"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die figuurlike betekenis is dat jy tot baie laat slaap, sodat ’n groot stuk van die dag “weg” is. ’n Gat in die grond is die letterlike betekenis, wat nie bedoel word nie.","en":"The figurative meaning is that you sleep until very late, so that a big part of the day is “gone”. A hole in the ground is the literal meaning, which is not what is meant."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Spreekwoord is ’n volledige sin wat ’n les of wysheid leer.","en":"A proverb (*spreekwoord*) is a complete sentence that teaches a lesson or wisdom."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Spreekwoord soos *Eendrag maak mag* is ’n hele sin met ’n les. ’n Idioom is net deel van ’n sin.","en":"True. A proverb such as *Eendrag maak mag* (Together we are strong) is a whole sentence with a lesson. An idiom is only part of a sentence."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Liam stap by die huis in en sê dadelik, sonder om te groet: “Ma, ek het die venster gebreek!” Watter idioom beskryf wat hy gedoen het?","en":"Liam walks into the house and says straight away, without greeting: “Ma, ek het die venster gebreek!” (Mom, I broke the window!) Which idiom describes what he did?"},"options":[{"af":"met die deur in die huis val","en":"met die deur in die huis val"},{"af":"die kat uit die boom kyk","en":"die kat uit die boom kyk"},{"af":"koue voete kry","en":"koue voete kry"},{"af":"’n gat in die dag slaap","en":"’n gat in die dag slaap"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Liam sê dadelik en reguit wat gebeur het, sonder ’n inleiding: hy val met die deur in die huis.","en":"Liam says straight away what happened, without an introduction: *hy val met die deur in die huis*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi die vergelyking: *Die water in die dam was so koud soos ___.*","en":"Complete the simile: *Die water in die dam was so koud soos ___.* (The water in the dam was as cold as ___.)"},"answers":{"af":["ys"],"en":["ys"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vuur","heuning","sand"],"en":["vuur","heuning","sand"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die vaste vergelyking is *so koud soos ys*. Ys is bevrore water en voel baie koud.","en":"The fixed simile is *so koud soos ys* (as cold as ice). Ice is frozen water and feels very cold."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo dra die swaar sak sement heeltemal alleen tot by die bakkie. Watter vaste vergelyking beskryf hom die beste?","en":"Thabo carries the heavy bag of cement all on his own to the bakkie. Which fixed simile describes him best?"},"options":[{"af":"so bang soos ’n muis","en":"so bang soos ’n muis"},{"af":"so stadig soos ’n skilpad","en":"so stadig soos ’n skilpad"},{"af":"so sterk soos ’n os","en":"so sterk soos ’n os"},{"af":"so lig soos ’n veer","en":"so lig soos ’n veer"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Om ’n swaar sak alleen te dra, moet jy baie sterk wees. ’n Os is bekend vir sy krag: *so sterk soos ’n os*.","en":"To carry a heavy bag alone you must be very strong. An ox is known for its strength: *so sterk soos ’n os* (as strong as an ox)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke uitdrukking by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each expression to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"die aap uit die mou laat","en":"die aap uit die mou laat"},"r":{"af":"’n geheim verklap","en":"give away a secret"}},{"l":{"af":"die kat uit die boom kyk","en":"die kat uit die boom kyk"},"r":{"af":"eers afwag en kyk wat gebeur","en":"first wait and see what happens"}},{"l":{"af":"twee vlieë met een klap slaan","en":"twee vlieë met een klap slaan"},"r":{"af":"twee dinge tegelyk regkry","en":"get two things done at once"}},{"l":{"af":"Haastige hond verbrand sy mond.","en":"Haastige hond verbrand sy mond."},"r":{"af":"As jy te gou maak, maak jy foute.","en":"If you rush, you make mistakes."}},{"l":{"af":"Eendrag maak mag.","en":"Eendrag maak mag."},"r":{"af":"Saam is ons sterk.","en":"Together we are strong."}}],"explain":{"af":"Onthou die figuurlike betekenis, nie die letterlike nie: daar is nie regtig ’n aap, ’n kat of vlieë nie. Die laaste twee is spreekwoorde: hele sinne met ’n les.","en":"Remember the figurative meaning, not the literal one: there is not really a monkey, a cat or flies. The last two are proverbs: whole sentences with a lesson."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken die spreekwoord *Stille waters, diepe grond*?","en":"What does the proverb *Stille waters, diepe grond* mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Stil water in ’n dam is altyd baie diep.","en":"Still water in a dam is always very deep."},{"af":"’n Stil mens weet dikwels meer as wat jy dink.","en":"A quiet person often knows more than you think."},{"af":"Jy moet stilbly as grootmense praat.","en":"You must keep quiet when adults are talking."},{"af":"Mense wat stil is, weet niks nie.","en":"People who are quiet know nothing."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die spreekwoord gaan oor mense, nie oor water nie: iemand wat min praat, kan baie slim wees en diep dink. Die eerste opsie is die letterlike betekenis.","en":"The proverb is about people, not water: someone who talks little can be very clever and think deeply. The first option is the literal meaning."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi die spreekwoord: *Oefening baar ___.*","en":"Complete the proverb: *Oefening baar ___.* (Practice makes perfect.)"},"answers":{"af":["kuns"],"en":["kuns"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kennis","krag","vrugte"],"en":["kennis","krag","vrugte"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die spreekwoord is *Oefening baar kuns*: as jy aanhou oefen, word jy goed in iets. ’n Spreekwoord se woorde verander nie.","en":"The proverb is *Oefening baar kuns*: if you keep practising, you become good at something. The words of a proverb do not change."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter sin word *sy hande vol hê* reg gebruik?","en":"In which sentence is *sy hande vol hê* used correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Pa het sy hande vol met die nuwe hondjie wat alles stukkend kou.","en":"Pa het sy hande vol met die nuwe hondjie wat alles stukkend kou."},{"af":"Pa het sy hande vol, want hy het vandag niks om te doen nie.","en":"Pa het sy hande vol, want hy het vandag niks om te doen nie."},{"af":"Pa het sy hande vol gehad toe hy die hele dag in die bed gelê het.","en":"Pa het sy hande vol gehad toe hy die hele dag in die bed gelê het."},{"af":"Pa het sy hande vol, want hy is so bly oor die mooi weer.","en":"Pa het sy hande vol, want hy is so bly oor die mooi weer."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Sy hande vol hê* beteken baie besig wees. ’n Hondjie wat alles stukkend kou, hou Pa baie besig. In die ander sinne het Pa niks te doen nie of is hy net bly.","en":"*Sy hande vol hê* means being very busy. A puppy that chews everything to pieces keeps Dad very busy. In the other sentences Dad has nothing to do or is just happy."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die letterlike betekenis van ’n idioom is altyd die betekenis wat bedoel word.","en":"The literal meaning of an idiom is always the meaning that is intended."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. By ’n idioom word die **figuurlike** betekenis bedoel. Wie *koue voete kry*, se voete is nie regtig koud nie; hy is bang.","en":"False. With an idiom the **figurative** meaning is intended. Someone who *koue voete kry* (gets cold feet) does not really have cold feet; they are scared."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n **vaste vergelyking**?","en":"Which one is a **fixed simile**?"},"options":[{"af":"alle baat help","en":"alle baat help"},{"af":"die kat uit die boom kyk","en":"die kat uit die boom kyk"},{"af":"sy hande vol hê","en":"sy hande vol hê"},{"af":"so wit soos sneeu","en":"so wit soos sneeu"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Vaste vergelyking vergelyk met *so … soos*. *Alle baat help* is ’n spreekwoord, en die ander twee is idiome.","en":"A fixed simile compares with *so … soos* (as … as). *Alle baat help* is a proverb, and the other two are idioms."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Nomsa sit elke week ’n paar rand in haar spaarbussie. Ná ’n jaar het sy genoeg geld om ’n boek te koop. Watter spreekwoord pas?","en":"Nomsa puts a few rand in her money box every week. After a year she has enough money to buy a book. Which proverb fits?"},"options":[{"af":"Stille waters, diepe grond.","en":"Stille waters, diepe grond."},{"af":"Alle baat help.","en":"Alle baat help."},{"af":"Haastige hond verbrand sy mond.","en":"Haastige hond verbrand sy mond."},{"af":"Die appel val nie ver van die boom nie.","en":"Die appel val nie ver van die boom nie."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Elke paar rand is min, maar al die klein bietjies saam word genoeg vir ’n boek: *Alle baat help.*","en":"A few rand is not much, but all the small bits together become enough for a book: *Alle baat help.* (Every little bit helps.)"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Die tas met net een trui in is so lig soos ’n ___.*","en":"Complete: *Die tas met net een trui in is so lig soos ’n ___.* (The bag with only one jersey in it is as light as a ___.)"},"answers":{"af":["veer"],"en":["veer"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["klip","os","muis"],"en":["klip","os","muis"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die vaste vergelyking is *so lig soos ’n veer*, want ’n veer weeg amper niks nie.","en":"The fixed simile is *so lig soos ’n veer* (as light as a feather), because a feather weighs almost nothing."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **figuurlike** betekenis van *koue voete kry*?","en":"What is the **figurative** meaning of *koue voete kry*?"},"options":[{"af":"jou voete word koud in die winter","en":"your feet get cold in winter"},{"af":"vinnig weghardloop omdat dit koud is","en":"run away quickly because it is cold"},{"af":"bang word en iets nie meer wil doen nie","en":"become scared and not want to do something any more"},{"af":"siek word ná ’n koue nag","en":"get sick after a cold night"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Figuurlik beteken dit dat iemand bang word en terugtrek, soos iemand wat nie meer op die verhoog wil sing nie. Koue voete in die winter is die letterlike betekenis.","en":"Figuratively it means someone becomes scared and backs out, like someone who no longer wants to sing on stage. Cold feet in winter is the literal meaning."}}]},{"id":"afr5-t3-beeldspraak-gedigte","title":{"af":"Beeldspraak, klank en gedigte","en":"Figures of speech, sound and poems"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal beeldspraak en klankeffekte in ’n gedig kan raaksien en benoem, die rympatroon kan bepaal en vrae oor die spreker, strofes en stemming van ’n gedig kan beantwoord.","en":"You will be able to spot and name figures of speech and sound effects in a poem, work out the rhyme scheme and answer questions about the speaker, stanzas and mood of a poem."},"summary":{"af":"## Lees eers hierdie gedig\n\n**Storm oor die Hoëveld**\n\n*Strofe 1*\n\n1. Die wolke is grys olifante\n2. wat stamp en stoot aan alle kante.\n3. Boem! brul die donder by die dam,\n4. die weerlig flits so fel soos ’n vlam.\n\n*Strofe 2*\n\n5. Die wind fluit wild deur die bloekomboom,\n6. die reën kom tik-tik-tik op die dak.\n7. Ek kruip in my bed, en ek lê en droom,\n8. so veilig en warm, op my gemak.\n\n## Beeldspraak\n\n**Beeldspraak** is wanneer ’n digter woorde op ’n spesiale manier gebruik om ’n **prentjie in jou kop** te skep.\n\n| Soort | Wat dit doen | Voorbeeld uit die gedig |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Vergelyking** | vergelyk twee dinge met *soos* | *so fel soos ’n vlam* (reël 4) |\n| **Metafoor** | sê iets **is** iets anders, sonder *soos* | *Die wolke is grys olifante* (reël 1) |\n| **Personifikasie** | gee ’n ding of dier menslike eienskappe | *Die wind fluit* (reël 5) |\n\nHoekom olifante? Die stormwolke is groot, swaar en grys, en hulle stoot teen mekaar, net soos ’n trop olifante.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** As *soos* in die beeld is, is dit ’n **vergelyking**, nie ’n metafoor nie. *Die maan is soos ’n silwer bord* = vergelyking. *Die maan is ’n silwer bord* = metafoor.\n\n## Klank in ’n gedig\n\n- **Alliterasie** (allitererende klanke): dieselfde **beginklank** word herhaal: *stamp en stoot* (reël 2).\n- **Klanknabootsing:** ’n woord klink soos die geluid self: *Boem!* en *tik-tik-tik*, maar ook *zoem, tjirp, sis* en *klop-klop*.\n- **Rym:** woorde wat aan die einde dieselfde klink: *dam – vlam*.\n- **Rympatroon:** gee elke nuwe rymklank ’n letter. Strofe 1: *olifante* (a), *kante* (a), *dam* (b), *vlam* (b) = **aabb** (paarrym). Strofe 2: *bloekomboom* (a), *dak* (b), *droom* (a), *gemak* (b) = **abab** (kruisrym).\n- **Ritme:** die maat of klop van die woorde, soos die slag in musiek. Lees die gedig hardop en tik saam.\n- **Herhaling:** ’n woord of klank word herhaal om dit te beklemtoon, soos *tik-tik-tik*.\n\n## Gedig-terme\n\n| Term | Betekenis | In die gedig |\n|---|---|---|\n| titel | die naam van die gedig | *Storm oor die Hoëveld* |\n| digter | die mens wat die gedig geskryf het | iemand wat ’n storm goed ken |\n| versreël | een reël van die gedig | 8 versreëls |\n| strofe | ’n groep versreëls wat ’n blokkie vorm | 2 strofes |\n| spreker | die stem wat in die gedig praat | ’n kind in die bed (*ek*) |\n| stemming | die gevoel van die gedig | eers dreigend, dan rustig |\n\n> **Onthou:** Die **spreker** is nie altyd die **digter** nie. ’n Grootmens kan ’n gedig skryf waarin ’n kind of selfs ’n dier die *ek* is.\n\nDie **stemming** verander in die gedig. Strofe 1 is vol harde geluide (*Boem!, brul, flits*), so dit voel **dreigend** en opwindend. In strofe 2 lê die spreker *veilig en warm* in die bed, en die stemming word **rustig**.\n\n## Vrae oor ’n gedig beantwoord\n\n1. Lees die titel en die hele gedig twee keer, een keer hardop.\n2. Vra jouself: Wie praat? Waaroor gaan dit? Hoe voel die spreker?\n3. Noem by beeldspraak of klank altyd **watter woorde** dit is en **waarom** die digter dit gebruik: *Die metafoor wys hoe groot en swaar die wolke is.*\n4. Haal woorde uit die gedig presies aan, in aanhalingstekens.","en":"## First read this poem\n\n**Storm oor die Hoëveld**\n\n*Strofe 1*\n\n1. Die wolke is grys olifante\n2. wat stamp en stoot aan alle kante.\n3. Boem! brul die donder by die dam,\n4. die weerlig flits so fel soos ’n vlam.\n\n*Strofe 2*\n\n5. Die wind fluit wild deur die bloekomboom,\n6. die reën kom tik-tik-tik op die dak.\n7. Ek kruip in my bed, en ek lê en droom,\n8. so veilig en warm, op my gemak.\n\n*In English:* The clouds are grey elephants that bump and push on all sides. Boom! roars the thunder by the dam; the lightning flashes as fierce as a flame. The wind whistles wildly through the gum tree; the rain comes tap-tap-tap on the roof. I creep into my bed, and I lie and dream, so safe and warm, at ease.\n\n## Figures of speech\n\n**Figures of speech** (*beeldspraak*) are when a poet uses words in a special way to create a **picture in your head**.\n\n| Kind | What it does | Example from the poem |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Simile** (*vergelyking*) | compares two things with *soos* (like/as) | *so fel soos ’n vlam* (line 4) |\n| **Metaphor** (*metafoor*) | says something **is** something else, without *soos* | *Die wolke is grys olifante* (line 1) |\n| **Personification** (*personifikasie*) | gives a thing or animal human qualities | *Die wind fluit* (the wind whistles, line 5) |\n\nWhy elephants? The storm clouds are big, heavy and grey, and they push against each other, just like a herd of elephants.\n\n> **Common mistake:** If *soos* is in the image, it is a **simile**, not a metaphor. *Die maan is soos ’n silwer bord* (The moon is like a silver plate) = simile. *Die maan is ’n silwer bord* (The moon is a silver plate) = metaphor.\n\n## Sound in a poem\n\n- **Alliteration** (*alliterasie*): the same **starting sound** is repeated: *stamp en stoot* (line 2).\n- **Onomatopoeia** (*klanknabootsing*): a word sounds like the noise itself: *Boem!* and *tik-tik-tik*, but also *zoem* (buzz), *tjirp* (chirp), *sis* (hiss) and *klop-klop* (knock-knock).\n- **Rhyme** (*rym*): words that sound the same at the end: *dam – vlam*.\n- **Rhyme scheme** (*rympatroon*): give each new rhyming sound a letter. Stanza 1: *olifante* (a), *kante* (a), *dam* (b), *vlam* (b) = **aabb** (*paarrym*, rhyming couplets). Stanza 2: *bloekomboom* (a), *dak* (b), *droom* (a), *gemak* (b) = **abab** (*kruisrym*, alternate rhyme).\n- **Rhythm** (*ritme*): the beat of the words, like the beat in music. Read the poem aloud and tap along.\n- **Repetition** (*herhaling*): a word or sound is repeated to stress it, like *tik-tik-tik*.\n\n## Poetry terms\n\n| Term | Meaning | In the poem |\n|---|---|---|\n| title (*titel*) | the name of the poem | *Storm oor die Hoëveld* |\n| poet (*digter*) | the person who wrote the poem | someone who knows storms well |\n| line (*versreël*) | one line of the poem | 8 lines |\n| stanza (*strofe*) | a group of lines that forms a block | 2 stanzas |\n| speaker (*spreker*) | the voice that speaks in the poem | a child in bed (*ek*) |\n| mood (*stemming*) | the feeling of the poem | first threatening, then calm |\n\n> **Remember:** The **speaker** is not always the **poet**. An adult can write a poem in which a child or even an animal is the *ek* (I).\n\nThe **mood** changes in the poem. Stanza 1 is full of loud sounds (*Boem!, brul, flits*), so it feels **threatening** and exciting. In stanza 2 the speaker lies *veilig en warm* (safe and warm) in bed, and the mood becomes **calm**.\n\n## Answering questions about a poem\n\n1. Read the title and the whole poem twice, once aloud.\n2. Ask yourself: Who is speaking? What is it about? How does the speaker feel?\n3. For figures of speech or sound, always say **which words** they are and **why** the poet uses them: *The metaphor shows how big and heavy the clouds are.*\n4. Quote words from the poem exactly, in quotation marks."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Beeldspraak","en":"Figures of speech (beeldspraak)"},"def":{"af":"Woorde wat op ’n spesiale manier gebruik word om ’n prentjie in jou kop te skep.","en":"Words used in a special way to create a picture in your head."}},{"term":{"af":"Vergelyking","en":"Simile (vergelyking)"},"def":{"af":"Beeldspraak wat twee dinge met *soos* vergelyk: *so fel soos ’n vlam*.","en":"A figure of speech that compares two things with *soos* (like/as): *so fel soos ’n vlam* (as fierce as a flame)."}},{"term":{"af":"Metafoor","en":"Metaphor (metafoor)"},"def":{"af":"Beeldspraak wat sê iets ís iets anders, sonder *soos*: *Die wolke is grys olifante.*","en":"A figure of speech that says something is something else, without *soos*: *Die wolke is grys olifante.* (The clouds are grey elephants.)"}},{"term":{"af":"Personifikasie","en":"Personification (personifikasie)"},"def":{"af":"Beeldspraak wat ’n ding of dier menslike eienskappe gee: *Die wind fluit.*","en":"A figure of speech that gives a thing or animal human qualities: *Die wind fluit.* (The wind whistles.)"}},{"term":{"af":"Alliterasie","en":"Alliteration (alliterasie)"},"def":{"af":"Die herhaling van dieselfde beginklank in woorde naby mekaar: *stamp en stoot*.","en":"The repetition of the same starting sound in words close together: *stamp en stoot* (bump and push)."}},{"term":{"af":"Klanknabootsing","en":"Onomatopoeia (klanknabootsing)"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat klink soos die geluid wat dit beskryf: *Boem!, tik-tik, zoem*.","en":"A word that sounds like the noise it describes: *Boem!* (boom), *tik-tik* (tap-tap), *zoem* (buzz)."}},{"term":{"af":"Rympatroon","en":"Rhyme scheme (rympatroon)"},"def":{"af":"Die patroon van rymende woorde aan die einde van die reëls, met letters aangedui, soos *aabb* of *abab*.","en":"The pattern of rhyming words at the ends of the lines, shown with letters, such as *aabb* or *abab*."}},{"term":{"af":"Strofe","en":"Stanza (strofe)"},"def":{"af":"’n Groep versreëls in ’n gedig wat saam ’n blokkie vorm.","en":"A group of lines in a poem that together form a block."}},{"term":{"af":"Spreker","en":"Speaker (spreker)"},"def":{"af":"Die stem wat in die gedig praat, dikwels die *ek*; nie altyd die digter self nie.","en":"The voice that speaks in the poem, often the *ek* (I); not always the poet."}},{"term":{"af":"Stemming","en":"Mood (stemming)"},"def":{"af":"Die gevoel wat ’n gedig oordra, soos rustig, dreigend of hartseer.","en":"The feeling a poem gives, such as calm, threatening or sad."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Benoem die beeldspraak","en":"Name the figure of speech"},"problem":{"af":"Watter soort beeldspraak is elk? (a) *Die ou hek kla elke keer as jy hom oopmaak.* (b) *Haar hare is so geel soos mielies.* (c) *Die see is ’n blou kombers.*","en":"Which figure of speech is each? (a) *Die ou hek kla elke keer as jy hom oopmaak.* (The old gate complains every time you open it.) (b) *Haar hare is so geel soos mielies.* (Her hair is as yellow as maize.) (c) *Die see is ’n blou kombers.* (The sea is a blue blanket.)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) ’n Hek kan nie regtig kla nie; kla is iets wat mense doen. Dit is **personifikasie**.","en":"(a) A gate cannot really complain; complaining is something people do. It is **personification**."},{"af":"(b) Twee dinge word met *so … soos* vergelyk. Dit is ’n **vergelyking**.","en":"(b) Two things are compared with *so … soos*. It is a **simile**."},{"af":"(c) Die see **is** ’n kombers, sonder *soos*. Dit is ’n **metafoor**.","en":"(c) The sea **is** a blanket, without *soos*. It is a **metaphor**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) personifikasie (b) vergelyking (c) metafoor","en":"(a) personification (b) simile (c) metaphor"}},{"title":{"af":"Bepaal die rympatroon","en":"Work out the rhyme scheme"},"problem":{"af":"Bepaal die rympatroon van hierdie strofe: *Die maan kom op, so rond en wit, / die sterre knipoog in die nag. / Op die stoep bly Oupa sit / en luister hoe die uile lag.*","en":"Work out the rhyme scheme of this stanza: *Die maan kom op, so rond en wit, / die sterre knipoog in die nag. / Op die stoep bly Oupa sit / en luister hoe die uile lag.* (The moon comes up, so round and white, / the stars wink in the night. / On the stoep Grandpa stays sitting / and listens to the owls laughing.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Kyk na die laaste woord van elke reël: *wit, nag, sit, lag*.","en":"Look at the last word of each line: *wit, nag, sit, lag*."},{"af":"*wit* kry **a**. *nag* rym nie met *wit* nie, so dit kry ’n nuwe letter: **b**.","en":"*wit* gets **a**. *nag* does not rhyme with *wit*, so it gets a new letter: **b**."},{"af":"*sit* rym met *wit*, so dit is weer **a**. *lag* rym met *nag*, so dit is weer **b**.","en":"*sit* rhymes with *wit*, so it is **a** again. *lag* rhymes with *nag*, so it is **b** again."}],"answer":{"af":"abab (kruisrym)","en":"abab (*kruisrym*, alternate rhyme)"}},{"title":{"af":"Vrae oor die gedig","en":"Questions about the poem"},"problem":{"af":"Beantwoord oor *Storm oor die Hoëveld*: (a) Wie is die spreker? (b) Hoe verander die stemming van strofe 1 na strofe 2? (c) Noem een voorbeeld van alliterasie.","en":"Answer about *Storm oor die Hoëveld*: (a) Who is the speaker? (b) How does the mood change from stanza 1 to stanza 2? (c) Give one example of alliteration."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die spreker praat in die ek-vorm en kruip in die bed: ’n **kind** by die huis.","en":"(a) The speaker talks in the *ek* (I) form and creeps into bed: a **child** at home."},{"af":"(b) Strofe 1 is vol harde klanke (*Boem!, brul, flits*), so dit voel **dreigend**. In strofe 2 lê die spreker *veilig en warm*, so die stemming word **rustig**.","en":"(b) Stanza 1 is full of loud sounds (*Boem!, brul, flits*), so it feels **threatening**. In stanza 2 the speaker lies *veilig en warm* (safe and warm), so the mood becomes **calm**."},{"af":"(c) In *stamp en stoot* word die *st*-klank aan die begin van twee woorde herhaal.","en":"(c) In *stamp en stoot* the *st* sound is repeated at the start of two words."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) ’n kind in die bed (b) van dreigend na rustig en veilig (c) *stamp en stoot*","en":"(a) a child in bed (b) from threatening to calm and safe (c) *stamp en stoot*"}},{"title":{"af":"Van vergelyking na metafoor","en":"From simile to metaphor"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf as ’n metafoor: *Die pad is soos ’n lang, grys slang.*","en":"Rewrite as a metaphor: *Die pad is soos ’n lang, grys slang.* (The road is like a long, grey snake.)"},"steps":[{"af":"’n Metafoor sê iets **is** iets anders.","en":"A metaphor says something **is** something else."},{"af":"Haal *soos* uit, sodat die pad die slang **is**.","en":"Take out *soos*, so that the road **is** the snake."}],"answer":{"af":"Die pad is ’n lang, grys slang.","en":"*Die pad is ’n lang, grys slang.*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*Die wolke is grys olifante.* Watter soort beeldspraak is dit?","en":"*Die wolke is grys olifante.* Which figure of speech is this?"},"options":[{"af":"vergelyking","en":"simile (*vergelyking*)"},{"af":"personifikasie","en":"personification (*personifikasie*)"},{"af":"metafoor","en":"metaphor (*metafoor*)"},{"af":"klanknabootsing","en":"onomatopoeia (*klanknabootsing*)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die wolke **is** olifante, sonder *soos*. Dit is ’n metafoor. Met *soos* (*Die wolke is soos olifante*) sou dit ’n vergelyking gewees het.","en":"The clouds **are** elephants, without *soos*. That is a metaphor. With *soos* (*Die wolke is soos olifante*) it would have been a simile."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Groep versreëls wat saam ’n blokkie in ’n gedig vorm, heet ’n ___.","en":"In Afrikaans, a group of lines that together form a block in a poem is called a ___ (stanza)."},"answers":{"af":["strofe"],"en":["strofe","stanza"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["versreël","titel","rympatroon"],"en":["versreël","titel","rympatroon"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n **Strofe** is ’n groep versreëls. *Storm oor die Hoëveld* het twee strofes van vier versreëls elk.","en":"A **strofe** (stanza) is a group of lines. *Storm oor die Hoëveld* has two stanzas of four lines each."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter versreël uit die gedig bevat ’n **vergelyking**?","en":"Which line from the poem contains a **simile**?"},"options":[{"af":"Die wind fluit wild deur die bloekomboom","en":"Die wind fluit wild deur die bloekomboom"},{"af":"die weerlig flits so fel soos ’n vlam","en":"die weerlig flits so fel soos ’n vlam"},{"af":"Boem! brul die donder by die dam","en":"Boem! brul die donder by die dam"},{"af":"Die wolke is grys olifante","en":"Die wolke is grys olifante"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*so fel soos ’n vlam* vergelyk die weerlig met ’n vlam deur *so … soos* te gebruik. Reël 1 is ’n metafoor en reël 5 bevat personifikasie.","en":"*so fel soos ’n vlam* compares the lightning to a flame using *so … soos* (as … as). Line 1 is a metaphor and line 5 contains personification."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In die gedig is *Boem!* en *tik-tik-tik* voorbeelde van klanknabootsing.","en":"In the poem, *Boem!* and *tik-tik-tik* are examples of onomatopoeia (*klanknabootsing*)."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Albei woorde klink soos die geluide self: die donder wat slaan en die reën op die dak.","en":"True. Both words sound like the noises themselves: the thunder crashing and the rain on the roof."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die rympatroon van strofe 1?","en":"What is the rhyme scheme of stanza 1?"},"options":[{"af":"aabb","en":"aabb"},{"af":"abab","en":"abab"},{"af":"abba","en":"abba"},{"af":"abcb","en":"abcb"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*olifante* en *kante* rym (a, a), en *dam* en *vlam* rym (b, b). Twee rymende pare na mekaar is **aabb** (paarrym).","en":"*olifante* and *kante* rhyme (a, a), and *dam* and *vlam* rhyme (b, b). Two rhyming pairs one after the other give **aabb** (*paarrym*, rhyming couplets)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin bevat **personifikasie**?","en":"Which sentence contains **personification**?"},"options":[{"af":"Die bome is so hoog soos torings.","en":"Die bome is so hoog soos torings."},{"af":"Die bome is groen reuse.","en":"Die bome is groen reuse."},{"af":"Die bome langs die pad is baie oud.","en":"Die bome langs die pad is baie oud."},{"af":"Die bome dans in die wind.","en":"Die bome dans in die wind."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Bome kan nie regtig dans nie; dans is iets wat mense doen. *So hoog soos torings* is ’n vergelyking, *groen reuse* is ’n metafoor, en *Die bome langs die pad is baie oud* het geen beeldspraak nie.","en":"Trees cannot really dance; dancing is something people do. *so hoog soos torings* (as tall as towers) is a simile, *groen reuse* (green giants) is a metaphor, and *Die bome langs die pad is baie oud* (The trees along the road are very old) has no figure of speech."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke gedig-term by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each poetry term to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"titel","en":"title (*titel*)"},"r":{"af":"die naam van die gedig","en":"the name of the poem"}},{"l":{"af":"digter","en":"poet (*digter*)"},"r":{"af":"die mens wat die gedig skryf","en":"the person who writes the poem"}},{"l":{"af":"versreël","en":"line (*versreël*)"},"r":{"af":"een reël in ’n gedig","en":"one line in a poem"}},{"l":{"af":"spreker","en":"speaker (*spreker*)"},"r":{"af":"die stem wat in die gedig praat","en":"the voice that speaks in the poem"}},{"l":{"af":"stemming","en":"mood (*stemming*)"},"r":{"af":"die gevoel van die gedig","en":"the feeling of the poem"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hierdie terme help jou om oor enige gedig te praat. Onthou veral dat die spreker en die digter nie altyd dieselfde persoon is nie.","en":"These terms help you talk about any poem. Remember especially that the speaker and the poet are not always the same person."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In *Sewe sterk seuns sing saam* word die *s*-klank aan die begin van woorde herhaal. Dit heet ___.","en":"In *Sewe sterk seuns sing saam* (Seven strong boys sing together) the *s* sound is repeated at the start of words. In Afrikaans this is called ___ (alliteration)."},"answers":{"af":["alliterasie"],"en":["alliterasie","alliteration"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["rym","personifikasie","klanknabootsing"],"en":["rym","personifikasie","klanknabootsing"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die herhaling van dieselfde **beginklank** heet **alliterasie**. Rym gaan oor klanke aan die **einde** van woorde.","en":"The repetition of the same **starting sound** is **alliterasie** (alliteration). Rhyme is about sounds at the **end** of words."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die stemming in die laaste strofe van die gedig?","en":"What is the mood in the last stanza of the poem?"},"options":[{"af":"kwaad en ongeduldig","en":"angry and impatient"},{"af":"bang en paniekerig","en":"scared and panicky"},{"af":"hartseer en eensaam","en":"sad and lonely"},{"af":"veilig en rustig","en":"safe and calm"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die spreker lê *veilig en warm, op my gemak* in die bed en droom. Al storm dit buite, voel die spreker rustig en veilig.","en":"The speaker lies *veilig en warm, op my gemak* (safe and warm, at ease) in bed and dreams. Even though there is a storm outside, the speaker feels calm and safe."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die spreker in ’n gedig is altyd die digter self.","en":"The speaker in a poem is always the poet."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die digter kan ’n gedig skryf waarin iemand anders, soos ’n kind of ’n dier, die *ek* is.","en":"False. The poet can write a poem in which someone else, such as a child or an animal, is the *ek* (I)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter twee woorde rym in strofe 2?","en":"Which two words rhyme in stanza 2?"},"options":[{"af":"bloekomboom – droom","en":"bloekomboom – droom"},{"af":"dak – droom","en":"dak – droom"},{"af":"reën – bed","en":"reën – bed"},{"af":"wind – wild","en":"wind – wild"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*bloekomboom* en *droom* eindig albei op die klank *-oom*, en *dak* rym met *gemak*. *wind* en *wild* begin met dieselfde klank (alliterasie), maar hulle rym nie.","en":"*bloekomboom* and *droom* both end in the sound *-oom*, and *dak* rhymes with *gemak*. *wind* and *wild* start with the same sound (alliteration), but they do not rhyme."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die woord ___ in *Die son glimlag vir die blomme* maak die sin ’n personifikasie.","en":"The word ___ in *Die son glimlag vir die blomme* (The sun smiles at the flowers) makes the sentence a personification."},"answers":{"af":["glimlag"],"en":["glimlag"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["son","blomme","vir"],"en":["son","blomme","vir"]}},"explain":{"af":"Net mense kan glimlag. Omdat die son iets menslik doen, is dit personifikasie.","en":"Only people can smile (*glimlag*). Because the sun does something human, it is personification."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin bevat **klanknabootsing**?","en":"Which sentence contains **onomatopoeia**?"},"options":[{"af":"Die by vlieg vinnig na die blom.","en":"Die by vlieg vinnig na die blom."},{"af":"Die by zoem om die blom.","en":"Die by zoem om die blom."},{"af":"Die by is so geel soos botter.","en":"Die by is so geel soos botter."},{"af":"Die besige by werk die hele dag.","en":"Die besige by werk die hele dag."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*zoem* klink soos die geluid wat ’n by maak. Die ander sinne beskryf wat die by doen of hoe dit lyk, maar boots nie ’n klank na nie.","en":"*zoem* (buzz) sounds like the noise a bee makes. The other sentences describe what the bee does or looks like, but do not imitate a sound."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is **ritme** in ’n gedig?","en":"What is **rhythm** (*ritme*) in a poem?"},"options":[{"af":"woorde aan die einde van reëls wat dieselfde klink","en":"words at the ends of lines that sound the same"},{"af":"die gevoel wat die gedig by jou wek","en":"the feeling the poem gives you"},{"af":"die maat of klop van die woorde, soos die slag in musiek","en":"the beat of the words, like the beat in music"},{"af":"die naam wat bo-aan die gedig staan","en":"the name at the top of the poem"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Ritme is die klop wat jy hoor as jy die gedig hardop lees. Woorde wat aan die einde dieselfde klink, is rym; die gevoel is die stemming; die naam is die titel.","en":"Rhythm is the beat you hear when you read the poem aloud. Words that sound the same at the end are rhyme; the feeling is the mood; the name is the title."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Tekste lees en skryf","en":"Reading and writing texts"},"topics":[{"id":"afr5-t4-verhale-volksverhale","title":{"af":"Verhale, volksverhale en fabels","en":"Stories, folk tales and fables"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die elemente van ’n verhaal (karakters, tyd en ruimte, intrige en verteller) kan uitken en ’n volksverhaal of fabel en sy les kan verstaan en bespreek.","en":"You will be able to identify the elements of a story (characters, time and setting, plot and narrator) and understand and discuss a folk tale or fable and its lesson."},"summary":{"af":"## Lees eers hierdie fabel\n\n**Spikkels en Mossie**\n\nEen warm somersoggend in die Karoo stap Spikkels die tarentaal na die dam. Sy kyk na haar gespikkelde vere in die water en sê hardop: “Ek is die mooiste voël in die hele veld!”\n\n’n Klein bruin mossie sit op ’n klip. “Môre, Spikkels,” tjirp hy vriendelik.\n\nSpikkels lag. “Jy is so vaal soos stof. Moenie met my praat nie!”\n\nSkielik sien Mossie iets in die lang gras beweeg. Dit is ’n rooikat wat stil-stil nader sluip. “Spikkels, pasop!” roep hy. Maar Spikkels kyk net na haarself in die water.\n\nMossie vlieg reg voor haar oë verby en skree so hard hy kan. Op die nippertjie sien Spikkels die rooikat. Sy fladder op tot bo in die doringboom, net toe die rooikat spring. Die rooikat land met ’n plons in die modder.\n\nDaardie aand sê Spikkels skaam: “Dankie, Mossie. Jou vere is dalk vaal, maar jou hart is goud.” Van toe af is hulle groot vriende.\n\n*Les: Moenie iemand op sy voorkoms oordeel nie.*\n\n## Die elemente van ’n verhaal\n\n- **Karakters:** die mense of diere in die verhaal. Die **hoofkarakter** is die belangrikste: Spikkels. Die **byfigure** speel ’n kleiner rol: Mossie en die rooikat.\n- **Tyd:** wanneer die verhaal afspeel: ’n warm somersoggend tot die aand.\n- **Ruimte:** waar die verhaal afspeel: by ’n dam in die Karoo. Tyd en ruimte saam is die **agtergrond**.\n- **Verteller:** wie die verhaal vertel. Hier is dit ’n **derdepersoonsverteller** (*sy, hy*). As ’n karakter self vertel (*ek, ons*), is dit ’n **eerstepersoonsverteller**.\n\n## Die intrige\n\nDie **intrige** is die gebeure van die verhaal in volgorde:\n\n| Deel | Wat gebeur? | In die fabel |\n|---|---|---|\n| Begin | Ons leer die karakters en agtergrond ken. | Spikkels bewonder haar vere by die dam. |\n| Konflik | ’n Probleem ontstaan. | Spikkels spot met Mossie en luister nie na sy waarskuwing nie, terwyl die rooikat nader sluip. |\n| Klimaks | Die spanning is op sy hoogste. | Die rooikat spring, en Spikkels vlieg op die nippertjie weg. |\n| Oplossing | Die probleem word opgelos. | Spikkels bedank Mossie, en hulle word vriende. |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die klimaks is nie die einde nie. Dit is die **spannendste oomblik**; die oplossing kom daarna.\n\n## Volksverhale en fabels\n\n’n **Volksverhaal** is ’n ou storie wat mense oor baie jare aan mekaar oorvertel het. Niemand weet meer wie dit eerste vertel het nie. Bekende Suid-Afrikaanse volksverhale is die stories oor **Jakkals en Wolf**, waarin die slim Jakkals die sterk Wolf uitoorlê.\n\n’n **Fabel** is ’n kort verhaal waarin:\n- **diere** praat, dink en soos **mense** optree;\n- elke dier gewoonlik een duidelike **eienskap** het (Spikkels is ydel, Mossie is dapper en goedhartig);\n- daar aan die einde ’n **les** of **moraal** is.\n\n## Feit en fiksie\n\n’n **Feit** is waar en kan bewys word. **Fiksie** is ’n verhaal wat iemand uitgedink het.\n- Feite: *Rooikatte jag voëls. Tarentale slaap snags in bome.*\n- Fiksie: *’n Mossie praat met ’n tarentaal.*\n\n> **Onthou:** ’n Fabel is fiksie, maar dit leer ’n ware les vir die lewe.","en":"## First read this fable\n\n**Spikkels en Mossie**\n\nEen warm somersoggend in die Karoo stap Spikkels die tarentaal na die dam. Sy kyk na haar gespikkelde vere in die water en sê hardop: “Ek is die mooiste voël in die hele veld!”\n\n’n Klein bruin mossie sit op ’n klip. “Môre, Spikkels,” tjirp hy vriendelik.\n\nSpikkels lag. “Jy is so vaal soos stof. Moenie met my praat nie!”\n\nSkielik sien Mossie iets in die lang gras beweeg. Dit is ’n rooikat wat stil-stil nader sluip. “Spikkels, pasop!” roep hy. Maar Spikkels kyk net na haarself in die water.\n\nMossie vlieg reg voor haar oë verby en skree so hard hy kan. Op die nippertjie sien Spikkels die rooikat. Sy fladder op tot bo in die doringboom, net toe die rooikat spring. Die rooikat land met ’n plons in die modder.\n\nDaardie aand sê Spikkels skaam: “Dankie, Mossie. Jou vere is dalk vaal, maar jou hart is goud.” Van toe af is hulle groot vriende.\n\n*Les: Moenie iemand op sy voorkoms oordeel nie.*\n\n*In English:* One warm summer morning in the Karoo, Spikkels the guineafowl walks to the dam. She looks at her spotted feathers in the water and says out loud: “I am the most beautiful bird in the whole veld!” A small brown sparrow sits on a rock. “Morning, Spikkels,” he chirps in a friendly way. Spikkels laughs. “You are as dull as dust. Don’t talk to me!” Suddenly Sparrow sees something moving in the long grass. It is a caracal sneaking closer very quietly. “Spikkels, watch out!” he calls. But Spikkels only looks at herself in the water. Sparrow flies right past her eyes and screams as loud as he can. Just in time Spikkels sees the caracal. She flutters up to the top of the thorn tree, just as the caracal jumps. The caracal lands with a splash in the mud. That evening Spikkels says shyly: “Thank you, Sparrow. Your feathers may be dull, but your heart is gold.” From then on they are great friends. *Lesson: Don’t judge someone by their looks.*\n\n## The elements of a story\n\n- **Characters** (*karakters*): the people or animals in the story. The **main character** (*hoofkarakter*) is the most important: Spikkels. The **minor characters** (*byfigure*) play a smaller role: Mossie and the caracal.\n- **Time** (*tyd*): when the story happens: a warm summer morning until the evening.\n- **Setting** (*ruimte*): where the story happens: at a dam in the Karoo. Time and setting together are the **background** (*agtergrond*).\n- **Narrator** (*verteller*): who tells the story. Here it is a **third-person narrator** (*sy, hy*: she, he). If a character tells the story (*ek, ons*: I, we), it is a **first-person narrator**.\n\n## The plot\n\nThe **plot** (*intrige*) is the events of the story in order:\n\n| Part | What happens? | In the fable |\n|---|---|---|\n| Beginning (*begin*) | We get to know the characters and background. | Spikkels admires her feathers at the dam. |\n| Conflict (*konflik*) | A problem arises. | Spikkels mocks Mossie and ignores his warning while the caracal sneaks closer. |\n| Climax (*klimaks*) | The tension is at its highest. | The caracal jumps, and Spikkels flies away just in time. |\n| Resolution (*oplossing*) | The problem is solved. | Spikkels thanks Mossie, and they become friends. |\n\n> **Common mistake:** The climax is not the end. It is the **most exciting moment**; the resolution comes after it.\n\n## Folk tales and fables\n\nA **folk tale** (*volksverhaal*) is an old story that people have retold to each other over many years. Nobody knows any more who told it first. Well-known South African folk tales are the stories about **Jakkals and Wolf**, in which clever Jackal outwits strong Wolf.\n\nA **fable** (*fabel*) is a short story in which:\n- **animals** talk, think and behave like **people**;\n- each animal usually has one clear **quality** (Spikkels is vain, Mossie is brave and kind);\n- there is a **lesson** or **moral** (*moraal*) at the end.\n\n## Fact and fiction\n\nA **fact** (*feit*) is true and can be proved. **Fiction** (*fiksie*) is a story that someone made up.\n- Facts: *Rooikatte jag voëls.* (Caracals hunt birds.) *Tarentale slaap snags in bome.* (Guineafowl sleep in trees at night.)\n- Fiction: *’n Mossie praat met ’n tarentaal.* (A sparrow talks to a guineafowl.)\n\n> **Remember:** A fable is fiction, but it teaches a true lesson for life."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Hoofkarakter","en":"Main character (hoofkarakter)"},"def":{"af":"Die belangrikste karakter, om wie die verhaal draai.","en":"The most important character, whom the story is about."}},{"term":{"af":"Byfiguur","en":"Minor character (byfiguur)"},"def":{"af":"’n Karakter wat ’n kleiner rol in die verhaal speel as die hoofkarakter.","en":"A character who plays a smaller role in the story than the main character."}},{"term":{"af":"Ruimte","en":"Setting (ruimte)"},"def":{"af":"Die plek waar die verhaal afspeel, soos ’n dam in die Karoo.","en":"The place where the story happens, such as a dam in the Karoo."}},{"term":{"af":"Intrige","en":"Plot (intrige)"},"def":{"af":"Die gebeure van die verhaal in volgorde: begin, konflik, klimaks en oplossing.","en":"The events of the story in order: beginning, conflict, climax and resolution."}},{"term":{"af":"Klimaks","en":"Climax (klimaks)"},"def":{"af":"Die spannendste oomblik in die verhaal, net voordat die probleem opgelos word.","en":"The most exciting moment in the story, just before the problem is solved."}},{"term":{"af":"Verteller","en":"Narrator (verteller)"},"def":{"af":"Die stem wat die verhaal vertel, in die eerste persoon (*ek*) of die derde persoon (*hy, sy*).","en":"The voice that tells the story, in the first person (*ek*, I) or the third person (*hy, sy*: he, she)."}},{"term":{"af":"Volksverhaal","en":"Folk tale (volksverhaal)"},"def":{"af":"’n Ou storie wat mense oor baie jare aan mekaar oorvertel het.","en":"An old story that people have retold to each other over many years."}},{"term":{"af":"Fabel","en":"Fable (fabel)"},"def":{"af":"’n Kort verhaal waarin diere soos mense praat en optree, met ’n les aan die einde.","en":"A short story in which animals talk and act like people, with a lesson at the end."}},{"term":{"af":"Moraal","en":"Moral (moraal)"},"def":{"af":"Die les wat ’n fabel of verhaal leer, soos *Moenie iemand op sy voorkoms oordeel nie.*","en":"The lesson a fable or story teaches, such as *Moenie iemand op sy voorkoms oordeel nie.* (Don’t judge someone by their looks.)"}},{"term":{"af":"Fiksie","en":"Fiction (fiksie)"},"def":{"af":"’n Verhaal wat iemand uitgedink het en wat nie regtig gebeur het nie.","en":"A story that someone made up and that did not really happen."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Karakters en agtergrond","en":"Characters and background"},"problem":{"af":"Noem die hoofkarakter, die byfigure, die tyd en die ruimte in *Spikkels en Mossie*.","en":"Name the main character, the minor characters, the time and the setting in *Spikkels en Mossie*."},"steps":[{"af":"Die verhaal draai om Spikkels en wat sy leer: sy is die **hoofkarakter**.","en":"The story is about Spikkels and what she learns: she is the **main character**."},{"af":"Mossie en die rooikat speel ’n kleiner rol: hulle is **byfigure**.","en":"Mossie and the caracal play a smaller role: they are **minor characters**."},{"af":"**Tyd:** ’n warm somersoggend tot die aand. **Ruimte:** by ’n dam in die Karoo.","en":"**Time:** a warm summer morning until the evening. **Setting:** at a dam in the Karoo."}],"answer":{"af":"Hoofkarakter: Spikkels. Byfigure: Mossie en die rooikat. Tyd: ’n somersoggend tot die aand. Ruimte: by ’n dam in die Karoo.","en":"Main character: Spikkels. Minor characters: Mossie and the caracal. Time: a summer morning until the evening. Setting: at a dam in the Karoo."}},{"title":{"af":"Die intrige in volgorde","en":"The plot in order"},"problem":{"af":"Rangskik die gebeure en sê watter deel van die intrige elkeen is: A *Spikkels en Mossie word vriende.* B *Spikkels bewonder haar vere.* C *Die rooikat spring en Spikkels vlieg weg.* D *Spikkels spot met Mossie en ignoreer sy waarskuwing.*","en":"Put the events in order and say which part of the plot each is: A *Spikkels en Mossie word vriende.* (become friends) B *Spikkels bewonder haar vere.* (admires her feathers) C *Die rooikat spring en Spikkels vlieg weg.* (the caracal jumps and Spikkels flies away) D *Spikkels spot met Mossie en ignoreer sy waarskuwing.* (mocks Mossie and ignores his warning)"},"steps":[{"af":"Die verhaal begin by die dam waar Spikkels na haarself kyk: B is die **begin**.","en":"The story begins at the dam where Spikkels looks at herself: B is the **beginning**."},{"af":"Die probleem ontstaan toe sy spot en nie luister nie: D is die **konflik**.","en":"The problem arises when she mocks and doesn’t listen: D is the **conflict**."},{"af":"Die spannendste oomblik is die rooikat se sprong: C is die **klimaks**.","en":"The most exciting moment is the caracal’s jump: C is the **climax**."},{"af":"Aan die einde word alles reggemaak: A is die **oplossing**.","en":"At the end everything is put right: A is the **resolution**."}],"answer":{"af":"B (begin), D (konflik), C (klimaks), A (oplossing)","en":"B (beginning), D (conflict), C (climax), A (resolution)"}},{"title":{"af":"Feit of fiksie?","en":"Fact or fiction?"},"problem":{"af":"Is elke stelling feit of fiksie? (a) *Rooikatte jag voëls.* (b) *Spikkels sê: “Dankie, Mossie.”* (c) *Tarentale het gespikkelde vere.* (d) *’n Mossie en ’n tarentaal word groot vriende.*","en":"Is each statement fact or fiction? (a) *Rooikatte jag voëls.* (Caracals hunt birds.) (b) *Spikkels sê: “Dankie, Mossie.”* (Spikkels says: “Thank you, Sparrow.”) (c) *Tarentale het gespikkelde vere.* (Guineafowl have spotted feathers.) (d) *’n Mossie en ’n tarentaal word groot vriende.* (A sparrow and a guineafowl become great friends.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Vra by elke stelling: Is dit regtig so in die natuur, en kan ek dit bewys?","en":"Ask for each statement: Is it really like this in nature, and can I prove it?"},{"af":"(a) en (c) is waar oor regte diere: **feite**.","en":"(a) and (c) are true about real animals: **facts**."},{"af":"(b) en (d) gebeur net in die storie, want diere praat nie en word nie soos mense vriende nie: **fiksie**.","en":"(b) and (d) only happen in the story, because animals do not talk or become friends like people: **fiction**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) feit (b) fiksie (c) feit (d) fiksie","en":"(a) fact (b) fiction (c) fact (d) fiction"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wie is die **hoofkarakter** in *Spikkels en Mossie*?","en":"Who is the **main character** in *Spikkels en Mossie*?"},"options":[{"af":"Spikkels die tarentaal","en":"Spikkels the guineafowl"},{"af":"die klein bruin mossie","en":"the small brown sparrow"},{"af":"die rooikat in die gras","en":"the caracal in the grass"},{"af":"die verteller van die storie","en":"the narrator of the story"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die verhaal draai om Spikkels: sy maak die fout, sy is in gevaar en sy leer die les. Mossie is belangrik, maar hy is ’n byfiguur.","en":"The story is about Spikkels: she makes the mistake, she is in danger and she learns the lesson. Mossie is important, but he is a minor character."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*Spikkels en Mossie* word deur ’n eerstepersoonsverteller (*ek*) vertel.","en":"*Spikkels en Mossie* is told by a first-person narrator (*ek*, I)."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die verteller sê *sy* en *hy*, nie *ek* nie. Dit is ’n derdepersoonsverteller wat van buite af vertel.","en":"False. The narrator says *sy* (she) and *hy* (he), not *ek* (I). It is a third-person narrator who tells the story from the outside."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **klimaks** van die fabel?","en":"What is the **climax** of the fable?"},"options":[{"af":"Spikkels lag vir Mossie en sê hy is vaal.","en":"Spikkels laughs at Mossie and says he is dull."},{"af":"Spikkels bedank Mossie, en hulle word vriende.","en":"Spikkels thanks Mossie, and they become friends."},{"af":"Spikkels stap op ’n somersoggend na die dam.","en":"Spikkels walks to the dam on a summer morning."},{"af":"Die rooikat spring, en Spikkels vlieg op die nippertjie weg.","en":"The caracal jumps, and Spikkels flies away just in time."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die klimaks is die spannendste oomblik: sal die rooikat Spikkels vang? Die bedanking is die oplossing, en die stap na die dam is die begin.","en":"The climax is the most exciting moment: will the caracal catch Spikkels? The thank-you is the resolution, and the walk to the dam is the beginning."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die les aan die einde van ’n fabel heet die ___.","en":"In Afrikaans, the lesson at the end of a fable is called the ___ (moral)."},"answers":{"af":["moraal"],"en":["moraal","moral"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["klimaks","intrige","ruimte"],"en":["klimaks","intrige","ruimte"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die **moraal** is die les van die fabel. Hier is dit: *Moenie iemand op sy voorkoms oordeel nie.*","en":"The **moraal** (moral) is the lesson of the fable. Here it is: *Moenie iemand op sy voorkoms oordeel nie.* (Don’t judge someone by their looks.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **konflik** in die verhaal?","en":"What is the **conflict** in the story?"},"options":[{"af":"Mossie en Spikkels word aan die einde goeie vriende.","en":"Mossie and Spikkels become good friends at the end."},{"af":"Spikkels luister nie na Mossie se waarskuwing nie terwyl ’n rooikat nader sluip.","en":"Spikkels ignores Mossie’s warning while a caracal sneaks closer."},{"af":"Dit is ’n warm somersoggend in die Karoo.","en":"It is a warm summer morning in the Karoo."},{"af":"Mossie sit op ’n klip naby die dam.","en":"Mossie sits on a rock near the dam."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die konflik is die probleem: Spikkels is ydel en luister nie, en ’n gevaarlike rooikat kom nader. Die ander opsies is die oplossing of deel van die agtergrond.","en":"The conflict is the problem: Spikkels is vain and does not listen, and a dangerous caracal is coming closer. The other options are the resolution or part of the background."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke verhaalelement by die voorbeeld uit die fabel.","en":"Match each story element to the example from the fable."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"byfiguur","en":"minor character (*byfiguur*)"},"r":{"af":"die rooikat","en":"the caracal"}},{"l":{"af":"ruimte","en":"setting (*ruimte*)"},"r":{"af":"by ’n dam in die Karoo","en":"at a dam in the Karoo"}},{"l":{"af":"begin","en":"beginning (*begin*)"},"r":{"af":"Spikkels bewonder haar vere in die water.","en":"Spikkels admires her feathers in the water."}},{"l":{"af":"oplossing","en":"resolution (*oplossing*)"},"r":{"af":"Spikkels en Mossie word vriende.","en":"Spikkels and Mossie become friends."}}],"explain":{"af":"Die rooikat speel ’n klein rol (byfiguur), die dam in die Karoo is die plek (ruimte), die verhaal begin by die dam, en die vriendskap aan die einde is die oplossing.","en":"The caracal plays a small role (minor character), the dam in the Karoo is the place (setting), the story begins at the dam, and the friendship at the end is the resolution."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoekom sê Spikkels aan die einde: *Jou hart is goud*?","en":"Why does Spikkels say at the end: *Jou hart is goud* (Your heart is gold)?"},"options":[{"af":"Mossie het ’n goue kleur op sy bors.","en":"Mossie has a golden colour on his chest."},{"af":"Mossie het vir haar ’n stukkie goud gegee.","en":"Mossie gave her a piece of gold."},{"af":"Sy besef dat Mossie ’n goeie en dapper vriend is.","en":"She realises that Mossie is a good and brave friend."},{"af":"Sy wil hê dat Mossie moet weggaan.","en":"She wants Mossie to go away."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Jou hart is goud* is ’n metafoor: Mossie is goedhartig, want hy het haar gered al was sy lelik met hom. Hy het nie regtig goud nie.","en":"*Jou hart is goud* is a metaphor: Mossie is kind-hearted, because he saved her even though she was nasty to him. He does not really have gold."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Karakters wat ’n kleiner rol as die hoofkarakter speel, heet ___.","en":"In Afrikaans, characters who play a smaller role than the main character are called ___ (minor characters)."},"answers":{"af":["byfigure","byfiguur"],"en":["byfigure","byfiguur","minor characters"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["hooffigure","vertellers","skrywers"],"en":["hooffigure","vertellers","skrywers"]}},"explain":{"af":"**Byfigure** help die verhaal aan, maar die verhaal draai nie om hulle nie. In die fabel is Mossie en die rooikat byfigure.","en":"**Byfigure** (minor characters) help the story along, but the story is not about them. In the fable Mossie and the caracal are minor characters."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter les leer die fabel?","en":"What lesson does the fable teach?"},"options":[{"af":"Moenie iemand op sy voorkoms oordeel nie.","en":"Moenie iemand op sy voorkoms oordeel nie."},{"af":"Moenie naby ’n dam gaan speel nie.","en":"Moenie naby ’n dam gaan speel nie."},{"af":"Rooikatte is gevaarlik vir alle voëls.","en":"Rooikatte is gevaarlik vir alle voëls."},{"af":"Wie eerste kom, kry die beste plek.","en":"Wie eerste kom, kry die beste plek."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Spikkels het gedink Mossie is minder werd omdat hy vaal is, maar hy het haar lewe gered. Die les gaan oor hoe ons ander behandel, nie oor damme of rooikatte nie.","en":"Spikkels thought Mossie was worth less because he is dull, but he saved her life. The lesson is about how we treat others, not about dams or caracals."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Dat die diere in die verhaal met mekaar praat, wys dat dit fiksie is.","en":"The fact that the animals in the story talk to each other shows that it is fiction."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Diere kan nie regtig praat nie, so die verhaal is uitgedink. Dit is fiksie, al leer dit ’n ware les.","en":"True. Animals cannot really talk, so the story is made up. It is fiction, even though it teaches a true lesson."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat maak *Spikkels en Mossie* ’n **fabel**?","en":"What makes *Spikkels en Mossie* a **fable**?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit het regtig so in die Karoo gebeur.","en":"It really happened like this in the Karoo."},{"af":"Dit is ’n lang storie met baie hoofstukke.","en":"It is a long story with many chapters."},{"af":"Diere praat en tree soos mense op, en daar is ’n les.","en":"Animals talk and act like people, and there is a lesson."},{"af":"Dit is ’n gedig met rym en ritme.","en":"It is a poem with rhyme and rhythm."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Fabel is ’n kort, uitgedinkte verhaal met diere wat soos mense optree en ’n les aan die einde. Dit het nie regtig gebeur nie.","en":"A fable is a short, made-up story with animals that act like people and a lesson at the end. It did not really happen."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die verhaal begin op ’n warm ___ in die Karoo.","en":"Use the Afrikaans word from the fable: *Die verhaal begin op ’n warm ___ in die Karoo.* (The story begins on a warm summer morning in the Karoo.)"},"answers":{"af":["somersoggend"],"en":["somersoggend"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["winteraand","lentemiddag","herfsoggend"],"en":["winteraand","lentemiddag","herfsoggend"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die eerste sin sê: *Een warm somersoggend in die Karoo …* Dit gee die **tyd** van die verhaal.","en":"The first sentence says: *Een warm somersoggend in die Karoo …* (One warm summer morning in the Karoo …) This gives the **time** of the story."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is ’n **feit**?","en":"Which statement is a **fact**?"},"options":[{"af":"Mossie tjirp: “Môre, Spikkels.”","en":"Sparrow chirps: “Morning, Spikkels.”"},{"af":"Spikkels is die mooiste voël in die veld.","en":"Spikkels is the most beautiful bird in the veld."},{"af":"Die tarentaal en die mossie word vriende.","en":"The guineafowl and the sparrow become friends."},{"af":"Tarentale slaap snags in bome.","en":"Guineafowl sleep in trees at night."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Dat tarentale snags in bome slaap, is waar en kan bewys word. ’n Praatende mossie en die vriendskap is fiksie, en *die mooiste voël* is ’n mening.","en":"That guineafowl sleep in trees at night is true and can be proved. A talking sparrow and the friendship are fiction, and *the most beautiful bird* is an opinion."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is ’n **volksverhaal**?","en":"What is a **folk tale**?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Ware berig wat in die koerant verskyn het","en":"A true report that appeared in the newspaper"},{"af":"’n Ou storie wat mense oor baie jare aan mekaar oorvertel het","en":"An old story that people have retold to each other over many years"},{"af":"’n Gedig met strofes, rym en ritme","en":"A poem with stanzas, rhyme and rhythm"},{"af":"’n Storie wat ’n skrywer verlede jaar uitgedink het","en":"A story that a writer made up last year"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Volksverhaal is oud en is van mond tot mond oorvertel, soos die stories oor Jakkals en Wolf. Niemand weet meer wie dit eerste vertel het nie.","en":"A folk tale is old and has been passed on by word of mouth, like the stories about Jakkals and Wolf. Nobody knows any more who told it first."}}]},{"id":"afr5-t4-visuele-tekste","title":{"af":"Visuele tekste","en":"Visual texts"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal strokiesprente, advertensies, plakkate en tabelle kan lees, kan verduidelik hoe prente en woorde saamwerk en vrae oor ’n beskryfde visuele teks kan beantwoord.","en":"You will be able to read comic strips, advertisements, posters and tables, explain how pictures and words work together and answer questions about a described visual text."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is ’n visuele teks?\n\n’n **Visuele teks** gebruik **prente en woorde saam** om ’n boodskap oor te dra. Die prent trek jou aandag en wys gevoelens; die woorde gee die besonderhede. In ’n toets word die prent dikwels in woorde beskryf. Lees die beskrywing dan net so noukeurig as wat jy na ’n prent sou kyk.\n\nLet altyd op:\n- **kleur**: helder rooi en geel trek aandag;\n- **grootte van die letters**: die belangrikste woorde is die grootste;\n- **gesigsuitdrukkings en lyftaal**: dit wys hoe karakters voel.\n\n## Strokiesprente\n\n’n **Strokiesprent** vertel ’n storie in ’n reeks **panele** (blokkies) wat jy van links na regs lees.\n- ’n **Spraakborrel** met ’n puntjie na die karakter wys wat hy of sy **sê**.\n- ’n **Dinkborrel** (’n wolkie met klein sirkeltjies) wys wat die karakter **dink**.\n- **Klanknabootsing** in groot letters, soos *KRAAK!* of *BOEM!*, laat jou die geluid “hoor”.\n\n**Voorbeeld (beskryf):**\n- *Paneel 1:* Sipho staan in die kombuis voor ’n sjokoladekoek. Op ’n briefie langs die koek staan: *Vir die partytjie – MOENIE EET NIE!* Sipho se dinkborrel: *Net een klein stukkie …*\n- *Paneel 2:* Sipho se hand reik na die koek. Die vloer onder sy voete gaan *KRAAK!*\n- *Paneel 3:* Ma staan in die deur met haar arms gevou. Spraakborrel: *Sipho! Kan jy nie lees nie?* Sipho se wange is rooi en hy kyk af.\n\nDie prente vertel wat die woorde nie sê nie: Ma se gevoude arms wys sy is **kwaad**, en Sipho se rooi wange wys hy is **skaam**.\n\n## Advertensies\n\n’n **Advertensie** wil jou **oortuig** om iets te koop of te doen.\n\n**Voorbeeld (beskryf):** ’n Meisie in sportklere hardloop so vinnig dat sy ’n jagluiperd verbysteek. Bo-aan staan in groot letters: **SPOEDVOET-TEKKIES**. Onder die prent: *Hardloop soos die wind!* In ’n helder rooi sirkel: *Nou net R299!* Klein onderaan: *Slegs hierdie maand by jou naaste sportwinkel.*\n\n- Die **slagspreuk** is ’n kort, pakkende sin wat jy maklik onthou: *Hardloop soos die wind!*\n- **Oortuigende taal**: woorde soos *nou net, die beste, gratis, slegs hierdie maand* laat jou voel jy moet gou koop.\n- Die **teikengroep** is die mense vir wie die advertensie bedoel is: hier kinders wat graag hardloop en sport speel (en hulle ouers, wat betaal).\n- Die prent **oordryf**: geen tekkie kan jou vinniger as ’n jagluiperd maak nie!\n\n> **Algemene fout:** ’n Advertensie gee nie net feite nie. *Die prys is R299* is ’n feit, maar *die beste tekkies in die land* is ’n **mening** wat jou wil oortuig.\n\n## Plakkate\n\n’n **Plakkaat** gee kort, duidelike inligting oor ’n gebeurtenis. Soek altyd **wie, wat, waar en wanneer**.\n\n**HELP ONS DIE STRAND SKOONMAAK!**\n- **Wie:** die omgewingsklub van jou skool en hulle gesinne\n- **Wat:** ’n strandskoonmaak\n- **Waar:** Muizenberg-strand, Kaapstad\n- **Wanneer:** 8 November, van 08:00 tot 11:00\n- **Bring saam:** ’n hoed, water en tuinhandskoene\n\n## Tabelle\n\nLees eers die **opskrif** en die **kolomopskrifte**, en soek dan die ry wat jy nodig het.\n\n| Tyd | Item | Plek |\n|---|---|---|\n| 08:00 | 100 m-naelloop | atletiekbaan |\n| 09:30 | verspring | sandput |\n| 11:00 | aflos | atletiekbaan |\n\n*Waar vind die verspring plaas?* Gaan na die ry *verspring* en kyk in die kolom *Plek*: by die **sandput**.\n\n> **Onthou:** Beantwoord vrae net uit wat die teks sê of wys, en verduidelik hoe die **prent en die woorde saamwerk**.","en":"## What is a visual text?\n\nA **visual text** (*visuele teks*) uses **pictures and words together** to get a message across. The picture catches your attention and shows feelings; the words give the details. In a test the picture is often described in words. Then read the description as carefully as you would look at a picture.\n\nAlways look at:\n- **colour**: bright red and yellow catch attention;\n- **size of the letters**: the most important words are the biggest;\n- **facial expressions and body language**: they show how characters feel.\n\n## Comic strips\n\nA **comic strip** (*strokiesprent*) tells a story in a series of **panels** (*panele*, blocks) that you read from left to right.\n- A **speech bubble** (*spraakborrel*) with a point towards the character shows what he or she **says**.\n- A **thought bubble** (*dinkborrel*, a little cloud with small circles) shows what the character **thinks**.\n- **Onomatopoeia** (*klanknabootsing*) in big letters, such as *KRAAK!* (creak) or *BOEM!* (boom), lets you “hear” the sound.\n\n**Example (described):**\n- *Panel 1:* Sipho stands in the kitchen in front of a chocolate cake. A note next to the cake says: *Vir die partytjie – MOENIE EET NIE!* (For the party – DON’T EAT!) Sipho’s thought bubble: *Net een klein stukkie …* (Just one small piece …)\n- *Panel 2:* Sipho’s hand reaches for the cake. The floor under his feet goes *KRAAK!*\n- *Panel 3:* Mom stands in the doorway with her arms folded. Speech bubble: *Sipho! Kan jy nie lees nie?* (Sipho! Can’t you read?) Sipho’s cheeks are red and he looks down.\n\nThe pictures tell what the words don’t say: Mom’s folded arms show she is **angry**, and Sipho’s red cheeks show he is **embarrassed** (*skaam*).\n\n## Advertisements\n\nAn **advertisement** (*advertensie*) wants to **persuade** you to buy or do something.\n\n**Example (described):** A girl in sports clothes runs so fast that she overtakes a cheetah. At the top in big letters: **SPOEDVOET-TEKKIES** (Speedfoot sneakers). Under the picture: *Hardloop soos die wind!* (Run like the wind!) In a bright red circle: *Nou net R299!* (Now only R299!) Small at the bottom: *Slegs hierdie maand by jou naaste sportwinkel.* (Only this month at your nearest sports shop.)\n\n- The **slogan** (*slagspreuk*) is a short, catchy sentence that you remember easily: *Hardloop soos die wind!*\n- **Persuasive language** (*oortuigende taal*): words like *nou net* (now only), *die beste* (the best), *gratis* (free), *slegs hierdie maand* (only this month) make you feel you must buy quickly.\n- The **target group** (*teikengroep*) is the people the advertisement is meant for: here children who love running and sport (and their parents, who pay).\n- The picture **exaggerates**: no sneaker can make you faster than a cheetah!\n\n> **Common mistake:** An advertisement does not only give facts. *Die prys is R299* (The price is R299) is a fact, but *die beste tekkies in die land* (the best sneakers in the country) is an **opinion** that wants to persuade you.\n\n## Posters\n\nA **poster** (*plakkaat*) gives short, clear information about an event. Always look for **who, what, where and when** (*wie, wat, waar, wanneer*).\n\n**HELP ONS DIE STRAND SKOONMAAK!** (Help us clean the beach!)\n- **Who:** your school’s environmental club and their families\n- **What:** a beach clean-up\n- **Where:** Muizenberg beach, Cape Town\n- **When:** 8 November, from 08:00 to 11:00\n- **Bring along:** a hat, water and garden gloves\n\n## Tables\n\nFirst read the **heading** and the **column headings**, then find the row you need.\n\n| Tyd (Time) | Item | Plek (Place) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 08:00 | 100 m-naelloop (100 m sprint) | atletiekbaan (athletics track) |\n| 09:30 | verspring (long jump) | sandput (sandpit) |\n| 11:00 | aflos (relay) | atletiekbaan (athletics track) |\n\n*Waar vind die verspring plaas?* (Where does the long jump take place?) Go to the row *verspring* and look in the column *Plek*: at the **sandpit** (*sandput*).\n\n> **Remember:** Answer questions only from what the text says or shows, and explain how the **picture and the words work together**."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Visuele teks","en":"Visual text (visuele teks)"},"def":{"af":"’n Teks wat prente en woorde saam gebruik om ’n boodskap oor te dra.","en":"A text that uses pictures and words together to get a message across."}},{"term":{"af":"Strokiesprent","en":"Comic strip (strokiesprent)"},"def":{"af":"’n Storie wat in ’n reeks prentjies (panele) met spraak- en dinkborrels vertel word.","en":"A story told in a series of pictures (panels) with speech and thought bubbles."}},{"term":{"af":"Paneel","en":"Panel (paneel)"},"def":{"af":"Een blokkie of prentjie in ’n strokiesprent.","en":"One block or picture in a comic strip."}},{"term":{"af":"Spraakborrel","en":"Speech bubble (spraakborrel)"},"def":{"af":"’n Borrel met ’n puntjie na ’n karakter, wat wys wat die karakter sê.","en":"A bubble with a point towards a character, showing what the character says."}},{"term":{"af":"Dinkborrel","en":"Thought bubble (dinkborrel)"},"def":{"af":"’n Wolkie met klein sirkeltjies, wat wys wat ’n karakter dink.","en":"A little cloud with small circles, showing what a character thinks."}},{"term":{"af":"Advertensie","en":"Advertisement (advertensie)"},"def":{"af":"’n Teks wat jou wil oortuig om iets te koop of te doen.","en":"A text that wants to persuade you to buy or do something."}},{"term":{"af":"Slagspreuk","en":"Slogan (slagspreuk)"},"def":{"af":"’n Kort, pakkende sin in ’n advertensie wat jy maklik onthou: *Hardloop soos die wind!*","en":"A short, catchy sentence in an advertisement that you remember easily: *Hardloop soos die wind!* (Run like the wind!)"}},{"term":{"af":"Oortuigende taal","en":"Persuasive language (oortuigende taal)"},"def":{"af":"Woorde wat jou wil oorhaal om iets te glo, te koop of te doen, soos *nou net* en *die beste*.","en":"Words that try to win you over to believe, buy or do something, such as *nou net* (now only) and *die beste* (the best)."}},{"term":{"af":"Teikengroep","en":"Target group (teikengroep)"},"def":{"af":"Die mense vir wie ’n advertensie of teks bedoel is.","en":"The people an advertisement or text is meant for."}},{"term":{"af":"Plakkaat","en":"Poster (plakkaat)"},"def":{"af":"’n Kennisgewing met kort, duidelike inligting oor ’n gebeurtenis: wie, wat, waar en wanneer.","en":"A notice with short, clear information about an event: who, what, where and when."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"’n Advertensie ontleed","en":"Analysing an advertisement"},"problem":{"af":"’n Advertensie vir **Koel-Kan-waterbottels** wys ’n seun wat ná ’n sokkerwedstryd koel water drink terwyl sweet van sy voorkop drup. Bo staan: *Koel water, die hele dag lank!* Onder: *Koop een, kry een GRATIS – net hierdie week!* (a) Wat is die slagspreuk? (b) Wie is die teikengroep? (c) Noem twee voorbeelde van oortuigende taal. (d) Hoe werk die prent en die woorde saam?","en":"An advertisement for **Koel-Kan water bottles** shows a boy drinking cool water after a soccer match while sweat drips from his forehead. At the top: *Koel water, die hele dag lank!* (Cool water, all day long!) At the bottom: *Koop een, kry een GRATIS – net hierdie week!* (Buy one, get one FREE – this week only!) (a) What is the slogan? (b) Who is the target group? (c) Give two examples of persuasive language. (d) How do the picture and the words work together?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die kort, pakkende sin bo-aan is die slagspreuk: *Koel water, die hele dag lank!*","en":"(a) The short, catchy sentence at the top is the slogan: *Koel water, die hele dag lank!*"},{"af":"(b) Die prent wys ’n seun op die sportveld, so die advertensie is bedoel vir **kinders wat sport speel** (en hulle ouers).","en":"(b) The picture shows a boy on the sports field, so the advertisement is meant for **children who play sport** (and their parents)."},{"af":"(c) *GRATIS* en *net hierdie week* wil jou laat voel dat jy dadelik moet koop.","en":"(c) *GRATIS* (free) and *net hierdie week* (this week only) want to make you feel you must buy at once."},{"af":"(d) Die sweet wys hoe warm en dors die seun is, en die woorde belowe dat die bottel sy water koel hou: die prent maak die belofte geloofwaardig.","en":"(d) The sweat shows how hot and thirsty the boy is, and the words promise that the bottle keeps his water cool: the picture makes the promise believable."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Koel water, die hele dag lank! (b) kinders wat sport speel (c) GRATIS; net hierdie week (d) die prent wys die dors, die woorde gee die oplossing.","en":"(a) *Koel water, die hele dag lank!* (b) children who play sport (c) *GRATIS*; *net hierdie week* (d) the picture shows the thirst, the words give the solution."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Plakkaat lees","en":"Reading a poster"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die plakkaat en noem wie, wat, waar en wanneer: *KOM NA ONS KOEKVERKOPING! Graad 5-leerders verkoop koeke en koeksisters in die skoolsaal, 14 November, 13:00–14:30. Alle geld gaan na die skoolbiblioteek.*","en":"Read the poster and name who, what, where and when: *KOM NA ONS KOEKVERKOPING! Graad 5-leerders verkoop koeke en koeksisters in die skoolsaal, 14 November, 13:00–14:30. Alle geld gaan na die skoolbiblioteek.* (Come to our cake sale! Grade 5 learners sell cakes and koeksisters in the school hall, 14 November, 13:00–14:30. All money goes to the school library.)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Wie?** Die mense wat dit reël: Graad 5-leerders.","en":"**Who?** The people organising it: Grade 5 learners."},{"af":"**Wat?** Die gebeurtenis: ’n koekverkoping.","en":"**What?** The event: a cake sale."},{"af":"**Waar?** Die plek: die skoolsaal. **Wanneer?** 14 November, van 13:00 tot 14:30.","en":"**Where?** The place: the school hall. **When?** 14 November, from 13:00 to 14:30."},{"af":"Ekstra: die laaste sin sê **waarom**: die geld gaan na die biblioteek.","en":"Extra: the last sentence says **why**: the money goes to the library."}],"answer":{"af":"Wie: Graad 5-leerders. Wat: koekverkoping. Waar: skoolsaal. Wanneer: 14 November, 13:00–14:30.","en":"Who: Grade 5 learners. What: a cake sale. Where: the school hall. When: 14 November, 13:00–14:30."}},{"title":{"af":"Die strokiesprent verstaan","en":"Understanding the comic strip"},"problem":{"af":"Verwys na die strokiesprent van Sipho: (a) Wat is die verskil tussen die borrel in paneel 1 en die borrel in paneel 3? (b) Wat doen die woord *KRAAK!* in paneel 2? (c) Hoe weet jy hoe Ma voel?","en":"Refer to the comic strip about Sipho: (a) What is the difference between the bubble in panel 1 and the bubble in panel 3? (b) What does the word *KRAAK!* do in panel 2? (c) How do you know how Mom feels?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Paneel 1 het ’n **dinkborrel**: Sipho dink net. Paneel 3 het ’n **spraakborrel**: Ma praat hardop.","en":"(a) Panel 1 has a **thought bubble**: Sipho only thinks. Panel 3 has a **speech bubble**: Mom speaks out loud."},{"af":"(b) *KRAAK!* is **klanknabootsing**: die krakende vloer verklap Sipho en bou spanning op.","en":"(b) *KRAAK!* is **onomatopoeia**: the creaking floor gives Sipho away and builds tension."},{"af":"(c) Ma staan met **gevoude arms** en roep sy naam met ’n uitroepteken: sy is **kwaad**.","en":"(c) Mom stands with **folded arms** and calls his name with an exclamation mark: she is **angry**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) dinkborrel teenoor spraakborrel (b) klanknabootsing wat Sipho verklap (c) haar gevoude arms en uitroep wys sy is kwaad","en":"(a) thought bubble versus speech bubble (b) onomatopoeia that gives Sipho away (c) her folded arms and exclamation show she is angry"}},{"title":{"af":"’n Tabel lees","en":"Reading a table"},"problem":{"af":"Gebruik die sportprogram: (a) Wat gebeur om 11:00? (b) Watter twee items vind op die atletiekbaan plaas?","en":"Use the sports programme: (a) What happens at 11:00? (b) Which two items take place on the athletics track?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Soek *11:00* in die kolom *Tyd* en lees oor na die kolom *Item*: *aflos*.","en":"(a) Find *11:00* in the column *Tyd* (Time) and read across to the column *Item*: *aflos* (relay)."},{"af":"(b) Kyk af in die kolom *Plek* en soek *atletiekbaan*: dit staan by *100 m-naelloop* en *aflos*.","en":"(b) Look down the column *Plek* (Place) and find *atletiekbaan*: it appears next to *100 m-naelloop* and *aflos*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) die aflos (b) die 100 m-naelloop en die aflos","en":"(a) the relay (*aflos*) (b) the 100 m sprint and the relay"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In ’n strokiesprent sien jy ’n wolkie met klein sirkeltjies wat na ’n karakter se kop lei. Wat wys dit?","en":"In a comic strip you see a little cloud with small circles leading to a character’s head. What does it show?"},"options":[{"af":"wat die karakter hardop sê","en":"what the character says out loud"},{"af":"watter geluid iets maak","en":"what sound something makes"},{"af":"waar die storie afspeel","en":"where the story takes place"},{"af":"wat die karakter dink","en":"what the character thinks"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Dit is ’n **dinkborrel**: dit wys gedagtes wat die ander karakters nie kan hoor nie. ’n Spraakborrel met ’n puntjie wys wat iemand sê.","en":"This is a **thought bubble** (*dinkborrel*): it shows thoughts the other characters cannot hear. A speech bubble with a point shows what someone says."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Op ’n plakkaat moet die leser vinnig kan sien wie, wat, waar en wanneer.","en":"On a poster the reader must be able to see quickly who, what, where and when."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Plakkaat moet van ver af gelees kan word, so die belangrikste inligting staan kort en duidelik.","en":"True. A poster must be readable from far away, so the most important information is short and clear."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **slagspreuk** in die Spoedvoet-advertensie?","en":"What is the **slogan** in the Spoedvoet advertisement?"},"options":[{"af":"Nou net R299!","en":"Nou net R299!"},{"af":"Hardloop soos die wind!","en":"Hardloop soos die wind!"},{"af":"Spoedvoet-tekkies","en":"Spoedvoet-tekkies"},{"af":"Slegs hierdie maand","en":"Slegs hierdie maand"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die slagspreuk is die kort, pakkende sin wat jy onthou. *Spoedvoet-tekkies* is die naam van die produk, en *Nou net R299!* gee die prys.","en":"The slogan is the short, catchy sentence you remember. *Spoedvoet-tekkies* is the name of the product, and *Nou net R299!* gives the price."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Woorde soos *KRAAK!* en *BOEM!* in ’n strokiesprent is voorbeelde van ___.","en":"Words like *KRAAK!* and *BOEM!* in a comic strip are examples of ___ (give the Afrikaans term for onomatopoeia)."},"answers":{"af":["klanknabootsing"],"en":["klanknabootsing","onomatopoeia"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["alliterasie","personifikasie","oordrywing"],"en":["alliterasie","personifikasie","oordrywing"]}},"explain":{"af":"**Klanknabootsing** is ’n woord wat klink soos die geluid self. In strokiesprente staan dit dikwels in groot, vet letters.","en":"**Klanknabootsing** (onomatopoeia) is a word that sounds like the noise itself. In comic strips it often appears in big, bold letters."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wie is die **teikengroep** van die Spoedvoet-advertensie?","en":"Who is the **target group** of the Spoedvoet advertisement?"},"options":[{"af":"oupas en oumas wat graag tuinmaak","en":"grandparents who love gardening"},{"af":"boere wat nuwe trekkers soek","en":"farmers looking for new tractors"},{"af":"kinders wat graag hardloop en sport speel","en":"children who love running and playing sport"},{"af":"onderwysers wat skoolboeke bestel","en":"teachers who order school books"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die prent wys ’n meisie wat hardloop, en die produk is tekkies vir spoed. Die advertensie is dus bedoel vir sportlike kinders (en hulle ouers wat betaal).","en":"The picture shows a girl running, and the product is sneakers for speed. So the advertisement is meant for sporty children (and the parents who pay)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoekom staan *Nou net R299!* in ’n helder rooi sirkel?","en":"Why is *Nou net R299!* in a bright red circle?"},"options":[{"af":"om die leser se aandag te trek en die prys te laat uitstaan","en":"to catch the reader’s attention and make the price stand out"},{"af":"omdat die tekkies self ook rooi is","en":"because the sneakers themselves are red too"},{"af":"omdat dit die naam van die tekkies is","en":"because it is the name of the sneakers"},{"af":"omdat die drukker net rooi ink gehad het","en":"because the printer only had red ink"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Helder kleure en vorms trek die oog. Die adverteerder wil hê jy moet die “lae” prys dadelik raaksien, sodat jy wil koop.","en":"Bright colours and shapes catch the eye. The advertiser wants you to notice the “low” price at once, so that you want to buy."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke term by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each term to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"paneel","en":"panel (*paneel*)"},"r":{"af":"een blokkie in ’n strokiesprent","en":"one block in a comic strip"}},{"l":{"af":"spraakborrel","en":"speech bubble (*spraakborrel*)"},"r":{"af":"wys wat ’n karakter sê","en":"shows what a character says"}},{"l":{"af":"slagspreuk","en":"slogan (*slagspreuk*)"},"r":{"af":"’n kort, pakkende sin wat jy onthou","en":"a short, catchy sentence you remember"}},{"l":{"af":"teikengroep","en":"target group (*teikengroep*)"},"r":{"af":"die mense vir wie die advertensie bedoel is","en":"the people the advertisement is meant for"}},{"l":{"af":"plakkaat","en":"poster (*plakkaat*)"},"r":{"af":"kennisgewing oor ’n gebeurtenis","en":"a notice about an event"}}],"explain":{"af":"Panele en spraakborrels hoort by strokiesprente, die slagspreuk en teikengroep by advertensies, en ’n plakkaat kondig ’n gebeurtenis aan.","en":"Panels and speech bubbles belong to comic strips, the slogan and target group to advertisements, and a poster announces an event."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Volgens die plakkaat begin die strandskoonmaak om ___.","en":"According to the poster, the beach clean-up starts at ___."},"answers":{"af":["08:00","8:00","agtuur","8 uur"],"en":["08:00","8:00","8 am","8 o’clock","8 o'clock"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["11:00","09:00","08:30"],"en":["11:00","09:00","08:30"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die plakkaat sê *van 08:00 tot 11:00*. Dit begin om 08:00 en eindig om 11:00.","en":"The poster says *van 08:00 tot 11:00* (from 08:00 to 11:00). It starts at 08:00 and ends at 11:00."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe voel Sipho in paneel 3, en hoe weet jy?","en":"How does Sipho feel in panel 3, and how do you know?"},"options":[{"af":"Kwaad – hy staan met sy arms gevou.","en":"Angry – he stands with his arms folded."},{"af":"Skaam – sy wange is rooi en hy kyk af.","en":"Embarrassed – his cheeks are red and he looks down."},{"af":"Bly – hy glimlag breed vir Ma.","en":"Happy – he smiles broadly at Mom."},{"af":"Bang – hy hardloop by die deur uit.","en":"Scared – he runs out of the door."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Rooi wange en afgekykte oë wys skaamte: Sipho is betrap. Dit is Ma, nie Sipho nie, wat met gevoude arms staan.","en":"Red cheeks and eyes looking down show embarrassment: Sipho has been caught. It is Mom, not Sipho, who stands with folded arms."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Advertensie gee net feite en probeer nooit om jou te oortuig nie.","en":"An advertisement only gives facts and never tries to persuade you."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Advertensie wil jou oortuig om te koop. Dit gebruik menings, oordrywing en woorde soos *die beste* en *nou net*.","en":"False. An advertisement wants to persuade you to buy. It uses opinions, exaggeration and words like *die beste* (the best) and *nou net* (now only)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin uit ’n advertensie is ’n **mening** wat jou wil oortuig?","en":"Which sentence from an advertisement is an **opinion** that wants to persuade you?"},"options":[{"af":"Beskikbaar in groottes 1 tot 6.","en":"Beskikbaar in groottes 1 tot 6."},{"af":"Die prys is R299.","en":"Die prys is R299."},{"af":"Te koop by sportwinkels.","en":"Te koop by sportwinkels."},{"af":"Die beste tekkies in die hele land!","en":"Die beste tekkies in die hele land!"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Die beste* kan nie bewys word nie; dit is ’n mening. Die groottes, die prys en waar jy dit kan koop, is feite.","en":"*Die beste* (the best) cannot be proved; it is an opinion. The sizes, the price and where you can buy them are facts."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat moet jy **eerste** lees as jy ’n vraag oor ’n tabel beantwoord?","en":"What should you read **first** when you answer a question about a table?"},"options":[{"af":"die opskrif en die kolomopskrifte","en":"the heading and the column headings"},{"af":"net die laaste ry van die tabel","en":"only the last row of the table"},{"af":"die getalle in die eerste kolom","en":"the numbers in the first column"},{"af":"die kleinste letters onderaan","en":"the smallest letters at the bottom"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die opskrifte sê wat in elke kolom staan. Eers dan weet jy waar om die antwoord te soek.","en":"The headings tell you what is in each column. Only then do you know where to look for the answer."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Volgens die sportprogram begin die verspring om ___.","en":"According to the sports programme, the long jump (*verspring*) starts at ___."},"answers":{"af":["09:30","9:30"],"en":["09:30","9:30"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["08:00","11:00","10:30"],"en":["08:00","11:00","10:30"]}},"explain":{"af":"Soek die ry *verspring* en kyk in die kolom *Tyd*: 09:30.","en":"Find the row *verspring* and look in the column *Tyd* (Time): 09:30."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat moet jy volgens die plakkaat na die strandskoonmaak saambring?","en":"According to the poster, what must you bring to the beach clean-up?"},"options":[{"af":"’n hoed, ’n swembroek en ’n handdoek","en":"a hat, a swimsuit and a towel"},{"af":"water, toebroodjies en ’n bal","en":"water, sandwiches and a ball"},{"af":"’n hoed, water en tuinhandskoene","en":"a hat, water and garden gloves"},{"af":"tuinhandskoene, ’n graaf en ’n emmer","en":"garden gloves, a spade and a bucket"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die plakkaat sê presies: *Bring saam: ’n hoed, water en tuinhandskoene.* Die ander opsies het een of meer dinge wat nie op die plakkaat staan nie.","en":"The poster says exactly: *Bring saam: ’n hoed, water en tuinhandskoene.* (Bring along: a hat, water and garden gloves.) The other options include things that are not on the poster."}}]},{"id":"afr5-t4-kort-skryfstukke","title":{"af":"Kort skryfstukke en opsomming","en":"Short writing pieces and summary"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal ’n vriendskaplike brief, dagboekinskrywing, uitnodiging, resep en e-pos in die regte formaat kan skryf en ’n teks in puntvorm kan opsom.","en":"You will be able to write a friendly letter, diary entry, invitation, recipe and e-mail in the correct format and summarise a text in point form."},"summary":{"af":"## Die vriendskaplike brief\n\nJy skryf ’n **vriendskaplike brief** aan iemand wat jy goed ken, soos ’n maat of jou ouma. Die **formaat** (uitleg) is belangrik:\n1. **Jou adres** regs bo: straat en nommer, dorp of stad, poskode (elk op sy eie reël).\n2. **Datum** onder die adres: *14 Oktober 2026*.\n3. **Aanhef** links: *Liewe Ouma* of *Liewe Thabo*. In Afrikaans skryf ons gewoonlik geen komma ná die aanhef nie.\n4. **Inhoud** in paragrawe: begin vriendelik (vra hoe dit gaan), vertel jou nuus, en rond af.\n5. **Slot** links onder: *Baie liefde* of *Groete*, op die volgende reël *Jou kleinkind* of *Jou maat*, en dan jou **naam**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie die adres en datum vergeet nie, en moenie jou van (familienaam) by ’n brief aan ’n maat of familielid skryf nie: net jou naam is genoeg.\n\n## Dagboek, uitnodiging en e-pos\n\n**Dagboekinskrywing:** jou eie, private skryfstuk oor jou dag.\n- Skryf die datum bo-aan, en begin dikwels met *Liewe Dagboek*.\n- Skryf in die **ek-vorm**, meestal in die **verlede tyd**, en vertel hoe jy **voel**: *Vandag het ek my eerste doel geskop. Ek was so trots!*\n\n**Uitnodiging:** nooi iemand na ’n geleentheid. Dit moet sê:\n- **wie** nooi en **wie** genooi word;\n- **wat** die geleentheid is;\n- **waar** en **wanneer** (datum en tyd);\n- **RSVP**: teen watter datum en by wie die gas moet laat weet of hy of sy kom.\n\n**E-pos:**\n- **Aan:** die ontvanger se e-posadres.\n- **Onderwerp:** ’n paar woorde wat sê waaroor dit gaan, soos *Wiskunde-huiswerkblad kwyt*.\n- Daarna ’n aanhef, ’n kort, duidelike boodskap en ’n groet met jou naam. Aan ’n onderwyser skryf jy beleefd, sonder slengtaal.\n\n## Instruksies en resepte\n\n’n **Resep** of instruksies sê vir iemand **hoe** om iets te doen.\n- **Titel:** *Piesangmelkskommel*\n- **Bestanddele** met hoeveelhede: *1 piesang, 250 ml koue melk, 1 teelepel heuning, 3 ysblokkies*\n- **Metode** in **genommerde stappe**, in die regte volgorde.\n- Elke stap begin met ’n werkwoord in die **bevelvorm**: *Skil die piesang. Sny dit in skyfies. Gooi alles in die menger. Vra ’n grootmens om die menger aan te skakel.*\n\n> **Onthou:** In die bevelvorm staan die werkwoord **voor** in die sin, sonder *jy*. Nie *Jy moet die piesang skil* nie, maar *Skil die piesang.*\n\n## Opsomming in puntvorm\n\n’n **Opsomming** gee net die **hoofpunte** van ’n teks, kort en in jou eie woorde.\n1. Lees die teks twee keer en onderstreep die **hoofgedagte** van elke paragraaf.\n2. Laat **voorbeelde**, **herhaling**, beskrywings en direkte rede uit.\n3. Skryf elke punt as ’n **volsin** in **jou eie woorde**, en nommer die punte.\n4. Hou by die **woordlimiet** (bv. hoogstens 40 woorde) en skryf onderaan: *Aantal woorde: 34*.\n\nKyk hoe ’n lang sin ’n kort punt word:\n*Terwyl die groep kos soek, staan een meerkat op sy agterpote op die uitkyk, en as hy ’n arend of ’n jakkals sien, maak hy ’n skerp geluid.* → *’n Wag waarsku die groep teen gevaar.*\n\nDie voorbeelde (*arend, jakkals*) en die besonderhede (*op sy agterpote*) val weg; net die hoofgedagte bly oor.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie sinne woord vir woord uit die teks oorskryf nie, en moenie jou eie mening byvoeg nie.","en":"## The friendly letter\n\nYou write a **friendly letter** (*vriendskaplike brief*) to someone you know well, like a friend or your granny. The **format** (*formaat*, layout) is important:\n1. **Your address** top right: street and number, town or city, postal code (each on its own line).\n2. **Date** under the address: *14 Oktober 2026*.\n3. **Greeting** (*aanhef*) on the left: *Liewe Ouma* (Dear Granny) or *Liewe Thabo*. In Afrikaans we usually write no comma after the greeting.\n4. **Body** (*inhoud*) in paragraphs: start in a friendly way (ask how they are), tell your news, and round off.\n5. **Ending** (*slot*) bottom left: *Baie liefde* (Lots of love) or *Groete* (Regards), on the next line *Jou kleinkind* (Your grandchild) or *Jou maat* (Your friend), and then your **name**.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Don’t forget the address and date, and don’t write your surname in a letter to a friend or family member: your first name is enough.\n\n## Diary, invitation and e-mail\n\n**Diary entry** (*dagboekinskrywing*): your own, private piece of writing about your day.\n- Write the date at the top, and often begin with *Liewe Dagboek* (Dear Diary).\n- Write in the **first person** (*ek*), mostly in the **past tense**, and tell how you **feel**: *Vandag het ek my eerste doel geskop. Ek was so trots!* (Today I scored my first goal. I was so proud!)\n\n**Invitation** (*uitnodiging*): invites someone to an event. It must say:\n- **who** is inviting and **who** is invited;\n- **what** the event is;\n- **where** and **when** (date and time);\n- **RSVP**: by which date and to whom the guest must say whether he or she is coming.\n\n**E-mail** (*e-pos*):\n- **To** (*Aan*): the receiver’s e-mail address.\n- **Subject** (*Onderwerp*): a few words saying what it is about, such as *Wiskunde-huiswerkblad kwyt* (Maths homework sheet lost).\n- Then a greeting, a short, clear message and a closing with your name. To a teacher you write politely, without slang.\n\n## Instructions and recipes\n\nA **recipe** (*resep*) or instructions tell someone **how** to do something.\n- **Title:** *Piesangmelkskommel* (banana milkshake)\n- **Ingredients** (*bestanddele*) with amounts: *1 piesang, 250 ml koue melk, 1 teelepel heuning, 3 ysblokkies* (1 banana, 250 ml cold milk, 1 teaspoon honey, 3 ice cubes)\n- **Method** (*metode*) in **numbered steps**, in the right order.\n- Each step starts with a verb in the **command form** (*bevelvorm*): *Skil die piesang. Sny dit in skyfies. Gooi alles in die menger. Vra ’n grootmens om die menger aan te skakel.* (Peel the banana. Cut it into slices. Put everything in the blender. Ask an adult to switch on the blender.)\n\n> **Remember:** In the command form the verb stands **first** in the sentence, without *jy* (you). Not *Jy moet die piesang skil* (You must peel the banana), but *Skil die piesang.* (Peel the banana.)\n\n## Summary in point form\n\nA **summary** (*opsomming*) gives only the **main points** of a text, briefly and in your own words.\n1. Read the text twice and underline the **main idea** of each paragraph.\n2. Leave out **examples**, **repetition**, descriptions and direct speech.\n3. Write each point as a **full sentence** in **your own words**, and number the points.\n4. Keep to the **word limit** (e.g. at most 40 words) and write at the bottom: *Aantal woorde: 34* (Number of words: 34).\n\nSee how a long sentence becomes a short point:\n*Terwyl die groep kos soek, staan een meerkat op sy agterpote op die uitkyk, en as hy ’n arend of ’n jakkals sien, maak hy ’n skerp geluid.* (While the group looks for food, one meerkat stands on its hind legs on the lookout, and if it sees an eagle or a jackal, it makes a sharp sound.) → *’n Wag waarsku die groep teen gevaar.* (A guard warns the group of danger.)\n\nThe examples (*arend, jakkals*: eagle, jackal) and the details (*op sy agterpote*: on its hind legs) fall away; only the main idea is left.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Don’t copy sentences word for word from the text, and don’t add your own opinion."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Formaat","en":"Format (formaat)"},"def":{"af":"Die vaste uitleg van ’n skryfstuk: watter dele dit het en waar elke deel op die bladsy kom.","en":"The fixed layout of a piece of writing: which parts it has and where each part goes on the page."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanhef","en":"Greeting (aanhef)"},"def":{"af":"Die begin van ’n brief of e-pos waarin jy die persoon groet, soos *Liewe Oupa*.","en":"The start of a letter or e-mail where you greet the person, such as *Liewe Oupa* (Dear Grandpa)."}},{"term":{"af":"Slot","en":"Ending (slot)"},"def":{"af":"Die einde van ’n brief, met ’n groet soos *Baie liefde* en jou naam.","en":"The end of a letter, with a closing such as *Baie liefde* (Lots of love) and your name."}},{"term":{"af":"Dagboekinskrywing","en":"Diary entry (dagboekinskrywing)"},"def":{"af":"’n Private stukkie skryfwerk in die ek-vorm oor wat met jou gebeur het en hoe jy voel.","en":"A private piece of writing in the first person about what happened to you and how you feel."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitnodiging","en":"Invitation (uitnodiging)"},"def":{"af":"’n Skryfstuk wat iemand na ’n geleentheid nooi en sê wat, waar en wanneer.","en":"A piece of writing that invites someone to an event and says what, where and when."}},{"term":{"af":"RSVP","en":"RSVP"},"def":{"af":"’n Afkorting wat vra dat die gas moet laat weet of hy of sy sal kom.","en":"An abbreviation asking the guest to let you know whether he or she will come."}},{"term":{"af":"Bevelvorm","en":"Command form (bevelvorm)"},"def":{"af":"’n Sin wat sê wat iemand moet doen, met die werkwoord voor: *Meng die meel.*","en":"A sentence that tells someone what to do, with the verb first: *Meng die meel.* (Mix the flour.)"}},{"term":{"af":"Bestanddele","en":"Ingredients (bestanddele)"},"def":{"af":"Die lys van alles wat jy vir ’n resep nodig het, met hoeveelhede.","en":"The list of everything you need for a recipe, with amounts."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderwerpreël","en":"Subject line (onderwerpreël)"},"def":{"af":"Die paar woorde in ’n e-pos wat sê waaroor die boodskap gaan.","en":"The few words in an e-mail that say what the message is about."}},{"term":{"af":"Opsomming","en":"Summary (opsomming)"},"def":{"af":"’n Kort weergawe van ’n teks met net die hoofpunte, in jou eie woorde.","en":"A short version of a text with only the main points, in your own words."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Die formaat van ’n brief","en":"The format of a letter"},"problem":{"af":"Aisha skryf aan haar oupa. Sit hierdie dele in die regte volgorde: *Baie liefde* / *Liewe Oupa* / *Rosestraat 15, Bloemfontein, 9301* / *Ek het die leesprys gewen!* / *14 Oktober 2026* / *Aisha*","en":"Aisha writes to her grandpa. Put these parts in the correct order: *Baie liefde* (Lots of love) / *Liewe Oupa* (Dear Grandpa) / *Rosestraat 15, Bloemfontein, 9301* / *Ek het die leesprys gewen!* (I won the reading prize!) / *14 Oktober 2026* / *Aisha*"},"steps":[{"af":"Die **adres** kom eerste, regs bo: *Rosestraat 15, Bloemfontein, 9301*, elk op ’n eie reël.","en":"The **address** comes first, top right: *Rosestraat 15, Bloemfontein, 9301*, each on its own line."},{"af":"Die **datum** kom reg onder die adres: *14 Oktober 2026*.","en":"The **date** comes right under the address: *14 Oktober 2026*."},{"af":"Dan links die **aanhef** (*Liewe Oupa*) en die **inhoud** (*Ek het die leesprys gewen!*).","en":"Then on the left the **greeting** (*Liewe Oupa*) and the **body** (*Ek het die leesprys gewen!*)."},{"af":"Laaste kom die **slot** (*Baie liefde*) en op die volgende reël haar **naam**.","en":"Last comes the **ending** (*Baie liefde*) and on the next line her **name**."}],"answer":{"af":"adres → datum → Liewe Oupa → inhoud → Baie liefde → Aisha","en":"address → date → *Liewe Oupa* → body → *Baie liefde* → *Aisha*"}},{"title":{"af":"Instruksies in die bevelvorm","en":"Instructions in the command form"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf as genommerde instruksies in die bevelvorm: *Jy moet die piesang skil. Dan sny jy dit in skyfies. Jy gooi die melk by.*","en":"Rewrite as numbered instructions in the command form: *Jy moet die piesang skil. Dan sny jy dit in skyfies. Jy gooi die melk by.* (You must peel the banana. Then you cut it into slices. You add the milk.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Haal *jy* en *moet* uit: die leser weet dat die instruksies vir hom of haar is.","en":"Take out *jy* (you) and *moet* (must): the reader knows the instructions are for him or her."},{"af":"Sit die werkwoord voor in elke sin: *Skil …, Sny …, Gooi …*","en":"Put the verb first in every sentence: *Skil …, Sny …, Gooi …*"},{"af":"Die nommers wys die volgorde, so woorde soos *dan* is nie meer nodig nie.","en":"The numbers show the order, so words like *dan* (then) are no longer needed."}],"answer":{"af":"1. Skil die piesang. 2. Sny dit in skyfies. 3. Gooi die melk by.","en":"*1. Skil die piesang. 2. Sny dit in skyfies. 3. Gooi die melk by.*"}},{"title":{"af":"’n Uitnodiging nagaan","en":"Checking an invitation"},"problem":{"af":"Watter inligting ontbreek? *Liewe Fatima / Kom na my swempartytjie op 22 November by Rosestraat 15! / Groete / Johan*","en":"What information is missing? *Liewe Fatima / Kom na my swempartytjie op 22 November by Rosestraat 15! / Groete / Johan* (Dear Fatima, come to my swimming party on 22 November at 15 Rose Street! Regards, Johan)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Wie** nooi en wie word genooi? Johan nooi Fatima. (Ja.)","en":"**Who** is inviting and who is invited? Johan invites Fatima. (Yes.)"},{"af":"**Wat** en **waar**? ’n Swempartytjie by Rosestraat 15. (Ja.)","en":"**What** and **where**? A swimming party at 15 Rose Street. (Yes.)"},{"af":"**Wanneer?** Die datum is daar, maar nie die **tyd** nie. (Ontbreek!)","en":"**When?** The date is there, but not the **time**. (Missing!)"},{"af":"**RSVP?** Fatima weet nie teen wanneer sy moet laat weet of sy kom nie. (Ontbreek!)","en":"**RSVP?** Fatima does not know by when she must say whether she is coming. (Missing!)"}],"answer":{"af":"Die tyd en die RSVP (teen wanneer en by wie sy moet laat weet).","en":"The time and the RSVP (by when and to whom she must reply)."}},{"title":{"af":"Opsomming in puntvorm","en":"Summary in point form"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die teks en som dit op in vyf punte van hoogstens 40 woorde:\n\n*Meerkatte woon in droë dele van Suider-Afrika, soos die Kalahari. Hulle leef in groot groepe en grawe tonnels in die grond, waar hulle slaap en wegkruip. Elke oggend lê die meerkatte eers in die son om warm te word – dit lyk amper of hulle sonbaai soos mense op ’n strand! Terwyl die groep kos soek, staan een meerkat op sy agterpote op die uitkyk. As hy ’n arend of ’n jakkals sien, maak hy ’n skerp geluid en almal hardloop na die tonnels. Meerkatte eet meestal insekte, maar hulle vang ook skerpioene en akkedisse.*","en":"Read the text and summarise it in five points of at most 40 words:\n\n*Meerkatte woon in droë dele van Suider-Afrika, soos die Kalahari. Hulle leef in groot groepe en grawe tonnels in die grond, waar hulle slaap en wegkruip. Elke oggend lê die meerkatte eers in die son om warm te word – dit lyk amper of hulle sonbaai soos mense op ’n strand! Terwyl die groep kos soek, staan een meerkat op sy agterpote op die uitkyk. As hy ’n arend of ’n jakkals sien, maak hy ’n skerp geluid en almal hardloop na die tonnels. Meerkatte eet meestal insekte, maar hulle vang ook skerpioene en akkedisse.*\n\n(Meerkats live in dry parts of Southern Africa, such as the Kalahari. They live in big groups and dig tunnels in the ground, where they sleep and hide. Every morning the meerkats first lie in the sun to get warm – it almost looks as if they are sunbathing like people on a beach! While the group looks for food, one meerkat stands on its hind legs on the lookout. If it sees an eagle or a jackal, it makes a sharp sound and they all run to the tunnels. Meerkats mostly eat insects, but they also catch scorpions and lizards.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Onderstreep die hoofgedagtes: waar hulle woon, die tonnels, die son, die wag en hulle kos.","en":"Underline the main ideas: where they live, the tunnels, the sun, the guard and their food."},{"af":"Laat voorbeelde en ekstra besonderhede uit: *soos die Kalahari*, *soos mense op ’n strand*, *arend of jakkals*.","en":"Leave out examples and extra details: *soos die Kalahari* (such as the Kalahari), *soos mense op ’n strand* (like people on a beach), *arend of jakkals* (eagle or jackal)."},{"af":"Skryf elke hoofgedagte as ’n kort volsin in jou eie woorde, en nommer dit.","en":"Write each main idea as a short full sentence in your own words, and number it."},{"af":"Tel die woorde: 7 + 6 + 7 + 7 + 7 = 34. Dit is binne die limiet van 40.","en":"Count the words: 7 + 6 + 7 + 7 + 7 = 34. That is within the limit of 40."}],"answer":{"af":"1. Meerkatte leef in groepe in droë gebiede. 2. Hulle slaap en skuil in tonnels. 3. Soggens warm hulle in die son op. 4. ’n Wag waarsku die groep teen gevaar. 5. Hulle eet meestal insekte en klein diertjies. (Aantal woorde: 34)","en":"*1. Meerkatte leef in groepe in droë gebiede. 2. Hulle slaap en skuil in tonnels. 3. Soggens warm hulle in die son op. 4. ’n Wag waarsku die groep teen gevaar. 5. Hulle eet meestal insekte en klein diertjies.* (*Aantal woorde: 34*)"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar skryf jy jou adres in ’n vriendskaplike brief?","en":"Where do you write your address in a friendly letter?"},"options":[{"af":"links onderaan, ná jou naam","en":"at the bottom left, after your name"},{"af":"regs bo-aan die bladsy","en":"at the top right of the page"},{"af":"in die middel, ná die aanhef","en":"in the middle, after the greeting"},{"af":"net op die koevert, nie in die brief nie","en":"only on the envelope, not in the letter"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die adres kom regs bo, met die datum daaronder. So weet die ontvanger dadelik waarheen om terug te skryf.","en":"The address goes at the top right, with the date under it. That way the receiver knows at once where to write back to."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"*Baie liefde* en jou naam onderaan ’n brief vorm die ___ van die brief.","en":"*Baie liefde* (Lots of love) and your name at the bottom of a letter form the ___ of the letter (give the Afrikaans term)."},"answers":{"af":["slot"],"en":["slot","ending","closing"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["aanhef","adres","inhoud"],"en":["aanhef","adres","inhoud"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die **slot** is die einde van die brief: ’n groet soos *Baie liefde* of *Groete* en jou naam. Die **aanhef** (*Liewe …*) kom aan die begin.","en":"The **slot** (ending) is the end of the letter: a closing such as *Baie liefde* or *Groete* and your name. The **aanhef** (greeting, *Liewe …*) comes at the beginning."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter aanhef pas die beste in ’n brief aan jou oupa?","en":"Which greeting fits best in a letter to your grandpa?"},"options":[{"af":"Liewe Oupa","en":"Liewe Oupa"},{"af":"Geagte Meneer","en":"Geagte Meneer"},{"af":"Groete Oupa","en":"Groete Oupa"},{"af":"Beste Kliënt","en":"Beste Kliënt"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"In ’n vriendskaplike brief aan familie skryf jy *Liewe …*. *Geagte Meneer* is vir ’n formele brief, en *Groete* hoort in die slot.","en":"In a friendly letter to family you write *Liewe …* (Dear …). *Geagte Meneer* (Dear Sir) is for a formal letter, and *Groete* (Regards) belongs in the ending."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In ’n opsomming laat jy voorbeelde en herhaling uit.","en":"In a summary you leave out examples and repetition."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Opsomming bevat net die hoofpunte. Voorbeelde en herhaling maak dit langer sonder om nuwe hoofgedagtes by te voeg.","en":"True. A summary contains only the main points. Examples and repetition make it longer without adding new main ideas."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is in die **bevelvorm**?","en":"Which sentence is in the **command form**?"},"options":[{"af":"Jy moet die piesang skil.","en":"Jy moet die piesang skil."},{"af":"Ek skil nou die piesang.","en":"Ek skil nou die piesang."},{"af":"Die piesang word geskil.","en":"Die piesang word geskil."},{"af":"Skil die piesang en sny dit in skyfies.","en":"Skil die piesang en sny dit in skyfies."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"In die bevelvorm staan die werkwoord voor en is daar geen *jy* nie: *Skil … sny …*. Die ander sinne vertel of beskryf, maar gee nie ’n bevel nie.","en":"In the command form the verb comes first and there is no *jy* (you): *Skil … sny …* (Peel … cut …). The other sentences tell or describe, but do not give a command."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy het jou wiskunde-huiswerkblad verloor en skryf ’n e-pos aan jou onderwyser. Watter **onderwerpreël** is die beste?","en":"You lost your maths homework sheet and write an e-mail to your teacher. Which **subject line** is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Hallo!!!","en":"Hallo!!!"},{"af":"Ek","en":"Ek"},{"af":"Wiskunde-huiswerkblad kwyt","en":"Wiskunde-huiswerkblad kwyt"},{"af":"Lees dit asseblief dadelik, dis baie baie belangrik","en":"Lees dit asseblief dadelik, dis baie baie belangrik"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Goeie onderwerpreël is kort en sê presies waaroor die e-pos gaan. *Hallo!!!* en *Ek* sê niks, en die lang sin is te lank en nie beleefd nie.","en":"A good subject line is short and says exactly what the e-mail is about. *Hallo!!!* and *Ek* (I) say nothing, and the long sentence is too long and not polite."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die afkorting op ’n uitnodiging wat vra dat jy moet laat weet of jy kom, is ___.","en":"The abbreviation on an invitation that asks you to let them know whether you are coming is ___."},"answers":{"af":["RSVP","R.S.V.P."],"en":["RSVP","R.S.V.P."]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["NS","NB","bv."],"en":["NS","NB","bv."]}},"explain":{"af":"**RSVP** vra dat die gas moet antwoord. *NS* (naskrif) kom onderaan ’n brief, *NB* beteken ‘let wel’ en *bv.* beteken ‘byvoorbeeld’.","en":"**RSVP** asks the guest to reply. *NS* (*naskrif*, postscript) comes at the bottom of a letter, *NB* means ‘note well’ and *bv.* means ‘for example’."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke teksoort by sy kenmerk.","en":"Match each type of text to its feature."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"vriendskaplike brief","en":"friendly letter"},"r":{"af":"adres, datum, aanhef en slot","en":"address, date, greeting and ending"}},{"l":{"af":"dagboekinskrywing","en":"diary entry"},"r":{"af":"ek-vorm, gevoelens en die datum bo-aan","en":"first person, feelings and the date at the top"}},{"l":{"af":"uitnodiging","en":"invitation"},"r":{"af":"wat, waar, wanneer en teen wanneer jy moet antwoord","en":"what, where, when and by when you must reply"}},{"l":{"af":"resep","en":"recipe"},"r":{"af":"’n lys van wat jy nodig het en genommerde stappe","en":"a list of what you need and numbered steps"}},{"l":{"af":"e-pos","en":"e-mail"},"r":{"af":"’n onderwerpreël en ’n kort boodskap","en":"a subject line and a short message"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke teksoort het sy eie formaat. As jy die kenmerke ken, weet jy presies wat in jou skryfstuk moet staan.","en":"Each type of text has its own format. If you know the features, you know exactly what must be in your piece of writing."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is die beste **opsommingspunt** vir: *Elke oggend lê die meerkatte eers in die son om warm te word – dit lyk amper of hulle sonbaai soos mense op ’n strand!*","en":"Which sentence is the best **summary point** for: *Elke oggend lê die meerkatte eers in die son om warm te word – dit lyk amper of hulle sonbaai soos mense op ’n strand!* (Every morning the meerkats first lie in the sun to get warm – it almost looks as if they are sunbathing like people on a beach!)"},"options":[{"af":"Dit lyk of meerkatte soos mense op ’n strand sonbaai.","en":"Dit lyk of meerkatte soos mense op ’n strand sonbaai."},{"af":"Elke oggend lê die meerkatte eers in die son om warm te word.","en":"Elke oggend lê die meerkatte eers in die son om warm te word."},{"af":"Soggens warm meerkatte in die son op.","en":"Soggens warm meerkatte in die son op."},{"af":"Mense hou daarvan om op ’n strand te sonbaai.","en":"Mense hou daarvan om op ’n strand te sonbaai."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die hoofgedagte is dat meerkatte soggens in die son opwarm, kort en in eie woorde. Die vergelyking met mense is ’n voorbeeld wat wegval, en om die sin net oor te skryf, is nie ’n opsomming nie.","en":"The main idea is that meerkats warm up in the sun in the morning, said briefly and in your own words. The comparison with people is an example that falls away, and simply copying the sentence is not summarising."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Dagboekinskrywing word gewoonlik in die derde persoon (*hy* of *sy*) geskryf.","en":"A diary entry is usually written in the third person (*hy* or *sy*: he or she)."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Dagboek is jou eie storie, so jy skryf in die **ek-vorm**: *Vandag het ek …*","en":"False. A diary is your own story, so you write in the **first person** (*ek*): *Vandag het ek …* (Today I …)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter inligting ontbreek in hierdie uitnodiging? *Liewe Ravi / Kom na my verjaarsdagpartytjie op 22 November om 14:00. RSVP by my voor 15 November. / Groete / Thabo*","en":"What information is missing in this invitation? *Liewe Ravi / Kom na my verjaarsdagpartytjie op 22 November om 14:00. RSVP by my voor 15 November. / Groete / Thabo* (Dear Ravi, come to my birthday party on 22 November at 14:00. RSVP to me before 15 November. Regards, Thabo)"},"options":[{"af":"die datum","en":"the date"},{"af":"die plek","en":"the place"},{"af":"die tyd","en":"the time"},{"af":"wie die uitnodiging stuur","en":"who sends the invitation"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die uitnodiging sê wat (verjaarsdagpartytjie), wanneer (22 November om 14:00), wie (Thabo nooi Ravi) en RSVP, maar nie **waar** die partytjie is nie.","en":"The invitation says what (a birthday party), when (22 November at 14:00), who (Thabo invites Ravi) and RSVP, but not **where** the party is."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die lys van alles wat jy vir ’n resep gebruik, soos melk en piesang, heet die ___.","en":"The list of everything you use for a recipe, such as milk and banana, is called the ___ (give the Afrikaans term)."},"answers":{"af":["bestanddele"],"en":["bestanddele","ingredients"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["stappe","metode","titel"],"en":["stappe","metode","titel"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die **bestanddele** is die kos en goed wat jy nodig het, met hoeveelhede. Die **metode** is die genommerde stappe.","en":"The **bestanddele** (ingredients) are the food and things you need, with amounts. The **metode** (method) is the numbered steps."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin pas die beste in ’n **dagboekinskrywing**?","en":"Which sentence fits best in a **diary entry**?"},"options":[{"af":"Vandag het ek my eerste doel geskop, en ek voel so trots!","en":"Vandag het ek my eerste doel geskop, en ek voel so trots!"},{"af":"Hiermee wil ek formeel kla oor die toestand van die sokkerveld.","en":"Hiermee wil ek formeel kla oor die toestand van die sokkerveld."},{"af":"Meng die meel en die suiker in ’n groot bak.","en":"Meng die meel en die suiker in ’n groot bak."},{"af":"Kom na ons sokkerdag om 10:00!","en":"Kom na ons sokkerdag om 10:00!"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Dagboekinskrywing is in die ek-vorm en vertel wat gebeur het en hoe jy voel. Die ander sinne kom uit ’n formele brief, ’n resep en ’n uitnodiging.","en":"A diary entry is in the first person and tells what happened and how you feel. The other sentences come from a formal letter, a recipe and an invitation."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jou opsomming mag hoogstens 40 woorde hê, maar jou eerste poging het 52. Wat doen jy?","en":"Your summary may have at most 40 words, but your first attempt has 52. What do you do?"},"options":[{"af":"Skryf kleiner sodat dit minder lyk.","en":"Write smaller so that it looks like less."},{"af":"Los dit so, want 52 is naby genoeg aan 40.","en":"Leave it, because 52 is close enough to 40."},{"af":"Voeg nog ’n punt by sodat dit volledig is.","en":"Add another point so that it is complete."},{"af":"Haal voorbeelde en onnodige woorde uit totdat dit 40 of minder is.","en":"Remove examples and unnecessary words until it is 40 or fewer."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die woordlimiet is ’n reël, nie ’n voorstel nie. Skrap voorbeelde, beskrywings en herhaling totdat jy binne die limiet is, en tel weer.","en":"The word limit is a rule, not a suggestion. Cut examples, descriptions and repetition until you are within the limit, and count again."}}]},{"id":"afr5-t4-opstel","title":{"af":"Die opstel: verhalend en beskrywend","en":"The essay: narrative and descriptive"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die skryfproses kan volg, paragrawe met kernsinne kan skryf en ’n verhalende of beskrywende opstel met ’n pakkende titel kan beplan, skryf en verbeter.","en":"You will be able to follow the writing process, write paragraphs with topic sentences and plan, write and improve a narrative or descriptive essay with a catchy title."},"summary":{"af":"## Die skryfproses\n\n’n Goeie opstel skryf jy nie in een keer nie. Volg die vyf stappe van die **skryfproses**:\n1. **Beplan:** Maak ’n **woordweb**. Skryf die onderwerp in die middel en jou idees op lyne daarom. Besluit wat in elke paragraaf kom.\n2. **Konsep:** Skryf jou eerste weergawe. Moenie nou oor elke fout bekommer nie; kry jou idees op papier.\n3. **Redigeer:** Lees die konsep krities. Is die volgorde logies? Kan jy ’n beter woord kies? Is daar herhaling?\n4. **Proeflees:** Soek spel-, leesteken- en taalfoute, woord vir woord.\n5. **Netskrif:** Skryf die finale weergawe netjies en leesbaar oor.\n\n## Paragrawe en kernsinne\n\nElke **paragraaf** gaan oor **een hoofgedagte**. Die **kernsin**, gewoonlik die eerste sin, sê waaroor die paragraaf gaan. Die ander sinne gee besonderhede.\n\n*Ons hond, Wollie, is ’n regte deugniet. Hy steel Pa se sokkies van die wasgoeddraad. Hy grawe gate in Ma se groentetuin. Tog kan niemand lank vir hom kwaad bly nie.* (Die eerste sin is die kernsin.)\n\nBegin ’n nuwe paragraaf wanneer die tyd, plek of gedagte verander.\n\n## Die verhalende opstel\n\n’n **Verhalende opstel** vertel ’n storie, gewoonlik in die **verlede tyd** (*het … ge-*).\n- **Inleiding:** Stel die karakters, tyd en plek bekend, en vang die leser se aandag.\n- **Middel:** Die gebeure ontwikkel. Daar is ’n **probleem**, en die spanning bou op tot die **klimaks**.\n- **Slot:** Die probleem word opgelos. Vertel hoe die karakters voel of wat hulle geleer het.\n\nGebruik **volgordewoorde** om die gebeure te verbind: *eers, toe, daarna, later, skielik, uiteindelik*. Ná so ’n woord vooraan kom die werkwoord op die tweede plek: *Daarna **het** ons koek geëet.*\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *En toe … en toe … en toe …* maak jou storie vervelig. Wissel jou volgordewoorde af en begin sinne op verskillende maniere.\n\n## Die beskrywende opstel\n\n’n **Beskrywende opstel** skilder ’n **prent met woorde** van ’n plek, mens, dier of oomblik. Gebruik:\n- al jou **sintuie**: wat sien, hoor, ruik, proe en voel jy?\n- treffende **byvoeglike naamwoorde**: nie net *mooi* nie, maar *glinsterend, helderblou, sonnig*;\n- **beeldspraak**, soos ’n vergelyking of metafoor.\n\n| Swak | Beter |\n|---|---|\n| Die mark was besig. | Die mark gons soos ’n byenes: verkopers roep hard, en die soet geur van vars koeksisters hang in die lug. |\n| Die see was mooi. | Die helderblou see glinster in die son, en die golwe sis oor die warm sand. |\n\n## Titel en algemene foute\n\n- Kies ’n **kort, pakkende titel** wat nuuskierig maak, maar nie die hele storie verklap nie: *Waar is Wollie?*\n- Bly in **een tyd**: moenie tussen *is* en *was* rondspring nie.\n- Onthou die **dubbele ontkenning**: *Ons het die bus **nie** gehaal **nie**.*\n- Vermy **anglisismes**: *Ons het die bus gehaal* (nie *gevang* nie). *Ons het lekker gekuier* (nie *Ons het ’n goeie tyd gehad* nie).\n- Gebruik **hoofletters** en **leestekens** reg, en kontroleer jou spelling.\n\n> **Onthou:** Beplan → konsep → redigeer → proeflees → netskrif. Elke stap maak jou opstel beter.","en":"## The writing process\n\nYou don’t write a good essay (*opstel*) in one go. Follow the five steps of the **writing process** (*skryfproses*):\n1. **Plan** (*beplan*): Make a **word web** (*woordweb*). Write the topic in the middle and your ideas on lines around it. Decide what goes in each paragraph.\n2. **Draft** (*konsep*): Write your first version. Don’t worry about every mistake now; get your ideas on paper.\n3. **Edit** (*redigeer*): Read the draft critically. Is the order logical? Can you choose a better word? Is there repetition?\n4. **Proofread** (*proeflees*): Look for spelling, punctuation and language mistakes, word by word.\n5. **Final copy** (*netskrif*): Copy the final version out neatly and legibly.\n\n## Paragraphs and topic sentences\n\nEach **paragraph** (*paragraaf*) is about **one main idea**. The **topic sentence** (*kernsin*), usually the first sentence, says what the paragraph is about. The other sentences give details.\n\n*Ons hond, Wollie, is ’n regte deugniet. Hy steel Pa se sokkies van die wasgoeddraad. Hy grawe gate in Ma se groentetuin. Tog kan niemand lank vir hom kwaad bly nie.* (Our dog, Wollie, is a real rascal. He steals Dad’s socks from the washing line. He digs holes in Mom’s vegetable garden. Yet nobody can stay angry with him for long.) The first sentence is the topic sentence.\n\nStart a new paragraph when the time, place or idea changes.\n\n## The narrative essay\n\nA **narrative essay** (*verhalende opstel*) tells a story, usually in the **past tense** (*het … ge-*).\n- **Introduction** (*inleiding*): Introduce the characters, time and place, and catch the reader’s attention.\n- **Middle** (*middel*): The events develop. There is a **problem**, and the tension builds up to the **climax**.\n- **Conclusion** (*slot*): The problem is solved. Tell how the characters feel or what they learnt.\n\nUse **sequence words** (*volgordewoorde*) to link the events: *eers* (first), *toe* (then), *daarna* (after that), *later*, *skielik* (suddenly), *uiteindelik* (finally). After such a word at the start, the verb comes in second place: *Daarna **het** ons koek geëet.* (After that we ate cake.)\n\n> **Common mistake:** *En toe … en toe … en toe …* (and then … and then …) makes your story boring. Vary your sequence words and start sentences in different ways.\n\n## The descriptive essay\n\nA **descriptive essay** (*beskrywende opstel*) paints a **picture with words** of a place, person, animal or moment. Use:\n- all your **senses** (*sintuie*): what do you see, hear, smell, taste and feel?\n- striking **adjectives** (*byvoeglike naamwoorde*): not just *mooi* (pretty), but *glinsterend* (sparkling), *helderblou* (bright blue), *sonnig* (sunny);\n- **figures of speech** (*beeldspraak*), such as a simile or metaphor.\n\n| Weak | Better |\n|---|---|\n| *Die mark was besig.* (The market was busy.) | *Die mark gons soos ’n byenes: verkopers roep hard, en die soet geur van vars koeksisters hang in die lug.* (The market buzzes like a beehive: sellers call loudly, and the sweet smell of fresh koeksisters hangs in the air.) |\n| *Die see was mooi.* (The sea was pretty.) | *Die helderblou see glinster in die son, en die golwe sis oor die warm sand.* (The bright blue sea sparkles in the sun, and the waves hiss over the warm sand.) |\n\n## Title and common mistakes\n\n- Choose a **short, catchy title** that makes the reader curious but does not give away the whole story: *Waar is Wollie?* (Where is Wollie?)\n- Stay in **one tense**: don’t jump between *is* and *was*.\n- Remember the **double negative**: *Ons het die bus **nie** gehaal **nie**.* (We did not catch the bus.)\n- Avoid **anglicisms** (*anglisismes*): *Ons het die bus gehaal* (not *gevang*, a direct translation of “caught”). *Ons het lekker gekuier* (not *Ons het ’n goeie tyd gehad*, from the English “We had a good time”).\n- Use **capital letters** and **punctuation** correctly, and check your spelling.\n\n> **Remember:** Plan → draft → edit → proofread → final copy. Every step makes your essay better."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Woordweb","en":"Word web (woordweb)"},"def":{"af":"’n Beplanningsprentjie met die onderwerp in die middel en idees op lyne daarom.","en":"A planning diagram with the topic in the middle and ideas on lines around it."}},{"term":{"af":"Konsep","en":"Draft (konsep)"},"def":{"af":"Die eerste weergawe van jou opstel, wat jy nog gaan verbeter.","en":"The first version of your essay, which you will still improve."}},{"term":{"af":"Redigeer","en":"Edit (redigeer)"},"def":{"af":"Jou konsep verbeter: die volgorde, woordkeuse en sinne beter maak.","en":"Improve your draft: make the order, choice of words and sentences better."}},{"term":{"af":"Proeflees","en":"Proofread (proeflees)"},"def":{"af":"Woord vir woord na spel-, leesteken- en taalfoute soek en dit regmaak.","en":"Look for spelling, punctuation and language mistakes word by word and correct them."}},{"term":{"af":"Netskrif","en":"Final copy (netskrif)"},"def":{"af":"Die finale, netjiese weergawe van jou opstel wat jy inhandig.","en":"The final, neat version of your essay that you hand in."}},{"term":{"af":"Kernsin","en":"Topic sentence (kernsin)"},"def":{"af":"Die sin, gewoonlik die eerste, wat sê waaroor ’n paragraaf gaan.","en":"The sentence, usually the first, that says what a paragraph is about."}},{"term":{"af":"Verhalende opstel","en":"Narrative essay (verhalende opstel)"},"def":{"af":"’n Opstel wat ’n storie vertel, met ’n inleiding, middel en slot.","en":"An essay that tells a story, with an introduction, middle and conclusion."}},{"term":{"af":"Beskrywende opstel","en":"Descriptive essay (beskrywende opstel)"},"def":{"af":"’n Opstel wat met sintuie, byvoeglike naamwoorde en beeldspraak ’n prent met woorde skilder.","en":"An essay that paints a picture with words using the senses, adjectives and figures of speech."}},{"term":{"af":"Volgordewoorde","en":"Sequence words (volgordewoorde)"},"def":{"af":"Woorde wat wys in watter volgorde dinge gebeur: *eers, daarna, later, uiteindelik*.","en":"Words that show in which order things happen: *eers, daarna, later, uiteindelik* (first, after that, later, finally)."}},{"term":{"af":"Anglisisme","en":"Anglicism (anglisisme)"},"def":{"af":"’n Fout waar ’n Engelse uitdrukking woord vir woord in Afrikaans vertaal word: *die bus gevang* in plaas van *die bus gehaal*.","en":"A mistake where an English expression is translated word for word into Afrikaans: *die bus gevang* instead of *die bus gehaal* (caught the bus)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Beplan met ’n woordweb","en":"Planning with a word web"},"problem":{"af":"Beplan ’n verhalende opstel oor ’n aand toe die krag skielik uitgegaan het.","en":"Plan a narrative essay about an evening when the power suddenly went off."},"steps":[{"af":"Skryf *Krag af!* in die middel van jou woordweb.","en":"Write *Krag af!* (Power off!) in the middle of your word web."},{"af":"Trek lyne na idees: **wie** (ek, my sussie, Ma), **waar** (by die huis, met aandete), **probleem** (stikdonker, kerse soek, ’n vreemde geluid), **klimaks** (die “spook” is die kat), **slot** (ons lag en speel speletjies by kerslig).","en":"Draw lines to ideas: **who** (me, my little sister, Mom), **where** (at home, during supper), **problem** (pitch dark, looking for candles, a strange noise), **climax** (the “ghost” is the cat), **ending** (we laugh and play games by candlelight)."},{"af":"Rangskik die idees in paragrawe: inleiding, middel (probleem en klimaks) en slot.","en":"Arrange the ideas into paragraphs: introduction, middle (problem and climax) and conclusion."}],"answer":{"af":"Paragraaf 1: aandete, en die krag gaan af. Paragraaf 2: kerse soek en ’n vreemde geluid. Paragraaf 3: die “spook” is die kat. Paragraaf 4: lekker lag en speletjies by kerslig.","en":"Paragraph 1: supper, and the power goes off. Paragraph 2: looking for candles and a strange noise. Paragraph 3: the “ghost” is the cat. Paragraph 4: laughing and games by candlelight."}},{"title":{"af":"Maak ’n sin beskrywend","en":"Make a sentence descriptive"},"problem":{"af":"Verbeter die sin met sintuie, byvoeglike naamwoorde en beeldspraak: *Die kombuis is lekker.*","en":"Improve the sentence with the senses, adjectives and figures of speech: *Die kombuis is lekker.* (The kitchen is nice.)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Reuk:** wat ruik jy? *die geur van vars brood*","en":"**Smell:** what do you smell? *die geur van vars brood* (the smell of fresh bread)"},{"af":"**Gehoor:** wat hoor jy? *die oond tik saggies*","en":"**Hearing:** what do you hear? *die oond tik saggies* (the oven ticks softly)"},{"af":"**Gevoel** en **beeldspraak:** die warmte voel soos ’n drukkie: *so warm soos ’n drukkie*.","en":"**Touch** and **figure of speech:** the warmth feels like a hug: *so warm soos ’n drukkie* (as warm as a hug)."},{"af":"Sit alles saam in een of twee sinne in die teenwoordige tyd.","en":"Put everything together in one or two sentences in the present tense."}],"answer":{"af":"Die kombuis is so warm soos ’n drukkie: die geur van vars brood hang in die lug, en die oond tik saggies.","en":"*Die kombuis is so warm soos ’n drukkie: die geur van vars brood hang in die lug, en die oond tik saggies.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Vervang *en toe*","en":"Replace *en toe*"},"problem":{"af":"Verbeter: *Ons het by die dam gekom en toe het ons geswem en toe het ons geëet en toe het ons huis toe gegaan.*","en":"Improve: *Ons het by die dam gekom en toe het ons geswem en toe het ons geëet en toe het ons huis toe gegaan.* (We got to the dam and then we swam and then we ate and then we went home.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Breek die lang sin op in korter sinne.","en":"Break the long sentence up into shorter sentences."},{"af":"Gebruik verskillende volgordewoorde: *eers, daarna, uiteindelik*.","en":"Use different sequence words: *eers, daarna, uiteindelik*."},{"af":"Ná ’n volgordewoord vooraan kom die werkwoord op die tweede plek: *Daarna **het** ons …*","en":"After a sequence word at the start, the verb comes in second place: *Daarna **het** ons …*"},{"af":"Voeg ’n paar besonderhede by sodat die leser die prent sien: *onder die bome, moeg maar gelukkig*.","en":"Add a few details so the reader can see the picture: *onder die bome* (under the trees), *moeg maar gelukkig* (tired but happy)."}],"answer":{"af":"Ons het by die dam aangekom. Eers het ons geswem. Daarna het ons onder die bome geëet. Uiteindelik het ons moeg maar gelukkig huis toe gegaan.","en":"*Ons het by die dam aangekom. Eers het ons geswem. Daarna het ons onder die bome geëet. Uiteindelik het ons moeg maar gelukkig huis toe gegaan.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Proeflees","en":"Proofreading"},"problem":{"af":"Vind en verbeter die vier foute: *gister het Lerato en Ek in die reen gespeel, en ons het nie koud gekry.*","en":"Find and correct the four mistakes: *gister het Lerato en Ek in die reen gespeel, en ons het nie koud gekry.* (Yesterday Lerato and I played in the rain, and we did not get cold.)"},"steps":[{"af":"’n Sin begin met ’n hoofletter: *Gister*.","en":"A sentence starts with a capital letter: *Gister*."},{"af":"*ek* kry net vooraan in ’n sin ’n hoofletter: *Lerato en ek*.","en":"*ek* only takes a capital at the start of a sentence: *Lerato en ek*."},{"af":"*reën* kry ’n deelteken.","en":"*reën* (rain) takes a diaeresis."},{"af":"Die ontkenning het twee keer *nie* nodig: *nie koud gekry nie*.","en":"The negative needs *nie* twice: *nie koud gekry nie*."}],"answer":{"af":"Gister het Lerato en ek in die reën gespeel, en ons het nie koud gekry nie.","en":"*Gister het Lerato en ek in die reën gespeel, en ons het nie koud gekry nie.*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **eerste** stap van die skryfproses?","en":"What is the **first** step of the writing process?"},"options":[{"af":"beplan, byvoorbeeld met ’n woordweb","en":"plan, for example with a word web"},{"af":"skryf die netskrif","en":"write the final copy"},{"af":"proeflees vir spelfoute","en":"proofread for spelling mistakes"},{"af":"redigeer die konsep","en":"edit the draft"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Eers beplan jy: jy versamel idees in ’n woordweb en besluit op die volgorde. Jy kan nie ’n konsep redigeer of proeflees voordat jy dit geskryf het nie.","en":"First you plan: you collect ideas in a word web and decide on the order. You cannot edit or proofread a draft before you have written it."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Verhalende opstel word gewoonlik in die verlede tyd geskryf.","en":"A narrative essay is usually written in the past tense."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Verhaal vertel wat gebeur het, so jy skryf meestal in die verlede tyd: *Ons het … gespeel.*","en":"True. A story tells what happened, so you mostly write in the past tense: *Ons het … gespeel.* (We played …)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sintuig gebruik jy in *die soet geur van vars koeksisters*?","en":"Which sense do you use in *die soet geur van vars koeksisters* (the sweet smell of fresh koeksisters)?"},"options":[{"af":"smaak","en":"taste (*smaak*)"},{"af":"gehoor","en":"hearing (*gehoor*)"},{"af":"reuk","en":"smell (*reuk*)"},{"af":"gesig","en":"sight (*gesig*)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n *Geur* is iets wat jy ruik, so dit is die sintuig **reuk**. As jy die koeksister eet en beskryf hoe dit proe, gebruik jy smaak.","en":"A *geur* (smell) is something you smell, so it is the sense of **smell**. If you eat the koeksister and describe how it tastes, you use taste."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die sin wat sê waaroor ’n paragraaf gaan, heet die ___.","en":"In Afrikaans, the sentence that says what a paragraph is about is called the ___ (topic sentence)."},"answers":{"af":["kernsin"],"en":["kernsin","topic sentence"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["slotsin","titel","konsep"],"en":["slotsin","titel","konsep"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die **kernsin** is gewoonlik die eerste sin van die paragraaf. Die ander sinne gee besonderhede daaroor.","en":"The **kernsin** (topic sentence) is usually the first sentence of the paragraph. The other sentences give details about it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die beste volgordewoord: *Ons het die hele middag gesoek. ___ het ons die hondjie onder die stoep gekry.*","en":"Choose the best sequence word: *Ons het die hele middag gesoek. ___ het ons die hondjie onder die stoep gekry.* (We searched the whole afternoon. ___ we found the puppy under the stoep.)"},"options":[{"af":"Eers","en":"Eers"},{"af":"Môre","en":"Môre"},{"af":"Volgende week","en":"Volgende week"},{"af":"Uiteindelik","en":"Uiteindelik"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ná ’n lang soektog vind hulle die hondjie aan die einde: *Uiteindelik*. *Eers* is vir die begin, en *môre* en *volgende week* verwys na die toekoms, terwyl die sin in die verlede tyd is.","en":"After a long search they find the puppy at the end: *Uiteindelik* (finally). *Eers* (first) is for the beginning, and *môre* (tomorrow) and *volgende week* (next week) refer to the future, while the sentence is in the past tense."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke stap van die skryfproses by wat jy doen.","en":"Match each step of the writing process to what you do."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"beplan","en":"plan (*beplan*)"},"r":{"af":"maak ’n woordweb met idees","en":"make a word web with ideas"}},{"l":{"af":"konsep","en":"draft (*konsep*)"},"r":{"af":"skryf jou eerste weergawe","en":"write your first version"}},{"l":{"af":"redigeer","en":"edit (*redigeer*)"},"r":{"af":"verbeter die volgorde en woordkeuse","en":"improve the order and choice of words"}},{"l":{"af":"proeflees","en":"proofread (*proeflees*)"},"r":{"af":"soek spel- en leestekenfoute","en":"look for spelling and punctuation mistakes"}},{"l":{"af":"netskrif","en":"final copy (*netskrif*)"},"r":{"af":"skryf die finale weergawe netjies oor","en":"copy out the final version neatly"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die stappe volg in hierdie volgorde op mekaar. Redigeer gaan oor die inhoud en woordkeuse; proeflees gaan oor klein foute soos spelling.","en":"The steps follow each other in this order. Editing is about the content and choice of words; proofreading is about small mistakes such as spelling."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is die **beste beskrywende sin**?","en":"Which sentence is the **best descriptive sentence**?"},"options":[{"af":"Die kombuis is mooi en lekker.","en":"Die kombuis is mooi en lekker."},{"af":"Die warm, soet geur van vars brood vul die kombuis, en die oond tik saggies.","en":"Die warm, soet geur van vars brood vul die kombuis, en die oond tik saggies."},{"af":"Ma bak elke Saterdag brood.","en":"Ma bak elke Saterdag brood."},{"af":"Daar is brood in die kombuis.","en":"Daar is brood in die kombuis."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Hierdie sin gebruik verskeie sintuie (reuk, gevoel, gehoor) en treffende byvoeglike naamwoorde (*warm, soet, vars*). Die ander sinne gee net feite of vae woorde soos *mooi*.","en":"This sentence uses several senses (smell, touch, hearing) and striking adjectives (*warm, soet, vars*: warm, sweet, fresh). The other sentences only give facts or vague words like *mooi* (pretty)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vermy die anglisisme: *Ons het die bus net betyds ___.* (nie *gevang* nie)","en":"Avoid the anglicism: *Ons het die bus net betyds ___.* (We caught the bus just in time.) (not *gevang*)"},"answers":{"af":["gehaal"],"en":["gehaal"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["gekry","geneem","gegryp"],"en":["gekry","geneem","gegryp"]}},"explain":{"af":"In Afrikaans **haal** jy ’n bus: *Ons het die bus gehaal.* *Gevang* is ’n direkte vertaling van die Engelse *caught*.","en":"In Afrikaans you **haal** a bus: *Ons het die bus gehaal.* *Gevang* is a direct translation of the English *caught*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter titel is die beste vir ’n verhalende opstel oor ’n hond wat verdwaal en weer gevind word?","en":"Which title is best for a narrative essay about a dog that gets lost and is found again?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Opstel oor ons hond wat weggeraak het en wat ons toe weer gekry het","en":"’n Opstel oor ons hond wat weggeraak het en wat ons toe weer gekry het"},{"af":"Waar is Wollie?","en":"Waar is Wollie?"},{"af":"Hond","en":"Hond"},{"af":"My opstel","en":"My opstel"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Goeie titel is kort en pakkend en maak jou nuuskierig, sonder om die einde te verklap. Die lang titel vertel alles, en *Hond* en *My opstel* is te vaag.","en":"A good title is short and catchy and makes you curious, without giving away the ending. The long title tells everything, and *Hond* (Dog) and *My opstel* (My essay) are too vague."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Hoe meer keer jy *en toe* gebruik, hoe beter vloei jou storie.","en":"The more times you use *en toe* (and then), the better your story flows."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. *En toe … en toe …* maak ’n storie eentonig. Gebruik verskillende volgordewoorde soos *eers, daarna, skielik* en *uiteindelik*.","en":"False. *En toe … en toe …* makes a story monotonous. Use different sequence words such as *eers, daarna, skielik* and *uiteindelik*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat hoort in die **slot** van ’n verhalende opstel?","en":"What belongs in the **conclusion** of a narrative essay?"},"options":[{"af":"die eerste kennismaking met die karakters en die plek","en":"the first introduction to the characters and the place"},{"af":"die spannendste oomblik, wanneer die probleem op sy ergste is","en":"the most exciting moment, when the problem is at its worst"},{"af":"’n lys van al die idees uit jou woordweb","en":"a list of all the ideas from your word web"},{"af":"hoe die probleem opgelos word en hoe die karakters voel","en":"how the problem is solved and how the characters feel"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"In die slot word die probleem opgelos en rond jy die storie af. Die karakters word in die inleiding voorgestel, en die klimaks kom in die middel.","en":"In the conclusion the problem is solved and you round off the story. The characters are introduced in the introduction, and the climax comes in the middle."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi met die regte ontkenning: *Ek het my huiswerk nie vergeet ___.*","en":"Complete with the correct negative: *Ek het my huiswerk nie vergeet ___.* (I did not forget my homework.)"},"answers":{"af":["nie"],"en":["nie"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["niks","nooit","ook"],"en":["niks","nooit","ook"]}},"explain":{"af":"Afrikaans het ’n **dubbele ontkenning**: die eerste *nie* staan voor *vergeet* en die tweede *nie* heel aan die einde: *… nie vergeet nie.*","en":"Afrikaans has a **double negative**: the first *nie* comes before *vergeet* (forgotten) and the second *nie* right at the end: *… nie vergeet nie.*"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is die beste **inleiding** vir ’n verhalende opstel?","en":"Which sentence is the best **introduction** for a narrative essay?"},"options":[{"af":"Ek gaan nou vir julle ’n storie oor iets vertel.","en":"Ek gaan nou vir julle ’n storie oor iets vertel."},{"af":"Dit is die einde van my storie.","en":"Dit is die einde van my storie."},{"af":"Die oomblik toe ek die vreemde geluid op die solder hoor, het my hart in my keel geklop.","en":"Die oomblik toe ek die vreemde geluid op die solder hoor, het my hart in my keel geklop."},{"af":"Hierdie opstel gaan oor ’n dag.","en":"Hierdie opstel gaan oor ’n dag."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Goeie inleiding vang die leser se aandag dadelik en maak hom nuuskierig. Die ander sinne is vervelig of hoort nie aan die begin nie.","en":"A good introduction catches the reader’s attention at once and makes them curious. The other sentences are boring or do not belong at the beginning."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wanneer begin jy ’n **nuwe paragraaf**?","en":"When do you start a **new paragraph**?"},"options":[{"af":"wanneer die tyd, plek of gedagte verander","en":"when the time, place or idea changes"},{"af":"ná elke derde sin","en":"after every third sentence"},{"af":"wanneer die bladsy vol is","en":"when the page is full"},{"af":"net aan die begin van die opstel","en":"only at the beginning of the essay"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Elke paragraaf het een hoofgedagte. As die storie na ’n nuwe tyd, plek of gedagte beweeg, begin jy ’n nuwe paragraaf, nie ná ’n vaste aantal sinne nie.","en":"Each paragraph has one main idea. When the story moves to a new time, place or idea, you start a new paragraph, not after a fixed number of sentences."}}]}]}]},"english":{"id":"english","grade":5,"name":{"af":"Engels Eerste Addisionele Taal","en":"English First Additional Language"},"short":{"af":"Eng","en":"Eng"},"icon":"🗣️","color":"#dc2626","intro":{"af":"Engels Eerste Addisionele Taal in Graad 5 bou jou lees-, skryf- en taalvaardighede in Engels: jy lees verskillende tekste met begrip, leer grammatika soos tye, woordsoorte en leestekens, en skryf kort stukke soos briewe, dagboekinskrywings en paragrawe. In die Novembereksamen lees jy tekste en beantwoord vrae daaroor, beantwoord taalvrae in konteks en skryf jy ’n kort stuk, soos ’n paragraaf, ’n brief of ’n storie.","en":"English First Additional Language in Grade 5 builds your reading, writing and language skills in English: you read different texts with understanding, learn grammar such as tenses, parts of speech and punctuation, and write short pieces such as letters, diary entries and paragraphs. In the November exam you read texts and answer questions about them, answer language questions in context and write a short piece, such as a paragraph, a letter or a story."},"examTips":[{"af":"Lees eers die vrae, vluglees dan die leesstuk en soeklees daarna vir die antwoorde.","en":"Read the questions first, then skim the passage, and then scan it for the answers."},{"af":"Antwoord in Engelse volsinne en in jou eie woorde, tensy die vraag sê jy moet aanhaal. Kyk na die punte: 2 punte vra dikwels twee feite.","en":"Answer in full English sentences and in your own words, unless the question asks you to quote. Look at the marks: 2 marks often ask for two facts."},{"af":"Kyk na die tydsaanduider (*yesterday, now, tomorrow*) voor jy ’n werkwoord skryf, en onthou die -s by *he, she, it*: *she walks*.","en":"Look at the time word (*yesterday, now, tomorrow*) before you write a verb, and remember the -s with *he, she, it*: *she walks*."},{"af":"Leer onreëlmatige meervoude (*children, mice, feet*) en onreëlmatige werkwoorde (*went, saw, bought*) uit jou kop – hulle kom gereeld in die eksamen voor.","en":"Learn irregular plurals (*children, mice, feet*) and irregular verbs (*went, saw, bought*) by heart – they often appear in the exam."},{"af":"Lees jou antwoorde aan die einde oor: hoofletters, punte, vraagtekens, afkappingstekens en spelling.","en":"Read through your answers at the end: capital letters, full stops, question marks, apostrophes and spelling."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"DBE Reënboog-werkboeke (Graad 5)","en":"DBE Rainbow Workbooks (Grade 5)"},"url":"https://www.education.gov.za/Curriculum/Workbooks.aspx","note":{"af":"Gratis amptelike CAPS-werkboeke, ook vir Engels Eerste Addisionele Taal.","en":"Free official CAPS workbooks, also for English First Additional Language."}},{"title":{"af":"Siyavula: oop handboeke en oefening","en":"Siyavula: open textbooks and practice"},"url":"https://www.siyavula.com","note":{"af":"Gratis oop handboeke en oefenvrae.","en":"Free open textbooks and practice questions."}}],"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Lees en woorde","en":"Reading and words"},"topics":[{"id":"eng5-t1-reading-comprehension","title":{"af":"Leesbegrip","en":"Reading comprehension"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal ’n Engelse leesstuk kan vluglees en soeklees, die hoofgedagte en feite kan vind, feit en mening kan onderskei en vrae in volsinne en in jou eie woorde kan beantwoord.","en":"You will be able to skim and scan an English passage, find the main idea and facts, tell fact from opinion and answer questions in full sentences and in your own words."},"summary":{"af":"## Vluglees en soeklees\n\nGoeie lesers lees nie elke teks op dieselfde manier nie.\n\n- **Vluglees** (*skimming*) beteken jy lees **vinnig** om die **algemene idee** te kry. Lees die titel, die eerste en laaste sin van elke paragraaf, en kyk na die prente.\n- **Soeklees** (*scanning*) beteken jy soek vinnig na **een spesifieke besonderheid**, soos ’n naam, ’n getal, ’n dag of ’n sleutelwoord. Jou oë spring oor die teks totdat jy dit kry.\n\n> **Onthou:** Lees eers die vrae en dan die leesstuk. Dan weet jy waarna jy moet soek.\n\n## Die leesstuk\n\nDie leesstuk bly in Engels, want jy oefen jou Engels.\n\n**A Visit to the Penguins**\n\nLast Saturday, Nomsa and her grandfather drove to a beach near Simon’s Town. They walked along a wooden path and soon heard a loud noise. “Is that a donkey?” Nomsa asked. Her grandfather laughed. “No, those are African penguins. They bray like donkeys to call each other.”\n\nHundreds of black-and-white birds stood on the big rocks. Some waddled down to the cold water to catch small fish. A sign next to the path said that African penguins are endangered. There are fewer fish in the sea for them to eat, and oil from ships can harm them.\n\nNomsa took out her notebook and drew a penguin. “These are the cutest birds in the world,” she said. On the way home, she was very quiet. Then she said, “Grandpa, one day I want to help the penguins.”\n\nNuttige woorde: *bray* = balk, *waddled* = gewaggel, *endangered* = bedreig, *harm* = skade doen.\n\n## Hoofgedagte en feite\n\nDie **hoofgedagte** (*main idea*) is waaroor die hele teks hoofsaaklik gaan. Vra: Oor *wie* of *wat* gaan dit, en wat *gebeur*? Hier: *Nomsa visits African penguins, learns that they are in danger and wants to help them.*\n\n’n Sin soos *the birds stood on the big rocks* is net ’n **besonderheid** (*detail*), nie die hoofgedagte nie.\n\n## Letterlike vrae en afleidingsvrae\n\n| Soort vraag | Waar is die antwoord? | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Letterlik** (*literal*) | Dit staan in die teks. Soeklees om dit te kry. | *Who went to the beach with Nomsa?* – *Her grandfather went with her.* |\n| **Afleiding** (*inferential*) | Dit staan nie presies daar nie. Gebruik leidrade in die teks en wat jy self weet. | *Why was Nomsa quiet on the way home?* – *She was probably thinking about how she could help the penguins.* |\n\nBy ’n afleidingsvraag wys jy jou **leidraad**: sy was stil, en daarna het sy gesê sy wil die pikkewyne help.\n\n## Feit of mening?\n\n- ’n **Feit** (*fact*) kan **bewys** of nagegaan word: *African penguins bray like donkeys.*\n- ’n **Mening** (*opinion*) is wat iemand **dink of voel**. Ander mense kan daarmee verskil: *These are the cutest birds in the world.*\n\nWoorde soos *best, cutest, beautiful, boring, I think* en *I feel* wys dikwels ’n mening.\n\n## Woordbetekenis uit die konteks\n\nDie **konteks** is die woorde en sinne rondom ’n nuwe woord. Soek leidrade daarin. *Some waddled down to the cold water* – pikkewyne het kort beentjies, so *waddled* beteken hulle het met kort treetjies geloop en van kant tot kant geswaai. Toets jou raaiskoot: sit jou betekenis in die plek van die woord en kyk of die sin nog sin maak.\n\n## Antwoord in volsinne en in jou eie woorde\n\n- Gebruik ’n deel van die **vraag** in jou antwoord. *Where did they go?* → *They went to a beach near Simon’s Town.* (nie net *a beach* nie)\n- **Eie woorde:** verduidelik self; moenie net ’n hele sin oorskryf nie. **Haal** net **aan** (*quote*) as die vraag dit vra.\n- Kyk na die **punte**: 2 punte beteken dikwels twee feite.\n- Antwoord altyd in **Engels**, al dink jy eers in Afrikaans.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om met een woord of ’n oorgeskrewe reël te antwoord. *Grandfather.* is nie ’n volsin nie. Skryf: *Nomsa went to the beach with her grandfather.*","en":"## Skimming and scanning\n\nGood readers do not read every text in the same way.\n\n- **Skimming** means reading **quickly** to get the **general idea**. Read the title, the first and last sentence of each paragraph, and look at the pictures.\n- **Scanning** means looking quickly for **one specific detail**, such as a name, a number, a day or a key word. Your eyes jump over the text until you find it.\n\n> **Remember:** Read the questions first and then the passage. Then you know what to look for.\n\n## The reading passage\n\n**A Visit to the Penguins**\n\nLast Saturday, Nomsa and her grandfather drove to a beach near Simon’s Town. They walked along a wooden path and soon heard a loud noise. “Is that a donkey?” Nomsa asked. Her grandfather laughed. “No, those are African penguins. They bray like donkeys to call each other.”\n\nHundreds of black-and-white birds stood on the big rocks. Some waddled down to the cold water to catch small fish. A sign next to the path said that African penguins are endangered. There are fewer fish in the sea for them to eat, and oil from ships can harm them.\n\nNomsa took out her notebook and drew a penguin. “These are the cutest birds in the world,” she said. On the way home, she was very quiet. Then she said, “Grandpa, one day I want to help the penguins.”\n\nUseful words: *bray* = make a loud “hee-haw” sound, *waddled* = walked with short, swaying steps, *endangered* = in danger of dying out, *harm* = hurt or damage.\n\n## Main idea and facts\n\nThe **main idea** is what the whole text is mostly about. Ask: *Who* or *what* is it about, and what *happens*? Here: *Nomsa visits African penguins, learns that they are in danger and wants to help them.*\n\nA sentence such as *the birds stood on the big rocks* is only a **detail**, not the main idea.\n\n## Literal and inferential questions\n\n| Type of question | Where is the answer? | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Literal** | It is written in the text. Scan to find it. | *Who went to the beach with Nomsa?* – *Her grandfather went with her.* |\n| **Inferential** | It is not written exactly. Use clues in the text and what you already know. | *Why was Nomsa quiet on the way home?* – *She was probably thinking about how she could help the penguins.* |\n\nFor an inferential question, show your **clue**: she was quiet, and afterwards she said she wanted to help the penguins.\n\n## Fact or opinion?\n\n- A **fact** can be **proven** or checked: *African penguins bray like donkeys.*\n- An **opinion** is what someone **thinks or feels**. Other people may disagree: *These are the cutest birds in the world.*\n\nWords such as *best, cutest, beautiful, boring, I think* and *I feel* often show an opinion.\n\n## Word meaning from context\n\nThe **context** is the words and sentences around a new word. Look for clues in them. *Some waddled down to the cold water* – penguins have short legs, so *waddled* means they walked with short steps, swaying from side to side. Test your guess: put your meaning in the place of the word and check that the sentence still makes sense.\n\n## Answer in full sentences and in your own words\n\n- Use part of the **question** in your answer. *Where did they go?* → *They went to a beach near Simon’s Town.* (not just *a beach*)\n- **Own words:** explain it yourself; do not just copy a whole sentence. Only **quote** when the question asks you to.\n- Look at the **marks**: 2 marks often means two facts.\n- Always answer in **English**, even if you first think in another language.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Answering with one word or a copied line. *Grandfather.* is not a full sentence. Write: *Nomsa went to the beach with her grandfather.*"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Vluglees (*skimming*)","en":"Skimming"},"def":{"af":"Vinnig deur ’n teks lees om die algemene idee te kry.","en":"Reading a text quickly to get the general idea."}},{"term":{"af":"Soeklees (*scanning*)","en":"Scanning"},"def":{"af":"Vinnig deur ’n teks kyk om een spesifieke besonderheid, soos ’n naam of ’n getal, te vind.","en":"Looking quickly through a text to find one specific detail, such as a name or a number."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoofgedagte (*main idea*)","en":"Main idea"},"def":{"af":"Waaroor die hele teks hoofsaaklik gaan.","en":"What the whole text is mostly about."}},{"term":{"af":"Feit (*fact*)","en":"Fact"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat bewys of nagegaan kan word, soos *Penguins are birds.*","en":"Something that can be proven or checked, such as *Penguins are birds.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Mening (*opinion*)","en":"Opinion"},"def":{"af":"Wat iemand dink of voel; ander mense kan daarmee verskil.","en":"What someone thinks or feels; other people may disagree with it."}},{"term":{"af":"Letterlike vraag (*literal question*)","en":"Literal question"},"def":{"af":"’n Vraag waarvan die antwoord net so in die teks staan.","en":"A question whose answer is written in the text."}},{"term":{"af":"Afleidingsvraag (*inferential question*)","en":"Inferential question"},"def":{"af":"’n Vraag waarvoor jy leidrade in die teks en jou eie kennis gebruik, want die antwoord staan nie presies daar nie.","en":"A question for which you use clues in the text and what you know, because the answer is not written exactly."}},{"term":{"af":"Konteks (*context*)","en":"Context"},"def":{"af":"Die woorde en sinne rondom ’n nuwe woord wat jou help om die betekenis te raai.","en":"The words and sentences around a new word that help you work out its meaning."}},{"term":{"af":"Volsin (*full sentence*)","en":"Full sentence"},"def":{"af":"’n Volledige sin met ’n onderwerp en ’n werkwoord, wat met ’n hoofletter begin en met ’n punt eindig.","en":"A complete sentence with a subject and a verb that starts with a capital letter and ends with a full stop."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanhaal (*quote*)","en":"Quote"},"def":{"af":"Woorde presies uit die teks oorskryf en tussen aanhalingstekens sit.","en":"To copy words exactly from the text and put them in inverted commas."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"’n Feit soek met soeklees","en":"Scanning for a fact"},"problem":{"af":"Beantwoord in ’n volsin: *When did Nomsa and her grandfather go to the beach?*","en":"Answer in a full sentence: *When did Nomsa and her grandfather go to the beach?*"},"steps":[{"af":"Die vraagwoord is *When* (wanneer). Jy soek dus ’n tydwoord, soos ’n dag of ’n tyd.","en":"The question word is *When*, so you are looking for a time word, such as a day or a time."},{"af":"Soeklees die leesstuk vir tydwoorde. Die eerste sin begin met *Last Saturday*.","en":"Scan the passage for time words. The first sentence starts with *Last Saturday*."},{"af":"Gebruik woorde uit die vraag om ’n volsin te maak, en skryf dit in Engels.","en":"Use words from the question to make a full sentence."}],"answer":{"af":"*Nomsa and her grandfather went to the beach last Saturday.*","en":"*Nomsa and her grandfather went to the beach last Saturday.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Feit of mening?","en":"Fact or opinion?"},"problem":{"af":"Sê of elke sin ’n feit of ’n mening is en gee ’n rede: (a) *African penguins bray like donkeys.* (b) *These are the cutest birds in the world.*","en":"Say whether each sentence is a fact or an opinion and give a reason: (a) *African penguins bray like donkeys.* (b) *These are the cutest birds in the world.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Sin (a) kan nagegaan word: jy kan na pikkewyne luister of dit in ’n boek naslaan. Dit is ’n feit.","en":"Sentence (a) can be checked: you can listen to penguins or look it up in a book. It is a fact."},{"af":"Sin (b) het die woord *cutest*. Dit is Nomsa se gevoel, en iemand anders dink dalk ’n ander voël is die oulikste. Dit is ’n mening.","en":"Sentence (b) has the word *cutest*. It is Nomsa’s feeling, and someone else may think a different bird is the cutest. It is an opinion."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) feit (*fact*) – dit kan bewys word; (b) mening (*opinion*) – dit is wat Nomsa voel.","en":"(a) fact – it can be proven; (b) opinion – it is what Nomsa feels."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Afleidingsvraag","en":"An inferential question"},"problem":{"af":"Beantwoord: *Why do you think Nomsa was quiet on the way home?*","en":"Answer: *Why do you think Nomsa was quiet on the way home?*"},"steps":[{"af":"Die antwoord staan nie presies in die leesstuk nie, so dit is ’n afleidingsvraag. Jy moet leidrade soek.","en":"The answer is not written exactly in the passage, so it is an inferential question. You must look for clues."},{"af":"Leidraad 1: Sy het pas gelees dat die pikkewyne bedreig is. Leidraad 2: Ná die stilte sê sy *one day I want to help the penguins*.","en":"Clue 1: She has just read that the penguins are endangered. Clue 2: After being quiet she says *one day I want to help the penguins*."},{"af":"Sit die leidrade saam en antwoord in ’n Engelse volsin. Begin gerus met *I think*.","en":"Put the clues together and answer in a full sentence. You may start with *I think*."}],"answer":{"af":"*I think Nomsa was quiet because she was thinking about the penguins and how she could help them.*","en":"*I think Nomsa was quiet because she was thinking about the penguins and how she could help them.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Woordbetekenis uit die konteks","en":"Word meaning from context"},"problem":{"af":"Wat beteken die woord *endangered* in paragraaf 2?","en":"What does the word *endangered* mean in paragraph 2?"},"steps":[{"af":"Lees die sin met die woord en die sin daarna: daar is minder vis vir die pikkewyne en olie van skepe kan hulle skade doen.","en":"Read the sentence with the word and the next sentence: there are fewer fish for the penguins and oil from ships can harm them."},{"af":"Al die leidrade is slegte dinge wat die pikkewyne bedreig. Jou raaiskoot: *in danger of dying out*.","en":"All the clues are bad things that threaten the penguins. Your guess: *in danger of dying out*."},{"af":"Toets dit: *African penguins are in danger of dying out.* Die sin maak sin, so jou betekenis is reg.","en":"Test it: *African penguins are in danger of dying out.* The sentence makes sense, so your meaning is right."}],"answer":{"af":"*Endangered* beteken *in danger of dying out* (in gevaar om uit te sterf).","en":"*Endangered* means *in danger of dying out*."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is **vluglees** (*skimming*)?","en":"What is **skimming**?"},"options":[{"af":"Om stadig elke woord te lees","en":"Reading every word slowly"},{"af":"Om na een spesifieke besonderheid te soek","en":"Looking for one specific detail"},{"af":"Om vinnig te lees vir die algemene idee","en":"Reading quickly for the general idea"},{"af":"Om die teks in jou eie woorde oor te skryf","en":"Rewriting the text in your own words"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Vluglees is vinnige lees om die algemene idee te kry. Om na een besonderheid te soek, is soeklees (*scanning*).","en":"Skimming is quick reading to get the general idea. Looking for one detail is scanning."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees die vraag oor die leesstuk: *Who went to the beach with Nomsa?* Watter antwoord is reg?","en":"Read the question about the passage: *Who went to the beach with Nomsa?* Which answer is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Her grandfather went with her.","en":"Her grandfather went with her."},{"af":"Her mother went with her.","en":"Her mother went with her."},{"af":"Her teacher went with her.","en":"Her teacher went with her."},{"af":"Her friend went with her.","en":"Her friend went with her."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Dit is ’n letterlike vraag. Die eerste sin sê: *Nomsa and her grandfather drove to a beach.*","en":"This is a literal question. The first sentence says: *Nomsa and her grandfather drove to a beach.*"}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die vraag *Why do you think Nomsa was quiet?* is ’n afleidingsvraag (*inferential question*).","en":"The question *Why do you think Nomsa was quiet?* is an inferential question."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die rede staan nie in die leesstuk nie. Jy moet dit uit leidrade aflei – en *do you think* wys ook dat jy self moet dink.","en":"True. The reason is not written in the passage. You must work it out from clues – and *do you think* also shows that you must think for yourself."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin uit die leesstuk is ’n **mening** (*opinion*)?","en":"Which sentence from the passage is an **opinion**?"},"options":[{"af":"African penguins bray like donkeys.","en":"African penguins bray like donkeys."},{"af":"These are the cutest birds in the world.","en":"These are the cutest birds in the world."},{"af":"Some penguins waddled down to the water.","en":"Some penguins waddled down to the water."},{"af":"Nomsa took out her notebook.","en":"Nomsa took out her notebook."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Cutest* is Nomsa se gevoel; ander mense kan verskil. Die ander sinne kan nagegaan word, so hulle is feite.","en":"*Cutest* is Nomsa’s feeling; other people may disagree. The other sentences can be checked, so they are facts."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Soeklees die leesstuk en voltooi: *The penguins bray like* ___ *to call each other.*","en":"Scan the passage and complete: *The penguins bray like* ___ *to call each other.*"},"answers":{"af":["donkeys"],"en":["donkeys"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["dogs","cows","horses"],"en":["dogs","cows","horses"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die oupa sê: *They bray like donkeys to call each other.* Daarom het Nomsa eers gedink sy hoor ’n donkie.","en":"The grandfather says: *They bray like donkeys to call each other.* That is why Nomsa first thought she heard a donkey."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **hoofgedagte** (*main idea*) van die leesstuk?","en":"What is the **main idea** of the passage?"},"options":[{"af":"Nomsa learns about African penguins and wants to help them.","en":"Nomsa learns about African penguins and wants to help them."},{"af":"Nomsa and her grandfather drive to a beach on Saturday.","en":"Nomsa and her grandfather drive to a beach on Saturday."},{"af":"Black-and-white penguins stand together on big rocks.","en":"Black-and-white penguins stand together on big rocks."},{"af":"Nomsa takes out her notebook and draws a penguin.","en":"Nomsa takes out her notebook and draws a penguin."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die hoofgedagte gaan oor die hele teks: Nomsa leer van die pikkewyne en wil hulle help. Die ander is net besonderhede uit een deel.","en":"The main idea covers the whole text: Nomsa learns about the penguins and wants to help them. The others are only details from one part."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke leeswoord by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each reading word to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"vluglees (*skimming*)","en":"skimming"},"r":{"af":"vinnig lees vir die algemene idee","en":"reading quickly for the general idea"}},{"l":{"af":"soeklees (*scanning*)","en":"scanning"},"r":{"af":"vinnig soek na een spesifieke besonderheid","en":"looking quickly for one specific detail"}},{"l":{"af":"hoofgedagte (*main idea*)","en":"main idea"},"r":{"af":"waaroor die hele teks hoofsaaklik gaan","en":"what the whole text is mostly about"}},{"l":{"af":"mening (*opinion*)","en":"opinion"},"r":{"af":"wat iemand dink of voel","en":"what someone thinks or feels"}},{"l":{"af":"konteks (*context*)","en":"context"},"r":{"af":"die woorde rondom ’n nuwe woord","en":"the words around a new word"}}],"explain":{"af":"Vluglees gee die algemene idee, soeklees vind een besonderheid, die hoofgedagte is waaroor alles gaan, ’n mening is ’n gevoel, en die konteks gee leidrade vir nuwe woorde.","en":"Skimming gives the general idea, scanning finds one detail, the main idea is what everything is about, an opinion is a feeling, and the context gives clues to new words."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees: *Some waddled down to the cold water.* Wat beteken **waddled** hier?","en":"Read: *Some waddled down to the cold water.* What does **waddled** mean here?"},"options":[{"af":"baie vinnig geswem","en":"swam very fast"},{"af":"laag oor die water gevlieg","en":"flew low over the water"},{"af":"hoog in die lug gespring","en":"jumped high into the air"},{"af":"met kort, swaaiende treetjies geloop","en":"walked with short, swaying steps"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die pikkewyne gaan *down to the water* – hulle is nog nie in die water nie, so hulle swem nie. Met hul kort beentjies loop hulle met swaaiende treetjies: hulle waggel.","en":"The penguins go *down to the water* – they are not in the water yet, so they are not swimming. With their short legs they walk with swaying steps: they waddle."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer jy vinnig na een spesifieke besonderheid soos ’n naam of ’n getal soek, heet dit ___.","en":"When you look quickly for one specific detail, such as a name or a number, you are ___."},"answers":{"af":["soeklees","scanning"],"en":["scanning"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vluglees","opsomming","voorspelling"],"en":["skimming","summarising","predicting"]}},"explain":{"af":"Soeklees (*scanning*) is om na een besonderheid te soek. Vluglees (*skimming*) is om vinnig vir die algemene idee te lees.","en":"Scanning means looking for one detail. Skimming means reading quickly for the general idea."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter antwoord op *Where did Nomsa and her grandfather go?* is die beste?","en":"Which answer to *Where did Nomsa and her grandfather go?* is the best?"},"options":[{"af":"Beach.","en":"Beach."},{"af":"They went to a beach near Simon’s Town.","en":"They went to a beach near Simon’s Town."},{"af":"Last Saturday, Nomsa and her grandfather drove.","en":"Last Saturday, Nomsa and her grandfather drove."},{"af":"The penguins were near Simon’s Town.","en":"The penguins were near Simon’s Town."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Dit is ’n volsin wat woorde uit die vraag gebruik en die plek volledig noem. *Beach.* is nie ’n volsin nie, en die ander twee beantwoord nie die vraag nie.","en":"It is a full sentence that uses words from the question and gives the full place. *Beach.* is not a full sentence, and the other two do not answer the question."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*These are the cutest birds in the world* is ’n feit, want dit staan in die leesstuk.","en":"*These are the cutest birds in the world* is a fact because it is written in the passage."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Mening bly ’n mening, al staan dit in die teks. *Cutest* wys wat Nomsa voel, en dit kan nie bewys word nie.","en":"False. An opinion is still an opinion, even when it is in the text. *Cutest* shows what Nomsa feels, and it cannot be proven."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*How do you know that Nomsa liked the penguins?* Kies die beste antwoord.","en":"*How do you know that Nomsa liked the penguins?* Choose the best answer."},"options":[{"af":"She heard a loud noise next to the wooden path.","en":"She heard a loud noise next to the wooden path."},{"af":"Her grandfather drove her to a beach on Saturday.","en":"Her grandfather drove her to a beach on Saturday."},{"af":"The penguins stood together on the big rocks.","en":"The penguins stood together on the big rocks."},{"af":"She drew a penguin and called them the cutest birds.","en":"She drew a penguin and called them the cutest birds."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die leidrade is wat Nomsa doen en sê: sy teken ’n pikkewyn en sê hulle is die oulikste voëls. Die ander sinne sê niks oor haar gevoelens nie.","en":"The clues are what Nomsa does and says: she draws a penguin and says they are the cutest birds. The other sentences say nothing about her feelings."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die woord uit paragraaf 2 wat *in danger of dying out* beteken: ___","en":"Write the word from paragraph 2 that means *in danger of dying out*: ___"},"answers":{"af":["endangered"],"en":["endangered"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["waddled","fewer","harm"],"en":["waddled","fewer","harm"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Endangered* beteken in gevaar om uit te sterf. Die volgende sin gee die redes: minder vis en olie van skepe.","en":"*Endangered* means in danger of dying out. The next sentence gives the reasons: fewer fish and oil from ships."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken dit om ’n vraag *in your own words* te beantwoord?","en":"What does it mean to answer a question *in your own words*?"},"options":[{"af":"Skryf die hele sin uit die leesstuk oor","en":"Copy the whole sentence from the passage"},{"af":"Skryf net een woord as antwoord neer","en":"Write only one word as the answer"},{"af":"Verduidelik die antwoord in jou eie sin","en":"Explain the answer in your own sentence"},{"af":"Skryf die antwoord in Afrikaans","en":"Write the answer in your home language"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Jy verduidelik self in ’n Engelse volsin. Jy skryf nie net oor nie, en jy antwoord altyd in Engels.","en":"You explain it yourself in a full English sentence. You do not just copy, and you always answer in English."}}]},{"id":"eng5-t1-nouns-articles","title":{"af":"Selfstandige naamwoorde en lidwoorde","en":"Nouns and articles"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal soortname, eiename, versamelname en abstrakte naamwoorde in Engels kan herken, die regte meervoud kan skryf en *a, an* en *the* korrek kan gebruik.","en":"You will be able to recognise common, proper, collective and abstract nouns, write the correct plural and use *a, an* and *the* correctly."},"summary":{"af":"## Soorte selfstandige naamwoorde\n\n’n **Selfstandige naamwoord** (*noun*) is die naam van ’n mens, dier, plek, ding of idee. Engels het dieselfde soorte as Afrikaans:\n\n| Soort | Wat dit noem | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Soortnaam** (*common noun*) | enige mens, dier, plek of ding van ’n soort; kleinletter | *girl, dog, city, river* |\n| **Eienaam** (*proper noun*) | een spesifieke mens, plek, dag of maand; altyd ’n **hoofletter** | *Lerato, Durban, the Orange River, Monday, June* |\n| **Versamelnaam** (*collective noun*) | een woord vir ’n hele groep | *a herd of elephants, a flock of sheep, a swarm of bees, a pride of lions, a troop of baboons* |\n| **Abstrakte naamwoord** (*abstract noun*) | ’n gevoel, eienskap of idee wat jy nie kan sien of vat nie | *love, fear, kindness, friendship, courage* |\n\n> **Onthou:** As jy dit kan sien, hoor, aanraak, ruik of proe, is dit nie abstrak nie. *Happiness* (geluk) is abstrak, maar *smile* (glimlag) is ’n soortnaam.\n\n## Meervoude\n\n| Reël | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| Die meeste woorde: voeg **-s** by | *book → books, girl → girls* |\n| Eindig op **-s, -ss, -sh, -ch, -x**: voeg **-es** by | *bus → buses, glass → glasses, dish → dishes, watch → watches, box → boxes* |\n| Medeklinker + **y**: die y word **-ies** | *baby → babies, city → cities, lady → ladies* |\n| Klinker + **y**: voeg net **-s** by | *boy → boys, day → days, key → keys* |\n| Eindig op **-f** of **-fe**: dikwels **-ves** | *leaf → leaves, wolf → wolves, knife → knives, wife → wives* |\n| Party woorde op **-o**: voeg **-es** by | *tomato → tomatoes, potato → potatoes, hero → heroes* |\n\nMaar *photo → photos, piano → pianos* en *roof → roofs* kry net -s.\n\nWaarom -es? Ná ’n sisklank soos *s, sh* of *ch* kan jy ’n ekstra -s nie hoor nie. Die ekstra lettergreep (*box-es*) maak die woord maklik om te sê.\n\n**Onreëlmatige meervoude** volg nie die reëls nie – leer hulle uit jou kop: *child → children, man → men, woman → women, mouse → mice, foot → feet, tooth → teeth, goose → geese, person → people*. Party woorde bly **dieselfde**: *one sheep → two sheep, one fish → three fish, one deer → many deer*.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *childs, mouses, sheeps* en *foots* is verkeerd. Skryf *children, mice, sheep* en *feet*.\n\n## Telbare en ontelbare naamwoorde\n\n**Telbare** naamwoorde (*countable nouns*) kan jy tel: *one apple, two apples*. Hulle het ’n meervoud en kan *a* of *an* kry.\n\n**Ontelbare** naamwoorde (*uncountable nouns*) kan jy nie een vir een tel nie: *water, milk, sugar, rice, bread, money, information, homework*. Hulle het **geen meervoud** nie en kry nie *a* of *an* nie.\n\n- Verkeerd: *a water, two breads, informations*. Reg: *some water, two slices of bread, a glass of milk*.\n- *many* + telbaar (*many apples*); *much* + ontelbaar (*much water*).\n\n## Lidwoorde: a, an en the\n\nAfrikaans het net twee **lidwoorde** (*articles*): *’n* en *die*. Engels het drie: *a, an* en *the*.\n\n- *A* en *an* (= ’n) gebruik jy vir **een** ding wat **nie spesifiek** is nie.\n- *The* (= die) gebruik jy vir ’n **spesifieke** ding wat ons reeds ken, of vir iets waarvan daar net een is: *the sun, the moon*.\n- *I saw **a** dog. **The** dog was barking.* (die eerste keer *a*, daarna *the*)\n\nKies *a* of *an* volgens die **klank** aan die begin van die volgende woord, nie volgens die letter nie:\n\n| a + medeklinkerklank | an + klinkerklank |\n|---|---|\n| *a book, a tree* | *an apple, an egg, an orange* |\n| *a uniform, a unicorn* (begin met ’n “joe”-klank) | *an hour, an honest boy* (die h is stil) |\n| *a horse, a house* (jy hoor die h) | *an umbrella, an uncle* |\n\nDie **volgende** woord tel, ook as dit ’n byvoeglike naamwoord is: *an elephant*, maar *a big elephant*; *a car*, maar *an old car*.","en":"## Kinds of nouns\n\nA **noun** is a naming word for a person, animal, place, thing or idea. There are four main kinds:\n\n| Kind | What it names | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Common noun** | any person, animal, place or thing of a kind; small letter | *girl, dog, city, river* |\n| **Proper noun** | one particular person, place, day or month; always a **capital letter** | *Lerato, Durban, the Orange River, Monday, June* |\n| **Collective noun** | one word for a whole group | *a herd of elephants, a flock of sheep, a swarm of bees, a pride of lions, a troop of baboons* |\n| **Abstract noun** | a feeling, quality or idea that you cannot see or touch | *love, fear, kindness, friendship, courage* |\n\n> **Remember:** If you can see, hear, touch, smell or taste it, it is not abstract. *Happiness* is abstract, but *smile* is a common noun.\n\n## Plurals\n\n| Rule | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| Most words: add **-s** | *book → books, girl → girls* |\n| Ends in **-s, -ss, -sh, -ch, -x**: add **-es** | *bus → buses, glass → glasses, dish → dishes, watch → watches, box → boxes* |\n| Consonant + **y**: the y becomes **-ies** | *baby → babies, city → cities, lady → ladies* |\n| Vowel + **y**: just add **-s** | *boy → boys, day → days, key → keys* |\n| Ends in **-f** or **-fe**: often **-ves** | *leaf → leaves, wolf → wolves, knife → knives, wife → wives* |\n| Some words ending in **-o**: add **-es** | *tomato → tomatoes, potato → potatoes, hero → heroes* |\n\nBut *photo → photos, piano → pianos* and *roof → roofs* just add -s.\n\nWhy -es? After a hissing sound such as *s, sh* or *ch*, you cannot hear an extra -s. The extra syllable (*box-es*) makes the word easy to say.\n\n**Irregular plurals** do not follow the rules – learn them by heart: *child → children, man → men, woman → women, mouse → mice, foot → feet, tooth → teeth, goose → geese, person → people*. Some words stay **the same**: *one sheep → two sheep, one fish → three fish, one deer → many deer*.\n\n> **Common mistake:** *childs, mouses, sheeps* and *foots* are wrong. Write *children, mice, sheep* and *feet*.\n\n## Countable and uncountable nouns\n\n**Countable nouns** can be counted: *one apple, two apples*. They have a plural and can take *a* or *an*.\n\n**Uncountable nouns** cannot be counted one by one: *water, milk, sugar, rice, bread, money, information, homework*. They have **no plural** and do not take *a* or *an*.\n\n- Wrong: *a water, two breads, informations*. Right: *some water, two slices of bread, a glass of milk*.\n- *many* + countable (*many apples*); *much* + uncountable (*much water*).\n\n## Articles: a, an and the\n\nAfrikaans has only two **articles**: *’n* and *die*. English has three: *a, an* and *the*.\n\n- Use *a* or *an* for **one** thing that is **not specific** (any one).\n- Use *the* for a **specific** thing that we already know about, or for something there is only one of: *the sun, the moon*.\n- *I saw **a** dog. **The** dog was barking.* (*a* the first time, *the* after that)\n\nChoose *a* or *an* by the **sound** at the start of the next word, not by the letter:\n\n| a + consonant sound | an + vowel sound |\n|---|---|\n| *a book, a tree* | *an apple, an egg, an orange* |\n| *a uniform, a unicorn* (starts with a “you” sound) | *an hour, an honest boy* (the h is silent) |\n| *a horse, a house* (you hear the h) | *an umbrella, an uncle* |\n\nThe **next** word counts, even if it is an adjective: *an elephant*, but *a big elephant*; *a car*, but *an old car*."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Selfstandige naamwoord (*noun*)","en":"Noun"},"def":{"af":"’n Naamwoord vir ’n mens, dier, plek, ding of idee, soos *girl* of *river*.","en":"A naming word for a person, animal, place, thing or idea, such as *girl* or *river*."}},{"term":{"af":"Soortnaam (*common noun*)","en":"Common noun"},"def":{"af":"’n Gewone naam vir enige ding van ’n soort; dit begin met ’n kleinletter: *city, dog*.","en":"A general name for any thing of a kind; it starts with a small letter: *city, dog*."}},{"term":{"af":"Eienaam (*proper noun*)","en":"Proper noun"},"def":{"af":"Die naam van een spesifieke mens, plek, dag of maand; dit kry altyd ’n hoofletter: *Durban, Monday*.","en":"The name of one particular person, place, day or month; it always has a capital letter: *Durban, Monday*."}},{"term":{"af":"Versamelnaam (*collective noun*)","en":"Collective noun"},"def":{"af":"Een woord vir ’n hele groep, soos *a herd of elephants*.","en":"One word for a whole group, such as *a herd of elephants*."}},{"term":{"af":"Abstrakte naamwoord (*abstract noun*)","en":"Abstract noun"},"def":{"af":"Die naam van ’n gevoel, eienskap of idee wat jy nie kan sien of vat nie, soos *kindness*.","en":"The name of a feeling, quality or idea that you cannot see or touch, such as *kindness*."}},{"term":{"af":"Meervoud (*plural*)","en":"Plural"},"def":{"af":"Die vorm van ’n naamwoord vir meer as een: *books, boxes, babies*.","en":"The form of a noun for more than one: *books, boxes, babies*."}},{"term":{"af":"Onreëlmatige meervoud (*irregular plural*)","en":"Irregular plural"},"def":{"af":"’n Meervoud wat nie die reëls volg nie en wat jy moet leer: *child → children, mouse → mice*.","en":"A plural that does not follow the rules, so you must learn it: *child → children, mouse → mice*."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontelbare naamwoord (*uncountable noun*)","en":"Uncountable noun"},"def":{"af":"’n Naamwoord wat jy nie een vir een kan tel nie en wat geen meervoud het nie, soos *water* of *sugar*.","en":"A noun that you cannot count one by one and that has no plural, such as *water* or *sugar*."}},{"term":{"af":"Lidwoord (*article*)","en":"Article"},"def":{"af":"Die woordjies *a, an* en *the* wat voor ’n naamwoord staan.","en":"The small words *a, an* and *the* that stand before a noun."}},{"term":{"af":"Klinkerklank (*vowel sound*)","en":"Vowel sound"},"def":{"af":"Die klank van a, e, i, o of u aan die begin van ’n woord; dit bepaal of jy *an* gebruik: *an egg, an hour*.","en":"The sound of a, e, i, o or u at the start of a word; it tells you to use *an*: *an egg, an hour*."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Meervoude volgens die reëls","en":"Plurals by the rules"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die meervoud van *box, baby, knife, child* en *sheep*.","en":"Write the plural of *box, baby, knife, child* and *sheep*."},"steps":[{"af":"*box* eindig op -x, so voeg -es by: *boxes*.","en":"*box* ends in -x, so add -es: *boxes*."},{"af":"*baby* eindig op medeklinker + y. Die y word -ies: *babies*.","en":"*baby* ends in consonant + y. The y becomes -ies: *babies*."},{"af":"*knife* eindig op -fe, so dit word -ves: *knives*.","en":"*knife* ends in -fe, so it becomes -ves: *knives*."},{"af":"*child* en *sheep* is onreëlmatig: *children*, en *sheep* bly dieselfde.","en":"*child* and *sheep* are irregular: *children*, and *sheep* stays the same."}],"answer":{"af":"*boxes, babies, knives, children, sheep*","en":"*boxes, babies, knives, children, sheep*"}},{"title":{"af":"a of an?","en":"a or an?"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf *a* of *an*: ___ *hour*, ___ *uniform*, ___ *elephant*, ___ *big elephant*, ___ *umbrella*.","en":"Write *a* or *an*: ___ *hour*, ___ *uniform*, ___ *elephant*, ___ *big elephant*, ___ *umbrella*."},"steps":[{"af":"Sê elke woord hardop en luister na die eerste **klank**, nie na die letter nie.","en":"Say each word out loud and listen to the first **sound**, not the letter."},{"af":"*hour* begin met ’n stil h, so jy hoor ’n klinker: *an hour*. *uniform* begin met ’n “joe”-klank (medeklinker): *a uniform*.","en":"*hour* starts with a silent h, so you hear a vowel: *an hour*. *uniform* starts with a “you” sound (a consonant sound): *a uniform*."},{"af":"*elephant* en *umbrella* begin met ’n klinkerklank: *an*. By *big elephant* is *big* die volgende woord, so: *a big elephant*.","en":"*elephant* and *umbrella* start with a vowel sound: *an*. In *big elephant*, *big* is the next word, so: *a big elephant*."}],"answer":{"af":"*an hour, a uniform, an elephant, a big elephant, an umbrella*","en":"*an hour, a uniform, an elephant, a big elephant, an umbrella*"}},{"title":{"af":"Soorte naamwoorde in ’n sin","en":"Kinds of nouns in a sentence"},"problem":{"af":"Lees: *Thabo felt great joy when a herd of elephants crossed the road in the Kruger National Park.* Noem die eiename, soortname, versamelnaam en abstrakte naamwoord.","en":"Read: *Thabo felt great joy when a herd of elephants crossed the road in the Kruger National Park.* Name the proper nouns, common nouns, collective noun and abstract noun."},"steps":[{"af":"Eiename het hoofletters en noem een spesifieke mens of plek: *Thabo* en *Kruger National Park*.","en":"Proper nouns have capital letters and name one particular person or place: *Thabo* and *Kruger National Park*."},{"af":"Soortname is gewone dinge wat jy kan sien: *elephants* en *road*.","en":"Common nouns are ordinary things you can see: *elephants* and *road*."},{"af":"*herd* is een woord vir ’n groep olifante: die versamelnaam. *joy* (vreugde) is ’n gevoel wat jy nie kan vat nie: die abstrakte naamwoord.","en":"*herd* is one word for a group of elephants: the collective noun. *joy* is a feeling you cannot touch: the abstract noun."}],"answer":{"af":"Eiename: *Thabo, Kruger National Park*. Soortname: *elephants, road*. Versamelnaam: *herd*. Abstrak: *joy*.","en":"Proper nouns: *Thabo, Kruger National Park*. Common nouns: *elephants, road*. Collective noun: *herd*. Abstract noun: *joy*."}},{"title":{"af":"Verbeter die foute","en":"Correct the mistakes"},"problem":{"af":"Verbeter die sin: *Lerato needs an informations about the sheeps.*","en":"Correct the sentence: *Lerato needs an informations about the sheeps.*"},"steps":[{"af":"*information* is ontelbaar: dit kry nie *a/an* nie en het geen -s nie. Gebruik *some* of niks.","en":"*information* is uncountable: it takes no *a/an* and has no -s. Use *some* or nothing."},{"af":"*sheep* bly in die meervoud dieselfde, so *sheeps* is verkeerd.","en":"*sheep* stays the same in the plural, so *sheeps* is wrong."},{"af":"Skryf die hele sin weer oor en kyk of dit nou reg klink.","en":"Rewrite the whole sentence and check that it sounds right now."}],"answer":{"af":"*Lerato needs some information about the sheep.*","en":"*Lerato needs some information about the sheep.*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is ’n **abstrakte naamwoord** (*abstract noun*)?","en":"Which word is an **abstract noun**?"},"options":[{"af":"table","en":"table"},{"af":"kindness","en":"kindness"},{"af":"teacher","en":"teacher"},{"af":"river","en":"river"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Kindness* (vriendelikheid) is ’n eienskap wat jy nie kan sien of vat nie. *Table, teacher* en *river* kan jy sien, so hulle is soortname.","en":"*Kindness* is a quality that you cannot see or touch. You can see a *table*, a *teacher* and a *river*, so they are common nouns."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die meervoud: *one leaf, two* ___","en":"Write the plural: *one leaf, two* ___"},"answers":{"af":["leaves"],"en":["leaves"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["leafs","leafes","leavs"],"en":["leafs","leafes","leavs"]}},"explain":{"af":"Baie woorde op -f kry -ves in die meervoud: *leaf → leaves*, net soos *wolf → wolves*.","en":"Many words ending in -f take -ves in the plural: *leaf → leaves*, just like *wolf → wolves*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die korrekte meervoud van *baby*?","en":"What is the correct plural of *baby*?"},"options":[{"af":"babys","en":"babys"},{"af":"babyes","en":"babyes"},{"af":"babbies","en":"babbies"},{"af":"babies","en":"babies"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*baby* eindig op medeklinker (b) + y, so die y word -ies: *babies*. Net ná ’n klinker + y voeg jy -s by, soos *boy → boys*.","en":"*baby* ends in consonant (b) + y, so the y becomes -ies: *babies*. Only after vowel + y do you just add -s, as in *boy → boys*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Ons skryf *an hour*, want die h in *hour* is stil en die woord begin met ’n klinkerklank.","en":"We write *an hour* because the h in *hour* is silent and the word starts with a vowel sound."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Jy kies *a* of *an* volgens die klank. *Hour* klink asof dit met ’n klinker begin, so jy skryf *an hour*.","en":"True. You choose *a* or *an* by the sound. *Hour* sounds as if it starts with a vowel, so you write *an hour*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte versamelnaam: *a ___ of lions*","en":"Choose the correct collective noun: *a ___ of lions*"},"options":[{"af":"pride","en":"pride"},{"af":"herd","en":"herd"},{"af":"flock","en":"flock"},{"af":"swarm","en":"swarm"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Groep leeus is *a pride of lions*. *Herd* is vir olifante of beeste, *flock* vir skape of voëls en *swarm* vir bye.","en":"A group of lions is *a pride of lions*. *Herd* is for elephants or cattle, *flock* for sheep or birds and *swarm* for bees."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is korrek?","en":"Which one is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"an uniform","en":"an uniform"},{"af":"a hour","en":"a hour"},{"af":"a uniform","en":"a uniform"},{"af":"a umbrella","en":"a umbrella"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Uniform* begin met ’n “joe”-klank, ’n medeklinkerklank, so: *a uniform*. Dit moet *an hour* en *an umbrella* wees.","en":"*Uniform* starts with a “you” sound, which is a consonant sound, so: *a uniform*. It must be *an hour* and *an umbrella*."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke enkelvoud by sy meervoud.","en":"Match each singular to its plural."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"child","en":"child"},"r":{"af":"children","en":"children"}},{"l":{"af":"tooth","en":"tooth"},"r":{"af":"teeth","en":"teeth"}},{"l":{"af":"wolf","en":"wolf"},"r":{"af":"wolves","en":"wolves"}},{"l":{"af":"potato","en":"potato"},"r":{"af":"potatoes","en":"potatoes"}},{"l":{"af":"mouse","en":"mouse"},"r":{"af":"mice","en":"mice"}}],"explain":{"af":"*child, tooth* en *mouse* is onreëlmatig, *wolf* kry -ves en *potato* kry -es.","en":"*child, tooth* and *mouse* are irregular, *wolf* takes -ves and *potato* takes -es."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die meervoud: *one foot, two* ___","en":"Write the plural: *one foot, two* ___"},"answers":{"af":["feet"],"en":["feet"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["foots","feets","footes"],"en":["foots","feets","footes"]}},"explain":{"af":"*foot* is onreëlmatig: die oo word ee en daar kom geen -s by nie, net soos *tooth → teeth*.","en":"*foot* is irregular: the oo becomes ee and no -s is added, just like *tooth → teeth*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter naamwoord is **ontelbaar** (*uncountable*)?","en":"Which noun is **uncountable**?"},"options":[{"af":"apple","en":"apple"},{"af":"chair","en":"chair"},{"af":"sugar","en":"sugar"},{"af":"pencil","en":"pencil"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Jy kan nie *sugar* een vir een tel nie; jy sê *some sugar* of *a spoon of sugar*. Appels, stoele en potlode kan jy tel.","en":"You cannot count *sugar* one by one; you say *some sugar* or *a spoon of sugar*. You can count apples, chairs and pencils."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter sin is die **eienaam** reg geskryf?","en":"In which sentence is the **proper noun** written correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Aisha visited Cape Town in July.","en":"Aisha visited Cape Town in July."},{"af":"We swam in the orange river.","en":"We swam in the orange river."},{"af":"My cousin lives in durban.","en":"My cousin lives in durban."},{"af":"On monday we play netball.","en":"On monday we play netball."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Eiename, ook name van dae en maande, kry altyd ’n hoofletter: *Cape Town, July*. Dit moet *the Orange River, Durban* en *Monday* wees.","en":"Proper nouns, also names of days and months, always have a capital letter: *Cape Town, July*. It must be *the Orange River, Durban* and *Monday*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die meervoud van *sheep* is *sheeps*.","en":"The plural of *sheep* is *sheeps*."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. *Sheep* bly dieselfde: *one sheep, ten sheep*.","en":"False. *Sheep* stays the same: *one sheep, ten sheep*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is korrek?","en":"Which sentence is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Can I have a water, please?","en":"Can I have a water, please?"},{"af":"She gave me some good advices.","en":"She gave me some good advices."},{"af":"We need two loafs of bread.","en":"We need two loafs of bread."},{"af":"There is too much sugar in my tea.","en":"There is too much sugar in my tea."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Sugar* is ontelbaar en kry *much*. *Water* en *advice* is ook ontelbaar (geen *a* of -s nie), en die meervoud van *loaf* is *loaves*.","en":"*Sugar* is uncountable and takes *much*. *Water* and *advice* are also uncountable (no *a* or -s), and the plural of *loaf* is *loaves*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi met die regte lidwoord: *Look at ___ sun! It is so bright today.*","en":"Complete with the correct article: *Look at ___ sun! It is so bright today.*"},"answers":{"af":["the"],"en":["the"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["a","an","some"],"en":["a","an","some"]}},"explain":{"af":"Daar is net een son, so ons gebruik *the*: *the sun, the moon*.","en":"There is only one sun, so we use *the*: *the sun, the moon*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte lidwoorde: *I saw ___ elephant and ___ big giraffe.*","en":"Choose the correct articles: *I saw ___ elephant and ___ big giraffe.*"},"options":[{"af":"a … an","en":"a … an"},{"af":"an … a","en":"an … a"},{"af":"an … an","en":"an … an"},{"af":"a … a","en":"a … a"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Elephant* begin met ’n klinkerklank: *an elephant*. Voor *giraffe* staan *big*, wat met ’n medeklinkerklank begin: *a big giraffe*.","en":"*Elephant* starts with a vowel sound: *an elephant*. *Big* comes before *giraffe* and starts with a consonant sound: *a big giraffe*."}}]},{"id":"eng5-t1-pronouns","title":{"af":"Voornaamwoorde","en":"Pronouns"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal Engelse voornaamwoorde as onderwerp en voorwerp kan gebruik, besitlike, aanwysende en vraende voornaamwoorde reg kan kies en herhaling in jou sinne kan vermy.","en":"You will be able to use pronouns as subject and object, choose the correct possessive, demonstrative and question pronouns and avoid repetition in your sentences."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is ’n voornaamwoord?\n\n’n **Voornaamwoord** (*pronoun*) staan in die plek van ’n selfstandige naamwoord. Dit keer dat ons dieselfde naam oor en oor **herhaal**.\n\n- *Pieter fed Pieter’s dog, and then Pieter took Pieter’s dog for a walk.* (klink snaaks)\n- *Pieter fed **his** dog, and then **he** took **it** for a walk.* (baie beter)\n\nKies ’n voornaamwoord wat by die naamwoord pas: een seun → *he*, een meisie → *she*, ’n ding of dier → *it*, meer as een → *they*. Maak ook seker die leser weet na wie die voornaamwoord verwys. As daar twee meisies in die sin is, gebruik eerder weer ’n naam.\n\n## Onderwerp- en voorwerpvorm\n\n| Onderwerp (doen die handeling) | Voorwerp (ontvang die handeling) |\n|---|---|\n| I (ek) | me (my) |\n| you (jy) | you (jou) |\n| he (hy) | him (hom) |\n| she (sy) | her (haar) |\n| it (dit) | it (dit) |\n| we (ons) | us (ons) |\n| they (hulle) | them (hulle) |\n\n- Die **onderwerp** (*subject*) staan gewoonlik **voor** die werkwoord: ***She** helps her brother.*\n- Die **voorwerp** (*object*) staan **ná** die werkwoord of ná woorde soos *with, to, for*: *Her brother thanks **her**. Come with **us**.*\n\nToets met twee mense: bedek die ander persoon. *Sipho and (I/me) went to the shop.* → *I went to the shop.* Dus: *Sipho and I went to the shop.* En *Mom gave Sipho and (I/me) an apple.* → *Mom gave me an apple.* Dus: *Mom gave Sipho and me an apple.*\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *Me and Ravi played soccer.* Skryf *Ravi and I played soccer.* Noem die ander persoon eerste en gebruik *I* as onderwerp.\n\n## Besitlike voornaamwoorde\n\n| Voor ’n naamwoord | Alleen |\n|---|---|\n| my (my) | mine (myne) |\n| your (jou) | yours (joune) |\n| his (sy) | his (syne) |\n| her (haar) | hers (hare) |\n| our (ons) | ours (ons s’n) |\n| their (hulle) | theirs (hulle s’n) |\n\n- *This is **my** bag.* = *This bag is **mine**.*\n- *That is **their** house.* = *That house is **theirs**.*\n- Vir ’n dier of ding gebruik jy *its*: *The dog wagged **its** tail.*\n\nPas op: Afrikaans *sy* kan *she* of *his* beteken. *Sy lees* = *She reads*, maar *sy boek* = *his book*.\n\nBesitlike voornaamwoorde kry **nooit** ’n afkappingsteken nie: *yours, hers, ours, theirs, its*.\n\n> **Onthou:** *its* = wat aan dit behoort (*The cat licked its paw.*); *it’s* = *it is* (*It’s raining.*).\n\n## Aanwysende voornaamwoorde: this, that, these, those\n\n| | Naby (hier) | Ver (daar) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Een (enkelvoud) | this | that |\n| Meer as een (meervoud) | these | those |\n\n- ***This** pencil here is blue. **That** bird over there is a hadeda.*\n- ***These** shoes are new. **Those** clouds look dark.*\n\nAfrikaans gebruik *hierdie* en *daardie* vir een sowel as baie. Engels verander die woord in die meervoud, so kyk altyd of dit een of meer as een is.\n\n## Vraende voornaamwoorde: who, what, which, whose\n\n- **Who** vra na ’n **persoon**: *Who is your best friend?*\n- **What** vra na ’n **ding** of ’n handeling: *What is in the box?*\n- **Which** vra dat jy **kies** uit ’n groep: *Which colour do you like, red or blue?*\n- **Whose** vra na die **eienaar**: *Whose jersey is this?* (*who’s* = *who is*)\n\nJy antwoord ’n *whose*-vraag met ’n besitlike vorm: *Whose jersey is this? It is mine.* of *It is Thabo’s.*","en":"## What is a pronoun?\n\nA **pronoun** takes the place of a noun. It stops us from **repeating** the same name over and over.\n\n- *Pieter fed Pieter’s dog, and then Pieter took Pieter’s dog for a walk.* (sounds strange)\n- *Pieter fed **his** dog, and then **he** took **it** for a walk.* (much better)\n\nChoose a pronoun that matches the noun: one boy → *he*, one girl → *she*, a thing or an animal → *it*, more than one → *they*. Also make sure the reader knows who the pronoun points to. If there are two girls in the sentence, rather use a name again.\n\n## Subject and object pronouns\n\n| Subject (does the action) | Object (receives the action) |\n|---|---|\n| I | me |\n| you | you |\n| he | him |\n| she | her |\n| it | it |\n| we | us |\n| they | them |\n\n- The **subject** usually comes **before** the verb: ***She** helps her brother.*\n- The **object** comes **after** the verb or after words such as *with, to, for*: *Her brother thanks **her**. Come with **us**.*\n\nTest with two people: cover the other person. *Sipho and (I/me) went to the shop.* → *I went to the shop.* So: *Sipho and I went to the shop.* And *Mom gave Sipho and (I/me) an apple.* → *Mom gave me an apple.* So: *Mom gave Sipho and me an apple.*\n\n> **Common mistake:** *Me and Ravi played soccer.* Write *Ravi and I played soccer.* Name the other person first and use *I* as the subject.\n\n## Possessive pronouns\n\n| Before a noun | On its own |\n|---|---|\n| my | mine |\n| your | yours |\n| his | his |\n| her | hers |\n| our | ours |\n| their | theirs |\n\n- *This is **my** bag.* = *This bag is **mine**.*\n- *That is **their** house.* = *That house is **theirs**.*\n- For an animal or a thing, use *its*: *The dog wagged **its** tail.*\n\nBe careful if your home language is Afrikaans: *sy* can mean *she* or *his*. *Sy lees* = *She reads*, but *sy boek* = *his book*.\n\nPossessive pronouns **never** take an apostrophe: *yours, hers, ours, theirs, its*.\n\n> **Remember:** *its* = belonging to it (*The cat licked its paw.*); *it’s* = *it is* (*It’s raining.*).\n\n## Demonstrative pronouns: this, that, these, those\n\n| | Near (here) | Far (there) |\n|---|---|---|\n| One (singular) | this | that |\n| More than one (plural) | these | those |\n\n- ***This** pencil here is blue. **That** bird over there is a hadeda.*\n- ***These** shoes are new. **Those** clouds look dark.*\n\nAfrikaans uses *hierdie* and *daardie* for one or many. English changes the word in the plural, so always check whether it is one or more than one.\n\n## Question pronouns: who, what, which, whose\n\n- **Who** asks about a **person**: *Who is your best friend?*\n- **What** asks about a **thing** or an action: *What is in the box?*\n- **Which** asks you to **choose** from a group: *Which colour do you like, red or blue?*\n- **Whose** asks about the **owner**: *Whose jersey is this?* (*who’s* = *who is*)\n\nYou answer a *whose* question with a possessive: *Whose jersey is this? It is mine.* or *It is Thabo’s.*"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Voornaamwoord (*pronoun*)","en":"Pronoun"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat in die plek van ’n selfstandige naamwoord staan, soos *he, it* of *them*.","en":"A word that takes the place of a noun, such as *he, it* or *them*."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderwerp (*subject*)","en":"Subject"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon of ding wat die handeling doen; dit staan gewoonlik voor die werkwoord: ***We** play.*","en":"The person or thing doing the action; it usually comes before the verb: ***We** play.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Voorwerp (*object*)","en":"Object"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon of ding wat die handeling ontvang; dit staan ná die werkwoord: *She helps **us**.*","en":"The person or thing receiving the action; it comes after the verb: *She helps **us**.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Persoonlike voornaamwoord (*personal pronoun*)","en":"Personal pronoun"},"def":{"af":"’n Voornaamwoord vir mense of dinge, soos *I/me, he/him, they/them*.","en":"A pronoun for people or things, such as *I/me, he/him, they/them*."}},{"term":{"af":"Besitlike voornaamwoord (*possessive pronoun*)","en":"Possessive pronoun"},"def":{"af":"’n Voornaamwoord wat wys wie iets besit, soos *my/mine* of *their/theirs*.","en":"A pronoun that shows who owns something, such as *my/mine* or *their/theirs*."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanwysende voornaamwoord (*demonstrative pronoun*)","en":"Demonstrative pronoun"},"def":{"af":"*This, that, these* of *those*: dit wys na iets naby of ver.","en":"*This, that, these* or *those*: it points to something near or far."}},{"term":{"af":"Vraende voornaamwoord (*question pronoun*)","en":"Question pronoun"},"def":{"af":"*Who, what, which* of *whose*: dit begin ’n vraag oor ’n persoon, ding, keuse of eienaar.","en":"*Who, what, which* or *whose*: it starts a question about a person, thing, choice or owner."}},{"term":{"af":"Herhaling (*repetition*)","en":"Repetition"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer jy dieselfde woord oor en oor gebruik; voornaamwoorde help jou om dit te vermy.","en":"Using the same word over and over; pronouns help you to avoid it."}},{"term":{"af":"*its* en *it’s*","en":"*its* and *it’s*"},"def":{"af":"*Its* wys besit (*its tail*); *it’s* is die kort vorm van *it is*.","en":"*Its* shows ownership (*its tail*); *it’s* is the short form of *it is*."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Vermy herhaling","en":"Avoid repetition"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf met voornaamwoorde: *Nomsa and Nomsa’s brother washed Nomsa’s mother’s car. Nomsa’s mother thanked Nomsa and Nomsa’s brother.*","en":"Rewrite using pronouns: *Nomsa and Nomsa’s brother washed Nomsa’s mother’s car. Nomsa’s mother thanked Nomsa and Nomsa’s brother.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Die eerste *Nomsa* bly, sodat ons weet oor wie dit gaan. *Nomsa’s brother* word *her brother*.","en":"Keep the first *Nomsa* so that we know who it is about. *Nomsa’s brother* becomes *her brother*."},{"af":"Die ma is hulle albei se ma, so *Nomsa’s mother’s car* word *their mother’s car*.","en":"The mother belongs to both of them, so *Nomsa’s mother’s car* becomes *their mother’s car*."},{"af":"In die tweede sin is *She thanked them* onduidelik (Nomsa of die ma?). Hou *Their mother* en vervang *Nomsa and Nomsa’s brother* met die voorwerpvorm *them*.","en":"In the second sentence *She thanked them* is unclear (Nomsa or the mother?). Keep *Their mother* and replace *Nomsa and Nomsa’s brother* with the object pronoun *them*."}],"answer":{"af":"*Nomsa and her brother washed their mother’s car. Their mother thanked them.*","en":"*Nomsa and her brother washed their mother’s car. Their mother thanked them.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Onderwerp of voorwerp?","en":"Subject or object?"},"problem":{"af":"Kies die regte woord: (a) *(We/Us) planted a tree.* (b) *The teacher showed (we/us) the map.* (c) *Liam and (I/me) are in the same class.* (d) *Gran baked a cake for Zanele and (I/me).*","en":"Choose the correct word: (a) *(We/Us) planted a tree.* (b) *The teacher showed (we/us) the map.* (c) *Liam and (I/me) are in the same class.* (d) *Gran baked a cake for Zanele and (I/me).*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die woord staan voor die werkwoord *planted* en doen die handeling: onderwerp, dus *We*.","en":"(a) The word comes before the verb *planted* and does the action: subject, so *We*."},{"af":"(b) Die woord kom ná die werkwoord *showed* en ontvang die handeling: voorwerp, dus *us*.","en":"(b) The word comes after the verb *showed* and receives the action: object, so *us*."},{"af":"(c) Bedek *Liam and*: *I am in the class* klink reg, dus *I*. (d) Bedek *Zanele and*: *for me* klink reg, dus *me*.","en":"(c) Cover *Liam and*: *I am in the class* sounds right, so *I*. (d) Cover *Zanele and*: *for me* sounds right, so *me*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *We* (b) *us* (c) *I* (d) *me*","en":"(a) *We* (b) *us* (c) *I* (d) *me*"}},{"title":{"af":"Besitlike voornaamwoorde","en":"Possessive pronouns"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf met ’n besitlike voornaamwoord wat alleen staan: (a) *This is my ruler.* (b) *These are their books.* (c) *That is her hat.*","en":"Rewrite with a possessive pronoun that stands on its own: (a) *This is my ruler.* (b) *These are their books.* (c) *That is her hat.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Skuif die naamwoord na voor: *This ruler is …, These books are …, That hat is …*","en":"Move the noun to the front: *This ruler is …, These books are …, That hat is …*"},{"af":"Kies die alleenstaande vorm: *my → mine, their → theirs, her → hers*. Geen afkappingsteken nie!","en":"Choose the form that stands alone: *my → mine, their → theirs, her → hers*. No apostrophe!"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *This ruler is mine.* (b) *These books are theirs.* (c) *That hat is hers.*","en":"(a) *This ruler is mine.* (b) *These books are theirs.* (c) *That hat is hers.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Die regte vraagwoord","en":"The correct question word"},"problem":{"af":"Vul *who, what, which* of *whose* in: (a) ___ *is knocking at the door?* (b) ___ *bag is this?* (c) ___ *juice do you want, orange or apple?* (d) ___ *did you eat for lunch?*","en":"Fill in *who, what, which* or *whose*: (a) ___ *is knocking at the door?* (b) ___ *bag is this?* (c) ___ *juice do you want, orange or apple?* (d) ___ *did you eat for lunch?*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Iemand klop – ons vra na ’n **persoon**: *Who*.","en":"(a) Someone is knocking – we ask about a **person**: *Who*."},{"af":"(b) Ons wil weet wie die **eienaar** is: *Whose*.","en":"(b) We want to know who the **owner** is: *Whose*."},{"af":"(c) Daar is ’n **keuse** tussen twee: *Which*. (d) Ons vra na ’n **ding** (kos): *What*.","en":"(c) There is a **choice** between two: *Which*. (d) We ask about a **thing** (food): *What*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *Who* (b) *Whose* (c) *Which* (d) *What*","en":"(a) *Who* (b) *Whose* (c) *Which* (d) *What*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte woord: *Thabo and ___ went to the shop.*","en":"Choose the correct word: *Thabo and ___ went to the shop.*"},"options":[{"af":"me","en":"me"},{"af":"us","en":"us"},{"af":"him","en":"him"},{"af":"I","en":"I"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Bedek *Thabo and*: *I went to the shop.* Die woord is deel van die onderwerp, so gebruik *I*.","en":"Cover *Thabo and*: *I went to the shop.* The word is part of the subject, so use *I*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte voorwerpvorm: *The teacher gave ___ our books.*","en":"Choose the correct object pronoun: *The teacher gave ___ our books.*"},"options":[{"af":"us","en":"us"},{"af":"we","en":"we"},{"af":"our","en":"our"},{"af":"ours","en":"ours"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die woord kom ná die werkwoord *gave* en ontvang die boeke, so dit is die voorwerpvorm *us*.","en":"The word comes after the verb *gave* and receives the books, so it is the object pronoun *us*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *This ruler belongs to me. It is* ___.","en":"Complete: *This ruler belongs to me. It is* ___."},"answers":{"af":["mine"],"en":["mine"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["my","me","mines"],"en":["my","me","mines"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die besitlike voornaamwoord wat alleen staan, is *mine*. *My* het ’n naamwoord ná hom nodig (*my ruler*), en *mines* bestaan nie.","en":"The possessive pronoun that stands alone is *mine*. *My* needs a noun after it (*my ruler*), and *mines* does not exist."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die sin *The dog wagged it’s tail.* is korrek.","en":"The sentence *The dog wagged it’s tail.* is correct."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die stert behoort aan die hond, so dit moet *its tail* wees. *It’s* beteken *it is*.","en":"False. The tail belongs to the dog, so it must be *its tail*. *It’s* means *it is*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voornaamwoord kan **Lerato and Aisha** vervang? ***Lerato and Aisha** are reading in the library.*","en":"Which pronoun can replace **Lerato and Aisha**? ***Lerato and Aisha** are reading in the library.*"},"options":[{"af":"She","en":"She"},{"af":"Her","en":"Her"},{"af":"They","en":"They"},{"af":"Them","en":"Them"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Dit is twee mense (meervoud) en hulle is die onderwerp, so *They*. *Them* is die voorwerpvorm, en *She/Her* is net vir een persoon.","en":"It is two people (plural) and they are the subject, so *They*. *Them* is the object form, and *She/Her* is for one person only."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke onderwerpvorm by sy voorwerpvorm.","en":"Match each subject pronoun to its object pronoun."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"I","en":"I"},"r":{"af":"me","en":"me"}},{"l":{"af":"he","en":"he"},"r":{"af":"him","en":"him"}},{"l":{"af":"she","en":"she"},"r":{"af":"her","en":"her"}},{"l":{"af":"we","en":"we"},"r":{"af":"us","en":"us"}},{"l":{"af":"they","en":"they"},"r":{"af":"them","en":"them"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die onderwerpvorm staan voor die werkwoord, die voorwerpvorm daarna: *I/me, he/him, she/her, we/us, they/them*.","en":"The subject form comes before the verb and the object form after it: *I/me, he/him, she/her, we/us, they/them*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte woord: *Look at ___ birds in the tree over there!*","en":"Choose the correct word: *Look at ___ birds in the tree over there!*"},"options":[{"af":"this","en":"this"},{"af":"those","en":"those"},{"af":"these","en":"these"},{"af":"that","en":"that"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die voëls is **ver** (*over there*) en daar is **meer as een**, so *those*. *These* is vir meer as een naby jou.","en":"The birds are **far** (*over there*) and there is **more than one**, so *those*. *These* is for more than one near you."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi die vraag: ___ *shoes are these? They are Sipho’s.*","en":"Complete the question: ___ *shoes are these? They are Sipho’s.*"},"answers":{"af":["Whose"],"en":["Whose"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Who’s","Who","Where"],"en":["Who’s","Who","Where"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die antwoord noem die eienaar (*Sipho’s*), so die vraag begin met *Whose*. *Who’s* beteken *who is*.","en":"The answer names the owner (*Sipho’s*), so the question starts with *Whose*. *Who’s* means *who is*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin vermy herhaling op die regte manier?","en":"Which sentence avoids repetition correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Pieter lost his cap, so he looked for it.","en":"Pieter lost his cap, so he looked for it."},{"af":"Pieter lost Pieter’s cap, so Pieter looked for it.","en":"Pieter lost Pieter’s cap, so Pieter looked for it."},{"af":"Pieter lost him cap, so he looked for it.","en":"Pieter lost him cap, so he looked for it."},{"af":"Pieter lost his cap, so him looked for it.","en":"Pieter lost his cap, so him looked for it."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*his* wys besit, *he* is die onderwerp en *it* vervang die pet. Die ander sinne herhaal die naam of gebruik die verkeerde vorm (*him cap, him looked*).","en":"*his* shows ownership, *he* is the subject and *it* replaces the cap. The other sentences repeat the name or use the wrong form (*him cap, him looked*)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter besitlike voornaamwoord kan **alleen** staan, sonder ’n naamwoord?","en":"Which possessive pronoun can stand **on its own**, without a noun?"},"options":[{"af":"their","en":"their"},{"af":"our","en":"our"},{"af":"my","en":"my"},{"af":"hers","en":"hers"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Hers* staan alleen: *The pen is hers.* *Their, our* en *my* het ’n naamwoord nodig: *their pen, our pen, my pen*.","en":"*Hers* stands alone: *The pen is hers.* *Their, our* and *my* need a noun: *their pen, our pen, my pen*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*These* gebruik jy vir meer as een ding wat naby jou is.","en":"You use *these* for more than one thing that is near you."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. *This* = een, naby; *these* = meer as een, naby: *these shoes here*.","en":"True. *This* = one, near; *these* = more than one, near: *these shoes here*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte vraagwoord: *___ pen do you want, the red one or the blue one?*","en":"Choose the correct question word: *___ pen do you want, the red one or the blue one?*"},"options":[{"af":"Who","en":"Who"},{"af":"Which","en":"Which"},{"af":"Whose","en":"Whose"},{"af":"Where","en":"Where"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Daar is ’n **keuse** tussen twee penne, so *Which*. *Who* vra na ’n persoon en *Whose* na die eienaar.","en":"There is a **choice** between two pens, so *Which*. *Who* asks about a person and *Whose* about the owner."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi met die regte voornaamwoord: *My brother is sick, so I made soup for* ___.","en":"Complete with the correct pronoun: *My brother is sick, so I made soup for* ___."},"answers":{"af":["him"],"en":["him"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["he","his","her"],"en":["he","his","her"]}},"explain":{"af":"Ná *for* kom die voorwerpvorm, en die broer is manlik: *him*. *He* is die onderwerpvorm en *his* wys besit.","en":"After *for* comes the object form, and the brother is male: *him*. *He* is the subject form and *his* shows ownership."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is korrek?","en":"Which sentence is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Them are my friends from school.","en":"Them are my friends from school."},{"af":"Ravi and me are in the choir.","en":"Ravi and me are in the choir."},{"af":"She and I walk to school together.","en":"She and I walk to school together."},{"af":"Us like to play in the park.","en":"Us like to play in the park."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*She* en *I* is albei onderwerpvorme voor die werkwoord *walk*. Die ander sinne gebruik voorwerpvorme (*them, me, us*) as onderwerp.","en":"*She* and *I* are both subject pronouns before the verb *walk*. The other sentences use object pronouns (*them, me, us*) as the subject."}}]},{"id":"eng5-t1-present-tenses","title":{"af":"Werkwoorde en die teenwoordige tyd","en":"Verbs and the present tenses"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal handelings- en hulpwerkwoorde kan herken, die eenvoudige en die voortdurende teenwoordige tyd in Engels reg kan gebruik en spel, en die werkwoord by die onderwerp laat pas.","en":"You will be able to recognise action and helping verbs, use and spell the simple present and present continuous tenses correctly, and make the verb agree with the subject."},"summary":{"af":"## Werkwoorde en hulpwerkwoorde\n\n’n **Werkwoord** (*verb*) sê wat iemand of iets **doen** of **is**.\n\n- **Handelingswerkwoorde** (*action verbs*) wys ’n handeling: *run, eat, write, swim, laugh*.\n- **Hulpwerkwoorde** (*helping verbs*) help die hoofwerkwoord of staan alleen: *am, is, are, have, has, do, does*.\n\n| Onderwerp | be (wees) | have (hê) | do (doen) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| I | am | have | do |\n| he / she / it | is | has | does |\n| you / we / they | are | have | do |\n\n## Die eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd\n\nGebruik die **eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd** (*simple present*) vir:\n- **gewoontes** en dinge wat gereeld gebeur: *I brush my teeth every morning.*\n- **feite** wat altyd waar is: *The sun rises in the east.*\n\n**Seinwoorde:** *always, usually, often, sometimes, never, every day, on Mondays*.\n\nDie werkwoord bly in sy **stam** (basisvorm), **behalwe** by *he, she, it* (of een persoon of ding). Dan kry dit **-s**: *I walk, you walk, we walk, they walk*, maar *he walks, she walks, it walks*.\n\nWaarom vergeet Afrikaanssprekendes die -s? In Afrikaans verander die werkwoord nooit nie: *ek loop, hy loop*. In Engels kry *he/she/it* altyd die -s.\n\n## Spelling: -s, -es of -ies?\n\n| Werkwoord eindig op … | Voeg by | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| die meeste werkwoorde | **-s** | *play → plays, run → runs, eat → eats* |\n| -s, -ss, -sh, -ch, -x, -o | **-es** | *miss → misses, wash → washes, catch → catches, fix → fixes, go → goes, do → does* |\n| medeklinker + y | y word **-ies** | *cry → cries, carry → carries, study → studies* |\n| klinker + y | **-s** | *play → plays, buy → buys, say → says* |\n\n*have* is onreëlmatig: *he **has***.\n\n## Die voortdurende teenwoordige tyd\n\nGebruik die **voortdurende teenwoordige tyd** (*present continuous*) vir iets wat **nou** gebeur, terwyl jy praat.\n\n**am / is / are + werkwoord + -ing**\n- *I **am reading** a book.* (Ek lees nou ’n boek.)\n- *Lerato **is drawing** a picture.*\n- *They **are playing** soccer.*\n\n**Seinwoorde:** *now, right now, at the moment, Look! Listen!*\n\nAfrikaans sê *Ek is besig om te lees* of net *Ek lees nou*. Engels het die hulpwerkwoord **én** die -ing nodig: *I am reading.*\n\n## Spelling van -ing\n\n| Reël | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| Die meeste werkwoorde: voeg -ing by | *read → reading, play → playing, eat → eating* |\n| Stil e aan die einde: laat die e weg | *make → making, write → writing, ride → riding* |\n| Kort woord met kort klinker + een medeklinker: verdubbel | *run → running, swim → swimming, sit → sitting, hop → hopping* |\n| -ie aan die einde: word y | *lie → lying, tie → tying* |\n\n## Ooreenstemming tussen onderwerp en werkwoord\n\nDie werkwoord moet by die onderwerp **pas**:\n- een persoon of ding (**enkelvoud**): *The dog **barks**. My sister **is** tall. He **does** his homework.*\n- meer as een (**meervoud**): *The dogs **bark**. My sisters **are** tall. They **do** their homework.*\n- Twee name met *and* is meervoud: *Thabo and Liam **play** chess.*\n\n> **Onthou:** Net *he, she, it* (of een persoon of ding) kry die -s in die eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd. *I* en *you* kry nooit -s nie: *I like, you like*.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *She walk to school.* → *She walks to school.* / *He is play.* → *He is playing.* / *They is happy.* → *They are happy.*","en":"## Action verbs and helping verbs\n\nA **verb** tells us what someone or something **does** or **is**.\n\n- **Action verbs** show an action: *run, eat, write, swim, laugh*.\n- **Helping verbs** help the main verb or stand on their own: *am, is, are, have, has, do, does*.\n\n| Subject | be | have | do |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| I | am | have | do |\n| he / she / it | is | has | does |\n| you / we / they | are | have | do |\n\n## The simple present tense\n\nUse the **simple present** for:\n- **habits** and things that happen regularly: *I brush my teeth every morning.*\n- **facts** that are always true: *The sun rises in the east.*\n\n**Signal words:** *always, usually, often, sometimes, never, every day, on Mondays*.\n\nThe verb stays in its **base form**, **except** with *he, she, it* (or one person or thing). Then it gets **-s**: *I walk, you walk, we walk, they walk*, but *he walks, she walks, it walks*.\n\nWhy do Afrikaans speakers often forget the -s? In Afrikaans the verb never changes: *ek loop, hy loop*. In English, *he/she/it* always needs the -s.\n\n## Spelling: -s, -es or -ies?\n\n| Verb ends in … | Add | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| most verbs | **-s** | *play → plays, run → runs, eat → eats* |\n| -s, -ss, -sh, -ch, -x, -o | **-es** | *miss → misses, wash → washes, catch → catches, fix → fixes, go → goes, do → does* |\n| consonant + y | y becomes **-ies** | *cry → cries, carry → carries, study → studies* |\n| vowel + y | **-s** | *play → plays, buy → buys, say → says* |\n\n*have* is irregular: *he **has***.\n\n## The present continuous tense\n\nUse the **present continuous** for something that is happening **now**, while you are speaking.\n\n**am / is / are + verb + -ing**\n- *I **am reading** a book.*\n- *Lerato **is drawing** a picture.*\n- *They **are playing** soccer.*\n\n**Signal words:** *now, right now, at the moment, Look! Listen!*\n\nAfrikaans says *Ek is besig om te lees* or just *Ek lees nou*. English needs the helping verb **and** the -ing: *I am reading.*\n\n## Spelling of -ing\n\n| Rule | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| Most verbs: add -ing | *read → reading, play → playing, eat → eating* |\n| Silent e at the end: drop the e | *make → making, write → writing, ride → riding* |\n| Short word with a short vowel + one consonant: double it | *run → running, swim → swimming, sit → sitting, hop → hopping* |\n| -ie at the end: becomes y | *lie → lying, tie → tying* |\n\n## Subject–verb agreement\n\nThe verb must **agree** with (match) the subject:\n- one person or thing (**singular**): *The dog **barks**. My sister **is** tall. He **does** his homework.*\n- more than one (**plural**): *The dogs **bark**. My sisters **are** tall. They **do** their homework.*\n- Two names joined by *and* are plural: *Thabo and Liam **play** chess.*\n\n> **Remember:** Only *he, she, it* (or one person or thing) gets the -s in the simple present. *I* and *you* never get -s: *I like, you like*.\n\n> **Common mistake:** *She walk to school.* → *She walks to school.* / *He is play.* → *He is playing.* / *They is happy.* → *They are happy.*"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Werkwoord (*verb*)","en":"Verb"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat sê wat iemand doen of is, soos *run* of *is*.","en":"A word that tells what someone does or is, such as *run* or *is*."}},{"term":{"af":"Handelingswerkwoord (*action verb*)","en":"Action verb"},"def":{"af":"’n Werkwoord wat ’n handeling wys: *jump, eat, write*.","en":"A verb that shows an action: *jump, eat, write*."}},{"term":{"af":"Hulpwerkwoord (*helping verb*)","en":"Helping verb"},"def":{"af":"’n Werkwoord soos *am, is, are, have, has, do, does* wat die hoofwerkwoord help.","en":"A verb such as *am, is, are, have, has, do, does* that helps the main verb."}},{"term":{"af":"Eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd (*simple present*)","en":"Simple present tense"},"def":{"af":"Die tyd vir gewoontes en feite: *She walks to school every day.*","en":"The tense for habits and facts: *She walks to school every day.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Voortdurende teenwoordige tyd (*present continuous*)","en":"Present continuous tense"},"def":{"af":"Die tyd vir iets wat nou gebeur: *am/is/are* + werkwoord + *-ing*: *He is eating.*","en":"The tense for something happening now: *am/is/are* + verb + *-ing*: *He is eating.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Onderwerp (*subject*)","en":"Subject"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon of ding wat die handeling doen: ***Lerato** sings.*","en":"The person or thing doing the action: ***Lerato** sings.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Ooreenstemming (*subject–verb agreement*)","en":"Subject–verb agreement"},"def":{"af":"Die werkwoord pas by die onderwerp: *he plays*, maar *they play*.","en":"The verb matches the subject: *he plays*, but *they play*."}},{"term":{"af":"Stam (*base form*)","en":"Base form"},"def":{"af":"Die werkwoord sonder enige uitgang, soos *play* of *go*.","en":"The verb without any ending, such as *play* or *go*."}},{"term":{"af":"Seinwoorde (*signal words*)","en":"Signal words"},"def":{"af":"Woorde soos *every day* of *now* wat wys watter tyd jy moet gebruik.","en":"Words such as *every day* or *now* that show which tense to use."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Die -s in die eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd","en":"The -s in the simple present"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die regte vorm van die werkwoord: (a) *Ravi (watch) TV every evening.* (b) *My baby brother (cry) at night.* (c) *We (play) netball on Fridays.* (d) *Fatima (have) two cats.*","en":"Write the correct form of the verb: (a) *Ravi (watch) TV every evening.* (b) *My baby brother (cry) at night.* (c) *We (play) netball on Fridays.* (d) *Fatima (have) two cats.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Seinwoorde *every evening, at night, on Fridays* wys dit is gewoontes: eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd.","en":"The signal words *every evening, at night, on Fridays* show habits: simple present."},{"af":"(a) *Ravi* = *he*, en *watch* eindig op -ch: *watches*. (b) *brother* = *he*, en *cry* eindig op medeklinker + y: *cries*.","en":"(a) *Ravi* = *he*, and *watch* ends in -ch: *watches*. (b) *brother* = *he*, and *cry* ends in consonant + y: *cries*."},{"af":"(c) *We* kry geen -s nie: *play*. (d) *Fatima* = *she*, en *have* is onreëlmatig: *has*.","en":"(c) *We* gets no -s: *play*. (d) *Fatima* = *she*, and *have* is irregular: *has*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *watches* (b) *cries* (c) *play* (d) *has*","en":"(a) *watches* (b) *cries* (c) *play* (d) *has*"}},{"title":{"af":"Die voortdurende teenwoordige tyd","en":"The present continuous"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf in die voortdurende teenwoordige tyd: *Look! The children (swim) and Johan (ride) his bike.*","en":"Write in the present continuous: *Look! The children (swim) and Johan (ride) his bike.*"},"steps":[{"af":"*Look!* wys dit gebeur nou: gebruik *am/is/are* + -ing.","en":"*Look!* shows it is happening now: use *am/is/are* + -ing."},{"af":"*The children* is meervoud, so *are*. *Swim* het ’n kort klinker + een medeklinker: verdubbel die m: *swimming*.","en":"*The children* is plural, so *are*. *Swim* has a short vowel + one consonant: double the m: *swimming*."},{"af":"*Johan* = *he*, so *is*. *Ride* eindig op ’n stil e: laat dit weg: *riding*.","en":"*Johan* = *he*, so *is*. *Ride* ends in a silent e: drop it: *riding*."}],"answer":{"af":"*Look! The children are swimming and Johan is riding his bike.*","en":"*Look! The children are swimming and Johan is riding his bike.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Watter tyd?","en":"Which tense?"},"problem":{"af":"Voltooi: *Anika usually (walk) to school, but today she (go) by car.*","en":"Complete: *Anika usually (walk) to school, but today she (go) by car.*"},"steps":[{"af":"*usually* wys ’n gewoonte: eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd, en *Anika* = *she*: *walks*.","en":"*usually* shows a habit: simple present, and *Anika* = *she*: *walks*."},{"af":"*today* wys iets wat nou anders gebeur: voortdurende teenwoordige tyd: *is going*.","en":"*today* shows something different happening now: present continuous: *is going*."}],"answer":{"af":"*Anika usually walks to school, but today she is going by car.*","en":"*Anika usually walks to school, but today she is going by car.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Verbeter die foute","en":"Correct the mistakes"},"problem":{"af":"Verbeter: *My mother work in a shop. She are selling clothes now.*","en":"Correct: *My mother work in a shop. She are selling clothes now.*"},"steps":[{"af":"*My mother* is een persoon (*she*), so die eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd kry -s: *works*.","en":"*My mother* is one person (*she*), so the simple present gets -s: *works*."},{"af":"By *she* is die hulpwerkwoord *is*, nie *are* nie: *She is selling*.","en":"With *she* the helping verb is *is*, not *are*: *She is selling*."}],"answer":{"af":"*My mother works in a shop. She is selling clothes now.*","en":"*My mother works in a shop. She is selling clothes now.*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is in die **eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd** (*simple present*)?","en":"Which sentence is in the **simple present**?"},"options":[{"af":"Sipho plays the drums every Saturday.","en":"Sipho plays the drums every Saturday."},{"af":"Sipho is playing the drums now.","en":"Sipho is playing the drums now."},{"af":"Sipho played the drums yesterday.","en":"Sipho played the drums yesterday."},{"af":"Sipho will play the drums tomorrow.","en":"Sipho will play the drums tomorrow."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Every Saturday* wys ’n gewoonte, en *plays* is die eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd. *Is playing* is voortdurend, *played* is verlede tyd en *will play* is toekomend.","en":"*Every Saturday* shows a habit, and *plays* is the simple present. *Is playing* is present continuous, *played* is past and *will play* is future."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *My sister ___ (wash) the dishes every evening.*","en":"Complete: *My sister ___ (wash) the dishes every evening.*"},"answers":{"af":["washes"],"en":["washes"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["wash","washs","washies"],"en":["wash","washs","washies"]}},"explain":{"af":"*My sister* = *she*, so die werkwoord kry ’n uitgang. *Wash* eindig op -sh, so dit kry -es: *washes*.","en":"*My sister* = *she*, so the verb needs an ending. *Wash* ends in -sh, so it takes -es: *washes*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die korrekte *-ing*-vorm van *swim*?","en":"What is the correct *-ing* form of *swim*?"},"options":[{"af":"swiming","en":"swiming"},{"af":"swimeing","en":"swimeing"},{"af":"swimming","en":"swimming"},{"af":"swims","en":"swims"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Swim* is ’n kort woord met ’n kort klinker (i) en een medeklinker (m) aan die einde, so die m word verdubbel: *swimming*.","en":"*Swim* is a short word with a short vowel (i) and one consonant (m) at the end, so the m is doubled: *swimming*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte hulpwerkwoord: *The children ___ singing in the hall.*","en":"Choose the correct helping verb: *The children ___ singing in the hall.*"},"options":[{"af":"is","en":"is"},{"af":"am","en":"am"},{"af":"be","en":"be"},{"af":"are","en":"are"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*The children* is meervoud (*they*), so die hulpwerkwoord is *are*: *The children are singing.*","en":"*The children* is plural (*they*), so the helping verb is *are*: *The children are singing.*"}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Ons gebruik die voortdurende teenwoordige tyd vir gewoontes, soos *I am brushing my teeth every morning.*","en":"We use the present continuous for habits, such as *I am brushing my teeth every morning.*"},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Vir gewoontes (*every morning*) gebruik jy die eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd: *I brush my teeth every morning.* Die voortdurende tyd is vir wat nou gebeur.","en":"False. For habits (*every morning*) you use the simple present: *I brush my teeth every morning.* The present continuous is for what is happening now."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte spelling: *He ___ (carry) his bag to school every day.*","en":"Choose the correct spelling: *He ___ (carry) his bag to school every day.*"},"options":[{"af":"carrys","en":"carrys"},{"af":"carries","en":"carries"},{"af":"carryes","en":"carryes"},{"af":"carry","en":"carry"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Carry* eindig op medeklinker (r) + y, so die y word -ies: *carries*. *Carry* sonder uitgang is verkeerd by *he*.","en":"*Carry* ends in consonant (r) + y, so the y becomes -ies: *carries*. *Carry* without an ending is wrong with *he*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Look! It ___ raining.*","en":"Complete: *Look! It ___ raining.*"},"answers":{"af":["is"],"en":["is"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["are","am","be"],"en":["are","am","be"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Look!* wys dit gebeur nou: voortdurende teenwoordige tyd. By *it* is die hulpwerkwoord *is*.","en":"*Look!* shows it is happening now: present continuous. With *it* the helping verb is *is*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is korrek? (Let op die ooreenstemming tussen onderwerp en werkwoord.)","en":"Which sentence is correct? (Check subject–verb agreement.)"},"options":[{"af":"The dogs barks at night.","en":"The dogs barks at night."},{"af":"My friends live in Polokwane.","en":"My friends live in Polokwane."},{"af":"Thabo and Liam plays chess.","en":"Thabo and Liam plays chess."},{"af":"The cat sleep on my bed.","en":"The cat sleep on my bed."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*My friends* is meervoud, so geen -s nie: *live*. *The dogs* en *Thabo and Liam* is meervoud (geen -s nie), en *the cat* is enkelvoud (kry -s: *sleeps*).","en":"*My friends* is plural, so no -s: *live*. *The dogs* and *Thabo and Liam* are plural (no -s), and *the cat* is singular (needs -s: *sleeps*)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke werkwoord by sy *he/she*-vorm in die eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd.","en":"Match each verb to its *he/she* form in the simple present."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"go","en":"go"},"r":{"af":"goes","en":"goes"}},{"l":{"af":"fly","en":"fly"},"r":{"af":"flies","en":"flies"}},{"l":{"af":"have","en":"have"},"r":{"af":"has","en":"has"}},{"l":{"af":"catch","en":"catch"},"r":{"af":"catches","en":"catches"}},{"l":{"af":"play","en":"play"},"r":{"af":"plays","en":"plays"}}],"explain":{"af":"*go* en *catch* kry -es, *fly* (medeklinker + y) kry -ies, *have* word *has*, en *play* (klinker + y) kry net -s.","en":"*go* and *catch* take -es, *fly* (consonant + y) takes -ies, *have* becomes *has*, and *play* (vowel + y) just takes -s."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is die **hulpwerkwoord** in *She is reading a book*?","en":"Which word is the **helping verb** in *She is reading a book*?"},"options":[{"af":"She","en":"She"},{"af":"reading","en":"reading"},{"af":"book","en":"book"},{"af":"is","en":"is"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Is* help die hoofwerkwoord *reading* om die voortdurende teenwoordige tyd te vorm. *She* is die onderwerp en *book* is ’n naamwoord.","en":"*Is* helps the main verb *reading* to form the present continuous. *She* is the subject and *book* is a noun."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Dit is ’n feit. Kies die regte vorm: *Water ___ at 100 °C.*","en":"This is a fact. Choose the correct form: *Water ___ at 100 °C.*"},"options":[{"af":"boils","en":"boils"},{"af":"is boiling","en":"is boiling"},{"af":"boil","en":"boil"},{"af":"are boiling","en":"are boiling"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Feite wat altyd waar is, staan in die eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd. *Water* is enkelvoud (*it*), so: *boils*.","en":"Facts that are always true are in the simple present. *Water* is singular (*it*), so: *boils*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*Make* word *making*, want jy laat die stil e weg voor jy -ing byvoeg.","en":"*Make* becomes *making*, because you drop the silent e before adding -ing."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Werkwoorde wat op ’n stil e eindig, verloor die e: *make → making, write → writing*.","en":"True. Verbs that end in a silent e lose the e: *make → making, write → writing*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi in die voortdurende teenwoordige tyd: *Listen! The baby ___ (cry).*","en":"Complete in the present continuous: *Listen! The baby ___ (cry).*"},"answers":{"af":["is crying"],"en":["is crying"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["cries","is cry","are crying"],"en":["cries","is cry","are crying"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Listen!* wys dit gebeur nou. *The baby* = *it/he/she*, so *is*, en *cry* + -ing = *crying* (die y bly).","en":"*Listen!* shows it is happening now. *The baby* is singular, so *is*, and *cry* + -ing = *crying* (the y stays)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter seinwoord wys dat jy die **voortdurende teenwoordige tyd** moet gebruik?","en":"Which signal word shows that you should use the **present continuous**?"},"options":[{"af":"every day","en":"every day"},{"af":"always","en":"always"},{"af":"at the moment","en":"at the moment"},{"af":"on Sundays","en":"on Sundays"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*At the moment* beteken nou, terwyl jy praat. *Every day, always* en *on Sundays* wys gewoontes, so hulle hoort by die eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd.","en":"*At the moment* means now, while you are speaking. *Every day, always* and *on Sundays* show habits, so they go with the simple present."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Sinne bou","en":"Building sentences"},"topics":[{"id":"eng5-t2-past-future-tenses","title":{"af":"Die verlede en toekomende tyd","en":"Past and future tenses"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal Engelse werkwoorde reg in die verlede tyd kan skryf (ook onreëlmatige werkwoorde), die voortdurende verlede tyd en die toekomende tyd met *will* en *going to* kan gebruik, en tydsaanduiders kan raaksien.","en":"You will be able to write verbs correctly in the past tense (also irregular verbs), use the past continuous and the future tense with *will* and *going to*, and notice the time words that signal the tense."},"summary":{"af":"## Die verlede tyd: reëlmatige werkwoorde\n\nGebruik die **eenvoudige verlede tyd** (*simple past*) vir iets wat in die verlede **gebeur het en klaar is**: *Yesterday I **walked** to the shop.*\n\n**Reëlmatige werkwoorde** kry **-ed**. Die vorm is dieselfde vir elke persoon: *I walked, she walked, they walked.*\n\n| Reël | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| Die meeste werkwoorde: voeg -ed by | *walk → walked, jump → jumped, help → helped* |\n| Eindig op -e: voeg net -d by | *bake → baked, smile → smiled, dance → danced* |\n| Medeklinker + y: y word -ied | *cry → cried, carry → carried, study → studied* |\n| Klinker + y: voeg -ed by | *play → played, stay → stayed* |\n| Kort woord, kort klinker + een medeklinker: verdubbel | *stop → stopped, hop → hopped, clap → clapped, plan → planned* |\n\nAfrikaans vorm die verlede tyd met *het ge-*: *Ek **het** ge**stap***. Engels gebruik net een woord: *I **walked***. Moenie *I have walked yesterday* skryf nie.\n\n## Onreëlmatige werkwoorde\n\nBaie algemene werkwoorde is **onreëlmatig**: hulle kry nie -ed nie. Jy moet hulle leer.\n\n| Teenwoordig | Verlede | Teenwoordig | Verlede |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| go | went | write | wrote |\n| see | saw | buy | bought |\n| eat | ate | think | thought |\n| run | ran | come | came |\n| take | took | give | gave |\n| have | had | make | made |\n| sing | sang | swim | swam |\n| bring | brought | catch | caught |\n| sleep | slept | tell | told |\n\nLet op *buy – bought* (koop) en *bring – brought* (bring): hulle lyk amper eners.\n\nIn ontkennings en vrae gebruik jy **did** + die stam: *I **didn’t go**. **Did** you **see** it?* (nie *didn’t went* nie)\n\n## Die voortdurende verlede tyd\n\nGebruik die **voortdurende verlede tyd** (*past continuous*) vir ’n handeling wat op ’n tyd in die verlede **besig was om te gebeur**. Dikwels word dit **onderbreek** deur ’n korter handeling in die eenvoudige verlede tyd.\n\n**was / were + werkwoord + -ing**\n- *I / he / she / it **was** reading.*\n- *You / we / they **were** playing.*\n- *I **was doing** my homework when the lights **went** out.* (Ek was besig met my huiswerk toe die ligte afgaan.)\n\n## Die toekomende tyd: will en going to\n\n| Vorm | Gebruik | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **will** + stam | ’n belofte, ’n vinnige besluit of ’n raaiskoot oor die toekoms | *I **will help** you. It **will be** hot tomorrow.* |\n| **am/is/are going to** + stam | ’n plan wat jy reeds gemaak het, of iets wat jy sien kom | *We **are going to visit** Gran on Saturday. Look at those clouds! It **is going to rain**.* |\n\nKort vorme: *I’ll* = *I will*, *won’t* = *will not*. Ná *will* kry die werkwoord nooit -s nie: *She will go* (nie *will goes* nie).\n\n## Tydsaanduiders wys die tyd\n\n| Verlede | Teenwoordig | Toekoms |\n|---|---|---|\n| *yesterday, last week, two days ago, last year* | *now, every day, at the moment* | *tomorrow, next week, soon, later* |\n\n> **Onthou:** Soek eers die tydsaanduider. *Yesterday* → verlede tyd; *now* → teenwoordige tyd; *tomorrow* → toekomende tyd.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *Yesterday I goed to the park.* → *Yesterday I went to the park.* / *I didn’t saw him.* → *I didn’t see him.* / *They was playing.* → *They were playing.*","en":"## The simple past tense: regular verbs\n\nUse the **simple past** for something that **happened and is finished**: *Yesterday I **walked** to the shop.*\n\n**Regular verbs** add **-ed**. The form is the same for every person: *I walked, she walked, they walked.*\n\n| Rule | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| Most verbs: add -ed | *walk → walked, jump → jumped, help → helped* |\n| Ends in -e: add only -d | *bake → baked, smile → smiled, dance → danced* |\n| Consonant + y: y becomes -ied | *cry → cried, carry → carried, study → studied* |\n| Vowel + y: add -ed | *play → played, stay → stayed* |\n| Short word, short vowel + one consonant: double it | *stop → stopped, hop → hopped, clap → clapped, plan → planned* |\n\nAfrikaans makes the past tense with *het ge-*: *Ek **het** ge**stap***. English uses only one word: *I **walked***. Do not write *I have walked yesterday*.\n\n## Irregular verbs\n\nMany common verbs are **irregular**: they do not add -ed. You must learn them.\n\n| Present | Past | Present | Past |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| go | went | write | wrote |\n| see | saw | buy | bought |\n| eat | ate | think | thought |\n| run | ran | come | came |\n| take | took | give | gave |\n| have | had | make | made |\n| sing | sang | swim | swam |\n| bring | brought | catch | caught |\n| sleep | slept | tell | told |\n\nLook carefully at *buy – bought* and *bring – brought*: they look almost the same.\n\nIn negatives and questions, use **did** + the base form: *I **didn’t go**. **Did** you **see** it?* (not *didn’t went*)\n\n## The past continuous tense\n\nUse the **past continuous** for an action that was **busy happening** at a time in the past. Often it is **interrupted** by a shorter action in the simple past.\n\n**was / were + verb + -ing**\n- *I / he / she / it **was** reading.*\n- *You / we / they **were** playing.*\n- *I **was doing** my homework when the lights **went** out.*\n\n## The future tense: will and going to\n\n| Form | Use | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **will** + base form | a promise, a quick decision or a guess about the future | *I **will help** you. It **will be** hot tomorrow.* |\n| **am/is/are going to** + base form | a plan you have already made, or something you can see coming | *We **are going to visit** Gran on Saturday. Look at those clouds! It **is going to rain**.* |\n\nShort forms: *I’ll* = *I will*, *won’t* = *will not*. After *will* the verb never gets -s: *She will go* (not *will goes*).\n\n## Time words show the tense\n\n| Past | Present | Future |\n|---|---|---|\n| *yesterday, last week, two days ago, last year* | *now, every day, at the moment* | *tomorrow, next week, soon, later* |\n\n> **Remember:** Look for the time word first. *Yesterday* → past tense; *now* → present tense; *tomorrow* → future tense.\n\n> **Common mistake:** *Yesterday I goed to the park.* → *Yesterday I went to the park.* / *I didn’t saw him.* → *I didn’t see him.* / *They was playing.* → *They were playing.*"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Eenvoudige verlede tyd (*simple past*)","en":"Simple past tense"},"def":{"af":"Die tyd vir iets wat gebeur het en klaar is: *I walked, she ate*.","en":"The tense for something that happened and is finished: *I walked, she ate*."}},{"term":{"af":"Reëlmatige werkwoord (*regular verb*)","en":"Regular verb"},"def":{"af":"’n Werkwoord wat in die verlede tyd -ed kry: *jump → jumped*.","en":"A verb that adds -ed in the past tense: *jump → jumped*."}},{"term":{"af":"Onreëlmatige werkwoord (*irregular verb*)","en":"Irregular verb"},"def":{"af":"’n Werkwoord wat nie -ed kry nie en wat jy moet leer: *go → went, buy → bought*.","en":"A verb that does not add -ed, so you must learn it: *go → went, buy → bought*."}},{"term":{"af":"Voortdurende verlede tyd (*past continuous*)","en":"Past continuous tense"},"def":{"af":"*was/were* + werkwoord + *-ing* vir iets wat besig was om te gebeur: *We were eating.*","en":"*was/were* + verb + *-ing* for something that was busy happening: *We were eating.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Toekomende tyd (*future tense*)","en":"Future tense"},"def":{"af":"Die tyd vir iets wat nog gaan gebeur, met *will* of *going to*.","en":"The tense for something that is still going to happen, with *will* or *going to*."}},{"term":{"af":"*will*","en":"*will*"},"def":{"af":"Hulpwerkwoord vir ’n belofte, ’n vinnige besluit of ’n raaiskoot oor die toekoms: *I will help.*","en":"Helping verb for a promise, a quick decision or a guess about the future: *I will help.*"}},{"term":{"af":"*going to*","en":"*going to*"},"def":{"af":"*am/is/are going to* + stam vir ’n plan of iets wat jy sien kom: *It is going to rain.*","en":"*am/is/are going to* + base form for a plan or something you can see coming: *It is going to rain.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Tydsaanduider (*time word*)","en":"Time word"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord soos *yesterday, now* of *tomorrow* wat wys watter tyd jy moet gebruik.","en":"A word such as *yesterday, now* or *tomorrow* that shows which tense to use."}},{"term":{"af":"*did* + stam","en":"*did* + base form"},"def":{"af":"Die vorm vir vrae en ontkennings in die verlede tyd: *Did you go? I didn’t go.*","en":"The form for questions and negatives in the past tense: *Did you go? I didn’t go.*"}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Spelling van reëlmatige werkwoorde","en":"Spelling regular verbs"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die verlede tyd van *stop, cry, bake* en *play*.","en":"Write the past tense of *stop, cry, bake* and *play*."},"steps":[{"af":"*stop*: kort woord, kort klinker + een medeklinker. Verdubbel die p: *stopped*.","en":"*stop*: short word, short vowel + one consonant. Double the p: *stopped*."},{"af":"*cry*: medeklinker + y. Die y word -ied: *cried*.","en":"*cry*: consonant + y. The y becomes -ied: *cried*."},{"af":"*bake* eindig reeds op -e, so voeg net -d by: *baked*. *play*: klinker + y, so voeg net -ed by: *played*.","en":"*bake* already ends in -e, so add only -d: *baked*. *play*: vowel + y, so just add -ed: *played*."}],"answer":{"af":"*stopped, cried, baked, played*","en":"*stopped, cried, baked, played*"}},{"title":{"af":"Onreëlmatige werkwoorde","en":"Irregular verbs"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf in die verlede tyd en begin met *Yesterday*: *Today Sipho goes to the market. He buys mangoes and eats one.*","en":"Rewrite in the past tense, starting with *Yesterday*: *Today Sipho goes to the market. He buys mangoes and eats one.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Vervang *Today* met *Yesterday*. Die werkwoorde moet nou in die verlede tyd staan.","en":"Replace *Today* with *Yesterday*. The verbs must now be in the past tense."},{"af":"Al drie is onreëlmatig: *go → went, buy → bought, eat → ate*. Die -s van die teenwoordige tyd val weg.","en":"All three are irregular: *go → went, buy → bought, eat → ate*. The -s of the present tense falls away."}],"answer":{"af":"*Yesterday Sipho went to the market. He bought mangoes and ate one.*","en":"*Yesterday Sipho went to the market. He bought mangoes and ate one.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Voortdurende en eenvoudige verlede tyd saam","en":"Past continuous and simple past together"},"problem":{"af":"Voltooi: *Lerato (read) when the dog (bark).*","en":"Complete: *Lerato (read) when the dog (bark).*"},"steps":[{"af":"Die lang handeling wat besig was, is *read*: *was/were* + -ing. *Lerato* = *she*, so: *was reading*.","en":"The long action that was busy happening is *read*: *was/were* + -ing. *Lerato* = *she*, so: *was reading*."},{"af":"Die kort handeling wat dit onderbreek, staan in die eenvoudige verlede tyd: *barked*.","en":"The short action that interrupts it is in the simple past: *barked*."}],"answer":{"af":"*Lerato was reading when the dog barked.*","en":"*Lerato was reading when the dog barked.*"}},{"title":{"af":"will of going to?","en":"will or going to?"},"problem":{"af":"Kies *will* of *going to*: (a) *Look at that ball! It ___ break the window.* (b) *“I’m thirsty.” – “Wait, I ___ get you some water.”*","en":"Choose *will* or *going to*: (a) *Look at that ball! It ___ break the window.* (b) *“I’m thirsty.” – “Wait, I ___ get you some water.”*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Jy **sien** dit kom – die bal vlieg reeds na die venster. Gebruik *is going to*.","en":"(a) You can **see** it coming – the ball is already flying towards the window. Use *is going to*."},{"af":"(b) Dit is ’n **vinnige besluit** op die oomblik, nie ’n plan nie. Gebruik *will* (*I’ll*).","en":"(b) It is a **quick decision** at that moment, not a plan. Use *will* (*I’ll*)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *is going to* (b) *will*","en":"(a) *is going to* (b) *will*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die verlede tyd van *carry*?","en":"What is the past tense of *carry*?"},"options":[{"af":"carryed","en":"carryed"},{"af":"carried","en":"carried"},{"af":"carred","en":"carred"},{"af":"caried","en":"caried"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Carry* eindig op medeklinker (r) + y, so die y word -ied: *carried*. Die dubbel r bly.","en":"*Carry* ends in consonant (r) + y, so the y becomes -ied: *carried*. The double r stays."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte vorm: *Yesterday we ___ to the beach.*","en":"Choose the correct form: *Yesterday we ___ to the beach.*"},"options":[{"af":"went","en":"went"},{"af":"goed","en":"goed"},{"af":"go","en":"go"},{"af":"going","en":"going"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Yesterday* wys die verlede tyd, en *go* is onreëlmatig: *went*. *Goed* bestaan nie.","en":"*Yesterday* shows the past tense, and *go* is irregular: *went*. *Goed* does not exist."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Last week Ravi ___ (buy) a new soccer ball.*","en":"Complete: *Last week Ravi ___ (buy) a new soccer ball.*"},"answers":{"af":["bought"],"en":["bought"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["buyed","brought","buys"],"en":["buyed","brought","buys"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Last week* wys die verlede tyd. *Buy* is onreëlmatig: *bought*. Pas op: *brought* is die verlede tyd van *bring*.","en":"*Last week* shows the past tense. *Buy* is irregular: *bought*. Careful: *brought* is the past tense of *bring*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is in die **voortdurende verlede tyd** (*past continuous*)?","en":"Which sentence is in the **past continuous**?"},"options":[{"af":"Thabo played soccer.","en":"Thabo played soccer."},{"af":"Thabo is playing soccer.","en":"Thabo is playing soccer."},{"af":"Thabo will play soccer.","en":"Thabo will play soccer."},{"af":"Thabo was playing soccer.","en":"Thabo was playing soccer."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die voortdurende verlede tyd is *was/were* + -ing: *was playing*. *Is playing* is teenwoordig, *played* is eenvoudige verlede tyd en *will play* is toekomend.","en":"The past continuous is *was/were* + -ing: *was playing*. *Is playing* is present, *played* is simple past and *will play* is future."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die sin *I didn’t went to school.* is korrek.","en":"The sentence *I didn’t went to school.* is correct."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Ná *did* of *didn’t* kom die stam: *I didn’t go to school.* Die *did* wys reeds die verlede tyd.","en":"False. After *did* or *didn’t* comes the base form: *I didn’t go to school.* The *did* already shows the past tense."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke werkwoord by sy verlede tyd.","en":"Match each verb to its past tense."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"see","en":"see"},"r":{"af":"saw","en":"saw"}},{"l":{"af":"eat","en":"eat"},"r":{"af":"ate","en":"ate"}},{"l":{"af":"take","en":"take"},"r":{"af":"took","en":"took"}},{"l":{"af":"write","en":"write"},"r":{"af":"wrote","en":"wrote"}},{"l":{"af":"think","en":"think"},"r":{"af":"thought","en":"thought"}}],"explain":{"af":"Al vyf is onreëlmatige werkwoorde wat jy moet leer: *see – saw, eat – ate, take – took, write – wrote, think – thought*.","en":"All five are irregular verbs that you must learn: *see – saw, eat – ate, take – took, write – wrote, think – thought*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte woord: *We ___ watching TV when the lights went out.*","en":"Choose the correct word: *We ___ watching TV when the lights went out.*"},"options":[{"af":"was","en":"was"},{"af":"are","en":"are"},{"af":"were","en":"were"},{"af":"is","en":"is"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Dit is die voortdurende verlede tyd, en *we* is meervoud: *were*. *Was* is vir *I, he, she, it*.","en":"This is the past continuous, and *we* is plural: *were*. *Was* is for *I, he, she, it*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf *stop* in die verlede tyd: *The bus ___ at the corner.*","en":"Write *stop* in the past tense: *The bus ___ at the corner.*"},"answers":{"af":["stopped"],"en":["stopped"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["stoped","stopt","stopping"],"en":["stoped","stopt","stopping"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Stop* is ’n kort woord met ’n kort klinker + een medeklinker, so die p word verdubbel voor -ed: *stopped*.","en":"*Stop* is a short word with a short vowel + one consonant, so the p is doubled before -ed: *stopped*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter tydsaanduider wys dat jy die **toekomende tyd** moet gebruik?","en":"Which time word shows that you should use the **future tense**?"},"options":[{"af":"yesterday","en":"yesterday"},{"af":"ago","en":"ago"},{"af":"now","en":"now"},{"af":"tomorrow","en":"tomorrow"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Tomorrow* (môre) is in die toekoms. *Yesterday* en *ago* is verlede tyd en *now* is teenwoordige tyd.","en":"*Tomorrow* is in the future. *Yesterday* and *ago* go with the past tense and *now* with the present tense."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die beste antwoord: *Look at those dark clouds! It ___ rain.*","en":"Choose the best answer: *Look at those dark clouds! It ___ rain.*"},"options":[{"af":"will be","en":"will be"},{"af":"is going to","en":"is going to"},{"af":"was","en":"was"},{"af":"going","en":"going"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Jy kan sien dit kom (donker wolke), so *is going to*. *It will be rain* en *It going rain* is verkeerd, en *was* is verlede tyd.","en":"You can see it coming (dark clouds), so *is going to*. *It will be rain* and *It going rain* are wrong, and *was* is past tense."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die verlede tyd van *bake* is *baked*: jy voeg net -d by, want die werkwoord eindig reeds op e.","en":"The past tense of *bake* is *baked*: you add only -d because the verb already ends in e."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Werkwoorde wat op -e eindig, kry net -d: *bake → baked, smile → smiled*.","en":"True. Verbs ending in -e only add -d: *bake → baked, smile → smiled*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is korrek?","en":"Which sentence is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"She will goes to the shop later.","en":"She will goes to the shop later."},{"af":"She will going to the shop later.","en":"She will going to the shop later."},{"af":"She will go to the shop later.","en":"She will go to the shop later."},{"af":"She wills go to the shop later.","en":"She wills go to the shop later."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Ná *will* kom die stam sonder -s of -ing: *will go*. *Will* self kry ook nooit -s nie.","en":"After *will* comes the base form without -s or -ing: *will go*. *Will* itself never gets -s either."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf in die voortdurende verlede tyd: *They are swimming.* → *They ___ swimming.*","en":"Change to the past continuous: *They are swimming.* → *They ___ swimming.*"},"answers":{"af":["were"],"en":["were"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["was","are","been"],"en":["was","are","been"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Are* word *were* in die verlede tyd. *They* is meervoud, so nie *was* nie.","en":"*Are* becomes *were* in the past tense. *They* is plural, so not *was*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte vorm: *Yesterday Aisha ___ a letter to her gran.*","en":"Choose the correct form: *Yesterday Aisha ___ a letter to her gran.*"},"options":[{"af":"wrote","en":"wrote"},{"af":"writed","en":"writed"},{"af":"writes","en":"writes"},{"af":"will write","en":"will write"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Yesterday* wys die verlede tyd, en *write* is onreëlmatig: *wrote*. *Writes* is teenwoordig en *will write* toekomend.","en":"*Yesterday* shows the past tense, and *write* is irregular: *wrote*. *Writes* is present and *will write* is future."}}]},{"id":"eng5-t2-adjectives-degrees","title":{"af":"Byvoeglike naamwoorde en trappe van vergelyking","en":"Adjectives and degrees of comparison"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal Engelse byvoeglike naamwoorde in die regte volgorde kan gebruik, die vergrotende en oortreffende trap reg kan vorm en spel (ook onreëlmatige trappe) en *than* reg kan gebruik.","en":"You will be able to use adjectives in the correct order, form and spell the comparative and superlative correctly (also irregular ones) and use *than* correctly."},"summary":{"af":"## Byvoeglike naamwoorde beskryf naamwoorde\n\n’n **Byvoeglike naamwoord** (*adjective*) beskryf ’n selfstandige naamwoord. Dit sê **watter soort**, **hoeveel** of **hoe dit lyk**: *a **tall** tree, **three** dogs, a **friendly** girl, **red** shoes*.\n\nDie byvoeglike naamwoord kan staan:\n- **voor** die naamwoord: *a **hot** day*\n- **ná** *is, are, was, were, looks, feels*: *The day is **hot**.*\n\nIn Engels verander ’n byvoeglike naamwoord **nie** as dit na ’n ander plek in die sin skuif nie. Afrikaans sê *Die hond is vinnig*, maar *die vinnig**e** hond*. Engels sê *The dog is fast* én *the fast dog*. Dit kry ook nie -s in die meervoud nie: *two red apples* (nie *reds apples* nie).\n\n## Die volgorde van byvoeglike naamwoorde\n\nAs jy meer as een byvoeglike naamwoord gebruik, volg hulle ’n vaste volgorde:\n\n**getal → mening → grootte → ouderdom → vorm → kleur → materiaal → naamwoord**\n\n| Voorbeeld | Volgorde |\n|---|---|\n| *a big red ball* | grootte → kleur |\n| *two lovely little kittens* | getal → mening → grootte |\n| *an old wooden chair* | ouderdom → materiaal |\n| *a beautiful long blue dress* | mening → grootte → kleur |\n\nSê dit hardop: *a red big ball* klink vir ’n Engelse oor verkeerd.\n\n## Trappe van vergelyking\n\n| Trap | Gebruik | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Stellende trap** (*positive*) | beskryf een ding | *Thabo is **tall**.* |\n| **Vergrotende trap** (*comparative*) | vergelyk **twee** dinge; gebruik **than** | *Thabo is **taller than** Sipho.* |\n| **Oortreffende trap** (*superlative*) | die meeste van **drie of meer**; gebruik **the** | *Thabo is **the tallest** in the class.* |\n\n## Spelreëls\n\n| Reël | Stellend | Vergrotend | Oortreffend |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Die meeste kort woorde: -er / -est | tall, fast | taller, faster | tallest, fastest |\n| Eindig op -e: net -r / -st | nice, large | nicer, larger | nicest, largest |\n| Kort klinker + een medeklinker: verdubbel | big, hot, thin | bigger, hotter, thinner | biggest, hottest, thinnest |\n| Medeklinker + y: y word i | happy, easy, funny | happier, easier, funnier | happiest, easiest, funniest |\n| Lang woorde: more / most | beautiful, careful | more beautiful | most beautiful |\n\nHoe weet jy of dit *-er* of *more* is? Tel die **lettergrepe**: een lettergreep (*tall, big*) kry -er/-est. Twee lettergrepe wat op -y eindig (*hap-py, fun-ny*) kry -ier/-iest. Die meeste ander woorde met twee of meer lettergrepe (*care-ful, dan-ger-ous, ex-pen-sive*) kry *more/most*.\n\n## Onreëlmatige trappe\n\n| Stellend | Vergrotend | Oortreffend |\n|---|---|---|\n| good | better | best |\n| bad | worse | worst |\n| many / much | more | most |\n| little | less | least |\n\n## Than, nie then nie\n\nNá ’n vergrotende trap kom **than** (as): *A cheetah is faster **than** a lion.* *Then* beteken “daarna”.\n\nAs twee dinge **ewe** groot of vinnig is, gebruik jy **as … as** met die stellende trap: *Sipho is **as tall as** Thabo.* (Sipho is net so lank soos Thabo.)\n\n> **Onthou:** Twee dinge → -er/more + *than*. Drie of meer → *the* + -est/most.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie *more* en -er saam gebruik nie: *more bigger* is verkeerd; skryf *bigger*. Moenie *gooder* of *baddest* skryf nie, maar *better* en *worst*.","en":"## Adjectives describe nouns\n\nAn **adjective** describes a noun. It tells us **what kind**, **how many** or **what it looks like**: *a **tall** tree, **three** dogs, a **friendly** girl, **red** shoes*.\n\nAn adjective can stand:\n- **before** the noun: *a **hot** day*\n- **after** *is, are, was, were, looks, feels*: *The day is **hot**.*\n\nIn English an adjective does **not** change when it moves to another place in the sentence. Afrikaans says *Die hond is vinnig*, but *die vinnig**e** hond*. English says *The dog is fast* and *the fast dog*. It also does not get -s in the plural: *two red apples* (not *reds apples*).\n\n## The order of adjectives\n\nWhen you use more than one adjective, they follow a fixed order:\n\n**number → opinion → size → age → shape → colour → material → noun**\n\n| Example | Order |\n|---|---|\n| *a big red ball* | size → colour |\n| *two lovely little kittens* | number → opinion → size |\n| *an old wooden chair* | age → material |\n| *a beautiful long blue dress* | opinion → size → colour |\n\nSay it out loud: *a red big ball* sounds wrong to an English ear.\n\n## Degrees of comparison\n\n| Degree | Use | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Positive** | describes one thing | *Thabo is **tall**.* |\n| **Comparative** | compares **two** things; use **than** | *Thabo is **taller than** Sipho.* |\n| **Superlative** | the most of **three or more**; use **the** | *Thabo is **the tallest** in the class.* |\n\n## Spelling rules\n\n| Rule | Positive | Comparative | Superlative |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Most short words: -er / -est | tall, fast | taller, faster | tallest, fastest |\n| Ends in -e: only -r / -st | nice, large | nicer, larger | nicest, largest |\n| Short vowel + one consonant: double it | big, hot, thin | bigger, hotter, thinner | biggest, hottest, thinnest |\n| Consonant + y: y becomes i | happy, easy, funny | happier, easier, funnier | happiest, easiest, funniest |\n| Long words: more / most | beautiful, careful | more beautiful | most beautiful |\n\nHow do you know whether to use *-er* or *more*? Count the **syllables**: one syllable (*tall, big*) takes -er/-est. Two syllables ending in -y (*hap-py, fun-ny*) take -ier/-iest. Most other words with two or more syllables (*care-ful, dan-ger-ous, ex-pen-sive*) take *more/most*.\n\n## Irregular adjectives\n\n| Positive | Comparative | Superlative |\n|---|---|---|\n| good | better | best |\n| bad | worse | worst |\n| many / much | more | most |\n| little | less | least |\n\n## Than, not then\n\nAfter a comparative we use **than**: *A cheetah is faster **than** a lion.* *Then* means “after that”.\n\nIf two things are **equal**, use **as … as** with the positive degree: *Sipho is **as tall as** Thabo.*\n\n> **Remember:** Two things → -er/more + *than*. Three or more → *the* + -est/most.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not use *more* and -er together: *more bigger* is wrong; write *bigger*. Do not write *gooder* or *baddest*, but *better* and *worst*."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Byvoeglike naamwoord (*adjective*)","en":"Adjective"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat ’n selfstandige naamwoord beskryf, soos *tall, red* of *friendly*.","en":"A word that describes a noun, such as *tall, red* or *friendly*."}},{"term":{"af":"Trappe van vergelyking (*degrees of comparison*)","en":"Degrees of comparison"},"def":{"af":"Die drie vorme van ’n byvoeglike naamwoord: *tall, taller, tallest*.","en":"The three forms of an adjective: *tall, taller, tallest*."}},{"term":{"af":"Stellende trap (*positive degree*)","en":"Positive degree"},"def":{"af":"Die gewone vorm wat een ding beskryf: *fast*.","en":"The ordinary form that describes one thing: *fast*."}},{"term":{"af":"Vergrotende trap (*comparative degree*)","en":"Comparative degree"},"def":{"af":"Die vorm wat twee dinge vergelyk, met *-er* of *more* en *than*: *faster than*.","en":"The form that compares two things, with *-er* or *more* and *than*: *faster than*."}},{"term":{"af":"Oortreffende trap (*superlative degree*)","en":"Superlative degree"},"def":{"af":"Die vorm vir die meeste van drie of meer, met *the* en *-est* of *most*: *the fastest*.","en":"The form for the most of three or more, with *the* and *-est* or *most*: *the fastest*."}},{"term":{"af":"*more* en *most*","en":"*more* and *most*"},"def":{"af":"Woorde wat jy voor lang byvoeglike naamwoorde gebruik: *more careful, most beautiful*.","en":"Words you use before long adjectives: *more careful, most beautiful*."}},{"term":{"af":"Onreëlmatige trappe (*irregular adjectives*)","en":"Irregular adjectives"},"def":{"af":"Trappe wat nie die reëls volg nie: *good – better – best, bad – worse – worst*.","en":"Forms that do not follow the rules: *good – better – best, bad – worse – worst*."}},{"term":{"af":"*than*","en":"*than*"},"def":{"af":"Die woord wat ná die vergrotende trap kom wanneer jy twee dinge vergelyk: *bigger than*.","en":"The word that comes after the comparative when you compare two things: *bigger than*."}},{"term":{"af":"Volgorde van byvoeglike naamwoorde (*order of adjectives*)","en":"Order of adjectives"},"def":{"af":"Die vaste volgorde: getal, mening, grootte, ouderdom, vorm, kleur, materiaal: *a lovely big red ball*.","en":"The fixed order: number, opinion, size, age, shape, colour, material: *a lovely big red ball*."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Trappe met spelreëls","en":"Degrees with spelling rules"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die vergrotende en oortreffende trap van *big, happy, nice* en *beautiful*.","en":"Write the comparative and superlative of *big, happy, nice* and *beautiful*."},"steps":[{"af":"*big*: kort klinker + een medeklinker, so verdubbel die g: *bigger, biggest*.","en":"*big*: short vowel + one consonant, so double the g: *bigger, biggest*."},{"af":"*happy*: medeklinker + y, so die y word i: *happier, happiest*.","en":"*happy*: consonant + y, so the y becomes i: *happier, happiest*."},{"af":"*nice* eindig op -e, so net -r en -st: *nicer, nicest*. *beautiful* is ’n lang woord: *more beautiful, most beautiful*.","en":"*nice* ends in -e, so only -r and -st: *nicer, nicest*. *beautiful* is a long word: *more beautiful, most beautiful*."}],"answer":{"af":"*bigger – biggest; happier – happiest; nicer – nicest; more beautiful – most beautiful*","en":"*bigger – biggest; happier – happiest; nicer – nicest; more beautiful – most beautiful*"}},{"title":{"af":"Onreëlmatige trappe","en":"Irregular adjectives"},"problem":{"af":"Voltooi: (a) *My mark is ___ (good) than yours.* (b) *This is the ___ (bad) storm in years.*","en":"Complete: (a) *My mark is ___ (good) than yours.* (b) *This is the ___ (bad) storm in years.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *than* wys twee dinge word vergelyk: vergrotende trap. *Good* is onreëlmatig: *better*.","en":"(a) *than* shows that two things are compared: comparative. *Good* is irregular: *better*."},{"af":"(b) *the* en *in years* wys die ergste van baie: oortreffende trap. *Bad* is onreëlmatig: *worst*.","en":"(b) *the* and *in years* show the worst of many: superlative. *Bad* is irregular: *worst*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *better* (b) *worst*","en":"(a) *better* (b) *worst*"}},{"title":{"af":"Die regte volgorde","en":"The correct order"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die byvoeglike naamwoorde in die regte volgorde: (a) *Zanele has a (red / beautiful / long) dress.* (b) *He found two (brown / little) puppies.*","en":"Write the adjectives in the correct order: (a) *Zanele has a (red / beautiful / long) dress.* (b) *He found two (brown / little) puppies.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Mening (*beautiful*) kom eerste, dan grootte (*long*), dan kleur (*red*).","en":"(a) Opinion (*beautiful*) comes first, then size (*long*), then colour (*red*)."},{"af":"(b) Die getal (*two*) staan reeds voor. Dan grootte (*little*) en dan kleur (*brown*).","en":"(b) The number (*two*) is already first. Then size (*little*) and then colour (*brown*)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *Zanele has a beautiful long red dress.* (b) *He found two little brown puppies.*","en":"(a) *Zanele has a beautiful long red dress.* (b) *He found two little brown puppies.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Vergrotend of oortreffend?","en":"Comparative or superlative?"},"problem":{"af":"Voltooi: (a) *The Orange River is the ___ (long) river in South Africa.* (b) *An elephant is ___ (heavy) than a rhino.*","en":"Complete: (a) *The Orange River is the ___ (long) river in South Africa.* (b) *An elephant is ___ (heavy) than a rhino.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Dit vergelyk al die riviere in die land (meer as twee) en daar staan *the*: oortreffende trap, *longest*.","en":"(a) It compares all the rivers in the country (more than two) and there is *the*: superlative, *longest*."},{"af":"(b) Twee diere en die woord *than*: vergrotende trap. *Heavy* eindig op medeklinker + y: *heavier*.","en":"(b) Two animals and the word *than*: comparative. *Heavy* ends in consonant + y: *heavier*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *longest* (b) *heavier*","en":"(a) *longest* (b) *heavier*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is die **byvoeglike naamwoord** in *The friendly dog wagged its tail*?","en":"Which word is the **adjective** in *The friendly dog wagged its tail*?"},"options":[{"af":"dog","en":"dog"},{"af":"wagged","en":"wagged"},{"af":"friendly","en":"friendly"},{"af":"tail","en":"tail"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Friendly* beskryf die hond. *Dog* en *tail* is naamwoorde, en *wagged* is ’n werkwoord.","en":"*Friendly* describes the dog. *Dog* and *tail* are nouns, and *wagged* is a verb."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Today is ___ (hot) than yesterday.*","en":"Complete: *Today is ___ (hot) than yesterday.*"},"answers":{"af":["hotter"],"en":["hotter"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["hoter","more hot","hottest"],"en":["hoter","more hot","hottest"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Than* wys twee dae word vergelyk. *Hot* het ’n kort klinker + een medeklinker, so die t word verdubbel: *hotter*.","en":"*Than* shows that two days are compared. *Hot* has a short vowel + one consonant, so the t is doubled: *hotter*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die oortreffende trap van *happy*?","en":"What is the superlative of *happy*?"},"options":[{"af":"happyest","en":"happyest"},{"af":"most happiest","en":"most happiest"},{"af":"happier","en":"happier"},{"af":"happiest","en":"happiest"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Happy* eindig op medeklinker + y, so die y word i voor -est: *happiest*. *Happier* is die vergrotende trap. *Most happiest* is verkeerd, want dit gebruik *most* en -est saam.","en":"*Happy* ends in consonant + y, so the y becomes i before -est: *happiest*. *Happier* is the comparative. *Most happiest* is wrong because it uses *most* and -est together."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die sin *My house is more bigger than yours.* is korrek.","en":"The sentence *My house is more bigger than yours.* is correct."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. *Bigger* is reeds die vergrotende trap, so jy los *more* uit: *My house is bigger than yours.*","en":"False. *Bigger* is already the comparative, so you leave out *more*: *My house is bigger than yours.*"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte woord: *A cheetah is faster ___ a lion.*","en":"Choose the correct word: *A cheetah is faster ___ a lion.*"},"options":[{"af":"than","en":"than"},{"af":"then","en":"then"},{"af":"as","en":"as"},{"af":"that","en":"that"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Ná ’n vergrotende trap kom *than*. *Then* beteken “daarna” en is ’n algemene spelfout hier.","en":"After a comparative comes *than*. *Then* means “after that” and is a common spelling mistake here."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een het die byvoeglike naamwoorde in die regte volgorde?","en":"Which one has the adjectives in the correct order?"},"options":[{"af":"a red big ball","en":"a red big ball"},{"af":"a big red ball","en":"a big red ball"},{"af":"a ball big red","en":"a ball big red"},{"af":"big a red ball","en":"big a red ball"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Grootte kom voor kleur: *a big red ball*. In Engels staan die byvoeglike naamwoorde voor die naamwoord, en *a* staan heel voor.","en":"Size comes before colour: *a big red ball*. In English the adjectives stand before the noun, and *a* comes first."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke byvoeglike naamwoord by sy vergrotende trap.","en":"Match each adjective to its comparative."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"good","en":"good"},"r":{"af":"better","en":"better"}},{"l":{"af":"bad","en":"bad"},"r":{"af":"worse","en":"worse"}},{"l":{"af":"little","en":"little"},"r":{"af":"less","en":"less"}},{"l":{"af":"many","en":"many"},"r":{"af":"more","en":"more"}},{"l":{"af":"easy","en":"easy"},"r":{"af":"easier","en":"easier"}}],"explain":{"af":"*Good, bad, little* en *many* is onreëlmatig. *Easy* eindig op medeklinker + y, so die y word i: *easier*.","en":"*Good, bad, little* and *many* are irregular. *Easy* ends in consonant + y, so the y becomes i: *easier*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte vorm: *This is the ___ book I have ever read!* (interesting)","en":"Choose the correct form: *This is the ___ book I have ever read!* (interesting)"},"options":[{"af":"interestingest","en":"interestingest"},{"af":"more interesting","en":"more interesting"},{"af":"interesting","en":"interesting"},{"af":"most interesting","en":"most interesting"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Dit is die beste van al die boeke (oortreffend), en *interesting* is ’n lang woord, so: *the most interesting*. *-est* pas nie by lang woorde nie.","en":"It is the best of all the books (superlative), and *interesting* is a long word, so: *the most interesting*. *-est* does not go with long words."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Of all the learners, Pieter has the ___ (good) handwriting.*","en":"Complete: *Of all the learners, Pieter has the ___ (good) handwriting.*"},"answers":{"af":["best"],"en":["best"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["goodest","better","most good"],"en":["goodest","better","most good"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Of all the learners* en *the* wys die oortreffende trap. *Good* is onreëlmatig: *good – better – best*.","en":"*Of all the learners* and *the* show the superlative. *Good* is irregular: *good – better – best*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin vergelyk **twee** dinge?","en":"Which sentence compares **two** things?"},"options":[{"af":"Lerato is taller than her brother.","en":"Lerato is taller than her brother."},{"af":"Lerato is the tallest girl in Grade 5.","en":"Lerato is the tallest girl in Grade 5."},{"af":"Lerato is a very tall girl.","en":"Lerato is a very tall girl."},{"af":"Lerato has a tall, kind friend.","en":"Lerato has a tall, kind friend."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Taller than* vergelyk Lerato met een ander persoon: vergrotende trap. *The tallest* vergelyk haar met baie mense.","en":"*Taller than* compares Lerato with one other person: comparative. *The tallest* compares her with many people."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die vergrotende trap van *beautiful*?","en":"What is the comparative of *beautiful*?"},"options":[{"af":"beautifuller","en":"beautifuller"},{"af":"beautifullest","en":"beautifullest"},{"af":"more beautiful","en":"more beautiful"},{"af":"most beautiful","en":"most beautiful"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Beautiful* is ’n lang woord, so jy gebruik *more*: *more beautiful*. *Most beautiful* is die oortreffende trap.","en":"*Beautiful* is a long word, so you use *more*: *more beautiful*. *Most beautiful* is the superlative."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In Engels bly ’n byvoeglike naamwoord dieselfde as die naamwoord meervoud is: *two red cars*.","en":"In English an adjective stays the same when the noun is plural: *two red cars*."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Engelse byvoeglike naamwoorde kry nooit -s of -e nie: *a red car, two red cars*.","en":"True. English adjectives never take -s or -e: *a red car, two red cars*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *My bag is heavy, but Ravi’s bag is even* ___.","en":"Complete: *My bag is heavy, but Ravi’s bag is even* ___."},"answers":{"af":["heavier"],"en":["heavier"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["heavyer","more heavy","heaviest"],"en":["heavyer","more heavy","heaviest"]}},"explain":{"af":"Twee sakke word vergelyk: vergrotende trap. *Heavy* eindig op medeklinker + y, so die y word i: *heavier*.","en":"Two bags are compared: comparative. *Heavy* ends in consonant + y, so the y becomes i: *heavier*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte vorm: *The Orange River is the ___ river in South Africa.*","en":"Choose the correct form: *The Orange River is the ___ river in South Africa.*"},"options":[{"af":"longer","en":"longer"},{"af":"longest","en":"longest"},{"af":"most long","en":"most long"},{"af":"long","en":"long"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Dit vergelyk al die riviere in die land, en *the* staan voor: oortreffende trap, *longest*. *Long* is kort, so nie *most long* nie.","en":"It compares all the rivers in the country, and *the* comes before it: superlative, *longest*. *Long* is short, so not *most long*."}}]},{"id":"eng5-t2-adverbs-prepositions","title":{"af":"Bywoorde en voorsetsels","en":"Adverbs and prepositions"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal Engelse bywoorde van wyse, tyd, plek en frekwensie kan vorm en reg in ’n sin kan plaas, en die regte voorsetsel van plek en tyd kan kies.","en":"You will be able to form adverbs of manner, time, place and frequency and put them in the right place in a sentence, and choose the correct preposition of place and time."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is ’n bywoord?\n\n’n **Bywoord** (*adverb*) sê meer oor ’n **werkwoord**. Dit beantwoord die vrae **hoe?**, **wanneer?**, **waar?** en **hoe dikwels?**\n\n*Nomsa sang **beautifully**.* (hoe?) *We left **early**.* (wanneer?) *The children played **outside**.* (waar?) *I **always** walk to school.* (hoe dikwels?)\n\n## Bywoorde van wyse (hoe?)\n\nDie meeste **bywoorde van wyse** maak jy deur **-ly** by ’n byvoeglike naamwoord te voeg:\n\n| Byvoeglike naamwoord | Bywoord | Reël |\n|---|---|---|\n| quick, slow, loud | quickly, slowly, loudly | voeg -ly by |\n| careful, quiet | carefully, quietly | voeg -ly by (*careful* + *-ly* gee twee l’e: *carefully*) |\n| happy, easy, angry | happily, easily, angrily | y word i + ly |\n| gentle, simple | gently, simply | -le word -ly |\n| good | **well** | onreëlmatig |\n| fast, hard | fast, hard | bly dieselfde |\n\nAfrikaans gebruik dikwels dieselfde woord: *’n stadige motor* en *Hy ry stadig*. Engels voeg -ly by: *a slow car*, maar *He drives slowly*. Die byvoeglike naamwoord beskryf die naamwoord (*a careful driver*); die bywoord beskryf die werkwoord (*He drives carefully*).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *She sings good.* → *She sings **well**.* / *He ran quick.* → *He ran **quickly**.*\n\n## Bywoorde van tyd en plek\n\n- **Tyd** (wanneer?): *yesterday, today, tomorrow, now, soon, later, already, early, late*\n- **Plek** (waar?): *here, there, outside, inside, upstairs, downstairs, everywhere, nearby*\n\n## Bywoorde van frekwensie (hoe dikwels?)\n\n**always** (altyd, 100%) → **usually** (gewoonlik) → **often** (dikwels) → **sometimes** (soms) → **rarely** (selde) → **never** (nooit, 0%)\n\nHulle staan gewoonlik **voor** die hoofwerkwoord, maar **ná** *am, is, are, was, were*:\n- *I **usually** eat porridge for breakfast.*\n- *Thabo is **never** late.*\n\n## Voorsetsels van plek\n\n’n **Voorsetsel** (*preposition*) wys waar iets is of wanneer iets gebeur. Dit staan voor ’n naamwoord of voornaamwoord.\n\n| Voorsetsel | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|\n| in (in) | *The milk is **in** the fridge.* |\n| on (op) | *The book is **on** the table.* |\n| under (onder) | *The cat is **under** the bed.* |\n| behind (agter) | *The ball is **behind** the door.* |\n| in front of (voor) | *The car is **in front of** the house.* |\n| next to (langs) | *Ravi sits **next to** Liam.* |\n| between (tussen) | *The shop is **between** the bank and the school.* |\n| at (by) | *Meet me **at** the gate.* |\n\n## Voorsetsels van tyd\n\n| Voorsetsel | Gebruik | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| at | kloktye, *night*, *break* | *at 7 o’clock, at night, at break* |\n| on | dae en datums | *on Monday, on 24 September* |\n| in | maande, jare, seisoene, dele van die dag | *in July, in 2026, in winter, in the morning* |\n| before / after | voor / ná iets anders | *Wash your hands **before** you eat. We play **after** school.* |\n| during | tydens, regdeur die tyd van iets | *Do not talk **during** the test.* |\n\nAfrikaanssprekendes skryf dikwels *on 7 o’clock*, want ons sê *om sewe-uur*. Skryf *at 7 o’clock*.\n\n> **Onthou:** *at night*, maar *in the morning, in the afternoon* en *in the evening*.","en":"## What is an adverb?\n\nAn **adverb** tells us more about a **verb**. It answers the questions **how?**, **when?**, **where?** and **how often?**\n\n*Nomsa sang **beautifully**.* (how?) *We left **early**.* (when?) *The children played **outside**.* (where?) *I **always** walk to school.* (how often?)\n\n## Adverbs of manner (how?)\n\nMost **adverbs of manner** are made by adding **-ly** to an adjective:\n\n| Adjective | Adverb | Rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| quick, slow, loud | quickly, slowly, loudly | add -ly |\n| careful, quiet | carefully, quietly | add -ly (*careful* + *-ly* gives two l’s: *carefully*) |\n| happy, easy, angry | happily, easily, angrily | y becomes i + ly |\n| gentle, simple | gently, simply | -le becomes -ly |\n| good | **well** | irregular |\n| fast, hard | fast, hard | stays the same |\n\nAfrikaans often uses the same word: *’n stadige motor* and *Hy ry stadig*. English adds -ly: *a slow car*, but *He drives slowly*. The adjective describes the noun (*a careful driver*); the adverb describes the verb (*He drives carefully*).\n\n> **Common mistake:** *She sings good.* → *She sings **well**.* / *He ran quick.* → *He ran **quickly**.*\n\n## Adverbs of time and place\n\n- **Time** (when?): *yesterday, today, tomorrow, now, soon, later, already, early, late*\n- **Place** (where?): *here, there, outside, inside, upstairs, downstairs, everywhere, nearby*\n\n## Adverbs of frequency (how often?)\n\n**always** (100%) → **usually** → **often** → **sometimes** → **rarely** → **never** (0%)\n\nThey usually stand **before** the main verb, but **after** *am, is, are, was, were*:\n- *I **usually** eat porridge for breakfast.*\n- *Thabo is **never** late.*\n\n## Prepositions of place\n\nA **preposition** shows where something is or when something happens. It stands before a noun or pronoun.\n\n| Preposition | Example |\n|---|---|\n| in | *The milk is **in** the fridge.* |\n| on | *The book is **on** the table.* |\n| under | *The cat is **under** the bed.* |\n| behind | *The ball is **behind** the door.* |\n| in front of | *The car is **in front of** the house.* |\n| next to | *Ravi sits **next to** Liam.* |\n| between | *The shop is **between** the bank and the school.* |\n| at | *Meet me **at** the gate.* |\n\n## Prepositions of time\n\n| Preposition | Use | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| at | clock times, *night*, *break* | *at 7 o’clock, at night, at break* |\n| on | days and dates | *on Monday, on 24 September* |\n| in | months, years, seasons, parts of the day | *in July, in 2026, in winter, in the morning* |\n| before / after | earlier / later than something else | *Wash your hands **before** you eat. We play **after** school.* |\n| during | all through the time of something | *Do not talk **during** the test.* |\n\nAfrikaans speakers often write *on 7 o’clock*, because in Afrikaans we say *om sewe-uur*. Write *at 7 o’clock*.\n\n> **Remember:** *at night*, but *in the morning, in the afternoon* and *in the evening*."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Bywoord (*adverb*)","en":"Adverb"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat meer oor ’n werkwoord sê: hoe, wanneer, waar of hoe dikwels.","en":"A word that tells more about a verb: how, when, where or how often."}},{"term":{"af":"Bywoord van wyse (*adverb of manner*)","en":"Adverb of manner"},"def":{"af":"Sê **hoe** iets gebeur; dit eindig dikwels op -ly: *slowly, carefully*.","en":"Tells **how** something happens; it often ends in -ly: *slowly, carefully*."}},{"term":{"af":"Bywoord van tyd (*adverb of time*)","en":"Adverb of time"},"def":{"af":"Sê **wanneer** iets gebeur: *yesterday, soon, now*.","en":"Tells **when** something happens: *yesterday, soon, now*."}},{"term":{"af":"Bywoord van plek (*adverb of place*)","en":"Adverb of place"},"def":{"af":"Sê **waar** iets gebeur: *here, outside, upstairs*.","en":"Tells **where** something happens: *here, outside, upstairs*."}},{"term":{"af":"Bywoord van frekwensie (*adverb of frequency*)","en":"Adverb of frequency"},"def":{"af":"Sê **hoe dikwels** iets gebeur: *always, usually, sometimes, never*.","en":"Tells **how often** something happens: *always, usually, sometimes, never*."}},{"term":{"af":"*well*","en":"*well*"},"def":{"af":"Die bywoord van *good*: *She sings well* (nie *good* nie).","en":"The adverb of *good*: *She sings well* (not *good*)."}},{"term":{"af":"Voorsetsel (*preposition*)","en":"Preposition"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord voor ’n naamwoord wat plek of tyd wys, soos *in, on, under, at*.","en":"A word before a noun that shows place or time, such as *in, on, under, at*."}},{"term":{"af":"Voorsetsel van plek (*preposition of place*)","en":"Preposition of place"},"def":{"af":"Wys **waar** iets is: *under the bed, between the trees, next to me*.","en":"Shows **where** something is: *under the bed, between the trees, next to me*."}},{"term":{"af":"Voorsetsel van tyd (*preposition of time*)","en":"Preposition of time"},"def":{"af":"Wys **wanneer**: *at 7 o’clock, on Monday, in July, during the holiday*.","en":"Shows **when**: *at 7 o’clock, on Monday, in July, during the holiday*."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Van byvoeglike naamwoord na bywoord","en":"From adjective to adverb"},"problem":{"af":"Verander die woord tussen hakies in ’n bywoord: (a) *The baby slept (peaceful).* (b) *Aisha answered (correct).* (c) *The dog barked (angry).* (d) *Liam plays soccer (good).*","en":"Change the word in brackets into an adverb: (a) *The baby slept (peaceful).* (b) *Aisha answered (correct).* (c) *The dog barked (angry).* (d) *Liam plays soccer (good).*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) en (b): voeg net -ly by: *peacefully, correctly*.","en":"(a) and (b): just add -ly: *peacefully, correctly*."},{"af":"(c) *angry* eindig op medeklinker + y, so die y word i: *angrily*.","en":"(c) *angry* ends in consonant + y, so the y becomes i: *angrily*."},{"af":"(d) *good* is onreëlmatig: die bywoord is *well*.","en":"(d) *good* is irregular: the adverb is *well*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *peacefully* (b) *correctly* (c) *angrily* (d) *well*","en":"(a) *peacefully* (b) *correctly* (c) *angrily* (d) *well*"}},{"title":{"af":"Die plek van ’n bywoord van frekwensie","en":"Where an adverb of frequency goes"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die bywoord op die regte plek: (a) *I eat breakfast.* (always) (b) *She is late.* (never)","en":"Put the adverb in the right place: (a) *I eat breakfast.* (always) (b) *She is late.* (never)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die hoofwerkwoord is *eat*. Die bywoord staan **voor** die hoofwerkwoord: *I always eat*.","en":"(a) The main verb is *eat*. The adverb goes **before** the main verb: *I always eat*."},{"af":"(b) Die werkwoord is *is*. Ná *am, is, are* staan die bywoord **agter** die werkwoord: *She is never*.","en":"(b) The verb is *is*. After *am, is, are* the adverb goes **after** the verb: *She is never*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *I always eat breakfast.* (b) *She is never late.*","en":"(a) *I always eat breakfast.* (b) *She is never late.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Voorsetsels van tyd","en":"Prepositions of time"},"problem":{"af":"Vul *at, on* of *in* in: *We have a party ___ Saturday ___ 3 o’clock. My birthday is ___ March.*","en":"Fill in *at, on* or *in*: *We have a party ___ Saturday ___ 3 o’clock. My birthday is ___ March.*"},"steps":[{"af":"*Saturday* is ’n dag: *on Saturday*.","en":"*Saturday* is a day: *on Saturday*."},{"af":"*3 o’clock* is ’n kloktyd: *at 3 o’clock* (nie *on* nie, al sê ons *om* in Afrikaans).","en":"*3 o’clock* is a clock time: *at 3 o’clock* (not *on*)."},{"af":"*March* is ’n maand: *in March*.","en":"*March* is a month: *in March*."}],"answer":{"af":"*We have a party on Saturday at 3 o’clock. My birthday is in March.*","en":"*We have a party on Saturday at 3 o’clock. My birthday is in March.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Voorsetsels van plek","en":"Prepositions of place"},"problem":{"af":"Kies die regte voorsetsel: (a) *The keys are ___ my pocket.* (b) *The clock hangs ___ the wall.* (c) *The bank is ___ the post office and the library.*","en":"Choose the correct preposition: (a) *The keys are ___ my pocket.* (b) *The clock hangs ___ the wall.* (c) *The bank is ___ the post office and the library.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die sleutels is binne-in die sak: *in*.","en":"(a) The keys are inside the pocket: *in*."},{"af":"(b) Die horlosie is teen die oppervlak van die muur: *on*.","en":"(b) The clock is against the surface of the wall: *on*."},{"af":"(c) Die bank is in die middel van **twee** geboue: *between*.","en":"(c) The bank is in the middle of **two** buildings: *between*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *in* (b) *on* (c) *between*","en":"(a) *in* (b) *on* (c) *between*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is die **bywoord** in *The tortoise walked slowly across the road*?","en":"Which word is the **adverb** in *The tortoise walked slowly across the road*?"},"options":[{"af":"tortoise","en":"tortoise"},{"af":"walked","en":"walked"},{"af":"road","en":"road"},{"af":"slowly","en":"slowly"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Slowly* sê **hoe** die skilpad geloop het, so dit is ’n bywoord van wyse. *Walked* is die werkwoord, en *tortoise* en *road* is naamwoorde.","en":"*Slowly* tells **how** the tortoise walked, so it is an adverb of manner. *Walked* is the verb, and *tortoise* and *road* are nouns."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die sin *She sings good.* is korrek, want *good* sê hoe sy sing.","en":"The sentence *She sings good.* is correct, because *good* tells how she sings."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Om te sê **hoe** iemand iets doen, het jy ’n bywoord nodig. Die bywoord van *good* is *well*: *She sings well.*","en":"False. To say **how** someone does something, you need an adverb. The adverb of *good* is *well*: *She sings well.*"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die bywoord van *happy*?","en":"What is the adverb of *happy*?"},"options":[{"af":"happyly","en":"happyly"},{"af":"happily","en":"happily"},{"af":"happly","en":"happly"},{"af":"happier","en":"happier"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Happy* eindig op medeklinker + y, so die y word i voor -ly: *happily*. *Happier* is die vergrotende trap.","en":"*Happy* ends in consonant + y, so the y becomes i before -ly: *happily*. *Happier* is the comparative."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi met ’n bywoord van wyse: *Please close the door ___ (quiet).*","en":"Complete with an adverb of manner: *Please close the door ___ (quiet).*"},"answers":{"af":["quietly"],"en":["quietly"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["quiet","quitely","quietlly"],"en":["quiet","quitely","quietlly"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die woord sê **hoe** jy die deur moet toemaak, so voeg -ly by: *quietly*. Pas op vir die spelling: *qui-et-ly*, nie *quitely* nie.","en":"The word tells **how** to close the door, so add -ly: *quietly*. Watch the spelling: *qui-et-ly*, not *quitely*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte voorsetsel: *My birthday is ___ June.*","en":"Choose the correct preposition: *My birthday is ___ June.*"},"options":[{"af":"in","en":"in"},{"af":"on","en":"on"},{"af":"at","en":"at"},{"af":"during","en":"during"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*June* is ’n maand, en maande kry *in*: *in June*. *On* is vir dae en datums, *at* vir kloktye.","en":"*June* is a month, and months take *in*: *in June*. *On* is for days and dates, *at* for clock times."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin het die bywoord van frekwensie op die regte plek?","en":"Which sentence has the adverb of frequency in the right place?"},"options":[{"af":"Sipho late is never.","en":"Sipho late is never."},{"af":"Sipho never is late.","en":"Sipho never is late."},{"af":"Sipho is never late.","en":"Sipho is never late."},{"af":"Never Sipho is late.","en":"Never Sipho is late."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Ná *am, is, are* staan die bywoord van frekwensie **agter** die werkwoord: *Sipho is never late.*","en":"After *am, is, are* the adverb of frequency comes **after** the verb: *Sipho is never late.*"}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke bywoord by die vraag wat dit beantwoord.","en":"Match each adverb to the question it answers."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"carefully","en":"carefully"},"r":{"af":"hoe?","en":"how?"}},{"l":{"af":"yesterday","en":"yesterday"},"r":{"af":"wanneer?","en":"when?"}},{"l":{"af":"outside","en":"outside"},"r":{"af":"waar?","en":"where?"}},{"l":{"af":"sometimes","en":"sometimes"},"r":{"af":"hoe dikwels?","en":"how often?"}}],"explain":{"af":"*Carefully* is ’n bywoord van wyse (hoe?), *yesterday* van tyd (wanneer?), *outside* van plek (waar?) en *sometimes* van frekwensie (hoe dikwels?).","en":"*Carefully* is an adverb of manner (how?), *yesterday* of time (when?), *outside* of place (where?) and *sometimes* of frequency (how often?)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte voorsetsel: *We have a test ___ Friday.*","en":"Choose the correct preposition: *We have a test ___ Friday.*"},"options":[{"af":"on","en":"on"},{"af":"in","en":"in"},{"af":"at","en":"at"},{"af":"between","en":"between"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Friday* is ’n dag van die week, en dae kry *on*: *on Friday*.","en":"*Friday* is a day of the week, and days take *on*: *on Friday*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *The school bell rings ___ 8 o’clock.*","en":"Complete: *The school bell rings ___ 8 o’clock.*"},"answers":{"af":["at"],"en":["at"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["on","in","during"],"en":["on","in","during"]}},"explain":{"af":"Kloktye kry *at*: *at 8 o’clock*. In Afrikaans sê ons *om agtuur*, maar dit is nie *on* in Engels nie.","en":"Clock times take *at*: *at 8 o’clock*. Afrikaans says *om agtuur*, but in English it is not *on*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is die **voorsetsel** in *The cat is hiding under the car*?","en":"Which word is the **preposition** in *The cat is hiding under the car*?"},"options":[{"af":"cat","en":"cat"},{"af":"hiding","en":"hiding"},{"af":"car","en":"car"},{"af":"under","en":"under"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Under* wys waar die kat is in verhouding tot die motor, so dit is ’n voorsetsel van plek.","en":"*Under* shows where the cat is compared to the car, so it is a preposition of place."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*Between* gebruik jy vir iets wat in die middel van twee dinge is.","en":"You use *between* for something that is in the middle of two things."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. *The shop is between the bank and the school* – die winkel is in die middel van twee geboue.","en":"True. *The shop is between the bank and the school* – the shop is in the middle of two buildings."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte woord: *Lerato fell asleep ___ the long film and missed the end.*","en":"Choose the correct word: *Lerato fell asleep ___ the long film and missed the end.*"},"options":[{"af":"before","en":"before"},{"af":"after","en":"after"},{"af":"during","en":"during"},{"af":"between","en":"between"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Sy het aan die slaap geraak terwyl die film gewys is, en toe die einde gemis: *during*. As dit *before* of *after* was, sou sy nie net die einde gemis het nie.","en":"She fell asleep while the film was showing and so missed the end: *during*. With *before* or *after*, she would not have missed just the end."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter bywoord beteken dat iets **0%** van die tyd gebeur?","en":"Which adverb means that something happens **0%** of the time?"},"options":[{"af":"always","en":"always"},{"af":"never","en":"never"},{"af":"usually","en":"usually"},{"af":"often","en":"often"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Never* (nooit) is 0%. *Always* is 100%, en *usually* en *often* is baie keer.","en":"*Never* is 0%. *Always* is 100%, and *usually* and *often* mean many times."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: *Liam is very good at maths. He did ___ in the test.*","en":"Complete: *Liam is very good at maths. He did ___ in the test.*"},"answers":{"af":["well"],"en":["well"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["good","goodly","greatly"],"en":["good","goodly","greatly"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die woord sê **hoe** hy gevaar het, so jy het die bywoord nodig. Die bywoord van *good* is *well*.","en":"The word tells **how** he did, so you need the adverb. The adverb of *good* is *well*."}}]},{"id":"eng5-t2-conjunctions-sentences","title":{"af":"Voegwoorde en sinsoorte","en":"Conjunctions and sentence types"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal Engelse sinne met die regte voegwoord kan verbind, enkelvoudige en saamgestelde sinne en die vier sinsoorte kan herken en punktueer, vrae kan vorm en sinne reg kan ontken.","en":"You will be able to join sentences with the correct conjunction, recognise and punctuate simple and compound sentences and the four sentence types, form questions and make sentences negative correctly."},"summary":{"af":"## Voegwoorde verbind idees\n\n’n **Voegwoord** (*conjunction*) is ’n verbindingswoord. Dit verbind twee woorde, idees of sinne.\n\n| Voegwoord | Gebruik | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| and (en) | voeg inligting by | *I washed the dishes **and** Thabo dried them.* |\n| but (maar) | wys ’n teenstelling | *I like rice, **but** I don’t like beans.* |\n| or (of) | gee ’n keuse | *Do you want tea **or** juice?* |\n| so (dus) | wys ’n gevolg | *It was raining, **so** we stayed inside.* |\n| because (omdat) | gee ’n rede | *We stayed inside **because** it was raining.* |\n| when (wanneer) | sê wanneer iets gebeur | *Call me **when** you get home.* |\n| until (totdat) | tot op ’n sekere tyd | *Wait here **until** the bell rings.* |\n| before / after (voordat / nadat) | wat eerste gebeur | *Brush your teeth **before** you go to bed.* |\n\nKyk na *so* en *because*: ná *so* kom die **gevolg**, ná *because* kom die **rede**. Dieselfde feite, ander volgorde.\n\n## Enkelvoudige en saamgestelde sinne\n\n- ’n **Enkelvoudige sin** (*simple sentence*) het een onderwerp en een werkwoordgedagte: *Nomsa reads a book.*\n- ’n **Saamgestelde sin** (*compound sentence*) is twee enkelvoudige sinne wat met **and, but, or, so** verbind is: *Nomsa reads a book, **and** her brother plays outside.*\n\nOns sit dikwels ’n komma voor *but* en *so*. Moenie twee sinne net met ’n komma aanmekaarlas nie (*I was tired, I went to bed* is verkeerd); gebruik ’n voegwoord of ’n punt.\n\n## Vier soorte sinne\n\n| Soort | Wat dit doen | Leesteken aan die einde | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Stelsin (*statement*) | sê vir jou iets | punt (.) | *The bus is late.* |\n| Vraagsin (*question*) | vra iets | vraagteken (?) | *Is the bus late?* |\n| Bevelsin (*command*) | sê iemand moet iets doen | punt of uitroepteken | *Close the window. Stop!* |\n| Uitroepsin (*exclamation*) | wys sterk gevoel | uitroepteken (!) | *What a beautiful sunset!* |\n\n## Vraagwoorde\n\n*who* (persoon), *what* (ding), *where* (plek), *when* (tyd), *why* (rede), *how* (hoe), *which* (keuse), *whose* (eienaar), *how many* (telbaar), *how much* (ontelbaar, geld).\n\nJa/nee-vrae begin met ’n hulpwerkwoord: *Do you…? Does she…? Did they…? Is it…? Can you…?*\n\n## Ontkennende sinne\n\n| Sin | Ontkenning |\n|---|---|\n| *I am hungry.* | *I am **not** hungry.* |\n| *He is at home.* | *He is **not** (isn’t) at home.* |\n| *We like soup.* | *We **don’t** like soup.* |\n| *She likes soup.* | *She **doesn’t** like soup.* |\n| *They went home.* | *They **didn’t** go home.* |\n\nNá *don’t, doesn’t, didn’t* staan die werkwoord in die **stam**: *She doesn’t like* (nie *likes* nie), *They didn’t go* (nie *went* nie). *Never* is ook ontkennend: *I never eat meat.*\n\nAfrikaans het twee ontkenningswoorde: *Ek eet **nie** vleis **nie***. Engels gebruik net **een**: *I do**n’t** eat meat.* Moenie twee ontkenningswoorde gebruik nie: skryf *I don’t have anything* of *I have nothing*, nie *I don’t have nothing* nie.\n\n> **Onthou:** *don’t* by *I, you, we, they*; *doesn’t* by *he, she, it*; *didn’t* by almal in die verlede tyd.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *He don’t like it.* → *He doesn’t like it.* / *She doesn’t likes it.* → *She doesn’t like it.*","en":"## Conjunctions join ideas\n\nA **conjunction** is a joining word. It joins two words, ideas or sentences.\n\n| Conjunction | Use | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| and | adds information | *I washed the dishes **and** Thabo dried them.* |\n| but | shows a contrast | *I like rice, **but** I don’t like beans.* |\n| or | gives a choice | *Do you want tea **or** juice?* |\n| so | shows a result | *It was raining, **so** we stayed inside.* |\n| because | gives a reason | *We stayed inside **because** it was raining.* |\n| when | tells when something happens | *Call me **when** you get home.* |\n| until | up to a certain time | *Wait here **until** the bell rings.* |\n| before / after | shows what happens first | *Brush your teeth **before** you go to bed.* |\n\nLook at *so* and *because*: after *so* comes the **result**, after *because* comes the **reason**. The same facts, a different order.\n\n## Simple and compound sentences\n\n- A **simple sentence** has one subject and one verb idea: *Nomsa reads a book.*\n- A **compound sentence** is two simple sentences joined by **and, but, or, so**: *Nomsa reads a book, **and** her brother plays outside.*\n\nWe often put a comma before *but* and *so*. Do not join two sentences with only a comma (*I was tired, I went to bed* is wrong); use a conjunction or a full stop.\n\n## Four kinds of sentences\n\n| Kind | What it does | End punctuation | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Statement | tells you something | full stop (.) | *The bus is late.* |\n| Question | asks something | question mark (?) | *Is the bus late?* |\n| Command | tells someone to do something | full stop or exclamation mark | *Close the window. Stop!* |\n| Exclamation | shows strong feeling | exclamation mark (!) | *What a beautiful sunset!* |\n\n## Question words\n\n*who* (person), *what* (thing), *where* (place), *when* (time), *why* (reason), *how* (manner), *which* (choice), *whose* (owner), *how many* (countable), *how much* (uncountable, money).\n\nYes/no questions start with a helping verb: *Do you…? Does she…? Did they…? Is it…? Can you…?*\n\n## Negative sentences\n\n| Sentence | Negative |\n|---|---|\n| *I am hungry.* | *I am **not** hungry.* |\n| *He is at home.* | *He is **not** (isn’t) at home.* |\n| *We like soup.* | *We **don’t** like soup.* |\n| *She likes soup.* | *She **doesn’t** like soup.* |\n| *They went home.* | *They **didn’t** go home.* |\n\nAfter *don’t, doesn’t, didn’t* the verb is in the **base form**: *She doesn’t like* (not *likes*), *They didn’t go* (not *went*). *Never* is also negative: *I never eat meat.*\n\nAfrikaans has two negative words: *Ek eet **nie** vleis **nie***. English uses only **one**: *I do**n’t** eat meat.* Do not use two negative words: write *I don’t have anything* or *I have nothing*, not *I don’t have nothing*.\n\n> **Remember:** *don’t* with *I, you, we, they*; *doesn’t* with *he, she, it*; *didn’t* with everyone in the past tense.\n\n> **Common mistake:** *He don’t like it.* → *He doesn’t like it.* / *She doesn’t likes it.* → *She doesn’t like it.*"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Voegwoord (*conjunction*)","en":"Conjunction"},"def":{"af":"’n Verbindingswoord soos *and, but, so, because* wat woorde of sinne verbind.","en":"A joining word such as *and, but, so, because* that joins words or sentences."}},{"term":{"af":"Enkelvoudige sin (*simple sentence*)","en":"Simple sentence"},"def":{"af":"’n Sin met een onderwerp en een werkwoordgedagte: *The dog barks.*","en":"A sentence with one subject and one verb idea: *The dog barks.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Saamgestelde sin (*compound sentence*)","en":"Compound sentence"},"def":{"af":"Twee enkelvoudige sinne wat met *and, but, or* of *so* verbind is.","en":"Two simple sentences joined by *and, but, or* or *so*."}},{"term":{"af":"Stelsin (*statement*)","en":"Statement"},"def":{"af":"’n Sin wat iets meedeel en met ’n punt eindig.","en":"A sentence that tells something and ends with a full stop."}},{"term":{"af":"Vraagsin (*question*)","en":"Question"},"def":{"af":"’n Sin wat iets vra en met ’n vraagteken eindig.","en":"A sentence that asks something and ends with a question mark."}},{"term":{"af":"Bevelsin (*command*)","en":"Command"},"def":{"af":"’n Sin wat iemand sê om iets te doen: *Sit down.*","en":"A sentence that tells someone to do something: *Sit down.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Uitroepsin (*exclamation*)","en":"Exclamation"},"def":{"af":"’n Sin wat sterk gevoel wys en met ’n uitroepteken eindig: *What a mess!*","en":"A sentence that shows strong feeling and ends with an exclamation mark: *What a mess!*"}},{"term":{"af":"Vraagwoord (*question word*)","en":"Question word"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord waarmee ’n vraag begin, soos *who, where, why, how many*.","en":"A word that starts a question, such as *who, where, why, how many*."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontkenning (*negative*)","en":"Negative"},"def":{"af":"’n Sin wat sê iets is nie so nie, met *not, don’t, doesn’t, didn’t* of *never*.","en":"A sentence that says something is not so, with *not, don’t, doesn’t, didn’t* or *never*."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Verbind die sinne","en":"Join the sentences"},"problem":{"af":"Verbind elke paar sinne met die voegwoord tussen hakies: (a) *I was hungry. I made a sandwich.* (so) (b) *Lerato stayed at home. She was sick.* (because) (c) *Pieter wanted to swim. The pool was closed.* (but)","en":"Join each pair of sentences with the conjunction in brackets: (a) *I was hungry. I made a sandwich.* (so) (b) *Lerato stayed at home. She was sick.* (because) (c) *Pieter wanted to swim. The pool was closed.* (but)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die toebroodjie is die **gevolg** van die honger, dus kom *so* voor die gevolg. Die punt word ’n komma en die *I* bly ’n hoofletter.","en":"(a) The sandwich is the **result** of being hungry, so *so* comes before the result. The full stop becomes a comma and *I* keeps its capital letter."},{"af":"(b) *She was sick* is die **rede**, so *because* kom voor die rede. Die *S* van *She* word ’n kleinletter.","en":"(b) *She was sick* is the **reason**, so *because* comes before the reason. The *S* of *She* becomes a small letter."},{"af":"(c) Die twee idees werk teen mekaar (wou swem – swembad toe), so *but*, met ’n komma voor.","en":"(c) The two ideas go against each other (wanted to swim – pool closed), so *but*, with a comma before it."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *I was hungry, so I made a sandwich.* (b) *Lerato stayed at home because she was sick.* (c) *Pieter wanted to swim, but the pool was closed.*","en":"(a) *I was hungry, so I made a sandwich.* (b) *Lerato stayed at home because she was sick.* (c) *Pieter wanted to swim, but the pool was closed.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Sinsoorte en leestekens","en":"Sentence types and punctuation"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf reg oor en noem die sinsoort: (a) *where is my bag* (b) *watch out* (c) *the shop closes at five* (d) *what a lovely surprise*","en":"Rewrite correctly and name the sentence type: (a) *where is my bag* (b) *watch out* (c) *the shop closes at five* (d) *what a lovely surprise*"},"steps":[{"af":"Elke sin begin met ’n hoofletter.","en":"Every sentence starts with a capital letter."},{"af":"(a) vra iets: vraagsin met **?**. (b) sê iemand moet iets doen, dringend: bevelsin met **!**.","en":"(a) asks something: question with **?**. (b) tells someone to do something urgently: command with **!**."},{"af":"(c) deel net iets mee: stelsin met **.**. (d) wys sterk gevoel: uitroepsin met **!**.","en":"(c) just tells something: statement with **.**. (d) shows strong feeling: exclamation with **!**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *Where is my bag?* – vraagsin (b) *Watch out!* – bevelsin (c) *The shop closes at five.* – stelsin (d) *What a lovely surprise!* – uitroepsin","en":"(a) *Where is my bag?* – question (b) *Watch out!* – command (c) *The shop closes at five.* – statement (d) *What a lovely surprise!* – exclamation"}},{"title":{"af":"Maak die sinne ontkennend","en":"Make the sentences negative"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf in die ontkenning: (a) *Sipho plays cricket.* (b) *We went to the zoo.* (c) *I am tired.*","en":"Write in the negative: (a) *Sipho plays cricket.* (b) *We went to the zoo.* (c) *I am tired.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Teenwoordige tyd met *he* (Sipho): *doesn’t* + stam. Die -s van *plays* val weg: *doesn’t play*.","en":"(a) Present tense with *he* (Sipho): *doesn’t* + base form. The -s of *plays* falls away: *doesn’t play*."},{"af":"(b) Verlede tyd: *didn’t* + stam. *Went* word *go*: *didn’t go*.","en":"(b) Past tense: *didn’t* + base form. *Went* becomes *go*: *didn’t go*."},{"af":"(c) By *am, is, are* sit jy net *not* ná die werkwoord: *am not*.","en":"(c) With *am, is, are* you just put *not* after the verb: *am not*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *Sipho doesn’t play cricket.* (b) *We didn’t go to the zoo.* (c) *I am not tired.*","en":"(a) *Sipho doesn’t play cricket.* (b) *We didn’t go to the zoo.* (c) *I am not tired.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Vorm ’n vraag","en":"Form a question"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf ’n vraag waarvan die vetgedrukte deel die antwoord is: *Thabo lives in **Mthatha**.*","en":"Write a question to which the part in bold is the answer: *Thabo lives in **Mthatha**.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Die antwoord is ’n plek, so die vraagwoord is *Where*.","en":"The answer is a place, so the question word is *Where*."},{"af":"*Thabo* = *he* in die teenwoordige tyd, so ons gebruik *does*. Ná *does* kom die stam: *live* (sonder -s).","en":"*Thabo* = *he* in the present tense, so we use *does*. After *does* comes the base form: *live* (without -s)."},{"af":"Volgorde: vraagwoord + *does* + onderwerp + werkwoord, en ’n vraagteken aan die einde.","en":"Order: question word + *does* + subject + verb, and a question mark at the end."}],"answer":{"af":"*Where does Thabo live?*","en":"*Where does Thabo live?*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte voegwoord: *I wanted to play outside, ___ it was raining.*","en":"Choose the correct conjunction: *I wanted to play outside, ___ it was raining.*"},"options":[{"af":"but","en":"but"},{"af":"so","en":"so"},{"af":"because","en":"because"},{"af":"or","en":"or"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die twee idees werk teen mekaar: jy wou buite speel, maar die reën keer dit. ’n Teenstelling kry *but*.","en":"The two ideas go against each other: you wanted to play outside, but the rain stopped you. A contrast takes *but*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi met ’n voegwoord: *We were late ___ the taxi broke down.*","en":"Complete with a conjunction: *We were late ___ the taxi broke down.*"},"answers":{"af":["because"],"en":["because"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["so","but","or"],"en":["so","but","or"]}},"explain":{"af":"*The taxi broke down* is die **rede** waarom julle laat was, so jy gebruik *because*.","en":"*The taxi broke down* is the **reason** why you were late, so you use *because*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is ’n **bevelsin** (*command*)?","en":"Which sentence is a **command**?"},"options":[{"af":"Is the door open?","en":"Is the door open?"},{"af":"The door is open.","en":"The door is open."},{"af":"What a big door!","en":"What a big door!"},{"af":"Please close the door.","en":"Please close the door."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Please close the door.* sê vir iemand om iets te doen. Die ander is ’n vraagsin, ’n stelsin en ’n uitroepsin.","en":"*Please close the door.* tells someone to do something. The others are a question, a statement and an exclamation."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die sin *Do you like chocolate.* het die regte leesteken aan die einde.","en":"The sentence *Do you like chocolate.* has the correct end punctuation."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Dit vra iets, so dit is ’n vraagsin en moet met ’n vraagteken eindig: *Do you like chocolate?*","en":"False. It asks something, so it is a question and must end with a question mark: *Do you like chocolate?*"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die ontkenning van *She likes spinach*?","en":"What is the negative of *She likes spinach*?"},"options":[{"af":"She don’t like spinach.","en":"She don’t like spinach."},{"af":"She doesn’t like spinach.","en":"She doesn’t like spinach."},{"af":"She doesn’t likes spinach.","en":"She doesn’t likes spinach."},{"af":"She not likes spinach.","en":"She not likes spinach."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"By *she* gebruik jy *doesn’t*, en daarna kom die stam sonder -s: *doesn’t like*.","en":"With *she* you use *doesn’t*, and after it comes the base form without -s: *doesn’t like*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter vraagwoord vra na ’n **rede**?","en":"Which question word asks for a **reason**?"},"options":[{"af":"Where","en":"Where"},{"af":"When","en":"When"},{"af":"Why","en":"Why"},{"af":"Who","en":"Who"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Why* vra na ’n rede, en die antwoord begin dikwels met *because*. *Where* vra na ’n plek, *when* na ’n tyd en *who* na ’n persoon.","en":"*Why* asks for a reason, and the answer often starts with *because*. *Where* asks about a place, *when* about a time and *who* about a person."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf in die ontkenning: *They went to the park.* → *They ___ go to the park.*","en":"Make it negative: *They went to the park.* → *They ___ go to the park.*"},"answers":{"af":["didn’t","did not"],"en":["didn’t","did not"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["don’t","doesn’t","not"],"en":["don’t","doesn’t","not"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die sin is in die verlede tyd (*went*), so gebruik *didn’t*, en *went* word die stam *go*.","en":"The sentence is in the past tense (*went*), so use *didn’t*, and *went* becomes the base form *go*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is ’n **saamgestelde sin** (*compound sentence*)?","en":"Which sentence is a **compound sentence**?"},"options":[{"af":"Ravi rode his bike to school.","en":"Ravi rode his bike to school."},{"af":"My little brother is five.","en":"My little brother is five."},{"af":"Ravi rode his bike, but Liam walked.","en":"Ravi rode his bike, but Liam walked."},{"af":"The children ran to the gate.","en":"The children ran to the gate."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Dit is twee enkelvoudige sinne (*Ravi rode his bike* en *Liam walked*) wat met *but* verbind is. Die ander sinne het elk net een werkwoordgedagte.","en":"It is two simple sentences (*Ravi rode his bike* and *Liam walked*) joined by *but*. The other sentences each have only one verb idea."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke sin by die soort sin.","en":"Match each sentence to its type."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Where is the bus?","en":"Where is the bus?"},"r":{"af":"vraagsin","en":"question"}},{"l":{"af":"Watch out!","en":"Watch out!"},"r":{"af":"bevelsin","en":"command"}},{"l":{"af":"The bus is late.","en":"The bus is late."},"r":{"af":"stelsin","en":"statement"}},{"l":{"af":"What a huge bus!","en":"What a huge bus!"},"r":{"af":"uitroepsin","en":"exclamation"}}],"explain":{"af":"’n Vraagsin vra iets (?), ’n bevelsin sê iemand moet iets doen, ’n stelsin deel iets mee (.) en ’n uitroepsin wys sterk gevoel (!).","en":"A question asks something (?), a command tells someone to do something, a statement tells something (.) and an exclamation shows strong feeling (!)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte woord: *Lerato ___ eat meat. She is a vegetarian.*","en":"Choose the correct word: *Lerato ___ eat meat. She is a vegetarian.*"},"options":[{"af":"don’t","en":"don’t"},{"af":"doesn’t","en":"doesn’t"},{"af":"isn’t","en":"isn’t"},{"af":"not","en":"not"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Lerato* = *she* in die teenwoordige tyd, so *doesn’t* + stam: *doesn’t eat*. *Don’t* is vir *I, you, we, they*.","en":"*Lerato* = *she* in the present tense, so *doesn’t* + base form: *doesn’t eat*. *Don’t* is for *I, you, we, they*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is korrek?","en":"Which sentence is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"I don’t have no homework.","en":"I don’t have no homework."},{"af":"I not have homework.","en":"I not have homework."},{"af":"I doesn’t have homework.","en":"I doesn’t have homework."},{"af":"I don’t have any homework.","en":"I don’t have any homework."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Engels gebruik net een ontkenningswoord: *don’t … any*. *Don’t … no* is ’n dubbele ontkenning, en by *I* is dit *don’t*, nie *doesn’t* nie.","en":"English uses only one negative word: *don’t … any*. *Don’t … no* is a double negative, and with *I* it is *don’t*, not *doesn’t*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Ná *so* kom die gevolg, en ná *because* kom die rede.","en":"After *so* comes the result, and after *because* comes the reason."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. *It rained, so we stayed inside* (gevolg). *We stayed inside because it rained* (rede).","en":"True. *It rained, so we stayed inside* (result). *We stayed inside because it rained* (reason)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die vraagwoorde: ___ *apples did you buy? – I bought six.*","en":"Write the question words: ___ *apples did you buy? – I bought six.*"},"answers":{"af":["How many"],"en":["How many"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["How much","What","Which"],"en":["How much","What","Which"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die antwoord is ’n getal appels, en appels is telbaar, so *How many*. *How much* is vir ontelbare dinge of geld.","en":"The answer is a number of apples, and apples are countable, so *How many*. *How much* is for uncountable things or money."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin verbind *Wait here.* en *The bell rings.* op die beste manier?","en":"Which sentence joins *Wait here.* and *The bell rings.* best?"},"options":[{"af":"Wait here until the bell rings.","en":"Wait here until the bell rings."},{"af":"Wait here but the bell rings.","en":"Wait here but the bell rings."},{"af":"Wait here or the bell rings.","en":"Wait here or the bell rings."},{"af":"Wait here so the bell rings.","en":"Wait here so the bell rings."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Until* beteken “tot op die tyd dat”: jy wag tot die klok lui. Die ander voegwoorde maak nie sin hier nie.","en":"*Until* means “up to the time that”: you wait up to the moment the bell rings. The other conjunctions do not make sense here."}}]},{"id":"eng5-t2-punctuation-direct-speech","title":{"af":"Leestekens en direkte rede","en":"Punctuation and direct speech"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal hoofletters, punte, kommas, vraagtekens, uitroeptekens en die afkappingsteken in Engels reg kan gebruik, direkte rede korrek kan punktueer en ’n eenvoudige sin in indirekte rede kan oorskryf.","en":"You will be able to use capital letters, full stops, commas, question marks, exclamation marks and the apostrophe correctly, punctuate direct speech correctly and change a simple sentence into reported speech."},"summary":{"af":"## Hoofletters\n\nGebruik ’n **hoofletter** vir:\n- die **eerste woord** van ’n sin: *My dog is called Max.*\n- **name** van mense, plekke, dae, maande, tale en spesiale dae: *Fatima, Bloemfontein, Monday, April, English, Heritage Day*\n- die woord **I**: *Sipho and I are friends.*\n- die **eerste woord** van die gesproke woorde in direkte rede: *She said, “**We** must hurry.”*\n\nAfrikaans skryf *ek* met ’n kleinletter, maar Engelse *I* kry **altyd** ’n hoofletter.\n\n## Punt, vraagteken en uitroepteken\n\n- **Punt (.)** aan die einde van ’n stelsin of ’n kalm bevel: *We are going home.*\n- **Vraagteken (?)** aan die einde van ’n vraag: *Are you ready?*\n- **Uitroepteken (!)** ná sterk gevoel of ’n skerp bevel: *Watch out! What a surprise!*\n\n## Kommas\n\n- Tussen die items in ’n **lys**. Voor die laaste item staan *and* (geen komma nodig nie): *I packed a cap, a towel, sunscreen and a book.*\n- Ná **yes** en **no** aan die begin van ’n antwoord: *Yes, I can help. No, thank you.*\n- In direkte rede, om die gesproke woorde van die res te skei (sien onder).\n\n## Die afkappingsteken (’)\n\n**1. Sametrekkings** (*contractions*) – die afkappingsteken wys waar letters weggelaat is:\n\n| Lang vorm | Kort vorm |\n|---|---|\n| do not | don’t |\n| it is | it’s |\n| I am | I’m |\n| cannot | can’t |\n| they are | they’re |\n| will not | won’t |\n\n**2. Besit** – die afkappingsteken wys wie iets besit:\n- **een** eienaar: voeg **’s** by – *the girl’s bag* (een meisie)\n- **meer as een** eienaar wat op -s eindig: voeg net **’** by – *the girls’ bags* (baie meisies)\n- meervoud wat nie op -s eindig nie: voeg **’s** by – *the children’s toys, the men’s shoes*\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moet nooit ’n afkappingsteken by ’n gewone meervoud sit nie: *apple’s for sale* is verkeerd; skryf *apples for sale*. En *its* (wat aan dit behoort) het geen afkappingsteken nie; *it’s* beteken *it is*.\n\n## Direkte rede\n\n**Direkte rede** (*direct speech*) gee die **presiese woorde** wat iemand gesê het. Sit die gesproke woorde tussen **aanhalingstekens** (*inverted commas*: “ ”).\n\n**Spreker eerste:** *Lerato said, “I am hungry.”*\n- komma ná *said*\n- hoofletter vir die eerste gesproke woord\n- punt **binne** die aanhalingstekens\n\n**Spreker laaste:** *“I am hungry,” said Lerato.*\n- ’n komma (nie ’n punt nie) binne die aanhalingstekens\n- punt aan die einde van die hele sin\n\n**Vrae en uitroepe:** die **?** of **!** staan binne: *“Where is my hat?” asked Liam.* / *“Look out!” shouted Johan.*\n\n> **Onthou:** Alles wat die persoon gesê het – en die leesteken wat daarby hoort – staan **binne** die aanhalingstekens.\n\n## Van direkte na indirekte rede (eerste kennismaking)\n\nIn **indirekte rede** (*reported speech*) vertel jy wat iemand gesê het, **sonder** sy presiese woorde. Daar is geen aanhalingstekens nie, jy voeg dikwels **that** by, en die werkwoord skuif terug na die verlede tyd:\n\n| Direkte rede | Indirekte rede |\n|---|---|\n| *Lerato said, “I am hungry.”* | *Lerato said that she was hungry.* |\n| *Sipho said, “We are tired.”* | *Sipho said that they were tired.* |\n\n*I* word *he/she*, *we* word *they*, *am/is* word *was*, *are* word *were*.","en":"## Capital letters\n\nUse a **capital letter** for:\n- the **first word** of a sentence: *My dog is called Max.*\n- **names** of people, places, days, months, languages and special days: *Fatima, Bloemfontein, Monday, April, English, Heritage Day*\n- the word **I**: *Sipho and I are friends.*\n- the **first word** of the spoken words in direct speech: *She said, “**We** must hurry.”*\n\nAfrikaans writes *ek* with a small letter, but the English *I* **always** has a capital letter.\n\n## Full stop, question mark and exclamation mark\n\n- **Full stop (.)** at the end of a statement or a calm command: *We are going home.*\n- **Question mark (?)** at the end of a question: *Are you ready?*\n- **Exclamation mark (!)** after strong feeling or a sharp command: *Watch out! What a surprise!*\n\n## Commas\n\n- Between the items in a **list**. Before the last item comes *and* (no comma needed): *I packed a cap, a towel, sunscreen and a book.*\n- After **yes** and **no** at the start of an answer: *Yes, I can help. No, thank you.*\n- In direct speech, to separate the spoken words from the rest (see below).\n\n## The apostrophe (’)\n\n**1. Contractions** – the apostrophe shows where letters have been left out:\n\n| Long form | Short form |\n|---|---|\n| do not | don’t |\n| it is | it’s |\n| I am | I’m |\n| cannot | can’t |\n| they are | they’re |\n| will not | won’t |\n\n**2. Possession** – the apostrophe shows who owns something:\n- **one** owner: add **’s** – *the girl’s bag* (one girl)\n- **more than one** owner ending in -s: add only **’** – *the girls’ bags* (many girls)\n- a plural that does not end in -s: add **’s** – *the children’s toys, the men’s shoes*\n\n> **Common mistake:** Never put an apostrophe in an ordinary plural: *apple’s for sale* is wrong; write *apples for sale*. And *its* (belonging to it) has no apostrophe; *it’s* means *it is*.\n\n## Direct speech\n\n**Direct speech** gives the **exact words** that someone said. Put the spoken words inside **inverted commas** (“ ”).\n\n**Speaker first:** *Lerato said, “I am hungry.”*\n- comma after *said*\n- capital letter for the first spoken word\n- full stop **inside** the inverted commas\n\n**Speaker last:** *“I am hungry,” said Lerato.*\n- a comma (not a full stop) inside the inverted commas\n- full stop at the end of the whole sentence\n\n**Questions and exclamations:** the **?** or **!** goes inside: *“Where is my hat?” asked Liam.* / *“Look out!” shouted Johan.*\n\n> **Remember:** Everything the person said – and the punctuation mark that belongs to it – goes **inside** the inverted commas.\n\n## From direct to reported speech (a first look)\n\nIn **reported speech** you tell what someone said **without** using their exact words. There are no inverted commas, you often add **that**, and the verb moves back into the past tense:\n\n| Direct speech | Reported speech |\n|---|---|\n| *Lerato said, “I am hungry.”* | *Lerato said that she was hungry.* |\n| *Sipho said, “We are tired.”* | *Sipho said that they were tired.* |\n\n*I* becomes *he/she*, *we* becomes *they*, *am/is* becomes *was*, *are* becomes *were*."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Hoofletter (*capital letter*)","en":"Capital letter"},"def":{"af":"’n Groot letter aan die begin van ’n sin, ’n naam en die woord *I*.","en":"A big letter at the start of a sentence, a name and the word *I*."}},{"term":{"af":"Leesteken (*punctuation mark*)","en":"Punctuation mark"},"def":{"af":"’n Teken soos . , ? ! ’ of “ ” wat ’n sin duidelik maak.","en":"A mark such as . , ? ! ’ or “ ” that makes a sentence clear."}},{"term":{"af":"Komma (*comma*)","en":"Comma"},"def":{"af":"’n Leesteken wat items in ’n lys skei en ná *yes* of *no* staan.","en":"A punctuation mark that separates items in a list and comes after *yes* or *no*."}},{"term":{"af":"Afkappingsteken (*apostrophe*)","en":"Apostrophe"},"def":{"af":"Die teken ’ wat wys waar letters weggelaat is of wie iets besit.","en":"The mark ’ that shows where letters are left out or who owns something."}},{"term":{"af":"Sametrekking (*contraction*)","en":"Contraction"},"def":{"af":"Twee woorde wat saamgetrek is met ’n afkappingsteken: *do not → don’t*.","en":"Two words joined into one with an apostrophe: *do not → don’t*."}},{"term":{"af":"Besitlike ’s (*possessive apostrophe*)","en":"Possessive apostrophe"},"def":{"af":"Die ’s of ’ wat besit wys: *the girl’s bag, the girls’ bags*.","en":"The ’s or ’ that shows ownership: *the girl’s bag, the girls’ bags*."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanhalingstekens (*inverted commas*)","en":"Inverted commas"},"def":{"af":"Die tekens “ ” rondom die presiese woorde wat iemand sê.","en":"The marks “ ” around the exact words someone says."}},{"term":{"af":"Direkte rede (*direct speech*)","en":"Direct speech"},"def":{"af":"Die presiese woorde van ’n spreker tussen aanhalingstekens: *Liam said, “I’m ready.”*","en":"The exact words of a speaker inside inverted commas: *Liam said, “I’m ready.”*"}},{"term":{"af":"Indirekte rede (*reported speech*)","en":"Reported speech"},"def":{"af":"Vertel wat iemand gesê het sonder aanhalingstekens: *Liam said that he was ready.*","en":"Telling what someone said without inverted commas: *Liam said that he was ready.*"}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Hoofletters en ’n punt","en":"Capital letters and a full stop"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf reg oor: *on friday thabo and i went to durban with our gran*","en":"Rewrite correctly: *on friday thabo and i went to durban with our gran*"},"steps":[{"af":"Die eerste woord van die sin kry ’n hoofletter: *On*.","en":"The first word of the sentence gets a capital letter: *On*."},{"af":"Name kry hoofletters: *Friday* (dag), *Thabo* (persoon), *Durban* (plek). Die woord *I* is altyd ’n hoofletter.","en":"Names get capital letters: *Friday* (day), *Thabo* (person), *Durban* (place). The word *I* is always a capital."},{"af":"*gran* is hier nie ’n naam nie (*our gran*), so dit bly klein. Dit is ’n stelsin, so sit ’n punt aan die einde.","en":"*gran* is not a name here (*our gran*), so it stays small. It is a statement, so put a full stop at the end."}],"answer":{"af":"*On Friday Thabo and I went to Durban with our gran.*","en":"*On Friday Thabo and I went to Durban with our gran.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Die afkappingsteken","en":"The apostrophe"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf met ’n afkappingsteken: (a) *the tail of the dog* (b) *the books of the boys* (c) *the toys of the children* (d) *they are*","en":"Write with an apostrophe: (a) *the tail of the dog* (b) *the books of the boys* (c) *the toys of the children* (d) *they are*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Een hond is die eienaar: voeg ’s by: *the dog’s tail*.","en":"(a) One dog is the owner: add ’s: *the dog’s tail*."},{"af":"(b) Baie seuns, en *boys* eindig reeds op -s: voeg net ’ by: *the boys’ books*.","en":"(b) Many boys, and *boys* already ends in -s: add only ’: *the boys’ books*."},{"af":"(c) *children* is meervoud maar eindig nie op -s nie: voeg ’s by: *the children’s toys*.","en":"(c) *children* is plural but does not end in -s: add ’s: *the children’s toys*."},{"af":"(d) Die a van *are* val weg, en die afkappingsteken kom in sy plek: *they’re*.","en":"(d) The a of *are* falls away and the apostrophe takes its place: *they’re*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *the dog’s tail* (b) *the boys’ books* (c) *the children’s toys* (d) *they’re*","en":"(a) *the dog’s tail* (b) *the boys’ books* (c) *the children’s toys* (d) *they’re*"}},{"title":{"af":"Punktueer direkte rede","en":"Punctuate direct speech"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf reg oor: (a) *where are you going asked mom* (b) *zanele said i am going to the shop*","en":"Rewrite correctly: (a) *where are you going asked mom* (b) *zanele said i am going to the shop*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die gesproke woorde is *where are you going*. Dit is ’n vraag, so die **?** staan binne die aanhalingstekens. Die spreker kom laaste.","en":"(a) The spoken words are *where are you going*. It is a question, so the **?** goes inside the inverted commas. The speaker comes last."},{"af":"Hoofletters: *Where* (eerste gesproke woord) en *Mom* (hier gebruik as ’n naam). Punt aan die einde van die hele sin.","en":"Capital letters: *Where* (first spoken word) and *Mom* (used as a name here). Full stop at the end of the whole sentence."},{"af":"(b) Die spreker kom eerste: *Zanele said,* + komma. Die gesproke woorde begin met ’n hoofletter, en die punt staan binne die aanhalingstekens.","en":"(b) The speaker comes first: *Zanele said,* + comma. The spoken words start with a capital letter, and the full stop goes inside the inverted commas."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) *“Where are you going?” asked Mom.* (b) *Zanele said, “I am going to the shop.”*","en":"(a) *“Where are you going?” asked Mom.* (b) *Zanele said, “I am going to the shop.”*"}},{"title":{"af":"Na indirekte rede","en":"Into reported speech"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf in indirekte rede: *Ravi said, “I am tired.”*","en":"Change into reported speech: *Ravi said, “I am tired.”*"},"steps":[{"af":"Haal die komma en die aanhalingstekens weg en voeg *that* by: *Ravi said that …*","en":"Remove the comma and the inverted commas and add *that*: *Ravi said that …*"},{"af":"Ravi praat oor homself, so *I* word *he*.","en":"Ravi is talking about himself, so *I* becomes *he*."},{"af":"Die werkwoord skuif terug na die verlede tyd: *am* word *was*.","en":"The verb moves back into the past tense: *am* becomes *was*."}],"answer":{"af":"*Ravi said that he was tired.*","en":"*Ravi said that he was tired.*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woorde moet hoofletters kry? *last week aisha visited her aunt in polokwane.*","en":"Which words need capital letters? *last week aisha visited her aunt in polokwane.*"},"options":[{"af":"Aisha, Polokwane","en":"Aisha, Polokwane"},{"af":"Last, Aisha, Polokwane","en":"Last, Aisha, Polokwane"},{"af":"Last, Aisha, Aunt, Polokwane","en":"Last, Aisha, Aunt, Polokwane"},{"af":"Last, Week, Aisha, Polokwane","en":"Last, Week, Aisha, Polokwane"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Last* is die eerste woord van die sin, *Aisha* is ’n persoon se naam en *Polokwane* is ’n plek. *aunt* en *week* is gewone woorde, so hulle bly klein.","en":"*Last* is the first word of the sentence, *Aisha* is a person’s name and *Polokwane* is a place. *aunt* and *week* are ordinary words, so they stay small."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die kort vorm: *do not* → ___","en":"Write the short form: *do not* → ___"},"answers":{"af":["don’t"],"en":["don’t"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["dont","do’nt","doesn’t"],"en":["dont","do’nt","doesn’t"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die o van *not* val weg, en die afkappingsteken kom op daardie plek: *don’t*. *Dont* het glad nie ’n afkappingsteken nie, en *do’nt* het dit op die verkeerde plek.","en":"The o of *not* falls away, and the apostrophe goes in that place: *don’t*. *Dont* has no apostrophe at all, and *do’nt* has it in the wrong place."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Skryf met ’n afkappingsteken: *the bags of the girls* (baie meisies)","en":"Write with an apostrophe: *the bags of the girls* (many girls)"},"options":[{"af":"the girl’s bags","en":"the girl’s bags"},{"af":"the girls bags","en":"the girls bags"},{"af":"the girls’ bags","en":"the girls’ bags"},{"af":"the girls’s bags","en":"the girls’s bags"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Daar is meer as een meisie, en *girls* eindig reeds op -s, so voeg net ’ by: *the girls’ bags*. *The girl’s bags* is vir een meisie.","en":"There is more than one girl, and *girls* already ends in -s, so add only ’: *the girls’ bags*. *The girl’s bags* is for one girl."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin in direkte rede is reg gepunktueer?","en":"Which sentence in direct speech is punctuated correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Ravi said “I like cricket.”","en":"Ravi said “I like cricket.”"},{"af":"Ravi said. “I like cricket.”","en":"Ravi said. “I like cricket.”"},{"af":"Ravi said, “I like cricket”.","en":"Ravi said, “I like cricket”."},{"af":"Ravi said, “I like cricket.”","en":"Ravi said, “I like cricket.”"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Daar is ’n komma (nie ’n punt nie) ná *said*, die gesproke woorde begin met ’n hoofletter, en die punt staan binne die aanhalingstekens. Elke ander sin het een fout.","en":"There is a comma (not a full stop) after *said*, the spoken words start with a capital letter, and the full stop is inside the inverted commas. Each other sentence has one mistake."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As daar baie appels is, skryf ons *apple’s for sale*.","en":"When there are many apples, we write *apple’s for sale*."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Gewone meervoud kry net -s, sonder ’n afkappingsteken: *apples for sale*.","en":"False. An ordinary plural just takes -s, without an apostrophe: *apples for sale*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar hoort die komma? *Yes I would like some juice.*","en":"Where does the comma go? *Yes I would like some juice.*"},"options":[{"af":"Yes, I would like some juice.","en":"Yes, I would like some juice."},{"af":"Yes I, would like some juice.","en":"Yes I, would like some juice."},{"af":"Yes I would like, some juice.","en":"Yes I would like, some juice."},{"af":"Yes I would like some, juice.","en":"Yes I would like some, juice."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Aan die begin van ’n antwoord kom daar ’n komma ná *yes* of *no*: *Yes, I would like some juice.*","en":"At the start of an answer, a comma comes after *yes* or *no*: *Yes, I would like some juice.*"}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke lang vorm by sy sametrekking.","en":"Match each long form to its contraction."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"I am","en":"I am"},"r":{"af":"I’m","en":"I’m"}},{"l":{"af":"it is","en":"it is"},"r":{"af":"it’s","en":"it’s"}},{"l":{"af":"cannot","en":"cannot"},"r":{"af":"can’t","en":"can’t"}},{"l":{"af":"they are","en":"they are"},"r":{"af":"they’re","en":"they’re"}},{"l":{"af":"will not","en":"will not"},"r":{"af":"won’t","en":"won’t"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die afkappingsteken staan waar letters weggelaat is. *Will not → won’t* is spesiaal: die woord verander ook.","en":"The apostrophe stands where letters are left out. *Will not → won’t* is special: the word also changes."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi met *its* of *it’s*: *The bird built ___ nest in the tree.*","en":"Complete with *its* or *it’s*: *The bird built ___ nest in the tree.*"},"answers":{"af":["its"],"en":["its"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["it’s","its’","it is"],"en":["it’s","its’","it is"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die nes behoort aan die voël, so dit is die besitlike *its* sonder afkappingsteken. *It’s* beteken *it is*, en *the bird built it is nest* maak nie sin nie.","en":"The nest belongs to the bird, so it is the possessive *its* without an apostrophe. *It’s* means *it is*, and *the bird built it is nest* makes no sense."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*“Where is my hat___” asked Liam.* Watter leesteken hoort in die gaping?","en":"*“Where is my hat___” asked Liam.* Which punctuation mark belongs in the gap?"},"options":[{"af":"punt (.)","en":"full stop (.)"},{"af":"komma (,)","en":"comma (,)"},{"af":"uitroepteken (!)","en":"exclamation mark (!)"},{"af":"vraagteken (?)","en":"question mark (?)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Liam vra ’n vraag, so ’n vraagteken staan binne die aanhalingstekens. Dit vervang die komma wat andersins daar sou staan.","en":"Liam asks a question, so a question mark goes inside the inverted commas. It replaces the comma that would otherwise be there."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter lys is reg gepunktueer?","en":"Which list is punctuated correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"I bought bread milk, eggs and apples.","en":"I bought bread milk, eggs and apples."},{"af":"I bought, bread, milk, eggs and apples.","en":"I bought, bread, milk, eggs and apples."},{"af":"I bought bread, milk, eggs and apples.","en":"I bought bread, milk, eggs and apples."},{"af":"I bought bread, milk, eggs, and, apples.","en":"I bought bread, milk, eggs, and, apples."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Kommas skei die items in die lys, en voor die laaste item staan *and*. Daar is geen komma ná *bought* of ná *and* nie.","en":"Commas separate the items in the list, and *and* comes before the last item. There is no comma after *bought* or after *and*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In *“I am hungry,” said Lerato.* staan daar ’n komma binne die aanhalingstekens, want die sin gaan ná die gesproke woorde voort.","en":"In *“I am hungry,” said Lerato.* there is a comma inside the inverted commas because the sentence continues after the spoken words."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. As die spreker laaste kom, eindig die gesproke woorde met ’n komma binne die aanhalingstekens, en die punt kom heel aan die einde.","en":"True. When the speaker comes last, the spoken words end with a comma inside the inverted commas, and the full stop comes at the very end."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Skryf in indirekte rede: *Nomsa said, “I am tired.”*","en":"Change into reported speech: *Nomsa said, “I am tired.”*"},"options":[{"af":"Nomsa said that she was tired.","en":"Nomsa said that she was tired."},{"af":"Nomsa said that I am tired.","en":"Nomsa said that I am tired."},{"af":"Nomsa said, she is tired.","en":"Nomsa said, she is tired."},{"af":"Nomsa said that “she was tired.”","en":"Nomsa said that “she was tired.”"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"In indirekte rede is daar geen aanhalingstekens nie, *I* word *she* en *am* word *was*: *Nomsa said that she was tired.*","en":"In reported speech there are no inverted commas, *I* becomes *she* and *am* becomes *was*: *Nomsa said that she was tired.*"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf met ’n afkappingsteken: *the toys of the children* → *the ___ toys*","en":"Write with an apostrophe: *the toys of the children* → *the ___ toys*"},"answers":{"af":["children’s"],"en":["children’s"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["childrens’","childrens","children’"],"en":["childrens’","childrens","children’"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Children* is meervoud, maar dit eindig nie op -s nie, so jy voeg ’s by: *children’s*.","en":"*Children* is plural, but it does not end in -s, so you add ’s: *children’s*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin het ’n **uitroepteken** nodig?","en":"Which sentence needs an **exclamation mark**?"},"options":[{"af":"Where do you live","en":"Where do you live"},{"af":"What a fantastic goal","en":"What a fantastic goal"},{"af":"The shop is open","en":"The shop is open"},{"af":"My sister is ten","en":"My sister is ten"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*What a fantastic goal* wys sterk gevoel (opgewondenheid), so dit is ’n uitroepsin met **!**. Die eerste een is ’n vraag (?) en die ander twee is stelsinne (.).","en":"*What a fantastic goal* shows strong feeling (excitement), so it is an exclamation with **!**. The first one is a question (?) and the other two are statements (.)."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Woordbetekenis en beelde","en":"Word meaning and images"},"topics":[{"id":"eng5-t3-vocabulary","title":{"af":"Woordeskat en woordbou","en":"Vocabulary and word building"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal Engelse sinonieme, antonieme en homofone kan gebruik, woorde met voorvoegsels en agtervoegsels kan bou en die betekenis van ’n nuwe woord uit die konteks kan uitwerk.","en":"You will be able to use synonyms, antonyms and homophones, build words with prefixes and suffixes and work out the meaning of a new word from its context."},"summary":{"af":"## Sinonieme en antonieme\n\n’n **Sinoniem** is ’n woord wat dieselfde, of amper dieselfde, beteken as ’n ander woord. Met sinonieme hoef jy nie dieselfde woord oor en oor te gebruik nie, en jou skryfwerk word interessanter.\n\n- *big – large, huge* (groot)\n- *happy – glad, cheerful* (gelukkig, bly)\n- *begin – start* (begin)\n- *quick – fast* (vinnig)\n\n’n **Antoniem** is ’n woord met die teenoorgestelde betekenis: *hot – cold* (warm – koud), *early – late* (vroeg – laat), *full – empty* (vol – leeg).\n\nJy kan baie antonieme maak deur ’n **voorvoegsel** voor die woord te sit, net soos *gelukkig → ongelukkig* in Afrikaans:\n\n| Voorvoegsel | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| **un-** | *happy → unhappy, kind → unkind, lock → unlock, tidy → untidy* |\n| **dis-** | *agree → disagree, like → dislike, honest → dishonest, appear → disappear* |\n| **im-** | *possible → impossible, polite → impolite, patient → impatient* |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Jy kan nie sommer enige voorvoegsel kies nie. Ons sê *impossible* (nie *unpossible* nie) en *disagree* (nie *unagree* nie). Leer elke woord saam met sy eie voorvoegsel. Die meeste woorde wat **im-** kry, begin met ’n *p* of ’n *m*.\n\n## Homofone\n\n**Homofone** is woorde wat **dieselfde klink**, maar ’n **ander spelling en betekenis** het. Jou oor kan hulle nie uitmekaar ken nie, daarom moet jy na die betekenis van die sin kyk.\n\n| Woord | Betekenis | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| *there* | daar (’n plek) | *Put the box over there.* |\n| *their* | hulle s’n | *The girls fed their dog.* |\n| *they’re* | *they are* (hulle is) | *They’re late for school.* |\n| *to* | na; ook voor ’n werkwoord | *We walk to the shop to buy bread.* |\n| *too* | ook; te (veel) | *The tea is too hot. I want some too.* |\n| *two* | twee (2) | *I have two sisters.* |\n| *see / sea* | sien / see (oseaan) | *I can see the sea.* |\n| *right / write* | reg of regs / skryf | *Write the right answer.* |\n\n> **Onthou:** As jy *they are* in die plek van die woord kan sê, skryf *they’re*. As die woord wys dat iets aan mense behoort, skryf *their*.\n\n## Samestellings, voorvoegsels en agtervoegsels\n\n’n **Samestelling** (*compound word*) bestaan uit twee woorde wat aan mekaar geskryf word: *sun + flower = sunflower* (sonneblom), *foot + ball = football*, *tooth + brush = toothbrush* (tandeborsel).\n\nDie **stamwoord** (*base word*) is die woord waarmee jy begin. ’n **Voorvoegsel** (*prefix*) kom voor die stamwoord en ’n **agtervoegsel** (*suffix*) kom agter die stamwoord. Elkeen verander die betekenis:\n\n| Deel | Betekenis | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| **re-** | weer, oor | *redo, rewrite, replay* |\n| **un-** | nie, die teenoorgestelde | *unfair, unlock* |\n| **-ful** | vol van | *helpful, careful, hopeful* |\n| **-less** | sonder | *helpless, careless, homeless* |\n| **-er** | iemand wat dit doen | *teacher, farmer, painter* |\n| **-ness** | maak van ’n byvoeglike naamwoord ’n selfstandige naamwoord | *kindness, darkness, sadness* |\n\nLet op die spelling: eindig die stamwoord op ’n medeklinker + **y**, dan verander die y na **i**: *happy → happiness, beauty → beautiful*.\n\n## Woordfamilies\n\n’n **Woordfamilie** is ’n groep woorde wat van dieselfde stamwoord gebou is. As jy die stamwoord ken, kan jy dikwels die betekenis van die ander raai: *help → helper, helpful, helpless, unhelpful, helping*.\n\n## Betekenis uit die konteks\n\nKry jy ’n woord wat jy nie ken nie? Die **konteks** (die woorde en sinne rondom die woord) kan jou help:\n\n1. Lees die hele sin, en ook die sin voor en ná dit.\n2. Soek **leidrade**: ’n voorbeeld, ’n verduideliking of ’n teenoorgestelde.\n3. Sit ’n woord wat jy ken in sy plek.\n4. Kyk of die sin steeds sin maak.\n\n*Thabo was so famished after the match that he ate three sandwiches.* Die leidraad *ate three sandwiches* (het drie toebroodjies geëet) wys dat **famished** *baie honger* beteken.","en":"## Synonyms and antonyms\n\nA **synonym** is a word that means the same, or almost the same, as another word. Synonyms help you to avoid using the same word again and again, and they make your writing more interesting.\n\n- *big – large, huge*\n- *happy – glad, cheerful*\n- *begin – start*\n- *quick – fast*\n\nAn **antonym** is a word with the opposite meaning: *hot – cold, early – late, full – empty*.\n\nYou can make many antonyms by putting a **prefix** in front of a word:\n\n| Prefix | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| **un-** | *happy → unhappy, kind → unkind, lock → unlock, tidy → untidy* |\n| **dis-** | *agree → disagree, like → dislike, honest → dishonest, appear → disappear* |\n| **im-** | *possible → impossible, polite → impolite, patient → impatient* |\n\n> **Common mistake:** You cannot choose just any prefix. We say *impossible* (not *unpossible*) and *disagree* (not *unagree*). Learn each word together with its own prefix. Most words that take **im-** begin with a *p* or an *m*.\n\n## Homophones\n\n**Homophones** are words that **sound the same** but have a **different spelling and meaning**. Your ear cannot tell them apart, so you must look at the meaning of the sentence.\n\n| Word | Meaning | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| *there* | a place | *Put the box over there.* |\n| *their* | belonging to them | *The girls fed their dog.* |\n| *they’re* | they are | *They’re late for school.* |\n| *to* | towards; also before a verb | *We walk to the shop to buy bread.* |\n| *too* | also; more than enough | *The tea is too hot. I want some too.* |\n| *two* | the number 2 | *I have two sisters.* |\n| *see / sea* | look with your eyes / the ocean | *I can see the sea.* |\n| *right / write* | correct or not left / put words on paper | *Write the right answer.* |\n\n> **Remember:** If you can say *they are* in the place of the word, write *they’re*. If the word shows that something belongs to people, write *their*.\n\n## Compound words, prefixes and suffixes\n\nA **compound word** is made of two words written together as one: *sun + flower = sunflower, foot + ball = football, tooth + brush = toothbrush*.\n\nThe **base word** is the word you start with. A **prefix** goes in front of the base word and a **suffix** goes at the end. Each one changes the meaning:\n\n| Part | Meaning | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| **re-** | again | *redo, rewrite, replay* |\n| **un-** | not, the opposite | *unfair, unlock* |\n| **-ful** | full of | *helpful, careful, hopeful* |\n| **-less** | without | *helpless, careless, homeless* |\n| **-er** | a person who does it | *teacher, farmer, painter* |\n| **-ness** | turns an adjective into a noun | *kindness, darkness, sadness* |\n\nWatch the spelling: if the base word ends in a consonant + **y**, the y changes to **i**: *happy → happiness, beauty → beautiful*.\n\n## Word families\n\nA **word family** is a group of words built from the same base word. If you know the base word, you can often work out the meaning of the others: *help → helper, helpful, helpless, unhelpful, helping*.\n\n## Meaning from context\n\nDo you meet a word you do not know? The **context** (the words and sentences around it) can help you:\n\n1. Read the whole sentence, and also the sentence before and after it.\n2. Look for **clues**: an example, an explanation or an opposite.\n3. Put a word you know in its place.\n4. Check that the sentence still makes sense.\n\n*Thabo was so famished after the match that he ate three sandwiches.* The clue *ate three sandwiches* shows that **famished** means *very hungry*."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Sinoniem (*synonym*)","en":"Synonym"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat dieselfde of amper dieselfde beteken as ’n ander woord, soos *begin* en *start*.","en":"A word that means the same or almost the same as another word, like *begin* and *start*."}},{"term":{"af":"Antoniem (*antonym*)","en":"Antonym"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord met die teenoorgestelde betekenis, soos *hot* en *cold* of *agree* en *disagree*.","en":"A word with the opposite meaning, like *hot* and *cold* or *agree* and *disagree*."}},{"term":{"af":"Homofoon (*homophone*)","en":"Homophone"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat dieselfde klink as ’n ander woord, maar anders gespel word en iets anders beteken, soos *see* en *sea*.","en":"A word that sounds the same as another word but is spelt differently and means something else, like *see* and *sea*."}},{"term":{"af":"Samestelling (*compound word*)","en":"Compound word"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat uit twee woorde bestaan wat aan mekaar geskryf word, soos *football* (*foot + ball*).","en":"A word made of two words written together as one, like *football* (*foot + ball*)."}},{"term":{"af":"Stamwoord (*base word*)","en":"Base word"},"def":{"af":"Die basiese woord waarby jy ’n voorvoegsel of agtervoegsel voeg, soos *help* in *helpful*.","en":"The basic word to which you add a prefix or a suffix, like *help* in *helpful*."}},{"term":{"af":"Voorvoegsel (*prefix*)","en":"Prefix"},"def":{"af":"’n Deeltjie voor ’n woord wat die betekenis verander, soos *re-* in *rewrite* (weer skryf).","en":"A small part in front of a word that changes its meaning, like *re-* in *rewrite* (write again)."}},{"term":{"af":"Agtervoegsel (*suffix*)","en":"Suffix"},"def":{"af":"’n Deeltjie agter ’n woord wat die betekenis of woordsoort verander, soos *-less* in *careless* (sonder sorg).","en":"A small part at the end of a word that changes its meaning or word type, like *-less* in *careless* (without care)."}},{"term":{"af":"Woordfamilie (*word family*)","en":"Word family"},"def":{"af":"’n Groep woorde wat van dieselfde stamwoord gebou is, soos *play, player, playful* en *replay*.","en":"A group of words built from the same base word, like *play, player, playful* and *replay*."}},{"term":{"af":"Konteks (*context*)","en":"Context"},"def":{"af":"Die woorde en sinne rondom ’n woord wat jou help om sy betekenis uit te werk.","en":"The words and sentences around a word that help you to work out its meaning."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Antonieme met voorvoegsels","en":"Antonyms with prefixes"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die antoniem van elke woord deur *un-*, *dis-* of *im-* by te voeg: *happy, agree, possible, lock*.","en":"Write the antonym of each word by adding *un-*, *dis-* or *im-*: *happy, agree, possible, lock*."},"steps":[{"af":"*happy* (gelukkig) kry *un-*: *unhappy* (ongelukkig).","en":"*happy* takes *un-*: *unhappy*."},{"af":"*agree* (saamstem) kry *dis-*: *disagree* (nie saamstem nie). *Unagree* bestaan nie.","en":"*agree* takes *dis-*: *disagree*. *Unagree* is not a word."},{"af":"*possible* (moontlik) kry *im-*, soos baie woorde wat met ’n *p* begin: *impossible* (onmoontlik).","en":"*possible* takes *im-*, like many words that begin with a *p*: *impossible*."},{"af":"*lock* (sluit) kry *un-*: *unlock* (oopsluit).","en":"*lock* takes *un-*: *unlock*."}],"answer":{"af":"*unhappy, disagree, impossible, unlock*","en":"*unhappy, disagree, impossible, unlock*"}},{"title":{"af":"Kies die regte homofoon","en":"Choose the correct homophone"},"problem":{"af":"Vul *there, their* of *they’re* in: *___ going to visit ___ granny who lives over ___.*","en":"Fill in *there, their* or *they’re*: *___ going to visit ___ granny who lives over ___.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Eerste gaping: jy kan *They are going* sê, so skryf *They’re* (met ’n hoofletter, want dit begin die sin).","en":"First gap: you can say *They are going*, so write *They’re* (with a capital letter, because it starts the sentence)."},{"af":"Tweede gaping: die ouma behoort aan hulle (hulle ouma), so skryf *their*.","en":"Second gap: the granny belongs to them, so write *their*."},{"af":"Derde gaping: *over there* wys na ’n plek (daar), so skryf *there*.","en":"Third gap: *over there* points to a place, so write *there*."}],"answer":{"af":"*They’re going to visit their granny who lives over there.*","en":"*They’re going to visit their granny who lives over there.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Bou woorde met agtervoegsels","en":"Build words with suffixes"},"problem":{"af":"Voeg die regte agtervoegsel by die woord tussen hakies: *Lerato is always ___ (help) in class. Leaving the gate open was ___ (care).*","en":"Add the correct suffix to the word in brackets: *Lerato is always ___ (help) in class. Leaving the gate open was ___ (care).*"},"steps":[{"af":"Lerato help graag, sy is vol hulp. *-ful* beteken *vol van*, so skryf *helpful* (behulpsaam).","en":"Lerato likes to help; she is full of help. *-ful* means *full of*, so write *helpful*."},{"af":"Om die hek oop te los, wys dat iemand nie versigtig was nie: sonder sorg. *-less* beteken *sonder*, so skryf *careless* (agteloos, onverskillig).","en":"Leaving the gate open shows that someone was not careful: without care. *-less* means *without*, so write *careless*."},{"af":"Lees die sinne weer om seker te maak dat hulle sin maak.","en":"Read the sentences again to check that they make sense."}],"answer":{"af":"*helpful; careless*","en":"*helpful; careless*"}},{"title":{"af":"Betekenis uit die konteks","en":"Meaning from context"},"problem":{"af":"Lees: *After the long hike up the mountain, Sipho was exhausted and fell asleep on the couch.* Wat beteken *exhausted*?","en":"Read: *After the long hike up the mountain, Sipho was exhausted and fell asleep on the couch.* What does *exhausted* mean?"},"steps":[{"af":"Soek leidrade in die sin: *long hike up the mountain* (lang staptog teen die berg op) en *fell asleep* (aan die slaap geraak).","en":"Look for clues in the sentence: *long hike up the mountain* and *fell asleep*."},{"af":"Hoe voel iemand ná ’n lang staptog as hy dadelik aan die slaap raak? Baie moeg.","en":"How does someone feel after a long hike if they fall asleep at once? Very tired."},{"af":"Toets: *Sipho was very tired and fell asleep.* Die sin maak steeds sin.","en":"Test it: *Sipho was very tired and fell asleep.* The sentence still makes sense."}],"answer":{"af":"*Exhausted* beteken *very tired* (baie moeg, uitgeput).","en":"*Exhausted* means *very tired*."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is ’n **sinoniem** van *begin*?","en":"Which word is a **synonym** of *begin*?"},"options":[{"af":"finish","en":"finish"},{"af":"start","en":"start"},{"af":"began","en":"began"},{"af":"stop","en":"stop"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*start* beteken dieselfde as *begin*. *finish* en *stop* is antonieme (teenoorgesteldes), en *began* is net die verlede tyd van *begin*.","en":"*start* means the same as *begin*. *finish* and *stop* are antonyms (opposites), and *began* is just the past tense of *begin*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vul die regte homofoon in: *The children packed ___ bags for the school camp.*","en":"Fill in the correct homophone: *The children packed ___ bags for the school camp.*"},"answers":{"af":["their"],"en":["their"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["there","they’re","thier"],"en":["there","they’re","thier"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die tasse behoort aan die kinders (hulle tasse), so dis *their*. *there* is ’n plek, *they’re* beteken *they are*, en *thier* is ’n spelfout.","en":"The bags belong to the children, so it is *their*. *there* is a place, *they’re* means *they are*, and *thier* is a spelling mistake."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **antoniem** van *possible*?","en":"What is the **antonym** of *possible*?"},"options":[{"af":"unpossible","en":"unpossible"},{"af":"dispossible","en":"dispossible"},{"af":"impossible","en":"impossible"},{"af":"possibly","en":"possibly"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*possible* begin met ’n *p* en kry die voorvoegsel *im-*: *impossible* (onmoontlik). *unpossible* en *dispossible* bestaan nie, en *possibly* is nie ’n teenoorgestelde nie.","en":"*possible* begins with a *p* and takes the prefix *im-*: *impossible*. *unpossible* and *dispossible* are not words, and *possibly* is not an opposite."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord beteken *sonder hoop*?","en":"Which word means *without hope*?"},"options":[{"af":"hopeless","en":"hopeless"},{"af":"hopeful","en":"hopeful"},{"af":"hoping","en":"hoping"},{"af":"unhope","en":"unhope"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die agtervoegsel *-less* beteken *sonder*, so *hopeless* = sonder hoop. *hopeful* beteken juis *vol hoop*.","en":"The suffix *-less* means *without*, so *hopeless* = without hope. *hopeful* means the opposite: *full of hope*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*Sunflower* is ’n samestelling wat uit die woorde *sun* en *flower* bestaan.","en":"*Sunflower* is a compound word made from the words *sun* and *flower*."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Twee woorde, *sun* en *flower*, word aan mekaar geskryf om een nuwe woord te vorm.","en":"True. Two words, *sun* and *flower*, are written together to form one new word."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter sin is die homofone **reg** gebruik?","en":"In which sentence are the homophones used **correctly**?"},"options":[{"af":"I can sea the see from my window.","en":"I can sea the see from my window."},{"af":"I can see the see from my window.","en":"I can see the see from my window."},{"af":"I can sea the sea from my window.","en":"I can sea the sea from my window."},{"af":"I can see the sea from my window.","en":"I can see the sea from my window."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*see* is wat jy met jou oë doen (sien) en *sea* is die oseaan. Daarom: *I can see the sea.*","en":"*see* is what you do with your eyes and *sea* is the ocean. So: *I can see the sea.*"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voeg *-ness* by: *happy* + *ness* = ___","en":"Add *-ness*: *happy* + *ness* = ___"},"answers":{"af":["happiness"],"en":["happiness"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["happyness","hapiness","happines"],"en":["happyness","hapiness","happines"]}},"explain":{"af":"*happy* eindig op ’n medeklinker + *y*, so die *y* word *i* voordat jy *-ness* byvoeg: *happiness*. Die woord het twee *p*’s en twee *s*’e.","en":"*happy* ends in a consonant + *y*, so the *y* changes to *i* before you add *-ness*: *happiness*. The word has two *p*’s and two *s*’s."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken *rewrite*?","en":"What does *rewrite* mean?"},"options":[{"af":"weer skryf","en":"write again"},{"af":"nie skryf nie","en":"not write"},{"af":"sleg skryf","en":"write badly"},{"af":"iemand wat skryf","en":"someone who writes"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die voorvoegsel *re-* beteken *weer*, so *rewrite* beteken om iets weer (oor) te skryf. *Iemand wat skryf* is ’n *writer*, met die agtervoegsel *-er*.","en":"The prefix *re-* means *again*, so *rewrite* means to write something again. *Someone who writes* is a *writer*, with the suffix *-er*."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke voorvoegsel of agtervoegsel by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each prefix or suffix to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"re-","en":"re-"},"r":{"af":"weer","en":"again"}},{"l":{"af":"un-","en":"un-"},"r":{"af":"nie, die teenoorgestelde","en":"not, the opposite"}},{"l":{"af":"-ful","en":"-ful"},"r":{"af":"vol van","en":"full of"}},{"l":{"af":"-less","en":"-less"},"r":{"af":"sonder","en":"without"}},{"l":{"af":"-er","en":"-er"},"r":{"af":"iemand wat dit doen","en":"a person who does it"}}],"explain":{"af":"*re-* = weer (*replay*), *un-* = nie (*unfair*), *-ful* = vol van (*careful*), *-less* = sonder (*careless*), *-er* = iemand wat dit doen (*teacher*).","en":"*re-* = again (*replay*), *un-* = not (*unfair*), *-ful* = full of (*careful*), *-less* = without (*careless*), *-er* = a person who does it (*teacher*)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees: *The road was so narrow that two cars could not pass each other.* Wat beteken *narrow*?","en":"Read: *The road was so narrow that two cars could not pass each other.* What does *narrow* mean?"},"options":[{"af":"baie lank","en":"very long"},{"af":"baie besig","en":"very busy"},{"af":"nie breed nie","en":"not wide"},{"af":"nie gelyk nie","en":"not smooth"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die leidraad is dat twee motors nie by mekaar kon verbykom nie. Dit gebeur as die pad **nie breed** genoeg is nie. *Narrow* beteken smal.","en":"The clue is that two cars could not pass each other. That happens when the road is **not wide** enough. *Narrow* is the opposite of *wide*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*Two*, *too* en *to* is sinonieme omdat hulle dieselfde klink.","en":"*Two*, *too* and *to* are synonyms because they sound the same."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Hulle is **homofone**: hulle klink dieselfde, maar het verskillende betekenisse. Sinonieme het dieselfde betekenis, soos *big* en *large*.","en":"False. They are **homophones**: they sound the same but have different meanings. Synonyms have the same meaning, like *big* and *large*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord behoort **nie** aan die woordfamilie van *help* nie?","en":"Which word does **not** belong to the word family of *help*?"},"options":[{"af":"helpful","en":"helpful"},{"af":"helper","en":"helper"},{"af":"unhelpful","en":"unhelpful"},{"af":"hello","en":"hello"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*helpful, helper* en *unhelpful* is almal van die stamwoord *help* gebou. *hello* begin net met dieselfde letters, maar het niks met *help* te doen nie.","en":"*helpful, helper* and *unhelpful* are all built from the base word *help*. *hello* only starts with the same letters; it has nothing to do with *help*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die antoniem van *agree* is ___.","en":"The antonym of *agree* is ___."},"answers":{"af":["disagree"],"en":["disagree"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["unagree","imagree","misagree"],"en":["unagree","imagree","misagree"]}},"explain":{"af":"*agree* kry die voorvoegsel *dis-*: *disagree* (nie saamstem nie). Die ander woorde bestaan nie in Engels nie.","en":"*agree* takes the prefix *dis-*: *disagree*. The other words do not exist in English."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is ’n **samestelling**?","en":"Which word is a **compound word**?"},"options":[{"af":"careful","en":"careful"},{"af":"toothbrush","en":"toothbrush"},{"af":"unhappy","en":"unhappy"},{"af":"teacher","en":"teacher"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*toothbrush* bestaan uit twee volledige woorde: *tooth + brush*. Die ander woorde bestaan uit een woord plus ’n voor- of agtervoegsel (*care + -ful, un- + happy, teach + -er*).","en":"*toothbrush* is made of two whole words: *tooth + brush*. The other words are one word plus a prefix or suffix (*care + -ful, un- + happy, teach + -er*)."}}]},{"id":"eng5-t3-spelling-dictionary","title":{"af":"Spelling en woordeboekvaardighede","en":"Spelling and dictionary skills"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die belangrikste Engelse spelreëls en stil letters ken, woorde in alfabetiese volgorde kan rangskik en ’n woordeboek met gidswoorde en afkortings vinnig kan gebruik.","en":"You will know the main English spelling rules and silent letters, be able to put words in alphabetical order and use a dictionary quickly with guide words and abbreviations."},"summary":{"af":"## Vier spelreëls\n\nEngelse spelling lyk soms deurmekaar, maar baie woorde volg ’n **patroon**. Leer hierdie vier reëls:\n\n| Reël | Voorbeelde | Maar … |\n|---|---|---|\n| **i voor e**, behalwe ná *c* (vir die *ee*-klank) | *believe, field, piece; receive, ceiling* | *eight, weigh* sê *ay*; *weird* is ’n uitsondering |\n| **Verdubbel die laaste medeklinker** ná ’n kort klinker | *run → running, stop → stopped, big → bigger* | nie ná twee medeklinkers (*jump → jumping*) of ’n lang klank (*rain → raining*) nie |\n| **Laat die stil e weg** voor *-ing, -ed, -er* | *make → making, smile → smiled, nice → nicer* | hou die e voor *-ful, -ly*: *hopeful, safely* |\n| **y word i** ná ’n medeklinker | *baby → babies, cry → cried, happy → happier* | hou die y ná ’n klinker (*boy → boys*) en voor *-ing* (*crying*) |\n\nWaarom verdubbel ons? Die dubbele medeklinker hou die klinker **kort**. Vergelyk: *hopping* (spring, van *hop*) en *hoping* (hoop, van *hope*).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *hoping* en *hopping* is twee verskillende woorde! *hope → hoping* (laat die e weg), maar *hop → hopping* (verdubbel die p).\n\n## Stil letters en moeilike woorde\n\nPartykeer skryf ons ’n letter wat ons nie sê nie. Dit is ’n **stil letter**.\n\n| Stil letter | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| **k** voor *n* | *knee, knife, know, knock* |\n| **w** voor *r* | *write, wrong, wrist* |\n| **b** ná *m* | *lamb, climb, thumb, comb* |\n| **gh** | *night, light, daughter* |\n| **h** | *hour, honest* |\n| **t** | *listen, castle* |\n\nLeer ook hierdie woorde wat baie mense verkeerd spel: *because, friend, beautiful, Wednesday, tomorrow, until, different, which*. **Wenk:** Sê die woord in jou kop in dele: *Wed-nes-day, to-mor-row, be-cause*.\n\n## Alfabetiese volgorde\n\nWoorde in ’n woordeboek staan in **alfabetiese volgorde**:\n\n1. Kyk na die **eerste** letter: *apple, bird, cow*.\n2. Is die eerste letters dieselfde? Kyk na die **tweede** letter: *bat, bed, bus* (a, e, u).\n3. Is die eerste twee letters dieselfde? Kyk na die **derde** letter: *shell, shine, shop* (e, i, o).\n\n## Gidswoorde en ’n woordeboekinskrywing\n\nBo-aan elke bladsy staan twee **gidswoorde** (*guide words*): die eerste en die laaste woord op daardie bladsy. Jou woord is op die bladsy as dit alfabeties **tussen** die twee gidswoorde val.\n\nGidswoorde *pan – pear*: *park* is op die bladsy (*par* kom ná *pan*), maar *pack* nie (*pac* kom vóór *pan*) en *pet* ook nie (*pet* kom ná *pea*).\n\n’n **Inskrywing** in ’n woordeboek het gewoonlik hierdie dele:\n\n- die **trefwoord** in vetdruk: die woord wat jy opsoek\n- soms die **uitspraak**: hoe jy die woord sê\n- die **woordsoort** as ’n afkorting\n- die **betekenis** (genommer as daar meer as een is)\n- ’n **voorbeeldsin**\n- **ander vorme**, soos die meervoud of verlede tyd\n\n**brave** *adj.* not afraid of danger. *The brave lifeguard swam out to help the boy.* **braver, bravest**\n\n| Afkorting | Woordsoort |\n|---|---|\n| *n.* | *noun* (selfstandige naamwoord) |\n| *v.* | *verb* (werkwoord) |\n| *adj.* | *adjective* (byvoeglike naamwoord) |\n| *adv.* | *adverb* (bywoord) |\n| *pl.* | *plural* (meervoud) |\n\n> **Onthou:** Gebruik die gidswoorde om vinnig die regte bladsy te kry. Moenie elke woord op elke bladsy lees nie!","en":"## Four spelling rules\n\nEnglish spelling can look confusing, but many words follow a **pattern**. Learn these four rules:\n\n| Rule | Examples | But … |\n|---|---|---|\n| **i before e**, except after *c* (for the *ee* sound) | *believe, field, piece; receive, ceiling* | *eight, weigh* say *ay*; *weird* is an exception |\n| **Double the last consonant** after a short vowel | *run → running, stop → stopped, big → bigger* | not after two consonants (*jump → jumping*) or a long vowel (*rain → raining*) |\n| **Drop the silent e** before *-ing, -ed, -er* | *make → making, smile → smiled, nice → nicer* | keep the e before *-ful, -ly*: *hopeful, safely* |\n| **y changes to i** after a consonant | *baby → babies, cry → cried, happy → happier* | keep the y after a vowel (*boy → boys*) and before *-ing* (*crying*) |\n\nWhy do we double? The double consonant keeps the vowel **short**. Compare *hopping* (jumping, from *hop*) and *hoping* (wishing, from *hope*).\n\n> **Common mistake:** *hoping* and *hopping* are two different words! *hope → hoping* (drop the e), but *hop → hopping* (double the p).\n\n## Silent letters and tricky words\n\nSometimes we write a letter that we do not say. This is a **silent letter**.\n\n| Silent letter | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| **k** before *n* | *knee, knife, know, knock* |\n| **w** before *r* | *write, wrong, wrist* |\n| **b** after *m* | *lamb, climb, thumb, comb* |\n| **gh** | *night, light, daughter* |\n| **h** | *hour, honest* |\n| **t** | *listen, castle* |\n\nAlso learn these words that many people spell wrongly: *because, friend, beautiful, Wednesday, tomorrow, until, different, which*. **Tip:** Say the word in parts in your head: *Wed-nes-day, to-mor-row, be-cause*.\n\n## Alphabetical order\n\nWords in a dictionary are in **alphabetical order**:\n\n1. Look at the **first** letter: *apple, bird, cow*.\n2. Are the first letters the same? Look at the **second** letter: *bat, bed, bus* (a, e, u).\n3. Are the first two letters the same? Look at the **third** letter: *shell, shine, shop* (e, i, o).\n\n## Guide words and a dictionary entry\n\nAt the top of every page there are two **guide words**: the first and the last word on that page. Your word is on the page if it comes alphabetically **between** the two guide words.\n\nGuide words *pan – pear*: *park* is on the page (*par* comes after *pan*), but *pack* is not (*pac* comes before *pan*), and neither is *pet* (*pet* comes after *pea*).\n\nAn **entry** in a dictionary usually has these parts:\n\n- the **headword** in bold: the word you look up\n- sometimes the **pronunciation**: how you say the word\n- the **part of speech** as an abbreviation\n- the **meaning** (numbered if there is more than one)\n- an **example sentence**\n- **other forms**, such as the plural or the past tense\n\n**brave** *adj.* not afraid of danger. *The brave lifeguard swam out to help the boy.* **braver, bravest**\n\n| Abbreviation | Part of speech |\n|---|---|\n| *n.* | noun |\n| *v.* | verb |\n| *adj.* | adjective |\n| *adv.* | adverb |\n| *pl.* | plural |\n\n> **Remember:** Use the guide words to find the right page quickly. Do not read every word on every page!"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Spelreël (*spelling rule*)","en":"Spelling rule"},"def":{"af":"’n Patroon wat jou help om baie woorde reg te spel, soos *baby → babies*.","en":"A pattern that helps you to spell many words correctly, like *baby → babies*."}},{"term":{"af":"Stil letter (*silent letter*)","en":"Silent letter"},"def":{"af":"’n Letter wat jy skryf maar nie sê nie, soos die *k* in *knee* of die *b* in *lamb*.","en":"A letter that you write but do not say, like the *k* in *knee* or the *b* in *lamb*."}},{"term":{"af":"Klinker (*vowel*)","en":"Vowel"},"def":{"af":"Een van die letters *a, e, i, o, u*; die ander letters is medeklinkers.","en":"One of the letters *a, e, i, o, u*; the other letters are consonants."}},{"term":{"af":"Alfabetiese volgorde (*alphabetical order*)","en":"Alphabetical order"},"def":{"af":"Die volgorde van woorde volgens die alfabet, soos in ’n woordeboek: *bat, bed, bus*.","en":"The order of words according to the alphabet, as in a dictionary: *bat, bed, bus*."}},{"term":{"af":"Gidswoorde (*guide words*)","en":"Guide words"},"def":{"af":"Die twee woorde bo-aan ’n woordeboekbladsy wat die eerste en laaste woord op die bladsy wys.","en":"The two words at the top of a dictionary page that show the first and last word on that page."}},{"term":{"af":"Trefwoord (*headword*)","en":"Headword"},"def":{"af":"Die woord in vetdruk aan die begin van ’n woordeboekinskrywing; die woord wat jy opsoek.","en":"The word in bold at the start of a dictionary entry; the word you look up."}},{"term":{"af":"Inskrywing (*entry*)","en":"Entry"},"def":{"af":"Al die inligting oor een trefwoord in ’n woordeboek: woordsoort, betekenis, voorbeeldsin en ander vorme.","en":"All the information about one headword in a dictionary: part of speech, meaning, example sentence and other forms."}},{"term":{"af":"Woordsoort (*part of speech*)","en":"Part of speech"},"def":{"af":"Die soort woord, soos *noun, verb* of *adjective*, wat in ’n woordeboek met ’n afkorting gewys word.","en":"The kind of word, such as *noun, verb* or *adjective*, which a dictionary shows with an abbreviation."}},{"term":{"af":"Afkorting (*abbreviation*)","en":"Abbreviation"},"def":{"af":"’n Kort vorm van ’n woord, soos *adj.* vir *adjective*.","en":"A short form of a word, like *adj.* for *adjective*."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Voeg -ing by","en":"Add -ing"},"problem":{"af":"Voeg *-ing* by elke werkwoord: *run, make, cry, play*.","en":"Add *-ing* to each verb: *run, make, cry, play*."},"steps":[{"af":"*run* is kort en eindig op een klinker + een medeklinker, so verdubbel die *n*: *running*.","en":"*run* is short and ends in one vowel + one consonant, so double the *n*: *running*."},{"af":"*make* eindig op ’n stil *e*. *-ing* begin met ’n klinker, so laat die *e* weg: *making*.","en":"*make* ends in a silent *e*. *-ing* begins with a vowel, so drop the *e*: *making*."},{"af":"*cry* eindig op ’n medeklinker + *y*, maar voor *-ing* bly die *y*: *crying*.","en":"*cry* ends in a consonant + *y*, but before *-ing* the *y* stays: *crying*."},{"af":"*play* eindig op ’n klinker + *y*, so jy voeg net *-ing* by: *playing*.","en":"*play* ends in a vowel + *y*, so you just add *-ing*: *playing*."}],"answer":{"af":"*running, making, crying, playing*","en":"*running, making, crying, playing*"}},{"title":{"af":"Alfabetiese volgorde tot die derde letter","en":"Alphabetical order to the third letter"},"problem":{"af":"Rangskik in alfabetiese volgorde: *shop, sand, shell, shine*.","en":"Put in alphabetical order: *shop, sand, shell, shine*."},"steps":[{"af":"Al die woorde begin met *s*, so kyk na die tweede letter: *a* (sand) en *h* (shop, shell, shine). *sand* kom eerste.","en":"All the words begin with *s*, so look at the second letter: *a* (sand) and *h* (shop, shell, shine). *sand* comes first."},{"af":"Die ander drie begin almal met *sh*, so kyk na die derde letter: *e* (shell), *i* (shine), *o* (shop).","en":"The other three all begin with *sh*, so look at the third letter: *e* (shell), *i* (shine), *o* (shop)."},{"af":"*e* kom voor *i*, en *i* kom voor *o*.","en":"*e* comes before *i*, and *i* comes before *o*."}],"answer":{"af":"*sand, shell, shine, shop*","en":"*sand, shell, shine, shop*"}},{"title":{"af":"Gebruik gidswoorde","en":"Use guide words"},"problem":{"af":"Die gidswoorde op ’n bladsy is *mango – milk*. Watter van hierdie woorde staan op die bladsy: *map, melon, mice, mud*?","en":"The guide words on a page are *mango – milk*. Which of these words are on the page: *map, melon, mice, mud*?"},"steps":[{"af":"*map*: die eerste twee letters is *ma*, net soos *mango*. Die derde letter *p* kom ná *n*, so *map* kom ná *mango*. Dit is op die bladsy.","en":"*map*: the first two letters are *ma*, just like *mango*. The third letter *p* comes after *n*, so *map* comes after *mango*. It is on the page."},{"af":"*melon*: *me* kom ná *ma* en vóór *mi*, so dit is op die bladsy.","en":"*melon*: *me* comes after *ma* and before *mi*, so it is on the page."},{"af":"*mice*: *mi* is dieselfde as by *milk*, maar die derde letter *c* kom vóór *l*. Dit is op die bladsy.","en":"*mice*: *mi* is the same as in *milk*, but the third letter *c* comes before *l*. It is on the page."},{"af":"*mud*: *mu* kom ná *mi*, so dit kom ná *milk*. Dit is op ’n latere bladsy.","en":"*mud*: *mu* comes after *mi*, so it comes after *milk*. It is on a later page."}],"answer":{"af":"*map, melon* en *mice* is op die bladsy; *mud* nie.","en":"*map, melon* and *mice* are on the page; *mud* is not."}},{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n woordeboekinskrywing","en":"Read a dictionary entry"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die inskrywing: **climb** *v.* to go up something using your hands and feet. *The monkey climbed the tree.* **climbed, climbing**. Noem die trefwoord, die woordsoort, die betekenis en die stil letter.","en":"Read the entry: **climb** *v.* to go up something using your hands and feet. *The monkey climbed the tree.* **climbed, climbing**. Name the headword, the part of speech, the meaning and the silent letter."},"steps":[{"af":"Die trefwoord is die eerste woord in vetdruk: *climb*.","en":"The headword is the first word in bold: *climb*."},{"af":"*v.* is die afkorting vir *verb*, so *climb* is ’n werkwoord.","en":"*v.* is the abbreviation for *verb*, so *climb* is a verb."},{"af":"Die betekenis staan ná die woordsoort: *to go up something using your hands and feet* (om iets met jou hande en voete uit te klim).","en":"The meaning comes after the part of speech: *to go up something using your hands and feet*."},{"af":"Die *b* ná die *m* word nie gesê nie, so dit is ’n stil letter.","en":"The *b* after the *m* is not said, so it is a silent letter."}],"answer":{"af":"Trefwoord: *climb*; woordsoort: *verb* (werkwoord); betekenis: *to go up something using your hands and feet*; stil letter: *b*.","en":"Headword: *climb*; part of speech: verb; meaning: *to go up something using your hands and feet*; silent letter: *b*."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is **reg** gespel?","en":"Which word is spelt **correctly**?"},"options":[{"af":"recieve","en":"recieve"},{"af":"receive","en":"receive"},{"af":"receeve","en":"receeve"},{"af":"resieve","en":"resieve"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die reël is *i voor e, behalwe ná c*. Hier kom die klank ná ’n *c*, so dit is *ei*: *receive*.","en":"The rule is *i before e, except after c*. Here the sound comes after a *c*, so it is *ei*: *receive*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die woord *knife* begin met ’n stil *k*.","en":"The word *knife* begins with a silent *k*."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Voor ’n *n* aan die begin van ’n woord sê ons nie die *k* nie: *knife, knee, know*.","en":"True. Before an *n* at the start of a word, we do not say the *k*: *knife, knee, know*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die padda spring rond. Wat is *hop* + *ing*?","en":"The frog is jumping around. What is *hop* + *ing*?"},"options":[{"af":"hoping","en":"hoping"},{"af":"hopeing","en":"hopeing"},{"af":"hopping","en":"hopping"},{"af":"hopiing","en":"hopiing"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*hop* is kort met ’n kort klinker en een medeklinker aan die einde, so die *p* verdubbel: *hopping*. *hoping* kom van *hope* (hoop).","en":"*hop* is short, with a short vowel and one consonant at the end, so the *p* is doubled: *hopping*. *hoping* comes from *hope*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voeg *-ing* by: *smile* → ___","en":"Add *-ing*: *smile* → ___"},"answers":{"af":["smiling"],"en":["smiling"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["smileing","smilling","smilng"],"en":["smileing","smilling","smilng"]}},"explain":{"af":"*smile* eindig op ’n stil *e*. Laat die *e* weg voor *-ing*: *smiling*. Moenie die *l* verdubbel nie, want die *i* is ’n lang klank.","en":"*smile* ends in a silent *e*. Drop the *e* before *-ing*: *smiling*. Do not double the *l*, because the *i* is a long sound."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die meervoud van *baby*?","en":"What is the plural of *baby*?"},"options":[{"af":"babies","en":"babies"},{"af":"babys","en":"babys"},{"af":"babyes","en":"babyes"},{"af":"babis","en":"babis"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*baby* eindig op ’n medeklinker (*b*) + *y*, so die *y* word *i* en jy voeg *-es* by: *babies*.","en":"*baby* ends in a consonant (*b*) + *y*, so the *y* changes to *i* and you add *-es*: *babies*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter letter is stil in *lamb*?","en":"Which letter is silent in *lamb*?"},"options":[{"af":"l","en":"l"},{"af":"a","en":"a"},{"af":"m","en":"m"},{"af":"b","en":"b"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ná ’n *m* aan die einde van ’n woord sê ons nie die *b* nie: *lamb, climb, thumb, comb*.","en":"After an *m* at the end of a word we do not say the *b*: *lamb, climb, thumb, comb*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voeg *-ed* by: *cry* → ___","en":"Add *-ed*: *cry* → ___"},"answers":{"af":["cried"],"en":["cried"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["cryed","cride","cryied"],"en":["cryed","cride","cryied"]}},"explain":{"af":"*cry* eindig op ’n medeklinker + *y*. Die *y* word *i* voordat jy *-ed* byvoeg: *cried*.","en":"*cry* ends in a consonant + *y*. The *y* changes to *i* before you add *-ed*: *cried*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter lys is in **alfabetiese volgorde**?","en":"Which list is in **alphabetical order**?"},"options":[{"af":"cake, cat, cloud, cup","en":"cake, cat, cloud, cup"},{"af":"cat, cake, cloud, cup","en":"cat, cake, cloud, cup"},{"af":"cat, cloud, cup, cake","en":"cat, cloud, cup, cake"},{"af":"cup, cloud, cat, cake","en":"cup, cloud, cat, cake"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Al die woorde begin met *c*. Tweede letter: *a, a, l, u*. *cake* en *cat* begin albei met *ca*, so kyk na die derde letter: *k* kom voor *t*. Dus: *cake, cat, cloud, cup*.","en":"All the words begin with *c*. Second letter: *a, a, l, u*. *cake* and *cat* both begin with *ca*, so look at the third letter: *k* comes before *t*. So: *cake, cat, cloud, cup*."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke woordeboekafkorting by die woordsoort.","en":"Match each dictionary abbreviation to the part of speech."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"n.","en":"n."},"r":{"af":"*noun* (selfstandige naamwoord)","en":"noun"}},{"l":{"af":"v.","en":"v."},"r":{"af":"*verb* (werkwoord)","en":"verb"}},{"l":{"af":"adj.","en":"adj."},"r":{"af":"*adjective* (byvoeglike naamwoord)","en":"adjective"}},{"l":{"af":"adv.","en":"adv."},"r":{"af":"*adverb* (bywoord)","en":"adverb"}},{"l":{"af":"pl.","en":"pl."},"r":{"af":"*plural* (meervoud)","en":"plural"}}],"explain":{"af":"Woordeboeke gebruik afkortings om plek te spaar: *n.* = *noun*, *v.* = *verb*, *adj.* = *adjective*, *adv.* = *adverb* en *pl.* = *plural*.","en":"Dictionaries use abbreviations to save space: *n.* = noun, *v.* = verb, *adj.* = adjective, *adv.* = adverb and *pl.* = plural."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die gidswoorde op ’n bladsy is *bell – bird*. Watter woord sal jy op dié bladsy kry?","en":"The guide words on a page are *bell – bird*. Which word will you find on this page?"},"options":[{"af":"bean","en":"bean"},{"af":"blue","en":"blue"},{"af":"bake","en":"bake"},{"af":"bin","en":"bin"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*bin* (*bi-n*) kom ná *bell* (*be*) en vóór *bird* (*bi-r*, want *n* kom voor *r*). *bean* (*bea*) en *bake* (*ba*) kom vóór *bell*, en *blue* (*bl*) kom ná *bird*.","en":"*bin* (*bi-n*) comes after *bell* (*be*) and before *bird* (*bi-r*, because *n* comes before *r*). *bean* (*bea*) and *bake* (*ba*) come before *bell*, and *blue* (*bl*) comes after *bird*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In ’n woordeboek kom *cup* vóór *cat*.","en":"In a dictionary, *cup* comes before *cat*."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Albei begin met *c*, so kyk na die tweede letter: *a* (cat) kom voor *u* (cup). *cat* kom dus eerste.","en":"False. Both begin with *c*, so look at the second letter: *a* (cat) comes before *u* (cup). So *cat* comes first."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarvoor staan *adj.* in ’n woordeboekinskrywing?","en":"What does *adj.* stand for in a dictionary entry?"},"options":[{"af":"adverb","en":"adverb"},{"af":"article","en":"article"},{"af":"adjective","en":"adjective"},{"af":"address","en":"address"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*adj.* is die afkorting vir *adjective* (byvoeglike naamwoord). Die afkorting vir *adverb* is *adv.*","en":"*adj.* is the abbreviation for *adjective*. The abbreviation for *adverb* is *adv.*"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die twee woorde bo-aan ’n woordeboekbladsy wat die eerste en laaste woord op die bladsy wys, is die ___.","en":"The two words at the top of a dictionary page that show the first and last word on the page are the ___."},"answers":{"af":["guide words","gidswoorde","guidewords"],"en":["guide words","guidewords"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["headwords","key words","page words"],"en":["headwords","key words","page words"]}},"explain":{"af":"Dit is die **gidswoorde** (*guide words*). ’n Trefwoord (*headword*) is die woord in vetdruk aan die begin van een inskrywing.","en":"They are the **guide words**. A headword is the word in bold at the start of one entry."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is **verkeerd** gespel?","en":"Which word is spelt **wrongly**?"},"options":[{"af":"friend","en":"friend"},{"af":"tomorow","en":"tomorow"},{"af":"because","en":"because"},{"af":"until","en":"until"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*tomorrow* het een *m* en twee *r*’e: *to-mor-row*. Die ander woorde is reg gespel.","en":"*tomorrow* has one *m* and two *r*’s: *to-mor-row*. The other words are spelt correctly."}}]},{"id":"eng5-t3-figurative-language","title":{"af":"Beeldspraak en idiome","en":"Figurative language and idioms"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal vergelykings, metafore, personifikasie, alliterasie, onomatopee en rym in Engels kan herken en verduidelik, en die betekenis van bekende Engelse idiome ken.","en":"You will be able to recognise and explain similes, metaphors, personification, alliteration, onomatopoeia and rhyme, and know the meaning of well-known English idioms."},"summary":{"af":"## Letterlik en figuurlik\n\nAs taal **letterlik** is, beteken die woorde presies wat hulle sê: *It is raining hard.* (Dit reën hard.) As taal **figuurlik** is, skep die woorde ’n prentjie in jou kop en beteken hulle nie presies wat hulle sê nie: *My schoolbag weighs a ton!* (My skooltas weeg ’n ton!) Die tas weeg nie regtig 1 000 kg nie; dit is net baie swaar. Skrywers gebruik figuurlike taal of **beeldspraak** om hul skryfwerk lewendig en interessant te maak.\n\n## Stylfigure\n\n| Stylfiguur | Hoe herken jy dit? | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Vergelyking** (*simile*) | vergelyk twee dinge met *like* of *as* | *Nomsa runs like the wind. The kitten’s fur was as soft as silk.* |\n| **Metafoor** (*metaphor*) | sê een ding **is** ’n ander ding, sonder *like* of *as* | *The classroom was a zoo. Ravi is a walking dictionary.* |\n| **Personifikasie** (*personification*) | gee menslike dade of gevoelens aan ’n ding of dier | *The wind whispered in the trees. The old car coughed.* |\n| **Alliterasie** (*alliteration*) | woorde naby mekaar begin met dieselfde klank | *Six silly sheep sat in the sun.* |\n| **Onomatopee** (*onomatopoeia*) | ’n woord wat klink soos die geluid wat dit noem | *buzz, bang, hiss, splash, crunch, tick-tock* |\n| **Rym** (*rhyme*) | woorde wat met dieselfde klank eindig | *cat – hat, night – light, cake – lake* |\n\nHoe ken jy ’n vergelyking en ’n metafoor uitmekaar? Soek die woordjie *like* of *as*. *Her hands were as cold as ice* is ’n vergelyking. *Her hands were ice* is ’n metafoor.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Nie elke sin met *like* is ’n vergelyking nie. In *I like ice cream* (Ek hou van roomys) word niks vergelyk nie, so dit is nie ’n vergelyking nie.\n\n## Idiome\n\n’n **Idioom** is ’n groep woorde met ’n spesiale betekenis wat anders is as die betekenis van die losse woorde. Jy moet idiome leer, want jy kan hulle nie woord vir woord uitwerk nie.\n\n| Idioom | Betekenis | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| *It’s raining cats and dogs.* | Dit reën baie hard. | *Take an umbrella – it’s raining cats and dogs!* |\n| *a piece of cake* | baie maklik | *The spelling test was a piece of cake.* |\n| *Break a leg!* | Sterkte! (voor ’n optrede) | *Break a leg in the school play tonight!* |\n| *under the weather* | ’n bietjie siek | *Aisha stayed home because she felt under the weather.* |\n| *over the moon* | baie bly | *Johan was over the moon when he won the race.* |\n| *let the cat out of the bag* | ’n geheim verklap | *Liam let the cat out of the bag about the surprise party.* |\n| *Hold your horses!* | Wag ’n bietjie! Wees geduldig! | *Hold your horses – the bus is not here yet.* |\n\n> **Onthou:** Moet nooit ’n idioom woord vir woord in ’n ander taal oorsit nie. Die Afrikaanse idioom *dit reën ou vrouens met knopkieries* beteken dieselfde as *it’s raining cats and dogs*, maar die woorde is heeltemal anders.\n\n## Verduidelik die betekenis\n\nAs jy ’n vraag oor beeldspraak beantwoord:\n\n1. Noem die stylfiguur.\n2. Sê wat vergelyk word of watter prentjie geskep word.\n3. Verduidelik die betekenis in jou eie woorde.\n\n*The thunder grumbled angrily over the hills.* Dit is **personifikasie**: donderweer kan nie soos ’n kwaai mens brom nie, maar die sin laat ons ’n diep, rommelende geluid hoor.\n\n*The baby’s cheeks were as red as tomatoes.* Dit is ’n **vergelyking** met *as … as*: die wange word met tamaties vergelyk. Dit beteken die baba se wange was baie rooi.","en":"## Literal and figurative\n\nWhen language is **literal**, the words mean exactly what they say: *It is raining hard.* When language is **figurative**, the words paint a picture in your mind and do not mean exactly what they say: *My schoolbag weighs a ton!* The bag does not really weigh 1 000 kg; it is just very heavy. Writers use figurative language to make their writing lively and interesting.\n\n## Figures of speech\n\n| Figure of speech | How do you recognise it? | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Simile** | compares two things using *like* or *as* | *Nomsa runs like the wind. The kitten’s fur was as soft as silk.* |\n| **Metaphor** | says one thing **is** another thing, without *like* or *as* | *The classroom was a zoo. Ravi is a walking dictionary.* |\n| **Personification** | gives human actions or feelings to a thing or an animal | *The wind whispered in the trees. The old car coughed.* |\n| **Alliteration** | words close together start with the same sound | *Six silly sheep sat in the sun.* |\n| **Onomatopoeia** | a word that sounds like the noise it names | *buzz, bang, hiss, splash, crunch, tick-tock* |\n| **Rhyme** | words that end with the same sound | *cat – hat, night – light, cake – lake* |\n\nHow do you tell a simile and a metaphor apart? Look for the little word *like* or *as*. *Her hands were as cold as ice* is a simile. *Her hands were ice* is a metaphor.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Not every sentence with *like* is a simile. In *I like ice cream* nothing is compared, so it is not a simile.\n\n## Idioms\n\nAn **idiom** is a group of words with a special meaning that is different from the meaning of the separate words. You have to learn idioms, because you cannot work them out word for word.\n\n| Idiom | Meaning | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| *It’s raining cats and dogs.* | It is raining very hard. | *Take an umbrella – it’s raining cats and dogs!* |\n| *a piece of cake* | very easy | *The spelling test was a piece of cake.* |\n| *Break a leg!* | Good luck! (before a performance) | *Break a leg in the school play tonight!* |\n| *under the weather* | feeling a little ill | *Aisha stayed home because she felt under the weather.* |\n| *over the moon* | very happy | *Johan was over the moon when he won the race.* |\n| *let the cat out of the bag* | tell a secret by mistake | *Liam let the cat out of the bag about the surprise party.* |\n| *Hold your horses!* | Wait a moment! Be patient! | *Hold your horses – the bus is not here yet.* |\n\n> **Remember:** Never translate an idiom word for word into another language. The Afrikaans idiom *dit reën ou vrouens met knopkieries* means the same as *it’s raining cats and dogs*, but the words are completely different.\n\n## Explain the meaning\n\nWhen you answer a question on figurative language:\n\n1. Name the figure of speech.\n2. Say what is compared or what picture is created.\n3. Explain the meaning in your own words.\n\n*The thunder grumbled angrily over the hills.* This is **personification**: thunder cannot grumble like an angry person, but the sentence makes us hear a deep, rumbling sound.\n\n*The baby’s cheeks were as red as tomatoes.* This is a **simile** with *as … as*: the cheeks are compared with tomatoes. It means the baby’s cheeks were very red."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Letterlik (*literal*)","en":"Literal"},"def":{"af":"Die woorde beteken presies wat hulle sê: *It is raining hard.*","en":"The words mean exactly what they say: *It is raining hard.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Figuurlik (*figurative*)","en":"Figurative"},"def":{"af":"Die woorde skep ’n prentjie en beteken nie presies wat hulle sê nie: *My bag weighs a ton.*","en":"The words create a picture and do not mean exactly what they say: *My bag weighs a ton.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Vergelyking (*simile*)","en":"Simile"},"def":{"af":"’n Stylfiguur wat twee dinge met *like* of *as* vergelyk: *as soft as silk*.","en":"A figure of speech that compares two things using *like* or *as*: *as soft as silk*."}},{"term":{"af":"Metafoor (*metaphor*)","en":"Metaphor"},"def":{"af":"’n Stylfiguur wat sê een ding **is** ’n ander ding, sonder *like* of *as*: *The classroom was a zoo.*","en":"A figure of speech that says one thing **is** another thing, without *like* or *as*: *The classroom was a zoo.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Personifikasie (*personification*)","en":"Personification"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n ding of dier menslike dade of gevoelens kry: *The wind whispered.*","en":"When a thing or an animal is given human actions or feelings: *The wind whispered.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Alliterasie (*alliteration*)","en":"Alliteration"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer woorde naby mekaar met dieselfde klank begin: *six silly sheep*.","en":"When words close together begin with the same sound: *six silly sheep*."}},{"term":{"af":"Onomatopee (*onomatopoeia*)","en":"Onomatopoeia"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord wat klink soos die geluid wat dit beskryf: *buzz, bang, splash*.","en":"A word that sounds like the noise it describes: *buzz, bang, splash*."}},{"term":{"af":"Rym (*rhyme*)","en":"Rhyme"},"def":{"af":"Woorde wat met dieselfde klank eindig, soos *night* en *light*.","en":"Words that end with the same sound, like *night* and *light*."}},{"term":{"af":"Idioom (*idiom*)","en":"Idiom"},"def":{"af":"’n Vaste groep woorde met ’n spesiale betekenis, soos *a piece of cake* (baie maklik).","en":"A fixed group of words with a special meaning, like *a piece of cake* (very easy)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Noem en verduidelik die stylfiguur","en":"Name and explain the figure of speech"},"problem":{"af":"Noem die stylfiguur en verduidelik dit: *The thunder grumbled angrily over the hills.*","en":"Name the figure of speech and explain it: *The thunder grumbled angrily over the hills.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Kyk wat die donderweer doen: dit *grumbled angrily* (brom kwaai). Net mense kan kwaai brom.","en":"Look at what the thunder does: it *grumbled angrily*. Only people can grumble angrily."},{"af":"’n Ding wat ’n menslike daad of gevoel kry, is **personifikasie**.","en":"A thing that is given a human action or feeling is **personification**."},{"af":"Verduidelik die prentjie: die donderweer klink soos ’n kwaai mens wat aanhoudend diep en laag brom.","en":"Explain the picture: the thunder sounds like an angry person who keeps grumbling in a deep, low voice."}],"answer":{"af":"Personifikasie: die donderweer word beskryf asof dit ’n kwaai mens is wat brom; dit wys hoe diep en dreigend die geluid is.","en":"Personification: the thunder is described as if it were an angry person grumbling; it shows how deep and threatening the sound is."}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyking of metafoor?","en":"Simile or metaphor?"},"problem":{"af":"Is dit ’n vergelyking of ’n metafoor? (a) *Her hands were as cold as ice.* (b) *Her hands were ice.*","en":"Is it a simile or a metaphor? (a) *Her hands were as cold as ice.* (b) *Her hands were ice.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Soek *like* of *as*. In (a) staan *as cold as ice*, so die hande word **met** ys vergelyk.","en":"Look for *like* or *as*. Sentence (a) has *as cold as ice*, so the hands are compared **with** ice."},{"af":"In (b) is daar geen *like* of *as* nie. Die sin sê die hande **is** ys.","en":"Sentence (b) has no *like* or *as*. The sentence says the hands **are** ice."},{"af":"Albei sinne beteken dat haar hande baie koud was.","en":"Both sentences mean that her hands were very cold."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) is ’n vergelyking (*simile*); (b) is ’n metafoor (*metaphor*).","en":"(a) is a simile; (b) is a metaphor."}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik ’n idioom","en":"Explain an idiom"},"problem":{"af":"Wat beteken die idioom in hierdie sin? *Pieter was over the moon when his new puppy came home.*","en":"What does the idiom in this sentence mean? *Pieter was over the moon when his new puppy came home.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Vind die idioom: *over the moon*. Pieter het nie regtig oor die maan gespring nie, so dit is figuurlik.","en":"Find the idiom: *over the moon*. Pieter did not really jump over the moon, so it is figurative."},{"af":"Gebruik die konteks: ’n nuwe hondjie kom huis toe. Hoe sal ’n kind voel? Baie bly.","en":"Use the context: a new puppy comes home. How would a child feel? Very happy."},{"af":"Skryf die betekenis in jou eie woorde.","en":"Write the meaning in your own words."}],"answer":{"af":"*Over the moon* beteken *very happy* (baie bly): Pieter was baie bly oor sy nuwe hondjie.","en":"*Over the moon* means *very happy*: Pieter was very happy about his new puppy."}},{"title":{"af":"Letterlik of figuurlik?","en":"Literal or figurative?"},"problem":{"af":"Is hierdie sin letterlik of figuurlik? Verduidelik. *Zanele has a heart of gold.*","en":"Is this sentence literal or figurative? Explain. *Zanele has a heart of gold.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Vra: Kan dit letterlik waar wees? Nee, niemand se hart is van goud gemaak nie.","en":"Ask: Can it be literally true? No, nobody’s heart is made of gold."},{"af":"Die sin is dus figuurlik. Dit is ’n metafoor, want daar is geen *like* of *as* nie.","en":"So the sentence is figurative. It is a metaphor, because there is no *like* or *as*."},{"af":"Goud is kosbaar en goed. ’n *Heart of gold* beteken ’n baie goeie, vriendelike hart.","en":"Gold is precious and good. A *heart of gold* means a very good, kind heart."}],"answer":{"af":"Figuurlik: Zanele is baie goedhartig en vriendelik.","en":"Figurative: Zanele is very kind and good-hearted."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin bevat ’n **vergelyking** (*simile*)?","en":"Which sentence contains a **simile**?"},"options":[{"af":"Thabo is a hungry lion.","en":"Thabo is a hungry lion."},{"af":"Thabo likes lions.","en":"Thabo likes lions."},{"af":"Thabo eats like a hungry lion.","en":"Thabo eats like a hungry lion."},{"af":"Thabo saw a hungry lion.","en":"Thabo saw a hungry lion."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Thabo eats like a hungry lion* vergelyk Thabo met ’n leeu deur *like* te gebruik. *Thabo is a hungry lion* is ’n metafoor, en in *Thabo likes lions* beteken *like* ‘hou van’.","en":"*Thabo eats like a hungry lion* compares Thabo with a lion using *like*. *Thabo is a hungry lion* is a metaphor, and in *Thabo likes lions* the word *like* means ‘enjoy’."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*The leaves danced in the wind.* Watter stylfiguur is dit?","en":"*The leaves danced in the wind.* Which figure of speech is this?"},"options":[{"af":"vergelyking (*simile*)","en":"simile"},{"af":"personifikasie (*personification*)","en":"personification"},{"af":"alliterasie (*alliteration*)","en":"alliteration"},{"af":"onomatopee (*onomatopoeia*)","en":"onomatopoeia"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Blare kan nie regtig dans nie; dit is iets wat mense doen. ’n Ding wat ’n menslike daad kry, is personifikasie.","en":"Leaves cannot really dance; that is something people do. A thing that is given a human action is personification."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi die vergelyking: *as busy as a* ___","en":"Complete the simile: *as busy as a* ___"},"answers":{"af":["bee"],"en":["bee"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["lion","fish","mouse"],"en":["lion","fish","mouse"]}},"explain":{"af":"Bye werk die hele dag, daarom sê ons *as busy as a bee* vir iemand wat baie besig is.","en":"Bees work all day, so we say *as busy as a bee* about someone who is very busy."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is ’n voorbeeld van **onomatopee**?","en":"Which word is an example of **onomatopoeia**?"},"options":[{"af":"splash","en":"splash"},{"af":"quiet","en":"quiet"},{"af":"water","en":"water"},{"af":"slowly","en":"slowly"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Splash* klink soos die geluid van iets wat in water val. Die ander woorde boots nie ’n geluid na nie.","en":"*Splash* sounds like the noise of something falling into water. The other words do not copy a sound."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*She is as quick as a cheetah* is ’n metafoor.","en":"*She is as quick as a cheetah* is a metaphor."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die sin gebruik *as … as* om haar met ’n jagluiperd te vergelyk, so dit is ’n vergelyking (*simile*).","en":"False. The sentence uses *as … as* to compare her with a cheetah, so it is a simile."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken *under the weather*?","en":"What does *under the weather* mean?"},"options":[{"af":"buite in die reën","en":"outside in the rain"},{"af":"baie bly","en":"very happy"},{"af":"baie koud","en":"very cold"},{"af":"’n bietjie siek","en":"feeling a little ill"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Under the weather* is ’n idioom wat beteken dat jy ’n bietjie siek voel. Dit het niks met die weer self te doen nie.","en":"*Under the weather* is an idiom that means you feel a little ill. It has nothing to do with the weather itself."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke stylfiguur by die regte voorbeeld.","en":"Match each figure of speech to the correct example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"vergelyking (*simile*)","en":"simile"},"r":{"af":"as brave as a lion","en":"as brave as a lion"}},{"l":{"af":"metafoor (*metaphor*)","en":"metaphor"},"r":{"af":"The sun is a golden coin.","en":"The sun is a golden coin."}},{"l":{"af":"personifikasie (*personification*)","en":"personification"},"r":{"af":"The stars winked at us.","en":"The stars winked at us."}},{"l":{"af":"alliterasie (*alliteration*)","en":"alliteration"},"r":{"af":"Big brown bears bounce balls.","en":"Big brown bears bounce balls."}},{"l":{"af":"onomatopee (*onomatopoeia*)","en":"onomatopoeia"},"r":{"af":"Crash! Bang! Boom!","en":"Crash! Bang! Boom!"}}],"explain":{"af":"*as brave as a lion* gebruik *as* (vergelyking); die son **is** ’n muntstuk (metafoor); sterre kan nie knipoog nie (personifikasie); *b*-klanke herhaal (alliterasie); *Crash! Bang! Boom!* klink soos die geluide (onomatopee).","en":"*as brave as a lion* uses *as* (simile); the sun **is** a coin (metaphor); stars cannot wink (personification); the *b* sound repeats (alliteration); *Crash! Bang! Boom!* sound like the noises (onomatopoeia)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*Lerato’s little lamb leapt over the log.* Watter stylfiguur is dit?","en":"*Lerato’s little lamb leapt over the log.* Which figure of speech is this?"},"options":[{"af":"alliterasie (*alliteration*)","en":"alliteration"},{"af":"rym (*rhyme*)","en":"rhyme"},{"af":"vergelyking (*simile*)","en":"simile"},{"af":"personifikasie (*personification*)","en":"personification"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Baie woorde naby mekaar begin met dieselfde *l*-klank: *Lerato’s, little, lamb, leapt, log*. Dit is alliterasie. Rym gaan oor die **einde** van woorde, nie die begin nie.","en":"Many words close together begin with the same *l* sound: *Lerato’s, little, lamb, leapt, log*. That is alliteration. Rhyme is about the **end** of words, not the beginning."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Watter woord in die sin is onomatopee? *The fat frog went plop into the pond.* → ___","en":"Which word in the sentence is onomatopoeia? *The fat frog went plop into the pond.* → ___"},"answers":{"af":["plop"],"en":["plop"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["fat","frog","pond"],"en":["fat","frog","pond"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Plop* klink soos die geluid van die padda wat in die water val. (*fat frog* is alliterasie, maar nie onomatopee nie.)","en":"*Plop* sounds like the noise of the frog falling into the water. (*fat frog* is alliteration, but not onomatopoeia.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jou maat gaan in die skoolkonsert sing. Wat sê jy vir haar net voor sy op die verhoog gaan?","en":"Your friend is going to sing in the school concert. What do you say to her just before she goes on stage?"},"options":[{"af":"It’s raining cats and dogs!","en":"It’s raining cats and dogs!"},{"af":"You look under the weather!","en":"You look under the weather!"},{"af":"Break a leg!","en":"Break a leg!"},{"af":"I’m over the moon!","en":"I’m over the moon!"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Break a leg!* beteken *sterkte* en word voor ’n optrede gesê. Jy wens jou maat nie regtig ’n gebreekte been toe nie!","en":"*Break a leg!* means *good luck* and is said before a performance. You do not really wish your friend a broken leg!"}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*The test was a piece of cake* beteken dat die toets baie maklik was.","en":"*The test was a piece of cake* means that the test was very easy."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. *A piece of cake* is ’n idioom vir iets wat baie maklik is. Daar was geen koek by die toets nie!","en":"True. *A piece of cake* is an idiom for something that is very easy. There was no cake at the test!"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*Ravi is a walking dictionary.* Wat beteken dit?","en":"*Ravi is a walking dictionary.* What does this mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Ravi dra ’n woordeboek as hy loop.","en":"Ravi carries a dictionary when he walks."},{"af":"Ravi loop baie stadig.","en":"Ravi walks very slowly."},{"af":"Ravi skryf woordeboeke.","en":"Ravi writes dictionaries."},{"af":"Ravi ken die betekenis van baie woorde.","en":"Ravi knows the meaning of many words."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Dit is ’n metafoor: Ravi word ’n woordeboek genoem omdat hy, soos ’n woordeboek, die betekenis van baie woorde ken. Dit is figuurlik, nie letterlik nie.","en":"It is a metaphor: Ravi is called a dictionary because, like a dictionary, he knows the meaning of many words. It is figurative, not literal."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Vergelyking (*simile*) vergelyk twee dinge met die woord *like* of ___.","en":"A simile compares two things using the word *like* or ___."},"answers":{"af":["as"],"en":["as"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["is","and","so"],"en":["is","and","so"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Vergelyking gebruik *like* of *as*: *runs like the wind, as soft as silk*. ’n Metafoor gebruik nie hierdie woorde nie.","en":"A simile uses *like* or *as*: *runs like the wind, as soft as silk*. A metaphor does not use these words."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is **letterlik** (nie figuurlik nie)?","en":"Which sentence is **literal** (not figurative)?"},"options":[{"af":"It’s raining cats and dogs.","en":"It’s raining cats and dogs."},{"af":"It is raining very hard today.","en":"It is raining very hard today."},{"af":"The rain drummed its fingers on the roof.","en":"The rain drummed its fingers on the roof."},{"af":"The rain was a grey curtain.","en":"The rain was a grey curtain."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*It is raining very hard today* beteken presies wat dit sê. Die ander is figuurlik: ’n idioom, personifikasie (reën het nie vingers nie) en ’n metafoor.","en":"*It is raining very hard today* means exactly what it says. The others are figurative: an idiom, personification (rain has no fingers) and a metaphor."}}]},{"id":"eng5-t3-poetry","title":{"af":"Gedigte","en":"Poetry"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die dele van ’n Engelse gedig kan noem, die rymskema kan uitwerk, ritme, herhaling en stemming kan raaksien en vrae oor ’n gedig in volsinne kan beantwoord.","en":"You will be able to name the parts of a poem, work out its rhyme scheme, notice rhythm, repetition and mood, and answer questions on a poem in full sentences."},"summary":{"af":"## Lees die gedig\n\n**The Highveld Storm**\n\n*The afternoon is hot and still,*  \n*Grey clouds are piling on the hill.*  \n*The chickens scuttle to their shed,*  \n*The sky grows dark above my head.*\n\n*Then crash! The thunder shakes the ground,*  \n*The rain comes pouring all around.*  \n*It drums and drums on roofs of tin,*  \n*And Gran calls, “Bring the washing in!”*\n\n*But soon the rumbling fades away,*  \n*The sun peeps out to end the day.*  \n*The puddles shine, the air smells sweet,*  \n*And frogs sing loudly in the street.*\n\nWoordjies: *scuttle* = vinnig wegskarrel, *shed* = skuur, *washing* = wasgoed, *puddles* = plasse water.\n\n## Die dele van ’n gedig\n\n- ’n **Gedig** (*poem*) is skryfwerk in **reëls**, dikwels met rym en ritme, wat met min woorde ’n prentjie of gevoel deel.\n- Die **digter** (*poet*) is die persoon wat die gedig geskryf het.\n- Die **titel** (*title*) is die naam van die gedig: *The Highveld Storm*.\n- ’n **Reël** (*line*) is een ry woorde. Hierdie gedig het 12 reëls.\n- ’n **Strofe** (*stanza*) is ’n groep reëls, soos ’n paragraaf in ’n storie. Hierdie gedig het 3 strofes van 4 reëls elk.\n- Die **spreker** (*speaker*) is die stem wat in die gedig praat. Hier is dit iemand wat by Ouma tuis is (*my head*). Die spreker is nie altyd die digter nie!\n\n## Rym en rymskema\n\nWoorde **rym** as hulle met dieselfde klank eindig: *still – hill, shed – head*. Die **rymskema** (*rhyme scheme*) wys watter reëls rym. Gee die eerste eindklank die letter **a**, die volgende nuwe klank **b**, ensovoorts.\n\n| Reël | Laaste woord | Letter |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | *still* | a |\n| 2 | *hill* | a |\n| 3 | *shed* | b |\n| 4 | *head* | b |\n\nDie rymskema van die eerste strofe is dus **aabb**. In die strofe hieronder rym reëls 1 en 3, en reëls 2 en 4, so die rymskema is **abab**:\n\n*My kite is red and yellow too,*  \n*It dances when the wind is strong,*  \n*It climbs into the cloudless blue*  \n*And tugs my string the whole day long.*\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie **rym** (*rhyme*) en **ritme** (*rhythm*) verwar nie. Rym gaan oor die klank aan die **einde** van woorde; ritme is die **maat** of slag van die reëls.\n\n## Ritme, herhaling en klank\n\n- **Ritme** is die maat wat jy kan klap: *the AF-ter-NOON is HOT and STILL* het vier sterk slae. Elke reël van die stormgedig het vier slae, soos reëndruppels wat eweredig val.\n- **Herhaling** (*repetition*) beteken jy gebruik ’n woord of reël meer as een keer. *It drums and drums* laat ons hoor hoe die reën oor en oor op die dak slaan.\n- Klanknabootsende woorde soos *crash* (onomatopee) laat die storm lewe.\n\n## Stemming en voorlees\n\nDie **stemming** (*mood*) is die gevoel wat die gedig vir jou gee. In strofe 1 is die stemming stil en gespanne: almal wag vir die storm. In strofe 2 is dit lawaaierig en opwindend. In strofe 3 is dit kalm en vreedsaam.\n\nAs jy ’n gedig hardop lees:\n\n1. Rus by kommas en punte, nie net aan die einde van elke reël nie.\n2. Laat jou stem die stemming wys: sag en stadig vir kalm dele, harder vir *crash!*\n3. Lees duidelik en nie te vinnig nie.\n\n> **Onthou:** As jy ’n vraag oor ’n gedig beantwoord, lees die gedig twee keer, antwoord in volsinne en haal woorde uit die gedig aan om jou antwoord te bewys, bv. *The word “crash” shows that the thunder is loud.*","en":"## Read the poem\n\n**The Highveld Storm**\n\n*The afternoon is hot and still,*  \n*Grey clouds are piling on the hill.*  \n*The chickens scuttle to their shed,*  \n*The sky grows dark above my head.*\n\n*Then crash! The thunder shakes the ground,*  \n*The rain comes pouring all around.*  \n*It drums and drums on roofs of tin,*  \n*And Gran calls, “Bring the washing in!”*\n\n*But soon the rumbling fades away,*  \n*The sun peeps out to end the day.*  \n*The puddles shine, the air smells sweet,*  \n*And frogs sing loudly in the street.*\n\n## The parts of a poem\n\n- A **poem** is a piece of writing in **lines**, often with rhyme and rhythm, that shares a picture or a feeling in few words.\n- The **poet** is the person who wrote the poem.\n- The **title** is the name of the poem: *The Highveld Storm*.\n- A **line** is one row of words. This poem has 12 lines.\n- A **stanza** is a group of lines, like a paragraph in a story. This poem has 3 stanzas of 4 lines each.\n- The **speaker** is the voice that talks in the poem. Here it is someone at home with Gran (*my head*). The speaker is not always the poet!\n\n## Rhyme and rhyme scheme\n\nWords **rhyme** when they end with the same sound: *still – hill, shed – head*. The **rhyme scheme** shows which lines rhyme. Give the first ending sound the letter **a**, the next new sound **b**, and so on.\n\n| Line | Last word | Letter |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | *still* | a |\n| 2 | *hill* | a |\n| 3 | *shed* | b |\n| 4 | *head* | b |\n\nSo the rhyme scheme of the first stanza is **aabb**. In the stanza below, lines 1 and 3 rhyme, and lines 2 and 4 rhyme, so the rhyme scheme is **abab**:\n\n*My kite is red and yellow too,*  \n*It dances when the wind is strong,*  \n*It climbs into the cloudless blue*  \n*And tugs my string the whole day long.*\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not mix up **rhyme** and **rhythm**. Rhyme is about the sound at the **end** of words; rhythm is the **beat** of the lines.\n\n## Rhythm, repetition and sound\n\n- **Rhythm** is the beat you can clap: *the AF-ter-NOON is HOT and STILL* has four strong beats. Every line of the storm poem has four beats, like raindrops falling evenly.\n- **Repetition** means using a word or line more than once. *It drums and drums* lets us hear the rain beating on the roof again and again.\n- Sound words such as *crash* (onomatopoeia) bring the storm to life.\n\n## Mood and reading aloud\n\nThe **mood** is the feeling the poem gives you. In stanza 1 the mood is still and tense: everyone waits for the storm. In stanza 2 it is noisy and exciting. In stanza 3 it is calm and peaceful.\n\nWhen you read a poem aloud:\n\n1. Pause at commas and full stops, not only at the end of every line.\n2. Let your voice show the mood: soft and slow for calm parts, louder for *crash!*\n3. Read clearly and not too fast.\n\n> **Remember:** When you answer a question on a poem, read the poem twice, answer in full sentences and quote words from the poem to prove your answer, e.g. *The word “crash” shows that the thunder is loud.*"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Digter (*poet*)","en":"Poet"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon wat ’n gedig skryf.","en":"The person who writes a poem."}},{"term":{"af":"Titel (*title*)","en":"Title"},"def":{"af":"Die naam van die gedig, wat bo-aan staan.","en":"The name of the poem, written at the top."}},{"term":{"af":"Reël (*line*)","en":"Line"},"def":{"af":"Een ry woorde in ’n gedig.","en":"One row of words in a poem."}},{"term":{"af":"Strofe (*stanza*)","en":"Stanza"},"def":{"af":"’n Groep reëls in ’n gedig, soos ’n paragraaf in ’n storie.","en":"A group of lines in a poem, like a paragraph in a story."}},{"term":{"af":"Rymskema (*rhyme scheme*)","en":"Rhyme scheme"},"def":{"af":"Die patroon van rym in ’n strofe, met letters gewys, soos *aabb* of *abab*.","en":"The pattern of rhyme in a stanza, shown with letters, such as *aabb* or *abab*."}},{"term":{"af":"Ritme (*rhythm*)","en":"Rhythm"},"def":{"af":"Die maat of slag van ’n gedig wat jy kan klap.","en":"The beat of a poem that you can clap."}},{"term":{"af":"Herhaling (*repetition*)","en":"Repetition"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n woord of reël meer as een keer gebruik word om iets te beklemtoon.","en":"When a word or line is used more than once to make something stand out."}},{"term":{"af":"Stemming (*mood*)","en":"Mood"},"def":{"af":"Die gevoel wat ’n gedig vir die leser gee, soos kalm, opgewonde of hartseer.","en":"The feeling a poem gives the reader, such as calm, excited or sad."}},{"term":{"af":"Spreker (*speaker*)","en":"Speaker"},"def":{"af":"Die stem wat in die gedig praat; dit is nie altyd die digter self nie.","en":"The voice that talks in the poem; it is not always the poet."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Rymskema van strofe 2","en":"Rhyme scheme of stanza 2"},"problem":{"af":"Wat is die rymskema van strofe 2 van *The Highveld Storm*?","en":"What is the rhyme scheme of stanza 2 of *The Highveld Storm*?"},"steps":[{"af":"Skryf die laaste woord van elke reël neer: *ground, around, tin, in*.","en":"Write down the last word of each line: *ground, around, tin, in*."},{"af":"*ground* is die eerste klank: **a**. *around* eindig met dieselfde klank: **a**.","en":"*ground* is the first sound: **a**. *around* ends with the same sound: **a**."},{"af":"*tin* is ’n nuwe klank: **b**. *in* rym met *tin*: **b**.","en":"*tin* is a new sound: **b**. *in* rhymes with *tin*: **b**."}],"answer":{"af":"**aabb**","en":"**aabb**"}},{"title":{"af":"Rymskema van die vlieërstrofe","en":"Rhyme scheme of the kite stanza"},"problem":{"af":"Wat is die rymskema van die strofe oor die vlieër (*kite*)?","en":"What is the rhyme scheme of the stanza about the kite?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die laaste woorde is *too, strong, blue, long*.","en":"The last words are *too, strong, blue, long*."},{"af":"*too* = **a**; *strong* is ’n nuwe klank = **b**.","en":"*too* = **a**; *strong* is a new sound = **b**."},{"af":"*blue* rym met *too* = **a**; *long* rym met *strong* = **b**.","en":"*blue* rhymes with *too* = **a**; *long* rhymes with *strong* = **b**."}],"answer":{"af":"**abab**","en":"**abab**"}},{"title":{"af":"Hoe verander die stemming?","en":"How does the mood change?"},"problem":{"af":"Hoe verander die stemming van strofe 1 tot strofe 3? Haal woorde aan om jou antwoord te bewys.","en":"How does the mood change from stanza 1 to stanza 3? Quote words to prove your answer."},"steps":[{"af":"Strofe 1: *hot and still, the sky grows dark* – die stemming is stil en gespanne, want almal wag vir die storm.","en":"Stanza 1: *hot and still, the sky grows dark* – the mood is still and tense, because everyone is waiting for the storm."},{"af":"Strofe 3: *the sun peeps out, the air smells sweet, frogs sing* – die stemming is kalm, vars en vrolik.","en":"Stanza 3: *the sun peeps out, the air smells sweet, frogs sing* – the mood is calm, fresh and cheerful."},{"af":"Skryf jou antwoord in ’n volsin en gebruik die aanhalings as bewys.","en":"Write your answer in a full sentence and use the quotes as proof."}],"answer":{"af":"Die stemming verander van gespanne (*the sky grows dark*) na kalm en vreedsaam (*the sun peeps out, the air smells sweet*).","en":"The mood changes from tense (*the sky grows dark*) to calm and peaceful (*the sun peeps out, the air smells sweet*)."}},{"title":{"af":"Spreker en herhaling","en":"Speaker and repetition"},"problem":{"af":"Wie is die spreker in *The Highveld Storm*, en waarom gebruik die digter die herhaling *drums and drums*?","en":"Who is the speaker in *The Highveld Storm*, and why does the poet use the repetition *drums and drums*?"},"steps":[{"af":"Soek woorde soos *my* en *I*: *above my head*. Die spreker sê ook *Gran calls*, so die spreker is iemand wat by Ouma tuis is.","en":"Look for words such as *my* and *I*: *above my head*. The speaker also says *Gran calls*, so the speaker is someone at home with Gran."},{"af":"*drums* word twee keer gebruik. Die herhaling laat ons die reën hoor wat oor en oor op die sinkdak slaan, soos ’n trom.","en":"*drums* is used twice. The repetition lets us hear the rain beating on the tin roof over and over, like a drum."}],"answer":{"af":"Die spreker is iemand (waarskynlik ’n kind) wat by Ouma tuis is. Die herhaling wys dat die reën aanhoudend en hard op die dak slaan.","en":"The speaker is someone (probably a child) at home with Gran. The repetition shows that the rain keeps beating loudly on the roof."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel strofes het *The Highveld Storm*?","en":"How many stanzas does *The Highveld Storm* have?"},"options":[{"af":"12","en":"12"},{"af":"4","en":"4"},{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"2","en":"2"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die gedig het 3 strofes (groepe reëls) van 4 reëls elk. 12 is die getal **reëls**, nie strofes nie.","en":"The poem has 3 stanzas (groups of lines) of 4 lines each. 12 is the number of **lines**, not stanzas."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die spreker in ’n gedig is altyd die digter self.","en":"The speaker in a poem is always the poet."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die spreker is die stem wat in die gedig praat. ’n Digter kan skryf asof ’n kind, ’n dier of selfs ’n ding praat.","en":"False. The speaker is the voice that talks in the poem. A poet can write as if a child, an animal or even a thing is talking."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die rymskema van die **eerste** strofe van *The Highveld Storm*?","en":"What is the rhyme scheme of the **first** stanza of *The Highveld Storm*?"},"options":[{"af":"abab","en":"abab"},{"af":"aabb","en":"aabb"},{"af":"abba","en":"abba"},{"af":"abcb","en":"abcb"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*still* en *hill* rym (a, a), en *shed* en *head* rym (b, b). Dus **aabb**.","en":"*still* and *hill* rhyme (a, a), and *shed* and *head* rhyme (b, b). So **aabb**."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In strofe 1 rym die woord *still* met ___.","en":"In stanza 1 the word *still* rhymes with ___."},"answers":{"af":["hill"],"en":["hill"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["shed","head","hot"],"en":["shed","head","hot"]}},"explain":{"af":"*still* en *hill* eindig albei op die klank *-ill*. *shed* en *head* rym met mekaar, nie met *still* nie.","en":"*still* and *hill* both end in the sound *-ill*. *shed* and *head* rhyme with each other, not with *still*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat noem ons ’n groep reëls in ’n gedig?","en":"What do we call a group of lines in a poem?"},"options":[{"af":"stanza","en":"stanza"},{"af":"paragraph","en":"paragraph"},{"af":"title","en":"title"},{"af":"chapter","en":"chapter"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Groep reëls in ’n gedig is ’n *stanza* (strofe). ’n *Paragraph* is ’n groep sinne in ’n storie, en ’n *chapter* is ’n deel van ’n boek.","en":"A group of lines in a poem is a *stanza*. A *paragraph* is a group of sentences in a story, and a *chapter* is a part of a book."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord uit strofe 2 is ’n voorbeeld van onomatopee?","en":"Which word from stanza 2 is an example of onomatopoeia?"},"options":[{"af":"pouring","en":"pouring"},{"af":"ground","en":"ground"},{"af":"washing","en":"washing"},{"af":"crash","en":"crash"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Crash* klink soos die geluid van die donderweer self. Die ander woorde boots nie ’n geluid na nie.","en":"*Crash* sounds like the noise of the thunder itself. The other words do not copy a sound."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke woord by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each word to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"digter (*poet*)","en":"poet"},"r":{"af":"die persoon wat die gedig geskryf het","en":"the person who wrote the poem"}},{"l":{"af":"titel (*title*)","en":"title"},"r":{"af":"die naam van die gedig","en":"the name of the poem"}},{"l":{"af":"strofe (*stanza*)","en":"stanza"},"r":{"af":"’n groep reëls","en":"a group of lines"}},{"l":{"af":"spreker (*speaker*)","en":"speaker"},"r":{"af":"die stem wat in die gedig praat","en":"the voice that talks in the poem"}},{"l":{"af":"stemming (*mood*)","en":"mood"},"r":{"af":"die gevoel wat die gedig gee","en":"the feeling the poem gives"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die digter skryf die gedig, die titel is sy naam, ’n strofe is ’n groep reëls, die spreker is die stem in die gedig en die stemming is die gevoel wat dit gee.","en":"The poet writes the poem, the title is its name, a stanza is a group of lines, the speaker is the voice in the poem and the mood is the feeling it gives."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe is die stemming in die **laaste** strofe van *The Highveld Storm*?","en":"What is the mood in the **last** stanza of *The Highveld Storm*?"},"options":[{"af":"kalm en vreedsaam","en":"calm and peaceful"},{"af":"lawaaierig en skrikwekkend","en":"noisy and frightening"},{"af":"hartseer en eensaam","en":"sad and lonely"},{"af":"kwaad en wild","en":"angry and wild"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Woorde soos *the sun peeps out*, *the air smells sweet* en *frogs sing* skep ’n kalm, vreedsame stemming. Die lawaai was in strofe 2.","en":"Words such as *the sun peeps out*, *the air smells sweet* and *frogs sing* create a calm, peaceful mood. The noise was in stanza 2."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die maat of slag van ’n gedig wat jy kan klap, is sy ___.","en":"The beat of a poem that you can clap is its ___."},"answers":{"af":["rhythm","ritme"],"en":["rhythm"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["rhyme","title","stanza"],"en":["rhyme","title","stanza"]}},"explain":{"af":"Dit is die **ritme** (*rhythm*). Moenie dit met **rym** (*rhyme*) verwar nie: rym gaan oor die klank aan die einde van woorde.","en":"It is the **rhythm**. Do not confuse it with **rhyme**: rhyme is about the sound at the end of words."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom skryf die digter *It drums and drums on roofs of tin*?","en":"Why does the poet write *It drums and drums on roofs of tin*?"},"options":[{"af":"Om te wys dat Ouma op ’n trom speel","en":"To show that Gran is playing a drum"},{"af":"Om te wys dat die dakke van sink is","en":"To show that the roofs are made of tin"},{"af":"Om te wys dat die reën aanhou slaan","en":"To show that the rain keeps beating"},{"af":"Om te wys dat die storm verbygaan","en":"To show that the storm is passing"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die herhaling van *drums* laat ons hoor hoe die reën oor en oor op die dak slaan. Die dakke is wel van sink, maar dit verklaar nie waarom die woord herhaal word nie.","en":"Repeating *drums* lets us hear the rain beating on the roof over and over. The roofs are made of tin, but that does not explain why the word is repeated."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In ’n **aabb**-rymskema rym reëls 1 en 2 met mekaar.","en":"In an **aabb** rhyme scheme, lines 1 and 2 rhyme with each other."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Reëls met dieselfde letter rym. Reëls 1 en 2 het albei **a**, en reëls 3 en 4 het albei **b**.","en":"True. Lines with the same letter rhyme. Lines 1 and 2 both have **a**, and lines 3 and 4 both have **b**."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In die vlieërstrofe: watter woord rym met *strong*?","en":"In the kite stanza: which word rhymes with *strong*?"},"options":[{"af":"string","en":"string"},{"af":"long","en":"long"},{"af":"kite","en":"kite"},{"af":"blue","en":"blue"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*strong* en *long* eindig albei op die klank *-ong*. *string* lyk amper dieselfde, maar eindig op *-ing*, so dit rym nie.","en":"*strong* and *long* both end in the sound *-ong*. *string* looks almost the same, but it ends in *-ing*, so it does not rhyme."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die rymskema van die vlieërstrofe (*My kite is red and yellow too …*) is ___.","en":"The rhyme scheme of the kite stanza (*My kite is red and yellow too …*) is ___."},"answers":{"af":["abab"],"en":["abab"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["aabb","abba","abcb"],"en":["aabb","abba","abcb"]}},"explain":{"af":"*too* en *blue* (reëls 1 en 3) rym, en *strong* en *long* (reëls 2 en 4) rym. Dus **abab**.","en":"*too* and *blue* (lines 1 and 3) rhyme, and *strong* and *long* (lines 2 and 4) rhyme. So **abab**."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wie is die spreker in *The Highveld Storm*?","en":"Who is the speaker in *The Highveld Storm*?"},"options":[{"af":"Ouma","en":"Gran"},{"af":"die donderweer","en":"the thunder"},{"af":"die hoenders","en":"the chickens"},{"af":"iemand wat by Ouma tuis is","en":"someone at home with Gran"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die spreker sê *above my head* en vertel dat *Gran calls*. Die spreker praat dus oor Ouma; dit is iemand wat saam met haar tuis is, nie Ouma self nie.","en":"The speaker says *above my head* and tells us that *Gran calls*. So the speaker talks about Gran; it is someone at home with her, not Gran herself."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Tekste lees en skryf","en":"Reading and writing texts"},"topics":[{"id":"eng5-t4-stories","title":{"af":"Verhale, volksverhale en fabels","en":"Stories, folk tales and fables"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die karakters, agtergrond, storielyn en verteller van ’n Engelse storie kan uitwys, gebeure in die regte volgorde kan sit en die sedeles van ’n fabel kan verduidelik.","en":"You will be able to identify the characters, setting, plot and narrator of a story, put events in the correct order and explain the moral of a fable."},"summary":{"af":"## Lees die storie\n\n**Guineafowl Learns to Share the Work**\n\nOnce upon a time, in the dry Karoo, there lived a guineafowl who loved to boast. “My feathers have the prettiest spots in the veld,” she told everyone, “and nobody can run as fast as I can!”\n\nOne hot summer, the old waterhole began to dry up. The animals met under the thorn tree to make a plan. “Let us dig the waterhole deeper,” said Old Meerkat. “If we all help, we will finish before sunset.”\n\nEveryone started to dig – everyone except Guineafowl. “My pretty feet are not made for mud,” she said, and she sat in the shade to admire her spots.\n\nBy sunset the hole was deep and full of cool, clean water. Guineafowl ran to drink, but the tired animals stood in a row in front of the water.\n\n“Where were your fast feet when we needed them?” asked Old Meerkat.\n\nGuineafowl hung her head. “I am sorry,” she said softly. “Tomorrow I will help to clean the waterhole.” The animals let her drink, and from that day on Guineafowl was always the first to help.\n\n*Moral: If you want to share the reward, you must also share the work.*\n\nWoordjies: *guineafowl* = tarentaal, *boast* = spog, *waterhole* = watergat, *reward* = beloning.\n\n## Die elemente van ’n storie\n\n- **Karakters** (*characters*) is die mense of diere in die storie. Die **hoofkarakter** (*main character*) is die belangrikste; die storie gaan oor hom of haar: *Guineafowl*. **Byfigure** (*minor characters*) is minder belangrik en help die storie aan: *Old Meerkat* en die ander diere.\n- Die **agtergrond** (*setting*) is **waar** en **wanneer** die storie afspeel. Plek: die droë Karoo, by die watergat. Tyd: lank gelede (*Once upon a time*), op ’n warm somersdag tot sononder.\n- Die **verteller** (*narrator*) is die een wat die storie vertel. Hier vertel iemand buite die storie, wat *she* en *they* gebruik (derde persoon). As ’n karakter self vertel en *I* gebruik, is dit ’n eerstepersoonverteller.\n\n## Die storielyn\n\n| Deel | Wat gebeur? | In ons storie |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Begin** | ons ontmoet die karakters en leer die agtergrond ken | Ons ontmoet die spoggerige tarentaal in die Karoo. |\n| **Probleem** | iets gaan verkeerd | Die watergat droog op en Guineafowl wil nie help grawe nie. |\n| **Klimaks** | die spannendste oomblik, die keerpunt | Die diere staan voor die water: *Where were your fast feet?* |\n| **Einde** | die probleem word opgelos | Guineafowl sê jammer, drink en help daarna altyd eerste. |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie die klimaks met die einde verwar nie. Die klimaks is die spannendste oomblik **voordat** die probleem opgelos word; die einde kom daarna.\n\n## Volksverhale en fabels\n\n- ’n **Volksverhaal** (*folk tale*) is ’n baie ou storie wat oor baie jare mondeling van grootouers na kinders oorvertel is. Dit verduidelik dikwels hoekom iets so is, soos *why the zebra has stripes*.\n- ’n **Fabel** (*fable*) is ’n kort storie waarin diere praat en optree soos mense. Dit leer ’n **sedeles** (*moral*), wat dikwels in die laaste reël staan.\n\n> **Onthou:** Die sedeles is ’n les vir die regte lewe. Skryf dit as ’n reël vir almal, nie net oor die karakters nie: *If you want to share the reward, you must also share the work.*\n\n## Feit of fiksie? Gebeure in volgorde\n\n**Fiksie** (*fiction*) is uitgedink. **Feite** (*facts*) is waar en kan nagegaan word. Ons storie is fiksie, want tarentale kan nie praat nie! Tog gebruik die skrywer feite: tarentale het gespikkelde vere, meerkatte is goeie grawers en die Karoo is droog.\n\nOm gebeure in **volgorde** te sit, soek **tydwoorde** soos *once upon a time, one hot summer, then, by sunset, from that day on*. Nommer die gebeure 1, 2, 3 … en kyk of elke stap logies op die vorige een volg.","en":"## Read the story\n\n**Guineafowl Learns to Share the Work**\n\nOnce upon a time, in the dry Karoo, there lived a guineafowl who loved to boast. “My feathers have the prettiest spots in the veld,” she told everyone, “and nobody can run as fast as I can!”\n\nOne hot summer, the old waterhole began to dry up. The animals met under the thorn tree to make a plan. “Let us dig the waterhole deeper,” said Old Meerkat. “If we all help, we will finish before sunset.”\n\nEveryone started to dig – everyone except Guineafowl. “My pretty feet are not made for mud,” she said, and she sat in the shade to admire her spots.\n\nBy sunset the hole was deep and full of cool, clean water. Guineafowl ran to drink, but the tired animals stood in a row in front of the water.\n\n“Where were your fast feet when we needed them?” asked Old Meerkat.\n\nGuineafowl hung her head. “I am sorry,” she said softly. “Tomorrow I will help to clean the waterhole.” The animals let her drink, and from that day on Guineafowl was always the first to help.\n\n*Moral: If you want to share the reward, you must also share the work.*\n\n## The elements of a story\n\n- **Characters** are the people or animals in the story. The **main character** is the most important one; the story is about him or her: *Guineafowl*. **Minor characters** are less important and help the story along: *Old Meerkat* and the other animals.\n- The **setting** is **where** and **when** the story takes place. Place: the dry Karoo, at the waterhole. Time: long ago (*Once upon a time*), on a hot summer day until sunset.\n- The **narrator** is the one who tells the story. Here someone outside the story tells it, using *she* and *they* (third person). If a character tells the story and uses *I*, it is a first-person narrator.\n\n## The plot\n\n| Part | What happens? | In our story |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Beginning** | we meet the characters and get to know the setting | We meet the boastful guineafowl in the Karoo. |\n| **Problem** | something goes wrong | The waterhole dries up and Guineafowl will not help to dig. |\n| **Climax** | the most exciting moment, the turning point | The animals stand in front of the water: *Where were your fast feet?* |\n| **Ending** | the problem is solved | Guineafowl says sorry, drinks and is always first to help after that. |\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not confuse the climax with the ending. The climax is the most exciting moment **before** the problem is solved; the ending comes after it.\n\n## Folk tales and fables\n\n- A **folk tale** is a very old story that was retold by word of mouth, from grandparents to children, over many years. It often explains why something is the way it is, such as *why the zebra has stripes*.\n- A **fable** is a short story in which animals talk and act like people. It teaches a **moral** (a lesson), which is often written in the last line.\n\n> **Remember:** The moral is a lesson for real life. Write it as a rule for everyone, not only about the characters: *If you want to share the reward, you must also share the work.*\n\n## Fact or fiction? Events in order\n\n**Fiction** is made up. **Facts** are true and can be checked. Our story is fiction, because guineafowl cannot talk! But the writer still uses facts: guineafowl have spotted feathers, meerkats are good diggers and the Karoo is dry.\n\nTo put events in **order** (sequencing), look for **time words** such as *once upon a time, one hot summer, then, by sunset, from that day on*. Number the events 1, 2, 3 … and check that each step follows logically from the one before."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Hoofkarakter (*main character*)","en":"Main character"},"def":{"af":"Die belangrikste karakter; die storie gaan oor hom of haar.","en":"The most important character; the story is about him or her."}},{"term":{"af":"Byfiguur (*minor character*)","en":"Minor character"},"def":{"af":"’n Minder belangrike karakter wat die storie aanhelp.","en":"A less important character who helps the story along."}},{"term":{"af":"Agtergrond (*setting*)","en":"Setting"},"def":{"af":"Die tyd en plek waar ’n storie afspeel.","en":"The time and place in which a story happens."}},{"term":{"af":"Storielyn (*plot*)","en":"Plot"},"def":{"af":"Die gebeure van die storie in volgorde: begin, probleem, klimaks en einde.","en":"The events of the story in order: beginning, problem, climax and ending."}},{"term":{"af":"Klimaks (*climax*)","en":"Climax"},"def":{"af":"Die spannendste oomblik in ’n storie, net voordat die probleem opgelos word.","en":"The most exciting moment in a story, just before the problem is solved."}},{"term":{"af":"Verteller (*narrator*)","en":"Narrator"},"def":{"af":"Die een wat die storie vertel, met *I* (eerste persoon) of *he, she, they* (derde persoon).","en":"The one who tells the story, using *I* (first person) or *he, she, they* (third person)."}},{"term":{"af":"Volksverhaal (*folk tale*)","en":"Folk tale"},"def":{"af":"’n Ou storie wat oor baie jare mondeling oorvertel is en dikwels verduidelik hoekom iets so is.","en":"An old story that was retold by word of mouth over many years and often explains why something is the way it is."}},{"term":{"af":"Fabel (*fable*)","en":"Fable"},"def":{"af":"’n Kort storie waarin diere soos mense optree en wat ’n sedeles leer.","en":"A short story in which animals act like people and which teaches a moral."}},{"term":{"af":"Sedeles (*moral*)","en":"Moral"},"def":{"af":"Die les wat ’n fabel ons vir die regte lewe leer.","en":"The lesson that a fable teaches us for real life."}},{"term":{"af":"Fiksie (*fiction*)","en":"Fiction"},"def":{"af":"’n Storie wat uitgedink is en nie regtig gebeur het nie.","en":"A story that is made up and did not really happen."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Hoofkarakter en byfigure","en":"Main and minor characters"},"problem":{"af":"Wie is die hoofkarakter en wie is die byfigure in *Guineafowl Learns to Share the Work*? Gee ’n rede.","en":"Who is the main character and who are the minor characters in *Guineafowl Learns to Share the Work*? Give a reason."},"steps":[{"af":"Vra: Oor wie gaan die storie? Die titel en byna elke paragraaf noem *Guineafowl*.","en":"Ask: Who is the story about? The title and almost every paragraph mention *Guineafowl*."},{"af":"Vra: Wie verander in die storie? Guineafowl verander van spoggerig en lui na behulpsaam.","en":"Ask: Who changes in the story? Guineafowl changes from boastful and lazy to helpful."},{"af":"Old Meerkat en die ander diere help die storie aan, maar die storie gaan nie oor hulle nie.","en":"Old Meerkat and the other animals help the story along, but the story is not about them."}],"answer":{"af":"Hoofkarakter: Guineafowl, want die storie gaan oor haar en sy verander. Byfigure: Old Meerkat en die ander diere.","en":"Main character: Guineafowl, because the story is about her and she changes. Minor characters: Old Meerkat and the other animals."}},{"title":{"af":"Die agtergrond","en":"The setting"},"problem":{"af":"Beskryf die agtergrond (tyd en plek) van die storie.","en":"Describe the setting (time and place) of the story."},"steps":[{"af":"Plek: soek plekwoorde. *in the dry Karoo, the waterhole, under the thorn tree*.","en":"Place: look for place words. *in the dry Karoo, the waterhole, under the thorn tree*."},{"af":"Tyd: soek tydwoorde. *Once upon a time* (lank gelede), *one hot summer*, *by sunset*.","en":"Time: look for time words. *Once upon a time* (long ago), *one hot summer*, *by sunset*."},{"af":"Sit albei in een volsin saam.","en":"Put both together in one full sentence."}],"answer":{"af":"Die storie speel lank gelede af in die droë Karoo, by ’n watergat, op ’n warm somersdag tot sononder.","en":"The story takes place long ago in the dry Karoo, at a waterhole, on a hot summer day until sunset."}},{"title":{"af":"Sit die gebeure in volgorde","en":"Put the events in order"},"problem":{"af":"Rangskik in die regte volgorde: (a) *The animals stood in front of the water.* (b) *The waterhole began to dry up.* (c) *Guineafowl promised to help.* (d) *Guineafowl sat in the shade.*","en":"Put in the correct order: (a) *The animals stood in front of the water.* (b) *The waterhole began to dry up.* (c) *Guineafowl promised to help.* (d) *Guineafowl sat in the shade.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Die probleem begin wanneer die watergat opdroog: (b) is eerste.","en":"The problem starts when the waterhole dries up: (b) is first."},{"af":"Terwyl die diere grawe, sit Guineafowl in die skaduwee: (d).","en":"While the animals dig, Guineafowl sits in the shade: (d)."},{"af":"*By sunset* staan die diere voor die water: (a). Daarna sê sy jammer en belowe om te help: (c).","en":"*By sunset* the animals stand in front of the water: (a). After that she says sorry and promises to help: (c)."}],"answer":{"af":"(b), (d), (a), (c)","en":"(b), (d), (a), (c)"}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik die sedeles","en":"Explain the moral"},"problem":{"af":"Wat is die sedeles van die fabel? Verduidelik hoe die storie dit wys.","en":"What is the moral of the fable? Explain how the story shows it."},"steps":[{"af":"Die sedeles staan in die laaste reël: *If you want to share the reward, you must also share the work.*","en":"The moral is in the last line: *If you want to share the reward, you must also share the work.*"},{"af":"Die beloning is die koel water. Die werk is om die watergat dieper te grawe.","en":"The reward is the cool water. The work is digging the waterhole deeper."},{"af":"Guineafowl wou drink sonder om te werk, en die diere het haar eers gekeer. Sy het geleer dat sy ook moet help.","en":"Guineafowl wanted to drink without working, and at first the animals stopped her. She learnt that she must help too."}],"answer":{"af":"Die sedeles is dat jy ook moet help werk as jy die beloning wil deel. Guineafowl kon eers drink nadat sy jammer gesê en belowe het om te help.","en":"The moral is that you must help with the work if you want to share the reward. Guineafowl could only drink after she said sorry and promised to help."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wie is die **hoofkarakter** in die storie?","en":"Who is the **main character** in the story?"},"options":[{"af":"Old Meerkat","en":"Old Meerkat"},{"af":"die diere by die watergat","en":"the animals at the waterhole"},{"af":"Guineafowl","en":"Guineafowl"},{"af":"die verteller","en":"the narrator"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die storie gaan oor Guineafowl: sy is in die titel, sy het die probleem en sy verander aan die einde. Old Meerkat is ’n byfiguur.","en":"The story is about Guineafowl: she is in the title, she has the problem and she changes at the end. Old Meerkat is a minor character."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die tyd en plek van ’n storie word in Engels die ___ genoem.","en":"The time and place of a story is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["setting","agtergrond"],"en":["setting"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["plot","moral","climax"],"en":["plot","moral","climax"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die **agtergrond** (*setting*) sê waar en wanneer ’n storie afspeel, soos *the dry Karoo, long ago*.","en":"The **setting** tells where and when a story takes place, such as *the dry Karoo, long ago*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar speel die storie af?","en":"Where does the story take place?"},"options":[{"af":"in die droë Karoo","en":"in the dry Karoo"},{"af":"in ’n groot stad","en":"in a big city"},{"af":"by die see","en":"at the seaside"},{"af":"in ’n digte woud","en":"in a thick forest"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die eerste sin sê: *in the dry Karoo*. Die watergat en die doringboom pas ook by ’n droë plek.","en":"The first sentence says: *in the dry Karoo*. The waterhole and the thorn tree also fit a dry place."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Old Meerkat is ’n byfiguur in die storie.","en":"Old Meerkat is a minor character in the story."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Old Meerkat speel ’n belangrike rol en praat, maar die storie gaan oor Guineafowl. Daarom is hy ’n byfiguur.","en":"True. Old Meerkat plays an important part and speaks, but the story is about Guineafowl. That makes him a minor character."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe verander Guineafowl van die begin tot die einde van die storie?","en":"How does Guineafowl change from the beginning to the end of the story?"},"options":[{"af":"Sy verander van behulpsaam na lui.","en":"She changes from helpful to lazy."},{"af":"Sy verander van vinnig na stadig.","en":"She changes from fast to slow."},{"af":"Sy verander glad nie.","en":"She does not change at all."},{"af":"Sy verander van spoggerig en lui na behulpsaam.","en":"She changes from boastful and lazy to helpful."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Aan die begin spog sy en weier om te grawe. Aan die einde sê sy jammer en is sy *always the first to help*.","en":"At the beginning she boasts and refuses to dig. At the end she says sorry and is *always the first to help*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom het die diere voor die water gaan staan?","en":"Why did the animals stand in front of the water?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle wou eerste drink omdat hulle ouer was.","en":"They wanted to drink first because they were older."},{"af":"Guineafowl het nie gehelp grawe nie, so hulle wou haar ’n les leer.","en":"Guineafowl had not helped to dig, so they wanted to teach her a lesson."},{"af":"Die water was te vuil om te drink.","en":"The water was too dirty to drink."},{"af":"Hulle wou haar mooi kolle bekyk.","en":"They wanted to look at her pretty spots."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Old Meerkat vra: *Where were your fast feet when we needed them?* Dit wys hulle was teleurgesteld omdat sy nie gehelp het nie. Die water was juis *cool and clean*.","en":"Old Meerkat asks: *Where were your fast feet when we needed them?* This shows they were disappointed because she had not helped. The water was in fact *cool and clean*."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke deel van die storielyn by die regte gebeurtenis.","en":"Match each part of the plot to the correct event."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"begin (*beginning*)","en":"beginning"},"r":{"af":"Guineafowl spog oor haar kolle.","en":"Guineafowl boasts about her spots."}},{"l":{"af":"probleem (*problem*)","en":"problem"},"r":{"af":"Die watergat droog op en sy wil nie help nie.","en":"The waterhole dries up and she will not help."}},{"l":{"af":"klimaks (*climax*)","en":"climax"},"r":{"af":"Die diere keer haar by die water.","en":"The animals block her at the water."}},{"l":{"af":"einde (*ending*)","en":"ending"},"r":{"af":"Sy sê jammer en help daarna altyd.","en":"She says sorry and always helps after that."}}],"explain":{"af":"Die begin stel die karakter voor, die probleem is wanneer iets verkeerd gaan, die klimaks is die spannendste oomblik, en aan die einde word die probleem opgelos.","en":"The beginning introduces the character, the problem is when something goes wrong, the climax is the most exciting moment, and at the end the problem is solved."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die les aan die einde van ’n fabel word in Engels die ___ genoem.","en":"The lesson at the end of a fable is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["moral","sedeles"],"en":["moral"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["title","setting","problem"],"en":["title","setting","problem"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die **sedeles** (*moral*) is die les vir die regte lewe, soos *If you want to share the reward, you must also share the work.*","en":"The **moral** is the lesson for real life, such as *If you want to share the reward, you must also share the work.*"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is ’n **fabel**?","en":"What is a **fable**?"},"options":[{"af":"’n ware storie oor ’n bekende mens","en":"a true story about a famous person"},{"af":"’n gedig met ’n rymskema","en":"a poem with a rhyme scheme"},{"af":"’n kort storie waarin diere soos mense optree en wat ’n les leer","en":"a short story in which animals act like people and which teaches a lesson"},{"af":"’n verslag met feite oor diere","en":"a report with facts about animals"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"In ’n fabel praat en dink diere soos mense, en die storie leer ’n sedeles. ’n Verslag met feite is nie fiksie nie.","en":"In a fable animals talk and think like people, and the story teaches a moral. A report with facts is not fiction."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Volksverhaal is altyd ’n ware storie oor regte mense.","en":"A folk tale is always a true story about real people."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Volksverhaal is ’n ou, oorvertelde storie wat dikwels pratende diere of towery het, en wat verduidelik hoekom iets so is. Dit is fiksie.","en":"False. A folk tale is an old, retold story that often has talking animals or magic and explains why something is the way it is. It is fiction."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is ’n **feit** en nie fiksie nie?","en":"Which sentence is a **fact** and not fiction?"},"options":[{"af":"Guineafowl have spotted feathers.","en":"Guineafowl have spotted feathers."},{"af":"Guineafowl can talk to meerkats.","en":"Guineafowl can talk to meerkats."},{"af":"Meerkats make plans under thorn trees.","en":"Meerkats make plans under thorn trees."},{"af":"Guineafowl say sorry when they are wrong.","en":"Guineafowl say sorry when they are wrong."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Jy kan nagaan dat tarentale gespikkelde vere het; dit is ’n feit. Diere wat praat, planne maak en jammer sê, is uitgedink (fiksie).","en":"You can check that guineafowl have spotted feathers; it is a fact. Animals that talk, make plans and say sorry are made up (fiction)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die spannendste oomblik in ’n storie, net voordat die probleem opgelos word, is in Engels die ___.","en":"The most exciting moment in a story, just before the problem is solved, is the ___."},"answers":{"af":["climax","klimaks"],"en":["climax"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["beginning","ending","setting"],"en":["beginning","ending","setting"]}},"explain":{"af":"Dit is die **klimaks** (*climax*), die keerpunt van die storie. Die einde kom eers daarna, wanneer die probleem opgelos is.","en":"It is the **climax**, the turning point of the story. The ending only comes after that, when the problem has been solved."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wie vertel die storie?","en":"Who tells the story?"},"options":[{"af":"Guineafowl, wat *I* gebruik","en":"Guineafowl, who uses *I*"},{"af":"Old Meerkat, wat *I* gebruik","en":"Old Meerkat, who uses *I*"},{"af":"al die diere saam, wat *we* gebruik","en":"all the animals together, who use *we*"},{"af":"’n verteller buite die storie, wat *she* en *they* gebruik","en":"a narrator outside the story, who uses *she* and *they*"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die storie sê *she told everyone* en *the animals met*. Iemand buite die storie vertel dit (derde persoon). Die *I* verskyn net binne aanhalingstekens, wanneer ’n karakter praat.","en":"The story says *she told everyone* and *the animals met*. Someone outside the story tells it (third person). *I* only appears inside inverted commas, when a character speaks."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter van hierdie gebeure het **eerste** plaasgevind?","en":"Which of these events happened **first**?"},"options":[{"af":"Guineafowl sat in the shade.","en":"Guineafowl sat in the shade."},{"af":"The animals met under the thorn tree.","en":"The animals met under the thorn tree."},{"af":"The animals stood in a row in front of the water.","en":"The animals stood in a row in front of the water."},{"af":"Guineafowl said sorry.","en":"Guineafowl said sorry."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Eers het die diere onder die doringboom vergader om ’n plan te maak. Daarna het hulle gegrawe terwyl Guineafowl in die skaduwee gesit het, toe het hulle voor die water gestaan, en laaste het sy jammer gesê.","en":"First the animals met under the thorn tree to make a plan. Then they dug while Guineafowl sat in the shade, then they stood in front of the water, and last she said sorry."}}]},{"id":"eng5-t4-visual-texts","title":{"af":"Visuele tekste","en":"Visual texts"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal Engelse strokiesprente, advertensies, plakkate, tabelle en kaarte kan lees en vrae daaroor kan beantwoord deur na die woorde én die prente te kyk.","en":"You will be able to read comic strips, advertisements, posters, tables and maps and answer questions on them by looking at both the words and the pictures."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is ’n visuele teks?\n\n’n **Visuele teks** gebruik prente en woorde saam om ’n boodskap oor te dra: strokiesprente, advertensies, plakkate, tabelle en kaarte. Kyk na alles: die prente, die woorde, die kleure, die grootte van die letters en die gesigte van die karakters.\n\n## Strokiesprente\n\n’n **Strokiesprent** (*comic strip*) vertel ’n kort storie in ’n ry prentjies wat **rame** (*frames*) genoem word. Lees die rame van links na regs en van bo na onder.\n\n- **Spraakborrel** (*speech bubble*): het ’n puntige stertjie na die spreker en wys wat ’n karakter **sê**.\n- **Gedagteborrel** (*thought bubble*): ’n wolkie met klein sirkeltjies; wys wat ’n karakter **dink**.\n- **Onderskrif** (*caption*): ’n blokkie met die verteller se woorde, bv. *Later that day …*\n- **Klankwoorde** soos *SPLASH!*, **hoofletters** vir ’n harde stem en **gesigsuitdrukkings** wys geluide en gevoelens.\n\n**Ravi se strokiesprent, in woorde beskryf:**\n\n1. Ravi sit met ’n visstok by ’n dam. Spraakborrel: *“Today I’ll catch the biggest fish in this dam!”*\n2. Hy wag; die son brand. Gedagteborrel: *“Hmm … nothing is biting.”*\n3. Die stok buig. Groot letters: *SPLASH!* Ravi trek hard met groot oë.\n4. Ravi hou ’n ou, nat stewel op. Sy suster Aisha lag: *“Well, it IS the biggest boot in the dam!”*\n\nDit is snaaks omdat Ravi ’n groot vis verwag, maar ’n ou stewel vang.\n\n## Advertensies\n\n’n **Advertensie** (*advertisement*) wil jou **oorreed** om iets te koop of te doen.\n\n- **Slagspreuk** (*slogan*): ’n kort, pakkende sinnetjie wat maklik onthou word.\n- **Teikengehoor** (*target audience*): die groep mense op wie die advertensie gemik is.\n- **Oorredingswoorde**: *new, best, free, amazing, only, now, hurry*.\n\n**Die advertensie:** ’n Laggende meisie jaag op ’n blink rooi fiets teen ’n heuwel af. Groot letters: **ROCKET RIDER bicycles**. Slagspreuk: *Fly down the road!* Ander woorde: *NEW! The fastest bike in town! Only R1 499. FREE helmet with every bike! Hurry – offer ends 30 November!*\n\nDie teikengehoor is kinders van so 8 tot 12 jaar (en hul ouers, wat betaal).\n\n## Plakkate\n\n’n **Plakkaat** (*poster*) gee inligting oor ’n geleentheid. ’n Goeie plakkaat beantwoord **wie, wat, waar** en **wanneer** (*who, what, where, when*).\n\n**Die plakkaat:** *SPRING FUN DAY* (grootste letters). *Games, food stalls, a jumping castle and a talent show! Where: your school’s sports field. When: 12 September, 09:00–14:00. Adults R20, children free. Organised by the Grade 5 class.*\n\n> **Onthou:** Die belangrikste inligting staan gewoonlik in die **grootste** letters, sodat dit jou oog vang.\n\n## Tabelle en kaarte\n\nLees eers die **titel** van ’n tabel, dan die **kolomopskrifte**, en soek dan die regte ry.\n\n**Tuck Shop Prices**\n\n| Item | Price |\n|---|---|\n| Apple | R5 |\n| Fruit juice | R10 |\n| Muffin | R12 |\n| Cheese sandwich | R15 |\n\nBy ’n **kaart** kyk jy na die titel, die **sleutel** (*key*) wat die simbole verduidelik, en die **kompas** wat noord, suid, oos en wes wys (*N, S, E, W*).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie net die woorde lees nie. Baie vrae vra oor die prent: ’n frons, groot letters of ’n kleur dra ook ’n boodskap.","en":"## What is a visual text?\n\nA **visual text** uses pictures and words together to give a message: comic strips, advertisements, posters, tables and maps. Look at everything: the pictures, the words, the colours, the size of the letters and the faces of the characters.\n\n## Comic strips\n\nA **comic strip** tells a short story in a row of pictures called **frames**. Read the frames from left to right and from top to bottom.\n\n- **Speech bubble**: has a pointed tail towards the speaker and shows what a character **says**.\n- **Thought bubble**: a little cloud with small circles; shows what a character **thinks**.\n- **Caption**: a box with the narrator’s words, e.g. *Later that day …*\n- **Sound words** such as *SPLASH!*, **capital letters** for a loud voice and **facial expressions** show sounds and feelings.\n\n**Ravi’s comic strip, described in words:**\n\n1. Ravi sits at a dam with a fishing rod. Speech bubble: *“Today I’ll catch the biggest fish in this dam!”*\n2. He waits; the sun is burning. Thought bubble: *“Hmm … nothing is biting.”*\n3. The rod bends. Big letters: *SPLASH!* Ravi pulls hard with wide eyes.\n4. Ravi holds up an old, wet boot. His sister Aisha laughs: *“Well, it IS the biggest boot in the dam!”*\n\nIt is funny because Ravi expects a big fish, but he catches an old boot.\n\n## Advertisements\n\nAn **advertisement** (advert) wants to **persuade** you to buy something or to do something.\n\n- **Slogan**: a short, catchy phrase that is easy to remember.\n- **Target audience**: the group of people the advert is aimed at.\n- **Persuasive words**: *new, best, free, amazing, only, now, hurry*.\n\n**The advert:** A laughing girl races down a hill on a shiny red bicycle. Big letters: **ROCKET RIDER bicycles**. Slogan: *Fly down the road!* Other words: *NEW! The fastest bike in town! Only R1 499. FREE helmet with every bike! Hurry – offer ends 30 November!*\n\nThe target audience is children of about 8 to 12 years old (and their parents, who pay).\n\n## Posters\n\nA **poster** gives information about an event. A good poster answers **who, what, where** and **when**.\n\n**The poster:** *SPRING FUN DAY* (biggest letters). *Games, food stalls, a jumping castle and a talent show! Where: your school’s sports field. When: 12 September, 09:00–14:00. Adults R20, children free. Organised by the Grade 5 class.*\n\n> **Remember:** The most important information is usually in the **biggest** letters, so that it catches your eye.\n\n## Tables and maps\n\nFirst read the **title** of a table, then the **column headings**, and then find the correct row.\n\n**Tuck Shop Prices**\n\n| Item | Price |\n|---|---|\n| Apple | R5 |\n| Fruit juice | R10 |\n| Muffin | R12 |\n| Cheese sandwich | R15 |\n\nOn a **map**, look at the title, the **key** that explains the symbols, and the **compass** that shows north, south, east and west (*N, S, E, W*).\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not read only the words. Many questions ask about the picture: a frown, big letters or a colour also carries a message."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Visuele teks (*visual text*)","en":"Visual text"},"def":{"af":"’n Teks wat prente en woorde saam gebruik om ’n boodskap oor te dra.","en":"A text that uses pictures and words together to give a message."}},{"term":{"af":"Raam (*frame*)","en":"Frame"},"def":{"af":"Een prentjie of blokkie in ’n strokiesprent.","en":"One picture or box in a comic strip."}},{"term":{"af":"Spraakborrel (*speech bubble*)","en":"Speech bubble"},"def":{"af":"’n Borrel met ’n puntige stertjie wat wys wat ’n karakter sê.","en":"A bubble with a pointed tail that shows what a character says."}},{"term":{"af":"Gedagteborrel (*thought bubble*)","en":"Thought bubble"},"def":{"af":"’n Wolkvormige borrel met klein sirkeltjies wat wys wat ’n karakter dink.","en":"A cloud-shaped bubble with small circles that shows what a character thinks."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderskrif (*caption*)","en":"Caption"},"def":{"af":"’n Blokkie met die verteller se woorde in ’n strokiesprent, soos *Later that day …*","en":"A box with the narrator’s words in a comic strip, such as *Later that day …*"}},{"term":{"af":"Slagspreuk (*slogan*)","en":"Slogan"},"def":{"af":"’n Kort, pakkende sinnetjie in ’n advertensie wat maklik onthou word.","en":"A short, catchy phrase in an advertisement that is easy to remember."}},{"term":{"af":"Teikengehoor (*target audience*)","en":"Target audience"},"def":{"af":"Die groep mense op wie ’n advertensie of plakkaat gemik is.","en":"The group of people an advertisement or poster is aimed at."}},{"term":{"af":"Oorredingswoorde (*persuasive words*)","en":"Persuasive words"},"def":{"af":"Woorde wat jou wil oortuig om iets te koop of te doen, soos *free, new* en *best*.","en":"Words that try to convince you to buy or do something, such as *free, new* and *best*."}},{"term":{"af":"Plakkaat (*poster*)","en":"Poster"},"def":{"af":"’n Groot kennisgewing wat sê wie, wat, waar en wanneer ’n geleentheid is.","en":"A large notice that tells who, what, where and when an event is."}},{"term":{"af":"Sleutel (*key*)","en":"Key"},"def":{"af":"Die deel van ’n kaart wat verduidelik wat elke simbool beteken.","en":"The part of a map that explains what each symbol means."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lees die strokiesprent","en":"Read the comic strip"},"problem":{"af":"Kyk na Ravi se strokiesprent. (a) Wat wys die borrel in raam 2? (b) Waarom is *SPLASH!* in groot hoofletters? (c) Wat maak raam 4 snaaks?","en":"Look at Ravi’s comic strip. (a) What does the bubble in frame 2 show? (b) Why is *SPLASH!* in big capital letters? (c) What makes frame 4 funny?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Raam 2 het ’n gedagteborrel, so dit wys wat Ravi **dink**, nie wat hy sê nie: hy dink niks byt nie.","en":"(a) Frame 2 has a thought bubble, so it shows what Ravi **thinks**, not what he says: he thinks nothing is biting."},{"af":"(b) *SPLASH!* is ’n klankwoord. Die groot hoofletters wys dat die geluid hard is en dat iets groots gebeur.","en":"(b) *SPLASH!* is a sound word. The big capital letters show that the noise is loud and that something big is happening."},{"af":"(c) In raam 1 sê Ravi hy sal die grootste vis vang. In raam 4 vang hy ’n ou stewel, en Aisha maak ’n grap dat dit *the biggest boot in the dam* is.","en":"(c) In frame 1 Ravi says he will catch the biggest fish. In frame 4 he catches an old boot, and Aisha jokes that it is *the biggest boot in the dam*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Wat Ravi dink. (b) Om te wys dat die geluid hard is. (c) Ravi verwag ’n groot vis, maar vang ’n ou stewel.","en":"(a) What Ravi thinks. (b) To show that the noise is loud. (c) Ravi expects a big fish, but he catches an old boot."}},{"title":{"af":"Ontleed die advertensie","en":"Analyse the advert"},"problem":{"af":"Kyk na die *Rocket Rider*-advertensie. Noem die slagspreuk, die teikengehoor en twee oorredingswoorde.","en":"Look at the *Rocket Rider* advert. Name the slogan, the target audience and two persuasive words."},"steps":[{"af":"Die slagspreuk is die kort, pakkende sinnetjie: *Fly down the road!*","en":"The slogan is the short, catchy phrase: *Fly down the road!*"},{"af":"Die prent wys ’n meisie op ’n fiets en dit gaan oor spoed en pret. Die teikengehoor is dus kinders van so 8 tot 12 jaar (en hul ouers).","en":"The picture shows a girl on a bicycle, and the advert is about speed and fun. So the target audience is children of about 8 to 12 years old (and their parents)."},{"af":"Oorredingswoorde wil jou oortuig: *NEW, FREE, fastest, Only, Hurry*.","en":"Persuasive words try to convince you: *NEW, FREE, fastest, Only, Hurry*."}],"answer":{"af":"Slagspreuk: *Fly down the road!* Teikengehoor: kinders van 8 tot 12 jaar. Oorredingswoorde: bv. *FREE* en *NEW*.","en":"Slogan: *Fly down the road!* Target audience: children of 8 to 12 years old. Persuasive words: e.g. *FREE* and *NEW*."}},{"title":{"af":"Wie, wat, waar, wanneer?","en":"Who, what, where, when?"},"problem":{"af":"Gebruik die plakkaat en beantwoord: wie reël dit, wat gebeur, waar en wanneer?","en":"Use the poster and answer: who organises it, what is happening, where and when?"},"steps":[{"af":"Wie: *Organised by the Grade 5 class*.","en":"Who: *Organised by the Grade 5 class*."},{"af":"Wat: ’n *Spring Fun Day* met speletjies, kosstalletjies, ’n springkasteel en ’n talentkompetisie.","en":"What: a *Spring Fun Day* with games, food stalls, a jumping castle and a talent show."},{"af":"Waar: *your school’s sports field*. Wanneer: *12 September, 09:00–14:00*.","en":"Where: *your school’s sports field*. When: *12 September, 09:00–14:00*."}],"answer":{"af":"Die Graad 5-klas reël ’n Spring Fun Day op die skool se sportveld op 12 September van 09:00 tot 14:00.","en":"The Grade 5 class is organising a Spring Fun Day on the school’s sports field on 12 September from 09:00 to 14:00."}},{"title":{"af":"Lees die tabel","en":"Read the table"},"problem":{"af":"Nomsa het R20. Kan sy ’n muffin en ’n vrugtesap by die snoepie koop? As nie, wat kan sy eerder saam met die muffin koop?","en":"Nomsa has R20. Can she buy a muffin and a fruit juice at the tuck shop? If not, what can she buy with the muffin instead?"},"steps":[{"af":"Kry die pryse in die tabel: *Muffin* R12, *Fruit juice* R10.","en":"Find the prices in the table: Muffin R12, Fruit juice R10."},{"af":"Tel op: R12 + R10 = R22. Dit is R2 meer as R20, so sy het nie genoeg geld nie.","en":"Add: R12 + R10 = R22. That is R2 more than R20, so she does not have enough money."},{"af":"Probeer die goedkoopste item: *Apple* R5. R12 + R5 = R17, en sy kry R3 kleingeld.","en":"Try the cheapest item: Apple R5. R12 + R5 = R17, and she gets R3 change."}],"answer":{"af":"Nee, dit kos R22. Sy kan ’n muffin en ’n appel vir R17 koop.","en":"No, it costs R22. She can buy a muffin and an apple for R17."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat noem ons elke prentjie of blokkie in ’n strokiesprent?","en":"What do we call each picture or box in a comic strip?"},"options":[{"af":"bubble","en":"bubble"},{"af":"frame","en":"frame"},{"af":"caption","en":"caption"},{"af":"slogan","en":"slogan"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Elke prentjie is ’n *frame* (raam). ’n *Caption* is net die blokkie met die verteller se woorde binne ’n raam.","en":"Each picture is a *frame*. A *caption* is only the box with the narrator’s words inside a frame."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat wys ’n wolkvormige borrel met klein sirkeltjies?","en":"What does a cloud-shaped bubble with small circles show?"},"options":[{"af":"wat ’n karakter sê","en":"what a character says"},{"af":"’n harde geluid","en":"a loud noise"},{"af":"die verteller se woorde","en":"the narrator’s words"},{"af":"wat ’n karakter dink","en":"what a character thinks"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Dit is ’n gedagteborrel (*thought bubble*): dit wys wat ’n karakter dink. ’n Spraakborrel met ’n puntige stertjie wys wat iemand sê.","en":"It is a thought bubble: it shows what a character thinks. A speech bubble with a pointed tail shows what someone says."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In raam 4 sê Aisha dis die grootste ___ in die dam.","en":"In frame 4 Aisha says it is the biggest ___ in the dam."},"answers":{"af":["boot"],"en":["boot"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["fish","rod","splash"],"en":["fish","rod","splash"]}},"explain":{"af":"Aisha sê: *Well, it IS the biggest boot in the dam!* Ravi wou die grootste *fish* vang, maar hy het ’n stewel (*boot*) gevang.","en":"Aisha says: *Well, it IS the biggest boot in the dam!* Ravi wanted to catch the biggest *fish*, but he caught a *boot*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **slagspreuk** van die *Rocket Rider*-advertensie?","en":"What is the **slogan** of the *Rocket Rider* advert?"},"options":[{"af":"Fly down the road!","en":"Fly down the road!"},{"af":"Only R1 499","en":"Only R1 499"},{"af":"FREE helmet with every bike!","en":"FREE helmet with every bike!"},{"af":"Rocket Rider bicycles","en":"Rocket Rider bicycles"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die slagspreuk is die kort, pakkende sinnetjie wat jy onthou: *Fly down the road!* *Rocket Rider* is die naam van die produk, en die prys en die gratis helm is spesiale aanbiedinge.","en":"The slogan is the short, catchy phrase you remember: *Fly down the road!* *Rocket Rider* is the name of the product, and the price and the free helmet are special offers."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Goeie plakkaat sê vir jou wie, wat, waar en wanneer.","en":"A good poster tells you who, what, where and when."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Plakkaat gee inligting oor ’n geleentheid, so dit moet sê wie dit reël, wat gebeur, waar en wanneer.","en":"True. A poster gives information about an event, so it must say who organises it, what is happening, where and when."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wie is die **teikengehoor** van die *Rocket Rider*-advertensie?","en":"Who is the **target audience** of the *Rocket Rider* advert?"},"options":[{"af":"boere wat ’n trekker nodig het","en":"farmers who need a tractor"},{"af":"grootmense wat werk toe ry","en":"adults who drive to work"},{"af":"kinders van so 8 tot 12 jaar","en":"children of about 8 to 12 years old"},{"af":"kleuters wat leer loop","en":"toddlers who are learning to walk"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die prent wys ’n kind op ’n fiets, en die woorde gaan oor spoed en pret. Die advertensie is dus op kinders gemik (en hul ouers, wat betaal).","en":"The picture shows a child on a bicycle, and the words are about speed and fun. So the advert is aimed at children (and their parents, who pay)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord in die advertensie is ’n **oorredingswoord**?","en":"Which word in the advert is a **persuasive word**?"},"options":[{"af":"bicycle","en":"bicycle"},{"af":"helmet","en":"helmet"},{"af":"road","en":"road"},{"af":"FREE","en":"FREE"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*FREE* (gratis) wil jou oortuig om die fiets te koop, want jy kry iets ekstra. Die ander woorde noem net dinge.","en":"*FREE* tries to convince you to buy the bike, because you get something extra. The other words just name things."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke kenmerk by wat dit doen.","en":"Match each feature to what it does."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"spraakborrel (*speech bubble*)","en":"speech bubble"},"r":{"af":"wys wat ’n karakter sê","en":"shows what a character says"}},{"l":{"af":"gedagteborrel (*thought bubble*)","en":"thought bubble"},"r":{"af":"wys wat ’n karakter dink","en":"shows what a character thinks"}},{"l":{"af":"onderskrif (*caption*)","en":"caption"},"r":{"af":"gee die verteller se woorde","en":"gives the narrator’s words"}},{"l":{"af":"slagspreuk (*slogan*)","en":"slogan"},"r":{"af":"’n pakkende sinnetjie oor ’n produk","en":"a catchy phrase about a product"}},{"l":{"af":"sleutel (*key*)","en":"key"},"r":{"af":"verduidelik die simbole op ’n kaart","en":"explains the symbols on a map"}}],"explain":{"af":"Borrels wys wat karakters sê of dink, die onderskrif is die verteller se stem, die slagspreuk help jou om ’n produk te onthou, en die sleutel verduidelik ’n kaart se simbole.","en":"Bubbles show what characters say or think, the caption is the narrator’s voice, the slogan helps you remember a product, and the key explains a map’s symbols."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar is die *Spring Fun Day*?","en":"Where is the *Spring Fun Day*?"},"options":[{"af":"in die skoolsaal","en":"in the school hall"},{"af":"op jou skool se sportveld","en":"on your school’s sports field"},{"af":"in die skoolbiblioteek","en":"in the school library"},{"af":"in die Graad 5-klaskamer","en":"in the Grade 5 classroom"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die plakkaat sê: *Where: your school’s sports field.* Die Graad 5-klas reël die dag, maar dit vind nie in hul klaskamer plaas nie.","en":"The poster says: *Where: your school’s sports field.* The Grade 5 class organises the day, but it does not take place in their classroom."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die hoofdoel van ’n advertensie is om ’n snaakse storie te vertel.","en":"The main purpose of an advertisement is to tell a funny story."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Advertensie wil jou **oorreed** om iets te koop of te doen. ’n Strokiesprent vertel eerder ’n (snaakse) storie.","en":"False. An advertisement wants to **persuade** you to buy or do something. A comic strip is what usually tells a (funny) story."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die kort, pakkende sinnetjie in ’n advertensie word in Engels ’n ___ genoem.","en":"The short, catchy phrase in an advertisement is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["slogan"],"en":["slogan"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["caption","frame","poster"],"en":["caption","frame","poster"]}},"explain":{"af":"Dit is ’n *slogan* (slagspreuk), soos *Fly down the road!* ’n *Caption* hoort by ’n strokiesprent.","en":"It is a *slogan*, such as *Fly down the road!* A *caption* belongs to a comic strip."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom staan *SPRING FUN DAY* in die grootste letters op die plakkaat?","en":"Why is *SPRING FUN DAY* in the biggest letters on the poster?"},"options":[{"af":"Die ontwerper het nie meer klein letters gehad nie.","en":"The designer had no small letters left."},{"af":"Dit is die naam van die skool.","en":"It is the name of the school."},{"af":"Dit is die belangrikste inligting en moet jou oog vang.","en":"It is the most important information and must catch your eye."},{"af":"Dit wys hoeveel die kaartjies kos.","en":"It shows how much the tickets cost."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Ontwerpers sit die belangrikste inligting – wat die geleentheid is – in die grootste letters, sodat mense dit van ver af raaksien.","en":"Designers put the most important information – what the event is – in the biggest letters, so that people notice it from far away."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Kyk na die snoepietabel. ’n Muffin en ’n appel kos saam ___.","en":"Look at the tuck shop table. A muffin and an apple cost ___ together."},"answers":{"af":["R17","R17,00","17"],"en":["R17","R17.00","17"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["R22","R15","R27"],"en":["R22","R15","R27"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Muffin* R12 + *Apple* R5 = R17. R22 is ’n muffin en ’n vrugtesap, en R15 is die prys van die kaastoebroodjie.","en":"Muffin R12 + Apple R5 = R17. R22 is a muffin and a fruit juice, and R15 is the price of the cheese sandwich."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter item in die snoepietabel is die **goedkoopste**?","en":"Which item in the tuck shop table is the **cheapest**?"},"options":[{"af":"Apple","en":"Apple"},{"af":"Fruit juice","en":"Fruit juice"},{"af":"Muffin","en":"Muffin"},{"af":"Cheese sandwich","en":"Cheese sandwich"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die appel kos net R5; dit is die laagste prys in die tabel. Die kaastoebroodjie (R15) is die duurste.","en":"The apple costs only R5; that is the lowest price in the table. The cheese sandwich (R15) is the most expensive."}}]},{"id":"eng5-t4-short-writing","title":{"af":"Kort skryfstukke","en":"Short writing pieces"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal ’n vriendskaplike brief, dagboekinskrywing, uitnodiging, e-pos, resep en boodskap in Engels kan skryf, met die regte formaat en ’n vriendelike, informele toon.","en":"You will be able to write a friendly letter, diary entry, invitation, email, recipe and message with the correct format and a friendly, informal tone."},"summary":{"af":"## Skryf vir ’n leser\n\nVra jouself voordat jy skryf: **Vir wie** skryf ek (die leser)? **Hoekom** skryf ek (die doel)? Watter **formaat** (uitleg) moet ek gebruik? Al die skryfstukke in hierdie les is **informeel**: jy skryf aan vriende en familie in ’n vriendelike, geselsende **toon** (*tone*). Jy mag sametrekkings soos *I’m* en *can’t* gebruik.\n\n> **Onthou:** Informeel beteken nie slordig nie. Jou spelling, hoofletters en leestekens moet steeds reg wees.\n\n## Die vriendskaplike brief\n\n| Deel | Waar? | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Jou adres | regs bo | *12 Protea Street, Durban, 4001* |\n| Datum | regs, onder die adres | *3 November 2026* |\n| Aanhef (*greeting*) | links, met ’n komma | *Dear Lerato,* |\n| Inhoud (*body*) | in paragrawe | nuus, vrae, gevoelens |\n| Slot (*closing*) | links, met ’n komma | *Lots of love,* / *Your friend,* |\n| Naam | onder die slot | net jou voornaam: *Anika* |\n\n’n Kort voorbeeld van die inhoud en slot:\n\n*Dear Lerato,*\n\n*Thank you for your letter. I loved the photo of your new puppy! Guess what? Our class visited the aquarium last week. I touched a starfish and it felt rough and bumpy.*\n\n*Please write back soon and tell me the puppy’s name.*\n\n*Lots of love,*  \n*Anika*\n\n## Dagboek, uitnodiging, e-pos en boodskap\n\n| Teks | Wat moet daarin wees? | Wenk |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Dagboekinskrywing** (*diary entry*) | datum, *Dear Diary,* (as jy wil), wat gebeur het en hoe jy gevoel het | eerste persoon (*I*), meestal verlede tyd |\n| **Uitnodiging** (*invitation*) | wie nooi, wat, waar, wanneer (datum en tyd), RSVP | *RSVP* beteken ‘antwoord asseblief’ |\n| **E-pos** (*email*) | *To*-adres, *Subject*-lyn, aanhef, kort boodskap, slot en naam | die *subject* sê in ’n paar woorde waaroor dit gaan |\n| **Boodskap** (*message/note*) | vir wie, die boodskap, van wie, tyd of datum | baie kort; net die belangrike feite |\n\nVoorbeeld van ’n dagboekinskrywing: *14 November. Dear Diary, Today we went to the beach with my cousins. The water was freezing, but we laughed so much! I feel tired but very happy.*\n\nVoorbeeld van ’n uitnodiging: *You’re invited to Aisha’s 11th birthday party! Where: 8 Baobab Avenue, Polokwane. When: 21 November, 14:00 to 17:00. Bring your swimming costume. RSVP to Aisha by 15 November.*\n\nVoorbeeld van ’n boodskap: *Liam, Coach phoned. Soccer practice is on Thursday at 15:00, not Wednesday. Bring your boots. – Mom, 14:15*\n\n## Instruksies en resepte\n\n- **Titel**: wat jy gaan maak, bv. *How to make a cheese and tomato sandwich*\n- **What you need**: die **bestanddele** (*ingredients*) of toerusting\n- **Method**: **genommerde stappe** in die regte volgorde\n- Elke stap begin met ’n **bevelvorm** van die werkwoord (*imperative verb*): *Spread, Cut, Mix, Pour, Stir, Bake*.\n\n*You need: 2 slices of bread, butter, 1 slice of cheese, 1 tomato.*\n\n1. *Spread butter on both slices of bread.*\n2. *Cut the tomato into thin slices.*\n3. *Put the cheese and tomato on one slice.*\n4. *Cover it with the other slice and cut it in half.*\n\nVra ’n grootmens om te help as jy ’n skerp mes gebruik.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie skryf *You must take two slices* of *Then you should cut …* nie. Begin elke stap met die werkwoord self: *Take two slices of bread. Cut the tomato.*","en":"## Writing for a reader\n\nBefore you write, ask yourself: **Who** am I writing to (the reader)? **Why** am I writing (the purpose)? Which **format** (layout) must I use? All the pieces in this lesson are **informal**: you write to friends and family in a friendly, chatty **tone**. You may use contractions such as *I’m* and *can’t*.\n\n> **Remember:** Informal does not mean careless. Your spelling, capital letters and punctuation must still be correct.\n\n## The friendly letter\n\n| Part | Where? | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Your address | top right | *12 Protea Street, Durban, 4001* |\n| Date | right, under the address | *3 November 2026* |\n| Greeting | left, with a comma | *Dear Lerato,* |\n| Body | in paragraphs | news, questions, feelings |\n| Closing | left, with a comma | *Lots of love,* / *Your friend,* |\n| Name | under the closing | only your first name: *Anika* |\n\nA short example of the body and closing:\n\n*Dear Lerato,*\n\n*Thank you for your letter. I loved the photo of your new puppy! Guess what? Our class visited the aquarium last week. I touched a starfish and it felt rough and bumpy.*\n\n*Please write back soon and tell me the puppy’s name.*\n\n*Lots of love,*  \n*Anika*\n\n## Diary, invitation, email and message\n\n| Text | What must be in it? | Tip |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Diary entry** | date, *Dear Diary,* (if you like), what happened and how you felt | first person (*I*), mostly past tense |\n| **Invitation** | who is inviting, what, where, when (date and time), RSVP | *RSVP* means ‘please reply’ |\n| **Email** | *To* address, *Subject* line, greeting, short message, closing and name | the *subject* says in a few words what it is about |\n| **Message/note** | who it is for, the message, who it is from, time or date | very short; only the important facts |\n\nExample of a diary entry: *14 November. Dear Diary, Today we went to the beach with my cousins. The water was freezing, but we laughed so much! I feel tired but very happy.*\n\nExample of an invitation: *You’re invited to Aisha’s 11th birthday party! Where: 8 Baobab Avenue, Polokwane. When: 21 November, 14:00 to 17:00. Bring your swimming costume. RSVP to Aisha by 15 November.*\n\nExample of a message: *Liam, Coach phoned. Soccer practice is on Thursday at 15:00, not Wednesday. Bring your boots. – Mom, 14:15*\n\n## Instructions and recipes\n\n- **Title**: what you are going to make, e.g. *How to make a cheese and tomato sandwich*\n- **What you need**: the **ingredients** or equipment\n- **Method**: **numbered steps** in the correct order\n- Each step begins with an **imperative verb** (a command word): *Spread, Cut, Mix, Pour, Stir, Bake*.\n\n*You need: 2 slices of bread, butter, 1 slice of cheese, 1 tomato.*\n\n1. *Spread butter on both slices of bread.*\n2. *Cut the tomato into thin slices.*\n3. *Put the cheese and tomato on one slice.*\n4. *Cover it with the other slice and cut it in half.*\n\nAsk an adult to help when you use a sharp knife.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not write *You must take two slices* or *Then you should cut …*. Begin each step with the verb itself: *Take two slices of bread. Cut the tomato.*"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Formaat (*format*)","en":"Format"},"def":{"af":"Die uitleg van ’n skryfstuk: watter dele daar is en waar elkeen staan.","en":"The layout of a piece of writing: which parts it has and where each one goes."}},{"term":{"af":"Informele toon (*informal tone*)","en":"Informal tone"},"def":{"af":"’n Vriendelike, geselsende manier van skryf aan iemand wat jy goed ken.","en":"A friendly, chatty way of writing to someone you know well."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanhef (*greeting*)","en":"Greeting"},"def":{"af":"Die woorde waarmee ’n brief of e-pos begin, soos *Dear Lerato,*","en":"The words a letter or email begins with, such as *Dear Lerato,*"}},{"term":{"af":"Slot (*closing*)","en":"Closing"},"def":{"af":"Die woorde voor jou naam aan die einde van ’n brief, soos *Lots of love,*","en":"The words before your name at the end of a letter, such as *Lots of love,*"}},{"term":{"af":"Dagboekinskrywing (*diary entry*)","en":"Diary entry"},"def":{"af":"Privaat skryfwerk oor jou eie dag en gevoelens, met ’n datum, in die eerste persoon.","en":"Private writing about your own day and feelings, with a date, in the first person."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitnodiging (*invitation*)","en":"Invitation"},"def":{"af":"’n Kort teks wat iemand na ’n geleentheid nooi en sê wat, waar en wanneer dit is.","en":"A short text that invites someone to an event and says what, where and when it is."}},{"term":{"af":"RSVP","en":"RSVP"},"def":{"af":"’n Afkorting op ’n uitnodiging wat beteken ‘antwoord asseblief’ – laat weet of jy kom.","en":"An abbreviation on an invitation that means ‘please reply’ – let the person know if you are coming."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderwerplyn (*subject line*)","en":"Subject line"},"def":{"af":"Die lyn bo-aan ’n e-pos wat in ’n paar woorde sê waaroor die e-pos gaan.","en":"The line at the top of an email that says in a few words what the email is about."}},{"term":{"af":"Bevelvorm (*imperative verb*)","en":"Imperative verb"},"def":{"af":"’n Werkwoord wat ’n opdrag gee en ’n instruksie begin, soos *Mix* of *Cut*.","en":"A verb that gives a command and begins an instruction, such as *Mix* or *Cut*."}},{"term":{"af":"Bestanddele (*ingredients*)","en":"Ingredients"},"def":{"af":"Die kos wat jy nodig het om ’n resep te maak.","en":"The food items you need to make a recipe."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Die uitleg van ’n vriendskaplike brief","en":"The layout of a friendly letter"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter woon by *5 Kudu Road, Kimberley, 8301*. Hy skryf op 2 November aan sy neef Johan oor sy nuwe fiets. Beplan die uitleg van sy brief.","en":"Pieter lives at *5 Kudu Road, Kimberley, 8301*. On 2 November he writes to his cousin Johan about his new bike. Plan the layout of his letter."},"steps":[{"af":"Regs bo: die adres in drie reëls (*5 Kudu Road / Kimberley / 8301*) en die datum daaronder (*2 November*).","en":"Top right: the address on three lines (*5 Kudu Road / Kimberley / 8301*) and the date under it (*2 November*)."},{"af":"Links: die aanhef met ’n komma: *Dear Johan,*","en":"Left: the greeting with a comma: *Dear Johan,*"},{"af":"Inhoud: paragraaf 1 vra hoe dit gaan; paragraaf 2 vertel van die nuwe fiets; paragraaf 3 sluit vriendelik af, bv. *Write back soon!*","en":"Body: paragraph 1 asks how he is; paragraph 2 tells about the new bike; paragraph 3 ends in a friendly way, e.g. *Write back soon!*"},{"af":"Links onder: die slot met ’n komma (*Your cousin,*) en Pieter se voornaam daaronder.","en":"Bottom left: the closing with a comma (*Your cousin,*) and Pieter’s first name under it."}],"answer":{"af":"Adres en datum regs bo → *Dear Johan,* → drie paragrawe → *Your cousin,* → *Pieter*","en":"Address and date top right → *Dear Johan,* → three paragraphs → *Your cousin,* → *Pieter*"}},{"title":{"af":"Skryf instruksies met bevelvorme","en":"Write instructions with imperative verbs"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf as genommerde instruksies: *First you must wash your hands. Then you should put the flour in a bowl. After that you can add the milk.*","en":"Rewrite as numbered instructions: *First you must wash your hands. Then you should put the flour in a bowl. After that you can add the milk.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Vind die werkwoord in elke sin: *wash, put, add*.","en":"Find the verb in each sentence: *wash, put, add*."},{"af":"Laat *you must, you should, you can* weg en begin elke stap met die werkwoord (bevelvorm).","en":"Leave out *you must, you should, you can* and begin each step with the verb (imperative)."},{"af":"Die nommers wys nou die volgorde, so jy het nie *First, Then* en *After that* nodig nie.","en":"The numbers now show the order, so you do not need *First, Then* and *After that*."}],"answer":{"af":"1. *Wash your hands.* 2. *Put the flour in a bowl.* 3. *Add the milk.*","en":"1. *Wash your hands.* 2. *Put the flour in a bowl.* 3. *Add the milk.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Wat kort in die uitnodiging?","en":"What is missing from the invitation?"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho skryf: *Come to my party! It’s at my house. From Sipho.* Watter belangrike inligting kort?","en":"Sipho writes: *Come to my party! It’s at my house. From Sipho.* What important information is missing?"},"steps":[{"af":"Gaan die vrae na: **Wie** nooi? Sipho – dit is daar. **Wat**? ’n Partytjie – maar watter soort (bv. verjaarsdag)?","en":"Check the questions: **Who** is inviting? Sipho – that is there. **What**? A party – but what kind (e.g. a birthday)?"},{"af":"**Waar**? *my house* is nie genoeg nie; die gaste het die adres nodig.","en":"**Where**? *my house* is not enough; the guests need the address."},{"af":"**Wanneer**? Daar is geen datum of tyd nie. En daar is geen **RSVP** nie, so Sipho sal nie weet hoeveel gaste kom nie.","en":"**When**? There is no date or time. And there is no **RSVP**, so Sipho will not know how many guests are coming."}],"answer":{"af":"Die soort partytjie, die adres, die datum en tyd, en ’n RSVP (teen wanneer en aan wie om te antwoord).","en":"The kind of party, the address, the date and time, and an RSVP (by when and to whom to reply)."}},{"title":{"af":"Skryf ’n boodskap","en":"Write a message"},"problem":{"af":"Die afrigter het om 14:15 vir Liam gebel, maar Liam was nie tuis nie. Die oefening is Donderdag om 15:00 in plaas van Woensdag, en Liam moet sy stewels bring. Skryf Ma se boodskap aan Liam in Engels.","en":"The coach phoned Liam at 14:15, but Liam was not home. Practice is on Thursday at 15:00 instead of Wednesday, and Liam must bring his boots. Write Mom’s message to Liam."},"steps":[{"af":"Begin met vir wie die boodskap is: *Liam,*","en":"Start with who the message is for: *Liam,*"},{"af":"Skryf net die belangrike feite: wie gebel het, die nuwe dag en tyd, en wat hy moet bring.","en":"Write only the important facts: who phoned, the new day and time, and what he must bring."},{"af":"Eindig met van wie dit is en die tyd.","en":"End with who it is from and the time."}],"answer":{"af":"*Liam, Coach phoned. Soccer practice is on Thursday at 15:00, not Wednesday. Bring your boots. – Mom, 14:15*","en":"*Liam, Coach phoned. Soccer practice is on Thursday at 15:00, not Wednesday. Bring your boots. – Mom, 14:15*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar skryf jy jou adres in ’n vriendskaplike brief?","en":"Where do you write your address in a friendly letter?"},"options":[{"af":"regs bo","en":"in the top right corner"},{"af":"links bo","en":"in the top left corner"},{"af":"onderaan, onder jou naam","en":"at the bottom, under your name"},{"af":"direk ná die aanhef","en":"straight after the greeting"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"In ’n vriendskaplike brief staan jou adres regs bo, met die datum daaronder. Die aanhef (*Dear …,*) kom links.","en":"In a friendly letter your address goes in the top right corner, with the date under it. The greeting (*Dear …,*) goes on the left."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter aanhef is die beste vir ’n brief aan jou ouma?","en":"Which greeting is best for a letter to your gran?"},"options":[{"af":"Dear Sir or Madam,","en":"Dear Sir or Madam,"},{"af":"To the Manager,","en":"To the Manager,"},{"af":"Dear Gran,","en":"Dear Gran,"},{"af":"Yours faithfully,","en":"Yours faithfully,"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Jy ken jou ouma goed, so jy gebruik ’n informele aanhef met haar naam: *Dear Gran,*. *Dear Sir or Madam* is vir ’n formele brief aan ’n vreemdeling, en *Yours faithfully* is ’n slot, nie ’n aanhef nie.","en":"You know your gran well, so you use an informal greeting with her name: *Dear Gran,*. *Dear Sir or Madam* is for a formal letter to a stranger, and *Yours faithfully* is a closing, not a greeting."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In ’n resep word die lys kos wat jy nodig het, in Engels die ___ genoem.","en":"In a recipe, the list of food that you need is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["ingredients","bestanddele"],"en":["ingredients"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["method","steps","utensils"],"en":["method","steps","utensils"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die kos wat jy nodig het, is die *ingredients* (bestanddele). Die *method* is die genommerde stappe, en *utensils* is gereedskap soos ’n lepel of mes.","en":"The food you need is the *ingredients*. The *method* is the numbered steps, and *utensils* are tools such as a spoon or a knife."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die stappe in ’n resep moet genommer wees en in die regte volgorde staan.","en":"The steps in a recipe must be numbered and in the correct order."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Genommerde stappe in die regte volgorde help die leser om niks oor te slaan of om te ruil nie.","en":"True. Numbered steps in the correct order help the reader not to skip or swap anything."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter slot pas by ’n vriendskaplike brief?","en":"Which closing fits a friendly letter?"},"options":[{"af":"Yours faithfully,","en":"Yours faithfully,"},{"af":"Dear Thabo,","en":"Dear Thabo,"},{"af":"Subject: party","en":"Subject: party"},{"af":"Lots of love,","en":"Lots of love,"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Lots of love,* is ’n warm, informele slot. *Yours faithfully* is formeel, *Dear Thabo* is ’n aanhef, en *Subject* hoort in ’n e-pos.","en":"*Lots of love,* is a warm, informal closing. *Yours faithfully* is formal, *Dear Thabo* is a greeting, and *Subject* belongs in an email."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is ’n instruksie wat met ’n bevelvorm begin?","en":"Which sentence is an instruction that begins with an imperative verb?"},"options":[{"af":"The flour was mixed with the milk.","en":"The flour was mixed with the milk."},{"af":"Mix the flour and the milk.","en":"Mix the flour and the milk."},{"af":"I like to mix flour.","en":"I like to mix flour."},{"af":"Mixing flour is fun.","en":"Mixing flour is fun."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Mix the flour and the milk* begin met die werkwoord *Mix* en sê vir jou wat om te doen. Die ander sinne vertel net iets; hulle gee nie ’n opdrag nie.","en":"*Mix the flour and the milk* begins with the verb *Mix* and tells you what to do. The other sentences only tell something; they do not give a command."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke teks by sy kenmerk.","en":"Match each text to its feature."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"vriendskaplike brief (*friendly letter*)","en":"friendly letter"},"r":{"af":"adres regs bo, aanhef en slot","en":"address top right, greeting and closing"}},{"l":{"af":"dagboekinskrywing (*diary entry*)","en":"diary entry"},"r":{"af":"privaat skryfwerk oor jou dag en gevoelens","en":"private writing about your day and feelings"}},{"l":{"af":"uitnodiging (*invitation*)","en":"invitation"},"r":{"af":"wat, waar, wanneer en RSVP","en":"what, where, when and RSVP"}},{"l":{"af":"resep (*recipe*)","en":"recipe"},"r":{"af":"bestanddele en genommerde stappe","en":"ingredients and numbered steps"}},{"l":{"af":"e-pos (*email*)","en":"email"},"r":{"af":"’n *To*-adres en ’n onderwerplyn","en":"a *To* address and a subject line"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke teks het sy eie formaat: die brief se adres en aanhef, die dagboek se gevoelens, die uitnodiging se feite, die resep se stappe en die e-pos se onderwerplyn.","en":"Each text has its own format: the letter’s address and greeting, the diary’s feelings, the invitation’s facts, the recipe’s steps and the email’s subject line."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat moet ’n uitnodiging altyd bevat?","en":"What must an invitation always include?"},"options":[{"af":"’n lys bestanddele","en":"a list of ingredients"},{"af":"’n onderwerplyn","en":"a subject line"},{"af":"die datum, tyd en plek van die geleentheid","en":"the date, time and place of the event"},{"af":"die woorde *Dear Diary*","en":"the words *Dear Diary*"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Gaste moet weet **waar** en **wanneer** om te kom, so die datum, tyd en plek is noodsaaklik. Die ander kenmerke hoort by ’n resep, e-pos en dagboek.","en":"Guests must know **where** and **when** to come, so the date, time and place are essential. The other features belong to a recipe, an email and a diary."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Maak ’n instruksie: *You must stir the soup.* → ___ *the soup.*","en":"Make it an instruction: *You must stir the soup.* → ___ *the soup.*"},"answers":{"af":["Stir"],"en":["Stir"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Stirs","Stirring","Stirred"],"en":["Stirs","Stirring","Stirred"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Instruksie begin met die basiese vorm van die werkwoord (bevelvorm): *Stir the soup.* Laat *You must* weg.","en":"An instruction begins with the base form of the verb (imperative): *Stir the soup.* Leave out *You must*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe word ’n dagboekinskrywing gewoonlik geskryf?","en":"How is a diary entry usually written?"},"options":[{"af":"in die eerste persoon (*I*) en meestal in die verlede tyd","en":"in the first person (*I*) and mostly in the past tense"},{"af":"in die derde persoon (*he/she*) en in die toekomende tyd","en":"in the third person (*he/she*) and in the future tense"},{"af":"in genommerde stappe met bevelvorme","en":"in numbered steps with imperative verbs"},{"af":"in baie formele taal vir ’n vreemdeling","en":"in very formal language for a stranger"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"In ’n dagboek skryf jy oor wat **jy** vandag beleef het, dus *I* en meestal die verlede tyd: *Today I went …*. Genommerde stappe hoort by instruksies.","en":"In a diary you write about what **you** experienced today, so *I* and mostly the past tense: *Today I went …*. Numbered steps belong to instructions."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In ’n brief aan jou beste maat eindig jy met *Yours faithfully* en teken jy jou volle naam en van.","en":"In a letter to your best friend you end with *Yours faithfully* and sign your full name and surname."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. *Yours faithfully* is ’n formele slot. Aan ’n maat skryf jy iets soos *Your friend,* of *Lots of love,* en net jou voornaam.","en":"False. *Yours faithfully* is a formal closing. To a friend you write something like *Your friend,* or *Lots of love,* and only your first name."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken *RSVP* op ’n uitnodiging?","en":"What does *RSVP* on an invitation mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Bring ’n geskenk","en":"Bring a present"},{"af":"Die partytjie begin nou","en":"The party starts now"},{"af":"Trek ’n kostuum aan","en":"Wear a costume"},{"af":"Antwoord asseblief","en":"Please reply"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*RSVP* beteken ‘antwoord asseblief’: laat die persoon weet of jy kom, sodat hulle weet vir hoeveel gaste om voor te berei.","en":"*RSVP* means ‘please reply’: let the person know whether you are coming, so that they know how many guests to prepare for."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In ’n e-pos sê die ___ *line* vir die leser in ’n paar woorde waaroor die e-pos gaan.","en":"In an email the ___ line tells the reader in a few words what the email is about."},"answers":{"af":["subject"],"en":["subject"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["greeting","address","closing"],"en":["greeting","address","closing"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die *subject line* (onderwerplyn) gee ’n kort opsomming, bv. *Subject: Netball practice on Friday*. Die leser weet dan waaroor dit gaan voordat hy dit oopmaak.","en":"The *subject line* gives a short summary, e.g. *Subject: Netball practice on Friday*. Then the reader knows what it is about before opening it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is fout met hierdie boodskap? *Liam, someone phoned. Phone back.*","en":"What is wrong with this message? *Liam, someone phoned. Phone back.*"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is heeltemal te lank.","en":"It is far too long."},{"af":"Dit sê nie wie gebel het of wat hulle wou hê nie.","en":"It does not say who phoned or what they wanted."},{"af":"Dit begin met die persoon se naam.","en":"It starts with the person’s name."},{"af":"Dit gebruik ’n bevelvorm.","en":"It uses an imperative verb."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Boodskap moet kort wees, maar die belangrike feite moet daarin staan: wie gebel het, wat die boodskap is, van wie die briefie is en hoe laat. Om met die naam te begin, is juis reg.","en":"A message must be short, but it must contain the important facts: who phoned, what the message is, who the note is from and what time. Starting with the name is actually correct."}}]},{"id":"eng5-t4-summary-paragraphs","title":{"af":"Opsomming en paragrawe skryf","en":"Summaries and writing paragraphs"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal ’n Engelse opsomming in puntvorm binne ’n woordlimiet kan skryf, ’n paragraaf met ’n kernsin en ondersteunende sinne kan bou en ’n verhalende of beskrywende opstel kan beplan, skryf, redigeer en proeflees.","en":"You will be able to write a summary in point form within a word limit, build a paragraph with a topic sentence and supporting sentences, and plan, write, edit and proofread a narrative or descriptive essay."},"summary":{"af":"## Lees die leesstuk\n\n**Saving Water at Home**\n\nWater is precious in South Africa, because many parts of our country get little rain. Every family can help to save water at home. First, turn off the tap while you brush your teeth. A running tap wastes many litres of water every minute. Next, take a short shower instead of a bath. You can also collect rainwater in a tank or a bucket and use it to water the garden. Plants such as aloes and spekboom need very little water, so they are a good choice for a garden. Finally, fix dripping taps quickly. Even a small drip, drip, drip can waste many litres of water in a day.\n\n## ’n Opsomming in puntvorm\n\n’n **Opsomming** (*summary*) is ’n kort weergawe van ’n teks met net die **hoofpunte**. So skryf jy een:\n\n1. Lees die teks twee keer en onderstreep die hoofpunte.\n2. Skryf elke hoofpunt as ’n kort, volledige sin, in **jou eie woorde**, en nommer dit.\n3. Laat weg: **voorbeelde**, **herhaling**, beskrywings, direkte rede en jou eie mening.\n4. Tel jou woorde en bly binne die **woordlimiet**. Skryf die getal woorde aan die einde.\n\n**Opsomming in hoogstens 40 woorde:**\n\n1. *South Africa gets little rain, so we must save water.*\n2. *Turn off the tap while brushing your teeth.*\n3. *Take short showers instead of baths.*\n4. *Water the garden with rainwater.*\n5. *Plant water-wise plants.*\n6. *Fix dripping taps.*\n\n*(35 words)* Let op: *aloes and spekboom* is voorbeelde, en *a running tap wastes many litres* is ’n detail. Albei is weggelaat.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie hele sinne uit die teks oorskryf nie. Dan sluip die voorbeelde en ekstra woorde in en gaan jy oor die woordlimiet.\n\n## ’n Goeie paragraaf\n\n’n **Paragraaf** is ’n groep sinne oor **een hoofgedagte**.\n\n- Die **kernsin** (*topic sentence*) staan gewoonlik eerste en sê waaroor die paragraaf gaan.\n- **Ondersteunende sinne** (*supporting sentences*) gee besonderhede, voorbeelde en redes.\n- ’n **Slotsin** rond die paragraaf soms af.\n\n*Our school garden is a busy place.* (kernsin) *Every morning the Grade 5 learners water the spinach and carrots. Bees buzz around the yellow flowers, and mousebirds hide in the hedge.* (ondersteunende sinne) *There is always something happening in our garden!* (slotsin)\n\n## Verhalend en beskrywend\n\n- ’n **Verhalende** opstel (*narrative*) vertel ’n storie met ’n begin, ’n probleem en ’n einde, meestal in die verlede tyd.\n- ’n **Beskrywende** opstel (*descriptive*) skilder ’n prent met woorde. Gebruik jou **sintuie**: wat sien, hoor, ruik, proe en voel jy? *The market was noisy and colourful. Sellers shouted prices and ripe mangoes smelt sweet.*\n\n## Die skryfproses en verbindingswoorde\n\n1. **Beplan** (*plan*): maak ’n **breinkaart** (*mind map*) met die onderwerp in die middel en idees op die takke.\n2. **Skryf ’n konsep** (*draft*): skryf jou idees in sinne en paragrawe.\n3. **Redigeer** (*edit*): verbeter jou idees, sinne en woordkeuse.\n4. **Proeflees** (*proofread*): verbeter spelling, leestekens en hoofletters.\n5. **Finale weergawe** (*final copy*): skryf dit netjies oor.\n\n**Verbindingswoorde** (*linking words*) wys die volgorde: *first, then, next, after that, finally*.\n\n> **Onthou:** Een paragraaf = een hoofgedagte. Begin ’n nuwe paragraaf wanneer jy oor iets nuuts skryf.","en":"## Read the passage\n\n**Saving Water at Home**\n\nWater is precious in South Africa, because many parts of our country get little rain. Every family can help to save water at home. First, turn off the tap while you brush your teeth. A running tap wastes many litres of water every minute. Next, take a short shower instead of a bath. You can also collect rainwater in a tank or a bucket and use it to water the garden. Plants such as aloes and spekboom need very little water, so they are a good choice for a garden. Finally, fix dripping taps quickly. Even a small drip, drip, drip can waste many litres of water in a day.\n\n## A summary in point form\n\nA **summary** is a short version of a text with only the **main points**. This is how you write one:\n\n1. Read the text twice and underline the main points.\n2. Write each main point as a short, complete sentence in **your own words**, and number it.\n3. Leave out **examples**, **repetition**, descriptions, direct speech and your own opinion.\n4. Count your words and stay within the **word limit**. Write the number of words at the end.\n\n**Summary in no more than 40 words:**\n\n1. *South Africa gets little rain, so we must save water.*\n2. *Turn off the tap while brushing your teeth.*\n3. *Take short showers instead of baths.*\n4. *Water the garden with rainwater.*\n5. *Plant water-wise plants.*\n6. *Fix dripping taps.*\n\n*(35 words)* Notice: *aloes and spekboom* are examples, and *a running tap wastes many litres* is a detail. Both were left out.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not copy whole sentences from the text. Then the examples and extra words creep in and you go over the word limit.\n\n## A good paragraph\n\nA **paragraph** is a group of sentences about **one main idea**.\n\n- The **topic sentence** usually comes first and says what the paragraph is about.\n- **Supporting sentences** give details, examples and reasons.\n- A **concluding sentence** sometimes rounds the paragraph off.\n\n*Our school garden is a busy place.* (topic sentence) *Every morning the Grade 5 learners water the spinach and carrots. Bees buzz around the yellow flowers, and mousebirds hide in the hedge.* (supporting sentences) *There is always something happening in our garden!* (concluding sentence)\n\n## Narrative and descriptive\n\n- A **narrative** essay tells a story with a beginning, a problem and an ending, mostly in the past tense.\n- A **descriptive** essay paints a picture with words. Use your **senses**: what do you see, hear, smell, taste and feel? *The market was noisy and colourful. Sellers shouted prices and ripe mangoes smelt sweet.*\n\n## The writing process and linking words\n\n1. **Plan**: make a **mind map** with the topic in the middle and ideas on the branches.\n2. **Write a draft**: put your ideas into sentences and paragraphs.\n3. **Edit**: improve your ideas, sentences and choice of words.\n4. **Proofread**: correct spelling, punctuation and capital letters.\n5. **Final copy**: write it out neatly.\n\n**Linking words** show the order: *first, then, next, after that, finally*.\n\n> **Remember:** One paragraph = one main idea. Start a new paragraph when you write about something new."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Opsomming (*summary*)","en":"Summary"},"def":{"af":"’n Kort weergawe van ’n teks met net die hoofpunte, in jou eie woorde.","en":"A short version of a text with only the main points, in your own words."}},{"term":{"af":"Puntvorm (*point form*)","en":"Point form"},"def":{"af":"Elke hoofpunt word as ’n aparte, genommerde kort sin geskryf.","en":"Each main point is written as a separate, numbered short sentence."}},{"term":{"af":"Woordlimiet (*word limit*)","en":"Word limit"},"def":{"af":"Die meeste woorde wat jy mag gebruik, bv. *no more than 40 words*.","en":"The most words you may use, e.g. *no more than 40 words*."}},{"term":{"af":"Kernsin (*topic sentence*)","en":"Topic sentence"},"def":{"af":"Die sin, gewoonlik eerste, wat sê waaroor ’n paragraaf gaan.","en":"The sentence, usually first, that says what a paragraph is about."}},{"term":{"af":"Ondersteunende sinne (*supporting sentences*)","en":"Supporting sentences"},"def":{"af":"Sinne wat besonderhede, voorbeelde of redes oor die kernsin gee.","en":"Sentences that give details, examples or reasons about the topic sentence."}},{"term":{"af":"Verhalende opstel (*narrative essay*)","en":"Narrative essay"},"def":{"af":"’n Opstel wat ’n storie vertel met ’n begin, probleem en einde.","en":"An essay that tells a story with a beginning, a problem and an ending."}},{"term":{"af":"Beskrywende opstel (*descriptive essay*)","en":"Descriptive essay"},"def":{"af":"’n Opstel wat met die sintuie ’n prent met woorde skilder.","en":"An essay that uses the senses to paint a picture with words."}},{"term":{"af":"Breinkaart (*mind map*)","en":"Mind map"},"def":{"af":"’n Beplanningskets met die onderwerp in die middel en idees op takke rondom dit.","en":"A planning drawing with the topic in the middle and ideas on branches around it."}},{"term":{"af":"Proeflees (*proofread*)","en":"Proofread"},"def":{"af":"Om jou skryfwerk na te gaan vir foute in spelling, leestekens en hoofletters.","en":"To check your writing for mistakes in spelling, punctuation and capital letters."}},{"term":{"af":"Verbindingswoorde (*linking words*)","en":"Linking words"},"def":{"af":"Woorde wat sinne en idees verbind en die volgorde wys, soos *first, then, finally*.","en":"Words that join sentences and ideas and show the order, such as *first, then, finally*."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Skryf ’n opsomming in puntvorm","en":"Write a summary in point form"},"problem":{"af":"Som *Saving Water at Home* in puntvorm op. Gebruik hoogstens 40 woorde.","en":"Summarise *Saving Water at Home* in point form. Use no more than 40 words."},"steps":[{"af":"Vind die hoofpunte: die rede om water te spaar, en vyf maniere: draai die kraan toe, stort kort, gebruik reënwater, plant waterwyse plante en maak lekkende krane reg.","en":"Find the main points: the reason to save water, and five ways: turn off the tap, take short showers, use rainwater, grow water-wise plants and fix dripping taps."},{"af":"Laat voorbeelde en besonderhede weg: *aloes and spekboom*, *a tank or a bucket*, *drip, drip, drip* en hoeveel liter vermors word.","en":"Leave out examples and details: *aloes and spekboom*, *a tank or a bucket*, *drip, drip, drip* and how many litres are wasted."},{"af":"Skryf elke punt as ’n kort, genommerde sin in jou eie woorde.","en":"Write each point as a short, numbered sentence in your own words."},{"af":"Tel die woorde: 10 + 8 + 6 + 5 + 3 + 3 = 35. Dit is binne die limiet van 40.","en":"Count the words: 10 + 8 + 6 + 5 + 3 + 3 = 35. That is within the limit of 40."}],"answer":{"af":"1. *South Africa gets little rain, so we must save water.* 2. *Turn off the tap while brushing your teeth.* 3. *Take short showers instead of baths.* 4. *Water the garden with rainwater.* 5. *Plant water-wise plants.* 6. *Fix dripping taps.* (35 woorde)","en":"1. *South Africa gets little rain, so we must save water.* 2. *Turn off the tap while brushing your teeth.* 3. *Take short showers instead of baths.* 4. *Water the garden with rainwater.* 5. *Plant water-wise plants.* 6. *Fix dripping taps.* (35 words)"}},{"title":{"af":"Vind die kernsin","en":"Find the topic sentence"},"problem":{"af":"Lees: *Lerato loves Saturdays. She sleeps late and eats pancakes for breakfast. In the afternoon she plays netball with her friends.* Wat is die kernsin, en wat doen die ander sinne?","en":"Read: *Lerato loves Saturdays. She sleeps late and eats pancakes for breakfast. In the afternoon she plays netball with her friends.* What is the topic sentence, and what do the other sentences do?"},"steps":[{"af":"Vra: Watter sin sê waaroor die hele paragraaf gaan? *Lerato loves Saturdays.*","en":"Ask: Which sentence says what the whole paragraph is about? *Lerato loves Saturdays.*"},{"af":"Die ander twee sinne gee voorbeelde van waarom sy Saterdae geniet: laat slaap, pannekoek, netbal.","en":"The other two sentences give examples of why she enjoys Saturdays: sleeping late, pancakes, netball."}],"answer":{"af":"Kernsin: *Lerato loves Saturdays.* Die ander sinne is ondersteunende sinne wat besonderhede gee.","en":"Topic sentence: *Lerato loves Saturdays.* The other sentences are supporting sentences that give details."}},{"title":{"af":"Gebruik verbindingswoorde","en":"Use linking words"},"problem":{"af":"Verbeter die paragraaf met verbindingswoorde: *We packed the car. We drove to the beach. We built a sandcastle. We went home.*","en":"Improve the paragraph with linking words: *We packed the car. We drove to the beach. We built a sandcastle. We went home.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Die sinne begin almal met *We* en klink eentonig. Sit ’n verbindingswoord voor elke sin.","en":"The sentences all begin with *We* and sound boring. Put a linking word in front of each sentence."},{"af":"Kies woorde wat die volgorde wys: *First* vir die eerste stap, *Then* en *Next* vir die middel, *Finally* vir die laaste.","en":"Choose words that show the order: *First* for the first step, *Then* and *Next* for the middle, *Finally* for the last."},{"af":"Sit ’n komma ná *First, Next* en *Finally* aan die begin van ’n sin.","en":"Put a comma after *First, Next* and *Finally* at the start of a sentence."}],"answer":{"af":"*First, we packed the car. Then we drove to the beach. Next, we built a sandcastle. Finally, we went home.*","en":"*First, we packed the car. Then we drove to the beach. Next, we built a sandcastle. Finally, we went home.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Beplan ’n beskrywende paragraaf","en":"Plan a descriptive paragraph"},"problem":{"af":"Beplan met ’n breinkaart ’n beskrywende paragraaf oor *A rainy day* en skryf ’n kernsin.","en":"Use a mind map to plan a descriptive paragraph about *A rainy day* and write a topic sentence."},"steps":[{"af":"Skryf *A rainy day* in die middel van jou bladsy en trek vyf takke: *see, hear, smell, taste, feel*.","en":"Write *A rainy day* in the middle of your page and draw five branches: *see, hear, smell, taste, feel*."},{"af":"Skryf idees op elke tak: *grey clouds* (sien), *rain on the roof* (hoor), *wet soil* (ruik), *hot soup* (proe), *cold feet* (voel).","en":"Write ideas on each branch: *grey clouds* (see), *rain on the roof* (hear), *wet soil* (smell), *hot soup* (taste), *cold feet* (feel)."},{"af":"Skryf ’n kernsin wat die hoofgedagte gee, en gebruik dan die takke vir jou ondersteunende sinne.","en":"Write a topic sentence that gives the main idea, then use the branches for your supporting sentences."}],"answer":{"af":"Byvoorbeeld: *A rainy day at home is cosy and quiet.* Daarna volg sinne oor elke sintuig.","en":"For example: *A rainy day at home is cosy and quiet.* Sentences about each sense follow."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat moet jy uit ’n opsomming **weglaat**?","en":"What must you **leave out** of a summary?"},"options":[{"af":"die hoofpunte","en":"the main points"},{"af":"’n nommer vir elke punt","en":"a number for each point"},{"af":"voorbeelde en herhaling","en":"examples and repetition"},{"af":"die belangrikste feite","en":"the most important facts"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Opsomming hou net die hoofpunte. Voorbeelde (soos *aloes and spekboom*) en herhaling maak dit net langer.","en":"A summary keeps only the main points. Examples (like *aloes and spekboom*) and repetition only make it longer."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die kernsin sê vir die leser waaroor die paragraaf gaan.","en":"The topic sentence tells the reader what the paragraph is about."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die kernsin gee die hoofgedagte, en die ondersteunende sinne gee besonderhede daaroor.","en":"True. The topic sentence gives the main idea, and the supporting sentences give details about it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is die beste kernsin vir ’n paragraaf oor waterbesparing tuis?","en":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for a paragraph about saving water at home?"},"options":[{"af":"Every family can help to save water at home.","en":"Every family can help to save water at home."},{"af":"Aloes need very little water.","en":"Aloes need very little water."},{"af":"Drip, drip, drip!","en":"Drip, drip, drip!"},{"af":"My gran has a green bucket.","en":"My gran has a green bucket."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Hierdie sin gee die hoofgedagte van die hele paragraaf. Die ander sinne is klein besonderhede wat hoogstens ’n ondersteunende sin kan wees.","en":"This sentence gives the main idea of the whole paragraph. The other sentences are small details that could at most be a supporting sentence."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Vinnige beplanningskets met die onderwerp in die middel en idees op takke, is ’n *mind* ___.","en":"A quick planning drawing with the topic in the middle and ideas on branches is a *mind* ___."},"answers":{"af":["map"],"en":["map"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["list","book","draft"],"en":["list","book","draft"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n *Mind map* (breinkaart) help jou om idees te versamel voordat jy begin skryf. ’n *Draft* is jou eerste geskrewe weergawe.","en":"A *mind map* helps you to collect ideas before you start writing. A *draft* is your first written version."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe moet die punte van ’n opsomming geskryf word?","en":"How must the points of a summary be written?"},"options":[{"af":"woord vir woord uit die teks oorgeskryf","en":"copied word for word from the text"},{"af":"in jou eie woorde","en":"in your own words"},{"af":"met jou eie mening bygevoeg","en":"with your own opinion added"},{"af":"as een lang sin","en":"as one long sentence"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Jy wys dat jy die teks verstaan as jy die hoofpunte in jou eie woorde skryf, elkeen as ’n kort, genommerde sin.","en":"You show that you understand the text when you write the main points in your own words, each as a short, numbered sentence."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter verbindingswoord wys die **laaste** stap?","en":"Which linking word shows the **last** step?"},"options":[{"af":"First","en":"First"},{"af":"Next","en":"Next"},{"af":"Then","en":"Then"},{"af":"Finally","en":"Finally"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Finally* beteken *laastens* of *uiteindelik*. *First* begin die volgorde, en *Next* en *Then* hoort in die middel.","en":"*Finally* means *last of all*. *First* starts the order, and *Next* and *Then* belong in the middle."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke stap van die skryfproses by wat jy doen.","en":"Match each step of the writing process to what you do."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"beplan (*plan*)","en":"plan"},"r":{"af":"maak ’n breinkaart van jou idees","en":"make a mind map of your ideas"}},{"l":{"af":"konsep (*draft*)","en":"draft"},"r":{"af":"skryf ’n eerste weergawe in sinne","en":"write a first version in sentences"}},{"l":{"af":"redigeer (*edit*)","en":"edit"},"r":{"af":"verbeter idees, sinne en woordkeuse","en":"improve ideas, sentences and word choice"}},{"l":{"af":"proeflees (*proofread*)","en":"proofread"},"r":{"af":"verbeter spelling, leestekens en hoofletters","en":"correct spelling, punctuation and capitals"}},{"l":{"af":"finale weergawe (*final copy*)","en":"final copy"},"r":{"af":"skryf alles netjies oor","en":"write everything out neatly"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die skryfproses gaan in volgorde: beplan, konsep, redigeer (inhoud beter maak), proeflees (foute regmaak) en die finale weergawe.","en":"The writing process goes in order: plan, draft, edit (make the content better), proofread (fix mistakes) and final copy."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jou opsomming mag hoogstens 40 woorde hê, maar jy het 52. Wat doen jy?","en":"Your summary may have no more than 40 words, but you have 52. What do you do?"},"options":[{"af":"Laat voorbeelde en herhaalde idees weg.","en":"Leave out examples and repeated ideas."},{"af":"Voeg nog punte by.","en":"Add more points."},{"af":"Skryf kleiner.","en":"Write smaller."},{"af":"Los dit so; 52 is naby genoeg.","en":"Leave it; 52 is close enough."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Jy moet binne die woordlimiet bly, anders verloor jy punte. Sny eers voorbeelde, herhaling en onnodige beskrywende woorde uit.","en":"You must stay within the word limit, or you lose marks. First cut examples, repetition and unnecessary describing words."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vul die verbindingswoord in soos in die leesstuk: ___, *take a short shower instead of a bath.*","en":"Fill in the linking word as in the passage: ___, *take a short shower instead of a bath.*"},"answers":{"af":["Next"],"en":["Next"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Finally","First","Because"],"en":["Finally","First","Because"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die leesstuk gebruik *First* (kraan), dan *Next* (stort) en laastens *Finally* (lekkende krane). Die stort is die tweede wenk, so dit is *Next*.","en":"The passage uses *First* (tap), then *Next* (shower) and last *Finally* (dripping taps). The shower is the second tip, so it is *Next*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In ’n opsomming moet jy jou eie mening byvoeg.","en":"In a summary you should add your own opinion."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Opsomming gee net die hoofpunte van die teks. Jou eie mening, soos *I think this is a good idea*, hoort nie daarin nie.","en":"False. A summary gives only the main points of the text. Your own opinion, such as *I think this is a good idea*, does not belong in it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die kernsin is *Our school garden is a busy place.* Watter sin is ’n goeie **ondersteunende sin**?","en":"The topic sentence is *Our school garden is a busy place.* Which sentence is a good **supporting sentence**?"},"options":[{"af":"My uncle drives a taxi to Durban.","en":"My uncle drives a taxi to Durban."},{"af":"The school library has new books.","en":"The school library has new books."},{"af":"Every morning the Grade 5 learners water the spinach.","en":"Every morning the Grade 5 learners water the spinach."},{"af":"Our school hall needs a new roof.","en":"Our school hall needs a new roof."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Ondersteunende sin moet oor die hoofgedagte gaan – die besige tuin. Om die spinasie nat te maak, wys wat in die tuin gebeur. Die ander sinne gaan oor iets anders.","en":"A supporting sentence must be about the main idea – the busy garden. Watering the spinach shows what happens in the garden. The other sentences are about something else."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat doen ’n **beskrywende** paragraaf?","en":"What does a **descriptive** paragraph do?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit vertel gebeure in volgorde, met ’n probleem en ’n einde.","en":"It tells events in order, with a problem and an ending."},{"af":"Dit skilder ’n prent met woorde deur die sintuie te gebruik.","en":"It paints a picture with words by using the senses."},{"af":"Dit gee genommerde stappe met bevelvorme.","en":"It gives numbered steps with imperative verbs."},{"af":"Dit probeer jou oorreed om iets te koop.","en":"It tries to persuade you to buy something."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Beskrywende paragraaf laat die leser sien, hoor, ruik, proe en voel. ’n Storie met ’n probleem en einde is verhalend.","en":"A descriptive paragraph lets the reader see, hear, smell, taste and feel. A story with a problem and an ending is narrative."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel woorde is in hierdie opsommingspunt? *Fix dripping taps quickly.* → ___","en":"How many words are in this summary point? *Fix dripping taps quickly.* → ___"},"answers":{"af":["4","vier"],"en":["4","four"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3","5","6"],"en":["3","5","6"]}},"explain":{"af":"Tel elke woord: *Fix* (1) *dripping* (2) *taps* (3) *quickly* (4). Die punt aan die einde is nie ’n woord nie.","en":"Count each word: *Fix* (1) *dripping* (2) *taps* (3) *quickly* (4). The full stop at the end is not a word."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n **hoofpunt** uit die leesstuk, en nie ’n voorbeeld of detail nie?","en":"Which one is a **main point** from the passage, and not an example or a detail?"},"options":[{"af":"Aloes and spekboom are good examples.","en":"Aloes and spekboom are good examples."},{"af":"Drip, drip, drip!","en":"Drip, drip, drip!"},{"af":"A running tap wastes many litres every minute.","en":"A running tap wastes many litres every minute."},{"af":"Collect rainwater to water the garden.","en":"Collect rainwater to water the garden."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Om reënwater vir die tuin op te vang, is een van die maniere om water te spaar – ’n hoofpunt. Die ander is voorbeelde, ’n klankwoord of ’n ekstra detail.","en":"Collecting rainwater for the garden is one of the ways to save water – a main point. The others are examples, a sound word or an extra detail."}}]}]}]},"wiskunde":{"id":"wiskunde","grade":5,"name":{"af":"Wiskunde","en":"Mathematics"},"short":{"af":"Wisk","en":"Maths"},"icon":"📐","color":"#2f6df6","intro":{"af":"Wiskunde in Graad 5 bou jou getalbegrip met telgetalle tot 999 999, die vier bewerkings en gewone breuke, en werk ook met patrone, meetkunde (2D-vorms, 3D-voorwerpe en simmetrie), meting, tyd, geld en data. Die Novembereksamen dek die werk van die hele jaar en word sonder ’n sakrekenaar geskryf, dus moet jy vinnig en akkuraat met die hand en in jou kop kan reken en woordprobleme stap vir stap kan oplos.","en":"Mathematics in Grade 5 builds your number sense with whole numbers up to 999 999, the four operations and common fractions, and also covers patterns, geometry (2D shapes, 3D objects and symmetry), measurement, time, money and data. The November exam covers the whole year’s work and is written without a calculator, so you must be able to calculate quickly and accurately by hand and in your head and solve word problems step by step."},"examTips":[{"af":"Ken jou tafels tot 10 × 10 uit jou kop – in die eksamen is daar geen sakrekenaar nie, en vermenigvuldiging en deling hang van jou tafels af.","en":"Know your times tables up to 10 × 10 by heart – there is no calculator in the exam, and multiplication and division depend on your tables."},{"af":"Skat eers deur af te rond, en kontroleer jou antwoord met die inverse bewerking (optel vir aftrek, vermenigvuldig vir deel).","en":"Estimate first by rounding off, and check your answer with the inverse operation (addition for subtraction, multiplication for division)."},{"af":"Wys al jou stappe en bewerkings netjies – onderwysers kan dikwels punte vir die regte metode gee, selfs as die eindantwoord verkeerd is.","en":"Show all your steps and working neatly – teachers can often give marks for the correct method, even if the final answer is wrong."},{"af":"Lees woordprobleme twee keer, onderstreep die vraag en skryf die antwoord in ’n volsin met die regte eenheid (cm, kg, ml, minute of R).","en":"Read word problems twice, underline the question and write the answer in a full sentence with the correct unit (cm, kg, ml, minutes or R)."},{"af":"Begin met die vrae wat jy goed ken, hou die tyd dop en gaan aan die einde terug na die moeilike vrae om alles te kontroleer.","en":"Start with the questions you know well, keep an eye on the time and go back to the difficult questions at the end to check everything."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"DBE Reënboog-werkboeke (Graad 5)","en":"DBE Rainbow Workbooks (Grade 5)"},"url":"https://www.education.gov.za/Curriculum/Workbooks.aspx","note":{"af":"Gratis amptelike werkboeke volgens CAPS, in Afrikaans en Engels.","en":"Free official CAPS workbooks, in English and Afrikaans."}},{"title":{"af":"Siyavula: oop handboeke en oefening","en":"Siyavula: open textbooks and practice"},"url":"https://www.siyavula.com","note":{"af":"Gratis oop handboeke en oefenvrae.","en":"Free open textbooks and practice questions."}}],"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Getalle, bewerkings en verwantskappe","en":"Numbers, operations and relationships"},"topics":[{"id":"w5-t1-telgetalle","title":{"af":"Telgetalle: plekwaarde, vergelyk en afrond","en":"Whole numbers: place value, comparing and rounding"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal getalle tot 999 999 kan lees en in woorde skryf, die plekwaarde en waarde van elke syfer kan gee, getalle kan vergelyk en orden, en tot die naaste 5; 10; 100 en 1 000 kan afrond.","en":"You will be able to read numbers up to 999 999 and write them in words, give the place value and value of each digit, compare and order numbers, and round off to the nearest 5, 10, 100 and 1 000."},"summary":{"af":"## Groot getalle lees en skryf\n\nIn Graad 5 werk jy met **telgetalle** tot **999 999** – getalle met tot **6 syfers**. Ons los ’n **spasie** tussen die duisende en die honderde, sodat die getal maklik lees: 345 678, nie 345678 nie.\n\nLees ’n groot getal in twee dele: eers die deel vóór die spasie (dit sê hoeveel **duisend**), en dan die res.\n\n- 345 678 → driehonderd vyf-en-veertigduisend seshonderd agt-en-sewentig\n- 72 486 → twee-en-sewentigduisend vierhonderd ses-en-tagtig\n\n## Plekwaarde\n\nElke syfer staan in ’n kolom. Die kolom gee die syfer sy **plekwaarde**. Van regs na links word elke kolom **10 keer groter**.\n\n| HD | TD | D | H | T | E |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 |\n\n(HD = honderdduisende, TD = tienduisende, D = duisende, H = honderde, T = tiene, E = ene)\n\nIn 345 678 staan die 3 by die honderdduisende, dus is sy **waarde** 300 000. Die 5 staan by die duisende en is 5 000 werd. Die 7 is net 70 werd.\n\nAs jy ’n getal as die som van die waardes van sy syfers skryf, gebruik jy **uitgebreide notasie**:\n\n345 678 = 300 000 + 40 000 + 5 000 + 600 + 70 + 8\n\nAs ’n kolom leeg is, skryf ons ’n **0 as plekhouer**: 305 040 = 300 000 + 5 000 + 40. Sonder die nulle sou dit 354 wees – ’n heeltemal ander getal!\n\n> **Onthou:** Die **plekwaarde** is die kolom waarin ’n syfer staan; die **waarde** is hoeveel die syfer daar werd is. In 52 000 is die 5 vyftigduisend werd, maar in 25 000 net vyfduisend.\n\n## Vergelyk en orden\n\n1. Tel die syfers. Die getal met **meer syfers** is groter: 100 000 > 99 999.\n2. Het die getalle ewe veel syfers, vergelyk hulle **van links af**, kolom vir kolom, totdat die syfers verskil.\n3. Voorbeeld: 486 390 en 486 309. Die HD, TD, D en H is dieselfde. By die tiene is 9 > 0, dus is 486 390 > 486 309.\n\nOns gebruik die tekens **<** (kleiner as), **>** (groter as) en **=** (gelyk aan). Die oop kant van die teken wys altyd na die groter getal.\n\n- **Stygende orde:** van klein na groot.\n- **Dalende orde:** van groot na klein.\n\n## Afrond\n\nAs ons **afrond**, vervang ons ’n getal met ’n getal naby daaraan wat makliker is om mee te werk. Kyk na die syfer **net regs** van die plek waarheen jy afrond:\n\n- 0; 1; 2; 3 of 4: rond **af** (die syfer bly dieselfde).\n- 5; 6; 7; 8 of 9: rond **op** (die syfer word een meer).\n\nAl die syfers regs daarvan word nulle.\n\n| Getal | Naaste 10 | Naaste 100 | Naaste 1 000 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 4 386 | 4 390 | 4 400 | 4 000 |\n| 27 650 | 27 650 | 27 700 | 28 000 |\n\nOm tot die **naaste 5** af te rond, kies jy die naaste getal wat op 0 of 5 eindig: 43 → 45; 41 → 40; 48 → 50 en 1 237 → 1 235.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Tot die naaste 100 kyk jy net na die **tiene**-syfer. 4 349 word 4 300, want die tiene-syfer is 4. Moenie eers 4 350 maak en dan na 4 400 opspring nie!\n\n## Ewe en onewe getalle\n\n- **Ewe** getalle eindig op 0; 2; 4; 6 of 8. Hulle kan presies in twee gelyke groepe verdeel word.\n- **Onewe** getalle eindig op 1; 3; 5; 7 of 9.\n\nNet die **laaste syfer** tel: 246 803 is onewe, al is al die ander syfers ewe.\n\n## Tel in veelvoude\n\nJy kan vorentoe of agtertoe tel in treë van 2; 5; 10; 25; 50; 100 of 1 000. Die getalle wat jy sê, is **veelvoude** van die trede.\n\n- Vorentoe in treë van 25: 1 450; 1 475; 1 500; 1 525\n- Agtertoe in treë van 1 000: 63 200; 62 200; 61 200; 60 200\n\nKyk watter kolom verander: as jy in treë van 1 000 tel, verander die duisende-syfer elke keer.","en":"## Reading and writing big numbers\n\nIn Grade 5 you work with **whole numbers** up to **999 999** – numbers with up to **6 digits**. We leave a **space** between the thousands and the hundreds so that the number is easy to read: 345 678, not 345678.\n\nRead a big number in two parts: first the part before the space (it tells you how many **thousand**), and then the rest.\n\n- 345 678 → three hundred and forty-five thousand six hundred and seventy-eight\n- 72 486 → seventy-two thousand four hundred and eighty-six\n\n## Place value\n\nEvery digit stands in a column. The column gives the digit its **place value**. From right to left, every column is **10 times bigger**.\n\n| HTh | TTh | Th | H | T | U |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 |\n\n(HTh = hundred thousands, TTh = ten thousands, Th = thousands, H = hundreds, T = tens, U = units)\n\nIn 345 678 the 3 is in the hundred thousands, so its **value** is 300 000. The 5 is in the thousands and is worth 5 000. The 7 is worth only 70.\n\nWhen you write a number as the sum of the values of its digits, you use **expanded notation**:\n\n345 678 = 300 000 + 40 000 + 5 000 + 600 + 70 + 8\n\nWhen a column is empty, we write a **0 as a placeholder**: 305 040 = 300 000 + 5 000 + 40. Without the zeros it would be 354 – a completely different number!\n\n> **Remember:** The **place value** is the column a digit stands in; the **value** is how much the digit is worth there. In 52 000 the 5 is worth fifty thousand, but in 25 000 only five thousand.\n\n## Comparing and ordering\n\n1. Count the digits. The number with **more digits** is bigger: 100 000 > 99 999.\n2. If the numbers have the same number of digits, compare them **from the left**, column by column, until the digits are different.\n3. Example: 486 390 and 486 309. The HTh, TTh, Th and H are the same. In the tens, 9 > 0, so 486 390 > 486 309.\n\nWe use the signs **<** (less than), **>** (greater than) and **=** (equal to). The open side of the sign always points to the bigger number.\n\n- **Ascending order:** from small to big.\n- **Descending order:** from big to small.\n\n## Rounding off\n\nWhen we **round off**, we replace a number with a number close to it that is easier to work with. Look at the digit **just to the right** of the place you are rounding to:\n\n- 0, 1, 2, 3 or 4: round **down** (the digit stays the same).\n- 5, 6, 7, 8 or 9: round **up** (the digit becomes one more).\n\nAll the digits to the right of it become zeros.\n\n| Number | Nearest 10 | Nearest 100 | Nearest 1 000 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 4 386 | 4 390 | 4 400 | 4 000 |\n| 27 650 | 27 650 | 27 700 | 28 000 |\n\nTo round off to the **nearest 5**, choose the closest number that ends in 0 or 5: 43 → 45, 41 → 40, 48 → 50 and 1 237 → 1 235.\n\n> **Common mistake:** To the nearest 100 you look only at the **tens** digit. 4 349 becomes 4 300, because the tens digit is 4. Don’t first make it 4 350 and then jump up to 4 400!\n\n## Even and odd numbers\n\n- **Even** numbers end in 0, 2, 4, 6 or 8. They can be split into two equal groups exactly.\n- **Odd** numbers end in 1, 3, 5, 7 or 9.\n\nOnly the **last digit** counts: 246 803 is odd, even though all the other digits are even.\n\n## Counting in multiples\n\nYou can count forwards or backwards in steps of 2, 5, 10, 25, 50, 100 or 1 000. The numbers you say are **multiples** of the step.\n\n- Forwards in steps of 25: 1 450, 1 475, 1 500, 1 525\n- Backwards in steps of 1 000: 63 200, 62 200, 61 200, 60 200\n\nLook at which column changes: when you count in steps of 1 000, the thousands digit changes every time."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Syfer","en":"Digit"},"def":{"af":"Een van die tekens 0 tot 9 waarmee ons getalle skryf.","en":"One of the symbols 0 to 9 that we use to write numbers."}},{"term":{"af":"Plekwaarde","en":"Place value"},"def":{"af":"Die kolom waarin ’n syfer staan, soos tiene of duisende, wat bepaal hoeveel die syfer werd is.","en":"The column a digit stands in, such as tens or thousands, which decides how much the digit is worth."}},{"term":{"af":"Waarde","en":"Value"},"def":{"af":"Hoeveel ’n syfer op sy plek werd is; in 45 300 is die waarde van die 5 vyfduisend (5 000).","en":"How much a digit is worth in its place; in 45 300 the value of the 5 is five thousand (5 000)."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitgebreide notasie","en":"Expanded notation"},"def":{"af":"’n Getal geskryf as die som van die waardes van sy syfers, bv. 3 407 = 3 000 + 400 + 7.","en":"A number written as the sum of the values of its digits, e.g. 3 407 = 3 000 + 400 + 7."}},{"term":{"af":"Plekhouer","en":"Placeholder"},"def":{"af":"’n Nul wat ’n leë kolom oophou, soos die nulle in 305 040.","en":"A zero that keeps an empty column open, like the zeros in 305 040."}},{"term":{"af":"Stygende orde","en":"Ascending order"},"def":{"af":"Getalle gerangskik van die kleinste na die grootste.","en":"Numbers arranged from the smallest to the biggest."}},{"term":{"af":"Dalende orde","en":"Descending order"},"def":{"af":"Getalle gerangskik van die grootste na die kleinste.","en":"Numbers arranged from the biggest to the smallest."}},{"term":{"af":"Afrond","en":"Round off"},"def":{"af":"’n Getal vervang met ’n naby, maklike getal, soos die naaste 10; 100 of 1 000.","en":"To replace a number with a close, easy number, such as the nearest 10, 100 or 1 000."}},{"term":{"af":"Ewe getal","en":"Even number"},"def":{"af":"’n Getal wat op 0; 2; 4; 6 of 8 eindig en presies in twee gelyke groepe verdeel kan word.","en":"A number that ends in 0, 2, 4, 6 or 8 and can be split exactly into two equal groups."}},{"term":{"af":"Veelvoud","en":"Multiple"},"def":{"af":"Die antwoord as jy ’n getal met ’n telgetal maal; die veelvoude van 25 is 25; 50; 75; 100 ensovoorts.","en":"The answer when you multiply a number by a whole number; the multiples of 25 are 25, 50, 75, 100 and so on."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Woorde en uitgebreide notasie","en":"Words and expanded notation"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf 482 056 in woorde en in uitgebreide notasie. Wat is die waarde van die 8?","en":"Write 482 056 in words and in expanded notation. What is the value of the 8?"},"steps":[{"af":"Sit die syfers in die kolomme: HD = 4, TD = 8, D = 2, H = 0, T = 5, E = 6.","en":"Put the digits in the columns: HTh = 4, TTh = 8, Th = 2, H = 0, T = 5, U = 6."},{"af":"Lees eers die duisende (482) en dan die res (056): vierhonderd twee-en-tagtigduisend ses-en-vyftig.","en":"First read the thousands (482) and then the rest (056): four hundred and eighty-two thousand and fifty-six."},{"af":"Uitgebreide notasie: 400 000 + 80 000 + 2 000 + 50 + 6. Die 0 by die honderde is ’n plekhouer, so ons skryf niks vir die honderde nie.","en":"Expanded notation: 400 000 + 80 000 + 2 000 + 50 + 6. The 0 in the hundreds is a placeholder, so we write nothing for the hundreds."},{"af":"Die 8 staan by die tienduisende, dus is sy waarde 80 000.","en":"The 8 is in the ten thousands, so its value is 80 000."}],"answer":{"af":"Vierhonderd twee-en-tagtigduisend ses-en-vyftig; 400 000 + 80 000 + 2 000 + 50 + 6; die 8 is 80 000 werd.","en":"Four hundred and eighty-two thousand and fifty-six; 400 000 + 80 000 + 2 000 + 50 + 6; the 8 is worth 80 000."}},{"title":{"af":"Orden in stygende orde","en":"Order in ascending order"},"problem":{"af":"Rangskik in stygende orde: 54 870; 548 700; 54 807; 45 870","en":"Arrange in ascending order: 54 870, 548 700, 54 807, 45 870"},"steps":[{"af":"Tel die syfers: 548 700 het 6 syfers, die ander net 5. Dus is 548 700 die grootste.","en":"Count the digits: 548 700 has 6 digits, the others only 5. So 548 700 is the biggest."},{"af":"Vergelyk die tienduisende van die ander: 5; 5 en 4. Dus is 45 870 die kleinste.","en":"Compare the ten thousands of the others: 5, 5 and 4. So 45 870 is the smallest."},{"af":"54 870 en 54 807: die TD, D en H is gelyk (5; 4; 8). By die tiene is 0 < 7, dus is 54 807 kleiner.","en":"54 870 and 54 807: the TTh, Th and H are equal (5, 4, 8). In the tens, 0 < 7, so 54 807 is smaller."}],"answer":{"af":"45 870; 54 807; 54 870; 548 700","en":"45 870, 54 807, 54 870, 548 700"}},{"title":{"af":"Afrond op vier maniere","en":"Rounding off in four ways"},"problem":{"af":"Rond 63 748 af tot die naaste 5; 10; 100 en 1 000.","en":"Round off 63 748 to the nearest 5, 10, 100 and 1 000."},"steps":[{"af":"Naaste 5: 63 748 lê tussen 63 745 en 63 750. Dit is 3 van 63 745 af en net 2 van 63 750 af, dus 63 750.","en":"Nearest 5: 63 748 lies between 63 745 and 63 750. It is 3 away from 63 745 and only 2 away from 63 750, so 63 750."},{"af":"Naaste 10: kyk na die ene-syfer, 8. Dit is 5 of meer, rond op: 63 750.","en":"Nearest 10: look at the units digit, 8. It is 5 or more, so round up: 63 750."},{"af":"Naaste 100: kyk na die tiene-syfer, 4. Dit is minder as 5, rond af: 63 700.","en":"Nearest 100: look at the tens digit, 4. It is less than 5, so round down: 63 700."},{"af":"Naaste 1 000: kyk na die honderde-syfer, 7. Rond op: 64 000.","en":"Nearest 1 000: look at the hundreds digit, 7. Round up: 64 000."}],"answer":{"af":"63 750; 63 750; 63 700; 64 000","en":"63 750, 63 750, 63 700, 64 000"}},{"title":{"af":"Afrond in ’n woordprobleem","en":"Rounding off in a word problem"},"problem":{"af":"51 862 toeskouers het ’n sokkerwedstryd in Durban bygewoon. ’n Koerant rond die getal tot die naaste 1 000 af en ’n radiostasie tot die naaste 100. Watter getalle gebruik hulle?","en":"51 862 spectators attended a soccer match in Durban. A newspaper rounds the number off to the nearest 1 000 and a radio station to the nearest 100. Which numbers do they use?"},"steps":[{"af":"Naaste 1 000: die honderde-syfer is 8, dus rond op. 51 862 → 52 000.","en":"Nearest 1 000: the hundreds digit is 8, so round up. 51 862 → 52 000."},{"af":"Naaste 100: die tiene-syfer is 6, dus rond op. 51 862 → 51 900.","en":"Nearest 100: the tens digit is 6, so round up. 51 862 → 51 900."},{"af":"Kontroleer of die antwoorde sin maak: albei is naby aan 51 862.","en":"Check that the answers make sense: both are close to 51 862."}],"answer":{"af":"Die koerant skryf 52 000 en die radiostasie sê 51 900.","en":"The newspaper writes 52 000 and the radio station says 51 900."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die waarde van die syfer 7 in 372 615?","en":"What is the value of the digit 7 in 372 615?"},"options":[{"af":"7 000","en":"7 000"},{"af":"70 000","en":"70 000"},{"af":"700 000","en":"700 000"},{"af":"7","en":"7"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In 372 615 staan die 7 in die tweede kolom van links, die tienduisende. Sy waarde is dus 70 000. 7 000 sou die waarde by die duisende wees.","en":"In 372 615 the 7 is in the second column from the left, the ten thousands. So its value is 70 000. 7 000 would be its value in the thousands."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter getal is *sewentigduisend vierhonderd ses-en-dertig*?","en":"Which number is *seventy thousand four hundred and thirty-six*?"},"options":[{"af":"74 036","en":"74 036"},{"af":"7 436","en":"7 436"},{"af":"70 436","en":"70 436"},{"af":"700 436","en":"700 436"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Sewentigduisend is 70 000 (die duisende-kolom is 0) en dan kom 436 by: 70 436. In 74 036 is die 4 by die duisende, en 7 436 is net seweduisend.","en":"Seventy thousand is 70 000 (the thousands column is 0) and then 436 is added: 70 436. In 74 036 the 4 is in the thousands, and 7 436 is only seven thousand."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"300 000 + 6 000 + 80 + 2 = ___","en":"300 000 + 6 000 + 80 + 2 = ___"},"answers":{"af":["306 082","306082"],"en":["306 082","306082"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["360 082","306 820","36 082"],"en":["360 082","306 820","36 082"]}},"explain":{"af":"Daar is 3 honderdduisende, 0 tienduisende, 6 duisende, 0 honderde, 8 tiene en 2 ene: 306 082. Die nulle is plekhouers vir die leë kolomme.","en":"There are 3 hundred thousands, 0 ten thousands, 6 thousands, 0 hundreds, 8 tens and 2 units: 306 082. The zeros are placeholders for the empty columns."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Telgetal met 6 syfers is altyd groter as ’n telgetal met 5 syfers.","en":"A whole number with 6 digits is always bigger than a whole number with 5 digits."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die kleinste 6-syfergetal is 100 000 en die grootste 5-syfergetal is 99 999. Elke 6-syfergetal is dus groter.","en":"True. The smallest 6-digit number is 100 000 and the biggest 5-digit number is 99 999. So every 6-digit number is bigger."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter getal is die grootste?","en":"Which number is the biggest?"},"options":[{"af":"98 765","en":"98 765"},{"af":"119 999","en":"119 999"},{"af":"102 400","en":"102 400"},{"af":"120 004","en":"120 004"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"98 765 het net 5 syfers, so dit is die kleinste, al lyk die syfers groot. Van die 6-syfergetalle het 120 004 die meeste tienduisende (2), so dit is die grootste.","en":"98 765 has only 5 digits, so it is the smallest, even though its digits look big. Of the 6-digit numbers, 120 004 has the most ten thousands (2), so it is the biggest."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Rond 27 465 af tot die naaste 1 000.","en":"Round off 27 465 to the nearest 1 000."},"options":[{"af":"28 000","en":"28 000"},{"af":"27 500","en":"27 500"},{"af":"27 000","en":"27 000"},{"af":"30 000","en":"30 000"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Kyk net na die honderde-syfer: 4. Dit is minder as 5, dus rond af na 27 000. As jy eers na 27 500 afrond en dan na 28 000, maak jy die algemene fout.","en":"Look only at the hundreds digit: 4. It is less than 5, so round down to 27 000. If you first round to 27 500 and then to 28 000, you make the common mistake."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"38 afgerond tot die naaste 5 is ___.","en":"38 rounded off to the nearest 5 is ___."},"answers":{"af":["40"],"en":["40"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["35","30","45"],"en":["35","30","45"]}},"explain":{"af":"38 lê tussen 35 en 40. Dit is 3 van 35 af, maar net 2 van 40 af, dus is 40 die naaste veelvoud van 5.","en":"38 lies between 35 and 40. It is 3 away from 35 but only 2 away from 40, so 40 is the nearest multiple of 5."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die regte voorbeeld.","en":"Match each term to the correct example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Stygende orde","en":"Ascending order"},"r":{"af":"12 300; 13 200; 21 300","en":"12 300, 13 200, 21 300"}},{"l":{"af":"Dalende orde","en":"Descending order"},"r":{"af":"21 300; 13 200; 12 300","en":"21 300, 13 200, 12 300"}},{"l":{"af":"Uitgebreide notasie","en":"Expanded notation"},"r":{"af":"70 000 + 300 + 9","en":"70 000 + 300 + 9"}},{"l":{"af":"Plekhouer","en":"Placeholder"},"r":{"af":"Die 0 in 4 058","en":"The 0 in 4 058"}},{"l":{"af":"Ewe getal","en":"Even number"},"r":{"af":"78 314","en":"78 314"}}],"explain":{"af":"Stygend gaan van klein na groot en dalend van groot na klein. 70 000 + 300 + 9 wys die waarde van elke syfer. Die 0 in 4 058 hou die honderde-kolom oop. 78 314 eindig op 4, dus is dit ewe.","en":"Ascending goes from small to big and descending from big to small. 70 000 + 300 + 9 shows the value of every digit. The 0 in 4 058 keeps the hundreds column open. 78 314 ends in 4, so it is even."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter getal is 1 000 meer as 89 450?","en":"Which number is 1 000 more than 89 450?"},"options":[{"af":"90 450","en":"90 450"},{"af":"89 550","en":"89 550"},{"af":"99 450","en":"99 450"},{"af":"89 460","en":"89 460"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Tel 1 by die duisende-syfer: 9 duisende + 1 = 10 duisende, so die tienduisende word 9 en die duisende 0: 90 450. 89 550 is net 100 meer en 99 450 is 10 000 meer.","en":"Add 1 to the thousands digit: 9 thousands + 1 = 10 thousands, so the ten thousands become 9 and the thousands 0: 90 450. 89 550 is only 100 more and 99 450 is 10 000 more."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"4 349 afgerond tot die naaste 100 is 4 400.","en":"4 349 rounded off to the nearest 100 is 4 400."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Kyk net na die tiene-syfer, wat 4 is. Dit is minder as 5, dus rond af na 4 300. Om eers na 4 350 af te rond, is die algemene fout.","en":"False. Look only at the tens digit, which is 4. It is less than 5, so round down to 4 300. Rounding to 4 350 first is the common mistake."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter getal is onewe?","en":"Which number is odd?"},"options":[{"af":"57 932","en":"57 932"},{"af":"30 008","en":"30 008"},{"af":"13 574","en":"13 574"},{"af":"98 765","en":"98 765"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Net die laaste syfer bepaal of ’n getal ewe of onewe is. 98 765 eindig op 5, dus is dit onewe. 57 932 begin met onewe syfers, maar eindig op 2, dus is dit ewe.","en":"Only the last digit decides whether a number is even or odd. 98 765 ends in 5, so it is odd. 57 932 starts with odd digits, but ends in 2, so it is even."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Tel agtertoe in treë van 100: 40 250; 40 150; 40 050; ___","en":"Count backwards in steps of 100: 40 250, 40 150, 40 050, ___"},"answers":{"af":["39 950","39950"],"en":["39 950","39950"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["40 000","39 050","40 950"],"en":["40 000","39 050","40 950"]}},"explain":{"af":"40 050 − 100 = 39 950. Daar is net 0 honderde, so jy moet een duisend opbreek: die duisende gaan van 40 na 39 en die honderde word 9.","en":"40 050 − 100 = 39 950. There are 0 hundreds, so you must break up one thousand: the thousands go from 40 to 39 and the hundreds become 9."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter getal het die syfer 5 die grootste waarde?","en":"In which number does the digit 5 have the greatest value?"},"options":[{"af":"512 400","en":"512 400"},{"af":"251 400","en":"251 400"},{"af":"125 400","en":"125 400"},{"af":"214 500","en":"214 500"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"In 512 400 staan die 5 by die honderdduisende: 500 000. In 251 400 is dit 50 000, in 125 400 is dit 5 000 en in 214 500 net 500.","en":"In 512 400 the 5 is in the hundred thousands: 500 000. In 251 400 it is 50 000, in 125 400 it is 5 000 and in 214 500 only 500."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Rond 6 995 af tot die naaste 10.","en":"Round off 6 995 to the nearest 10."},"options":[{"af":"6 990","en":"6 990"},{"af":"7 000","en":"7 000"},{"af":"6 900","en":"6 900"},{"af":"7 100","en":"7 100"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"6 995 lê tussen 6 990 en 7 000. Die ene-syfer is 5, dus rond op na die volgende tiental: 7 000. 6 990 sou die antwoord wees as jy verkeerdelik afgerond het.","en":"6 995 lies between 6 990 and 7 000. The units digit is 5, so round up to the next ten: 7 000. 6 990 would be the answer if you wrongly rounded down."}}]},{"id":"w5-t1-optel-aftrek","title":{"af":"Optel en aftrek","en":"Addition and subtraction"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal getalle tot 5 syfers kan optel en aftrek met die kolommetode, die opbreekmetode en ’n getallelyn, eers kan skat en jou antwoord met die inverse bewerking kan kontroleer.","en":"You will be able to add and subtract numbers of up to 5 digits with the column method, the breaking-down method and a number line, estimate first and check your answer with the inverse operation."},"summary":{"af":"## Skat eers\n\nVoordat jy optel of aftrek, maak ’n **skatting**: rond die getalle af en reken in jou kop. Die skatting wys of jou antwoord sin maak. Die teken **≈** beteken *is ongeveer gelyk aan*.\n\n- 34 768 + 25 459 ≈ 35 000 + 25 000 = 60 000\n- 52 304 − 18 657 ≈ 52 000 − 19 000 = 33 000\n\nDie antwoord van ’n optelsom is die **som**; die antwoord van ’n aftreksom is die **verskil**.\n\n## Optel met die kolommetode\n\nSkryf die getalle **onder mekaar**: ene onder ene, tiene onder tiene, ensovoorts. Begin altyd by die **ene** (regs).\n\n| | TD | D | H | T | E |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | 3 | 4 | 7 | 6 | 8 |\n| + | 2 | 5 | 4 | 5 | 9 |\n| = | 6 | 0 | 2 | 2 | 7 |\n\n1. E: 8 + 9 = 17. Skryf 7 en **dra 1 oor** na die tiene.\n2. T: 6 + 5 + 1 = 12. Skryf 2, dra 1 oor.\n3. H: 7 + 4 + 1 = 12. Skryf 2, dra 1 oor.\n4. D: 4 + 5 + 1 = 10. Skryf 0, dra 1 oor.\n5. TD: 3 + 2 + 1 = 6.\n\nDie som is 60 227 – baie naby aan die skatting van 60 000.\n\n## Aftrek met die kolommetode\n\n| | TD | D | H | T | E |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | 5 | 2 | 3 | 0 | 4 |\n| − | 1 | 8 | 6 | 5 | 7 |\n| = | 3 | 3 | 6 | 4 | 7 |\n\n1. E: 4 − 7 gaan nie. Jy moet **leen (hergroepeer)**, maar daar is 0 tiene. Leen eers by die honderde: 3 H word 2 H en 10 T. Leen dan by die tiene: 10 T word 9 T en die ene word 14. 14 − 7 = 7.\n2. T: 9 − 5 = 4.\n3. H: 2 − 6 gaan nie. Leen by die duisende: 12 − 6 = 6, en daar bly 1 D oor.\n4. D: 1 − 8 gaan nie. Leen by die tienduisende: 11 − 8 = 3, en daar bly 4 TD oor.\n5. TD: 4 − 1 = 3.\n\nDie verskil is 33 647.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie in ’n kolom die kleiner syfer van die groter syfer aftrek net omdat dit makliker is nie. By 4 − 7 skryf baie leerders 3, maar jy moet leen: 14 − 7 = 7.\n\n## Opbreek en die getallelyn\n\nMet die **opbreekmetode** breek jy die getalle in hul plekwaardes op:\n\n4 567 + 2 345 = (4 000 + 2 000) + (500 + 300) + (60 + 40) + (7 + 5) = 6 000 + 800 + 100 + 12 = 6 912\n\nOp ’n **getallelyn** spring jy in maklike treë. Vir 8 003 − 2 995 begin jy by 2 995 en spring tot by 8 003: +5 (tot 3 000), +5 000 (tot 8 000), +3 (tot 8 003). Altesaam is dit 5 + 5 000 + 3 = 5 008.\n\n## Kontroleer met die inverse bewerking\n\nOptel en aftrek is **inverse bewerkings**: die een maak die ander ongedaan.\n\n- 52 304 − 18 657 = 33 647. Kontroleer: 33 647 + 18 657 = 52 304. Dit klop.\n- 34 768 + 25 459 = 60 227. Kontroleer: 60 227 − 25 459 = 34 768. Dit klop.\n\n## Eienskappe van optel\n\n| Eienskap | Wat dit sê | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Kommutatief (omruil) | Die volgorde maak nie saak nie. | 3 458 + 1 200 = 1 200 + 3 458 |\n| Assosiatief (groepeer) | Jy kies watter twee getalle jy eerste optel. | (250 + 375) + 125 = 250 + (375 + 125) |\n| Nul | As jy 0 bytel, verander die getal nie. | 4 567 + 0 = 4 567 |\n\nSlim groepeer maak somme makliker: 375 + 125 = 500, en 250 + 500 = 750.\n\n> **Onthou:** Die omruil- en groepeer-eienskappe werk vir **optel**, nie vir aftrek nie. 50 − 20 = 30, maar 20 − 50 is beslis nie 30 nie.\n\n## Woordprobleme\n\n1. Lees die probleem twee keer en onderstreep die vraag.\n2. Besluit: kom daar iets **by** (optel), of gaan daar iets **af** of soek jy die **verskil** (aftrek)?\n3. Skat, bereken en kontroleer.\n4. Skryf die antwoord in ’n volsin, met die eenheid.\n\nWoorde soos *altesaam*, *totaal* en *som* wys gewoonlik na optel. Woorde soos *verskil*, *oor*, *minder as* en *hoeveel meer* wys gewoonlik na aftrek.","en":"## Estimate first\n\nBefore you add or subtract, make an **estimate**: round the numbers off and work it out in your head. The estimate shows whether your answer makes sense. The sign **≈** means *is approximately equal to*.\n\n- 34 768 + 25 459 ≈ 35 000 + 25 000 = 60 000\n- 52 304 − 18 657 ≈ 52 000 − 19 000 = 33 000\n\nThe answer to an addition is the **sum**; the answer to a subtraction is the **difference**.\n\n## Adding with the column method\n\nWrite the numbers **underneath each other**: units under units, tens under tens, and so on. Always start with the **units** (on the right).\n\n| | TTh | Th | H | T | U |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | 3 | 4 | 7 | 6 | 8 |\n| + | 2 | 5 | 4 | 5 | 9 |\n| = | 6 | 0 | 2 | 2 | 7 |\n\n1. U: 8 + 9 = 17. Write 7 and **carry 1** to the tens.\n2. T: 6 + 5 + 1 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n3. H: 7 + 4 + 1 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n4. Th: 4 + 5 + 1 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n5. TTh: 3 + 2 + 1 = 6.\n\nThe sum is 60 227 – very close to the estimate of 60 000.\n\n## Subtracting with the column method\n\n| | TTh | Th | H | T | U |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | 5 | 2 | 3 | 0 | 4 |\n| − | 1 | 8 | 6 | 5 | 7 |\n| = | 3 | 3 | 6 | 4 | 7 |\n\n1. U: 4 − 7 does not work. You must **borrow (regroup)**, but there are 0 tens. First borrow from the hundreds: 3 H become 2 H and 10 T. Then borrow from the tens: 10 T become 9 T and the units become 14. 14 − 7 = 7.\n2. T: 9 − 5 = 4.\n3. H: 2 − 6 does not work. Borrow from the thousands: 12 − 6 = 6, and 1 Th is left.\n4. Th: 1 − 8 does not work. Borrow from the ten thousands: 11 − 8 = 3, and 4 TTh are left.\n5. TTh: 4 − 1 = 3.\n\nThe difference is 33 647.\n\n> **Common mistake:** In a column, don’t subtract the smaller digit from the bigger digit just because it is easier. For 4 − 7 many learners write 3, but you must borrow: 14 − 7 = 7.\n\n## Breaking down and the number line\n\nWith the **breaking-down method** you break the numbers up into their place values:\n\n4 567 + 2 345 = (4 000 + 2 000) + (500 + 300) + (60 + 40) + (7 + 5) = 6 000 + 800 + 100 + 12 = 6 912\n\nOn a **number line** you jump in easy steps. For 8 003 − 2 995 you start at 2 995 and jump up to 8 003: +5 (to 3 000), +5 000 (to 8 000), +3 (to 8 003). Altogether that is 5 + 5 000 + 3 = 5 008.\n\n## Checking with the inverse operation\n\nAddition and subtraction are **inverse operations**: the one undoes the other.\n\n- 52 304 − 18 657 = 33 647. Check: 33 647 + 18 657 = 52 304. It is correct.\n- 34 768 + 25 459 = 60 227. Check: 60 227 − 25 459 = 34 768. It is correct.\n\n## Properties of addition\n\n| Property | What it says | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Commutative (swap) | The order does not matter. | 3 458 + 1 200 = 1 200 + 3 458 |\n| Associative (group) | You choose which two numbers to add first. | (250 + 375) + 125 = 250 + (375 + 125) |\n| Zero | When you add 0, the number does not change. | 4 567 + 0 = 4 567 |\n\nClever grouping makes sums easier: 375 + 125 = 500, and 250 + 500 = 750.\n\n> **Remember:** The swap and group properties work for **addition**, not for subtraction. 50 − 20 = 30, but 20 − 50 is definitely not 30.\n\n## Word problems\n\n1. Read the problem twice and underline the question.\n2. Decide: is something **added** (addition), or is something **taken away**, or are you looking for the **difference** (subtraction)?\n3. Estimate, calculate and check.\n4. Write the answer in a full sentence, with the unit.\n\nWords like *altogether*, *total* and *sum* usually point to addition. Words like *difference*, *left*, *less than* and *how many more* usually point to subtraction."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Som","en":"Sum"},"def":{"af":"Die antwoord as jy getalle bymekaartel.","en":"The answer when you add numbers together."}},{"term":{"af":"Verskil","en":"Difference"},"def":{"af":"Die antwoord as jy een getal van ’n ander aftrek; hoeveel meer die een is as die ander.","en":"The answer when you subtract one number from another; how much more the one is than the other."}},{"term":{"af":"Skatting","en":"Estimate"},"def":{"af":"’n Antwoord wat naby die regte antwoord is, wat jy kry deur die getalle eers af te rond.","en":"An answer close to the real answer, which you get by rounding off the numbers first."}},{"term":{"af":"Oordra","en":"Carry"},"def":{"af":"As ’n kolom 10 of meer gee, skuif jy die tiental na die volgende kolom links.","en":"When a column gives 10 or more, you move the ten over to the next column on the left."}},{"term":{"af":"Leen (hergroepeer)","en":"Borrow (regroup)"},"def":{"af":"Een uit die kolom links neem en as 10 in jou kolom gebruik, sodat jy kan aftrek.","en":"Taking one from the column on the left and using it as 10 in your column, so that you can subtract."}},{"term":{"af":"Inverse bewerking","en":"Inverse operation"},"def":{"af":"Die bewerking wat ’n ander ongedaan maak; optel en aftrek is inverse bewerkings.","en":"The operation that undoes another one; addition and subtraction are inverse operations."}},{"term":{"af":"Kommutatiewe eienskap","en":"Commutative property"},"def":{"af":"Jy kan die getalle in ’n optelsom omruil en die som bly dieselfde.","en":"You can swap the numbers in an addition and the sum stays the same."}},{"term":{"af":"Assosiatiewe eienskap","en":"Associative property"},"def":{"af":"As jy drie getalle optel, kan jy kies watter twee jy eerste bymekaartel.","en":"When you add three numbers, you can choose which two to add first."}},{"term":{"af":"Opbreekmetode","en":"Breaking-down method"},"def":{"af":"Getalle in duisende, honderde, tiene en ene opbreek en elke deel apart optel.","en":"Breaking numbers up into thousands, hundreds, tens and units and adding each part separately."}},{"term":{"af":"Getallelyn","en":"Number line"},"def":{"af":"’n Lyn met getalle in volgorde waarop jy in treë vorentoe of agtertoe kan spring.","en":"A line with numbers in order on which you can jump forwards or backwards in steps."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Optel met oordra","en":"Adding with carrying"},"problem":{"af":"Bereken 47 586 + 36 978. Skat eers.","en":"Calculate 47 586 + 36 978. Estimate first."},"steps":[{"af":"Skat: 48 000 + 37 000 = 85 000.","en":"Estimate: 48 000 + 37 000 = 85 000."},{"af":"E: 6 + 8 = 14, skryf 4, dra 1 oor. T: 8 + 7 + 1 = 16, skryf 6, dra 1 oor.","en":"U: 6 + 8 = 14, write 4, carry 1. T: 8 + 7 + 1 = 16, write 6, carry 1."},{"af":"H: 5 + 9 + 1 = 15, skryf 5, dra 1 oor. D: 7 + 6 + 1 = 14, skryf 4, dra 1 oor.","en":"H: 5 + 9 + 1 = 15, write 5, carry 1. Th: 7 + 6 + 1 = 14, write 4, carry 1."},{"af":"TD: 4 + 3 + 1 = 8. Die som is 84 564, naby aan die skatting van 85 000.","en":"TTh: 4 + 3 + 1 = 8. The sum is 84 564, close to the estimate of 85 000."}],"answer":{"af":"84 564","en":"84 564"}},{"title":{"af":"Aftrek oor nulle heen","en":"Subtracting across zeros"},"problem":{"af":"Bereken 70 005 − 23 468 en kontroleer jou antwoord.","en":"Calculate 70 005 − 23 468 and check your answer."},"steps":[{"af":"Skat: 70 000 − 23 000 = 47 000.","en":"Estimate: 70 000 − 23 000 = 47 000."},{"af":"By die ene is 5 − 8 onmoontlik, en die T, H en D is almal 0. Leen by die tienduisende: 70 005 word 6 TD, 9 D, 9 H, 9 T en 15 E.","en":"In the units 5 − 8 is impossible, and the T, H and Th are all 0. Borrow from the ten thousands: 70 005 becomes 6 TTh, 9 Th, 9 H, 9 T and 15 U."},{"af":"Trek kolom vir kolom af: 15 − 8 = 7; 9 − 6 = 3; 9 − 4 = 5; 9 − 3 = 6; 6 − 2 = 4. Dit gee 46 537.","en":"Subtract column by column: 15 − 8 = 7, 9 − 6 = 3, 9 − 4 = 5, 9 − 3 = 6, 6 − 2 = 4. That gives 46 537."},{"af":"Kontroleer met die inverse bewerking: 46 537 + 23 468 = 70 005. Dit klop.","en":"Check with the inverse operation: 46 537 + 23 468 = 70 005. It is correct."}],"answer":{"af":"46 537","en":"46 537"}},{"title":{"af":"Aftrek op ’n getallelyn","en":"Subtracting on a number line"},"problem":{"af":"Bereken 6 002 − 3 998 met ’n getallelyn.","en":"Calculate 6 002 − 3 998 with a number line."},"steps":[{"af":"Begin by die kleiner getal, 3 998, en spring tot by 6 002.","en":"Start at the smaller number, 3 998, and jump up to 6 002."},{"af":"Spring +2 tot by 4 000, dan +2 000 tot by 6 000, dan +2 tot by 6 002.","en":"Jump +2 to 4 000, then +2 000 to 6 000, then +2 to 6 002."},{"af":"Tel die spronge bymekaar: 2 + 2 000 + 2 = 2 004.","en":"Add the jumps together: 2 + 2 000 + 2 = 2 004."}],"answer":{"af":"2 004","en":"2 004"}},{"title":{"af":"Woordprobleem in twee stappe","en":"Two-step word problem"},"problem":{"af":"’n Boer in die Vrystaat oes 23 650 kg mielies op een land en 18 975 kg op ’n ander land. Hy verkoop 35 000 kg. Hoeveel kilogram mielies het hy oor?","en":"A farmer in the Free State harvests 23 650 kg of maize on one field and 18 975 kg on another field. He sells 35 000 kg. How many kilograms of maize does he have left?"},"steps":[{"af":"Skat: 24 000 + 19 000 = 43 000 en 43 000 − 35 000 = 8 000.","en":"Estimate: 24 000 + 19 000 = 43 000 and 43 000 − 35 000 = 8 000."},{"af":"Stap 1 – tel die oes bymekaar: 23 650 + 18 975 = 42 625 kg.","en":"Step 1 – add the harvests together: 23 650 + 18 975 = 42 625 kg."},{"af":"Stap 2 – trek af wat hy verkoop: 42 625 − 35 000 = 7 625 kg.","en":"Step 2 – subtract what he sells: 42 625 − 35 000 = 7 625 kg."},{"af":"Kontroleer: 7 625 + 35 000 = 42 625. Die antwoord is naby die skatting van 8 000.","en":"Check: 7 625 + 35 000 = 42 625. The answer is close to the estimate of 8 000."}],"answer":{"af":"Die boer het 7 625 kg mielies oor.","en":"The farmer has 7 625 kg of maize left."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die beste skatting vir 38 912 + 21 345?","en":"What is the best estimate for 38 912 + 21 345?"},"options":[{"af":"59 000","en":"59 000"},{"af":"60 000","en":"60 000"},{"af":"50 000","en":"50 000"},{"af":"70 000","en":"70 000"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Rond elke getal tot die naaste 1 000 af: 38 912 ≈ 39 000 en 21 345 ≈ 21 000. 39 000 + 21 000 = 60 000. 59 000 kry jy as jy 38 912 na 38 000 afkap in plaas van afrond.","en":"Round each number to the nearest 1 000: 38 912 ≈ 39 000 and 21 345 ≈ 21 000. 39 000 + 21 000 = 60 000. You get 59 000 if you chop 38 912 down to 38 000 instead of rounding."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bereken 45 386 + 27 857.","en":"Calculate 45 386 + 27 857."},"options":[{"af":"62 133","en":"62 133"},{"af":"73 233","en":"73 233"},{"af":"63 243","en":"63 243"},{"af":"73 243","en":"73 243"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"E: 6 + 7 = 13 (dra 1 oor); T: 8 + 5 + 1 = 14; H: 3 + 8 + 1 = 12; D: 5 + 7 + 1 = 13; TD: 4 + 2 + 1 = 7. Die som is 73 243. Die ander antwoorde vergeet een of meer van die oorgedraagde ene.","en":"U: 6 + 7 = 13 (carry 1); T: 8 + 5 + 1 = 14; H: 3 + 8 + 1 = 12; Th: 5 + 7 + 1 = 13; TTh: 4 + 2 + 1 = 7. The sum is 73 243. The other answers forget one or more of the carried ones."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"2 345 + 6 789 = 6 789 + 2 345","en":"2 345 + 6 789 = 6 789 + 2 345"},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Optel is kommutatief: as jy die getalle omruil, bly die som dieselfde (9 134).","en":"True. Addition is commutative: when you swap the numbers, the sum stays the same (9 134)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Thabo bereken 9 482 − 3 765 = 5 717. Hy kontroleer met die inverse bewerking: 5 717 + 3 765 = ___","en":"Thabo calculates 9 482 − 3 765 = 5 717. He checks with the inverse operation: 5 717 + 3 765 = ___"},"answers":{"af":["9 482","9482"],"en":["9 482","9482"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["9 472","8 482","9 582"],"en":["9 472","8 482","9 582"]}},"explain":{"af":"As die verskil plus die getal wat afgetrek is, weer die begingetal gee, is die aftreksom reg. 5 717 + 3 765 = 9 482, dus is Thabo se antwoord korrek.","en":"If the difference plus the number that was subtracted gives the starting number again, the subtraction is right. 5 717 + 3 765 = 9 482, so Thabo’s answer is correct."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bereken 60 003 − 27 465.","en":"Calculate 60 003 − 27 465."},"options":[{"af":"32 538","en":"32 538"},{"af":"42 538","en":"42 538"},{"af":"47 462","en":"47 462"},{"af":"32 548","en":"32 548"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Leen by die tienduisende: 60 003 word 5 TD, 9 D, 9 H, 9 T en 13 E. Dan: 13 − 5 = 8; 9 − 6 = 3; 9 − 4 = 5; 9 − 7 = 2; 5 − 2 = 3. Antwoord: 32 538. 47 462 kry jy as jy in elke kolom die kleiner syfer van die groter aftrek.","en":"Borrow from the ten thousands: 60 003 becomes 5 TTh, 9 Th, 9 H, 9 T and 13 U. Then: 13 − 5 = 8, 9 − 6 = 3, 9 − 4 = 5, 9 − 7 = 2, 5 − 2 = 3. Answer: 32 538. You get 47 462 if you subtract the smaller digit from the bigger one in every column."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die regte voorbeeld.","en":"Match each term to the correct example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Kommutatiewe eienskap","en":"Commutative property"},"r":{"af":"450 + 230 = 230 + 450","en":"450 + 230 = 230 + 450"}},{"l":{"af":"Assosiatiewe eienskap","en":"Associative property"},"r":{"af":"(45 + 55) + 30 = 45 + (55 + 30)","en":"(45 + 55) + 30 = 45 + (55 + 30)"}},{"l":{"af":"Optel van nul","en":"Adding zero"},"r":{"af":"8 765 + 0 = 8 765","en":"8 765 + 0 = 8 765"}},{"l":{"af":"Inverse bewerking","en":"Inverse operation"},"r":{"af":"900 − 350 = 550, dus 550 + 350 = 900","en":"900 − 350 = 550, so 550 + 350 = 900"}},{"l":{"af":"Skatting","en":"Estimate"},"r":{"af":"4 890 + 3 120 ≈ 8 000","en":"4 890 + 3 120 ≈ 8 000"}}],"explain":{"af":"Omruil is kommutatief en hakies skuif is assosiatief. Om 0 by te tel, verander niks. Optel maak aftrek ongedaan (inverse). ’n Skatting gebruik afgeronde getalle: 5 000 + 3 000 = 8 000.","en":"Swapping is commutative and moving the brackets is associative. Adding 0 changes nothing. Addition undoes subtraction (inverse). An estimate uses rounded numbers: 5 000 + 3 000 = 8 000."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die skole in ’n dorp samel 12 486 blikkies in die eerste kwartaal en 9 758 in die tweede kwartaal in. Hoeveel meer blikkies is in die eerste kwartaal ingesamel?","en":"The schools in a town collect 12 486 cans in the first term and 9 758 in the second term. How many more cans were collected in the first term?"},"options":[{"af":"22 244","en":"22 244"},{"af":"2 738","en":"2 738"},{"af":"2 728","en":"2 728"},{"af":"3 728","en":"3 728"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Hoeveel meer* vra na die verskil, dus trek af: 12 486 − 9 758 = 2 728. Kontroleer: 2 728 + 9 758 = 12 486. 22 244 is die som – dit beantwoord ’n ander vraag.","en":"*How many more* asks for the difference, so subtract: 12 486 − 9 758 = 2 728. Check: 2 728 + 9 758 = 12 486. 22 244 is the sum – it answers a different question."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Groepeer slim: 467 + 250 + 750 = 467 + ___","en":"Group cleverly: 467 + 250 + 750 = 467 + ___"},"answers":{"af":["1 000","1000"],"en":["1 000","1000"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["717","500","1 217"],"en":["717","500","1 217"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die assosiatiewe eienskap laat jou 250 + 750 eerste optel, want dit gee ’n ronde 1 000. Dan is 467 + 1 000 = 1 467 maklik.","en":"The associative property lets you add 250 + 750 first, because it gives a round 1 000. Then 467 + 1 000 = 1 467 is easy."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho bereken 5 000 − 1 = 4 999. Watter berekening kontroleer sy antwoord met die inverse bewerking?","en":"Sipho calculates 5 000 − 1 = 4 999. Which calculation checks his answer with the inverse operation?"},"options":[{"af":"5 000 + 1","en":"5 000 + 1"},{"af":"4 999 − 1","en":"4 999 − 1"},{"af":"4 999 + 1","en":"4 999 + 1"},{"af":"5 000 + 4 999","en":"5 000 + 4 999"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die inverse van aftrek is optel: tel die antwoord en die getal wat afgetrek is, bymekaar. 4 999 + 1 = 5 000, die begingetal, dus is die antwoord reg.","en":"The inverse of subtraction is addition: add the answer and the number that was subtracted. 4 999 + 1 = 5 000, the starting number, so the answer is right."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Aftrek is kommutatief, dus is 800 − 300 dieselfde as 300 − 800.","en":"Subtraction is commutative, so 800 − 300 is the same as 300 − 800."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 800 − 300 = 500, maar as jy 800 van 300 wil aftrek, kry jy nie 500 nie. By aftrek maak die volgorde saak; net optel is kommutatief.","en":"False. 800 − 300 = 500, but if you try to take 800 away from 300, you do not get 500. In subtraction the order matters; only addition is commutative."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Aisha bereken 9 000 − 3 997 op ’n getallelyn. Sy spring van 3 997 tot by 4 000 en dan tot by 9 000. Wat is die antwoord?","en":"Aisha calculates 9 000 − 3 997 on a number line. She jumps from 3 997 to 4 000 and then to 9 000. What is the answer?"},"options":[{"af":"5 000","en":"5 000"},{"af":"5 003","en":"5 003"},{"af":"5 997","en":"5 997"},{"af":"4 997","en":"4 997"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die spronge is +3 (tot by 4 000) en +5 000 (tot by 9 000). Altesaam is dit 3 + 5 000 = 5 003. As jy die klein sprong van 3 vergeet, kry jy 5 000.","en":"The jumps are +3 (to 4 000) and +5 000 (to 9 000). Altogether that is 3 + 5 000 = 5 003. If you forget the small jump of 3, you get 5 000."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die som van twee getalle is 50 000. Een van die getalle is 27 384. Wat is die ander getal?","en":"The sum of two numbers is 50 000. One of the numbers is 27 384. What is the other number?"},"options":[{"af":"77 384","en":"77 384"},{"af":"23 616","en":"23 616"},{"af":"37 384","en":"37 384"},{"af":"22 616","en":"22 616"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die ontbrekende deel kry jy deur af te trek: 50 000 − 27 384 = 22 616. Kontroleer: 22 616 + 27 384 = 50 000. 77 384 kry jy as jy optel in plaas van aftrek.","en":"You find the missing part by subtracting: 50 000 − 27 384 = 22 616. Check: 22 616 + 27 384 = 50 000. You get 77 384 if you add instead of subtract."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Woorde soos *altesaam*, *totaal* en *som* beteken gewoonlik dat jy moet ___.","en":"Words like *altogether*, *total* and *sum* usually mean that you must ___."},"answers":{"af":["optel","bymekaartel"],"en":["add","add up"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["aftrek","vermenigvuldig","deel"],"en":["subtract","multiply","divide"]}},"explain":{"af":"As jy die *totaal* of die *som* soek, sit jy hoeveelhede bymekaar – dit is optel. Woorde soos *verskil* en *oor* wys na aftrek.","en":"When you look for the *total* or the *sum*, you put amounts together – that is addition. Words like *difference* and *left* point to subtraction."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato bereken 6 748 + 2 375 met die opbreekmetode. Watter lyn is reg?","en":"Lerato calculates 6 748 + 2 375 with the breaking-down method. Which line is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"8 000 + 1 000 + 110 + 13","en":"8 000 + 1 000 + 110 + 13"},{"af":"8 000 + 1 000 + 11 + 13","en":"8 000 + 1 000 + 11 + 13"},{"af":"8 000 + 100 + 110 + 13","en":"8 000 + 100 + 110 + 13"},{"af":"8 000 + 1 000 + 110 + 3","en":"8 000 + 1 000 + 110 + 3"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Duisende: 6 000 + 2 000 = 8 000; honderde: 700 + 300 = 1 000; tiene: 40 + 70 = 110; ene: 8 + 5 = 13. Die som is 9 123. Die ander lyne skryf ’n deel met die verkeerde plekwaarde.","en":"Thousands: 6 000 + 2 000 = 8 000; hundreds: 700 + 300 = 1 000; tens: 40 + 70 = 110; units: 8 + 5 = 13. The sum is 9 123. The other lines write a part with the wrong place value."}}]},{"id":"w5-t1-getalsinne-patrone","title":{"af":"Getalpatrone, vloeidiagramme en getalsinne","en":"Number patterns, flow diagrams and number sentences"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal getalpatrone kan voortsit en die reël in woorde kan beskryf, vloeidiagramme en tabelle kan voltooi, en getalsinne met ’n onbekende kan skryf en oplos.","en":"You will be able to extend number patterns and describe the rule in words, complete flow diagrams and tables, and write and solve number sentences with an unknown."},"summary":{"af":"## Patrone met ’n konstante verskil\n\nIn ’n **getalpatroon** volg die getalle (die **terme**) ’n **reël**. As jy elke keer **dieselfde getal bytel of aftrek**, het die patroon ’n **konstante verskil**.\n\n- 7; 12; 17; 22; 27; … Reël: **tel 5 by**. Die volgende terme is 32 en 37.\n- 250; 225; 200; 175; … Reël: **trek 25 af**. Die volgende terme is 150 en 125.\n\nOm die reël te vind, trek jy elke term van die volgende term af. Is die verskil elke keer dieselfde? Dan het jy die reël.\n\n## Patrone met ’n konstante verhouding\n\nSoms **vermenigvuldig** of **deel** jy elke keer met dieselfde getal. Dan het die patroon ’n **konstante verhouding**.\n\n- 3; 6; 12; 24; … Reël: **maal 2** (verdubbel). Volgende: 48; 96.\n- 5 000; 1 000; 200; 40; … Reël: **deel deur 5**. Volgende: 8.\n\nHier groei (of krimp) die sprong tussen die terme elke keer, want jy maal of deel.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Kyk altyd na **meer as twee** terme. Die patroon 2; 4; … kan *tel 2 by* wees (2; 4; 6; 8) of *maal 2* (2; 4; 8; 16). Eers die derde term wys watter reël dit is.\n\n## Patrone in ’n tabel\n\n’n Tabel wys die **posisie** van elke term. Dan kan jy ’n term ver vorentoe vind sonder om al die terme te skryf.\n\n| Posisie | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 10 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Term | 4 | 8 | 12 | 16 | 40 |\n\nReël: **posisie × 4**. Die 10de term is dus 10 × 4 = 40.\n\nIn die patroon 5; 8; 11; 14; … is die verskil 3, maar elke term is 2 meer as die 3-maaltafel. Die reël is **posisie × 3 + 2**, so die 10de term is 10 × 3 + 2 = 32.\n\n## Vloeidiagramme\n\n’n **Vloeidiagram** wys hoe ’n **invoergetal** deur een of meer bewerkings gaan om ’n **uitvoergetal** te gee.\n\n**Invoer → × 6 → + 4 → Uitvoer**\n\n| Invoer | 2 | 5 | 10 | 12 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Uitvoer | 16 | 34 | 64 | 76 |\n\nVir invoer 5: 5 × 6 = 30 en 30 + 4 = 34. Doen die bewerkings altyd in die volgorde van die pyle.\n\nAs die uitvoer gegee is, werk jy **terug**. Uitvoer 46: 46 − 4 = 42 en 42 ÷ 6 = 7. Die invoer was 7.\n\n> **Onthou:** As jy terugwerk, draai jy die volgorde **en** die bewerkings om: + word −, en × word ÷.\n\n## Getalsinne met ’n onbekende\n\n’n **Getalsin** is ’n wiskundige sin, soos 35 + 25 = 60. ’n **Oop getalsin** het ’n **onbekende**, wat ons met ’n blokkie wys: □ + 25 = 60.\n\nDrie maniere om die onbekende te vind:\n\n1. **Inspeksie** – kyk en dink: watter getal plus 25 gee 60? Dit is 35.\n2. **Inverse bewerking** – □ = 60 − 25 = 35.\n3. **Probeer-en-verbeter** – vir □ × 7 = 84: probeer 10 → 70 (te klein); probeer 12 → 84. Reg!\n\nElke bewerking het ’n inverse bewerking wat jy kan gebruik:\n\n| Getalsin | Inverse bewerking | □ |\n|---|---|---|\n| □ + 25 = 60 | 60 − 25 | 35 |\n| □ − 14 = 30 | 30 + 14 | 44 |\n| □ × 9 = 72 | 72 ÷ 9 | 8 |\n| □ ÷ 4 = 15 | 15 × 4 | 60 |\n\nDie **gelykaanteken** (=) beteken *is dieselfde as*: albei kante moet ewe veel wees. In 30 + 20 = 45 + □ is die linkerkant 50, dus moet □ = 5 wees – nie 50 nie.\n\nKontroleer altyd: sit jou antwoord in die blokkie en kyk of die sin waar is.\n\n## Woordprobleme as getalsinne\n\nSkryf ’n oop getalsin wat by die storie pas en los dit dan op.\n\n- *Nomsa het ’n paar plakkers. Sy kry nog 18 en het nou 45.* → □ + 18 = 45, dus □ = 27.\n- *Ravi deel 96 lekkers gelyk tussen 8 vriende.* → 96 ÷ 8 = □, dus □ = 12.","en":"## Patterns with a constant difference\n\nIn a **number pattern** the numbers (the **terms**) follow a **rule**. When you **add or subtract the same number** every time, the pattern has a **constant difference**.\n\n- 7, 12, 17, 22, 27, … Rule: **add 5**. The next terms are 32 and 37.\n- 250, 225, 200, 175, … Rule: **subtract 25**. The next terms are 150 and 125.\n\nTo find the rule, subtract each term from the next term. Is the difference the same every time? Then you have the rule.\n\n## Patterns with a constant ratio\n\nSometimes you **multiply** or **divide** by the same number every time. Then the pattern has a **constant ratio**.\n\n- 3, 6, 12, 24, … Rule: **multiply by 2** (double). Next: 48, 96.\n- 5 000, 1 000, 200, 40, … Rule: **divide by 5**. Next: 8.\n\nHere the jump between the terms grows (or shrinks) every time, because you multiply or divide.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Always look at **more than two** terms. The pattern 2, 4, … can be *add 2* (2, 4, 6, 8) or *multiply by 2* (2, 4, 8, 16). Only the third term shows which rule it is.\n\n## Patterns in a table\n\nA table shows the **position** of every term. Then you can find a term far ahead without writing all the terms.\n\n| Position | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 10 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Term | 4 | 8 | 12 | 16 | 40 |\n\nRule: **position × 4**. So the 10th term is 10 × 4 = 40.\n\nIn the pattern 5, 8, 11, 14, … the difference is 3, but every term is 2 more than the 3 times table. The rule is **position × 3 + 2**, so the 10th term is 10 × 3 + 2 = 32.\n\n## Flow diagrams\n\nA **flow diagram** shows how an **input number** goes through one or more operations to give an **output number**.\n\n**Input → × 6 → + 4 → Output**\n\n| Input | 2 | 5 | 10 | 12 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Output | 16 | 34 | 64 | 76 |\n\nFor input 5: 5 × 6 = 30 and 30 + 4 = 34. Always do the operations in the order of the arrows.\n\nWhen the output is given, you work **backwards**. Output 46: 46 − 4 = 42 and 42 ÷ 6 = 7. The input was 7.\n\n> **Remember:** When you work backwards, you reverse the order **and** the operations: + becomes −, and × becomes ÷.\n\n## Number sentences with an unknown\n\nA **number sentence** is a mathematical sentence, such as 35 + 25 = 60. An **open number sentence** has an **unknown**, which we show with a box: □ + 25 = 60.\n\nThree ways to find the unknown:\n\n1. **Inspection** – look and think: which number plus 25 gives 60? It is 35.\n2. **Inverse operation** – □ = 60 − 25 = 35.\n3. **Trial and improvement** – for □ × 7 = 84: try 10 → 70 (too small); try 12 → 84. Correct!\n\nEvery operation has an inverse operation that you can use:\n\n| Number sentence | Inverse operation | □ |\n|---|---|---|\n| □ + 25 = 60 | 60 − 25 | 35 |\n| □ − 14 = 30 | 30 + 14 | 44 |\n| □ × 9 = 72 | 72 ÷ 9 | 8 |\n| □ ÷ 4 = 15 | 15 × 4 | 60 |\n\nThe **equals sign** (=) means *is the same as*: both sides must be worth the same. In 30 + 20 = 45 + □ the left side is 50, so □ must be 5 – not 50.\n\nAlways check: put your answer in the box and see whether the sentence is true.\n\n## Word problems as number sentences\n\nWrite an open number sentence that fits the story and then solve it.\n\n- *Nomsa has some stickers. She gets 18 more and now has 45.* → □ + 18 = 45, so □ = 27.\n- *Ravi shares 96 sweets equally among 8 friends.* → 96 ÷ 8 = □, so □ = 12."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Getalpatroon","en":"Number pattern"},"def":{"af":"’n Ry getalle wat volgens ’n vaste reël verander.","en":"A row of numbers that changes according to a fixed rule."}},{"term":{"af":"Term","en":"Term"},"def":{"af":"Elke getal in ’n patroon; in 7; 12; 17 is 12 die tweede term.","en":"Each number in a pattern; in 7, 12, 17 the number 12 is the second term."}},{"term":{"af":"Reël","en":"Rule"},"def":{"af":"Die instruksie wat sê hoe jy van een term na die volgende kom, bv. *tel 5 by*.","en":"The instruction that says how you get from one term to the next, e.g. *add 5*."}},{"term":{"af":"Konstante verskil","en":"Constant difference"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer jy elke keer dieselfde getal bytel of aftrek om die volgende term te kry.","en":"When you add or subtract the same number every time to get the next term."}},{"term":{"af":"Konstante verhouding","en":"Constant ratio"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer jy elke keer met dieselfde getal maal of deel om die volgende term te kry.","en":"When you multiply or divide by the same number every time to get the next term."}},{"term":{"af":"Vloeidiagram","en":"Flow diagram"},"def":{"af":"’n Diagram met pyle wat wys watter bewerkings op ’n invoergetal gedoen word.","en":"A diagram with arrows that shows which operations are done to an input number."}},{"term":{"af":"Invoer en uitvoer","en":"Input and output"},"def":{"af":"Die getal wat jy in ’n vloeidiagram insit (invoer) en die getal wat uitkom (uitvoer).","en":"The number you put into a flow diagram (input) and the number that comes out (output)."}},{"term":{"af":"Getalsin","en":"Number sentence"},"def":{"af":"’n Wiskundige sin met getalle, bewerkings en ’n gelykaanteken, soos 35 + 25 = 60.","en":"A mathematical sentence with numbers, operations and an equals sign, such as 35 + 25 = 60."}},{"term":{"af":"Onbekende","en":"Unknown"},"def":{"af":"Die getal in ’n oop getalsin wat jy moet vind, dikwels as □ geskryf.","en":"The number in an open number sentence that you must find, often written as □."}},{"term":{"af":"Probeer-en-verbeter","en":"Trial and improvement"},"def":{"af":"’n Getal probeer, kyk hoe naby jy is, en dan ’n beter getal probeer totdat dit klop.","en":"Trying a number, seeing how close you are, and then trying a better number until it works."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Sit ’n patroon voort","en":"Extend a pattern"},"problem":{"af":"Beskryf die reël en gee die volgende drie terme: 13; 21; 29; 37; … Wat is die 10de term?","en":"Describe the rule and give the next three terms: 13, 21, 29, 37, … What is the 10th term?"},"steps":[{"af":"Vind die verskille: 21 − 13 = 8; 29 − 21 = 8; 37 − 29 = 8. Die verskil is konstant, dus is die reël *tel 8 by*.","en":"Find the differences: 21 − 13 = 8, 29 − 21 = 8, 37 − 29 = 8. The difference is constant, so the rule is *add 8*."},{"af":"Volgende terme: 37 + 8 = 45; 45 + 8 = 53; 53 + 8 = 61.","en":"Next terms: 37 + 8 = 45, 45 + 8 = 53, 53 + 8 = 61."},{"af":"Gaan voort tot by die 10de term: 61 (7de); 69 (8ste); 77 (9de); 85 (10de).","en":"Carry on to the 10th term: 61 (7th), 69 (8th), 77 (9th), 85 (10th)."}],"answer":{"af":"Reël: tel 8 by. Volgende terme: 45; 53; 61. Die 10de term is 85.","en":"Rule: add 8. Next terms: 45, 53, 61. The 10th term is 85."}},{"title":{"af":"Konstante verskil of verhouding?","en":"Constant difference or ratio?"},"problem":{"af":"Is die patroon 4; 12; 36; … ’n patroon met ’n konstante verskil of ’n konstante verhouding? Gee die volgende twee terme.","en":"Is the pattern 4, 12, 36, … a pattern with a constant difference or a constant ratio? Give the next two terms."},"steps":[{"af":"Kyk na die verskille: 12 − 4 = 8 en 36 − 12 = 24. Hulle is nie dieselfde nie, dus is daar nie ’n konstante verskil nie.","en":"Look at the differences: 12 − 4 = 8 and 36 − 12 = 24. They are not the same, so there is no constant difference."},{"af":"Kyk of jy met dieselfde getal maal: 4 × 3 = 12 en 12 × 3 = 36. Ja – die reël is *maal 3*.","en":"Check whether you multiply by the same number: 4 × 3 = 12 and 12 × 3 = 36. Yes – the rule is *multiply by 3*."},{"af":"Volgende terme: 36 × 3 = 108 en 108 × 3 = 324.","en":"Next terms: 36 × 3 = 108 and 108 × 3 = 324."}],"answer":{"af":"’n Konstante verhouding (maal 3). Die volgende terme is 108 en 324.","en":"A constant ratio (multiply by 3). The next terms are 108 and 324."}},{"title":{"af":"Vloeidiagram vorentoe en terug","en":"Flow diagram forwards and backwards"},"problem":{"af":"Invoer → × 8 → − 5 → Uitvoer. Vind die uitvoer vir die invoere 3; 6 en 9. Watter invoer gee ’n uitvoer van 75?","en":"Input → × 8 → − 5 → Output. Find the output for the inputs 3, 6 and 9. Which input gives an output of 75?"},"steps":[{"af":"Vorentoe, in die volgorde van die pyle: 3 × 8 − 5 = 19; 6 × 8 − 5 = 43; 9 × 8 − 5 = 67.","en":"Forwards, in the order of the arrows: 3 × 8 − 5 = 19, 6 × 8 − 5 = 43, 9 × 8 − 5 = 67."},{"af":"Terug van 75: draai die volgorde en die bewerkings om. Eers 75 + 5 = 80.","en":"Backwards from 75: reverse the order and the operations. First 75 + 5 = 80."},{"af":"Dan 80 ÷ 8 = 10. Kontroleer: 10 × 8 − 5 = 75. Dit klop.","en":"Then 80 ÷ 8 = 10. Check: 10 × 8 − 5 = 75. It is correct."}],"answer":{"af":"Uitvoere: 19; 43; 67. ’n Invoer van 10 gee 75.","en":"Outputs: 19, 43, 67. An input of 10 gives 75."}},{"title":{"af":"Skryf en los ’n getalsin op","en":"Write and solve a number sentence"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter spaar elke week R35. Na hoeveel weke het hy R280 gespaar? Skryf ’n oop getalsin en los dit op.","en":"Pieter saves R35 every week. After how many weeks has he saved R280? Write an open number sentence and solve it."},"steps":[{"af":"Die aantal weke is onbekend: □ × 35 = 280.","en":"The number of weeks is unknown: □ × 35 = 280."},{"af":"Probeer-en-verbeter: 5 × 35 = 175 (te min). 10 × 35 = 350 (te veel). 8 × 35 = 280. Reg!","en":"Trial and improvement: 5 × 35 = 175 (too little). 10 × 35 = 350 (too much). 8 × 35 = 280. Correct!"},{"af":"Of gebruik die inverse bewerking: 280 ÷ 35 = 8.","en":"Or use the inverse operation: 280 ÷ 35 = 8."}],"answer":{"af":"□ × 35 = 280; □ = 8. Pieter het na 8 weke R280 gespaar.","en":"□ × 35 = 280; □ = 8. Pieter has saved R280 after 8 weeks."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die volgende term? 18; 27; 36; 45; …","en":"What is the next term? 18, 27, 36, 45, …"},"options":[{"af":"55","en":"55"},{"af":"54","en":"54"},{"af":"63","en":"63"},{"af":"50","en":"50"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die verskil tussen die terme is elke keer 9, dus is die reël *tel 9 by*: 45 + 9 = 54. 63 is die term daarna.","en":"The difference between the terms is 9 every time, so the rule is *add 9*: 45 + 9 = 54. 63 is the term after that."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter reël beskryf die patroon 2; 6; 18; 54?","en":"Which rule describes the pattern 2, 6, 18, 54?"},"options":[{"af":"Tel 4 by","en":"Add 4"},{"af":"Maal 2","en":"Multiply by 2"},{"af":"Tel 12 by","en":"Add 12"},{"af":"Maal 3","en":"Multiply by 3"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"2 × 3 = 6; 6 × 3 = 18; 18 × 3 = 54. *Tel 4 by* werk net vir die eerste twee terme – daarom moet jy altyd meer as twee terme toets.","en":"2 × 3 = 6, 6 × 3 = 18, 18 × 3 = 54. *Add 4* only works for the first two terms – that is why you must always test more than two terms."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"□ + 47 = 120, dus □ = ___","en":"□ + 47 = 120, so □ = ___"},"answers":{"af":["73"],"en":["73"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["167","83","63"],"en":["167","83","63"]}},"explain":{"af":"Gebruik die inverse bewerking: □ = 120 − 47 = 73. Kontroleer: 73 + 47 = 120. 167 kry jy as jy optel in plaas van aftrek.","en":"Use the inverse operation: □ = 120 − 47 = 73. Check: 73 + 47 = 120. You get 167 if you add instead of subtract."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die patroon 5; 10; 20; 40 het ’n konstante verskil.","en":"The pattern 5, 10, 20, 40 has a constant difference."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die verskille is 5; 10 en 20 – hulle verander. Elke term is egter die vorige term maal 2, dus het die patroon ’n konstante verhouding.","en":"False. The differences are 5, 10 and 20 – they change. But every term is the previous term multiplied by 2, so the pattern has a constant ratio."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Invoer → × 7 → + 3 → Uitvoer. Wat is die uitvoer as die invoer 9 is?","en":"Input → × 7 → + 3 → Output. What is the output when the input is 9?"},"options":[{"af":"66","en":"66"},{"af":"84","en":"84"},{"af":"63","en":"63"},{"af":"19","en":"19"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Volg die pyle: 9 × 7 = 63, dan 63 + 3 = 66. 84 kry jy as jy eers 3 bytel en dan maal – die verkeerde volgorde. 63 vergeet die + 3.","en":"Follow the arrows: 9 × 7 = 63, then 63 + 3 = 66. You get 84 if you add 3 first and then multiply – the wrong order. 63 forgets the + 3."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Invoer → × 5 → − 4 → Uitvoer. Die uitvoer is 46. Wat was die invoer?","en":"Input → × 5 → − 4 → Output. The output is 46. What was the input?"},"options":[{"af":"50","en":"50"},{"af":"226","en":"226"},{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"9","en":"9"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Werk terug met die inverse bewerkings in die omgekeerde volgorde: 46 + 4 = 50 en 50 ÷ 5 = 10. Kontroleer: 10 × 5 − 4 = 46. 50 is net die eerste stap.","en":"Work backwards with the inverse operations in the reverse order: 46 + 4 = 50 and 50 ÷ 5 = 10. Check: 10 × 5 − 4 = 46. 50 is only the first step."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke getalsin by die storie wat daarby pas.","en":"Match each number sentence to the story that fits it."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"□ + 15 = 40","en":"□ + 15 = 40"},"r":{"af":"Ek het ’n paar albasters. Ek kry nog 15 en het nou 40.","en":"I have some marbles. I get 15 more and now have 40."}},{"l":{"af":"40 − □ = 15","en":"40 − □ = 15"},"r":{"af":"Ek het 40 albasters en gee ’n paar weg. Nou het ek 15.","en":"I have 40 marbles and give some away. Now I have 15."}},{"l":{"af":"□ − 15 = 40","en":"□ − 15 = 40"},"r":{"af":"Ek verloor 15 albasters en het nog 40 oor.","en":"I lose 15 marbles and still have 40 left."}},{"l":{"af":"□ × 4 = 40","en":"□ × 4 = 40"},"r":{"af":"4 sakkies het elk ewe veel albasters. Altesaam is daar 40.","en":"4 bags each have the same number of marbles. Altogether there are 40."}},{"l":{"af":"40 ÷ 5 = □","en":"40 ÷ 5 = □"},"r":{"af":"Ek deel 40 albasters gelyk tussen 5 vriende.","en":"I share 40 marbles equally among 5 friends."}}],"explain":{"af":"Kyk wat onbekend is en wat gebeur. *Kry nog* is optel; *gee weg* en *verloor* is aftrek; *elk ewe veel* is vermenigvuldig; *deel gelyk* is deel.","en":"Look at what is unknown and what happens. *Get more* is addition; *give away* and *lose* are subtraction; *each the same* is multiplication; *share equally* is division."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi die patroon: 400; 350; 300; 250; ___","en":"Complete the pattern: 400, 350, 300, 250, ___"},"answers":{"af":["200"],"en":["200"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["150","225","240"],"en":["150","225","240"]}},"explain":{"af":"Elke term is 50 minder as die vorige een (konstante verskil): 250 − 50 = 200.","en":"Every term is 50 less than the one before (constant difference): 250 − 50 = 200."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In ’n tabel is die terme in posisie 1; 2; 3 en 4: 6; 12; 18; 24. Wat is die term in posisie 10?","en":"In a table the terms in positions 1, 2, 3 and 4 are: 6, 12, 18, 24. What is the term in position 10?"},"options":[{"af":"30","en":"30"},{"af":"54","en":"54"},{"af":"66","en":"66"},{"af":"60","en":"60"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die reël is *posisie × 6*, want 1 × 6 = 6; 2 × 6 = 12 ensovoorts. Posisie 10: 10 × 6 = 60. 30 is die term in posisie 5, nie 10 nie.","en":"The rule is *position × 6*, because 1 × 6 = 6, 2 × 6 = 12 and so on. Position 10: 10 × 6 = 60. 30 is the term in position 5, not 10."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy in ’n vloeidiagram terugwerk, gebruik jy die inverse bewerkings in die omgekeerde volgorde.","en":"When you work backwards in a flow diagram, you use the inverse operations in the reverse order."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Jy begin by die uitvoer en maak die laaste bewerking eerste ongedaan: + word −, − word +, × word ÷ en ÷ word ×.","en":"True. You start at the output and undo the last operation first: + becomes −, − becomes +, × becomes ÷ and ÷ becomes ×."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gebruik probeer-en-verbeter. Watter getal maak die getalsin waar? □ × 6 = 102","en":"Use trial and improvement. Which number makes the number sentence true? □ × 6 = 102"},"options":[{"af":"16","en":"16"},{"af":"17","en":"17"},{"af":"18","en":"18"},{"af":"96","en":"96"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"16 × 6 = 96 (te klein) en 18 × 6 = 108 (te groot), maar 17 × 6 = 102. Reg! 96 kry jy as jy 6 aftrek in plaas daarvan om te deel.","en":"16 × 6 = 96 (too small) and 18 × 6 = 108 (too big), but 17 × 6 = 102. Correct! You get 96 if you subtract 6 instead of dividing."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Fatima het R85. Sy koop ’n boek en het daarna R27 oor. Watter getalsin pas by die storie?","en":"Fatima has R85. She buys a book and then has R27 left. Which number sentence fits the story?"},"options":[{"af":"85 − □ = 27","en":"85 − □ = 27"},{"af":"85 + 27 = □","en":"85 + 27 = □"},{"af":"□ − 85 = 27","en":"□ − 85 = 27"},{"af":"27 − □ = 85","en":"27 − □ = 85"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Sy begin met R85, die prys van die boek (onbekend) gaan af, en R27 bly oor: 85 − □ = 27. Die boek kos dus R58.","en":"She starts with R85, the price of the book (unknown) is taken away, and R27 is left: 85 − □ = 27. So the book costs R58."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die patroon 1; 3; 9; 27; 81 het ’n konstante verhouding. Elke term word met ___ vermenigvuldig om die volgende term te kry.","en":"The pattern 1, 3, 9, 27, 81 has a constant ratio. Each term is multiplied by ___ to get the next term."},"answers":{"af":["3","drie"],"en":["3","three"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["2","6","9"],"en":["2","6","9"]}},"explain":{"af":"1 × 3 = 3; 3 × 3 = 9; 9 × 3 = 27; 27 × 3 = 81. Die eerste sprong is 2, maar die volgende sprong is 6, dus is dit nie *tel 2 by* nie.","en":"1 × 3 = 3, 3 × 3 = 9, 9 × 3 = 27, 27 × 3 = 81. The first jump is 2, but the next jump is 6, so it is not *add 2*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Patroon begin by 7 en die reël is *tel 6 by*. Watter een van hierdie getalle sal in die patroon wees?","en":"A pattern starts at 7 and the rule is *add 6*. Which one of these numbers will be in the pattern?"},"options":[{"af":"50","en":"50"},{"af":"52","en":"52"},{"af":"55","en":"55"},{"af":"58","en":"58"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die patroon is 7; 13; 19; 25; 31; 37; 43; 49; 55; … Elke term is 7 plus ’n veelvoud van 6. 55 = 7 + 48 en 48 = 8 × 6, dus is 55 in die patroon. Die ander getalle word oorgeslaan.","en":"The pattern is 7, 13, 19, 25, 31, 37, 43, 49, 55, … Every term is 7 plus a multiple of 6. 55 = 7 + 48 and 48 = 8 × 6, so 55 is in the pattern. The other numbers are skipped."}}]},{"id":"w5-t1-tyd","title":{"af":"Tyd","en":"Time"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die tyd op analoë en digitale horlosies kan lees, tussen 12-uur- en 24-uurtyd kan omskakel, tydseenhede kan omskakel en kan bereken hoe lank iets duur met behulp van kalenders en roosters.","en":"You will be able to read the time on analogue and digital clocks, convert between 12-hour and 24-hour time, convert units of time and calculate how long something lasts using calendars and timetables."},"summary":{"af":"## Analoë en digitale horlosies\n\n’n **Analoë horlosie** het **wysers**. Die kort **uurwyser** wys die uur en die lang **minuutwyser** wys die minute. Elke getal op die wyserplaat staan vir **5 minute** van die minuutwyser: by die 3 is dit 15 minute, by die 6 is dit 30 minute en by die 9 is dit 45 minute.\n\n’n **Digitale horlosie** wys die tyd net met syfers, soos 07:45. Die uur staan voor die dubbelpunt en die minute daarna.\n\n- 3:15 – kwart oor drie\n- 3:30 – halfvier (in Afrikaans is *halfvier* half pad na vier)\n- 3:40 – twintig voor vier\n- 3:45 – kwart voor vier\n\nBy 3:45 is die uurwyser al amper by die 4, maar dit is nog nie 4 uur nie. Die uur is die getal waarby die uurwyser **laaste verby** is.\n\n## 12-uurtyd en 24-uurtyd\n\nIn **12-uurtyd** tel ons elke dag twee keer van 1 tot 12. **vm.** (voormiddag) is van middernag tot 12 uur middag, en **nm.** (namiddag) is van 12 uur middag tot middernag. In **24-uurtyd** tel ons die ure van 00 tot 23, dus het ons nie vm. of nm. nodig nie.\n\n| 12-uurtyd | 24-uurtyd |\n|---|---|\n| 12:30 vm. (ná middernag) | 00:30 |\n| 6:30 vm. | 06:30 |\n| 12:00 middag | 12:00 |\n| 2:15 nm. | 14:15 |\n| 9:40 nm. | 21:40 |\n\n- **nm. na 24-uurtyd:** tel 12 by die uur: 2:15 nm. → 14:15. (Tussen 12 uur middag en 1 nm. bly die uur 12.)\n- **24-uurtyd na nm.:** trek 12 van die uur af: 21:40 → 9:40 nm.\n- **vm.-tye** bly dieselfde, met ’n 0 voor: 6:30 vm. → 06:30.\n\n> **Onthou:** In 24-uurtyd gaan die ure net tot 23:59. Ná 23:59 kom 00:00 – dit is middernag, en ’n nuwe dag begin.\n\n## Tydseenhede\n\n| Eenheid | Gelyk aan |\n|---|---|\n| 1 minuut | 60 sekondes |\n| 1 uur | 60 minute |\n| 1 dag | 24 uur |\n| 1 week | 7 dae |\n| 1 jaar | 12 maande, of 52 weke en 1 dag, of 365 dae |\n| 1 skrikkeljaar | 366 dae |\n| 1 dekade | 10 jaar |\n| 1 eeu | 100 jaar |\n\nVan ’n **groot eenheid na ’n klein eenheid maal** jy: 3 uur = 3 × 60 = 180 minute. Van **klein na groot deel** jy: 150 minute = 120 minute + 30 minute = 2 uur 30 minute.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Tyd werk in **sestigs**, nie in honderde nie. 1 uur 30 minute is 90 minute, nie 130 minute nie. Van 10:50 tot 11:20 is 30 minute – nie 70 nie, al is 1 120 − 1 050 = 70.\n\n## Tydsverloop\n\n**Tydsverloop** is hoe lank iets duur, van die **begintyd** tot die **eindtyd**. Spring op ’n tydlyn in maklike treë: eers tot by die volgende heel uur, dan heel ure, en dan die minute wat oorbly.\n\nVan 08:45 tot 11:20: 08:45 → 09:00 is 15 minute; 09:00 → 11:00 is 2 uur; 11:00 → 11:20 is 20 minute. Altesaam is dit **2 uur 35 minute**.\n\nOm die **eindtyd** te vind, tel jy die tydsduur by die begintyd: 14:40 + 1 uur → 15:40, en 15:40 + 35 minute → 16:15.\n\n## Kalenders\n\n- 30 dae: April, Junie, September en November.\n- Februarie: 28 dae, of **29** in ’n **skrikkeljaar**.\n- Al die ander maande het 31 dae.\n\n’n Skrikkeljaar kom gewoonlik elke vier jaar: 2024 was een en 2028 sal die volgende een wees.\n\nOm dae te tel, kyk op die kalender hoeveel dae elke maand het. Van 25 Maart tot 8 April is 6 dae (tot 31 Maart) plus 8 dae = **14 dae**.\n\n## Roosters\n\n’n **Rooster**, soos ’n busrooster, ’n TV-gids of ’n sportdagprogram, wys wanneer dinge begin en eindig. Lees eers die regte ry en kolom, en bereken dan die tydsverloop. Kyk mooi of die tye in 12-uurtyd of 24-uurtyd geskryf is.","en":"## Analogue and digital clocks\n\nAn **analogue clock** has **hands**. The short **hour hand** shows the hour and the long **minute hand** shows the minutes. Each number on the clock face stands for **5 minutes** of the minute hand: at the 3 it is 15 minutes, at the 6 it is 30 minutes and at the 9 it is 45 minutes.\n\nA **digital clock** shows the time with digits only, such as 07:45. The hour is before the colon and the minutes come after it.\n\n- 3:15 – quarter past three\n- 3:30 – half past three (in Afrikaans this is *halfvier*: half way to four)\n- 3:40 – twenty to four\n- 3:45 – quarter to four\n\nAt 3:45 the hour hand is almost at the 4, but it is not 4 o’clock yet. The hour is the number the hour hand has **last passed**.\n\n## 12-hour time and 24-hour time\n\nIn **12-hour time** we count from 1 to 12 twice every day. **a.m.** is from midnight to 12 noon, and **p.m.** is from 12 noon to midnight. In **24-hour time** we count the hours from 00 to 23, so we do not need a.m. or p.m.\n\n| 12-hour time | 24-hour time |\n|---|---|\n| 12:30 a.m. (after midnight) | 00:30 |\n| 6:30 a.m. | 06:30 |\n| 12:00 noon | 12:00 |\n| 2:15 p.m. | 14:15 |\n| 9:40 p.m. | 21:40 |\n\n- **p.m. to 24-hour time:** add 12 to the hour: 2:15 p.m. → 14:15. (Between 12 noon and 1 p.m. the hour stays 12.)\n- **24-hour time to p.m.:** subtract 12 from the hour: 21:40 → 9:40 p.m.\n- **a.m. times** stay the same, with a 0 in front: 6:30 a.m. → 06:30.\n\n> **Remember:** In 24-hour time the hours only go up to 23:59. After 23:59 comes 00:00 – that is midnight, and a new day begins.\n\n## Units of time\n\n| Unit | Equal to |\n|---|---|\n| 1 minute | 60 seconds |\n| 1 hour | 60 minutes |\n| 1 day | 24 hours |\n| 1 week | 7 days |\n| 1 year | 12 months, or 52 weeks and 1 day, or 365 days |\n| 1 leap year | 366 days |\n| 1 decade | 10 years |\n| 1 century | 100 years |\n\nFrom a **big unit to a small unit you multiply**: 3 hours = 3 × 60 = 180 minutes. From **small to big you divide**: 150 minutes = 120 minutes + 30 minutes = 2 hours 30 minutes.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Time works in **sixties**, not in hundreds. 1 hour 30 minutes is 90 minutes, not 130 minutes. From 10:50 to 11:20 is 30 minutes – not 70, even though 1 120 − 1 050 = 70.\n\n## Elapsed time\n\n**Elapsed time** is how long something lasts, from the **start time** to the **end time**. Jump along a time line in easy steps: first to the next whole hour, then whole hours, and then the minutes that are left.\n\nFrom 08:45 to 11:20: 08:45 → 09:00 is 15 minutes; 09:00 → 11:00 is 2 hours; 11:00 → 11:20 is 20 minutes. Altogether that is **2 hours 35 minutes**.\n\nTo find the **end time**, you add the duration to the start time: 14:40 + 1 hour → 15:40, and 15:40 + 35 minutes → 16:15.\n\n## Calendars\n\n- 30 days: April, June, September and November.\n- February: 28 days, or **29** in a **leap year**.\n- All the other months have 31 days.\n\nA leap year usually comes every four years: 2024 was one and 2028 will be the next one.\n\nTo count days, check on the calendar how many days each month has. From 25 March to 8 April is 6 days (to 31 March) plus 8 days = **14 days**.\n\n## Timetables\n\nA **timetable**, such as a bus timetable, a TV guide or a sports day programme, shows when things start and end. First read the correct row and column, and then calculate the elapsed time. Check carefully whether the times are written in 12-hour or 24-hour time."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Analoë horlosie","en":"Analogue clock"},"def":{"af":"’n Horlosie met ’n uurwyser en ’n minuutwyser wat op ’n wyserplaat met getalle wys.","en":"A clock with an hour hand and a minute hand that point to a clock face with numbers."}},{"term":{"af":"Digitale horlosie","en":"Digital clock"},"def":{"af":"’n Horlosie wat die tyd net met syfers wys, soos 14:25.","en":"A clock that shows the time with digits only, such as 14:25."}},{"term":{"af":"vm. en nm.","en":"a.m. and p.m."},"def":{"af":"vm. (voormiddag) is van middernag tot 12 uur middag; nm. (namiddag) is van 12 uur middag tot middernag.","en":"a.m. is from midnight to 12 noon; p.m. is from 12 noon to midnight."}},{"term":{"af":"24-uurtyd","en":"24-hour time"},"def":{"af":"’n Manier om tyd te skryf waar die ure van 00 tot 23 tel, soos 18:30 vir 6:30 nm.","en":"A way of writing time where the hours count from 00 to 23, such as 18:30 for 6:30 p.m."}},{"term":{"af":"Middernag","en":"Midnight"},"def":{"af":"12 uur in die nag, wanneer ’n nuwe dag begin; in 24-uurtyd is dit 00:00.","en":"12 o’clock at night, when a new day begins; in 24-hour time it is 00:00."}},{"term":{"af":"Tydsverloop","en":"Elapsed time"},"def":{"af":"Hoe lank iets duur, van die begintyd tot die eindtyd.","en":"How long something lasts, from the start time to the end time."}},{"term":{"af":"Skrikkeljaar","en":"Leap year"},"def":{"af":"’n Jaar met 366 dae, want Februarie het dan 29 dae; dit kom gewoonlik elke vier jaar.","en":"A year with 366 days, because February then has 29 days; it usually comes every four years."}},{"term":{"af":"Dekade","en":"Decade"},"def":{"af":"’n Tydperk van 10 jaar.","en":"A period of 10 years."}},{"term":{"af":"Eeu","en":"Century"},"def":{"af":"’n Tydperk van 100 jaar.","en":"A period of 100 years."}},{"term":{"af":"Rooster","en":"Timetable"},"def":{"af":"’n Tabel wat wys wanneer dinge begin en eindig, soos ’n busrooster of skoolrooster.","en":"A table that shows when things start and end, such as a bus timetable or school timetable."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Skakel tussen 12-uur- en 24-uurtyd om","en":"Convert between 12-hour and 24-hour time"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf in 24-uurtyd: (a) 4:25 nm. (b) 7:05 vm. Skryf in 12-uurtyd: (c) 19:50 (d) 00:40","en":"Write in 24-hour time: (a) 4:25 p.m. (b) 7:05 a.m. Write in 12-hour time: (c) 19:50 (d) 00:40"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Dit is nm., dus tel 12 by die uur: 4 + 12 = 16. Antwoord: 16:25.","en":"(a) It is p.m., so add 12 to the hour: 4 + 12 = 16. Answer: 16:25."},{"af":"(b) Dit is vm., dus bly die tyd dieselfde met ’n 0 voor: 07:05.","en":"(b) It is a.m., so the time stays the same with a 0 in front: 07:05."},{"af":"(c) Die uur is meer as 12, dus trek 12 af: 19 − 12 = 7. Antwoord: 7:50 nm.","en":"(c) The hour is more than 12, so subtract 12: 19 − 12 = 7. Answer: 7:50 p.m."},{"af":"(d) 00 is die uur ná middernag, dus is dit 12:40 vm.","en":"(d) 00 is the hour after midnight, so it is 12:40 a.m."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 16:25 (b) 07:05 (c) 7:50 nm. (d) 12:40 vm.","en":"(a) 16:25 (b) 07:05 (c) 7:50 p.m. (d) 12:40 a.m."}},{"title":{"af":"Hoe lank duur die fliek?","en":"How long is the film?"},"problem":{"af":"’n Fliek begin om 14:35 en eindig om 16:20. Hoe lank duur die fliek?","en":"A film starts at 14:35 and ends at 16:20. How long is the film?"},"steps":[{"af":"Spring van 14:35 tot by die volgende heel uur, 15:00: dit is 25 minute.","en":"Jump from 14:35 to the next whole hour, 15:00: that is 25 minutes."},{"af":"Spring van 15:00 tot 16:00: dit is 1 uur.","en":"Jump from 15:00 to 16:00: that is 1 hour."},{"af":"Spring van 16:00 tot 16:20: dit is 20 minute.","en":"Jump from 16:00 to 16:20: that is 20 minutes."},{"af":"Tel bymekaar: 1 uur + 25 minute + 20 minute = 1 uur 45 minute.","en":"Add up: 1 hour + 25 minutes + 20 minutes = 1 hour 45 minutes."}],"answer":{"af":"Die fliek duur 1 uur 45 minute.","en":"The film lasts 1 hour 45 minutes."}},{"title":{"af":"Tydseenhede omskakel","en":"Converting units of time"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato oefen elke week 3 uur 45 minute netbal. (a) Hoeveel minute is dit? (b) Sy oefen al 4 weke en 5 dae lank vir ’n toernooi. Hoeveel dae is dit?","en":"Lerato practises netball for 3 hours 45 minutes every week. (a) How many minutes is that? (b) She has been practising for a tournament for 4 weeks and 5 days. How many days is that?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Uur na minute is groot na klein, dus maal: 3 × 60 = 180 minute.","en":"(a) Hours to minutes is big to small, so multiply: 3 × 60 = 180 minutes."},{"af":"Tel die ekstra minute by: 180 + 45 = 225 minute.","en":"Add the extra minutes: 180 + 45 = 225 minutes."},{"af":"(b) Weke na dae: 4 × 7 = 28 dae, en 28 + 5 = 33 dae.","en":"(b) Weeks to days: 4 × 7 = 28 days, and 28 + 5 = 33 days."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 225 minute (b) 33 dae","en":"(a) 225 minutes (b) 33 days"}},{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n sportdagprogram","en":"Read a sports day programme"},"problem":{"af":"Jou skool se sportdagprogram: 100 m-wedlope 09:15–10:00; verspring 10:10–11:25; ete-pouse 11:25–12:00. (a) Hoe lank duur die verspring? (b) Hoeveel minute is daar tussen die einde van die wedlope en die begin van die verspring? (c) Skryf die begintyd van die ete-pouse in 12-uurtyd.","en":"Your school’s sports day programme: 100 m races 09:15–10:00; long jump 10:10–11:25; lunch break 11:25–12:00. (a) How long does the long jump last? (b) How many minutes are there between the end of the races and the start of the long jump? (c) Write the start time of the lunch break in 12-hour time."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) 10:10 → 11:10 is 1 uur, en 11:10 → 11:25 is 15 minute. Die verspring duur 1 uur 15 minute.","en":"(a) 10:10 → 11:10 is 1 hour, and 11:10 → 11:25 is 15 minutes. The long jump lasts 1 hour 15 minutes."},{"af":"(b) Die wedlope eindig om 10:00 en die verspring begin om 10:10: dit is 10 minute.","en":"(b) The races end at 10:00 and the long jump starts at 10:10: that is 10 minutes."},{"af":"(c) 11:25 is voor 12 uur middag, dus is dit 11:25 vm.","en":"(c) 11:25 is before 12 noon, so it is 11:25 a.m."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 1 uur 15 minute (b) 10 minute (c) 11:25 vm.","en":"(a) 1 hour 15 minutes (b) 10 minutes (c) 11:25 a.m."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 3:45 nm. in 24-uurtyd?","en":"What is 3:45 p.m. in 24-hour time?"},"options":[{"af":"13:45","en":"13:45"},{"af":"15:45","en":"15:45"},{"af":"03:45","en":"03:45"},{"af":"16:45","en":"16:45"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Vir ’n nm.-tyd tel jy 12 by die uur: 3 + 12 = 15, dus 15:45. 03:45 is in die nag, voor dagbreek.","en":"For a p.m. time you add 12 to the hour: 3 + 12 = 15, so 15:45. 03:45 is in the night, before sunrise."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel minute is 2 uur 15 minute?","en":"How many minutes is 2 hours 15 minutes?"},"options":[{"af":"135 minute","en":"135 minutes"},{"af":"215 minute","en":"215 minutes"},{"af":"120 minute","en":"120 minutes"},{"af":"75 minute","en":"75 minutes"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"1 uur = 60 minute, dus 2 uur = 120 minute. 120 + 15 = 135 minute. 215 kry jy as jy dink daar is 100 minute in ’n uur.","en":"1 hour = 60 minutes, so 2 hours = 120 minutes. 120 + 15 = 135 minutes. You get 215 if you think there are 100 minutes in an hour."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Skrikkeljaar het ___ dae.","en":"A leap year has ___ days."},"answers":{"af":["366"],"en":["366"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["365","364","360"],"en":["365","364","360"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Gewone jaar het 365 dae. In ’n skrikkeljaar het Februarie 29 dae in plaas van 28, dus is daar een dag meer: 366.","en":"An ordinary year has 365 days. In a leap year February has 29 days instead of 28, so there is one more day: 366."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"17:30 in 24-uurtyd is dieselfde as 5:30 nm.","en":"17:30 in 24-hour time is the same as 5:30 p.m."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die uur is meer as 12, dus trek jy 12 af: 17 − 12 = 5. Dit is in die middag, dus 5:30 nm.","en":"True. The hour is more than 12, so you subtract 12: 17 − 12 = 5. It is in the afternoon, so 5:30 p.m."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Rugbywedstryd begin om 15:30 en eindig om 17:05. Hoe lank het dit geduur?","en":"A rugby match starts at 15:30 and ends at 17:05. How long did it last?"},"options":[{"af":"2 uur 35 minute","en":"2 hours 35 minutes"},{"af":"1 uur 75 minute","en":"1 hour 75 minutes"},{"af":"1 uur 35 minute","en":"1 hour 35 minutes"},{"af":"1 uur 25 minute","en":"1 hour 25 minutes"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"15:30 → 16:00 is 30 minute; 16:00 → 17:00 is 1 uur; 17:00 → 17:05 is 5 minute. Altesaam 1 uur 35 minute. *1 uur 75 minute* kom van 1 705 − 1 530 = 175, maar tyd werk nie in honderde nie.","en":"15:30 → 16:00 is 30 minutes; 16:00 → 17:00 is 1 hour; 17:00 → 17:05 is 5 minutes. Altogether 1 hour 35 minutes. *1 hour 75 minutes* comes from 1 705 − 1 530 = 175, but time does not work in hundreds."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel jaar is 2 eeue en 3 dekades?","en":"How many years are 2 centuries and 3 decades?"},"options":[{"af":"23 jaar","en":"23 years"},{"af":"203 jaar","en":"203 years"},{"af":"2 030 jaar","en":"2 030 years"},{"af":"230 jaar","en":"230 years"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"1 eeu = 100 jaar, dus 2 eeue = 200 jaar. 1 dekade = 10 jaar, dus 3 dekades = 30 jaar. 200 + 30 = 230 jaar.","en":"1 century = 100 years, so 2 centuries = 200 years. 1 decade = 10 years, so 3 decades = 30 years. 200 + 30 = 230 years."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke tydseenheid by wat dit gelyk aan is.","en":"Match each unit of time to what it is equal to."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"1 minuut","en":"1 minute"},"r":{"af":"60 sekondes","en":"60 seconds"}},{"l":{"af":"1 dag","en":"1 day"},"r":{"af":"24 uur","en":"24 hours"}},{"l":{"af":"1 week","en":"1 week"},"r":{"af":"7 dae","en":"7 days"}},{"l":{"af":"1 dekade","en":"1 decade"},"r":{"af":"10 jaar","en":"10 years"}},{"l":{"af":"1 eeu","en":"1 century"},"r":{"af":"100 jaar","en":"100 years"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hierdie omskakelings moet jy uit jou kop ken. Let op: ’n dekade is 10 jaar en ’n eeu is 100 jaar – moenie die twee omruil nie.","en":"You must know these conversions by heart. Note: a decade is 10 years and a century is 100 years – don’t swap the two."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Fliek begin om 18:40 en duur 1 uur 50 minute. Dit eindig om ___.","en":"A film starts at 18:40 and lasts 1 hour 50 minutes. It ends at ___."},"answers":{"af":["20:30","20h30","20.30"],"en":["20:30","20h30","20.30"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["19:30","20:20","20:40"],"en":["19:30","20:20","20:40"]}},"explain":{"af":"Tel eers die uur by: 18:40 + 1 uur = 19:40. Tel dan 50 minute by: 19:40 + 20 minute = 20:00, en nog 30 minute = 20:30.","en":"First add the hour: 18:40 + 1 hour = 19:40. Then add 50 minutes: 19:40 + 20 minutes = 20:00, and 30 more minutes = 20:30."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op ’n analoë horlosie is die uurwyser amper by die 6 en die minuutwyser wys na die 9. Hoe laat is dit?","en":"On an analogue clock the hour hand is almost at the 6 and the minute hand points to the 9. What time is it?"},"options":[{"af":"6:45","en":"6:45"},{"af":"5:45","en":"5:45"},{"af":"9:30","en":"9:30"},{"af":"5:15","en":"5:15"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die minuutwyser by die 9 beteken 45 minute (9 × 5). Die uurwyser is amper by die 6, maar nog nie daar nie, dus is die uur 5. Dit is 5:45, oftewel kwart voor ses.","en":"The minute hand at the 9 means 45 minutes (9 × 5). The hour hand is almost at the 6 but not there yet, so the hour is 5. It is 5:45, or quarter to six."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Van 10:50 tot 11:20 is 70 minute.","en":"From 10:50 to 11:20 is 70 minutes."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 10:50 → 11:00 is 10 minute en 11:00 → 11:20 is 20 minute, altesaam 30 minute. 70 kry jy as jy die tye soos gewone getalle aftrek (1 120 − 1 050).","en":"False. 10:50 → 11:00 is 10 minutes and 11:00 → 11:20 is 20 minutes, altogether 30 minutes. You get 70 if you subtract the times like ordinary numbers (1 120 − 1 050)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo verjaar op 3 Mei. Vandag is 18 April. Oor hoeveel dae verjaar hy?","en":"Thabo’s birthday is on 3 May. Today is 18 April. In how many days is his birthday?"},"options":[{"af":"15 dae","en":"15 days"},{"af":"16 dae","en":"16 days"},{"af":"14 dae","en":"14 days"},{"af":"21 dae","en":"21 days"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"April het 30 dae. Van 18 April tot 30 April is 12 dae, en dan nog 3 dae tot 3 Mei: 12 + 3 = 15 dae. As jy dink April het 31 dae, kry jy 16.","en":"April has 30 days. From 18 April to 30 April is 12 days, and then 3 more days to 3 May: 12 + 3 = 15 days. If you think April has 31 days, you get 16."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"180 sekondes = ___ minute","en":"180 seconds = ___ minutes"},"answers":{"af":["3","drie"],"en":["3","three"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["18","30","2"],"en":["18","30","2"]}},"explain":{"af":"Van klein (sekondes) na groot (minute) deel jy: 180 ÷ 60 = 3 minute. 18 kry jy as jy deur 10 deel.","en":"From small (seconds) to big (minutes) you divide: 180 ÷ 60 = 3 minutes. You get 18 if you divide by 10."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 00:25 in 12-uurtyd?","en":"What is 00:25 in 12-hour time?"},"options":[{"af":"12:25 nm.","en":"12:25 p.m."},{"af":"0:25 nm.","en":"0:25 p.m."},{"af":"10:25 vm.","en":"10:25 a.m."},{"af":"12:25 vm.","en":"12:25 a.m."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"00:25 is 25 minute ná middernag. Dit is in die nag, dus vm.: 12:25 vm. 12:25 nm. is 25 minute ná 12 uur middag (12:25 in 24-uurtyd).","en":"00:25 is 25 minutes after midnight. It is in the night, so a.m.: 12:25 a.m. 12:25 p.m. is 25 minutes after 12 noon (12:25 in 24-hour time)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Bus vertrek om 07:15 by die stasie en kom om 08:05 by die skool aan. Hoe lank is die rit?","en":"A bus leaves the station at 07:15 and arrives at the school at 08:05. How long is the trip?"},"options":[{"af":"90 minute","en":"90 minutes"},{"af":"1 uur 50 minute","en":"1 hour 50 minutes"},{"af":"50 minute","en":"50 minutes"},{"af":"40 minute","en":"40 minutes"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"07:15 → 08:00 is 45 minute en 08:00 → 08:05 is 5 minute: 45 + 5 = 50 minute. 90 kom van 805 − 715, maar tyd werk in sestigs.","en":"07:15 → 08:00 is 45 minutes and 08:00 → 08:05 is 5 minutes: 45 + 5 = 50 minutes. 90 comes from 805 − 715, but time works in sixties."}}]},{"id":"w5-t1-2d-vorms","title":{"af":"2D-vorms en hoeke","en":"2D shapes and angles"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal veelhoeke en vierhoeke kan benoem en beskryf, hoeke as regte hoeke, skerphoeke of stomphoeke kan klassifiseer, en vorms volgens hul eienskappe kan sorteer.","en":"You will be able to name and describe polygons and quadrilaterals, classify angles as right, acute or obtuse angles, and sort shapes according to their properties."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is ’n 2D-vorm?\n\n’n **2D-vorm** (tweedimensionele vorm) is plat: dit het net lengte en breedte, soos ’n tekening op papier. Die sye kan **reguit** of **geboë** wees. ’n **Sirkel** het een geboë sy en geen hoeke nie.\n\n’n **Veelhoek** is ’n geslote 2D-vorm met **net reguit sye**. Die punt waar twee sye bymekaarkom, is ’n **hoekpunt**, en daar vorm ’n **hoek**. In ’n veelhoek is die getal sye, hoeke en hoekpunte altyd dieselfde.\n\n| Naam | Sye en hoeke | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Driehoek | 3 | ’n padteken wat waarsku |\n| Vierhoek | 4 | ’n deur of ’n boek |\n| Vyfhoek | 5 | ’n huisie met ’n puntdak in ’n tekening |\n| Seshoek | 6 | ’n sel van ’n heuningkoek |\n| Sewehoek | 7 | kom minder voor |\n| Agthoek | 8 | ’n stopteken |\n\n’n Sirkel is **nie** ’n veelhoek nie, want sy sy is geboë.\n\n## Hoeke\n\n’n **Hoek** wys hoe ver twee lyne van mekaar af **oopdraai**. Ons meet hoeke in **grade (°)**. Vergelyk elke hoek met ’n **regte hoek** – die hoek van ’n blad papier.\n\n| Hoek | Grootte | Hoe dit lyk |\n|---|---|---|\n| Regte hoek | presies 90° | soos die hoek van ’n boek; ons merk dit met ’n klein vierkantjie |\n| Skerphoek | kleiner as 90° | meer toe as ’n regte hoek |\n| Stomphoek | groter as 90° maar kleiner as 180° | meer oop as ’n regte hoek |\n\n**Toets met papier:** hou die hoek van ’n blad papier teen die hoek. Pas die hoek binne-in die papierhoek? Dan is dit ’n skerphoek. Pas dit presies? ’n Regte hoek. Steek dit by die papier uit? ’n Stomphoek.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die grootte van ’n hoek hang **nie** af van hoe lank sy arms is nie, net van hoe ver hulle oopdraai. ’n Klein tekening kan ’n groter hoek hê as ’n groot tekening.\n\nPas ook op met twee woorde wat amper dieselfde klink: ’n **reghoek** is ’n vorm, maar ’n **regte hoek** is ’n hoek van 90°.\n\n## Vierhoeke\n\n**Parallelle lyne** bly altyd ewe ver van mekaar af en kruis nooit, soos die twee spore van ’n treinspoor.\n\n| Vierhoek | Sye | Hoeke |\n|---|---|---|\n| Vierkant | 4 ewe lang sye; oorkantste sye parallel | 4 regte hoeke |\n| Reghoek | oorkantste sye ewe lank en parallel | 4 regte hoeke |\n| Parallelogram | oorkantste sye ewe lank en parallel | oorkantste hoeke ewe groot |\n\n’n Parallelogram lyk soos ’n reghoek wat skeef gedruk is: dit het gewoonlik 2 skerphoeke en 2 stomphoeke. ’n **Vierkant is ’n spesiale reghoek** – dit het al die eienskappe van ’n reghoek, plus 4 ewe lang sye.\n\n## Reëlmatig en onreëlmatig\n\n’n **Reëlmatige veelhoek** het **al sy sye ewe lank én al sy hoeke ewe groot**. As een van die twee nie waar is nie, is die veelhoek **onreëlmatig**.\n\n- ’n Vierkant is ’n reëlmatige vierhoek.\n- ’n Reghoek wat nie ’n vierkant is nie, is onreëlmatig: sy hoeke is gelyk, maar sy sye nie.\n- ’n Stopteken is ’n reëlmatige agthoek.\n- ’n Driehoek met drie ewe lang sye is ’n reëlmatige driehoek.\n\n> **Onthou:** Vir ’n reëlmatige veelhoek moet **albei** waar wees: gelyke sye **en** gelyke hoeke.\n\n## Vorms sorteer\n\nJy kan vorms volgens hul **eienskappe** sorteer:\n\n1. Reguit of geboë sye?\n2. Hoeveel sye en hoeke?\n3. Watter soort hoeke: regte, skerp of stomp?\n4. Is daar parallelle sye?\n5. Reëlmatig of onreëlmatig?\n\nVoorbeeld: ’n vierkant, ’n reghoek en ’n driehoek met ’n regte hoek het almal ten minste een regte hoek. ’n Sirkel en ’n halfsirkel het albei ’n geboë sy. ’n Reëlmatige seshoek het geen regte hoeke nie, want al ses sy hoeke is stomphoeke.","en":"## What is a 2D shape?\n\nA **2D shape** (two-dimensional shape) is flat: it has only length and breadth, like a drawing on paper. The sides can be **straight** or **curved**. A **circle** has one curved side and no angles.\n\nA **polygon** is a closed 2D shape with **only straight sides**. The point where two sides meet is a **vertex**, and an **angle** forms there. In a polygon the number of sides, angles and vertices is always the same.\n\n| Name | Sides and angles | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Triangle | 3 | a road sign that warns |\n| Quadrilateral | 4 | a door or a book |\n| Pentagon | 5 | a little house with a pointed roof in a drawing |\n| Hexagon | 6 | a cell of a honeycomb |\n| Heptagon | 7 | not seen as often |\n| Octagon | 8 | a stop sign |\n\nA circle is **not** a polygon, because its side is curved.\n\n## Angles\n\nAn **angle** shows how far two lines **open** away from each other. We measure angles in **degrees (°)**. Compare every angle with a **right angle** – the corner of a sheet of paper.\n\n| Angle | Size | What it looks like |\n|---|---|---|\n| Right angle | exactly 90° | like the corner of a book; we mark it with a small square |\n| Acute angle | smaller than 90° | more closed than a right angle |\n| Obtuse angle | bigger than 90° but smaller than 180° | more open than a right angle |\n\n**Test with paper:** hold the corner of a sheet of paper against the angle. Does the angle fit inside the paper corner? Then it is an acute angle. Does it fit exactly? A right angle. Does it stick out past the paper? An obtuse angle.\n\n> **Common mistake:** The size of an angle does **not** depend on how long its arms are, only on how far they open. A small drawing can have a bigger angle than a big drawing.\n\nIn Afrikaans, also be careful with two words that sound almost the same: a *reghoek* is a rectangle, but a *regte hoek* is a right angle of 90°.\n\n## Quadrilaterals\n\n**Parallel lines** always stay the same distance apart and never cross, like the two rails of a railway line.\n\n| Quadrilateral | Sides | Angles |\n|---|---|---|\n| Square | 4 equal sides; opposite sides parallel | 4 right angles |\n| Rectangle | opposite sides equal and parallel | 4 right angles |\n| Parallelogram | opposite sides equal and parallel | opposite angles equal |\n\nA parallelogram looks like a rectangle that has been pushed over: it usually has 2 acute angles and 2 obtuse angles. A **square is a special rectangle** – it has all the properties of a rectangle, plus 4 equal sides.\n\n## Regular and irregular\n\nA **regular polygon** has **all its sides equal and all its angles equal**. If one of the two is not true, the polygon is **irregular**.\n\n- A square is a regular quadrilateral.\n- A rectangle that is not a square is irregular: its angles are equal, but its sides are not.\n- A stop sign is a regular octagon.\n- A triangle with three equal sides is a regular triangle.\n\n> **Remember:** For a regular polygon **both** must be true: equal sides **and** equal angles.\n\n## Sorting shapes\n\nYou can sort shapes according to their **properties**:\n\n1. Straight or curved sides?\n2. How many sides and angles?\n3. Which kind of angles: right, acute or obtuse?\n4. Are there parallel sides?\n5. Regular or irregular?\n\nExample: a square, a rectangle and a triangle with a right angle all have at least one right angle. A circle and a semicircle both have a curved side. A regular hexagon has no right angles, because all six of its angles are obtuse."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Veelhoek","en":"Polygon"},"def":{"af":"’n Geslote 2D-vorm met net reguit sye, soos ’n driehoek of ’n seshoek.","en":"A closed 2D shape with only straight sides, such as a triangle or a hexagon."}},{"term":{"af":"Vierhoek","en":"Quadrilateral"},"def":{"af":"Enige veelhoek met 4 sye en 4 hoeke, soos ’n vierkant, reghoek of parallelogram.","en":"Any polygon with 4 sides and 4 angles, such as a square, rectangle or parallelogram."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoekpunt","en":"Vertex"},"def":{"af":"Die punt waar twee sye van ’n vorm bymekaarkom.","en":"The point where two sides of a shape meet."}},{"term":{"af":"Regte hoek","en":"Right angle"},"def":{"af":"’n Hoek van presies 90°, soos die hoek van ’n blad papier.","en":"An angle of exactly 90°, like the corner of a sheet of paper."}},{"term":{"af":"Skerphoek","en":"Acute angle"},"def":{"af":"’n Hoek wat kleiner as ’n regte hoek (90°) is.","en":"An angle that is smaller than a right angle (90°)."}},{"term":{"af":"Stomphoek","en":"Obtuse angle"},"def":{"af":"’n Hoek wat groter as ’n regte hoek (90°) maar kleiner as 180° is.","en":"An angle that is bigger than a right angle (90°) but smaller than 180°."}},{"term":{"af":"Parallelle lyne","en":"Parallel lines"},"def":{"af":"Lyne wat altyd ewe ver van mekaar af bly en mekaar nooit kruis nie.","en":"Lines that always stay the same distance apart and never cross each other."}},{"term":{"af":"Parallelogram","en":"Parallelogram"},"def":{"af":"’n Vierhoek waarvan die oorkantste sye ewe lank en parallel is.","en":"A quadrilateral whose opposite sides are equal in length and parallel."}},{"term":{"af":"Reëlmatige veelhoek","en":"Regular polygon"},"def":{"af":"’n Veelhoek waarvan al die sye ewe lank en al die hoeke ewe groot is.","en":"A polygon whose sides are all equal and whose angles are all equal."}},{"term":{"af":"Onreëlmatige veelhoek","en":"Irregular polygon"},"def":{"af":"’n Veelhoek waarvan die sye of die hoeke nie almal ewe groot is nie.","en":"A polygon whose sides or angles are not all the same size."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Benoem ’n veelhoek","en":"Name a polygon"},"problem":{"af":"’n Vorm het 6 reguit sye wat nie almal ewe lank is nie. Wat is sy naam? Hoeveel hoeke en hoekpunte het dit? Is dit reëlmatig?","en":"A shape has 6 straight sides that are not all the same length. What is its name? How many angles and vertices does it have? Is it regular?"},"steps":[{"af":"Net reguit sye, dus is dit ’n veelhoek. 6 sye beteken dit is ’n seshoek.","en":"Only straight sides, so it is a polygon. 6 sides means it is a hexagon."},{"af":"In ’n veelhoek is die getal sye, hoeke en hoekpunte dieselfde: 6 hoeke en 6 hoekpunte.","en":"In a polygon the number of sides, angles and vertices is the same: 6 angles and 6 vertices."},{"af":"Die sye is nie almal ewe lank nie, dus kan dit nie reëlmatig wees nie.","en":"The sides are not all the same length, so it cannot be regular."}],"answer":{"af":"’n Onreëlmatige seshoek met 6 hoeke en 6 hoekpunte.","en":"An irregular hexagon with 6 angles and 6 vertices."}},{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer hoeke","en":"Classify angles"},"problem":{"af":"Sê of elke hoek ’n regte hoek, skerphoek of stomphoek is: 45°; 90°; 120°; 89°; 170°","en":"Say whether each angle is a right angle, an acute angle or an obtuse angle: 45°, 90°, 120°, 89°, 170°"},"steps":[{"af":"Vergelyk elkeen met 90°. Presies 90° is ’n regte hoek.","en":"Compare each one with 90°. Exactly 90° is a right angle."},{"af":"Kleiner as 90° is skerp: 45° en 89°. (89° is baie naby, maar steeds kleiner.)","en":"Smaller than 90° is acute: 45° and 89°. (89° is very close, but still smaller.)"},{"af":"Groter as 90° (maar kleiner as 180°) is stomp: 120° en 170°.","en":"Bigger than 90° (but smaller than 180°) is obtuse: 120° and 170°."}],"answer":{"af":"45° – skerp; 90° – regte hoek; 120° – stomp; 89° – skerp; 170° – stomp","en":"45° – acute; 90° – right angle; 120° – obtuse; 89° – acute; 170° – obtuse"}},{"title":{"af":"Hoeke in ’n parallelogram","en":"Angles in a parallelogram"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho teken ’n parallelogram wat skeef lê (dit is nie ’n reghoek nie). Hoeveel regte hoeke, skerphoeke en stomphoeke het dit?","en":"Sipho draws a parallelogram that leans over (it is not a rectangle). How many right angles, acute angles and obtuse angles does it have?"},"steps":[{"af":"’n Parallelogram het 4 hoeke. Omdat dit skeef lê, is geen van die hoeke 90° nie: 0 regte hoeke.","en":"A parallelogram has 4 angles. Because it leans over, none of the angles is 90°: 0 right angles."},{"af":"Twee oorkantste hoeke is ‘toegedruk’ – kleiner as 90°: 2 skerphoeke.","en":"Two opposite angles are ‘squashed’ – smaller than 90°: 2 acute angles."},{"af":"Die ander twee oorkantste hoeke is ‘oopgetrek’ – groter as 90°: 2 stomphoeke.","en":"The other two opposite angles are ‘pulled open’ – bigger than 90°: 2 obtuse angles."}],"answer":{"af":"0 regte hoeke, 2 skerphoeke en 2 stomphoeke.","en":"0 right angles, 2 acute angles and 2 obtuse angles."}},{"title":{"af":"Sorteer vorms","en":"Sort shapes"},"problem":{"af":"Sorteer hierdie vorms in drie groepe: (a) het ten minste een regte hoek, (b) het ’n geboë sy, (c) nie een van die twee nie. Vorms: vierkant, sirkel, reëlmatige seshoek, reghoek, driehoek met ’n regte hoek, halfsirkel.","en":"Sort these shapes into three groups: (a) has at least one right angle, (b) has a curved side, (c) neither of the two. Shapes: square, circle, regular hexagon, rectangle, triangle with a right angle, semicircle."},"steps":[{"af":"Regte hoeke: ’n vierkant en ’n reghoek het elk 4; die driehoek het 1.","en":"Right angles: a square and a rectangle each have 4; the triangle has 1."},{"af":"Geboë sye: die sirkel en die halfsirkel.","en":"Curved sides: the circle and the semicircle."},{"af":"Die reëlmatige seshoek het net reguit sye, en al sy hoeke is stomp, dus pas dit in groep (c).","en":"The regular hexagon has only straight sides, and all its angles are obtuse, so it fits in group (c)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) vierkant, reghoek, driehoek met ’n regte hoek; (b) sirkel, halfsirkel; (c) reëlmatige seshoek","en":"(a) square, rectangle, triangle with a right angle; (b) circle, semicircle; (c) regular hexagon"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel sye het ’n agthoek?","en":"How many sides does an octagon have?"},"options":[{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"7","en":"7"},{"af":"8","en":"8"},{"af":"10","en":"10"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Agt*-hoek: ’n agthoek het 8 sye en 8 hoeke, soos ’n stopteken. ’n Seshoek het 6 en ’n sewehoek 7.","en":"*Octa* means eight: an octagon has 8 sides and 8 angles, like a stop sign. A hexagon has 6 and a heptagon 7."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter hoek is ’n stomphoek?","en":"Which angle is an obtuse angle?"},"options":[{"af":"45°","en":"45°"},{"af":"90°","en":"90°"},{"af":"85°","en":"85°"},{"af":"130°","en":"130°"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Stomphoek is groter as 90° (maar kleiner as 180°). Net 130° is groter as 90°. 45° en 85° is skerphoeke, en 90° is ’n regte hoek.","en":"An obtuse angle is bigger than 90° (but smaller than 180°). Only 130° is bigger than 90°. 45° and 85° are acute angles, and 90° is a right angle."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Sirkel is ’n veelhoek.","en":"A circle is a polygon."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Veelhoek het net reguit sye. ’n Sirkel het ’n geboë sy en geen hoeke nie, dus is dit nie ’n veelhoek nie.","en":"False. A polygon has only straight sides. A circle has a curved side and no angles, so it is not a polygon."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Hoek van presies 90° heet ’n ___.","en":"An angle of exactly 90° is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["regte hoek"],"en":["right angle"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["skerphoek","stomphoek","reghoek"],"en":["acute angle","obtuse angle","straight angle"]}},"explain":{"af":"90° is ’n regte hoek. Pas op: ’n *reghoek* is ’n vorm met vier regte hoeke, nie ’n hoek nie. ’n Skerphoek is kleiner en ’n stomphoek groter as 90°.","en":"90° is a right angle. An acute angle is smaller and an obtuse angle bigger than 90°. A straight angle is a straight line (180°)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter vorm is ’n reëlmatige veelhoek?","en":"Which shape is a regular polygon?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Reghoek van 6 cm by 3 cm","en":"A rectangle of 6 cm by 3 cm"},{"af":"’n Vierkant met sye van 4 cm","en":"A square with sides of 4 cm"},{"af":"’n Driehoek met sye van 3 cm; 4 cm en 5 cm","en":"A triangle with sides of 3 cm, 4 cm and 5 cm"},{"af":"’n Parallelogram met sye van 4 cm en 6 cm","en":"A parallelogram with sides of 4 cm and 6 cm"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Vierkant het 4 ewe lang sye en 4 ewe groot hoeke (90°), dus is dit reëlmatig. Die reghoek het gelyke hoeke, maar nie gelyke sye nie – dit is onreëlmatig.","en":"A square has 4 equal sides and 4 equal angles (90°), so it is regular. The rectangle has equal angles, but not equal sides – it is irregular."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter eienskap het ’n reghoek en ’n vierkant albei?","en":"Which property do a rectangle and a square both have?"},"options":[{"af":"4 ewe lang sye","en":"4 equal sides"},{"af":"4 regte hoeke","en":"4 right angles"},{"af":"2 stomphoeke","en":"2 obtuse angles"},{"af":"Geen parallelle sye nie","en":"No parallel sides"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Albei het 4 regte hoeke en twee pare parallelle sye. Net die vierkant het 4 ewe lang sye – daarom is ’n vierkant ’n spesiale reghoek.","en":"Both have 4 right angles and two pairs of parallel sides. Only the square has 4 equal sides – that is why a square is a special rectangle."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke veelhoek by die getal sye.","en":"Match each polygon to its number of sides."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Driehoek","en":"Triangle"},"r":{"af":"3 sye","en":"3 sides"}},{"l":{"af":"Vyfhoek","en":"Pentagon"},"r":{"af":"5 sye","en":"5 sides"}},{"l":{"af":"Seshoek","en":"Hexagon"},"r":{"af":"6 sye","en":"6 sides"}},{"l":{"af":"Sewehoek","en":"Heptagon"},"r":{"af":"7 sye","en":"7 sides"}},{"l":{"af":"Agthoek","en":"Octagon"},"r":{"af":"8 sye","en":"8 sides"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die naam sê hoeveel hoeke die vorm het, en ’n veelhoek het ewe veel sye as hoeke: drie, vyf, ses, sewe en agt.","en":"The name tells you how many angles the shape has, and a polygon has as many sides as angles: three, five, six, seven and eight."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Seshoek het ___ hoekpunte.","en":"A hexagon has ___ vertices."},"answers":{"af":["6","ses"],"en":["6","six"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["5","8","12"],"en":["5","8","12"]}},"explain":{"af":"In ’n veelhoek is daar ewe veel hoekpunte as sye. ’n Seshoek het 6 sye, dus 6 hoekpunte.","en":"In a polygon there are as many vertices as sides. A hexagon has 6 sides, so 6 vertices."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato sê: ‘Hierdie hoek is groter, want sy arms is langer.’ Hoe vergelyk jy die grootte van twee hoeke reg?","en":"Lerato says: ‘This angle is bigger, because its arms are longer.’ How do you compare the size of two angles correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Kyk hoe ver die arms oopdraai","en":"Look at how far the arms open"},{"af":"Meet hoe lank die arms is","en":"Measure how long the arms are"},{"af":"Tel hoeveel hoekpunte daar is","en":"Count how many vertices there are"},{"af":"Kyk watter hoek hoër op die bladsy is","en":"See which angle is higher on the page"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die grootte van ’n hoek is hoe ver die twee arms van mekaar af oopdraai. Lang of kort arms maak nie die hoek groter of kleiner nie – Lerato maak die algemene fout.","en":"The size of an angle is how far the two arms open away from each other. Long or short arms do not make the angle bigger or smaller – Lerato makes the common mistake."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Vierkant is ’n spesiale soort reghoek.","en":"A square is a special kind of rectangle."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Reghoek het 4 regte hoeke en oorkantste sye wat ewe lank is. ’n Vierkant het dit alles, en boonop is al 4 sye ewe lank.","en":"True. A rectangle has 4 right angles and opposite sides that are equal. A square has all of that, and on top of it all 4 sides are equal."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Driehoek het hoeke van 30°; 40° en 110°. Watter soort hoeke het dit?","en":"A triangle has angles of 30°, 40° and 110°. Which kinds of angles does it have?"},"options":[{"af":"3 skerphoeke","en":"3 acute angles"},{"af":"1 skerphoek en 2 stomphoeke","en":"1 acute angle and 2 obtuse angles"},{"af":"2 skerphoeke en 1 regte hoek","en":"2 acute angles and 1 right angle"},{"af":"2 skerphoeke en 1 stomphoek","en":"2 acute angles and 1 obtuse angle"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"30° en 40° is kleiner as 90°, dus skerp. 110° is groter as 90°, dus stomp. Geen hoek is presies 90° nie.","en":"30° and 40° are smaller than 90°, so acute. 110° is bigger than 90°, so obtuse. No angle is exactly 90°."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Lyne wat altyd ewe ver van mekaar af bly en mekaar nooit kruis nie, is ___ lyne.","en":"Lines that always stay the same distance apart and never cross are ___ lines."},"answers":{"af":["parallelle","ewewydige","parallel"],"en":["parallel"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kruisende","geboë","gebreekte"],"en":["intersecting","curved","broken"]}},"explain":{"af":"Parallelle lyne is soos die twee spore van ’n treinspoor: hulle bly ewe ver van mekaar af en ontmoet nooit. ’n Vierkant, reghoek en parallelogram het elk twee pare parallelle sye.","en":"Parallel lines are like the two rails of a railway line: they stay the same distance apart and never meet. A square, rectangle and parallelogram each have two pairs of parallel sides."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter vorm het 4 sye, oorkantste sye wat ewe lank en parallel is, maar geen regte hoeke nie?","en":"Which shape has 4 sides, opposite sides that are equal and parallel, but no right angles?"},"options":[{"af":"Vierkant","en":"Square"},{"af":"Reghoek","en":"Rectangle"},{"af":"Parallelogram","en":"Parallelogram"},{"af":"Vyfhoek","en":"Pentagon"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Parallelogram het oorkantste sye wat ewe lank en parallel is. Die vierkant en reghoek het ook sulke sye, maar hulle het 4 regte hoeke. ’n Vyfhoek het 5 sye.","en":"A parallelogram has opposite sides that are equal and parallel. The square and rectangle also have such sides, but they have 4 right angles. A pentagon has 5 sides."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Een sy van ’n reëlmatige vyfhoek is 6 cm lank. Hoe lank is al die sye saam?","en":"One side of a regular pentagon is 6 cm long. How long are all the sides together?"},"options":[{"af":"30 cm","en":"30 cm"},{"af":"24 cm","en":"24 cm"},{"af":"36 cm","en":"36 cm"},{"af":"11 cm","en":"11 cm"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Reëlmatig beteken al die sye is ewe lank. ’n Vyfhoek het 5 sye: 5 × 6 cm = 30 cm. 24 cm tel net 4 sye en 36 cm tel 6 sye.","en":"Regular means all the sides are equal. A pentagon has 5 sides: 5 × 6 cm = 30 cm. 24 cm counts only 4 sides and 36 cm counts 6 sides."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Bewerkings, breuke en voorwerpe","en":"Operations, fractions and objects"},"topics":[{"id":"w5-t2-vermenigvuldiging","title":{"af":"Vermenigvuldiging","en":"Multiplication"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal jou tafels tot 10 × 10 kan gebruik, met 10; 100 en 1 000 kan maal, 2-syfer- en 3-syfergetalle met ’n 2-syfergetal kan vermenigvuldig en woordprobleme oor groepe en koerse kan oplos.","en":"You will be able to use your times tables up to 10 × 10, multiply by 10, 100 and 1 000, multiply 2-digit and 3-digit numbers by a 2-digit number and solve word problems about groups and rates."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is vermenigvuldiging?\n\nVermenigvuldiging is ’n kort manier om **gelyke groepe** bymekaar te tel. 6 groepe van 4 is 4 + 4 + 4 + 4 + 4 + 4 = 24, of kort: **6 × 4 = 24**. Die getalle wat jy maal, is **faktore** en die antwoord is die **produk**.\n\nKen jou **tafels tot 10 × 10** uit jou kop – dit maak al die groter somme vinniger. Die antwoorde in die 7-tafel is die **veelvoude** van 7: 7; 14; 21; 28; 35; …\n\nHandige truuks:\n\n- **× 4:** verdubbel twee keer. 4 × 13: 26, dan 52.\n- **× 5:** maal met 10 en halveer. 5 × 18: 180 ÷ 2 = 90.\n- **× 9:** maal met 10 en trek die getal een keer af. 9 × 7 = 70 − 7 = 63.\n\n## Maal met 10; 100 en 1 000\n\nAs jy met 10 maal, word elke syfer **10 keer groter** en skuif dit een plek na **links**. ’n 0 vul die ene-plek.\n\n| Som | Antwoord |\n|---|---|\n| 46 × 10 | 460 |\n| 46 × 100 | 4 600 |\n| 46 × 1 000 | 46 000 |\n| 30 × 400 | 3 × 4 × 1 000 = 12 000 |\n\nBy 30 × 400 maal jy eers 3 × 4 = 12 en maal dan met 10 × 100 = 1 000.\n\n## Eienskappe van vermenigvuldiging\n\n| Eienskap | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|\n| Kommutatief (omruil) | 8 × 6 = 6 × 8 = 48 |\n| Assosiatief (groepeer) | (7 × 5) × 2 = 7 × (5 × 2) = 7 × 10 = 70 |\n| Distributief (versprei) | 6 × 23 = 6 × 20 + 6 × 3 = 120 + 18 = 138 |\n| Maal met 1 | 345 × 1 = 345 |\n| Maal met 0 | 345 × 0 = 0 |\n\nDie **distributiewe eienskap** is die rede waarom die opbreekmetode werk.\n\n## Verdubbel en halveer\n\nAs jy een faktor **verdubbel** en die ander **halveer**, bly die produk dieselfde. Dit maak sommige somme baie makliker:\n\n16 × 25 = 8 × 50 = 4 × 100 = **400**\n\nDit werk omdat 16 × 25 = 8 × 2 × 25 = 8 × 50 (die assosiatiewe eienskap).\n\n## Skat eers\n\nRond elke getal af en maal in jou kop. 43 × 36 ≈ 40 × 40 = 1 600. Jou antwoord moet naby 1 600 wees.\n\n## 2-syfer × 2-syfer: opbreekmetode\n\nBreek een getal in tiene en ene op en maal elke deel:\n\n43 × 36 = 43 × 30 + 43 × 6 = 1 290 + 258 = **1 548**\n\nDit is naby die skatting van 1 600, dus maak die antwoord sin.\n\n## 3-syfer × 2-syfer: kolommetode\n\nBereken 214 × 38. Skat: 200 × 40 = 8 000.\n\n| | D | H | T | E |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | | 2 | 1 | 4 |\n| × | | | 3 | 8 |\n| 214 × 8 | 1 | 7 | 1 | 2 |\n| 214 × 30 | 6 | 4 | 2 | 0 |\n| = | 8 | 1 | 3 | 2 |\n\n1. Maal met die ene-syfer: 214 × 8 = 1 712.\n2. Maal met die tiene-syfer. Die 3 is eintlik **30**, dus skryf eers ’n **0** in die ene-kolom en maal dan met 3: 214 × 30 = 6 420.\n3. Tel die twee rye bymekaar: 1 712 + 6 420 = **8 132**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Baie leerders vergeet die **0** in die tweede ry. Dan tel hulle 214 × 3 = 642 by in plaas van 214 × 30 = 6 420, en die antwoord is heeltemal te klein.\n\n## Woordprobleme\n\n- **Groepe:** In die saal is 24 rye met 35 stoele in elke ry. 24 × 35 = 840 stoele.\n- **Koers oor tyd:** ’n Trein ry 60 km per uur. In 3 uur ry dit 3 × 60 = 180 km.\n- **Koers:** ’n Brood kos R18. 12 brode kos 12 × R18 = R216. ’n **Koers** sê hoeveel vir **een** (per brood, per uur, per dag).\n\nWoorde soos *elk*, *per*, *rye van* en *keer* wys dikwels na vermenigvuldiging.\n\n> **Onthou:** Skat altyd eers. As jou antwoord ver van die skatting af is, kyk weer of jy die 0 vergeet het of verkeerd oorgedra het.","en":"## What is multiplication?\n\nMultiplication is a short way of adding **equal groups**. 6 groups of 4 is 4 + 4 + 4 + 4 + 4 + 4 = 24, or in short: **6 × 4 = 24**. The numbers you multiply are **factors** and the answer is the **product**.\n\nKnow your **times tables up to 10 × 10** by heart – it makes all the bigger sums faster. The answers in the 7 times table are the **multiples** of 7: 7, 14, 21, 28, 35, …\n\nHandy tricks:\n\n- **× 4:** double twice. 4 × 13: 26, then 52.\n- **× 5:** multiply by 10 and halve. 5 × 18: 180 ÷ 2 = 90.\n- **× 9:** multiply by 10 and subtract the number once. 9 × 7 = 70 − 7 = 63.\n\n## Multiplying by 10, 100 and 1 000\n\nWhen you multiply by 10, every digit becomes **10 times bigger** and moves one place to the **left**. A 0 fills the units place.\n\n| Sum | Answer |\n|---|---|\n| 46 × 10 | 460 |\n| 46 × 100 | 4 600 |\n| 46 × 1 000 | 46 000 |\n| 30 × 400 | 3 × 4 × 1 000 = 12 000 |\n\nFor 30 × 400 you first multiply 3 × 4 = 12 and then multiply by 10 × 100 = 1 000.\n\n## Properties of multiplication\n\n| Property | Example |\n|---|---|\n| Commutative (swap) | 8 × 6 = 6 × 8 = 48 |\n| Associative (group) | (7 × 5) × 2 = 7 × (5 × 2) = 7 × 10 = 70 |\n| Distributive (spread) | 6 × 23 = 6 × 20 + 6 × 3 = 120 + 18 = 138 |\n| Multiplying by 1 | 345 × 1 = 345 |\n| Multiplying by 0 | 345 × 0 = 0 |\n\nThe **distributive property** is the reason why the breaking-down method works.\n\n## Doubling and halving\n\nIf you **double** one factor and **halve** the other, the product stays the same. This makes some sums much easier:\n\n16 × 25 = 8 × 50 = 4 × 100 = **400**\n\nThis works because 16 × 25 = 8 × 2 × 25 = 8 × 50 (the associative property).\n\n## Estimate first\n\nRound each number off and multiply in your head. 43 × 36 ≈ 40 × 40 = 1 600. Your answer must be close to 1 600.\n\n## 2-digit × 2-digit: breaking-down method\n\nBreak one number up into tens and units and multiply each part:\n\n43 × 36 = 43 × 30 + 43 × 6 = 1 290 + 258 = **1 548**\n\nThis is close to the estimate of 1 600, so the answer makes sense.\n\n## 3-digit × 2-digit: column method\n\nCalculate 214 × 38. Estimate: 200 × 40 = 8 000.\n\n| | Th | H | T | U |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | | 2 | 1 | 4 |\n| × | | | 3 | 8 |\n| 214 × 8 | 1 | 7 | 1 | 2 |\n| 214 × 30 | 6 | 4 | 2 | 0 |\n| = | 8 | 1 | 3 | 2 |\n\n1. Multiply by the units digit: 214 × 8 = 1 712.\n2. Multiply by the tens digit. The 3 is really **30**, so first write a **0** in the units column and then multiply by 3: 214 × 30 = 6 420.\n3. Add the two rows together: 1 712 + 6 420 = **8 132**.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Many learners forget the **0** in the second row. Then they add 214 × 3 = 642 instead of 214 × 30 = 6 420, and the answer is far too small.\n\n## Word problems\n\n- **Groups:** In the hall there are 24 rows with 35 chairs in each row. 24 × 35 = 840 chairs.\n- **Rate over time:** A train travels 60 km per hour. In 3 hours it travels 3 × 60 = 180 km.\n- **Rate:** A loaf of bread costs R18. 12 loaves cost 12 × R18 = R216. A **rate** tells you how much for **one** (per loaf, per hour, per day).\n\nWords like *each*, *per*, *rows of* and *times* often point to multiplication.\n\n> **Remember:** Always estimate first. If your answer is far from the estimate, check again whether you forgot the 0 or carried incorrectly."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Vermenigvuldig","en":"Multiply"},"def":{"af":"Gelyke groepe vinnig bymekaartel; 6 × 4 beteken 6 groepe van 4.","en":"Adding equal groups quickly; 6 × 4 means 6 groups of 4."}},{"term":{"af":"Faktor","en":"Factor"},"def":{"af":"Een van die getalle wat jy met mekaar maal; in 6 × 4 = 24 is 6 en 4 faktore.","en":"One of the numbers you multiply together; in 6 × 4 = 24, 6 and 4 are factors."}},{"term":{"af":"Produk","en":"Product"},"def":{"af":"Die antwoord van ’n vermenigvuldigsom.","en":"The answer to a multiplication."}},{"term":{"af":"Veelvoud","en":"Multiple"},"def":{"af":"Die produk van ’n getal en ’n telgetal; 14; 21 en 28 is veelvoude van 7.","en":"The product of a number and a whole number; 14, 21 and 28 are multiples of 7."}},{"term":{"af":"Kommutatiewe eienskap","en":"Commutative property"},"def":{"af":"Jy kan die faktore omruil en die produk bly dieselfde: 8 × 6 = 6 × 8.","en":"You can swap the factors and the product stays the same: 8 × 6 = 6 × 8."}},{"term":{"af":"Assosiatiewe eienskap","en":"Associative property"},"def":{"af":"As jy drie getalle maal, kan jy kies watter twee jy eerste maal.","en":"When you multiply three numbers, you can choose which two to multiply first."}},{"term":{"af":"Distributiewe eienskap","en":"Distributive property"},"def":{"af":"Jy kan ’n getal opbreek en elke deel apart maal: 6 × 23 = 6 × 20 + 6 × 3.","en":"You can break a number up and multiply each part separately: 6 × 23 = 6 × 20 + 6 × 3."}},{"term":{"af":"Kolommetode","en":"Column method"},"def":{"af":"Vermenigvuldig onder mekaar, eers met die ene-syfer en dan met die tiene-syfer, en tel die rye bymekaar.","en":"Multiplying underneath each other, first by the units digit and then by the tens digit, and adding the rows."}},{"term":{"af":"Skatting","en":"Estimate"},"def":{"af":"’n Antwoord naby die regte antwoord wat jy kry deur eers die getalle af te rond.","en":"An answer close to the real answer that you get by rounding off the numbers first."}},{"term":{"af":"Koers","en":"Rate"},"def":{"af":"Hoeveel daar vir een eenheid is, soos R18 per brood of 60 km per uur.","en":"How much there is for one unit, such as R18 per loaf or 60 km per hour."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Maal met 10; 100 en 1 000","en":"Multiply by 10, 100 and 1 000"},"problem":{"af":"Bereken: (a) 385 × 10 (b) 72 × 100 (c) 60 × 300 (d) 9 × 1 000","en":"Calculate: (a) 385 × 10 (b) 72 × 100 (c) 60 × 300 (d) 9 × 1 000"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Elke syfer skuif een plek na links: 385 × 10 = 3 850.","en":"(a) Every digit moves one place to the left: 385 × 10 = 3 850."},{"af":"(b) Twee plekke na links: 72 × 100 = 7 200.","en":"(b) Two places to the left: 72 × 100 = 7 200."},{"af":"(c) 60 × 300 = 6 × 3 × 10 × 100 = 18 × 1 000 = 18 000.","en":"(c) 60 × 300 = 6 × 3 × 10 × 100 = 18 × 1 000 = 18 000."},{"af":"(d) Drie plekke na links: 9 × 1 000 = 9 000.","en":"(d) Three places to the left: 9 × 1 000 = 9 000."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 3 850 (b) 7 200 (c) 18 000 (d) 9 000","en":"(a) 3 850 (b) 7 200 (c) 18 000 (d) 9 000"}},{"title":{"af":"Opbreekmetode","en":"Breaking-down method"},"problem":{"af":"Bereken 58 × 24 met die opbreekmetode.","en":"Calculate 58 × 24 with the breaking-down method."},"steps":[{"af":"Skat: 60 × 20 = 1 200 (die antwoord sal ’n bietjie meer wees, want 24 is meer as 20).","en":"Estimate: 60 × 20 = 1 200 (the answer will be a bit more, because 24 is more than 20)."},{"af":"Breek 24 op in 20 + 4: 58 × 24 = 58 × 20 + 58 × 4.","en":"Break 24 up into 20 + 4: 58 × 24 = 58 × 20 + 58 × 4."},{"af":"58 × 20 = 1 160 en 58 × 4 = 232.","en":"58 × 20 = 1 160 and 58 × 4 = 232."},{"af":"Tel bymekaar: 1 160 + 232 = 1 392.","en":"Add together: 1 160 + 232 = 1 392."}],"answer":{"af":"1 392","en":"1 392"}},{"title":{"af":"Kolommetode: 3-syfer × 2-syfer","en":"Column method: 3-digit × 2-digit"},"problem":{"af":"Bereken 326 × 47.","en":"Calculate 326 × 47."},"steps":[{"af":"Skat: 300 × 50 = 15 000.","en":"Estimate: 300 × 50 = 15 000."},{"af":"Ry 1 – maal met 7: 326 × 7 = 2 282.","en":"Row 1 – multiply by 7: 326 × 7 = 2 282."},{"af":"Ry 2 – maal met 40: skryf ’n 0 by die ene en maal met 4: 326 × 40 = 13 040.","en":"Row 2 – multiply by 40: write a 0 in the units and multiply by 4: 326 × 40 = 13 040."},{"af":"Tel die rye bymekaar: 2 282 + 13 040 = 15 322. Dit is naby die skatting.","en":"Add the rows together: 2 282 + 13 040 = 15 322. This is close to the estimate."}],"answer":{"af":"15 322","en":"15 322"}},{"title":{"af":"Woordprobleem met ’n slim metode","en":"Word problem with a clever method"},"problem":{"af":"Jou skool koop 36 woordeboeke teen R125 elk. Wat is die totale koste?","en":"Your school buys 36 dictionaries at R125 each. What is the total cost?"},"steps":[{"af":"*Elk* wys na vermenigvuldiging: 36 × R125.","en":"*Each* points to multiplication: 36 × R125."},{"af":"Slim metode: 36 = 4 × 9, en 125 × 4 = 500. Dus is 125 × 36 = 125 × 4 × 9 = 500 × 9 = 4 500.","en":"Clever method: 36 = 4 × 9, and 125 × 4 = 500. So 125 × 36 = 125 × 4 × 9 = 500 × 9 = 4 500."},{"af":"Kontroleer met die kolommetode: 125 × 6 = 750 en 125 × 30 = 3 750. Dan is 750 + 3 750 = 4 500.","en":"Check with the column method: 125 × 6 = 750 and 125 × 30 = 3 750. Then 750 + 3 750 = 4 500."}],"answer":{"af":"Die woordeboeke kos altesaam R4 500.","en":"The dictionaries cost R4 500 altogether."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 7 × 8?","en":"What is 7 × 8?"},"options":[{"af":"54","en":"54"},{"af":"56","en":"56"},{"af":"63","en":"63"},{"af":"48","en":"48"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"7 × 8 = 56. ’n Handige kontrole: 7 × 4 = 28, en dubbel 28 is 56. 63 is 7 × 9 en 48 is 6 × 8.","en":"7 × 8 = 56. A handy check: 7 × 4 = 28, and double 28 is 56. 63 is 7 × 9 and 48 is 6 × 8."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 64 × 100?","en":"What is 64 × 100?"},"options":[{"af":"640","en":"640"},{"af":"64 000","en":"64 000"},{"af":"6 400","en":"6 400"},{"af":"64 100","en":"64 100"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Met 100 maal skuif elke syfer twee plekke na links: 64 → 6 400. 640 is net × 10 en 64 000 is × 1 000.","en":"Multiplying by 100 moves every digit two places to the left: 64 → 6 400. 640 is only × 10 and 64 000 is × 1 000."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"40 × 600 = ___","en":"40 × 600 = ___"},"answers":{"af":["24 000","24000"],"en":["24 000","24000"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["2 400","240 000","24 600"],"en":["2 400","240 000","24 600"]}},"explain":{"af":"Maal eers 4 × 6 = 24. Dan is daar nog 10 × 100 = 1 000, dus 24 × 1 000 = 24 000. Tel die nulle: 40 het een en 600 het twee – altesaam drie.","en":"First multiply 4 × 6 = 24. Then there is still 10 × 100 = 1 000, so 24 × 1 000 = 24 000. Count the zeros: 40 has one and 600 has two – three altogether."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"6 × 47 = 6 × 40 + 6 × 7","en":"6 × 47 = 6 × 40 + 6 × 7"},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Dit is die distributiewe eienskap: 6 × 40 = 240 en 6 × 7 = 42, en 240 + 42 = 282 = 6 × 47.","en":"True. This is the distributive property: 6 × 40 = 240 and 6 × 7 = 42, and 240 + 42 = 282 = 6 × 47."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bereken 37 × 24.","en":"Calculate 37 × 24."},"options":[{"af":"888","en":"888"},{"af":"222","en":"222"},{"af":"828","en":"828"},{"af":"878","en":"878"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"37 × 4 = 148 en 37 × 20 = 740. 148 + 740 = 888. 222 kry jy as jy die 0 vergeet en 37 × 2 = 74 bytel in plaas van 740.","en":"37 × 4 = 148 and 37 × 20 = 740. 148 + 740 = 888. You get 222 if you forget the 0 and add 37 × 2 = 74 instead of 740."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die beste skatting vir 49 × 31?","en":"What is the best estimate for 49 × 31?"},"options":[{"af":"1 200","en":"1 200"},{"af":"2 000","en":"2 000"},{"af":"150","en":"150"},{"af":"1 500","en":"1 500"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Rond af tot die naaste 10: 49 ≈ 50 en 31 ≈ 30. 50 × 30 = 1 500. (Die presiese antwoord is 1 519.) 150 vergeet een van die nulle.","en":"Round off to the nearest 10: 49 ≈ 50 and 31 ≈ 30. 50 × 30 = 1 500. (The exact answer is 1 519.) 150 forgets one of the zeros."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke eienskap by die regte voorbeeld.","en":"Match each property to the correct example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Kommutatief","en":"Commutative"},"r":{"af":"9 × 7 = 7 × 9","en":"9 × 7 = 7 × 9"}},{"l":{"af":"Assosiatief","en":"Associative"},"r":{"af":"(2 × 5) × 13 = 2 × (5 × 13)","en":"(2 × 5) × 13 = 2 × (5 × 13)"}},{"l":{"af":"Distributief","en":"Distributive"},"r":{"af":"8 × 34 = 8 × 30 + 8 × 4","en":"8 × 34 = 8 × 30 + 8 × 4"}},{"l":{"af":"Maal met 0","en":"Multiplying by 0"},"r":{"af":"568 × 0 = 0","en":"568 × 0 = 0"}},{"l":{"af":"Maal met 1","en":"Multiplying by 1"},"r":{"af":"568 × 1 = 568","en":"568 × 1 = 568"}}],"explain":{"af":"Omruil is kommutatief; hakies skuif is assosiatief; opbreek en elke deel maal is distributief. Enige getal maal 0 is 0, en enige getal maal 1 bly dieselfde.","en":"Swapping is commutative; moving brackets is associative; breaking up and multiplying each part is distributive. Any number times 0 is 0, and any number times 1 stays the same."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die veelvoude van 8 tussen 50 en 70 is 56 en ___.","en":"The multiples of 8 between 50 and 70 are 56 and ___."},"answers":{"af":["64"],"en":["64"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["60","63","66"],"en":["60","63","66"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die 8-tafel: … 48; 56; 64; 72 … Tussen 50 en 70 is daar net 56 (7 × 8) en 64 (8 × 8). 63 is ’n veelvoud van 7 en 9, nie van 8 nie.","en":"The 8 times table: … 48, 56, 64, 72 … Between 50 and 70 there are only 56 (7 × 8) and 64 (8 × 8). 63 is a multiple of 7 and 9, not of 8."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Minibustaxi het 15 sitplekke. Hoeveel passasiers kan 23 vol taxi’s vervoer?","en":"A minibus taxi has 15 seats. How many passengers can 23 full taxis carry?"},"options":[{"af":"38","en":"38"},{"af":"330","en":"330"},{"af":"360","en":"360"},{"af":"345","en":"345"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"23 groepe van 15: 23 × 15 = 23 × 10 + 23 × 5 = 230 + 115 = 345. 38 kry jy as jy optel in plaas van maal.","en":"23 groups of 15: 23 × 15 = 23 × 10 + 23 × 5 = 230 + 115 = 345. You get 38 if you add instead of multiply."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy ’n getal met 0 maal, bly die getal dieselfde.","en":"When you multiply a number by 0, the number stays the same."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Enige getal maal 0 is 0 – nul groepe van iets is niks. Dit is wanneer jy met **1** maal dat die getal dieselfde bly.","en":"False. Any number times 0 is 0 – zero groups of something is nothing. It is when you multiply by **1** that the number stays the same."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bereken 213 × 32.","en":"Calculate 213 × 32."},"options":[{"af":"6 816","en":"6 816"},{"af":"1 065","en":"1 065"},{"af":"6 806","en":"6 806"},{"af":"7 816","en":"7 816"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"213 × 2 = 426 en 213 × 30 = 6 390. 426 + 6 390 = 6 816. Skatting: 200 × 30 = 6 000, dus is 6 816 redelik. 1 065 kry jy as jy die 0 in die tweede ry vergeet.","en":"213 × 2 = 426 and 213 × 30 = 6 390. 426 + 6 390 = 6 816. Estimate: 200 × 30 = 6 000, so 6 816 is reasonable. You get 1 065 if you forget the 0 in the second row."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Groepeer slim: 25 × 37 × 4 = ___","en":"Group cleverly: 25 × 37 × 4 = ___"},"answers":{"af":["3 700","3700"],"en":["3 700","3700"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["370","37 000","925"],"en":["370","37 000","925"]}},"explain":{"af":"Ruil om en groepeer: 25 × 4 = 100, en 100 × 37 = 3 700. 925 is net 25 × 37 – dan het jy die × 4 vergeet.","en":"Swap and group: 25 × 4 = 100, and 100 × 37 = 3 700. 925 is only 25 × 37 – then you forgot the × 4."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In die skoolsaal is daar 28 rye met 45 stoele in elke ry. Hoeveel stoele is daar altesaam?","en":"In the school hall there are 28 rows with 45 chairs in each row. How many chairs are there altogether?"},"options":[{"af":"73","en":"73"},{"af":"1 120","en":"1 120"},{"af":"1 260","en":"1 260"},{"af":"1 360","en":"1 360"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"28 × 45 = 28 × 40 + 28 × 5 = 1 120 + 140 = 1 260. 1 120 is net 28 × 40 – die 28 × 5 is vergeet.","en":"28 × 45 = 28 × 40 + 28 × 5 = 1 120 + 140 = 1 260. 1 120 is only 28 × 40 – the 28 × 5 was forgotten."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter berekening gee dieselfde antwoord as 16 × 25?","en":"Which calculation gives the same answer as 16 × 25?"},"options":[{"af":"16 × 20 + 5","en":"16 × 20 + 5"},{"af":"4 × 100","en":"4 × 100"},{"af":"10 × 25 + 6","en":"10 × 25 + 6"},{"af":"16 × 5 × 2","en":"16 × 5 × 2"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"16 = 4 × 4 en 4 × 25 = 100, dus 16 × 25 = 4 × 100 = 400. By *16 × 20 + 5* is die 5 nie met 16 gemaal nie; dit moes 16 × 20 + 16 × 5 gewees het.","en":"16 = 4 × 4 and 4 × 25 = 100, so 16 × 25 = 4 × 100 = 400. In *16 × 20 + 5* the 5 was not multiplied by 16; it should have been 16 × 20 + 16 × 5."}}]},{"id":"w5-t2-deling","title":{"af":"Deling","en":"Division"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal 3-syfergetalle deur ’n 1-syfergetal (en eenvoudige getalle deur ’n 2-syfergetal) kan deel, kan besluit wat om met die res in ’n woordprobleem te doen en jou antwoord met vermenigvuldiging kan kontroleer.","en":"You will be able to divide 3-digit numbers by a 1-digit number (and simple numbers by a 2-digit number), decide what to do with the remainder in a word problem and check your answer with multiplication."},"summary":{"af":"## Twee soorte deling\n\nDeling beantwoord twee soorte vrae:\n\n- **Verdeling:** 24 lekkers word gelyk tussen 4 kinders verdeel. Hoeveel kry elkeen? 24 ÷ 4 = 6 lekkers.\n- **Groepering:** 24 lekkers word in pakkies van 4 gepak. Hoeveel pakkies is daar? 24 ÷ 4 = 6 pakkies.\n\nDie berekening is dieselfde, maar die vraag verskil. In 24 ÷ 4 = 6 is 24 die **deeltal**, 4 die **deler** en 6 die **kwosiënt** (die antwoord).\n\n## Deling en vermenigvuldiging\n\nDeling en vermenigvuldiging is **inverse bewerkings**. As jy weet 6 × 4 = 24, weet jy ook 24 ÷ 4 = 6 en 24 ÷ 6 = 4. Daarom help jou tafels jou om te deel.\n\nJy kontroleer ’n deelsom met vermenigvuldiging: 456 ÷ 6 = 76, want 76 × 6 = 456.\n\n## Deel deur 10 en 100\n\nAs jy deur 10 deel, word elke syfer **10 keer kleiner** en skuif dit een plek na **regs**.\n\n- 4 500 ÷ 10 = 450\n- 4 500 ÷ 100 = 45\n- 70 000 ÷ 100 = 700\n\n## Die opbreekmetode\n\nBreek die deeltal op in dele wat maklik deur die deler gedeel kan word – gebruik veelvoude van die deler.\n\n456 ÷ 6: 456 = 420 + 36. Dan is 420 ÷ 6 = 70 en 36 ÷ 6 = 6, dus 456 ÷ 6 = **76**.\n\n## Lang deling\n\nBy **lang deling** werk jy van **links na regs** en herhaal vier stappe: **deel, maal, trek af, bring af**. Kyk na 875 ÷ 7:\n\n1. Honderde: 8 ÷ 7 = 1 en 1 bly oor. Skryf 1 bo die 8.\n2. Bring die 7 af: dit word 17. 17 ÷ 7 = 2 en 3 bly oor. Skryf 2.\n3. Bring die 5 af: dit word 35. 35 ÷ 7 = 5 en niks bly oor nie. Skryf 5.\n4. Antwoord: 875 ÷ 7 = **125**. Kontroleer: 125 × 7 = 875.\n\nOm deur ’n **2-syfergetal** te deel, gebruik maklike veelvoude van die deler. 312 ÷ 24: 24 × 10 = 240, en 312 − 240 = 72. 24 × 3 = 72. Dus is die antwoord 10 + 3 = **13**.\n\n## Die res\n\nAs ’n getal nie presies deelbaar is nie, bly daar iets oor: die **res**. 47 ÷ 5 = 9 res 2, want 9 × 5 = 45 en 47 − 45 = 2. Die res moet altyd **kleiner as die deler** wees.\n\nIn ’n woordprobleem moet jy dink wat die res in die storie beteken:\n\n| Storie | Berekening | Antwoord |\n|---|---|---|\n| 130 leerders gaan op ’n uitstappie; elke bus neem 60. | 130 ÷ 60 = 2 res 10 | **Rond op:** 3 busse, anders bly 10 leerders agter. |\n| Jy het R50 en ’n pastei kos R15. | 50 ÷ 15 = 3 res 5 | **Rond af:** 3 pasteie; R5 is nie genoeg vir nog een nie. |\n| 50 eiers word in houers van 12 gepak. | 50 ÷ 12 = 4 res 2 | 4 vol houers en 2 eiers bly oor. |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om net *2 res 10* te skryf, beantwoord nie die vraag oor die busse nie. Lees die vraag weer: hoeveel busse is **nodig**? Die antwoord is 3 busse.\n\n## Vinnige deelbaarheidstoetse\n\nJy kan dadelik sien of ’n getal **deelbaar** is (sonder ’n res) deur:\n\n- **2** – as dit ewe is, dus op 0; 2; 4; 6 of 8 eindig: 3 576 ÷ 2 werk presies.\n- **5** – as dit op 0 of 5 eindig: 4 385 ÷ 5 werk presies.\n- **10** – as dit op 0 eindig: 7 290 ÷ 10 werk presies.\n\nOnthou ook: deling is **nie** kommutatief nie. 24 ÷ 4 = 6, maar 4 ÷ 24 is nie 6 nie.\n\n## Faktore\n\n’n **Faktor** van ’n getal deel presies in die getal, sonder ’n res. Vind faktore in pare:\n\n24 = 1 × 24 = 2 × 12 = 3 × 8 = 4 × 6\n\nDie faktore van 24 is dus 1; 2; 3; 4; 6; 8; 12 en 24. Die getal 5 is nie ’n faktor van 24 nie, want 24 ÷ 5 = 4 res 4.\n\n> **Onthou:** Kontroleer elke deelsom: **kwosiënt × deler + res = deeltal**. Vir 47 ÷ 5 = 9 res 2: 9 × 5 + 2 = 47.","en":"## Two kinds of division\n\nDivision answers two kinds of questions:\n\n- **Sharing:** 24 sweets are shared equally among 4 children. How many does each get? 24 ÷ 4 = 6 sweets.\n- **Grouping:** 24 sweets are packed in packets of 4. How many packets are there? 24 ÷ 4 = 6 packets.\n\nThe calculation is the same, but the question is different. In 24 ÷ 4 = 6, 24 is the **dividend**, 4 is the **divisor** and 6 is the **quotient** (the answer).\n\n## Division and multiplication\n\nDivision and multiplication are **inverse operations**. If you know 6 × 4 = 24, you also know 24 ÷ 4 = 6 and 24 ÷ 6 = 4. That is why your times tables help you to divide.\n\nYou check a division with multiplication: 456 ÷ 6 = 76, because 76 × 6 = 456.\n\n## Dividing by 10 and 100\n\nWhen you divide by 10, every digit becomes **10 times smaller** and moves one place to the **right**.\n\n- 4 500 ÷ 10 = 450\n- 4 500 ÷ 100 = 45\n- 70 000 ÷ 100 = 700\n\n## The breaking-down method\n\nBreak the dividend up into parts that are easy to divide by the divisor – use multiples of the divisor.\n\n456 ÷ 6: 456 = 420 + 36. Then 420 ÷ 6 = 70 and 36 ÷ 6 = 6, so 456 ÷ 6 = **76**.\n\n## Long division\n\nIn **long division** you work from **left to right** and repeat four steps: **divide, multiply, subtract, bring down**. Look at 875 ÷ 7:\n\n1. Hundreds: 8 ÷ 7 = 1 and 1 is left over. Write 1 above the 8.\n2. Bring down the 7: it becomes 17. 17 ÷ 7 = 2 and 3 is left over. Write 2.\n3. Bring down the 5: it becomes 35. 35 ÷ 7 = 5 and nothing is left over. Write 5.\n4. Answer: 875 ÷ 7 = **125**. Check: 125 × 7 = 875.\n\nTo divide by a **2-digit number**, use easy multiples of the divisor. 312 ÷ 24: 24 × 10 = 240, and 312 − 240 = 72. 24 × 3 = 72. So the answer is 10 + 3 = **13**.\n\n## The remainder\n\nWhen a number cannot be divided exactly, something is left over: the **remainder**. 47 ÷ 5 = 9 remainder 2, because 9 × 5 = 45 and 47 − 45 = 2. The remainder must always be **smaller than the divisor**.\n\nIn a word problem you must think about what the remainder means in the story:\n\n| Story | Calculation | Answer |\n|---|---|---|\n| 130 learners go on an outing; each bus takes 60. | 130 ÷ 60 = 2 remainder 10 | **Round up:** 3 buses, otherwise 10 learners stay behind. |\n| You have R50 and a pie costs R15. | 50 ÷ 15 = 3 remainder 5 | **Round down:** 3 pies; R5 is not enough for another one. |\n| 50 eggs are packed in boxes of 12. | 50 ÷ 12 = 4 remainder 2 | 4 full boxes and 2 eggs are left over. |\n\n> **Common mistake:** Just writing *2 remainder 10* does not answer the question about the buses. Read the question again: how many buses are **needed**? The answer is 3 buses.\n\n## Quick divisibility tests\n\nYou can see straight away whether a number is **divisible** (without a remainder) by:\n\n- **2** – if it is even, so it ends in 0, 2, 4, 6 or 8: 3 576 ÷ 2 works exactly.\n- **5** – if it ends in 0 or 5: 4 385 ÷ 5 works exactly.\n- **10** – if it ends in 0: 7 290 ÷ 10 works exactly.\n\nAlso remember: division is **not** commutative. 24 ÷ 4 = 6, but 4 ÷ 24 is not 6.\n\n## Factors\n\nA **factor** of a number divides into the number exactly, without a remainder. Find factors in pairs:\n\n24 = 1 × 24 = 2 × 12 = 3 × 8 = 4 × 6\n\nSo the factors of 24 are 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12 and 24. The number 5 is not a factor of 24, because 24 ÷ 5 = 4 remainder 4.\n\n> **Remember:** Check every division: **quotient × divisor + remainder = dividend**. For 47 ÷ 5 = 9 remainder 2: 9 × 5 + 2 = 47."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Deeltal","en":"Dividend"},"def":{"af":"Die getal wat gedeel word; in 24 ÷ 4 = 6 is 24 die deeltal.","en":"The number that is divided; in 24 ÷ 4 = 6, 24 is the dividend."}},{"term":{"af":"Deler","en":"Divisor"},"def":{"af":"Die getal waardeur jy deel; in 24 ÷ 4 = 6 is 4 die deler.","en":"The number you divide by; in 24 ÷ 4 = 6, 4 is the divisor."}},{"term":{"af":"Kwosiënt","en":"Quotient"},"def":{"af":"Die antwoord van ’n deelsom.","en":"The answer to a division."}},{"term":{"af":"Res","en":"Remainder"},"def":{"af":"Wat oorbly as ’n getal nie presies gedeel kan word nie; dit is altyd kleiner as die deler.","en":"What is left over when a number cannot be divided exactly; it is always smaller than the divisor."}},{"term":{"af":"Verdeling","en":"Sharing"},"def":{"af":"Deling waar jy ’n hoeveelheid gelyk tussen ’n aantal mense of groepe uitdeel.","en":"Division where you hand out an amount equally among a number of people or groups."}},{"term":{"af":"Groepering","en":"Grouping"},"def":{"af":"Deling waar jy uitvind hoeveel groepe van ’n sekere grootte jy kan maak.","en":"Division where you find out how many groups of a certain size you can make."}},{"term":{"af":"Inverse bewerking","en":"Inverse operation"},"def":{"af":"Die bewerking wat ’n ander ongedaan maak; deling en vermenigvuldiging is inverse bewerkings.","en":"The operation that undoes another one; division and multiplication are inverse operations."}},{"term":{"af":"Faktor","en":"Factor"},"def":{"af":"’n Getal wat presies, sonder ’n res, in ’n ander getal deel; 6 is ’n faktor van 24.","en":"A number that divides exactly, without a remainder, into another number; 6 is a factor of 24."}},{"term":{"af":"Deelbaar","en":"Divisible"},"def":{"af":"’n Getal is deelbaar deur ’n ander getal as die res 0 is; 35 is deelbaar deur 7.","en":"A number is divisible by another number if the remainder is 0; 35 is divisible by 7."}},{"term":{"af":"Lang deling","en":"Long division"},"def":{"af":"’n Metode waar jy van links na regs deel, maal, aftrek en die volgende syfer afbring.","en":"A method where you divide, multiply, subtract and bring down the next digit, from left to right."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Opbreekmetode","en":"Breaking-down method"},"problem":{"af":"Bereken 684 ÷ 4.","en":"Calculate 684 ÷ 4."},"steps":[{"af":"Breek 684 op in veelvoude van 4: 684 = 400 + 280 + 4.","en":"Break 684 up into multiples of 4: 684 = 400 + 280 + 4."},{"af":"Deel elke deel: 400 ÷ 4 = 100; 280 ÷ 4 = 70; 4 ÷ 4 = 1.","en":"Divide each part: 400 ÷ 4 = 100, 280 ÷ 4 = 70, 4 ÷ 4 = 1."},{"af":"Tel die antwoorde bymekaar: 100 + 70 + 1 = 171.","en":"Add the answers together: 100 + 70 + 1 = 171."},{"af":"Kontroleer: 171 × 4 = 684. Dit klop.","en":"Check: 171 × 4 = 684. It is correct."}],"answer":{"af":"171","en":"171"}},{"title":{"af":"Lang deling met ’n res","en":"Long division with a remainder"},"problem":{"af":"Bereken 758 ÷ 6.","en":"Calculate 758 ÷ 6."},"steps":[{"af":"Honderde: 7 ÷ 6 = 1 en 1 bly oor. Skryf 1.","en":"Hundreds: 7 ÷ 6 = 1 and 1 is left over. Write 1."},{"af":"Bring die 5 af: 15 ÷ 6 = 2 (want 2 × 6 = 12) en 3 bly oor. Skryf 2.","en":"Bring down the 5: 15 ÷ 6 = 2 (because 2 × 6 = 12) and 3 is left over. Write 2."},{"af":"Bring die 8 af: 38 ÷ 6 = 6 (want 6 × 6 = 36) en 2 bly oor. Skryf 6; die res is 2.","en":"Bring down the 8: 38 ÷ 6 = 6 (because 6 × 6 = 36) and 2 is left over. Write 6; the remainder is 2."},{"af":"Kontroleer: 126 × 6 + 2 = 756 + 2 = 758. Dit klop.","en":"Check: 126 × 6 + 2 = 756 + 2 = 758. It is correct."}],"answer":{"af":"126 res 2","en":"126 remainder 2"}},{"title":{"af":"Wat doen jy met die res?","en":"What do you do with the remainder?"},"problem":{"af":"245 leerders gaan op ’n uitstappie. Elke bus kan 45 leerders neem. Hoeveel busse is nodig?","en":"245 learners go on an outing. Each bus can take 45 learners. How many buses are needed?"},"steps":[{"af":"Dit is groepering: hoeveel groepe van 45 is daar in 245?","en":"This is grouping: how many groups of 45 are there in 245?"},{"af":"Gebruik veelvoude van 45: 45 × 5 = 225, en 245 − 225 = 20. Dus 245 ÷ 45 = 5 res 20.","en":"Use multiples of 45: 45 × 5 = 225, and 245 − 225 = 20. So 245 ÷ 45 = 5 remainder 20."},{"af":"5 busse is vol, maar 20 leerders het nog plek nodig. Niemand mag agterbly nie, dus rond op.","en":"5 buses are full, but 20 learners still need a place. Nobody may stay behind, so round up."}],"answer":{"af":"6 busse is nodig.","en":"6 buses are needed."}},{"title":{"af":"Deel deur ’n 2-syfergetal","en":"Dividing by a 2-digit number"},"problem":{"af":"Ravi pak 432 appels in kratte van 18. Hoeveel kratte vul hy?","en":"Ravi packs 432 apples into crates of 18. How many crates does he fill?"},"steps":[{"af":"Bereken 432 ÷ 18. Begin met ’n maklike veelvoud: 18 × 20 = 360.","en":"Calculate 432 ÷ 18. Start with an easy multiple: 18 × 20 = 360."},{"af":"Wat bly oor? 432 − 360 = 72.","en":"What is left? 432 − 360 = 72."},{"af":"18 × 4 = 72, dus nog 4 kratte. Altesaam: 20 + 4 = 24.","en":"18 × 4 = 72, so 4 more crates. Altogether: 20 + 4 = 24."},{"af":"Kontroleer: 24 × 18 = 432. Dit klop.","en":"Check: 24 × 18 = 432. It is correct."}],"answer":{"af":"Ravi vul 24 kratte.","en":"Ravi fills 24 crates."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 63 ÷ 7?","en":"What is 63 ÷ 7?"},"options":[{"af":"8","en":"8"},{"af":"9","en":"9"},{"af":"7","en":"7"},{"af":"56","en":"56"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Gebruik die inverse bewerking: 9 × 7 = 63, dus 63 ÷ 7 = 9. 56 is 63 − 7 – dit is aftrek, nie deel nie.","en":"Use the inverse operation: 9 × 7 = 63, so 63 ÷ 7 = 9. 56 is 63 − 7 – that is subtraction, not division."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"36 kinders word in spanne van 4 ingedeel. Watter soort deling is dit, en hoeveel spanne is daar?","en":"36 children are divided into teams of 4. Which kind of division is this, and how many teams are there?"},"options":[{"af":"Verdeling; 4 spanne","en":"Sharing; 4 teams"},{"af":"Groepering; 32 spanne","en":"Grouping; 32 teams"},{"af":"Groepering; 9 spanne","en":"Grouping; 9 teams"},{"af":"Verdeling; 40 spanne","en":"Sharing; 40 teams"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die grootte van elke groep (4) is bekend en jy soek die aantal groepe – dit is groepering. 36 ÷ 4 = 9 spanne.","en":"The size of each group (4) is known and you are looking for the number of groups – that is grouping. 36 ÷ 4 = 9 teams."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"8 400 ÷ 100 = ___","en":"8 400 ÷ 100 = ___"},"answers":{"af":["84"],"en":["84"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["840","804","8 300"],"en":["840","804","8 300"]}},"explain":{"af":"As jy deur 100 deel, skuif elke syfer twee plekke na regs: 8 400 → 84. 840 is net ÷ 10, en 8 300 is 8 400 − 100.","en":"When you divide by 100, every digit moves two places to the right: 8 400 → 84. 840 is only ÷ 10, and 8 300 is 8 400 − 100."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Jy kan 47 ÷ 5 = 9 res 2 so kontroleer: 9 × 5 + 2 = 47.","en":"You can check 47 ÷ 5 = 9 remainder 2 like this: 9 × 5 + 2 = 47."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Kwosiënt × deler + res = deeltal: 9 × 5 = 45 en 45 + 2 = 47. Die antwoord is dus reg.","en":"True. Quotient × divisor + remainder = dividend: 9 × 5 = 45 and 45 + 2 = 47. So the answer is right."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bereken 516 ÷ 4.","en":"Calculate 516 ÷ 4."},"options":[{"af":"129","en":"129"},{"af":"119","en":"119"},{"af":"139","en":"139"},{"af":"2 064","en":"2 064"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Breek op: 516 = 400 + 80 + 36. 400 ÷ 4 = 100; 80 ÷ 4 = 20; 36 ÷ 4 = 9. 100 + 20 + 9 = 129. Kontroleer: 129 × 4 = 516. 2 064 is 516 × 4.","en":"Break up: 516 = 400 + 80 + 36. 400 ÷ 4 = 100, 80 ÷ 4 = 20, 36 ÷ 4 = 9. 100 + 20 + 9 = 129. Check: 129 × 4 = 516. 2 064 is 516 × 4."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"150 leerders gaan na ’n sportbyeenkoms. Elke bus neem 40 leerders. Hoeveel busse is nodig?","en":"150 learners go to a sports meeting. Each bus takes 40 learners. How many buses are needed?"},"options":[{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"3 res 30","en":"3 remainder 30"},{"af":"5","en":"5"},{"af":"4","en":"4"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"150 ÷ 40 = 3 res 30. Drie busse vat 120 leerders, maar 30 leerders het nog ’n bus nodig. Rond op: 4 busse. *3 res 30* is nie ’n antwoord op die vraag nie.","en":"150 ÷ 40 = 3 remainder 30. Three buses take 120 learners, but 30 learners still need a bus. Round up: 4 buses. *3 remainder 30* is not an answer to the question."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke deelsom by die regte antwoord.","en":"Match each division to the correct answer."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"29 ÷ 4","en":"29 ÷ 4"},"r":{"af":"7 res 1","en":"7 remainder 1"}},{"l":{"af":"38 ÷ 5","en":"38 ÷ 5"},"r":{"af":"7 res 3","en":"7 remainder 3"}},{"l":{"af":"52 ÷ 6","en":"52 ÷ 6"},"r":{"af":"8 res 4","en":"8 remainder 4"}},{"l":{"af":"75 ÷ 9","en":"75 ÷ 9"},"r":{"af":"8 res 3","en":"8 remainder 3"}},{"l":{"af":"83 ÷ 9","en":"83 ÷ 9"},"r":{"af":"9 res 2","en":"9 remainder 2"}}],"explain":{"af":"Kontroleer elkeen met kwosiënt × deler + res: 7 × 4 + 1 = 29; 7 × 5 + 3 = 38; 8 × 6 + 4 = 52; 8 × 9 + 3 = 75; 9 × 9 + 2 = 83.","en":"Check each one with quotient × divisor + remainder: 7 × 4 + 1 = 29, 7 × 5 + 3 = 38, 8 × 6 + 4 = 52, 8 × 9 + 3 = 75, 9 × 9 + 2 = 83."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die faktore van 18 is 1; 2; 3; ___; 9 en 18.","en":"The factors of 18 are 1, 2, 3, ___, 9 and 18."},"answers":{"af":["6","ses"],"en":["6","six"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4","5","8"],"en":["4","5","8"]}},"explain":{"af":"Vind die faktore in pare: 1 × 18; 2 × 9 en 3 × 6. Die ontbrekende faktor is 6. 4 is nie ’n faktor nie, want 18 ÷ 4 = 4 res 2.","en":"Find the factors in pairs: 1 × 18, 2 × 9 and 3 × 6. The missing factor is 6. 4 is not a factor, because 18 ÷ 4 = 4 remainder 2."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pasteie kos R15 elk. Hoeveel pasteie kan Liam met R100 koop?","en":"Pies cost R15 each. How many pies can Liam buy with R100?"},"options":[{"af":"7","en":"7"},{"af":"6 res 10","en":"6 remainder 10"},{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"5","en":"5"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"100 ÷ 15 = 6 res 10, want 6 × 15 = 90. Die R10 wat oorbly, is nie genoeg vir nog ’n pastei nie, dus rond af: 6 pasteie. 7 pasteie sou R105 kos.","en":"100 ÷ 15 = 6 remainder 10, because 6 × 15 = 90. The R10 that is left is not enough for another pie, so round down: 6 pies. 7 pies would cost R105."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die res van ’n deelsom kan groter as die deler wees.","en":"The remainder of a division can be bigger than the divisor."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. As die res groter as (of gelyk aan) die deler is, kan jy nog ’n groep maak. Die res moet altyd kleiner as die deler wees.","en":"False. If the remainder is bigger than (or equal to) the divisor, you can still make another group. The remainder must always be smaller than the divisor."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter getal is nie ’n faktor van 24 nie?","en":"Which number is not a factor of 24?"},"options":[{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"9","en":"9"},{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"8","en":"8"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die faktore van 24 is 1; 2; 3; 4; 6; 8; 12 en 24. 24 ÷ 9 = 2 res 6, dus is 9 nie ’n faktor nie. 3; 6 en 8 deel almal presies in 24.","en":"The factors of 24 are 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12 and 24. 24 ÷ 9 = 2 remainder 6, so 9 is not a factor. 3, 6 and 8 all divide exactly into 24."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"384 ÷ 16 = ___","en":"384 ÷ 16 = ___"},"answers":{"af":["24"],"en":["24"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["22","26","368"],"en":["22","26","368"]}},"explain":{"af":"16 × 20 = 320 en 384 − 320 = 64. 16 × 4 = 64, dus is die antwoord 20 + 4 = 24. Kontroleer: 24 × 16 = 384.","en":"16 × 20 = 320 and 384 − 320 = 64. 16 × 4 = 64, so the answer is 20 + 4 = 24. Check: 24 × 16 = 384."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bereken 945 ÷ 7 met lang deling.","en":"Calculate 945 ÷ 7 with long division."},"options":[{"af":"125","en":"125"},{"af":"1 035","en":"1 035"},{"af":"145","en":"145"},{"af":"135","en":"135"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"9 ÷ 7 = 1 res 2. Bring die 4 af: 24 ÷ 7 = 3 res 3. Bring die 5 af: 35 ÷ 7 = 5. Antwoord: 135. Kontroleer: 135 × 7 = 945.","en":"9 ÷ 7 = 1 remainder 2. Bring down the 4: 24 ÷ 7 = 3 remainder 3. Bring down the 5: 35 ÷ 7 = 5. Answer: 135. Check: 135 × 7 = 945."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Nomsa deel 250 albasters gelyk tussen 8 vriende en hou die res vir haarself. Hoeveel albasters hou sy?","en":"Nomsa shares 250 marbles equally among 8 friends and keeps the remainder for herself. How many marbles does she keep?"},"options":[{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"31","en":"31"},{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"10","en":"10"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"250 ÷ 8 = 31 res 2, want 31 × 8 = 248 en 250 − 248 = 2. Elke vriend kry 31 en Nomsa hou 2. 10 kry jy as jy by 30 × 8 = 240 ophou – maar 10 is groter as 8, dus kan elkeen nog een kry.","en":"250 ÷ 8 = 31 remainder 2, because 31 × 8 = 248 and 250 − 248 = 2. Each friend gets 31 and Nomsa keeps 2. You get 10 if you stop at 30 × 8 = 240 – but 10 is bigger than 8, so each friend can get one more."}}]},{"id":"w5-t2-gewone-breuke","title":{"af":"Gewone breuke","en":"Common fractions"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal breuke van halwes tot twaalfdes kan lees, teken en op ’n getallelyn kan wys, ekwivalente breuke kan vind, breuke kan vergelyk, optel en aftrek, en ’n breuk van ’n heelgetal kan bereken.","en":"You will be able to read, draw and show fractions from halves to twelfths on a number line, find equivalent fractions, compare, add and subtract fractions, and calculate a fraction of a whole number."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is ’n breuk?\n\n’n **Breuk** beskryf ’n **deel van ’n geheel** wat in **gelyke dele** verdeel is. Kyk na 3/4 (drie kwart):\n\n- Die **noemer** (onder, 4) sê in hoeveel gelyke dele die geheel verdeel is. Dit *noem* die soort deel: kwarte.\n- Die **teller** (bo, 3) *tel* hoeveel van daardie dele ons het.\n\nIn Graad 5 werk jy met halwes, derdes, kwarte, vyfdes, sesdes, sewendes, agtstes, negendes, tiendes, elfdes en twaalfdes. 2/5 lees ons as *twee vyfdes* en 5/12 as *vyf twaalfdes*.\n\nDie dele moet **ewe groot** wees. As ’n koek in 4 stukke van verskillende grootte gesny is, is elke stuk nie ’n kwart nie.\n\n## Breuke in diagramme en op ’n getallelyn\n\n’n Sjokoladestafie het 6 gelyke blokkies. As jy 5 eet, het jy 5/6 geëet en 1/6 bly oor. Saam is dit 6/6 = 1 heel stafie.\n\nOp ’n **getallelyn** verdeel jy die stuk tussen 0 en 1 in gelyke dele – die noemer sê hoeveel. Vir agtstes is die merkies 1/8; 2/8; 3/8; … tot 8/8 = 1. Die breuk 3/8 lê drie spronge ná 0.\n\n## Ekwivalente breuke\n\n**Ekwivalente breuke** is ewe groot, maar het ander name. Jy kry hulle deur die teller **en** die noemer met dieselfde getal te maal (of te deel).\n\n| Breuk | × 2 | × 3 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1/2 | 2/4 | 3/6 |\n| 1/3 | 2/6 | 3/9 |\n| 1/4 | 2/8 | 3/12 |\n| 3/4 | 6/8 | 9/12 |\n\nDus is 1/2 = 2/4 = 3/6 = 4/8 = 5/10 = 6/12. Teken dit gerus: die helfte van ’n strook is ewe groot as 3 sesdes van dieselfde strook.\n\n## Vergelyk en orden\n\n- **Dieselfde noemer:** die breuk met die groter teller is groter: 5/8 > 3/8.\n- **Dieselfde teller:** die breuk met die **kleiner noemer** is groter, want die dele is groter: 1/3 > 1/5 en 3/4 > 3/8.\n\nIn stygende orde: 2/9; 4/9; 7/9 en 1/10; 1/6; 1/2.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** 1/8 is **nie** groter as 1/4 nie, al is 8 groter as 4. As jy ’n koek in 8 stukke sny, is elke stuk kleiner as wanneer jy dit in 4 stukke sny.\n\n## Gemengde getalle en onegte breuke\n\n- ’n **Egte breuk** se teller is kleiner as die noemer, soos 3/4. Dit is minder as 1 heel.\n- ’n **Onegte breuk** se teller is groter as (of gelyk aan) die noemer, soos 7/4. Dit is 1 heel of meer.\n- ’n **Gemengde getal** is ’n heelgetal en ’n breuk saam, soos 1 3/4 (een en drie kwart).\n\n**Onegte breuk na gemengde getal:** deel die teller deur die noemer. 11/4: 11 ÷ 4 = 2 res 3, dus 11/4 = 2 3/4.\n\n**Gemengde getal na onegte breuk:** heelgetal × noemer + teller. 2 3/4: 2 × 4 + 3 = 11, dus 11/4.\n\n## Optel en aftrek met dieselfde noemer\n\nTel die tellers bymekaar of trek hulle af. Die noemer bly dieselfde, want die soort deel verander nie.\n\n- 2/7 + 3/7 = 5/7\n- 7/8 − 3/8 = 4/8, en dit is ekwivalent aan 1/2\n- 3/5 + 4/5 = 7/5 = 1 2/5\n\n> **Onthou:** By optel en aftrek bly die **noemer dieselfde**. 2/7 + 3/7 is 5/7, nie 5/14 nie – twee sewendes plus drie sewendes is vyf sewendes.\n\n## ’n Breuk van ’n heelgetal\n\nOm 1/4 van 20 te kry, deel jy 20 in 4 gelyke groepe: 20 ÷ 4 = **5**. Vir 3/4 van 20 neem jy 3 sulke groepe: 3 × 5 = **15**.\n\nReël: **deel deur die noemer, maal met die teller**.\n\nLerato het R60 en spandeer 2/5 daarvan aan ’n boek. 60 ÷ 5 = 12 en 2 × 12 = 24, dus kos die boek R24. Sy het R60 − R24 = R36 oor – dit is die ander 3/5.","en":"## What is a fraction?\n\nA **fraction** describes a **part of a whole** that has been divided into **equal parts**. Look at 3/4 (three quarters):\n\n- The **denominator** (at the bottom, 4) tells you into how many equal parts the whole is divided. It *names* the kind of part: quarters.\n- The **numerator** (at the top, 3) *counts* how many of those parts we have.\n\nIn Grade 5 you work with halves, thirds, quarters, fifths, sixths, sevenths, eighths, ninths, tenths, elevenths and twelfths. We read 2/5 as *two fifths* and 5/12 as *five twelfths*.\n\nThe parts must be **equal**. If a cake is cut into 4 pieces of different sizes, each piece is not a quarter.\n\n## Fractions in diagrams and on a number line\n\nA chocolate bar has 6 equal blocks. If you eat 5, you have eaten 5/6 and 1/6 is left. Together that is 6/6 = 1 whole bar.\n\nOn a **number line** you divide the space between 0 and 1 into equal parts – the denominator tells you how many. For eighths the marks are 1/8, 2/8, 3/8, … up to 8/8 = 1. The fraction 3/8 is three jumps after 0.\n\n## Equivalent fractions\n\n**Equivalent fractions** are the same size, but have different names. You get them by multiplying (or dividing) the numerator **and** the denominator by the same number.\n\n| Fraction | × 2 | × 3 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1/2 | 2/4 | 3/6 |\n| 1/3 | 2/6 | 3/9 |\n| 1/4 | 2/8 | 3/12 |\n| 3/4 | 6/8 | 9/12 |\n\nSo 1/2 = 2/4 = 3/6 = 4/8 = 5/10 = 6/12. Draw it if you like: half of a strip is the same size as 3 sixths of the same strip.\n\n## Comparing and ordering\n\n- **Same denominator:** the fraction with the bigger numerator is bigger: 5/8 > 3/8.\n- **Same numerator:** the fraction with the **smaller denominator** is bigger, because the parts are bigger: 1/3 > 1/5 and 3/4 > 3/8.\n\nIn ascending order: 2/9, 4/9, 7/9 and 1/10, 1/6, 1/2.\n\n> **Common mistake:** 1/8 is **not** bigger than 1/4, even though 8 is bigger than 4. If you cut a cake into 8 pieces, each piece is smaller than when you cut it into 4 pieces.\n\n## Mixed numbers and improper fractions\n\n- A **proper fraction** has a numerator smaller than the denominator, such as 3/4. It is less than 1 whole.\n- An **improper fraction** has a numerator bigger than (or equal to) the denominator, such as 7/4. It is 1 whole or more.\n- A **mixed number** is a whole number and a fraction together, such as 1 3/4 (one and three quarters).\n\n**Improper fraction to mixed number:** divide the numerator by the denominator. 11/4: 11 ÷ 4 = 2 remainder 3, so 11/4 = 2 3/4.\n\n**Mixed number to improper fraction:** whole number × denominator + numerator. 2 3/4: 2 × 4 + 3 = 11, so 11/4.\n\n## Adding and subtracting with the same denominator\n\nAdd or subtract the numerators. The denominator stays the same, because the kind of part does not change.\n\n- 2/7 + 3/7 = 5/7\n- 7/8 − 3/8 = 4/8, and this is equivalent to 1/2\n- 3/5 + 4/5 = 7/5 = 1 2/5\n\n> **Remember:** When you add and subtract, the **denominator stays the same**. 2/7 + 3/7 is 5/7, not 5/14 – two sevenths plus three sevenths is five sevenths.\n\n## A fraction of a whole number\n\nTo find 1/4 of 20, you divide 20 into 4 equal groups: 20 ÷ 4 = **5**. For 3/4 of 20 you take 3 such groups: 3 × 5 = **15**.\n\nRule: **divide by the denominator, multiply by the numerator**.\n\nLerato has R60 and spends 2/5 of it on a book. 60 ÷ 5 = 12 and 2 × 12 = 24, so the book costs R24. She has R60 − R24 = R36 left – that is the other 3/5."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Breuk","en":"Fraction"},"def":{"af":"’n Getal wat ’n deel van ’n geheel beskryf wat in gelyke dele verdeel is, soos 3/4.","en":"A number that describes a part of a whole that is divided into equal parts, such as 3/4."}},{"term":{"af":"Teller","en":"Numerator"},"def":{"af":"Die getal bo in ’n breuk; dit tel hoeveel dele ons het.","en":"The number at the top of a fraction; it counts how many parts we have."}},{"term":{"af":"Noemer","en":"Denominator"},"def":{"af":"Die getal onder in ’n breuk; dit sê in hoeveel gelyke dele die geheel verdeel is.","en":"The number at the bottom of a fraction; it tells into how many equal parts the whole is divided."}},{"term":{"af":"Geheel","en":"Whole"},"def":{"af":"Die hele voorwerp of hoeveelheid; ’n geheel is gelyk aan 1, soos 4/4 of 8/8.","en":"The whole object or amount; a whole is equal to 1, such as 4/4 or 8/8."}},{"term":{"af":"Eenheidsbreuk","en":"Unit fraction"},"def":{"af":"’n Breuk met 1 as teller, soos 1/3 of 1/8.","en":"A fraction with 1 as the numerator, such as 1/3 or 1/8."}},{"term":{"af":"Ekwivalente breuke","en":"Equivalent fractions"},"def":{"af":"Breuke wat ewe groot is, al lyk hulle anders, soos 1/2 en 3/6.","en":"Fractions that are the same size even though they look different, such as 1/2 and 3/6."}},{"term":{"af":"Egte breuk","en":"Proper fraction"},"def":{"af":"’n Breuk waarvan die teller kleiner as die noemer is, soos 5/8; dit is minder as 1.","en":"A fraction whose numerator is smaller than its denominator, such as 5/8; it is less than 1."}},{"term":{"af":"Onegte breuk","en":"Improper fraction"},"def":{"af":"’n Breuk waarvan die teller groter as of gelyk aan die noemer is, soos 9/4.","en":"A fraction whose numerator is bigger than or equal to its denominator, such as 9/4."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemengde getal","en":"Mixed number"},"def":{"af":"’n Heelgetal en ’n breuk saam, soos 2 1/4 (twee en een kwart).","en":"A whole number and a fraction together, such as 2 1/4 (two and a quarter)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Vind ekwivalente breuke","en":"Find equivalent fractions"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf drie breuke wat ekwivalent is aan 2/3, met noemers van hoogstens 12.","en":"Write three fractions that are equivalent to 2/3, with denominators of at most 12."},"steps":[{"af":"Maal die teller en die noemer met dieselfde getal. × 2: 2/3 = 4/6.","en":"Multiply the numerator and the denominator by the same number. × 2: 2/3 = 4/6."},{"af":"× 3: 2/3 = 6/9.","en":"× 3: 2/3 = 6/9."},{"af":"× 4: 2/3 = 8/12. (× 5 sou 10/15 gee, maar 15 is groter as 12.)","en":"× 4: 2/3 = 8/12. (× 5 would give 10/15, but 15 is bigger than 12.)"}],"answer":{"af":"4/6; 6/9; 8/12","en":"4/6, 6/9, 8/12"}},{"title":{"af":"Orden eenheidsbreuke","en":"Order unit fractions"},"problem":{"af":"Rangskik van klein na groot: 1/3; 1/8; 1/2; 1/5","en":"Arrange from small to big: 1/3, 1/8, 1/2, 1/5"},"steps":[{"af":"Al die tellers is 1, dus vergelyk die noemers.","en":"All the numerators are 1, so compare the denominators."},{"af":"Hoe groter die noemer, hoe kleiner die dele. 1/8 is die kleinste en 1/2 die grootste.","en":"The bigger the denominator, the smaller the parts. 1/8 is the smallest and 1/2 the biggest."},{"af":"Orden die noemers van groot na klein (8; 5; 3; 2) om die breuke van klein na groot te kry.","en":"Order the denominators from big to small (8, 5, 3, 2) to get the fractions from small to big."}],"answer":{"af":"1/8; 1/5; 1/3; 1/2","en":"1/8, 1/5, 1/3, 1/2"}},{"title":{"af":"Tel op en skryf as ’n gemengde getal","en":"Add and write as a mixed number"},"problem":{"af":"Bereken 5/6 + 4/6 en skryf die antwoord as ’n gemengde getal.","en":"Calculate 5/6 + 4/6 and write the answer as a mixed number."},"steps":[{"af":"Die noemers is dieselfde, dus tel net die tellers op: 5 + 4 = 9. Die antwoord is 9/6.","en":"The denominators are the same, so just add the numerators: 5 + 4 = 9. The answer is 9/6."},{"af":"9/6 is ’n onegte breuk. Deel: 9 ÷ 6 = 1 res 3, dus 9/6 = 1 3/6.","en":"9/6 is an improper fraction. Divide: 9 ÷ 6 = 1 remainder 3, so 9/6 = 1 3/6."},{"af":"3/6 is ekwivalent aan 1/2, dus kan jy ook 1 1/2 skryf.","en":"3/6 is equivalent to 1/2, so you can also write 1 1/2."}],"answer":{"af":"1 3/6, wat dieselfde is as 1 1/2","en":"1 3/6, which is the same as 1 1/2"}},{"title":{"af":"’n Breuk van ’n hoeveelheid","en":"A fraction of an amount"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo se ma bak 24 koekies. Die gesin eet 3/8 van die koekies. Hoeveel koekies is geëet, en hoeveel bly oor?","en":"Thabo’s mother bakes 24 biscuits. The family eats 3/8 of the biscuits. How many biscuits were eaten, and how many are left?"},"steps":[{"af":"Deel deur die noemer: 1/8 van 24 = 24 ÷ 8 = 3.","en":"Divide by the denominator: 1/8 of 24 = 24 ÷ 8 = 3."},{"af":"Maal met die teller: 3/8 van 24 = 3 × 3 = 9 koekies geëet.","en":"Multiply by the numerator: 3/8 of 24 = 3 × 3 = 9 biscuits eaten."},{"af":"Trek af om te kry wat oorbly: 24 − 9 = 15. (Dit is 5/8 van 24: 5 × 3 = 15.)","en":"Subtract to find what is left: 24 − 9 = 15. (That is 5/8 of 24: 5 × 3 = 15.)"}],"answer":{"af":"9 koekies is geëet en 15 bly oor.","en":"9 biscuits were eaten and 15 are left."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die noemer in die breuk 5/8?","en":"What is the denominator in the fraction 5/8?"},"options":[{"af":"5","en":"5"},{"af":"8","en":"8"},{"af":"13","en":"13"},{"af":"3","en":"3"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die noemer is die getal onder: 8. Dit sê dat die geheel in 8 gelyke dele verdeel is. Die 5 bo is die teller.","en":"The denominator is the number at the bottom: 8. It tells you the whole is divided into 8 equal parts. The 5 at the top is the numerator."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Pizza word in 6 gelyke stukke gesny. Sipho eet 2 stukke. Watter breuk van die pizza het hy geëet?","en":"A pizza is cut into 6 equal pieces. Sipho eats 2 pieces. What fraction of the pizza did he eat?"},"options":[{"af":"6/2","en":"6/2"},{"af":"2/4","en":"2/4"},{"af":"4/6","en":"4/6"},{"af":"2/6","en":"2/6"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die pizza het 6 gelyke dele (noemer 6) en Sipho het 2 daarvan geëet (teller 2): 2/6. 4/6 is die deel wat oorbly.","en":"The pizza has 6 equal parts (denominator 6) and Sipho ate 2 of them (numerator 2): 2/6. 4/6 is the part that is left."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"1/2 = ___/10","en":"1/2 = ___/10"},"answers":{"af":["5","vyf"],"en":["5","five"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["2","4","20"],"en":["2","4","20"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die noemer is met 5 gemaal (2 × 5 = 10), dus moet die teller ook met 5 gemaal word: 1 × 5 = 5. Dus is 1/2 = 5/10.","en":"The denominator was multiplied by 5 (2 × 5 = 10), so the numerator must also be multiplied by 5: 1 × 5 = 5. So 1/2 = 5/10."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"1/8 is groter as 1/4, want 8 is groter as 4.","en":"1/8 is bigger than 1/4, because 8 is bigger than 4."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Hoe meer stukke jy ’n geheel in sny, hoe kleiner is elke stuk. ’n Agtste is kleiner as ’n kwart: 1/8 < 1/4.","en":"False. The more pieces you cut a whole into, the smaller each piece is. An eighth is smaller than a quarter: 1/8 < 1/4."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter breuk is die grootste?","en":"Which fraction is the biggest?"},"options":[{"af":"3/10","en":"3/10"},{"af":"3/8","en":"3/8"},{"af":"3/4","en":"3/4"},{"af":"3/5","en":"3/5"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die tellers is almal 3. Die breuk met die kleinste noemer het die grootste dele, dus is 3/4 die grootste. 3/10 is die kleinste.","en":"The numerators are all 3. The fraction with the smallest denominator has the biggest parts, so 3/4 is the biggest. 3/10 is the smallest."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 11/4 as ’n gemengde getal?","en":"What is 11/4 as a mixed number?"},"options":[{"af":"1 3/4","en":"1 3/4"},{"af":"2 1/4","en":"2 1/4"},{"af":"2 3/4","en":"2 3/4"},{"af":"3 1/4","en":"3 1/4"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"11 ÷ 4 = 2 res 3: dit is 2 hele (8 kwarte) en 3 kwarte oor. Dus 11/4 = 2 3/4. Kontroleer: 2 × 4 + 3 = 11.","en":"11 ÷ 4 = 2 remainder 3: that is 2 wholes (8 quarters) and 3 quarters left. So 11/4 = 2 3/4. Check: 2 × 4 + 3 = 11."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke breuk by die ekwivalente breuk in twaalfdes.","en":"Match each fraction to the equivalent fraction in twelfths."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"1/2","en":"1/2"},"r":{"af":"6/12","en":"6/12"}},{"l":{"af":"1/3","en":"1/3"},"r":{"af":"4/12","en":"4/12"}},{"l":{"af":"1/4","en":"1/4"},"r":{"af":"3/12","en":"3/12"}},{"l":{"af":"2/3","en":"2/3"},"r":{"af":"8/12","en":"8/12"}},{"l":{"af":"5/6","en":"5/6"},"r":{"af":"10/12","en":"10/12"}}],"explain":{"af":"Maal die teller en noemer met dieselfde getal om 12 as noemer te kry: 1/2 (× 6) = 6/12; 1/3 (× 4) = 4/12; 1/4 (× 3) = 3/12; 2/3 (× 4) = 8/12; 5/6 (× 2) = 10/12.","en":"Multiply the numerator and denominator by the same number to get 12 as the denominator: 1/2 (× 6) = 6/12, 1/3 (× 4) = 4/12, 1/4 (× 3) = 3/12, 2/3 (× 4) = 8/12, 5/6 (× 2) = 10/12."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"3/4 van 28 = ___","en":"3/4 of 28 = ___"},"answers":{"af":["21"],"en":["21"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["7","84","24"],"en":["7","84","24"]}},"explain":{"af":"Deel deur die noemer: 28 ÷ 4 = 7. Maal met die teller: 3 × 7 = 21. 7 is net 1/4 van 28, en 84 is 3 × 28.","en":"Divide by the denominator: 28 ÷ 4 = 7. Multiply by the numerator: 3 × 7 = 21. 7 is only 1/4 of 28, and 84 is 3 × 28."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bereken 2/9 + 5/9.","en":"Calculate 2/9 + 5/9."},"options":[{"af":"7/9","en":"7/9"},{"af":"7/18","en":"7/18"},{"af":"10/9","en":"10/9"},{"af":"3/9","en":"3/9"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die noemer bly 9 en jy tel die tellers op: 2 + 5 = 7, dus 7/9. 7/18 is die algemene fout om die noemers ook op te tel. 3/9 is die verskil, nie die som nie.","en":"The denominator stays 9 and you add the numerators: 2 + 5 = 7, so 7/9. 7/18 is the common mistake of adding the denominators too. 3/9 is the difference, not the sum."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"2 1/3 is dieselfde as 7/3.","en":"2 1/3 is the same as 7/3."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 2 hele is 6 derdes (2 × 3 = 6), plus nog 1 derde: 6 + 1 = 7 derdes, dus 7/3.","en":"True. 2 wholes are 6 thirds (2 × 3 = 6), plus 1 more third: 6 + 1 = 7 thirds, so 7/3."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ma het R80. Sy gee 1/5 daarvan vir Zanele as sakgeld. Hoeveel kry Zanele?","en":"Mom has R80. She gives 1/5 of it to Zanele as pocket money. How much does Zanele get?"},"options":[{"af":"R5","en":"R5"},{"af":"R16","en":"R16"},{"af":"R400","en":"R400"},{"af":"R75","en":"R75"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"1/5 van R80 beteken R80 in 5 gelyke dele: 80 ÷ 5 = 16. Zanele kry R16. R400 is 80 × 5 – dan het jy gemaal in plaas van gedeel.","en":"1/5 of R80 means R80 in 5 equal parts: 80 ÷ 5 = 16. Zanele gets R16. R400 is 80 × 5 – then you multiplied instead of dividing."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"7/10 − 4/10 = ___","en":"7/10 − 4/10 = ___"},"answers":{"af":["3/10","drie tiendes"],"en":["3/10","three tenths"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["11/10","3/20","1/10"],"en":["11/10","3/20","1/10"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die noemer bly 10 en jy trek die tellers af: 7 − 4 = 3, dus 3/10. 11/10 is die som, en 3/20 tel die noemers verkeerdelik op.","en":"The denominator stays 10 and you subtract the numerators: 7 − 4 = 3, so 3/10. 11/10 is the sum, and 3/20 wrongly adds the denominators."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Getallelyn van 0 tot 1 is in 5 gelyke dele verdeel. Watter breuk staan by die derde merkie ná 0?","en":"A number line from 0 to 1 is divided into 5 equal parts. Which fraction is at the third mark after 0?"},"options":[{"af":"3/5","en":"3/5"},{"af":"1/3","en":"1/3"},{"af":"5/3","en":"5/3"},{"af":"3/6","en":"3/6"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"5 gelyke dele beteken vyfdes (noemer 5). Die merkies is 1/5; 2/5; 3/5; 4/5 en 5/5 = 1. Die derde merkie is 3/5.","en":"5 equal parts means fifths (denominator 5). The marks are 1/5, 2/5, 3/5, 4/5 and 5/5 = 1. The third mark is 3/5."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter breuke is in stygende orde (van klein na groot)?","en":"Which fractions are in ascending order (from small to big)?"},"options":[{"af":"1/2; 1/5; 1/9","en":"1/2, 1/5, 1/9"},{"af":"1/5; 1/2; 1/9","en":"1/5, 1/2, 1/9"},{"af":"1/2; 1/9; 1/5","en":"1/2, 1/9, 1/5"},{"af":"1/9; 1/5; 1/2","en":"1/9, 1/5, 1/2"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die tellers is almal 1, dus is die breuk met die grootste noemer die kleinste. 1/9 < 1/5 < 1/2. Die eerste opsie is in dalende orde.","en":"The numerators are all 1, so the fraction with the biggest denominator is the smallest. 1/9 < 1/5 < 1/2. The first option is in descending order."}}]},{"id":"w5-t2-3d-voorwerpe","title":{"af":"3D-voorwerpe","en":"3D objects"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal 3D-voorwerpe kan benoem, hul plat en geboë vlakke, rande en hoekpunte kan tel, prismas en piramides kan onderskei en nette van ’n kubus en ’n reghoekige prisma kan herken.","en":"You will be able to name 3D objects, count their flat and curved surfaces, edges and vertices, tell prisms and pyramids apart and recognise nets of a cube and a rectangular prism."},"summary":{"af":"## Van 2D na 3D\n\n’n 2D-vorm is plat, soos ’n tekening op papier. ’n **3D-voorwerp** het **lengte, breedte en hoogte** – jy kan dit optel, vashou en van alle kante af bekyk, soos ’n doos of ’n bal.\n\n## Die dele van ’n 3D-voorwerp\n\n- ’n **Vlak** is ’n buiteoppervlak van die voorwerp. ’n Vlak kan **plat** wees (soos die kante van ’n doos) of **geboë** (soos die buitekant van ’n bal).\n- ’n **Rand** is waar twee vlakke bymekaarkom.\n- ’n **Hoekpunt** is waar rande in ’n punt bymekaarkom.\n\nVoorwerpe met ’n geboë vlak kan **rol**; voorwerpe met net plat vlakke kan **gly** en mooi **op mekaar gestapel** word.\n\n## Die voorwerpe wat jy moet ken\n\n| Voorwerp | Plat vlakke | Geboë vlakke | Rande | Hoekpunte |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Kubus | 6 vierkante | 0 | 12 | 8 |\n| Reghoekige prisma | 6 reghoeke | 0 | 12 | 8 |\n| Driehoekige prisma | 5 (2 driehoeke, 3 reghoeke) | 0 | 9 | 6 |\n| Vierkantige piramide | 5 (1 vierkant, 4 driehoeke) | 0 | 8 | 5 |\n| Silinder | 2 sirkels | 1 | 2 (geboë) | 0 |\n| Keël | 1 sirkel | 1 | 1 (geboë) | 1 (die punt bo) |\n| Bol | 0 | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Op ’n tekening sien jy nie al die vlakke nie. ’n Tekening van ’n kubus wys dalk net 3 vlakke, maar die kubus het **6**: voor en agter, bo en onder, links en regs. Dink aan die kante wat jy nie kan sien nie.\n\n## Prismas en piramides\n\n’n **Prisma** het **twee eindvlakke** wat dieselfde vorm en grootte het en **parallel** is. Hulle word deur reghoeke verbind. As jy ’n prisma regdeur sny, parallel aan die eindvlakke, kry jy elke keer dieselfde vorm.\n\n- Driehoekige prisma: die eindvlakke is driehoeke.\n- Reghoekige prisma: die eindvlakke is reghoeke.\n- ’n **Kubus** is ’n spesiale reghoekige prisma waarvan al ses vlakke vierkante is.\n\n’n **Piramide** het **een grondvlak**. Al die ander vlakke is **driehoeke** wat bo in **een punt** (die apeks) bymekaarkom. ’n Vierkantige piramide het ’n vierkant as grondvlak.\n\n> **Onthou:** Prismas word genoem na die vorm van hul **eindvlakke** en piramides na die vorm van hul **grondvlak**.\n\n## 3D-voorwerpe om jou\n\n| Voorwerp | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| Bol | sokkerbal, lemoen |\n| Silinder | koeldrankblikkie, kers |\n| Keël | roomyshorinkie, verkeerskeël |\n| Kubus | dobbelsteen, suikerklontjie |\n| Reghoekige prisma | baksteen, graanvlokkiesdoos |\n| Driehoekige prisma | ’n A-vormige tent |\n| Vierkantige piramide | die piramides in Egipte |\n\n## Nette\n\n’n **Net** is ’n plat vorm wat jy kan uitknip en vou om ’n 3D-voorwerp te maak. As jy ’n doos versigtig langs sy rande oopsny en plat druk, sien jy sy net.\n\n- Die net van ’n **kubus** bestaan uit **6 ewe groot vierkante**. ’n Bekende net lyk soos ’n kruis: ’n ry van 4 vierkante met een vierkant bo en een onder.\n- Die net van ’n **reghoekige prisma** bestaan uit **6 reghoeke** in **3 pare** wat ewe groot is.\n\nNie elke rangskikking van 6 vierkante is ’n net van ’n kubus nie. 6 vierkante in een lang ry sal oorvleuel as jy dit vou, en daar bly twee kante oop. Daar is 11 verskillende nette vir ’n kubus.\n\nOm te toets of ’n net werk, kies een vierkant as die bodem en vou die ander in jou kop op. Elke vlak moet presies een plek kry.","en":"## From 2D to 3D\n\nA 2D shape is flat, like a drawing on paper. A **3D object** has **length, breadth and height** – you can pick it up, hold it and look at it from all sides, like a box or a ball.\n\n## The parts of a 3D object\n\n- A **face** is an outside surface of the object. A face can be **flat** (like the sides of a box) or **curved** (like the outside of a ball).\n- An **edge** is where two faces meet.\n- A **vertex** is where edges meet in a point.\n\nObjects with a curved surface can **roll**; objects with only flat faces can **slide** and be **stacked** neatly on top of each other.\n\n## The objects you must know\n\n| Object | Flat faces | Curved surfaces | Edges | Vertices |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Cube | 6 squares | 0 | 12 | 8 |\n| Rectangular prism | 6 rectangles | 0 | 12 | 8 |\n| Triangular prism | 5 (2 triangles, 3 rectangles) | 0 | 9 | 6 |\n| Square pyramid | 5 (1 square, 4 triangles) | 0 | 8 | 5 |\n| Cylinder | 2 circles | 1 | 2 (curved) | 0 |\n| Cone | 1 circle | 1 | 1 (curved) | 1 (the point at the top) |\n| Sphere | 0 | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n\n> **Common mistake:** In a drawing you do not see all the faces. A drawing of a cube may show only 3 faces, but the cube has **6**: front and back, top and bottom, left and right. Think of the sides you cannot see.\n\n## Prisms and pyramids\n\nA **prism** has **two end faces** that have the same shape and size and are **parallel**. They are joined by rectangles. If you slice a prism straight through, parallel to the end faces, you get the same shape every time.\n\n- Triangular prism: the end faces are triangles.\n- Rectangular prism: the end faces are rectangles.\n- A **cube** is a special rectangular prism whose six faces are all squares.\n\nA **pyramid** has **one base**. All the other faces are **triangles** that meet at the top in **one point** (the apex). A square pyramid has a square as its base.\n\n> **Remember:** Prisms are named after the shape of their **end faces** and pyramids after the shape of their **base**.\n\n## 3D objects around you\n\n| Object | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| Sphere | soccer ball, orange |\n| Cylinder | cooldrink can, candle |\n| Cone | ice-cream cone, traffic cone |\n| Cube | dice, sugar cube |\n| Rectangular prism | brick, cereal box |\n| Triangular prism | an A-shaped tent |\n| Square pyramid | the pyramids in Egypt |\n\n## Nets\n\nA **net** is a flat shape that you can cut out and fold to make a 3D object. If you carefully cut a box open along its edges and press it flat, you see its net.\n\n- The net of a **cube** is made of **6 equal squares**. A well-known net looks like a cross: a row of 4 squares with one square above and one below.\n- The net of a **rectangular prism** is made of **6 rectangles** in **3 pairs** that are the same size.\n\nNot every arrangement of 6 squares is a net of a cube. 6 squares in one long row will overlap when you fold it, and two sides stay open. There are 11 different nets for a cube.\n\nTo test whether a net works, choose one square as the bottom and fold the others up in your head. Every face must get exactly one place."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"3D-voorwerp","en":"3D object"},"def":{"af":"’n Voorwerp met lengte, breedte en hoogte, soos ’n doos of ’n bal.","en":"An object with length, breadth and height, such as a box or a ball."}},{"term":{"af":"Plat vlak","en":"Flat face"},"def":{"af":"’n Plat buiteoppervlak van ’n 3D-voorwerp, soos een kant van ’n dobbelsteen.","en":"A flat outside surface of a 3D object, such as one side of a dice."}},{"term":{"af":"Geboë vlak","en":"Curved surface"},"def":{"af":"’n Rond buiteoppervlak wat ’n voorwerp laat rol, soos die buitekant van ’n bal.","en":"A round outside surface that lets an object roll, such as the outside of a ball."}},{"term":{"af":"Rand","en":"Edge"},"def":{"af":"Die lyn waar twee vlakke van ’n 3D-voorwerp bymekaarkom.","en":"The line where two faces of a 3D object meet."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoekpunt","en":"Vertex"},"def":{"af":"Die punt waar rande van ’n 3D-voorwerp bymekaarkom; ’n kubus het 8.","en":"The point where edges of a 3D object meet; a cube has 8."}},{"term":{"af":"Prisma","en":"Prism"},"def":{"af":"’n 3D-voorwerp met twee ewe groot, parallelle eindvlakke wat deur reghoeke verbind word.","en":"A 3D object with two equal, parallel end faces that are joined by rectangles."}},{"term":{"af":"Piramide","en":"Pyramid"},"def":{"af":"’n 3D-voorwerp met een grondvlak en driehoekige vlakke wat bo in een punt bymekaarkom.","en":"A 3D object with one base and triangular faces that meet at the top in one point."}},{"term":{"af":"Grondvlak","en":"Base"},"def":{"af":"Die vlak waarop ’n piramide (of ander voorwerp) staan; dit gee die piramide sy naam.","en":"The face that a pyramid (or other object) stands on; it gives the pyramid its name."}},{"term":{"af":"Kubus","en":"Cube"},"def":{"af":"’n Prisma met 6 ewe groot vierkantige vlakke, soos ’n dobbelsteen.","en":"A prism with 6 equal square faces, like a dice."}},{"term":{"af":"Net","en":"Net"},"def":{"af":"’n Plat vorm wat jy kan vou om ’n 3D-voorwerp te maak.","en":"A flat shape that you can fold to make a 3D object."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Tel vlakke, rande en hoekpunte","en":"Count faces, edges and vertices"},"problem":{"af":"Hoeveel vlakke, rande en hoekpunte het ’n driehoekige prisma?","en":"How many faces, edges and vertices does a triangular prism have?"},"steps":[{"af":"Vlakke: 2 driehoekige eindvlakke en 3 reghoeke wat hulle verbind: 2 + 3 = 5 vlakke.","en":"Faces: 2 triangular end faces and 3 rectangles that join them: 2 + 3 = 5 faces."},{"af":"Rande: elke driehoek het 3 rande (3 + 3 = 6), en 3 lang rande verbind die twee driehoeke: 6 + 3 = 9 rande.","en":"Edges: each triangle has 3 edges (3 + 3 = 6), and 3 long edges join the two triangles: 6 + 3 = 9 edges."},{"af":"Hoekpunte: elke driehoek het 3 hoekpunte: 3 + 3 = 6 hoekpunte.","en":"Vertices: each triangle has 3 vertices: 3 + 3 = 6 vertices."}],"answer":{"af":"5 vlakke, 9 rande en 6 hoekpunte","en":"5 faces, 9 edges and 6 vertices"}},{"title":{"af":"Prisma of piramide?","en":"Prism or pyramid?"},"problem":{"af":"’n Voorwerp het ’n vierkantige grondvlak en 4 driehoekige vlakke wat bo in een punt bymekaarkom. Benoem dit en tel sy vlakke, rande en hoekpunte.","en":"An object has a square base and 4 triangular faces that meet at the top in one point. Name it and count its faces, edges and vertices."},"steps":[{"af":"Een grondvlak en driehoeke wat in ’n punt bymekaarkom: dit is ’n piramide. Die grondvlak is ’n vierkant, dus ’n vierkantige piramide.","en":"One base and triangles that meet in a point: it is a pyramid. The base is a square, so a square pyramid."},{"af":"Vlakke: 1 vierkant + 4 driehoeke = 5.","en":"Faces: 1 square + 4 triangles = 5."},{"af":"Rande: 4 om die grondvlak + 4 wat na die punt toe loop = 8.","en":"Edges: 4 around the base + 4 that run up to the point = 8."},{"af":"Hoekpunte: 4 by die grondvlak + 1 bo = 5.","en":"Vertices: 4 at the base + 1 on top = 5."}],"answer":{"af":"’n Vierkantige piramide met 5 vlakke, 8 rande en 5 hoekpunte","en":"A square pyramid with 5 faces, 8 edges and 5 vertices"}},{"title":{"af":"Is dit ’n net van ’n kubus?","en":"Is it a net of a cube?"},"problem":{"af":"Aisha teken twee rangskikkings van 6 vierkante. A: ’n ry van 4 vierkante met een vierkant bo en een onder die tweede vierkant. B: 6 vierkante in een lang ry. Watter een is ’n net van ’n kubus?","en":"Aisha draws two arrangements of 6 squares. A: a row of 4 squares with one square above and one below the second square. B: 6 squares in one long row. Which one is a net of a cube?"},"steps":[{"af":"A: kies die tweede vierkant as die bodem. Die vierkante langsaan vou op as die linker- en regterkant; die een bo en die een onder vou op as die voor- en agterkant; die laaste vierkant in die ry vou oor as die deksel. Al 6 vlakke pas.","en":"A: choose the second square as the bottom. The squares next to it fold up as the left and right sides; the one above and the one below fold up as the front and back; the last square in the row folds over as the lid. All 6 faces fit."},{"af":"B: as jy ’n ry van 6 vou, gaan die eerste 4 rondom soos ’n buis, en die laaste 2 vou oor vlakke wat reeds daar is. Die twee punte van die buis bly oop.","en":"B: if you fold a row of 6, the first 4 go around like a tube, and the last 2 fold over faces that are already there. The two ends of the tube stay open."}],"answer":{"af":"A is ’n net van ’n kubus; B is nie.","en":"A is a net of a cube; B is not."}},{"title":{"af":"Voorwerpe in die alledaagse lewe","en":"Objects in everyday life"},"problem":{"af":"Benoem die 3D-vorm van elke voorwerp: ’n koeldrankblikkie, ’n dobbelsteen, ’n roomyshorinkie, ’n baksteen en ’n sokkerbal. Watter van hulle kan rol?","en":"Name the 3D shape of each object: a cooldrink can, a dice, an ice-cream cone, a brick and a soccer ball. Which of them can roll?"},"steps":[{"af":"Blikkie: twee sirkelvlakke en ’n geboë vlak – ’n silinder. Dobbelsteen: 6 vierkante – ’n kubus.","en":"Can: two circular faces and a curved surface – a cylinder. Dice: 6 squares – a cube."},{"af":"Horinkie: een sirkel en ’n geboë vlak wat in ’n punt eindig – ’n keël. Baksteen: 6 reghoeke – ’n reghoekige prisma. Sokkerbal: net ’n geboë vlak – ’n bol.","en":"Ice-cream cone: one circle and a curved surface ending in a point – a cone. Brick: 6 rectangles – a rectangular prism. Soccer ball: only a curved surface – a sphere."},{"af":"Voorwerpe met ’n geboë vlak kan rol: die silinder, die keël en die bol.","en":"Objects with a curved surface can roll: the cylinder, the cone and the sphere."}],"answer":{"af":"Silinder, kubus, keël, reghoekige prisma, bol. Die blikkie, horinkie en bal kan rol.","en":"Cylinder, cube, cone, rectangular prism, sphere. The can, cone and ball can roll."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel rande het ’n kubus?","en":"How many edges does a cube have?"},"options":[{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"8","en":"8"},{"af":"12","en":"12"},{"af":"4","en":"4"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Kubus het 4 rande bo, 4 onder en 4 wat bo en onder verbind: 12 rande. 6 is die getal vlakke en 8 die getal hoekpunte.","en":"A cube has 4 edges on top, 4 at the bottom and 4 that join top and bottom: 12 edges. 6 is the number of faces and 8 the number of vertices."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voorwerp het net een geboë vlak en geen rande of hoekpunte nie?","en":"Which object has only one curved surface and no edges or vertices?"},"options":[{"af":"Silinder","en":"Cylinder"},{"af":"Keël","en":"Cone"},{"af":"Kubus","en":"Cube"},{"af":"Bol","en":"Sphere"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Bol, soos ’n bal, is heeltemal rond: een geboë vlak, geen rande en geen hoekpunte nie. ’n Silinder en keël het ook plat sirkelvlakke en geboë rande.","en":"A sphere, like a ball, is completely round: one curved surface, no edges and no vertices. A cylinder and cone also have flat circular faces and curved edges."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Driehoekige prisma het ___ vlakke.","en":"A triangular prism has ___ faces."},"answers":{"af":["5","vyf"],"en":["5","five"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3","6","9"],"en":["3","6","9"]}},"explain":{"af":"2 driehoekige eindvlakke + 3 reghoekige vlakke = 5 vlakke. 9 is die getal rande en 6 die getal hoekpunte.","en":"2 triangular end faces + 3 rectangular faces = 5 faces. 9 is the number of edges and 6 the number of vertices."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Silinder kan rol, want dit het ’n geboë vlak.","en":"A cylinder can roll, because it has a curved surface."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. As ’n silinder op sy geboë vlak lê, rol dit. As dit op ’n plat sirkelvlak staan, kan dit gly en gestapel word.","en":"True. When a cylinder lies on its curved surface, it rolls. When it stands on a flat circular face, it can slide and be stacked."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter alledaagse voorwerp het die vorm van ’n reghoekige prisma?","en":"Which everyday object has the shape of a rectangular prism?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Sokkerbal","en":"A soccer ball"},{"af":"’n Graanvlokkiesdoos","en":"A cereal box"},{"af":"’n Roomyshorinkie","en":"An ice-cream cone"},{"af":"’n Koeldrankblikkie","en":"A cooldrink can"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Graanvlokkiesdoos het 6 reghoekige vlakke, 12 rande en 8 hoekpunte – ’n reghoekige prisma. Die bal is ’n bol, die horinkie ’n keël en die blikkie ’n silinder.","en":"A cereal box has 6 rectangular faces, 12 edges and 8 vertices – a rectangular prism. The ball is a sphere, the ice-cream cone a cone and the can a cylinder."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die verskil tussen ’n prisma en ’n piramide?","en":"What is the difference between a prism and a pyramid?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Prisma het twee gelyke, parallelle eindvlakke; ’n piramide se vlakke kom in een punt bymekaar","en":"A prism has two equal, parallel end faces; a pyramid’s faces meet in one point"},{"af":"’n Prisma het geboë vlakke; ’n piramide het net plat vlakke","en":"A prism has curved surfaces; a pyramid has only flat faces"},{"af":"’n Prisma het altyd 6 vlakke; ’n piramide het altyd 4 vlakke","en":"A prism always has 6 faces; a pyramid always has 4 faces"},{"af":"’n Prisma het geen hoekpunte nie; ’n piramide het net een hoekpunt","en":"A prism has no vertices; a pyramid has only one vertex"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Prisma het twee eindvlakke wat ewe groot en parallel is. ’n Piramide het een grondvlak en driehoekige vlakke wat in een punt bymekaarkom. Albei het net plat vlakke, en die getal vlakke hang van die vorm van die eindvlak of grondvlak af.","en":"A prism has two end faces that are equal and parallel. A pyramid has one base and triangular faces that meet in one point. Both have only flat faces, and the number of faces depends on the shape of the end face or base."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke 3D-voorwerp by ’n alledaagse voorbeeld.","en":"Match each 3D object to an everyday example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Bol","en":"Sphere"},"r":{"af":"Sokkerbal","en":"Soccer ball"}},{"l":{"af":"Silinder","en":"Cylinder"},"r":{"af":"Koeldrankblikkie","en":"Cooldrink can"}},{"l":{"af":"Keël","en":"Cone"},"r":{"af":"Verkeerskeël","en":"Traffic cone"}},{"l":{"af":"Kubus","en":"Cube"},"r":{"af":"Dobbelsteen","en":"Dice"}},{"l":{"af":"Vierkantige piramide","en":"Square pyramid"},"r":{"af":"Die piramides in Egipte","en":"The pyramids in Egypt"}}],"explain":{"af":"’n Bal is rond (bol), ’n blikkie het twee sirkels en ’n geboë vlak (silinder), ’n verkeerskeël eindig in ’n punt (keël), ’n dobbelsteen het 6 vierkante (kubus) en die piramides in Egipte het ’n vierkantige grondvlak.","en":"A ball is round (sphere), a can has two circles and a curved surface (cylinder), a traffic cone ends in a point (cone), a dice has 6 squares (cube) and the pyramids in Egypt have a square base."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Vierkantige piramide het ___ hoekpunte.","en":"A square pyramid has ___ vertices."},"answers":{"af":["5","vyf"],"en":["5","five"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4","8","6"],"en":["4","8","6"]}},"explain":{"af":"4 hoekpunte by die vierkantige grondvlak plus 1 bo-op waar die driehoeke bymekaarkom: 4 + 1 = 5. 8 is die getal rande.","en":"4 vertices at the square base plus 1 on top where the triangles meet: 4 + 1 = 5. 8 is the number of edges."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel vierkante het die net van ’n kubus?","en":"How many squares does the net of a cube have?"},"options":[{"af":"4","en":"4"},{"af":"8","en":"8"},{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"12","en":"12"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Kubus het 6 vierkantige vlakke, dus het sy net 6 ewe groot vierkante – een vir elke vlak. 8 is die hoekpunte en 12 die rande.","en":"A cube has 6 square faces, so its net has 6 equal squares – one for each face. 8 is the vertices and 12 the edges."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Enige 6 vierkante wat aan mekaar vas is, kan altyd tot ’n kubus gevou word.","en":"Any 6 squares that are joined together can always be folded into a cube."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 6 vierkante in een lang ry vou byvoorbeeld tot ’n buis met twee oop punte, en sommige vierkante oorvleuel. Net sekere rangskikkings is nette van ’n kubus.","en":"False. 6 squares in one long row, for example, fold into a tube with two open ends, and some squares overlap. Only certain arrangements are nets of a cube."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Voorwerp het 6 reghoekige vlakke (nie almal vierkante nie), 12 rande en 8 hoekpunte. Wat is dit?","en":"An object has 6 rectangular faces (not all squares), 12 edges and 8 vertices. What is it?"},"options":[{"af":"Kubus","en":"Cube"},{"af":"Reghoekige prisma","en":"Rectangular prism"},{"af":"Driehoekige prisma","en":"Triangular prism"},{"af":"Vierkantige piramide","en":"Square pyramid"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Kubus en ’n reghoekige prisma het albei 6 vlakke, 12 rande en 8 hoekpunte, maar ’n kubus se vlakke is almal vierkante. Omdat die vlakke nie almal vierkante is nie, is dit ’n reghoekige prisma.","en":"A cube and a rectangular prism both have 6 faces, 12 edges and 8 vertices, but a cube’s faces are all squares. Because the faces are not all squares, it is a rectangular prism."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Silinder het ___ plat vlakke.","en":"A cylinder has ___ flat faces."},"answers":{"af":["2","twee"],"en":["2","two"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1","0","3"],"en":["1","0","3"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Silinder het ’n plat sirkel bo en een onder (2 plat vlakke) en een geboë vlak om die kant. ’n Keël het net 1 plat vlak.","en":"A cylinder has a flat circle on top and one at the bottom (2 flat faces) and one curved surface around the side. A cone has only 1 flat face."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voorwerp het 5 vlakke, 9 rande en 6 hoekpunte?","en":"Which object has 5 faces, 9 edges and 6 vertices?"},"options":[{"af":"Driehoekige prisma","en":"Triangular prism"},{"af":"Vierkantige piramide","en":"Square pyramid"},{"af":"Kubus","en":"Cube"},{"af":"Keël","en":"Cone"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Driehoekige prisma het 5 vlakke, 9 rande en 6 hoekpunte. ’n Vierkantige piramide het ook 5 vlakke, maar net 8 rande en 5 hoekpunte – daarom moet jy al drie getalle nagaan.","en":"A triangular prism has 5 faces, 9 edges and 6 vertices. A square pyramid also has 5 faces, but only 8 edges and 5 vertices – that is why you must check all three numbers."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van hierdie voorwerpe is nie ’n prisma nie?","en":"Which one of these objects is not a prism?"},"options":[{"af":"Kubus","en":"Cube"},{"af":"Reghoekige prisma","en":"Rectangular prism"},{"af":"Driehoekige prisma","en":"Triangular prism"},{"af":"Vierkantige piramide","en":"Square pyramid"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Piramide het net een grondvlak, en sy driehoekige vlakke kom in ’n punt bymekaar – dit het nie twee parallelle eindvlakke nie. ’n Kubus is ’n spesiale reghoekige prisma.","en":"A pyramid has only one base, and its triangular faces meet in a point – it does not have two parallel end faces. A cube is a special rectangular prism."}}]},{"id":"w5-t2-simmetrie-patrone","title":{"af":"Simmetrie en meetkundige patrone","en":"Symmetry and geometric patterns"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal simmetrielyne in vorms, letters en die natuur kan vind en teken, kan sê hoeveel simmetrielyne ’n vorm het, en meetkundige patrone kan voortsit, in ’n tabel kan wys en die reël kan beskryf.","en":"You will be able to find and draw lines of symmetry in shapes, letters and nature, say how many lines of symmetry a shape has, and extend geometric patterns, show them in a table and describe the rule."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is simmetrie?\n\n’n Vorm is **simmetries** as jy dit langs ’n lyn kan vou sodat die twee helftes **presies op mekaar pas**. Die voulyn heet die **simmetrielyn**. Die een helfte is die **spieëlbeeld** van die ander helfte.\n\nJy kan simmetrie op twee maniere toets:\n\n1. **Vou** die vorm langs die lyn. Pas die helftes presies? Dan is dit ’n simmetrielyn.\n2. Hou ’n **spieël** regop op die lyn. As die helfte plus sy spieëlbeeld presies die hele vorm wys, is dit ’n simmetrielyn.\n\n’n Simmetrielyn kan **vertikaal** (regop), **horisontaal** (plat, soos die horison) of **skuins** (diagonaal) wees.\n\n## Simmetrielyne in vorms\n\n| Vorm | Aantal simmetrielyne |\n|---|---|\n| Vierkant | 4: vertikaal, horisontaal en 2 diagonale |\n| Reghoek | 2: vertikaal en horisontaal |\n| Driehoek met 3 ewe lang sye | 3 |\n| Reëlmatige seshoek | 6 |\n| Sirkel | oneindig baie: elke lyn deur die middelpunt |\n| Parallelogram wat skeef lê | 0 |\n\n’n **Reëlmatige veelhoek** het ewe veel simmetrielyne as sye: ’n reëlmatige vyfhoek het 5 en ’n reëlmatige agthoek 8.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die **diagonale van ’n reghoek is nie simmetrielyne nie**. As jy ’n reghoekige papier van hoek tot hoek vou, pas die twee helftes nie op mekaar nie – probeer dit! Net by ’n vierkant is die diagonale simmetrielyne.\n\n## Simmetrie in letters\n\nIn eenvoudige drukletters (hoofletters):\n\n| Simmetrielyn | Letters |\n|---|---|\n| Net vertikaal | A, M, T, U, V, W, Y |\n| Net horisontaal | B, C, D, E |\n| Vertikaal én horisontaal | H, O |\n| Geen | F, G, J, L, N, P, R, S, Z |\n\nLetters wat met die hand of in ’n sierlike lettertipe geskryf is, is dikwels nie presies simmetries nie.\n\n## Simmetrie in die natuur\n\nBaie dinge in die natuur is **byna** simmetries: ’n skoenlapper se vlerke, baie blare en ’n mens se gesig het ’n vertikale simmetrielyn. In die natuur is die twee helftes nooit presies dieselfde nie, daarom sê ons *byna* simmetries.\n\n## Meetkundige patrone\n\n’n **Meetkundige patroon** bestaan uit vorms wat volgens ’n **reël** groei. Kyk na vierkante wat in ’n ry met vuurhoutjies gebou word:\n\n| Aantal vierkante | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 10 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Aantal vuurhoutjies | 4 | 7 | 10 | 13 | 31 |\n\nDie eerste vierkant het 4 vuurhoutjies nodig. Elke nuwe vierkant **deel een sy** met die vorige een, dus het dit net **3 ekstra** vuurhoutjies nodig. Die reël is: **aantal vierkante × 3 + 1**. Vir 10 vierkante: 10 × 3 + 1 = 31.\n\n> **Onthou:** Toets jou reël altyd op die figure wat jy reeds het. Vir 2 vierkante: 2 × 3 + 1 = 7. Dit klop met die tabel.\n\n## Hoe om ’n patroonvraag te beantwoord\n\n1. Teken of bou die volgende figuur.\n2. Maak ’n **tabel** met die figuurnommer en die aantal dele.\n3. Kyk hoeveel elke keer bykom (die **konstante verskil**).\n4. Skryf die reël in woorde en toets dit.\n5. Gebruik die reël vir ’n figuur ver vorentoe, soos die 20ste.\n\nMoenie die vuurhoutjies van 10 vierkante as 10 × 4 = 40 bereken nie – die vierkante deel sye, dus tel jy dan te veel.","en":"## What is symmetry?\n\nA shape is **symmetrical** if you can fold it along a line so that the two halves **fit exactly on top of each other**. The fold line is called the **line of symmetry**. The one half is the **mirror image** of the other half.\n\nYou can test symmetry in two ways:\n\n1. **Fold** the shape along the line. Do the halves fit exactly? Then it is a line of symmetry.\n2. Hold a **mirror** upright on the line. If the half plus its mirror image shows exactly the whole shape, it is a line of symmetry.\n\nA line of symmetry can be **vertical** (upright), **horizontal** (flat, like the horizon) or **slanting** (diagonal).\n\n## Lines of symmetry in shapes\n\n| Shape | Number of lines of symmetry |\n|---|---|\n| Square | 4: vertical, horizontal and 2 diagonals |\n| Rectangle | 2: vertical and horizontal |\n| Triangle with 3 equal sides | 3 |\n| Regular hexagon | 6 |\n| Circle | infinitely many: every line through the centre |\n| Parallelogram that leans over | 0 |\n\nA **regular polygon** has as many lines of symmetry as sides: a regular pentagon has 5 and a regular octagon 8.\n\n> **Common mistake:** The **diagonals of a rectangle are not lines of symmetry**. If you fold a rectangular piece of paper from corner to corner, the two halves do not fit on top of each other – try it! Only in a square are the diagonals lines of symmetry.\n\n## Symmetry in letters\n\nIn simple printed capital letters:\n\n| Line of symmetry | Letters |\n|---|---|\n| Only vertical | A, M, T, U, V, W, Y |\n| Only horizontal | B, C, D, E |\n| Vertical and horizontal | H, O |\n| None | F, G, J, L, N, P, R, S, Z |\n\nLetters that are handwritten or in a fancy font are often not exactly symmetrical.\n\n## Symmetry in nature\n\nMany things in nature are **almost** symmetrical: a butterfly’s wings, many leaves and a person’s face have a vertical line of symmetry. In nature the two halves are never exactly the same, which is why we say *almost* symmetrical.\n\n## Geometric patterns\n\nA **geometric pattern** is made of shapes that grow according to a **rule**. Look at squares built in a row with matchsticks:\n\n| Number of squares | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 10 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Number of matchsticks | 4 | 7 | 10 | 13 | 31 |\n\nThe first square needs 4 matchsticks. Every new square **shares one side** with the one before, so it needs only **3 extra** matchsticks. The rule is: **number of squares × 3 + 1**. For 10 squares: 10 × 3 + 1 = 31.\n\n> **Remember:** Always test your rule on the figures you already have. For 2 squares: 2 × 3 + 1 = 7. That matches the table.\n\n## How to answer a pattern question\n\n1. Draw or build the next figure.\n2. Make a **table** with the figure number and the number of parts.\n3. See how many are added each time (the **constant difference**).\n4. Write the rule in words and test it.\n5. Use the rule for a figure far ahead, such as the 20th.\n\nDon’t work out the matchsticks for 10 squares as 10 × 4 = 40 – the squares share sides, so then you count too many."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Simmetries","en":"Symmetrical"},"def":{"af":"’n Vorm is simmetries as die twee helftes presies op mekaar pas wanneer jy dit langs ’n lyn vou.","en":"A shape is symmetrical if the two halves fit exactly on top of each other when you fold it along a line."}},{"term":{"af":"Simmetrielyn","en":"Line of symmetry"},"def":{"af":"Die lyn waarlangs jy ’n vorm kan vou sodat die twee helftes presies pas.","en":"The line along which you can fold a shape so that the two halves match exactly."}},{"term":{"af":"Spieëlbeeld","en":"Mirror image"},"def":{"af":"Die omgekeerde beeld van ’n vorm, soos jy dit in ’n spieël sien.","en":"The reversed picture of a shape, as you see it in a mirror."}},{"term":{"af":"Vertikaal","en":"Vertical"},"def":{"af":"Regop, van bo na onder, soos ’n vlagpaal.","en":"Upright, from top to bottom, like a flagpole."}},{"term":{"af":"Horisontaal","en":"Horizontal"},"def":{"af":"Plat, van links na regs, soos die horison.","en":"Flat, from left to right, like the horizon."}},{"term":{"af":"Diagonaal","en":"Diagonal"},"def":{"af":"’n Skuins lyn, byvoorbeeld van een hoek van ’n vierkant na die oorkantste hoek.","en":"A slanting line, for example from one corner of a square to the opposite corner."}},{"term":{"af":"Meetkundige patroon","en":"Geometric pattern"},"def":{"af":"’n Patroon van vorms wat volgens ’n reël groei of herhaal.","en":"A pattern of shapes that grows or repeats according to a rule."}},{"term":{"af":"Reël","en":"Rule"},"def":{"af":"Die instruksie wat sê hoe die patroon van een figuur na die volgende groei.","en":"The instruction that says how the pattern grows from one figure to the next."}},{"term":{"af":"Konstante verskil","en":"Constant difference"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer elke figuur in ’n patroon dieselfde aantal dele meer as die vorige een het.","en":"When every figure in a pattern has the same number of parts more than the one before."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Vierkant en reghoek","en":"Square and rectangle"},"problem":{"af":"Hoeveel simmetrielyne het ’n vierkant en hoeveel het ’n reghoek wat nie ’n vierkant is nie? Verduidelik die verskil.","en":"How many lines of symmetry does a square have and how many does a rectangle that is not a square have? Explain the difference."},"steps":[{"af":"Vou albei vertikaal en horisontaal deur die middel: albei keer pas die helftes presies. Albei vorms het dus hierdie 2 lyne.","en":"Fold both vertically and horizontally through the middle: both times the halves fit exactly. So both shapes have these 2 lines."},{"af":"Vou die vierkant van hoek tot hoek: die helftes pas, want al die sye is ewe lank. Dit gee nog 2 diagonale lyne.","en":"Fold the square from corner to corner: the halves fit, because all the sides are equal. This gives 2 more diagonal lines."},{"af":"Vou die reghoek van hoek tot hoek: die punte steek uit en die helftes pas nie, want die sye is nie ewe lank nie.","en":"Fold the rectangle from corner to corner: the corners stick out and the halves do not fit, because the sides are not equal."}],"answer":{"af":"’n Vierkant het 4 simmetrielyne; ’n reghoek het net 2.","en":"A square has 4 lines of symmetry; a rectangle has only 2."}},{"title":{"af":"Simmetrie in letters","en":"Symmetry in letters"},"problem":{"af":"Kyk na die letters van die woord BOTTEL. Watter letters het ’n simmetrielyn, en is die lyn vertikaal of horisontaal?","en":"Look at the letters of the word BOTTLE. Which letters have a line of symmetry, and is the line vertical or horizontal?"},"steps":[{"af":"B en E: die boonste en onderste helftes pas – ’n horisontale lyn.","en":"B and E: the top and bottom halves match – a horizontal line."},{"af":"T: die linker- en regterkant pas – ’n vertikale lyn. O het albei.","en":"T: the left and right sides match – a vertical line. O has both."},{"af":"L: geen vou laat die helftes pas nie – geen simmetrielyn nie.","en":"L: no fold makes the halves match – no line of symmetry."}],"answer":{"af":"B en E: horisontaal; T: vertikaal; O: vertikaal en horisontaal; L: geen","en":"B and E: horizontal; T: vertical; O: vertical and horizontal; L: none"}},{"title":{"af":"Vuurhoutjiepatroon","en":"Matchstick pattern"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato bou vierkante in ’n ry met vuurhoutjies: 1 vierkant het 4 vuurhoutjies, 2 vierkante 7 en 3 vierkante 10. Hoeveel vuurhoutjies het sy vir 6 vierkante en vir 20 vierkante nodig?","en":"Lerato builds squares in a row with matchsticks: 1 square has 4 matchsticks, 2 squares 7 and 3 squares 10. How many matchsticks does she need for 6 squares and for 20 squares?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die verskil is elke keer 3, want elke nuwe vierkant deel een sy met die vorige een.","en":"The difference is 3 every time, because every new square shares one side with the one before."},{"af":"Reël: aantal vierkante × 3 + 1. Toets: 3 × 3 + 1 = 10. Dit klop.","en":"Rule: number of squares × 3 + 1. Test: 3 × 3 + 1 = 10. It is correct."},{"af":"6 vierkante: 6 × 3 + 1 = 19. 20 vierkante: 20 × 3 + 1 = 61.","en":"6 squares: 6 × 3 + 1 = 19. 20 squares: 20 × 3 + 1 = 61."}],"answer":{"af":"19 vuurhoutjies vir 6 vierkante en 61 vir 20 vierkante.","en":"19 matchsticks for 6 squares and 61 for 20 squares."}},{"title":{"af":"Tafels en stoele","en":"Tables and chairs"},"problem":{"af":"Vierkantige tafels word in ’n ry teen mekaar geskuif. 1 tafel het plek vir 4 stoele, 2 tafels vir 6 en 3 tafels vir 8. Hoeveel stoele pas by 10 tafels? Hoeveel tafels is nodig vir 30 stoele?","en":"Square tables are pushed together in a row. 1 table has room for 4 chairs, 2 tables for 6 and 3 tables for 8. How many chairs fit at 10 tables? How many tables are needed for 30 chairs?"},"steps":[{"af":"Maak ’n tabel: tafels 1; 2; 3 → stoele 4; 6; 8. Elke ekstra tafel gee 2 stoele meer (een aan elke lang kant).","en":"Make a table: tables 1, 2, 3 → chairs 4, 6, 8. Every extra table gives 2 more chairs (one on each long side)."},{"af":"Reël: aantal tafels × 2 + 2 (die 2 ekstra stoele sit aan die twee punte). Toets: 3 × 2 + 2 = 8. Dit klop.","en":"Rule: number of tables × 2 + 2 (the 2 extra chairs are at the two ends). Test: 3 × 2 + 2 = 8. It is correct."},{"af":"10 tafels: 10 × 2 + 2 = 22 stoele.","en":"10 tables: 10 × 2 + 2 = 22 chairs."},{"af":"Werk terug vir 30 stoele: 30 − 2 = 28 en 28 ÷ 2 = 14 tafels.","en":"Work backwards for 30 chairs: 30 − 2 = 28 and 28 ÷ 2 = 14 tables."}],"answer":{"af":"22 stoele by 10 tafels; 14 tafels vir 30 stoele.","en":"22 chairs at 10 tables; 14 tables for 30 chairs."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel simmetrielyne het ’n vierkant?","en":"How many lines of symmetry does a square have?"},"options":[{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"4","en":"4"},{"af":"1","en":"1"},{"af":"8","en":"8"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Vierkant het ’n vertikale lyn, ’n horisontale lyn en 2 diagonale lyne: 4 altesaam. 2 is die antwoord vir ’n reghoek.","en":"A square has a vertical line, a horizontal line and 2 diagonal lines: 4 altogether. 2 is the answer for a rectangle."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel simmetrielyne het ’n reghoek wat nie ’n vierkant is nie?","en":"How many lines of symmetry does a rectangle that is not a square have?"},"options":[{"af":"4","en":"4"},{"af":"0","en":"0"},{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"1","en":"1"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Reghoek het ’n vertikale en ’n horisontale simmetrielyn. Sy diagonale is nie simmetrielyne nie, dus is die antwoord 2, nie 4 nie.","en":"A rectangle has a vertical and a horizontal line of symmetry. Its diagonals are not lines of symmetry, so the answer is 2, not 4."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Sirkel het ___ simmetrielyne.","en":"A circle has ___ lines of symmetry."},"answers":{"af":["oneindig baie","oneindig"],"en":["infinitely many","infinite","an infinite number of"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["presies 2","presies 4","geen"],"en":["exactly 2","exactly 4","no"]}},"explain":{"af":"Elke lyn wat deur die middelpunt van ’n sirkel gaan, verdeel dit in twee helftes wat presies pas. Daar is oneindig baie sulke lyne.","en":"Every line that goes through the centre of a circle divides it into two halves that match exactly. There are infinitely many such lines."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die letter H het ’n vertikale en ’n horisontale simmetrielyn.","en":"The letter H has a vertical and a horizontal line of symmetry."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. As jy H regop deur die middel vou, pas die linker- en regterkant. As jy dit plat deur die middel vou, pas die boonste en onderste helfte.","en":"True. If you fold H upright through the middle, the left and right sides match. If you fold it flat through the middle, the top and bottom halves match."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter letter het geen simmetrielyn nie?","en":"Which letter has no line of symmetry?"},"options":[{"af":"A","en":"A"},{"af":"E","en":"E"},{"af":"T","en":"T"},{"af":"F","en":"F"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"A en T het ’n vertikale simmetrielyn en E het ’n horisontale een. By F pas die helftes nie, hoe jy dit ook al vou nie.","en":"A and T have a vertical line of symmetry and E has a horizontal one. In F the halves do not match, however you fold it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter letter het net ’n horisontale simmetrielyn?","en":"Which letter has only a horizontal line of symmetry?"},"options":[{"af":"C","en":"C"},{"af":"A","en":"A"},{"af":"M","en":"M"},{"af":"L","en":"L"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"As jy C plat deur die middel vou, pas die boonste en onderste helfte. A en M het ’n vertikale lyn, en L het geen simmetrielyn nie.","en":"If you fold C flat through the middle, the top and bottom halves match. A and M have a vertical line, and L has no line of symmetry."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke vorm by die aantal simmetrielyne.","en":"Match each shape to its number of lines of symmetry."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Vierkant","en":"Square"},"r":{"af":"4 simmetrielyne","en":"4 lines of symmetry"}},{"l":{"af":"Reghoek","en":"Rectangle"},"r":{"af":"2 simmetrielyne","en":"2 lines of symmetry"}},{"l":{"af":"Driehoek met 3 ewe lang sye","en":"Triangle with 3 equal sides"},"r":{"af":"3 simmetrielyne","en":"3 lines of symmetry"}},{"l":{"af":"Reëlmatige seshoek","en":"Regular hexagon"},"r":{"af":"6 simmetrielyne","en":"6 lines of symmetry"}},{"l":{"af":"Parallelogram wat skeef lê","en":"Parallelogram that leans over"},"r":{"af":"Geen simmetrielyne nie","en":"No lines of symmetry"}}],"explain":{"af":"’n Reëlmatige veelhoek het ewe veel simmetrielyne as sye (vierkant 4, driehoek 3, seshoek 6). ’n Reghoek het net 2, en ’n skewe parallelogram se helftes pas nooit as jy dit vou nie.","en":"A regular polygon has as many lines of symmetry as sides (square 4, triangle 3, hexagon 6). A rectangle has only 2, and a leaning parallelogram’s halves never match when you fold it."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vuurhoutjievierkante in ’n ry: 1 vierkant het 4 vuurhoutjies, 2 vierkante 7 en 3 vierkante 10. Vir 5 vierkante het jy ___ vuurhoutjies nodig.","en":"Matchstick squares in a row: 1 square has 4 matchsticks, 2 squares 7 and 3 squares 10. For 5 squares you need ___ matchsticks."},"answers":{"af":["16"],"en":["16"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["20","13","15"],"en":["20","13","15"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die reël is aantal vierkante × 3 + 1: 5 × 3 + 1 = 16. 20 kry jy met 5 × 4, maar die vierkante deel sye. 13 is die antwoord vir 4 vierkante.","en":"The rule is number of squares × 3 + 1: 5 × 3 + 1 = 16. You get 20 with 5 × 4, but the squares share sides. 13 is the answer for 4 squares."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Anika vou ’n reghoekige stuk papier (nie ’n vierkant nie) langs die diagonaal, van hoek tot hoek. Wat gebeur?","en":"Anika folds a rectangular piece of paper (not a square) along the diagonal, from corner to corner. What happens?"},"options":[{"af":"Die twee helftes pas presies op mekaar","en":"The two halves fit exactly on top of each other"},{"af":"Die helftes pas nie, dus is die diagonaal nie ’n simmetrielyn nie","en":"The halves do not fit, so the diagonal is not a line of symmetry"},{"af":"Sy kry twee vierkante wat ewe groot is","en":"She gets two squares of the same size"},{"af":"Die reghoek kry nou 4 simmetrielyne","en":"The rectangle now gets 4 lines of symmetry"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"By ’n reghoek is die lang en kort sye nie ewe lank nie, dus steek die punte uit as jy diagonaal vou. Die diagonaal is nie ’n simmetrielyn nie – dit is die algemene fout.","en":"In a rectangle the long and short sides are not equal, so the corners stick out when you fold diagonally. The diagonal is not a line of symmetry – this is the common mistake."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Elke driehoek het 3 simmetrielyne.","en":"Every triangle has 3 lines of symmetry."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Net ’n driehoek met 3 ewe lang sye het 3 simmetrielyne. ’n Driehoek met net 2 ewe lang sye het 1, en ’n driehoek met 3 verskillende sye het geen.","en":"False. Only a triangle with 3 equal sides has 3 lines of symmetry. A triangle with only 2 equal sides has 1, and a triangle with 3 different sides has none."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vuurhoutjiedriehoeke in ’n ry: 1 driehoek het 3 vuurhoutjies, 2 driehoeke 5 en 3 driehoeke 7. Watter reël gee die aantal vuurhoutjies?","en":"Matchstick triangles in a row: 1 triangle has 3 matchsticks, 2 triangles 5 and 3 triangles 7. Which rule gives the number of matchsticks?"},"options":[{"af":"Aantal driehoeke × 3","en":"Number of triangles × 3"},{"af":"Aantal driehoeke + 2","en":"Number of triangles + 2"},{"af":"Aantal driehoeke × 2","en":"Number of triangles × 2"},{"af":"Aantal driehoeke × 2 + 1","en":"Number of triangles × 2 + 1"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Toets elke reël: 1 × 2 + 1 = 3; 2 × 2 + 1 = 5; 3 × 2 + 1 = 7. Dit klop elke keer. *+ 2* werk net vir die eerste figuur, en *× 3* vergeet dat die driehoeke sye deel.","en":"Test each rule: 1 × 2 + 1 = 3, 2 × 2 + 1 = 5, 3 × 2 + 1 = 7. It works every time. *+ 2* only works for the first figure, and *× 3* forgets that the triangles share sides."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Tafels in ’n ry: 1 tafel het plek vir 4 stoele, 2 tafels vir 6 en 3 tafels vir 8. By 10 tafels is daar plek vir ___ stoele.","en":"Tables in a row: 1 table has room for 4 chairs, 2 tables for 6 and 3 tables for 8. At 10 tables there is room for ___ chairs."},"answers":{"af":["22"],"en":["22"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["40","20","24"],"en":["40","20","24"]}},"explain":{"af":"Elke tafel gee 2 stoele, plus 2 aan die punte: 10 × 2 + 2 = 22. 40 kry jy met 10 × 4, maar die tafels staan teen mekaar.","en":"Every table gives 2 chairs, plus 2 at the ends: 10 × 2 + 2 = 22. You get 40 with 10 × 4, but the tables stand against each other."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel simmetrielyne het ’n reëlmatige agthoek, soos die vorm van ’n stopteken sonder die woord daarop?","en":"How many lines of symmetry does a regular octagon have, like the shape of a stop sign without the word on it?"},"options":[{"af":"4","en":"4"},{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"8","en":"8"},{"af":"16","en":"16"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Reëlmatige veelhoek het ewe veel simmetrielyne as sye. ’n Agthoek het 8 sye, dus 8 simmetrielyne. (Die woord STOP self is nie simmetries nie.)","en":"A regular polygon has as many lines of symmetry as sides. An octagon has 8 sides, so 8 lines of symmetry. (The word STOP itself is not symmetrical.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In ’n patroon het figuur 1 een vierkant, figuur 2 drie vierkante en figuur 3 vyf vierkante. Hoeveel vierkante het figuur 10?","en":"In a pattern figure 1 has one square, figure 2 has three squares and figure 3 has five squares. How many squares does figure 10 have?"},"options":[{"af":"19","en":"19"},{"af":"20","en":"20"},{"af":"21","en":"21"},{"af":"30","en":"30"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Elke figuur het 2 vierkante meer. Die reël is figuurnommer × 2 − 1: 1 × 2 − 1 = 1 en 3 × 2 − 1 = 5. Figuur 10: 10 × 2 − 1 = 19.","en":"Every figure has 2 more squares. The rule is figure number × 2 − 1: 1 × 2 − 1 = 1 and 3 × 2 − 1 = 5. Figure 10: 10 × 2 − 1 = 19."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Meting en meetkunde","en":"Measurement and geometry"},"topics":[{"id":"w5-t3-lengte","title":{"af":"Lengte","en":"Length"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal lengtes kan skat en meet in mm, cm, m en km, die regte meetinstrument kan kies, tussen eenhede kan omskakel en woordprobleme oor lengte kan oplos.","en":"You will be able to estimate and measure lengths in mm, cm, m and km, choose the right measuring instrument, convert between units and solve word problems about length."},"summary":{"af":"## Eenhede van lengte\n\n**Lengte** sê hoe lank, breed, hoog of ver iets is. Ons gebruik vier **standaardeenhede**:\n\n| Eenheid | Afkorting | Ons meet daarmee … |\n|---|---|---|\n| millimeter | mm | baie klein dinge: ’n mier, die dikte van ’n boek |\n| sentimeter | cm | kort dinge: ’n potlood, jou hand, ’n blaar |\n| meter | m | langer dinge: ’n klaskamer, ’n tou, ’n swembad |\n| kilometer | km | lang afstande: van jou huis na die dorp |\n\nOm goed te **skat**, help dit om ’n paar verwysings te ken: ’n vingernael is omtrent **1 cm** breed, ’n deur is omtrent **2 m** hoog en jy stap **1 km** in omtrent 15 minute. ’n Millimeter is baie klein – omtrent die dikte van ’n bankkaart.\n\n## Meetinstrumente\n\n- **Liniaal** – vir kort, reguit lyne. Die nommers is sentimeters en die klein streepies tussen hulle is millimeters.\n- **Maatband** – vir langer dinge en dinge wat buig, soos jou middel of ’n boomstam.\n- **Trapwiel** – vir lang afstande, soos ’n sportveld. Die wiel is presies 1 m rondom, so elke klik is 1 m.\n- **Afstandmeter** in ’n motor – wys hoeveel kilometer die motor gery het.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Begin by die **0** op die liniaal, nie by die rand nie. As ’n lyn by 2 cm begin en by 9 cm eindig, is dit 9 − 2 = **7 cm** lank, nie 9 cm nie.\n\n## Omskakel tussen eenhede\n\nOns metrieke stelsel werk met tiene, honderde en duisende:\n\n| Klein eenheid | Groot eenheid |\n|---|---|\n| 10 mm | 1 cm |\n| 100 cm | 1 m |\n| 1 000 m | 1 km |\n\n**Groot eenheid na klein eenheid: vermenigvuldig**, want jy het meer van die klein eenhede nodig.\n\n- 4 m = 4 × 100 cm = **400 cm**\n- 6 cm 3 mm = 60 mm + 3 mm = **63 mm**\n- 3 km 250 m = 3 000 m + 250 m = **3 250 m**\n\n**Klein eenheid na groot eenheid: deel.**\n\n- 90 mm = 90 ÷ 10 = **9 cm**\n- 735 cm = 700 cm + 35 cm = **7 m 35 cm**\n- 5 400 m = 5 000 m + 400 m = **5 km 400 m**\n\nBreuke help ook: ½ m = 50 cm, ¼ m = 25 cm, ¾ m = 75 cm, ½ km = 500 m en ¼ km = 250 m. Soms sien jy 1,5 m – dit is 1½ m, dus 150 cm.\n\n> **Onthou:** Kyk of jou antwoord sin maak. Daar is altyd **meer** sentimeters as meters, want ’n sentimeter is kleiner.\n\n## Vergelyk en orden\n\nSkakel eers alles na **dieselfde eenheid** om. Orden byvoorbeeld 1 m 20 cm; 112 cm; 1½ m; 1 m 2 cm:\n\n1. In sentimeter: 120 cm; 112 cm; 150 cm; 102 cm.\n2. Van kortste na langste: **1 m 2 cm; 112 cm; 1 m 20 cm; 1½ m**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** 1 m 2 cm is **102 cm** (100 + 2), nie 12 cm of 120 cm nie.\n\n## Woordprobleme\n\nLees die vraag twee keer en kyk mooi na die **eenhede**. Thabo het 3 m lint. Hy sny 8 stukke van 25 cm elk af. Hoeveel lint bly oor?\n\n- Maak die eenhede dieselfde: 3 m = 300 cm.\n- 8 × 25 cm = 200 cm\n- 300 cm − 200 cm = **100 cm = 1 m**\n\n## ’n Bietjie geskiedenis\n\nLank gelede het mense met hul **liggame** gemeet: die **span** (hand oopgesprei van duim tot pinkie), die **voet**, die **el** (van elmboog tot vingerpunt) en die **tree**. Maar almal se hande en voete is nie ewe groot nie, so twee mense kon dieselfde tafel meet en verskillende antwoorde kry. Daarom gebruik ons vandag **standaardeenhede** soos die meter, wat oral dieselfde is.","en":"## Units of length\n\n**Length** tells how long, wide, high or far something is. We use four **standard units**:\n\n| Unit | Abbreviation | We use it to measure … |\n|---|---|---|\n| millimetre | mm | very small things: an ant, the thickness of a book |\n| centimetre | cm | short things: a pencil, your hand, a leaf |\n| metre | m | longer things: a classroom, a rope, a swimming pool |\n| kilometre | km | long distances: from your home to town |\n\nTo **estimate** well, it helps to know a few benchmarks: a fingernail is about **1 cm** wide, a door is about **2 m** high and you walk **1 km** in about 15 minutes. A millimetre is very small – about the thickness of a bank card.\n\n## Measuring instruments\n\n- **Ruler** – for short, straight lines. The numbers are centimetres and the small marks between them are millimetres.\n- **Measuring tape** – for longer things and things that bend, like your waist or a tree trunk.\n- **Trundle wheel** – for long distances, like a sports field. The wheel is exactly 1 m around, so every click is 1 m.\n- **Odometer** in a car – shows how many kilometres the car has travelled.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Start at the **0** on the ruler, not at the edge. If a line starts at 2 cm and ends at 9 cm, it is 9 − 2 = **7 cm** long, not 9 cm.\n\n## Converting between units\n\nOur metric system works with tens, hundreds and thousands:\n\n| Small unit | Big unit |\n|---|---|\n| 10 mm | 1 cm |\n| 100 cm | 1 m |\n| 1 000 m | 1 km |\n\n**Big unit to small unit: multiply**, because you need more of the small units.\n\n- 4 m = 4 × 100 cm = **400 cm**\n- 6 cm 3 mm = 60 mm + 3 mm = **63 mm**\n- 3 km 250 m = 3 000 m + 250 m = **3 250 m**\n\n**Small unit to big unit: divide.**\n\n- 90 mm = 90 ÷ 10 = **9 cm**\n- 735 cm = 700 cm + 35 cm = **7 m 35 cm**\n- 5 400 m = 5 000 m + 400 m = **5 km 400 m**\n\nFractions help too: ½ m = 50 cm, ¼ m = 25 cm, ¾ m = 75 cm, ½ km = 500 m and ¼ km = 250 m. Sometimes you see 1.5 m – this is 1½ m, so 150 cm.\n\n> **Remember:** Check that your answer makes sense. There are always **more** centimetres than metres, because a centimetre is smaller.\n\n## Comparing and ordering\n\nFirst convert everything to the **same unit**. For example, order 1 m 20 cm, 112 cm, 1½ m, 1 m 2 cm:\n\n1. In centimetres: 120 cm, 112 cm, 150 cm, 102 cm.\n2. From shortest to longest: **1 m 2 cm, 112 cm, 1 m 20 cm, 1½ m**.\n\n> **Common mistake:** 1 m 2 cm is **102 cm** (100 + 2), not 12 cm or 120 cm.\n\n## Word problems\n\nRead the question twice and look carefully at the **units**. Thabo has 3 m of ribbon. He cuts off 8 pieces of 25 cm each. How much ribbon is left?\n\n- Make the units the same: 3 m = 300 cm.\n- 8 × 25 cm = 200 cm\n- 300 cm − 200 cm = **100 cm = 1 m**\n\n## A little history\n\nLong ago people measured with their **bodies**: the **hand span** (hand spread out from thumb to little finger), the **foot**, the **cubit** (from elbow to fingertip) and the **pace**. But not everyone’s hands and feet are the same size, so two people could measure the same table and get different answers. That is why today we use **standard units** like the metre, which are the same everywhere."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Lengte","en":"Length"},"def":{"af":"Hoe lank, breed, hoog of ver iets is.","en":"How long, wide, high or far something is."}},{"term":{"af":"Millimeter (mm)","en":"Millimetre (mm)"},"def":{"af":"Die kleinste eenheid op jou liniaal; 10 mm = 1 cm.","en":"The smallest unit on your ruler; 10 mm = 1 cm."}},{"term":{"af":"Sentimeter (cm)","en":"Centimetre (cm)"},"def":{"af":"’n Eenheid vir kort lengtes, omtrent so breed soos ’n vingernael; 100 cm = 1 m.","en":"A unit for short lengths, about as wide as a fingernail; 100 cm = 1 m."}},{"term":{"af":"Meter (m)","en":"Metre (m)"},"def":{"af":"’n Eenheid vir langer lengtes, omtrent ’n groot tree van ’n grootmens.","en":"A unit for longer lengths, about one big step of an adult."}},{"term":{"af":"Kilometer (km)","en":"Kilometre (km)"},"def":{"af":"’n Eenheid vir lang afstande; 1 km = 1 000 m.","en":"A unit for long distances; 1 km = 1 000 m."}},{"term":{"af":"Liniaal","en":"Ruler"},"def":{"af":"’n Reguit meetinstrument vir kort lengtes in sentimeter en millimeter.","en":"A straight measuring instrument for short lengths in centimetres and millimetres."}},{"term":{"af":"Maatband","en":"Measuring tape"},"def":{"af":"’n Lang, buigsame meetinstrument vir langer dinge of dinge wat rond is.","en":"A long, bendable measuring instrument for longer things or things that are round."}},{"term":{"af":"Trapwiel","en":"Trundle wheel"},"def":{"af":"’n Wiel van presies 1 m rondom wat by elke meter klik; ons meet lang afstande daarmee.","en":"A wheel exactly 1 m around that clicks at every metre; we use it to measure long distances."}},{"term":{"af":"Skat","en":"Estimate"},"def":{"af":"’n Slim raaiskoot maak oor ’n maat voordat jy dit presies meet.","en":"To make a clever guess about a measurement before you measure it exactly."}},{"term":{"af":"Standaardeenheid","en":"Standard unit"},"def":{"af":"’n Meeteenheid wat oral dieselfde is, soos die meter – anders as ’n span of ’n voet.","en":"A unit of measurement that is the same everywhere, like the metre – unlike a hand span or a foot."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Skakel lengtes om","en":"Convert lengths"},"problem":{"af":"Skakel om: (a) 4 m 35 cm na cm (b) 2 750 m na km en m (c) 68 mm na cm en mm","en":"Convert: (a) 4 m 35 cm to cm (b) 2 750 m to km and m (c) 68 mm to cm and mm"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Groot na klein: vermenigvuldig. 4 m = 4 × 100 cm = 400 cm. Tel die 35 cm by: 400 + 35 = 435 cm.","en":"(a) Big to small: multiply. 4 m = 4 × 100 cm = 400 cm. Add the 35 cm: 400 + 35 = 435 cm."},{"af":"(b) Klein na groot: deel. Breek op: 2 750 m = 2 000 m + 750 m. 2 000 m = 2 km, so dit is 2 km 750 m.","en":"(b) Small to big: divide. Break it up: 2 750 m = 2 000 m + 750 m. 2 000 m = 2 km, so it is 2 km 750 m."},{"af":"(c) 10 mm = 1 cm. 68 mm = 60 mm + 8 mm, en 60 mm = 6 cm, so dit is 6 cm 8 mm.","en":"(c) 10 mm = 1 cm. 68 mm = 60 mm + 8 mm, and 60 mm = 6 cm, so it is 6 cm 8 mm."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 435 cm (b) 2 km 750 m (c) 6 cm 8 mm","en":"(a) 435 cm (b) 2 km 750 m (c) 6 cm 8 mm"}},{"title":{"af":"Wie het die verste gespring?","en":"Who jumped the furthest?"},"problem":{"af":"By die atletiekbyeenkoms spring Anika 2 m 5 cm, Sipho 230 cm, Lerato 2½ m en Pieter 2 m 45 cm. Orden die spronge van die langste na die kortste.","en":"At the athletics meeting Anika jumps 2 m 5 cm, Sipho 230 cm, Lerato 2½ m and Pieter 2 m 45 cm. Order the jumps from longest to shortest."},"steps":[{"af":"Skakel alles na sentimeter om: Anika 2 m 5 cm = 200 + 5 = 205 cm.","en":"Convert everything to centimetres: Anika 2 m 5 cm = 200 + 5 = 205 cm."},{"af":"Sipho is reeds 230 cm. Lerato: 2½ m = 200 cm + 50 cm = 250 cm. Pieter: 2 m 45 cm = 245 cm.","en":"Sipho is already 230 cm. Lerato: 2½ m = 200 cm + 50 cm = 250 cm. Pieter: 2 m 45 cm = 245 cm."},{"af":"Vergelyk: 250 > 245 > 230 > 205.","en":"Compare: 250 > 245 > 230 > 205."}],"answer":{"af":"Lerato (2½ m); Pieter (2 m 45 cm); Sipho (230 cm); Anika (2 m 5 cm). Lerato het die verste gespring.","en":"Lerato (2½ m), Pieter (2 m 45 cm), Sipho (230 cm), Anika (2 m 5 cm). Lerato jumped the furthest."}},{"title":{"af":"Hoeveel tou bly oor?","en":"How much rope is left?"},"problem":{"af":"Aisha het ’n tou van 5 m. Sy sny 6 stukke van 75 cm elk af. Hoeveel tou bly oor?","en":"Aisha has a rope of 5 m. She cuts off 6 pieces of 75 cm each. How much rope is left?"},"steps":[{"af":"Maak die eenhede dieselfde: 5 m = 500 cm.","en":"Make the units the same: 5 m = 500 cm."},{"af":"Bereken hoeveel sy afgesny het: 6 × 75 cm = 450 cm.","en":"Work out how much she cut off: 6 × 75 cm = 450 cm."},{"af":"Trek af: 500 cm − 450 cm = 50 cm.","en":"Subtract: 500 cm − 450 cm = 50 cm."},{"af":"Kontroleer: 450 cm + 50 cm = 500 cm = 5 m. ✓","en":"Check: 450 cm + 50 cm = 500 cm = 5 m. ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"Daar bly 50 cm (½ m) tou oor.","en":"There is 50 cm (½ m) of rope left."}},{"title":{"af":"Afstand oor ’n week","en":"Distance over a week"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho hardloop elke middag 4 rondtes om ’n baan van 400 m. Hoeveel kilometer hardloop hy in 5 middae?","en":"Sipho runs 4 laps of a 400 m track every afternoon. How many kilometres does he run in 5 afternoons?"},"steps":[{"af":"Een middag: 4 × 400 m = 1 600 m.","en":"One afternoon: 4 × 400 m = 1 600 m."},{"af":"Vyf middae: 5 × 1 600 m = 8 000 m.","en":"Five afternoons: 5 × 1 600 m = 8 000 m."},{"af":"Skakel om na kilometer: 1 000 m = 1 km, so 8 000 m ÷ 1 000 = 8 km.","en":"Convert to kilometres: 1 000 m = 1 km, so 8 000 m ÷ 1 000 = 8 km."}],"answer":{"af":"Sipho hardloop 8 km in 5 middae.","en":"Sipho runs 8 km in 5 afternoons."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter eenheid is die beste om die afstand van Durban na Pietermaritzburg te meet?","en":"Which unit is best for measuring the distance from Durban to Pietermaritzburg?"},"options":[{"af":"kilometer (km)","en":"kilometre (km)"},{"af":"meter (m)","en":"metre (m)"},{"af":"sentimeter (cm)","en":"centimetre (cm)"},{"af":"millimeter (mm)","en":"millimetre (mm)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Lang afstande tussen dorpe en stede meet ons in kilometer. In meter of sentimeter sou die getal onnodig groot wees.","en":"We measure long distances between towns and cities in kilometres. In metres or centimetres the number would be unnecessarily big."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"7 m = ___ cm","en":"7 m = ___ cm"},"answers":{"af":["700"],"en":["700"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["70","7 000","0,7"],"en":["70","7 000","0.7"]}},"explain":{"af":"1 m = 100 cm. Van groot na klein vermenigvuldig ons: 7 × 100 = 700 cm.","en":"1 m = 100 cm. From big to small we multiply: 7 × 100 = 700 cm."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel meter is 3 km 40 m?","en":"How many metres is 3 km 40 m?"},"options":[{"af":"3 400 m","en":"3 400 m"},{"af":"340 m","en":"340 m"},{"af":"3 040 m","en":"3 040 m"},{"af":"30 040 m","en":"30 040 m"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"3 km = 3 000 m. Tel die 40 m by: 3 000 + 40 = 3 040 m. Die 40 m staan in die tiene-plek, nie die honderde-plek nie – daarom is 3 400 m verkeerd.","en":"3 km = 3 000 m. Add the 40 m: 3 000 + 40 = 3 040 m. The 40 m is in the tens place, not the hundreds place – that is why 3 400 m is wrong."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Om meter na sentimeter om te skakel, deel jy deur 100.","en":"To convert metres to centimetres, you divide by 100."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Meter is die groter eenheid, so jy kry méér sentimeters: jy vermenigvuldig met 100. Byvoorbeeld 3 m = 300 cm.","en":"False. A metre is the bigger unit, so you get more centimetres: you multiply by 100. For example 3 m = 300 cm."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Lyn op ’n liniaal begin by 2 cm en eindig by 9 cm 5 mm. Hoe lank is die lyn?","en":"A line on a ruler starts at 2 cm and ends at 9 cm 5 mm. How long is the line?"},"options":[{"af":"95 mm","en":"95 mm"},{"af":"75 mm","en":"75 mm"},{"af":"115 mm","en":"115 mm"},{"af":"7 mm","en":"7 mm"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die lyn begin nie by 0 nie, so trek af: 9 cm 5 mm − 2 cm = 7 cm 5 mm = 75 mm. 95 mm is die antwoord as jy vergeet dat die lyn by 2 cm begin.","en":"The line does not start at 0, so subtract: 9 cm 5 mm − 2 cm = 7 cm 5 mm = 75 mm. 95 mm is the answer if you forget that the line starts at 2 cm."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter instrument is die beste om die lengte van ’n rugbyveld te meet?","en":"Which instrument is best for measuring the length of a rugby field?"},"options":[{"af":"’n 30 cm-liniaal","en":"a 30 cm ruler"},{"af":"’n kombuisskaal","en":"a kitchen scale"},{"af":"’n maatbeker","en":"a measuring jug"},{"af":"’n trapwiel","en":"a trundle wheel"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Trapwiel klik by elke meter en is ideaal vir lang afstande. Met ’n 30 cm-liniaal sal dit baie lank vat, en ’n skaal en ’n maatbeker meet glad nie lengte nie.","en":"A trundle wheel clicks at every metre and is ideal for long distances. With a 30 cm ruler it would take very long, and a scale and a measuring jug do not measure length at all."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"85 mm = 8 cm ___ mm","en":"85 mm = 8 cm ___ mm"},"answers":{"af":["5"],"en":["5"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["50","85","8"],"en":["50","85","8"]}},"explain":{"af":"80 mm = 8 cm, en daar bly 5 mm oor. Dus 85 mm = 8 cm 5 mm.","en":"80 mm = 8 cm, and 5 mm is left over. So 85 mm = 8 cm 5 mm."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke lengte by die gelyke lengte.","en":"Match each length to the equal length."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"10 mm","en":"10 mm"},"r":{"af":"1 cm","en":"1 cm"}},{"l":{"af":"100 cm","en":"100 cm"},"r":{"af":"1 m","en":"1 m"}},{"l":{"af":"1 000 m","en":"1 000 m"},"r":{"af":"1 km","en":"1 km"}},{"l":{"af":"50 cm","en":"50 cm"},"r":{"af":"½ m","en":"½ m"}},{"l":{"af":"250 m","en":"250 m"},"r":{"af":"¼ km","en":"¼ km"}}],"explain":{"af":"10 mm = 1 cm, 100 cm = 1 m en 1 000 m = 1 km. Die helfte van 100 cm is 50 cm, en ’n kwart van 1 000 m is 250 m.","en":"10 mm = 1 cm, 100 cm = 1 m and 1 000 m = 1 km. Half of 100 cm is 50 cm, and a quarter of 1 000 m is 250 m."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die beste skatting vir die hoogte van ’n klaskamerdeur?","en":"What is the best estimate for the height of a classroom door?"},"options":[{"af":"20 cm","en":"20 cm"},{"af":"20 m","en":"20 m"},{"af":"2 m","en":"2 m"},{"af":"2 km","en":"2 km"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Deur is ’n bietjie hoër as ’n grootmens, so omtrent 2 m. 20 cm is korter as ’n liniaal en 20 m is so hoog soos ’n gebou van ’n paar verdiepings.","en":"A door is a little taller than an adult, so about 2 m. 20 cm is shorter than a ruler and 20 m is as tall as a building with several floors."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Span is nie ’n goeie standaardeenheid nie, want almal se hande is nie ewe groot nie.","en":"A hand span is not a good standard unit, because not everyone’s hands are the same size."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Twee mense wat dieselfde tafel in spanne meet, kan verskillende antwoorde kry. Daarom gebruik ons standaardeenhede soos die sentimeter en meter.","en":"True. Two people who measure the same table in hand spans can get different answers. That is why we use standard units like the centimetre and the metre."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Johan sny ’n lint van 2 m in stukke van 25 cm elk. Hoeveel stukke kry hy?","en":"Johan cuts a 2 m ribbon into pieces of 25 cm each. How many pieces does he get?"},"options":[{"af":"8","en":"8"},{"af":"4","en":"4"},{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"80","en":"80"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Maak eers die eenhede dieselfde: 2 m = 200 cm. Dan 200 ÷ 25 = 8 stukke. Kontroleer: 8 × 25 = 200.","en":"First make the units the same: 2 m = 200 cm. Then 200 ÷ 25 = 8 pieces. Check: 8 × 25 = 200."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Nomsa stap elke dag 800 m skool toe en 800 m terug huis toe. In 5 skooldae stap sy ___ km.","en":"Every day Nomsa walks 800 m to school and 800 m back home. In 5 school days she walks ___ km."},"answers":{"af":["8"],"en":["8"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4","80","8 000"],"en":["4","80","8 000"]}},"explain":{"af":"Een dag: 800 + 800 = 1 600 m. Vyf dae: 5 × 1 600 = 8 000 m = 8 km. As jy die pad terug vergeet, kry jy 4 km; 8 000 is die antwoord in meter, nie kilometer nie.","en":"One day: 800 + 800 = 1 600 m. Five days: 5 × 1 600 = 8 000 m = 8 km. If you forget the walk back, you get 4 km; 8 000 is the answer in metres, not kilometres."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel sentimeter is 1 m 5 cm?","en":"How many centimetres is 1 m 5 cm?"},"options":[{"af":"150 cm","en":"150 cm"},{"af":"15 cm","en":"15 cm"},{"af":"1 005 cm","en":"1 005 cm"},{"af":"105 cm","en":"105 cm"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"1 m = 100 cm, plus 5 cm is 105 cm. 150 cm sou 1 m 50 cm wees – ’n algemene fout.","en":"1 m = 100 cm, plus 5 cm is 105 cm. 150 cm would be 1 m 50 cm – a common mistake."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter lys is van die kortste na die langste georden?","en":"Which list is ordered from shortest to longest?"},"options":[{"af":"1 km; 950 m; 1 200 m; 1½ km","en":"1 km, 950 m, 1 200 m, 1½ km"},{"af":"950 m; 1 km; 1 200 m; 1½ km","en":"950 m, 1 km, 1 200 m, 1½ km"},{"af":"1½ km; 1 200 m; 1 km; 950 m","en":"1½ km, 1 200 m, 1 km, 950 m"},{"af":"950 m; 1 200 m; 1 km; 1½ km","en":"950 m, 1 200 m, 1 km, 1½ km"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Skakel na meter om: 1 km = 1 000 m en 1½ km = 1 500 m. Van kortste na langste: 950; 1 000; 1 200; 1 500. Die derde lys is van langste na kortste.","en":"Convert to metres: 1 km = 1 000 m and 1½ km = 1 500 m. From shortest to longest: 950, 1 000, 1 200, 1 500. The third list goes from longest to shortest."}}]},{"id":"w5-t3-massa","title":{"af":"Massa","en":"Mass"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal massa in gram en kilogram kan skat, skale kan lees, tussen g en kg kan omskakel, massas kan vergelyk en woordprobleme met verpakkings kan oplos.","en":"You will be able to estimate mass in grams and kilograms, read scales, convert between g and kg, compare masses and solve word problems with packaging."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is massa?\n\n**Massa** sê hoe swaar iets is. Ons meet massa in **gram (g)** en **kilogram (kg)**:\n\n**1 000 g = 1 kg**\n\nLigte dinge meet ons in gram en swaar dinge in kilogram. Hierdie verwysings help jou om te **skat**:\n\n- ’n Skuifspeld het ’n massa van omtrent **1 g**.\n- ’n Appel is omtrent **150 g**.\n- 1 liter water het ’n massa van omtrent **1 kg**.\n- ’n Graad 5-leerder is omtrent **30 tot 40 kg**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Groot beteken nie altyd swaar nie! ’n Groot kussing is ligter as ’n klein baksteen. Massa hang af van waarvan iets gemaak is, nie net van hoe groot dit is nie.\n\n## Skale en hoe om hulle te lees\n\n| Skaal | Waarvoor gebruik ons dit? |\n|---|---|\n| Badkamerskaal | om mense te weeg (in kg) |\n| Kombuisskaal | om bestanddele vir kos te weeg (in g en kg) |\n| Weegskaal (balansskaal) | om twee massas te vergelyk: die swaarder kant sak af |\n| Digitale skaal | wys die massa as ’n getal op ’n skerm |\n\nOp ’n skaal met ’n **wyser** is nie elke streepie 1 g nie. So lees jy dit:\n\n1. Kies twee getalle wat langs mekaar staan, bv. 0 en 1 kg.\n2. Tel die **spasies** tussen hulle (nie die streepies nie), bv. 10.\n3. Deel: 1 000 g ÷ 10 = **100 g** per spasie.\n4. Begin by die laaste getal voor die wyser en tel aan. Wys die wyser 3 streepies ná 2 kg, is die massa 2 kg 300 g.\n\n> **Onthou:** Vind eers uit hoeveel **elke klein spasie** werd is. Dit kan 10 g; 50 g; 100 g of iets anders wees.\n\n## Omskakel tussen g en kg\n\n**kg na g: vermenigvuldig met 1 000.**\n\n- 3 kg = 3 × 1 000 = **3 000 g**\n- 2 kg 450 g = 2 000 g + 450 g = **2 450 g**\n- 2,5 kg = 2½ kg = 2 000 g + 500 g = **2 500 g**\n\n**g na kg: deel deur 1 000, of breek die getal op.**\n\n- 6 000 g = 6 000 ÷ 1 000 = **6 kg**\n- 4 075 g = 4 000 g + 75 g = **4 kg 75 g**\n\nBreuke: ½ kg = 500 g, ¼ kg = 250 g en ¾ kg = 750 g.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** 2 kg 50 g is **2 050 g**, nie 2 500 g nie. Die 50 g is vyf tiene, nie vyf honderde nie.\n\n## Vergelyk en orden\n\nSkakel eers alles na **gram** om en vergelyk dan die getalle. Watter is die swaarste: 1 kg 200 g; 1 020 g of 1½ kg?\n\n- 1 kg 200 g = 1 200 g\n- 1 020 g bly 1 020 g\n- 1½ kg = 1 500 g\n\nVan ligste na swaarste: **1 020 g; 1 kg 200 g; 1½ kg**. Die swaarste is 1½ kg.\n\nJy kan ook twee voorwerpe op ’n **weegskaal** vergelyk sonder om getalle te gebruik: die swaarder kant sak af. As die twee kante **gelyk** hang, het die voorwerpe dieselfde massa.\n\n## Woordprobleme met verpakkings\n\nOp ’n pak staan die **massa van die inhoud** (die **netto massa**), soos 500 g of 2,5 kg. Ons gebruik dit om te bereken hoeveel ons het of nodig het:\n\n- Ma koop 3 pakke maalvleis van 750 g elk: 3 × 750 g = 2 250 g = **2 kg 250 g**.\n- ’n Sak meel van 2,5 kg is 2 500 g. ’n Resep vir koekies gebruik 250 g meel. Jy kan 2 500 ÷ 250 = **10 keer** bak.\n- 500 g rys kos R18 en 1 kg rys kos R32. Twee pakke van 500 g kos 2 × R18 = R36. Dus is die pak van 1 kg **goedkoper** vir dieselfde hoeveelheid rys.\n\nSkat altyd eers. 3 pakke van 750 g is ’n bietjie meer as 2 kg – so ’n antwoord van 22 kg kan nie reg wees nie.","en":"## What is mass?\n\n**Mass** tells how heavy something is. We measure mass in **grams (g)** and **kilograms (kg)**:\n\n**1 000 g = 1 kg**\n\nWe measure light things in grams and heavy things in kilograms. These benchmarks help you to **estimate**:\n\n- A paper clip has a mass of about **1 g**.\n- An apple is about **150 g**.\n- 1 litre of water has a mass of about **1 kg**.\n- A Grade 5 learner is about **30 to 40 kg**.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Big does not always mean heavy! A big pillow is lighter than a small brick. Mass depends on what something is made of, not only on how big it is.\n\n## Scales and how to read them\n\n| Scale | What do we use it for? |\n|---|---|\n| Bathroom scale | to weigh people (in kg) |\n| Kitchen scale | to weigh ingredients for food (in g and kg) |\n| Balance scale | to compare two masses: the heavier side goes down |\n| Digital scale | shows the mass as a number on a screen |\n\nOn a scale with a **pointer**, not every mark is 1 g. This is how you read it:\n\n1. Choose two numbers next to each other, e.g. 0 and 1 kg.\n2. Count the **spaces** between them (not the marks), e.g. 10.\n3. Divide: 1 000 g ÷ 10 = **100 g** per space.\n4. Start at the last number before the pointer and count on. If the pointer is 3 marks after 2 kg, the mass is 2 kg 300 g.\n\n> **Remember:** First work out what **each small space** is worth. It can be 10 g, 50 g, 100 g or something else.\n\n## Converting between g and kg\n\n**kg to g: multiply by 1 000.**\n\n- 3 kg = 3 × 1 000 = **3 000 g**\n- 2 kg 450 g = 2 000 g + 450 g = **2 450 g**\n- 2.5 kg = 2½ kg = 2 000 g + 500 g = **2 500 g**\n\n**g to kg: divide by 1 000, or break the number up.**\n\n- 6 000 g = 6 000 ÷ 1 000 = **6 kg**\n- 4 075 g = 4 000 g + 75 g = **4 kg 75 g**\n\nFractions: ½ kg = 500 g, ¼ kg = 250 g and ¾ kg = 750 g.\n\n> **Common mistake:** 2 kg 50 g is **2 050 g**, not 2 500 g. The 50 g is five tens, not five hundreds.\n\n## Comparing and ordering\n\nFirst convert everything to **grams** and then compare the numbers. Which is the heaviest: 1 kg 200 g, 1 020 g or 1½ kg?\n\n- 1 kg 200 g = 1 200 g\n- 1 020 g stays 1 020 g\n- 1½ kg = 1 500 g\n\nFrom lightest to heaviest: **1 020 g, 1 kg 200 g, 1½ kg**. The heaviest is 1½ kg.\n\nYou can also compare two objects on a **balance scale** without using numbers: the heavier side goes down. If the two sides hang **level**, the objects have the same mass.\n\n## Word problems with packaging\n\nA packet shows the **mass of the contents** (the **net mass**), like 500 g or 2.5 kg. We use it to work out how much we have or need:\n\n- Mom buys 3 packets of mince of 750 g each: 3 × 750 g = 2 250 g = **2 kg 250 g**.\n- A bag of flour of 2.5 kg is 2 500 g. A biscuit recipe uses 250 g of flour. You can bake 2 500 ÷ 250 = **10 times**.\n- 500 g of rice costs R18 and 1 kg of rice costs R32. Two packets of 500 g cost 2 × R18 = R36. So the 1 kg packet is **cheaper** for the same amount of rice.\n\nAlways estimate first. 3 packets of 750 g is a little more than 2 kg – so an answer of 22 kg cannot be right."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Massa","en":"Mass"},"def":{"af":"Hoe swaar iets is; ons meet dit in gram en kilogram.","en":"How heavy something is; we measure it in grams and kilograms."}},{"term":{"af":"Gram (g)","en":"Gram (g)"},"def":{"af":"’n Klein eenheid van massa, omtrent die massa van ’n skuifspeld.","en":"A small unit of mass, about the mass of a paper clip."}},{"term":{"af":"Kilogram (kg)","en":"Kilogram (kg)"},"def":{"af":"’n Groter eenheid van massa; 1 kg = 1 000 g.","en":"A bigger unit of mass; 1 kg = 1 000 g."}},{"term":{"af":"Weegskaal (balansskaal)","en":"Balance scale"},"def":{"af":"’n Skaal met twee kante waarmee jy massas vergelyk: die swaarder kant sak af.","en":"A scale with two sides for comparing masses: the heavier side goes down."}},{"term":{"af":"Badkamerskaal","en":"Bathroom scale"},"def":{"af":"’n Skaal waarop mense staan om hul massa in kilogram te meet.","en":"A scale that people stand on to measure their mass in kilograms."}},{"term":{"af":"Kombuisskaal","en":"Kitchen scale"},"def":{"af":"’n Skaal om bestanddele vir kos in gram en kilogram te weeg.","en":"A scale for weighing ingredients for food in grams and kilograms."}},{"term":{"af":"Wyser","en":"Pointer"},"def":{"af":"Die naald op ’n skaal wat na die massa wys.","en":"The needle on a scale that points to the mass."}},{"term":{"af":"Netto massa","en":"Net mass"},"def":{"af":"Die massa van die inhoud van ’n pak, sonder die verpakking.","en":"The mass of what is inside a packet, without the packaging."}},{"term":{"af":"Skat","en":"Estimate"},"def":{"af":"’n Slim raaiskoot maak oor die massa voordat jy weeg of bereken.","en":"To make a clever guess about the mass before you weigh or calculate."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n kombuisskaal","en":"Read a kitchen scale"},"problem":{"af":"Op Fatima se kombuisskaal is daar 10 gelyke spasies tussen 0 en 1 kg, en ook 10 tussen 1 kg en 2 kg. Die wyser wys 3 streepies ná 1 kg. Wat is die massa?","en":"On Fatima’s kitchen scale there are 10 equal spaces between 0 and 1 kg, and also 10 between 1 kg and 2 kg. The pointer is 3 marks after 1 kg. What is the mass?"},"steps":[{"af":"Vind wat een spasie werd is: 1 kg = 1 000 g en 1 000 g ÷ 10 = 100 g.","en":"Find what one space is worth: 1 kg = 1 000 g and 1 000 g ÷ 10 = 100 g."},{"af":"Die wyser is 3 spasies ná 1 kg: 3 × 100 g = 300 g.","en":"The pointer is 3 spaces after 1 kg: 3 × 100 g = 300 g."},{"af":"Tel bymekaar: 1 kg + 300 g = 1 kg 300 g = 1 300 g.","en":"Add: 1 kg + 300 g = 1 kg 300 g = 1 300 g."}],"answer":{"af":"1 kg 300 g (1 300 g)","en":"1 kg 300 g (1 300 g)"}},{"title":{"af":"Orden pakkies","en":"Order parcels"},"problem":{"af":"Ravi pos vier pakkies: 2 kg 40 g; 2 400 g; 2¼ kg en 2 004 g. Orden hulle van die ligste na die swaarste.","en":"Ravi posts four parcels: 2 kg 40 g, 2 400 g, 2¼ kg and 2 004 g. Order them from lightest to heaviest."},"steps":[{"af":"Skakel alles na gram om: 2 kg 40 g = 2 000 + 40 = 2 040 g.","en":"Convert everything to grams: 2 kg 40 g = 2 000 + 40 = 2 040 g."},{"af":"2¼ kg = 2 000 g + 250 g = 2 250 g. Die ander twee is reeds in gram: 2 400 g en 2 004 g.","en":"2¼ kg = 2 000 g + 250 g = 2 250 g. The other two are already in grams: 2 400 g and 2 004 g."},{"af":"Vergelyk: 2 004 < 2 040 < 2 250 < 2 400.","en":"Compare: 2 004 < 2 040 < 2 250 < 2 400."}],"answer":{"af":"2 004 g; 2 kg 40 g; 2¼ kg; 2 400 g","en":"2 004 g, 2 kg 40 g, 2¼ kg, 2 400 g"}},{"title":{"af":"Bak met ’n sak meel","en":"Baking with a bag of flour"},"problem":{"af":"Mev. Dlamini het ’n sak meel van 2,5 kg. Een bak beskuitjies gebruik 250 g meel. (a) Hoeveel bakke kan sy met die hele sak bak? (b) Sy bak 6 bakke. Hoeveel meel bly oor?","en":"Mrs Dlamini has a 2.5 kg bag of flour. One batch of biscuits uses 250 g of flour. (a) How many batches can she bake with the whole bag? (b) She bakes 6 batches. How much flour is left?"},"steps":[{"af":"Maak die eenhede dieselfde: 2,5 kg = 2 500 g.","en":"Make the units the same: 2.5 kg = 2 500 g."},{"af":"(a) 2 500 g ÷ 250 g = 10 bakke. Kontroleer: 10 × 250 = 2 500. ✓","en":"(a) 2 500 g ÷ 250 g = 10 batches. Check: 10 × 250 = 2 500. ✓"},{"af":"(b) 6 bakke gebruik 6 × 250 g = 1 500 g.","en":"(b) 6 batches use 6 × 250 g = 1 500 g."},{"af":"Trek af: 2 500 g − 1 500 g = 1 000 g = 1 kg.","en":"Subtract: 2 500 g − 1 500 g = 1 000 g = 1 kg."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 10 bakke (b) 1 kg meel bly oor.","en":"(a) 10 batches (b) 1 kg of flour is left."}},{"title":{"af":"Watter pak is die beter koop?","en":"Which bag is the better buy?"},"problem":{"af":"’n Sak mieliemeel van 2,5 kg kos R30. ’n Sak van 5 kg kos R55. Watter is die beter koop?","en":"A 2.5 kg bag of maize meal costs R30. A 5 kg bag costs R55. Which is the better buy?"},"steps":[{"af":"Kyk hoe die massas verband hou: 2 × 2,5 kg = 5 kg. Twee klein sakke gee dieselfde hoeveelheid as een groot sak.","en":"See how the masses are related: 2 × 2.5 kg = 5 kg. Two small bags give the same amount as one big bag."},{"af":"Twee klein sakke kos 2 × R30 = R60.","en":"Two small bags cost 2 × R30 = R60."},{"af":"Vergelyk: R55 is minder as R60, en jy kry dieselfde 5 kg.","en":"Compare: R55 is less than R60, and you get the same 5 kg."}],"answer":{"af":"Die sak van 5 kg is die beter koop – jy spaar R5.","en":"The 5 kg bag is the better buy – you save R5."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een sal jy in gram weeg, nie in kilogram nie?","en":"Which one would you weigh in grams, not in kilograms?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Sak aartappels","en":"A bag of potatoes"},{"af":"’n Potlood","en":"A pencil"},{"af":"’n Hond","en":"A dog"},{"af":"’n Fiets","en":"A bicycle"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Potlood is baie lig – net ’n paar gram. Aartappels, ’n hond en ’n fiets is swaar en word in kilogram geweeg.","en":"A pencil is very light – only a few grams. Potatoes, a dog and a bicycle are heavy and are weighed in kilograms."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel gram is 4 kg?","en":"How many grams is 4 kg?"},"options":[{"af":"40 g","en":"40 g"},{"af":"400 g","en":"400 g"},{"af":"40 000 g","en":"40 000 g"},{"af":"4 000 g","en":"4 000 g"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"1 kg = 1 000 g, so 4 kg = 4 × 1 000 = 4 000 g. Moenie met 10 of 100 vermenigvuldig nie – dit is die reël vir lengte.","en":"1 kg = 1 000 g, so 4 kg = 4 × 1 000 = 4 000 g. Do not multiply by 10 or 100 – those are rules for length."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"3 kg 75 g = ___ g","en":"3 kg 75 g = ___ g"},"answers":{"af":["3 075","3075"],"en":["3 075","3075"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3 750","375","3 007"],"en":["3 750","375","3 007"]}},"explain":{"af":"3 kg = 3 000 g. Tel 75 g by: 3 000 + 75 = 3 075 g. 3 750 is verkeerd, want 75 g is nie 750 g nie.","en":"3 kg = 3 000 g. Add 75 g: 3 000 + 75 = 3 075 g. 3 750 is wrong, because 75 g is not 750 g."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Groot voorwerp is altyd swaarder as ’n klein voorwerp.","en":"A big object is always heavier than a small object."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Massa hang af van waarvan iets gemaak is. ’n Groot kussing vol vere is ligter as ’n klein baksteen.","en":"False. Mass depends on what something is made of. A big pillow full of feathers is lighter than a small brick."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op ’n kombuisskaal is daar 4 gelyke spasies tussen 0 g en 200 g. Hoeveel is elke spasie werd?","en":"On a kitchen scale there are 4 equal spaces between 0 g and 200 g. How much is each space worth?"},"options":[{"af":"50 g","en":"50 g"},{"af":"40 g","en":"40 g"},{"af":"25 g","en":"25 g"},{"af":"4 g","en":"4 g"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Deel die verskil deur die aantal spasies: 200 g ÷ 4 = 50 g. 40 g kry jy as jy die 5 streepies tel in plaas van die 4 spasies.","en":"Divide the difference by the number of spaces: 200 g ÷ 4 = 50 g. You get 40 g if you count the 5 marks instead of the 4 spaces."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke voorwerp by sy mees waarskynlike massa.","en":"Match each object to its most likely mass."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"’n Skuifspeld","en":"A paper clip"},"r":{"af":"1 g","en":"1 g"}},{"l":{"af":"’n Appel","en":"An apple"},"r":{"af":"150 g","en":"150 g"}},{"l":{"af":"’n Brood","en":"A loaf of bread"},"r":{"af":"700 g","en":"700 g"}},{"l":{"af":"’n Pak suiker","en":"A packet of sugar"},"r":{"af":"2,5 kg","en":"2.5 kg"}},{"l":{"af":"’n Graad 5-leerder","en":"A Grade 5 learner"},"r":{"af":"35 kg","en":"35 kg"}}],"explain":{"af":"Gebruik verwysings: ’n skuifspeld is omtrent 1 g, ’n appel omtrent 150 g en ’n brood 700 g. ’n Pak suiker is ’n paar kilogram, en ’n kind is baie swaarder as al die ander.","en":"Use benchmarks: a paper clip is about 1 g, an apple about 150 g and a loaf of bread 700 g. A packet of sugar is a few kilograms, and a child is much heavier than all the others."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op ’n weegskaal (balansskaal) sak die kant met ’n boek af en die kant met ’n appel gaan op. Wat beteken dit?","en":"On a balance scale the side with a book goes down and the side with an apple goes up. What does this mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Die appel is swaarder as die boek","en":"The apple is heavier than the book"},{"af":"Die boek en die appel is ewe swaar","en":"The book and the apple are equally heavy"},{"af":"Die boek is swaarder as die appel","en":"The book is heavier than the apple"},{"af":"Die boek is groter as die appel","en":"The book is bigger than the apple"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Op ’n weegskaal sak die swaarder kant af, so die boek is swaarder. ’n Weegskaal vergelyk massa, nie grootte nie.","en":"On a balance scale the heavier side goes down, so the book is heavier. A balance scale compares mass, not size."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"¾ kg = ___ g","en":"¾ kg = ___ g"},"answers":{"af":["750"],"en":["750"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["75","250","7 500"],"en":["75","250","7 500"]}},"explain":{"af":"¼ kg = 1 000 g ÷ 4 = 250 g, so ¾ kg = 3 × 250 g = 750 g. 250 g is net ’n kwart kilogram.","en":"¼ kg = 1 000 g ÷ 4 = 250 g, so ¾ kg = 3 × 250 g = 750 g. 250 g is only a quarter kilogram."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ma koop 3 pakke maalvleis van 750 g elk. Wat is die totale massa?","en":"Mom buys 3 packets of mince of 750 g each. What is the total mass?"},"options":[{"af":"2 kg 50 g","en":"2 kg 50 g"},{"af":"2 kg 500 g","en":"2 kg 500 g"},{"af":"3 kg 750 g","en":"3 kg 750 g"},{"af":"2 kg 250 g","en":"2 kg 250 g"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"3 × 750 g = 2 250 g. 2 250 g = 2 000 g + 250 g = 2 kg 250 g.","en":"3 × 750 g = 2 250 g. 2 250 g = 2 000 g + 250 g = 2 kg 250 g."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"1 liter water het ’n massa van omtrent 1 kg.","en":"1 litre of water has a mass of about 1 kg."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Dit is ’n handige verwysing: ’n bottel van 1 liter vol water weeg omtrent 1 kg (plus die bottel).","en":"True. This is a handy benchmark: a 1 litre bottle full of water weighs about 1 kg (plus the bottle)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter pakkie is die swaarste?","en":"Which parcel is the heaviest?"},"options":[{"af":"2 kg 90 g","en":"2 kg 90 g"},{"af":"2¼ kg","en":"2¼ kg"},{"af":"2 009 g","en":"2 009 g"},{"af":"2 200 g","en":"2 200 g"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Skakel na gram om: 2 kg 90 g = 2 090 g, 2¼ kg = 2 250 g, 2 009 g en 2 200 g. Die grootste getal is 2 250 g, dus is 2¼ kg die swaarste.","en":"Convert to grams: 2 kg 90 g = 2 090 g, 2¼ kg = 2 250 g, 2 009 g and 2 200 g. The biggest number is 2 250 g, so 2¼ kg is the heaviest."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Lerato het ’n sak meel van 2 kg. Elke koek gebruik 250 g meel. Sy kan ___ koeke bak.","en":"Lerato has a 2 kg bag of flour. Each cake uses 250 g of flour. She can bake ___ cakes."},"answers":{"af":["8"],"en":["8"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4","10","80"],"en":["4","10","80"]}},"explain":{"af":"2 kg = 2 000 g. 2 000 ÷ 250 = 8 koeke. Kontroleer: 8 × 250 = 2 000. ✓","en":"2 kg = 2 000 g. 2 000 ÷ 250 = 8 cakes. Check: 8 × 250 = 2 000. ✓"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Pak kaas van 500 g kos R45. ’n Pak van 1 kg kos R84. Watter is die beter koop?","en":"A 500 g pack of cheese costs R45. A 1 kg pack costs R84. Which is the better buy?"},"options":[{"af":"Die pak van 1 kg, want 2 × R45 = R90 is meer as R84","en":"The 1 kg pack, because 2 × R45 = R90 is more than R84"},{"af":"Die pak van 500 g, want R45 is minder as R84","en":"The 500 g pack, because R45 is less than R84"},{"af":"Albei is ewe goed, want kaas is kaas","en":"Both are equally good, because cheese is cheese"},{"af":"Die pak van 500 g, want dit is kleiner en ligter","en":"The 500 g pack, because it is smaller and lighter"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Vergelyk dieselfde hoeveelheid: 1 kg = 2 × 500 g. Twee klein pakke kos R90, maar die groot pak kos net R84. Die klein pak is goedkoper, maar jy kry ook minder kaas.","en":"Compare the same amount: 1 kg = 2 × 500 g. Two small packs cost R90, but the big pack costs only R84. The small pack is cheaper, but you also get less cheese."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Doos hou 6 blikkies boontjies van 410 g elk. Wat is die beste skatting van die totale massa van die blikkies?","en":"A box holds 6 tins of beans of 410 g each. What is the best estimate of the total mass of the tins?"},"options":[{"af":"250 g","en":"250 g"},{"af":"25 kg","en":"25 kg"},{"af":"2½ kg","en":"2½ kg"},{"af":"6 kg","en":"6 kg"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Rond af: 410 g is omtrent 400 g. 6 × 400 g = 2 400 g, en dit is omtrent 2½ kg. (Presies: 6 × 410 = 2 460 g.)","en":"Round off: 410 g is about 400 g. 6 × 400 g = 2 400 g, which is about 2½ kg. (Exactly: 6 × 410 = 2 460 g.)"}}]},{"id":"w5-t3-kapasiteit-temperatuur","title":{"af":"Kapasiteit, volume en temperatuur","en":"Capacity, volume and temperature"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kapasiteit en volume in ml en l kan skat, meet, omskakel en vergelyk, ’n maatbeker en termometer kan lees en temperatuurverskille kan bereken.","en":"You will be able to estimate, measure, convert and compare capacity and volume in ml and l, read a measuring jug and a thermometer, and calculate temperature differences."},"summary":{"af":"## Kapasiteit en volume\n\n**Kapasiteit** is hoeveel ’n houer kan hou as dit **vol** is. **Volume** (of **inhoud**) is hoeveel daar **werklik** in die houer is.\n\n’n Bottel van 2 l het ’n kapasiteit van 2 l. As dit half vol koeldrank is, is die volume koeldrank 1 l – maar die kapasiteit bly 2 l!\n\nOns meet kapasiteit en volume in **milliliter (ml)** en **liter (l)**. Soms word liter as **ℓ** geskryf.\n\n**1 000 ml = 1 l**\n\nHierdie verwysings help jou om te skat:\n\n- ’n Teelepel hou **5 ml** en ’n eetlepel **15 ml** (3 teelepels).\n- ’n Maatkoppie hou **250 ml**, so 4 koppies is 1 l.\n- ’n Groot bottel melk hou **2 l**.\n- ’n Emmer hou omtrent **10 l**.\n\n## Maatbekers en maatlepels\n\n’n **Maatbeker** het merke aan die kant. So lees jy dit:\n\n1. Sit die beker op ’n **plat** oppervlak.\n2. Buk sodat jou oë **gelyk** is met die oppervlak van die vloeistof.\n3. Vind uit hoeveel elke klein spasie werd is. Is daar 5 spasies tussen 0 en 500 ml, is elke spasie 500 ÷ 5 = **100 ml**.\n\nIn resepte gebruik ons **maatlepels** (teelepel 5 ml, eetlepel 15 ml) en **maatkoppies** (250 ml). Vul die lepel tot bo en vee dit gelyk af.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** ’n Hoë, smal glas lyk asof dit meer hou, maar ’n lae, wye bak kan meer hou. Moenie net na die hoogte kyk nie – meet!\n\n## Omskakel en vergelyk\n\n**l na ml: vermenigvuldig met 1 000. ml na l: deel deur 1 000.**\n\n- 3 l = 3 × 1 000 = **3 000 ml**\n- 2 l 400 ml = 2 000 ml + 400 ml = **2 400 ml**\n- 4 750 ml = 4 000 ml + 750 ml = **4 l 750 ml**\n- ½ l = 500 ml, ¼ l = 250 ml, ¾ l = 750 ml en 1½ l = 1 500 ml\n\nOm te vergelyk, skakel alles na **ml** om. Watter is meer: 1 l 50 ml of 1 500 ml? 1 l 50 ml = 1 050 ml, so **1 500 ml is meer**.\n\nSipho maak 2 l koeldrank en skink glase van 250 ml. Hoeveel glase? 2 000 ÷ 250 = **8 glase**.\n\n> **Onthou:** Kyk altyd na die eenheid. 2 l is baie meer as 200 ml – dit is 2 000 ml.\n\n## Temperatuur\n\n**Temperatuur** sê hoe warm of koud iets is. Ons meet dit in **grade Celsius (°C)** met ’n **termometer**. As dit warmer word, styg die vloeistof in die buisie; as dit koeler word, sak dit.\n\n| Wat? | Temperatuur |\n|---|---|\n| Water vries (word ys) | 0 °C |\n| Koel lentedag | omtrent 15 °C |\n| Warm somersdag | 30 °C of meer |\n| Gesonde mens se liggaam | omtrent 37 °C |\n| Water kook | 100 °C |\n\nAs jou liggaamstemperatuur hoër as omtrent 38 °C is, het jy **koors**. Lees ’n termometer soos ’n skaal: is daar 5 spasies tussen 20 °C en 30 °C, is elke spasie **2 °C**.\n\n## Temperatuurverskil\n\nOm te bereken hoeveel warmer of koeler dit geword het, **trek** jy die laer temperatuur van die hoër temperatuur **af**:\n\n**verskil = hoër temperatuur − laer temperatuur**\n\nOp ’n wintersdag is dit 7 °C om 07:00 en 24 °C om 14:00. Die verskil is 24 − 7 = **17 °C**. Dit het 17 °C warmer geword.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die verskil is nie die twee temperature bymekaar getel nie. 24 °C en 7 °C verskil met 17 °C, nie met 31 °C nie.","en":"## Capacity and volume\n\n**Capacity** is how much a container can hold when it is **full**. **Volume** (or **contents**) is how much is **really** in the container.\n\nA 2 l bottle has a capacity of 2 l. If it is half full of cooldrink, the volume of cooldrink is 1 l – but the capacity stays 2 l!\n\nWe measure capacity and volume in **millilitres (ml)** and **litres (l)**. Sometimes litre is written as **ℓ**.\n\n**1 000 ml = 1 l**\n\nThese benchmarks help you to estimate:\n\n- A teaspoon holds **5 ml** and a tablespoon **15 ml** (3 teaspoons).\n- A measuring cup holds **250 ml**, so 4 cups make 1 l.\n- A big bottle of milk holds **2 l**.\n- A bucket holds about **10 l**.\n\n## Measuring jugs and measuring spoons\n\nA **measuring jug** has marks on the side. This is how you read it:\n\n1. Put the jug on a **flat** surface.\n2. Bend down so that your eyes are **level** with the surface of the liquid.\n3. Work out what each small space is worth. If there are 5 spaces between 0 and 500 ml, each space is 500 ÷ 5 = **100 ml**.\n\nIn recipes we use **measuring spoons** (teaspoon 5 ml, tablespoon 15 ml) and **measuring cups** (250 ml). Fill the spoon to the top and level it off.\n\n> **Common mistake:** A tall, thin glass looks as if it holds more, but a low, wide bowl can hold more. Do not only look at the height – measure!\n\n## Converting and comparing\n\n**l to ml: multiply by 1 000. ml to l: divide by 1 000.**\n\n- 3 l = 3 × 1 000 = **3 000 ml**\n- 2 l 400 ml = 2 000 ml + 400 ml = **2 400 ml**\n- 4 750 ml = 4 000 ml + 750 ml = **4 l 750 ml**\n- ½ l = 500 ml, ¼ l = 250 ml, ¾ l = 750 ml and 1½ l = 1 500 ml\n\nTo compare, convert everything to **ml**. Which is more: 1 l 50 ml or 1 500 ml? 1 l 50 ml = 1 050 ml, so **1 500 ml is more**.\n\nSipho makes 2 l of cooldrink and pours glasses of 250 ml. How many glasses? 2 000 ÷ 250 = **8 glasses**.\n\n> **Remember:** Always look at the unit. 2 l is much more than 200 ml – it is 2 000 ml.\n\n## Temperature\n\n**Temperature** tells how hot or cold something is. We measure it in **degrees Celsius (°C)** with a **thermometer**. When it gets warmer, the liquid in the tube rises; when it gets cooler, it goes down.\n\n| What? | Temperature |\n|---|---|\n| Water freezes (becomes ice) | 0 °C |\n| Cool spring day | about 15 °C |\n| Hot summer day | 30 °C or more |\n| Healthy person’s body | about 37 °C |\n| Water boils | 100 °C |\n\nIf your body temperature is higher than about 38 °C, you have a **fever**. Read a thermometer like a scale: if there are 5 spaces between 20 °C and 30 °C, each space is **2 °C**.\n\n## Temperature difference\n\nTo work out how much warmer or cooler it has become, you **subtract** the lower temperature from the higher temperature:\n\n**difference = higher temperature − lower temperature**\n\nOn a winter’s day it is 7 °C at 07:00 and 24 °C at 14:00. The difference is 24 − 7 = **17 °C**. It became 17 °C warmer.\n\n> **Common mistake:** The difference is not the two temperatures added together. 24 °C and 7 °C differ by 17 °C, not by 31 °C."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Kapasiteit","en":"Capacity"},"def":{"af":"Hoeveel ’n houer kan hou as dit heeltemal vol is.","en":"How much a container can hold when it is completely full."}},{"term":{"af":"Volume (inhoud)","en":"Volume (contents)"},"def":{"af":"Hoeveel vloeistof of ruimte daar werklik in ’n houer is.","en":"How much liquid or space there really is in a container."}},{"term":{"af":"Milliliter (ml)","en":"Millilitre (ml)"},"def":{"af":"’n Klein eenheid vir kapasiteit en volume; ’n teelepel hou 5 ml.","en":"A small unit for capacity and volume; a teaspoon holds 5 ml."}},{"term":{"af":"Liter (l)","en":"Litre (l)"},"def":{"af":"’n Groter eenheid vir kapasiteit en volume; 1 l = 1 000 ml.","en":"A bigger unit for capacity and volume; 1 l = 1 000 ml."}},{"term":{"af":"Maatbeker","en":"Measuring jug"},"def":{"af":"’n Houer met merke aan die kant om vloeistof af te meet.","en":"A container with marks on the side for measuring liquid."}},{"term":{"af":"Maatlepel","en":"Measuring spoon"},"def":{"af":"’n Lepel wat ’n vaste hoeveelheid meet, soos ’n teelepel (5 ml) of eetlepel (15 ml).","en":"A spoon that measures a fixed amount, like a teaspoon (5 ml) or a tablespoon (15 ml)."}},{"term":{"af":"Temperatuur","en":"Temperature"},"def":{"af":"Hoe warm of koud iets is.","en":"How hot or cold something is."}},{"term":{"af":"Termometer","en":"Thermometer"},"def":{"af":"’n Instrument wat temperatuur meet; die vloeistof in die buisie styg as dit warmer word.","en":"An instrument that measures temperature; the liquid in the tube rises when it gets warmer."}},{"term":{"af":"Graad Celsius (°C)","en":"Degree Celsius (°C)"},"def":{"af":"Die eenheid vir temperatuur; water vries by 0 °C en kook by 100 °C.","en":"The unit for temperature; water freezes at 0 °C and boils at 100 °C."}},{"term":{"af":"Temperatuurverskil","en":"Temperature difference"},"def":{"af":"Hoeveel twee temperature verskil: die hoër temperatuur min die laer temperatuur.","en":"How much two temperatures differ: the higher temperature minus the lower temperature."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n maatbeker","en":"Read a measuring jug"},"problem":{"af":"’n Maatbeker het merke by 0 ml; 500 ml en 1 l, met 5 gelyke spasies tussen elke twee merke met getalle. Die water kom 2 streepies bo die 500 ml-merk. Hoeveel water is in die beker?","en":"A measuring jug has marks at 0 ml, 500 ml and 1 l, with 5 equal spaces between each two numbered marks. The water reaches 2 marks above the 500 ml mark. How much water is in the jug?"},"steps":[{"af":"Vind wat een spasie werd is: 500 ml ÷ 5 = 100 ml.","en":"Find what one space is worth: 500 ml ÷ 5 = 100 ml."},{"af":"Die water is 2 spasies bo 500 ml: 2 × 100 ml = 200 ml.","en":"The water is 2 spaces above 500 ml: 2 × 100 ml = 200 ml."},{"af":"Tel bymekaar: 500 ml + 200 ml = 700 ml.","en":"Add: 500 ml + 200 ml = 700 ml."}],"answer":{"af":"700 ml water","en":"700 ml of water"}},{"title":{"af":"Is daar genoeg koeldrank?","en":"Is there enough cooldrink?"},"problem":{"af":"Zanele koop 3 bottels koeldrank van 2 l elk vir ’n partytjie. Elkeen van die 25 kinders kry een glas van 250 ml. Is daar genoeg koeldrank?","en":"Zanele buys 3 bottles of cooldrink of 2 l each for a party. Each of the 25 children gets one glass of 250 ml. Is there enough cooldrink?"},"steps":[{"af":"Hoeveel koeldrank is daar? 3 × 2 l = 6 l = 6 000 ml.","en":"How much cooldrink is there? 3 × 2 l = 6 l = 6 000 ml."},{"af":"Hoeveel is nodig? 25 × 250 ml = 6 250 ml.","en":"How much is needed? 25 × 250 ml = 6 250 ml."},{"af":"Vergelyk: 6 000 ml is minder as 6 250 ml. Kort: 6 250 − 6 000 = 250 ml.","en":"Compare: 6 000 ml is less than 6 250 ml. Short: 6 250 − 6 000 = 250 ml."}],"answer":{"af":"Nee, daar is 250 ml (een glas) te min.","en":"No, there is 250 ml (one glass) too little."}},{"title":{"af":"Eetlepels en teelepels","en":"Tablespoons and teaspoons"},"problem":{"af":"’n Resep vir pannekoek vra 3 eetlepels olie, maar Liam kan net ’n teelepel kry. Hoeveel teelepels olie moet hy gebruik?","en":"A pancake recipe asks for 3 tablespoons of oil, but Liam can only find a teaspoon. How many teaspoons of oil must he use?"},"steps":[{"af":"1 eetlepel = 15 ml, so 3 eetlepels = 3 × 15 ml = 45 ml.","en":"1 tablespoon = 15 ml, so 3 tablespoons = 3 × 15 ml = 45 ml."},{"af":"1 teelepel = 5 ml. Hoeveel keer gaan 5 ml in 45 ml? 45 ÷ 5 = 9.","en":"1 teaspoon = 5 ml. How many times does 5 ml go into 45 ml? 45 ÷ 5 = 9."},{"af":"Kontroleer: 1 eetlepel = 3 teelepels, so 3 eetlepels = 3 × 3 = 9 teelepels. ✓","en":"Check: 1 tablespoon = 3 teaspoons, so 3 tablespoons = 3 × 3 = 9 teaspoons. ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"9 teelepels (45 ml)","en":"9 teaspoons (45 ml)"}},{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n termometer en bereken die verskil","en":"Read a thermometer and work out the difference"},"problem":{"af":"Om 07:00 is die temperatuur 9 °C. Om 14:00 is die vloeistof in die termometer 3 streepies bo 20 °C. Daar is 5 gelyke spasies tussen 20 °C en 30 °C. (a) Wat is die temperatuur om 14:00? (b) Hoeveel warmer het dit geword?","en":"At 07:00 the temperature is 9 °C. At 14:00 the liquid in the thermometer is 3 marks above 20 °C. There are 5 equal spaces between 20 °C and 30 °C. (a) What is the temperature at 14:00? (b) How much warmer did it become?"},"steps":[{"af":"Een spasie: (30 − 20) ÷ 5 = 10 ÷ 5 = 2 °C.","en":"One space: (30 − 20) ÷ 5 = 10 ÷ 5 = 2 °C."},{"af":"(a) 3 spasies bo 20 °C: 20 + 3 × 2 = 20 + 6 = 26 °C.","en":"(a) 3 spaces above 20 °C: 20 + 3 × 2 = 20 + 6 = 26 °C."},{"af":"(b) Verskil = hoër − laer = 26 − 9 = 17 °C.","en":"(b) Difference = higher − lower = 26 − 9 = 17 °C."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 26 °C (b) 17 °C warmer","en":"(a) 26 °C (b) 17 °C warmer"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die kapasiteit van ’n teelepel?","en":"What is the capacity of a teaspoon?"},"options":[{"af":"15 ml","en":"15 ml"},{"af":"1 l","en":"1 l"},{"af":"5 ml","en":"5 ml"},{"af":"250 ml","en":"250 ml"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Teelepel hou 5 ml. ’n Eetlepel hou 15 ml en ’n maatkoppie 250 ml.","en":"A teaspoon holds 5 ml. A tablespoon holds 15 ml and a measuring cup 250 ml."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"3 l 250 ml = ___ ml","en":"3 l 250 ml = ___ ml"},"answers":{"af":["3 250","3250"],"en":["3 250","3250"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3 025","325","32 500"],"en":["3 025","325","32 500"]}},"explain":{"af":"3 l = 3 000 ml. Tel 250 ml by: 3 000 + 250 = 3 250 ml.","en":"3 l = 3 000 ml. Add 250 ml: 3 000 + 250 = 3 250 ml."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Bottel met ’n kapasiteit van 2 l is half vol water. Wat is die volume water in die bottel?","en":"A bottle with a capacity of 2 l is half full of water. What is the volume of water in the bottle?"},"options":[{"af":"1 l","en":"1 l"},{"af":"2 l","en":"2 l"},{"af":"500 ml","en":"500 ml"},{"af":"4 l","en":"4 l"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die kapasiteit (2 l) is hoeveel die bottel kan hou. Die volume is hoeveel daar werklik in is: die helfte van 2 l is 1 l.","en":"The capacity (2 l) is how much the bottle can hold. The volume is how much is really in it: half of 2 l is 1 l."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Maatbeker het 5 gelyke spasies tussen 0 ml en 500 ml. Die water kom tot by die 4de streepie bo 0. Hoeveel water is in die beker?","en":"A measuring jug has 5 equal spaces between 0 ml and 500 ml. The water reaches the 4th mark above 0. How much water is in the jug?"},"options":[{"af":"4 ml","en":"4 ml"},{"af":"40 ml","en":"40 ml"},{"af":"500 ml","en":"500 ml"},{"af":"400 ml","en":"400 ml"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Elke spasie is 500 ÷ 5 = 100 ml. Vier spasies is 4 × 100 = 400 ml. Elke streepie is nie 1 ml nie!","en":"Each space is 500 ÷ 5 = 100 ml. Four spaces are 4 × 100 = 400 ml. Each mark is not 1 ml!"}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Water vries by 0 °C en kook by 100 °C.","en":"Water freezes at 0 °C and boils at 100 °C."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Dit is twee belangrike temperature om te onthou: 0 °C (ys) en 100 °C (kookwater).","en":"True. These are two important temperatures to remember: 0 °C (ice) and 100 °C (boiling water)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter hoeveelheid is die meeste?","en":"Which amount is the most?"},"options":[{"af":"1 l 5 ml","en":"1 l 5 ml"},{"af":"1¼ l","en":"1¼ l"},{"af":"1 050 ml","en":"1 050 ml"},{"af":"1 l 200 ml","en":"1 l 200 ml"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Skakel na ml om: 1 l 5 ml = 1 005 ml, 1¼ l = 1 250 ml, 1 050 ml en 1 l 200 ml = 1 200 ml. Die meeste is 1 250 ml, dus 1¼ l.","en":"Convert to ml: 1 l 5 ml = 1 005 ml, 1¼ l = 1 250 ml, 1 050 ml and 1 l 200 ml = 1 200 ml. The most is 1 250 ml, so 1¼ l."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke houer by sy kapasiteit.","en":"Match each container to its capacity."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Teelepel","en":"Teaspoon"},"r":{"af":"5 ml","en":"5 ml"}},{"l":{"af":"Eetlepel","en":"Tablespoon"},"r":{"af":"15 ml","en":"15 ml"}},{"l":{"af":"Maatkoppie","en":"Measuring cup"},"r":{"af":"250 ml","en":"250 ml"}},{"l":{"af":"Groot bottel melk","en":"Big bottle of milk"},"r":{"af":"2 l","en":"2 l"}},{"l":{"af":"Emmer","en":"Bucket"},"r":{"af":"10 l","en":"10 l"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hoe groter die houer, hoe groter die kapasiteit: teelepel 5 ml, eetlepel 15 ml, maatkoppie 250 ml, bottel melk 2 l en emmer omtrent 10 l.","en":"The bigger the container, the bigger the capacity: teaspoon 5 ml, tablespoon 15 ml, measuring cup 250 ml, bottle of milk 2 l and bucket about 10 l."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die temperatuur was 8 °C in die oggend en 23 °C in die middag. Dit het ___ °C warmer geword.","en":"The temperature was 8 °C in the morning and 23 °C in the afternoon. It became ___ °C warmer."},"answers":{"af":["15"],"en":["15"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["31","25","5"],"en":["31","25","5"]}},"explain":{"af":"Verskil = hoër − laer = 23 − 8 = 15 °C. 31 is die twee getalle bymekaar getel, en 25 kry jy as jy in die ene-kolom 8 − 3 doen in plaas van te leen.","en":"Difference = higher − lower = 23 − 8 = 15 °C. 31 is the two numbers added together, and you get 25 if you do 8 − 3 in the units column instead of borrowing."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter instrument gebruik jy om 250 ml melk vir ’n resep af te meet?","en":"Which instrument do you use to measure 250 ml of milk for a recipe?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Maatkoppie of maatbeker","en":"A measuring cup or measuring jug"},{"af":"’n Termometer","en":"A thermometer"},{"af":"’n Badkamerskaal","en":"A bathroom scale"},{"af":"’n Liniaal","en":"A ruler"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Milliliter is ’n eenheid vir volume, en ons meet dit met ’n maatkoppie of maatbeker. ’n Termometer meet temperatuur, ’n skaal meet massa en ’n liniaal meet lengte.","en":"Millilitres are a unit of volume, and we measure them with a measuring cup or jug. A thermometer measures temperature, a scale measures mass and a ruler measures length."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Aisha het 3 l sap. Sy skink glase van 250 ml. Hoeveel vol glase kan sy skink?","en":"Aisha has 3 l of juice. She pours glasses of 250 ml. How many full glasses can she pour?"},"options":[{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"120","en":"120"},{"af":"12","en":"12"},{"af":"10","en":"10"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"3 l = 3 000 ml. 3 000 ÷ 250 = 12 glase. Of: 4 glase is 1 l, so 3 l is 3 × 4 = 12 glase.","en":"3 l = 3 000 ml. 3 000 ÷ 250 = 12 glasses. Or: 4 glasses make 1 l, so 3 l is 3 × 4 = 12 glasses."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Gesonde mens se liggaamstemperatuur is omtrent 30 °C.","en":"A healthy person’s body temperature is about 30 °C."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Gesonde mens se liggaamstemperatuur is omtrent 37 °C. Hoër as omtrent 38 °C beteken koors.","en":"False. A healthy person’s body temperature is about 37 °C. Higher than about 38 °C means a fever."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op ’n termometer is daar 5 gelyke spasies tussen 30 °C en 40 °C. Die vloeistof is 3 streepies bo 30 °C. Wat is die temperatuur?","en":"On a thermometer there are 5 equal spaces between 30 °C and 40 °C. The liquid is 3 marks above 30 °C. What is the temperature?"},"options":[{"af":"33 °C","en":"33 °C"},{"af":"36 °C","en":"36 °C"},{"af":"35 °C","en":"35 °C"},{"af":"38 °C","en":"38 °C"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Elke spasie is (40 − 30) ÷ 5 = 2 °C. Drie spasies is 3 × 2 = 6 °C, so 30 + 6 = 36 °C. 33 °C kry jy as jy dink elke streepie is 1 °C.","en":"Each space is (40 − 30) ÷ 5 = 2 °C. Three spaces are 3 × 2 = 6 °C, so 30 + 6 = 36 °C. You get 33 °C if you think each mark is 1 °C."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"1½ l = ___ ml","en":"1½ l = ___ ml"},"answers":{"af":["1 500","1500"],"en":["1 500","1500"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["150","1 050","15 000"],"en":["150","1 050","15 000"]}},"explain":{"af":"1 l = 1 000 ml en ½ l = 500 ml. 1 000 + 500 = 1 500 ml. 1 050 ml is 1 l 50 ml, nie 1½ l nie.","en":"1 l = 1 000 ml and ½ l = 500 ml. 1 000 + 500 = 1 500 ml. 1 050 ml is 1 l 50 ml, not 1½ l."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Resep vra 2 eetlepels olie, maar jy het net ’n teelepel. Hoeveel teelepels olie moet jy gebruik?","en":"A recipe asks for 2 tablespoons of oil, but you only have a teaspoon. How many teaspoons of oil must you use?"},"options":[{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"6","en":"6"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"2 eetlepels = 2 × 15 ml = 30 ml. Een teelepel is 5 ml, so 30 ÷ 5 = 6 teelepels. (1 eetlepel = 3 teelepels, so 2 eetlepels = 6 teelepels.)","en":"2 tablespoons = 2 × 15 ml = 30 ml. One teaspoon is 5 ml, so 30 ÷ 5 = 6 teaspoons. (1 tablespoon = 3 teaspoons, so 2 tablespoons = 6 teaspoons.)"}}]},{"id":"w5-t3-omtrek-oppervlakte-volume","title":{"af":"Omtrek, oppervlakte en volume","en":"Perimeter, area and volume"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die omtrek van vorms kan bereken, oppervlakte kan vind deur vierkante te tel, die verskil tussen omtrek en oppervlakte kan verduidelik en die volume van ’n boks kan vind deur kubusse te tel.","en":"You will be able to calculate the perimeter of shapes, find area by counting squares, explain the difference between perimeter and area, and find the volume of a box by counting cubes."},"summary":{"af":"## Omtrek\n\nDie **omtrek** van ’n vorm is die **totale lengte rondom** die vorm – soos ’n heining om ’n tuin of ’n raam om ’n prent. Jy vind dit deur **al die sye bymekaar te tel**. Omtrek is ’n lengte, so ons meet dit in **mm, cm, m of km**.\n\n- Driehoek met sye van 5 cm; 6 cm en 7 cm: 5 + 6 + 7 = **18 cm**\n- Vierkant met sye van 4 cm: 4 + 4 + 4 + 4 = 4 × 4 = **16 cm**\n\n’n **Reghoek** het twee ewe lang sye (die **lengte**, l) en twee ewe kort sye (die **breedte**, b). Daarom sien ons ’n patroon:\n\n**Omtrek van ’n reghoek = l + b + l + b = 2 × l + 2 × b**\n\n’n Reghoek van 8 cm by 5 cm: 2 × 8 + 2 × 5 = 16 + 10 = **26 cm**.\n\nAs ’n vorm op ’n **rooster** geteken is, kan jy die omtrek tel: loop met jou vinger rondom die buitekant en tel die **rande** van die vierkante, nie die vierkante self nie.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om net die twee sye wat jy sien, bymekaar te tel (8 + 5 = 13 cm). ’n Reghoek het **vier** sye!\n\n## Oppervlakte\n\nDie **oppervlakte** is hoeveel **plek binne** ’n plat vorm is – soos die mat op ’n vloer of die verf op ’n muur. Ons vind dit deur **vierkante eenhede te tel**.\n\n’n Vierkant van 1 cm by 1 cm het ’n oppervlakte van **1 vierkante sentimeter (1 cm²)**. Groot oppervlaktes, soos ’n klaskamervloer, meet ons in **vierkante meter (m²)**.\n\n’n Reghoek wat 6 vierkante lank en 4 vierkante breed is, het 4 rye van 6 vierkante. In plaas daarvan om een vir een te tel, kan jy vermenigvuldig: 4 × 6 = **24 cm²**.\n\nBy ’n **onreëlmatige vorm** op ’n rooster:\n\n1. Tel die **heel** vierkante.\n2. Tel die **halwe** vierkante: twee halwes maak een heel vierkant.\n3. Tel bymekaar. Byvoorbeeld 10 heel vierkante en 4 halwes: 10 + 2 = **12 cm²**.\n\n## Omtrek of oppervlakte?\n\n| Vraag | Omtrek | Oppervlakte |\n|---|---|---|\n| Wat is dit? | die lengte **rondom** | die plek **binne** |\n| Hoe vind ek dit? | tel die sye bymekaar | tel die vierkante |\n| Eenhede | cm, m | cm², m² |\n| Voorbeeld | heining om ’n tuin | gras in die tuin |\n\nVorms met **dieselfde oppervlakte** kan ’n **verskillende omtrek** hê. Elkeen van hierdie reghoeke het ’n oppervlakte van 12 cm²:\n\n| Reghoek | Oppervlakte | Omtrek |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 cm by 12 cm | 12 cm² | 26 cm |\n| 2 cm by 6 cm | 12 cm² | 16 cm |\n| 3 cm by 4 cm | 12 cm² | 14 cm |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om cm vir oppervlakte te skryf. Omtrek is in **cm**, maar oppervlakte is in **cm²** (vierkante sentimeter).\n\n## Volume van ’n reghoekige prisma\n\n**Volume** is hoeveel **ruimte** ’n 3D-voorwerp inneem. Ons vind die volume van ’n boks (**reghoekige prisma**) deur die **kubusse te tel** wat dit presies opvul. As elke kubus 1 cm by 1 cm by 1 cm is, is sy volume **1 kubieke sentimeter (1 cm³)**. (So ’n kubus kan presies 1 ml water hou.)\n\nTel slim in **lae**:\n\n1. Tel die kubusse in die **onderste laag**: 4 lank en 3 breed = 4 × 3 = 12 kubusse.\n2. Tel hoeveel **lae** daar is: 2.\n3. Vermenigvuldig: 12 × 2 = **24 kubusse**, dus 24 cm³.\n\n> **Onthou:** Tel ook die kubusse wat jy **nie kan sien nie** – dié aan die agterkant en binne-in. Elke laag het ewe veel kubusse.","en":"## Perimeter\n\nThe **perimeter** of a shape is the **total length around** the shape – like a fence around a garden or a frame around a picture. You find it by **adding all the sides**. Perimeter is a length, so we measure it in **mm, cm, m or km**.\n\n- Triangle with sides of 5 cm, 6 cm and 7 cm: 5 + 6 + 7 = **18 cm**\n- Square with sides of 4 cm: 4 + 4 + 4 + 4 = 4 × 4 = **16 cm**\n\nA **rectangle** has two equally long sides (the **length**, l) and two equally short sides (the **breadth**, b). That is why we see a pattern:\n\n**Perimeter of a rectangle = l + b + l + b = 2 × l + 2 × b**\n\nA rectangle of 8 cm by 5 cm: 2 × 8 + 2 × 5 = 16 + 10 = **26 cm**.\n\nIf a shape is drawn on a **grid**, you can count the perimeter: move your finger around the outside and count the **edges** of the squares, not the squares themselves.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Adding only the two sides you can see (8 + 5 = 13 cm). A rectangle has **four** sides!\n\n## Area\n\nThe **area** is how much **space inside** a flat shape there is – like the carpet on a floor or the paint on a wall. We find it by **counting square units**.\n\nA square of 1 cm by 1 cm has an area of **1 square centimetre (1 cm²)**. Big areas, like a classroom floor, are measured in **square metres (m²)**.\n\nA rectangle that is 6 squares long and 4 squares wide has 4 rows of 6 squares. Instead of counting one by one, you can multiply: 4 × 6 = **24 cm²**.\n\nFor an **irregular shape** on a grid:\n\n1. Count the **whole** squares.\n2. Count the **half** squares: two halves make one whole square.\n3. Add them. For example 10 whole squares and 4 halves: 10 + 2 = **12 cm²**.\n\n## Perimeter or area?\n\n| Question | Perimeter | Area |\n|---|---|---|\n| What is it? | the length **around** | the space **inside** |\n| How do I find it? | add the sides | count the squares |\n| Units | cm, m | cm², m² |\n| Example | fence around a garden | grass in the garden |\n\nShapes with the **same area** can have a **different perimeter**. Each of these rectangles has an area of 12 cm²:\n\n| Rectangle | Area | Perimeter |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 cm by 12 cm | 12 cm² | 26 cm |\n| 2 cm by 6 cm | 12 cm² | 16 cm |\n| 3 cm by 4 cm | 12 cm² | 14 cm |\n\n> **Common mistake:** Writing cm for area. Perimeter is in **cm**, but area is in **cm²** (square centimetres).\n\n## Volume of a rectangular prism\n\n**Volume** is how much **space** a 3D object takes up. We find the volume of a box (**rectangular prism**) by **counting the cubes** that fill it exactly. If each cube is 1 cm by 1 cm by 1 cm, its volume is **1 cubic centimetre (1 cm³)**. (Such a cube can hold exactly 1 ml of water.)\n\nCount cleverly in **layers**:\n\n1. Count the cubes in the **bottom layer**: 4 long and 3 wide = 4 × 3 = 12 cubes.\n2. Count how many **layers** there are: 2.\n3. Multiply: 12 × 2 = **24 cubes**, so 24 cm³.\n\n> **Remember:** Also count the cubes you **cannot see** – those at the back and inside. Every layer has the same number of cubes."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Omtrek","en":"Perimeter"},"def":{"af":"Die totale lengte rondom ’n vorm; jy tel al die sye bymekaar.","en":"The total length around a shape; you add up all the sides."}},{"term":{"af":"Oppervlakte","en":"Area"},"def":{"af":"Hoeveel plek binne ’n plat vorm is; jy tel die vierkante eenhede.","en":"How much space there is inside a flat shape; you count the square units."}},{"term":{"af":"Vierkante sentimeter (cm²)","en":"Square centimetre (cm²)"},"def":{"af":"Die oppervlakte van ’n vierkant van 1 cm by 1 cm.","en":"The area of a square of 1 cm by 1 cm."}},{"term":{"af":"Vierkante meter (m²)","en":"Square metre (m²)"},"def":{"af":"Die oppervlakte van ’n vierkant van 1 m by 1 m; vir groot oppervlaktes soos vloere.","en":"The area of a square of 1 m by 1 m; for big areas like floors."}},{"term":{"af":"Lengte en breedte","en":"Length and breadth"},"def":{"af":"Die lang sy (l) en die kort sy (b) van ’n reghoek.","en":"The long side (l) and the short side (b) of a rectangle."}},{"term":{"af":"Onreëlmatige vorm","en":"Irregular shape"},"def":{"af":"’n Vorm met sye en hoeke wat nie almal ewe groot is nie.","en":"A shape whose sides and angles are not all the same size."}},{"term":{"af":"Rooster","en":"Grid"},"def":{"af":"’n Patroon van gelyke vierkante waarop jy vorms teken en vierkante tel.","en":"A pattern of equal squares on which you draw shapes and count squares."}},{"term":{"af":"Volume","en":"Volume"},"def":{"af":"Hoeveel ruimte ’n 3D-voorwerp inneem.","en":"How much space a 3D object takes up."}},{"term":{"af":"Kubieke sentimeter (cm³)","en":"Cubic centimetre (cm³)"},"def":{"af":"Die volume van ’n kubus van 1 cm by 1 cm by 1 cm.","en":"The volume of a cube of 1 cm by 1 cm by 1 cm."}},{"term":{"af":"Reghoekige prisma","en":"Rectangular prism"},"def":{"af":"’n 3D-voorwerp soos ’n boks, met ses reghoekige vlakke.","en":"A 3D object like a box, with six rectangular faces."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"’n Draad om die groentetuin","en":"A fence around the vegetable garden"},"problem":{"af":"Die skool se groentetuin is ’n reghoek van 12 m by 7 m. Mnr. Mokoena span ’n draad om die hele tuin. Die draad kos R15 per meter. (a) Hoeveel draad het hy nodig? (b) Hoeveel kos die draad?","en":"The school’s vegetable garden is a rectangle of 12 m by 7 m. Mr Mokoena puts a wire fence around the whole garden. The wire costs R15 per metre. (a) How much wire does he need? (b) How much does the wire cost?"},"steps":[{"af":"Draad gaan rondom die tuin, so ons soek die omtrek.","en":"The wire goes around the garden, so we need the perimeter."},{"af":"(a) 2 × l + 2 × b = 2 × 12 + 2 × 7 = 24 + 14 = 38 m.","en":"(a) 2 × l + 2 × b = 2 × 12 + 2 × 7 = 24 + 14 = 38 m."},{"af":"(b) 38 × R15: 30 × 15 = 450 en 8 × 15 = 120, so 450 + 120 = R570.","en":"(b) 38 × R15: 30 × 15 = 450 and 8 × 15 = 120, so 450 + 120 = R570."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 38 m draad (b) R570","en":"(a) 38 m of wire (b) R570"}},{"title":{"af":"Oppervlakte en omtrek van een reghoek","en":"Area and perimeter of one rectangle"},"problem":{"af":"’n Reghoek op ’n rooster van sentimetervierkante is 7 vierkante lank en 3 vierkante breed. Vind (a) die oppervlakte en (b) die omtrek.","en":"A rectangle on a grid of centimetre squares is 7 squares long and 3 squares wide. Find (a) the area and (b) the perimeter."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Daar is 3 rye van 7 vierkante: 3 × 7 = 21 vierkante, dus 21 cm².","en":"(a) There are 3 rows of 7 squares: 3 × 7 = 21 squares, so 21 cm²."},{"af":"(b) Tel die sye: 2 × 7 + 2 × 3 = 14 + 6 = 20 cm.","en":"(b) Add the sides: 2 × 7 + 2 × 3 = 14 + 6 = 20 cm."},{"af":"Let op die eenhede: oppervlakte in cm², omtrek in cm.","en":"Look at the units: area in cm², perimeter in cm."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 21 cm² (b) 20 cm","en":"(a) 21 cm² (b) 20 cm"}},{"title":{"af":"Oppervlakte van ’n onreëlmatige vorm","en":"Area of an irregular shape"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato teken ’n blaar op ’n rooster van sentimetervierkante. Die blaar bedek 14 heel vierkante en 6 halwe vierkante. Wat is die oppervlakte van die blaar?","en":"Lerato draws a leaf on a grid of centimetre squares. The leaf covers 14 whole squares and 6 half squares. What is the area of the leaf?"},"steps":[{"af":"Heel vierkante: 14.","en":"Whole squares: 14."},{"af":"Halwe vierkante: twee halwes maak een heel, so 6 halwes = 6 ÷ 2 = 3 heel vierkante.","en":"Half squares: two halves make one whole, so 6 halves = 6 ÷ 2 = 3 whole squares."},{"af":"Tel bymekaar: 14 + 3 = 17 vierkante.","en":"Add: 14 + 3 = 17 squares."}],"answer":{"af":"Omtrent 17 cm²","en":"About 17 cm²"}},{"title":{"af":"Volume van ’n boks","en":"Volume of a box"},"problem":{"af":"’n Boks word presies met kubusse van 1 cm³ gevul. Die boks is 5 kubusse lank, 2 kubusse breed en 3 kubusse hoog. Wat is die volume van die boks?","en":"A box is filled exactly with cubes of 1 cm³. The box is 5 cubes long, 2 cubes wide and 3 cubes high. What is the volume of the box?"},"steps":[{"af":"Onderste laag: 5 × 2 = 10 kubusse.","en":"Bottom layer: 5 × 2 = 10 cubes."},{"af":"Daar is 3 lae (die boks is 3 kubusse hoog).","en":"There are 3 layers (the box is 3 cubes high)."},{"af":"Totaal: 10 × 3 = 30 kubusse = 30 cm³.","en":"Total: 10 × 3 = 30 cubes = 30 cm³."}],"answer":{"af":"30 cm³","en":"30 cm³"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die omtrek van ’n reghoek van 9 cm by 4 cm?","en":"What is the perimeter of a rectangle of 9 cm by 4 cm?"},"options":[{"af":"13 cm","en":"13 cm"},{"af":"36 cm","en":"36 cm"},{"af":"22 cm","en":"22 cm"},{"af":"26 cm","en":"26 cm"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"2 × 9 + 2 × 4 = 18 + 8 = 26 cm. 13 cm is net twee sye, en 36 is die oppervlakte (9 × 4), nie die omtrek nie.","en":"2 × 9 + 2 × 4 = 18 + 8 = 26 cm. 13 cm is only two sides, and 36 is the area (9 × 4), not the perimeter."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"By watter situasie soek jy die oppervlakte?","en":"In which situation do you need the area?"},"options":[{"af":"Om die lengte van ’n heining om ’n veld te vind","en":"To find the length of a fence around a field"},{"af":"Om te vind hoeveel mat nodig is om ’n vloer te bedek","en":"To find how much carpet is needed to cover a floor"},{"af":"Om te vind hoeveel water ’n bottel hou","en":"To find how much water a bottle holds"},{"af":"Om te vind hoe lank ’n raam om ’n prent moet wees","en":"To find how long a frame around a picture must be"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Mat bedek die plek binne die vloer – dit is oppervlakte. ’n Heining en ’n raam gaan rondom (omtrek), en water in ’n bottel is kapasiteit.","en":"Carpet covers the space inside the floor – that is area. A fence and a frame go around (perimeter), and water in a bottle is capacity."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Vierkant met sye van 5 cm het ’n omtrek van 20 cm.","en":"A square with sides of 5 cm has a perimeter of 20 cm."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Vierkant het 4 ewe lang sye: 4 × 5 = 20 cm.","en":"True. A square has 4 equal sides: 4 × 5 = 20 cm."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Reghoek op ’n rooster is 5 vierkante lank en 3 vierkante breed. Die oppervlakte is ___ vierkante.","en":"A rectangle on a grid is 5 squares long and 3 squares wide. The area is ___ squares."},"answers":{"af":["15"],"en":["15"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["16","8","30"],"en":["16","8","30"]}},"explain":{"af":"Daar is 3 rye van 5 vierkante: 3 × 5 = 15. 16 is die omtrek (2 × 5 + 2 × 3), nie die oppervlakte nie.","en":"There are 3 rows of 5 squares: 3 × 5 = 15. 16 is the perimeter (2 × 5 + 2 × 3), not the area."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Vorm op ’n rooster van sentimetervierkante bedek 9 heel vierkante en 4 halwe vierkante. Wat is sy oppervlakte?","en":"A shape on a grid of centimetre squares covers 9 whole squares and 4 half squares. What is its area?"},"options":[{"af":"11 cm²","en":"11 cm²"},{"af":"13 cm²","en":"13 cm²"},{"af":"9 cm²","en":"9 cm²"},{"af":"15 cm²","en":"15 cm²"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"4 halwe vierkante = 2 heel vierkante. 9 + 2 = 11 cm². 13 cm² kry jy as jy elke halwe vierkant as ’n heel een tel.","en":"4 half squares = 2 whole squares. 9 + 2 = 11 cm². You get 13 cm² if you count each half square as a whole one."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke woord of eenheid by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each word or unit to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Omtrek","en":"Perimeter"},"r":{"af":"Die lengte rondom ’n vorm","en":"The length around a shape"}},{"l":{"af":"Oppervlakte","en":"Area"},"r":{"af":"Die plek binne ’n plat vorm","en":"The space inside a flat shape"}},{"l":{"af":"Volume","en":"Volume"},"r":{"af":"Die ruimte wat ’n 3D-voorwerp inneem","en":"The space a 3D object takes up"}},{"l":{"af":"cm²","en":"cm²"},"r":{"af":"’n Eenheid vir oppervlakte","en":"A unit for area"}},{"l":{"af":"cm³","en":"cm³"},"r":{"af":"’n Eenheid vir volume","en":"A unit for volume"}}],"explain":{"af":"Omtrek is ’n lengte (cm), oppervlakte tel vierkante (cm²) en volume tel kubusse (cm³).","en":"Perimeter is a length (cm), area counts squares (cm²) and volume counts cubes (cm³)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Boks word met kubusse van 1 cm³ gevul. Die onderste laag het 4 rye van 5 kubusse, en daar is 3 lae. Wat is die volume?","en":"A box is filled with cubes of 1 cm³. The bottom layer has 4 rows of 5 cubes, and there are 3 layers. What is the volume?"},"options":[{"af":"12 cm³","en":"12 cm³"},{"af":"20 cm³","en":"20 cm³"},{"af":"60 cm³","en":"60 cm³"},{"af":"35 cm³","en":"35 cm³"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Een laag: 4 × 5 = 20 kubusse. Drie lae: 20 × 3 = 60 kubusse = 60 cm³. 20 cm³ is net een laag.","en":"One layer: 4 × 5 = 20 cubes. Three layers: 20 × 3 = 60 cubes = 60 cm³. 20 cm³ is only one layer."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die omtrek van ’n vierkant is 36 cm. Elke sy is ___ cm lank.","en":"The perimeter of a square is 36 cm. Each side is ___ cm long."},"answers":{"af":["9"],"en":["9"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["6","18","12"],"en":["6","18","12"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Vierkant het 4 ewe lang sye, so deel die omtrek deur 4: 36 ÷ 4 = 9 cm. Kontroleer: 4 × 9 = 36. ✓","en":"A square has 4 equal sides, so divide the perimeter by 4: 36 ÷ 4 = 9 cm. Check: 4 × 9 = 36. ✓"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Al drie hierdie reghoeke het ’n oppervlakte van 16 cm². Watter een het die kleinste omtrek?","en":"All three of these rectangles have an area of 16 cm². Which one has the smallest perimeter?"},"options":[{"af":"1 cm by 16 cm","en":"1 cm by 16 cm"},{"af":"2 cm by 8 cm","en":"2 cm by 8 cm"},{"af":"4 cm by 4 cm","en":"4 cm by 4 cm"},{"af":"Hulle het almal dieselfde omtrek","en":"They all have the same perimeter"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Omtrekke: 1 by 16 → 2 + 32 = 34 cm; 2 by 8 → 4 + 16 = 20 cm; 4 by 4 → 8 + 8 = 16 cm. Dieselfde oppervlakte beteken nie dieselfde omtrek nie.","en":"Perimeters: 1 by 16 → 2 + 32 = 34 cm; 2 by 8 → 4 + 16 = 20 cm; 4 by 4 → 8 + 8 = 16 cm. The same area does not mean the same perimeter."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As twee reghoeke dieselfde oppervlakte het, het hulle ook altyd dieselfde omtrek.","en":"If two rectangles have the same area, they always have the same perimeter too."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Reghoek van 2 cm by 6 cm en een van 3 cm by 4 cm het albei ’n oppervlakte van 12 cm², maar hul omtrekke is 16 cm en 14 cm.","en":"False. A rectangle of 2 cm by 6 cm and one of 3 cm by 4 cm both have an area of 12 cm², but their perimeters are 16 cm and 14 cm."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter eenheid is die beste vir die oppervlakte van ’n sokkerveld?","en":"Which unit is best for the area of a soccer field?"},"options":[{"af":"cm²","en":"cm²"},{"af":"m","en":"m"},{"af":"m³","en":"m³"},{"af":"m²","en":"m²"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Oppervlakte word in vierkante eenhede gemeet, en ’n sokkerveld is groot, so m². cm² is te klein, m is vir lengte en m³ is vir volume.","en":"Area is measured in square units, and a soccer field is big, so m². cm² is too small, m is for length and m³ is for volume."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pa wil ’n draad om ’n reghoekige groentetuin van 10 m by 6 m span. Hoeveel meter draad het hy nodig?","en":"Dad wants to put a wire fence around a rectangular vegetable garden of 10 m by 6 m. How many metres of wire does he need?"},"options":[{"af":"32 m","en":"32 m"},{"af":"16 m","en":"16 m"},{"af":"60 m","en":"60 m"},{"af":"26 m","en":"26 m"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die draad gaan rondom, so bereken die omtrek: 2 × 10 + 2 × 6 = 20 + 12 = 32 m. 60 is die oppervlakte in m².","en":"The wire goes around, so work out the perimeter: 2 × 10 + 2 × 6 = 20 + 12 = 32 m. 60 is the area in m²."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Kubus van 1 cm by 1 cm by 1 cm het ’n volume van 1 ___.","en":"A cube of 1 cm by 1 cm by 1 cm has a volume of 1 ___."},"answers":{"af":["cm³","cm3","kubieke sentimeter"],"en":["cm³","cm3","cubic centimetre","cubic centimeter"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["cm²","cm","m³"],"en":["cm²","cm","m³"]}},"explain":{"af":"Volume tel kubusse, so die eenheid is kubieke sentimeter (cm³). cm² is vir oppervlakte en cm vir lengte.","en":"Volume counts cubes, so the unit is the cubic centimetre (cm³). cm² is for area and cm for length."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo bou ’n blok wat 3 kubusse lank, 3 kubusse breed en 2 kubusse hoog is. Hy sê die volume is 14 kubusse, want hy kan net 14 sien. Hoeveel kubusse is daar werklik?","en":"Thabo builds a block that is 3 cubes long, 3 cubes wide and 2 cubes high. He says the volume is 14 cubes, because he can only see 14. How many cubes are there really?"},"options":[{"af":"14","en":"14"},{"af":"18","en":"18"},{"af":"9","en":"9"},{"af":"12","en":"12"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Elke laag het 3 × 3 = 9 kubusse en daar is 2 lae: 9 × 2 = 18. Thabo het die kubusse vergeet wat agter en binne-in versteek is.","en":"Each layer has 3 × 3 = 9 cubes and there are 2 layers: 9 × 2 = 18. Thabo forgot the cubes hidden at the back and inside."}}]},{"id":"w5-t3-transformasies-posisie","title":{"af":"Transformasies, aansigte en posisie","en":"Transformations, views and position"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal translasies, refleksies en rotasies kan herken en beskryf, teëlpatrone kan verduidelik, voorwerpe van voor, die kant en bo kan teken en posisies en roetes op ’n rooster kan beskryf.","en":"You will be able to recognise and describe translations, reflections and rotations, explain tessellations, draw objects from the front, side and top, and describe positions and routes on a grid."},"summary":{"af":"## Drie transformasies\n\n’n **Transformasie** beweeg ’n vorm na ’n nuwe plek of posisie. By al drie hieronder bly die **vorm en grootte presies dieselfde** – net die plek of die rigting waarin dit wys, verander.\n\n| Transformasie | Ander naam | Wat gebeur? | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Translasie** | skuif | die vorm gly in ’n reguit lyn, sonder om te draai | ’n boks wat oor die vloer geskuif word |\n| **Refleksie** | spieëlbeeld, omkeer | die vorm word oor ’n **spieëllyn** omgeflip | jou gesig in die spieël |\n| **Rotasie** | draai | die vorm draai om ’n vaste punt | die wysers van ’n horlosie |\n\n**Translasie:** Sê hoe ver en in watter rigting, bv. *3 blokke regs en 2 blokke op*. Elke punt van die vorm skuif ewe ver in dieselfde rigting.\n\n**Refleksie:** Elke punt is ewe ver van die spieëllyn af, maar aan die ander kant. Links en regs ruil om. Die letter **b** word **d** in ’n vertikale spieëllyn.\n\n**Rotasie:** ’n **Kwartdraai** is 90° (’n regte hoek), ’n **halfdraai** 180°, ’n **driekwartdraai** 270° en ’n **heeldraai** 360° – dan is die vorm terug waar dit begon het. Draai **kloksgewys** (soos die wysers van ’n horlosie) of **antikloksgewys**. ’n Pyl wat **op** wys, wys **regs** ná ’n kwartdraai kloksgewys, en **af** ná ’n halfdraai.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om ’n refleksie en ’n halfdraai te verwar. Die letter **b** word **d** in ’n vertikale spieëllyn, maar **q** ná ’n halfdraai.\n\n## Teëlpatrone (tessellasies)\n\n’n **Teëlpatroon** (tessellasie) is ’n patroon van vorms wat inmekaar pas **sonder gapings en sonder om oor mekaar te lê** – soos teëls op ’n vloer. Ons maak dit deur ’n vorm oor en oor te skuif, te draai of te reflekteer.\n\n- Vierkante, reghoeke, driehoeke en reëlmatige seshoeke vorm teëlpatrone. Bye bou hul heuningkoek met seshoeke!\n- Sirkels laat gapings tussen hulle, so hulle vorm nie ’n teëlpatroon nie.\n\n## Aansigte\n\n’n 3D-voorwerp lyk anders as jy van verskillende kante af kyk: die **vooraansig** (van voor), die **syaansig** (van die kant) en die **boaansig** (van bo, soos ’n voël).\n\n| Voorwerp (regop) | Vooraansig | Boaansig |\n|---|---|---|\n| Blikkie (silinder) | reghoek | sirkel |\n| Keël met die punt bo | driehoek | sirkel met ’n kolletjie in die middel |\n| Kubus | vierkant | vierkant |\n| Vierkantige piramide | driehoek | vierkant met twee skuins lyne wat in die middel kruis |\n\n## Posisie op ’n rooster\n\nOp ’n rooster of kaart wys die **letters** die **kolomme** en die **getalle** die **rye**. Jy skryf die letter eerste: **C4** beteken kolom C, ry 4.\n\n| Ry | A | B | C | D | E |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **4** | | | Skool | | |\n| **3** | | | | | Winkel |\n| **2** | Park | | | | |\n| **1** | | Huis | | | |\n\n- Die skool is in **C4** en die park in **A2**.\n- Op die meeste kaarte is **noord** bo. Die roete van die huis (B1) na die winkel (E3) is: 3 blokke **oos** en 2 blokke **noord**.\n\n> **Onthou:** Gaan eers **oor** (die letter) en dan **op of af** (die getal) – eers in die gang af, dan die trap op.","en":"## Three transformations\n\nA **transformation** moves a shape to a new place or position. In all three below the **shape and size stay exactly the same** – only the place or the direction it faces changes.\n\n| Transformation | Other name | What happens? | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Translation** | slide | the shape slides in a straight line, without turning | a box pushed across the floor |\n| **Reflection** | mirror image, flip | the shape is flipped over a **mirror line** | your face in the mirror |\n| **Rotation** | turn | the shape turns around a fixed point | the hands of a clock |\n\n**Translation:** Say how far and in which direction, e.g. *3 blocks right and 2 blocks up*. Every point of the shape moves the same distance in the same direction.\n\n**Reflection:** Every point is the same distance from the mirror line, but on the other side. Left and right swap. The letter **b** becomes **d** in a vertical mirror line.\n\n**Rotation:** A **quarter turn** is 90° (a right angle), a **half turn** 180°, a **three-quarter turn** 270° and a **full turn** 360° – then the shape is back where it started. Turn **clockwise** (like the hands of a clock) or **anticlockwise**. An arrow pointing **up** points **right** after a quarter turn clockwise, and **down** after a half turn.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Mixing up a reflection and a half turn. The letter **b** becomes **d** in a vertical mirror line, but **q** after a half turn.\n\n## Tessellations\n\nA **tessellation** is a pattern of shapes that fit together **without gaps and without overlapping** – like tiles on a floor. We make it by sliding, turning or reflecting a shape over and over.\n\n- Squares, rectangles, triangles and regular hexagons make tessellations. Bees build their honeycomb with hexagons!\n- Circles leave gaps between them, so they do not make a tessellation.\n\n## Views\n\nA 3D object looks different when you look at it from different sides: the **front view** (from the front), the **side view** (from the side) and the **top view** (from above, like a bird).\n\n| Object (upright) | Front view | Top view |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tin (cylinder) | rectangle | circle |\n| Cone with the point at the top | triangle | circle with a dot in the middle |\n| Cube | square | square |\n| Square pyramid | triangle | square with two slanted lines crossing in the middle |\n\n## Position on a grid\n\nOn a grid or map the **letters** show the **columns** and the **numbers** show the **rows**. You write the letter first: **C4** means column C, row 4.\n\n| Row | A | B | C | D | E |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **4** | | | School | | |\n| **3** | | | | | Shop |\n| **2** | Park | | | | |\n| **1** | | House | | | |\n\n- The school is in **C4** and the park in **A2**.\n- On most maps **north** is at the top. The route from the house (B1) to the shop (E3) is: 3 blocks **east** and 2 blocks **north**.\n\n> **Remember:** First go **across** (the letter) and then **up or down** (the number) – first along the corridor, then up the stairs."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Transformasie","en":"Transformation"},"def":{"af":"’n Beweging van ’n vorm na ’n nuwe posisie sonder dat sy vorm of grootte verander.","en":"A movement of a shape to a new position without changing its shape or size."}},{"term":{"af":"Translasie (skuif)","en":"Translation (slide)"},"def":{"af":"’n Vorm gly in ’n reguit lyn na ’n nuwe plek sonder om te draai.","en":"A shape slides in a straight line to a new place without turning."}},{"term":{"af":"Refleksie (spieëlbeeld)","en":"Reflection (mirror image)"},"def":{"af":"’n Vorm word oor ’n spieëllyn omgeflip sodat links en regs omruil.","en":"A shape is flipped over a mirror line so that left and right swap."}},{"term":{"af":"Spieëllyn","en":"Mirror line"},"def":{"af":"Die lyn waaroor ’n vorm gereflekteer word; elke punt is ewe ver daarvan af aan albei kante.","en":"The line over which a shape is reflected; every point is the same distance from it on both sides."}},{"term":{"af":"Rotasie (draai)","en":"Rotation (turn)"},"def":{"af":"’n Vorm draai om ’n vaste punt, kloksgewys of antikloksgewys.","en":"A shape turns around a fixed point, clockwise or anticlockwise."}},{"term":{"af":"Kwartdraai","en":"Quarter turn"},"def":{"af":"’n Draai van 90°, ’n regte hoek.","en":"A turn of 90°, a right angle."}},{"term":{"af":"Kloksgewys","en":"Clockwise"},"def":{"af":"In dieselfde rigting as die wysers van ’n horlosie.","en":"In the same direction as the hands of a clock."}},{"term":{"af":"Teëlpatroon (tessellasie)","en":"Tessellation"},"def":{"af":"’n Patroon van vorms wat sonder gapings of oorvleueling inmekaar pas.","en":"A pattern of shapes that fit together without gaps or overlaps."}},{"term":{"af":"Aansig","en":"View"},"def":{"af":"Hoe ’n voorwerp lyk as jy van voor, van die kant of van bo af daarna kyk.","en":"What an object looks like when you look at it from the front, the side or the top."}},{"term":{"af":"Roosterverwysing","en":"Grid reference"},"def":{"af":"’n Letter en ’n getal, soos C4, wat die kolom en ry van ’n blok op ’n rooster gee.","en":"A letter and a number, like C4, that give the column and row of a block on a grid."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Benoem die transformasie","en":"Name the transformation"},"problem":{"af":"Watter transformasie is elkeen? (a) ’n Vlag word 4 blokke regs geskuif en wys steeds na dieselfde kant. (b) ’n Pyl wat op gewys het, wys nou regs, en dit is nog op dieselfde plek. (c) Die letter b het die letter d geword.","en":"Which transformation is each one? (a) A flag is moved 4 blocks to the right and still faces the same way. (b) An arrow that pointed up now points right, and it is still in the same place. (c) The letter b has become the letter d."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die vlag het net gegly, nie gedraai of omgeflip nie: dit is ’n translasie (4 blokke regs).","en":"(a) The flag only slid, it did not turn or flip: this is a translation (4 blocks right)."},{"af":"(b) Die pyl het om ’n punt gedraai van op na regs: dit is ’n kwartdraai (90°) kloksgewys.","en":"(b) The arrow turned around a point from up to right: this is a quarter turn (90°) clockwise."},{"af":"(c) Links en regs het omgeruil: dit is ’n refleksie in ’n vertikale spieëllyn.","en":"(c) Left and right swapped: this is a reflection in a vertical mirror line."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) translasie (b) rotasie – kwartdraai kloksgewys (c) refleksie","en":"(a) translation (b) rotation – quarter turn clockwise (c) reflection"}},{"title":{"af":"Draai die minuutwyser","en":"Turn the minute hand"},"problem":{"af":"Die minuutwyser van ’n horlosie wys na 12. Na watter getal wys dit ná (a) ’n kwartdraai kloksgewys (b) ’n halfdraai (c) ’n driekwartdraai kloksgewys?","en":"The minute hand of a clock points to 12. Which number does it point to after (a) a quarter turn clockwise (b) a half turn (c) a three-quarter turn clockwise?"},"steps":[{"af":"’n Heeldraai gaan deur al 12 getalle, so ’n kwartdraai is 12 ÷ 4 = 3 getalle verder.","en":"A full turn goes through all 12 numbers, so a quarter turn is 12 ÷ 4 = 3 numbers further."},{"af":"(a) Van 12 af, 3 getalle kloksgewys: 3. (b) ’n Halfdraai is 6 getalle: 6.","en":"(a) From 12, 3 numbers clockwise: 3. (b) A half turn is 6 numbers: 6."},{"af":"(c) ’n Driekwartdraai is 3 × 3 = 9 getalle: 9.","en":"(c) A three-quarter turn is 3 × 3 = 9 numbers: 9."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 3 (b) 6 (c) 9","en":"(a) 3 (b) 6 (c) 9"}},{"title":{"af":"’n Roete op ’n rooster","en":"A route on a grid"},"problem":{"af":"Op ’n kaartrooster (noord is bo) is Nomsa se huis in B2 en die biblioteek in E5. (a) Beskryf die kortste roete langs die blokke. (b) Die bushalte is 2 blokke wes van die biblioteek. In watter blok is dit?","en":"On a map grid (north is at the top) Nomsa’s house is in B2 and the library is in E5. (a) Describe the shortest route along the blocks. (b) The bus stop is 2 blocks west of the library. In which block is it?"},"steps":[{"af":"Oor: van kolom B na kolom E is 3 blokke na regs, dus 3 blokke oos.","en":"Across: from column B to column E is 3 blocks to the right, so 3 blocks east."},{"af":"Op: van ry 2 na ry 5 is 3 blokke op, dus 3 blokke noord.","en":"Up: from row 2 to row 5 is 3 blocks up, so 3 blocks north."},{"af":"(b) Wes is links. Van E af 2 kolomme links: D, C. Die ry bly 5.","en":"(b) West is to the left. From E, 2 columns to the left: D, C. The row stays 5."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 3 blokke oos en 3 blokke noord (b) C5","en":"(a) 3 blocks east and 3 blocks north (b) C5"}},{"title":{"af":"Teken die aansigte","en":"Draw the views"},"problem":{"af":"Johan pak 3 kubusse in ’n ry van links na regs en sit ’n vierde kubus bo-op die middelste een. Beskryf die vooraansig, die boaansig en die syaansig (van regs).","en":"Johan puts 3 cubes in a row from left to right and puts a fourth cube on top of the middle one. Describe the front view, the top view and the side view (from the right)."},"steps":[{"af":"Vooraansig: jy sien 3 vierkante langs mekaar met een vierkant bo-op die middelste een, soos ’n podium.","en":"Front view: you see 3 squares next to each other with one square on top of the middle one, like a podium."},{"af":"Boaansig: van bo af sien jy net 3 vierkante in ’n ry. Jy kan nie sien dat die middelste een hoër is nie.","en":"Top view: from above you only see 3 squares in a row. You cannot see that the middle one is higher."},{"af":"Syaansig van regs: jy sien die kubus aan die regterkant en die boonste kubus daaragter: 2 vierkante bo-op mekaar.","en":"Side view from the right: you see the cube on the right and the top cube behind it: 2 squares on top of each other."}],"answer":{"af":"Vooraansig: 3 vierkante met 1 bo in die middel; boaansig: 3 vierkante in ’n ry; syaansig: 2 vierkante bo-op mekaar.","en":"Front view: 3 squares with 1 on top in the middle; top view: 3 squares in a row; side view: 2 squares on top of each other."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter transformasie is dit as ’n vorm in ’n reguit lyn gly sonder om te draai of om te flip?","en":"Which transformation is it when a shape slides in a straight line without turning or flipping?"},"options":[{"af":"Refleksie","en":"Reflection"},{"af":"Translasie","en":"Translation"},{"af":"Rotasie","en":"Rotation"},{"af":"Teëlpatroon","en":"Tessellation"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Translasie is ’n skuif: die vorm gly en wys steeds in dieselfde rigting. By ’n refleksie flip dit om en by ’n rotasie draai dit.","en":"A translation is a slide: the shape moves and still faces the same direction. In a reflection it flips over and in a rotation it turns."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Kwartdraai is ’n draai van ___°.","en":"A quarter turn is a turn of ___°."},"answers":{"af":["90"],"en":["90"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["45","180","360"],"en":["45","180","360"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Heeldraai is 360°. ’n Kwart daarvan is 360 ÷ 4 = 90°, ’n regte hoek. 180° is ’n halfdraai.","en":"A full turn is 360°. A quarter of it is 360 ÷ 4 = 90°, a right angle. 180° is a half turn."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat gebeur met die grootte van ’n vorm ná ’n translasie, refleksie of rotasie?","en":"What happens to the size of a shape after a translation, reflection or rotation?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit bly presies dieselfde","en":"It stays exactly the same"},{"af":"Dit word groter","en":"It gets bigger"},{"af":"Dit word kleiner","en":"It gets smaller"},{"af":"Dit hang af van die transformasie","en":"It depends on the transformation"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"By al drie hierdie transformasies bly die vorm en grootte dieselfde. Net die plek of die rigting waarin die vorm wys, verander.","en":"In all three of these transformations the shape and size stay the same. Only the place or the direction the shape faces changes."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Heeldraai (360°) bring ’n vorm terug na sy begin-posisie.","en":"A full turn (360°) brings a shape back to its starting position."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Ná ’n heeldraai het die vorm een keer heeltemal rond gedraai en lyk dit weer net soos aan die begin.","en":"True. After a full turn the shape has turned all the way around once and looks exactly as it did at the start."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Pyl wys op. Waarheen wys dit ná ’n kwartdraai kloksgewys?","en":"An arrow points up. Where does it point after a quarter turn clockwise?"},"options":[{"af":"Af","en":"Down"},{"af":"Links","en":"Left"},{"af":"Regs","en":"Right"},{"af":"Op","en":"Up"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Kloksgewys is soos ’n horlosie: van 12 na 3, dus van op na regs. Antikloksgewys sou dit links wys, en ná ’n halfdraai af.","en":"Clockwise is like a clock: from 12 to 3, so from up to right. Anticlockwise it would point left, and after a half turn down."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter vorm vorm NIE ’n teëlpatroon sonder gapings nie?","en":"Which shape does NOT make a tessellation without gaps?"},"options":[{"af":"Vierkant","en":"Square"},{"af":"Reghoek","en":"Rectangle"},{"af":"Reëlmatige seshoek","en":"Regular hexagon"},{"af":"Sirkel","en":"Circle"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Sirkels se geboë rande pas nie styf teen mekaar nie, so daar bly gapings oor. Vierkante, reghoeke en reëlmatige seshoeke pas sonder gapings inmekaar.","en":"The curved edges of circles do not fit tightly against each other, so gaps are left. Squares, rectangles and regular hexagons fit together without gaps."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke voorwerp en aansig by wat jy sien.","en":"Match each object and view to what you see."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Regop blikkie – boaansig","en":"Upright tin – top view"},"r":{"af":"Sirkel","en":"Circle"}},{"l":{"af":"Regop blikkie – vooraansig","en":"Upright tin – front view"},"r":{"af":"Reghoek","en":"Rectangle"}},{"l":{"af":"Regop keël – vooraansig","en":"Upright cone – front view"},"r":{"af":"Driehoek","en":"Triangle"}},{"l":{"af":"Kubus – vooraansig","en":"Cube – front view"},"r":{"af":"Vierkant","en":"Square"}},{"l":{"af":"Vierkantige piramide – boaansig","en":"Square pyramid – top view"},"r":{"af":"Vierkant met twee lyne wat in die middel kruis","en":"Square with two lines crossing in the middle"}}],"explain":{"af":"Dink hoe die voorwerp lyk as jy reg van voor of reg van bo kyk. ’n Blikkie is van bo rond en van voor reghoekig; ’n piramide se punt lê van bo in die middel van die vierkant.","en":"Think about what the object looks like straight from the front or straight from above. A tin is round from above and rectangular from the front; a pyramid’s point is in the middle of the square from above."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy is in blok D2 op ’n kaartrooster (noord is bo). Jy beweeg 2 blokke oos en 3 blokke noord. In watter blok eindig jy?","en":"You are in block D2 on a map grid (north is at the top). You move 2 blocks east and 3 blocks north. In which block do you end?"},"options":[{"af":"B5","en":"B5"},{"af":"E5","en":"E5"},{"af":"F4","en":"F4"},{"af":"F5","en":"F5"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Oos is regs: van D af 2 kolomme regs is E, F. Noord is op: van ry 2 af 3 rye op is ry 5. Dus F5. B5 kry jy as jy wes in plaas van oos gaan.","en":"East is right: from D, 2 columns to the right is E, F. North is up: from row 2, 3 rows up is row 5. So F5. You get B5 if you go west instead of east."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In die roosterverwysing C4 gee die letter C die ___.","en":"In the grid reference C4 the letter C gives the ___."},"answers":{"af":["kolom"],"en":["column"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["ry","rigting","skaal"],"en":["row","direction","scale"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die letter gee die kolom en die getal gee die ry. Jy gaan eers oor na kolom C en dan op na ry 4.","en":"The letter gives the column and the number gives the row. You first go across to column C and then up to row 4."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die letter b word ’n halfdraai gedraai. Watter letter kry jy?","en":"The letter b is turned through a half turn. Which letter do you get?"},"options":[{"af":"d","en":"d"},{"af":"q","en":"q"},{"af":"p","en":"p"},{"af":"b","en":"b"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Halfdraai draai die letter onderstebo én na die ander kant: b word q. Die letter d kry jy met ’n refleksie in ’n vertikale spieëllyn, en p met ’n refleksie in ’n horisontale spieëllyn.","en":"A half turn turns the letter upside down and to the other side: b becomes q. You get d with a reflection in a vertical mirror line, and p with a reflection in a horizontal mirror line."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"By ’n refleksie word die vorm groter of kleiner, afhangende van hoe ver dit van die spieëllyn af is.","en":"In a reflection the shape gets bigger or smaller, depending on how far it is from the mirror line."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Spieëlbeeld is presies ewe groot as die oorspronklike vorm. Net links en regs (of bo en onder) ruil om.","en":"False. A mirror image is exactly the same size as the original shape. Only left and right (or top and bottom) swap."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Johan kyk reg van bo af na ’n regop keël met die punt bo. Wat sien hy?","en":"Johan looks straight down from above at an upright cone with the point at the top. What does he see?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Driehoek","en":"A triangle"},{"af":"’n Vierkant","en":"A square"},{"af":"’n Sirkel met ’n kolletjie in die middel","en":"A circle with a dot in the middle"},{"af":"’n Reghoek","en":"A rectangle"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Van bo af sien jy die ronde grondvlak as ’n sirkel en die punt as ’n kolletjie in die middel. ’n Driehoek is die vooraansig van die keël.","en":"From above you see the round base as a circle and the point as a dot in the middle. A triangle is the front view of the cone."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die minuutwyser van ’n horlosie wys na 12. Ná ’n halfdraai wys dit na ___.","en":"The minute hand of a clock points to 12. After a half turn it points to ___."},"answers":{"af":["6"],"en":["6"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3","9","12"],"en":["3","9","12"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Halfdraai is die helfte van die 12 getalle op die horlosie, dus 6 getalle verder: van 12 na 6. 3 is ’n kwartdraai kloksgewys.","en":"A half turn is half of the 12 numbers on the clock, so 6 numbers further: from 12 to 6. 3 is a quarter turn clockwise."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Hoekpunt van ’n driehoek is in blok B2. Ná ’n translasie is dieselfde hoekpunt in blok E2. Beskryf die translasie.","en":"A vertex of a triangle is in block B2. After a translation the same vertex is in block E2. Describe the translation."},"options":[{"af":"3 blokke regs","en":"3 blocks right"},{"af":"3 blokke op","en":"3 blocks up"},{"af":"2 blokke regs","en":"2 blocks right"},{"af":"4 blokke regs","en":"4 blocks right"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die ry (2) bly dieselfde, so die driehoek het net oor geskuif. Van B na E: C, D, E – dit is 3 blokke regs. 4 kry jy as jy B ook tel.","en":"The row (2) stays the same, so the triangle only moved across. From B to E: C, D, E – that is 3 blocks right. You get 4 if you also count B."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Data, geld en waarskynlikheid","en":"Data, money and probability"},"topics":[{"id":"w5-t4-datahantering","title":{"af":"Datahantering","en":"Data handling"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal data kan versamel en met telmerke in ’n frekwensietabel kan sorteer, piktogramme en staafgrafieke kan teken en lees, die modus kan vind en gevolgtrekkings kan maak.","en":"You will be able to collect data and sort it with tally marks in a frequency table, draw and read pictographs and bar graphs, find the mode and draw conclusions."},"summary":{"af":"## Die datasiklus\n\n**Data** is inligting wat ons versamel, soos getalle, antwoorde of metings. Ons werk met data in ses stappe – die **datasiklus**:\n\n1. **Vra ’n vraag**, bv. *Watter vrug hou die leerders in ons graad die meeste van?*\n2. **Versamel** die data – met ’n **opname** (vraelys of hande opsteek), of deur te tel of te meet.\n3. **Sorteer** die data – met **telmerke** in ’n **frekwensietabel**.\n4. **Stel die data voor** – in ’n piktogram of staafgrafiek.\n5. **Lees en ontleed** die data – wat sê die grafiek?\n6. **Doen verslag** – skryf gevolgtrekkings in volsinne en beantwoord die vraag.\n\n’n Goeie opnamevraag is **duidelik** en het ’n beperkte aantal antwoorde. *Watter een van hierdie vier vrugte eet jy die graagste: appel, piesang, lemoen of druiwe?* is beter as *Wat eet jy graag?*, want die tweede vraag kan honderde verskillende antwoorde kry.\n\n## Telmerke en frekwensietabelle\n\nMet **telmerke** hou ons tel terwyl ons data versamel. Trek vier strepies en trek die vyfde strepie **skuins deur** die vier. Hier skryf ons so ’n bondel van 5 as ││││╱. So kan jy vinnig in vywe tel.\n\n30 leerders kies hul gunstelingvrug:\n\n| Vrug | Telmerke | Frekwensie |\n|---|---|---|\n| Appel | ││││╱ │││ | 8 |\n| Piesang | ││││╱ ││││╱ │ | 11 |\n| Lemoen | ││││╱ │ | 6 |\n| Druiwe | ││││╱ | 5 |\n| **Totaal** | | **30** |\n\nDie **frekwensie** is hoeveel keer iets voorkom. Tel die totaal om te kontroleer dat jy niemand uitgelaat het nie: 8 + 11 + 6 + 5 = 30. ✓\n\n## Piktogramme\n\n’n **Piktogram** gebruik prentjies of simbole. Een simbool kan **meer as een** voorstel – kyk altyd na die **sleutel**.\n\nSleutel: ● = 2 leerders en ◐ = 1 leerder\n\n| Vrug | Aantal leerders |\n|---|---|\n| Appel | ●●●● |\n| Piesang | ●●●●●◐ |\n| Lemoen | ●●● |\n| Druiwe | ●●◐ |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om net die simbole te tel. Piesang het 5½ simbole, maar elke heel simbool is 2 leerders: 5 × 2 + 1 = **11**, nie 6 nie.\n\n## Staafgrafieke\n\nIn ’n **staafgrafiek** wys die **lengte van elke staaf** die frekwensie. ’n Goeie staafgrafiek het:\n\n- ’n **titel** wat sê waaroor die grafiek gaan;\n- ’n **horisontale as** met die kategorieë (bv. die vrugte) en ’n byskrif;\n- ’n **vertikale as** met ’n **skaal** in gelyke stappe (bv. 0; 2; 4; 6 …) en ’n byskrif;\n- stawe wat **ewe breed** is, met **gelyke gapings** tussen hulle.\n\n’n **Dubbelstaafgrafiek** het **twee stawe** by elke kategorie, bv. een vir seuns en een vir dogters, met ’n **sleutel** wat sê watter kleur wie is. So kan jy twee groepe maklik vergelyk.\n\n## Die modus en gevolgtrekkings\n\nDie **modus** is die waarde wat **die meeste** voorkom. In die vrugte-data is die modus **piesang** (11 leerders). By getalle werk dit net so: die skoengroottes 4; 5; 5; 6; 5; 3; 4 het ’n modus van **5**, want 5 kom drie keer voor.\n\nSkryf **gevolgtrekkings** in volsinne:\n\n- Piesang is die gewildste vrug.\n- 3 meer leerders hou van piesang as van appels (11 − 8 = 3).\n- Die minste leerders hou van druiwe.\n\n> **Onthou:** Lees altyd die **titel, sleutel en skaal** voordat jy vrae oor ’n grafiek beantwoord.","en":"## The data cycle\n\n**Data** is information that we collect, like numbers, answers or measurements. We work with data in six steps – the **data cycle**:\n\n1. **Ask a question**, e.g. *Which fruit do the learners in our grade like most?*\n2. **Collect** the data – with a **survey** (questionnaire or a show of hands), or by counting or measuring.\n3. **Sort** the data – with **tally marks** in a **frequency table**.\n4. **Represent the data** – in a pictograph or bar graph.\n5. **Read and analyse** the data – what does the graph tell us?\n6. **Report** – write conclusions in full sentences and answer the question.\n\nA good survey question is **clear** and has a limited number of answers. *Which one of these four fruits do you like eating most: apple, banana, orange or grapes?* is better than *What do you like to eat?*, because the second question can get hundreds of different answers.\n\n## Tally marks and frequency tables\n\nWith **tally marks** we keep count while we collect data. Draw four lines and draw the fifth line **slanting through** the four. Here we write such a bundle of 5 as ││││╱. This way you can count quickly in fives.\n\n30 learners choose their favourite fruit:\n\n| Fruit | Tally marks | Frequency |\n|---|---|---|\n| Apple | ││││╱ │││ | 8 |\n| Banana | ││││╱ ││││╱ │ | 11 |\n| Orange | ││││╱ │ | 6 |\n| Grapes | ││││╱ | 5 |\n| **Total** | | **30** |\n\nThe **frequency** is how many times something occurs. Add up the total to check that you did not leave anyone out: 8 + 11 + 6 + 5 = 30. ✓\n\n## Pictographs\n\nA **pictograph** uses pictures or symbols. One symbol can stand for **more than one** – always look at the **key**.\n\nKey: ● = 2 learners and ◐ = 1 learner\n\n| Fruit | Number of learners |\n|---|---|\n| Apple | ●●●● |\n| Banana | ●●●●●◐ |\n| Orange | ●●● |\n| Grapes | ●●◐ |\n\n> **Common mistake:** Counting only the symbols. Banana has 5½ symbols, but each whole symbol is 2 learners: 5 × 2 + 1 = **11**, not 6.\n\n## Bar graphs\n\nIn a **bar graph** the **length of each bar** shows the frequency. A good bar graph has:\n\n- a **title** that says what the graph is about;\n- a **horizontal axis** with the categories (e.g. the fruits) and a label;\n- a **vertical axis** with a **scale** in equal steps (e.g. 0, 2, 4, 6 …) and a label;\n- bars that are **equally wide**, with **equal gaps** between them.\n\nA **double bar graph** has **two bars** for each category, e.g. one for boys and one for girls, with a **key** that says which colour is which. This way you can easily compare two groups.\n\n## The mode and conclusions\n\nThe **mode** is the value that occurs **most often**. In the fruit data the mode is **banana** (11 learners). With numbers it works the same way: the shoe sizes 4, 5, 5, 6, 5, 3, 4 have a mode of **5**, because 5 occurs three times.\n\nWrite **conclusions** in full sentences:\n\n- Banana is the most popular fruit.\n- 3 more learners like bananas than apples (11 − 8 = 3).\n- The fewest learners like grapes.\n\n> **Remember:** Always read the **title, key and scale** before you answer questions about a graph."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Data","en":"Data"},"def":{"af":"Inligting wat ons versamel, soos getalle, antwoorde of metings.","en":"Information that we collect, like numbers, answers or measurements."}},{"term":{"af":"Datasiklus","en":"Data cycle"},"def":{"af":"Die stappe om met data te werk: vra, versamel, sorteer, voorstel, ontleed en verslag doen.","en":"The steps for working with data: ask, collect, sort, represent, analyse and report."}},{"term":{"af":"Opname","en":"Survey"},"def":{"af":"’n Manier om data te versamel deur mense vrae te vra.","en":"A way of collecting data by asking people questions."}},{"term":{"af":"Telmerke","en":"Tally marks"},"def":{"af":"Strepies wat jy in bondels van vyf trek om te tel terwyl jy data versamel.","en":"Lines that you draw in bundles of five to keep count while you collect data."}},{"term":{"af":"Frekwensietabel","en":"Frequency table"},"def":{"af":"’n Tabel wat wys hoeveel keer elke antwoord of waarde voorkom.","en":"A table that shows how many times each answer or value occurs."}},{"term":{"af":"Piktogram","en":"Pictograph"},"def":{"af":"’n Grafiek wat data met prentjies of simbole wys.","en":"A graph that shows data with pictures or symbols."}},{"term":{"af":"Sleutel","en":"Key"},"def":{"af":"Sê wat elke simbool of kleur in ’n grafiek beteken, bv. ● = 2 leerders.","en":"Tells what each symbol or colour in a graph means, e.g. ● = 2 learners."}},{"term":{"af":"Staafgrafiek","en":"Bar graph"},"def":{"af":"’n Grafiek waarin die lengte van elke staaf die frekwensie wys.","en":"A graph in which the length of each bar shows the frequency."}},{"term":{"af":"Dubbelstaafgrafiek","en":"Double bar graph"},"def":{"af":"’n Staafgrafiek met twee stawe by elke kategorie om twee groepe te vergelyk.","en":"A bar graph with two bars for each category to compare two groups."}},{"term":{"af":"Modus","en":"Mode"},"def":{"af":"Die waarde of antwoord wat die meeste in ’n stel data voorkom.","en":"The value or answer that occurs most often in a set of data."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Maak ’n frekwensietabel","en":"Make a frequency table"},"problem":{"af":"Ravi vra 20 maats hoe hulle skool toe kom (S = stap, M = motor, T = taxi, B = bus). Die antwoorde is: S; M; T; S; B; S; M; T; S; S; M; B; T; S; M; S; T; S; M; B. Maak ’n frekwensietabel en vind die modus.","en":"Ravi asks 20 friends how they get to school (W = walk, C = car, T = taxi, B = bus). The answers are: W, C, T, W, B, W, C, T, W, W, C, B, T, W, C, W, T, W, C, B. Make a frequency table and find the mode."},"steps":[{"af":"Gaan een vir een deur die lys en trek ’n telmerk by die regte vervoer. Trek ’n lyn deur elke antwoord wat jy getel het.","en":"Go through the list one by one and draw a tally mark next to the right transport. Cross out each answer you have counted."},{"af":"Tel die telmerke: stap ││││╱ │││ = 8; motor ││││╱ = 5; taxi ││││ = 4; bus │││ = 3.","en":"Count the tally marks: walk ││││╱ │││ = 8; car ││││╱ = 5; taxi ││││ = 4; bus │││ = 3."},{"af":"Kontroleer die totaal: 8 + 5 + 4 + 3 = 20. ✓","en":"Check the total: 8 + 5 + 4 + 3 = 20. ✓"},{"af":"Die modus is die antwoord met die grootste frekwensie: stap (8).","en":"The mode is the answer with the biggest frequency: walk (8)."}],"answer":{"af":"Stap 8; motor 5; taxi 4; bus 3. Die modus is stap.","en":"Walk 8, car 5, taxi 4, bus 3. The mode is walk."}},{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n piktogram","en":"Read a pictograph"},"problem":{"af":"’n Piktogram wys hoeveel boeke uit die skoolbiblioteek uitgeneem is. Sleutel: ● = 4 boeke. Maandag ●●●; Dinsdag ●●◐; Woensdag ●●●●●; Donderdag ●◐. (a) Hoeveel boeke is Woensdag uitgeneem? (b) Hoeveel meer boeke is Maandag as Donderdag uitgeneem? (c) Hoeveel boeke altesaam?","en":"A pictograph shows how many books were taken out of the school library. Key: ● = 4 books. Monday ●●●, Tuesday ●●◐, Wednesday ●●●●●, Thursday ●◐. (a) How many books were taken out on Wednesday? (b) How many more books were taken out on Monday than on Thursday? (c) How many books altogether?"},"steps":[{"af":"Lees die sleutel: ● = 4, so ◐ (’n halwe simbool) = 2.","en":"Read the key: ● = 4, so ◐ (half a symbol) = 2."},{"af":"Maandag 3 × 4 = 12; Dinsdag 2 × 4 + 2 = 10; Woensdag 5 × 4 = 20; Donderdag 4 + 2 = 6.","en":"Monday 3 × 4 = 12; Tuesday 2 × 4 + 2 = 10; Wednesday 5 × 4 = 20; Thursday 4 + 2 = 6."},{"af":"(b) 12 − 6 = 6. (c) 12 + 10 + 20 + 6 = 48.","en":"(b) 12 − 6 = 6. (c) 12 + 10 + 20 + 6 = 48."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 20 boeke (b) 6 boeke meer (c) 48 boeke","en":"(a) 20 books (b) 6 more books (c) 48 books"}},{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n dubbelstaafgrafiek","en":"Read a double bar graph"},"problem":{"af":"’n Dubbelstaafgrafiek wys hoeveel seuns en dogters in Graad 5 elke sport speel: sokker – seuns 9, dogters 5; netbal – seuns 2, dogters 10; krieket – seuns 6, dogters 3; swem – seuns 4, dogters 4. (a) Watter sport speel die meeste dogters? (b) By watter sport is daar ewe veel seuns en dogters? (c) Hoeveel leerders speel sokker?","en":"A double bar graph shows how many boys and girls in Grade 5 play each sport: soccer – boys 9, girls 5; netball – boys 2, girls 10; cricket – boys 6, girls 3; swimming – boys 4, girls 4. (a) Which sport do most girls play? (b) In which sport are there as many boys as girls? (c) How many learners play soccer?"},"steps":[{"af":"Gebruik die sleutel om die dogters se stawe te vind. Die langste dogtersstaaf is by netbal (10).","en":"Use the key to find the girls’ bars. The longest girls’ bar is at netball (10)."},{"af":"Soek die kategorie waar albei stawe ewe lank is: swem (4 en 4).","en":"Look for the category where both bars are equally long: swimming (4 and 4)."},{"af":"Sokker: seuns plus dogters = 9 + 5 = 14.","en":"Soccer: boys plus girls = 9 + 5 = 14."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Netbal (b) Swem (c) 14 leerders","en":"(a) Netball (b) Swimming (c) 14 learners"}},{"title":{"af":"Teken ’n staafgrafiek","en":"Draw a bar graph"},"problem":{"af":"Teken ’n staafgrafiek van Ravi se data: stap 8; motor 5; taxi 4; bus 3. Watter stappe volg jy?","en":"Draw a bar graph of Ravi’s data: walk 8, car 5, taxi 4, bus 3. Which steps do you follow?"},"steps":[{"af":"Skryf ’n titel: *Hoe 20 leerders skool toe kom*.","en":"Write a title: *How 20 learners get to school*."},{"af":"Teken die horisontale as met die vier soorte vervoer en die byskrif *Vervoer*.","en":"Draw the horizontal axis with the four kinds of transport and the label *Transport*."},{"af":"Teken die vertikale as met die byskrif *Aantal leerders*. Die grootste getal is 8, so ’n skaal van 0 tot 10 in stappe van 1 of 2 werk goed.","en":"Draw the vertical axis with the label *Number of learners*. The biggest number is 8, so a scale from 0 to 10 in steps of 1 or 2 works well."},{"af":"Teken vier ewe breë stawe met gelyke gapings: stap tot by 8, motor tot by 5, taxi tot by 4 en bus tot by 3.","en":"Draw four equally wide bars with equal gaps: walk up to 8, car up to 5, taxi up to 4 and bus up to 3."}],"answer":{"af":"’n Staafgrafiek met ’n titel, twee benoemde asse, ’n skaal van 0 tot 10 en vier stawe (8; 5; 4; 3).","en":"A bar graph with a title, two labelled axes, a scale from 0 to 10 and four bars (8, 5, 4, 3)."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die eerste stap in die datasiklus?","en":"What is the first step in the data cycle?"},"options":[{"af":"Teken ’n grafiek","en":"Draw a graph"},{"af":"Versamel data","en":"Collect data"},{"af":"Vra ’n vraag","en":"Ask a question"},{"af":"Skryf ’n verslag","en":"Write a report"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Jy moet eers weet wat jy wil uitvind, dus begin jy met ’n vraag. Daarna versamel, sorteer en stel jy die data voor, en laastens doen jy verslag.","en":"You first need to know what you want to find out, so you start with a question. Then you collect, sort and represent the data, and finally you report."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In ’n piktogram stel elke simbool altyd net een ding voor.","en":"In a pictograph each symbol always stands for only one thing."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Een simbool kan 2; 5; 10 of meer voorstel. Die sleutel sê vir jou hoeveel.","en":"False. One symbol can stand for 2, 5, 10 or more. The key tells you how many."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel stel hierdie telmerke voor: ││││╱ ││││╱ ││","en":"How many do these tally marks show: ││││╱ ││││╱ ││"},"options":[{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"7","en":"7"},{"af":"12","en":"12"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Elke bondel met die skuins strepie is 5. Twee bondels is 10, plus 2 strepies is 12. 10 kry jy as jy die skuins strepies vergeet.","en":"Each bundle with the slanting line is 5. Two bundles are 10, plus 2 lines is 12. You get 10 if you forget the slanting lines."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die ___ is die waarde wat die meeste in ’n stel data voorkom.","en":"The ___ is the value that occurs most often in a set of data."},"answers":{"af":["modus"],"en":["mode"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["totaal","frekwensie","sleutel"],"en":["total","frequency","key"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die modus is die waarde met die grootste frekwensie. Die frekwensie self is hoeveel keer iets voorkom.","en":"The mode is the value with the biggest frequency. The frequency itself is how many times something occurs."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In ’n piktogram is ● = 4 motors. ’n Ry wys ●●●◐. Hoeveel motors is dit?","en":"In a pictograph ● = 4 cars. A row shows ●●●◐. How many cars is that?"},"options":[{"af":"14","en":"14"},{"af":"4","en":"4"},{"af":"16","en":"16"},{"af":"7","en":"7"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Drie heel simbole is 3 × 4 = 12. ’n Halwe simbool is die helfte van 4, dus 2. 12 + 2 = 14. 16 kry jy as jy die halwe simbool as ’n heel een tel.","en":"Three whole symbols are 3 × 4 = 12. A half symbol is half of 4, so 2. 12 + 2 = 14. You get 16 if you count the half symbol as a whole one."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die skoengroottes van 9 kinders is: 3; 5; 4; 6; 4; 5; 4; 7; 3. Wat is die modus?","en":"The shoe sizes of 9 children are: 3, 5, 4, 6, 4, 5, 4, 7, 3. What is the mode?"},"options":[{"af":"5","en":"5"},{"af":"4","en":"4"},{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"7","en":"7"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Tel elke grootte: 3 kom twee keer voor, 4 drie keer, 5 twee keer, 6 en 7 een keer elk. 4 kom die meeste voor, so die modus is 4. 7 is net die grootste getal.","en":"Count each size: 3 occurs twice, 4 three times, 5 twice, 6 and 7 once each. 4 occurs most often, so the mode is 4. 7 is just the biggest number."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke woord by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each word to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Telmerke","en":"Tally marks"},"r":{"af":"Strepies om te tel terwyl jy data versamel","en":"Lines to keep count while you collect data"}},{"l":{"af":"Frekwensie","en":"Frequency"},"r":{"af":"Hoeveel keer iets voorkom","en":"How many times something occurs"}},{"l":{"af":"Sleutel","en":"Key"},"r":{"af":"Sê wat elke simbool of kleur beteken","en":"Tells what each symbol or colour means"}},{"l":{"af":"Modus","en":"Mode"},"r":{"af":"Die waarde wat die meeste voorkom","en":"The value that occurs most often"}},{"l":{"af":"Titel","en":"Title"},"r":{"af":"Sê waaroor die grafiek gaan","en":"Says what the graph is about"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hierdie woorde help jou om data te sorteer (telmerke, frekwensie) en grafieke te lees (sleutel, titel). Die modus is die gewildste waarde.","en":"These words help you to sort data (tally marks, frequency) and read graphs (key, title). The mode is the most popular value."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarvoor is ’n dubbelstaafgrafiek die nuttigste?","en":"What is a double bar graph most useful for?"},"options":[{"af":"Om net een groep se data te wys","en":"To show only one group’s data"},{"af":"Om twee groepe se data langs mekaar te vergelyk","en":"To compare two groups’ data side by side"},{"af":"Om data met telmerke te tel","en":"To count data with tally marks"},{"af":"Om ’n vraag vir ’n opname te kies","en":"To choose a question for a survey"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Dubbelstaafgrafiek het twee stawe by elke kategorie, bv. seuns en dogters, sodat jy die twee groepe maklik kan vergelyk.","en":"A double bar graph has two bars for each category, e.g. boys and girls, so that you can easily compare the two groups."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In ’n frekwensietabel is appel 8, piesang 11, lemoen 6 en druiwe 5. Altesaam is daar ___ leerders.","en":"In a frequency table apple is 8, banana 11, orange 6 and grapes 5. Altogether there are ___ learners."},"answers":{"af":["30"],"en":["30"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["11","29","4"],"en":["11","29","4"]}},"explain":{"af":"Tel al die frekwensies bymekaar: 8 + 11 + 6 + 5 = 30. 11 is die modus se frekwensie en 4 is die aantal vrugte.","en":"Add all the frequencies: 8 + 11 + 6 + 5 = 30. 11 is the frequency of the mode and 4 is the number of fruits."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op ’n staafgrafiek tel die vertikale as in tweë (0; 2; 4; 6; 8; 10). Die staaf vir netbal eindig halfpad tussen 6 en 8. Hoeveel leerders speel netbal?","en":"On a bar graph the vertical axis counts in twos (0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10). The bar for netball ends halfway between 6 and 8. How many learners play netball?"},"options":[{"af":"7","en":"7"},{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"8","en":"8"},{"af":"14","en":"14"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Halfpad tussen 6 en 8 is 7. Lees die skaal mooi: die merke spring met 2, so daar is ’n waarde tussen elke twee getalle.","en":"Halfway between 6 and 8 is 7. Read the scale carefully: the marks jump by 2, so there is a value between each two numbers."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"30 leerders kies hul gunsteling-troeteldier: hond 12, kat 9, vis 3, voël 6. Watter gevolgtrekking is korrek?","en":"30 learners choose their favourite pet: dog 12, cat 9, fish 3, bird 6. Which conclusion is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Die meeste leerders hou van katte","en":"Most learners like cats"},{"af":"Twee keer soveel leerders hou van voëls as van honde","en":"Twice as many learners like birds as dogs"},{"af":"Vis is die modus","en":"Fish is the mode"},{"af":"Vier keer soveel leerders hou van honde as van visse","en":"Four times as many learners like dogs as fish"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"12 = 4 × 3, dus kies vier keer soveel leerders honde as visse. Die modus is hond (12), nie kat of vis nie. Dit is honde wat twee keer soveel as voëls is (12 = 2 × 6), nie andersom nie.","en":"12 = 4 × 3, so four times as many learners chose dogs as fish. The mode is dog (12), not cat or fish. It is dogs that are twice as many as birds (12 = 2 × 6), not the other way round."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Staafgrafiek moet ’n titel en byskrifte op albei asse hê.","en":"A bar graph must have a title and labels on both axes."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Sonder ’n titel en byskrifte weet die leser nie waaroor die grafiek gaan of wat die getalle beteken nie.","en":"True. Without a title and labels the reader does not know what the graph is about or what the numbers mean."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy teken ’n staafgrafiek van data wat van 0 tot 40 gaan. Watter skaal op die vertikale as is die beste?","en":"You draw a bar graph of data that goes from 0 to 40. Which scale on the vertical axis is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Tel met 1 op ’n slag (0; 1; 2; 3 …)","en":"Count by 1 at a time (0, 1, 2, 3 …)"},{"af":"Tel met 100 op ’n slag (0; 100; 200 …)","en":"Count by 100 at a time (0, 100, 200 …)"},{"af":"Tel met 5 op ’n slag (0; 5; 10 … 40)","en":"Count by 5 at a time (0, 5, 10 … 40)"},{"af":"Gebruik ongelyke stappe (0; 2; 10; 40)","en":"Use unequal steps (0, 2, 10, 40)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Met stappe van 5 pas 0 tot 40 netjies op die as (8 stappe). Stappe van 1 is te veel merke, 100 is te groot en ongelyke stappe maak die grafiek verkeerd.","en":"With steps of 5, 0 to 40 fits neatly on the axis (8 steps). Steps of 1 are too many marks, 100 is too big and unequal steps make the graph wrong."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In ’n piktogram is ● = 10 leerders. ’n Ry met ●●●●◐ stel ___ leerders voor.","en":"In a pictograph ● = 10 learners. A row with ●●●●◐ stands for ___ learners."},"answers":{"af":["45"],"en":["45"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["5","50","41"],"en":["5","50","41"]}},"explain":{"af":"Vier heel simbole is 4 × 10 = 40 en ’n halwe simbool is 5. 40 + 5 = 45.","en":"Four whole symbols are 4 × 10 = 40 and a half symbol is 5. 40 + 5 = 45."}}]},{"id":"w5-t4-geld-finansies","title":{"af":"Geld en finansies","en":"Money and finance"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal geldbedrae korrek kan skryf, geld kan optel en aftrek, kleingeld en die koste van ’n aantal items kan bereken, wins en verlies kan uitwerk en ’n eenvoudige begroting kan maak.","en":"You will be able to write amounts of money correctly, add and subtract money, work out change and the cost of a number of items, calculate profit and loss, and make a simple budget."},"summary":{"af":"## Rand en sent\n\nSuid-Afrika se geld is die **rand (R)**. Een rand bestaan uit 100 **sent (c)**:\n\n**100 c = R1**\n\nOns het muntstukke soos 10c; 20c; 50c; R1; R2 en R5, en note van R10; R20; R50; R100 en R200.\n\n| Bedrag | Ons skryf | Ons sê |\n|---|---|---|\n| 12 rand en 50 sent | R12,50 | twaalf rand vyftig |\n| 75 sent | 75c of R0,75 | vyf-en-sewentig sent |\n| 5 sent | 5c of R0,05 | vyf sent |\n| 3 rand | R3 of R3,00 | drie rand |\n\nDie sent kry altyd **twee syfers** ná die komma: R4,50 (nie R4,5 nie) en R4,05 (vier rand en vyf sent).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie R en c saam gebruik nie. Skryf R2,50 of 250c, maar nooit R2,50c nie.\n\n## Optel, aftrek en kleingeld\n\nHou die **kommas onder mekaar** as jy in kolomme werk, of tel eers die rande en dan die sent bymekaar:\n\n- R23,40 + R15,80: rande 23 + 15 = R38; sent 40c + 80c = 120c = R1,20. Totaal: **R39,20**.\n\n**Kleingeld** bereken jy deur af te trek, of deur **op te tel** soos ’n kassier. Lerato koop ’n boek vir R37,50 en betaal met R50:\n\n1. R37,50 tot R38,00 is 50c.\n2. R38,00 tot R40,00 is R2.\n3. R40,00 tot R50,00 is R10.\n4. Kleingeld: 50c + R2 + R10 = **R12,50**. Kontroleer: R37,50 + R12,50 = R50. ✓\n\n## Koste van ’n aantal items\n\nVermenigvuldig die prys van een item met die aantal items. Breek die prys op in rande en sent:\n\n- 6 koeldranke van R8,50 elk: 6 × R8 = R48 en 6 × 50c = 300c = R3. Totaal: **R51**.\n\nSkat eers: R8,50 is amper R9, en 6 × R9 = R54. Die antwoord moet dus ’n bietjie minder as R54 wees.\n\n**Hoeveel kan ek koop?** ’n Lekker kos R2,50. Hoeveel lekkers kan jy met R20 koop? 2 lekkers kos R5, so 4 lekkers kos R10 en **8 lekkers** kos R20. Kontroleer: 8 × R2 = R16 en 8 × 50c = R4, so R16 + R4 = R20. ✓\n\n## Wins en verlies\n\n- Die **koopprys** (kosprys) is wat jy betaal om iets te koop of te maak.\n- Die **verkoopprys** is die prys waarvoor jy dit verkoop.\n- **Wins** = verkoopprys − koopprys, as jy vir **meer** verkoop as wat dit gekos het.\n- **Verlies** = koopprys − verkoopprys, as jy vir **minder** verkoop.\n\nBy die skool se **tuisnywerheid** bak Zanele 24 muffins. Die bestanddele kos R60. Sy verkoop elke muffin vir R4: 24 × R4 = R96. Haar **wins** is R96 − R60 = **R36**.\n\n> **Onthou:** Jy maak eers wins as jy al jou koste terugverdien het. As Zanele net 12 muffins verkoop (12 × R4 = R48), het sy ’n **verlies** van R60 − R48 = R12.\n\n## Begroting en spaar\n\n’n **Begroting** is ’n plan vir jou geld: hoeveel jy **inkry** (inkomste) en hoeveel jy **uitgee** (uitgawes). Dink eers aan **behoeftes** – dinge wat jy regtig nodig het, soos kos en skoolklere – en dan aan **wense** – dinge wat lekker is om te hê, soos speletjies.\n\nAisha kry R50 sakgeld per week. Sy gee R20 uit aan skoolkos, R10 aan ’n strokiesboek en **spaar** die res: R50 − R20 − R10 = **R20**. Spaar sy so vir 5 weke, het sy 5 × R20 = R100.\n\nGeld in ’n **spaarrekening** by die bank is veilig, en die bank betaal jou ’n bietjie **rente** daarop.","en":"## Rand and cents\n\nSouth Africa’s money is the **rand (R)**. One rand is made up of 100 **cents (c)**:\n\n**100 c = R1**\n\nWe have coins such as 10c, 20c, 50c, R1, R2 and R5, and notes of R10, R20, R50, R100 and R200.\n\n| Amount | We write | We say |\n|---|---|---|\n| 12 rand and 50 cents | R12.50 | twelve rand fifty |\n| 75 cents | 75c or R0.75 | seventy-five cents |\n| 5 cents | 5c or R0.05 | five cents |\n| 3 rand | R3 or R3.00 | three rand |\n\nThe cents always get **two digits** after the decimal point: R4.50 (not R4.5) and R4.05 (four rand and five cents).\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not use R and c together. Write R2.50 or 250c, but never R2.50c.\n\n## Adding, subtracting and change\n\nKeep the **decimal points under each other** when you work in columns, or first add the rands and then the cents:\n\n- R23.40 + R15.80: rands 23 + 15 = R38; cents 40c + 80c = 120c = R1.20. Total: **R39.20**.\n\nYou work out **change** by subtracting, or by **counting up** like a cashier. Lerato buys a book for R37.50 and pays with R50:\n\n1. R37.50 to R38.00 is 50c.\n2. R38.00 to R40.00 is R2.\n3. R40.00 to R50.00 is R10.\n4. Change: 50c + R2 + R10 = **R12.50**. Check: R37.50 + R12.50 = R50. ✓\n\n## Cost of a number of items\n\nMultiply the price of one item by the number of items. Break the price up into rands and cents:\n\n- 6 cooldrinks at R8.50 each: 6 × R8 = R48 and 6 × 50c = 300c = R3. Total: **R51**.\n\nEstimate first: R8.50 is almost R9, and 6 × R9 = R54. So the answer must be a little less than R54.\n\n**How many can I buy?** A sweet costs R2.50. How many sweets can you buy with R20? 2 sweets cost R5, so 4 sweets cost R10 and **8 sweets** cost R20. Check: 8 × R2 = R16 and 8 × 50c = R4, so R16 + R4 = R20. ✓\n\n## Profit and loss\n\n- The **cost price** is what you pay to buy or make something.\n- The **selling price** is the price you sell it for.\n- **Profit** = selling price − cost price, when you sell for **more** than it cost.\n- **Loss** = cost price − selling price, when you sell for **less**.\n\nAt the school **market day** Zanele bakes 24 muffins. The ingredients cost R60. She sells each muffin for R4: 24 × R4 = R96. Her **profit** is R96 − R60 = **R36**.\n\n> **Remember:** You only make a profit once you have earned back all your costs. If Zanele sells only 12 muffins (12 × R4 = R48), she makes a **loss** of R60 − R48 = R12.\n\n## Budgeting and saving\n\nA **budget** is a plan for your money: how much you **get** (income) and how much you **spend** (expenses). Think first about **needs** – things you really need, like food and school clothes – and then about **wants** – things that are nice to have, like games.\n\nAisha gets R50 pocket money per week. She spends R20 on school lunch, R10 on a comic book and **saves** the rest: R50 − R20 − R10 = **R20**. If she saves like this for 5 weeks, she has 5 × R20 = R100.\n\nMoney in a **savings account** at the bank is safe, and the bank pays you a little **interest** on it."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Rand (R)","en":"Rand (R)"},"def":{"af":"Suid-Afrika se geldeenheid; R1 = 100c.","en":"South Africa’s unit of money; R1 = 100c."}},{"term":{"af":"Sent (c)","en":"Cent (c)"},"def":{"af":"’n Klein deel van ’n rand; 100 sent maak een rand.","en":"A small part of a rand; 100 cents make one rand."}},{"term":{"af":"Kleingeld","en":"Change"},"def":{"af":"Die geld wat jy terugkry as jy met meer betaal as wat iets kos.","en":"The money you get back when you pay more than something costs."}},{"term":{"af":"Koopprys (kosprys)","en":"Cost price"},"def":{"af":"Wat jy betaal om iets te koop of te maak.","en":"What you pay to buy or make something."}},{"term":{"af":"Verkoopprys","en":"Selling price"},"def":{"af":"Die prys waarvoor jy iets aan iemand anders verkoop.","en":"The price for which you sell something to someone else."}},{"term":{"af":"Wins","en":"Profit"},"def":{"af":"Die geld wat jy verdien as die verkoopprys meer as die koopprys is.","en":"The money you earn when the selling price is more than the cost price."}},{"term":{"af":"Verlies","en":"Loss"},"def":{"af":"Die geld wat jy verloor as die verkoopprys minder as die koopprys is.","en":"The money you lose when the selling price is less than the cost price."}},{"term":{"af":"Begroting","en":"Budget"},"def":{"af":"’n Plan wat wys hoeveel geld jy inkry, uitgee en spaar.","en":"A plan that shows how much money you get, spend and save."}},{"term":{"af":"Behoeftes en wense","en":"Needs and wants"},"def":{"af":"Behoeftes is dinge wat jy regtig nodig het; wense is dinge wat lekker is om te hê.","en":"Needs are things you really need; wants are things that are nice to have."}},{"term":{"af":"Spaar","en":"Save"},"def":{"af":"Om geld eenkant te sit vir later in plaas daarvan om dit nou uit te gee.","en":"To put money aside for later instead of spending it now."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Hoeveel kleingeld?","en":"How much change?"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho koop ’n brood vir R18,90 en melk vir R24,50. Hy betaal met ’n R50-noot. Hoeveel kleingeld kry hy?","en":"Sipho buys a loaf of bread for R18.90 and milk for R24.50. He pays with a R50 note. How much change does he get?"},"steps":[{"af":"Skat: omtrent R19 + R25 = R44, so die kleingeld is omtrent R6.","en":"Estimate: about R19 + R25 = R44, so the change is about R6."},{"af":"Totaal: rande 18 + 24 = R42; sent 90c + 50c = 140c = R1,40. R42 + R1,40 = R43,40.","en":"Total: rands 18 + 24 = R42; cents 90c + 50c = 140c = R1.40. R42 + R1.40 = R43.40."},{"af":"Tel op tot R50: R43,40 tot R44,00 is 60c; R44 tot R50 is R6. Kleingeld: R6,60.","en":"Count up to R50: R43.40 to R44.00 is 60c; R44 to R50 is R6. Change: R6.60."},{"af":"Kontroleer: R43,40 + R6,60 = R50. ✓ Dit pas by die skatting.","en":"Check: R43.40 + R6.60 = R50. ✓ This fits the estimate."}],"answer":{"af":"Sipho kry R6,60 kleingeld.","en":"Sipho gets R6.60 change."}},{"title":{"af":"Kaartjies vir die hele klas","en":"Tickets for the whole class"},"problem":{"af":"’n Kaartjie vir die skoolkonsert kos R12,50. Hoeveel kos kaartjies vir 28 leerders?","en":"A ticket for the school concert costs R12.50. How much do tickets for 28 learners cost?"},"steps":[{"af":"Breek die prys op: R12,50 = R12 + 50c.","en":"Break up the price: R12.50 = R12 + 50c."},{"af":"28 × R12 = R336 (20 × 12 = 240 en 8 × 12 = 96).","en":"28 × R12 = R336 (20 × 12 = 240 and 8 × 12 = 96)."},{"af":"28 × 50c = 1 400c = R14.","en":"28 × 50c = 1 400c = R14."},{"af":"Tel bymekaar: R336 + R14 = R350. Kontroleer: 4 kaartjies kos R50, en 28 ÷ 4 = 7, so 7 × R50 = R350. ✓","en":"Add: R336 + R14 = R350. Check: 4 tickets cost R50, and 28 ÷ 4 = 7, so 7 × R50 = R350. ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"R350","en":"R350"}},{"title":{"af":"Wins of verlies by die tuisnywerheid?","en":"Profit or loss at the market day?"},"problem":{"af":"Zanele bak 24 muffins vir die skool se tuisnywerheid. Die bestanddele kos R60. Sy verkoop elke muffin vir R4. (a) Wat is haar wins as sy al die muffins verkoop? (b) Wat gebeur as sy net 12 verkoop?","en":"Zanele bakes 24 muffins for the school market day. The ingredients cost R60. She sells each muffin for R4. (a) What is her profit if she sells all the muffins? (b) What happens if she sells only 12?"},"steps":[{"af":"Koopprys (koste): R60.","en":"Cost price (costs): R60."},{"af":"(a) Verkoopprys: 24 × R4 = R96. Wins = R96 − R60 = R36.","en":"(a) Selling price: 24 × R4 = R96. Profit = R96 − R60 = R36."},{"af":"(b) Verkoopprys: 12 × R4 = R48. Dit is minder as R60, so sy maak ’n verlies: R60 − R48 = R12.","en":"(b) Selling price: 12 × R4 = R48. This is less than R60, so she makes a loss: R60 − R48 = R12."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) R36 wins (b) R12 verlies","en":"(a) R36 profit (b) R12 loss"}},{"title":{"af":"Spaar vir ’n sokkerbal","en":"Saving for a soccer ball"},"problem":{"af":"Ravi kry R40 sakgeld per week. Hy gee R15 aan snoepgoed en R10 aan lugtyd uit en spaar die res. ’n Sokkerbal kos R120. Hoeveel weke moet hy spaar?","en":"Ravi gets R40 pocket money per week. He spends R15 on snacks and R10 on airtime and saves the rest. A soccer ball costs R120. How many weeks must he save?"},"steps":[{"af":"Uitgawes per week: R15 + R10 = R25.","en":"Expenses per week: R15 + R10 = R25."},{"af":"Spaargeld per week: R40 − R25 = R15.","en":"Savings per week: R40 − R25 = R15."},{"af":"Aantal weke: R120 ÷ R15 = 8. Kontroleer: 8 × R15 = R120. ✓","en":"Number of weeks: R120 ÷ R15 = 8. Check: 8 × R15 = R120. ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"8 weke","en":"8 weeks"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"R1 = ___ c","en":"R1 = ___ c"},"answers":{"af":["100"],"en":["100"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["10","1 000","50"],"en":["10","1 000","50"]}},"explain":{"af":"Een rand is 100 sent. Daarom het ’n bedrag soos R4,05 altyd twee syfers vir die sent.","en":"One rand is 100 cents. That is why an amount like R4.05 always has two digits for the cents."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe skryf ons sewe rand en vyf sent?","en":"How do we write seven rand and five cents?"},"options":[{"af":"R7,05","en":"R7.05"},{"af":"R7,5","en":"R7.5"},{"af":"R7,50","en":"R7.50"},{"af":"R75","en":"R75"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die sent kry twee syfers: 5 sent is 05. R7,50 is sewe rand en vyftig sent, en R7,5 is nie ’n korrekte manier om geld te skryf nie.","en":"The cents get two digits: 5 cents is 05. R7.50 is seven rand and fifty cents, and R7.5 is not a correct way to write money."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo koop ’n pastei vir R23,50 en betaal met ’n R50-noot. Hoeveel kleingeld kry hy?","en":"Thabo buys a pie for R23.50 and pays with a R50 note. How much change does he get?"},"options":[{"af":"R27,50","en":"R27.50"},{"af":"R73,50","en":"R73.50"},{"af":"R26,00","en":"R26.00"},{"af":"R26,50","en":"R26.50"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Tel op: R23,50 tot R24 is 50c; R24 tot R50 is R26. Kleingeld: R26,50. Kontroleer: R23,50 + R26,50 = R50. R73,50 kry jy as jy optel in plaas van aftrek.","en":"Count up: R23.50 to R24 is 50c; R24 to R50 is R26. Change: R26.50. Check: R23.50 + R26.50 = R50. You get R73.50 if you add instead of subtract."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"R2,50c is die regte manier om twee rand vyftig te skryf.","en":"R2.50c is the correct way to write two rand fifty."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Gebruik óf R óf c, nie albei nie: R2,50 of 250c.","en":"False. Use either R or c, not both: R2.50 or 250c."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Een pen kos R6,50. Hoeveel kos 4 penne?","en":"One pen costs R6.50. How much do 4 pens cost?"},"options":[{"af":"R24,50","en":"R24.50"},{"af":"R26,00","en":"R26.00"},{"af":"R26,50","en":"R26.50"},{"af":"R24,20","en":"R24.20"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"4 × R6 = R24 en 4 × 50c = 200c = R2. R24 + R2 = R26,00. R24,50 kry jy as jy vergeet om die sent ook met 4 te vermenigvuldig.","en":"4 × R6 = R24 and 4 × 50c = 200c = R2. R24 + R2 = R26.00. You get R24.50 if you forget to multiply the cents by 4 as well."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke woord by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each word to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Koopprys","en":"Cost price"},"r":{"af":"Wat jy betaal om iets te koop of te maak","en":"What you pay to buy or make something"}},{"l":{"af":"Verkoopprys","en":"Selling price"},"r":{"af":"Die prys waarvoor jy iets verkoop","en":"The price you sell something for"}},{"l":{"af":"Wins","en":"Profit"},"r":{"af":"Jy verkoop vir meer as wat dit gekos het","en":"You sell for more than it cost"}},{"l":{"af":"Verlies","en":"Loss"},"r":{"af":"Jy verkoop vir minder as wat dit gekos het","en":"You sell for less than it cost"}},{"l":{"af":"Begroting","en":"Budget"},"r":{"af":"’n Plan vir hoe jy jou geld gaan gebruik","en":"A plan for how you will use your money"}}],"explain":{"af":"Wins en verlies hang af van die verskil tussen die verkoopprys en die koopprys. ’n Begroting help jou om jou geld vooraf te beplan.","en":"Profit and loss depend on the difference between the selling price and the cost price. A budget helps you to plan your money ahead."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Nomsa koop ’n sak lemoene vir R45 en verkoop die lemoene vir altesaam R72. Wat is haar wins?","en":"Nomsa buys a bag of oranges for R45 and sells the oranges for R72 altogether. What is her profit?"},"options":[{"af":"R117","en":"R117"},{"af":"R37","en":"R37"},{"af":"R27","en":"R27"},{"af":"R33","en":"R33"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Wins = verkoopprys − koopprys = R72 − R45 = R27. R117 is die twee bedrae bymekaar getel. R33 kry jy as jy nie leen nie en in die ene-kolom 5 − 2 doen, en R37 as jy leen maar vergeet om die tiene een minder te maak.","en":"Profit = selling price − cost price = R72 − R45 = R27. R117 is the two amounts added together. You get R33 if you do not borrow and do 5 − 2 in the units column, and R37 if you borrow but forget to make the tens one less."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is R15,60 + R8,70?","en":"What is R15.60 + R8.70?"},"options":[{"af":"R23,30","en":"R23.30"},{"af":"R23,130","en":"R23.130"},{"af":"R24,30","en":"R24.30"},{"af":"R6,90","en":"R6.90"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Rande: 15 + 8 = R23. Sent: 60c + 70c = 130c = R1,30. R23 + R1,30 = R24,30. As jy die 130c nie na R1,30 omskakel nie, kry jy ’n verkeerde antwoord.","en":"Rands: 15 + 8 = R23. Cents: 60c + 70c = 130c = R1.30. R23 + R1.30 = R24.30. If you do not change 130c into R1.30, you get a wrong answer."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"50c + 50c + R2 + R5 = R___","en":"50c + 50c + R2 + R5 = R___"},"answers":{"af":["8","8,00"],"en":["8","8.00"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["7,50","107","6"],"en":["7.50","107","6"]}},"explain":{"af":"50c + 50c = 100c = R1. R1 + R2 + R5 = R8. 107 kry jy as jy sent en rande bymekaar tel sonder om eers om te skakel.","en":"50c + 50c = 100c = R1. R1 + R2 + R5 = R8. You get 107 if you add cents and rands together without converting first."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter koop ’n fiets vir R800 en verkoop dit later vir R650. Wat is die resultaat?","en":"Pieter buys a bicycle for R800 and later sells it for R650. What is the result?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Verlies van R150","en":"A loss of R150"},{"af":"’n Wins van R150","en":"A profit of R150"},{"af":"’n Verlies van R250","en":"A loss of R250"},{"af":"’n Wins van R1 450","en":"A profit of R1 450"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Hy het vir minder verkoop as wat hy betaal het, so dit is ’n verlies: R800 − R650 = R150.","en":"He sold for less than he paid, so it is a loss: R800 − R650 = R150."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Begroting help jou om te beplan hoeveel geld jy uitgee en hoeveel jy spaar.","en":"A budget helps you to plan how much money you spend and how much you save."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Begroting wys jou inkomste en uitgawes, sodat jy kan sien hoeveel oorbly om te spaar.","en":"True. A budget shows your income and expenses, so that you can see how much is left to save."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Anika spaar R25 per week. Hoeveel weke neem dit om R200 vir ’n paar tekkies te spaar?","en":"Anika saves R25 per week. How many weeks does it take to save R200 for a pair of sneakers?"},"options":[{"af":"5","en":"5"},{"af":"25","en":"25"},{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"8","en":"8"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"R200 ÷ R25 = 8 weke. Kontroleer: 8 × R25 = R200. ✓","en":"R200 ÷ R25 = 8 weeks. Check: 8 × R25 = R200. ✓"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n behoefte en nie ’n wens nie?","en":"Which one is a need and not a want?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Nuwe videospeletjie","en":"A new video game"},{"af":"Kos vir die huis","en":"Food for the home"},{"af":"’n Duur sonbril","en":"Expensive sunglasses"},{"af":"’n Tweede sokkerbal","en":"A second soccer ball"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Kos is iets wat jy regtig nodig het om te lewe – ’n behoefte. Die ander is lekker om te hê, maar jy kan sonder hulle klaarkom.","en":"Food is something you really need to live – a need. The others are nice to have, but you can manage without them."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die klas bak 30 koekies wat altesaam R45 kos om te maak. Hulle verkoop elkeen vir R3. Hul wins is R___.","en":"The class bakes 30 biscuits that cost R45 altogether to make. They sell each one for R3. Their profit is R___."},"answers":{"af":["45","45,00"],"en":["45","45.00"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["90","135","42"],"en":["90","135","42"]}},"explain":{"af":"Verkoopprys: 30 × R3 = R90. Wins = R90 − R45 = R45. R90 is wat hulle inkry, nie hul wins nie.","en":"Selling price: 30 × R3 = R90. Profit = R90 − R45 = R45. R90 is what they take in, not their profit."}}]},{"id":"w5-t4-waarskynlikheid","title":{"af":"Waarskynlikheid","en":"Probability"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan sê of ’n gebeurtenis seker, waarskynlik, ewe waarskynlik, onwaarskynlik of onmoontlik is, moontlike uitkomste kan lys, uitslae met telmerke kan aanteken en voorspellings met uitslae kan vergelyk.","en":"You will be able to say whether an event is certain, likely, equally likely, unlikely or impossible, list possible outcomes, record results with tally marks and compare predictions with results."},"summary":{"af":"## Hoe waarskynlik is dit?\n\n**Waarskynlikheid** sê hoe groot die kans is dat iets sal gebeur. Ons gebruik vyf woorde, van geen kans nie tot ’n volle kans:\n\n**onmoontlik → onwaarskynlik → ewe waarskynlik → waarskynlik → seker**\n\nKyk hoe hulle werk as jy een keer met ’n gewone dobbelsteen (getalle 1 tot 6) gooi:\n\n| Woord | Betekenis | Voorbeeld met ’n dobbelsteen |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Onmoontlik** | dit kan nooit gebeur nie | jy gooi ’n 7 |\n| **Onwaarskynlik** | dit kan gebeur, maar die kans is klein | jy gooi ’n 6 (net 1 van die 6 getalle) |\n| **Ewe waarskynlik** | dit is net so waarskynlik dat dit gebeur as dat dit nie gebeur nie | jy gooi ’n ewe getal (2; 4; 6 – 3 van die 6) |\n| **Waarskynlik** | die kans is groot | jy gooi ’n getal groter as 2 (4 van die 6) |\n| **Seker** | dit sal beslis gebeur | jy gooi ’n getal kleiner as 7 |\n\n## Moontlike uitkomste\n\n’n **Uitkoms** is een moontlike resultaat. Lys altyd **al** die moontlike uitkomste en tel hulle:\n\n- ’n **Muntstuk**: 2 uitkomste – kop (K) of stert (S).\n- ’n **Dobbelsteen**: 6 uitkomste – 1; 2; 3; 4; 5; 6.\n- ’n **Spinner** met 4 gelyke dele (rooi, blou, groen, geel): 4 uitkomste.\n- **Twee muntstukke** saam: KK; KS; SK; SS – 4 uitkomste. Kop op die eerste en stert op die tweede (KS) is ’n ander uitkoms as andersom (SK).\n\nAs die dele van ’n spinner **ewe groot** is, is elke kleur ewe waarskynlik. Maar by ’n spinner met 3 rooi dele en 1 blou deel is rooi **waarskynlik** en blou **onwaarskynlik**, want rooi bedek meer van die spinner.\n\n## Kanse vergelyk\n\nIn ’n sak is 5 rooi albasters en 2 groen albasters. Jy haal een uit sonder om te kyk. Daar is meer rooi as groen albasters, so rooi is **waarskynliker** as groen. Om ’n blou albaster uit te haal, is **onmoontlik**, want daar is geen blou albasters in die sak nie. Tel altyd hoeveel kanse elke uitkoms het en vergelyk dan.\n\n## Eksperimente en telmerke\n\nIn ’n **eksperiment** doen jy dieselfde ding baie kere en teken elke uitslag met **telmerke** in ’n tabel aan. Lerato gooi ’n muntstuk 20 keer:\n\n| Uitkoms | Telmerke | Frekwensie |\n|---|---|---|\n| Kop | ││││╱ ││││╱ ││ | 12 |\n| Stert | ││││╱ │││ | 8 |\n| **Totaal** | | **20** |\n\n## Voorspel en vergelyk\n\nVoor die eksperiment **voorspel** Lerato: kop en stert is ewe waarskynlik, so sy verwag omtrent 10 kop en 10 stert (20 ÷ 2). Sy kry 12 kop en 8 stert. Was sy verkeerd? **Nee!** ’n Voorspelling sê wat ons **omtrent** verwag. Die werklike uitslae verskil gewoonlik ’n bietjie. Hoe **meer kere** jy die eksperiment doen, hoe nader kom die uitslae gewoonlik aan half-half.\n\nMet ’n dobbelsteen werk dit net so: gooi jy 30 keer, verwag jy elke getal omtrent 30 ÷ 6 = **5 keer**.\n\n> **Onthou:** ’n Muntstuk het geen geheue nie. Al het jy 3 keer na mekaar kop gegooi, is kop en stert by die volgende gooi steeds ewe waarskynlik.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om te dink *ewe waarskynlik* beteken jy kry presies die helfte. As jy 10 keer gooi, kan jy 6 kop en 4 stert kry – dit is heeltemal normaal.","en":"## How likely is it?\n\n**Probability** tells how big the chance is that something will happen. We use five words, from no chance to a full chance:\n\n**impossible → unlikely → equally likely → likely → certain**\n\nSee how they work when you roll an ordinary die (numbers 1 to 6) once:\n\n| Word | Meaning | Example with a die |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Impossible** | it can never happen | you roll a 7 |\n| **Unlikely** | it can happen, but the chance is small | you roll a 6 (only 1 of the 6 numbers) |\n| **Equally likely** | it is just as likely to happen as not to happen | you roll an even number (2, 4, 6 – 3 of the 6) |\n| **Likely** | the chance is big | you roll a number greater than 2 (4 of the 6) |\n| **Certain** | it will definitely happen | you roll a number less than 7 |\n\n## Possible outcomes\n\nAn **outcome** is one possible result. Always list **all** the possible outcomes and count them:\n\n- A **coin**: 2 outcomes – heads (H) or tails (T).\n- A **die**: 6 outcomes – 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6.\n- A **spinner** with 4 equal parts (red, blue, green, yellow): 4 outcomes.\n- **Two coins** together: HH, HT, TH, TT – 4 outcomes. Heads on the first and tails on the second (HT) is a different outcome from the other way round (TH).\n\nIf the parts of a spinner are **equal in size**, each colour is equally likely. But on a spinner with 3 red parts and 1 blue part, red is **likely** and blue is **unlikely**, because red covers more of the spinner.\n\n## Comparing chances\n\nIn a bag there are 5 red marbles and 2 green marbles. You take one out without looking. There are more red than green marbles, so red is **more likely** than green. Taking out a blue marble is **impossible**, because there are no blue marbles in the bag. Always count how many chances each outcome has and then compare.\n\n## Experiments and tally marks\n\nIn an **experiment** you do the same thing many times and record each result with **tally marks** in a table. Lerato tosses a coin 20 times:\n\n| Outcome | Tally marks | Frequency |\n|---|---|---|\n| Heads | ││││╱ ││││╱ ││ | 12 |\n| Tails | ││││╱ │││ | 8 |\n| **Total** | | **20** |\n\n## Predicting and comparing\n\nBefore the experiment Lerato **predicts**: heads and tails are equally likely, so she expects about 10 heads and 10 tails (20 ÷ 2). She gets 12 heads and 8 tails. Was she wrong? **No!** A prediction says what we expect **roughly**. The real results usually differ a little. The **more times** you do the experiment, the closer the results usually get to half-half.\n\nWith a die it works the same way: if you roll 30 times, you expect each number about 30 ÷ 6 = **5 times**.\n\n> **Remember:** A coin has no memory. Even if you have tossed heads 3 times in a row, heads and tails are still equally likely on the next toss.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Thinking that *equally likely* means you get exactly half. If you toss 10 times, you may get 6 heads and 4 tails – that is completely normal."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Waarskynlikheid","en":"Probability"},"def":{"af":"Hoe groot die kans is dat iets sal gebeur.","en":"How big the chance is that something will happen."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitkoms","en":"Outcome"},"def":{"af":"Een moontlike resultaat van ’n eksperiment, bv. kop as jy ’n muntstuk gooi.","en":"One possible result of an experiment, e.g. heads when you toss a coin."}},{"term":{"af":"Eksperiment","en":"Experiment"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat jy baie kere herhaal om te sien watter uitslae jy kry.","en":"Something you repeat many times to see what results you get."}},{"term":{"af":"Voorspel","en":"Predict"},"def":{"af":"Vooraf sê wat jy omtrent verwag om te gebeur.","en":"To say beforehand roughly what you expect to happen."}},{"term":{"af":"Onmoontlik","en":"Impossible"},"def":{"af":"Dit kan nooit gebeur nie, bv. ’n 7 gooi met ’n gewone dobbelsteen.","en":"It can never happen, e.g. rolling a 7 with an ordinary die."}},{"term":{"af":"Onwaarskynlik","en":"Unlikely"},"def":{"af":"Dit kan gebeur, maar die kans is klein.","en":"It can happen, but the chance is small."}},{"term":{"af":"Ewe waarskynlik","en":"Equally likely"},"def":{"af":"Twee uitkomste het presies dieselfde kans, soos kop en stert.","en":"Two outcomes have exactly the same chance, like heads and tails."}},{"term":{"af":"Waarskynlik","en":"Likely"},"def":{"af":"Die kans is groot dat dit sal gebeur.","en":"The chance is big that it will happen."}},{"term":{"af":"Seker","en":"Certain"},"def":{"af":"Dit sal beslis gebeur.","en":"It will definitely happen."}},{"term":{"af":"Spinner","en":"Spinner"},"def":{"af":"’n Skyf met gekleurde dele en ’n wyser wat draai en op een deel stop.","en":"A disc with coloured parts and a pointer that spins and stops on one part."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Beskryf die kans met ’n dobbelsteen","en":"Describe the chance with a die"},"problem":{"af":"Anika gooi een keer ’n gewone dobbelsteen. Gebruik ’n waarskynlikheidswoord vir elkeen: (a) sy gooi ’n 8 (b) sy gooi ’n ewe getal (c) sy gooi ’n getal kleiner as 5 (d) sy gooi ’n 1.","en":"Anika rolls an ordinary die once. Use a probability word for each: (a) she rolls an 8 (b) she rolls an even number (c) she rolls a number less than 5 (d) she rolls a 1."},"steps":[{"af":"Lys die uitkomste: 1; 2; 3; 4; 5; 6.","en":"List the outcomes: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6."},{"af":"(a) 8 is nie op die dobbelsteen nie: onmoontlik. (b) Ewe getalle: 2; 4; 6 – 3 van die 6, die helfte: ewe waarskynlik.","en":"(a) 8 is not on the die: impossible. (b) Even numbers: 2, 4, 6 – 3 of the 6, half: equally likely."},{"af":"(c) Kleiner as 5: 1; 2; 3; 4 – 4 van die 6, meer as die helfte: waarskynlik.","en":"(c) Less than 5: 1, 2, 3, 4 – 4 of the 6, more than half: likely."},{"af":"(d) Net een getal is ’n 1 – 1 van die 6: onwaarskynlik.","en":"(d) Only one number is a 1 – 1 of the 6: unlikely."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) onmoontlik (b) ewe waarskynlik (c) waarskynlik (d) onwaarskynlik","en":"(a) impossible (b) equally likely (c) likely (d) unlikely"}},{"title":{"af":"Twee muntstukke","en":"Two coins"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho gooi twee muntstukke saam. (a) Lys al die moontlike uitkomste. (b) Is dit waarskynliker om twee kop te kry of om een kop en een stert te kry?","en":"Sipho tosses two coins together. (a) List all the possible outcomes. (b) Is it more likely to get two heads or to get one head and one tail?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die eerste muntstuk kan K of S wees, en vir elkeen kan die tweede K of S wees.","en":"The first coin can be H or T, and for each the second can be H or T."},{"af":"(a) KK; KS; SK; SS – 4 uitkomste.","en":"(a) HH, HT, TH, TT – 4 outcomes."},{"af":"(b) Twee kop: net KK – 1 van die 4. Een kop en een stert: KS en SK – 2 van die 4.","en":"(b) Two heads: only HH – 1 of the 4. One head and one tail: HT and TH – 2 of the 4."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) KK; KS; SK; SS (b) Een kop en een stert is waarskynliker.","en":"(a) HH, HT, TH, TT (b) One head and one tail is more likely."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Spinner met ongelyke kanse","en":"A spinner with unequal chances"},"problem":{"af":"’n Spinner het 8 gelyke dele: 4 rooi, 3 blou en 1 groen. Beskryf die kans dat die spinner stop op (a) rooi (b) groen (c) rooi of blou (d) geel.","en":"A spinner has 8 equal parts: 4 red, 3 blue and 1 green. Describe the chance that the spinner stops on (a) red (b) green (c) red or blue (d) yellow."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Rooi: 4 van die 8, die helfte: ewe waarskynlik (dit is net so waarskynlik as nie-rooi).","en":"(a) Red: 4 of the 8, half: equally likely (it is just as likely as not red)."},{"af":"(b) Groen: 1 van die 8: onwaarskynlik.","en":"(b) Green: 1 of the 8: unlikely."},{"af":"(c) Rooi of blou: 4 + 3 = 7 van die 8: waarskynlik. (d) Daar is geen geel deel nie: onmoontlik.","en":"(c) Red or blue: 4 + 3 = 7 of the 8: likely. (d) There is no yellow part: impossible."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) ewe waarskynlik (b) onwaarskynlik (c) waarskynlik (d) onmoontlik","en":"(a) equally likely (b) unlikely (c) likely (d) impossible"}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyk die uitslae met die voorspelling","en":"Compare the results with the prediction"},"problem":{"af":"Fatima gooi ’n dobbelsteen 30 keer. Haar uitslae: 1 – 4 keer; 2 – 6 keer; 3 – 5 keer; 4 – 3 keer; 5 – 7 keer; 6 – 5 keer. Wat het sy voorspel, en hoe vergelyk die uitslae?","en":"Fatima rolls a die 30 times. Her results: 1 – 4 times, 2 – 6 times, 3 – 5 times, 4 – 3 times, 5 – 7 times, 6 – 5 times. What did she predict, and how do the results compare?"},"steps":[{"af":"Elke getal is ewe waarskynlik, so sy voorspel elke getal omtrent 30 ÷ 6 = 5 keer.","en":"Each number is equally likely, so she predicts each number about 30 ÷ 6 = 5 times."},{"af":"Kontroleer die totaal: 4 + 6 + 5 + 3 + 7 + 5 = 30. ✓","en":"Check the total: 4 + 6 + 5 + 3 + 7 + 5 = 30. ✓"},{"af":"Die 5 het die meeste gekom (7 keer) en die 4 die minste (3 keer). Al die uitslae is naby aan 5.","en":"The 5 came up most (7 times) and the 4 least (3 times). All the results are close to 5."}],"answer":{"af":"Sy het omtrent 5 keer elk voorspel. Die uitslae is naby daaraan, maar nie presies nie – dit is normaal.","en":"She predicted about 5 times each. The results are close to that, but not exact – this is normal."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe waarskynlik is dit om ’n 7 met ’n gewone dobbelsteen te gooi?","en":"How likely is it to roll a 7 with an ordinary die?"},"options":[{"af":"Seker","en":"Certain"},{"af":"Waarskynlik","en":"Likely"},{"af":"Onwaarskynlik","en":"Unlikely"},{"af":"Onmoontlik","en":"Impossible"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Gewone dobbelsteen het net die getalle 1 tot 6. ’n 7 kan nooit gegooi word nie, so dit is onmoontlik – nie net onwaarskynlik nie.","en":"An ordinary die only has the numbers 1 to 6. A 7 can never be rolled, so it is impossible – not just unlikely."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel moontlike uitkomste is daar as jy een gewone dobbelsteen gooi?","en":"How many possible outcomes are there when you roll one ordinary die?"},"options":[{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"1","en":"1"},{"af":"12","en":"12"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die dobbelsteen kan op 1; 2; 3; 4; 5 of 6 land – 6 uitkomste. ’n Muntstuk het 2 uitkomste.","en":"The die can land on 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 or 6 – 6 outcomes. A coin has 2 outcomes."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy ’n muntstuk gooi, is kop en stert ewe waarskynlik.","en":"When you toss a coin, heads and tails are equally likely."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Eerlike muntstuk het twee kante en elkeen het dieselfde kans om bo te land.","en":"True. A fair coin has two sides and each has the same chance of landing face up."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As iets beslis gaan gebeur, sê ons dit is ___.","en":"If something will definitely happen, we say it is ___."},"answers":{"af":["seker"],"en":["certain"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["waarskynlik","onwaarskynlik","ewe waarskynlik"],"en":["likely","unlikely","equally likely"]}},"explain":{"af":"Seker beteken daar is geen kans dat dit nie gebeur nie, bv. om ’n getal kleiner as 7 met ’n dobbelsteen te gooi. Waarskynlik beteken net die kans is groot.","en":"Certain means there is no chance that it does not happen, e.g. rolling a number less than 7 with a die. Likely only means the chance is big."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato gooi ’n muntstuk 3 keer na mekaar en kry elke keer kop. Wat is waar van haar 4de gooi?","en":"Lerato tosses a coin 3 times in a row and gets heads every time. What is true about her 4th toss?"},"options":[{"af":"Stert is nou seker","en":"Tails is now certain"},{"af":"Kop is nou waarskynliker","en":"Heads is now more likely"},{"af":"Kop en stert is steeds ewe waarskynlik","en":"Heads and tails are still equally likely"},{"af":"Kop is nou onmoontlik","en":"Heads is now impossible"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Muntstuk onthou nie wat vroeër gebeur het nie. Elke gooi het weer dieselfde kans vir kop en stert.","en":"A coin does not remember what happened before. Every toss again has the same chance of heads and tails."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke gebeurtenis by die regte waarskynlikheidswoord.","en":"Match each event to the correct probability word."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Die son kom môre op","en":"The sun rises tomorrow"},"r":{"af":"Seker","en":"Certain"}},{"l":{"af":"Jy gooi ’n 7 met ’n dobbelsteen","en":"You roll a 7 with a die"},"r":{"af":"Onmoontlik","en":"Impossible"}},{"l":{"af":"’n Muntstuk land op stert","en":"A coin lands on tails"},"r":{"af":"Ewe waarskynlik","en":"Equally likely"}},{"l":{"af":"Jy gooi ’n 6 met een dobbelsteen","en":"You roll a 6 with one die"},"r":{"af":"Onwaarskynlik","en":"Unlikely"}},{"l":{"af":"Jy gooi ’n getal groter as 1 met ’n dobbelsteen","en":"You roll a number greater than 1 with a die"},"r":{"af":"Waarskynlik","en":"Likely"}}],"explain":{"af":"’n 6 is net 1 van die 6 getalle (onwaarskynlik), maar groter as 1 is 5 van die 6 getalle (waarskynlik). Kop of stert is half-half.","en":"A 6 is only 1 of the 6 numbers (unlikely), but greater than 1 is 5 of the 6 numbers (likely). Heads or tails is half-half."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Spinner het 6 gelyke dele: 4 is rooi en 2 is blou. Watter stelling is reg?","en":"A spinner has 6 equal parts: 4 are red and 2 are blue. Which statement is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Blou is waarskynliker as rooi","en":"Blue is more likely than red"},{"af":"Rooi is waarskynliker as blou","en":"Red is more likely than blue"},{"af":"Rooi en blou is ewe waarskynlik","en":"Red and blue are equally likely"},{"af":"Groen is waarskynlik","en":"Green is likely"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Rooi bedek 4 van die 6 dele en blou net 2, so rooi is waarskynliker. Daar is geen groen nie, so groen is onmoontlik.","en":"Red covers 4 of the 6 parts and blue only 2, so red is more likely. There is no green, so green is impossible."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As jy twee muntstukke saam gooi, is daar ___ moontlike uitkomste.","en":"When you toss two coins together, there are ___ possible outcomes."},"answers":{"af":["4","vier"],"en":["4","four"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["2","3","6"],"en":["2","3","6"]}},"explain":{"af":"KK; KS; SK; SS – 4 uitkomste. As jy 3 sê, het jy vergeet dat KS en SK twee verskillende uitkomste is.","en":"HH, HT, TH, TT – 4 outcomes. If you say 3, you forgot that HT and TH are two different outcomes."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe waarskynlik is dit om ’n ewe getal met ’n gewone dobbelsteen te gooi?","en":"How likely is it to roll an even number with an ordinary die?"},"options":[{"af":"Onmoontlik","en":"Impossible"},{"af":"Ewe waarskynlik","en":"Equally likely"},{"af":"Seker","en":"Certain"},{"af":"Onwaarskynlik","en":"Unlikely"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die ewe getalle is 2; 4 en 6 – 3 van die 6 getalle, presies die helfte. Dus is ewe en onewe ewe waarskynlik.","en":"The even numbers are 2, 4 and 6 – 3 of the 6 numbers, exactly half. So even and odd are equally likely."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy ’n muntstuk 10 keer gooi, sal jy altyd presies 5 kop en 5 stert kry.","en":"If you toss a coin 10 times, you will always get exactly 5 heads and 5 tails."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Ons verwag omtrent 5 van elk, maar die werklike uitslae verskil gewoonlik ’n bietjie, bv. 6 kop en 4 stert.","en":"False. We expect about 5 of each, but the real results usually differ a little, e.g. 6 heads and 4 tails."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo gaan ’n dobbelsteen 60 keer gooi. Omtrent hoeveel keer verwag hy om ’n 3 te gooi?","en":"Thabo is going to roll a die 60 times. About how many times does he expect to roll a 3?"},"options":[{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"20","en":"20"},{"af":"10","en":"10"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Elke getal is ewe waarskynlik, so 60 ÷ 6 = 10 keer. Dit is ’n voorspelling – die werklike getal kan ’n bietjie meer of minder wees.","en":"Each number is equally likely, so 60 ÷ 6 = 10 times. This is a prediction – the real number can be a little more or less."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter gebeurtenis is onwaarskynlik as jy een keer ’n gewone dobbelsteen gooi?","en":"Which event is unlikely when you roll an ordinary die once?"},"options":[{"af":"Jy gooi ’n 1","en":"You roll a 1"},{"af":"Jy gooi ’n ewe getal","en":"You roll an even number"},{"af":"Jy gooi ’n getal kleiner as 7","en":"You roll a number less than 7"},{"af":"Jy gooi ’n 0","en":"You roll a 0"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n 1 is net 1 van die 6 getalle: onwaarskynlik. ’n Ewe getal is ewe waarskynlik, kleiner as 7 is seker en ’n 0 is onmoontlik.","en":"A 1 is only 1 of the 6 numbers: unlikely. An even number is equally likely, less than 7 is certain and a 0 is impossible."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Op ’n gewone dobbelsteen is daar ___ getalle groter as 4.","en":"On an ordinary die there are ___ numbers greater than 4."},"answers":{"af":["2","twee"],"en":["2","two"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4","3","1"],"en":["4","3","1"]}},"explain":{"af":"Net 5 en 6 is groter as 4 – dit is 2 van die 6 getalle, so om ’n getal groter as 4 te gooi, is onwaarskynlik. 4 self is nie groter as 4 nie.","en":"Only 5 and 6 are greater than 4 – that is 2 of the 6 numbers, so rolling a number greater than 4 is unlikely. 4 itself is not greater than 4."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho gooi ’n eerlike dobbelsteen 30 keer. Hy kry ’n 5 sewe keer en ’n 4 net drie keer. Wat is die beste verduideliking?","en":"Sipho rolls a fair die 30 times. He gets a 5 seven times and a 4 only three times. What is the best explanation?"},"options":[{"af":"Die dobbelsteen is beslis vals","en":"The die is definitely unfair"},{"af":"’n 5 is altyd waarskynliker as ’n 4","en":"A 5 is always more likely than a 4"},{"af":"Uitslae verskil gewoonlik ’n bietjie van die voorspelling","en":"Results usually differ a little from the prediction"},{"af":"Hy het verkeerd getel, want elke getal moet 5 keer kom","en":"He counted wrongly, because each number must come 5 times"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Hy het omtrent 5 keer elk verwag (30 ÷ 6). Dat sommige getalle ’n bietjie meer of minder kom, is normaal by ’n eerlike dobbelsteen.","en":"He expected about 5 times each (30 ÷ 6). That some numbers come a little more or less is normal with a fair die."}}]},{"id":"w5-t4-probleemoplossing","title":{"af":"Probleemoplossing en hersiening","en":"Problem solving and revision"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal woordprobleme stap vir stap kan oplos, die regte bewerking kan kies, veelstap-probleme en eenvoudige koers- en verhoudingsprobleme kan doen en goed vir die Novembereksamen kan voorberei.","en":"You will be able to solve word problems step by step, choose the right operation, do multi-step problems and simple rate and ratio problems, and prepare well for the November exam."},"summary":{"af":"## Stappe om ’n woordprobleem op te los\n\n1. **Lees** die probleem twee keer. Wat word gevra?\n2. **Onderstreep** die belangrike getalle, eenhede en woorde.\n3. **Kies die bewerking** of bewerkings: +, −, × of ÷.\n4. **Skat** die antwoord deur af te rond.\n5. **Bereken** en wys jou werk.\n6. **Kontroleer** met die omgekeerde bewerking en vergelyk met jou skatting.\n7. Skryf die **antwoord in ’n volsin** met die **eenheid** (R, cm, kg, l …).\n\n## Leidraadwoorde\n\n| As jy lees … | dink aan … |\n|---|---|\n| altesaam, totaal, saam | optel (+) |\n| hoeveel oor, verskil, hoeveel meer, hoeveel minder | aftrek (−) |\n| keer soveel, ’n aantal groepe van, elkeen kos … | vermenigvuldig (×) |\n| deel gelykop, hoeveel kry elkeen, hoeveel groepe | deel (÷) |\n\nLeidraadwoorde help, maar **dink altyd** oor wat regtig gebeur. *Hoeveel meer* vra na ’n verskil, so jy trek af – al staan die woord *meer* daar.\n\n## Veelstap-probleme\n\nParty probleme het meer as een stap nodig. Die skool koop 12 dose met 24 potlode elk en gee 9 potlode aan elk van 30 leerders. Hoeveel potlode bly oor?\n\n- Stap 1: 12 × 24 = 288 potlode altesaam\n- Stap 2: 30 × 9 = 270 potlode uitgedeel\n- Stap 3: 288 − 270 = **18 potlode** bly oor.\n\n> **Onthou:** Skat eers! 12 × 24 is omtrent 10 × 24 = 240. ’n Antwoord van 2 880 kan dus nie reg wees nie.\n\n## Koers en verhouding\n\n’n **Koers** vergelyk twee verskillende soorte hoeveelhede, bv. **3 lekkers vir R5** of **60 km per uur**. ’n **Tabel** help jou om die koers uit te brei:\n\n| Rand | 5 | 10 | 15 | 20 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Lekkers | 3 | 6 | 9 | 12 |\n\nR20 is 4 × R5, so jy kry 4 × 3 = **12 lekkers**.\n\n’n **Verhouding** vergelyk hoeveelhede van dieselfde soort, bv. ’n resep met **2 koppies meel vir elke 1 koppie melk**. Vir 6 koppies meel het jy 3 koppies melk nodig – albei word 3 keer meer.\n\n## Patrone en tabelle\n\n’n Tabel help om ’n patroon raak te sien. Lerato het R30 en spaar elke week R15:\n\n| Week | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Geld (R) | 30 | 45 | 60 | 75 | 90 | 105 | 120 |\n\nNá **6 weke** het sy R120.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om sommer iets met die getalle in die vraag te doen sonder om te verstaan wat gevra word. Vra jouself: *Maak my antwoord sin?* Kan ’n kind 300 kg weeg? Kan ’n potlood R900 kos?\n\n## Ander strategieë\n\n- **Teken ’n prent of diagram** – veral by vorms, afstande en breuke.\n- **Probeer en verbeter** – raai, toets en pas aan. Twee getalle se som is 20 en hul verskil is 4. Probeer 11 en 9: die verskil is 2, te klein. Probeer 12 en 8: die verskil is 4. ✓\n- **Werk agteruit** – begin by die einde en doen die omgekeerde bewerkings.\n\n## Eksamenwenke vir November\n\n- Lees die **hele vraag** en al die inligting voordat jy begin.\n- **Wys jou werk** – jy kan punte kry vir die regte metode, al is die antwoord verkeerd.\n- Skryf die **eenheid** by: R, cm, m, kg, l, °C.\n- Begin met die vrae wat jy goed ken. Moenie te lank by een vraag vassit nie – kom later terug.\n- Gebruik die laaste paar minute om jou antwoorde te **kontroleer**.","en":"## Steps to solve a word problem\n\n1. **Read** the problem twice. What is being asked?\n2. **Underline** the important numbers, units and words.\n3. **Choose the operation** or operations: +, −, × or ÷.\n4. **Estimate** the answer by rounding.\n5. **Calculate** and show your working.\n6. **Check** with the inverse operation and compare with your estimate.\n7. Write the **answer in a full sentence** with the **unit** (R, cm, kg, l …).\n\n## Clue words\n\n| If you read … | think of … |\n|---|---|\n| altogether, total, together | addition (+) |\n| how many are left, difference, how many more, how many fewer | subtraction (−) |\n| times as many, a number of groups of, each one costs … | multiplication (×) |\n| share equally, how many does each get, how many groups | division (÷) |\n\nClue words help, but **always think** about what is really happening. *How many more* asks for a difference, so you subtract – even though the word *more* is there.\n\n## Multi-step problems\n\nSome problems need more than one step. The school buys 12 boxes with 24 pencils each and gives 9 pencils to each of 30 learners. How many pencils are left?\n\n- Step 1: 12 × 24 = 288 pencils altogether\n- Step 2: 30 × 9 = 270 pencils handed out\n- Step 3: 288 − 270 = **18 pencils** are left.\n\n> **Remember:** Estimate first! 12 × 24 is about 10 × 24 = 240. So an answer of 2 880 cannot be right.\n\n## Rate and ratio\n\nA **rate** compares two different kinds of quantities, e.g. **3 sweets for R5** or **60 km per hour**. A **table** helps you to extend the rate:\n\n| Rand | 5 | 10 | 15 | 20 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Sweets | 3 | 6 | 9 | 12 |\n\nR20 is 4 × R5, so you get 4 × 3 = **12 sweets**.\n\nA **ratio** compares quantities of the same kind, e.g. a recipe with **2 cups of flour for every 1 cup of milk**. For 6 cups of flour you need 3 cups of milk – both become 3 times more.\n\n## Patterns and tables\n\nA table helps you to see a pattern. Lerato has R30 and saves R15 every week:\n\n| Week | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Money (R) | 30 | 45 | 60 | 75 | 90 | 105 | 120 |\n\nAfter **6 weeks** she has R120.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Just doing something with the numbers in the question without understanding what is asked. Ask yourself: *Does my answer make sense?* Can a child weigh 300 kg? Can a pencil cost R900?\n\n## Other strategies\n\n- **Draw a picture or diagram** – especially with shapes, distances and fractions.\n- **Trial and improvement** – guess, test and adjust. Two numbers add up to 20 and their difference is 4. Try 11 and 9: the difference is 2, too small. Try 12 and 8: the difference is 4. ✓\n- **Work backwards** – start at the end and do the inverse operations.\n\n## Exam tips for November\n\n- Read the **whole question** and all the information before you start.\n- **Show your working** – you can get marks for the right method, even if the answer is wrong.\n- Write the **unit**: R, cm, m, kg, l, °C.\n- Start with the questions you know well. Do not get stuck on one question for too long – come back later.\n- Use the last few minutes to **check** your answers."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Woordprobleem","en":"Word problem"},"def":{"af":"’n Wiskundevraag wat in woorde vertel word, gewoonlik oor ’n alledaagse situasie.","en":"A maths question told in words, usually about an everyday situation."}},{"term":{"af":"Bewerking","en":"Operation"},"def":{"af":"Wat jy met getalle doen: optel, aftrek, vermenigvuldig of deel.","en":"What you do with numbers: add, subtract, multiply or divide."}},{"term":{"af":"Leidraadwoord","en":"Clue word"},"def":{"af":"’n Woord in ’n probleem wat ’n wenk gee oor watter bewerking om te gebruik, bv. *altesaam*.","en":"A word in a problem that gives a hint about which operation to use, e.g. *altogether*."}},{"term":{"af":"Skat","en":"Estimate"},"def":{"af":"Rond die getalle af en bereken vinnig ’n antwoord wat naby die regte antwoord is.","en":"Round the numbers and quickly work out an answer that is close to the real answer."}},{"term":{"af":"Omgekeerde bewerking","en":"Inverse operation"},"def":{"af":"Die bewerking wat ’n ander een ongedaan maak, soos × en ÷ of + en −; jy gebruik dit om te kontroleer.","en":"The operation that undoes another one, like × and ÷ or + and −; you use it to check."}},{"term":{"af":"Veelstap-probleem","en":"Multi-step problem"},"def":{"af":"’n Probleem waarvoor jy meer as een berekening moet doen.","en":"A problem for which you have to do more than one calculation."}},{"term":{"af":"Koers","en":"Rate"},"def":{"af":"’n Vergelyking van twee verskillende soorte hoeveelhede, soos R5 vir 3 lekkers of 60 km per uur.","en":"A comparison of two different kinds of quantities, like R5 for 3 sweets or 60 km per hour."}},{"term":{"af":"Verhouding","en":"Ratio"},"def":{"af":"’n Vergelyking van hoeveelhede van dieselfde soort, soos 2 koppies meel vir elke 1 koppie melk.","en":"A comparison of quantities of the same kind, like 2 cups of flour for every 1 cup of milk."}},{"term":{"af":"Patroon","en":"Pattern"},"def":{"af":"’n Reël wat herhaal, sodat jy kan voorspel wat volgende kom.","en":"A rule that repeats, so that you can predict what comes next."}},{"term":{"af":"Eenheid","en":"Unit"},"def":{"af":"Wat by ’n getal hoort om te sê wat dit meet, soos R, cm, kg of l.","en":"What goes with a number to say what it measures, like R, cm, kg or l."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Veelstap-probleem met geld","en":"Multi-step problem with money"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter se pa koop 3 sakke sement van R95 elk en 4 pakke spykers van R28 elk. Hy betaal met R500. Hoeveel kleingeld kry hy?","en":"Pieter’s dad buys 3 bags of cement at R95 each and 4 packets of nails at R28 each. He pays with R500. How much change does he get?"},"steps":[{"af":"Skat: 3 × R100 + 4 × R30 = R300 + R120 = R420, so die kleingeld is omtrent R80.","en":"Estimate: 3 × R100 + 4 × R30 = R300 + R120 = R420, so the change is about R80."},{"af":"Sement: 3 × R95 = R285. Spykers: 4 × R28 = R112.","en":"Cement: 3 × R95 = R285. Nails: 4 × R28 = R112."},{"af":"Totaal: R285 + R112 = R397.","en":"Total: R285 + R112 = R397."},{"af":"Kleingeld: R500 − R397 = R103. Kontroleer: R397 + R103 = R500. ✓","en":"Change: R500 − R397 = R103. Check: R397 + R103 = R500. ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"Hy kry R103 kleingeld.","en":"He gets R103 change."}},{"title":{"af":"Koers: petrol vir ’n reis","en":"Rate: petrol for a trip"},"problem":{"af":"Mev. Naidoo se motor gebruik 8 l petrol vir elke 100 km. Hoeveel petrol het sy nodig vir ’n reis van 350 km?","en":"Mrs Naidoo’s car uses 8 l of petrol for every 100 km. How much petrol does she need for a trip of 350 km?"},"steps":[{"af":"Breek 350 km op: 350 = 100 + 100 + 100 + 50.","en":"Break up 350 km: 350 = 100 + 100 + 100 + 50."},{"af":"300 km: 3 × 8 l = 24 l. 50 km is die helfte van 100 km, so die helfte van 8 l = 4 l.","en":"300 km: 3 × 8 l = 24 l. 50 km is half of 100 km, so half of 8 l = 4 l."},{"af":"Tel bymekaar: 24 l + 4 l = 28 l.","en":"Add: 24 l + 4 l = 28 l."}],"answer":{"af":"Sy het 28 l petrol nodig.","en":"She needs 28 l of petrol."}},{"title":{"af":"Verhouding: ’n groter resep","en":"Ratio: a bigger recipe"},"problem":{"af":"’n Resep vir 12 pannekoeke gebruik 2 koppies meel en 3 eiers. Nomsa wil 36 pannekoeke vir ’n kermis bak. Hoeveel meel en eiers het sy nodig?","en":"A recipe for 12 pancakes uses 2 cups of flour and 3 eggs. Nomsa wants to bake 36 pancakes for a fete. How much flour and how many eggs does she need?"},"steps":[{"af":"Hoeveel keer groter? 36 ÷ 12 = 3, so sy moet die resep 3 keer maak.","en":"How many times bigger? 36 ÷ 12 = 3, so she must make the recipe 3 times."},{"af":"Meel: 3 × 2 koppies = 6 koppies.","en":"Flour: 3 × 2 cups = 6 cups."},{"af":"Eiers: 3 × 3 = 9 eiers. Die verhouding meel tot eiers (2 tot 3) bly dieselfde.","en":"Eggs: 3 × 3 = 9 eggs. The ratio of flour to eggs (2 to 3) stays the same."}],"answer":{"af":"6 koppies meel en 9 eiers","en":"6 cups of flour and 9 eggs"}},{"title":{"af":"Los op met ’n patroon","en":"Solve with a pattern"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo bou driehoeke in ’n ry met vuurhoutjies. 1 driehoek het 3 vuurhoutjies nodig, 2 driehoeke 5 en 3 driehoeke 7. Hoeveel vuurhoutjies het hy vir 10 driehoeke nodig?","en":"Thabo builds triangles in a row with matches. 1 triangle needs 3 matches, 2 triangles need 5 and 3 triangles need 7. How many matches does he need for 10 triangles?"},"steps":[{"af":"Maak ’n tabel: 1 → 3; 2 → 5; 3 → 7. Elke nuwe driehoek het 2 ekstra vuurhoutjies nodig, want hy deel een kant met die vorige driehoek.","en":"Make a table: 1 → 3, 2 → 5, 3 → 7. Each new triangle needs 2 extra matches, because it shares one side with the previous triangle."},{"af":"Reël: aantal driehoeke × 2 + 1. Toets: 3 × 2 + 1 = 7. ✓","en":"Rule: number of triangles × 2 + 1. Test: 3 × 2 + 1 = 7. ✓"},{"af":"Vir 10 driehoeke: 10 × 2 + 1 = 21.","en":"For 10 triangles: 10 × 2 + 1 = 21."}],"answer":{"af":"Hy het 21 vuurhoutjies nodig.","en":"He needs 21 matches."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter bewerking gebruik jy? *Anika het 48 plakkers en deel hulle gelykop tussen 6 maats. Hoeveel kry elkeen?*","en":"Which operation do you use? *Anika has 48 stickers and shares them equally among 6 friends. How many does each one get?*"},"options":[{"af":"Deling","en":"Division"},{"af":"Vermenigvuldiging","en":"Multiplication"},{"af":"Aftrekking","en":"Subtraction"},{"af":"Optelling","en":"Addition"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Deel gelykop* en *hoeveel kry elkeen* wys na deling: 48 ÷ 6 = 8 plakkers elk.","en":"*Share equally* and *how many does each one get* point to division: 48 ÷ 6 = 8 stickers each."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"3 lekkers kos R5. Vir R20 kry jy ___ lekkers.","en":"3 sweets cost R5. For R20 you get ___ sweets."},"answers":{"af":["12"],"en":["12"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4","15","60"],"en":["4","15","60"]}},"explain":{"af":"R20 is 4 × R5, so jy kry 4 × 3 = 12 lekkers. 4 is net die aantal groepe van R5, en 60 kry jy as jy 3 × 20 doen.","en":"R20 is 4 × R5, so you get 4 × 3 = 12 sweets. 4 is only the number of groups of R5, and you get 60 if you do 3 × 20."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Skool koop 5 dose met 36 koekies elk. Hulle gee 4 koekies aan elk van 40 leerders. Hoeveel koekies bly oor?","en":"A school buys 5 boxes with 36 biscuits each. They give 4 biscuits to each of 40 learners. How many biscuits are left?"},"options":[{"af":"160","en":"160"},{"af":"20","en":"20"},{"af":"180","en":"180"},{"af":"140","en":"140"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Stap 1: 5 × 36 = 180 koekies. Stap 2: 40 × 4 = 160 uitgedeel. Stap 3: 180 − 160 = 20 bly oor. 160 en 180 is net tussenstappe.","en":"Step 1: 5 × 36 = 180 biscuits. Step 2: 40 × 4 = 160 handed out. Step 3: 180 − 160 = 20 left. 160 and 180 are only in-between steps."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Jy kan 72 ÷ 8 = 9 kontroleer deur 9 × 8 = 72 te bereken.","en":"You can check 72 ÷ 8 = 9 by working out 9 × 8 = 72."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Vermenigvuldiging is die omgekeerde bewerking van deling, dus is dit ’n goeie manier om te kontroleer.","en":"True. Multiplication is the inverse operation of division, so it is a good way to check."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die beste skatting vir 49 × 21?","en":"What is the best estimate for 49 × 21?"},"options":[{"af":"700","en":"700"},{"af":"100","en":"100"},{"af":"10 000","en":"10 000"},{"af":"1 000","en":"1 000"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Rond af: 49 is omtrent 50 en 21 is omtrent 20. 50 × 20 = 1 000. (Die presiese antwoord is 1 029.)","en":"Round off: 49 is about 50 and 21 is about 20. 50 × 20 = 1 000. (The exact answer is 1 029.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter antwoord is die beste vir hierdie vraag? *’n Tou van 120 m word in 8 gelyke stukke gesny. Hoe lank is elke stuk?*","en":"Which answer is best for this question? *A rope of 120 m is cut into 8 equal pieces. How long is each piece?*"},"options":[{"af":"Die antwoord is 15.","en":"The answer is 15."},{"af":"Elke stuk is 15 cm lank.","en":"Each piece is 15 cm long."},{"af":"Elke stuk is 15 m lank.","en":"Each piece is 15 m long."},{"af":"Elke stuk is 960 m lank.","en":"Each piece is 960 m long."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"120 ÷ 8 = 15, en die tou is in meter gemeet. Die beste antwoord is ’n volsin met die regte eenheid. 960 kry jy as jy vermenigvuldig in plaas van deel.","en":"120 ÷ 8 = 15, and the rope was measured in metres. The best answer is a full sentence with the correct unit. You get 960 if you multiply instead of divide."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke leidraadwoord by die bewerking wat dit gewoonlik beteken.","en":"Match each clue word to the operation it usually means."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"altesaam","en":"altogether"},"r":{"af":"optel (+)","en":"addition (+)"}},{"l":{"af":"verskil","en":"difference"},"r":{"af":"aftrek (−)","en":"subtraction (−)"}},{"l":{"af":"keer soveel","en":"times as many"},"r":{"af":"vermenigvuldig (×)","en":"multiplication (×)"}},{"l":{"af":"deel gelykop","en":"share equally"},"r":{"af":"deel (÷)","en":"division (÷)"}}],"explain":{"af":"Leidraadwoorde gee ’n wenk, maar lees altyd die hele vraag om seker te maak wat gebeur.","en":"Clue words give a hint, but always read the whole question to make sure what is happening."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Resep vir 12 muffins gebruik 2 eiers. Hoeveel eiers is nodig vir 36 muffins?","en":"A recipe for 12 muffins uses 2 eggs. How many eggs are needed for 36 muffins?"},"options":[{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"26","en":"26"},{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"72","en":"72"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"36 muffins is 3 keer soveel as 12 (36 ÷ 12 = 3), so jy het 3 × 2 = 6 eiers nodig. 26 kry jy as jy 24 by 2 tel in plaas van te vermenigvuldig.","en":"36 muffins is 3 times as many as 12 (36 ÷ 12 = 3), so you need 3 × 2 = 6 eggs. You get 26 if you add 24 to 2 instead of multiplying."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Thabo spaar R20 in week 1, R25 in week 2 en R30 in week 3. As die patroon so aangaan, spaar hy R___ in week 6.","en":"Thabo saves R20 in week 1, R25 in week 2 and R30 in week 3. If the pattern carries on, he saves R___ in week 6."},"answers":{"af":["45"],"en":["45"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["50","35","40"],"en":["50","35","40"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die bedrag word elke week R5 meer: week 4 – R35, week 5 – R40, week 6 – R45.","en":"The amount grows by R5 every week: week 4 – R35, week 5 – R40, week 6 – R45."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Johan koop 3 hamburgers van R35 elk en ’n koeldrank van R18. Hy betaal met R150. Hoeveel kleingeld kry hy?","en":"Johan buys 3 hamburgers at R35 each and a cooldrink for R18. He pays with R150. How much change does he get?"},"options":[{"af":"R45","en":"R45"},{"af":"R123","en":"R123"},{"af":"R27","en":"R27"},{"af":"R37","en":"R37"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"3 × R35 = R105. R105 + R18 = R123. R150 − R123 = R27. R45 kry jy as jy die koeldrank vergeet, en R123 is wat hy betaal, nie sy kleingeld nie.","en":"3 × R35 = R105. R105 + R18 = R123. R150 − R123 = R27. You get R45 if you forget the cooldrink, and R123 is what he pays, not his change."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Motor ry 80 km in 1 uur. Hoe ver ry dit in 3½ uur teen dieselfde spoed?","en":"A car travels 80 km in 1 hour. How far does it travel in 3½ hours at the same speed?"},"options":[{"af":"240 km","en":"240 km"},{"af":"280 km","en":"280 km"},{"af":"320 km","en":"320 km"},{"af":"250 km","en":"250 km"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"3 uur: 3 × 80 = 240 km. ½ uur: die helfte van 80 = 40 km. 240 + 40 = 280 km. 240 km is net die 3 uur.","en":"3 hours: 3 × 80 = 240 km. ½ hour: half of 80 = 40 km. 240 + 40 = 280 km. 240 km is only the 3 hours."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die woord *altesaam* in ’n probleem beteken altyd dat jy moet aftrek.","en":"The word *altogether* in a problem always means that you must subtract."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. *Altesaam* beteken gewoonlik dat jy alles bymekaar tel (optel), of soms vermenigvuldig as daar gelyke groepe is.","en":"False. *Altogether* usually means that you add everything together, or sometimes multiply when there are equal groups."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is NIE ’n goeie eksamenwenk nie?","en":"Which one is NOT a good exam tip?"},"options":[{"af":"Lees die hele vraag voordat jy begin","en":"Read the whole question before you start"},{"af":"Wys jou werk","en":"Show your working"},{"af":"Skryf die eenheid by jou antwoord","en":"Write the unit with your answer"},{"af":"Bly by ’n moeilike vraag totdat jy dit kan doen, al raak die tyd min","en":"Stay on a difficult question until you can do it, even if time runs out"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"As jy te lank by een vraag vassit, kry jy nie tyd vir die ander vrae nie. Gaan aan en kom later terug.","en":"If you get stuck on one question for too long, you do not have time for the other questions. Move on and come back later."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Bus hou 45 leerders. 160 leerders gaan op ’n uitstappie. Hulle het ___ busse nodig.","en":"A bus holds 45 learners. 160 learners go on an outing. They need ___ buses."},"answers":{"af":["4","vier"],"en":["4","four"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3","5","35"],"en":["3","5","35"]}},"explain":{"af":"160 ÷ 45 = 3 res 25. Drie busse neem net 135 leerders; die oorblywende 25 leerders het nog ’n bus nodig, dus 4 busse. Hier rond jy die res op.","en":"160 ÷ 45 = 3 remainder 25. Three buses take only 135 learners; the remaining 25 learners need another bus, so 4 buses. Here you round the remainder up."}}]}]}]},"nwt":{"id":"nwt","grade":5,"name":{"af":"Natuurwetenskappe en Tegnologie","en":"Natural Sciences and Technology"},"short":{"af":"NW&Teg","en":"NS&Tech"},"icon":"🔬","color":"#16a34a","intro":{"af":"Natuurwetenskappe en Tegnologie in Graad 5 ondersoek lewe en lewende dinge, materie en materiale, energie en verandering, en die aarde en die ruimte – en hoe ons met die ontwerpproses dinge ontwerp en maak om probleme op te los. In die Novembereksamen kry jy kort vrae (meervoudige keuse, invul en pas), vrae oor diagramme en tabelle, en langer vrae waarin jy ’n ondersoek of ’n ontwerp moet verduidelik.","en":"Natural Sciences and Technology in Grade 5 investigates life and living, matter and materials, energy and change, and planet Earth and beyond – and how we use the design process to design and make things that solve problems. In the November exam you get short questions (multiple choice, fill in and matching), questions on diagrams and tables, and longer questions in which you must explain an investigation or a design."},"examTips":[{"af":"Leer die sleutelterme met hul definisies – baie vrae vra presies wat ’n woord soos *produsent*, *metamorfose* of *isoleerder* beteken.","en":"Learn the key terms with their definitions – many questions ask exactly what a word like *producer*, *metamorphosis* or *insulator* means."},{"af":"By ’n ondersoek: sê wat verander word, wat gemeet word en wat dieselfde bly (regverdige toets), en skryf ’n gevolgtrekking in ’n volsin.","en":"For an investigation: say what is changed, what is measured and what stays the same (fair test), and write a conclusion in a full sentence."},{"af":"Teken voedselkettings altyd met die pyle na die eter, en begin by ’n plant. Benoem diagramme van skelette en lewensiklusse netjies.","en":"Always draw food chains with the arrows pointing to the eater, and start with a plant. Label diagrams of skeletons and life cycles neatly."},{"af":"Ken die vyf stappe van die ontwerpproses (ondersoek, ontwerp, maak, evalueer, kommunikeer) en die verskil tussen spesifikasies en beperkings.","en":"Know the five steps of the design process (investigate, design, make, evaluate, communicate) and the difference between specifications and constraints."},{"af":"Kyk na die punte langs elke vraag: 2 punte beteken gewoonlik dat jy twee feite of ’n feit en ’n rede moet gee.","en":"Look at the marks next to each question: 2 marks usually means you must give two facts, or a fact and a reason."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"DBE Reënboog-werkboeke (Graad 5)","en":"DBE Rainbow Workbooks (Grade 5)"},"url":"https://www.education.gov.za/Curriculum/Workbooks.aspx","note":{"af":"Gratis amptelike CAPS-werkboeke van die Departement van Basiese Onderwys, in Afrikaans en Engels.","en":"Free official CAPS workbooks from the Department of Basic Education, in Afrikaans and English."}},{"title":{"af":"Siyavula: oop handboeke en oefening","en":"Siyavula: open textbooks and practice"},"url":"https://www.siyavula.com","note":{"af":"Gratis oop CAPS-handboeke en oefenvrae.","en":"Free open CAPS textbooks and practice questions."}}],"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Lewe en lewende dinge","en":"Life and living"},"topics":[{"id":"nwt5-t1-plante-diere","title":{"af":"Plante en diere op aarde","en":"Plants and animals on Earth"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal habitatte kan beskryf, kan verduidelik hoe plante en diere mekaar nodig het, en diere as gewerweldes of ongewerweldes kan klassifiseer.","en":"You will be able to describe habitats, explain how plants and animals need each other, and classify animals as vertebrates or invertebrates."},"summary":{"af":"## Die groot verskeidenheid lewe\n\nDie aarde is vol lewende dinge – van piepklein miere tot reusagtige olifante, en van gras tot kremetartbome. Hierdie groot **verskeidenheid** plante en diere noem ons **biodiversiteit**. Suid-Afrika het ’n baie ryk verskeidenheid: dink aan die fynbos in die Wes-Kaap, die bosveld in die Krugerwildtuin en die kelpwoude langs die weskus.\n\nOm al hierdie lewende dinge te bestudeer, sorteer (**klassifiseer**) wetenskaplikes hulle in groepe volgens hul **kenmerke**.\n\n## Habitatte: waar plante en diere leef\n\n’n **Habitat** is die plek waar ’n plant of dier leef. Daar kry dit alles wat dit nodig het: **kos, water, skuiling** en ’n veilige plek vir sy kleintjies. Plante en diere is **aangepas** vir hul habitat. ’n Vis het byvoorbeeld kieue om in water asem te haal, en ’n vetplant stoor water in sy dik blare sodat dit droë tye kan oorleef.\n\n| Habitat | Hoe dit is | Plante en diere |\n|---|---|---|\n| Grasveld | oop veld met baie gras en min bome | gras, sebras, wildebeeste, blesbokke |\n| Woud | hoë bome dig bymekaar; koel en skaduryk | geelhoutbome, varings, loeries, bosbokke |\n| See | groot, diep, sout water | kelp, sardyne, dolfyne, haaie |\n| Varswater | riviere, damme en vleie | riete, paddas, visse, seekoeie |\n| Woestyn | baie droog; min reën | vetplante, kokerbome, gemsbokke, meerkatte |\n\nDroë gebiede soos die Karoo en die Kalahari is **halfwoestyne**.\n\n## Plante en diere het mekaar nodig\n\n**Interafhanklikheid** beteken dat lewende dinge van mekaar afhanklik is om te oorleef.\n\n**Diere het plante nodig vir:**\n\n- **kos** – ’n sebra eet gras en ’n kameelperd eet doringboomblare\n- **skuiling en neste** – wewers bou hul neste in bome en uile slaap in hol boomstamme\n- **suurstof** – plante gee die suurstof af wat diere inasem\n\n**Plante het diere nodig vir:**\n\n- **bestuiwing** – bye, kewers en suikerbekkies dra **stuifmeel** van een blom na ’n ander sodat die plant sade kan maak\n- **saadverspreiding** – voëls eet vrugte en die sade val ver weg in hul mis uit; klitse haak aan ’n dier se pels vas en val later elders af\n- **mis** – dieremis maak die grond vrugbaar sodat plante beter groei\n\n> **Onthou:** As een soort plant of dier uit ’n habitat verdwyn, raak dit ander ook. Sonder bye word baie blomme nie bestuif nie, en dan is daar minder vrugte en sade – en minder kos vir diere.\n\n## Gewerweldes: diere met ’n ruggraat\n\nDiere word in twee groot groepe verdeel. **Gewerweldes** het ’n **ruggraat** binne-in hul liggaam. Daar is vyf groepe gewerweldes:\n\n| Groep | Kenmerke | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| Soogdiere | hare of pels; die meeste kry lewendige kleintjies; kleintjies drink melk | mens, leeu, olifant, vlermuis, walvis |\n| Voëls | vere, ’n snawel en twee vlerke; lê eiers met ’n harde dop | arend, volstruis, pikkewyn |\n| Reptiele | droë vel met skubbe; die meeste lê eiers op land | slang, akkedis, skilpad, krokodil |\n| Amfibieë | gladde, klam vel; lê eiers in water; kleintjies leef eers in water | paddas, skurwepaddas |\n| Visse | skubbe, vinne en kieue; leef in water | haai, sardyn, goudvis |\n\n## Ongewerweldes: diere sonder ’n ruggraat\n\n**Ongewerweldes** het geen ruggraat nie. Die meeste diere op aarde is ongewerweldes.\n\n- **Insekte** het **6 pote** en **3 liggaamsdele** (kop, borsstuk en agterlyf), en meestal voelers en vlerke. Voorbeelde: miere, bye, skoenlappers en sprinkane.\n- **Spinnekoppe** het **8 pote** en **2 liggaamsdele**, en geen voelers of vlerke nie.\n- **Wurms** het ’n lang, sagte liggaam sonder pote, soos die erdwurm.\n- **Slakke** het ’n sagte, slymerige liggaam wat op een gespierde voet beweeg, en die meeste dra ’n dop.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** ’n Spinnekop is nie ’n insek nie – tel die pote! En ’n walvis is nie ’n vis nie: dit asem lug in met longe en sy kleintjie drink melk, so dit is ’n **soogdier**.","en":"## The great variety of life\n\nThe Earth is full of living things – from tiny ants to enormous elephants, and from grass to baobab trees. We call this great **variety** of plants and animals **biodiversity**. South Africa has a very rich variety: think of the fynbos in the Western Cape, the bushveld in the Kruger National Park and the kelp forests along the west coast.\n\nTo study all these living things, scientists sort (**classify**) them into groups according to their **features**.\n\n## Habitats: where plants and animals live\n\nA **habitat** is the place where a plant or animal lives. There it finds everything it needs: **food, water, shelter** and a safe place for its young. Plants and animals are **adapted** to their habitat. For example, a fish has gills to breathe in water, and a succulent stores water in its thick leaves so that it can survive dry times.\n\n| Habitat | What it is like | Plants and animals |\n|---|---|---|\n| Grassland | open veld with lots of grass and few trees | grass, zebras, wildebeest, blesbok |\n| Forest | tall trees close together; cool and shady | yellowwood trees, ferns, louries, bushbuck |\n| Sea | big, deep, salty water | kelp, sardines, dolphins, sharks |\n| Freshwater | rivers, dams and wetlands | reeds, frogs, fish, hippos |\n| Desert | very dry; little rain | succulents, quiver trees, gemsbok, meerkats |\n\nDry areas like the Karoo and the Kalahari are **semi-deserts**.\n\n## Plants and animals need each other\n\n**Interdependence** means that living things depend on each other to survive.\n\n**Animals need plants for:**\n\n- **food** – a zebra eats grass and a giraffe eats thorn-tree leaves\n- **shelter and nests** – weavers build their nests in trees and owls sleep in hollow tree trunks\n- **oxygen** – plants give off the oxygen that animals breathe in\n\n**Plants need animals for:**\n\n- **pollination** – bees, beetles and sunbirds carry **pollen** from one flower to another so that the plant can make seeds\n- **seed dispersal** – birds eat fruit and the seeds come out far away in their droppings; burrs hook onto an animal’s fur and fall off somewhere else later\n- **dung** – animal dung makes the soil fertile so that plants grow better\n\n> **Remember:** If one kind of plant or animal disappears from a habitat, it affects others too. Without bees, many flowers are not pollinated, and then there is less fruit and fewer seeds – and less food for animals.\n\n## Vertebrates: animals with a backbone\n\nAnimals are divided into two big groups. **Vertebrates** have a **backbone** inside their body. There are five groups of vertebrates:\n\n| Group | Features | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mammals | hair or fur; most give birth to live young; the young drink milk | human, lion, elephant, bat, whale |\n| Birds | feathers, a beak and two wings; lay eggs with a hard shell | eagle, ostrich, penguin |\n| Reptiles | dry skin with scales; most lay eggs on land | snake, lizard, tortoise, crocodile |\n| Amphibians | smooth, moist skin; lay eggs in water; the young live in water at first | frogs, toads |\n| Fish | scales, fins and gills; live in water | shark, sardine, goldfish |\n\n## Invertebrates: animals without a backbone\n\n**Invertebrates** have no backbone. Most animals on Earth are invertebrates.\n\n- **Insects** have **6 legs** and **3 body parts** (head, thorax and abdomen), and usually antennae and wings. Examples: ants, bees, butterflies and grasshoppers.\n- **Spiders** have **8 legs** and **2 body parts**, and no antennae or wings.\n- **Worms** have a long, soft body without legs, like the earthworm.\n- **Snails** have a soft, slimy body that moves on one muscular foot, and most carry a shell.\n\n> **Common mistake:** A spider is not an insect – count the legs! And a whale is not a fish: it breathes air with lungs and its calf drinks milk, so it is a **mammal**."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Biodiversiteit","en":"Biodiversity"},"def":{"af":"Die groot verskeidenheid plante en diere wat op aarde of in ’n gebied leef.","en":"The great variety of plants and animals that live on Earth or in an area."}},{"term":{"af":"Habitat","en":"Habitat"},"def":{"af":"Die plek waar ’n plant of dier leef en kos, water en skuiling kry.","en":"The place where a plant or animal lives and finds food, water and shelter."}},{"term":{"af":"Aangepas","en":"Adapted"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n plant of dier se liggaam en gedrag goed by sy habitat pas sodat dit daar kan oorleef.","en":"When a plant or animal’s body and behaviour suit its habitat well so that it can survive there."}},{"term":{"af":"Interafhanklikheid","en":"Interdependence"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer lewende dinge van mekaar afhanklik is om te oorleef, soos ’n by en ’n blom.","en":"When living things depend on each other to survive, like a bee and a flower."}},{"term":{"af":"Bestuiwing","en":"Pollination"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer stuifmeel van een blom na ’n ander gedra word sodat die plant sade kan maak.","en":"When pollen is carried from one flower to another so that the plant can make seeds."}},{"term":{"af":"Saadverspreiding","en":"Seed dispersal"},"def":{"af":"Die manier waarop sade ver weg van die moederplant versprei word, byvoorbeeld deur voëls of die wind.","en":"The way seeds are spread far away from the parent plant, for example by birds or the wind."}},{"term":{"af":"Gewerweldes","en":"Vertebrates"},"def":{"af":"Diere met ’n ruggraat: soogdiere, voëls, reptiele, amfibieë en visse.","en":"Animals with a backbone: mammals, birds, reptiles, amphibians and fish."}},{"term":{"af":"Ongewerweldes","en":"Invertebrates"},"def":{"af":"Diere sonder ’n ruggraat, soos insekte, spinnekoppe, wurms en slakke.","en":"Animals without a backbone, such as insects, spiders, worms and snails."}},{"term":{"af":"Soogdier","en":"Mammal"},"def":{"af":"’n Gewerwelde met hare of pels wie se kleintjies melk by die moeder drink.","en":"A vertebrate with hair or fur whose young drink milk from their mother."}},{"term":{"af":"Amfibie","en":"Amphibian"},"def":{"af":"’n Gewerwelde met ’n gladde, klam vel wat sy eiers in water lê, soos ’n padda.","en":"A vertebrate with smooth, moist skin that lays its eggs in water, like a frog."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer ’n dier","en":"Classify an animal"},"problem":{"af":"Fatima sien ’n dier in die Karoo. Dit het ’n droë vel met skubbe en lê eiers in ’n gat in die grond. Is dit ’n gewerwelde of ’n ongewerwelde, en in watter groep pas dit?","en":"Fatima sees an animal in the Karoo. It has dry skin with scales and lays eggs in a hole in the ground. Is it a vertebrate or an invertebrate, and which group does it fit into?"},"steps":[{"af":"Kyk na die vel: **skubbe** kom by visse en reptiele voor.","en":"Look at the skin: **scales** are found on fish and reptiles."},{"af":"Visse leef in water en het kieue en vinne. Hierdie dier leef op land en lê sy eiers op land, so dit is nie ’n vis nie.","en":"Fish live in water and have gills and fins. This animal lives on land and lays its eggs on land, so it is not a fish."},{"af":"’n **Droë, skubberige vel** en eiers op land is die kenmerke van ’n **reptiel**. Alle reptiele het ’n ruggraat.","en":"**Dry, scaly skin** and eggs on land are the features of a **reptile**. All reptiles have a backbone."}],"answer":{"af":"Dit is ’n gewerwelde, en dit is ’n reptiel (byvoorbeeld ’n skilpad of akkedis).","en":"It is a vertebrate, and it is a reptile (for example a tortoise or lizard)."}},{"title":{"af":"Insek of spinnekop?","en":"Insect or spider?"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho kry ’n klein diertjie in die tuin. Dit het 8 pote, 2 liggaamsdele en geen voelers of vlerke nie. Wat is dit?","en":"Sipho finds a small creature in the garden. It has 8 legs, 2 body parts and no antennae or wings. What is it?"},"steps":[{"af":"Dit het ’n harde buitekant en geen ruggraat nie, so dit is ’n **ongewerwelde**.","en":"It has a hard outside and no backbone, so it is an **invertebrate**."},{"af":"Tel die pote: insekte het **6** pote, maar hierdie diertjie het **8**. Dit is dus nie ’n insek nie.","en":"Count the legs: insects have **6** legs, but this creature has **8**. So it is not an insect."},{"af":"8 pote, 2 liggaamsdele en geen voelers nie pas by ’n **spinnekop**.","en":"8 legs, 2 body parts and no antennae match a **spider**."}],"answer":{"af":"Dit is ’n spinnekop, ’n ongewerwelde.","en":"It is a spider, an invertebrate."}},{"title":{"af":"Die suikerbekkie en die aalwyn","en":"The sunbird and the aloe"},"problem":{"af":"’n Suikerbekkie suig nektar uit die blomme van ’n aalwyn. Verduidelik hoe die voël en die plant mekaar help.","en":"A sunbird sucks nectar from the flowers of an aloe. Explain how the bird and the plant help each other."},"steps":[{"af":"Die **voël kry kos**: nektar is ’n soet sap in die blom.","en":"The **bird gets food**: nectar is a sweet juice in the flower."},{"af":"Terwyl die voël drink, kleef **stuifmeel** aan sy kop en snawel vas.","en":"While the bird drinks, **pollen** sticks to its head and beak."},{"af":"By die volgende blom vryf die stuifmeel af. So word die blom **bestuif** en kan die aalwyn sade maak.","en":"At the next flower the pollen rubs off. In this way the flower is **pollinated** and the aloe can make seeds."}],"answer":{"af":"Albei baat: die suikerbekkie kry kos, en die aalwyn word bestuif sodat dit sade kan maak. Dit is interafhanklikheid.","en":"Both benefit: the sunbird gets food, and the aloe is pollinated so that it can make seeds. This is interdependence."}},{"title":{"af":"Aangepas vir ’n habitat","en":"Adapted to a habitat"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik waarom ’n gemsbok in die halfwoestyn kan oorleef, maar ’n seekoei nie.","en":"Explain why a gemsbok can survive in the semi-desert, but a hippo cannot."},"steps":[{"af":"Dink eers aan die habitat: die halfwoestyn is baie droog en daar is min oop water.","en":"First think about the habitat: the semi-desert is very dry and there is little open water."},{"af":"’n Gemsbok kan lank sonder drinkwater klaarkom. Dit kry vog uit die plante wat dit eet.","en":"A gemsbok can manage for a long time without drinking water. It gets moisture from the plants it eats."},{"af":"’n Seekoei bly bedags in ’n rivier of dam om koel te bly en sy vel klam te hou. In die droë halfwoestyn sou dit nie kon oorleef nie.","en":"A hippo stays in a river or dam during the day to keep cool and keep its skin moist. In the dry semi-desert it would not survive."}],"answer":{"af":"Elke dier is aangepas vir sy eie habitat: die gemsbok vir ’n droë habitat en die seekoei vir ’n varswaterhabitat.","en":"Each animal is adapted to its own habitat: the gemsbok to a dry habitat and the hippo to a freshwater habitat."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van hierdie diere is ’n gewerwelde?","en":"Which one of these animals is a vertebrate?"},"options":[{"af":"Erdwurm","en":"Earthworm"},{"af":"Padda","en":"Frog"},{"af":"Slak","en":"Snail"},{"af":"Spinnekop","en":"Spider"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Padda is ’n amfibie, en alle amfibieë het ’n ruggraat. Die erdwurm, slak en spinnekop is ongewerweldes – hulle het geen ruggraat nie.","en":"A frog is an amphibian, and all amphibians have a backbone. The earthworm, snail and spider are invertebrates – they have no backbone."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is ’n habitat?","en":"What is a habitat?"},"options":[{"af":"Die plek waar ’n plant of dier leef en kos, water en skuiling kry","en":"The place where a plant or animal lives and finds food, water and shelter"},{"af":"Die kos wat ’n dier elke dag eet om te kan groei","en":"The food that an animal eats every day so that it can grow"},{"af":"’n Groep diere wat almal dieselfde kenmerke het","en":"A group of animals that all have the same features"},{"af":"Die manier waarop ’n plant sy sade ver weg versprei","en":"The way in which a plant spreads its seeds far away"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Habitat is ’n dier of plant se ‘huis’: die plek waar dit alles kry wat dit nodig het. Kos is net een van die dinge wat ’n habitat verskaf.","en":"A habitat is an animal or plant’s ‘home’: the place where it finds everything it needs. Food is only one of the things a habitat provides."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Walvis is ’n vis, want dit leef in die see.","en":"A whale is a fish, because it lives in the sea."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Walvis asem lug in met longe en sy kleintjie drink melk. Dit is ’n soogdier, al leef dit in die see.","en":"False. A whale breathes air with lungs and its calf drinks milk. It is a mammal, even though it lives in the sea."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Diere sonder ’n ruggraat word ___ genoem.","en":"Animals without a backbone are called ___."},"answers":{"af":["ongewerweldes","ongewerwelde","ongewerwelde diere"],"en":["invertebrates","invertebrate"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["gewerweldes","soogdiere","reptiele"],"en":["vertebrates","mammals","reptiles"]}},"explain":{"af":"*On-* beteken ‘nie’: ongewerweldes het nie ’n ruggraat nie. Soogdiere en reptiele is gewerweldes, want hulle het wel ’n ruggraat.","en":"*In-* means ‘not’: invertebrates do not have a backbone. Mammals and reptiles are vertebrates, because they do have a backbone."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Anika kry ’n diertjie met 6 pote, 3 liggaamsdele en twee voelers. Wat is dit?","en":"Anika finds a small creature with 6 legs, 3 body parts and two antennae. What is it?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Spinnekop","en":"A spider"},{"af":"’n Wurm","en":"A worm"},{"af":"’n Slak","en":"A snail"},{"af":"’n Insek","en":"An insect"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Insekte het 6 pote, 3 liggaamsdele (kop, borsstuk en agterlyf) en meestal voelers. ’n Spinnekop het 8 pote en geen voelers nie; wurms en slakke het geen pote nie.","en":"Insects have 6 legs, 3 body parts (head, thorax and abdomen) and usually antennae. A spider has 8 legs and no antennae; worms and snails have no legs."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke dier by sy groep gewerweldes.","en":"Match each animal to its group of vertebrates."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Volstruis","en":"Ostrich"},"r":{"af":"Voël","en":"Bird"}},{"l":{"af":"Krokodil","en":"Crocodile"},"r":{"af":"Reptiel","en":"Reptile"}},{"l":{"af":"Vlermuis","en":"Bat"},"r":{"af":"Soogdier","en":"Mammal"}},{"l":{"af":"Skurwepadda","en":"Toad"},"r":{"af":"Amfibie","en":"Amphibian"}},{"l":{"af":"Haai","en":"Shark"},"r":{"af":"Vis","en":"Fish"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die volstruis het vere (voël), die krokodil ’n droë, skubberige vel (reptiel), die vlermuis pels en melk vir sy kleintjies (soogdier), die skurwepadda lê eiers in water (amfibie) en die haai het kieue en vinne (vis).","en":"The ostrich has feathers (bird), the crocodile dry, scaly skin (reptile), the bat fur and milk for its young (mammal), the toad lays eggs in water (amphibian) and the shark has gills and fins (fish)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voorbeeld wys hoe ’n dier help met saadverspreiding?","en":"Which example shows how an animal helps with seed dispersal?"},"options":[{"af":"’n By suig nektar uit ’n blom","en":"A bee sucks nectar from a flower"},{"af":"’n Wewer bou ’n nes in ’n doringboom","en":"A weaver builds a nest in a thorn tree"},{"af":"’n Voël eet ’n vrug en die sade val elders in sy mis uit","en":"A bird eats a fruit and the seeds come out elsewhere in its droppings"},{"af":"’n Sebra eet gras in die oop grasveld","en":"A zebra eats grass in the open grassland"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Saadverspreiding beteken dat sade ver van die moederplant af beland. Die voël dra die sade in sy maag weg. Die by help met bestuiwing, nie saadverspreiding nie.","en":"Seed dispersal means that seeds end up far from the parent plant. The bird carries the seeds away in its stomach. The bee helps with pollination, not seed dispersal."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Bye dra ___ van blom na blom, en so word die blomme bestuif.","en":"Bees carry ___ from flower to flower, and in this way the flowers are pollinated."},"answers":{"af":["stuifmeel"],"en":["pollen"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["nektar","sade","water"],"en":["nectar","seeds","water"]}},"explain":{"af":"Bestuiwing gebeur wanneer stuifmeel van een blom na ’n ander gedra word. Nektar is die soet sap wat die by as kos drink – dit is die beloning, maar dit bestuif nie die blom nie.","en":"Pollination happens when pollen is carried from one flower to another. Nectar is the sweet juice the bee drinks as food – it is the reward, but it does not pollinate the flower."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die meeste diere op aarde is ongewerweldes.","en":"Most animals on Earth are invertebrates."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Daar is baie meer soorte insekte, spinnekoppe, wurms en slakke as soorte soogdiere, voëls, reptiele, amfibieë en visse saam.","en":"True. There are many more kinds of insects, spiders, worms and snails than kinds of mammals, birds, reptiles, amphibians and fish together."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter kenmerk het alle voëls?","en":"Which feature do all birds have?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle het vere","en":"They have feathers"},{"af":"Hulle kan vlieg","en":"They can fly"},{"af":"Hulle kry lewendige kleintjies","en":"They give birth to live young"},{"af":"Hulle leef in bome","en":"They live in trees"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Alle voëls het vere. ’n Volstruis en ’n pikkewyn kan nie vlieg nie, maar hulle is tog voëls. Voëls lê eiers; hulle kry nie lewendige kleintjies nie.","en":"All birds have feathers. An ostrich and a penguin cannot fly, but they are still birds. Birds lay eggs; they do not give birth to live young."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter dier is die beste aangepas om in ’n droë halfwoestyn te leef?","en":"Which animal is best adapted to live in a dry semi-desert?"},"options":[{"af":"Seekoei","en":"Hippo"},{"af":"Dolfyn","en":"Dolphin"},{"af":"Loerie","en":"Lourie"},{"af":"Gemsbok","en":"Gemsbok"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die gemsbok kan lank sonder drinkwater klaarkom en kry vog uit sy kos. Die seekoei het ’n rivier of dam nodig, die dolfyn leef in die see en die loerie in die woud.","en":"The gemsbok can manage for a long time without drinking water and gets moisture from its food. The hippo needs a river or dam, the dolphin lives in the sea and the lourie in the forest."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Padda het ’n gladde, klam vel en lê sy eiers in water. Daarom behoort ’n padda tot die groep ___.","en":"A frog has smooth, moist skin and lays its eggs in water. So a frog belongs to the group of ___."},"answers":{"af":["amfibieë","amfibiee","amfibie"],"en":["amphibians","amphibian"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["reptiele","insekte","soogdiere"],"en":["reptiles","insects","mammals"]}},"explain":{"af":"Amfibieë het ’n gladde, klam vel en lê eiers in water. Reptiele het ’n droë vel met skubbe en lê hul eiers op land.","en":"Amphibians have smooth, moist skin and lay eggs in water. Reptiles have dry skin with scales and lay their eggs on land."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Al die bye in ’n boord verdwyn. Wat sal waarskynlik met die vrugtebome gebeur?","en":"All the bees in an orchard disappear. What will most likely happen to the fruit trees?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle sal meer vrugte dra, want niks drink die nektar nie","en":"They will bear more fruit, because nothing drinks the nectar"},{"af":"Niks sal verander nie, want bome het net water en sonlig nodig","en":"Nothing will change, because trees only need water and sunlight"},{"af":"Hulle sal minder vrugte dra, want minder blomme word bestuif","en":"They will bear less fruit, because fewer flowers are pollinated"},{"af":"Hulle sal self hul stuifmeel na ander bome toe dra","en":"They will carry their own pollen to other trees"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Plante en diere is interafhanklik. Bye bestuif die blomme; sonder bestuiwing vorm daar minder vrugte en sade. Bome kan nie self stuifmeel van boom tot boom dra nie.","en":"Plants and animals are interdependent. Bees pollinate the flowers; without pollination fewer fruits and seeds form. Trees cannot carry pollen from tree to tree by themselves."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Vlermuis kan vlieg. Waarom is dit tog ’n soogdier en nie ’n voël nie?","en":"A bat can fly. Why is it still a mammal and not a bird?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit het vlerke en vlieg net snags","en":"It has wings and only flies at night"},{"af":"Dit het pels en sy kleintjies drink melk","en":"It has fur and its young drink milk"},{"af":"Dit slaap bedags onderstebo in grotte","en":"It sleeps upside down in caves by day"},{"af":"Dit lê sy eiers in ’n nes in ’n grot","en":"It lays its eggs in a nest in a cave"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Ons klassifiseer diere volgens hul kenmerke, nie volgens hoe hulle beweeg nie. ’n Vlermuis het pels en sy kleintjies drink melk – kenmerke van ’n soogdier. Dit het nie vere nie en lê nie eiers nie.","en":"We classify animals by their features, not by how they move. A bat has fur and its young drink milk – features of a mammal. It has no feathers and does not lay eggs."}}]},{"id":"nwt5-t1-dierskelette","title":{"af":"Dierskelette","en":"Animal skeletons"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die dele en werke van ’n skelet kan noem, kan verduidelik hoe bene, gewrigte en spiere saamwerk, en die skelette van verskillende diere kan vergelyk.","en":"You will be able to name the parts and jobs of a skeleton, explain how bones, joints and muscles work together, and compare the skeletons of different animals."},"summary":{"af":"## Waarom diere ’n skelet het\n\n’n **Skelet** is die raamwerk wat ’n dier se liggaam ondersteun. Sonder ’n skelet sou jy soos ’n sak water op die vloer lê! Die skelet het drie belangrike werke:\n\n1. **Steun en vorm** – dit hou die liggaam regop en gee dit sy vorm.\n2. **Beskerming** – dit beskerm die sagte organe binne-in die liggaam.\n3. **Beweging** – spiere trek aan die bene sodat die dier kan beweeg.\n\n## Die binneskelet van gewerweldes\n\nAlle gewerweldes – soogdiere, voëls, reptiele, amfibieë en visse – het ’n **binneskelet** of **endoskelet**. Dit lê binne-in die liggaam, onder die spiere en die vel, en dit **groei saam** met die dier. ’n Volwasse mens het 206 bene.\n\n| Deel | Waar dit is | Werk |\n|---|---|---|\n| Skedel | kop | beskerm die brein |\n| Ruggraat | middel van die rug | steun die liggaam en beskerm die rugmurg |\n| Ribbes (ribbekas) | bors | beskerm die hart en longe |\n| Ledemate | arms en bene (of vlerke en vinne) | help die dier om te beweeg |\n\nDie **ruggraat** bestaan uit baie klein bene, die **werwels**, wat soos krale aan ’n tou aanmekaar geryg is. Omdat daar so baie werwels is, kan jy jou rug buig en draai. Binne-in die werwels loop die **rugmurg**, ’n bondel senuwees wat boodskappe tussen die brein en die res van die liggaam dra.\n\n## Beweging: bene, gewrigte en spiere\n\n’n **Gewrig** is die plek waar twee bene bymekaarkom. Gewrigte laat die skelet buig en draai – dink aan jou knie, elmboog, skouer en heup. Bene kan nie self beweeg nie; **spiere** beweeg hulle.\n\n- Spiere is met taai **senings** aan die bene vas.\n- ’n Spier kan net **trek** (korter en dikker word); dit kan nie stoot nie.\n- Daarom werk spiere in **pare**. As jy jou arm buig, trek die **biseps** voor op jou bo-arm. As jy jou arm reguit maak, trek die **triseps** agter op jou bo-arm.\n\n> **Onthou:** Bene, gewrigte en spiere werk altyd saam. Die bene is die raam, die gewrigte is die skarniere en die spiere is die ‘motors’ wat trek.\n\n## Skelette vergelyk\n\nAl die gewerweldes het ’n skedel en ’n ruggraat, maar elke skelet is aangepas vir hoe die dier leef en beweeg.\n\n| Dier | Spesiale kenmerke van die skelet |\n|---|---|\n| Mens | regop ruggraat; twee bene om op te loop en twee arms met hande om dinge vas te hou; groot skedel vir ’n groot brein |\n| Voël | ligte, **hol bene** sodat dit maklik kan vlieg; die vlerke is die voorste ledemate; ’n groot borsbeen vir die sterk vliegspiere |\n| Vis | lang ruggraat met baie dun grate; geen arms of bene nie, maar vinne; spiere buig die ruggraat heen en weer om te swem |\n| Slang | baie lang ruggraat met **honderde werwels** en baie ribbes; geen ledemate nie; dit beweeg deur sy liggaam in kronkels te buig |\n\n## Ongewerweldes: buiteskelet of geen skelet\n\nOngewerweldes het geen ruggraat nie, maar party het tog ’n skelet.\n\n- **Insekte**, spinnekoppe en krappe het ’n harde **buiteskelet** of **eksoskelet** aan die buitekant van die liggaam, soos ’n wapenrusting. Dit steun en beskerm die liggaam, en die spiere is aan die binnekant daaraan vas. Die buiteskelet groei nie saam nie: die dier moet dit afwerp (**vervel**) en dan word ’n nuwe, groter een hard.\n- ’n **Erdwurm** het **geen skelet** van bene of ’n harde dop nie. Sy sagte liggaam is vol vloeistof, wat help dat dit sy vorm hou. Spiere maak die liggaam beurtelings lank en dun en dan kort en dik, en klein borseltjies help die wurm om vorentoe te kruip.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie dink die bene in jou liggaam is dood en droog nie. Hulle is lewend: hulle groei saam met jou, en ’n gebreekte been kan weer heel word. En ’n slang is nie ’n ongewerwelde nie – dit het ’n baie lang ruggraat!","en":"## Why animals have a skeleton\n\nA **skeleton** is the framework that supports an animal’s body. Without a skeleton you would lie on the floor like a bag of water! The skeleton has three important jobs:\n\n1. **Support and shape** – it holds the body up and gives it its shape.\n2. **Protection** – it protects the soft organs inside the body.\n3. **Movement** – muscles pull on the bones so that the animal can move.\n\n## The inner skeleton of vertebrates\n\nAll vertebrates – mammals, birds, reptiles, amphibians and fish – have an **inner skeleton** or **endoskeleton**. It lies inside the body, under the muscles and the skin, and it **grows with** the animal. An adult human has 206 bones.\n\n| Part | Where it is | Job |\n|---|---|---|\n| Skull | head | protects the brain |\n| Backbone | middle of the back | supports the body and protects the spinal cord |\n| Ribs (ribcage) | chest | protect the heart and lungs |\n| Limbs | arms and legs (or wings and fins) | help the animal to move |\n\nThe **backbone** is made of many small bones, the **vertebrae**, that are threaded together like beads on a string. Because there are so many vertebrae, you can bend and twist your back. The **spinal cord** runs inside the vertebrae. It is a bundle of nerves that carries messages between the brain and the rest of the body.\n\n## Movement: bones, joints and muscles\n\nA **joint** is the place where two bones meet. Joints let the skeleton bend and turn – think of your knee, elbow, shoulder and hip. Bones cannot move by themselves; **muscles** move them.\n\n- Muscles are attached to the bones by tough **tendons**.\n- A muscle can only **pull** (become shorter and fatter); it cannot push.\n- That is why muscles work in **pairs**. When you bend your arm, the **biceps** at the front of your upper arm pulls. When you straighten your arm, the **triceps** at the back of your upper arm pulls.\n\n> **Remember:** Bones, joints and muscles always work together. The bones are the frame, the joints are the hinges and the muscles are the ‘motors’ that pull.\n\n## Comparing skeletons\n\nAll vertebrates have a skull and a backbone, but each skeleton is adapted to how the animal lives and moves.\n\n| Animal | Special features of the skeleton |\n|---|---|\n| Human | upright backbone; two legs to walk on and two arms with hands to hold things; large skull for a large brain |\n| Bird | light, **hollow bones** so that it can fly easily; the wings are the front limbs; a large breastbone for the strong flying muscles |\n| Fish | long backbone with many thin fish bones; no arms or legs, but fins; muscles bend the backbone from side to side to swim |\n| Snake | very long backbone with **hundreds of vertebrae** and many ribs; no limbs; it moves by bending its body in curves |\n\n## Invertebrates: outer skeleton or no skeleton\n\nInvertebrates have no backbone, but some of them do have a skeleton.\n\n- **Insects**, spiders and crabs have a hard **outer skeleton** or **exoskeleton** on the outside of the body, like a suit of armour. It supports and protects the body, and the muscles are attached to the inside of it. The exoskeleton does not grow with the animal: the animal must shed it (**moult**), and then a new, bigger one hardens.\n- An **earthworm** has **no skeleton** of bones or a hard shell. Its soft body is full of fluid, which helps it keep its shape. Muscles make the body long and thin and then short and fat in turns, and tiny bristles help the worm to crawl forward.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Don’t think that the bones in your body are dead and dry. They are alive: they grow with you, and a broken bone can heal again. And a snake is not an invertebrate – it has a very long backbone!"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Skelet","en":"Skeleton"},"def":{"af":"Die raamwerk wat ’n dier se liggaam steun, beskerm en help beweeg.","en":"The framework that supports and protects an animal’s body and helps it to move."}},{"term":{"af":"Binneskelet (endoskelet)","en":"Inner skeleton (endoskeleton)"},"def":{"af":"’n Skelet van bene binne-in die liggaam wat saam met die dier groei, soos by alle gewerweldes.","en":"A skeleton of bones inside the body that grows with the animal, as in all vertebrates."}},{"term":{"af":"Buiteskelet (eksoskelet)","en":"Outer skeleton (exoskeleton)"},"def":{"af":"’n Harde bedekking aan die buitekant van die liggaam, soos by insekte en krappe.","en":"A hard covering on the outside of the body, as in insects and crabs."}},{"term":{"af":"Ruggraat","en":"Backbone"},"def":{"af":"Die ry werwels in die rug wat die liggaam steun en die rugmurg beskerm.","en":"The row of vertebrae in the back that supports the body and protects the spinal cord."}},{"term":{"af":"Werwels","en":"Vertebrae"},"def":{"af":"Die klein bene wat op mekaar gestapel is en saam die ruggraat vorm.","en":"The small bones that are stacked on top of each other and together form the backbone."}},{"term":{"af":"Skedel","en":"Skull"},"def":{"af":"Die harde bene van die kop wat die brein beskerm.","en":"The hard bones of the head that protect the brain."}},{"term":{"af":"Ribbekas","en":"Ribcage"},"def":{"af":"Die ribbes wat soos ’n hok om die hart en longe sit en hulle beskerm.","en":"The ribs that form a cage around the heart and lungs and protect them."}},{"term":{"af":"Gewrig","en":"Joint"},"def":{"af":"Die plek waar twee bene bymekaarkom en waar die skelet kan buig of draai.","en":"The place where two bones meet and where the skeleton can bend or turn."}},{"term":{"af":"Spier","en":"Muscle"},"def":{"af":"’n Deel van die liggaam wat korter word en aan ’n been trek om dit te beweeg.","en":"A part of the body that becomes shorter and pulls on a bone to move it."}},{"term":{"af":"Vervel","en":"Moult"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n dier sy ou buiteskelet afwerp sodat dit groter kan word.","en":"When an animal sheds its old outer skeleton so that it can grow bigger."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Watter deel beskerm die hart?","en":"Which part protects the heart?"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato val van haar fiets af en tref haar bors teen die grond. Sy is net bietjie seer. Watter deel van haar skelet het haar hart en longe beskerm, en hoe?","en":"Lerato falls off her bicycle and hits her chest on the ground. She is only a little bit sore. Which part of her skeleton protected her heart and lungs, and how?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die hart en longe lê in die **bors**.","en":"The heart and lungs lie in the **chest**."},{"af":"Die **ribbes** buig van die ruggraat om die bors en vorm ’n **ribbekas**, soos ’n hok.","en":"The **ribs** curve from the backbone around the chest and form a **ribcage**, like a cage."},{"af":"Die harde bene vang die stamp op sodat die sagte organe binne-in nie beseer word nie.","en":"The hard bones take the bump so that the soft organs inside are not injured."}],"answer":{"af":"Die ribbekas (ribbes) het haar hart en longe beskerm.","en":"The ribcage (ribs) protected her heart and lungs."}},{"title":{"af":"Spiere werk in pare","en":"Muscles work in pairs"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo lig ’n glas water na sy mond en sit dit dan weer neer. Verduidelik wat sy elmbooggewrig en sy armspiere doen.","en":"Thabo lifts a glass of water to his mouth and then puts it down again. Explain what his elbow joint and his arm muscles do."},"steps":[{"af":"Die **elmboog** is ’n gewrig: dit laat die onderarm op en af buig.","en":"The **elbow** is a joint: it lets the lower arm bend up and down."},{"af":"Om die glas op te lig, trek die **biseps** (voor op die bo-arm) saam en trek die onderarm op. Die triseps ontspan.","en":"To lift the glass, the **biceps** (front of the upper arm) contracts and pulls the lower arm up. The triceps relaxes."},{"af":"Om die glas neer te sit, trek die **triseps** (agter op die bo-arm) saam en trek die arm reguit. Nou ontspan die biseps.","en":"To put the glass down, the **triceps** (back of the upper arm) contracts and pulls the arm straight. Now the biceps relaxes."},{"af":"’n Spier kan net trek, nie stoot nie – daarom is twee spiere nodig.","en":"A muscle can only pull, not push – that is why two muscles are needed."}],"answer":{"af":"Die elmbooggewrig laat die arm buig; die biseps trek die arm op en die triseps trek dit weer reguit.","en":"The elbow joint lets the arm bend; the biceps pulls the arm up and the triceps pulls it straight again."}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyk ’n voël en ’n slang","en":"Compare a bird and a snake"},"problem":{"af":"Noem een ooreenkoms en twee verskille tussen die skelet van ’n voël en dié van ’n slang.","en":"Give one similarity and two differences between the skeleton of a bird and that of a snake."},"steps":[{"af":"**Ooreenkoms:** albei is gewerweldes, so albei het ’n binneskelet met ’n skedel en ’n ruggraat.","en":"**Similarity:** both are vertebrates, so both have an inner skeleton with a skull and a backbone."},{"af":"**Verskil 1 – ledemate:** die voël het vlerke en bene; die slang het geen ledemate nie.","en":"**Difference 1 – limbs:** the bird has wings and legs; the snake has no limbs."},{"af":"**Verskil 2 – ruggraat:** die slang se ruggraat is baie lank met honderde werwels en baie ribbes sodat dit kan kronkel; die voël se ruggraat is korter, en die werwels in sy rug is aan mekaar vasgegroei sodat dit styf en stewig is vir vlieg.","en":"**Difference 2 – backbone:** the snake’s backbone is very long with hundreds of vertebrae and many ribs so that it can wriggle; the bird’s backbone is shorter, and the vertebrae in its back are joined together so that it is stiff and steady for flying."},{"af":"Jy kan ook noem dat die voël se bene hol en lig is om te vlieg.","en":"You can also mention that the bird’s bones are hollow and light for flying."}],"answer":{"af":"Albei het ’n skedel en ruggraat. Die voël het ledemate (vlerke en bene) en hol bene; die slang het geen ledemate nie en ’n baie lang ruggraat met honderde werwels.","en":"Both have a skull and backbone. The bird has limbs (wings and legs) and hollow bones; the snake has no limbs and a very long backbone with hundreds of vertebrae."}},{"title":{"af":"Binneskelet of buiteskelet?","en":"Inner or outer skeleton?"},"problem":{"af":"Liam kyk na ’n sprinkaan en ’n akkedis. Hy kry ook die leë ‘dop’ van ’n sprinkaan op ’n blaar. Watter dier het watter soort skelet, en waar kom die leë dop vandaan?","en":"Liam looks at a grasshopper and a lizard. He also finds the empty ‘shell’ of a grasshopper on a leaf. Which animal has which kind of skeleton, and where does the empty shell come from?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die akkedis is ’n reptiel, ’n gewerwelde. Dit het ’n **binneskelet** met ’n ruggraat.","en":"The lizard is a reptile, a vertebrate. It has an **inner skeleton** with a backbone."},{"af":"Die sprinkaan is ’n insek, ’n ongewerwelde. Dit het ’n harde **buiteskelet**.","en":"The grasshopper is an insect, an invertebrate. It has a hard **outer skeleton**."},{"af":"’n Buiteskelet groei nie saam nie. Die sprinkaan het sy ou, te klein buiteskelet afgewerp (**vervel**). Dit is die leë dop.","en":"An outer skeleton does not grow with the animal. The grasshopper shed its old, too-small outer skeleton (**moulted**). That is the empty shell."}],"answer":{"af":"Die akkedis het ’n binneskelet en die sprinkaan ’n buiteskelet. Die leë dop is ’n afgewerpte buiteskelet van ’n sprinkaan wat vervel het.","en":"The lizard has an inner skeleton and the grasshopper an outer skeleton. The empty shell is a shed outer skeleton of a grasshopper that moulted."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter deel van die skelet beskerm die brein?","en":"Which part of the skeleton protects the brain?"},"options":[{"af":"Die ribbes","en":"The ribs"},{"af":"Die skedel","en":"The skull"},{"af":"Die ruggraat","en":"The backbone"},{"af":"Die ledemate","en":"The limbs"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die skedel is ’n harde ‘helm’ van been om die brein. Die ribbes beskerm die hart en longe, en die ruggraat beskerm die rugmurg.","en":"The skull is a hard ‘helmet’ of bone around the brain. The ribs protect the heart and lungs, and the backbone protects the spinal cord."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat noem ons die klein bene waaruit die ruggraat bestaan?","en":"What do we call the small bones that make up the backbone?"},"options":[{"af":"Gewrigte","en":"Joints"},{"af":"Senings","en":"Tendons"},{"af":"Werwels","en":"Vertebrae"},{"af":"Ribbes","en":"Ribs"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die ruggraat is ’n stapel klein bene wat werwels heet. Daarom word diere met ’n ruggraat gewerweldes genoem. Senings heg spiere aan bene vas.","en":"The backbone is a stack of small bones called vertebrae. That is why animals with a backbone are called vertebrates. Tendons attach muscles to bones."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die plek waar twee bene bymekaarkom, heet ’n ___.","en":"The place where two bones meet is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["gewrig"],"en":["joint"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["spier","sening","werwel"],"en":["muscle","tendon","vertebra"]}},"explain":{"af":"By ’n gewrig, soos die knie of elmboog, kan die skelet buig of draai. ’n Spier beweeg die bene, maar dit is nie die plek waar hulle bymekaarkom nie.","en":"At a joint, such as the knee or elbow, the skeleton can bend or turn. A muscle moves the bones, but it is not the place where they meet."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Spier kan ’n been stoot sowel as trek.","en":"A muscle can push a bone as well as pull it."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Spier kan net trek. Daarom werk spiere in pare: een spier trek die been in een rigting en die ander spier trek dit terug.","en":"False. A muscle can only pull. That is why muscles work in pairs: one muscle pulls the bone one way and the other muscle pulls it back."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom het voëls hol bene?","en":"Why do birds have hollow bones?"},"options":[{"af":"Om die liggaam lig te maak sodat die voël maklik kan vlieg","en":"To make the body light so that the bird can fly easily"},{"af":"Sodat die bene maklik breek as die voël val","en":"So that the bones break easily if the bird falls"},{"af":"Om water in te stoor vir droë tye","en":"To store water in for dry times"},{"af":"Sodat die voël in die winter warm bly","en":"So that the bird stays warm in winter"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Hol bene is lig maar tog sterk, soos ’n buis. ’n Ligte liggaam het minder krag nodig om in die lug te bly.","en":"Hollow bones are light but still strong, like a tube. A light body needs less force to stay in the air."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter dier het ’n buiteskelet?","en":"Which animal has an outer skeleton?"},"options":[{"af":"Slang","en":"Snake"},{"af":"Erdwurm","en":"Earthworm"},{"af":"Vis","en":"Fish"},{"af":"Kewer","en":"Beetle"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Kewer is ’n insek en insekte het ’n harde buiteskelet. Die slang en die vis het ’n binneskelet, en die erdwurm het geen skelet nie.","en":"A beetle is an insect, and insects have a hard outer skeleton. The snake and the fish have an inner skeleton, and the earthworm has no skeleton."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke deel by sy werk.","en":"Match each part to its job."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Skedel","en":"Skull"},"r":{"af":"Beskerm die brein","en":"Protects the brain"}},{"l":{"af":"Ribbekas","en":"Ribcage"},"r":{"af":"Beskerm die hart en longe","en":"Protects the heart and lungs"}},{"l":{"af":"Ruggraat","en":"Backbone"},"r":{"af":"Steun die liggaam en beskerm die rugmurg","en":"Supports the body and protects the spinal cord"}},{"l":{"af":"Gewrig","en":"Joint"},"r":{"af":"Laat die skelet buig","en":"Lets the skeleton bend"}},{"l":{"af":"Spier","en":"Muscle"},"r":{"af":"Trek aan ’n been om dit te beweeg","en":"Pulls on a bone to move it"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die skedel, ribbekas en ruggraat steun en beskerm. Gewrigte en spiere werk saam vir beweging: die gewrig is die skarnier en die spier trek.","en":"The skull, ribcage and backbone support and protect. Joints and muscles work together for movement: the joint is the hinge and the muscle pulls."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die ribbes beskerm die hart en die ___.","en":"The ribs protect the heart and the ___."},"answers":{"af":["longe","long"],"en":["lungs","lung"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["brein","maag","rugmurg"],"en":["brain","stomach","spinal cord"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die hart en longe lê saam in die bors, binne-in die ribbekas. Die brein word deur die skedel beskerm en die rugmurg deur die ruggraat.","en":"The heart and lungs lie together in the chest, inside the ribcage. The brain is protected by the skull and the spinal cord by the backbone."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling oor ’n slang se skelet is korrek?","en":"Which statement about a snake’s skeleton is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit het geen skelet nie, net sterk spiere","en":"It has no skeleton, only strong muscles"},{"af":"Dit het ’n baie lang ruggraat met honderde werwels","en":"It has a very long backbone with hundreds of vertebrae"},{"af":"Dit het ’n harde buiteskelet wat dit afwerp","en":"It has a hard outer skeleton that it sheds"},{"af":"Dit het ’n skedel, maar geen ruggraat nie","en":"It has a skull, but no backbone"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Slang is ’n reptiel en dus ’n gewerwelde. Sy baie lang ruggraat met honderde werwels en ribbes laat hom kronkel. ’n Slang vervel wel, maar dit is sy vel, nie ’n buiteskelet nie.","en":"A snake is a reptile and so a vertebrate. Its very long backbone with hundreds of vertebrae and ribs lets it wriggle. A snake does shed, but that is its skin, not an outer skeleton."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Erdwurm het geen bene of harde skelet nie.","en":"An earthworm has no bones and no hard skeleton."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Erdwurm het geen bene en geen harde buiteskelet nie. Sy liggaam is vol vloeistof, en spiere maak dit lank en kort sodat dit kan kruip.","en":"True. An earthworm has no bones and no hard outer skeleton. Its body is full of fluid, and muscles make it long and short so that it can crawl."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom moet ’n sprinkaan vervel om groter te word?","en":"Why must a grasshopper moult to grow bigger?"},"options":[{"af":"Sy harde buiteskelet groei nie saam met sy liggaam nie","en":"Its hard outer skeleton does not grow with its body"},{"af":"Sy bene word te swaar om mee te spring","en":"Its legs become too heavy to jump with"},{"af":"Sy binneskelet word te klein vir sy brein","en":"Its inner skeleton becomes too small for its brain"},{"af":"Dit moet van kleur verander om weg te kruip","en":"It must change colour to hide"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Buiteskelet is hard en kan nie rek nie. Die sprinkaan werp die ou een af, en ’n nuwe, groter een word hard. ’n Sprinkaan het nie ’n binneskelet nie.","en":"An outer skeleton is hard and cannot stretch. The grasshopper sheds the old one, and a new, bigger one hardens. A grasshopper does not have an inner skeleton."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Insek se harde skelet aan die buitekant van die liggaam heet ’n ___.","en":"An insect’s hard skeleton on the outside of the body is called its ___."},"answers":{"af":["buiteskelet","eksoskelet"],"en":["exoskeleton","outer skeleton"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["binneskelet","endoskelet","ruggraat"],"en":["endoskeleton","inner skeleton","backbone"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Ekso-* beteken buite en *endo-* beteken binne. Insekte, spinnekoppe en krappe het ’n buiteskelet; gewerweldes het ’n binneskelet.","en":"*Exo-* means outside and *endo-* means inside. Insects, spiders and crabs have an exoskeleton; vertebrates have an endoskeleton."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter buig sy arm om ’n swaar tas op te lig. Watter spier trek saam?","en":"Pieter bends his arm to lift a heavy bag. Which muscle contracts?"},"options":[{"af":"Die triseps agter op die bo-arm","en":"The triceps at the back of the upper arm"},{"af":"Die kuitspier agter op die been","en":"The calf muscle at the back of the leg"},{"af":"Albei armspiere stoot saam","en":"Both arm muscles push together"},{"af":"Die biseps voor op die bo-arm","en":"The biceps at the front of the upper arm"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Om die arm te buig, trek die biseps saam en trek die onderarm op, terwyl die triseps ontspan. Spiere stoot nooit nie – hulle trek net.","en":"To bend the arm, the biceps contracts and pulls the lower arm up, while the triceps relaxes. Muscles never push – they only pull."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Johan sê die skelet se enigste werk is om die liggaam te beskerm. Watter ander werke het die skelet ook?","en":"Johan says the skeleton’s only job is to protect the body. Which other jobs does the skeleton also have?"},"options":[{"af":"Om kos te verteer en asem te haal","en":"To digest food and to breathe"},{"af":"Om bloed te pomp en te dink","en":"To pump blood and to think"},{"af":"Om die liggaam te steun en beweging moontlik te maak","en":"To support the body and make movement possible"},{"af":"Om water te stoor en die liggaam warm te hou","en":"To store water and keep the body warm"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die skelet het drie werke: steun en vorm, beskerming, en beweging saam met die spiere. Vertering, asemhaling en bloed pomp is die werk van organe soos die maag, longe en hart.","en":"The skeleton has three jobs: support and shape, protection, and movement together with the muscles. Digesting, breathing and pumping blood are the work of organs like the stomach, lungs and heart."}}]},{"id":"nwt5-t1-skelette-strukture","title":{"af":"Skelette as strukture (Tegnologie)","en":"Skeletons as structures (Technology)"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal raam-, dop- en soliede strukture kan herken, kan verduidelik hoe driehoeke, kruisstutte en buise ’n struktuur sterker maak, en die ontwerpproses kan gebruik om ’n strooitjietoring te bou.","en":"You will be able to recognise frame, shell and solid structures, explain how triangles, cross braces and tubes make a structure stronger, and use the design process to build a straw tower."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is ’n struktuur?\n\n’n **Struktuur** is iets met ’n vaste vorm wat gewig kan dra, iets kan beskerm of iets kan ondersteun sonder om inmekaar te val. Daar is **natuurlike strukture**, soos jou skelet, ’n voëlnes en ’n eierdop, en **mensgemaakte strukture**, soos brûe, huise, kragmaste en stoele. Jou skelet is eintlik ’n struktuur: dit steun jou liggaam en beskerm jou organe, net soos die raam van ’n gebou.\n\n## Drie soorte strukture\n\n| Soort | Hoe dit werk | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| Raamstruktuur | ’n geraamte van dun, sterk dele wat by lasse aan mekaar vas is; dikwels met ’n bedekking oor | kragmas, fietsraam, dakkappe, tent, ’n mens se skelet |\n| Dopstruktuur | ’n dun, harde, dikwels geboë buitelaag; hol binne; beskerm wat binne is | eierdop, helm, koeldrankblikkie, skilpaddop |\n| Soliede struktuur | massief, deur en deur van dieselfde materiaal; sterk deur sy dikte en gewig | damwal, baksteenmuur, sandkasteel |\n\n**Raamstrukture** gebruik min materiaal en is daarom lig. ’n Tent se pale is die raam en die seil is die bedekking – net soos jou bene die raam is en jou vel die bedekking.\n\n**Dopstrukture** is sterk omdat die **geboë vorm** die krag oor die hele dop versprei. Daarom beskerm ’n helm jou kop: die stamp word oor die hele helm versprei. ’n Koeldrankblikkie is sterk as jy bo-op druk, maar as jy die kant effens indruk, val dit maklik inmekaar.\n\nDiere se skelette werk net so: ’n gewerwelde se binneskelet is soos ’n **raamstruktuur**, en ’n insek se buiteskelet of ’n skilpad se dop is soos ’n **dopstruktuur**.\n\n## Strukture sterker en stywer maak\n\n1. **Driehoeke** – ’n Vierkantige raam kan maklik skeef gedruk word; dit wikkel. ’n Driehoek hou sy vorm. Daarom is kragmaste, dakkappe en brûe vol driehoeke.\n2. **Kruisstutte** – ’n Skuins stuk van hoek tot hoek dwars oor ’n vierkant verdeel dit in twee driehoeke en maak dit styf. Kyk maar na ’n plaashek!\n3. **Buisvorms** – ’n Plat vel papier knak maklik, maar as jy dit in ’n **buis** oprol, dra dit baie meer gewig. Fietsrame is van hol buise gemaak: sterk, maar lig – net soos voëlbene.\n4. **Sterk lasse** – ’n **Las** is die plek waar twee dele aan mekaar vas is. As die lasse swak is, val die hele struktuur inmekaar. Jy kan lasse met gom, kleefband, tou, spykers of skroewe maak.\n5. **’n Wye basis** – ’n struktuur met ’n breë voet val nie maklik om nie; dit is **stabiel**.\n\n## Die ontwerpproses\n\nIngenieurs volg die **ontwerpproses** om probleme op te los:\n\n1. **Ondersoek** – Vind uit wat die probleem is, kyk na bestaande oplossings en toets materiale. Skryf ’n **ontwerpopdrag** (wat jy gaan maak, vir wie en waarom), **spesifikasies** (wat die produk moet kan doen) en **beperkings** (grense soos materiale, tyd en geld).\n2. **Ontwerp** – Dink aan verskillende idees, teken sketse met byskrifte en kies die beste een. Sê waarom.\n3. **Maak** – Beplan die stappe, kry die materiale en gereedskap, en bou veilig.\n4. **Evalueer** – Toets die produk. Voldoen dit aan die spesifikasies? Wat sou jy verbeter?\n5. **Kommunikeer** – Wys en verduidelik jou werk met tekeninge, notas of ’n kort aanbieding.\n\n> **Onthou:** Die vyf stappe is **ondersoek, ontwerp, maak, evalueer en kommunikeer**. As die toets wys dat iets nie werk nie, gaan terug en verbeter jou ontwerp.\n\n## Ontwerptaak: ’n toring van strooitjies\n\n**Ontwerpopdrag:** Ontwerp en maak ’n raamstruktuur van strooitjies, soos ’n model van ’n uitkyktoring, wat ’n klein boek bo-op kan dra.\n\n- **Spesifikasies:** minstens 30 cm hoog; dra ’n klein boek vir 10 sekondes sonder om in te val; staan op sy eie.\n- **Beperkings:** net 20 strooitjies, pypskoonmakers en 1 m kleefband; een les.\n\n**Wenke:** gebruik driehoeke en kruisstutte, maak die basis wyd, en druk pypskoonmakers in die punte van die strooitjies om sterk lasse te maak.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Baie leerders bou net vierkante. ’n Toring van vierkante wikkel en val om sodra jy gewig bo-op sit. Sit kruisstutte in sodat elke vierkant twee driehoeke word.","en":"## What is a structure?\n\nA **structure** is something with a fixed shape that can carry weight, protect something or support something without falling apart. There are **natural structures**, like your skeleton, a bird’s nest and an eggshell, and **human-made structures**, like bridges, houses, electricity pylons and chairs. Your skeleton is actually a structure: it supports your body and protects your organs, just like the frame of a building.\n\n## Three kinds of structures\n\n| Kind | How it works | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| Frame structure | a framework of thin, strong parts that are fixed to each other at joints; often with a covering over it | pylon, bicycle frame, roof trusses, tent, a human skeleton |\n| Shell structure | a thin, hard, often curved outer layer; hollow inside; protects what is inside | eggshell, helmet, cooldrink can, tortoise shell |\n| Solid structure | massive, made of the same material all the way through; strong because of its thickness and weight | dam wall, brick wall, sandcastle |\n\n**Frame structures** use little material, so they are light. A tent’s poles are the frame and the canvas is the covering – just like your bones are the frame and your skin is the covering.\n\n**Shell structures** are strong because the **curved shape** spreads the force over the whole shell. That is why a helmet protects your head: the bump is spread over the whole helmet. A cooldrink can is strong when you press on the top, but if you dent the side slightly, it collapses easily.\n\nAnimal skeletons work in the same way: a vertebrate’s inner skeleton is like a **frame structure**, and an insect’s outer skeleton or a tortoise’s shell is like a **shell structure**.\n\n## Making structures stronger and stiffer\n\n1. **Triangles** – A square frame can easily be pushed out of shape; it wobbles. A triangle keeps its shape. That is why pylons, roof trusses and bridges are full of triangles.\n2. **Cross braces** – A slanting piece from corner to corner across a square divides it into two triangles and makes it stiff. Just look at a farm gate!\n3. **Tubes** – A flat sheet of paper bends easily, but if you roll it into a **tube**, it carries much more weight. Bicycle frames are made of hollow tubes: strong, but light – just like bird bones.\n4. **Strong joints** – A **joint** is the place where two parts are fixed to each other. If the joints are weak, the whole structure falls apart. You can make joints with glue, tape, string, nails or screws.\n5. **A wide base** – a structure with a broad foot does not fall over easily; it is **stable**.\n\n## The design process\n\nEngineers follow the **design process** to solve problems:\n\n1. **Investigate** – Find out what the problem is, look at existing solutions and test materials. Write a **design brief** (what you are going to make, for whom and why), **specifications** (what the product must be able to do) and **constraints** (limits such as materials, time and money).\n2. **Design** – Think of different ideas, draw labelled sketches and choose the best one. Say why.\n3. **Make** – Plan the steps, get the materials and tools, and build safely.\n4. **Evaluate** – Test the product. Does it meet the specifications? What would you improve?\n5. **Communicate** – Show and explain your work with drawings, notes or a short presentation.\n\n> **Remember:** The five steps are **investigate, design, make, evaluate and communicate**. If the test shows that something does not work, go back and improve your design.\n\n## Design task: a tower of straws\n\n**Design brief:** Design and make a frame structure of straws, like a model of a lookout tower, that can carry a small book on top.\n\n- **Specifications:** at least 30 cm high; carries a small book for 10 seconds without collapsing; stands on its own.\n- **Constraints:** only 20 straws, pipe cleaners and 1 m of tape; one lesson.\n\n**Tips:** use triangles and cross braces, make the base wide, and push pipe cleaners into the ends of the straws to make strong joints.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Many learners build only squares. A tower of squares wobbles and falls over as soon as you put weight on top. Add cross braces so that every square becomes two triangles."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Struktuur","en":"Structure"},"def":{"af":"Iets met ’n vaste vorm wat gewig kan dra, iets kan beskerm of ondersteun sonder om inmekaar te val.","en":"Something with a fixed shape that can carry weight, protect or support something without falling apart."}},{"term":{"af":"Raamstruktuur","en":"Frame structure"},"def":{"af":"’n Struktuur wat uit ’n geraamte van dun, sterk dele bestaan, soos ’n kragmas of ’n tent.","en":"A structure made of a framework of thin, strong parts, like a pylon or a tent."}},{"term":{"af":"Dopstruktuur","en":"Shell structure"},"def":{"af":"’n Struktuur met ’n dun, harde, geboë buitelaag wat die binnekant beskerm, soos ’n eierdop of helm.","en":"A structure with a thin, hard, curved outer layer that protects the inside, like an eggshell or helmet."}},{"term":{"af":"Soliede struktuur","en":"Solid structure"},"def":{"af":"’n Massiewe struktuur wat deur en deur van dieselfde materiaal is, soos ’n damwal.","en":"A massive structure made of the same material all the way through, like a dam wall."}},{"term":{"af":"Kruisstut","en":"Cross brace"},"def":{"af":"’n Skuins stuk van hoek tot hoek wat ’n vierkantige raam in driehoeke verdeel en styf maak.","en":"A slanting piece from corner to corner that divides a square frame into triangles and makes it stiff."}},{"term":{"af":"Las","en":"Joint"},"def":{"af":"Die plek waar twee dele van ’n struktuur aan mekaar vasgemaak is.","en":"The place where two parts of a structure are fixed to each other."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontwerpproses","en":"Design process"},"def":{"af":"Die stappe om ’n probleem op te los: ondersoek, ontwerp, maak, evalueer en kommunikeer.","en":"The steps to solve a problem: investigate, design, make, evaluate and communicate."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontwerpopdrag","en":"Design brief"},"def":{"af":"’n Kort beskrywing van wat jy gaan maak, vir wie en waarom.","en":"A short description of what you are going to make, for whom and why."}},{"term":{"af":"Spesifikasies","en":"Specifications"},"def":{"af":"Die dinge wat die produk moet kan doen of moet wees, byvoorbeeld ‘minstens 30 cm hoog’.","en":"The things the product must be able to do or must be, for example ‘at least 30 cm high’."}},{"term":{"af":"Beperkings","en":"Constraints"},"def":{"af":"Die grense waarbinne jy moet werk, soos die materiale, tyd en geld wat jy het.","en":"The limits you must work within, such as the materials, time and money you have."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer strukture","en":"Classify structures"},"problem":{"af":"Klassifiseer elkeen as ’n raam-, dop- of soliede struktuur: ’n kragmas, ’n motorfietshelm, ’n damwal, ’n tent en ’n skilpaddop.","en":"Classify each one as a frame, shell or solid structure: a pylon, a motorcycle helmet, a dam wall, a tent and a tortoise shell."},"steps":[{"af":"Vra: Is dit ’n geraamte van dun dele? Die **kragmas** (staalstawe) en die **tent** (pale met seil oor) is raamstrukture.","en":"Ask: Is it a framework of thin parts? The **pylon** (steel bars) and the **tent** (poles with canvas over them) are frame structures."},{"af":"Vra: Is dit ’n dun, harde, geboë laag wat iets binne beskerm? Die **helm** en die **skilpaddop** is dopstrukture.","en":"Ask: Is it a thin, hard, curved layer that protects something inside? The **helmet** and the **tortoise shell** are shell structures."},{"af":"Vra: Is dit massief, deur en deur dieselfde materiaal? Die **damwal** is ’n soliede struktuur.","en":"Ask: Is it massive, the same material all the way through? The **dam wall** is a solid structure."}],"answer":{"af":"Raam: kragmas, tent. Dop: motorfietshelm, skilpaddop. Solied: damwal.","en":"Frame: pylon, tent. Shell: motorcycle helmet, tortoise shell. Solid: dam wall."}},{"title":{"af":"Die wikkelende vierkant","en":"The wobbly square"},"problem":{"af":"Nomsa maak ’n vierkant van vier strooitjies en pypskoonmakers. As sy aan een hoek druk, word dit skeef. Hoe kan sy dit styf maak, en waarom werk dit?","en":"Nomsa makes a square from four straws and pipe cleaners. When she pushes on one corner, it goes out of shape. How can she make it stiff, and why does it work?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die hoeke van ’n vierkant kan draai, so die vorm kan maklik verander.","en":"The corners of a square can turn, so the shape can change easily."},{"af":"Sit ’n vyfde strooitjie skuins van een hoek na die teenoorgestelde hoek: ’n **kruisstut**.","en":"Add a fifth straw slanting from one corner to the opposite corner: a **cross brace**."},{"af":"Nou bestaan die vierkant uit **twee driehoeke**. ’n Driehoek kan nie van vorm verander as sy sye nie buig of breek nie.","en":"Now the square is made of **two triangles**. A triangle cannot change shape unless its sides bend or break."}],"answer":{"af":"Sy moet ’n kruisstut van hoek tot hoek insit. Dit maak twee driehoeke, en driehoeke hou hul vorm.","en":"She must add a cross brace from corner to corner. This makes two triangles, and triangles keep their shape."}},{"title":{"af":"Skryf ’n ontwerpopdrag","en":"Write a design brief"},"problem":{"af":"Ravi se klas moet ’n brug van strooitjies maak waaroor ’n speelgoedmotor oor ’n gaping van 20 cm tussen twee tafels kan ry. Skryf ’n ontwerpopdrag, twee spesifikasies en twee beperkings.","en":"Ravi’s class must make a bridge of straws so that a toy car can drive across a 20 cm gap between two desks. Write a design brief, two specifications and two constraints."},"steps":[{"af":"**Ontwerpopdrag** – sê wat, vir wie en waarom: ‘Ek gaan ’n raambrug van strooitjies ontwerp en maak sodat ’n speelgoedmotor veilig oor ’n gaping kan ry.’","en":"**Design brief** – say what, for whom and why: ‘I am going to design and make a frame bridge of straws so that a toy car can drive safely across a gap.’"},{"af":"**Spesifikasies** – wat die brug moet kan doen: dit moet ’n gaping van 20 cm oorspan, en dit moet die motor dra sonder om te knak.","en":"**Specifications** – what the bridge must be able to do: it must span a 20 cm gap, and it must carry the car without bending."},{"af":"**Beperkings** – die grense: net 15 strooitjies en kleefband, en dit moet binne een les klaar wees.","en":"**Constraints** – the limits: only 15 straws and tape, and it must be finished within one lesson."}],"answer":{"af":"Ontwerpopdrag: ’n raambrug van strooitjies vir ’n speelgoedmotor. Spesifikasies: oorspan 20 cm; dra die motor sonder om te knak. Beperkings: net 15 strooitjies en kleefband; een les.","en":"Design brief: a frame bridge of straws for a toy car. Specifications: spans 20 cm; carries the car without bending. Constraints: only 15 straws and tape; one lesson."}},{"title":{"af":"Evalueer ’n strooitjietoring","en":"Evaluate a straw tower"},"problem":{"af":"Zanele se toring is 32 cm hoog en staan op sy eie, maar ná 4 sekondes met die boek bo-op buig dit by die onderste lasse en val om. Evalueer haar toring en stel twee verbeterings voor.","en":"Zanele’s tower is 32 cm high and stands on its own, but after 4 seconds with the book on top it bends at the bottom joints and falls over. Evaluate her tower and suggest two improvements."},"steps":[{"af":"Vergelyk met die spesifikasies: hoogte (32 cm ≥ 30 cm) – **ja**; staan op sy eie – **ja**; dra die boek 10 sekondes – **nee** (net 4 sekondes).","en":"Compare with the specifications: height (32 cm ≥ 30 cm) – **yes**; stands on its own – **yes**; carries the book for 10 seconds – **no** (only 4 seconds)."},{"af":"Vind die swak plek: dit het by die **onderste lasse** gebuig. Die lasse onder dra die meeste gewig.","en":"Find the weak spot: it bent at the **bottom joints**. The joints at the bottom carry the most weight."},{"af":"Verbeter: maak die onderste lasse sterker (ekstra pypskoonmakers of kleefband) en sit **kruisstutte** in die onderste deel sodat dit driehoeke vorm. ’n Wyer basis sal ook help.","en":"Improve: make the bottom joints stronger (extra pipe cleaners or tape) and add **cross braces** in the bottom section so that it forms triangles. A wider base will also help."}],"answer":{"af":"Die toring voldoen aan twee van die drie spesifikasies. Verbeterings: sterker onderste lasse en kruisstutte (driehoeke) onder, en ’n wyer basis.","en":"The tower meets two of the three specifications. Improvements: stronger bottom joints and cross braces (triangles) at the bottom, and a wider base."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n dopstruktuur?","en":"Which one is a shell structure?"},"options":[{"af":"Kragmas","en":"Pylon"},{"af":"Eierdop","en":"Eggshell"},{"af":"Damwal","en":"Dam wall"},{"af":"Fietsraam","en":"Bicycle frame"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Eierdop is ’n dun, harde, geboë laag wat die binnekant beskerm. Die kragmas en fietsraam is raamstrukture, en die damwal is ’n soliede struktuur.","en":"An eggshell is a thin, hard, curved layer that protects the inside. The pylon and bicycle frame are frame structures, and the dam wall is a solid structure."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is ’n kragmas vol driehoeke?","en":"Why is a pylon full of triangles?"},"options":[{"af":"Driehoeke lyk mooier as vierkante","en":"Triangles look nicer than squares"},{"af":"Driehoeke gebruik meer staal sodat die mas swaarder is","en":"Triangles use more steel so that the pylon is heavier"},{"af":"Driehoeke laat die mas in die wind buig","en":"Triangles let the pylon bend in the wind"},{"af":"’n Driehoek hou sy vorm en maak die raam styf","en":"A triangle keeps its shape and makes the frame stiff"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Vierkant kan skeef gedruk word, maar ’n driehoek hou sy vorm. Driehoeke maak ’n raamstruktuur sterk en styf sonder om baie materiaal te gebruik.","en":"A square can be pushed out of shape, but a triangle keeps its shape. Triangles make a frame structure strong and stiff without using a lot of material."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Tent is ’n raamstruktuur.","en":"A tent is a frame structure."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die pale vorm ’n raam en die seil is ’n bedekking oor die raam – net soos jou bene ’n raam vorm en jou vel die bedekking is.","en":"True. The poles form a frame and the canvas is a covering over the frame – just like your bones form a frame and your skin is the covering."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die eerste stap van die ontwerpproses is om te ___.","en":"The first step of the design process is to ___."},"answers":{"af":["ondersoek"],"en":["investigate"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["evalueer","maak","kommunikeer"],"en":["evaluate","make","communicate"]}},"explain":{"af":"Jy begin altyd deur te ondersoek: vind uit wat die probleem is en toets materiale. Daarna kom ontwerp, maak, evalueer en kommunikeer.","en":"You always start by investigating: find out what the problem is and test materials. After that come design, make, evaluate and communicate."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke stap van die ontwerpproses by wat jy in daardie stap doen.","en":"Match each step of the design process to what you do in that step."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Ondersoek","en":"Investigate"},"r":{"af":"Vind uit wat die probleem is en toets materiale","en":"Find out what the problem is and test materials"}},{"l":{"af":"Ontwerp","en":"Design"},"r":{"af":"Teken sketse en kies die beste idee","en":"Draw sketches and choose the best idea"}},{"l":{"af":"Maak","en":"Make"},"r":{"af":"Bou die produk veilig volgens jou plan","en":"Build the product safely according to your plan"}},{"l":{"af":"Evalueer","en":"Evaluate"},"r":{"af":"Toets of die produk aan die spesifikasies voldoen","en":"Test whether the product meets the specifications"}},{"l":{"af":"Kommunikeer","en":"Communicate"},"r":{"af":"Wys en verduidelik jou werk aan ander","en":"Show and explain your work to others"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die vyf stappe volg op mekaar: eers uitvind, dan beplan en teken, dan bou, dan toets, en laastens jou werk aan ander verduidelik.","en":"The five steps follow each other: first find out, then plan and draw, then build, then test, and finally explain your work to others."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is ’n beperking in ’n ontwerptaak?","en":"What is a constraint in a design task?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Grens soos die materiale, tyd of geld wat jy het","en":"A limit such as the materials, time or money you have"},{"af":"Iets wat die produk moet kan doen","en":"Something the product must be able to do"},{"af":"Die skets van jou beste idee","en":"The sketch of your best idea"},{"af":"Die toets aan die einde van die taak","en":"The test at the end of the task"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Beperkings is grense waarbinne jy moet werk, soos ‘net 20 strooitjies’ of ‘een les’. Wat die produk moet kan doen, is ’n spesifikasie.","en":"Constraints are limits you must work within, such as ‘only 20 straws’ or ‘one lesson’. What the product must be able to do is a specification."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Skuins stuk van hoek tot hoek wat ’n vierkantige raam styf maak, heet ’n ___.","en":"A slanting piece from corner to corner that makes a square frame stiff is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["kruisstut","kruisstutte","skuinsstut"],"en":["cross brace","cross-brace","brace","diagonal brace"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["las","dop","basis"],"en":["joint","shell","base"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Kruisstut verdeel die vierkant in twee driehoeke. ’n Las is net die plek waar twee dele aan mekaar vas is.","en":"A cross brace divides the square into two triangles. A joint is only the place where two parts are fixed to each other."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo het drie ewe groot velle papier. Watter een sal die meeste gewig dra as hy dit regop sit en ’n boek bo-op plaas?","en":"Thabo has three sheets of paper of the same size. Which one will carry the most weight if he stands it upright and puts a book on top?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Plat vel wat regop staan","en":"A flat sheet standing upright"},{"af":"’n Vel wat opgefrommel is","en":"A sheet that has been crumpled up"},{"af":"’n Vel wat in ’n buis opgerol en vasgeplak is","en":"A sheet that has been rolled into a tube and stuck"},{"af":"’n Vel wat net in die helfte gevou is","en":"A sheet that has only been folded in half"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Buis is sterk, want die krag word rondom die hele buis versprei. Daarom is fietsrame en voëlbene hol buise: sterk, maar lig.","en":"A tube is strong because the force is spread all around the tube. That is why bicycle frames and bird bones are hollow tubes: strong, but light."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Dopstruktuur is deur en deur solied, soos ’n baksteenmuur.","en":"A shell structure is solid all the way through, like a brick wall."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Dopstruktuur is ’n dun, harde buitelaag wat hol is aan die binnekant, soos ’n eierdop. ’n Baksteenmuur is ’n soliede struktuur.","en":"False. A shell structure is a thin, hard outer layer that is hollow inside, like an eggshell. A brick wall is a solid structure."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato se strooitjietoring wikkel heen en weer. Wat is die beste verbetering?","en":"Lerato’s straw tower wobbles from side to side. What is the best improvement?"},"options":[{"af":"Gebruik langer strooitjies","en":"Use longer straws"},{"af":"Maak die toring nog hoër","en":"Make the tower even taller"},{"af":"Verf die strooitjies met ’n dik laag verf","en":"Paint the straws with a thick layer of paint"},{"af":"Sit kruisstutte in sodat daar driehoeke vorm","en":"Add cross braces so that triangles form"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Wikkel beteken dat die vierkante skeef kan skuif. Kruisstutte maak driehoeke, en driehoeke hou hul vorm. ’n Hoër toring met langer strooitjies sal net meer wikkel.","en":"Wobbling means that the squares can slide out of shape. Cross braces make triangles, and triangles keep their shape. A taller tower with longer straws will just wobble more."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling vergelyk diereskelette en strukture korrek?","en":"Which statement compares animal skeletons and structures correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Skilpaddop is ’n raamstruktuur","en":"A tortoise shell is a frame structure"},{"af":"’n Gewerwelde se skelet is soos ’n raamstruktuur en ’n skilpaddop soos ’n dopstruktuur","en":"A vertebrate’s skeleton is like a frame structure and a tortoise shell is like a shell structure"},{"af":"’n Erdwurm se liggaam is ’n soliede struktuur van bene","en":"An earthworm’s body is a solid structure of bones"},{"af":"’n Mens se skelet is ’n dopstruktuur sonder lasse","en":"A human skeleton is a shell structure without joints"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die bene van ’n gewerwelde vorm ’n raam met gewrigte (lasse), net soos ’n kragmas. ’n Skilpaddop en ’n insek se buiteskelet is harde, geboë buitelae – dopstrukture.","en":"The bones of a vertebrate form a frame with joints, just like a pylon. A tortoise shell and an insect’s outer skeleton are hard, curved outer layers – shell structures."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die plek waar twee dele van ’n struktuur aan mekaar vasgemaak is, heet ’n ___.","en":"The place where two parts of a structure are fixed to each other is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["las"],"en":["joint"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["raam","dop","stut"],"en":["frame","shell","brace"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Las kan met gom, kleefband, tou, spykers of skroewe gemaak word. As die lasse swak is, val die hele struktuur inmekaar.","en":"A joint can be made with glue, tape, string, nails or screws. If the joints are weak, the whole structure falls apart."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n spesifikasie (nie ’n beperking nie) vir die strooitjietoring?","en":"Which one is a specification (not a constraint) for the straw tower?"},"options":[{"af":"Die toring moet minstens 30 cm hoog wees","en":"The tower must be at least 30 cm high"},{"af":"Jy mag net 20 strooitjies gebruik","en":"You may only use 20 straws"},{"af":"Jy het net een les om dit te maak","en":"You only have one lesson to make it"},{"af":"Jy mag net 1 m kleefband gebruik","en":"You may only use 1 m of tape"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Spesifikasie sê wat die produk moet kan doen of moet wees, soos die hoogte. Die getal strooitjies, die tyd en die kleefband is beperkings – grense waarbinne jy werk.","en":"A specification says what the product must be able to do or must be, like the height. The number of straws, the time and the tape are constraints – limits you work within."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom beskerm ’n fietshelm jou kop so goed?","en":"Why does a bicycle helmet protect your head so well?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is swaar, so dit hou jou kop stil","en":"It is heavy, so it keeps your head still"},{"af":"Dit is ’n raamstruktuur met baie gate","en":"It is a frame structure with lots of holes"},{"af":"Die geboë dop versprei die krag van ’n stamp oor die hele helm","en":"The curved shell spreads the force of a bump over the whole helmet"},{"af":"Dit is ’n soliede struktuur van dik metaal","en":"It is a solid structure of thick metal"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Helm is ’n dopstruktuur. Die geboë vorm versprei die krag sodat dit nie net op een plek op jou kop druk nie. ’n Helm is lig, nie swaar of solied nie.","en":"A helmet is a shell structure. The curved shape spreads the force so that it does not press on only one spot on your head. A helmet is light, not heavy or solid."}}]},{"id":"nwt5-t1-voedselkettings","title":{"af":"Voedselkettings","en":"Food chains"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal produsente en verskillende soorte verbruikers kan herken, ’n voedselketting met pyle in die regte rigting kan teken, en kan voorspel wat gebeur as een skakel verdwyn.","en":"You will be able to recognise producers and different kinds of consumers, draw a food chain with arrows in the right direction, and predict what happens if one link disappears."},"summary":{"af":"## Alle lewende dinge het energie nodig\n\nElke lewende ding het **energie** nodig om te groei, te beweeg en aan die lewe te bly. Hierdie energie kry hulle uit **kos**. Maar waar kom die energie in kos vandaan? Dit kom oorspronklik van die **son**.\n\n## Produsente en verbruikers\n\n**Groen plante** kan hul eie kos maak. Hulle gebruik **sonlig**, water en koolstofdioksied uit die lug om kos in hul blare te maak. Omdat plante kos maak (produseer), noem ons hulle **produsente**.\n\nDiere kan nie hul eie kos maak nie. Hulle moet plante of ander diere eet. Ons noem hulle **verbruikers**.\n\n| Soort verbruiker | Wat dit eet | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| Herbivoor (planteter) | net plante | sebra, koedoe, sprinkaan, olifant |\n| Karnivoor (vleiseter) | net ander diere | leeu, jagluiperd, arend, slang |\n| Omnivoor (alleseter) | plante én diere | mens, bobbejaan, hoender |\n\nHerbivore het plat tande om plante fyn te maal. Karnivore het skerp, puntige tande om vleis te skeur.\n\n## Roofdiere, prooi, aaseters en ontbinders\n\n- ’n **Roofdier** jag en vang ander diere vir kos, soos ’n leeu of ’n arend.\n- Die dier wat gejag en geëet word, is die **prooi**, soos ’n sebra of ’n muis.\n- ’n Dier kan albei wees: ’n slang is ’n roofdier as dit ’n padda vang, maar prooi as ’n arend dit vang.\n- **Aaseters** eet dooie diere wat hulle nie self gevang het nie, soos aasvoëls. Hiënas en jakkalse eet ook dikwels aas.\n- **Ontbinders**, soos swamme (sampioene) en bakterieë, breek dooie plante, dooie diere en mis af. So gaan die voedingstowwe terug in die grond, waar plante dit weer gebruik. Sonder ontbinders sou dooie blare en karkasse oral opstapel.\n\n## Wat is ’n voedselketting?\n\n’n **Voedselketting** wys wie vir wie eet, en hoe die energie van een lewende ding na die volgende gaan.\n\n**gras → sebra → leeu**\n\n- ’n Voedselketting **begin altyd by ’n plant** (die produsent), want net plante kan kos maak met die energie van die son.\n- Die **pyl wys na die eter**. Dit wys waarheen die kos en energie gaan. Lees dit so: die gras word deur die sebra geëet, en die sebra word deur die leeu geëet.\n- Die herbivoor kom ná die plant, en die karnivoor ná die herbivoor.\n\nNog Suid-Afrikaanse voorbeelde:\n\n- doringboomblare → kameelperd → leeu\n- gras → haas → rooijakkals\n- mielieplant → muis → slang → arend\n\n### Hoe om ’n voedselketting te teken\n\n1. Begin met die **plant**.\n2. Skryf die **herbivoor** wat die plant eet, en trek ’n pyl van die plant na die herbivoor.\n3. Skryf die **karnivoor** wat die herbivoor eet, en trek weer ’n pyl na die eter.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Baie leerders trek die pyle verkeerd om, soos leeu → sebra → gras. Die pyl wys **waarheen die energie gaan**: van die kos na die eter. ’n Ketting wat by ’n dier begin, is ook verkeerd.\n\n## Voedselwebbe en balans\n\nDie meeste diere eet meer as een soort kos en word deur meer as een soort dier geëet. Daarom skakel baie voedselkettings aan mekaar en vorm ’n **voedselweb**.\n\nAs een lewende ding in ’n voedselketting verdwyn, raak dit die ander ook. As al die jakkalse in ’n veld gevang word, kom daar al hoe meer hase. Die hase eet dan te veel gras, en later is daar nie genoeg kos vir hulle almal nie.\n\n> **Onthou:** Die energie vloei so: **son → plant → herbivoor → karnivoor**. Elke voedselketting begin by ’n plant.","en":"## All living things need energy\n\nEvery living thing needs **energy** to grow, to move and to stay alive. They get this energy from **food**. But where does the energy in food come from? It first comes from the **Sun**.\n\n## Producers and consumers\n\n**Green plants** can make their own food. They use **sunlight**, water and carbon dioxide from the air to make food in their leaves. Because plants make (produce) food, we call them **producers**.\n\nAnimals cannot make their own food. They must eat plants or other animals. We call them **consumers**.\n\n| Kind of consumer | What it eats | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| Herbivore (plant eater) | only plants | zebra, kudu, grasshopper, elephant |\n| Carnivore (meat eater) | only other animals | lion, cheetah, eagle, snake |\n| Omnivore (eats everything) | plants and animals | human, baboon, chicken |\n\nHerbivores have flat teeth to grind plants. Carnivores have sharp, pointed teeth to tear meat.\n\n## Predators, prey, scavengers and decomposers\n\n- A **predator** hunts and catches other animals for food, like a lion or an eagle.\n- The animal that is hunted and eaten is the **prey**, like a zebra or a mouse.\n- An animal can be both: a snake is a predator when it catches a frog, but prey when an eagle catches it.\n- **Scavengers** eat dead animals that they did not catch themselves, like vultures. Hyenas and jackals also often eat dead animals.\n- **Decomposers**, like fungi (mushrooms) and bacteria, break down dead plants, dead animals and dung. In this way the nutrients go back into the soil, where plants use them again. Without decomposers, dead leaves and carcasses would pile up everywhere.\n\n## What is a food chain?\n\nA **food chain** shows who eats whom, and how energy passes from one living thing to the next.\n\n**grass → zebra → lion**\n\n- A food chain **always starts with a plant** (the producer), because only plants can make food with the energy of the Sun.\n- The **arrow points to the eater**. It shows where the food and energy go. Read it like this: the grass is eaten by the zebra, and the zebra is eaten by the lion.\n- The herbivore comes after the plant, and the carnivore after the herbivore.\n\nMore South African examples:\n\n- thorn-tree leaves → giraffe → lion\n- grass → hare → black-backed jackal\n- maize plant → mouse → snake → eagle\n\n### How to draw a food chain\n\n1. Start with the **plant**.\n2. Write the **herbivore** that eats the plant, and draw an arrow from the plant to the herbivore.\n3. Write the **carnivore** that eats the herbivore, and again draw an arrow to the eater.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Many learners draw the arrows the wrong way round, like lion → zebra → grass. The arrow shows **where the energy goes**: from the food to the eater. A chain that starts with an animal is also wrong.\n\n## Food webs and balance\n\nMost animals eat more than one kind of food and are eaten by more than one kind of animal. That is why many food chains link up and form a **food web**.\n\nIf one living thing in a food chain disappears, it affects the others too. If all the jackals in a veld are caught, there will be more and more hares. The hares then eat too much grass, and later there is not enough food for all of them.\n\n> **Remember:** Energy flows like this: **Sun → plant → herbivore → carnivore**. Every food chain starts with a plant."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Produsent","en":"Producer"},"def":{"af":"’n Groen plant wat sy eie kos maak met die energie van sonlig.","en":"A green plant that makes its own food using the energy of sunlight."}},{"term":{"af":"Verbruiker","en":"Consumer"},"def":{"af":"’n Dier wat nie sy eie kos kan maak nie en plante of ander diere eet.","en":"An animal that cannot make its own food and eats plants or other animals."}},{"term":{"af":"Herbivoor","en":"Herbivore"},"def":{"af":"’n Dier wat net plante eet, soos ’n sebra.","en":"An animal that eats only plants, like a zebra."}},{"term":{"af":"Karnivoor","en":"Carnivore"},"def":{"af":"’n Dier wat net ander diere eet, soos ’n leeu.","en":"An animal that eats only other animals, like a lion."}},{"term":{"af":"Omnivoor","en":"Omnivore"},"def":{"af":"’n Dier wat plante sowel as diere eet, soos ’n bobbejaan of ’n mens.","en":"An animal that eats both plants and animals, like a baboon or a human."}},{"term":{"af":"Roofdier","en":"Predator"},"def":{"af":"’n Dier wat ander diere jag en vang vir kos.","en":"An animal that hunts and catches other animals for food."}},{"term":{"af":"Prooi","en":"Prey"},"def":{"af":"’n Dier wat deur ’n roofdier gejag en geëet word.","en":"An animal that is hunted and eaten by a predator."}},{"term":{"af":"Aaseter","en":"Scavenger"},"def":{"af":"’n Dier wat dooie diere eet wat dit nie self gevang het nie, soos ’n aasvoël.","en":"An animal that eats dead animals it did not catch itself, like a vulture."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontbinder","en":"Decomposer"},"def":{"af":"’n Organisme, soos ’n swam of bakterie, wat dooie plante en diere afbreek en voedingstowwe aan die grond teruggee.","en":"An organism, such as a fungus or bacterium, that breaks down dead plants and animals and returns nutrients to the soil."}},{"term":{"af":"Voedselketting","en":"Food chain"},"def":{"af":"’n Reeks lewende dinge met pyle wat wys hoe kos en energie van die een na die ander gaan.","en":"A series of living things with arrows that show how food and energy pass from one to the next."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Bou ’n voedselketting","en":"Build a food chain"},"problem":{"af":"Rangskik hierdie lewende dinge in ’n voedselketting: arend, mielieplant, slang, muis.","en":"Arrange these living things in a food chain: eagle, maize plant, snake, mouse."},"steps":[{"af":"Soek die **produsent**: die mielieplant maak sy eie kos. Dit kom eerste.","en":"Find the **producer**: the maize plant makes its own food. It comes first."},{"af":"Wie eet die mielieplant? Die **muis** eet die mielies. Trek ’n pyl van die mielieplant na die muis.","en":"Who eats the maize plant? The **mouse** eats the maize. Draw an arrow from the maize plant to the mouse."},{"af":"Wie eet die muis? Die **slang**. En die slang word deur die **arend** gevang.","en":"Who eats the mouse? The **snake**. And the snake is caught by the **eagle**."},{"af":"Kontroleer dat al die pyle na die eter wys.","en":"Check that all the arrows point to the eater."}],"answer":{"af":"mielieplant → muis → slang → arend","en":"maize plant → mouse → snake → eagle"}},{"title":{"af":"Gee elke skakel ’n naam","en":"Name each link"},"problem":{"af":"Kyk na die voedselketting gras → haas → rooijakkals. Gee vir elke lewende ding die regte name: produsent of verbruiker, herbivoor of karnivoor, roofdier of prooi.","en":"Look at the food chain grass → hare → black-backed jackal. Give each living thing the correct names: producer or consumer, herbivore or carnivore, predator or prey."},"steps":[{"af":"**Gras** maak sy eie kos met sonlig: dit is die **produsent**.","en":"**Grass** makes its own food with sunlight: it is the **producer**."},{"af":"Die **haas** eet net plante: dit is ’n **verbruiker** en ’n **herbivoor**. Die jakkals jag dit, so dit is **prooi**.","en":"The **hare** eats only plants: it is a **consumer** and a **herbivore**. The jackal hunts it, so it is **prey**."},{"af":"Die **rooijakkals** eet die haas: dit is ’n **verbruiker** en ’n **karnivoor**. Omdat dit die haas jag, is dit ’n **roofdier**.","en":"The **black-backed jackal** eats the hare: it is a **consumer** and a **carnivore**. Because it hunts the hare, it is a **predator**."}],"answer":{"af":"Gras: produsent. Haas: verbruiker, herbivoor, prooi. Rooijakkals: verbruiker, karnivoor, roofdier.","en":"Grass: producer. Hare: consumer, herbivore, prey. Black-backed jackal: consumer, carnivore, predator."}},{"title":{"af":"Wat as een skakel verdwyn?","en":"What if one link disappears?"},"problem":{"af":"’n Boer vang al die rooijakkalse op sy plaas. Gebruik die voedselketting gras → haas → rooijakkals om te voorspel wat met die hase en die gras sal gebeur.","en":"A farmer catches all the black-backed jackals on his farm. Use the food chain grass → hare → black-backed jackal to predict what will happen to the hares and the grass."},"steps":[{"af":"Die jakkalse was die hase se roofdiere. Sonder hulle word minder hase gevang, so die **getal hase neem toe**.","en":"The jackals were the hares’ predators. Without them fewer hares are caught, so the **number of hares increases**."},{"af":"Meer hase eet meer gras, so die **gras neem af**.","en":"More hares eat more grass, so the **grass decreases**."},{"af":"Later is daar nie genoeg gras vir al die hase nie, en baie hase sal honger ly of doodgaan.","en":"Later there is not enough grass for all the hares, and many hares will go hungry or die."}],"answer":{"af":"Die hase sal eers vermeerder, die gras sal afneem, en later sal die hase te min kos hê. Die balans word versteur.","en":"The hares will first increase, the grass will decrease, and later the hares will have too little food. The balance is upset."}},{"title":{"af":"Volg die energie terug","en":"Trace the energy back"},"problem":{"af":"’n Leeu gebruik baie energie om agter ’n sebra aan te hardloop. Waar kom hierdie energie oorspronklik vandaan?","en":"A lion uses a lot of energy to run after a zebra. Where does this energy first come from?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die leeu kry sy energie uit die **sebra** wat hy geëet het.","en":"The lion gets its energy from the **zebra** that it ate."},{"af":"Die sebra het sy energie uit die **gras** gekry.","en":"The zebra got its energy from the **grass**."},{"af":"Die gras het sy kos gemaak met die energie van **sonlig**.","en":"The grass made its food with the energy of **sunlight**."}],"answer":{"af":"Van die son: son → gras → sebra → leeu.","en":"From the Sun: Sun → grass → zebra → lion."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom begin elke voedselketting by ’n plant?","en":"Why does every food chain start with a plant?"},"options":[{"af":"Plante is die kleinste lewende dinge","en":"Plants are the smallest living things"},{"af":"Plante word deur alle diere geëet","en":"Plants are eaten by all animals"},{"af":"Plante maak hul eie kos met die energie van die son","en":"Plants make their own food with the energy of the Sun"},{"af":"Plante leef baie langer as diere","en":"Plants live much longer than animals"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Net plante kan hul eie kos maak; hulle is produsente. Al die energie in ’n voedselketting kom eers deur die plant in. Nie alle diere eet plante nie – karnivore eet vleis.","en":"Only plants can make their own food; they are producers. All the energy in a food chain first enters through the plant. Not all animals eat plants – carnivores eat meat."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat wys die pyl in ’n voedselketting?","en":"What does the arrow in a food chain show?"},"options":[{"af":"Waarheen die kos en energie gaan – na die eter","en":"Where the food and energy go – to the eater"},{"af":"Watter dier die grootste is","en":"Which animal is the biggest"},{"af":"Watter dier die vinnigste hardloop","en":"Which animal runs the fastest"},{"af":"Wie wie jag – van die roofdier na die prooi","en":"Who hunts whom – from the predator to the prey"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die pyl wys van die kos na die eter, want so beweeg die energie. Dit is ’n algemene fout om die pyl van die roofdier na die prooi te trek.","en":"The arrow points from the food to the eater, because that is how the energy moves. It is a common mistake to draw the arrow from the predator to the prey."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Omnivoor eet net vleis.","en":"An omnivore eats only meat."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Omnivoor eet plante én diere, soos ’n bobbejaan of ’n mens. ’n Dier wat net vleis eet, is ’n karnivoor.","en":"False. An omnivore eats plants and animals, like a baboon or a human. An animal that eats only meat is a carnivore."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Dier wat net plante eet, is ’n ___.","en":"An animal that eats only plants is a ___."},"answers":{"af":["herbivoor","planteter"],"en":["herbivore","plant eater"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["karnivoor","omnivoor","produsent"],"en":["carnivore","omnivore","producer"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Herbivoor (planteter) eet net plante, soos ’n sebra of koedoe. ’n Produsent is die plant self, nie die dier wat dit eet nie.","en":"A herbivore (plant eater) eats only plants, like a zebra or kudu. A producer is the plant itself, not the animal that eats it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voedselketting is reg geskryf?","en":"Which food chain is written correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"leeu → sebra → gras","en":"lion → zebra → grass"},{"af":"gras → sprinkaan → akkedis","en":"grass → grasshopper → lizard"},{"af":"sprinkaan → gras → akkedis","en":"grasshopper → grass → lizard"},{"af":"gras → akkedis → sprinkaan","en":"grass → lizard → grasshopper"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die ketting begin by die plant (gras), die sprinkaan eet die gras en die akkedis eet die sprinkaan. Die pyle wys elke keer na die eter.","en":"The chain starts with the plant (grass), the grasshopper eats the grass and the lizard eats the grasshopper. Each arrow points to the eater."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke lewende ding by sy rol.","en":"Match each living thing to its role."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Gras","en":"Grass"},"r":{"af":"Produsent","en":"Producer"}},{"l":{"af":"Aasvoël","en":"Vulture"},"r":{"af":"Aaseter","en":"Scavenger"}},{"l":{"af":"Sampioen","en":"Mushroom"},"r":{"af":"Ontbinder","en":"Decomposer"}},{"l":{"af":"Jagluiperd","en":"Cheetah"},"r":{"af":"Karnivoor","en":"Carnivore"}},{"l":{"af":"Bobbejaan","en":"Baboon"},"r":{"af":"Omnivoor","en":"Omnivore"}}],"explain":{"af":"Gras maak kos (produsent); die aasvoël eet dooie diere (aaseter); die sampioen breek dooie materiaal af (ontbinder); die jagluiperd eet net vleis (karnivoor); die bobbejaan eet plante en diere (omnivoor).","en":"Grass makes food (producer); the vulture eats dead animals (scavenger); the mushroom breaks down dead material (decomposer); the cheetah eats only meat (carnivore); the baboon eats plants and animals (omnivore)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In die voedselketting gras → haas → rooijakkals, watter een is die prooi?","en":"In the food chain grass → hare → black-backed jackal, which one is the prey?"},"options":[{"af":"Die gras","en":"The grass"},{"af":"Die rooijakkals","en":"The black-backed jackal"},{"af":"Die son","en":"The Sun"},{"af":"Die haas","en":"The hare"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Prooi is ’n dier wat gejag en geëet word. Die jakkals jag die haas, so die haas is die prooi. Gras is ’n plant (produsent), nie prooi nie.","en":"Prey is an animal that is hunted and eaten. The jackal hunts the hare, so the hare is the prey. Grass is a plant (producer), not prey."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Swamme en bakterieë wat dooie plante en diere afbreek, heet ___.","en":"Fungi and bacteria that break down dead plants and animals are called ___."},"answers":{"af":["ontbinders","ontbinder"],"en":["decomposers","decomposer"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["aaseters","produsente","roofdiere"],"en":["scavengers","producers","predators"]}},"explain":{"af":"Ontbinders breek dooie materiaal af en gee voedingstowwe aan die grond terug. Aaseters, soos aasvoëls, eet wel dooie diere, maar dit is diere, nie swamme of bakterieë nie.","en":"Decomposers break down dead material and return nutrients to the soil. Scavengers, like vultures, do eat dead animals, but they are animals, not fungi or bacteria."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In ’n wildtuin verdwyn al die leeus. Wat sal waarskynlik eerste gebeur?","en":"In a game reserve all the lions disappear. What will most likely happen first?"},"options":[{"af":"Die getal sebras sal toeneem","en":"The number of zebras will increase"},{"af":"Die gras sal vinniger groei","en":"The grass will grow faster"},{"af":"Die sebras sal ook verdwyn","en":"The zebras will also disappear"},{"af":"Die getal sebras sal dadelik afneem","en":"The number of zebras will decrease at once"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Leeus is roofdiere van sebras. Sonder leeus word minder sebras gevang, so hulle getal neem toe. Later sal die sebras te veel gras eet.","en":"Lions are predators of zebras. Without lions fewer zebras are caught, so their number increases. Later the zebras will eat too much grass."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die energie in ’n leeu se kos het eerste van die son gekom.","en":"The energy in a lion’s food first came from the Sun."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die gras het kos gemaak met sonlig, die sebra het die gras geëet en die leeu die sebra. Die energie het dus by die son begin.","en":"True. The grass made food with sunlight, the zebra ate the grass and the lion ate the zebra. So the energy started with the Sun."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter dier is ’n karnivoor?","en":"Which animal is a carnivore?"},"options":[{"af":"Koedoe","en":"Kudu"},{"af":"Olifant","en":"Elephant"},{"af":"Jagluiperd","en":"Cheetah"},{"af":"Bobbejaan","en":"Baboon"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die jagluiperd jag en eet net ander diere. Die koedoe en olifant is herbivore, en die bobbejaan is ’n omnivoor.","en":"The cheetah hunts and eats only other animals. The kudu and elephant are herbivores, and the baboon is an omnivore."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n ___ jag en vang ander diere vir kos.","en":"A ___ hunts and catches other animals for food."},"answers":{"af":["roofdier"],"en":["predator"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["prooi","herbivoor","ontbinder"],"en":["prey","herbivore","decomposer"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Roofdier jag, soos ’n leeu of ’n arend. Die prooi is die dier wat gejag word.","en":"A predator hunts, like a lion or an eagle. The prey is the animal that is hunted."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In die voedselketting mielieplant → muis → slang → arend, wat is die slang?","en":"In the food chain maize plant → mouse → snake → eagle, what is the snake?"},"options":[{"af":"Net ’n roofdier","en":"Only a predator"},{"af":"Net prooi","en":"Only prey"},{"af":"’n Produsent","en":"A producer"},{"af":"Roofdier én prooi","en":"Both predator and prey"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die slang jag die muis, so dit is ’n roofdier. Maar die arend vang die slang, so dit is ook prooi.","en":"The snake hunts the mouse, so it is a predator. But the eagle catches the snake, so it is also prey."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is ontbinders belangrik?","en":"Why are decomposers important?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle maak kos met sonlig vir die diere","en":"They make food with sunlight for the animals"},{"af":"Hulle breek dooie plante en diere af en gee voedingstowwe aan die grond terug","en":"They break down dead plants and animals and return nutrients to the soil"},{"af":"Hulle jag siek diere sodat die trop gesond bly","en":"They hunt sick animals so that the herd stays healthy"},{"af":"Hulle dra stuifmeel van blom na blom","en":"They carry pollen from flower to flower"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Ontbinders soos swamme en bakterieë maak die grond vrugbaar sodat nuwe plante kan groei. Sonder hulle sou dooie materiaal oral opstapel.","en":"Decomposers like fungi and bacteria make the soil fertile so that new plants can grow. Without them dead material would pile up everywhere."}}]},{"id":"nwt5-t1-lewensiklusse","title":{"af":"Lewensiklusse: groei en ontwikkeling","en":"Life cycles: growth and development"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die lewensiklusse van ’n plant, ’n padda, ’n skoenlapper, ’n hoender en ’n mens in die regte volgorde kan beskryf, en die verskil tussen groei en ontwikkeling kan verduidelik.","en":"You will be able to describe the life cycles of a plant, a frog, a butterfly, a chicken and a human in the correct order, and explain the difference between growth and development."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is ’n lewensiklus?\n\nAlle lewende dinge begin klein, **groei**, **ontwikkel**, plant voort (maak nuwe lewende dinge van hul soort) en gaan uiteindelik dood. Die stadiums wat ’n plant of dier deurgaan, is sy **lewensiklus**. Dit is ’n **siklus** (’n kringloop), want die volwasse plant of dier maak weer sade of kleintjies wat deur dieselfde stadiums gaan.\n\n- **Groei** beteken om groter en swaarder te word. ’n Baba word langer; ’n boom word dikker.\n- **Ontwikkeling** beteken dat die liggaam verander en nuwe dele of vermoëns kry. ’n Paddavis kry pote; ’n baba leer loop; ’n plant kry blomme.\n\n## Die lewensiklus van ’n plant\n\n1. **Saad** – binne-in is ’n piepklein plantjie en ’n voorraad kos.\n2. **Ontkieming** – die saad neem water op en swel, en die saadhuid bars oop. Eers groei ’n worteltjie af, dan ’n stingeltjie op.\n3. **Saailing** – die jong plantjie se eerste blare kom bo die grond uit.\n4. **Volwasse plant** – die plant groei groter en maak **blomme**.\n5. **Bestuiwing** – insekte, voëls of die wind dra **stuifmeel** van een blom na ’n ander.\n6. **Vrug en saad** – ná bestuiwing vorm die blom ’n **vrug** met **sade** binne-in. Die sade word versprei, en die siklus begin weer.\n\n### Wat ’n saad nodig het om te ontkiem\n\n’n Saad het **water**, **lug** en **warmte** (die regte temperatuur) nodig om te ontkiem. Dit het **nie grond of lig** nodig nie, want dit gebruik die kos wat in die saad gestoor is. Boontjies ontkiem byvoorbeeld op nat watte in ’n warm, donker kas. Maar sodra die saailing sy gestoorde kos opgebruik het, het dit **lig** nodig om self kos te maak, en voedingstowwe uit die grond om goed te groei.\n\n## Die lewensiklus van ’n padda\n\n’n Padda gaan deur **metamorfose**: sy liggaam verander heeltemal van vorm terwyl dit grootword.\n\n1. **Eiers** – die padda lê baie eiers in ’n jellieagtige massa in die water.\n2. **Paddavis** – ’n paddavis broei uit. Dit leef in water, swem met ’n stert en haal asem met **kieue**.\n3. **Paddavis met pote** – eers groei die agterpote, dan die voorpote, en die paddavis kry **longe**.\n4. **Jong padda** – die stert word al hoe korter, en die jong padda klim uit die water.\n5. **Volwasse padda** – geen stert nie; dit haal asem met longe en leef op land en in water. Dit lê weer eiers in die water.\n\n## Die lewensiklus van ’n skoenlapper\n\n1. **Eier** – die skoenlapper lê klein eiers op ’n blaar van die plant wat die ruspe sal eet.\n2. **Ruspe** – die ruspe eet aanhoudend en groei baie vinnig. Dit vervel ’n paar keer.\n3. **Papie** – die ruspe vorm ’n harde omhulsel. Van buite lyk dit of niks gebeur nie, maar binne-in word die liggaam heeltemal omgebou.\n4. **Volwasse skoenlapper** – dit kom met vlerke uit die papie en lê later weer eiers.\n\nOok die skoenlapper gaan dus deur **metamorfose**.\n\n## Hoender en mens\n\nHoenders en mense gaan **nie** deur metamorfose nie: die kleintjie lyk soos ’n klein weergawe van die volwassene.\n\n| Organisme | Stadiums | Metamorfose? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Padda | eier → paddavis → jong padda → volwasse padda | ja |\n| Skoenlapper | eier → ruspe → papie → volwasse skoenlapper | ja |\n| Hoender | eier → kuiken → jong hoender → hen of haan | nee |\n| Mens | baba → kind → tiener → volwassene | nee |\n\n’n Hen broei haar eiers sowat 21 dae lank uit; dan pik die **kuiken** deur die dop. ’n Menslike baba groei sowat nege maande in sy ma se liggaam voordat dit gebore word.\n\n> **Onthou:** Groei = groter word. Ontwikkeling = verander en nuwe dele of vermoëns kry. ’n Paddavis wat pote kry, **ontwikkel**; ’n kuiken wat swaarder word, **groei**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** ’n Ruspe is nie ’n wurm nie, en ’n paddavis is nie ’n vis nie! Hulle is die jong stadiums van ’n skoenlapper en ’n padda. Moet ook nie dink ’n saad het grond nodig om te ontkiem nie.","en":"## What is a life cycle?\n\nAll living things start small, **grow**, **develop**, reproduce (make new living things of their kind) and finally die. The stages that a plant or animal goes through are its **life cycle**. It is a **cycle** (a circle) because the adult plant or animal makes seeds or young again, and they go through the same stages.\n\n- **Growth** means getting bigger and heavier. A baby gets longer; a tree gets thicker.\n- **Development** means that the body changes and gets new parts or abilities. A tadpole gets legs; a baby learns to walk; a plant gets flowers.\n\n## The life cycle of a plant\n\n1. **Seed** – inside is a tiny plant and a store of food.\n2. **Germination** – the seed takes in water and swells, and the seed coat splits open. First a little root grows down, then a little stem grows up.\n3. **Seedling** – the young plant’s first leaves come out above the ground.\n4. **Adult plant** – the plant grows bigger and makes **flowers**.\n5. **Pollination** – insects, birds or the wind carry **pollen** from one flower to another.\n6. **Fruit and seed** – after pollination the flower forms a **fruit** with **seeds** inside. The seeds are spread, and the cycle starts again.\n\n### What a seed needs to germinate\n\nA seed needs **water**, **air** and **warmth** (the right temperature) to germinate. It does **not** need **soil or light**, because it uses the food stored in the seed. For example, beans germinate on wet cotton wool in a warm, dark cupboard. But once the seedling has used up its stored food, it needs **light** to make its own food, and nutrients from the soil to grow well.\n\n## The life cycle of a frog\n\nA frog goes through **metamorphosis**: its body changes shape completely as it grows up.\n\n1. **Eggs** – the frog lays many eggs in a jelly-like mass in the water.\n2. **Tadpole** – a tadpole hatches. It lives in water, swims with a tail and breathes with **gills**.\n3. **Tadpole with legs** – first the back legs grow, then the front legs, and the tadpole gets **lungs**.\n4. **Young frog** – the tail gets shorter and shorter, and the young frog climbs out of the water.\n5. **Adult frog** – no tail; it breathes with lungs and lives on land and in water. It lays eggs in the water again.\n\n## The life cycle of a butterfly\n\n1. **Egg** – the butterfly lays tiny eggs on a leaf of the plant that the caterpillar will eat.\n2. **Caterpillar** – the caterpillar eats all the time and grows very fast. It moults a few times.\n3. **Pupa** – the caterpillar forms a hard case. From the outside it looks as if nothing is happening, but inside the body is completely rebuilt.\n4. **Adult butterfly** – it comes out of the pupa with wings and later lays eggs again.\n\nSo the butterfly also goes through **metamorphosis**.\n\n## Chicken and human\n\nChickens and humans do **not** go through metamorphosis: the young one looks like a small version of the adult.\n\n| Organism | Stages | Metamorphosis? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Frog | egg → tadpole → young frog → adult frog | yes |\n| Butterfly | egg → caterpillar → pupa → adult butterfly | yes |\n| Chicken | egg → chick → young chicken → hen or rooster | no |\n| Human | baby → child → teenager → adult | no |\n\nA hen sits on her eggs for about 21 days; then the **chick** pecks through the shell. A human baby grows for about nine months inside its mother’s body before it is born.\n\n> **Remember:** Growth = getting bigger. Development = changing and getting new parts or abilities. A tadpole that gets legs **develops**; a chick that gets heavier **grows**.\n\n> **Common mistake:** A caterpillar is not a worm, and a tadpole is not a fish! They are the young stages of a butterfly and a frog. Also, don’t think that a seed needs soil to germinate."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Lewensiklus","en":"Life cycle"},"def":{"af":"Die stadiums wat ’n plant of dier van die begin van sy lewe tot volwassenheid deurgaan, en wat dan weer van voor af begin.","en":"The stages that a plant or animal goes through from the start of its life to adulthood, which then start all over again."}},{"term":{"af":"Groei","en":"Growth"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n lewende ding groter en swaarder word.","en":"When a living thing gets bigger and heavier."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontwikkeling","en":"Development"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n lewende ding se liggaam verander en nuwe dele of vermoëns kry.","en":"When a living thing’s body changes and gets new parts or abilities."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontkieming","en":"Germination"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n saad water opneem, oopbars en ’n worteltjie en stingeltjie begin groei.","en":"When a seed takes in water, splits open and a little root and stem start to grow."}},{"term":{"af":"Saailing","en":"Seedling"},"def":{"af":"’n Jong plantjie wat pas uit ’n saad gegroei het en sy eerste blare het.","en":"A young plant that has just grown from a seed and has its first leaves."}},{"term":{"af":"Bestuiwing","en":"Pollination"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer stuifmeel van een blom na ’n ander gedra word sodat vrugte en sade kan vorm.","en":"When pollen is carried from one flower to another so that fruit and seeds can form."}},{"term":{"af":"Metamorfose","en":"Metamorphosis"},"def":{"af":"’n Groot verandering in liggaamsvorm terwyl ’n dier grootword, soos van paddavis na padda.","en":"A big change in body shape while an animal grows up, like from tadpole to frog."}},{"term":{"af":"Paddavis","en":"Tadpole"},"def":{"af":"Die jong stadium van ’n padda wat in water leef, ’n stert het en met kieue asemhaal.","en":"The young stage of a frog that lives in water, has a tail and breathes with gills."}},{"term":{"af":"Ruspe","en":"Caterpillar"},"def":{"af":"Die jong stadium van ’n skoenlapper wat baie eet en vinnig groei.","en":"The young stage of a butterfly that eats a lot and grows fast."}},{"term":{"af":"Papie","en":"Pupa"},"def":{"af":"Die stadium in ’n harde omhulsel waarin ’n ruspe in ’n skoenlapper verander.","en":"The stage inside a hard case in which a caterpillar changes into a butterfly."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Rangskik die plant se lewensiklus","en":"Arrange the plant’s life cycle"},"problem":{"af":"Rangskik hierdie stadiums in die regte volgorde, begin by die saad: blom, saad, saailing, vrug met sade, ontkieming, bestuiwing, volwasse plant.","en":"Arrange these stages in the correct order, starting with the seed: flower, seed, seedling, fruit with seeds, germination, pollination, adult plant."},"steps":[{"af":"Begin by die **saad**. Dit moet eers **ontkiem** voordat iets bo die grond verskyn.","en":"Start with the **seed**. It must first **germinate** before anything appears above the ground."},{"af":"Die jong plantjie met sy eerste blare is die **saailing**; dit groei tot ’n **volwasse plant**.","en":"The young plant with its first leaves is the **seedling**; it grows into an **adult plant**."},{"af":"Die volwasse plant maak ’n **blom**. Stuifmeel moet dan na ’n ander blom gedra word: **bestuiwing**.","en":"The adult plant makes a **flower**. Pollen must then be carried to another flower: **pollination**."},{"af":"Ná bestuiwing vorm ’n **vrug met sade**, en die sade begin die siklus weer.","en":"After pollination a **fruit with seeds** forms, and the seeds start the cycle again."}],"answer":{"af":"saad → ontkieming → saailing → volwasse plant → blom → bestuiwing → vrug met sade","en":"seed → germination → seedling → adult plant → flower → pollination → fruit with seeds"}},{"title":{"af":"Ondersoek: wat het ’n saad nodig?","en":"Investigation: what does a seed need?"},"problem":{"af":"Liam sit boontjies op watte in drie flesse. Fles A: droë watte in ’n warm, donker kas. Fles B: nat watte in ’n warm, donker kas. Fles C: nat watte in die yskas. Ná ’n week het net die boontjies in fles B ontkiem. Wat leer hy hieruit?","en":"Liam puts beans on cotton wool in three jars. Jar A: dry cotton wool in a warm, dark cupboard. Jar B: wet cotton wool in a warm, dark cupboard. Jar C: wet cotton wool in the fridge. After a week only the beans in jar B have germinated. What does he learn from this?"},"steps":[{"af":"Vergelyk A en B: net die **water** verskil. B het ontkiem en A nie, so sade het **water** nodig.","en":"Compare A and B: only the **water** is different. B germinated and A did not, so seeds need **water**."},{"af":"Vergelyk B en C: net die **temperatuur** verskil. B het ontkiem en C nie, so sade het **warmte** nodig.","en":"Compare B and C: only the **temperature** is different. B germinated and C did not, so seeds need **warmth**."},{"af":"Fles B was in die **donker** en daar was **geen grond** nie, maar die boontjies het tog ontkiem. Lig en grond is dus nie nodig vir ontkieming nie.","en":"Jar B was in the **dark** and there was **no soil**, but the beans still germinated. So light and soil are not needed for germination."},{"af":"Dit is ’n **regverdige toets**, want hy het elke keer net een ding verander.","en":"It is a **fair test**, because each time he changed only one thing."}],"answer":{"af":"Sade het water en warmte nodig om te ontkiem, maar nie lig of grond nie.","en":"Seeds need water and warmth to germinate, but not light or soil."}},{"title":{"af":"Groei of ontwikkeling?","en":"Growth or development?"},"problem":{"af":"Sê of elkeen groei of ontwikkeling is: (a) ’n kuiken word swaarder; (b) ’n paddavis kry voorpote; (c) ’n boom word elke jaar hoër; (d) ’n ruspe verander in ’n skoenlapper.","en":"Say whether each one is growth or development: (a) a chick gets heavier; (b) a tadpole gets front legs; (c) a tree gets taller every year; (d) a caterpillar changes into a butterfly."},"steps":[{"af":"Vra by elkeen: word dit net **groter of swaarder**? Dan is dit **groei**.","en":"Ask for each one: does it just get **bigger or heavier**? Then it is **growth**."},{"af":"Kry dit **nuwe dele** of **verander die vorm**? Dan is dit **ontwikkeling**.","en":"Does it get **new parts** or does its **shape change**? Then it is **development**."},{"af":"(a) en (c) word net groter: groei. (b) kry nuwe dele en (d) verander heeltemal van vorm: ontwikkeling.","en":"(a) and (c) only get bigger: growth. (b) gets new parts and (d) changes shape completely: development."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) groei; (b) ontwikkeling; (c) groei; (d) ontwikkeling","en":"(a) growth; (b) development; (c) growth; (d) development"}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyk ’n padda en ’n hoender","en":"Compare a frog and a chicken"},"problem":{"af":"Albei begin as ’n eier. Verduidelik die belangrikste verskil tussen die lewensiklus van ’n padda en dié van ’n hoender.","en":"Both start as an egg. Explain the most important difference between the life cycle of a frog and that of a chicken."},"steps":[{"af":"Uit die padda-eier kom ’n **paddavis**: dit lyk glad nie soos ’n padda nie, het ’n stert en kieue, en leef in water.","en":"Out of the frog’s egg comes a **tadpole**: it does not look like a frog at all, has a tail and gills, and lives in water."},{"af":"Die paddavis verander heeltemal van vorm: pote, longe, geen stert nie. Dit is **metamorfose**.","en":"The tadpole changes shape completely: legs, lungs, no tail. This is **metamorphosis**."},{"af":"Uit die hoendereier kom ’n **kuiken** wat reeds soos ’n klein hoender lyk. Dit word net groter en kry vere – **geen metamorfose** nie.","en":"Out of the chicken’s egg comes a **chick** that already looks like a small chicken. It just gets bigger and grows feathers – **no metamorphosis**."}],"answer":{"af":"Die padda gaan deur metamorfose (sy liggaam verander heeltemal van vorm); die hoender nie – die kuiken lyk reeds soos ’n klein hoender.","en":"The frog goes through metamorphosis (its body changes shape completely); the chicken does not – the chick already looks like a small chicken."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat gebeur tydens ontkieming?","en":"What happens during germination?"},"options":[{"af":"Die plant maak blomme en vrugte","en":"The plant makes flowers and fruit"},{"af":"Stuifmeel word van blom na blom gedra","en":"Pollen is carried from flower to flower"},{"af":"Die volwasse plant gaan dood en laat sade val","en":"The adult plant dies and drops seeds"},{"af":"Die saad neem water op, bars oop en begin ’n wortel en stingel groei","en":"The seed takes in water, splits open and starts to grow a root and stem"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ontkieming is die begin van ’n nuwe plant: die saad swel, bars oop en ’n worteltjie en stingeltjie groei. Die oordra van stuifmeel is bestuiwing.","en":"Germination is the start of a new plant: the seed swells, splits open and a little root and stem grow. Carrying pollen is pollination."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ravi sit boontjies op nat watte in ’n warm kas, sonder enige grond. Hulle ontkiem tog. Wat wys dit?","en":"Ravi puts beans on wet cotton wool in a warm cupboard, without any soil. They still germinate. What does this show?"},"options":[{"af":"Sade het lig nodig om te ontkiem","en":"Seeds need light to germinate"},{"af":"Sade het nie grond nodig om te ontkiem nie","en":"Seeds do not need soil to germinate"},{"af":"Sade het nie water nodig om te ontkiem nie","en":"Seeds do not need water to germinate"},{"af":"Watte is beter vir plante as grond","en":"Cotton wool is better for plants than soil"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die saad gebruik sy eie gestoorde kos, so dit het nie grond nodig om te ontkiem nie. Dit het wel water gehad. Later het die saailing grond en lig nodig om goed te groei.","en":"The seed uses its own stored food, so it does not need soil to germinate. It did have water. Later the seedling needs soil and light to grow well."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Paddavis haal asem met kieue.","en":"A tadpole breathes with gills."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Paddavis leef in water en haal asem met kieue, soos ’n vis. Wanneer dit ’n padda word, kry dit longe.","en":"True. A tadpole lives in water and breathes with gills, like a fish. When it becomes a frog, it gets lungs."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die groot verandering in liggaamsvorm van ’n padda of skoenlapper terwyl dit grootword, heet ___.","en":"The big change in body shape of a frog or butterfly as it grows up is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["metamorfose"],"en":["metamorphosis"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["ontkieming","bestuiwing","groei"],"en":["germination","pollination","growth"]}},"explain":{"af":"Metamorfose beteken ’n volledige verandering van vorm, soos paddavis → padda en ruspe → skoenlapper. Groei beteken net om groter te word.","en":"Metamorphosis means a complete change of shape, like tadpole → frog and caterpillar → butterfly. Growth only means getting bigger."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die regte volgorde in ’n skoenlapper se lewensiklus?","en":"What is the correct order in a butterfly’s life cycle?"},"options":[{"af":"eier → ruspe → papie → skoenlapper","en":"egg → caterpillar → pupa → butterfly"},{"af":"eier → papie → ruspe → skoenlapper","en":"egg → pupa → caterpillar → butterfly"},{"af":"ruspe → eier → papie → skoenlapper","en":"caterpillar → egg → pupa → butterfly"},{"af":"eier → ruspe → skoenlapper → papie","en":"egg → caterpillar → butterfly → pupa"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die ruspe broei uit die eier, eet en groei, en vorm dan ’n papie. In die papie word die liggaam omgebou, en die skoenlapper kom uit.","en":"The caterpillar hatches from the egg, eats and grows, and then forms a pupa. Inside the pupa the body is rebuilt, and the butterfly comes out."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke jong stadium by die volwassene waarin dit sal verander.","en":"Match each young stage to the adult it will become."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Paddavis","en":"Tadpole"},"r":{"af":"Padda","en":"Frog"}},{"l":{"af":"Ruspe","en":"Caterpillar"},"r":{"af":"Skoenlapper","en":"Butterfly"}},{"l":{"af":"Kuiken","en":"Chick"},"r":{"af":"Hoender","en":"Chicken"}},{"l":{"af":"Saailing","en":"Seedling"},"r":{"af":"Volwasse plant","en":"Adult plant"}},{"l":{"af":"Baba","en":"Baby"},"r":{"af":"Volwasse mens","en":"Adult human"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke jong stadium groei en ontwikkel tot die volwassene van sy eie soort. Die paddavis en die ruspe verander heeltemal van vorm (metamorfose); die kuiken en die baba word net groter en ontwikkel.","en":"Each young stage grows and develops into the adult of its own kind. The tadpole and the caterpillar change shape completely (metamorphosis); the chick and the baby just get bigger and develop."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n voorbeeld van ontwikkeling en nie net groei nie?","en":"Which one is an example of development and not just growth?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Boom word elke jaar dikker","en":"A tree gets thicker every year"},{"af":"’n Baba word swaarder","en":"A baby gets heavier"},{"af":"’n Paddavis kry agterpote","en":"A tadpole gets back legs"},{"af":"’n Kuiken word langer","en":"A chick gets longer"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Pote is nuwe liggaamsdele, so dit is ontwikkeling. Dikker, swaarder en langer word beteken net dat iets groter word – dit is groei.","en":"Legs are new body parts, so this is development. Getting thicker, heavier and longer just means getting bigger – that is growth."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer stuifmeel van een blom na ’n ander gedra word, heet dit ___.","en":"When pollen is carried from one flower to another, it is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["bestuiwing"],"en":["pollination"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["ontkieming","metamorfose","saadverspreiding"],"en":["germination","metamorphosis","seed dispersal"]}},"explain":{"af":"Ná bestuiwing kan die blom ’n vrug met sade vorm. Saadverspreiding gebeur later, wanneer die sade weggedra word.","en":"After pollination the flower can form a fruit with seeds. Seed dispersal happens later, when the seeds are carried away."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Kuiken gaan deur metamorfose voordat dit ’n hoender word.","en":"A chick goes through metamorphosis before it becomes a chicken."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Kuiken lyk reeds soos ’n klein hoender. Dit groei net groter en kry volwasse vere; sy liggaam verander nie heeltemal van vorm nie.","en":"False. A chick already looks like a small chicken. It just grows bigger and gets adult feathers; its body does not change shape completely."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter stadium eet ’n skoenlapper die meeste en groei dit die vinnigste?","en":"In which stage does a butterfly eat the most and grow the fastest?"},"options":[{"af":"Eier","en":"Egg"},{"af":"Ruspe","en":"Caterpillar"},{"af":"Papie","en":"Pupa"},{"af":"Volwasse skoenlapper","en":"Adult butterfly"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die ruspe eet aanhoudend blare en groei baie vinnig; dit vervel selfs ’n paar keer. In die papie eet dit glad nie.","en":"The caterpillar eats leaves all the time and grows very fast; it even moults a few times. In the pupa it does not eat at all."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat vorm uit die blom ná bestuiwing?","en":"What forms from the flower after pollination?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Saailing","en":"A seedling"},{"af":"Nuwe blare","en":"New leaves"},{"af":"’n Nuwe wortel","en":"A new root"},{"af":"’n Vrug met sade binne-in","en":"A fruit with seeds inside"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ná bestuiwing vorm die blom ’n vrug met sade. ’n Saailing groei eers later, wanneer ’n saad ontkiem.","en":"After pollination the flower forms a fruit with seeds. A seedling only grows later, when a seed germinates."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Jong plantjie wat pas met sy eerste blare bo die grond uitgekom het, heet ’n ___.","en":"A young plant that has just come out above the ground with its first leaves is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["saailing"],"en":["seedling"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["saad","vrug","blom"],"en":["seed","fruit","flower"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die saad ontkiem en word ’n saailing. Die saailing groei later tot ’n volwasse plant met blomme en vrugte.","en":"The seed germinates and becomes a seedling. The seedling later grows into an adult plant with flowers and fruit."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom noem ons dit ’n lewens*siklus*?","en":"Why do we call it a life *cycle*?"},"options":[{"af":"Die volwassene maak sade of kleintjies wat weer deur dieselfde stadiums gaan","en":"The adult makes seeds or young that go through the same stages again"},{"af":"Alle plante en diere beweeg in ’n sirkel rond","en":"All plants and animals move around in a circle"},{"af":"Al die stadiums duur presies ewe lank","en":"All the stages last exactly the same length of time"},{"af":"Elke plant en dier leef presies een jaar","en":"Every plant and animal lives exactly one year"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Siklus is ’n kringloop wat oor en oor herhaal: die padda lê eiers, die eiers word paddavisse, en hulle word weer paddas wat eiers lê.","en":"A cycle is a circle that repeats over and over: the frog lays eggs, the eggs become tadpoles, and they become frogs again that lay eggs."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom kan ’n saad in die donker ontkiem, maar het die saailing later lig nodig?","en":"Why can a seed germinate in the dark, but the seedling needs light later?"},"options":[{"af":"Die saad bevat meer water as die saailing","en":"The seed contains more water than the seedling"},{"af":"Lig maak die saad se harde dop sag","en":"Light makes the seed’s hard coat soft"},{"af":"Die saad gebruik gestoorde kos; die saailing moet self kos maak met sonlig","en":"The seed uses stored food; the seedling must make its own food with sunlight"},{"af":"Saailinge groei net bedags en nooit snags nie","en":"Seedlings only grow by day and never at night"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Saad het ’n voorraad kos binne-in. Wanneer dit opgebruik is, moet die saailing self kos maak, en daarvoor het dit sonlig nodig.","en":"A seed has a store of food inside it. When that is used up, the seedling must make its own food, and for that it needs sunlight."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Materie en materiale","en":"Matter and materials"},"topics":[{"id":"nwt5-t2-metale-niemetale","title":{"af":"Metale en nie-metale","en":"Metals and non-metals"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die eienskappe van metale en nie-metale kan beskryf, kan sê watter metale magneties is, en eenvoudige ondersoeke kan doen om materiale te toets.","en":"You will be able to describe the properties of metals and non-metals, say which metals are magnetic, and do simple investigations to test materials."},"summary":{"af":"## Metale en nie-metale\n\nAlles om ons is van **materiale** gemaak. Ons kan materiale in twee groot groepe sorteer: **metale**, soos yster, staal, koper, aluminium, goud en silwer, en **nie-metale**, soos hout, plastiek, glas, rubber, klip en lap. Elke materiaal het **eienskappe** – dit is hoe die materiaal is en wat dit kan doen. Ons kies ’n materiaal vir ’n werk volgens sy eienskappe.\n\n## Eienskappe van metale\n\n| Eienskap | Wat dit beteken | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Blink | glim as dit nuut of gepoleer is | ’n nuwe lepel |\n| Hard en sterk | breek nie maklik nie | staalbalke in geboue |\n| Smeebaar | kan in ’n nuwe vorm gehamer of gedruk word sonder om te breek | aluminiumfoelie, motorlywe |\n| Rekbaar | kan in dun drade uitgetrek word | koperdraad |\n| Gelei hitte | hitte beweeg vinnig daardeur | kastrolle en potte |\n| Gelei elektrisiteit | elektrisiteit vloei daardeur | elektriese drade |\n| Klinkend | maak ’n helder geluid as jy dit slaan | ’n skoolklok |\n\nNie alle metale is ewe hard nie: goud is redelik sag, en aluminiumfoelie kan jy met jou vingers buig.\n\n### Magnetiese metale\n\n’n Magneet trek net **sommige** metale aan: **yster, staal, nikkel en kobalt**. Koper, aluminium, goud en silwer is **nie** magneties nie. ’n Herwinningsaanleg kan dus ’n magneet gebruik om staalblikkies van aluminiumblikkies te skei.\n\n> **Onthou:** **Nie alle metale is magneties nie.** Net yster, staal, nikkel en kobalt word deur ’n magneet aangetrek.\n\n## Eienskappe van nie-metale\n\n- Hulle is meestal **dof**: hulle blink nie soos metaal nie.\n- Hulle is **nie smeebaar nie**. As jy hulle slaan, **breek** party (glas, klip, klei), en ander **buig** en spring terug (rubber, plastiek).\n- Hulle gelei hitte en elektrisiteit swak. Ons noem hulle **isoleerders**. Daarom het potte handvatsels van hout of plastiek, en is elektriese drade met plastiek bedek.\n- Hulle maak net ’n dowwe klop as jy hulle slaan.\n- Hulle is nie magneties nie.\n\n## Eenvoudige ondersoeke\n\n1. **Magneettoets:** Hou ’n magneet teen elke voorwerp. As die magneet dit aantrek, bevat dit yster, staal, nikkel of kobalt.\n2. **Elektrisiteitstoets:** Bou ’n stroombaan met ’n sel, drade en ’n gloeilampie, en laat ’n gaping. Sit die voorwerp in die gaping. Brand die gloeilampie, is die voorwerp ’n **geleier**; brand dit nie, is dit ’n **isoleerder**.\n3. **Hittetoets:** Sit ’n metaallepel, ’n houtlepel en ’n plastieklepel in ’n beker warm water (laat ’n volwassene die water ingooi). Sit ’n ewe groot klontjie botter bo-op elke handvatsel. Die botter op die metaallepel smelt eerste, want metaal gelei hitte die beste.\n4. **Buigtoets:** ’n Stuk koperdraad kan jy buig en plat druk sonder dat dit breek; ’n houtstokkie knak as jy dit te ver buig.\n\nOm ’n toets **regverdig** te maak, verander jy net **een ding** (die materiaal) en hou jy alles anders dieselfde: die grootte van die lepels, die hoeveelheid water en botter, en die tyd.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** ‘Alles wat blink, is metaal.’ Glas en blink plastiek blink ook! ’n Beter toets is om te kyk of die voorwerp elektrisiteit gelei. En moenie die magneettoets gebruik om te besluit of iets ’n metaal is nie – koper en aluminium is metale, maar ’n magneet trek hulle nie aan nie.","en":"## Metals and non-metals\n\nEverything around us is made of **materials**. We can sort materials into two big groups: **metals**, like iron, steel, copper, aluminium, gold and silver, and **non-metals**, like wood, plastic, glass, rubber, stone and fabric. Every material has **properties** – that is what the material is like and what it can do. We choose a material for a job according to its properties.\n\n## Properties of metals\n\n| Property | What it means | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Shiny | gleams when it is new or polished | a new spoon |\n| Hard and strong | does not break easily | steel beams in buildings |\n| Malleable | can be hammered or pressed into a new shape without breaking | aluminium foil, car bodies |\n| Ductile | can be pulled out into thin wires | copper wire |\n| Conducts heat | heat moves through it quickly | saucepans and pots |\n| Conducts electricity | electricity flows through it | electrical wires |\n| Sonorous | makes a clear ringing sound when you hit it | a school bell |\n\nNot all metals are equally hard: gold is quite soft, and you can bend aluminium foil with your fingers.\n\n### Magnetic metals\n\nA magnet attracts only **some** metals: **iron, steel, nickel and cobalt**. Copper, aluminium, gold and silver are **not** magnetic. So a recycling plant can use a magnet to separate steel cans from aluminium cans.\n\n> **Remember:** **Not all metals are magnetic.** Only iron, steel, nickel and cobalt are attracted by a magnet.\n\n## Properties of non-metals\n\n- They are usually **dull**: they do not shine like metal.\n- They are **not malleable**. When you hit them, some **break** (glass, stone, clay), and others **bend** and spring back (rubber, plastic).\n- They conduct heat and electricity poorly. We call them **insulators**. That is why pots have handles of wood or plastic, and electrical wires are covered with plastic.\n- They only make a dull knock when you hit them.\n- They are not magnetic.\n\n## Simple investigations\n\n1. **Magnet test:** Hold a magnet against each object. If the magnet attracts it, it contains iron, steel, nickel or cobalt.\n2. **Electricity test:** Build a circuit with a cell, wires and a small bulb, and leave a gap. Put the object in the gap. If the bulb lights up, the object is a **conductor**; if it does not, it is an **insulator**.\n3. **Heat test:** Put a metal spoon, a wooden spoon and a plastic spoon into a beaker of hot water (let an adult pour the water). Put an equal-sized lump of butter on top of each handle. The butter on the metal spoon melts first, because metal conducts heat best.\n4. **Bending test:** You can bend a piece of copper wire and press it flat without it breaking; a wooden stick snaps if you bend it too far.\n\nTo make a test **fair**, you change only **one thing** (the material) and keep everything else the same: the size of the spoons, the amount of water and butter, and the time.\n\n> **Common mistake:** ‘Everything that shines is metal.’ Glass and shiny plastic shine too! A better test is to see whether the object conducts electricity. And don’t use the magnet test to decide whether something is a metal – copper and aluminium are metals, but a magnet does not attract them."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Metaal","en":"Metal"},"def":{"af":"’n Materiaal soos yster, koper of aluminium wat gewoonlik blink, sterk en smeebaar is en hitte en elektrisiteit gelei.","en":"A material like iron, copper or aluminium that is usually shiny, strong and malleable and conducts heat and electricity."}},{"term":{"af":"Nie-metaal","en":"Non-metal"},"def":{"af":"’n Materiaal soos hout, plastiek, glas of rubber wat meestal dof is en hitte en elektrisiteit swak gelei.","en":"A material like wood, plastic, glass or rubber that is usually dull and conducts heat and electricity poorly."}},{"term":{"af":"Eienskap","en":"Property"},"def":{"af":"Hoe ’n materiaal is of wat dit kan doen, byvoorbeeld hard, blink of buigsaam.","en":"What a material is like or what it can do, for example hard, shiny or flexible."}},{"term":{"af":"Smeebaar","en":"Malleable"},"def":{"af":"Kan in ’n nuwe vorm gehamer of gedruk word sonder om te breek.","en":"Can be hammered or pressed into a new shape without breaking."}},{"term":{"af":"Rekbaar","en":"Ductile"},"def":{"af":"Kan in dun drade uitgetrek word, soos koper.","en":"Can be pulled out into thin wires, like copper."}},{"term":{"af":"Geleier","en":"Conductor"},"def":{"af":"’n Materiaal wat hitte of elektrisiteit maklik deurlaat.","en":"A material that lets heat or electricity pass through easily."}},{"term":{"af":"Isoleerder","en":"Insulator"},"def":{"af":"’n Materiaal wat hitte of elektrisiteit swak deurlaat, soos plastiek of hout.","en":"A material that lets heat or electricity pass through poorly, like plastic or wood."}},{"term":{"af":"Magneties","en":"Magnetic"},"def":{"af":"Word deur ’n magneet aangetrek; net yster, staal, nikkel en kobalt is magneties.","en":"Is attracted by a magnet; only iron, steel, nickel and cobalt are magnetic."}},{"term":{"af":"Klinkend","en":"Sonorous"},"def":{"af":"Maak ’n helder, klinkende geluid as jy dit slaan, soos ’n klok.","en":"Makes a clear, ringing sound when you hit it, like a bell."}},{"term":{"af":"Dof","en":"Dull"},"def":{"af":"Blink nie; die meeste nie-metale, soos hout en klip, is dof.","en":"Does not shine; most non-metals, like wood and stone, are dull."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Sorteer met ’n magneet","en":"Sort with a magnet"},"problem":{"af":"Nomsa hou ’n magneet teen vyf voorwerpe: ’n ysterspyker, ’n aluminium-koeldrankblikkie, ’n stuk koperdraad, ’n staalskuifspeld en ’n houtwasgoedpennetjie. Watter voorwerpe sal die magneet aantrek, en wat leer sy daaruit?","en":"Nomsa holds a magnet against five objects: an iron nail, an aluminium cooldrink can, a piece of copper wire, a steel paper clip and a wooden clothes peg. Which objects will the magnet attract, and what does she learn from this?"},"steps":[{"af":"Onthou die magnetiese metale: **yster, staal, nikkel en kobalt**.","en":"Remember the magnetic metals: **iron, steel, nickel and cobalt**."},{"af":"Die **ysterspyker** en die **staalskuifspeld** word aangetrek.","en":"The **iron nail** and the **steel paper clip** are attracted."},{"af":"Die blikkie (aluminium) en die draad (koper) is metale, maar nie magneties nie. Die pennetjie is hout, ’n nie-metaal.","en":"The can (aluminium) and the wire (copper) are metals, but not magnetic. The peg is wood, a non-metal."}],"answer":{"af":"Net die ysterspyker en staalskuifspeld word aangetrek. Sy leer dat nie alle metale magneties is nie.","en":"Only the iron nail and the steel paper clip are attracted. She learns that not all metals are magnetic."}},{"title":{"af":"Die hittetoets met lepels","en":"The heat test with spoons"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter sit ’n metaal-, hout- en plastieklepel van dieselfde grootte in ’n beker warm water, met ’n ewe groot klontjie botter op elke handvatsel. Ná 3 minute het net die botter op die metaallepel gesmelt. Skryf die veranderlikes en die gevolgtrekking neer.","en":"Pieter puts a metal, a wooden and a plastic spoon of the same size into a beaker of hot water, with an equal-sized lump of butter on each handle. After 3 minutes only the butter on the metal spoon has melted. Write down the variables and the conclusion."},"steps":[{"af":"**Wat hy verander:** die materiaal van die lepel.","en":"**What he changes:** the material of the spoon."},{"af":"**Wat hy meet of waarneem:** watter botter smelt (hoe vinnig die hitte tot by die handvatsel kom).","en":"**What he measures or observes:** which butter melts (how quickly the heat reaches the handle)."},{"af":"**Wat dieselfde bly:** die grootte van die lepels, die water, die hoeveelheid botter en die tyd. Dit maak die toets regverdig.","en":"**What stays the same:** the size of the spoons, the water, the amount of butter and the time. This makes the test fair."},{"af":"Die hitte het die vinnigste deur die metaal beweeg.","en":"The heat moved through the metal the fastest."}],"answer":{"af":"Gevolgtrekking: metaal is ’n goeie geleier van hitte; hout en plastiek is isoleerders.","en":"Conclusion: metal is a good conductor of heat; wood and plastic are insulators."}},{"title":{"af":"Die kastrol en sy handvatsel","en":"The saucepan and its handle"},"problem":{"af":"’n Kastrol is van staal gemaak, maar die handvatsel is van plastiek. Verduidelik waarom elke deel van daardie materiaal gemaak is.","en":"A saucepan is made of steel, but the handle is made of plastic. Explain why each part is made of that material."},"steps":[{"af":"Die **pot** moet die hitte van die stoof vinnig na die kos oordra. Staal is ’n metaal en ’n goeie **geleier** van hitte. Dit is ook sterk en smelt nie op die stoof nie.","en":"The **pot** must pass the heat from the stove to the food quickly. Steel is a metal and a good **conductor** of heat. It is also strong and does not melt on the stove."},{"af":"Die **handvatsel** moet koel bly sodat jy jou nie brand nie. Plastiek is ’n **isoleerder**: hitte beweeg swak daardeur.","en":"The **handle** must stay cool so that you do not burn yourself. Plastic is an **insulator**: heat moves through it poorly."}],"answer":{"af":"Staal gelei hitte goed sodat die kos warm word; plastiek isoleer sodat die handvatsel koel bly.","en":"Steel conducts heat well so that the food gets hot; plastic insulates so that the handle stays cool."}},{"title":{"af":"Geleier of isoleerder?","en":"Conductor or insulator?"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo sit vyf voorwerpe een vir een in die gaping van ’n stroombaan: ’n staalsleutel, ’n rekkie, ’n stukkie aluminiumfoelie, ’n plastiekliniaal en ’n houtblokkie. By watter voorwerpe sal die gloeilampie brand?","en":"Thabo puts five objects one by one into the gap of a circuit: a steel key, a rubber band, a piece of aluminium foil, a plastic ruler and a wooden block. With which objects will the bulb light up?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die gloeilampie brand net as elektrisiteit deur die voorwerp kan vloei – dus net by **geleiers**.","en":"The bulb only lights up if electricity can flow through the object – so only with **conductors**."},{"af":"Metale gelei elektrisiteit: die **staalsleutel** en die **aluminiumfoelie**.","en":"Metals conduct electricity: the **steel key** and the **aluminium foil**."},{"af":"Rubber, plastiek en hout is nie-metale en **isoleerders**: die gloeilampie bly af.","en":"Rubber, plastic and wood are non-metals and **insulators**: the bulb stays off."}],"answer":{"af":"By die staalsleutel en die aluminiumfoelie.","en":"With the steel key and the aluminium foil."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter eienskap maak dit moontlik om koper in dun drade uit te trek?","en":"Which property makes it possible to pull copper out into thin wires?"},"options":[{"af":"Rekbaar","en":"Ductile"},{"af":"Magneties","en":"Magnetic"},{"af":"Klinkend","en":"Sonorous"},{"af":"Dof","en":"Dull"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Rekbaar beteken dat ’n metaal in dun drade uitgetrek kan word. Koper is boonop nie magneties nie.","en":"Ductile means that a metal can be pulled out into thin wires. Copper is also not magnetic."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voorwerp sal deur ’n magneet aangetrek word?","en":"Which object will be attracted by a magnet?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Aluminium-koeldrankblikkie","en":"An aluminium cooldrink can"},{"af":"’n Goue ring","en":"A gold ring"},{"af":"’n Ysterspyker","en":"An iron nail"},{"af":"’n Koperpyp","en":"A copper pipe"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Yster is een van die vier magnetiese metale (yster, staal, nikkel en kobalt). Aluminium, goud en koper is metale, maar ’n magneet trek hulle nie aan nie.","en":"Iron is one of the four magnetic metals (iron, steel, nickel and cobalt). Aluminium, gold and copper are metals, but a magnet does not attract them."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Alle metale word deur ’n magneet aangetrek.","en":"All metals are attracted by a magnet."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Net yster, staal, nikkel en kobalt is magneties. Koper, aluminium, goud en silwer word nie aangetrek nie.","en":"False. Only iron, steel, nickel and cobalt are magnetic. Copper, aluminium, gold and silver are not attracted."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Materiale wat hitte en elektrisiteit swak gelei, word ___ genoem.","en":"Materials that conduct heat and electricity poorly are called ___."},"answers":{"af":["isoleerders","isoleerder"],"en":["insulators","insulator"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["geleiers","metale","magnete"],"en":["conductors","metals","magnets"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Isoleerder, soos plastiek, hout of rubber, laat hitte en elektrisiteit swak deur. ’n Geleier laat dit maklik deur.","en":"An insulator, like plastic, wood or rubber, lets heat and electricity through poorly. A conductor lets it through easily."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is elektriese drade met plastiek bedek?","en":"Why are electrical wires covered with plastic?"},"options":[{"af":"Plastiek maak die draad sterker en swaarder","en":"Plastic makes the wire stronger and heavier"},{"af":"Plastiek lyk mooier as kaal koper","en":"Plastic looks nicer than bare copper"},{"af":"Plastiek gelei elektrisiteit beter as koper","en":"Plastic conducts electricity better than copper"},{"af":"Plastiek is ’n isoleerder en keer dat jy ’n skok kry","en":"Plastic is an insulator and stops you from getting a shock"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die koper binne-in gelei die elektrisiteit. Die plastiek rondom is ’n isoleerder: dit hou die elektrisiteit in die draad en beskerm jou teen ’n skok.","en":"The copper inside conducts the electricity. The plastic around it is an insulator: it keeps the electricity in the wire and protects you from a shock."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke woord by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each word to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Smeebaar","en":"Malleable"},"r":{"af":"Kan plat gehamer word sonder om te breek","en":"Can be hammered flat without breaking"}},{"l":{"af":"Rekbaar","en":"Ductile"},"r":{"af":"Kan in dun drade uitgetrek word","en":"Can be pulled out into thin wires"}},{"l":{"af":"Klinkend","en":"Sonorous"},"r":{"af":"Maak ’n helder geluid as jy dit slaan","en":"Makes a clear sound when you hit it"}},{"l":{"af":"Geleier","en":"Conductor"},"r":{"af":"Laat hitte of elektrisiteit maklik deur","en":"Lets heat or electricity through easily"}},{"l":{"af":"Isoleerder","en":"Insulator"},"r":{"af":"Laat hitte of elektrisiteit swak deur","en":"Lets heat or electricity through poorly"}}],"explain":{"af":"Smeebaar, rekbaar, klinkend en goeie geleiers is eienskappe van metale. Isoleerders is meestal nie-metale soos hout en plastiek.","en":"Malleable, ductile, sonorous and good conductors are properties of metals. Insulators are mostly non-metals like wood and plastic."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Aisha se onderwyser slaan ’n plat stukkie aluminium en ’n teël liggies met ’n hamer. Die aluminium buig in ’n nuwe vorm, maar die teël breek. Wat wys dit?","en":"Aisha’s teacher lightly hits a flat piece of aluminium and a tile with a hammer. The aluminium bends into a new shape, but the tile breaks. What does this show?"},"options":[{"af":"Die teël is magneties","en":"The tile is magnetic"},{"af":"Aluminium is smeebaar, maar die teël nie","en":"Aluminium is malleable, but the tile is not"},{"af":"Aluminium is ’n isoleerder","en":"Aluminium is an insulator"},{"af":"Die teël gelei hitte beter as aluminium","en":"The tile conducts heat better than aluminium"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Smeebare materiaal verander van vorm sonder om te breek as jy dit hamer. Metale is smeebaar; ’n teël is ’n nie-metaal en breek.","en":"A malleable material changes shape without breaking when you hammer it. Metals are malleable; a tile is a non-metal and breaks."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Metaal wat in ’n nuwe vorm gehamer kan word sonder om te breek, is ___.","en":"A metal that can be hammered into a new shape without breaking is ___."},"answers":{"af":["smeebaar"],"en":["malleable"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["rekbaar","dof","bros"],"en":["ductile","dull","brittle"]}},"explain":{"af":"Smeebaar gaan oor hamer of druk in ’n nuwe vorm. Rekbaar gaan oor uittrek in drade – albei is eienskappe van metale, maar hulle is nie dieselfde nie.","en":"Malleable is about hammering or pressing into a new shape. Ductile is about pulling out into wires – both are properties of metals, but they are not the same."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Hout is ’n swak geleier van hitte.","en":"Wood is a poor conductor of heat."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Hout is ’n isoleerder. Daarom word houtlepels en houthandvatsels gebruik vir warm kos – hulle word nie vinnig warm nie.","en":"True. Wood is an insulator. That is why wooden spoons and wooden handles are used for hot food – they do not get hot quickly."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho toets voorwerpe in die gaping van ’n stroombaan. By watter voorwerp sal die gloeilampie brand?","en":"Sipho tests objects in the gap of a circuit. With which object will the bulb light up?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Staalsleutel","en":"A steel key"},{"af":"’n Rekkie","en":"A rubber band"},{"af":"’n Plastiekliniaal","en":"A plastic ruler"},{"af":"’n Glasmarmer","en":"A glass marble"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Staal is ’n metaal en gelei elektrisiteit, so die stroombaan is volledig en die gloeilampie brand. Rubber, plastiek en glas is isoleerders.","en":"Steel is a metal and conducts electricity, so the circuit is complete and the bulb lights up. Rubber, plastic and glass are insulators."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In die hittetoets met lepels en botter, wat moet dieselfde bly om die toets regverdig te maak?","en":"In the heat test with spoons and butter, what must stay the same to make the test fair?"},"options":[{"af":"Die materiaal van die lepels","en":"The material of the spoons"},{"af":"Watter botter eerste smelt","en":"Which butter melts first"},{"af":"Die grootte van die lepels en die hoeveelheid botter en water","en":"The size of the spoons and the amount of butter and water"},{"af":"Hoe lank elke klontjie botter neem om te smelt","en":"How long each lump of butter takes to melt"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die materiaal is wat jy verander, en die smelt van die botter is wat jy waarneem. Alles anders – die grootte van die lepels, die botter en die water – moet dieselfde bly.","en":"The material is what you change, and the melting of the butter is what you observe. Everything else – the size of the spoons, the butter and the water – must stay the same."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die vier magnetiese metale is yster, staal, nikkel en ___.","en":"The four magnetic metals are iron, steel, nickel and ___."},"answers":{"af":["kobalt"],"en":["cobalt"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["koper","aluminium","goud"],"en":["copper","aluminium","gold"]}},"explain":{"af":"Net yster, staal, nikkel en kobalt word deur ’n magneet aangetrek. Koper, aluminium en goud is metale, maar hulle is nie magneties nie.","en":"Only iron, steel, nickel and cobalt are attracted by a magnet. Copper, aluminium and gold are metals, but they are not magnetic."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom word ’n kastrol van metaal gemaak?","en":"Why is a saucepan made of metal?"},"options":[{"af":"Metaal is lig en dryf op water","en":"Metal is light and floats on water"},{"af":"Metaal is ’n goeie isoleerder","en":"Metal is a good insulator"},{"af":"Metaal is altyd magneties","en":"Metal is always magnetic"},{"af":"Metaal gelei hitte goed, so die kos word vinnig warm","en":"Metal conducts heat well, so the food gets hot quickly"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Metaal is ’n goeie geleier van hitte: die hitte van die stoof gaan vinnig deur die pot na die kos. Metaal is nie ’n isoleerder nie, en nie alle metale is magneties nie.","en":"Metal is a good conductor of heat: the heat of the stove passes quickly through the pot to the food. Metal is not an insulator, and not all metals are magnetic."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter wil weet of ’n blink voorwerp van metaal gemaak is. Watter toets is die beste?","en":"Pieter wants to know whether a shiny object is made of metal. Which test is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Kyk net of dit blink","en":"Just look whether it shines"},{"af":"Toets of dit elektrisiteit gelei","en":"Test whether it conducts electricity"},{"af":"Toets of ’n magneet dit aantrek","en":"Test whether a magnet attracts it"},{"af":"Voel net of dit hard is","en":"Just feel whether it is hard"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Metale gelei elektrisiteit. Glas en plastiek kan ook blink en hard wees, en die magneettoets werk net vir yster, staal, nikkel en kobalt – nie vir koper of aluminium nie.","en":"Metals conduct electricity. Glass and plastic can also be shiny and hard, and the magnet test only works for iron, steel, nickel and cobalt – not for copper or aluminium."}}]},{"id":"nwt5-t2-gebruike-metale","title":{"af":"Gebruike van metale en roes","en":"Uses of metals and rust"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik waarom ’n spesifieke metaal vir ’n werk gekies word, wat yster nodig het om te roes, en hoe ons roes kan voorkom.","en":"You will be able to explain why a particular metal is chosen for a job, what iron needs to rust, and how we can prevent rust."},"summary":{"af":"## Die regte metaal vir die werk\n\nElke metaal het sy eie **eienskappe**. Ingenieurs en vervaardigers kies die metaal wat die beste by die werk pas.\n\n| Metaal | Belangrike eienskappe | Gebruike |\n|---|---|---|\n| Koper | gelei elektrisiteit en hitte baie goed; rekbaar; roes nie | elektriese drade, waterpype |\n| Aluminium | baie lig; roes nie; smeebaar | koeldrankblikkies, vensterrame, vliegtuie, foelie |\n| Staal | baie sterk en hard | brûe, motors, geboue, spykers |\n| Yster | sterk; bly lank warm | potjiepotte, hekke |\n| Goud en silwer | blink en mooi; roes nie; skaars en duur | juweliersware, medaljes |\n\n- **Staal** is yster waarby ’n bietjie koolstof gemeng is. Dit is sterker en harder as suiwer yster.\n- **Koper** word vir waterpype gebruik omdat dit nie roes nie en maklik gebuig kan word.\n- **Aluminium** is so lig dat vliegtuie en koeldrankblikkies daarvan gemaak word.\n- **Goud** is in 1886 aan die Witwatersrand ontdek, en Johannesburg het rondom die goudmyne gegroei.\n\n## Wat is roes?\n\n**Roes** is ’n rooibruin, skilferige laag wat op **yster** en **staal** vorm wanneer hulle vir ’n tyd lank met **water** en **suurstof** (uit die lug) in aanraking is.\n\n**yster + water + suurstof → roes**\n\n- Roes is swak en bros. Dit skilfer af, en dan roes die metaal daaronder ook. Uiteindelik kom daar gate in die metaal.\n- Geroeste hekke, motors en brûe word swak en kan gevaarlik wees.\n- **Soutwater** laat yster vinniger roes. Daarom roes motors en hekke by die see vinniger as in die binneland.\n- Net yster en staal **roes**. Ander metale kan wel verander – koper word groen en silwer word donker – maar dit is nie roes nie.\n\n## Ondersoek: Wat het yster nodig om te roes?\n\nLerato sit ’n skoon ysterspyker in elk van vier flesse en kyk ná ’n week na hulle:\n\n| Fles | Toestande | Resultaat ná ’n week |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | droë fles met ’n deksel en ’n sakkie silikajel (droë lug, geen water) | geen roes |\n| B | gekookte water met ’n laag olie bo-op (water, geen lug) | geen roes |\n| C | kraanwater, oop (water en lug) | roes |\n| D | soutwater, oop (water, lug en sout) | die meeste roes |\n\n- Die sakkie **silikajel** (soos dié in ’n nuwe skoendoos) trek die waterdamp uit die lug in fles A, sodat die lug heeltemal droog bly.\n- Die water in fles B is gekook om die lug daaruit te kry, en die olie keer dat nuwe lug inkom.\n- **Wat dieselfde bly:** dieselfde soort spykers van dieselfde grootte, op dieselfde plek, vir dieselfde tyd. Dit maak die toets **regverdig**.\n- **Gevolgtrekking:** yster het **water én suurstof** nodig om te roes; sout laat dit vinniger roes.\n\n## Hoe om roes te voorkom\n\nOm roes te keer, hou jy **water en lug weg** van die yster of staal:\n\n- **Verf** – hekke, brûe, motors en diefwering word geverf.\n- **Olie of ghries** – vir dele wat beweeg, soos ’n fietsketting. Verf sou net afskuur.\n- **Galvaniseer** – die yster of staal word met ’n dun laag **sink** bedek. Sinkplate vir dakke, emmers en draad word gegalvaniseer. Selfs as dit gekrap word, beskerm die sink die yster nog.\n- **Plastiekbedekking** – soos op skottelgoedrakke en sommige draadheinings.\n- **Vlekvrye staal** – staal waarby **chroom** gemeng is. Dit roes nie, en word vir messe, vurke en opwasbakke gebruik.\n- **Hou dit droog** – droog gereedskap af ná gebruik en bêre dit op ’n droë plek.\n\n> **Onthou:** Roes het water **én** suurstof nodig. Haal een van die twee weg, en die yster roes nie.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** ‘Alle metale roes.’ Net yster en staal roes. ’n Aluminium-koeldrankblikkie wat in die veld weggegooi is, roes nie – dit kan jare lank daar lê. Dis nog ’n rede om blikkies te herwin!","en":"## The right metal for the job\n\nEvery metal has its own **properties**. Engineers and manufacturers choose the metal that suits the job best.\n\n| Metal | Important properties | Uses |\n|---|---|---|\n| Copper | conducts electricity and heat very well; ductile; does not rust | electrical wires, water pipes |\n| Aluminium | very light; does not rust; malleable | cooldrink cans, window frames, aeroplanes, foil |\n| Steel | very strong and hard | bridges, cars, buildings, nails |\n| Iron | strong; stays hot for a long time | potjie pots, gates |\n| Gold and silver | shiny and beautiful; do not rust; rare and expensive | jewellery, medals |\n\n- **Steel** is iron with a little carbon mixed in. It is stronger and harder than pure iron.\n- **Copper** is used for water pipes because it does not rust and can be bent easily.\n- **Aluminium** is so light that aeroplanes and cooldrink cans are made from it.\n- **Gold** was discovered on the Witwatersrand in 1886, and Johannesburg grew up around the gold mines.\n\n## What is rust?\n\n**Rust** is a reddish-brown, flaky layer that forms on **iron** and **steel** when they are in contact with **water** and **oxygen** (from the air) for some time.\n\n**iron + water + oxygen → rust**\n\n- Rust is weak and crumbly. It flakes off, and then the metal underneath rusts too. In the end holes form in the metal.\n- Rusted gates, cars and bridges become weak and can be dangerous.\n- **Salt water** makes iron rust faster. That is why cars and gates at the coast rust faster than inland.\n- Only iron and steel **rust**. Other metals can change – copper turns green and silver turns dark – but that is not rust.\n\n## Investigation: What does iron need to rust?\n\nLerato puts a clean iron nail into each of four jars and looks at them after a week:\n\n| Jar | Conditions | Result after a week |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | dry jar with a lid and a sachet of silica gel (dry air, no water) | no rust |\n| B | boiled water with a layer of oil on top (water, no air) | no rust |\n| C | tap water, open (water and air) | rust |\n| D | salt water, open (water, air and salt) | the most rust |\n\n- The sachet of **silica gel** (like the one in a new shoebox) soaks up the water vapour from the air in jar A, so that the air stays completely dry.\n- The water in jar B was boiled to get the air out of it, and the oil stops new air from getting in.\n- **What stays the same:** the same kind of nails of the same size, in the same place, for the same time. This makes the test **fair**.\n- **Conclusion:** iron needs **water and oxygen** to rust; salt makes it rust faster.\n\n## How to prevent rust\n\nTo stop rust, you keep **water and air away** from the iron or steel:\n\n- **Paint** – gates, bridges, cars and burglar bars are painted.\n- **Oil or grease** – for parts that move, like a bicycle chain. Paint would just rub off.\n- **Galvanising** – the iron or steel is covered with a thin layer of **zinc**. Corrugated iron roof sheets, buckets and wire are galvanised. Even if it gets scratched, the zinc still protects the iron.\n- **Plastic coating** – as on dish racks and some wire fences.\n- **Stainless steel** – steel with **chromium** mixed in. It does not rust, and is used for knives, forks and sinks.\n- **Keep it dry** – dry tools after use and store them in a dry place.\n\n> **Remember:** Rust needs water **and** oxygen. Take away one of the two, and the iron does not rust.\n\n> **Common mistake:** ‘All metals rust.’ Only iron and steel rust. An aluminium cooldrink can that was thrown away in the veld does not rust – it can lie there for years. That is another reason to recycle cans!"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Roes","en":"Rust"},"def":{"af":"’n Rooibruin, skilferige laag wat op yster en staal vorm as hulle met water en suurstof in aanraking is.","en":"A reddish-brown, flaky layer that forms on iron and steel when they are in contact with water and oxygen."}},{"term":{"af":"Suurstof","en":"Oxygen"},"def":{"af":"’n Gas in die lug wat saam met water yster laat roes.","en":"A gas in the air that, together with water, makes iron rust."}},{"term":{"af":"Staal","en":"Steel"},"def":{"af":"’n Baie sterk metaal wat van yster met ’n bietjie koolstof gemaak word.","en":"A very strong metal made from iron with a little carbon."}},{"term":{"af":"Vlekvrye staal","en":"Stainless steel"},"def":{"af":"Staal waarby chroom gemeng is sodat dit nie roes nie.","en":"Steel with chromium mixed in so that it does not rust."}},{"term":{"af":"Galvaniseer","en":"Galvanise"},"def":{"af":"Om yster of staal met ’n dun laag sink te bedek sodat dit nie roes nie.","en":"To cover iron or steel with a thin layer of zinc so that it does not rust."}},{"term":{"af":"Sink","en":"Zinc"},"def":{"af":"’n Metaal wat as dun laag oor yster en staal gesit word om hulle teen roes te beskerm.","en":"A metal that is put as a thin layer over iron and steel to protect them from rust."}},{"term":{"af":"Koper","en":"Copper"},"def":{"af":"’n Rooibruin metaal wat elektrisiteit baie goed gelei en vir drade en waterpype gebruik word.","en":"A reddish-brown metal that conducts electricity very well and is used for wires and water pipes."}},{"term":{"af":"Aluminium","en":"Aluminium"},"def":{"af":"’n Baie ligte metaal wat nie roes nie en vir blikkies, vensterrame en vliegtuie gebruik word.","en":"A very light metal that does not rust and is used for cans, window frames and aeroplanes."}},{"term":{"af":"Regverdige toets","en":"Fair test"},"def":{"af":"’n Ondersoek waarin jy net een ding verander en alles anders dieselfde hou.","en":"An investigation in which you change only one thing and keep everything else the same."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Kies ’n metaal vir vensterrame","en":"Choose a metal for window frames"},"problem":{"af":"Johan se gesin bou ’n huis naby die see in Durban. Hulle moet kies tussen gewone yster, staal sonder verf en aluminium vir die vensterrame. Watter metaal is die beste, en waarom?","en":"Johan’s family is building a house near the sea in Durban. They must choose between plain iron, unpainted steel and aluminium for the window frames. Which metal is best, and why?"},"steps":[{"af":"Dink na oor die plek: by die see is die lug klam en souterig, en sout laat yster vinniger roes.","en":"Think about the place: at the sea the air is damp and salty, and salt makes iron rust faster."},{"af":"Yster en onbedekte staal sal gou roes en swak word.","en":"Iron and uncovered steel will soon rust and become weak."},{"af":"**Aluminium roes nie**, is lig en kan maklik in die vorm van ’n raam gemaak word.","en":"**Aluminium does not rust**, is light and can easily be made into the shape of a frame."}],"answer":{"af":"Aluminium, want dit roes nie in die souterige lug nie en is lig.","en":"Aluminium, because it does not rust in the salty air and is light."}},{"title":{"af":"Lees die roesondersoek","en":"Read the rust investigation"},"problem":{"af":"Kyk na Lerato se resultate: A (droë fles met deksel en silikajel) – geen roes; B (gekookte water met olie) – geen roes; C (oop kraanwater) – roes; D (oop soutwater) – die meeste roes. Wat het yster nodig om te roes?","en":"Look at Lerato’s results: A (dry jar with lid and silica gel) – no rust; B (boiled water with oil) – no rust; C (open tap water) – rust; D (open salt water) – the most rust. What does iron need to rust?"},"steps":[{"af":"Fles A het lug, maar geen water nie: **geen roes**. Lug alleen is dus nie genoeg nie.","en":"Jar A has air, but no water: **no rust**. So air alone is not enough."},{"af":"Fles B het water, maar geen lug nie: **geen roes**. Water alleen is ook nie genoeg nie.","en":"Jar B has water, but no air: **no rust**. So water alone is not enough either."},{"af":"Fles C het water én lug: **roes**. Fles D het ook sout bygekry en het die meeste geroes.","en":"Jar C has water and air: **rust**. Jar D also had salt added and rusted the most."}],"answer":{"af":"Yster het water én suurstof (lug) nodig om te roes. Sout laat dit vinniger roes.","en":"Iron needs water and oxygen (air) to rust. Salt makes it rust faster."}},{"title":{"af":"Voorkom roes","en":"Prevent rust"},"problem":{"af":"Kies die beste manier om roes te voorkom vir elkeen en sê waarom: (a) ’n fietsketting; (b) ’n tuinhek; (c) dakplate; (d) ’n opwasbak in die kombuis.","en":"Choose the best way to prevent rust for each one and say why: (a) a bicycle chain; (b) a garden gate; (c) roof sheets; (d) a kitchen sink."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die ketting se dele beweeg en skuur teen mekaar. Verf sal afskuur, so **olie of ghries** werk die beste.","en":"(a) The chain’s parts move and rub against each other. Paint will rub off, so **oil or grease** works best."},{"af":"(b) ’n Hek beweeg min en staan buite: **verf** hou water en lug weg.","en":"(b) A gate hardly moves and stands outside: **paint** keeps water and air away."},{"af":"(c) Dakplate is heeltyd in die reën: hulle word **gegalvaniseer** met sink.","en":"(c) Roof sheets are in the rain all the time: they are **galvanised** with zinc."},{"af":"(d) ’n Opwasbak is heeltyd nat en moet skoon en blink bly: **vlekvrye staal**.","en":"(d) A sink is wet all the time and must stay clean and shiny: **stainless steel**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) olie of ghries; (b) verf; (c) galvaniseer; (d) vlekvrye staal","en":"(a) oil or grease; (b) paint; (c) galvanise; (d) stainless steel"}},{"title":{"af":"Waarom koperdraad?","en":"Why copper wire?"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik waarom die drade in ’n huis se elektriese bedrading van koper gemaak word.","en":"Explain why the wires in a house’s electrical wiring are made of copper."},"steps":[{"af":"Koper **gelei elektrisiteit baie goed**, so die elektrisiteit vloei maklik daardeur.","en":"Copper **conducts electricity very well**, so the electricity flows through it easily."},{"af":"Koper is **rekbaar**: dit kan in lang, dun drade uitgetrek word wat maklik buig.","en":"Copper is **ductile**: it can be pulled out into long, thin wires that bend easily."},{"af":"Koper **roes nie**, so die drade bly lank goed werk.","en":"Copper **does not rust**, so the wires keep working well for a long time."}],"answer":{"af":"Koper gelei elektrisiteit goed, kan in dun drade uitgetrek word en roes nie.","en":"Copper conducts electricity well, can be pulled out into thin wires and does not rust."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat het yster nodig om te roes?","en":"What does iron need to rust?"},"options":[{"af":"Net water","en":"Only water"},{"af":"Water en suurstof","en":"Water and oxygen"},{"af":"Net lug","en":"Only air"},{"af":"Sout en sonlig","en":"Salt and sunlight"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Roes vorm net as yster water én suurstof kry. Sout laat dit vinniger roes, maar sonder water en suurstof roes yster nie.","en":"Rust only forms when iron gets water and oxygen. Salt makes it rust faster, but without water and oxygen iron does not rust."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom word vliegtuie hoofsaaklik van aluminium gemaak?","en":"Why are aeroplanes made mainly of aluminium?"},"options":[{"af":"Aluminium is magneties","en":"Aluminium is magnetic"},{"af":"Aluminium is die swaarste metaal","en":"Aluminium is the heaviest metal"},{"af":"Aluminium gelei glad nie elektrisiteit nie","en":"Aluminium does not conduct electricity at all"},{"af":"Aluminium is lig en roes nie","en":"Aluminium is light and does not rust"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Vliegtuig moet so lig moontlik wees, en dit vlieg deur reën en wolke. Aluminium is lig en roes nie. Dit is nie magneties nie en gelei wel elektrisiteit.","en":"An aeroplane must be as light as possible, and it flies through rain and clouds. Aluminium is light and does not rust. It is not magnetic and it does conduct electricity."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Aluminium-koeldrankblikkie sal roes as dit lank in die reën lê.","en":"An aluminium cooldrink can will rust if it lies in the rain for a long time."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Net yster en staal roes. Aluminium roes nie – daarom kan weggegooide blikkies jare lank in die veld lê.","en":"False. Only iron and steel rust. Aluminium does not rust – that is why thrown-away cans can lie in the veld for years."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As yster of staal met ’n dun laag sink bedek word, sê ons dit is ___.","en":"When iron or steel is covered with a thin layer of zinc, we say it is ___."},"answers":{"af":["gegalvaniseer"],"en":["galvanised","galvanized"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["geverf","geolie","geroes"],"en":["painted","oiled","rusted"]}},"explain":{"af":"Galvaniseer beteken om met sink te bedek. Sinkplate op dakke is gegalvaniseer. Verf en olie keer ook roes, maar hulle is nie sink nie.","en":"Galvanising means covering with zinc. Corrugated iron roof sheets are galvanised. Paint and oil also stop rust, but they are not zinc."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter spyker sal die vinnigste roes?","en":"Which nail will rust the fastest?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Ysterspyker in oop soutwater","en":"An iron nail in open salt water"},{"af":"’n Ysterspyker in ’n droë fles met ’n deksel","en":"An iron nail in a dry jar with a lid"},{"af":"’n Ysterspyker in gekookte water met olie bo-op","en":"An iron nail in boiled water with oil on top"},{"af":"’n Vlekvrye-staalspyker in kraanwater","en":"A stainless steel nail in tap water"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"In oop soutwater kry die spyker water, suurstof én sout, en sout laat yster vinniger roes. In die droë fles is daar geen water nie, onder die olie geen lug nie, en vlekvrye staal roes nie.","en":"In open salt water the nail gets water, oxygen and salt, and salt makes iron rust faster. In the dry jar there is no water, under the oil there is no air, and stainless steel does not rust."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke metaal by ’n goeie gebruik daarvan.","en":"Match each metal to a good use of it."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Koper","en":"Copper"},"r":{"af":"Elektriese drade","en":"Electrical wires"}},{"l":{"af":"Aluminium","en":"Aluminium"},"r":{"af":"Vliegtuie en koeldrankblikkies","en":"Aeroplanes and cooldrink cans"}},{"l":{"af":"Staal","en":"Steel"},"r":{"af":"Brûe en geboue","en":"Bridges and buildings"}},{"l":{"af":"Goud","en":"Gold"},"r":{"af":"Juweliersware","en":"Jewellery"}},{"l":{"af":"Sink","en":"Zinc"},"r":{"af":"’n Beskermlaag op dakplate","en":"A protective layer on roof sheets"}}],"explain":{"af":"Koper gelei goed, aluminium is lig, staal is baie sterk, goud is blink en roes nie, en sink beskerm yster teen roes (galvaniseer).","en":"Copper conducts well, aluminium is light, steel is very strong, gold is shiny and does not rust, and zinc protects iron from rust (galvanising)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom word ’n fietsketting geolie in plaas van geverf?","en":"Why is a bicycle chain oiled instead of painted?"},"options":[{"af":"Olie laat die ketting mooier blink","en":"Oil makes the chain shine more nicely"},{"af":"Verf kan nie op metaal vassit nie","en":"Paint cannot stick to metal"},{"af":"Die dele beweeg, so verf sou afskuur; olie hou water weg en laat dit glad loop","en":"The parts move, so paint would rub off; oil keeps water away and makes it run smoothly"},{"af":"Olie maak die ketting magneties","en":"Oil makes the chain magnetic"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Verf werk goed op dinge wat stilstaan, soos hekke. Die skakels van ’n ketting skuur teen mekaar, so verf sou afskuur. Olie bedek die metaal, hou water weg en help die ketting om glad te draai.","en":"Paint works well on things that stand still, like gates. The links of a chain rub against each other, so paint would rub off. Oil covers the metal, keeps water away and helps the chain to turn smoothly."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Staal waarby chroom gemeng is sodat dit nie roes nie, heet ___.","en":"Steel with chromium mixed in so that it does not rust is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["vlekvrye staal"],"en":["stainless steel"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["gegalvaniseerde staal","sink","aluminium"],"en":["galvanised steel","zinc","aluminium"]}},"explain":{"af":"Vlekvrye staal het chroom in die metaal self. Gegalvaniseerde staal het ’n laag sink aan die buitekant – dit is ’n ander manier om roes te keer.","en":"Stainless steel has chromium in the metal itself. Galvanised steel has a layer of zinc on the outside – that is a different way to stop rust."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Roes maak yster en staal swakker.","en":"Rust makes iron and steel weaker."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Roes is bros en skilfer af, en dan roes die metaal daaronder ook. Uiteindelik kom daar gate in, en geroeste hekke en brûe kan gevaarlik word.","en":"True. Rust is crumbly and flakes off, and then the metal underneath rusts too. In the end holes form, and rusted gates and bridges can become dangerous."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom word koper vir elektriese drade gebruik?","en":"Why is copper used for electrical wires?"},"options":[{"af":"Koper is magneties","en":"Copper is magnetic"},{"af":"Koper is die hardste metaal","en":"Copper is the hardest metal"},{"af":"Koper is ’n goeie isoleerder","en":"Copper is a good insulator"},{"af":"Koper gelei elektrisiteit goed en is rekbaar","en":"Copper conducts electricity well and is ductile"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Koper gelei elektrisiteit baie goed en kan in dun drade uitgetrek word. Dit is ’n geleier, nie ’n isoleerder nie – die plastiek om die draad is die isoleerder.","en":"Copper conducts electricity very well and can be pulled out into thin wires. It is a conductor, not an insulator – the plastic around the wire is the insulator."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In die roesondersoek is een spyker in gekookte water met ’n laag olie bo-op. Waarom die olie?","en":"In the rust investigation one nail is in boiled water with a layer of oil on top. Why the oil?"},"options":[{"af":"Om lug weg te hou van die water en die spyker","en":"To keep air away from the water and the nail"},{"af":"Om die spyker vinniger te laat roes","en":"To make the nail rust faster"},{"af":"Om die water lekker warm te hou","en":"To keep the water nice and warm"},{"af":"Om die spyker blink te poleer","en":"To polish the nail until it shines"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die water is gekook om die lug uit te kry, en die olie keer dat nuwe lug inkom. So kan jy toets of yster sonder lug roes – en dit roes nie.","en":"The water was boiled to get the air out, and the oil stops new air from getting in. In this way you can test whether iron rusts without air – and it does not."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Roes vorm wanneer yster of staal met water en ___ in aanraking kom.","en":"Rust forms when iron or steel comes into contact with water and ___."},"answers":{"af":["suurstof","lug"],"en":["oxygen","air"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["sout","sonlig","olie"],"en":["salt","sunlight","oil"]}},"explain":{"af":"Roes het water en suurstof uit die lug nodig. Sout laat dit vinniger gebeur, maar dit is nie nodig nie. Olie keer juis roes.","en":"Rust needs water and oxygen from the air. Salt makes it happen faster, but it is not needed. Oil actually prevents rust."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom word goud en silwer vir juweliersware gebruik?","en":"Why are gold and silver used for jewellery?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle is magneties en baie hard","en":"They are magnetic and very hard"},{"af":"Hulle is blink en mooi, roes nie en is skaars","en":"They are shiny and beautiful, do not rust and are rare"},{"af":"Hulle is baie lig en goedkoop","en":"They are very light and cheap"},{"af":"Hulle gelei glad nie hitte nie","en":"They do not conduct heat at all"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Juweliersware moet mooi bly en waardevol wees. Goud en silwer is blink, roes nie en is skaars en duur. Hulle is nie magneties nie, en goud is eintlik redelik sag.","en":"Jewellery must stay beautiful and be valuable. Gold and silver are shiny, do not rust and are rare and expensive. They are not magnetic, and gold is actually quite soft."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Fatima se gesin bou ’n stoep by die see. Watter een is die beste keuse vir die relings?","en":"Fatima’s family is building a stoep at the sea. Which one is the best choice for the railings?"},"options":[{"af":"Gewone yster, want dit is sterk","en":"Plain iron, because it is strong"},{"af":"Koper, want dit gelei elektrisiteit","en":"Copper, because it conducts electricity"},{"af":"Vlekvrye staal, want dit is sterk en roes nie","en":"Stainless steel, because it is strong and does not rust"},{"af":"Onbedekte staal, want dit is hard","en":"Uncovered steel, because it is hard"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"By die see is die lug klam en souterig, en dan roes gewone yster en onbedekte staal vinnig. Vlekvrye staal is sterk en roes nie. Elektriese geleiding is nie belangrik vir ’n reling nie.","en":"At the sea the air is damp and salty, and then plain iron and uncovered steel rust quickly. Stainless steel is strong and does not rust. Conducting electricity is not important for a railing."}}]},{"id":"nwt5-t2-materiale-prosesseer","title":{"af":"Materiale prosesseer en kombineer (Tegnologie)","en":"Processing and combining materials (Technology)"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe rou materiale geprosesseer word, waarom ons materiale kombineer om beter eienskappe te kry, en die ontwerpproses kan gebruik om ’n waterdigte potloodhouer te maak en te evalueer.","en":"You will be able to explain how raw materials are processed, why we combine materials to get better properties, and use the design process to make and evaluate a waterproof pencil holder."},"summary":{"af":"## Rou en geprosesseerde materiale\n\n**Rou materiale** kom reguit uit die natuur: hout, sand, klei, klip, katoen, wol en ystererts. Wanneer ons ’n rou materiaal in ’n fabriek of met die hand verander sodat dit nuttiger word, **prosesseer** ons dit. Die nuwe materiaal is ’n **geprosesseerde materiaal**.\n\n| Rou materiaal | Wat gebeur | Geprosesseerde materiaal |\n|---|---|---|\n| Hout | fyngemaak, met water tot pulp gemeng, platgedruk en gedroog | papier en karton |\n| Sand | saam met ’n paar ander stowwe baie warm verhit totdat dit smelt | glas |\n| Klei | gevorm en in ’n baie warm oond gebak | bakstene, teëls en potte |\n| Katoen | tot garing gespin en geweef | lap |\n| Ystererts | in ’n hoogoond gesmelt | yster en staal |\n\n## Materiale kombineer\n\nAs ons twee of meer materiale **kombineer** (saamvoeg), kry ons dikwels ’n nuwe materiaal met **beter eienskappe** as elkeen alleen.\n\n- **Papier-maché** = papierstroke + gom (of meel-en-water-pasta). Papier alleen is pap en swak. Saam, in lae, droog dit tot ’n **harde, sterk en ligte dop**. Ons maak maskers, bakke en modelle daarvan.\n- **Beton** = sement + sand + klip + water. Die pap mengsel word in ’n vorm gegooi en word dan so hard soos klip. Dit is baie sterk as jy daarop **druk**, en word vir fondamente, vloere en paadjies gebruik.\n- **Gewapende beton** = beton met **staalstawe** binne-in. Beton kraak maklik as dit **gebuig** word, maar staal kan buig sonder om te breek. Saam is hulle sterk genoeg vir brûe en hoë geboue.\n- **Modderstene met strooi** – modder alleen kraak as dit droog word. Die strooi hou die modder bymekaar, soos drade, sodat die stene sterker is.\n- **Gelamineerde karton** – as jy ’n paar lae karton op mekaar plak (**lamineer**), is dit baie sterker en stywer as een laag. Laaghout word op dieselfde manier van dun lae hout gemaak.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Sement en beton is nie dieselfde nie! **Sement** is net die grys poeier – een van die bestanddele. **Beton** is die harde mengsel van sement, sand, klip en water.\n\n## Materiale beter laat werk\n\n| Om dit … te maak | Wat jy kan doen | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| waterdig | vryf kerswas daaroor; bedek dit met plastiek; verf of vernis dit | melkkartonne met ’n dun laag plastiek; geverfde hout |\n| sterker | rol dit in buise op; vou dit in riffels; lamineer lae | papierbuise; riffelkarton |\n| buigsamer | sny dit in dun stroke; weef stroke of drade inmekaar | mandjies en lap |\n\n## Ontwerptaak: ’n waterdigte potloodhouer\n\n**Ontwerpopdrag:** Ontwerp en maak ’n potloodhouer van papier-maché vir jou lessenaar.\n\n- **Spesifikasies:** hou minstens 10 potlode; val nie om nie; die buitekant is waterdig; dit lyk netjies.\n- **Beperkings:** net herwinde papier, meelpasta, ’n kartonrol vir die vorm, en verf of kerswas; klaar binne twee weke (elke laag moet droog word).\n\nVolg die ontwerpproses:\n\n1. **Ondersoek** – kyk na potloodhouers en toets watter bedekking water die beste keer.\n2. **Ontwerp** – teken twee of drie sketse met byskrifte en kies die beste een.\n3. **Maak** – plak 4 tot 5 lae papierstroke om die kartonrol, laat elke laag droog word, maak ’n wye voet en verf of was die buitekant.\n4. **Evalueer** – toets elke spesifikasie: sit 10 potlode in, stamp liggies daaraan en drup water op die buitekant.\n5. **Kommunikeer** – wys jou houer aan die klas en verduidelik wat jy sou verbeter.\n\n> **Onthou:** Wanneer jy materiale kombineer, kry jy ’n nuwe materiaal met eienskappe wat die afsonderlike materiale nie gehad het nie.","en":"## Raw and processed materials\n\n**Raw materials** come straight from nature: wood, sand, clay, stone, cotton, wool and iron ore. When we change a raw material in a factory or by hand so that it becomes more useful, we **process** it. The new material is a **processed material**.\n\n| Raw material | What happens | Processed material |\n|---|---|---|\n| Wood | chopped up finely, mixed with water to make pulp, pressed flat and dried | paper and cardboard |\n| Sand | heated together with a few other substances until it melts | glass |\n| Clay | shaped and baked in a very hot kiln | bricks, tiles and pots |\n| Cotton | spun into thread and woven | fabric |\n| Iron ore | melted in a blast furnace | iron and steel |\n\n## Combining materials\n\nWhen we **combine** (put together) two or more materials, we often get a new material with **better properties** than each one alone.\n\n- **Papier-mâché** = strips of paper + glue (or flour-and-water paste). Paper alone is floppy and weak. Together, in layers, it dries into a **hard, strong and light shell**. We make masks, bowls and models from it.\n- **Concrete** = cement + sand + stone + water. The runny mixture is poured into a mould and then becomes as hard as stone. It is very strong when you **press** on it, and is used for foundations, floors and paths.\n- **Reinforced concrete** = concrete with **steel bars** inside. Concrete cracks easily when it is **bent**, but steel can bend without breaking. Together they are strong enough for bridges and tall buildings.\n- **Mud bricks with straw** – mud alone cracks when it dries. The straw holds the mud together, like threads, so that the bricks are stronger.\n- **Laminated cardboard** – if you glue a few layers of cardboard on top of each other (**laminate**), it is much stronger and stiffer than one layer. Plywood is made in the same way from thin layers of wood.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Cement and concrete are not the same! **Cement** is only the grey powder – one of the ingredients. **Concrete** is the hard mixture of cement, sand, stone and water.\n\n## Making materials work better\n\n| To make it … | What you can do | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| waterproof | rub candle wax over it; cover it with plastic; paint or varnish it | milk cartons with a thin layer of plastic; painted wood |\n| stronger | roll it into tubes; fold it into ridges; laminate layers | paper tubes; corrugated cardboard |\n| more flexible | cut it into thin strips; weave strips or threads together | baskets and fabric |\n\n## Design task: a waterproof pencil holder\n\n**Design brief:** Design and make a pencil holder from papier-mâché for your desk.\n\n- **Specifications:** holds at least 10 pencils; does not fall over; the outside is waterproof; it looks neat.\n- **Constraints:** only recycled paper, flour paste, a cardboard roll for the shape, and paint or candle wax; finished within two weeks (every layer must dry).\n\nFollow the design process:\n\n1. **Investigate** – look at pencil holders and test which covering keeps water out best.\n2. **Design** – draw two or three labelled sketches and choose the best one.\n3. **Make** – stick 4 to 5 layers of paper strips around the cardboard roll, let each layer dry, make a wide base and paint or wax the outside.\n4. **Evaluate** – test each specification: put in 10 pencils, bump it gently and drip water on the outside.\n5. **Communicate** – show your holder to the class and explain what you would improve.\n\n> **Remember:** When you combine materials, you get a new material with properties that the separate materials did not have."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Rou materiaal","en":"Raw material"},"def":{"af":"’n Materiaal wat reguit uit die natuur kom, soos hout, sand of klei.","en":"A material that comes straight from nature, like wood, sand or clay."}},{"term":{"af":"Prosesseer","en":"Process"},"def":{"af":"Om ’n rou materiaal te verander sodat dit nuttiger word, byvoorbeeld hout in papier.","en":"To change a raw material so that it becomes more useful, for example wood into paper."}},{"term":{"af":"Geprosesseerde materiaal","en":"Processed material"},"def":{"af":"’n Materiaal wat van ’n rou materiaal gemaak is, soos glas, papier of bakstene.","en":"A material that has been made from a raw material, like glass, paper or bricks."}},{"term":{"af":"Kombineer","en":"Combine"},"def":{"af":"Om twee of meer materiale saam te voeg om ’n nuwe materiaal met beter eienskappe te kry.","en":"To put two or more materials together to get a new material with better properties."}},{"term":{"af":"Papier-maché","en":"Papier-mâché"},"def":{"af":"’n Materiaal van papierstroke en gom wat in lae droog word tot ’n harde, ligte dop.","en":"A material of paper strips and glue that dries in layers into a hard, light shell."}},{"term":{"af":"Sement","en":"Cement"},"def":{"af":"’n Grys poeier wat met sand, klip en water gemeng word om beton te maak.","en":"A grey powder that is mixed with sand, stone and water to make concrete."}},{"term":{"af":"Beton","en":"Concrete"},"def":{"af":"’n Harde boumateriaal van sement, sand, klip en water.","en":"A hard building material made of cement, sand, stone and water."}},{"term":{"af":"Gewapende beton","en":"Reinforced concrete"},"def":{"af":"Beton met staalstawe binne-in sodat dit nie maklik kraak as dit buig nie.","en":"Concrete with steel bars inside so that it does not crack easily when it bends."}},{"term":{"af":"Lamineer","en":"Laminate"},"def":{"af":"Om lae van ’n materiaal op mekaar te plak om dit sterker en stywer te maak.","en":"To glue layers of a material on top of each other to make it stronger and stiffer."}},{"term":{"af":"Waterdig","en":"Waterproof"},"def":{"af":"Laat nie water deur nie, byvoorbeeld karton met ’n laag was of plastiek.","en":"Does not let water through, for example cardboard with a layer of wax or plastic."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Waarom strooi in modderstene?","en":"Why straw in mud bricks?"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho maak twee modderstene: een van net modder en een van modder met strooi. Ná ’n week in die son het die eerste een groot krake. Verduidelik waarom die steen met strooi beter is.","en":"Sipho makes two mud bricks: one of only mud and one of mud with straw. After a week in the sun the first one has big cracks. Explain why the brick with straw is better."},"steps":[{"af":"Wanneer modder droog word, krimp dit, en dan trek dit uitmekaar en kraak.","en":"When mud dries, it shrinks, and then it pulls apart and cracks."},{"af":"Die **strooi** loop soos drade deur die modder en **hou dit bymekaar**.","en":"The **straw** runs through the mud like threads and **holds it together**."},{"af":"Deur die twee materiale te **kombineer**, kry jy ’n steen wat sterker is as modder alleen.","en":"By **combining** the two materials, you get a brick that is stronger than mud alone."}],"answer":{"af":"Die strooi hou die modder bymekaar sodat die steen nie so maklik kraak nie; die gekombineerde materiaal is sterker.","en":"The straw holds the mud together so that the brick does not crack so easily; the combined material is stronger."}},{"title":{"af":"Gewapende beton vir ’n brug","en":"Reinforced concrete for a bridge"},"problem":{"af":"’n Ingenieur moet ’n brug oor ’n rivier bou. Waarom gebruik sy gewapende beton en nie gewone beton nie?","en":"An engineer must build a bridge across a river. Why does she use reinforced concrete and not ordinary concrete?"},"steps":[{"af":"Wanneer motors oor die brug ry, **buig** die brug effens in die middel.","en":"When cars drive over the bridge, the bridge **bends** slightly in the middle."},{"af":"Gewone beton is sterk as jy daarop druk, maar dit **kraak maklik as dit buig**.","en":"Ordinary concrete is strong when you press on it, but it **cracks easily when it bends**."},{"af":"Die **staalstawe** binne-in kan buig sonder om te breek. Saam met die beton maak hulle die brug sterk genoeg.","en":"The **steel bars** inside can bend without breaking. Together with the concrete they make the bridge strong enough."}],"answer":{"af":"Gewapende beton kombineer beton (sterk as dit gedruk word) met staal (breek nie as dit buig nie), so die brug kraak nie.","en":"Reinforced concrete combines concrete (strong when pressed) with steel (does not break when it bends), so the bridge does not crack."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Regverdige toets vir waterdigtheid","en":"A fair test for waterproofing"},"problem":{"af":"Nomsa wil uitvind watter bedekking karton waterdig maak. Sy neem drie ewe groot stukke karton: een sonder bedekking, een met kerswas en een met kleefplastiek. Sy drup 5 druppels water op elkeen en kyk ná 5 minute. Die water het in die onbedekte karton ingesyg, maar op die ander twee in druppels bly lê. Beskryf haar toets.","en":"Nomsa wants to find out which covering makes cardboard waterproof. She takes three equal pieces of cardboard: one with no covering, one with candle wax and one with cling wrap. She drips 5 drops of water on each and looks after 5 minutes. The water soaked into the uncovered cardboard, but stayed in drops on the other two. Describe her test."},"steps":[{"af":"**Wat sy verander:** die bedekking op die karton.","en":"**What she changes:** the covering on the cardboard."},{"af":"**Wat sy waarneem:** of die water insyg of in druppels bly lê.","en":"**What she observes:** whether the water soaks in or stays in drops."},{"af":"**Wat dieselfde bly:** die grootte en soort karton, 5 druppels water en 5 minute. Dit maak die toets **regverdig**.","en":"**What stays the same:** the size and kind of cardboard, 5 drops of water and 5 minutes. This makes the test **fair**."},{"af":"Die onbedekte karton is die **kontrole**: dit wys wat sonder ’n bedekking gebeur.","en":"The uncovered cardboard is the **control**: it shows what happens without a covering."}],"answer":{"af":"Gevolgtrekking: kerswas en kleefplastiek maak karton waterdig; onbedekte karton is nie waterdig nie.","en":"Conclusion: candle wax and cling wrap make cardboard waterproof; uncovered cardboard is not waterproof."}},{"title":{"af":"Evalueer ’n potloodhouer","en":"Evaluate a pencil holder"},"problem":{"af":"Ravi se papier-maché-potloodhouer hou 12 potlode en lyk netjies, maar dit val om as hy daaraan stamp, en die buitekant word pap as hy water daarop drup. Evalueer sy houer en stel verbeterings voor.","en":"Ravi’s papier-mâché pencil holder holds 12 pencils and looks neat, but it falls over when he bumps it, and the outside goes soft when he drips water on it. Evaluate his holder and suggest improvements."},"steps":[{"af":"Vergelyk met elke spesifikasie: minstens 10 potlode – **ja**; lyk netjies – **ja**; val nie om nie – **nee**; buitekant waterdig – **nee**.","en":"Compare with each specification: at least 10 pencils – **yes**; looks neat – **yes**; does not fall over – **no**; outside waterproof – **no**."},{"af":"Om dit stabiel te maak: plak ’n **wyer voet** van karton onder, of maak die onderkant swaarder.","en":"To make it stable: stick a **wider base** of cardboard underneath, or make the bottom heavier."},{"af":"Om dit waterdig te maak: **verf** die buitekant of vryf **kerswas** daaroor wanneer dit heeltemal droog is.","en":"To make it waterproof: **paint** the outside or rub **candle wax** over it when it is completely dry."}],"answer":{"af":"Die houer voldoen aan twee van die vier spesifikasies. Verbeterings: ’n wyer of swaarder voet, en verf of was aan die buitekant.","en":"The holder meets two of the four specifications. Improvements: a wider or heavier base, and paint or wax on the outside."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarvan word papier-maché gemaak?","en":"What is papier-mâché made of?"},"options":[{"af":"Papier en water alleen","en":"Paper and water only"},{"af":"Sement en sand","en":"Cement and sand"},{"af":"Papierstroke en gom of meelpasta","en":"Paper strips and glue or flour paste"},{"af":"Hout en plastiek","en":"Wood and plastic"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Papier-maché kombineer papier met gom of meelpasta. Die gom hou die lae papier bymekaar sodat dit tot ’n harde dop droog word. Papier en water alleen word net pap.","en":"Papier-mâché combines paper with glue or flour paste. The glue holds the layers of paper together so that it dries into a hard shell. Paper and water alone just go soggy."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom word staalstawe in die beton van ’n brug gesit?","en":"Why are steel bars put into the concrete of a bridge?"},"options":[{"af":"Om die beton ligter te maak","en":"To make the concrete lighter"},{"af":"Beton kraak maklik as dit buig, maar staal kan buig sonder om te breek","en":"Concrete cracks easily when it bends, but steel can bend without breaking"},{"af":"Om die beton vinniger droog te maak","en":"To make the concrete dry faster"},{"af":"Staal maak die beton waterdig","en":"Steel makes the concrete waterproof"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Gewapende beton kombineer die sterkte van beton (as dit gedruk word) met die sterkte van staal (as dit buig). Staal maak die beton swaarder, nie ligter nie.","en":"Reinforced concrete combines the strength of concrete (when it is pressed) with the strength of steel (when it bends). Steel makes the concrete heavier, not lighter."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Sement en beton is presies dieselfde ding.","en":"Cement and concrete are exactly the same thing."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Sement is ’n grys poeier en net een van die bestanddele. Beton is die harde mengsel van sement, sand, klip en water.","en":"False. Cement is a grey powder and only one of the ingredients. Concrete is the hard mixture of cement, sand, stone and water."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Om modderstene sterker te maak sodat hulle nie kraak nie, meng mense ___ by die modder.","en":"To make mud bricks stronger so that they do not crack, people mix ___ into the mud."},"answers":{"af":["strooi"],"en":["straw"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["water","sout","olie"],"en":["water","salt","oil"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die strooi hou die modder soos drade bymekaar. Meer water sal die modder net nat en swak maak.","en":"The straw holds the mud together like threads. More water will just make the mud wet and weak."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n geprosesseerde materiaal?","en":"Which one is a processed material?"},"options":[{"af":"Klei","en":"Clay"},{"af":"Sand","en":"Sand"},{"af":"Hout","en":"Wood"},{"af":"Papier","en":"Paper"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Papier word in ’n fabriek van hout gemaak, so dit is geprosesseer. Klei, sand en hout kom reguit uit die natuur – hulle is rou materiale.","en":"Paper is made from wood in a factory, so it is processed. Clay, sand and wood come straight from nature – they are raw materials."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke rou materiaal by die geprosesseerde materiaal wat daarvan gemaak word.","en":"Match each raw material to the processed material that is made from it."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Hout","en":"Wood"},"r":{"af":"Papier","en":"Paper"}},{"l":{"af":"Sand","en":"Sand"},"r":{"af":"Glas","en":"Glass"}},{"l":{"af":"Klei","en":"Clay"},"r":{"af":"Bakstene","en":"Bricks"}},{"l":{"af":"Katoen","en":"Cotton"},"r":{"af":"Lap","en":"Fabric"}},{"l":{"af":"Ystererts","en":"Iron ore"},"r":{"af":"Staal","en":"Steel"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hout word pulp en dan papier; sand word gesmelt tot glas; klei word in ’n oond tot bakstene gebak; katoen word gespin en tot lap geweef; ystererts word gesmelt om yster en staal te maak.","en":"Wood becomes pulp and then paper; sand is melted into glass; clay is baked into bricks in a kiln; cotton is spun and woven into fabric; iron ore is melted to make iron and steel."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat sal ’n kartondoos die beste waterdig maak?","en":"What will make a cardboard box waterproof best?"},"options":[{"af":"Vryf kerswas oor die hele buitekant","en":"Rub candle wax over the whole outside"},{"af":"Maak die karton eers nat","en":"Make the cardboard wet first"},{"af":"Sny klein gaatjies in die karton","en":"Cut small holes in the cardboard"},{"af":"Plak nog ’n laag droë papier daaroor","en":"Stick another layer of dry paper over it"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Was stoot water af, so die water bly in druppels lê en syg nie in nie. Nog ’n laag papier maak die doos sterker, maar papier suig steeds water op.","en":"Wax repels water, so the water stays in drops and does not soak in. Another layer of paper makes the box stronger, but paper still soaks up water."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As jy ’n paar lae karton op mekaar plak om dit sterker en stywer te maak, ___ jy die karton.","en":"When you glue a few layers of cardboard on top of each other to make it stronger and stiffer, you ___ the cardboard."},"answers":{"af":["lamineer"],"en":["laminate"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["galvaniseer","verf","weef"],"en":["galvanise","paint","weave"]}},"explain":{"af":"Lamineer beteken om lae op mekaar te plak. Laaghout word ook so gemaak. Galvaniseer is om yster met sink te bedek.","en":"Laminate means to glue layers on top of each other. Plywood is also made like this. Galvanise means to cover iron with zinc."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy materiale kombineer, kan die nuwe materiaal eienskappe hê wat die afsonderlike materiale nie gehad het nie.","en":"When you combine materials, the new material can have properties that the separate materials did not have."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Papier is pap en gom is taai, maar saam word papier-maché ’n harde, ligte dop. Dit is die rede waarom ons materiale kombineer.","en":"True. Paper is floppy and glue is sticky, but together papier-mâché becomes a hard, light shell. That is the reason why we combine materials."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato drup water op haar klaar potloodhouer om te kyk of dit waterdig is. In watter stap van die ontwerpproses is sy?","en":"Lerato drips water on her finished pencil holder to see whether it is waterproof. Which step of the design process is she in?"},"options":[{"af":"Ondersoek","en":"Investigate"},{"af":"Ontwerp","en":"Design"},{"af":"Evalueer","en":"Evaluate"},{"af":"Kommunikeer","en":"Communicate"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Wanneer jy jou klaar produk toets om te sien of dit aan die spesifikasies voldoen, evalueer jy. In die ondersoekstap toets jy materiale voordat jy begin ontwerp.","en":"When you test your finished product to see whether it meets the specifications, you are evaluating. In the investigate step you test materials before you start designing."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe word glas gemaak?","en":"How is glass made?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit word net so uit die grond gegrawe","en":"It is dug out of the ground just as it is"},{"af":"Sand en ’n paar ander stowwe word verhit totdat dit smelt","en":"Sand and a few other substances are heated until they melt"},{"af":"Houtpulp word platgedruk en gedroog","en":"Wood pulp is pressed flat and dried"},{"af":"Klei word in ’n oond gebak","en":"Clay is baked in a kiln"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Glas is ’n geprosesseerde materiaal: sand word saam met ander stowwe baie warm verhit totdat dit smelt, en dan gevorm. Houtpulp word papier en gebakte klei word bakstene.","en":"Glass is a processed material: sand is heated with other substances until it melts, and then shaped. Wood pulp becomes paper and baked clay becomes bricks."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Beton word gemaak van sement, sand, klip en ___.","en":"Concrete is made of cement, sand, stone and ___."},"answers":{"af":["water"],"en":["water"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["strooi","papier","gom"],"en":["straw","paper","glue"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die water meng met die sement sodat die mengsel hard word en die sand en klip vashou. Strooi word in modderstene gebruik, nie in beton nie.","en":"The water mixes with the cement so that the mixture hardens and holds the sand and stone together. Straw is used in mud bricks, not in concrete."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ravi se potloodhouer val om as hy 10 potlode insit. Wat is die beste verbetering?","en":"Ravi’s pencil holder falls over when he puts 10 pencils in. What is the best improvement?"},"options":[{"af":"Maak die voet wyer en swaarder","en":"Make the base wider and heavier"},{"af":"Maak die houer hoër en smaller","en":"Make the holder taller and narrower"},{"af":"Gebruik minder lae papier","en":"Use fewer layers of paper"},{"af":"Verf dit in ’n helderder kleur","en":"Paint it a brighter colour"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Wye, swaar voet maak ’n struktuur stabiel sodat dit nie maklik omval nie. ’n Hoër, smaller houer sal nog makliker omval, en verf help net teen water.","en":"A wide, heavy base makes a structure stable so that it does not fall over easily. A taller, narrower holder will fall over even more easily, and paint only helps against water."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Nomsa toets drie ewe groot stukke karton: een met kerswas, een met kleefplastiek en een sonder bedekking. Wat moet sy dieselfde hou?","en":"Nomsa tests three equal pieces of cardboard: one with candle wax, one with cling wrap and one with no covering. What must she keep the same?"},"options":[{"af":"Die bedekking op elke stuk karton","en":"The covering on each piece of cardboard"},{"af":"Of die water insyg of nie","en":"Whether the water soaks in or not"},{"af":"Die naam van elke bedekking","en":"The name of each covering"},{"af":"Die grootte van die karton en die hoeveelheid water","en":"The size of the cardboard and the amount of water"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die bedekking is wat sy verander, en of die water insyg, is wat sy waarneem. Om die toets regverdig te maak, moet die karton en die hoeveelheid water dieselfde bly.","en":"The covering is what she changes, and whether the water soaks in is what she observes. To make the test fair, the cardboard and the amount of water must stay the same."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Energie en verandering","en":"Energy and change"},"topics":[{"id":"nwt5-t3-brandstof","title":{"af":"Gestoorde energie in brandstof","en":"Stored energy in fuels"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe brandstof energie stoor en as hitte en lig vrystel, die vuurdriehoek gebruik om te sê hoe ’n vuur geblus word, en weet hoe om tuis veilig met vuur te wees.","en":"You will be able to explain how fuels store energy and release it as heat and light, use the fire triangle to say how a fire is put out, and know how to be safe with fire at home."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is brandstof?\n\n**Brandstof** is ’n stof wat **energie stoor** en wat ons kan **verbrand** om daardie energie vry te stel. Voorbeelde is **hout, steenkool, paraffien, gas, petrol, diesel** en **kerswas**. Wanneer brandstof brand, word die gestoorde energie vrygestel as **hitte** en **lig**.\n\nDie energie in brandstof het eintlik van die **son** gekom. Plante gebruik sonlig om kos te maak en te groei. As jy hout verbrand, kry jy die son se energie terug wat die boom jare lank gestoor het.\n\n## Fossielbrandstof\n\n**Steenkool, olie** en **aardgas** heet **fossielbrandstof**, want hulle het gevorm uit plante en diere wat **miljoene jare gelede** geleef het.\n\n- **Steenkool** het gevorm uit plante in moerasse. Die plante is onder lae modder en sand begrawe en oor miljoene jare saamgepers tot ’n swart rots wat kan brand.\n- **Ru-olie** en **aardgas** het gevorm uit baie klein plantjies en diertjies in die see wat op die seebodem begrawe is. **Petrol, diesel** en **paraffien** word van ru-olie gemaak.\n\nFossielbrandstof is **nie-hernubaar**: dit neem miljoene jare om te vorm, so wat ons opgebruik, is vir altyd weg. Hout is **hernubaar** as ons nuwe bome plant.\n\n## Waarvoor gebruik ons brandstof?\n\n| Brandstof | Gebruike |\n|---|---|\n| Hout | Kook, braai en verhitting in ’n kaggel |\n| Steenkool | Kragstasies wat elektrisiteit opwek, fabrieke en verhitting |\n| Paraffien | Stofies, lampe en verwarmers |\n| Gas | Gasstowe, gasbraaiers en verwarmers |\n| Petrol en diesel | Motors, vragmotors, busse, treine en kragopwekkers |\n| Kerswas | Kerse wat lig gee |\n\n## Die vuurdriehoek\n\n’n Vuur het **drie dinge** nodig: **brandstof**, **suurstof** (uit die lug) en **hitte**. Ons noem dit die **vuurdriehoek**. Haal een kant van die driehoek weg, en die vuur gaan dood:\n\n- **Brandstof weg:** draai die gas af.\n- **Suurstof weg:** gooi sand op die vuur, of sit ’n deksel op ’n pan wat brand.\n- **Hitte weg:** gooi water op ’n houtvuur om dit af te koel.\n\nAs jy ’n glasfles oor ’n brandende kers sit, gaan die vlam ná ’n rukkie dood, want die suurstof in die fles raak op.\n\n> **Onthou:** Gooi **nooit water** op brandende olie of paraffien nie – die brandende olie spat dan rond en die vuur word groter. Gooi ook nooit water op ’n elektriese toestel wat brand nie.\n\n## Vuurveiligheid tuis\n\n- **Paraffienstofies:** sit dit op ’n plat, stewige oppervlak, ver van gordyne. Moet dit nooit volmaak terwyl dit brand nie. Hou paraffien in ’n gemerkte houer – **nooit in ’n koeldrankbottel** nie, want ’n klein kind kan dit drink.\n- **Kerse:** gebruik ’n stewige kershouer, hou dit weg van gordyne en beddegoed, en blaas dit dood voordat jy gaan slaap.\n- **Gasbottels:** hou dit regop, draai die kraan toe ná gebruik, en toets vir lekke met seepwater (borrels wys ’n lek) – nooit met ’n vlam nie.\n- Hou **vuurhoutjies** en aanstekers weg van klein kinders.\n\n## As daar ’n brand is\n\n1. **Skree** om almal te waarsku en **gaan dadelik uit**.\n2. As daar rook is, **kruip laag** op die vloer, waar die lug skoner is.\n3. Gaan **nooit terug** in ’n brandende huis in nie.\n4. Bel die nooddienste: **10177**, of **112** van ’n selfoon.\n5. Brand jou klere? **Stop, val en rol.**\n6. Koel ’n brandwond onder koel lopende water vir omtrent **20 minute**. Moenie botter of tandepasta daarop smeer nie.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Brandstof *maak* nie energie nie. Die energie was al in die brandstof **gestoor**; die vuur stel dit net vry as hitte en lig.","en":"## What is a fuel?\n\nA **fuel** is a substance that **stores energy** and that we can **burn** to release that energy. Examples are **wood, coal, paraffin, gas, petrol, diesel** and **candle wax**. When a fuel burns, the stored energy is released as **heat** and **light**.\n\nThe energy in fuels actually came from the **Sun**. Plants use sunlight to make food and to grow. When you burn wood, you get back the Sun’s energy that the tree stored for many years.\n\n## Fossil fuels\n\n**Coal, oil** and **natural gas** are called **fossil fuels**, because they formed from plants and animals that lived **millions of years ago**.\n\n- **Coal** formed from plants in swamps. The plants were buried under layers of mud and sand and were pressed together over millions of years into a black rock that can burn.\n- **Crude oil** and **natural gas** formed from very tiny plants and animals in the sea that were buried on the sea floor. **Petrol, diesel** and **paraffin** are made from crude oil.\n\nFossil fuels are **non-renewable**: they take millions of years to form, so what we use up is gone forever. Wood is **renewable** if we plant new trees.\n\n## What do we use fuels for?\n\n| Fuel | Uses |\n|---|---|\n| Wood | Cooking, braaiing and heating in a fireplace |\n| Coal | Power stations that generate electricity, factories and heating |\n| Paraffin | Stoves, lamps and heaters |\n| Gas | Gas stoves, gas braais and heaters |\n| Petrol and diesel | Cars, trucks, buses, trains and generators |\n| Candle wax | Candles that give light |\n\n## The fire triangle\n\nA fire needs **three things**: **fuel**, **oxygen** (from the air) and **heat**. We call this the **fire triangle**. Take away one side of the triangle and the fire goes out:\n\n- **Take away fuel:** turn off the gas.\n- **Take away oxygen:** throw sand on the fire, or put a lid on a pan that is burning.\n- **Take away heat:** throw water on a wood fire to cool it down.\n\nIf you put a glass jar over a burning candle, the flame goes out after a while, because the oxygen in the jar runs out.\n\n> **Remember:** **Never** throw **water** on burning oil or paraffin – the burning oil then splashes around and the fire gets bigger. Also never throw water on an electrical appliance that is burning.\n\n## Fire safety at home\n\n- **Paraffin stoves:** put them on a flat, steady surface, far from curtains. Never fill one while it is burning. Keep paraffin in a labelled container – **never in a cooldrink bottle**, because a small child could drink it.\n- **Candles:** use a steady candle holder, keep them away from curtains and bedding, and blow them out before you go to sleep.\n- **Gas bottles:** keep them upright, close the tap after use, and test for leaks with soapy water (bubbles show a leak) – never with a flame.\n- Keep **matches** and lighters away from small children.\n\n## If there is a fire\n\n1. **Shout** to warn everyone and **get out at once**.\n2. If there is smoke, **crawl low** on the floor, where the air is cleaner.\n3. **Never go back** into a burning house.\n4. Phone the emergency services: **10177**, or **112** from a cellphone.\n5. Are your clothes burning? **Stop, drop and roll.**\n6. Cool a burn under cool running water for about **20 minutes**. Do not put butter or toothpaste on it.\n\n> **Common mistake:** A fuel does not *make* energy. The energy was already **stored** in the fuel; the fire only releases it as heat and light."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Brandstof","en":"Fuel"},"def":{"af":"’n Stof wat energie stoor en wat ons kan verbrand om hitte en lig te kry.","en":"A substance that stores energy and that we can burn to get heat and light."}},{"term":{"af":"Gestoorde energie","en":"Stored energy"},"def":{"af":"Energie wat in ’n stof bewaar word totdat dit gebruik word, soos die energie in hout of steenkool.","en":"Energy that is kept in a substance until it is used, like the energy in wood or coal."}},{"term":{"af":"Verbranding","en":"Burning (combustion)"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n brandstof met suurstof brand en sy gestoorde energie as hitte en lig vrystel.","en":"When a fuel burns with oxygen and releases its stored energy as heat and light."}},{"term":{"af":"Vuurdriehoek","en":"Fire triangle"},"def":{"af":"Die drie dinge wat ’n vuur nodig het: brandstof, suurstof en hitte.","en":"The three things a fire needs: fuel, oxygen and heat."}},{"term":{"af":"Suurstof","en":"Oxygen"},"def":{"af":"’n Gas in die lug wat ’n vuur nodig het om te kan brand.","en":"A gas in the air that a fire needs to be able to burn."}},{"term":{"af":"Fossielbrandstof","en":"Fossil fuel"},"def":{"af":"Brandstof soos steenkool, olie en aardgas wat gevorm het uit plante en diere van miljoene jare gelede.","en":"A fuel such as coal, oil and natural gas that formed from plants and animals of millions of years ago."}},{"term":{"af":"Nie-hernubaar","en":"Non-renewable"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat nie weer aangevul kan word nie, omdat dit miljoene jare neem om te vorm.","en":"Something that cannot be replaced, because it takes millions of years to form."}},{"term":{"af":"Ru-olie","en":"Crude oil"},"def":{"af":"Die dik, donker olie uit die grond waarvan petrol, diesel en paraffien gemaak word.","en":"The thick, dark oil from under the ground from which petrol, diesel and paraffin are made."}},{"term":{"af":"Nooddienste","en":"Emergency services"},"def":{"af":"Die mense wat in ’n noodgeval help, soos die brandweer en die ambulans; bel 10177, of 112 van ’n selfoon.","en":"The people who help in an emergency, such as the fire brigade and the ambulance; phone 10177, or 112 from a cellphone."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Die kers onder die fles","en":"The candle under the jar"},"problem":{"af":"Ravi sit ’n glasfles oor ’n brandende kers. Ná ’n rukkie gaan die vlam dood, al is daar nog baie kerswas oor. Gebruik die vuurdriehoek om te verduidelik waarom.","en":"Ravi puts a glass jar over a burning candle. After a while the flame goes out, even though there is still a lot of candle wax left. Use the fire triangle to explain why."},"steps":[{"af":"Noem die drie dinge wat ’n vuur nodig het: **brandstof**, **suurstof** en **hitte**.","en":"Name the three things a fire needs: **fuel**, **oxygen** and **heat**."},{"af":"Kyk wat nog daar is: daar is nog **kerswas** (brandstof) en die vlam was warm (hitte).","en":"Check what is still there: there is still **candle wax** (fuel) and the flame was hot (heat)."},{"af":"Die fles keer dat nuwe lug by die vlam kom. Die vlam gebruik die **suurstof** in die fles op.","en":"The jar stops new air from reaching the flame. The flame uses up the **oxygen** in the jar."},{"af":"Sonder suurstof is een kant van die vuurdriehoek weg, en die vuur kan nie aanhou brand nie.","en":"Without oxygen one side of the fire triangle is gone, and the fire cannot keep burning."}],"answer":{"af":"Die vlam het doodgegaan omdat die suurstof in die fles opgeraak het – een kant van die vuurdriehoek is weggeneem.","en":"The flame went out because the oxygen in the jar ran out – one side of the fire triangle was taken away."}},{"title":{"af":"Hoe steenkool gevorm het","en":"How coal formed"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik in ’n paar stappe hoe steenkool gevorm het. Waarom noem ons dit ’n fossielbrandstof, en waarom is dit nie-hernubaar?","en":"Explain in a few steps how coal formed. Why do we call it a fossil fuel, and why is it non-renewable?"},"steps":[{"af":"Miljoene jare gelede het baie plante in moerasse gegroei. Hulle het sonlig se energie gebruik om te groei.","en":"Millions of years ago many plants grew in swamps. They used the energy of sunlight to grow."},{"af":"Toe die plante doodgegaan het, is hulle onder lae modder en sand begrawe.","en":"When the plants died, they were buried under layers of mud and sand."},{"af":"Oor miljoene jare het die gewig van die lae bo-op die plante saamgepers tot ’n swart rots wat kan brand: **steenkool**.","en":"Over millions of years the weight of the layers on top pressed the plants together into a black rock that can burn: **coal**."},{"af":"Dit is ’n **fossielbrandstof**, want dit kom van plante van lank gelede. Dit is **nie-hernubaar**, want dit neem miljoene jare om nuwe steenkool te vorm.","en":"It is a **fossil fuel**, because it comes from plants of long ago. It is **non-renewable**, because it takes millions of years for new coal to form."}],"answer":{"af":"Steenkool is gevorm uit plante van miljoene jare gelede wat begrawe en saamgepers is. Ons kan dit nie vinnig weer maak nie, dus is dit nie-hernubaar.","en":"Coal formed from plants of millions of years ago that were buried and pressed together. We cannot make it again quickly, so it is non-renewable."}},{"title":{"af":"Gevare in die huis raaksien","en":"Spotting dangers in the home"},"problem":{"af":"By Anika se huis staan ’n paraffienstofie langs die gordyn. ’n Koeldrankbottel vol paraffien staan op die vloer, en ’n kers brand op die rak bo die bed terwyl almal slaap. Noem die drie gevare en sê hoe om elkeen veilig te maak.","en":"At Anika’s home a paraffin stove stands next to the curtain. A cooldrink bottle full of paraffin stands on the floor, and a candle burns on the shelf above the bed while everyone sleeps. Name the three dangers and say how to make each one safe."},"steps":[{"af":"**Stofie langs die gordyn:** die gordyn kan vlam vat. Skuif die stofie na ’n plat, stewige plek ver van gordyne.","en":"**Stove next to the curtain:** the curtain can catch fire. Move the stove to a flat, steady place far from curtains."},{"af":"**Paraffien in ’n koeldrankbottel:** ’n klein kind kan dink dit is koeldrank en dit drink. Gooi dit oor in ’n gemerkte houer en bêre dit hoog en weg.","en":"**Paraffin in a cooldrink bottle:** a small child may think it is cooldrink and drink it. Pour it into a labelled container and store it high up and away."},{"af":"**Kers wat brand terwyl almal slaap:** dit kan omval of die beddegoed aan die brand steek. Blaas kerse dood voordat julle gaan slaap.","en":"**Candle burning while everyone sleeps:** it can fall over or set the bedding alight. Blow candles out before you go to sleep."}],"answer":{"af":"Stofie weg van die gordyn, paraffien in ’n gemerkte houer buite kinders se bereik, en kers dood voor slaaptyd.","en":"Stove away from the curtain, paraffin in a labelled container out of children’s reach, and the candle blown out before bedtime."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Pan olie vat vlam","en":"A pan of oil catches fire"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter se ma bak skyfies. Die olie in die pan vat vlam. Wat moet sy doen, en waarom mag sy nie water daarop gooi nie?","en":"Pieter’s mother is frying chips. The oil in the pan catches fire. What should she do, and why may she not throw water on it?"},"steps":[{"af":"Skakel die stoof af, as dit veilig is. Dan kry die vuur nie nog hitte nie.","en":"Switch off the stove, if it is safe. Then the fire gets no more heat."},{"af":"Sit ’n deksel of ’n branddeken oor die pan. Dit keer dat **suurstof** by die vuur kom.","en":"Put a lid or a fire blanket over the pan. This stops **oxygen** from reaching the fire."},{"af":"Moenie die pan rondskuif nie, en gooi **nooit water** daarop nie: die water laat die brandende olie rondspat en die vuur word groter.","en":"Do not move the pan around, and **never** throw **water** on it: the water makes the burning oil splash and the fire gets bigger."},{"af":"As die vuur nie doodgaan nie, gaan almal uit en bel **10177**, of **112** van ’n selfoon.","en":"If the fire does not go out, everyone gets out and phones **10177**, or **112** from a cellphone."}],"answer":{"af":"Stoof af en sit ’n deksel op om die suurstof af te sny; nooit water nie, want brandende olie spat en die vuur versprei.","en":"Stove off and put a lid on to cut off the oxygen; never water, because burning oil splashes and the fire spreads."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter drie dinge het ’n vuur nodig?","en":"Which three things does a fire need?"},"options":[{"af":"Brandstof, water en hitte","en":"Fuel, water and heat"},{"af":"Suurstof, sand en hitte","en":"Oxygen, sand and heat"},{"af":"Brandstof, suurstof en hitte","en":"Fuel, oxygen and heat"},{"af":"Brandstof, koolstofdioksied en lig","en":"Fuel, carbon dioxide and light"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die vuurdriehoek is brandstof, suurstof en hitte. Water en sand word juis gebruik om ’n vuur dood te maak, en lig is iets wat die vuur gee, nie iets wat dit nodig het nie.","en":"The fire triangle is fuel, oxygen and heat. Water and sand are actually used to put a fire out, and light is something the fire gives off, not something it needs."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Steenkool is ’n fossielbrandstof wat gevorm het uit plante wat miljoene jare gelede geleef het.","en":"Coal is a fossil fuel that formed from plants that lived millions of years ago."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Plante in moerasse is begrawe en oor miljoene jare saamgepers tot steenkool. Daarom is dit ’n fossielbrandstof.","en":"True. Plants in swamps were buried and pressed together over millions of years into coal. That is why it is a fossil fuel."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar het die energie wat in hout gestoor is, oorspronklik vandaan gekom?","en":"Where did the energy stored in wood originally come from?"},"options":[{"af":"Van die son","en":"From the Sun"},{"af":"Uit die grond","en":"From the soil"},{"af":"Uit die reënwater","en":"From the rainwater"},{"af":"Van die wind","en":"From the wind"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die boom het sonlig se energie gebruik om kos te maak en te groei. Die grond en reën gee water en minerale, maar nie die energie nie.","en":"The tree used the energy of sunlight to make food and grow. The soil and rain give water and minerals, but not the energy."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Vuur het brandstof, hitte en ___ nodig om te brand.","en":"A fire needs fuel, heat and ___ to burn."},"answers":{"af":["suurstof","lug"],"en":["oxygen","air"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["water","koolstofdioksied","sand"],"en":["water","carbon dioxide","sand"]}},"explain":{"af":"Suurstof uit die lug is die derde kant van die vuurdriehoek. Water en sand blus ’n vuur.","en":"Oxygen from the air is the third side of the fire triangle. Water and sand put a fire out."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Nomsa sit ’n deksel op ’n pan wat brand, en die vuur gaan dood. Waarom?","en":"Nomsa puts a lid on a pan that is burning, and the fire goes out. Why?"},"options":[{"af":"Die deksel koel die olie baie vinnig af","en":"The lid cools the oil down very quickly"},{"af":"Die deksel haal die brandstof uit die pan","en":"The lid takes the fuel out of the pan"},{"af":"Die deksel keer dat die vuur lig kan gee","en":"The lid stops the fire from giving light"},{"af":"Die deksel keer dat suurstof by die vuur kom","en":"The lid stops oxygen from reaching the fire"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die deksel sny die lug, en dus die suurstof, af. Die olie (brandstof) is nog in die pan en dit is nog warm – net die suurstof is weg.","en":"The lid cuts off the air, and so the oxygen. The oil (fuel) is still in the pan and it is still hot – only the oxygen is gone."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van hierdie is NIE ’n fossielbrandstof nie?","en":"Which one of these is NOT a fossil fuel?"},"options":[{"af":"Steenkool","en":"Coal"},{"af":"Hout","en":"Wood"},{"af":"Aardgas","en":"Natural gas"},{"af":"Ru-olie","en":"Crude oil"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Hout kom van bome wat nou groei. Dit is hernubaar as ons nuwe bome plant. Steenkool, aardgas en ru-olie het oor miljoene jare gevorm.","en":"Wood comes from trees growing now. It is renewable if we plant new trees. Coal, natural gas and crude oil formed over millions of years."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke brandstof by ’n gebruik.","en":"Match each fuel to a use."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Paraffien","en":"Paraffin"},"r":{"af":"Stofies en lampe","en":"Stoves and lamps"}},{"l":{"af":"Petrol","en":"Petrol"},"r":{"af":"Motors","en":"Cars"}},{"l":{"af":"Steenkool","en":"Coal"},"r":{"af":"Kragstasies wat elektrisiteit opwek","en":"Power stations that generate electricity"}},{"l":{"af":"Kerswas","en":"Candle wax"},"r":{"af":"Kerse wat lig gee","en":"Candles that give light"}}],"explain":{"af":"Paraffien brand in stofies en lampe, petrol dryf motors aan, steenkool word in kragstasies verbrand en kerswas brand in kerse.","en":"Paraffin burns in stoves and lamps, petrol powers cars, coal is burnt in power stations and candle wax burns in candles."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar is die veiligste plek om paraffien tuis te hou?","en":"Where is the safest place to keep paraffin at home?"},"options":[{"af":"In ’n leë koeldrankbottel in die yskas","en":"In an empty cooldrink bottle in the fridge"},{"af":"In ’n gemerkte houer buite kinders se bereik","en":"In a labelled container out of children’s reach"},{"af":"In ’n oop emmer langs die stofie","en":"In an open bucket next to the stove"},{"af":"In ’n plastiekbottel onder die bed","en":"In a plastic bottle under the bed"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Gemerkte houer wys wat binne is, en hoog en weg kan klein kinders dit nie kry nie. In ’n koeldrankbottel kan ’n kind dit per ongeluk drink, en langs die stofie kan dit vlam vat.","en":"A labelled container shows what is inside, and high up and away small children cannot reach it. In a cooldrink bottle a child might drink it by accident, and next to the stove it can catch fire."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Van ’n selfoon kan jy die nooddienste bel by die nommer ___.","en":"From a cellphone you can phone the emergency services on the number ___."},"answers":{"af":["112","10177"],"en":["112","10177"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["911","999","116"],"en":["911","999","116"]}},"explain":{"af":"In Suid-Afrika bel jy 112 van ’n selfoon, of 10177 vir die brandweer en ambulans. 911 en 999 is nommers van ander lande, en 116 is Childline.","en":"In South Africa you phone 112 from a cellphone, or 10177 for the fire brigade and ambulance. 911 and 999 are numbers of other countries, and 116 is Childline."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Om ’n pan met brandende olie te blus, moet jy ’n emmer water daarop gooi.","en":"To put out a pan of burning oil, you should throw a bucket of water on it."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Water laat brandende olie rondspat en die vuur word groter. Skakel die stoof af en sit ’n deksel op om die suurstof af te sny.","en":"False. Water makes burning oil splash and the fire gets bigger. Switch off the stove and put a lid on to cut off the oxygen."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom sê ons fossielbrandstof is nie-hernubaar?","en":"Why do we say fossil fuels are non-renewable?"},"options":[{"af":"Want dit brand baie vinnig op","en":"Because it burns up very quickly"},{"af":"Want dit is baie duur om te koop","en":"Because it is very expensive to buy"},{"af":"Want dit gee baie rook af","en":"Because it gives off a lot of smoke"},{"af":"Want dit neem miljoene jare om te vorm","en":"Because it takes millions of years to form"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Nie-hernubaar beteken dit kan nie weer aangevul word nie. Fossielbrandstof neem miljoene jare om te vorm, so wat ons opgebruik, is weg.","en":"Non-renewable means it cannot be replaced. Fossil fuels take millions of years to form, so what we use up is gone."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Daar is ’n brand in julle huis en die gang is vol rook. Wat doen jy?","en":"There is a fire in your house and the passage is full of smoke. What do you do?"},"options":[{"af":"Kruip laag op die vloer na buite","en":"Crawl low on the floor to get outside"},{"af":"Gaan terug kamer toe vir jou selfoon","en":"Go back to your room for your cellphone"},{"af":"Kruip onder jou bed weg tot dit oor is","en":"Hide under your bed until it is over"},{"af":"Hardloop regop deur die rook na buite","en":"Run upright through the smoke to get out"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Rook styg op, so die lug naby die vloer is skoner. Moet nooit wegkruip of teruggaan vir goed nie – kom so gou moontlik veilig uit.","en":"Smoke rises, so the air near the floor is cleaner. Never hide or go back for things – get out safely as quickly as possible."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer brandstof brand, word die gestoorde energie vrygestel as hitte en ___.","en":"When a fuel burns, the stored energy is released as heat and ___."},"answers":{"af":["lig"],"en":["light"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["water","suurstof","elektrisiteit"],"en":["water","oxygen","electricity"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Vuur gee hitte (ons kan daarmee kook en warm word) en lig (ons kan sien). Suurstof is iets wat die vuur gebruik, nie iets wat dit vrystel nie.","en":"A fire gives heat (we can cook and get warm) and light (we can see). Oxygen is something the fire uses, not something it gives off."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato toets vir ’n gaslek by die gasbottel. Hoe moet sy dit doen?","en":"Lerato tests for a gas leak at the gas bottle. How should she do it?"},"options":[{"af":"Hou ’n brandende vuurhoutjie naby die kraan","en":"Hold a burning match near the tap"},{"af":"Draai die kraan heeltemal oop en luister","en":"Open the tap all the way and listen"},{"af":"Smeer seepwater oor die kraan en kyk vir borrels","en":"Brush soapy water on the tap and look for bubbles"},{"af":"Lê die gasbottel plat op sy kant neer","en":"Lay the gas bottle flat on its side"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Seepwater maak borrels waar gas uitlek, en dit is veilig. ’n Vlam naby ’n gaslek kan ’n ontploffing of brand veroorsaak, en ’n gasbottel moet regop staan.","en":"Soapy water makes bubbles where gas leaks out, and it is safe. A flame near a gas leak can cause an explosion or fire, and a gas bottle must stand upright."}}]},{"id":"nwt5-t3-energie-elektrisiteit","title":{"af":"Energie en elektrisiteit","en":"Energy and electricity"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe selle en batterye energie stoor, ’n eenvoudige stroombaan beskryf, sê waar hoofstroom-elektrisiteit vandaan kom en hoe om veilig met elektrisiteit te wees.","en":"You will be able to explain how cells and batteries store energy, describe a simple circuit, say where mains electricity comes from and how to be safe with electricity."},"summary":{"af":"## Selle en batterye\n\n’n **Sel** (wat mense dikwels ’n “battery” noem) stoor **chemiese energie**. Wanneer jy die sel in ’n stroombaan koppel, verander die chemiese energie in **elektriese energie**. Die toestel verander dit dan in ander energie: **lig** in ’n flits, **klank** in ’n radio of **beweging** in ’n speelgoedkarretjie.\n\nElke sel het twee **terminale**:\n\n- die **positiewe (+) terminaal** – die kant met die knoppie\n- die **negatiewe (−) terminaal** – die plat kant\n\n’n **Battery** is eintlik **twee of meer selle** wat aan mekaar gekoppel is: die + van een sel raak aan die − van die volgende. ’n Flits met twee selle het dus ’n battery.\n\nWanneer die chemikalieë in ’n sel opgebruik is, is die sel **pap**. Herlaaibare selle kan weer gelaai word. Gooi nooit ou selle in ’n vuur nie.\n\n## ’n Eenvoudige stroombaan\n\n’n **Stroombaan** is ’n volledige pad waarlangs elektrisiteit kan vloei.\n\n| Deel | Werk |\n|---|---|\n| Sel | Gee die energie wat die elektrisiteit laat vloei |\n| Geleidingsdrade | Vorm die pad van die sel na die gloeilamp en terug |\n| Gloeilamp | Verander elektriese energie in lig (en ook hitte) |\n| Skakelaar | Maak die pad oop of toe |\n\nDie gloeilamp brand net as die stroombaan **geslote** (volledig) is: van die + terminaal, deur die drade en die gloeilamp, terug na die − terminaal. As daar ’n **gaping** is – ’n los draad of ’n skakelaar wat **af** is – is die stroombaan **oop** en brand die lamp nie.\n\n## Hoofstroom-elektrisiteit\n\nDie elektrisiteit in die kragproppe (muurproppe) by die huis heet **hoofstroom**. Dit word in **kragstasies** opgewek:\n\n- **Steenkoolkragstasies** – steenkool word verbrand om water te kook; die stoom draai ’n **turbine** wat ’n **generator** laat draai, en die generator wek elektrisiteit op. Die meeste van Suid-Afrika se elektrisiteit kom van steenkool.\n- **Windplase** – die wind draai groot windturbines.\n- **Sonkragplase** – sonpanele verander sonlig in elektrisiteit.\n- **Hidro-elektriese kragstasies** – vloeiende water uit ’n dam draai turbines.\n\nDie elektrisiteit word met **kragdrade** op hoë **kragmaste** oor lang afstande vervoer na **substasies**, en dan met kleiner kragdrade na ons huise.\n\n> **Onthou:** ’n Sel is swak (omtrent 1,5 V) en veilig om mee te eksperimenteer. Hoofstroom is omtrent 230 V – sterk genoeg om jou **dood te maak**. Eksperimenteer **nooit** met hoofstroom nie.\n\n## Veilig met elektrisiteit\n\n- **Nat hande:** water gelei elektrisiteit. Raak nooit ’n skakelaar of toestel met nat hande aan nie, en gebruik nooit ’n haardroër naby die bad nie.\n- **Oorlaaide kragproppe:** moenie te veel proppe en multiproppe in een kragprop druk nie. Die drade word warm en kan ’n **brand** veroorsaak.\n- **Beskadigde koorde:** as die plastiek om ’n koord stukkend is en die draad uitsteek, kan jy ’n skok kry. Moenie dit gebruik nie – sê vir ’n volwassene.\n- Trek ’n prop uit deur die **prop** vas te hou, nie die koord nie. Steek nooit iets in ’n kragprop nie.\n- **Onwettige verbindings:** drade wat onwettig aan kragdrade gekoppel word, is lewensgevaarlik. Mense word geskok en huise brand af.\n- **Kragdrade en substasies:** klim nooit in ’n kragmas nie, vlieg nooit ’n vlieër naby kragdrade nie en gaan nooit in ’n substasie in nie.\n- As iemand ’n skok kry, **moenie aan die persoon raak nie** – jy kan ook geskok word. Skakel eers die krag by die hoofskakelaar af en roep hulp.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** ’n Kragdraad wat op die grond lê, is nie noodwendig “dood” nie. Behandel **elke** gevalle kragdraad asof daar krag in is: bly ver weg en vra ’n volwassene om die munisipaliteit of Eskom te bel.","en":"## Cells and batteries\n\nA **cell** (which people often call a “battery”) stores **chemical energy**. When you connect the cell in a circuit, the chemical energy changes into **electrical energy**. The device then changes it into other energy: **light** in a torch, **sound** in a radio or **movement** in a toy car.\n\nEvery cell has two **terminals**:\n\n- the **positive (+) terminal** – the end with the bump\n- the **negative (−) terminal** – the flat end\n\nA **battery** is really **two or more cells** joined together: the + of one cell touches the − of the next. So a torch with two cells has a battery.\n\nWhen the chemicals in a cell are used up, the cell is **flat**. Rechargeable cells can be charged again. Never throw old cells into a fire.\n\n## A simple circuit\n\nA **circuit** is a complete path along which electricity can flow.\n\n| Part | Job |\n|---|---|\n| Cell | Gives the energy that makes the electricity flow |\n| Connecting wires | Form the path from the cell to the bulb and back |\n| Bulb | Changes electrical energy into light (and also heat) |\n| Switch | Opens or closes the path |\n\nThe bulb only lights up if the circuit is **closed** (complete): from the + terminal, through the wires and the bulb, back to the − terminal. If there is a **gap** – a loose wire or a switch that is **off** – the circuit is **open** and the bulb does not light up.\n\n## Mains electricity\n\nThe electricity in the plug points (wall sockets) at home is called **mains electricity**. It is generated in **power stations**:\n\n- **Coal power stations** – coal is burnt to boil water; the steam turns a **turbine** that turns a **generator**, and the generator produces electricity. Most of South Africa’s electricity comes from coal.\n- **Wind farms** – the wind turns large wind turbines.\n- **Solar farms** – solar panels change sunlight into electricity.\n- **Hydroelectric power stations** – flowing water from a dam turns turbines.\n\nThe electricity is carried over long distances by **power lines** on tall **pylons** to **substations**, and then by smaller power lines to our homes.\n\n> **Remember:** A cell is weak (about 1.5 V) and safe to experiment with. Mains electricity is about 230 V – strong enough to **kill** you. **Never** experiment with mains electricity.\n\n## Safe with electricity\n\n- **Wet hands:** water conducts electricity. Never touch a switch or appliance with wet hands, and never use a hair dryer near the bath.\n- **Overloaded plug points:** do not push too many plugs and multi-plugs into one plug point. The wires get hot and can cause a **fire**.\n- **Damaged cords:** if the plastic around a cord is broken and the wire shows, you can get a shock. Do not use it – tell an adult.\n- Pull out a plug by holding the **plug**, not the cord. Never push anything into a plug point.\n- **Illegal connections:** wires that are illegally connected to power lines are deadly. People get shocked and houses burn down.\n- **Power lines and substations:** never climb a pylon, never fly a kite near power lines and never go into a substation.\n- If someone gets a shock, **do not touch the person** – you can get shocked too. First switch off the power at the main switch and call for help.\n\n> **Common mistake:** A power line lying on the ground is not necessarily “dead”. Treat **every** fallen power line as if it is live: stay far away and ask an adult to phone the municipality or Eskom."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Sel","en":"Cell"},"def":{"af":"’n Klein houer wat chemiese energie stoor en dit as elektriese energie aan ’n stroombaan gee.","en":"A small container that stores chemical energy and gives it to a circuit as electrical energy."}},{"term":{"af":"Battery","en":"Battery"},"def":{"af":"Twee of meer selle wat aan mekaar gekoppel is, die + van een teen die − van die volgende.","en":"Two or more cells joined together, the + of one against the − of the next."}},{"term":{"af":"Terminaal","en":"Terminal"},"def":{"af":"Een van die twee punte van ’n sel waaraan jy drade koppel: positief (+) of negatief (−).","en":"One of the two ends of a cell to which you connect wires: positive (+) or negative (−)."}},{"term":{"af":"Chemiese energie","en":"Chemical energy"},"def":{"af":"Energie wat in stowwe gestoor is, soos in die chemikalieë in ’n sel of in brandstof.","en":"Energy that is stored in substances, like in the chemicals in a cell or in fuel."}},{"term":{"af":"Stroombaan","en":"Circuit"},"def":{"af":"’n Volledige pad, sonder gapings, waarlangs elektrisiteit van die sel af en weer terug kan vloei.","en":"A complete path, without gaps, along which electricity can flow from the cell and back again."}},{"term":{"af":"Skakelaar","en":"Switch"},"def":{"af":"’n Deel van ’n stroombaan wat die pad oopmaak (af) of toemaak (aan).","en":"A part of a circuit that opens the path (off) or closes it (on)."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoofstroom","en":"Mains electricity"},"def":{"af":"Die sterk elektrisiteit van ’n kragstasie wat deur kragdrade na die kragproppe in ons huise kom.","en":"The strong electricity from a power station that comes through power lines to the plug points in our homes."}},{"term":{"af":"Kragstasie","en":"Power station"},"def":{"af":"’n Plek waar elektrisiteit opgewek word, byvoorbeeld met steenkool, wind, sonlig of water.","en":"A place where electricity is generated, for example with coal, wind, sunlight or water."}},{"term":{"af":"Substasie","en":"Substation"},"def":{"af":"’n Omheinde plek met groot elektriese toerusting waar die elektrisiteit van die kragdrade verander word voordat dit na huise gaan.","en":"A fenced place with large electrical equipment where the electricity from the power lines is changed before it goes to homes."}},{"term":{"af":"Onwettige verbinding","en":"Illegal connection"},"def":{"af":"’n Draad wat sonder toestemming aan ’n kragdraad gekoppel is; dit is baie gevaarlik.","en":"A wire connected to a power line without permission; it is very dangerous."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Waarom brand die gloeilamp nie?","en":"Why does the bulb not light up?"},"problem":{"af":"Zanele bou ’n stroombaan met ’n sel, drade, ’n skakelaar en ’n gloeilamp. Die skakelaar is aan, maar die gloeilamp brand nie. Sy sien die draad wat aan die − terminaal moet wees, hang los. Verduidelik wat fout is en hoe sy dit regmaak.","en":"Zanele builds a circuit with a cell, wires, a switch and a bulb. The switch is on, but the bulb does not light up. She sees that the wire that should be on the − terminal is hanging loose. Explain what is wrong and how she fixes it."},"steps":[{"af":"Elektrisiteit kan net vloei as die stroombaan **geslote** is: van die + terminaal, deur die gloeilamp, terug na die − terminaal.","en":"Electricity can only flow if the circuit is **closed**: from the + terminal, through the bulb, back to the − terminal."},{"af":"Die los draad maak ’n **gaping**, so die stroombaan is **oop**. Die elektrisiteit kan nie terug na die sel toe nie.","en":"The loose wire makes a **gap**, so the circuit is **open**. The electricity cannot get back to the cell."},{"af":"Sy moet die draad stewig teen die − terminaal vasmaak sodat die pad weer volledig is.","en":"She must fix the wire firmly against the − terminal so that the path is complete again."}],"answer":{"af":"Die stroombaan is oop weens die los draad. As sy die draad aan die − terminaal vasmaak, is die stroombaan geslote en brand die lamp.","en":"The circuit is open because of the loose wire. When she fixes the wire to the − terminal, the circuit is closed and the bulb lights up."}},{"title":{"af":"Die selle in ’n flits","en":"The cells in a torch"},"problem":{"af":"Liam se flits het twee selle nodig. Hy druk albei selle in met hul plat kante teen mekaar, en die flits werk nie. Hoe moet die selle lê, en is dit nou ’n sel of ’n battery?","en":"Liam’s torch needs two cells. He pushes both cells in with their flat ends against each other, and the torch does not work. How should the cells lie, and is it now a cell or a battery?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die plat kant is die **negatiewe (−)** terminaal en die kant met die knoppie is die **positiewe (+)** terminaal.","en":"The flat end is the **negative (−)** terminal and the end with the bump is the **positive (+)** terminal."},{"af":"Selle moet so lê dat die **+ van een sel teen die − van die volgende** sel druk. Twee − terminale teen mekaar werk nie.","en":"Cells must lie so that the **+ of one cell presses against the − of the next** cell. Two − terminals against each other do not work."},{"af":"Twee of meer selle wat so gekoppel is, vorm ’n **battery**.","en":"Two or more cells connected like this form a **battery**."}],"answer":{"af":"Draai een sel om sodat die + van een sel teen die − van die ander druk. Twee selle saam vorm ’n battery.","en":"Turn one cell around so that the + of one cell presses against the − of the other. Two cells together form a battery."}},{"title":{"af":"Van steenkool tot lig","en":"From coal to light"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die energieketting neer wat wys hoe die energie in steenkool by ’n kragstasie uiteindelik lig word in ’n lamp in Aisha se huis.","en":"Write down the energy chain that shows how the energy in coal at a power station finally becomes light in a lamp in Aisha’s home."},"steps":[{"af":"Steenkool stoor **chemiese energie**. In die kragstasie word dit verbrand en gee dit **hitte**.","en":"Coal stores **chemical energy**. In the power station it is burnt and gives off **heat**."},{"af":"Die hitte kook water. Die stoom draai die turbine en generator (**beweging**).","en":"The heat boils water. The steam turns the turbine and generator (**movement**)."},{"af":"Die generator wek **elektriese energie** op, wat met kragdrade, deur ’n substasie, na Aisha se huis vloei.","en":"The generator produces **electrical energy**, which flows through power lines, through a substation, to Aisha’s home."},{"af":"Die lamp verander die elektriese energie in **lig** (en ook hitte – ’n gloeilamp word warm).","en":"The lamp changes the electrical energy into **light** (and also heat – a bulb gets warm)."}],"answer":{"af":"Chemiese energie (steenkool) → hitte → beweging (turbine) → elektriese energie → lig in die lamp","en":"Chemical energy (coal) → heat → movement (turbine) → electrical energy → light in the lamp"}},{"title":{"af":"Gevare in die huis","en":"Dangers in the home"},"problem":{"af":"In Ravi se huis sien jy: drie multiproppe is in mekaar in een kragprop gedruk; sy suster gebruik ’n haardroër langs die vol bad; die ketel se koord is stukkend en die draad steek uit; Ravi trek proppe uit deur aan die koord te ruk. Noem die gevaar by elkeen en wat hulle moet doen.","en":"In Ravi’s home you see: three multi-plugs pushed into each other in one plug point; his sister uses a hair dryer next to the full bath; the kettle’s cord is broken and the wire shows; Ravi pulls out plugs by yanking the cord. Name the danger in each and what they should do."},"steps":[{"af":"**Multiproppe in mekaar:** die kragprop is oorlaai, die drade word warm en dit kan brand. Gebruik minder toestelle tegelyk.","en":"**Multi-plugs in each other:** the plug point is overloaded, the wires get hot and it can catch fire. Use fewer appliances at a time."},{"af":"**Haardroër by die bad:** water gelei elektrisiteit; as dit in die water val, kan sy ’n doodlike skok kry. Gebruik dit ver van water en met droë hande.","en":"**Hair dryer by the bath:** water conducts electricity; if it falls into the water she can get a deadly shock. Use it far from water and with dry hands."},{"af":"**Stukkende koord:** wie aan die kaal draad raak, kry ’n skok. Moenie die ketel gebruik nie; laat ’n volwassene dit regmaak of vervang.","en":"**Broken cord:** anyone who touches the bare wire gets a shock. Do not use the kettle; let an adult repair or replace it."},{"af":"**Aan die koord ruk:** die drade binne-in breek los. Hou die prop self vas wanneer jy dit uittrek.","en":"**Yanking the cord:** the wires inside break loose. Hold the plug itself when you pull it out."}],"answer":{"af":"Moenie kragproppe oorlaai nie, hou elektrisiteit weg van water, gebruik nooit beskadigde koorde nie en trek proppe aan die prop uit.","en":"Do not overload plug points, keep electricity away from water, never use damaged cords and pull plugs out by the plug."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter kant van ’n sel is die positiewe (+) terminaal?","en":"Which end of a cell is the positive (+) terminal?"},"options":[{"af":"Die plat kant","en":"The flat end"},{"af":"Die kant met die knoppie","en":"The end with the bump"},{"af":"Die middel van die sel","en":"The middle of the cell"},{"af":"Die kant met die etiket","en":"The end with the label"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die kant met die knoppie is positief (+) en die plat kant is negatief (−). Die etiket is om die middel van die sel.","en":"The end with the bump is positive (+) and the flat end is negative (−). The label is around the middle of the cell."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Battery bestaan uit twee of meer ___ wat aan mekaar gekoppel is.","en":"A battery is made of two or more ___ joined together."},"answers":{"af":["selle"],"en":["cells"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["gloeilampe","skakelaars","kragproppe"],"en":["bulbs","switches","plug points"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Battery is twee of meer selle, die + van een teen die − van die volgende. Een enkele sel is eintlik nie ’n battery nie, al noem mense dit so.","en":"A battery is two or more cells, the + of one against the − of the next. A single cell is really not a battery, even though people call it that."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo se stroombaan het ’n sel, drade, ’n skakelaar en ’n gloeilamp. Die gloeilamp brand nie. Wat kan die rede wees?","en":"Thabo’s circuit has a cell, wires, a switch and a bulb. The bulb does not light up. What could be the reason?"},"options":[{"af":"Die skakelaar is af, so die stroombaan is oop","en":"The switch is off, so the circuit is open"},{"af":"Die drade is van koper gemaak","en":"The wires are made of copper"},{"af":"Die stroombaan is heeltemal geslote","en":"The circuit is completely closed"},{"af":"Die gloeilamp is in ’n lamphouer vasgedraai","en":"The bulb is screwed into a holder"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"As die skakelaar af is, is daar ’n gaping en kan elektrisiteit nie vloei nie. Koperdrade en ’n lamphouer vir die gloeilamp is normaal, en ’n geslote stroombaan sou die lamp laat brand.","en":"If the switch is off, there is a gap and electricity cannot flow. Copper wires and a bulb holder are normal, and a closed circuit would make the bulb light up."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Water gelei elektrisiteit, daarom is dit gevaarlik om ’n skakelaar met nat hande aan te raak.","en":"Water conducts electricity, so it is dangerous to touch a switch with wet hands."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Water laat elektrisiteit maklik deur, so met nat hande kan die elektrisiteit deur jou liggaam vloei en jou skok.","en":"True. Water lets electricity through easily, so with wet hands the electricity can flow through your body and shock you."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter energieverandering vind in ’n sel plaas wanneer ’n flits aangeskakel word?","en":"Which energy change takes place in a cell when a torch is switched on?"},"options":[{"af":"Lig verander in chemiese energie","en":"Light changes into chemical energy"},{"af":"Elektriese energie verander in chemiese energie","en":"Electrical energy changes into chemical energy"},{"af":"Chemiese energie verander in elektriese energie","en":"Chemical energy changes into electrical energy"},{"af":"Hitte verander in elektriese energie","en":"Heat changes into electrical energy"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die sel stoor chemiese energie en gee dit as elektriese energie af. Die gloeilamp verander dit dan in lig. Die omgekeerde gebeur net wanneer jy ’n herlaaibare sel laai.","en":"The cell stores chemical energy and gives it out as electrical energy. The bulb then changes it into light. The opposite only happens when you charge a rechargeable cell."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar kom die meeste van Suid-Afrika se hoofstroom vandaan?","en":"Where does most of South Africa’s mains electricity come from?"},"options":[{"af":"Van windplase langs die kus","en":"From wind farms along the coast"},{"af":"Van sonpanele op huise se dakke","en":"From solar panels on the roofs of houses"},{"af":"Van hidro-elektriese damme","en":"From hydroelectric dams"},{"af":"Van steenkoolkragstasies","en":"From coal power stations"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Suid-Afrika wek die meeste van sy elektrisiteit op deur steenkool te verbrand. Wind, son en water word ook gebruik, maar hulle lewer minder.","en":"South Africa generates most of its electricity by burning coal. Wind, sun and water are also used, but they supply less."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke deel van ’n stroombaan by sy werk.","en":"Match each part of a circuit to its job."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Sel","en":"Cell"},"r":{"af":"Gee die energie","en":"Gives the energy"}},{"l":{"af":"Geleidingsdrade","en":"Connecting wires"},"r":{"af":"Vorm die pad vir die elektrisiteit","en":"Form the path for the electricity"}},{"l":{"af":"Gloeilamp","en":"Bulb"},"r":{"af":"Verander elektriese energie in lig","en":"Changes electrical energy into light"}},{"l":{"af":"Skakelaar","en":"Switch"},"r":{"af":"Maak die stroombaan oop of toe","en":"Opens or closes the circuit"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die sel gee energie, die drade vorm die pad, die gloeilamp gee lig en die skakelaar maak die pad oop of toe.","en":"The cell gives energy, the wires form the path, the bulb gives light and the switch opens or closes the path."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is dit gevaarlik om baie proppe en multiproppe in een kragprop te druk?","en":"Why is it dangerous to push many plugs and multi-plugs into one plug point?"},"options":[{"af":"Die elektrisiteit in die huis raak gou op","en":"The electricity in the house runs out quickly"},{"af":"Die drade word warm en kan ’n brand veroorsaak","en":"The wires get hot and can cause a fire"},{"af":"Die toestelle werk dan net half so vinnig","en":"The appliances then work only half as fast"},{"af":"Die kragprop word dan magneties en trek metaal","en":"The plug point then becomes magnetic and pulls metal"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Oorlaaide kragprop laat te veel elektrisiteit deur dieselfde drade vloei. Die drade word warm, en dit kan die plastiek laat smelt en ’n brand begin.","en":"An overloaded plug point makes too much electricity flow through the same wires. The wires get hot, which can melt the plastic and start a fire."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoofstroom-elektrisiteit word in ’n ___ opgewek en met kragdrade na ons huise gestuur.","en":"Mains electricity is generated in a ___ and sent to our homes through power lines."},"answers":{"af":["kragstasie"],"en":["power station"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["substasie","battery","kragprop"],"en":["substation","battery","plug point"]}},"explain":{"af":"Elektrisiteit word in ’n kragstasie opgewek. ’n Substasie is net ’n stop langs die pad, en ’n kragprop is waar ons die elektrisiteit in die huis gebruik.","en":"Electricity is generated in a power station. A substation is only a stop along the way, and a plug point is where we use the electricity at home."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho se bal val oor die heining van ’n substasie. Wat moet hy doen?","en":"Sipho’s ball falls over the fence of a substation. What should he do?"},"options":[{"af":"Versigtig oor die heining klim en dit gou gaan haal","en":"Climb carefully over the fence and fetch it quickly"},{"af":"Met ’n lang metaalpyp deur die heining na die bal stoot","en":"Push a long metal pipe through the fence to reach the ball"},{"af":"Die bal los en vir ’n volwassene vertel","en":"Leave the ball and tell an adult"},{"af":"Klippe gooi om die bal nader te stamp","en":"Throw stones to knock the ball closer"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"In ’n substasie is die elektrisiteit so sterk dat dit jou kan doodmaak, selfs as jy net naby kom. ’n Metaalpyp gelei elektrisiteit. Los die bal en vertel ’n volwassene.","en":"In a substation the electricity is so strong that it can kill you, even if you only come close. A metal pipe conducts electricity. Leave the ball and tell an adult."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Sel van 1,5 V is net so gevaarlik soos die hoofstroom in die huis.","en":"A 1.5 V cell is just as dangerous as the mains electricity in the house."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Sel is swak en veilig om mee te eksperimenteer. Hoofstroom is omtrent 230 V en kan jou doodmaak.","en":"False. A cell is weak and safe to experiment with. Mains electricity is about 230 V and can kill you."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Fatima se maat kry ’n skok van ’n stukkende ketel en hou nog daaraan vas. Wat moet Fatima eerste doen?","en":"Fatima’s friend gets a shock from a broken kettle and is still holding it. What should Fatima do first?"},"options":[{"af":"Haar maat met haar hande van die ketel af wegtrek","en":"Pull her friend away from the kettle with her hands"},{"af":"’n Beker water oor haar maat se hande gooi","en":"Pour a jug of water over her friend’s hands"},{"af":"Haar maat se arm vashou totdat die skok ophou","en":"Hold her friend’s arm until the shock stops"},{"af":"Die krag by die hoofskakelaar afskakel en hulp roep","en":"Switch off the power at the main switch and call for help"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"As Fatima aan haar maat raak, vloei die elektrisiteit ook deur haar. Water gelei elektrisiteit en maak dit erger. Skakel eers die krag af.","en":"If Fatima touches her friend, the electricity flows through her too. Water conducts electricity and makes it worse. First switch off the power."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die plat kant van ’n sel is die ___ terminaal.","en":"The flat end of a cell is the ___ terminal."},"answers":{"af":["negatiewe","−","-"],"en":["negative","−","-"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["positiewe","neutrale","boonste"],"en":["positive","neutral","top"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die plat kant is negatief (−). Die kant met die knoppie is positief (+).","en":"The flat end is negative (−). The end with the bump is positive (+)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter volgorde beweeg hoofstroom-elektrisiteit na jou huis?","en":"In which order does mains electricity travel to your home?"},"options":[{"af":"Kragstasie → kragdrade op kragmaste → substasie → huis","en":"Power station → power lines on pylons → substation → home"},{"af":"Kragstasie → huis → substasie → kragdrade op kragmaste","en":"Power station → home → substation → power lines on pylons"},{"af":"Substasie → kragstasie → kragdrade op kragmaste → huis","en":"Substation → power station → power lines on pylons → home"},{"af":"Huis → kragdrade op kragmaste → substasie → kragstasie","en":"Home → power lines on pylons → substation → power station"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die elektrisiteit word in die kragstasie opgewek, met kragdrade oor lang afstande vervoer, by ’n substasie verander en dan na die huise gestuur.","en":"The electricity is generated in the power station, carried over long distances by power lines, changed at a substation and then sent to homes."}}]},{"id":"nwt5-t3-energie-beweging","title":{"af":"Energie en beweging","en":"Energy and movement"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe rekkies en vere energie stoor wanneer hulle gerek, gedraai of saamgedruk word, hoe daardie energie beweging word, en ’n energieketting kan skryf.","en":"You will be able to explain how rubber bands and springs store energy when they are stretched, twisted or squashed, how that energy becomes movement, and write an energy chain."},"summary":{"af":"## Energie laat dinge beweeg\n\nNiks begin vanself beweeg nie: om iets te laat beweeg, moet daar **energie** ingesit word. Jy kry jou energie uit jou **kos**. Wanneer jy ’n rekkie rek of ’n veer saamdruk, gebruik jy jou spiere – en ’n deel van daardie energie word in die rekkie of veer **gestoor**.\n\n## Rekkies en vere stoor energie\n\n**Elastiese** voorwerpe, soos rekkies en **vere**, kan van vorm verander en dan weer terugspring na hul gewone vorm. Jy stoor energie in hulle deur hulle te:\n\n- **rek** – trek ’n rekkie lank\n- **draai** – draai ’n rekkie om en om, of draai die sleutel van ’n opwenspeelding\n- **saamdruk** – druk ’n veer korter\n\nSolank jy die rekkie of veer so hou, bly die energie **gestoor**. Wetenskaplikes noem dit **potensiële energie** – energie wat wag om gebruik te word. Sodra jy los, spring die rekkie of veer terug en word die gestoorde energie **bewegingsenergie**.\n\n## Voorbeelde rondom jou\n\n| Voorwerp | Hoe energie gestoor word | Wat gebeur dan |\n|---|---|---|\n| Opwenspeelding | Jy draai die sleutel en draai ’n veer styf op | Die veer draai oop en laat die wieletjies draai |\n| Trampolien | Jy land op die mat en die vere rondom word gerek | Die vere trek terug en gooi jou op |\n| Balpen | Die klein veertjie word saamgedruk as jy die knoppie druk | Die veer stoot die punt terug in |\n| Matras | Jou gewig druk die vere saam | Die vere stoot terug en die matras voel veerkragtig |\n| Rekkie-bootjie | Jy draai die rekkie om en om | Die rekkie draai die spaan en die bootjie vaar |\n\n## Hoe meer jy rek, hoe meer energie\n\nHoe **verder** jy ’n rekkie rek of hoe **meer** jy dit draai, hoe **meer energie** stoor dit – en hoe verder of vinniger beweeg die voorwerp. Pieter het dit met ’n rekkie-karretjie getoets:\n\n| Aantal draaie | Afstand wat die karretjie ry |\n|---|---|\n| 10 | 1,2 m |\n| 20 | 2,5 m |\n| 30 | 3,6 m |\n\nOm die toets **regverdig** te maak, het hy net die aantal draaie verander. Hy het dieselfde karretjie, dieselfde rekkie en dieselfde vloer gebruik. Maar pasop: as jy ’n rekkie te ver rek of te veel draai, **breek** dit.\n\n> **Onthou:** Energie word nie uit niks gemaak nie. ’n Rekkie of veer kan nooit meer energie teruggee as wat jy daarin gesit het nie.\n\n## Energie-oordrag in ’n ketting\n\nEnergie gaan van een ding na ’n ander oor. Ons noem dit **energie-oordrag**, en ons wys dit met ’n **energieketting**:\n\n**son → plant (kos) → jou spiere → gedraaide rekkie → bewegende karretjie**\n\n1. Die **son** gee energie aan plante, wat dit as kos stoor.\n2. Jy eet die kos, en jou **spiere** kry energie.\n3. Jou spiere draai die **rekkie**, en die energie word gestoor.\n4. Die rekkie draai los en die karretjie **beweeg**.\n\nElke pyl wys waarheen die energie gaan.\n\n## Veilig met rekkies en vere\n\nRek ’n rekkie nooit naby iemand se gesig nie – as dit breek of losskiet, kan dit ’n oog beseer. Mik ’n kettie nooit na mense of diere nie.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Baie leerders dink die energie kom uit die rekkie self. Die rekkie **stoor** net die energie wat **jy** ingesit het toe jy dit gerek of gedraai het.","en":"## Energy makes things move\n\nNothing starts moving by itself: to make something move, **energy** must be put in. You get your energy from your **food**. When you stretch a rubber band or squash a spring, you use your muscles – and part of that energy is **stored** in the rubber band or spring.\n\n## Rubber bands and springs store energy\n\n**Elastic** objects, such as rubber bands and **springs**, can change shape and then spring back to their normal shape. You store energy in them by:\n\n- **stretching** – pulling a rubber band longer\n- **twisting** – twisting a rubber band round and round, or winding the key of a wind-up toy\n- **squashing** (compressing) – pushing a spring shorter\n\nAs long as you hold the rubber band or spring like that, the energy stays **stored**. Scientists call this **potential energy** – energy that is waiting to be used. As soon as you let go, the rubber band or spring springs back and the stored energy becomes **movement energy**.\n\n## Examples around you\n\n| Object | How energy is stored | What happens then |\n|---|---|---|\n| Wind-up toy | You turn the key and wind a spring up tightly | The spring unwinds and turns the little wheels |\n| Trampoline | You land on the mat and the springs around it are stretched | The springs pull back and throw you up |\n| Ballpoint pen | The tiny spring is squashed when you press the button | The spring pushes the tip back in |\n| Mattress | Your weight squashes the springs | The springs push back and the mattress feels bouncy |\n| Rubber-band boat | You twist the rubber band round and round | The rubber band turns the paddle and the boat moves |\n\n## The more you stretch, the more energy\n\nThe **further** you stretch a rubber band or the **more** you twist it, the **more energy** it stores – and the further or faster the object moves. Pieter tested this with a rubber-band car:\n\n| Number of twists | Distance the car travels |\n|---|---|\n| 10 | 1.2 m |\n| 20 | 2.5 m |\n| 30 | 3.6 m |\n\nTo make the test **fair**, he only changed the number of twists. He used the same car, the same rubber band and the same floor. But be careful: if you stretch a rubber band too far or twist it too much, it **breaks**.\n\n> **Remember:** Energy is not made out of nothing. A rubber band or spring can never give back more energy than you put into it.\n\n## Energy transfer in a chain\n\nEnergy passes from one thing to another. We call this **energy transfer**, and we show it with an **energy chain**:\n\n**Sun → plant (food) → your muscles → twisted rubber band → moving car**\n\n1. The **Sun** gives energy to plants, which store it as food.\n2. You eat the food, and your **muscles** get energy.\n3. Your muscles twist the **rubber band**, and the energy is stored.\n4. The rubber band unwinds and the car **moves**.\n\nEach arrow shows where the energy goes.\n\n## Safe with rubber bands and springs\n\nNever stretch a rubber band near someone’s face – if it breaks or shoots off, it can injure an eye. Never aim a catapult at people or animals.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Many learners think the energy comes from the rubber band itself. The rubber band only **stores** the energy that **you** put in when you stretched or twisted it."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Energie","en":"Energy"},"def":{"af":"Wat nodig is om iets te laat beweeg, te laat werk of te laat verander.","en":"What is needed to make something move, work or change."}},{"term":{"af":"Elasties","en":"Elastic"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n voorwerp kan rek of saamgedruk word en dan weer terugspring na sy gewone vorm.","en":"When an object can be stretched or squashed and then springs back to its normal shape."}},{"term":{"af":"Veer","en":"Spring"},"def":{"af":"’n Opgerolde stuk metaaldraad wat energie stoor wanneer dit gerek of saamgedruk word.","en":"A coiled piece of metal wire that stores energy when it is stretched or squashed."}},{"term":{"af":"Gestoorde (potensiële) energie","en":"Stored (potential) energy"},"def":{"af":"Energie wat in iets wag om gebruik te word, soos in ’n gerekte rekkie.","en":"Energy that waits in something to be used, like in a stretched rubber band."}},{"term":{"af":"Bewegingsenergie","en":"Movement energy"},"def":{"af":"Die energie wat ’n voorwerp het terwyl dit beweeg.","en":"The energy an object has while it is moving."}},{"term":{"af":"Saamdruk","en":"Squash (compress)"},"def":{"af":"Om iets korter of kleiner te druk, soos wanneer jy ’n veer tussen jou vingers druk.","en":"To push something shorter or smaller, like when you press a spring between your fingers."}},{"term":{"af":"Opwenspeelding","en":"Wind-up toy"},"def":{"af":"’n Speelding met ’n sleutel wat ’n veer opdraai; die veer laat die speelding beweeg wanneer dit oopdraai.","en":"A toy with a key that winds up a spring; the spring makes the toy move when it unwinds."}},{"term":{"af":"Energie-oordrag","en":"Energy transfer"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer energie van een voorwerp of plek na ’n ander oorgaan.","en":"When energy passes from one object or place to another."}},{"term":{"af":"Energieketting","en":"Energy chain"},"def":{"af":"’n Reeks stappe met pyle wat wys hoe energie van een ding na die volgende oorgaan.","en":"A series of steps with arrows that shows how energy passes from one thing to the next."}},{"term":{"af":"Regverdige toets","en":"Fair test"},"def":{"af":"’n Ondersoek waarin jy net een ding verander en alles anders dieselfde hou.","en":"An investigation in which you change only one thing and keep everything else the same."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lees die resultate van ’n rekkie-karretjie","en":"Reading the results of a rubber-band car"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter se resultate: 10 draaie – 1,2 m; 20 draaie – 2,5 m; 30 draaie – 3,6 m. Wat sê die resultate, en hoe ver sal die karretjie omtrent ry met 40 draaie?","en":"Pieter’s results: 10 twists – 1.2 m; 20 twists – 2.5 m; 30 twists – 3.6 m. What do the results tell us, and about how far will the car travel with 40 twists?"},"steps":[{"af":"Kyk na die patroon: hoe meer draaie, hoe verder ry die karretjie.","en":"Look at the pattern: the more twists, the further the car travels."},{"af":"Verduidelik waarom: meer draaie stoor **meer energie** in die rekkie, so daar is meer energie vir beweging.","en":"Explain why: more twists store **more energy** in the rubber band, so there is more energy for movement."},{"af":"Elke 10 ekstra draaie laat die karretjie omtrent 1,2 m verder ry. Dus 3,6 m + 1,2 m = omtrent 4,8 m.","en":"Every 10 extra twists make the car go about 1.2 m further. So 3.6 m + 1.2 m = about 4.8 m."},{"af":"Maar as die rekkie te styf gedraai word, kan dit breek – dan ry die karretjie glad nie.","en":"But if the rubber band is twisted too tightly, it can break – then the car does not move at all."}],"answer":{"af":"Meer draaie stoor meer energie, so die karretjie ry verder. Met 40 draaie ry dit omtrent 4,8 m (as die rekkie nie breek nie).","en":"More twists store more energy, so the car travels further. With 40 twists it travels about 4.8 m (if the rubber band does not break)."}},{"title":{"af":"Hoe werk ’n opwenspeelding?","en":"How does a wind-up toy work?"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato draai die sleutel van ’n opwenpaddatjie en sit dit neer. Die paddatjie spring oor die tafel. Verduidelik met ’n energieketting waar die energie vandaan kom.","en":"Lerato turns the key of a wind-up toy frog and puts it down. The frog hops across the table. Use an energy chain to explain where the energy comes from."},"steps":[{"af":"Lerato se **spiere** het energie uit haar **kos** gekry.","en":"Lerato’s **muscles** got energy from her **food**."},{"af":"Toe sy die sleutel draai, het sy ’n **veer** binne-in styf opgedraai. Die energie is in die veer **gestoor**.","en":"When she turned the key, she wound up a **spring** inside tightly. The energy was **stored** in the spring."},{"af":"Toe sy die paddatjie los, het die veer stadig oopgedraai en die gestoorde energie in **bewegingsenergie** verander.","en":"When she let go of the frog, the spring slowly unwound and changed the stored energy into **movement energy**."}],"answer":{"af":"kos → Lerato se spiere → opgedraaide veer (gestoorde energie) → springende paddatjie (bewegingsenergie)","en":"food → Lerato’s muscles → wound-up spring (stored energy) → hopping frog (movement energy)"}},{"title":{"af":"Die trampolien","en":"The trampoline"},"problem":{"af":"Nomsa spring op ’n trampolien. Wanneer sy harder op die mat neerkom, spring sy hoër. Verduidelik waarom.","en":"Nomsa jumps on a trampoline. When she lands harder on the mat, she bounces higher. Explain why."},"steps":[{"af":"Wanneer Nomsa op die mat land, trek die mat die **vere** rondom die rand en hulle word **gerek**.","en":"When Nomsa lands on the mat, the mat pulls on the **springs** around the edge and they are **stretched**."},{"af":"Gerekte vere **stoor energie**. As sy harder land, word die vere **verder gerek** en stoor hulle **meer energie**.","en":"Stretched springs **store energy**. If she lands harder, the springs are **stretched further** and store **more energy**."},{"af":"Die vere trek terug na hul gewone lengte en die gestoorde energie word **bewegingsenergie** wat Nomsa opgooi.","en":"The springs pull back to their normal length and the stored energy becomes **movement energy** that throws Nomsa up."}],"answer":{"af":"Harder land rek die vere verder, sodat hulle meer energie stoor en haar hoër opgooi.","en":"Landing harder stretches the springs further, so they store more energy and throw her higher."}},{"title":{"af":"Is dit ’n regverdige toets?","en":"Is it a fair test?"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho wil uitvind of meer draaie ’n rekkie-bootjie verder laat vaar. Bootjie A kry 10 draaie met ’n dun rekkie. Bootjie B kry 30 draaie met ’n dik rekkie. Bootjie B vaar die verste. Kan hy sê dat dit oor die draaie is?","en":"Sipho wants to find out whether more twists make a rubber-band boat go further. Boat A gets 10 twists with a thin rubber band. Boat B gets 30 twists with a thick rubber band. Boat B goes furthest. Can he say it is because of the twists?"},"steps":[{"af":"In ’n **regverdige toets** verander jy net **een** ding en hou jy alles anders dieselfde.","en":"In a **fair test** you change only **one** thing and keep everything else the same."},{"af":"Sipho het **twee** dinge verander: die aantal draaie **en** die soort rekkie.","en":"Sipho changed **two** things: the number of twists **and** the kind of rubber band."},{"af":"Hy weet dus nie of bootjie B verder gevaar het weens die draaie of weens die dik rekkie nie. Hy moet dieselfde rekkie (en dieselfde bootjie en water) gebruik en net die draaie verander.","en":"So he does not know whether boat B went further because of the twists or because of the thick rubber band. He must use the same rubber band (and the same boat and water) and change only the twists."}],"answer":{"af":"Nee, dit is nie regverdig nie, want hy het twee dinge verander. Net die aantal draaie mag verskil.","en":"No, it is not fair, because he changed two things. Only the number of twists may be different."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe stoor jy energie in die veertjie van ’n balpen?","en":"How do you store energy in the little spring of a ballpoint pen?"},"options":[{"af":"Deur die veer te verf","en":"By painting the spring"},{"af":"Deur die veer warm te maak","en":"By heating the spring"},{"af":"Deur die veer nat te maak","en":"By wetting the spring"},{"af":"Deur die veer saam te druk","en":"By squashing the spring"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Vere stoor energie wanneer hulle gerek of saamgedruk word. In ’n balpen word die veertjie saamgedruk wanneer jy die knoppie druk.","en":"Springs store energy when they are stretched or squashed. In a ballpoint pen the little spring is squashed when you press the button."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Hoe meer draaie jy aan ’n rekkie gee, hoe meer energie stoor dit.","en":"The more twists you give a rubber band, the more energy it stores."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Meer draaie stoor meer energie, en daarom ry ’n rekkie-karretjie verder met meer draaie – solank die rekkie nie breek nie.","en":"True. More twists store more energy, which is why a rubber-band car goes further with more twists – as long as the rubber band does not break."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar kry jy die energie om ’n rekkie te rek?","en":"Where do you get the energy to stretch a rubber band?"},"options":[{"af":"Uit die lug om jou","en":"From the air around you"},{"af":"Uit die kos wat jy eet","en":"From the food you eat"},{"af":"Uit die rekkie self","en":"From the rubber band itself"},{"af":"Uit die tafel waarop jy werk","en":"From the table you work on"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Jou spiere kry hul energie uit kos. Die rekkie maak nie self energie nie – dit stoor net die energie wat jy insit.","en":"Your muscles get their energy from food. The rubber band does not make energy itself – it only stores the energy you put in."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Energie wat in ’n gerekte rekkie wag om gebruik te word, heet ___ energie.","en":"Energy that waits in a stretched rubber band to be used is called ___ energy."},"answers":{"af":["gestoorde","potensiële","potensiele"],"en":["stored","potential"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["elektriese","chemiese","magnetiese"],"en":["electrical","chemical","magnetic"]}},"explain":{"af":"Energie in ’n gerekte rekkie of saamgedrukte veer is gestoorde of potensiële energie. Dit word bewegingsenergie wanneer jy los.","en":"Energy in a stretched rubber band or squashed spring is stored or potential energy. It becomes movement energy when you let go."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke voorwerp by die manier waarop dit energie stoor.","en":"Match each object to the way it stores energy."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Opwenspeelding","en":"Wind-up toy"},"r":{"af":"’n Veer word met ’n sleutel opgedraai","en":"A spring is wound up with a key"}},{"l":{"af":"Trampolien","en":"Trampoline"},"r":{"af":"Die vere rondom die mat word gerek","en":"The springs around the mat are stretched"}},{"l":{"af":"Balpen","en":"Ballpoint pen"},"r":{"af":"’n Klein veertjie word saamgedruk","en":"A tiny spring is squashed"}},{"l":{"af":"Rekkie-bootjie","en":"Rubber-band boat"},"r":{"af":"’n Rekkie word om en om gedraai","en":"A rubber band is twisted round and round"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke voorwerp stoor energie deur ’n veer of rekkie te draai, te rek of saam te druk. Wanneer dit gelos word, word die energie beweging.","en":"Each object stores energy by winding, stretching or squashing a spring or rubber band. When it is released, the energy becomes movement."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter se karretjie ry 1,2 m met 10 draaie, 2,5 m met 20 draaie en 3,6 m met 30 draaie. Hoe ver sal dit omtrent met 40 draaie ry?","en":"Pieter’s car travels 1.2 m with 10 twists, 2.5 m with 20 twists and 3.6 m with 30 twists. About how far will it travel with 40 twists?"},"options":[{"af":"Omtrent 1,2 m","en":"About 1.2 m"},{"af":"Omtrent 3,6 m","en":"About 3.6 m"},{"af":"Omtrent 4,8 m","en":"About 4.8 m"},{"af":"Omtrent 12 m","en":"About 12 m"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Elke 10 ekstra draaie gee omtrent 1,2 m meer. Dus 3,6 m + 1,2 m is omtrent 4,8 m. 12 m sou veels te ver wees vir net 10 draaie meer.","en":"Every 10 extra twists give about 1.2 m more. So 3.6 m + 1.2 m is about 4.8 m. 12 m would be far too much for only 10 more twists."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter energieketting is in die regte volgorde?","en":"Which energy chain is in the correct order?"},"options":[{"af":"rekkie → spiere → kos → son → beweging","en":"rubber band → muscles → food → Sun → movement"},{"af":"son → kos → spiere → rekkie → beweging","en":"Sun → food → muscles → rubber band → movement"},{"af":"kos → son → rekkie → spiere → beweging","en":"food → Sun → rubber band → muscles → movement"},{"af":"beweging → rekkie → spiere → kos → son","en":"movement → rubber band → muscles → food → Sun"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die energie begin by die son, gaan na plante (kos), dan na jou spiere, word in die rekkie gestoor en word laastens beweging.","en":"The energy starts at the Sun, goes to plants (food), then to your muscles, is stored in the rubber band and finally becomes movement."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer jy ’n gerekte rekkie los, verander die gestoorde energie in ___.","en":"When you let go of a stretched rubber band, the stored energy changes into ___."},"answers":{"af":["bewegingsenergie","beweging"],"en":["movement energy","movement","motion","kinetic energy"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["chemiese energie","elektriese energie","kos"],"en":["chemical energy","electrical energy","food"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die rekkie spring terug en laat iets beweeg, so die gestoorde energie word bewegingsenergie.","en":"The rubber band springs back and makes something move, so the stored energy becomes movement energy."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho wil toets of meer draaie ’n rekkie-karretjie verder laat ry. Wat moet elke keer dieselfde bly?","en":"Sipho wants to test whether more twists make a rubber-band car go further. What must stay the same every time?"},"options":[{"af":"Die aantal draaie aan die rekkie","en":"The number of twists in the rubber band"},{"af":"Die afstand wat die karretjie ry","en":"The distance the car travels"},{"af":"Die karretjie, die rekkie en die vloer","en":"The car, the rubber band and the floor"},{"af":"Die naam van die leerder wat meet","en":"The name of the learner who measures"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die aantal draaie is wat hy verander, en die afstand is wat hy meet. Alles anders – die karretjie, rekkie en vloer – moet dieselfde bly sodat die toets regverdig is.","en":"The number of twists is what he changes, and the distance is what he measures. Everything else – the car, rubber band and floor – must stay the same so that the test is fair."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Rekkie wat net op die tafel lê, sonder dat iemand dit gerek of gedraai het, kan ’n karretjie laat ry.","en":"A rubber band that just lies on the table, without anyone stretching or twisting it, can make a car move."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Rekkie het net gestoorde energie as iemand dit gerek of gedraai het. Dit maak nie self energie nie.","en":"False. A rubber band only has stored energy if someone has stretched or twisted it. It does not make energy by itself."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Nomsa spring hoër op die trampolien wanneer sy harder neerkom. Waarom?","en":"Nomsa bounces higher on the trampoline when she lands harder. Why?"},"options":[{"af":"Die vere word verder gerek en stoor meer energie","en":"The springs are stretched further and store more energy"},{"af":"Die mat word harder en swaarder as sy land","en":"The mat becomes harder and heavier when she lands"},{"af":"Die vere word korter en swakker as sy land","en":"The springs become shorter and weaker when she lands"},{"af":"Sy word ligter hoe hoër sy op die mat spring","en":"She becomes lighter the higher she bounces on the mat"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Hoe harder sy land, hoe verder word die vere gerek en hoe meer energie stoor hulle. Die vere gee die energie terug as beweging en gooi haar hoër op.","en":"The harder she lands, the further the springs are stretched and the more energy they store. The springs give the energy back as movement and throw her higher."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van hierdie gebruik NIE ’n veer of rekkie om energie vir beweging te stoor nie?","en":"Which one of these does NOT use a spring or rubber band to store energy for movement?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Opwenspeelding","en":"A wind-up toy"},{"af":"’n Trampolien","en":"A trampoline"},{"af":"’n Kettie","en":"A catapult"},{"af":"’n Paraffienlamp","en":"A paraffin lamp"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Paraffienlamp kry sy energie uit brandstof wat brand en lig en hitte gee. Die ander drie stoor energie in vere of rekkies.","en":"A paraffin lamp gets its energy from fuel that burns and gives light and heat. The other three store energy in springs or rubber bands."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Voorwerp wat terugspring na sy gewone vorm nadat jy dit gerek of saamgedruk het, is ___.","en":"An object that springs back to its normal shape after you have stretched or squashed it is ___."},"answers":{"af":["elasties"],"en":["elastic"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["breekbaar","smeebaar","magneties"],"en":["brittle","malleable","magnetic"]}},"explain":{"af":"Elastiese voorwerpe, soos rekkies en vere, spring terug na hul vorm. Breekbare goed breek, en smeebare metale bly in die nuwe vorm.","en":"Elastic objects, like rubber bands and springs, spring back to their shape. Brittle things break, and malleable metals stay in the new shape."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom moet jy nooit ’n rekkie naby iemand se gesig rek nie?","en":"Why should you never stretch a rubber band near someone’s face?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit kan breek of losskiet en ’n oog beseer","en":"It can break or shoot off and injure an eye"},{"af":"Dit maak die rekkie se energie gou op","en":"It quickly uses up the rubber band’s energy"},{"af":"Dit laat die rekkie sy kleur verloor","en":"It makes the rubber band lose its colour"},{"af":"Dit laat die rekkie vinniger verslyt","en":"It makes the rubber band wear out faster"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Gerekte rekkie het baie gestoorde energie. As dit breek of losskiet, word daardie energie skielik beweging en kan dit iemand se oog tref.","en":"A stretched rubber band has a lot of stored energy. If it breaks or shoots off, that energy suddenly becomes movement and can hit someone’s eye."}}]},{"id":"nwt5-t3-wiele-asse","title":{"af":"Stelsels vir beweging: wiele en asse (Tegnologie)","en":"Systems for moving things: wheels and axles (Technology)"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe ’n wiel en as werk, ’n vaste as van ’n vrye as onderskei, sê waarom wiele wrywing verminder, en die ontwerpproses volg om ’n modelvoertuig te ontwerp, te maak en te evalueer.","en":"You will be able to explain how a wheel and axle works, tell a fixed axle from a free axle, say why wheels reduce friction, and follow the design process to design, make and evaluate a model vehicle."},"summary":{"af":"## Die wiel en as\n\n’n **Wiel en as** is ’n **eenvoudige masjien** – ’n eenvoudige toestel wat werk makliker maak. Die **wiel** is ’n ronde skyf, en die **as** is die staaf wat deur die middel van die wiel gaan.\n\n## Vaste as en vrye as\n\n| | Vaste as | Vrye (los) as |\n|---|---|---|\n| Hoe dit werk | Die wiele is aan die as vas; wiele en as draai **saam** | Die as is aan die raam vas; die wiel draai **om die as** |\n| Voorbeelde | Treinwiele; ’n model met wiele wat op die as vasgeplak is | ’n Fiets se wiele; ’n trollie se wieletjies |\n\nBy ’n vaste as draai die as in ’n **laer** (in ’n model is dit ’n stukkie strooitjie). By ’n vrye as moet die gat in die wiel net effens groter as die as wees sodat die wiel maklik draai.\n\n## Wrywing\n\n**Wrywing** is ’n krag wat beweging teëwerk wanneer twee oppervlakke teen mekaar skuur. Probeer ’n swaar boks oor die grond sleep: die hele bodem skuur teen die grond, so daar is baie wrywing en dit is swaar werk.\n\n- ’n **Slee** gly oor die grond, en ’n groot oppervlak skuur teen die grond: **baie wrywing**.\n- ’n **Kruiwa** se wiel **rol**. Net ’n klein deeltjie van die wiel raak op ’n slag aan die grond: **min wrywing**. Daarom is dit makliker om stene met ’n kruiwa te stoot as om hulle te sleep.\n\nDaar is ook wrywing tussen die wiel en die as. **Olie** of **ghries** verminder dié wrywing. Wrywing is nie altyd sleg nie: dit help dat ’n fiets se bande op die pad vashou en dat die remme werk.\n\n## Wiele en asse rondom ons\n\n- **Fiets** – die wiele draai om hul asse.\n- **Trollie** – klein wieletjies maak dit maklik om swaar inkopies te stoot.\n- **Deurknop** – die knop is die “wiel” en die staaf binne-in is die “as”. Die groot knop draai die dun staaf met min krag, sodat die deur maklik oopgaan.\n\n> **Onthou:** Wiele maak dit makliker om dinge te beweeg, want **rol** veroorsaak baie minder wrywing as **sleep**.\n\n## Die ontwerpproses\n\nIngenieurs volg die **ontwerpproses** wanneer hulle iets nuuts maak:\n\n1. **Ondersoek** – Kyk na bestaande voertuie. Hoe is die wiele aan die raam vas?\n2. **Ontwerp** – Skryf ’n **ontwerpopdrag** en **spesifikasies**, teken ’n paar idees met byskrifte en kies die beste een.\n3. **Maak** – Bou die model veilig en netjies.\n4. **Evalueer** – Toets die model. Doen dit wat die spesifikasies vra? Wat kan jy verbeter?\n5. **Kommunikeer** – Verduidelik jou ontwerp met tekeninge en ’n kort verslag.\n\n## Ontwerptaak: ’n modelvoertuig\n\n**Ontwerpopdrag:** Ontwerp en maak ’n modelvoertuig wat ’n klein boksie sap teen ’n helling kan afrol en dan reguit oor die vloer kan ry.\n\n**Spesifikasies:** vier wiele, ry reguit, dra die boksie sap. **Beperkings:** net skoon herwinbare materiaal, nie langer as 25 cm nie, klaar binne twee lesse.\n\n- **Onderstel (raam):** stewige karton of ’n leë sapboks\n- **Asse:** sosatiestokkies (knip eers die skerp punte af)\n- **Laers:** stukkies strooitjie wat aan die onderstel vasgeplak word\n- **Wiele:** bottelproppies of kartonsirkels met die gat presies in die middel\n\nWerk veilig: sny weg van jou liggaam en gebruik die skêr versigtig.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die gat is nie in die middel van die wiel nie, of die asse is nie ewewydig nie. Dan wikkel die voertuig of draai dit eenkant toe.","en":"## The wheel and axle\n\nA **wheel and axle** is a **simple machine** – a simple device that makes work easier. The **wheel** is a round disc, and the **axle** is the rod that goes through the middle of the wheel.\n\n## Fixed axle and free axle\n\n| | Fixed axle | Free (loose) axle |\n|---|---|---|\n| How it works | The wheels are fixed to the axle; wheels and axle turn **together** | The axle is fixed to the frame; the wheel turns **around the axle** |\n| Examples | Train wheels; a model with wheels glued onto the axle | A bicycle’s wheels; a trolley’s little wheels |\n\nWith a fixed axle, the axle turns in a **bearing** (in a model this is a piece of drinking straw). With a free axle, the hole in the wheel must be just a little bigger than the axle so that the wheel turns easily.\n\n## Friction\n\n**Friction** is a force that works against movement when two surfaces rub against each other. Try dragging a heavy box over the ground: the whole bottom rubs against the ground, so there is a lot of friction and it is hard work.\n\n- A **sled** slides over the ground, and a large surface rubs against the ground: **a lot of friction**.\n- A **wheelbarrow’s** wheel **rolls**. Only a small part of the wheel touches the ground at a time: **little friction**. That is why it is easier to push bricks in a wheelbarrow than to drag them.\n\nThere is also friction between the wheel and the axle. **Oil** or **grease** reduces this friction. Friction is not always bad: it helps a bicycle’s tyres grip the road and makes the brakes work.\n\n## Wheels and axles around us\n\n- **Bicycle** – the wheels turn around their axles.\n- **Trolley** – small wheels make it easy to push heavy shopping.\n- **Door knob** – the knob is the “wheel” and the rod inside is the “axle”. The big knob turns the thin rod with little force, so the door opens easily.\n\n> **Remember:** Wheels make it easier to move things, because **rolling** causes much less friction than **dragging**.\n\n## The design process\n\nEngineers follow the **design process** when they make something new:\n\n1. **Investigate** – Look at existing vehicles. How are the wheels attached to the frame?\n2. **Design** – Write a **design brief** and **specifications**, draw a few labelled ideas and choose the best one.\n3. **Make** – Build the model safely and neatly.\n4. **Evaluate** – Test the model. Does it do what the specifications ask? What can you improve?\n5. **Communicate** – Explain your design with drawings and a short report.\n\n## Design task: a model vehicle\n\n**Design brief:** Design and make a model vehicle that can roll down a slope carrying a small box of juice and then travel straight across the floor.\n\n**Specifications:** four wheels, travels straight, carries the box of juice. **Constraints:** only clean recycled materials, no longer than 25 cm, finished within two lessons.\n\n- **Chassis (frame):** strong cardboard or an empty juice box\n- **Axles:** kebab skewers (cut off the sharp points first)\n- **Bearings:** pieces of drinking straw glued to the chassis\n- **Wheels:** bottle caps or cardboard circles with the hole exactly in the middle\n\nWork safely: cut away from your body and use the scissors carefully.\n\n> **Common mistake:** The hole is not in the middle of the wheel, or the axles are not parallel. Then the vehicle wobbles or turns to one side."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Wiel en as","en":"Wheel and axle"},"def":{"af":"’n Eenvoudige masjien met ’n ronde wiel en ’n staaf (as) deur sy middel.","en":"A simple machine with a round wheel and a rod (axle) through its middle."}},{"term":{"af":"Eenvoudige masjien","en":"Simple machine"},"def":{"af":"’n Eenvoudige toestel, soos ’n wiel en as of ’n hefboom, wat werk makliker maak.","en":"A simple device, such as a wheel and axle or a lever, that makes work easier."}},{"term":{"af":"Vaste as","en":"Fixed axle"},"def":{"af":"’n As waaraan die wiele vas is, sodat die wiele en die as saam draai.","en":"An axle to which the wheels are fixed, so that the wheels and the axle turn together."}},{"term":{"af":"Vrye (los) as","en":"Free (loose) axle"},"def":{"af":"’n As wat aan die raam vas is, terwyl die wiel om die as draai.","en":"An axle that is fixed to the frame, while the wheel turns around the axle."}},{"term":{"af":"Wrywing","en":"Friction"},"def":{"af":"’n Krag wat beweging teëwerk wanneer twee oppervlakke teen mekaar skuur.","en":"A force that works against movement when two surfaces rub against each other."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderstel","en":"Chassis"},"def":{"af":"Die raam van ’n voertuig waaraan die asse en wiele vasgemaak word.","en":"The frame of a vehicle to which the axles and wheels are attached."}},{"term":{"af":"Laer","en":"Bearing"},"def":{"af":"Die deel waarin ’n as draai; in ’n model kan ’n stukkie strooitjie die laer wees.","en":"The part in which an axle turns; in a model a piece of drinking straw can be the bearing."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontwerpproses","en":"Design process"},"def":{"af":"Die stappe om iets nuuts te maak: ondersoek, ontwerp, maak, evalueer en kommunikeer.","en":"The steps for making something new: investigate, design, make, evaluate and communicate."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontwerpopdrag","en":"Design brief"},"def":{"af":"’n Kort beskrywing van wat jy gaan ontwerp en maak, vir wie en waarom.","en":"A short description of what you are going to design and make, for whom and why."}},{"term":{"af":"Spesifikasies","en":"Specifications"},"def":{"af":"Die lys van dinge wat jou ontwerp moet kan doen of moet hê.","en":"The list of things your design must be able to do or must have."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Vaste of vrye as?","en":"Fixed or free axle?"},"problem":{"af":"Sê of elkeen ’n vaste as of ’n vrye as het: (a) Thabo se model, waar die bottelproppies op ’n sosatiestokkie vasgeplak is en die stokkie in ’n strooitjie draai; (b) ’n trollie se wieletjie wat om ’n pen draai wat aan die raam vas is.","en":"Say whether each has a fixed axle or a free axle: (a) Thabo’s model, where the bottle caps are glued onto a kebab skewer and the skewer turns in a straw; (b) a trolley’s little wheel that turns around a pin fixed to the frame."},"steps":[{"af":"Vra by elkeen: draai die as **saam** met die wiel, of staan die as stil terwyl die wiel **om** die as draai?","en":"Ask for each one: does the axle turn **together** with the wheel, or does the axle stay still while the wheel turns **around** it?"},{"af":"(a) Die proppies is vasgeplak, so die wiele en die stokkie draai saam. Die strooitjie is die laer. Dit is ’n **vaste as**.","en":"(a) The caps are glued on, so the wheels and the skewer turn together. The straw is the bearing. This is a **fixed axle**."},{"af":"(b) Die pen is aan die raam vas en beweeg nie; net die wiel draai daarom. Dit is ’n **vrye as**.","en":"(b) The pin is fixed to the frame and does not move; only the wheel turns around it. This is a **free axle**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Vaste as  (b) Vrye as","en":"(a) Fixed axle  (b) Free axle"}},{"title":{"af":"Sleep of rol?","en":"Drag or roll?"},"problem":{"af":"Johan moet 20 stene na die agterkant van die erf skuif. Hy kan dit op ’n plat sinkplaat sleep of in ’n kruiwa stoot. Wat is makliker, en waarom?","en":"Johan must move 20 bricks to the back of the yard. He can drag them on a flat metal sheet or push them in a wheelbarrow. Which is easier, and why?"},"steps":[{"af":"Op die sinkplaat skuur die **hele onderkant** teen die grond: dit is soos ’n slee, met **baie wrywing**.","en":"On the metal sheet the **whole bottom** rubs against the ground: it is like a sled, with **a lot of friction**."},{"af":"Die kruiwa se wiel **rol**. Net ’n klein deeltjie van die wiel raak op ’n slag aan die grond, so daar is **min wrywing**.","en":"The wheelbarrow’s wheel **rolls**. Only a small part of the wheel touches the ground at a time, so there is **little friction**."},{"af":"Minder wrywing beteken hy het minder krag nodig om die stene te beweeg.","en":"Less friction means he needs less force to move the bricks."}],"answer":{"af":"Die kruiwa is makliker, want ’n wiel wat rol, veroorsaak baie minder wrywing as iets wat gesleep word.","en":"The wheelbarrow is easier, because a wheel that rolls causes much less friction than something that is dragged."}},{"title":{"af":"Evalueer ’n modelvoertuig","en":"Evaluate a model vehicle"},"problem":{"af":"Aisha toets haar modelvoertuig. Dit wikkel op en af, draai na links en stop gou omdat die wiele teen die onderstel skuur. Gee ’n moontlike oorsaak vir elke probleem en ’n verbetering.","en":"Aisha tests her model vehicle. It wobbles up and down, turns to the left and stops quickly because the wheels rub against the chassis. Give a possible cause for each problem and an improvement."},"steps":[{"af":"**Wikkel:** die gat is waarskynlik nie in die middel van die wiele nie. Meet en merk die middelpunt met ’n passer of liniaal en maak nuwe wiele.","en":"**Wobbles:** the hole is probably not in the middle of the wheels. Measure and mark the centre with a compass or ruler and make new wheels."},{"af":"**Draai links:** die asse is nie **ewewydig** nie, of die wiele is nie ewe groot nie. Plak die strooitjies reguit en ewewydig vas.","en":"**Turns left:** the axles are not **parallel**, or the wheels are not the same size. Glue the straws on straight and parallel."},{"af":"**Stop gou:** die wiele skuur teen die onderstel en veroorsaak **wrywing**. Skuif die wiele ’n bietjie verder na buite of maak die strooitjies langer as die onderstel se breedte.","en":"**Stops quickly:** the wheels rub against the chassis and cause **friction**. Move the wheels a little further out or make the straws stick out past the edges of the chassis."}],"answer":{"af":"Gate in die middel van die wiele, ewewydige asse en ewe groot wiele, en ’n gaping tussen die wiele en die onderstel.","en":"Holes in the middle of the wheels, parallel axles and equal-sized wheels, and a gap between the wheels and the chassis."}},{"title":{"af":"Kies die regte materiale","en":"Choose the right materials"},"problem":{"af":"Ravi kan kies tussen hierdie materiale vir sy modelvoertuig: dun papier, stewige karton, sosatiestokkies, strooitjies, bottelproppies en klei. Kies materiale vir die onderstel, asse, laers en wiele en gee ’n rede vir elkeen.","en":"Ravi can choose from these materials for his model vehicle: thin paper, strong cardboard, kebab skewers, drinking straws, bottle caps and clay. Choose materials for the chassis, axles, bearings and wheels and give a reason for each."},"steps":[{"af":"**Onderstel:** stewige karton – dit is sterk genoeg om die vrag te dra. Dun papier sal buig en skeur.","en":"**Chassis:** strong cardboard – it is strong enough to carry the load. Thin paper will bend and tear."},{"af":"**Asse:** sosatiestokkies – hulle is reguit, styf en dun genoeg om in ’n strooitjie te pas.","en":"**Axles:** kebab skewers – they are straight, stiff and thin enough to fit inside a straw."},{"af":"**Laers:** strooitjies – hulle is glad aan die binnekant, so die as draai met min wrywing.","en":"**Bearings:** straws – they are smooth on the inside, so the axle turns with little friction."},{"af":"**Wiele:** bottelproppies – hulle is rond, ewe groot en hard. Klei is sag en sal sy vorm verloor.","en":"**Wheels:** bottle caps – they are round, the same size and hard. Clay is soft and will lose its shape."}],"answer":{"af":"Karton vir die onderstel, sosatiestokkies vir die asse, strooitjies as laers en bottelproppies as wiele.","en":"Cardboard for the chassis, kebab skewers for the axles, straws as bearings and bottle caps as wheels."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is ’n as?","en":"What is an axle?"},"options":[{"af":"Die staaf wat deur die middel van ’n wiel gaan","en":"The rod that goes through the middle of a wheel"},{"af":"Die rubber wat om die buitekant van ’n wiel sit","en":"The rubber that fits around the outside of a wheel"},{"af":"Die raam waarop die vrag van ’n voertuig lê","en":"The frame on which a vehicle’s load rests"},{"af":"Die deel van ’n fiets wat dit laat stop","en":"The part of a bicycle that makes it stop"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die as is die staaf deur die middel van die wiel. Die raam is die onderstel, die rubber is die band en die deel wat stop, is die rem.","en":"The axle is the rod through the middle of the wheel. The frame is the chassis, the rubber is the tyre and the part that stops it is the brake."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Wanneer iets rol, is daar minder wrywing as wanneer dit gesleep word.","en":"When something rolls, there is less friction than when it is dragged."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Wiel raak net met ’n klein deeltjie op ’n slag aan die grond, terwyl die hele onderkant van iets wat gesleep word, teen die grond skuur.","en":"True. A wheel touches the ground with only a small part at a time, while the whole bottom of something that is dragged rubs against the ground."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat gebeur by ’n vaste as?","en":"What happens with a fixed axle?"},"options":[{"af":"Die wiel draai om die as, en die as staan stil","en":"The wheel turns around the axle, and the axle stays still"},{"af":"Die wiele en die as draai saam","en":"The wheels and the axle turn together"},{"af":"Die as draai, maar die wiele staan stil","en":"The axle turns, but the wheels stay still"},{"af":"Die wiele gly oor die grond sonder om te draai","en":"The wheels slide over the ground without turning"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"By ’n vaste as is die wiele aan die as vas, so hulle draai saam. As die wiel om ’n stilstaande as draai, is dit ’n vrye as.","en":"With a fixed axle the wheels are fixed to the axle, so they turn together. If the wheel turns around an axle that stays still, it is a free axle."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die krag wat beweging teëwerk wanneer twee oppervlakke teen mekaar skuur, heet ___.","en":"The force that works against movement when two surfaces rub against each other is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["wrywing"],"en":["friction"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["swaartekrag","magnetisme","energie"],"en":["gravity","magnetism","energy"]}},"explain":{"af":"Wrywing ontstaan wanneer oppervlakke teen mekaar skuur. Swaartekrag trek dinge na die aarde toe; dit is ’n ander krag.","en":"Friction happens when surfaces rub against each other. Gravity pulls things towards the Earth; it is a different force."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is dit makliker om sand in ’n kruiwa te stoot as om ’n sak sand oor die grond te sleep?","en":"Why is it easier to push sand in a wheelbarrow than to drag a bag of sand over the ground?"},"options":[{"af":"Die sand in die kruiwa word ligter","en":"The sand in the wheelbarrow becomes lighter"},{"af":"Die kruiwa se handvatsels trek die sand op","en":"The wheelbarrow’s handles pull the sand up"},{"af":"Die wiel rol en veroorsaak minder wrywing","en":"The wheel rolls and causes less friction"},{"af":"Die sak sand het geen wrywing nie","en":"The bag of sand has no friction"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die sand weeg dieselfde. Die verskil is wrywing: die wiel rol en raak net met ’n klein deeltjie aan die grond, terwyl die hele sak teen die grond skuur.","en":"The sand weighs the same. The difference is friction: the wheel rolls and touches the ground with only a small part, while the whole bag rubs against the ground."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato laat haar model teen ’n helling afrol om te sien of dit reguit ry en die boksie sap dra. Watter stap van die ontwerpproses is dit?","en":"Lerato lets her model roll down a slope to see whether it travels straight and carries the box of juice. Which step of the design process is this?"},"options":[{"af":"Ondersoek","en":"Investigate"},{"af":"Ontwerp","en":"Design"},{"af":"Kommunikeer","en":"Communicate"},{"af":"Evalueer","en":"Evaluate"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Wanneer jy jou model toets om te sien of dit aan die spesifikasies voldoen, evalueer jy dit. Dan besluit jy wat jy kan verbeter.","en":"When you test your model to see whether it meets the specifications, you are evaluating it. Then you decide what you can improve."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke stap van die ontwerpproses by wat jy in daardie stap doen.","en":"Match each step of the design process to what you do in that step."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Ondersoek","en":"Investigate"},"r":{"af":"Kyk hoe bestaande voertuie werk","en":"Look at how existing vehicles work"}},{"l":{"af":"Ontwerp","en":"Design"},"r":{"af":"Teken idees en kies die beste een","en":"Draw ideas and choose the best one"}},{"l":{"af":"Maak","en":"Make"},"r":{"af":"Bou die model veilig en netjies","en":"Build the model safely and neatly"}},{"l":{"af":"Evalueer","en":"Evaluate"},"r":{"af":"Toets of dit doen wat die spesifikasies vra","en":"Test whether it does what the specifications ask"}},{"l":{"af":"Kommunikeer","en":"Communicate"},"r":{"af":"Verduidelik jou ontwerp aan ander","en":"Explain your design to others"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die ontwerpproses gaan: ondersoek, ontwerp, maak, evalueer en kommunikeer. Elke stap het sy eie werk.","en":"The design process goes: investigate, design, make, evaluate and communicate. Each step has its own job."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Deurknop werk soos ’n wiel en as. Watter deel is die wiel?","en":"A door knob works like a wheel and axle. Which part is the wheel?"},"options":[{"af":"Die dun staaf binne-in die deur","en":"The thin rod inside the door"},{"af":"Die skarniere van die deur","en":"The hinges of the door"},{"af":"Die sleutelgat onder die knop","en":"The keyhole under the knob"},{"af":"Die groot ronde knop wat jy vashou","en":"The big round knob that you hold"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die groot knop is die wiel en die dun staaf is die as. Omdat die knop groot is, kan jy die staaf met min krag draai.","en":"The big knob is the wheel and the thin rod is the axle. Because the knob is big, you can turn the rod with little force."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Kort beskrywing van wat jy gaan ontwerp en maak, vir wie en waarom, heet ’n ___.","en":"A short description of what you are going to design and make, for whom and why, is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["ontwerpopdrag"],"en":["design brief","brief"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["spesifikasie","evaluering","onderstel"],"en":["specification","evaluation","chassis"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die ontwerpopdrag sê wat jy gaan maak en waarom. Die spesifikasies is die lys van dinge wat die ontwerp moet kan doen.","en":"The design brief says what you are going to make and why. The specifications are the list of things the design must be able to do."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Zanele se modelvoertuig wikkel op en af terwyl dit ry. Wat is die waarskynlikste oorsaak?","en":"Zanele’s model vehicle wobbles up and down as it moves. What is the most likely cause?"},"options":[{"af":"Die onderstel is van karton gemaak","en":"The chassis is made of cardboard"},{"af":"Die gate is nie in die middel van die wiele nie","en":"The holes are not in the middle of the wheels"},{"af":"Die asse draai binne strooitjies","en":"The axles turn inside straws"},{"af":"Die voertuig het vier wiele","en":"The vehicle has four wheels"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"As die gat nie in die middel is nie, is een kant van die wiel verder van die as af as die ander, en die voertuig wip op en af. Karton, strooitjies en vier wiele is almal goeie keuses.","en":"If the hole is not in the middle, one side of the wheel is further from the axle than the other, and the vehicle bobs up and down. Cardboard, straws and four wheels are all good choices."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Wrywing is altyd sleg, en ons wil dit altyd heeltemal wegneem.","en":"Friction is always bad, and we always want to remove it completely."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Ons het wrywing nodig sodat fietsbande op die pad vashou en remme werk. Ons wil net minder wrywing tussen ’n wiel en sy as hê.","en":"False. We need friction so that bicycle tyres grip the road and brakes work. We only want less friction between a wheel and its axle."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat kan jy op ’n as sit om die wrywing tussen die wiel en die as te verminder?","en":"What can you put on an axle to reduce the friction between the wheel and the axle?"},"options":[{"af":"Sand of gruis","en":"Sand or gravel"},{"af":"Gom of kleefband","en":"Glue or sticky tape"},{"af":"Olie of ghries","en":"Oil or grease"},{"af":"Water en seep","en":"Water and soap"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Olie en ghries maak die oppervlakke glad, sodat hulle maklik oor mekaar gly. Sand sal meer wrywing veroorsaak, en gom sal die wiel vasplak.","en":"Oil and grease make the surfaces slippery, so they slide over each other easily. Sand would cause more friction, and glue would stick the wheel in place."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die raam van ’n voertuig waaraan die asse en wiele vasgemaak word, heet die ___.","en":"The frame of a vehicle to which the axles and wheels are attached is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["onderstel","raam"],"en":["chassis","frame"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["laer","as","spesifikasie"],"en":["bearing","axle","specification"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die onderstel is die raam van die voertuig. Die asse draai in laers wat aan die onderstel vas is.","en":"The chassis is the frame of the vehicle. The axles turn in bearings that are attached to the chassis."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n voorbeeld van ’n vrye as, waar die wiel om ’n stilstaande as draai?","en":"Which one is an example of a free axle, where the wheel turns around an axle that stays still?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Trollie se wieletjie wat om ’n vaste pen draai","en":"A trolley’s little wheel that turns around a fixed pin"},{"af":"Treinwiele wat saam met hul as draai","en":"Train wheels that turn together with their axle"},{"af":"’n Model met wiele wat op die as vasgeplak is","en":"A model with wheels glued onto the axle"},{"af":"’n Waaier se lemme wat saam met die motor se as draai","en":"A fan’s blades that turn together with the motor’s shaft"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"By die trollie staan die pen (as) stil en draai net die wieletjie. By die ander drie draai die wiel of lemme saam met die as – dit is soos ’n vaste as.","en":"On the trolley the pin (axle) stays still and only the little wheel turns. In the other three the wheel or blades turn together with the axle – that is like a fixed axle."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Planeet Aarde en die ruimte","en":"Planet Earth and beyond"},"topics":[{"id":"nwt5-t4-aarde-beweeg","title":{"af":"Die aarde beweeg","en":"The Earth moves"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe die aarde se rotasie dag en nag veroorsaak, hoe sy omwenteling om die son ’n jaar vorm, waarom ons skrikkeljare het en waarom die son in die ooste opkom.","en":"You will be able to explain how the Earth’s rotation causes day and night, how its revolution around the Sun makes a year, why we have leap years and why the Sun rises in the east."},"summary":{"af":"## Die vorm van die aarde\n\nDie aarde is ’n **sfeer** – rond soos ’n bal. Foto’s wat uit die ruimte geneem is, wys dit duidelik. Die aarde het drie dele:\n\n- **land** – die kontinente en eilande, van rots en grond gemaak\n- **water** – oseane, riviere, mere en ys; meer as twee derdes van die aarde se oppervlak is water\n- **lug** – ’n laag gasse rondom die aarde, die **atmosfeer**\n\n## Die aarde draai om sy as: dag en nag\n\nDie aarde draai om ’n denkbeeldige lyn wat deur die **Noordpool** en die **Suidpool** loop. Hierdie lyn is die aarde se **as**. Die aarde draai een keer heeltemal om in **24 uur**. Ons noem dit **rotasie**.\n\n- Die kant van die aarde wat na die son toe gedraai is, het **dag**.\n- Die kant wat van die son af weggedraai is, het **nag**.\n\nTerwyl die aarde draai, beweeg Suid-Afrika uit die donker in die lig in (oggend) en later uit die lig in die donker in (aand). Wanneer dit by ons middag is, is dit aan die ander kant van die aarde middernag.\n\n## Die son se skynbare beweging\n\nDie aarde draai van **wes na oos**. Daarom lyk dit vir ons asof die son in die **ooste opkom**, oor die lug beweeg en in die **weste sak**. Maar die son beweeg nie om die aarde nie – dit is óns wat draai. Dit heet die son se **skynbare beweging**. Dit is soos wanneer jy in ’n bewegende motor sit en dit lyk asof die bome verbyhardloop.\n\nJy kan dit met ’n **skaduweestok** sien: soggens is die son in die ooste en wys die skaduwee na die weste. Teen die middag is die skaduwee op sy kortste, en smiddags wys dit na die ooste.\n\n## Die aarde wentel om die son: ’n jaar\n\nTerwyl die aarde om sy as draai, beweeg dit ook in ’n groot baan om die son. Die baan heet die **wentelbaan**, en die beweging heet **omwenteling**. Een omwenteling neem **365¼ dae** – dit is **een jaar**.\n\n’n Kalender het net heel dae, so ons tel 365 dae per jaar. Die ¼ dag wat elke jaar oorbly, tel op: ná **4 jaar** is dit ’n hele ekstra dag (4 × ¼ = 1). Daardie dag word as **29 Februarie** bygevoeg. ’n Jaar met 366 dae is ’n **skrikkeljaar**, byvoorbeeld 2024 en 2028.\n\n| | Rotasie | Omwenteling |\n|---|---|---|\n| Wat gebeur | Die aarde draai om sy eie as | Die aarde wentel om die son |\n| Hoe lank | 24 uur (een dag) | 365¼ dae (een jaar) |\n| Gevolg | Dag en nag | ’n Jaar, en saam met die skuins as, die seisoene |\n\n> **Onthou:** **Rotasie** (draai om die as, 24 uur) gee **dag en nag**. **Omwenteling** (wentel om die son, 365¼ dae) gee ’n **jaar**.\n\n## Die skuins as en die seisoene\n\nDie aarde se as staan **skuins** (omtrent 23,5°) en wys altyd in dieselfde rigting terwyl die aarde om die son wentel. Daarom is die **suidelike halfrond**, waar Suid-Afrika lê, ’n deel van die jaar na die son toe gekantel en ’n deel van die jaar daarvan weg.\n\n- Wanneer die suidelike halfrond na die son toe gekantel is, skyn die son meer direk en is die dae langer: dit is **somer** by ons (Desember).\n- Ses maande later is die suidelike halfrond weg gekantel: dit is **winter** by ons (Junie).\n- Die **noordelike halfrond** het dan die teenoorgestelde seisoen.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die seisoene word **nie** veroorsaak doordat die aarde soms nader aan die son is nie, maar deur die **skuins as**. As afstand die rede was, sou die hele aarde gelyk somer hê – maar wanneer dit by ons somer is, is dit in Europa winter.","en":"## The shape of the Earth\n\nThe Earth is a **sphere** – round like a ball. Photos taken from space show this clearly. The Earth has three parts:\n\n- **land** – the continents and islands, made of rock and soil\n- **water** – oceans, rivers, lakes and ice; more than two thirds of the Earth’s surface is water\n- **air** – a layer of gases around the Earth, the **atmosphere**\n\n## The Earth spins on its axis: day and night\n\nThe Earth spins around an imaginary line that runs through the **North Pole** and the **South Pole**. This line is the Earth’s **axis**. The Earth turns all the way around once in **24 hours**. We call this **rotation**.\n\n- The side of the Earth that is turned towards the Sun has **day**.\n- The side that is turned away from the Sun has **night**.\n\nAs the Earth turns, South Africa moves out of the dark into the light (morning) and later out of the light into the dark (evening). When it is midday here, it is midnight on the other side of the Earth.\n\n## The Sun’s apparent movement\n\nThe Earth turns from **west to east**. That is why it looks to us as if the Sun **rises in the east**, moves across the sky and **sets in the west**. But the Sun does not move around the Earth – it is we who are turning. This is called the Sun’s **apparent movement**. It is like sitting in a moving car when it looks as if the trees are running past.\n\nYou can see this with a **shadow stick**: in the morning the Sun is in the east and the shadow points west. Around midday the shadow is at its shortest, and in the afternoon it points east.\n\n## The Earth orbits the Sun: a year\n\nWhile the Earth spins on its axis, it also moves in a big path around the Sun. The path is called the **orbit**, and the movement is called **revolution**. One revolution takes **365¼ days** – this is **one year**.\n\nA calendar has only whole days, so we count 365 days in a year. The ¼ day left over each year adds up: after **4 years** it makes one whole extra day (4 × ¼ = 1). That day is added as **29 February**. A year with 366 days is a **leap year**, for example 2024 and 2028.\n\n| | Rotation | Revolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| What happens | The Earth spins on its own axis | The Earth orbits the Sun |\n| How long | 24 hours (one day) | 365¼ days (one year) |\n| Result | Day and night | A year, and together with the tilted axis, the seasons |\n\n> **Remember:** **Rotation** (spinning on the axis, 24 hours) gives **day and night**. **Revolution** (orbiting the Sun, 365¼ days) gives a **year**.\n\n## The tilted axis and the seasons\n\nThe Earth’s axis is **tilted** (about 23.5°) and always points in the same direction while the Earth orbits the Sun. That is why the **southern hemisphere**, where South Africa is, is tilted towards the Sun for part of the year and away from it for another part of the year.\n\n- When the southern hemisphere is tilted towards the Sun, the Sun shines more directly and the days are longer: it is **summer** here (December).\n- Six months later the southern hemisphere is tilted away: it is **winter** here (June).\n- The **northern hemisphere** then has the opposite season.\n\n> **Common mistake:** The seasons are **not** caused by the Earth sometimes being closer to the Sun, but by the **tilted axis**. If distance were the reason, the whole Earth would have summer at the same time – but when it is summer here, it is winter in Europe."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Sfeer","en":"Sphere"},"def":{"af":"’n Ronde vorm soos ’n bal; die aarde is ’n sfeer.","en":"A round shape like a ball; the Earth is a sphere."}},{"term":{"af":"Atmosfeer","en":"Atmosphere"},"def":{"af":"Die laag lug (gasse) wat rondom die aarde is.","en":"The layer of air (gases) around the Earth."}},{"term":{"af":"As (aardas)","en":"Axis (Earth’s axis)"},"def":{"af":"Die denkbeeldige lyn deur die Noordpool en die Suidpool waarom die aarde draai.","en":"The imaginary line through the North Pole and the South Pole around which the Earth spins."}},{"term":{"af":"Rotasie","en":"Rotation"},"def":{"af":"Die aarde se draai om sy eie as; een rotasie neem 24 uur en gee dag en nag.","en":"The Earth spinning on its own axis; one rotation takes 24 hours and gives day and night."}},{"term":{"af":"Omwenteling","en":"Revolution"},"def":{"af":"Die aarde se beweging in sy baan om die son; een omwenteling neem 365¼ dae.","en":"The Earth’s movement in its path around the Sun; one revolution takes 365¼ days."}},{"term":{"af":"Wentelbaan","en":"Orbit"},"def":{"af":"Die pad wat die aarde volg wanneer dit om die son beweeg.","en":"The path the Earth follows when it moves around the Sun."}},{"term":{"af":"Skrikkeljaar","en":"Leap year"},"def":{"af":"’n Jaar met 366 dae, wat elke vierde jaar voorkom; Februarie het dan 29 dae.","en":"A year with 366 days, which happens every fourth year; February then has 29 days."}},{"term":{"af":"Skynbare beweging","en":"Apparent movement"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer dit lyk asof iets beweeg, soos die son oor die lug, maar dit eintlik óns is wat beweeg.","en":"When something seems to move, like the Sun across the sky, but it is really us who are moving."}},{"term":{"af":"Halfrond","en":"Hemisphere"},"def":{"af":"Die helfte van die aarde; die ewenaar deel die aarde in ’n noordelike en ’n suidelike halfrond.","en":"Half of the Earth; the equator divides the Earth into a northern and a southern hemisphere."}},{"term":{"af":"Seisoene","en":"Seasons"},"def":{"af":"Die vier dele van die jaar – somer, herfs, winter en lente – wat ontstaan omdat die aarde se as skuins is.","en":"The four parts of the year – summer, autumn, winter and spring – which happen because the Earth’s axis is tilted."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Dag hier, nag daar","en":"Day here, night there"},"problem":{"af":"Om 12:00 in die middag wil Sipho in Durban sy neef aan die ander kant van die aarde bel, maar sy neef slaap. Verduidelik waarom.","en":"At 12:00 midday Sipho in Durban wants to phone his cousin on the other side of the Earth, but his cousin is asleep. Explain why."},"steps":[{"af":"Die son kan net een helfte van die aarde op ’n slag belig.","en":"The Sun can only light up one half of the Earth at a time."},{"af":"Om 12:00 is Durban se kant van die aarde na die son toe gedraai: dit is **dag**.","en":"At 12:00 Durban’s side of the Earth is turned towards the Sun: it is **day**."},{"af":"Die ander kant van die aarde is van die son af weggedraai: daar is dit **nag**, omtrent middernag.","en":"The other side of the Earth is turned away from the Sun: there it is **night**, about midnight."},{"af":"Omdat die aarde in 24 uur om sy as **roteer**, sal dit later by Sipho nag wees en by sy neef dag.","en":"Because the Earth **rotates** on its axis in 24 hours, it will later be night for Sipho and day for his cousin."}],"answer":{"af":"Die neef se kant van die aarde is van die son af weggedraai, so dit is nag daar terwyl dit in Durban dag is.","en":"The cousin’s side of the Earth is turned away from the Sun, so it is night there while it is day in Durban."}},{"title":{"af":"Is 2028 ’n skrikkeljaar?","en":"Is 2028 a leap year?"},"problem":{"af":"2024 was ’n skrikkeljaar. Is 2028 ook een? Hoeveel dae sal Februarie 2028 hê, en hoeveel dae die hele jaar?","en":"2024 was a leap year. Is 2028 one too? How many days will February 2028 have, and how many days the whole year?"},"steps":[{"af":"Een omwenteling om die son neem 365¼ dae, maar die kalender tel 365 dae.","en":"One revolution around the Sun takes 365¼ days, but the calendar counts 365 days."},{"af":"Elke jaar bly ¼ dag oor. Ná 4 jaar: 4 × ¼ = 1 ekstra dag. Daarom is daar elke **4 jaar** ’n skrikkeljaar.","en":"Every year ¼ day is left over. After 4 years: 4 × ¼ = 1 extra day. That is why there is a leap year every **4 years**."},{"af":"2024 + 4 = 2028, so 2028 is ’n skrikkeljaar.","en":"2024 + 4 = 2028, so 2028 is a leap year."},{"af":"Die ekstra dag is 29 Februarie, so Februarie het **29** dae en die jaar het 365 + 1 = **366** dae.","en":"The extra day is 29 February, so February has **29** days and the year has 365 + 1 = **366** days."}],"answer":{"af":"Ja. Februarie 2028 het 29 dae en die jaar het 366 dae.","en":"Yes. February 2028 has 29 days and the year has 366 days."}},{"title":{"af":"Die skaduweestok","en":"The shadow stick"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato steek ’n stok regop in die grond en merk sy skaduwee om 08:00, 12:00 en 16:00. Beskryf die rigting en lengte van die skaduwee elke keer en verduidelik wat dit wys.","en":"Lerato pushes a stick upright into the ground and marks its shadow at 08:00, 12:00 and 16:00. Describe the direction and length of the shadow each time and explain what it shows."},"steps":[{"af":"’n Skaduwee wys altyd **weg van die son af**.","en":"A shadow always points **away from the Sun**."},{"af":"**08:00:** die son is laag in die ooste, so die skaduwee is **lank** en wys na die **weste**.","en":"**08:00:** the Sun is low in the east, so the shadow is **long** and points **west**."},{"af":"**12:00:** die son is hoog in die lug, so die skaduwee is op sy **kortste**.","en":"**12:00:** the Sun is high in the sky, so the shadow is at its **shortest**."},{"af":"**16:00:** die son is laer in die weste, so die skaduwee is weer **lank** en wys na die **ooste**.","en":"**16:00:** the Sun is lower in the west, so the shadow is **long** again and points **east**."},{"af":"Dit lyk asof die son van oos na wes beweeg, maar dit is die aarde wat van wes na oos draai – die son se **skynbare beweging**.","en":"It looks as if the Sun moves from east to west, but it is the Earth turning from west to east – the Sun’s **apparent movement**."}],"answer":{"af":"Lank na die weste, dan kort, dan lank na die ooste. Dit wys die son se skynbare beweging van oos na wes, wat veroorsaak word deur die aarde se rotasie.","en":"Long towards the west, then short, then long towards the east. It shows the Sun’s apparent movement from east to west, caused by the Earth’s rotation."}},{"title":{"af":"Somer hier, winter daar","en":"Summer here, winter there"},"problem":{"af":"Anika se oupa en ouma in Engeland (noordelike halfrond) vier Kersfees in die koue winter, terwyl sy in Kaapstad op die strand is. Verduidelik waarom die seisoene verskil.","en":"Anika’s grandparents in England (northern hemisphere) celebrate Christmas in the cold winter, while she is on the beach in Cape Town. Explain why the seasons are different."},"steps":[{"af":"Die aarde se as is **skuins** en wys altyd in dieselfde rigting terwyl die aarde om die son wentel.","en":"The Earth’s axis is **tilted** and always points in the same direction while the Earth orbits the Sun."},{"af":"In Desember is die **suidelike halfrond** na die son toe gekantel: die son skyn meer direk en die dae is lank. Dit is **somer** in Kaapstad.","en":"In December the **southern hemisphere** is tilted towards the Sun: the Sun shines more directly and the days are long. It is **summer** in Cape Town."},{"af":"Terselfdertyd is die **noordelike halfrond** van die son af weg gekantel: die son skyn skuinser en die dae is kort. Dit is **winter** in Engeland.","en":"At the same time the **northern hemisphere** is tilted away from the Sun: the Sun shines at more of a slant and the days are short. It is **winter** in England."}],"answer":{"af":"Weens die skuins as is die suidelike halfrond in Desember na die son toe gekantel (somer) en die noordelike halfrond daarvan weg (winter).","en":"Because of the tilted axis, the southern hemisphere is tilted towards the Sun in December (summer) and the northern hemisphere away from it (winter)."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe lank neem die aarde om een keer om sy as te draai?","en":"How long does the Earth take to spin once on its axis?"},"options":[{"af":"365¼ dae","en":"365¼ days"},{"af":"Een week","en":"One week"},{"af":"24 uur","en":"24 hours"},{"af":"12 uur","en":"12 hours"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Een rotasie neem 24 uur en gee een dag en een nag. 365¼ dae is hoe lank een omwenteling om die son neem. 12 uur is net ongeveer die dag óf die nag.","en":"One rotation takes 24 hours and gives one day and one night. 365¼ days is how long one revolution around the Sun takes. 12 hours is only about the day or the night."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die aarde se beweging in sy baan om die son heet ___.","en":"The Earth’s movement in its path around the Sun is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["omwenteling"],"en":["revolution"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["rotasie","sirkulasie","kanteling"],"en":["rotation","circulation","tilting"]}},"explain":{"af":"Omwenteling is die beweging om die son (365¼ dae). Rotasie is die draai om die aarde se eie as (24 uur).","en":"Revolution is the movement around the Sun (365¼ days). Rotation is spinning on the Earth’s own axis (24 hours)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom het ons dag en nag?","en":"Why do we have day and night?"},"options":[{"af":"Die son wentel elke dag een keer om die aarde","en":"The Sun orbits the Earth once every day"},{"af":"Die aarde draai om sy as","en":"The Earth spins on its axis"},{"af":"Die maan bedek die son elke aand","en":"The Moon covers the Sun every evening"},{"af":"Die aarde wentel om die son","en":"The Earth orbits the Sun"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die aarde se rotasie draai elke plek eers na die son toe (dag) en dan weg (nag). Die omwenteling om die son gee ’n jaar, nie dag en nag nie.","en":"The Earth’s rotation turns each place first towards the Sun (day) and then away (night). The revolution around the Sun gives a year, not day and night."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die son kom in die ooste op en sak in die weste.","en":"The Sun rises in the east and sets in the west."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Omdat die aarde van wes na oos draai, lyk dit asof die son in die ooste opkom en in die weste sak.","en":"True. Because the Earth turns from west to east, it looks as if the Sun rises in the east and sets in the west."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel dae het ’n skrikkeljaar?","en":"How many days does a leap year have?"},"options":[{"af":"364","en":"364"},{"af":"365","en":"365"},{"af":"365¼","en":"365¼"},{"af":"366","en":"366"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Gewone jaar het 365 dae. Elke vier jaar word die vier kwarte (4 × ¼) ’n ekstra dag, 29 Februarie, so ’n skrikkeljaar het 366 dae. ’n Kalender kan nie ’n kwart dag hê nie.","en":"An ordinary year has 365 days. Every four years the four quarters (4 × ¼) become an extra day, 29 February, so a leap year has 366 days. A calendar cannot have a quarter of a day."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Om 08:00 die oggend is die son in die ooste. In watter rigting wys ’n regop stok se skaduwee?","en":"At 08:00 in the morning the Sun is in the east. In which direction does an upright stick’s shadow point?"},"options":[{"af":"Na die weste","en":"Towards the west"},{"af":"Na die ooste","en":"Towards the east"},{"af":"Reg na die son toe","en":"Straight towards the Sun"},{"af":"Daar is soggens geen skaduwee nie","en":"There is no shadow in the morning"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Skaduwee wys altyd weg van die son af. As die son in die ooste is, wys die skaduwee na die weste.","en":"A shadow always points away from the Sun. If the Sun is in the east, the shadow points west."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each term to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Rotasie","en":"Rotation"},"r":{"af":"Draai om die as in 24 uur","en":"Spinning on the axis in 24 hours"}},{"l":{"af":"Omwenteling","en":"Revolution"},"r":{"af":"Wentel om die son in 365¼ dae","en":"Orbiting the Sun in 365¼ days"}},{"l":{"af":"Skrikkeljaar","en":"Leap year"},"r":{"af":"’n Jaar met 366 dae","en":"A year with 366 days"}},{"l":{"af":"Skuins as","en":"Tilted axis"},"r":{"af":"Die rede vir die seisoene","en":"The reason for the seasons"}},{"l":{"af":"Atmosfeer","en":"Atmosphere"},"r":{"af":"Die laag lug rondom die aarde","en":"The layer of air around the Earth"}}],"explain":{"af":"Rotasie gee dag en nag, omwenteling gee ’n jaar, ’n skrikkeljaar het ’n ekstra dag, die skuins as veroorsaak die seisoene en die atmosfeer is die lug om die aarde.","en":"Rotation gives day and night, revolution gives a year, a leap year has an extra day, the tilted axis causes the seasons and the atmosphere is the air around the Earth."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter vorm het die aarde?","en":"What shape is the Earth?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Plat skyf, soos ’n bord","en":"A flat disc, like a plate"},{"af":"’n Silinder, soos ’n blik","en":"A cylinder, like a tin"},{"af":"’n Kubus, soos ’n dobbelsteen","en":"A cube, like a dice"},{"af":"’n Sfeer, rond soos ’n bal","en":"A sphere, round like a ball"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Foto’s uit die ruimte wys dat die aarde ’n sfeer is. Daarom kan die son net een helfte op ’n slag belig.","en":"Photos from space show that the Earth is a sphere. That is why the Sun can only light up one half at a time."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Jaar met 366 dae, waarin Februarie 29 dae het, heet ’n ___.","en":"A year with 366 days, in which February has 29 days, is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["skrikkeljaar"],"en":["leap year"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kalenderjaar","dekade","eeu"],"en":["calendar year","decade","century"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Skrikkeljaar kom elke vier jaar voor omdat die ekstra kwart dae saam ’n hele dag word. ’n Dekade is 10 jaar en ’n eeu is 100 jaar.","en":"A leap year happens every four years because the extra quarter days add up to a whole day. A decade is 10 years and a century is 100 years."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat veroorsaak die seisoene?","en":"What causes the seasons?"},"options":[{"af":"Die aarde is in die somer baie nader aan die son","en":"The Earth is much closer to the Sun in summer"},{"af":"Die aarde se as is skuins terwyl dit om die son wentel","en":"The Earth’s axis is tilted while it orbits the Sun"},{"af":"Die son brand in die winter minder helder","en":"The Sun burns less brightly in winter"},{"af":"Die aarde draai in die winter stadiger om sy as","en":"The Earth spins more slowly on its axis in winter"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die skuins as maak dat ’n halfrond deel van die jaar na die son toe en deel van die jaar daarvan weg gekantel is. As afstand die rede was, sou die hele aarde gelyk somer hê.","en":"The tilted axis means that a hemisphere is tilted towards the Sun for part of the year and away from it for another part. If distance were the reason, the whole Earth would have summer at the same time."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Wanneer dit in Suid-Afrika somer is, is dit ook somer in die noordelike halfrond.","en":"When it is summer in South Africa, it is also summer in the northern hemisphere."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die halfronde het teenoorgestelde seisoene. In Desember is dit somer in Suid-Afrika en winter in die noordelike halfrond.","en":"False. The hemispheres have opposite seasons. In December it is summer in South Africa and winter in the northern hemisphere."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Dit is middag in Johannesburg. Wat is dit omtrent aan die heel teenoorgestelde kant van die aarde?","en":"It is midday in Johannesburg. What is it at about the exact opposite side of the Earth?"},"options":[{"af":"Ook middag","en":"Also midday"},{"af":"Vroeg in die oggend","en":"Early in the morning"},{"af":"Middernag","en":"Midnight"},{"af":"Laat in die middag","en":"Late in the afternoon"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Johannesburg is reg na die son toe gedraai. Die teenoorgestelde kant van die sfeer is reg van die son af weggedraai, so dit is omtrent middernag daar.","en":"Johannesburg is turned straight towards the Sun. The opposite side of the sphere is turned straight away from the Sun, so it is about midnight there."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die denkbeeldige lyn deur die Noordpool en die Suidpool waarom die aarde draai, heet die aarde se ___.","en":"The imaginary line through the North Pole and the South Pole around which the Earth spins is called the Earth’s ___."},"answers":{"af":["as","aardas"],"en":["axis"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["ewenaar","wentelbaan","halfrond"],"en":["equator","orbit","hemisphere"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die aarde draai om sy as. Die ewenaar is ’n denkbeeldige lyn om die middel van die aarde, en die wentelbaan is die pad om die son.","en":"The Earth spins around its axis. The equator is an imaginary line around the middle of the Earth, and the orbit is the path around the Sun."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom lyk dit asof die son oor die lug beweeg?","en":"Why does it look as if the Sun moves across the sky?"},"options":[{"af":"Want die aarde draai van wes na oos","en":"Because the Earth turns from west to east"},{"af":"Want die son wentel om die aarde","en":"Because the Sun orbits the Earth"},{"af":"Want die wind waai die son weswaarts","en":"Because the wind blows the Sun westwards"},{"af":"Want die aarde wentel in 24 uur om die son","en":"Because the Earth orbits the Sun in 24 hours"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die son beweeg nie om die aarde nie; óns draai saam met die aarde van wes na oos. Dit is die son se skynbare beweging. ’n Omwenteling om die son neem 365¼ dae, nie 24 uur nie.","en":"The Sun does not travel around the Earth; we turn with the Earth from west to east. This is the Sun’s apparent movement. A revolution around the Sun takes 365¼ days, not 24 hours."}}]},{"id":"nwt5-t4-rotse-grond","title":{"af":"Die aarde se oppervlak: rotse en grond","en":"The surface of the Earth: rocks and soil"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe verwering rots afbreek, hoe grond uit rotsdeeltjies en humus gevorm word, en sandgrond, kleigrond en leemgrond met ’n eenvoudige ondersoek vergelyk.","en":"You will be able to explain how weathering breaks down rock, how soil forms from rock particles and humus, and compare sandy soil, clay soil and loam with a simple investigation."},"summary":{"af":"## Die aarde se oppervlak is rots\n\nDie buitenste laag van die aarde heet die **kors**, en die kors bestaan uit **rots**. Op baie plekke kan jy die rots sien, soos in berge en kranse. Op ander plekke lê daar grond, sand of water bo-op, maar as jy diep genoeg grawe, kom jy altyd op rots af.\n\n## Verwering breek rots af\n\n**Verwering** is wanneer rots stadig in kleiner en kleiner stukkies opgebreek word. Dit gebeur baie stadig, oor honderde en duisende jare.\n\n| Oorsaak | Hoe dit rots afbreek |\n|---|---|\n| Water | Reën en riviere skuur oor rotse en maak hulle glad en klein. Water kan sommige soorte rots ook stadig oplos. |\n| Ys | Water in ’n kraak vries en **sit uit**. Die ys druk die kraak wyer, totdat die rots breek. |\n| Temperatuurveranderinge | Rots sit in die warm dag uit en trek in die koue nag saam. Ná baie jare kraak en skilfer die buitekant af. |\n| Wind | Wind waai sand teen rotse, soos skuurpapier. |\n| Plantwortels | Wortels groei in krake in en druk die rots uitmekaar soos hulle dikker word. |\n\n## Hoe grond gevorm word\n\n**Grond** bestaan uit:\n\n- **fyn rotsdeeltjies** – van verwering\n- **humus** – ontbinde (vrot) plant- en dieremateriaal, soos blare, wortels, mis en dooie insekte\n- **lug** en **water** in die spasies tussen die deeltjies\n- **lewende dinge** – erdwurms, miere en piepklein organismes wat help om humus te maak\n\nHumus maak grond **donker** en **vrugbaar**: dit bevat **voedingstowwe** wat plante nodig het. Die boonste laag, die **bogrond**, het die meeste humus en is die donkerste. Dit neem baie lank vir nuwe grond om te vorm, daarom moet ons grond oppas.\n\n## Grondsoorte\n\n| Grondsoort | Deeltjies | Hoe voel dit? | Water |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Sandgrond | Groot korrels | Grof en los | Dreineer vinnig; droog gou uit |\n| Kleigrond | Baie fyn | Glad en taai as dit nat is; hard en gekraak as dit droog is | Hou baie water vas; kan deurweek raak |\n| Leemgrond | ’n Mengsel van sand, klei en baie humus | Krummelrig en donker | Hou genoeg water en lug |\n\n**Leemgrond** is die beste vir die meeste plante: dit hou genoeg water vas, maar nie te veel nie, en het baie humus.\n\n> **Onthou:** Grond = fyn rotsdeeltjies + humus + lug + water + lewende dinge.\n\n## Ondersoek: Hoe vinnig dreineer water deur grond?\n\nSit dieselfde hoeveelheid sand, klei en leem in drie tregters met watte onder in. Gooi **100 ml** water oor elkeen en meet ná **5 minute** hoeveel water deurgeloop het.\n\n- **Wat jy verander:** die grondsoort\n- **Wat jy meet:** hoeveel water deurloop\n- **Wat dieselfde bly:** die hoeveelheid grond en water, die tyd en die soort tregter\n- **Resultaat:** deur die sand loop die meeste water, deur die klei die minste\n- **Gevolgtrekking:** sand dreineer vinnig; klei hou die meeste water vas\n\nDie water wat nie deurloop nie, is in die grond agtergebly. As 70 ml deur die sand loop, het die sand 100 ml − 70 ml = 30 ml vasgehou.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Baie leerders dink klei is die beste grond omdat dit die meeste water hou. Maar te veel water verdring die lug, en wortels het ook lug nodig. Leem is die beste.","en":"## The Earth’s surface is rock\n\nThe outer layer of the Earth is called the **crust**, and the crust is made of **rock**. In many places you can see the rock, such as in mountains and cliffs. In other places there is soil, sand or water on top, but if you dig deep enough, you always reach rock.\n\n## Weathering breaks down rock\n\n**Weathering** is when rock is slowly broken up into smaller and smaller pieces. It happens very slowly, over hundreds and thousands of years.\n\n| Cause | How it breaks down rock |\n|---|---|\n| Water | Rain and rivers rub over rocks and make them smooth and small. Water can also slowly dissolve some kinds of rock. |\n| Ice | Water in a crack freezes and **expands**. The ice pushes the crack wider, until the rock breaks. |\n| Temperature changes | Rock expands in the hot day and contracts in the cold night. After many years the outside cracks and flakes off. |\n| Wind | Wind blows sand against rocks, like sandpaper. |\n| Plant roots | Roots grow into cracks and push the rock apart as they get thicker. |\n\n## How soil is formed\n\n**Soil** is made of:\n\n- **fine rock particles** – from weathering\n- **humus** – decayed (rotted) plant and animal material, such as leaves, roots, dung and dead insects\n- **air** and **water** in the spaces between the particles\n- **living things** – earthworms, ants and tiny organisms that help to make humus\n\nHumus makes soil **dark** and **fertile**: it contains **nutrients** that plants need. The top layer, the **topsoil**, has the most humus and is the darkest. It takes a very long time for new soil to form, so we must look after soil.\n\n## Types of soil\n\n| Soil type | Particles | How does it feel? | Water |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Sandy soil | Large grains | Rough and loose | Drains quickly; dries out fast |\n| Clay soil | Very fine | Smooth and sticky when wet; hard and cracked when dry | Holds a lot of water; can become waterlogged |\n| Loam | A mixture of sand, clay and lots of humus | Crumbly and dark | Holds enough water and air |\n\n**Loam** is the best for most plants: it holds enough water, but not too much, and has lots of humus.\n\n> **Remember:** Soil = fine rock particles + humus + air + water + living things.\n\n## Investigation: How fast does water drain through soil?\n\nPut the same amount of sand, clay and loam into three funnels with cotton wool at the bottom. Pour **100 ml** of water over each one and measure after **5 minutes** how much water has run through.\n\n- **What you change:** the type of soil\n- **What you measure:** how much water runs through\n- **What stays the same:** the amount of soil and water, the time and the type of funnel\n- **Result:** the most water runs through the sand, the least through the clay\n- **Conclusion:** sand drains quickly; clay holds the most water\n\nThe water that does not run through has stayed behind in the soil. If 70 ml runs through the sand, the sand has held 100 ml − 70 ml = 30 ml.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Many learners think clay is the best soil because it holds the most water. But too much water pushes out the air, and roots need air too. Loam is the best."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Kors","en":"Crust"},"def":{"af":"Die buitenste laag van die aarde, wat uit rots bestaan.","en":"The outer layer of the Earth, which is made of rock."}},{"term":{"af":"Verwering","en":"Weathering"},"def":{"af":"Die stadige afbreek van rots in kleiner stukkies deur water, ys, wind, temperatuurveranderinge en plantwortels.","en":"The slow breaking down of rock into smaller pieces by water, ice, wind, temperature changes and plant roots."}},{"term":{"af":"Humus","en":"Humus"},"def":{"af":"Ontbinde plant- en dieremateriaal in die grond wat dit donker en vrugbaar maak.","en":"Decayed plant and animal material in the soil that makes it dark and fertile."}},{"term":{"af":"Grond","en":"Soil"},"def":{"af":"’n Mengsel van fyn rotsdeeltjies, humus, lug, water en lewende dinge waarin plante groei.","en":"A mixture of fine rock particles, humus, air, water and living things in which plants grow."}},{"term":{"af":"Bogrond","en":"Topsoil"},"def":{"af":"Die boonste, donker laag grond met die meeste humus.","en":"The top, dark layer of soil with the most humus."}},{"term":{"af":"Sandgrond","en":"Sandy soil"},"def":{"af":"Grond met groot, growwe korrels waardeur water vinnig dreineer.","en":"Soil with large, rough grains through which water drains quickly."}},{"term":{"af":"Kleigrond","en":"Clay soil"},"def":{"af":"Grond met baie fyn deeltjies wat taai is as dit nat is en baie water vashou.","en":"Soil with very fine particles that is sticky when wet and holds a lot of water."}},{"term":{"af":"Leemgrond","en":"Loam"},"def":{"af":"’n Mengsel van sand, klei en baie humus; die beste grond vir die meeste plante.","en":"A mixture of sand, clay and lots of humus; the best soil for most plants."}},{"term":{"af":"Dreineer","en":"Drain"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer water deur die grond afloop en wegvloei.","en":"When water runs down through the soil and flows away."}},{"term":{"af":"Vrugbaar","en":"Fertile"},"def":{"af":"Grond wat baie voedingstowwe het sodat plante goed kan groei.","en":"Soil that has many nutrients so that plants can grow well."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lees die resultate van die dreineringsondersoek","en":"Reading the results of the drainage investigation"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter gooi 100 ml water oor elk van drie grondsoorte. Ná 5 minute het die volgende deurgeloop: sand 70 ml, leem 45 ml, klei 10 ml. Watter grond hou die meeste water vas, en hoeveel water het dit vasgehou? Waarom was dit ’n regverdige toets?","en":"Pieter pours 100 ml of water over each of three soil types. After 5 minutes the following has run through: sand 70 ml, loam 45 ml, clay 10 ml. Which soil holds the most water, and how much water did it hold? Why was it a fair test?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die minste water het deur die **klei** geloop (10 ml), so klei hou die meeste water vas.","en":"The least water ran through the **clay** (10 ml), so clay holds the most water."},{"af":"Bereken wat agtergebly het: 100 ml − 10 ml = **90 ml**.","en":"Work out what stayed behind: 100 ml − 10 ml = **90 ml**."},{"af":"Ter vergelyking: sand het 100 − 70 = 30 ml gehou en leem 100 − 45 = 55 ml.","en":"To compare: sand held 100 − 70 = 30 ml and loam held 100 − 45 = 55 ml."},{"af":"Dit was regverdig omdat net die **grondsoort** verskil het; die hoeveelheid grond, die 100 ml water, die 5 minute en die tregters was dieselfde.","en":"It was fair because only the **type of soil** was different; the amount of soil, the 100 ml of water, the 5 minutes and the funnels were the same."}],"answer":{"af":"Klei hou die meeste water vas: dit het 90 ml gehou. Net die grondsoort is verander, so die toets was regverdig.","en":"Clay holds the most water: it held 90 ml. Only the type of soil was changed, so the test was fair."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Boom breek ’n rots","en":"A tree breaks a rock"},"problem":{"af":"Op ’n koppie groei ’n wildevy uit ’n kraak in ’n groot rots. Ná baie jare is die rots in twee gebreek. Verduidelik hoe dit gebeur het.","en":"On a hill a wild fig tree grows out of a crack in a big rock. After many years the rock has broken in two. Explain how this happened."},"steps":[{"af":"’n Saadjie het in die kraak beland waar ’n bietjie grond en water was, en het begin groei.","en":"A seed landed in the crack where there was a little soil and water, and started to grow."},{"af":"Die **wortels** het al dieper in die kraak in gegroei.","en":"The **roots** grew deeper and deeper into the crack."},{"af":"Soos die wortels **dikker** geword het, het hulle teen die kante van die kraak gedruk en dit stadig wyer gemaak.","en":"As the roots got **thicker**, they pushed against the sides of the crack and slowly made it wider."},{"af":"Uiteindelik het die rots gebreek. Dit is **verwering** deur plantwortels.","en":"In the end the rock broke. This is **weathering** by plant roots."}],"answer":{"af":"Die wortels het in die kraak gegroei en dikker geword, die kraak wyer gedruk en die rots laat breek – verwering deur plantwortels.","en":"The roots grew into the crack and got thicker, pushed the crack wider and made the rock break – weathering by plant roots."}},{"title":{"af":"Rotse in die Karoo","en":"Rocks in the Karoo"},"problem":{"af":"In die Karoo reën dit min, maar die rotse kraak en skilfer tog af. Verduidelik hoe dit kan gebeur.","en":"In the Karoo it rains little, but the rocks still crack and flake off. Explain how this can happen."},"steps":[{"af":"In die Karoo is die dae **baie warm** en die nagte **koud**.","en":"In the Karoo the days are **very hot** and the nights are **cold**."},{"af":"Bedags word die buitekant van die rots warm en **sit uit**. Snags koel dit af en **trek saam**.","en":"In the day the outside of the rock gets hot and **expands**. At night it cools down and **contracts**."},{"af":"Dit gebeur elke dag, jaar ná jaar. Die rots word verswak en die buitenste laag kraak en skilfer af.","en":"This happens every day, year after year. The rock is weakened and the outer layer cracks and flakes off."},{"af":"Wind wat sand teen die rotse waai, help ook om hulle af te skuur.","en":"Wind blowing sand against the rocks also helps to wear them down."}],"answer":{"af":"Temperatuurveranderinge (warm dae, koue nagte) laat die rots uitsit en saamtrek totdat dit kraak – met hulp van die wind. Dit is verwering.","en":"Temperature changes (hot days, cold nights) make the rock expand and contract until it cracks – with help from the wind. This is weathering."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Beter groentetuin","en":"A better vegetable garden"},"problem":{"af":"Fatima se groentetuin het ligte, growwe sandgrond. Elke middag hang die plante slap, al lei sy soggens water nat. Waarom gebeur dit, en hoe kan sy die grond verbeter?","en":"Fatima’s vegetable garden has light, rough sandy soil. Every afternoon the plants droop, even though she waters in the morning. Why does this happen, and how can she improve the soil?"},"steps":[{"af":"Sandgrond het **groot korrels** met groot spasies tussen hulle, so water **dreineer vinnig** weg en die grond droog gou uit.","en":"Sandy soil has **large grains** with big spaces between them, so water **drains away quickly** and the soil dries out fast."},{"af":"Sandgrond het ook min **humus**, so daar is min voedingstowwe.","en":"Sandy soil also has little **humus**, so there are few nutrients."},{"af":"Sy kan **kompos** (vrot blare, groenteskille en mis) inwerk. Dit voeg humus by, sodat die grond meer water vashou en vrugbaarder word – meer soos **leem**.","en":"She can dig in **compost** (rotted leaves, vegetable peels and manure). This adds humus, so the soil holds more water and becomes more fertile – more like **loam**."}],"answer":{"af":"Die water dreineer te vinnig deur die sandgrond. Kompos (humus) byvoeg help die grond om water en voedingstowwe vas te hou.","en":"The water drains too quickly through the sandy soil. Adding compost (humus) helps the soil to hold water and nutrients."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is verwering?","en":"What is weathering?"},"options":[{"af":"Wanneer riviere grond na die see toe vervoer","en":"When rivers carry soil to the sea"},{"af":"Wanneer rots stadig in kleiner stukkies opgebreek word","en":"When rock is slowly broken up into smaller pieces"},{"af":"Wanneer die weer elke dag verander","en":"When the weather changes every day"},{"af":"Wanneer plante en diere in die grond vrot","en":"When plants and animals rot in the soil"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Verwering is die afbreek van rots in kleiner stukkies. Om grond weg te vervoer, is erosie, en vrot plante en diere vorm humus.","en":"Weathering is the breaking down of rock into smaller pieces. Carrying soil away is erosion, and rotting plants and animals form humus."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Humus is ontbinde plant- en dieremateriaal wat grond donker en vrugbaar maak.","en":"Humus is decayed plant and animal material that makes soil dark and fertile."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Blare, wortels, mis en dooie diertjies vrot en word humus. Dit gee voedingstowwe aan plante.","en":"True. Leaves, roots, dung and dead small animals rot and become humus. It gives nutrients to plants."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Deur watter grondsoort dreineer water die vinnigste?","en":"Through which type of soil does water drain the fastest?"},"options":[{"af":"Kleigrond","en":"Clay soil"},{"af":"Leemgrond","en":"Loam"},{"af":"Bogrond met baie humus","en":"Topsoil with lots of humus"},{"af":"Sandgrond","en":"Sandy soil"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Sandgrond het groot korrels met groot spasies tussen hulle, so water loop vinnig deur. Klei se deeltjies is baie fyn en hou die water vas.","en":"Sandy soil has large grains with big spaces between them, so water runs through quickly. Clay’s particles are very fine and hold the water."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die buitenste laag van die aarde, wat uit rots bestaan, heet die ___.","en":"The outer layer of the Earth, which is made of rock, is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["kors","aardkors"],"en":["crust","Earth’s crust"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kern","mantel","atmosfeer"],"en":["core","mantle","atmosphere"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die kors is die buitenste laag van die aarde en dit bestaan uit rots. Die atmosfeer is die lug bo die kors.","en":"The crust is the outer layer of the Earth and it is made of rock. The atmosphere is the air above the crust."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe breek ys ’n rots?","en":"How does ice break a rock?"},"options":[{"af":"Water in ’n kraak vries, sit uit en druk die kraak wyer","en":"Water in a crack freezes, expands and pushes the crack wider"},{"af":"Die koue ys los die rots heeltemal op","en":"The cold ice dissolves the rock completely"},{"af":"Die ys maak die rots so swaar dat dit omval","en":"The ice makes the rock so heavy that it falls over"},{"af":"Die ys smelt en die rots word sag soos klei","en":"The ice melts and the rock becomes soft like clay"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Wanneer water vries, sit dit uit (neem meer plek in). Die ys druk teen die kante van die kraak, en ná baie kere breek die rots.","en":"When water freezes, it expands (takes up more space). The ice pushes against the sides of the crack, and after many times the rock breaks."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke oorsaak van verwering by hoe dit rots afbreek.","en":"Match each cause of weathering to how it breaks down rock."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Ys","en":"Ice"},"r":{"af":"Vries in krake, sit uit en druk die krake oop","en":"Freezes in cracks, expands and pushes the cracks open"}},{"l":{"af":"Plantwortels","en":"Plant roots"},"r":{"af":"Groei in krake en druk die rots uitmekaar","en":"Grow into cracks and push the rock apart"}},{"l":{"af":"Wind","en":"Wind"},"r":{"af":"Waai sand teen rotse soos skuurpapier","en":"Blows sand against rocks like sandpaper"}},{"l":{"af":"Temperatuurveranderinge","en":"Temperature changes"},"r":{"af":"Rots sit bedags uit en trek snags saam","en":"Rock expands by day and contracts at night"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke oorsaak breek rots op sy eie manier stadig af: ys en wortels druk krake oop, wind skuur, en hitte en koue laat rots kraak.","en":"Each cause slowly breaks down rock in its own way: ice and roots push cracks open, wind sands, and heat and cold make rock crack."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo wil ’n groentetuin begin. Watter grond is die beste vir die meeste plante?","en":"Thabo wants to start a vegetable garden. Which soil is best for most plants?"},"options":[{"af":"Kleigrond, want dit hou die meeste water","en":"Clay soil, because it holds the most water"},{"af":"Sandgrond, want water loop vinnig deur","en":"Sandy soil, because water runs through quickly"},{"af":"Leemgrond, want dit hou genoeg water en het baie humus","en":"Loam, because it holds enough water and has lots of humus"},{"af":"Gruis, want dit het groot klippe tussen die grond","en":"Gravel, because it has big stones in the soil"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Leem hou genoeg water, maar nie te veel nie, en het baie humus vir voedingstowwe. Klei hou te veel water en lug kan nie by die wortels kom nie; sand droog te gou uit.","en":"Loam holds enough water, but not too much, and has lots of humus for nutrients. Clay holds too much water so air cannot reach the roots; sand dries out too quickly."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die ontbinde plant- en dieremateriaal in die grond heet ___.","en":"The decayed plant and animal material in the soil is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["humus"],"en":["humus"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["klei","leem","kors"],"en":["clay","loam","crust"]}},"explain":{"af":"Humus kom van plante en diere wat vrot. Klei en leem is grondsoorte, en die kors is die rotslaag van die aarde.","en":"Humus comes from plants and animals that rot. Clay and loam are soil types, and the crust is the Earth’s rock layer."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In die dreineringsondersoek wil jy grondsoorte regverdig vergelyk. Wat moet vir elke tregter dieselfde wees?","en":"In the drainage investigation you want to compare soil types fairly. What must be the same for every funnel?"},"options":[{"af":"Die soort grond in die tregter","en":"The type of soil in the funnel"},{"af":"Die hoeveelheid water wat deurloop","en":"The amount of water that runs through"},{"af":"Die hoeveelheid grond en water, en die tyd","en":"The amount of soil and water, and the time"},{"af":"Die kleur van die grond in die tregter","en":"The colour of the soil in the funnel"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die grondsoort is wat jy verander, en die water wat deurloop is wat jy meet. Die hoeveelheid grond en water en die tyd moet dieselfde bly.","en":"The type of soil is what you change, and the water that runs through is what you measure. The amount of soil and water and the time must stay the same."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe lyk kleigrond in die somer wanneer dit lank nie gereën het nie?","en":"What does clay soil look like in summer when it has not rained for a long time?"},"options":[{"af":"Hard en vol krake","en":"Hard and full of cracks"},{"af":"Los en korrelrig soos strandsand","en":"Loose and grainy like beach sand"},{"af":"Donker en krummelrig soos kompos","en":"Dark and crumbly like compost"},{"af":"Sag en taai soos deeg","en":"Soft and sticky like dough"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Klei is taai as dit nat is, maar as dit uitdroog, word dit hard en kraak dit. Los korrels pas by sand, en donker en krummelrig pas by leem.","en":"Clay is sticky when wet, but when it dries out it becomes hard and cracks. Loose grains fit sand, and dark and crumbly fits loam."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Verwering breek ’n groot rots gewoonlik binne ’n paar dae af.","en":"Weathering usually breaks down a big rock within a few days."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Verwering gebeur baie stadig, oor honderde en duisende jare. Daarom neem dit ook so lank vir nuwe grond om te vorm.","en":"False. Weathering happens very slowly, over hundreds and thousands of years. That is also why it takes so long for new soil to form."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is grond met baie humus goed vir plante?","en":"Why is soil with lots of humus good for plants?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit maak die grond so hard soos rots","en":"It makes the soil as hard as rock"},{"af":"Dit laat water baie vinnig wegloop","en":"It makes water run away very quickly"},{"af":"Dit hou alle lug uit die grond uit","en":"It keeps all air out of the soil"},{"af":"Dit bevat voedingstowwe wat plante nodig het","en":"It contains nutrients that plants need"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Humus bevat voedingstowwe en help die grond om water vas te hou, sodat plante goed groei. Wortels het ook lug nodig, so ons wil nie alle lug uithou nie.","en":"Humus contains nutrients and helps the soil hold water, so plants grow well. Roots also need air, so we do not want to keep all air out."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Grond met groot, growwe korrels waardeur water vinnig dreineer, is ___.","en":"Soil with large, rough grains through which water drains quickly is ___."},"answers":{"af":["sandgrond","sand"],"en":["sandy soil","sand"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kleigrond","leemgrond","bogrond"],"en":["clay soil","loam","topsoil"]}},"explain":{"af":"Sandgrond se groot korrels laat groot spasies waardeur water vinnig wegloop. Kleigrond het baie fyn deeltjies en hou water vas.","en":"Sandy soil’s large grains leave big spaces through which water runs away quickly. Clay soil has very fine particles and holds water."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Nomsa gooi 100 ml water oor kleigrond. Ná 5 minute het net 15 ml deurgeloop. Hoeveel water het die klei vasgehou?","en":"Nomsa pours 100 ml of water over clay soil. After 5 minutes only 15 ml has run through. How much water did the clay hold?"},"options":[{"af":"15 ml","en":"15 ml"},{"af":"85 ml","en":"85 ml"},{"af":"100 ml","en":"100 ml"},{"af":"115 ml","en":"115 ml"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die water wat nie deurgeloop het nie, het in die grond agtergebly: 100 ml − 15 ml = 85 ml. 15 ml is net wat deurgeloop het.","en":"The water that did not run through stayed behind in the soil: 100 ml − 15 ml = 85 ml. 15 ml is only what ran through."}}]},{"id":"nwt5-t4-sedimentere-gesteentes","title":{"af":"Sedimentêre gesteentes","en":"Sedimentary rocks"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe sedimentêre gesteentes oor miljoene jare in lae vorm, voorbeelde soos sandsteen, skalie, kalksteen en konglomeraat herken, en sê waarvoor ons hulle gebruik.","en":"You will be able to explain how sedimentary rocks form in layers over millions of years, recognise examples such as sandstone, shale, limestone and conglomerate, and say what we use them for."},"summary":{"af":"## Drie soorte gesteentes\n\nWetenskaplikes deel rotse (**gesteentes**) in drie groepe in:\n\n- **Stollingsgesteentes** vorm wanneer warm, gesmelte rots afkoel en hard word, soos graniet.\n- **Sedimentêre gesteentes** vorm uit lae sediment wat oor miljoene jare saamgepers word.\n- **Metamorfe gesteentes** vorm wanneer ander rotse diep onder die grond deur hitte en druk verander word, soos marmer.\n\nIn hierdie afdeling leer jy van **sedimentêre gesteentes**.\n\n## Hoe sedimentêre gesteente vorm\n\n1. **Verwering** – rotse word in klein stukkies (klippies, sand en modder) opgebreek. Hierdie stukkies heet **sediment**.\n2. **Erosie en vervoer** – riviere, wind en seegolwe dra die sediment weg.\n3. **Afsetting** – waar die water stadiger vloei, soos in ’n meer of die see, sak die sediment na die bodem en vorm ’n **laag**. Die swaarste stukke sak eerste.\n4. **Saampers** – nuwe lae sak bo-op die ou lae. Die gewig druk die onderste lae saam en druk die water uit.\n5. **Sementering** – minerale wat in die water opgelos is, werk soos gom en plak die korrels aan mekaar vas.\n\nDit neem **miljoene jare** voordat die sediment harde rots word.\n\n> **Onthou:** Die onderste laag is eerste neergelê, so dit is die **oudste**. Die boonste laag is die **jongste**.\n\n## Voorbeelde van sedimentêre gesteentes\n\n| Gesteente | Gevorm uit | Gebruike |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sandsteen | Sandkorrels wat saamgesementeer is | Boustene en plaveisel |\n| Skalie (modsteen) | Baie fyn modder en klei; breek in dun plaatjies | Bakstene word van klei en skalie gemaak |\n| Kalksteen | Skulpe en skelette van seediertjies | Om **sement** te maak; boustene |\n| Konglomeraat | Ronde klippies wat met sand saamgesementeer is | Die Witwatersrand se goud word in konglomeraat gevind |\n\nKalksteen **bruis** as jy ’n bietjie asyn daarop drup – so kan jy dit herken. **Steenkool** is ook ’n sedimentêre gesteente: dit het uit lae plantmateriaal gevorm.\n\n## Lae in kranse\n\nOmdat sedimentêre gesteentes in lae vorm, sien jy dikwels **strepe** of **lae** in kranse, klowe en waar paaie deur heuwels gesny is.\n\n- Die kranse van **Tafelberg** in Kaapstad bestaan grootliks uit **sandsteen** wat lank gelede as lae sand neergelê is.\n- In die **Golden Gate**-gebied in die Vrystaat staan groot geel en oranje sandsteenkranse.\n- In die **Karoo** lê sedimentêre lae oor groot afstande, en hulle bevat baie fossiele.\n\nFossiele word byna altyd in sedimentêre gesteentes gevind, want plante en diere is in die sagte sediment begrawe voordat dit rots geword het.\n\n## Maak self lae\n\nSit ’n bietjie gruis, sand en grond in ’n glasfles, gooi water by, maak dit toe en skud dit goed. Laat dit staan. Die **swaar gruis sak eerste** na die bodem, dan die sand, en die fyn modder sak laaste bo-op. So vorm lae ook in ’n meer of die see.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Sediment word nie oornag rots nie – dit neem miljoene jare se saampers en sementering. Moenie ook sê die boonste laag is die oudste nie; dit is die jongste.","en":"## Three kinds of rock\n\nScientists divide rocks into three groups:\n\n- **Igneous rocks** form when hot, melted rock cools down and becomes hard, such as granite.\n- **Sedimentary rocks** form from layers of sediment that are pressed together over millions of years.\n- **Metamorphic rocks** form when other rocks deep under the ground are changed by heat and pressure, such as marble.\n\nIn this section you learn about **sedimentary rocks**.\n\n## How sedimentary rock forms\n\n1. **Weathering** – rocks are broken up into small pieces (pebbles, sand and mud). These pieces are called **sediment**.\n2. **Erosion and transport** – rivers, wind and sea waves carry the sediment away.\n3. **Deposition** – where the water flows more slowly, such as in a lake or the sea, the sediment sinks to the bottom and forms a **layer**. The heaviest pieces sink first.\n4. **Compaction** – new layers settle on top of the old layers. The weight presses the bottom layers together and squeezes the water out.\n5. **Cementation** – minerals dissolved in the water act like glue and stick the grains together.\n\nIt takes **millions of years** before the sediment becomes hard rock.\n\n> **Remember:** The bottom layer was laid down first, so it is the **oldest**. The top layer is the **youngest**.\n\n## Examples of sedimentary rocks\n\n| Rock | Formed from | Uses |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sandstone | Grains of sand cemented together | Building stones and paving |\n| Shale (mudstone) | Very fine mud and clay; breaks into thin sheets | Bricks are made from clay and shale |\n| Limestone | Shells and skeletons of small sea animals | To make **cement**; building stones |\n| Conglomerate | Round pebbles cemented together with sand | The gold of the Witwatersrand is found in conglomerate |\n\nLimestone **fizzes** if you drip a little vinegar on it – that is how you can recognise it. **Coal** is also a sedimentary rock: it formed from layers of plant material.\n\n## Layers in cliffs\n\nBecause sedimentary rocks form in layers, you often see **stripes** or **layers** in cliffs, gorges and where roads have been cut through hills.\n\n- The cliffs of **Table Mountain** in Cape Town are made mostly of **sandstone** that was laid down long ago as layers of sand.\n- In the **Golden Gate** area in the Free State there are large yellow and orange sandstone cliffs.\n- In the **Karoo** sedimentary layers stretch over great distances, and they contain many fossils.\n\nFossils are nearly always found in sedimentary rocks, because plants and animals were buried in the soft sediment before it became rock.\n\n## Make your own layers\n\nPut a little gravel, sand and soil into a glass jar, add water, close it and shake it well. Let it stand. The **heavy gravel sinks first** to the bottom, then the sand, and the fine mud settles last on top. Layers form in the same way in a lake or the sea.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Sediment does not become rock overnight – it takes millions of years of compaction and cementation. Also, do not say the top layer is the oldest; it is the youngest."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Sediment","en":"Sediment"},"def":{"af":"Klein stukkies rots, soos klippies, sand en modder, wat deur water of wind vervoer en neergelê word.","en":"Small pieces of rock, such as pebbles, sand and mud, that are carried and laid down by water or wind."}},{"term":{"af":"Sedimentêre gesteente","en":"Sedimentary rock"},"def":{"af":"Rots wat vorm wanneer lae sediment oor miljoene jare saamgepers en aan mekaar vasgesementeer word.","en":"Rock that forms when layers of sediment are pressed and cemented together over millions of years."}},{"term":{"af":"Erosie","en":"Erosion"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer water, wind of ys stukkies rots en grond wegdra.","en":"When water, wind or ice carries away pieces of rock and soil."}},{"term":{"af":"Afsetting","en":"Deposition"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer sediment na die bodem sak en neergelê word, gewoonlik waar water stadiger vloei.","en":"When sediment sinks to the bottom and is laid down, usually where water flows more slowly."}},{"term":{"af":"Saampers","en":"Compaction"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer die gewig van boonste lae die onderste lae sediment saamdruk en die water uitdruk.","en":"When the weight of the top layers presses the bottom layers of sediment together and squeezes out the water."}},{"term":{"af":"Sementering","en":"Cementation"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer minerale uit die water die korrels sediment soos gom aan mekaar vasplak.","en":"When minerals from the water stick the grains of sediment together like glue."}},{"term":{"af":"Sandsteen","en":"Sandstone"},"def":{"af":"’n Sedimentêre gesteente van sandkorrels wat aan mekaar vasgesementeer is.","en":"A sedimentary rock made of grains of sand cemented together."}},{"term":{"af":"Skalie","en":"Shale"},"def":{"af":"’n Sedimentêre gesteente van baie fyn modder en klei wat in dun plaatjies breek.","en":"A sedimentary rock made of very fine mud and clay that breaks into thin sheets."}},{"term":{"af":"Kalksteen","en":"Limestone"},"def":{"af":"’n Sedimentêre gesteente wat uit skulpe en skelette van seediertjies vorm; dit word gebruik om sement te maak.","en":"A sedimentary rock that forms from shells and skeletons of small sea animals; it is used to make cement."}},{"term":{"af":"Konglomeraat","en":"Conglomerate"},"def":{"af":"’n Sedimentêre gesteente van ronde klippies wat met sand aan mekaar vasgesementeer is.","en":"A sedimentary rock made of round pebbles cemented together with sand."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Sit die stappe in volgorde","en":"Put the steps in order"},"problem":{"af":"Rangskik hierdie stappe in die regte volgorde om te wys hoe sandsteen vorm: saampers; verwering; afsetting; sementering; erosie.","en":"Arrange these steps in the correct order to show how sandstone forms: compaction, weathering, deposition, cementation, erosion."},"steps":[{"af":"Eers moet daar sediment wees: **verwering** breek rots in sandkorrels op.","en":"First there must be sediment: **weathering** breaks rock into grains of sand."},{"af":"Dan moet die sand weggedra word: **erosie** deur riviere of wind.","en":"Then the sand must be carried away: **erosion** by rivers or wind."},{"af":"Waar die water stadiger vloei, sak die sand en vorm ’n laag: **afsetting**.","en":"Where the water flows more slowly, the sand sinks and forms a layer: **deposition**."},{"af":"Nuwe lae druk van bo af: **saampers**. Laastens plak minerale die korrels vas: **sementering**.","en":"New layers press down from above: **compaction**. Finally minerals stick the grains together: **cementation**."}],"answer":{"af":"verwering → erosie → afsetting → saampers → sementering","en":"weathering → erosion → deposition → compaction → cementation"}},{"title":{"af":"Lees die lae in ’n krans","en":"Read the layers in a cliff"},"problem":{"af":"’n Krans het drie lae: bo is sandsteen (laag A), in die middel skalie (laag B) en onder kalksteen vol fossielskulpe (laag C). Watter laag is die oudste? Wat sê laag C oor die gebied lank gelede?","en":"A cliff has three layers: at the top is sandstone (layer A), in the middle shale (layer B) and at the bottom limestone full of fossil shells (layer C). Which layer is the oldest? What does layer C tell us about the area long ago?"},"steps":[{"af":"Lae word van onder na bo neergelê: die onderste laag was eerste daar.","en":"Layers are laid down from the bottom up: the bottom layer was there first."},{"af":"Dus is **laag C** die oudste en **laag A** die jongste.","en":"So **layer C** is the oldest and **layer A** is the youngest."},{"af":"Kalksteen vorm uit skulpe en skelette van **seediertjies**, en laag C het fossielskulpe.","en":"Limestone forms from shells and skeletons of **small sea animals**, and layer C has fossil shells."},{"af":"Dit beteken dat die gebied lank gelede **onder die see** was.","en":"This means that the area was **under the sea** long ago."}],"answer":{"af":"Laag C (die onderste) is die oudste. Die kalksteen met skulpe wys dat die gebied lank gelede onder die see was.","en":"Layer C (the bottom one) is the oldest. The limestone with shells shows that the area was under the sea long ago."}},{"title":{"af":"Herken die gesteente","en":"Identify the rock"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato kry drie rotse: (1) baie fyn korrels wat in dun, plat plaatjies breek; (2) ronde klippies wat aan mekaar vasgeplak lyk, soos beton; (3) ’n ligte grys rots met stukkies skulp wat bruis as sy asyn daarop drup. Benoem elkeen.","en":"Lerato finds three rocks: (1) very fine grains that break into thin, flat sheets; (2) round pebbles that look stuck together, like concrete; (3) a light grey rock with bits of shell that fizzes when she drips vinegar on it. Name each one."},"steps":[{"af":"(1) Fyn modder en klei wat in dun plaatjies breek, is **skalie**.","en":"(1) Fine mud and clay that breaks into thin sheets is **shale**."},{"af":"(2) Ronde klippies wat saamgesementeer is, is **konglomeraat**.","en":"(2) Round pebbles cemented together is **conglomerate**."},{"af":"(3) ’n Rots met skulpe wat met asyn bruis, is **kalksteen**.","en":"(3) A rock with shells that fizzes with vinegar is **limestone**."}],"answer":{"af":"(1) Skalie  (2) Konglomeraat  (3) Kalksteen","en":"(1) Shale  (2) Conglomerate  (3) Limestone"}},{"title":{"af":"Die fles met lae","en":"The jar with layers"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho skud gruis, sand en grond met water in ’n fles en laat dit ’n dag staan. Beskryf die lae van onder na bo, en verduidelik hoe dit wys hoe lae in die see vorm.","en":"Sipho shakes gravel, sand and soil with water in a jar and lets it stand for a day. Describe the layers from the bottom to the top, and explain how this shows how layers form in the sea."},"steps":[{"af":"Die **swaarste** stukke sak die vinnigste: die **gruis** lê onder.","en":"The **heaviest** pieces sink the fastest: the **gravel** lies at the bottom."},{"af":"Dan sak die **sand**, en die fyn **modder** sak laaste en lê bo-op.","en":"Then the **sand** sinks, and the fine **mud** settles last and lies on top."},{"af":"Net so dra ’n rivier sediment na die see. Waar die water stadiger word, sak die sediment en vorm dit lae: **afsetting**.","en":"In the same way a river carries sediment to the sea. Where the water slows down, the sediment sinks and forms layers: **deposition**."}],"answer":{"af":"Onder gruis, dan sand, bo modder. Dit wys afsetting: swaar sediment sak eerste en vorm lae.","en":"Gravel at the bottom, then sand, mud on top. It shows deposition: heavy sediment sinks first and forms layers."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is sediment?","en":"What is sediment?"},"options":[{"af":"Klein stukkies rots, sand en modder wat deur water of wind vervoer word","en":"Small pieces of rock, sand and mud that are carried by water or wind"},{"af":"Gesmelte rots wat diep onder die grond lê","en":"Melted rock that lies deep under the ground"},{"af":"Die gom wat sandkorrels aan mekaar vasplak","en":"The glue that sticks grains of sand together"},{"af":"’n Harde rots wat uit afgekoelde lawa vorm","en":"A hard rock that forms from cooled lava"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Sediment is die klein stukkies wat ná verwering oorbly en deur water of wind weggedra word. Gesmelte rots en lawa vorm stollingsgesteentes.","en":"Sediment is the small pieces left after weathering that are carried away by water or wind. Melted rock and lava form igneous rocks."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In ’n krans met sedimentêre lae is die onderste laag gewoonlik die oudste.","en":"In a cliff with sedimentary layers, the bottom layer is usually the oldest."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die onderste laag is eerste neergelê en die ander lae het later bo-op gekom.","en":"True. The bottom layer was laid down first and the other layers came on top later."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Van watter sedimentêre gesteente word sement hoofsaaklik gemaak?","en":"Which sedimentary rock is cement mainly made from?"},"options":[{"af":"Sandsteen","en":"Sandstone"},{"af":"Skalie","en":"Shale"},{"af":"Kalksteen","en":"Limestone"},{"af":"Konglomeraat","en":"Conglomerate"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Sement word hoofsaaklik van kalksteen gemaak. Sandsteen word as boustene gebruik, en skalie en klei vir bakstene.","en":"Cement is mainly made from limestone. Sandstone is used as building stone, and shale and clay for bricks."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer minerale in die water die korrels sediment soos gom aan mekaar vasplak, heet dit ___.","en":"When minerals in the water stick the grains of sediment together like glue, it is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["sementering"],"en":["cementation"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["verwering","afsetting","erosie"],"en":["weathering","deposition","erosion"]}},"explain":{"af":"Sementering is die laaste stap: die minerale plak die korrels vas sodat dit harde rots word. Afsetting is wanneer die sediment eers na die bodem sak.","en":"Cementation is the last step: the minerals stick the grains together so that it becomes hard rock. Deposition is when the sediment first sinks to the bottom."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Rivier loop in ’n dam in en die water vloei stadiger. Die sand en modder sak na die bodem. Wat noem ons hierdie stap?","en":"A river flows into a dam and the water flows more slowly. The sand and mud sink to the bottom. What do we call this step?"},"options":[{"af":"Verwering","en":"Weathering"},{"af":"Erosie","en":"Erosion"},{"af":"Sementering","en":"Cementation"},{"af":"Afsetting","en":"Deposition"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Wanneer sediment sak en neergelê word, is dit afsetting. Erosie is die wegdra van sediment, en verwering is die afbreek van rots.","en":"When sediment sinks and is laid down, it is deposition. Erosion is the carrying away of sediment, and weathering is the breaking down of rock."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke gesteente by waaruit dit gevorm het.","en":"Match each rock to what it formed from."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Sandsteen","en":"Sandstone"},"r":{"af":"Sandkorrels","en":"Grains of sand"}},{"l":{"af":"Skalie","en":"Shale"},"r":{"af":"Baie fyn modder en klei","en":"Very fine mud and clay"}},{"l":{"af":"Kalksteen","en":"Limestone"},"r":{"af":"Skulpe en skelette van seediertjies","en":"Shells and skeletons of small sea animals"}},{"l":{"af":"Konglomeraat","en":"Conglomerate"},"r":{"af":"Ronde klippies wat saamgesementeer is","en":"Round pebbles cemented together"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke sedimentêre gesteente kry sy naam en voorkoms van die soort sediment waaruit dit gevorm het.","en":"Each sedimentary rock gets its name and look from the kind of sediment it formed from."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo skud gruis, sand en grond met water in ’n fles en laat dit staan. Wat sak eerste na die bodem?","en":"Thabo shakes gravel, sand and soil with water in a jar and lets it stand. What sinks to the bottom first?"},"options":[{"af":"Die fyn modder","en":"The fine mud"},{"af":"Die gruis","en":"The gravel"},{"af":"Alles sak presies gelyk","en":"Everything sinks at exactly the same time"},{"af":"Die sand","en":"The sand"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die swaarste stukke sak die vinnigste, so die gruis lê onder. Die fyn modder sak laaste en vorm die boonste laag.","en":"The heaviest pieces sink the fastest, so the gravel lies at the bottom. The fine mud sinks last and forms the top layer."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe lank neem dit omtrent vir lae sediment om harde sedimentêre gesteente te word?","en":"About how long does it take for layers of sediment to become hard sedimentary rock?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Paar dae","en":"A few days"},{"af":"’n Paar jaar","en":"A few years"},{"af":"’n Paar honderd jaar","en":"A few hundred years"},{"af":"Miljoene jare","en":"Millions of years"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Saampers en sementering gebeur baie stadig. Dit neem miljoene jare voordat sediment harde rots word.","en":"Compaction and cementation happen very slowly. It takes millions of years before sediment becomes hard rock."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die kranse van Tafelberg in Kaapstad bestaan grootliks uit ___.","en":"The cliffs of Table Mountain in Cape Town are made mostly of ___."},"answers":{"af":["sandsteen"],"en":["sandstone"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kalksteen","marmer","steenkool"],"en":["limestone","marble","coal"]}},"explain":{"af":"Tafelberg se kranse is grootliks sandsteen – sand wat lank gelede in lae neergelê en tot rots saamgepers is. Jy kan die lae in die kranse sien.","en":"Table Mountain’s cliffs are mostly sandstone – sand that was laid down in layers long ago and pressed into rock. You can see the layers in the cliffs."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoog teen ’n berg kry Johan ’n laag kalksteen vol fossielskulpe. Wat sê dit vir ons?","en":"High up a mountain Johan finds a layer of limestone full of fossil shells. What does this tell us?"},"options":[{"af":"Mense het lank gelede skulpe daar gaan gooi","en":"People threw shells there long ago"},{"af":"Die skulpe het teen die berg opgekruip","en":"The shells crawled up the mountain"},{"af":"Die gebied was lank gelede onder die see","en":"The area was under the sea long ago"},{"af":"Die berg het uit gesmelte rots gevorm","en":"The mountain formed from melted rock"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Kalksteen vorm uit die skulpe van seediertjies op die seebodem. Die lae is later opgelig, so die gebied was eens onder die see. Gesmelte rots vorm stollingsgesteentes, nie kalksteen nie.","en":"Limestone forms from the shells of small sea animals on the sea floor. The layers were later lifted up, so the area was once under the sea. Melted rock forms igneous rocks, not limestone."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Sedimentêre gesteentes vorm wanneer gesmelte rots afkoel en hard word.","en":"Sedimentary rocks form when melted rock cools down and becomes hard."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Dit is hoe stollingsgesteentes, soos graniet, vorm. Sedimentêre gesteentes vorm uit lae sediment wat saamgepers en gesementeer word.","en":"False. That is how igneous rocks, such as granite, form. Sedimentary rocks form from layers of sediment that are compacted and cemented."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat druk die onderste lae sediment saam?","en":"What presses the bottom layers of sediment together?"},"options":[{"af":"Die gewig van die nuwe lae bo-op","en":"The weight of the new layers on top"},{"af":"Die wind wat oor die see waai","en":"The wind blowing over the sea"},{"af":"Die son wat op die water skyn","en":"The Sun shining on the water"},{"af":"Visse wat op die seebodem swem","en":"Fish swimming on the sea floor"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Elke nuwe laag is swaar. Die gewig druk die onderste lae saam en druk die water uit – dit is saampers.","en":"Every new layer is heavy. The weight presses the bottom layers together and squeezes out the water – this is compaction."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer riviere, wind en seegolwe sediment wegdra, noem ons dit ___.","en":"When rivers, wind and sea waves carry sediment away, we call it ___."},"answers":{"af":["erosie"],"en":["erosion"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["afsetting","sementering","saampers"],"en":["deposition","cementation","compaction"]}},"explain":{"af":"Erosie is die wegdra van sediment. Verwering breek die rots eers op, en afsetting is wanneer die sediment later weer neergelê word.","en":"Erosion is the carrying away of sediment. Weathering first breaks up the rock, and deposition is when the sediment is later laid down again."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ravi kry ’n rots wat soos beton lyk: ronde klippies wat met sand aan mekaar vas is. Watter gesteente is dit?","en":"Ravi finds a rock that looks like concrete: round pebbles stuck together with sand. Which rock is it?"},"options":[{"af":"Skalie","en":"Shale"},{"af":"Konglomeraat","en":"Conglomerate"},{"af":"Kalksteen","en":"Limestone"},{"af":"Marmer","en":"Marble"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Konglomeraat bestaan uit ronde klippies wat saamgesementeer is. Skalie is baie fyn, en marmer is ’n metamorfe gesteente.","en":"Conglomerate is made of round pebbles cemented together. Shale is very fine, and marble is a metamorphic rock."}}]},{"id":"nwt5-t4-fossiele","title":{"af":"Fossiele","en":"Fossils"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik wat ’n fossiel is en hoe dit in sedimentêre gesteente vorm, liggaamsfossiele van spoorfossiele onderskei en belangrike Suid-Afrikaanse fossiele noem.","en":"You will be able to explain what a fossil is and how it forms in sedimentary rock, tell body fossils from trace fossils and name important South African fossils."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is ’n fossiel?\n\n’n **Fossiel** is die **oorblyfsels** of **spore** van ’n plant of dier wat **baie lank gelede** geleef het – duisende of selfs miljoene jare gelede – en wat in rots bewaar gebly het.\n\nDie meeste fossiele is van **harde dele**, soos bene, tande, skulpe en hout. Sagte dele, soos vel en spiere, vrot gewoonlik weg voordat hulle ’n fossiel kan word.\n\n## Hoe ’n fossiel vorm\n\n1. ’n Dier sterf en sy liggaam beland in ’n rivier, ’n meer, die see of modder.\n2. Die **sagte dele vrot** weg; die harde dele (bene, tande, skulp) bly oor.\n3. Die oorblyfsels word vinnig met **sediment** (modder of sand) **toegemaak**. Dit beskerm hulle teen aasdiere en die weer.\n4. Meer lae sediment kom bo-op. Oor **miljoene jare** word die lae saamgepers tot **sedimentêre gesteente**.\n5. Water met **minerale** sypel deur die rots. Die minerale vervang stadig die been, totdat ’n klipkopie van die been oorbly.\n6. Baie later breek **verwering en erosie** die rots af, en die fossiel kom bloot.\n\nDaarom word fossiele byna net in **sedimentêre gesteentes** gevind. In stollingsgesteentes, wat uit warm gesmelte rots vorm, sou die oorblyfsels verbrand het.\n\n## Liggaamsfossiele en spoorfossiele\n\n| Liggaamsfossiele | Spoorfossiele |\n|---|---|\n| Dele van die plant of dier self | Tekens van wat die dier gedoen het |\n| Bene en skelette | Voetspore |\n| Tande | Gate en tonnels wat diere gegrawe het |\n| Skulpe | Eierdoppe en neste |\n| Blare en hout (of hul afdrukke) | Mis |\n\nFossieleiers en -neste tel as spoorfossiele, want hulle wys wat die dier gedoen het: dit het ’n nes gebou en eiers gelê.\n\n> **Onthou:** ’n **Liggaamsfossiel** is ’n deel van die organisme self; ’n **spoorfossiel** is ’n teken van wat dit gedoen het.\n\n## Paleontoloë\n\n**Paleontoloë** is wetenskaplikes wat fossiele bestudeer. Hulle grawe fossiele baie versigtig uit met klein pikke en kwaste, teken presies aan waar elke stuk gelê het, maak dit skoon en vergelyk dit met ander fossiele en met diere van vandag.\n\n## Belangrike Suid-Afrikaanse fossiele\n\n- **Die Karoo** is wêreldberoemd vir fossiele van **soogdieragtige reptiele**. Hierdie diere het eienskappe van reptiele én soogdiere gehad, en baie het al voor die dinosourusse geleef.\n- **Die Wieg van die Mensdom** naby Johannesburg is ’n **Wêrelderfenisgebied** met grotte vol fossiele van **vroeë mensagtiges**. Hier is **Mev Ples** gevind, ’n skedel van meer as 2 miljoen jaar oud, en **Little Foot**, een van die volledigste skelette van ’n vroeë mensagtige wat nog ooit gevind is.\n- **Die Taung-kind** is die skedel van ’n jong kind wat in **1924** naby Taung in Noordwes gevind is. Dit was die eerste fossiel van sy soort en het gewys hoe belangrik Afrika in die verhaal van die mens is.\n- **Die selakant** is ’n vis wat wetenskaplikes net uit fossiele geken het. Hulle het gedink dit is al miljoene jare **uitgesterf**, maar in **1938** is ’n lewende selakant naby Oos-Londen gevang. Daarom noem ons dit ’n **lewende fossiel**.\n\n## Waarom is fossiele belangrik?\n\n- Hulle wys watter plante en diere lank gelede geleef het, ook dié wat nou **uitgesterf** is, soos die dinosourusse.\n- Hulle wys hoe lewende dinge oor baie lang tye **verander** het.\n- Hulle vertel hoe ’n gebied lank gelede was: ’n visfossiel in ’n droë gebied wys dat daar eens water was.\n- In Suid-Afrika word fossiele deur die **wet beskerm**. As jy een kry, los dit waar dit is en vertel ’n museum.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Mense en dinosourusse het **nie** saam geleef nie. Die dinosourusse het miljoene jare voor die eerste mense uitgesterf.","en":"## What is a fossil?\n\nA **fossil** is the **remains** or **traces** of a plant or animal that lived **very long ago** – thousands or even millions of years ago – and that have been preserved in rock.\n\nMost fossils are of **hard parts**, such as bones, teeth, shells and wood. Soft parts, such as skin and muscles, usually rot away before they can become a fossil.\n\n## How a fossil forms\n\n1. An animal dies and its body ends up in a river, a lake, the sea or mud.\n2. The **soft parts rot** away; the hard parts (bones, teeth, shell) are left.\n3. The remains are quickly **covered** with **sediment** (mud or sand). This protects them from scavengers and the weather.\n4. More layers of sediment settle on top. Over **millions of years** the layers are pressed into **sedimentary rock**.\n5. Water with **minerals** seeps through the rock. The minerals slowly replace the bone, until a stone copy of the bone is left.\n6. Much later **weathering and erosion** wear the rock away, and the fossil is exposed.\n\nThat is why fossils are nearly only found in **sedimentary rocks**. In igneous rocks, which form from hot melted rock, the remains would have burnt up.\n\n## Body fossils and trace fossils\n\n| Body fossils | Trace fossils |\n|---|---|\n| Parts of the plant or animal itself | Signs of what the animal did |\n| Bones and skeletons | Footprints |\n| Teeth | Holes and tunnels that animals dug |\n| Shells | Eggshells and nests |\n| Leaves and wood (or their imprints) | Dung |\n\nFossil eggs and nests count as trace fossils, because they show what the animal did: it built a nest and laid eggs.\n\n> **Remember:** A **body fossil** is a part of the organism itself; a **trace fossil** is a sign of what it did.\n\n## Palaeontologists\n\n**Palaeontologists** are scientists who study fossils. They dig fossils out very carefully with small picks and brushes, record exactly where each piece lay, clean it and compare it with other fossils and with animals of today.\n\n## Important South African fossils\n\n- **The Karoo** is world-famous for fossils of **mammal-like reptiles**. These animals had features of reptiles and of mammals, and many lived even before the dinosaurs.\n- **The Cradle of Humankind** near Johannesburg is a **World Heritage Site** with caves full of fossils of **early hominids**. **Mrs Ples** was found here, a skull more than 2 million years old, and **Little Foot**, one of the most complete skeletons of an early hominid ever found.\n- **The Taung Child** is the skull of a young child found in **1924** near Taung in North West. It was the first fossil of its kind and showed how important Africa is in the story of humans.\n- **The coelacanth** is a fish that scientists knew only from fossils. They thought it had been **extinct** for millions of years, but in **1938** a living coelacanth was caught near East London. That is why we call it a **living fossil**.\n\n## Why are fossils important?\n\n- They show which plants and animals lived long ago, including those that are now **extinct**, such as the dinosaurs.\n- They show how living things have **changed** over very long times.\n- They tell us what an area was like long ago: a fish fossil in a dry area shows that there was once water there.\n- In South Africa fossils are **protected by law**. If you find one, leave it where it is and tell a museum.\n\n> **Common mistake:** People and dinosaurs did **not** live at the same time. The dinosaurs died out millions of years before the first people."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Fossiel","en":"Fossil"},"def":{"af":"Die oorblyfsels of spore van ’n plant of dier van baie lank gelede wat in rots bewaar is.","en":"The remains or traces of a plant or animal from very long ago that have been preserved in rock."}},{"term":{"af":"Liggaamsfossiel","en":"Body fossil"},"def":{"af":"’n Fossiel van ’n deel van die plant of dier self, soos ’n been, tand, skulp of blaar.","en":"A fossil of a part of the plant or animal itself, such as a bone, tooth, shell or leaf."}},{"term":{"af":"Spoorfossiel","en":"Trace fossil"},"def":{"af":"’n Fossiel wat wys wat ’n dier gedoen het, soos ’n voetspoor, ’n gat, ’n nes of eierdoppe.","en":"A fossil that shows what an animal did, such as a footprint, a burrow, a nest or eggshells."}},{"term":{"af":"Paleontoloog","en":"Palaeontologist"},"def":{"af":"’n Wetenskaplike wat fossiele uitgrawe en bestudeer.","en":"A scientist who digs up and studies fossils."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitgesterf","en":"Extinct"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n soort plant of dier nie meer op aarde leef nie.","en":"When a kind of plant or animal no longer lives on Earth."}},{"term":{"af":"Lewende fossiel","en":"Living fossil"},"def":{"af":"’n Organisme wat vandag nog leef en baie lyk soos sy fossiele van miljoene jare gelede, soos die selakant.","en":"An organism that still lives today and looks very much like its fossils of millions of years ago, such as the coelacanth."}},{"term":{"af":"Soogdieragtige reptiel","en":"Mammal-like reptile"},"def":{"af":"’n Dier van lank gelede met eienskappe van reptiele en soogdiere; die Karoo het baie van hul fossiele.","en":"An animal from long ago with features of reptiles and mammals; the Karoo has many of their fossils."}},{"term":{"af":"Wieg van die Mensdom","en":"Cradle of Humankind"},"def":{"af":"’n Wêrelderfenisgebied naby Johannesburg met grotte vol fossiele van vroeë mensagtiges.","en":"A World Heritage Site near Johannesburg with caves full of fossils of early hominids."}},{"term":{"af":"Vroeë mensagtige","en":"Early hominid"},"def":{"af":"’n Wese van miljoene jare gelede wat in sommige opsigte soos ’n mens was, soos Mev Ples en Little Foot.","en":"A being from millions of years ago that was like a human in some ways, such as Mrs Ples and Little Foot."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Hoe ’n visfossiel vorm","en":"How a fish fossil forms"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik stap vir stap hoe ’n vis wat miljoene jare gelede in ’n meer gesterf het, ’n fossiel geword het wat Nomsa vandag in ’n rots kan sien.","en":"Explain step by step how a fish that died in a lake millions of years ago became a fossil that Nomsa can see in a rock today."},"steps":[{"af":"Die vis het gesterf en na die bodem van die meer gesak. Die **sagte dele het weggevrot**; die bene het oorgebly.","en":"The fish died and sank to the bottom of the lake. The **soft parts rotted away**; the bones were left."},{"af":"Die bene is vinnig met **modder (sediment)** toegemaak, sodat aasdiere dit nie kon opeet of verstrooi nie.","en":"The bones were quickly covered with **mud (sediment)**, so that scavengers could not eat or scatter them."},{"af":"Oor **miljoene jare** het meer lae bo-op gekom en is die modder tot **sedimentêre gesteente** saamgepers.","en":"Over **millions of years** more layers settled on top and the mud was pressed into **sedimentary rock**."},{"af":"**Minerale** in water het die bene stadig vervang en ’n klipkopie gemaak.","en":"**Minerals** in water slowly replaced the bones and made a stone copy."},{"af":"Later het **verwering en erosie** die rots afgebreek en die fossiel blootgelê.","en":"Later **weathering and erosion** wore the rock away and exposed the fossil."}],"answer":{"af":"Sterf → sagte dele vrot → vinnig met sediment toegemaak → lae word sedimentêre gesteente → minerale vervang die bene → erosie stel die fossiel bloot.","en":"Dies → soft parts rot → quickly covered with sediment → layers become sedimentary rock → minerals replace the bones → erosion exposes the fossil."}},{"title":{"af":"Liggaam of spoor?","en":"Body or trace?"},"problem":{"af":"Sorteer hierdie fossiele as liggaamsfossiele of spoorfossiele: ’n haai se tand; ’n dinosourus se voetspoor; die afdruk van ’n varingblaar; ’n gat wat ’n wurm gegrawe het; fossiel-eierdoppe; ’n seeskulp.","en":"Sort these fossils into body fossils or trace fossils: a shark’s tooth; a dinosaur’s footprint; the imprint of a fern leaf; a hole a worm dug; fossil eggshells; a sea shell."},"steps":[{"af":"Vra by elkeen: is dit ’n **deel van die organisme self**, of ’n **teken van wat dit gedoen het**?","en":"Ask for each one: is it a **part of the organism itself**, or a **sign of what it did**?"},{"af":"Die tand, die blaarafdruk en die skulp is dele (of die vorm) van die organisme self: **liggaamsfossiele**.","en":"The tooth, the leaf imprint and the shell are parts (or the shape) of the organism itself: **body fossils**."},{"af":"Die voetspoor, die wurmgat en die eierdoppe wys wat die dier gedoen het – geloop, gegrawe, eiers gelê: **spoorfossiele**.","en":"The footprint, the worm hole and the eggshells show what the animal did – walked, dug, laid eggs: **trace fossils**."}],"answer":{"af":"Liggaamsfossiele: haai se tand, blaarafdruk, seeskulp. Spoorfossiele: voetspoor, wurmgat, eierdoppe.","en":"Body fossils: shark’s tooth, leaf imprint, sea shell. Trace fossils: footprint, worm hole, eggshells."}},{"title":{"af":"Waar soek ’n paleontoloog?","en":"Where does a palaeontologist look?"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter wil fossiele soek. Hy kan in ’n graniet-koppie soek of in die sandsteen- en skalielae van die Karoo. Waar is sy kans die beste, en waarom?","en":"Pieter wants to look for fossils. He can search on a granite hill or in the sandstone and shale layers of the Karoo. Where is his chance best, and why?"},"steps":[{"af":"Graniet is ’n **stollingsgesteente**: dit het uit warm, gesmelte rots gevorm. Enige plant of dier daarin sou verbrand het.","en":"Granite is an **igneous rock**: it formed from hot, melted rock. Any plant or animal in it would have burnt up."},{"af":"Sandsteen en skalie is **sedimentêre gesteentes**: hulle het uit lae sand en modder gevorm, waarin dooie plante en diere begrawe kon word.","en":"Sandstone and shale are **sedimentary rocks**: they formed from layers of sand and mud, in which dead plants and animals could be buried."},{"af":"Die Karoo is boonop wêreldberoemd vir fossiele van **soogdieragtige reptiele**.","en":"The Karoo is also world-famous for fossils of **mammal-like reptiles**."}],"answer":{"af":"In die Karoo se sedimentêre lae, want fossiele vorm in sediment, nie in gesmelte rots soos graniet nie.","en":"In the Karoo’s sedimentary layers, because fossils form in sediment, not in melted rock such as granite."}},{"title":{"af":"Die selakant as lewende fossiel","en":"The coelacanth as a living fossil"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik waarom die selakant wat in 1938 naby Oos-Londen gevang is, so ’n groot verrassing was, en waarom ons dit ’n lewende fossiel noem.","en":"Explain why the coelacanth caught near East London in 1938 was such a big surprise, and why we call it a living fossil."},"steps":[{"af":"Voor 1938 het wetenskaplikes die selakant net uit **fossiele** van miljoene jare gelede geken.","en":"Before 1938 scientists knew the coelacanth only from **fossils** of millions of years ago."},{"af":"Omdat hulle geen lewende selakante gekry het nie, het hulle gedink dit is al miljoene jare **uitgesterf**.","en":"Because they had not found any living coelacanths, they thought it had been **extinct** for millions of years."},{"af":"Toe word ’n **lewende** selakant gevang. Dit lyk nog baie soos sy fossiele, daarom noem ons dit ’n **lewende fossiel**.","en":"Then a **living** coelacanth was caught. It still looks very much like its fossils, so we call it a **living fossil**."}],"answer":{"af":"Wetenskaplikes het gedink die selakant is lankal uitgesterf, maar dit leef nog en lyk soos sy fossiele – ’n lewende fossiel.","en":"Scientists thought the coelacanth had died out long ago, but it is still alive and looks like its fossils – a living fossil."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is ’n fossiel?","en":"What is a fossil?"},"options":[{"af":"Enige ou klip wat glad en blink is","en":"Any old stone that is smooth and shiny"},{"af":"Die been van ’n koei wat verlede jaar gevrek het","en":"The bone of a cow that died last year"},{"af":"’n Stuk lawa wat baie vinnig afgekoel het","en":"A piece of lava that cooled down very quickly"},{"af":"Oorblyfsels of spore van lank gelede, bewaar in rots","en":"Remains or traces from long ago, preserved in rock"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Fossiel moet van ’n plant of dier van baie lank gelede wees en in rots bewaar wees. ’n Been van verlede jaar is nog nie ’n fossiel nie.","en":"A fossil must be of a plant or animal from very long ago and preserved in rock. A bone from last year is not yet a fossil."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Dinosourus se voetspoor in rots is ’n spoorfossiel.","en":"A dinosaur’s footprint in rock is a trace fossil."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Voetspoor is nie deel van die dier self nie, maar ’n teken van wat die dier gedoen het – dit het daar geloop.","en":"True. A footprint is not part of the animal itself, but a sign of what the animal did – it walked there."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter soort gesteente word fossiele byna altyd gevind?","en":"In which kind of rock are fossils nearly always found?"},"options":[{"af":"Sedimentêre gesteente","en":"Sedimentary rock"},{"af":"Stollingsgesteente","en":"Igneous rock"},{"af":"Gesmelte rots","en":"Melted rock"},{"af":"Graniet","en":"Granite"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Fossiele vorm wanneer plante en diere in sediment begrawe word wat later sedimentêre gesteente word. Graniet is ’n stollingsgesteente uit gesmelte rots.","en":"Fossils form when plants and animals are buried in sediment that later becomes sedimentary rock. Granite is an igneous rock from melted rock."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Wetenskaplike wat fossiele uitgrawe en bestudeer, is ’n ___.","en":"A scientist who digs up and studies fossils is a ___."},"answers":{"af":["paleontoloog"],"en":["palaeontologist","paleontologist"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["geoloog","argeoloog","sterrekundige"],"en":["geologist","archaeologist","astronomer"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Paleontoloog bestudeer fossiele. ’n Geoloog bestudeer rotse in die algemeen, ’n argeoloog bestudeer dinge wat mense lank gelede gemaak het, en ’n sterrekundige bestudeer die sterre.","en":"A palaeontologist studies fossils. A geologist studies rocks in general, an archaeologist studies things that people made long ago, and an astronomer studies the stars."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom moet ’n dooie dier vinnig met sediment toegemaak word om ’n fossiel te word?","en":"Why must a dead animal be covered with sediment quickly to become a fossil?"},"options":[{"af":"Sodat die bene vinniger kan groei","en":"So that the bones can grow faster"},{"af":"Sodat die sagte dele ook ’n fossiel word","en":"So that the soft parts also become a fossil"},{"af":"Om dit teen aasdiere en die weer te beskerm","en":"To protect it from scavengers and the weather"},{"af":"Om dit warm te hou sodat dit smelt","en":"To keep it warm so that it melts"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Sediment bedek die oorblyfsels sodat aasdiere dit nie opeet of verstrooi nie en die weer dit nie afbreek nie. Die sagte dele vrot gewoonlik in elk geval weg.","en":"Sediment covers the remains so that scavengers do not eat or scatter them and the weather does not break them down. The soft parts usually rot away anyway."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke Suid-Afrikaanse fossiel of plek by die regte feit.","en":"Match each South African fossil or place to the correct fact."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Die Karoo","en":"The Karoo"},"r":{"af":"Fossiele van soogdieragtige reptiele","en":"Fossils of mammal-like reptiles"}},{"l":{"af":"Mev Ples","en":"Mrs Ples"},"r":{"af":"’n Skedel uit die Wieg van die Mensdom","en":"A skull from the Cradle of Humankind"}},{"l":{"af":"Die Taung-kind","en":"The Taung Child"},"r":{"af":"’n Kind se skedel wat in 1924 gevind is","en":"A child’s skull found in 1924"}},{"l":{"af":"Die selakant","en":"The coelacanth"},"r":{"af":"’n Lewende fossiel wat in 1938 gevang is","en":"A living fossil caught in 1938"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die Karoo is beroemd vir soogdieragtige reptiele, Mev Ples is in die Wieg van die Mensdom gevind, die Taung-kind in 1924 en die selakant is in 1938 lewend gevang.","en":"The Karoo is famous for mammal-like reptiles, Mrs Ples was found in the Cradle of Humankind, the Taung Child in 1924 and the coelacanth was caught alive in 1938."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van hierdie is ’n liggaamsfossiel?","en":"Which one of these is a body fossil?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Dinosourus se voetspoor","en":"A dinosaur’s footprint"},{"af":"’n Haai se tand","en":"A shark’s tooth"},{"af":"’n Gat wat ’n wurm gegrawe het","en":"A hole that a worm dug"},{"af":"’n Fossielnes met eierdoppe","en":"A fossil nest with eggshells"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die tand is ’n deel van die haai self, dus ’n liggaamsfossiel. Voetspore, gate en neste wys wat ’n dier gedoen het – spoorfossiele.","en":"The tooth is a part of the shark itself, so it is a body fossil. Footprints, holes and nests show what an animal did – trace fossils."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato sien ’n fossiel van ’n vis in ’n rots in ’n droë gebied ver van die see. Wat sê dit vir ons?","en":"Lerato sees a fossil of a fish in a rock in a dry area far from the sea. What does this tell us?"},"options":[{"af":"Visse kon lank gelede op droë land loop","en":"Fish could walk on dry land long ago"},{"af":"Die gebied was lank gelede onder water","en":"The area was under water long ago"},{"af":"Iemand het onlangs ’n vis daar begrawe","en":"Someone buried a fish there recently"},{"af":"Die rots het uit warm lawa gevorm","en":"The rock formed from hot lava"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Visse leef in water, so daar was eens ’n meer, rivier of see. ’n Fossiel is baie oud, nie iets wat onlangs begrawe is nie, en in lawa sou die vis verbrand het.","en":"Fish live in water, so there was once a lake, river or sea. A fossil is very old, not something buried recently, and in lava the fish would have burnt up."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Soort dier wat glad nie meer op aarde leef nie, soos die dinosourusse, is ___.","en":"A kind of animal that no longer lives on Earth at all, like the dinosaurs, is ___."},"answers":{"af":["uitgesterf","uitgestorwe"],"en":["extinct"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["bedreig","versteen","seldsaam"],"en":["endangered","petrified","rare"]}},"explain":{"af":"Uitgesterf beteken daar is geen lewende diere van daardie soort oor nie. ’n Bedreigde of seldsame dier leef nog, maar daar is min van hulle.","en":"Extinct means there are no living animals of that kind left. An endangered or rare animal still lives, but there are few of them."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom kry ons byna nooit fossiele in stollingsgesteentes soos graniet nie?","en":"Why do we almost never find fossils in igneous rocks such as granite?"},"options":[{"af":"Graniet is te hard vir paleontoloë om te breek","en":"Granite is too hard for palaeontologists to break"},{"af":"Graniet lê altyd te diep onder die grond om te grawe","en":"Granite always lies too deep under the ground to dig"},{"af":"Die warm gesmelte rots sou die oorblyfsels verbrand het","en":"The hot melted rock would have burnt up the remains"},{"af":"Graniet vorm net onder die see, waar geen diere is nie","en":"Granite only forms under the sea, where there are no animals"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Stollingsgesteentes vorm uit warm, gesmelte rots wat alle plant- en dieremateriaal sou verbrand. Fossiele bly net in sagte sediment bewaar.","en":"Igneous rocks form from hot, melted rock that would burn up any plant and animal material. Fossils are only preserved in soft sediment."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die eerste mense het saam met die dinosourusse geleef.","en":"The first people lived at the same time as the dinosaurs."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die dinosourusse het miljoene jare voor die eerste mense uitgesterf. Ons weet dit omdat hul fossiele in baie ouer rotslae lê.","en":"False. The dinosaurs died out millions of years before the first people. We know this because their fossils lie in much older rock layers."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Zanele kry op ’n staptoer ’n fossiel wat uit ’n rots steek. Wat moet sy doen?","en":"On a hike Zanele finds a fossil sticking out of a rock. What should she do?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit los waar dit is en ’n museum vertel","en":"Leave it where it is and tell a museum"},{"af":"Dit uitkap en aanlyn verkoop","en":"Chip it out and sell it online"},{"af":"’n Stukkie afbreek om skool toe te neem","en":"Break off a piece to take to school"},{"af":"Dit met verf merk sodat ander dit sien","en":"Mark it with paint so others can see it"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Fossiele word in Suid-Afrika deur die wet beskerm. As jy dit uitkap of beskadig, kan wetenskaplikes nie meer sien hoe en waar dit gelê het nie.","en":"Fossils are protected by law in South Africa. If you chip it out or damage it, scientists can no longer see how and where it lay."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Vis soos die selakant, wat net uit fossiele bekend was en toe lewend gevang is, noem ons ’n ___.","en":"A fish like the coelacanth, which was known only from fossils and was then caught alive, is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["lewende fossiel"],"en":["living fossil"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["spoorfossiel","liggaamsfossiel","paleontoloog"],"en":["trace fossil","body fossil","palaeontologist"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die selakant leef nog en lyk baie soos sy fossiele van miljoene jare gelede, daarom is dit ’n lewende fossiel.","en":"The coelacanth still lives and looks very much like its fossils of millions of years ago, so it is a living fossil."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar is die skedel wat ons Mev Ples noem, gevind?","en":"Where was the skull we call Mrs Ples found?"},"options":[{"af":"In die Karoo","en":"In the Karoo"},{"af":"Naby Oos-Londen","en":"Near East London"},{"af":"Op Tafelberg","en":"On Table Mountain"},{"af":"In die Wieg van die Mensdom","en":"In the Cradle of Humankind"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Mev Ples is in die grotte van die Wieg van die Mensdom naby Johannesburg gevind. Die selakant is naby Oos-Londen gevang, en die Karoo is bekend vir soogdieragtige reptiele.","en":"Mrs Ples was found in the caves of the Cradle of Humankind near Johannesburg. The coelacanth was caught near East London, and the Karoo is known for mammal-like reptiles."}}]}]}]},"geografie":{"id":"geografie","grade":5,"name":{"af":"Geografie","en":"Geography"},"short":{"af":"Geo","en":"Geo"},"icon":"🗺️","color":"#d97706","intro":{"af":"In Graad 5 gaan Geografie oor Suid-Afrika: kaartvaardighede en die provinsies, die land se fisiese kenmerke soos berge, plato’s en riviere, weer en klimaat, en minerale en mynbou. Geografie is saam met Geskiedenis deel van Sosiale Wetenskappe. Die Novembereksamen het gewoonlik kaartwerk, vrae oor tabelle, grafieke en bronne, en kort en langer antwoorde – vra jou onderwyser presies watter onderwerpe ingesluit is.","en":"In Grade 5 Geography is about South Africa: map skills and the provinces, the country’s physical features such as mountains, plateaus and rivers, weather and climate, and minerals and mining. Together with History, Geography is part of Social Sciences. The November exam usually has map work, questions on tables, graphs and sources, and short and longer answers – ask your teacher exactly which topics are included."},"examTips":[{"af":"Lees altyd eers die titel en die sleutel van ’n kaart voordat jy ’n kaartvraag beantwoord.","en":"Always read the title and the key of a map first before you answer a map question."},{"af":"Leer die nege provinsies met hul hoofstede, en oefen om hulle op ’n leë kaart van Suid-Afrika in te vul.","en":"Learn the nine provinces with their capitals, and practise filling them in on a blank map of South Africa."},{"af":"By rigtingvrae: kyk waar noord is, en onthou dat noord of suid altyd eerste kom (noordoos, suidwes).","en":"For direction questions: check where north is, and remember that north or south always comes first (north-east, south-west)."},{"af":"By skaalvrae: meet in sentimeter, vermenigvuldig met die skaal en skryf die eenheid (km of m) by jou antwoord.","en":"For scale questions: measure in centimetres, multiply by the scale and write the unit (km or m) with your answer."},{"af":"By ‘verduidelik’-vrae: gee ’n rede met *omdat* of *want*, bv. ‘Die weste is droog omdat die meeste vog van die Indiese Oseaan in die ooste kom.’","en":"For ‘explain’ questions: give a reason with *because*, e.g. ‘The west is dry because most moisture comes from the Indian Ocean in the east.’"}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"DBE Reënboog-werkboeke","en":"DBE Rainbow Workbooks"},"url":"https://www.education.gov.za/Curriculum/Workbooks.aspx","note":{"af":"Gratis amptelike CAPS-werkboeke van die Departement van Basiese Onderwys, in Afrikaans en Engels. Kyk watter vakke vir Graad 5 beskikbaar is.","en":"Free official CAPS workbooks from the Department of Basic Education, in Afrikaans and English. Check which subjects are available for Grade 5."}},{"title":{"af":"Siyavula: oop handboeke en oefening","en":"Siyavula: open textbooks and practice"},"url":"https://www.siyavula.com","note":{"af":"Gratis oop handboeke en oefenvrae volgens CAPS.","en":"Free open textbooks and practice questions following CAPS."}}],"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Kaartvaardighede: Suid-Afrika","en":"Map skills: South Africa"},"topics":[{"id":"sw5-t1-geo-kaarte-roosters","title":{"af":"Kaarte, simbole, rigtings en roosters","en":"Maps, symbols, directions and grids"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die dele van ’n kaart kan noem, simbole met die sleutel kan lees, die agt kompasrigtings kan gebruik en plekke met ’n roosterverwysing kan vind.","en":"You will be able to name the parts of a map, read symbols using the key, use the eight compass directions and find places with a grid reference."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is ’n kaart?\n\n’n **Kaart** is ’n tekening van ’n plek soos jy dit van **bo af** sien. Dit is baie kleiner as die werklike plek, maar dit wys waar dinge is en hoe ver hulle van mekaar af is.\n\nAs jy reg van bo af na iets kyk, soos ’n voël wat oor jou skool vlieg, sien jy dit uit ’n **voëlvlugperspektief**. Van bo af sien jy net die dakke van huise en die toppe van bome, nie die mure of die stamme nie. Kaarte word uit hierdie perspektief geteken, want dan sien jy die vorm van paaie, velde en geboue en die afstand tussen hulle duidelik.\n\n## Die dele van ’n kaart\n\n| Deel | Wat dit doen |\n|---|---|\n| **Titel** | Sê wat die kaart wys, bv. *Suid-Afrika se provinsies*. |\n| **Sleutel (legende)** | Verduidelik wat elke simbool beteken. |\n| **Noordpyl (kompas)** | Wys waar noord is. |\n| **Skaal** | Wys hoeveel kleiner die kaart is as die werklike plek. |\n| **Rooster** | Lyne met letters en getalle wat jou help om plekke te vind. |\n\n## Simbole\n\nDaar is nie plek om alles op ’n kaart te teken nie. Daarom gebruik ons **simbole**: klein tekeninge, letters of kleure wat iets voorstel.\n\n- **Prentsimbole** lyk soos die ding self, bv. ’n kruisie vir ’n kerk of ’n boompie vir ’n bos.\n- **Lettersimbole** gebruik ’n letter, bv. **H** vir ’n hospitaal of **P** vir parkering.\n- **Kleursimbole** gebruik ’n kleur, bv. **blou** vir water (riviere, damme, die see) en **groen** vir ’n park of bos.\n\n> **Onthou:** Kyk altyd eers na die **sleutel** voordat jy ’n kaart lees. Dieselfde simbool kan op twee kaarte iets anders beteken.\n\n## Kompasrigtings\n\nDie vier **hoofrigtings** is **noord (N)**, **oos (O)**, **suid (S)** en **wes (W)**. Onthou die volgorde kloksgewys met ’n rympie: *Nooit Ontbyt Sonder Wors nie!*\n\nTussen die hoofrigtings lê die vier **tussenrigtings**: **noordoos (NO)**, **suidoos (SO)**, **suidwes (SW)** en **noordwes (NW)**. Noordoos lê presies halfpad tussen noord en oos.\n\nOp die meeste kaarte is **noord bo**. Dan is suid onder, oos regs en wes links. Buite help die son jou: dit kom in die **ooste** op en sak in die **weste**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders skryf soms *oosnoord* of *ON*. By ’n tussenrigting kom **noord of suid altyd eerste**: noordoos (NO), suidwes (SW).\n\n## Roosters en roosterverwysings\n\n’n **Rooster** is lyne wat ’n kaart in blokke verdeel. Die kolomme het **letters** en die rye het **getalle**. ’n **Roosterverwysing** gee eers die **letter** en dan die **getal**, bv. **C2**. Om C2 te vind, gaan af in kolom C tot by ry 2. Die blok waar hulle kruis, is C2.\n\nHier is ’n rooster van ’n klein dorp. Noord is bo, en ry 1 is die boonste ry.\n\n|   | A | B | C | D |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **1** | dam | bos | – | treinstasie |\n| **2** | – | kerk | skool | – |\n| **3** | hospitaal | – | park | winkels |\n\n- Die skool is in blok **C2**.\n- Die dam is in **A1**, links bo, dus in die **noordweste** van die dorp.\n- Van die kerk (B2) na die skool (C2) beweeg jy **oos**.\n- Van die skool (C2) na die winkels (D3) beweeg jy **suidoos**.\n\nMet ’n roosterverwysing kan jy vir iemand presies sê waar iets op ’n kaart is, sonder om lank te verduidelik.","en":"## What is a map?\n\nA **map** is a drawing of a place as you see it from **above**. It is much smaller than the real place, but it shows where things are and how far apart they are.\n\nWhen you look at something from directly above, like a bird flying over your school, you see it from a **bird’s-eye view**. From above you only see the roofs of houses and the tops of trees, not the walls or the trunks. Maps are drawn from this view, because then you can clearly see the shape of roads, fields and buildings and the distance between them.\n\n## The parts of a map\n\n| Part | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **Title** | Says what the map shows, e.g. *The provinces of South Africa*. |\n| **Key (legend)** | Explains what each symbol means. |\n| **North arrow (compass)** | Shows where north is. |\n| **Scale** | Shows how much smaller the map is than the real place. |\n| **Grid** | Lines with letters and numbers that help you find places. |\n\n## Symbols\n\nThere is no space to draw everything on a map. So we use **symbols**: small drawings, letters or colours that stand for something.\n\n- **Picture symbols** look like the thing itself, e.g. a small cross for a church or a little tree for a forest.\n- **Letter symbols** use a letter, e.g. **H** for a hospital or **P** for parking.\n- **Colour symbols** use a colour, e.g. **blue** for water (rivers, dams, the sea) and **green** for a park or forest.\n\n> **Remember:** Always look at the **key** first before you read a map. The same symbol can mean something different on two maps.\n\n## Compass directions\n\nThe four **main directions** are **north (N)**, **east (E)**, **south (S)** and **west (W)**. Remember the clockwise order with a rhyme: *Never Eat Slimy Worms!*\n\nBetween the main directions are the four **intermediate directions**: **north-east (NE)**, **south-east (SE)**, **south-west (SW)** and **north-west (NW)**. North-east lies exactly halfway between north and east.\n\nOn most maps **north is at the top**. Then south is at the bottom, east is on the right and west is on the left. Outside, the sun helps you: it rises in the **east** and sets in the **west**.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners sometimes write *east-north* or *EN*. In an intermediate direction, **north or south always comes first**: north-east (NE), south-west (SW).\n\n## Grids and grid references\n\nA **grid** is lines that divide a map into blocks. The columns have **letters** and the rows have **numbers**. A **grid reference** gives the **letter** first and then the **number**, e.g. **C2**. To find C2, go down column C to row 2. The block where they cross is C2.\n\nHere is a grid of a small town. North is at the top, and row 1 is the top row.\n\n|   | A | B | C | D |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **1** | dam | forest | – | railway station |\n| **2** | – | church | school | – |\n| **3** | hospital | – | park | shops |\n\n- The school is in block **C2**.\n- The dam is in **A1**, top left, so it is in the **north-west** of the town.\n- From the church (B2) to the school (C2) you move **east**.\n- From the school (C2) to the shops (D3) you move **south-east**.\n\nWith a grid reference you can tell someone exactly where something is on a map, without a long explanation."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Kaart","en":"Map"},"def":{"af":"’n Tekening van ’n plek soos dit van bo af lyk, baie kleiner as die werklike plek.","en":"A drawing of a place as it looks from above, much smaller than the real place."}},{"term":{"af":"Voëlvlugperspektief","en":"Bird’s-eye view"},"def":{"af":"Om reg van bo af na iets te kyk, soos ’n voël wat daaroor vlieg.","en":"Looking at something from directly above, like a bird flying over it."}},{"term":{"af":"Titel","en":"Title"},"def":{"af":"Die opskrif van die kaart wat sê wat die kaart wys.","en":"The heading of the map that tells you what the map shows."}},{"term":{"af":"Sleutel (legende)","en":"Key (legend)"},"def":{"af":"Die lys op ’n kaart wat verduidelik wat elke simbool beteken.","en":"The list on a map that explains what each symbol means."}},{"term":{"af":"Simbool","en":"Symbol"},"def":{"af":"’n Klein tekening, letter of kleur wat iets op ’n kaart voorstel.","en":"A small drawing, letter or colour that stands for something on a map."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoofrigtings","en":"Main (cardinal) directions"},"def":{"af":"Die vier belangrikste kompasrigtings: noord, oos, suid en wes.","en":"The four most important compass directions: north, east, south and west."}},{"term":{"af":"Tussenrigtings","en":"Intermediate directions"},"def":{"af":"Die vier rigtings tussen die hoofrigtings: noordoos, suidoos, suidwes en noordwes.","en":"The four directions between the main directions: north-east, south-east, south-west and north-west."}},{"term":{"af":"Rooster","en":"Grid"},"def":{"af":"Lyne wat ’n kaart in blokke verdeel, met letters en getalle langs die kante.","en":"Lines that divide a map into blocks, with letters and numbers along the sides."}},{"term":{"af":"Roosterverwysing","en":"Grid reference"},"def":{"af":"’n Letter en ’n getal, bv. C2, wat sê in watter blok van die rooster iets lê.","en":"A letter and a number, e.g. C2, that tell you in which block of the grid something is."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Vind ’n plek met ’n roosterverwysing","en":"Find a place with a grid reference"},"problem":{"af":"Kyk na die dorpsrooster in die les. (a) Wat is in blok A3? (b) Gee die roosterverwysing van die treinstasie.","en":"Look at the town grid in the lesson. (a) What is in block A3? (b) Give the grid reference of the railway station."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die letter kom eerste: vind kolom **A** (heel links).","en":"(a) The letter comes first: find column **A** (far left)."},{"af":"Gaan in kolom A af tot by ry **3** (die onderste ry). Daar staan *hospitaal*.","en":"Go down column A to row **3** (the bottom row). It says *hospital*."},{"af":"(b) Soek die treinstasie. Dit is in kolom **D** en in ry **1**.","en":"(b) Look for the railway station. It is in column **D** and in row **1**."},{"af":"Skryf eers die letter en dan die getal: **D1**.","en":"Write the letter first and then the number: **D1**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Die hospitaal (b) D1","en":"(a) The hospital (b) D1"}},{"title":{"af":"Gee ’n rigting op die rooster","en":"Give a direction on the grid"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato is by die hospitaal (A3) en wil na die treinstasie (D1) gaan. Noord is bo. In watter rigting moet sy beweeg?","en":"Lerato is at the hospital (A3) and wants to go to the railway station (D1). North is at the top. In which direction must she move?"},"steps":[{"af":"Kyk links/regs: van kolom A na kolom D is na **regs**, en regs is **oos**.","en":"Look left/right: from column A to column D is to the **right**, and right is **east**."},{"af":"Kyk bo/onder: van ry 3 na ry 1 is na **bo**, en bo is **noord**.","en":"Look up/down: from row 3 to row 1 is **up**, and up is **north**."},{"af":"Sit die twee saam. Noord kom eerste: **noordoos**.","en":"Put the two together. North comes first: **north-east**."}],"answer":{"af":"Noordoos (NO)","en":"North-east (NE)"}},{"title":{"af":"Soorte simbole","en":"Kinds of symbols"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho se kaart het die volgende in die sleutel: ’n blou ingekleurde gebied (dam), die letter **P** (parkering) en ’n klein boompie (bos). Watter soort simbool is elkeen?","en":"Sipho’s map has the following in the key: a blue coloured-in area (dam), the letter **P** (parking) and a small tree (forest). What kind of symbol is each one?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die dam word net met ’n **kleur** gewys, dus is dit ’n **kleursimbool**.","en":"The dam is shown only with a **colour**, so it is a **colour symbol**."},{"af":"Parkering word met ’n **letter** gewys, dus is dit ’n **lettersimbool**.","en":"Parking is shown with a **letter**, so it is a **letter symbol**."},{"af":"Die boompie lyk soos die ding wat dit voorstel, dus is dit ’n **prentsimbool**.","en":"The little tree looks like the thing it stands for, so it is a **picture symbol**."}],"answer":{"af":"Dam – kleursimbool; P – lettersimbool; boompie – prentsimbool","en":"Dam – colour symbol; P – letter symbol; little tree – picture symbol"}},{"title":{"af":"Teken uit voëlvlugperspektief","en":"Draw from a bird’s-eye view"},"problem":{"af":"Anika teken haar slaapkamer uit voëlvlugperspektief. Sy het ’n reghoekige bed en ’n ronde tafel met vier pote. Hoe moet sy die bed en die tafel teken?","en":"Anika draws her bedroom from a bird’s-eye view. She has a rectangular bed and a round table with four legs. How must she draw the bed and the table?"},"steps":[{"af":"Voëlvlugperspektief beteken sy kyk **reg van bo af**.","en":"A bird’s-eye view means she looks from **directly above**."},{"af":"Van bo af sien sy net die **bokant** van elke ding: die bed lyk soos ’n reghoek en die tafelblad soos ’n sirkel.","en":"From above she only sees the **top** of each thing: the bed looks like a rectangle and the table top like a circle."},{"af":"Die tafel se pote is onder die tafelblad weggesteek, so sy teken hulle nie.","en":"The table’s legs are hidden under the table top, so she does not draw them."}],"answer":{"af":"Die bed as ’n reghoek en die tafel as ’n sirkel, sonder pote.","en":"The bed as a rectangle and the table as a circle, without legs."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Uit watter perspektief word ’n kaart geteken?","en":"From which view is a map drawn?"},"options":[{"af":"Van die kant af, soos ’n foto van ’n huis se voorkant","en":"From the side, like a photo of the front of a house"},{"af":"Van reg bo af, uit voëlvlugperspektief","en":"From directly above, from a bird’s-eye view"},{"af":"Van onder af, soos ’n mier wat opkyk","en":"From below, like an ant looking up"},{"af":"Skuins van voor af, soos van ’n heuwel af","en":"At a slant from the front, like from a hill"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Kaarte word reg van bo af geteken (voëlvlugperspektief). So kan jy die vorm van paaie en geboue en die afstand tussen hulle sien.","en":"Maps are drawn from directly above (bird’s-eye view). That way you can see the shape of roads and buildings and the distance between them."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter deel van ’n kaart verduidelik wat die simbole beteken?","en":"Which part of a map explains what the symbols mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Die titel","en":"The title"},{"af":"Die skaal","en":"The scale"},{"af":"Die sleutel","en":"The key"},{"af":"Die noordpyl","en":"The north arrow"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die sleutel (legende) lys al die simbole en sê wat elkeen beteken. Die titel sê net waaroor die kaart gaan.","en":"The key (legend) lists all the symbols and says what each one means. The title only says what the map is about."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Noordwes (NW) lê halfpad tussen noord en wes.","en":"North-west (NW) lies halfway between north and west."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Noordwes is ’n tussenrigting: dit lê presies tussen die hoofrigtings noord en wes.","en":"True. North-west is an intermediate direction: it lies exactly between the main directions north and west."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Simbool wat ’n letter gebruik, soos H vir hospitaal, is ’n ___.","en":"A symbol that uses a letter, like H for hospital, is a ___."},"answers":{"af":["lettersimbool"],"en":["letter symbol"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["prentsimbool","kleursimbool","woordsimbool"],"en":["picture symbol","colour symbol","word symbol"]}},"explain":{"af":"H is ’n letter, dus is dit ’n lettersimbool. ’n Prentsimbool lyk soos die ding self, en ’n kleursimbool gebruik ’n kleur.","en":"H is a letter, so it is a letter symbol. A picture symbol looks like the thing itself, and a colour symbol uses a colour."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op ’n kaart is noord bo. Watter rigting is aan die regterkant?","en":"On a map north is at the top. Which direction is on the right-hand side?"},"options":[{"af":"Oos","en":"East"},{"af":"Wes","en":"West"},{"af":"Suid","en":"South"},{"af":"Noordoos","en":"North-east"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"As noord bo is, is oos regs, wes links en suid onder. Noordoos sou regs bo in die hoek wees, nie reg regs nie.","en":"If north is at the top, east is on the right, west on the left and south at the bottom. North-east would be in the top right corner, not straight to the right."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter rigting is die teenoorgestelde van noordoos?","en":"Which direction is the opposite of north-east?"},"options":[{"af":"Suidoos","en":"South-east"},{"af":"Noordwes","en":"North-west"},{"af":"Wes","en":"West"},{"af":"Suidwes","en":"South-west"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die teenoorgestelde van noord is suid en die teenoorgestelde van oos is wes. Dus is die teenoorgestelde van noordoos suidwes.","en":"The opposite of north is south and the opposite of east is west. So the opposite of north-east is south-west."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In die roosterverwysing D4 is D die kolom en 4 die ___.","en":"In the grid reference D4, D is the column and 4 is the ___."},"answers":{"af":["ry"],"en":["row"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kolom","blok","rigting"],"en":["column","block","direction"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die letter gee die kolom en die getal gee die ry. Waar die kolom en die ry kruis, is die blok.","en":"The letter gives the column and the number gives the row. Where the column and the row cross is the block."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke deel van ’n kaart by sy werk.","en":"Match each part of a map to its job."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Titel","en":"Title"},"r":{"af":"Sê waaroor die kaart gaan","en":"Says what the map is about"}},{"l":{"af":"Sleutel","en":"Key"},"r":{"af":"Verduidelik wat die simbole beteken","en":"Explains what the symbols mean"}},{"l":{"af":"Skaal","en":"Scale"},"r":{"af":"Wys hoeveel kleiner die kaart is as die werklike plek","en":"Shows how much smaller the map is than the real place"}},{"l":{"af":"Noordpyl","en":"North arrow"},"r":{"af":"Wys waar noord is","en":"Shows where north is"}},{"l":{"af":"Rooster","en":"Grid"},"r":{"af":"Help jou om plekke met letters en getalle te vind","en":"Helps you find places with letters and numbers"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke deel van die kaart het ’n eie werk. Saam help hulle jou om die kaart reg te lees.","en":"Each part of the map has its own job. Together they help you read the map correctly."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op ’n rooster is noord bo en ry 1 is die boonste ry. Die skool is in C2 en die park in C3. In watter rigting is die park van die skool af?","en":"On a grid north is at the top and row 1 is the top row. The school is in C2 and the park is in C3. In which direction is the park from the school?"},"options":[{"af":"Noord","en":"North"},{"af":"Suid","en":"South"},{"af":"Oos","en":"East"},{"af":"Wes","en":"West"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Albei is in kolom C, so jy beweeg nie oos of wes nie. Ry 3 is onder ry 2, en onder is suid.","en":"Both are in column C, so you do not move east or west. Row 3 is below row 2, and down is south."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In ’n roosterverwysing skryf jy eers die getal en dan die letter, bv. 3B.","en":"In a grid reference you write the number first and then the letter, e.g. 3B."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die letter kom eerste en dan die getal, bv. B3.","en":"False. The letter comes first and then the number, e.g. B3."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van hierdie is ’n kleursimbool?","en":"Which one of these is a colour symbol?"},"options":[{"af":"Die letter H vir ’n hospitaal","en":"The letter H for a hospital"},{"af":"’n Klein kruisie vir ’n kerk","en":"A small cross for a church"},{"af":"’n Boompie-tekening vir ’n bos","en":"A little tree drawing for a forest"},{"af":"’n Blou ingekleurde gebied vir ’n dam","en":"A blue coloured-in area for a dam"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die dam word net met die kleur blou gewys, dus is dit ’n kleursimbool. H is ’n lettersimbool; die kruisie en die boompie is prentsimbole.","en":"The dam is shown only with the colour blue, so it is a colour symbol. H is a letter symbol; the cross and the little tree are picture symbols."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die son kom in die ___ op.","en":"The sun rises in the ___."},"answers":{"af":["ooste","oos"],"en":["east"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["weste","noorde","suide"],"en":["west","north","south"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die son kom in die ooste op en sak in die weste. Dit help jou om buite die rigtings te vind.","en":"The sun rises in the east and sets in the west. This helps you find directions outside."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo is by die winkels in D3 en loop na die dam in A1. Noord is bo, kolom A is links en ry 1 is bo. In watter rigting loop hy?","en":"Thabo is at the shops in D3 and walks to the dam in A1. North is at the top, column A is on the left and row 1 is at the top. In which direction does he walk?"},"options":[{"af":"Noordoos","en":"North-east"},{"af":"Suidwes","en":"South-west"},{"af":"Noordwes","en":"North-west"},{"af":"Suidoos","en":"South-east"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Van D na A is na links (wes) en van ry 3 na ry 1 is na bo (noord). Noord kom eerste: noordwes.","en":"From D to A is to the left (west) and from row 3 to row 1 is up (north). North comes first: north-west."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter tussenrigting lê tussen suid en oos?","en":"Which intermediate direction lies between south and east?"},"options":[{"af":"Suidoos","en":"South-east"},{"af":"Oossuid","en":"East-south"},{"af":"Suidwes","en":"South-west"},{"af":"Noordoos","en":"North-east"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Tussen suid en oos lê suidoos (SO). Daar is nie ’n rigting *oossuid* nie, want suid of noord kom altyd eerste.","en":"Between south and east is south-east (SE). There is no direction *east-south*, because south or north always comes first."}}]},{"id":"sw5-t1-geo-provinsies-skaal","title":{"af":"Suid-Afrika se provinsies en skaal","en":"South Africa’s provinces and scale"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die nege provinsies met hul hoofstede, die land se drie hoofstede, ons buurlande en twee oseane kan noem, en met ’n skaal werklike afstande op ’n kaart kan uitwerk.","en":"You will be able to name the nine provinces and their capitals, the country’s three capitals, our neighbouring countries and two oceans, and work out real distances on a map using a scale."},"summary":{"af":"## Suid-Afrika se nege provinsies\n\nSuid-Afrika is in **nege provinsies** verdeel. Elke provinsie het ’n **hoofstad**, waar die provinsie se regering werk.\n\n| Provinsie | Hoofstad | Waar in Suid-Afrika? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Wes-Kaap | Kaapstad | suidweste, aan die kus |\n| Oos-Kaap | Bhisho | suide en suidooste, aan die kus |\n| Noord-Kaap | Kimberley | weste; die **grootste** provinsie |\n| Vrystaat | Bloemfontein | in die middel van die land |\n| KwaZulu-Natal | Pietermaritzburg | ooste, aan die kus |\n| Gauteng | Johannesburg | binneland; die **kleinste** provinsie |\n| Limpopo | Polokwane | heel in die noorde |\n| Mpumalanga | Mbombela (voorheen Nelspruit) | noordooste |\n| Noordwes | Mahikeng | noorde, langs Botswana |\n\nGauteng is die kleinste provinsie, maar die meeste mense woon daar. Vier provinsies het ’n **kuslyn**: Noord-Kaap, Wes-Kaap, Oos-Kaap en KwaZulu-Natal. Die ander vyf lê in die **binneland**.\n\nHierdie baie eenvoudige rooster wys min of meer waar die provinsies lê (noord is bo):\n\n|   | Wes | Middel | Oos |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Noord** | Noord-Kaap | Noordwes | Limpopo, Gauteng, Mpumalanga |\n| **Middel** | Noord-Kaap | Vrystaat | KwaZulu-Natal |\n| **Suid** | Wes-Kaap | Oos-Kaap | Oos-Kaap |\n\n## Die land se drie hoofstede\n\nSuid-Afrika het **drie hoofstede**. Elkeen het ’n ander werk:\n\n- **Pretoria** (in die stad **Tshwane**): hier werk die **president** en die regering se departemente.\n- **Kaapstad**: hier is die **Parlement**, wat die land se wette maak.\n- **Bloemfontein**: hier is die **Hoogste Hof van Appèl**, een van die land se hoogste howe.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie die land se hoofstede en die provinsies se hoofstede deurmekaar maak nie. Johannesburg is Gauteng se hoofstad, maar dit is **nie** een van die land se drie hoofstede nie. Kaapstad en Bloemfontein is albei: ’n provinsiale hoofstad én een van die land se hoofstede.\n\n## Buurlande en oseane\n\nSuid-Afrika se **buurlande** is:\n\n- **Namibië** in die noordweste, langs die Noord-Kaap\n- **Botswana** in die noorde\n- **Zimbabwe** in die noorde, anderkant die Limpoporivier\n- **Mosambiek** in die noordooste en ooste\n- **Eswatini** in die ooste, tussen Mpumalanga, KwaZulu-Natal en Mosambiek\n- **Lesotho**, wat heeltemal **deur Suid-Afrika omring** word\n\nTwee **oseane** spoel teen ons kus: die **Atlantiese Oseaan** in die weste en die **Indiese Oseaan** in die ooste en suide. Hulle ontmoet mekaar naby **Kaap Agulhas**, die suidelikste punt van Afrika.\n\n## Skaal\n\n’n Kaart is baie kleiner as die werklike plek. Die **skaal** sê hoeveel kleiner. Met die skaal kan jy uitwerk hoe ver plekke werklik van mekaar af is.\n\n- ’n **Woordskaal** gebruik woorde, bv. *1 cm stel 20 km voor*. Elke sentimeter op die kaart is 20 km op die grond.\n- ’n **Lynskaal** lyk soos ’n klein liniaal op die kaart, bv. 0 – 20 – 40 – 60 km, met elke stukkie 1 cm lank.\n\n**Hoe om afstand te meet:**\n\n1. Meet die afstand tussen die twee plekke op die kaart met ’n liniaal (in cm).\n2. Kyk na die skaal: hoeveel kilometer stel 1 cm voor?\n3. Vermenigvuldig: aantal cm × km vir 1 cm.\n\n*Voorbeeld:* Twee dorpe is 6 cm uit mekaar op die kaart en 1 cm stel 20 km voor. 6 × 20 = **120 km**.\n\n**Omskakel:** 1 km = 1 000 m en 1 m = 100 cm. As 1 cm 500 m voorstel, is 4 cm = 2 000 m = **2 km**.\n\n> **Onthou:** Op ’n kaart meet jy die afstand **in ’n reguit lyn**, soos ’n voël vlieg. ’n Pad met draaie is langer as die reguit afstand.","en":"## South Africa’s nine provinces\n\nSouth Africa is divided into **nine provinces**. Each province has a **capital**, where the province’s government works.\n\n| Province | Capital | Where in South Africa? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Western Cape | Cape Town | south-west, on the coast |\n| Eastern Cape | Bhisho | south and south-east, on the coast |\n| Northern Cape | Kimberley | west; the **largest** province |\n| Free State | Bloemfontein | in the middle of the country |\n| KwaZulu-Natal | Pietermaritzburg | east, on the coast |\n| Gauteng | Johannesburg | inland; the **smallest** province |\n| Limpopo | Polokwane | in the far north |\n| Mpumalanga | Mbombela (formerly Nelspruit) | north-east |\n| North West | Mahikeng | north, next to Botswana |\n\nGauteng is the smallest province, but the most people live there. Four provinces have a **coastline**: Northern Cape, Western Cape, Eastern Cape and KwaZulu-Natal. The other five lie in the **interior** (inland).\n\nThis very simple grid shows roughly where the provinces lie (north is at the top):\n\n|   | West | Middle | East |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **North** | Northern Cape | North West | Limpopo, Gauteng, Mpumalanga |\n| **Middle** | Northern Cape | Free State | KwaZulu-Natal |\n| **South** | Western Cape | Eastern Cape | Eastern Cape |\n\n## The country’s three capitals\n\nSouth Africa has **three capitals**. Each one has a different job:\n\n- **Pretoria** (in the city of **Tshwane**): this is where the **President** and the government departments work.\n- **Cape Town**: this is where **Parliament** is, which makes the country’s laws.\n- **Bloemfontein**: this is where the **Supreme Court of Appeal** is, one of the country’s highest courts.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not mix up the country’s capitals and the provinces’ capitals. Johannesburg is the capital of Gauteng, but it is **not** one of the country’s three capitals. Cape Town and Bloemfontein are both: a provincial capital and one of the country’s capitals.\n\n## Neighbouring countries and oceans\n\nSouth Africa’s **neighbouring countries** are:\n\n- **Namibia** in the north-west, next to the Northern Cape\n- **Botswana** in the north\n- **Zimbabwe** in the north, across the Limpopo River\n- **Mozambique** in the north-east and east\n- **Eswatini** in the east, between Mpumalanga, KwaZulu-Natal and Mozambique\n- **Lesotho**, which is completely **surrounded by South Africa**\n\nTwo **oceans** wash against our coast: the **Atlantic Ocean** in the west and the **Indian Ocean** in the east and south. They meet near **Cape Agulhas**, the southernmost point of Africa.\n\n## Scale\n\nA map is much smaller than the real place. The **scale** tells you how much smaller. With the scale you can work out how far apart places really are.\n\n- A **word scale** uses words, e.g. *1 cm represents 20 km*. Every centimetre on the map is 20 km on the ground.\n- A **line scale** looks like a small ruler on the map, e.g. 0 – 20 – 40 – 60 km, with each piece 1 cm long.\n\n**How to measure distance:**\n\n1. Measure the distance between the two places on the map with a ruler (in cm).\n2. Look at the scale: how many kilometres does 1 cm represent?\n3. Multiply: number of cm × km for 1 cm.\n\n*Example:* Two towns are 6 cm apart on the map and 1 cm represents 20 km. 6 × 20 = **120 km**.\n\n**Converting:** 1 km = 1 000 m and 1 m = 100 cm. If 1 cm represents 500 m, then 4 cm = 2 000 m = **2 km**.\n\n> **Remember:** On a map you measure the distance **in a straight line**, as the crow flies. A road with bends is longer than the straight distance."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Provinsie","en":"Province"},"def":{"af":"’n Groot deel van ’n land met sy eie regering; Suid-Afrika het nege.","en":"A large part of a country with its own government; South Africa has nine."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoofstad","en":"Capital"},"def":{"af":"Die stad waar die regering van ’n land of provinsie werk.","en":"The city where the government of a country or province works."}},{"term":{"af":"Buurland","en":"Neighbouring country"},"def":{"af":"’n Land wat ’n grens met ons land deel, soos Botswana of Namibië.","en":"A country that shares a border with our country, such as Botswana or Namibia."}},{"term":{"af":"Kuslyn","en":"Coastline"},"def":{"af":"Die rand van die land waar dit aan die see grens.","en":"The edge of the land where it meets the sea."}},{"term":{"af":"Binneland","en":"Interior (inland)"},"def":{"af":"Die deel van die land wat ver van die see af lê.","en":"The part of the country that lies far from the sea."}},{"term":{"af":"Oseaan","en":"Ocean"},"def":{"af":"’n Baie groot see; die Atlantiese en Indiese Oseaan spoel teen Suid-Afrika se kus.","en":"A very large sea; the Atlantic and Indian Oceans wash against South Africa’s coast."}},{"term":{"af":"Skaal","en":"Scale"},"def":{"af":"Wys hoeveel kleiner ’n kaart is as die werklike plek, sodat jy werklike afstande kan uitwerk.","en":"Shows how much smaller a map is than the real place, so that you can work out real distances."}},{"term":{"af":"Woordskaal","en":"Word scale"},"def":{"af":"’n Skaal in woorde, bv. ‘1 cm stel 20 km voor’.","en":"A scale in words, e.g. ‘1 cm represents 20 km’."}},{"term":{"af":"Lynskaal","en":"Line scale"},"def":{"af":"’n Skaal wat soos ’n klein liniaal lyk, met die werklike afstande daarop gemerk.","en":"A scale that looks like a small ruler, with the real distances marked on it."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Gebruik ’n woordskaal","en":"Use a word scale"},"problem":{"af":"Op ’n kaart stel 1 cm 50 km voor. Johan meet 7 cm tussen twee dorpe. Hoe ver is die dorpe werklik van mekaar af?","en":"On a map 1 cm represents 50 km. Johan measures 7 cm between two towns. How far apart are the towns really?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die skaal sê: elke 1 cm op die kaart = 50 km op die grond.","en":"The scale says: every 1 cm on the map = 50 km on the ground."},{"af":"Johan het 7 cm gemeet, dus is dit 7 keer 50 km.","en":"Johan measured 7 cm, so it is 7 times 50 km."},{"af":"7 × 50 = 350","en":"7 × 50 = 350"}],"answer":{"af":"350 km","en":"350 km"}},{"title":{"af":"Gebruik ’n lynskaal","en":"Use a line scale"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato se kaart van ’n wildtuin het ’n lynskaal: 0 – 10 – 20 – 30 km, met elke stukkie 1 cm lank. Op die kaart is die kamp 4,5 cm van die hek af. Hoe ver is dit werklik?","en":"Lerato’s map of a game reserve has a line scale: 0 – 10 – 20 – 30 km, with each piece 1 cm long. On the map the camp is 4.5 cm from the gate. How far is it really?"},"steps":[{"af":"Lees die lynskaal: elke stukkie van 1 cm stel **10 km** voor.","en":"Read the line scale: each 1 cm piece represents **10 km**."},{"af":"4 cm = 4 × 10 = 40 km.","en":"4 cm = 4 × 10 = 40 km."},{"af":"Die halwe sentimeter (0,5 cm) is die helfte van 10 km = 5 km.","en":"The half centimetre (0.5 cm) is half of 10 km = 5 km."},{"af":"Tel bymekaar: 40 km + 5 km = 45 km.","en":"Add: 40 km + 5 km = 45 km."}],"answer":{"af":"45 km","en":"45 km"}},{"title":{"af":"Skaal en omskakeling","en":"Scale and converting"},"problem":{"af":"Op ’n kaart van Pieter se dorp stel 1 cm 200 m voor. Die skool is 5 cm van sy huis af op die kaart. Hoeveel meter is dit, en hoeveel kilometer?","en":"On a map of Pieter’s town 1 cm represents 200 m. The school is 5 cm from his house on the map. How many metres is that, and how many kilometres?"},"steps":[{"af":"Vermenigvuldig: 5 × 200 m = 1 000 m.","en":"Multiply: 5 × 200 m = 1 000 m."},{"af":"Onthou: 1 000 m = 1 km.","en":"Remember: 1 000 m = 1 km."}],"answer":{"af":"1 000 m, dit is 1 km","en":"1 000 m, which is 1 km"}},{"title":{"af":"Hoofstede en rigting","en":"Capitals and direction"},"problem":{"af":"Fatima ry van Kimberley na Polokwane. (a) Van watter provinsies is hierdie stede die hoofstede? (b) In watter rigting ry sy?","en":"Fatima drives from Kimberley to Polokwane. (a) Of which provinces are these cities the capitals? (b) In which direction does she drive?"},"steps":[{"af":"Kimberley is die hoofstad van die **Noord-Kaap**.","en":"Kimberley is the capital of the **Northern Cape**."},{"af":"Polokwane is die hoofstad van **Limpopo**, die provinsie heel in die noorde.","en":"Polokwane is the capital of **Limpopo**, the province in the far north."},{"af":"Limpopo lê noord en oos van die Noord-Kaap. Noord kom eerste: **noordoos**.","en":"Limpopo lies north and east of the Northern Cape. North comes first: **north-east**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Noord-Kaap en Limpopo (b) Noordoos","en":"(a) Northern Cape and Limpopo (b) North-east"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die hoofstad van KwaZulu-Natal?","en":"What is the capital of KwaZulu-Natal?"},"options":[{"af":"Durban","en":"Durban"},{"af":"Pietermaritzburg","en":"Pietermaritzburg"},{"af":"Bloemfontein","en":"Bloemfontein"},{"af":"Mbombela","en":"Mbombela"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Pietermaritzburg is die hoofstad van KwaZulu-Natal. Durban is die provinsie se grootste stad, maar nie die hoofstad nie.","en":"Pietermaritzburg is the capital of KwaZulu-Natal. Durban is the province’s biggest city, but not the capital."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter provinsie is die grootste?","en":"Which province is the largest?"},"options":[{"af":"Gauteng","en":"Gauteng"},{"af":"Limpopo","en":"Limpopo"},{"af":"Oos-Kaap","en":"Eastern Cape"},{"af":"Noord-Kaap","en":"Northern Cape"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die Noord-Kaap is die grootste provinsie. Gauteng is die kleinste, al woon die meeste mense daar.","en":"The Northern Cape is the largest province. Gauteng is the smallest, even though the most people live there."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die land wat heeltemal deur Suid-Afrika omring word, is ___.","en":"The country that is completely surrounded by South Africa is ___."},"answers":{"af":["Lesotho"],"en":["Lesotho"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Eswatini","Botswana","Namibië"],"en":["Eswatini","Botswana","Namibia"]}},"explain":{"af":"Lesotho lê binne Suid-Afrika. Eswatini lê ook naby, maar dit grens aan Mosambiek ook, so dit is nie heeltemal deur Suid-Afrika omring nie.","en":"Lesotho lies inside South Africa. Eswatini is also close by, but it borders Mozambique too, so it is not completely surrounded by South Africa."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Johannesburg is een van Suid-Afrika se drie hoofstede.","en":"Johannesburg is one of South Africa’s three capitals."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die land se drie hoofstede is Pretoria, Kaapstad en Bloemfontein. Johannesburg is wel die hoofstad van die provinsie Gauteng.","en":"False. The country’s three capitals are Pretoria, Cape Town and Bloemfontein. Johannesburg is, however, the capital of the province of Gauteng."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter oseaan lê aan Suid-Afrika se weskus?","en":"Which ocean lies along South Africa’s west coast?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Indiese Oseaan","en":"The Indian Ocean"},{"af":"Die Stille Oseaan","en":"The Pacific Ocean"},{"af":"Die Atlantiese Oseaan","en":"The Atlantic Ocean"},{"af":"Die Suidelike Oseaan","en":"The Southern Ocean"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die Atlantiese Oseaan is in die weste en die Indiese Oseaan in die ooste en suide. Hulle ontmoet mekaar naby Kaap Agulhas.","en":"The Atlantic Ocean is in the west and the Indian Ocean in the east and south. They meet near Cape Agulhas."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op ’n kaart stel 1 cm 30 km voor. Twee dorpe is 5 cm uit mekaar op die kaart. Hoe ver is hulle werklik van mekaar af?","en":"On a map 1 cm represents 30 km. Two towns are 5 cm apart on the map. How far apart are they really?"},"options":[{"af":"35 km","en":"35 km"},{"af":"150 km","en":"150 km"},{"af":"6 km","en":"6 km"},{"af":"1 500 km","en":"1 500 km"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Vermenigvuldig die aantal sentimeter met die afstand vir 1 cm: 5 × 30 = 150 km. Moenie optel (35) of deel (6) nie.","en":"Multiply the number of centimetres by the distance for 1 cm: 5 × 30 = 150 km. Do not add (35) or divide (6)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke provinsie by sy hoofstad.","en":"Match each province to its capital."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Limpopo","en":"Limpopo"},"r":{"af":"Polokwane","en":"Polokwane"}},{"l":{"af":"Mpumalanga","en":"Mpumalanga"},"r":{"af":"Mbombela","en":"Mbombela"}},{"l":{"af":"Noordwes","en":"North West"},"r":{"af":"Mahikeng","en":"Mahikeng"}},{"l":{"af":"Oos-Kaap","en":"Eastern Cape"},"r":{"af":"Bhisho","en":"Bhisho"}},{"l":{"af":"Vrystaat","en":"Free State"},"r":{"af":"Bloemfontein","en":"Bloemfontein"}}],"explain":{"af":"Leer die nege provinsies saam met hul hoofstede, bv. Limpopo – Polokwane en Mpumalanga – Mbombela.","en":"Learn the nine provinces together with their capitals, e.g. Limpopo – Polokwane and Mpumalanga – Mbombela."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter hoofstad sit die Parlement, wat die land se wette maak?","en":"In which capital does Parliament, which makes the country’s laws, sit?"},"options":[{"af":"Kaapstad","en":"Cape Town"},{"af":"Pretoria","en":"Pretoria"},{"af":"Bloemfontein","en":"Bloemfontein"},{"af":"Johannesburg","en":"Johannesburg"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die Parlement is in Kaapstad. In Pretoria werk die president en die regering se departemente, en in Bloemfontein is die Hoogste Hof van Appèl.","en":"Parliament is in Cape Town. In Pretoria the President and the government departments work, and Bloemfontein has the Supreme Court of Appeal."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Skaal wat sê ‘1 cm stel 10 km voor’, is ’n ___.","en":"A scale that says ‘1 cm represents 10 km’ is a ___."},"answers":{"af":["woordskaal"],"en":["word scale"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["lynskaal","getalskaal","kompasskaal"],"en":["line scale","number scale","compass scale"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die skaal is in woorde geskryf, dus is dit ’n woordskaal. ’n Lynskaal lyk soos ’n klein liniaal.","en":"The scale is written in words, so it is a word scale. A line scale looks like a small ruler."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Gauteng is die kleinste provinsie, maar die meeste mense in Suid-Afrika woon daar.","en":"Gauteng is the smallest province, but the most people in South Africa live there."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Gauteng is klein, maar dit het groot stede soos Johannesburg en Pretoria, so baie mense woon daar.","en":"True. Gauteng is small, but it has big cities such as Johannesburg and Pretoria, so many people live there."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter buurland lê in die noordweste, langs die Noord-Kaap?","en":"Which neighbouring country lies in the north-west, next to the Northern Cape?"},"options":[{"af":"Zimbabwe","en":"Zimbabwe"},{"af":"Mosambiek","en":"Mozambique"},{"af":"Eswatini","en":"Eswatini"},{"af":"Namibië","en":"Namibia"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Namibië lê in die noordweste. Zimbabwe lê in die noorde langs Limpopo, en Mosambiek en Eswatini lê in die ooste.","en":"Namibia lies in the north-west. Zimbabwe lies in the north next to Limpopo, and Mozambique and Eswatini lie in the east."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"1 km = ___ m","en":"1 km = ___ m"},"answers":{"af":["1 000","1000"],"en":["1 000","1000"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["100","10 000","10"],"en":["100","10 000","10"]}},"explain":{"af":"Kilo beteken duisend, dus is 1 kilometer = 1 000 meter. Jy het dit nodig om met skaal af te skakel.","en":"Kilo means thousand, so 1 kilometre = 1 000 metres. You need this to convert when working with scale."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter rigting lê Polokwane van Kaapstad af?","en":"In which direction does Polokwane lie from Cape Town?"},"options":[{"af":"Noordwes","en":"North-west"},{"af":"Suidoos","en":"South-east"},{"af":"Noordoos","en":"North-east"},{"af":"Wes","en":"West"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Kaapstad is in die suidweste en Polokwane in Limpopo heel in die noorde. Om daar te kom, gaan jy noord én oos: noordoos.","en":"Cape Town is in the south-west and Polokwane is in Limpopo in the far north. To get there you go north and east: north-east."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op ’n kaart stel 1 cm 500 m voor. Die park is 6 cm van die skool af op die kaart. Hoe ver is dit werklik?","en":"On a map 1 cm represents 500 m. The park is 6 cm from the school on the map. How far is it really?"},"options":[{"af":"3 km","en":"3 km"},{"af":"30 km","en":"30 km"},{"af":"0,3 km","en":"0.3 km"},{"af":"300 km","en":"300 km"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"6 × 500 m = 3 000 m. Omdat 1 000 m = 1 km, is 3 000 m = 3 km.","en":"6 × 500 m = 3 000 m. Because 1 000 m = 1 km, 3 000 m = 3 km."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Fisiese kenmerke van Suid-Afrika","en":"Physical features of South Africa"},"topics":[{"id":"sw5-t2-geo-landvorme","title":{"af":"Hooglande, laaglande en berge","en":"High land, low land and mountains"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal hoë en lae grond op ’n hoogtekaart kan herken, die kusvlakte, Groot Eskarpement en binnelandse plato kan beskryf, Suid-Afrika se belangrike bergreekse kan noem en verduidelik hoe landvorme mense se lewens raak.","en":"You will be able to recognise high and low land on a height map, describe the coastal plain, Great Escarpment and interior plateau, name South Africa’s important mountain ranges and explain how landforms affect people’s lives."},"summary":{"af":"## Hoë grond en lae grond\n\nDie land is nie oral ewe hoog nie. Ons meet hoogte **bo seespieël**: die vlak van die see is 0 m, en ’n plek se hoogte sê hoeveel meter hoër as die see dit lê. Durban lê aan die kus, naby seespieël, maar Johannesburg lê meer as 1 500 m bo seespieël.\n\nOp ’n **hoogtekaart** wys kleure hoe hoog die land is:\n\n| Kleur | Hoogte |\n|---|---|\n| Donkergroen | baie laag, naby seespieël |\n| Liggroen | laag |\n| Geel | middelmatig hoog |\n| Ligbruin | hoog |\n| Donkerbruin | baie hoog, soos bergtoppe |\n\nBlou wys water, nie hoogte nie. Kyk altyd na die sleutel, want kaarte gebruik nie almal presies dieselfde kleure nie.\n\n## Suid-Afrika se drie groot dele\n\nAs jy van die see af na die middel van die land reis, gaan jy deur drie dele:\n\n| Deel | Hoe dit lyk |\n|---|---|\n| **Kusvlakte** | ’n Strook lae, redelik plat land langs die see. Op sommige plekke is dit breed, op ander baie smal. |\n| **Groot Eskarpement** | ’n Steil rand waar die land skielik baie hoër word. Dit loop in ’n groot boog langs die ooste, suide en weste van die land. |\n| **Binnelandse plato** | ’n Groot, hoë en redelik plat gebied in die middel van die land. |\n\nDie Groot Eskarpement word ook die **Groot Platorand** genoem. Die hoogste en bekendste deel daarvan is die **Drakensberg**, waar sommige pieke meer as 3 000 m hoog is. Ander dele is byvoorbeeld die Sneeuberge en Nuweveldberge in die Karoo. Die hoë, plat grasveld op die plato in Gauteng, die Vrystaat en dele van Mpumalanga en Noordwes heet die **Hoëveld**.\n\n## Bergreekse\n\n’n **Bergreeks** is ’n ry berge wat aan mekaar vas lê.\n\n| Bergreeks | Waar | Iets om te weet |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Drakensberg** | KwaZulu-Natal langs Lesotho, en Mpumalanga | Deel van die Groot Eskarpement; Suid-Afrika se hoogste berge; sneeu in die winter |\n| **Kaapse Plooiberge** | Wes-Kaap en Oos-Kaap | Lang, parallelle rye, bv. die Swartberg, Cederberg en Langeberg. Hulle het lank gelede gevorm toe rotslae gevou (geplooi) is. |\n| **Magaliesberg** | tussen Pretoria en Rustenburg | Lang, smal bergreeks in Gauteng en Noordwes |\n| **Soutpansberg** | Limpopo | Die noordelikste bergreeks in Suid-Afrika |\n\n## Landvorme\n\n| Landvorm | Beskrywing |\n|---|---|\n| **Berg** | Baie hoë land met steil hange en ’n hoë top |\n| **Heuwel** | Hoër as die land rondom, maar laer en ronder as ’n berg; ’n klein heuwel heet ’n **koppie** |\n| **Vallei** | Lae land tussen heuwels of berge, dikwels met ’n rivier daarin |\n| **Plato** | Hoë, plat land met minstens een steil kant |\n| **Vlakte** | Groot, plat stuk land, meestal laag |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** ’n **Plato** en ’n **vlakte** is albei plat. Die verskil is die **hoogte**: ’n plato is **hoog** (soos die Hoëveld), en ’n vlakte is gewoonlik **laag** (soos die kusvlakte).\n\n## Hoe landvorme mense raak\n\n- Op **plat grond** is dit maklik om paaie, huise en plase te bou. Groot stede soos Johannesburg en Pretoria lê op die plato. Die Hoëveld is plat en kry somerreën, so daar word baie **mielies** verbou.\n- **Berge** is steil en koud. Dit is moeilik om daar paaie te bou: paaie gaan oor **passe** of deur tonnels. Berge lok **toeriste** wat stap en klim, en baie **riviere ontspring** in die berge.\n- Op die **kusvlakte** is dit warmer. Daar is hawens, vakansiedorpe en, in KwaZulu-Natal, **suikerrietplase**.\n- **Valleie** het dikwels vrugbare grond en water uit die rivier, so mense boer graag daar.\n\n> **Onthou:** Riviere vloei altyd van **hoë grond na lae grond** – van die berge af na die see.","en":"## High land and low land\n\nThe land is not equally high everywhere. We measure height **above sea level**: the level of the sea is 0 m, and a place’s height tells you how many metres higher than the sea it lies. Durban lies on the coast, close to sea level, but Johannesburg lies more than 1 500 m above sea level.\n\nOn a **height map** colours show how high the land is:\n\n| Colour | Height |\n|---|---|\n| Dark green | very low, close to sea level |\n| Light green | low |\n| Yellow | medium height |\n| Light brown | high |\n| Dark brown | very high, like mountain tops |\n\nBlue shows water, not height. Always look at the key, because not all maps use exactly the same colours.\n\n## South Africa’s three big parts\n\nIf you travel from the sea to the middle of the country, you go through three parts:\n\n| Part | What it looks like |\n|---|---|\n| **Coastal plain** | A strip of low, fairly flat land next to the sea. In some places it is wide, in others very narrow. |\n| **Great Escarpment** | A steep edge where the land suddenly becomes much higher. It runs in a big curve along the east, south and west of the country. |\n| **Interior plateau** | A large, high and fairly flat area in the middle of the country. |\n\nThe highest and best-known part of the Great Escarpment is the **Drakensberg**, where some peaks are more than 3 000 m high. Other parts are, for example, the Sneeuberg and Nuweveld mountains in the Karoo. The high, flat grassland on the plateau in Gauteng, the Free State and parts of Mpumalanga and North West is called the **Highveld**.\n\n## Mountain ranges\n\nA **mountain range** is a row of mountains joined together.\n\n| Mountain range | Where | Something to know |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Drakensberg** | KwaZulu-Natal next to Lesotho, and Mpumalanga | Part of the Great Escarpment; South Africa’s highest mountains; snow in winter |\n| **Cape Fold Mountains** | Western Cape and Eastern Cape | Long, parallel rows, e.g. the Swartberg, Cederberg and Langeberg. They formed long ago when layers of rock were folded. |\n| **Magaliesberg** | between Pretoria and Rustenburg | Long, narrow mountain range in Gauteng and North West |\n| **Soutpansberg** | Limpopo | The most northern mountain range in South Africa |\n\n## Landforms\n\n| Landform | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Mountain** | Very high land with steep slopes and a high top |\n| **Hill** | Higher than the land around it, but lower and rounder than a mountain; a small hill is called a **koppie** |\n| **Valley** | Low land between hills or mountains, often with a river in it |\n| **Plateau** | High, flat land with at least one steep side |\n| **Plain** | A large, flat piece of land, usually low |\n\n> **Common mistake:** A **plateau** and a **plain** are both flat. The difference is the **height**: a plateau is **high** (like the Highveld), and a plain is usually **low** (like the coastal plain).\n\n## How landforms affect people\n\n- On **flat land** it is easy to build roads, houses and farms. Big cities such as Johannesburg and Pretoria lie on the plateau. The Highveld is flat and gets summer rain, so a lot of **maize** is grown there.\n- **Mountains** are steep and cold. It is hard to build roads there: roads go over **passes** or through tunnels. Mountains attract **tourists** who hike and climb, and many **rivers start** in the mountains.\n- On the **coastal plain** it is warmer. There are harbours, holiday towns and, in KwaZulu-Natal, **sugar cane farms**.\n- **Valleys** often have fertile soil and water from the river, so people like to farm there.\n\n> **Remember:** Rivers always flow from **high land to low land** – from the mountains to the sea."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Hoogte bo seespieël","en":"Height above sea level"},"def":{"af":"Hoeveel meter hoër ’n plek lê as die vlak van die see, wat 0 m is.","en":"How many metres higher a place lies than the level of the sea, which is 0 m."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoogtekaart","en":"Height map"},"def":{"af":"’n Kaart wat met kleure wys hoe hoog die land is, van groen (laag) tot bruin (hoog).","en":"A map that uses colours to show how high the land is, from green (low) to brown (high)."}},{"term":{"af":"Binnelandse plato","en":"Interior plateau"},"def":{"af":"Die groot, hoë en redelik plat gebied in die middel van Suid-Afrika.","en":"The large, high and fairly flat area in the middle of South Africa."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoëveld","en":"Highveld"},"def":{"af":"Die hoë, plat grasveld op die binnelandse plato, onder meer in Gauteng en die Vrystaat.","en":"The high, flat grassland on the interior plateau, in places such as Gauteng and the Free State."}},{"term":{"af":"Groot Eskarpement","en":"Great Escarpment"},"def":{"af":"Die steil rand tussen die kusvlakte en die binnelandse plato; die Drakensberg is die hoogste deel daarvan.","en":"The steep edge between the coastal plain and the interior plateau; the Drakensberg is its highest part."}},{"term":{"af":"Kusvlakte","en":"Coastal plain"},"def":{"af":"’n Strook lae, redelik plat land langs die see.","en":"A strip of low, fairly flat land next to the sea."}},{"term":{"af":"Bergreeks","en":"Mountain range"},"def":{"af":"’n Ry berge wat aan mekaar vas lê, soos die Drakensberg.","en":"A row of mountains joined together, like the Drakensberg."}},{"term":{"af":"Vallei","en":"Valley"},"def":{"af":"Lae land tussen heuwels of berge, dikwels met ’n rivier daarin.","en":"Low land between hills or mountains, often with a river in it."}},{"term":{"af":"Plato","en":"Plateau"},"def":{"af":"Hoë, plat land met minstens een steil kant.","en":"High, flat land with at least one steep side."}},{"term":{"af":"Vlakte","en":"Plain"},"def":{"af":"’n Groot, plat stuk land wat gewoonlik laag lê.","en":"A large, flat piece of land that usually lies low."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n hoogtekaart","en":"Read a height map"},"problem":{"af":"Op ’n hoogtekaart van KwaZulu-Natal is die gebied om Durban donkergroen en die Drakensberg donkerbruin. Wat vertel die kleure vir jou oor die land tussen die twee plekke?","en":"On a height map of KwaZulu-Natal the area around Durban is dark green and the Drakensberg is dark brown. What do the colours tell you about the land between the two places?"},"steps":[{"af":"Kyk na die sleutel: groen is laag en bruin is hoog.","en":"Look at the key: green is low and brown is high."},{"af":"Donkergroen by Durban beteken die land is baie laag, naby seespieël – dit is die kusvlakte.","en":"Dark green at Durban means the land is very low, close to sea level – this is the coastal plain."},{"af":"Donkerbruin by die Drakensberg beteken die land is baie hoog – dit is die Groot Eskarpement.","en":"Dark brown at the Drakensberg means the land is very high – this is the Great Escarpment."},{"af":"Die land word dus al hoe hoër hoe verder jy van die see af na die Drakensberg reis.","en":"So the land gets higher and higher the further you travel from the sea towards the Drakensberg."}],"answer":{"af":"Die land styg van laag by die see (Durban) tot baie hoog by die Drakensberg.","en":"The land rises from low at the sea (Durban) to very high at the Drakensberg."}},{"title":{"af":"Die reis van die kus na die binneland","en":"The journey from the coast to the interior"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo ry met die bus van Durban na Bloemfontein. Noem die drie groot dele van die landskap waardeur hy ry, in die regte volgorde, en beskryf elkeen kort.","en":"Thabo travels by bus from Durban to Bloemfontein. Name the three big parts of the landscape he travels through, in the right order, and describe each one briefly."},"steps":[{"af":"Durban lê aan die see, op die **kusvlakte**: lae land naby seespieël. Daarna word dit heuwelagtig.","en":"Durban lies by the sea, on the **coastal plain**: low land close to sea level. After that it becomes hilly."},{"af":"Dan klim die pad teen die **Groot Eskarpement** (hier die Drakensberg) op: ’n steil rand waar die land skielik baie hoër word.","en":"Then the road climbs up the **Great Escarpment** (here the Drakensberg): a steep edge where the land suddenly becomes much higher."},{"af":"Bo-op is hy op die **binnelandse plato**: hoë, redelik plat land. Bloemfontein lê in die Vrystaat op die plato.","en":"At the top he is on the **interior plateau**: high, fairly flat land. Bloemfontein lies in the Free State on the plateau."}],"answer":{"af":"Kusvlakte → Groot Eskarpement → binnelandse plato","en":"Coastal plain → Great Escarpment → interior plateau"}},{"title":{"af":"Plato of vlakte?","en":"Plateau or plain?"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik die verskil tussen ’n plato en ’n vlakte, en gee ’n voorbeeld van elk in Suid-Afrika.","en":"Explain the difference between a plateau and a plain, and give an example of each in South Africa."},"steps":[{"af":"Wat is dieselfde? Albei is groot stukke **plat** land.","en":"What is the same? Both are large pieces of **flat** land."},{"af":"Wat verskil? ’n Plato lê **hoog** en het minstens een steil kant. ’n Vlakte lê gewoonlik **laag**.","en":"What is different? A plateau lies **high** and has at least one steep side. A plain usually lies **low**."},{"af":"Voorbeelde: die **Hoëveld** op die binnelandse plato, en die **kusvlakte** langs die see.","en":"Examples: the **Highveld** on the interior plateau, and the **coastal plain** next to the sea."}],"answer":{"af":"’n Plato is hoog en plat (bv. die Hoëveld); ’n vlakte is laag en plat (bv. die kusvlakte).","en":"A plateau is high and flat (e.g. the Highveld); a plain is low and flat (e.g. the coastal plain)."}},{"title":{"af":"Landvorme en mense","en":"Landforms and people"},"problem":{"af":"Waarom woon daar min mense hoog in die Drakensberg, maar baie mense op die Hoëveld?","en":"Why do few people live high up in the Drakensberg, but many people on the Highveld?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die Drakensberg is **steil** en baie **koud**, met sneeu in die winter. Dit is moeilik om daar paaie, huise en plase te bou.","en":"The Drakensberg is **steep** and very **cold**, with snow in winter. It is hard to build roads, houses and farms there."},{"af":"Die Hoëveld is **plat**, so dit is maklik om stede, paaie en plase te bou. Dit kry somerreën, wat goed is vir mielies.","en":"The Highveld is **flat**, so it is easy to build cities, roads and farms. It gets summer rain, which is good for maize."},{"af":"Daarom het groot stede soos Johannesburg op die plato ontstaan, en nie in die hoë berge nie.","en":"That is why big cities such as Johannesburg grew up on the plateau, and not in the high mountains."}],"answer":{"af":"Die berge is steil en koud en moeilik om op te bou; die Hoëveld is plat en goed vir stede en boerdery.","en":"The mountains are steep and cold and hard to build on; the Highveld is flat and good for cities and farming."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken dit as ’n dorp 1 500 m bo seespieël lê?","en":"What does it mean if a town lies 1 500 m above sea level?"},"options":[{"af":"Die dorp is 1 500 m van die see af","en":"The town is 1 500 m away from the sea"},{"af":"Die dorp is 1 500 m hoër as die vlak van die see","en":"The town is 1 500 m higher than the level of the sea"},{"af":"Die see is 1 500 m diep naby die dorp","en":"The sea is 1 500 m deep near the town"},{"af":"Die dorp is 1 500 m laer as die see","en":"The town is 1 500 m lower than the sea"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Hoogte bo seespieël sê hoe hoog ’n plek is, gemeet vanaf die vlak van die see (0 m). Dit sê niks oor hoe ver die see is nie.","en":"Height above sea level tells you how high a place is, measured from the level of the sea (0 m). It says nothing about how far away the sea is."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die Drakensberg is deel van die Groot Eskarpement.","en":"The Drakensberg is part of the Great Escarpment."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die Drakensberg is die hoogste en bekendste deel van die Groot Eskarpement, die steil rand om die binnelandse plato.","en":"True. The Drakensberg is the highest and best-known part of the Great Escarpment, the steep edge around the interior plateau."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter kleur wys gewoonlik die hoogste grond op ’n hoogtekaart?","en":"Which colour usually shows the highest land on a height map?"},"options":[{"af":"Donkergroen","en":"Dark green"},{"af":"Blou","en":"Blue"},{"af":"Geel","en":"Yellow"},{"af":"Donkerbruin","en":"Dark brown"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die kleure gaan van groen (laag) na geel en bruin (hoog). Donkerbruin wys die hoogste grond. Blou wys water.","en":"The colours go from green (low) to yellow and brown (high). Dark brown shows the highest land. Blue shows water."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die hoë, redelik plat gebied in die middel van Suid-Afrika heet die binnelandse ___.","en":"The high, fairly flat area in the middle of South Africa is called the interior ___."},"answers":{"af":["plato"],"en":["plateau"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vlakte","eskarpement","vallei"],"en":["plain","escarpment","valley"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die binnelandse plato is hoog en plat. ’n Vlakte is gewoonlik laag, en die eskarpement is die steil rand om die plato.","en":"The interior plateau is high and flat. A plain is usually low, and the escarpment is the steep edge around the plateau."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter landvorm is lae land tussen heuwels of berge, dikwels met ’n rivier daarin?","en":"Which landform is low land between hills or mountains, often with a river in it?"},"options":[{"af":"Plato","en":"Plateau"},{"af":"Eskarpement","en":"Escarpment"},{"af":"Kusvlakte","en":"Coastal plain"},{"af":"Vallei","en":"Valley"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Vallei is lae land tussen heuwels of berge. Riviere vloei dikwels deur valleie, want water vloei na die laagste plek.","en":"A valley is low land between hills or mountains. Rivers often flow through valleys, because water flows to the lowest place."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke landvorm by sy beskrywing.","en":"Match each landform to its description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Berg","en":"Mountain"},"r":{"af":"Baie hoë land met steil hange","en":"Very high land with steep slopes"}},{"l":{"af":"Heuwel","en":"Hill"},"r":{"af":"Hoër as die land rondom, maar laer en ronder as ’n berg","en":"Higher than the land around it, but lower and rounder than a mountain"}},{"l":{"af":"Vallei","en":"Valley"},"r":{"af":"Lae land tussen heuwels of berge","en":"Low land between hills or mountains"}},{"l":{"af":"Plato","en":"Plateau"},"r":{"af":"Hoë, plat land met minstens een steil kant","en":"High, flat land with at least one steep side"}},{"l":{"af":"Vlakte","en":"Plain"},"r":{"af":"Groot, plat stuk land wat gewoonlik laag lê","en":"Large, flat piece of land that usually lies low"}}],"explain":{"af":"Let op die hoogte en die vorm: berge en heuwels steek uit, valleie lê laag, en plato’s en vlaktes is plat – hoog of laag.","en":"Look at the height and the shape: mountains and hills stick up, valleys lie low, and plateaus and plains are flat – high or low."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter provinsie is die Soutpansberg?","en":"In which province is the Soutpansberg?"},"options":[{"af":"Limpopo","en":"Limpopo"},{"af":"Wes-Kaap","en":"Western Cape"},{"af":"Vrystaat","en":"Free State"},{"af":"KwaZulu-Natal","en":"KwaZulu-Natal"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die Soutpansberg is in Limpopo; dit is die noordelikste bergreeks in Suid-Afrika. Die Kaapse Plooiberge is in die Wes-Kaap en Oos-Kaap.","en":"The Soutpansberg is in Limpopo; it is the most northern mountain range in South Africa. The Cape Fold Mountains are in the Western Cape and Eastern Cape."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Ry berge wat aan mekaar vas lê, heet ’n ___.","en":"A row of mountains joined together is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["bergreeks"],"en":["mountain range","range"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vallei","plato","kusvlakte"],"en":["valley","plateau","coastal plain"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Bergreeks is ’n hele ry berge, soos die Drakensberg of die Magaliesberg.","en":"A mountain range is a whole row of mountains, like the Drakensberg or the Magaliesberg."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die verskil tussen ’n plato en ’n vlakte?","en":"What is the difference between a plateau and a plain?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Plato het altyd ’n rivier; ’n vlakte het nooit een nie","en":"A plateau always has a river; a plain never has one"},{"af":"’n Plato lê altyd by die see; ’n vlakte in die binneland","en":"A plateau always lies by the sea; a plain lies inland"},{"af":"’n Plato is hoog en plat; ’n vlakte is gewoonlik laag en plat","en":"A plateau is high and flat; a plain is usually low and flat"},{"af":"’n Plato is ’n ry berge; ’n vlakte is een enkele berg","en":"A plateau is a row of mountains; a plain is one single mountain"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Albei is plat; die verskil is die hoogte. Die Hoëveld is ’n voorbeeld van ’n plato, en die kusvlakte is ’n voorbeeld van ’n vlakte.","en":"Both are flat; the difference is the height. The Highveld is an example of a plateau, and the coastal plain is an example of a plain."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter berge het lang, parallelle rye wat gevorm het toe rotslae lank gelede gevou is?","en":"Which mountains have long, parallel rows that formed when layers of rock were folded long ago?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Magaliesberg","en":"The Magaliesberg"},{"af":"Die Soutpansberg","en":"The Soutpansberg"},{"af":"Die Kaapse Plooiberge","en":"The Cape Fold Mountains"},{"af":"Die Drakensberg","en":"The Drakensberg"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die naam sê dit: die Kaapse **Plooi**berge het gevorm toe rotslae geplooi (gevou) is. Voorbeelde is die Swartberg en die Cederberg.","en":"The name tells you: the Cape **Fold** Mountains formed when layers of rock were folded. Examples are the Swartberg and the Cederberg."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die kusvlakte lê hoër as die binnelandse plato.","en":"The coastal plain lies higher than the interior plateau."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die kusvlakte is laag, naby seespieël. Die binnelandse plato is hoog – jy moet teen die Groot Eskarpement uitklim om daar te kom.","en":"False. The coastal plain is low, close to sea level. The interior plateau is high – you have to climb up the Great Escarpment to get there."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Riviere vloei altyd van hoë grond na ___ grond.","en":"Rivers always flow from high land to ___ land."},"answers":{"af":["lae","laer"],"en":["low","lower"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["hoë","rotsagtige","droë"],"en":["high","rocky","dry"]}},"explain":{"af":"Water vloei afdraand. Daarom ontspring riviere in die berge (hoog) en vloei hulle na die see (laag).","en":"Water flows downhill. That is why rivers start in the mountains (high) and flow to the sea (low)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom word daar baie mielies op die Hoëveld verbou?","en":"Why is a lot of maize grown on the Highveld?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is plat en kry somerreën, so dit is goeie boerderygrond","en":"It is flat and gets summer rain, so it is good farmland"},{"af":"Dit lê laag en warm langs die see, net soos die kus","en":"It lies low and warm next to the sea, just like the coast"},{"af":"Dit is baie steil, so die water bly lank op die lande staan","en":"It is very steep, so the water stays on the fields for a long time"},{"af":"Dit is die hoogste bergreeks, waar sneeu die grond natmaak","en":"It is the highest mountain range, where snow wets the soil"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die Hoëveld is deel van die plato: plat land wat in die somer reën kry. Dit is ideaal vir mielies. Dit lê nie by die see nie en is nie ’n bergreeks nie.","en":"The Highveld is part of the plateau: flat land that gets rain in summer. This is ideal for maize. It does not lie by the sea and it is not a mountain range."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo ry van Durban na Bloemfontein. In watter volgorde ry hy deur die drie groot dele van die landskap?","en":"Thabo travels from Durban to Bloemfontein. In which order does he travel through the three big parts of the landscape?"},"options":[{"af":"Plato → eskarpement → kusvlakte","en":"Plateau → escarpment → coastal plain"},{"af":"Kusvlakte → eskarpement → plato","en":"Coastal plain → escarpment → plateau"},{"af":"Eskarpement → kusvlakte → plato","en":"Escarpment → coastal plain → plateau"},{"af":"Kusvlakte → plato → eskarpement","en":"Coastal plain → plateau → escarpment"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Durban lê op die kusvlakte. Die pad klim dan teen die Groot Eskarpement (Drakensberg) uit tot op die binnelandse plato, waar Bloemfontein lê.","en":"Durban lies on the coastal plain. The road then climbs the Great Escarpment (Drakensberg) up to the interior plateau, where Bloemfontein lies."}}]},{"id":"sw5-t2-geo-riviere","title":{"af":"Riviere en damme","en":"Rivers and dams"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die dele van ’n rivier kan benoem, Suid-Afrika se groot riviere en waarheen hulle vloei kan beskryf, kan verduidelik waarom ons damme bou en maniere kan noem om water te bewaar.","en":"You will be able to name the parts of a river, describe South Africa’s big rivers and where they flow, explain why we build dams and name ways to save water."},"summary":{"af":"## Die dele van ’n rivier\n\n’n **Rivier** is water wat in ’n bedding van hoë grond na lae grond vloei. Van bo af lyk ’n rivier met al sy kleiner riviertjies soos die takke van ’n boom.\n\n| Deel | Wat dit is |\n|---|---|\n| **Oorsprong (bron)** | Die plek waar die rivier begin, gewoonlik in die berge |\n| **Loop** | Die pad wat die rivier volg, van sy oorsprong tot by sy monding |\n| **Sytak** | ’n Kleiner rivier wat in ’n groter rivier invloei |\n| **Samevloeiing** | Die plek waar twee riviere bymekaarkom |\n| **Monding** | Die plek waar die rivier in die see (of in ’n ander rivier) invloei |\n| **Opvanggebied** | Al die grond waarvandaan reënwater in die rivier en sy sytakke invloei |\n\n> **Onthou:** ’n Rivier se **oorsprong** lê altyd **hoër** as sy **monding**, want water vloei afdraand.\n\n## Suid-Afrika se groot riviere\n\n| Rivier | Waar dit vloei | Waarin dit uitmond |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Oranje** | Ontspring in die berge van Lesotho en vloei weswaarts oor die land; vorm later die grens met Namibië. Die **langste** rivier in Suid-Afrika. | Atlantiese Oseaan |\n| **Vaal** | Ontspring in Mpumalanga en vloei suidwes. Dit is die grootste **sytak** van die Oranje. | Oranjerivier, in die Noord-Kaap |\n| **Limpopo** | Vorm die grens met Botswana en Zimbabwe en vloei dan deur Mosambiek. | Indiese Oseaan |\n| **Tugela (Thukela)** | Ontspring in die Drakensberg; die grootste rivier in KwaZulu-Natal. | Indiese Oseaan |\n| **Groot-Vis** | Vloei deur die Oos-Kaap. | Indiese Oseaan |\n| **Olifants** | Vloei deur Mpumalanga en Limpopo en deur die Krugerwildtuin. | Limpoporivier, in Mosambiek |\n| **Breë** | Vloei deur die Wes-Kaap. | Indiese Oseaan |\n\n(Daar is ook ’n ander Olifantsrivier in die Wes-Kaap.)\n\nDie meeste riviere vloei óf **oos** na die Indiese Oseaan óf **wes** na die Atlantiese Oseaan. Riviere aan die oostekant is korter: hulle vloei vinnig van die Groot Eskarpement af see toe. In die droë weste vloei baie riviere net ná goeie reën.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders dink soms die **Vaal** is die langste rivier, omdat dit so bekend is. Die **Oranje** is die langste; die Vaal is ’n **sytak** wat in die Oranje invloei.\n\n## Damme\n\n’n **Dam** word gemaak deur ’n sterk muur, die **damwal**, oor ’n rivier te bou. Die water dam agter die wal op en vorm ’n groot meer.\n\nWaarom bou ons damme?\n\n- om water te **stoor** vir droë tye en droogtes\n- om **drinkwater** vir dorpe en stede te gee\n- vir **besproeiing**: boere lei water na hul lande\n- om **elektrisiteit** op te wek: vallende water draai turbines (**hidro-elektrisiteit**)\n- om **vloede** te help beheer\n- vir **ontspanning**, soos visvang en bootry\n\nDie **Gariepdam** op die Oranjerivier is die **grootste dam** in Suid-Afrika. Dit lê op die grens tussen die Vrystaat en die Oos-Kaap. Die **Vaaldam** op die Vaalrivier gee water aan Gauteng.\n\nDamme het ook nadele: plase en diere se lewensruimte raak onder water, en minder water vloei verder af in die rivier.\n\n## Water is skaars – bewaar dit!\n\nSuid-Afrika is ’n **droë land**. Ons kry minder reën as die gemiddeld vir die wêreld, en mense, plase en fabrieke gebruik al hoe meer water. Elke druppel tel. So kan jy water **bewaar**:\n\n- Draai die kraan toe terwyl jy jou tande borsel.\n- Stort kort eerder as om in ’n vol bad te bad.\n- Laat lekkende krane en pype regmaak.\n- Vang reënwater in ’n tenk op en gebruik dit in die tuin.\n- Gee die tuin in die koel oggend of aand water, sodat minder verdamp.\n- Moenie rommel of chemikalieë in riviere gooi nie – besoedelde water is gevaarlik vir mense en diere.","en":"## The parts of a river\n\nA **river** is water that flows in a bed from high land to low land. From above, a river with all its smaller streams looks like the branches of a tree.\n\n| Part | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| **Source** | The place where the river starts, usually in the mountains |\n| **Course** | The path the river follows, from its source to its mouth |\n| **Tributary** | A smaller river that flows into a bigger river |\n| **Confluence** | The place where two rivers meet |\n| **Mouth** | The place where the river flows into the sea (or into another river) |\n| **Catchment area** | All the land from which rainwater flows into the river and its tributaries |\n\n> **Remember:** A river’s **source** always lies **higher** than its **mouth**, because water flows downhill.\n\n## South Africa’s big rivers\n\n| River | Where it flows | Where it ends |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Orange** | Starts in the mountains of Lesotho and flows west across the country; later forms the border with Namibia. The **longest** river in South Africa. | Atlantic Ocean |\n| **Vaal** | Starts in Mpumalanga and flows south-west. It is the biggest **tributary** of the Orange. | Orange River, in the Northern Cape |\n| **Limpopo** | Forms the border with Botswana and Zimbabwe and then flows through Mozambique. | Indian Ocean |\n| **Tugela (Thukela)** | Starts in the Drakensberg; the biggest river in KwaZulu-Natal. | Indian Ocean |\n| **Great Fish** | Flows through the Eastern Cape. | Indian Ocean |\n| **Olifants** | Flows through Mpumalanga and Limpopo and through the Kruger National Park. | Limpopo River, in Mozambique |\n| **Breede** | Flows through the Western Cape. | Indian Ocean |\n\n(There is also a different Olifants River in the Western Cape.)\n\nMost rivers flow either **east** to the Indian Ocean or **west** to the Atlantic Ocean. Rivers on the eastern side are shorter: they flow quickly down from the Great Escarpment to the sea. In the dry west many rivers only flow after good rain.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners sometimes think the **Vaal** is the longest river, because it is so well known. The **Orange** is the longest; the Vaal is a **tributary** that flows into the Orange.\n\n## Dams\n\nA **dam** is made by building a strong wall, the **dam wall**, across a river. The water builds up behind the wall and forms a big lake.\n\nWhy do we build dams?\n\n- to **store** water for dry times and droughts\n- to provide **drinking water** for towns and cities\n- for **irrigation**: farmers lead water to their fields\n- to make **electricity**: falling water turns turbines (**hydro-electricity**)\n- to help control **floods**\n- for **recreation**, such as fishing and boating\n\nThe **Gariep Dam** on the Orange River is the **largest dam** in South Africa. It lies on the border between the Free State and the Eastern Cape. The **Vaal Dam** on the Vaal River supplies water to Gauteng.\n\nDams also have disadvantages: farms and animals’ habitats end up under water, and less water flows further down the river.\n\n## Water is scarce – save it!\n\nSouth Africa is a **dry country**. We get less rain than the average for the world, and people, farms and factories use more and more water. Every drop counts. This is how you can **save** water:\n\n- Turn off the tap while you brush your teeth.\n- Take a short shower rather than a full bath.\n- Have leaking taps and pipes fixed.\n- Catch rainwater in a tank and use it in the garden.\n- Water the garden in the cool morning or evening, so that less evaporates.\n- Do not throw rubbish or chemicals into rivers – polluted water is dangerous for people and animals."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Oorsprong (bron)","en":"Source"},"def":{"af":"Die plek waar ’n rivier begin, gewoonlik hoog in die berge.","en":"The place where a river starts, usually high in the mountains."}},{"term":{"af":"Loop","en":"Course"},"def":{"af":"Die pad wat ’n rivier volg van sy oorsprong tot by sy monding.","en":"The path a river follows from its source to its mouth."}},{"term":{"af":"Sytak","en":"Tributary"},"def":{"af":"’n Kleiner rivier wat in ’n groter rivier invloei, soos die Vaal in die Oranje.","en":"A smaller river that flows into a bigger river, like the Vaal into the Orange."}},{"term":{"af":"Samevloeiing","en":"Confluence"},"def":{"af":"Die plek waar twee riviere bymekaarkom.","en":"The place where two rivers meet."}},{"term":{"af":"Monding","en":"Mouth"},"def":{"af":"Die plek waar ’n rivier in die see of in ’n ander rivier invloei.","en":"The place where a river flows into the sea or into another river."}},{"term":{"af":"Opvanggebied","en":"Catchment area"},"def":{"af":"Al die grond waarvandaan reënwater in ’n rivier en sy sytakke invloei.","en":"All the land from which rainwater flows into a river and its tributaries."}},{"term":{"af":"Dam","en":"Dam"},"def":{"af":"’n Groot meer wat vorm wanneer ’n muur oor ’n rivier gebou word om water te stoor.","en":"A large lake that forms when a wall is built across a river to store water."}},{"term":{"af":"Damwal","en":"Dam wall"},"def":{"af":"Die sterk muur oor ’n rivier wat die water agter hom laat opdam.","en":"The strong wall across a river that makes the water build up behind it."}},{"term":{"af":"Besproeiing","en":"Irrigation"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer boere water uit ’n dam of rivier na hul lande lei om gewasse nat te maak.","en":"When farmers lead water from a dam or river to their fields to water their crops."}},{"term":{"af":"Waterbewaring","en":"Water conservation"},"def":{"af":"Om water te spaar en skoon te hou sodat daar genoeg vir almal is.","en":"Saving water and keeping it clean so that there is enough for everyone."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n riviertekening in woorde","en":"Read a river map in words"},"problem":{"af":"’n Kaart wys: die Vaalrivier begin in Mpumalanga en vloei suidwes. In die Noord-Kaap vloei dit in die Oranjerivier in. Die Oranje begin in Lesotho en vloei weswaarts tot in die Atlantiese Oseaan. (a) Watter rivier is die sytak? (b) Wat noem ons die plek waar die Vaal en die Oranje bymekaarkom? (c) Waar is die Oranje se monding?","en":"A map shows: the Vaal River starts in Mpumalanga and flows south-west. In the Northern Cape it flows into the Orange River. The Orange starts in Lesotho and flows west into the Atlantic Ocean. (a) Which river is the tributary? (b) What do we call the place where the Vaal and the Orange meet? (c) Where is the Orange’s mouth?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) ’n Sytak vloei in ’n groter rivier in. Die Vaal vloei in die Oranje in, dus is die **Vaal** die sytak.","en":"(a) A tributary flows into a bigger river. The Vaal flows into the Orange, so the **Vaal** is the tributary."},{"af":"(b) Die plek waar twee riviere bymekaarkom, is ’n **samevloeiing**. Dit is in die Noord-Kaap.","en":"(b) The place where two rivers meet is a **confluence**. It is in the Northern Cape."},{"af":"(c) Die monding is waar die rivier in die see invloei: die Oranje vloei in die **Atlantiese Oseaan** in, aan die weskus.","en":"(c) The mouth is where the river flows into the sea: the Orange flows into the **Atlantic Ocean**, on the west coast."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Die Vaal (b) ’n Samevloeiing (c) In die Atlantiese Oseaan aan die weskus","en":"(a) The Vaal (b) A confluence (c) In the Atlantic Ocean on the west coast"}},{"title":{"af":"Waarom vloei die Tugela na die ooste?","en":"Why does the Tugela flow east?"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik waarom die Tugelarivier na die Indiese Oseaan vloei en nie na die Atlantiese Oseaan nie.","en":"Explain why the Tugela River flows to the Indian Ocean and not to the Atlantic Ocean."},"steps":[{"af":"Die Tugela **ontspring hoog in die Drakensberg**, op die Groot Eskarpement.","en":"The Tugela **starts high in the Drakensberg**, on the Great Escarpment."},{"af":"Oos van die eskarpement **daal die land steil** na die kus van KwaZulu-Natal.","en":"East of the escarpment the **land drops steeply** to the coast of KwaZulu-Natal."},{"af":"Water vloei altyd **afdraand** na die laagste plek, en die naaste lae grond is die see in die ooste: die Indiese Oseaan.","en":"Water always flows **downhill** to the lowest place, and the nearest low land is the sea in the east: the Indian Ocean."}],"answer":{"af":"Dit begin hoog in die Drakensberg, en die land daal van daar ooswaarts na die Indiese Oseaan.","en":"It starts high in the Drakensberg, and from there the land drops eastwards to the Indian Ocean."}},{"title":{"af":"Voordele en nadele van ’n dam","en":"Advantages and disadvantages of a dam"},"problem":{"af":"Die munisipaliteit wil ’n nuwe dam in ’n rivier bou. Gee drie redes vir die dam en een nadeel.","en":"The municipality wants to build a new dam in a river. Give three reasons for the dam and one disadvantage."},"steps":[{"af":"Dink aan wie water nodig het: mense in die dorp (**drinkwater**) en boere (**besproeiing**).","en":"Think about who needs water: people in the town (**drinking water**) and farmers (**irrigation**)."},{"af":"Dink aan droë tye: die dam **stoor water** vir droogtes en kan help om **vloede** te beheer.","en":"Think about dry times: the dam **stores water** for droughts and can help to control **floods**."},{"af":"Dink aan die nadele: grond en diere se lewensruimte raak **onder water**, en minder water vloei verder af in die rivier.","en":"Think about the disadvantages: land and animals’ habitats end up **under water**, and less water flows further down the river."}],"answer":{"af":"Redes: drinkwater, besproeiing, water stoor vir droogtes (of vloedbeheer). Nadeel: grond en lewensruimte raak onder water.","en":"Reasons: drinking water, irrigation, storing water for droughts (or flood control). Disadvantage: land and habitats end up under water."}},{"title":{"af":"Hoeveel water mors ’n oop kraan?","en":"How much water does an open tap waste?"},"problem":{"af":"Ravi laat die kraan 2 minute lank loop terwyl hy sy tande borsel, twee keer per dag. Die kraan gee 6 liter per minuut. Hoeveel water mors hy per dag en per week?","en":"Ravi leaves the tap running for 2 minutes while he brushes his teeth, twice a day. The tap gives 6 litres per minute. How much water does he waste per day and per week?"},"steps":[{"af":"Een keer borsel: 2 minute × 6 liter = 12 liter.","en":"One brushing: 2 minutes × 6 litres = 12 litres."},{"af":"Twee keer per dag: 2 × 12 liter = 24 liter per dag.","en":"Twice a day: 2 × 12 litres = 24 litres per day."},{"af":"’n Week het 7 dae: 7 × 24 liter = 168 liter per week.","en":"A week has 7 days: 7 × 24 litres = 168 litres per week."},{"af":"As hy die kraan toedraai terwyl hy borsel, spaar hy byna al hierdie water.","en":"If he turns off the tap while he brushes, he saves almost all of this water."}],"answer":{"af":"24 liter per dag en 168 liter per week","en":"24 litres per day and 168 litres per week"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is ’n sytak?","en":"What is a tributary?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Kleiner rivier wat in ’n groter rivier invloei","en":"A smaller river that flows into a bigger river"},{"af":"Die plek waar ’n rivier in die see invloei","en":"The place where a river flows into the sea"},{"af":"Die plek hoog in die berge waar ’n rivier begin","en":"The place high in the mountains where a river starts"},{"af":"’n Sterk muur wat oor ’n rivier gebou word","en":"A strong wall that is built across a river"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Sytak is ’n kleiner rivier wat in ’n groter rivier invloei, soos die Vaal in die Oranje. Die ander opsies beskryf die monding, die oorsprong en ’n damwal.","en":"A tributary is a smaller river that flows into a bigger river, like the Vaal into the Orange. The other options describe the mouth, the source and a dam wall."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter rivier is die langste in Suid-Afrika?","en":"Which river is the longest in South Africa?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Vaal","en":"The Vaal"},{"af":"Die Limpopo","en":"The Limpopo"},{"af":"Die Oranje","en":"The Orange"},{"af":"Die Tugela","en":"The Tugela"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die Oranje is die langste rivier. Dit begin in Lesotho en vloei oor die hele land tot in die Atlantiese Oseaan. Die Vaal is net ’n sytak daarvan.","en":"The Orange is the longest river. It starts in Lesotho and flows across the whole country into the Atlantic Ocean. The Vaal is only a tributary of it."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die Vaalrivier is ’n sytak van die Oranjerivier.","en":"The Vaal River is a tributary of the Orange River."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die Vaal vloei in die Noord-Kaap by die Oranje in. Dit is die Oranje se grootste sytak.","en":"True. The Vaal flows into the Orange in the Northern Cape. It is the Orange’s biggest tributary."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die plek waar ’n rivier in die see invloei, is sy ___.","en":"The place where a river flows into the sea is its ___."},"answers":{"af":["monding"],"en":["mouth"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["oorsprong","sytak","samevloeiing"],"en":["source","tributary","confluence"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die monding is aan die einde van die rivier se loop, by die see. Die oorsprong is aan die begin, hoog in die berge.","en":"The mouth is at the end of the river’s course, at the sea. The source is at the beginning, high in the mountains."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter oseaan vloei die Oranjerivier uit?","en":"Into which ocean does the Orange River flow?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Indiese Oseaan","en":"The Indian Ocean"},{"af":"Die Atlantiese Oseaan","en":"The Atlantic Ocean"},{"af":"Die Suidelike Oseaan","en":"The Southern Ocean"},{"af":"Die Stille Oseaan","en":"The Pacific Ocean"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die Oranje vloei weswaarts en mond aan die weskus in die Atlantiese Oseaan uit, waar dit die grens met Namibië vorm. Riviere soos die Tugela vloei oos na die Indiese Oseaan.","en":"The Orange flows west and reaches the Atlantic Ocean on the west coast, where it forms the border with Namibia. Rivers like the Tugela flow east to the Indian Ocean."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke deel van ’n rivier by sy beskrywing.","en":"Match each part of a river to its description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Oorsprong","en":"Source"},"r":{"af":"Waar die rivier begin","en":"Where the river starts"}},{"l":{"af":"Sytak","en":"Tributary"},"r":{"af":"Kleiner rivier wat in ’n groter rivier invloei","en":"Smaller river that flows into a bigger river"}},{"l":{"af":"Samevloeiing","en":"Confluence"},"r":{"af":"Waar twee riviere bymekaarkom","en":"Where two rivers meet"}},{"l":{"af":"Monding","en":"Mouth"},"r":{"af":"Waar die rivier in die see invloei","en":"Where the river flows into the sea"}},{"l":{"af":"Opvanggebied","en":"Catchment area"},"r":{"af":"Al die grond waarvandaan reënwater in die rivier vloei","en":"All the land from which rainwater flows into the river"}}],"explain":{"af":"Volg ’n rivier van begin tot einde: oorsprong → loop (met sytakke en samevloeiings) → monding. Die opvanggebied is al die grond wat water na die rivier stuur.","en":"Follow a river from start to end: source → course (with tributaries and confluences) → mouth. The catchment area is all the land that sends water to the river."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter dam is die grootste in Suid-Afrika?","en":"Which dam is the largest in South Africa?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Vaaldam","en":"The Vaal Dam"},{"af":"Die Hartbeespoortdam","en":"The Hartbeespoort Dam"},{"af":"Die Clanwilliamdam","en":"The Clanwilliam Dam"},{"af":"Die Gariepdam","en":"The Gariep Dam"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die Gariepdam op die Oranjerivier, op die grens van die Vrystaat en die Oos-Kaap, is die grootste dam. Die Vaaldam is belangrik vir Gauteng, maar dit is kleiner.","en":"The Gariep Dam on the Orange River, on the border of the Free State and the Eastern Cape, is the largest dam. The Vaal Dam is important for Gauteng, but it is smaller."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Boere lei water uit ’n dam na hul lande om gewasse nat te maak. Dit heet ___.","en":"Farmers lead water from a dam to their fields to water their crops. This is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["besproeiing"],"en":["irrigation"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["verdamping","besoedeling","oorstroming"],"en":["evaporation","pollution","flooding"]}},"explain":{"af":"Besproeiing is wanneer boere water na hul lande lei. Dit is een van die hoofredes waarom ons damme bou.","en":"Irrigation is when farmers lead water to their fields. It is one of the main reasons why we build dams."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter rivier vorm die grens tussen Suid-Afrika en Zimbabwe?","en":"Which river forms the border between South Africa and Zimbabwe?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Oranje","en":"The Orange"},{"af":"Die Vaal","en":"The Vaal"},{"af":"Die Limpopo","en":"The Limpopo"},{"af":"Die Olifants","en":"The Olifants"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die Limpopo vorm die grens met Botswana en Zimbabwe in die noorde. Die Oranje vorm die grens met Namibië in die weste.","en":"The Limpopo forms the border with Botswana and Zimbabwe in the north. The Orange forms the border with Namibia in the west."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Suid-Afrika het baie water, so ons hoef nie water te spaar nie.","en":"South Africa has plenty of water, so we do not need to save water."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Suid-Afrika is ’n droë land wat minder reën kry as die wêreldgemiddeld. Almal moet water spaar.","en":"False. South Africa is a dry country that gets less rain than the world average. Everyone must save water."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom vloei die meeste riviere in KwaZulu-Natal na die ooste?","en":"Why do most rivers in KwaZulu-Natal flow to the east?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle begin hoog in die Drakensberg, en die land daal ooswaarts na die see","en":"They start high in the Drakensberg, and the land drops eastwards to the sea"},{"af":"Die wind waai die water elke dag ooswaarts na die see toe","en":"The wind blows the water eastwards to the sea every day"},{"af":"Die Atlantiese Oseaan lê aan die oostekant van die provinsie","en":"The Atlantic Ocean lies on the eastern side of the province"},{"af":"Die land is in die ooste by die see hoër as in die berge","en":"The land in the east by the sea is higher than in the mountains"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Water vloei afdraand. Die riviere ontspring hoog in die Drakensberg en vloei na die laer land by die Indiese Oseaan in die ooste.","en":"Water flows downhill. The rivers start high in the Drakensberg and flow to the lower land by the Indian Ocean in the east."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die plek waar twee riviere bymekaarkom, heet ’n ___.","en":"The place where two rivers meet is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["samevloeiing"],"en":["confluence"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["sytak","oorsprong","opvanggebied"],"en":["tributary","source","catchment area"]}},"explain":{"af":"By ’n samevloeiing kom twee riviere bymekaar, bv. waar die Vaal by die Oranje invloei. ’n Sytak is die kleiner rivier self, nie die plek waar die twee riviere bymekaarkom nie.","en":"At a confluence two rivers meet, e.g. where the Vaal flows into the Orange. A tributary is the smaller river itself, not the place where the two rivers meet."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter gewoonte help om water te bewaar?","en":"Which habit helps to save water?"},"options":[{"af":"Gee die tuin water in die middag as dit die warmste is","en":"Water the garden at midday when it is hottest"},{"af":"Stort kort eerder as om in ’n vol bad te bad","en":"Take a short shower rather than a full bath"},{"af":"Laat die kraan loop terwyl jy jou tande borsel","en":"Leave the tap running while you brush your teeth"},{"af":"Was die motor elke dag met ’n oop tuinslang","en":"Wash the car every day with an open hosepipe"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Kort stort gebruik minder water as ’n vol bad. In die middag verdamp tuinwater vinnig, en ’n oop kraan of tuinslang mors baie water.","en":"A short shower uses less water than a full bath. At midday garden water evaporates quickly, and an open tap or hosepipe wastes a lot of water."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vallende water uit ’n dam draai turbines en maak elektrisiteit. Wat noem ons hierdie soort elektrisiteit?","en":"Falling water from a dam turns turbines and makes electricity. What do we call this kind of electricity?"},"options":[{"af":"Sonkrag","en":"Solar power"},{"af":"Windkrag","en":"Wind power"},{"af":"Steenkoolkrag","en":"Coal power"},{"af":"Hidro-elektrisiteit","en":"Hydro-electricity"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Hidro* het met water te doen. Hidro-elektrisiteit word gemaak deur vallende water wat turbines draai – dit is een rede waarom ons damme bou.","en":"*Hydro* has to do with water. Hydro-electricity is made by falling water turning turbines – this is one reason why we build dams."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Weer en klimaat","en":"Weather and climate"},"topics":[{"id":"sw5-t3-geo-weer","title":{"af":"Weer en weervoorspellings","en":"Weather and weather forecasts"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die weerelemente en die instrumente wat hulle meet kan noem, weersimbole en ’n weervoorspelling kan lees en jou eie weerkaart kan hou.","en":"You will be able to name the weather elements and the instruments that measure them, read weather symbols and a weather forecast, and keep your own weather chart."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is weer?\n\n**Weer** is die toestand van die **lug** (die atmosfeer) op ’n sekere plek en tyd – vandag, môre of nou. Die weer kan vinnig verander: ’n sonnige oggend kan ’n stormagtige middag word. Die weer bepaal wat ons aantrek, of ons buite kan speel en wanneer boere plant of oes.\n\n## Die weerelemente en hul instrumente\n\nOm die weer te beskryf, kyk ons na die **weerelemente**:\n\n| Weerelement | Wat ons wil weet | Instrument | Eenheid |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Temperatuur** | Hoe warm of koud is die lug? | **termometer** | grade Celsius (°C) |\n| **Reënval** | Hoeveel reën het geval? | **reënmeter** | millimeter (mm) |\n| **Windrigting** | Waarvandaan waai die wind? | **windwyser** of **windkous** | kompasrigting |\n| **Windspoed** | Hoe vinnig waai die wind? | **windmeter** (anemometer) | kilometer per uur (km/h) |\n| **Wolke** | Hoeveel van die lug is bedek? | jou oë | helder, gedeeltelik bewolk, bewolk |\n| **Sonskyn** | Skyn die son? | jou oë | sonnig of nie |\n\nWater vries by 0 °C en kook by 100 °C. ’n Warm somersdag is omtrent 30 °C.\n\nSo gebruik jy die instrumente reg:\n\n- **Termometer:** hang dit in die **skadu**, want in die son wys dit warmer as die lug werklik is.\n- **Reënmeter:** sit dit in ’n **oop plek**, weg van bome en geboue wat die reën kan keer. Lees die mm-merk af en maak dit dan leeg.\n- **Windwyser:** die pyl draai en wys na die rigting waar die wind **vandaan** kom.\n- **Windkous:** die kous waai saam met die wind. As die wind uit die noorde kom, waai die kous na die suide uit.\n- **Windmeter:** die koppies draai al vinniger hoe harder die wind waai.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** ’n Wind word genoem na die rigting waar dit **vandaan** kom, nie waarheen dit waai nie. ’n **Suidoostewind** waai **uit** die suidooste na die noordweste.\n\n## Weervoorspellings en weersimbole\n\n’n **Weervoorspelling** sê vooruit hoe die weer gaan wees. **Weerkundiges** by die Suid-Afrikaanse Weerdiens gebruik metings van weerstasies en foto’s van satelliete om dit uit te werk. Jy kry voorspellings op die TV- of radionuus, in die koerant en op ’n app.\n\nOp ’n **weerkaart** word **weersimbole** gebruik:\n\n| Simbool (beskrywing) | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| ’n Geel son | sonnig |\n| ’n Son half agter ’n wolk | gedeeltelik bewolk |\n| ’n Grys wolk | bewolk |\n| ’n Wolk met reëndruppels | reën |\n| ’n Wolk met ’n weerligstraal | donderstorm |\n| ’n Sneeuvlokkie | sneeu |\n| Horisontale strepe | mis |\n\nLangs elke stad staan die **minimum**temperatuur (die laagste, vroeg in die oggend) en die **maksimum**temperatuur (die hoogste, in die middag). *4/19* beteken: laagste 4 °C, hoogste 19 °C. Voorbeeld van ’n wintervoorspelling:\n\n| Stad | Simbool | Min. | Maks. |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Kaapstad | wolk met reëndruppels | 9 °C | 16 °C |\n| Johannesburg | geel son | 3 °C | 18 °C |\n| Durban | son half agter ’n wolk | 14 °C | 24 °C |\n| Bloemfontein | geel son | 0 °C | 17 °C |\n\nDie **temperatuurverskil** is die maksimum min die minimum. In Johannesburg is dit 18 – 3 = 15 grade.\n\n> **Onthou:** **Weer** is die toestand van die lug **nou of vir ’n paar dae**. **Klimaat** is die gemiddelde weer oor **baie jare**.\n\n## Hou jou eie weerkaart\n\nHou ’n week lank ’n **weerkaart** (weerdagboek). Meet elke dag op **dieselfde tyd** en skryf neer: die datum, temperatuur, reënval, windrigting, wolke en ’n weersimbool. Aan die einde van die week kan jy **patrone** sien, bv. watter dag die warmste was, hoeveel reën altesaam geval het en of dit ná reën koeler geword het.","en":"## What is weather?\n\n**Weather** is the condition of the **air** (the atmosphere) at a certain place and time – today, tomorrow or right now. The weather can change quickly: a sunny morning can become a stormy afternoon. The weather decides what we wear, whether we can play outside and when farmers plant or harvest.\n\n## The weather elements and their instruments\n\nTo describe the weather, we look at the **weather elements**:\n\n| Weather element | What we want to know | Instrument | Unit |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Temperature** | How hot or cold is the air? | **thermometer** | degrees Celsius (°C) |\n| **Rainfall** | How much rain has fallen? | **rain gauge** | millimetres (mm) |\n| **Wind direction** | Where is the wind blowing from? | **wind vane** or **windsock** | compass direction |\n| **Wind speed** | How fast is the wind blowing? | **anemometer** (wind meter) | kilometres per hour (km/h) |\n| **Clouds** | How much of the sky is covered? | your eyes | clear, partly cloudy, cloudy |\n| **Sunshine** | Is the sun shining? | your eyes | sunny or not |\n\nWater freezes at 0 °C and boils at 100 °C. A hot summer’s day is about 30 °C.\n\nThis is how to use the instruments correctly:\n\n- **Thermometer:** hang it in the **shade**, because in the sun it shows a higher temperature than the air really has.\n- **Rain gauge:** put it in an **open place**, away from trees and buildings that can block the rain. Read the mm mark and then empty it.\n- **Wind vane:** the arrow turns and points to the direction the wind is coming **from**.\n- **Windsock:** the sock blows along with the wind. If the wind comes from the north, the sock blows out towards the south.\n- **Anemometer:** the cups spin faster the harder the wind blows.\n\n> **Common mistake:** A wind is named after the direction it comes **from**, not where it is blowing to. A **south-easterly wind** blows **from** the south-east towards the north-west.\n\n## Weather forecasts and weather symbols\n\nA **weather forecast** tells you in advance what the weather is going to be like. **Meteorologists** (weather forecasters) at the South African Weather Service use measurements from weather stations and photos from satellites to work it out. You get forecasts on the TV or radio news, in the newspaper and on an app.\n\nOn a **weather map**, **weather symbols** are used:\n\n| Symbol (description) | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| A yellow sun | sunny |\n| A sun half behind a cloud | partly cloudy |\n| A grey cloud | cloudy |\n| A cloud with raindrops | rain |\n| A cloud with a lightning bolt | thunderstorm |\n| A snowflake | snow |\n| Horizontal lines | fog |\n\nNext to each city are the **minimum** temperature (the lowest, early in the morning) and the **maximum** temperature (the highest, in the afternoon). *4/19* means: lowest 4 °C, highest 19 °C. Example of a winter forecast:\n\n| City | Symbol | Min. | Max. |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Cape Town | cloud with raindrops | 9 °C | 16 °C |\n| Johannesburg | yellow sun | 3 °C | 18 °C |\n| Durban | sun half behind a cloud | 14 °C | 24 °C |\n| Bloemfontein | yellow sun | 0 °C | 17 °C |\n\nThe **temperature difference** is the maximum minus the minimum. In Johannesburg it is 18 – 3 = 15 degrees.\n\n> **Remember:** **Weather** is the condition of the air **now or for a few days**. **Climate** is the average weather over **many years**.\n\n## Keep your own weather chart\n\nKeep a **weather chart** (weather diary) for a week. Measure every day at the **same time** and write down: the date, temperature, rainfall, wind direction, clouds and a weather symbol. At the end of the week you can see **patterns**, e.g. which day was the warmest, how much rain fell altogether and whether it became cooler after rain."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Weer","en":"Weather"},"def":{"af":"Die toestand van die lug op ’n sekere plek en tyd, soos vandag.","en":"The condition of the air at a certain place and time, such as today."}},{"term":{"af":"Weerelemente","en":"Weather elements"},"def":{"af":"Die dele van die weer wat ons meet of waarneem: temperatuur, reënval, wind, wolke en sonskyn.","en":"The parts of the weather that we measure or observe: temperature, rainfall, wind, clouds and sunshine."}},{"term":{"af":"Termometer","en":"Thermometer"},"def":{"af":"’n Instrument wat die temperatuur in grade Celsius (°C) meet.","en":"An instrument that measures temperature in degrees Celsius (°C)."}},{"term":{"af":"Reënmeter","en":"Rain gauge"},"def":{"af":"’n Instrument wat meet hoeveel reën geval het, in millimeter (mm).","en":"An instrument that measures how much rain has fallen, in millimetres (mm)."}},{"term":{"af":"Windwyser","en":"Wind vane"},"def":{"af":"’n Instrument met ’n pyl wat wys uit watter rigting die wind waai.","en":"An instrument with an arrow that shows which direction the wind is blowing from."}},{"term":{"af":"Windkous","en":"Windsock"},"def":{"af":"’n Buis van lap op ’n paal wat saam met die wind waai en die windrigting wys.","en":"A fabric tube on a pole that blows along with the wind and shows the wind direction."}},{"term":{"af":"Windmeter (anemometer)","en":"Anemometer"},"def":{"af":"’n Instrument met draaiende koppies wat meet hoe vinnig die wind waai.","en":"An instrument with spinning cups that measures how fast the wind blows."}},{"term":{"af":"Weervoorspelling","en":"Weather forecast"},"def":{"af":"’n Beskrywing vooruit van hoe die weer gaan wees.","en":"A description in advance of what the weather is going to be like."}},{"term":{"af":"Weerkundige","en":"Meteorologist"},"def":{"af":"Iemand wat die weer bestudeer en voorspel.","en":"Someone who studies and forecasts the weather."}},{"term":{"af":"Weersimbool","en":"Weather symbol"},"def":{"af":"’n Klein prentjie op ’n weerkaart wat wys hoe die weer is, bv. ’n wolk met reëndruppels vir reën.","en":"A small picture on a weather map that shows what the weather is like, e.g. a cloud with raindrops for rain."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n weervoorspelling","en":"Read a weather forecast"},"problem":{"af":"Gebruik die wintervoorspelling in die les. (a) Watter stad sal in die middag die warmste wees? (b) Watter stad kry reën? (c) Watter stad het die grootste verskil tussen die minimum- en maksimumtemperatuur?","en":"Use the winter forecast in the lesson. (a) Which city will be the warmest in the afternoon? (b) Which city gets rain? (c) Which city has the biggest difference between the minimum and maximum temperature?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die middag is wanneer die **maksimum** bereik word. Die hoogste maks. is 24 °C: **Durban**.","en":"(a) The afternoon is when the **maximum** is reached. The highest max. is 24 °C: **Durban**."},{"af":"(b) Soek die simbool *wolk met reëndruppels*: **Kaapstad**.","en":"(b) Look for the symbol *cloud with raindrops*: **Cape Town**."},{"af":"(c) Trek die min. van die maks. af: Kaapstad 16 – 9 = 7; Johannesburg 18 – 3 = 15; Durban 24 – 14 = 10; Bloemfontein 17 – 0 = 17.","en":"(c) Subtract the min. from the max.: Cape Town 16 – 9 = 7; Johannesburg 18 – 3 = 15; Durban 24 – 14 = 10; Bloemfontein 17 – 0 = 17."},{"af":"Die grootste verskil is 17 grade: **Bloemfontein**.","en":"The biggest difference is 17 degrees: **Bloemfontein**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Durban (b) Kaapstad (c) Bloemfontein (17 grade)","en":"(a) Durban (b) Cape Town (c) Bloemfontein (17 degrees)"}},{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n windwyser","en":"Read a wind vane"},"problem":{"af":"Die pyl van die windwyser by Aisha se skool wys na die noordweste. (a) Waarvandaan kom die wind? (b) Wat noem ons hierdie wind? (c) In watter rigting waai die wind?","en":"The arrow of the wind vane at Aisha’s school points to the north-west. (a) Where is the wind coming from? (b) What do we call this wind? (c) In which direction is the wind blowing?"},"steps":[{"af":"’n Windwyser se pyl wys na die rigting waar die wind **vandaan** kom. Die wind kom dus uit die **noordweste**.","en":"A wind vane’s arrow points to the direction the wind comes **from**. So the wind comes from the **north-west**."},{"af":"’n Wind word genoem na waar dit vandaan kom: ’n **noordwestewind**.","en":"A wind is named after where it comes from: a **north-westerly wind**."},{"af":"Die wind waai na die teenoorgestelde kant: die teenoorgestelde van noordwes is **suidoos**.","en":"The wind blows to the opposite side: the opposite of north-west is **south-east**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Uit die noordweste (b) ’n Noordwestewind (c) Na die suidooste","en":"(a) From the north-west (b) A north-westerly wind (c) Towards the south-east"}},{"title":{"af":"Kies die regte instrument","en":"Choose the right instrument"},"problem":{"af":"Nomsa wil meet: (a) hoeveel reën in die nag geval het, (b) hoe vinnig die wind waai en (c) hoe warm dit om 12:00 is. Watter instrument en watter eenheid moet sy vir elkeen gebruik?","en":"Nomsa wants to measure: (a) how much rain fell during the night, (b) how fast the wind is blowing and (c) how warm it is at 12:00. Which instrument and which unit must she use for each?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Reën word met ’n **reënmeter** in **millimeter (mm)** gemeet.","en":"(a) Rain is measured with a **rain gauge** in **millimetres (mm)**."},{"af":"(b) Windspoed word met ’n **windmeter (anemometer)** in **km/h** gemeet.","en":"(b) Wind speed is measured with an **anemometer** in **km/h**."},{"af":"(c) Temperatuur word met ’n **termometer** in **°C** gemeet – in die skadu.","en":"(c) Temperature is measured with a **thermometer** in **°C** – in the shade."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Reënmeter, mm (b) Windmeter, km/h (c) Termometer, °C","en":"(a) Rain gauge, mm (b) Anemometer, km/h (c) Thermometer, °C"}},{"title":{"af":"Ontleed ’n weerdagboek","en":"Analyse a weather diary"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho se weerdagboek (om 12:00 gemeet): Maandag 22 °C, 0 mm; Dinsdag 25 °C, 0 mm; Woensdag 18 °C, 12 mm; Donderdag 16 °C, 6 mm; Vrydag 20 °C, 0 mm. (a) Watter dag was die warmste? (b) Hoeveel reën het altesaam geval? (c) Watter patroon sien jy?","en":"Sipho’s weather diary (measured at 12:00): Monday 22 °C, 0 mm; Tuesday 25 °C, 0 mm; Wednesday 18 °C, 12 mm; Thursday 16 °C, 6 mm; Friday 20 °C, 0 mm. (a) Which day was the warmest? (b) How much rain fell altogether? (c) What pattern do you see?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die hoogste temperatuur is 25 °C: **Dinsdag**.","en":"(a) The highest temperature is 25 °C: **Tuesday**."},{"af":"(b) Tel die reën bymekaar: 0 + 0 + 12 + 6 + 0 = **18 mm**.","en":"(b) Add the rain: 0 + 0 + 12 + 6 + 0 = **18 mm**."},{"af":"(c) Op die reëndae (Woensdag en Donderdag) was dit **koeler**; toe die reën ophou, het dit weer warmer geword.","en":"(c) On the rainy days (Wednesday and Thursday) it was **cooler**; when the rain stopped, it became warmer again."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Dinsdag (b) 18 mm (c) Dit was koeler op die reëndae.","en":"(a) Tuesday (b) 18 mm (c) It was cooler on the rainy days."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is weer?","en":"What is weather?"},"options":[{"af":"Die toestand van die lug op ’n sekere plek en tyd","en":"The condition of the air at a certain place and time"},{"af":"Die gemiddelde reënval van ’n plek oor baie jare","en":"The average rainfall of a place over many years"},{"af":"Die hoogte van ’n plek bo seespieël","en":"The height of a place above sea level"},{"af":"Die vier seisoene van die jaar","en":"The four seasons of the year"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Weer is hoe die lug nou of vandag is. Die gemiddelde weer oor baie jare is klimaat, nie weer nie.","en":"Weather is what the air is like now or today. The average weather over many years is climate, not weather."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter instrument meet temperatuur?","en":"Which instrument measures temperature?"},"options":[{"af":"Reënmeter","en":"Rain gauge"},{"af":"Termometer","en":"Thermometer"},{"af":"Windmeter","en":"Anemometer"},{"af":"Windwyser","en":"Wind vane"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Termometer meet temperatuur in °C. ’n Reënmeter meet reën, ’n windmeter meet windspoed en ’n windwyser wys die windrigting.","en":"A thermometer measures temperature in °C. A rain gauge measures rain, an anemometer measures wind speed and a wind vane shows wind direction."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Noordewind waai uit die noorde.","en":"A northerly wind blows from the north."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Wind word genoem na die rigting waar dit vandaan kom. ’n Noordewind kom uit die noorde en waai na die suide.","en":"True. A wind is named after the direction it comes from. A northerly wind comes from the north and blows towards the south."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Reënval word met ’n reënmeter in ___ gemeet.","en":"Rainfall is measured with a rain gauge in ___."},"answers":{"af":["millimeter","mm"],"en":["millimetres","mm","millimeters"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["grade Celsius","kilometer per uur","liter"],"en":["degrees Celsius","kilometres per hour","litres"]}},"explain":{"af":"Reënval word in millimeter (mm) gemeet: hoe diep die water in die reënmeter is. Grade Celsius is vir temperatuur en km/h vir windspoed.","en":"Rainfall is measured in millimetres (mm): how deep the water in the rain gauge is. Degrees Celsius are for temperature and km/h for wind speed."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom moet ’n termometer in die skadu hang?","en":"Why must a thermometer hang in the shade?"},"options":[{"af":"Sodat die reën dit nie kan natmaak nie","en":"So that the rain cannot make it wet"},{"af":"Sodat die wind dit nie kan omwaai nie","en":"So that the wind cannot blow it over"},{"af":"Omdat dit makliker is om in die skadu te lees","en":"Because it is easier to read in the shade"},{"af":"Omdat die son dit warmer laat wys as die lug werklik is","en":"Because the sun makes it show a higher temperature than the air really has"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ons wil die temperatuur van die lug meet. Direkte sonlig verhit die termometer self, so dan wys dit te warm.","en":"We want to measure the temperature of the air. Direct sunlight heats the thermometer itself, so then it shows too high a temperature."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op ’n weerkaart staan ‘Polokwane 12/27’. Wat beteken die 27?","en":"On a weather map it says ‘Polokwane 12/27’. What does the 27 mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Die minimumtemperatuur in °C","en":"The minimum temperature in °C"},{"af":"Die reënval in mm","en":"The rainfall in mm"},{"af":"Die maksimumtemperatuur in °C","en":"The maximum temperature in °C"},{"af":"Die windspoed in km/h","en":"The wind speed in km/h"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die eerste getal is die minimum (12 °C, vroegoggend) en die tweede die maksimum (27 °C, middag).","en":"The first number is the minimum (12 °C, early morning) and the second is the maximum (27 °C, afternoon)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke instrument by wat dit meet.","en":"Match each instrument to what it measures."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Termometer","en":"Thermometer"},"r":{"af":"Temperatuur","en":"Temperature"}},{"l":{"af":"Reënmeter","en":"Rain gauge"},"r":{"af":"Reënval","en":"Rainfall"}},{"l":{"af":"Windwyser","en":"Wind vane"},"r":{"af":"Windrigting","en":"Wind direction"}},{"l":{"af":"Windmeter","en":"Anemometer"},"r":{"af":"Windspoed","en":"Wind speed"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke weerelement het sy eie instrument. Moenie die windwyser (rigting) en die windmeter (spoed) deurmekaar maak nie.","en":"Each weather element has its own instrument. Do not mix up the wind vane (direction) and the anemometer (speed)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Weersimbool van ’n wolk met ’n weerligstraal beteken ’n ___.","en":"A weather symbol of a cloud with a lightning bolt means a ___."},"answers":{"af":["donderstorm"],"en":["thunderstorm"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["sneeustorm","misdag","sonnige dag"],"en":["snowstorm","foggy day","sunny day"]}},"explain":{"af":"Weerlig hoort by ’n donderstorm. Sneeu word met ’n sneeuvlokkie gewys en mis met horisontale strepe.","en":"Lightning belongs with a thunderstorm. Snow is shown with a snowflake and fog with horizontal lines."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar moet jy ’n reënmeter sit?","en":"Where must you put a rain gauge?"},"options":[{"af":"Onder ’n groot boom, waar dit veilig is","en":"Under a big tree, where it is safe"},{"af":"In ’n oop plek, weg van bome en geboue","en":"In an open place, away from trees and buildings"},{"af":"Teen die huis se muur, onder die dak","en":"Against the wall of the house, under the roof"},{"af":"Binne in die klaskamer op ’n rak","en":"Inside the classroom on a shelf"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die reënmeter moet al die reën vang wat val. Bome, mure en dakke keer die reën, so die meting sal te laag wees.","en":"The rain gauge must catch all the rain that falls. Trees, walls and roofs block the rain, so the reading will be too low."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Windwyser meet hoe vinnig die wind waai.","en":"A wind vane measures how fast the wind blows."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. ’n Windwyser wys die windrigting. Die windspoed word met ’n windmeter (anemometer) gemeet.","en":"False. A wind vane shows the wind direction. Wind speed is measured with an anemometer."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op ’n dag is die minimumtemperatuur 6 °C en die maksimum 21 °C. Wat is die temperatuurverskil?","en":"On a day the minimum temperature is 6 °C and the maximum is 21 °C. What is the temperature difference?"},"options":[{"af":"27 grade","en":"27 degrees"},{"af":"16 grade","en":"16 degrees"},{"af":"21 grade","en":"21 degrees"},{"af":"15 grade","en":"15 degrees"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Verskil = maks. – min. = 21 – 6 = 15 grade. Moenie die twee getalle bymekaartel nie (27).","en":"Difference = max. – min. = 21 – 6 = 15 degrees. Do not add the two numbers (27)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Mense wat die weer bestudeer en voorspel, heet ___.","en":"People who study and forecast the weather are called ___."},"answers":{"af":["weerkundiges","weerkundige"],"en":["meteorologists","weather forecasters","meteorologist"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["geoloë","sterrekundiges","mynwerkers"],"en":["geologists","astronomers","miners"]}},"explain":{"af":"Weerkundiges gebruik metings van weerstasies en satelliete om die weer te voorspel. Sterrekundiges bestudeer die sterre en geoloë die rotse.","en":"Meteorologists use measurements from weather stations and satellites to forecast the weather. Astronomers study the stars and geologists study rocks."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die windkous by ’n vliegveld waai na die suide uit. Waarvandaan kom die wind?","en":"The windsock at an airport blows out towards the south. Where is the wind coming from?"},"options":[{"af":"Uit die suide","en":"From the south"},{"af":"Uit die ooste","en":"From the east"},{"af":"Uit die noorde","en":"From the north"},{"af":"Uit die weste","en":"From the west"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die windkous waai saam met die wind. As dit na die suide uitwaai, druk die wind dit vanuit die teenoorgestelde kant: die noorde.","en":"The windsock blows along with the wind. If it blows out towards the south, the wind is pushing it from the opposite side: the north."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato sê: ‘Die lug is heeltemal grys en toe.’ Watter weerelement beskryf sy?","en":"Lerato says: ‘The sky is completely grey and covered.’ Which weather element is she describing?"},"options":[{"af":"Wolke","en":"Clouds"},{"af":"Temperatuur","en":"Temperature"},{"af":"Reënval","en":"Rainfall"},{"af":"Windspoed","en":"Wind speed"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Sy beskryf hoeveel van die lug bedek is – dit is die wolke. Dit is bewolk, maar sy sê niks oor reën, temperatuur of wind nie.","en":"She describes how much of the sky is covered – that is the clouds. It is cloudy, but she says nothing about rain, temperature or wind."}}]},{"id":"sw5-t3-geo-klimaat","title":{"af":"Klimaat in Suid-Afrika","en":"Climate in South Africa"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die verskil tussen weer en klimaat kan verduidelik, Suid-Afrika se reënvalgebiede kan beskryf, ’n eenvoudige klimaatgrafiek kan lees en kan sê hoe klimaat boerdery, huise, klere en mense se lewens raak.","en":"You will be able to explain the difference between weather and climate, describe South Africa’s rainfall regions, read a simple climate graph and say how climate affects farming, houses, clothes and people’s lives."},"summary":{"af":"## Weer en klimaat\n\n**Klimaat** is die **gemiddelde weer** van ’n plek oor **baie jare**. Weer verander elke dag, maar klimaat vertel jou wat jy gewoonlik op ’n plek in ’n seisoen kan verwag. *Dit reën vandag in Kaapstad* gaan oor weer. *Kaapstad kry meestal in die winter reën* gaan oor klimaat.\n\nOns woon in die **suidelike halfrond**. Daarom is dit by ons **somer** in Desember, Januarie en Februarie en **winter** in Junie, Julie en Augustus.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie dink dit is oral in die wêreld op dieselfde tyd winter nie. In Suid-Afrika val Kersfees in die **somer**.\n\n## Reënvalgebiede\n\n| Gebied | Waar | Wanneer reën dit? |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Somerreënvalgebied** | Die grootste deel van die land: die binneland, die noorde en die ooste | In die somer, dikwels as **donderstorms** in die middag; die winter is droog |\n| **Winterreënvalgebied** | Die suidweste: Kaapstad en die Wes-Kaap rondom | In die winter, wanneer **koue fronte** van die see af inkom; die somer is warm en droog |\n| **Reën dwarsdeur die jaar** | Die suidkus, bv. George en Knysna | In alle seisoene |\n\n## Die ooste is natter, die kus is matiger\n\n- Die meeste vog kom van die **warm Indiese Oseaan** in die ooste. Wanneer die vogtige lug teen die eskarpement opstyg, vorm wolke en val reën. Hoe verder wes, hoe minder vog bly oor. Dele van die Noord-Kaap kry minder as 200 mm reën per jaar; dele van KwaZulu-Natal en Mpumalanga kry meer as 800 mm.\n- Langs die weskus vloei die **koue Benguelastroom**. Koue water verdamp min, so daar vorm min reënwolke, maar dikwels mis. Die **warm Agulhasstroom** langs die ooskus maak Durban warm en vogtig.\n- Die see word stadig warm en stadig koud. Daarom is die **kus matiger** as die binneland: die somers is nie so warm nie en die winters nie so koud nie.\n- In die **binneland** en op **hoë grond** is die winternagte koud. Op die Hoëveld is daar dikwels **ryp**, en op hoë berge soos die Drakensberg val soms **sneeu**.\n\n## Droogtes en vloede\n\n- ’n **Droogte** is ’n lang tyd met baie minder reën as gewoonlik. Damme raak leeg, oeste misluk en vee kry te min kos en water.\n- ’n **Vloed** gebeur wanneer baie reën in ’n kort tyd val en riviere oor hul walle loop. Vloede beskadig huise, paaie en brûe. Moet nooit deur vloedwater loop of ry nie.\n\n## Hoe klimaat ons lewens raak\n\n| Wat word geraak? | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| **Boerdery** | Koring en druiwe in die winterreënvalgebied; mielies op die Hoëveld; suikerriet aan die warm, nat KwaZulu-Natalse kus; skape in die droë Karoo |\n| **Huise** | Warm plekke: stoepe, breë dakrande en groot vensters. Koue plekke: dik mure en ’n kaggel of verwarmer |\n| **Klere** | Ligte klere in Durban se somer; warm baadjies en musse in ’n Hoëveldse winter |\n\n## ’n Klimaatgrafiek lees\n\n’n **Klimaatgrafiek** wys die gemiddelde weer van ’n plek vir elke maand: **stawe** wys die **reënval** (mm) en ’n **lyn** wys die **temperatuur** (°C). Hier is ’n paar maande se waardes vir twee dorpe:\n\n|   | Jan | Apr | Jul | Okt |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Dorp A: reën (mm) | 120 | 50 | 5 | 70 |\n| Dorp A: temperatuur (°C) | 22 | 16 | 10 | 19 |\n| Dorp B: reën (mm) | 15 | 50 | 90 | 35 |\n\nDorp A kry die meeste reën in Januarie (somer), dus is dit in die **somerreënvalgebied**. Dorp B kry die meeste reën in Julie (winter), dus is dit in die **winterreënvalgebied**.\n\n> **Onthou:** Soek die **hoogste stawe**. Is hulle in Desember tot Februarie, is dit somerreën; is hulle in Junie tot Augustus, is dit winterreën.","en":"## Weather and climate\n\n**Climate** is the **average weather** of a place over **many years**. Weather changes every day, but climate tells you what you can usually expect at a place in a season. *It is raining in Cape Town today* is about weather. *Cape Town gets most of its rain in winter* is about climate.\n\nWe live in the **southern hemisphere**. That is why we have **summer** in December, January and February and **winter** in June, July and August.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not think it is winter everywhere in the world at the same time. In South Africa, Christmas falls in **summer**.\n\n## Rainfall regions\n\n| Region | Where | When does it rain? |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Summer rainfall region** | Most of the country: the interior, the north and the east | In summer, often as afternoon **thunderstorms**; winter is dry |\n| **Winter rainfall region** | The south-west: Cape Town and the Western Cape around it | In winter, when **cold fronts** come in from the sea; summer is hot and dry |\n| **Rain all year round** | The south coast, e.g. George and Knysna | In all seasons |\n\n## The east is wetter, the coast is milder\n\n- Most moisture comes from the **warm Indian Ocean** in the east. When the moist air rises up against the escarpment, clouds form and rain falls. The further west, the less moisture is left. Parts of the Northern Cape get less than 200 mm of rain a year; parts of KwaZulu-Natal and Mpumalanga get more than 800 mm.\n- Along the west coast flows the **cold Benguela Current**. Cold water evaporates little, so few rain clouds form, but there is often fog. The **warm Agulhas Current** along the east coast makes Durban warm and humid.\n- The sea warms up slowly and cools down slowly. That is why the **coast is milder** than the interior: the summers are not as hot and the winters not as cold.\n- In the **interior** and on **high land** the winter nights are cold. On the Highveld there is often **frost**, and on high mountains like the Drakensberg **snow** sometimes falls.\n\n## Droughts and floods\n\n- A **drought** is a long time with much less rain than usual. Dams run dry, crops fail and livestock get too little food and water.\n- A **flood** happens when a lot of rain falls in a short time and rivers overflow their banks. Floods damage houses, roads and bridges. Never walk or drive through floodwater.\n\n## How climate affects our lives\n\n| What is affected? | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| **Farming** | Wheat and grapes in the winter rainfall region; maize on the Highveld; sugar cane on the warm, wet KwaZulu-Natal coast; sheep in the dry Karoo |\n| **Houses** | Hot places: verandas, wide roof overhangs and big windows. Cold places: thick walls and a fireplace or heater |\n| **Clothes** | Light clothes in Durban’s summer; warm jackets and beanies in a Highveld winter |\n\n## Reading a climate graph\n\nA **climate graph** shows the average weather of a place for every month: **bars** show the **rainfall** (mm) and a **line** shows the **temperature** (°C). Here are the values for a few months for two towns:\n\n|   | Jan | Apr | Jul | Oct |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Town A: rain (mm) | 120 | 50 | 5 | 70 |\n| Town A: temperature (°C) | 22 | 16 | 10 | 19 |\n| Town B: rain (mm) | 15 | 50 | 90 | 35 |\n\nTown A gets the most rain in January (summer), so it is in the **summer rainfall region**. Town B gets the most rain in July (winter), so it is in the **winter rainfall region**.\n\n> **Remember:** Look for the **highest bars**. If they are in December to February, it is summer rain; if they are in June to August, it is winter rain."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Klimaat","en":"Climate"},"def":{"af":"Die gemiddelde weer van ’n plek oor baie jare.","en":"The average weather of a place over many years."}},{"term":{"af":"Somerreënvalgebied","en":"Summer rainfall region"},"def":{"af":"’n Gebied wat die meeste van sy reën in die somer kry, dikwels as donderstorms.","en":"A region that gets most of its rain in summer, often as thunderstorms."}},{"term":{"af":"Winterreënvalgebied","en":"Winter rainfall region"},"def":{"af":"’n Gebied wat die meeste van sy reën in die winter kry, soos Kaapstad en die suidweste.","en":"A region that gets most of its rain in winter, like Cape Town and the south-west."}},{"term":{"af":"Koue front","en":"Cold front"},"def":{"af":"’n Band koue lug wat van die see af inbeweeg en in die winter reën en wind na die suidweste bring.","en":"A band of cold air that moves in from the sea and brings rain and wind to the south-west in winter."}},{"term":{"af":"Matige klimaat","en":"Mild (moderate) climate"},"def":{"af":"’n Klimaat sonder baie warm somers of baie koue winters, soos aan die kus.","en":"A climate without very hot summers or very cold winters, like at the coast."}},{"term":{"af":"Ryp","en":"Frost"},"def":{"af":"’n Dun wit lagie ys wat op koue, helder winternagte op die grond en plante vorm.","en":"A thin white layer of ice that forms on the ground and plants on cold, clear winter nights."}},{"term":{"af":"Droogte","en":"Drought"},"def":{"af":"’n Lang tyd met baie minder reën as gewoonlik.","en":"A long time with much less rain than usual."}},{"term":{"af":"Vloed","en":"Flood"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer baie reën in ’n kort tyd val en water oor die walle van riviere loop.","en":"When a lot of rain falls in a short time and water flows over the banks of rivers."}},{"term":{"af":"Klimaatgrafiek","en":"Climate graph"},"def":{"af":"’n Grafiek met stawe vir die reënval en ’n lyn vir die temperatuur van elke maand.","en":"A graph with bars for the rainfall and a line for the temperature of each month."}},{"term":{"af":"Suidelike halfrond","en":"Southern hemisphere"},"def":{"af":"Die helfte van die aarde suid van die ewenaar, waar Suid-Afrika lê en somer in Desember is.","en":"The half of the Earth south of the equator, where South Africa lies and summer is in December."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lees die klimaatgegewens","en":"Read the climate data"},"problem":{"af":"Gebruik die tabel vir Dorp A in die les. (a) In watter van die maande kry Dorp A die meeste reën? (b) Is Dorp A in ’n somer- of winterreënvalgebied? (c) Hoeveel warmer is dit in Januarie as in Julie?","en":"Use the table for Town A in the lesson. (a) In which of the months does Town A get the most rain? (b) Is Town A in a summer or winter rainfall region? (c) How much warmer is it in January than in July?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Vergelyk die reënsyfers: 120; 50; 5 en 70 mm. Die grootste is 120 mm in **Januarie**.","en":"(a) Compare the rain figures: 120, 50, 5 and 70 mm. The biggest is 120 mm in **January**."},{"af":"(b) Januarie is in die somer, en Julie (die winter) is baie droog met net 5 mm. Dit is ’n **somerreënvalgebied**.","en":"(b) January is in summer, and July (winter) is very dry with only 5 mm. It is a **summer rainfall region**."},{"af":"(c) Januarie 22 °C – Julie 10 °C = **12 grade** warmer.","en":"(c) January 22 °C – July 10 °C = **12 degrees** warmer."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Januarie (b) Somerreënvalgebied (c) 12 grade","en":"(a) January (b) Summer rainfall region (c) 12 degrees"}},{"title":{"af":"Oos teenoor wes","en":"East versus west"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik waarom Durban aan die ooskus baie meer reën kry as ’n dorp aan die weskus van die Noord-Kaap.","en":"Explain why Durban on the east coast gets much more rain than a town on the west coast of the Northern Cape."},"steps":[{"af":"Durban lê langs die **warm Indiese Oseaan** en die warm Agulhasstroom. Warm water verdamp maklik, so die lug is vol vog.","en":"Durban lies next to the **warm Indian Ocean** and the warm Agulhas Current. Warm water evaporates easily, so the air is full of moisture."},{"af":"Die weskus lê langs die **koue Benguelastroom**. Koue water verdamp min, so daar vorm min reënwolke.","en":"The west coast lies next to the **cold Benguela Current**. Cold water evaporates little, so few rain clouds form."},{"af":"Die vog wat van die ooste af kom, val meestal as reën voordat dit die weste bereik.","en":"The moisture that comes from the east mostly falls as rain before it reaches the west."}],"answer":{"af":"Durban kry vog van die warm Indiese Oseaan; die weskus lê by die koue Benguelastroom en kry min vog, so dit is droog.","en":"Durban gets moisture from the warm Indian Ocean; the west coast lies by the cold Benguela Current and gets little moisture, so it is dry."}},{"title":{"af":"Ryp in Johannesburg, nie in Durban nie","en":"Frost in Johannesburg, not in Durban"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter woon in Johannesburg en sy neef Ravi in Durban. In Julie is die gras by Pieter soggens wit van die ryp, maar by Ravi nie. Verduidelik waarom.","en":"Pieter lives in Johannesburg and his cousin Ravi in Durban. In July the grass at Pieter’s house is white with frost in the mornings, but not at Ravi’s. Explain why."},"steps":[{"af":"Johannesburg lê **hoog** op die Hoëveld, meer as 1 500 m bo seespieël. Hoe hoër die grond, hoe kouer.","en":"Johannesburg lies **high** on the Highveld, more than 1 500 m above sea level. The higher the land, the colder it is."},{"af":"Johannesburg lê ook in die **binneland**, ver van die see. Op helder winternagte koel dit baie af.","en":"Johannesburg also lies in the **interior**, far from the sea. On clear winter nights it cools down a lot."},{"af":"Durban lê **laag by die see**. Die see hou die temperatuur matig, so dit word nie koud genoeg vir ryp nie.","en":"Durban lies **low by the sea**. The sea keeps the temperature mild, so it does not get cold enough for frost."}],"answer":{"af":"Johannesburg is hoog en in die binneland, waar winternagte baie koud word; Durban is laag by die see, wat dit matig hou.","en":"Johannesburg is high and inland, where winter nights get very cold; Durban is low by the sea, which keeps it mild."}},{"title":{"af":"Klimaat en boerdery","en":"Climate and farming"},"problem":{"af":"Waarom plant boere in die Wes-Kaap koring sodat dit in die winter groei, terwyl boere op die Hoëveld mielies plant sodat dit in die somer groei?","en":"Why do farmers in the Western Cape plant wheat so that it grows in winter, while farmers on the Highveld plant maize so that it grows in summer?"},"steps":[{"af":"Gewasse het die meeste water nodig terwyl hulle **groei**.","en":"Crops need the most water while they are **growing**."},{"af":"Die Wes-Kaap is ’n **winterreënvalgebied**, so daar is genoeg reën in die winter.","en":"The Western Cape is a **winter rainfall region**, so there is enough rain in winter."},{"af":"Die Hoëveld is ’n **somerreënvalgebied**, so die reën kom in die somer. Die winter is daar droog en koud, met ryp.","en":"The Highveld is a **summer rainfall region**, so the rain comes in summer. Winter there is dry and cold, with frost."}],"answer":{"af":"Elke boer laat sy gewas groei in die seisoen wanneer sy gebied reën kry.","en":"Each farmer lets the crop grow in the season when the region gets rain."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is klimaat?","en":"What is climate?"},"options":[{"af":"Die weer van vandag","en":"Today’s weather"},{"af":"Die temperatuur om 12:00","en":"The temperature at 12:00"},{"af":"’n Weervoorspelling vir môre","en":"A weather forecast for tomorrow"},{"af":"Die gemiddelde weer oor baie jare","en":"The average weather over many years"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Klimaat is die gemiddelde weer oor baie jare. Die weer van vandag, ’n meting om 12:00 en ’n voorspelling vir môre gaan almal oor weer.","en":"Climate is the average weather over many years. Today’s weather, a reading at 12:00 and a forecast for tomorrow are all about weather."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die grootste deel van Suid-Afrika is ’n somerreënvalgebied.","en":"Most of South Africa is a summer rainfall region."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die binneland, die noorde en die ooste kry die meeste reën in die somer, dikwels as donderstorms. Net die suidweste is ’n winterreënvalgebied, en die suidkus kry reën dwarsdeur die jaar.","en":"True. The interior, the north and the east get most of their rain in summer, often as thunderstorms. Only the south-west is a winter rainfall region, and the south coast gets rain all year round."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wanneer kry Kaapstad die meeste reën?","en":"When does Cape Town get the most rain?"},"options":[{"af":"In die somer","en":"In summer"},{"af":"In die winter","en":"In winter"},{"af":"Ewe veel in alle seisoene","en":"Equally in all seasons"},{"af":"Net ná donderstorms in Januarie","en":"Only after thunderstorms in January"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Kaapstad is in die winterreënvalgebied. Koue fronte bring reën in die winter; die somer is warm en droog.","en":"Cape Town is in the winter rainfall region. Cold fronts bring rain in winter; summer is hot and dry."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die suidkus, bv. by George en Knysna, kry reën ___.","en":"The south coast, e.g. at George and Knysna, gets rain ___."},"answers":{"af":["dwarsdeur die jaar","die hele jaar","regdeur die jaar"],"en":["all year round","throughout the year","all year"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["net in die somer","net in die winter","net in die lente"],"en":["only in summer","only in winter","only in spring"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die suidkus kry reën in alle seisoene. Dit is anders as die somerreënvalgebied (binneland) en die winterreënvalgebied (suidweste).","en":"The south coast gets rain in all seasons. This is different from the summer rainfall region (interior) and the winter rainfall region (south-west)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is die weste van Suid-Afrika droër as die ooste?","en":"Why is the west of South Africa drier than the east?"},"options":[{"af":"Die meeste vog kom van die warm Indiese Oseaan in die ooste","en":"Most moisture comes from the warm Indian Ocean in the east"},{"af":"Die weste lê baie hoër as die ooste en is daarom droog","en":"The west lies much higher than the east and is therefore dry"},{"af":"Die son skyn minder in die weste as in die ooste","en":"The sun shines less in the west than in the east"},{"af":"Die weste het meer riviere wat al die reën wegvat","en":"The west has more rivers that carry all the rain away"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Vog kom van die warm Indiese Oseaan in die ooste en val meestal as reën voordat dit die weste bereik. Die koue Benguelastroom in die weste bring min vog.","en":"Moisture comes from the warm Indian Ocean in the east and mostly falls as rain before it reaches the west. The cold Benguela Current in the west brings little moisture."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter maande is dit somer in Suid-Afrika?","en":"In which months is it summer in South Africa?"},"options":[{"af":"Junie, Julie en Augustus","en":"June, July and August"},{"af":"Maart, April en Mei","en":"March, April and May"},{"af":"September, Oktober en November","en":"September, October and November"},{"af":"Desember, Januarie en Februarie","en":"December, January and February"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Suid-Afrika lê in die suidelike halfrond, so ons somer is in Desember, Januarie en Februarie. Junie tot Augustus is ons winter.","en":"South Africa lies in the southern hemisphere, so our summer is in December, January and February. June to August is our winter."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke plek by sy klimaat.","en":"Match each place to its climate."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Kaapstad","en":"Cape Town"},"r":{"af":"Reën in die winter, droë somers","en":"Rain in winter, dry summers"}},{"l":{"af":"Hoëveld","en":"Highveld"},"r":{"af":"Somerdonderstorms en ryp in die winter","en":"Summer thunderstorms and frost in winter"}},{"l":{"af":"Durban","en":"Durban"},"r":{"af":"Warm en vogtig deur die warm Agulhasstroom","en":"Warm and humid because of the warm Agulhas Current"}},{"l":{"af":"Weskus van die Noord-Kaap","en":"West coast of the Northern Cape"},"r":{"af":"Baie droog, met mis van die koue see","en":"Very dry, with fog from the cold sea"}},{"l":{"af":"Hoë pieke van die Drakensberg","en":"High peaks of the Drakensberg"},"r":{"af":"Soms sneeu in die winter","en":"Sometimes snow in winter"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die ligging bepaal die klimaat: hoe hoog ’n plek is, hoe ver van die see dit is, en of die see daar warm of koud is.","en":"The location decides the climate: how high a place is, how far it is from the sea, and whether the sea there is warm or cold."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Klimaatgrafiek van ’n dorp het die hoogste reënvalstawe in Junie, Julie en Augustus. Watter soort reënvalgebied is dit?","en":"A climate graph of a town has the highest rainfall bars in June, July and August. What kind of rainfall region is it?"},"options":[{"af":"Somerreënvalgebied","en":"Summer rainfall region"},{"af":"Reën dwarsdeur die jaar","en":"Rain all year round"},{"af":"Winterreënvalgebied","en":"Winter rainfall region"},{"af":"’n Gebied sonder reën","en":"A region without rain"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Junie, Julie en Augustus is ons wintermaande. As die meeste reën dan val, is dit ’n winterreënvalgebied, soos Kaapstad.","en":"June, July and August are our winter months. If most rain falls then, it is a winter rainfall region, like Cape Town."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Lang tyd met baie minder reën as gewoonlik heet ’n ___.","en":"A long time with much less rain than usual is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["droogte"],"en":["drought"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vloed","ryp","koue front"],"en":["flood","frost","cold front"]}},"explain":{"af":"In ’n droogte raak damme leeg en oeste misluk. ’n Vloed is die teenoorgestelde: te veel reën in ’n kort tyd.","en":"In a drought dams run dry and crops fail. A flood is the opposite: too much rain in a short time."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die kus het groter temperatuurverskille tussen somer en winter as die binneland.","en":"The coast has bigger temperature differences between summer and winter than the interior."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die see word stadig warm en stadig koud, so die kus is matiger. Die binneland het warmer somerdae en kouer winternagte.","en":"False. The sea warms up slowly and cools down slowly, so the coast is milder. The interior has hotter summer days and colder winter nights."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter gewas pas die beste by die warm, nat kus van KwaZulu-Natal?","en":"Which crop suits the warm, wet coast of KwaZulu-Natal best?"},"options":[{"af":"Koring","en":"Wheat"},{"af":"Druiwe vir wyn","en":"Grapes for wine"},{"af":"Suikerriet","en":"Sugar cane"},{"af":"Rooibostee","en":"Rooibos tea"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Suikerriet hou van warm, nat toestande, soos aan die KwaZulu-Natalse kus. Koring en druiwe word in die winterreënvalgebied van die Wes-Kaap verbou.","en":"Sugar cane likes warm, wet conditions, like on the KwaZulu-Natal coast. Wheat and grapes are grown in the winter rainfall region of the Western Cape."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Op ’n klimaatgrafiek wys die ___ die reënval vir elke maand.","en":"On a climate graph the ___ show the rainfall for each month."},"answers":{"af":["stawe","staaf"],"en":["bars","bar"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["lyn","kolletjies","pyle"],"en":["line","dots","arrows"]}},"explain":{"af":"Stawe wys die reënval in mm, en ’n lyn wys die temperatuur in °C.","en":"Bars show the rainfall in mm, and a line shows the temperature in °C."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom kry Johannesburg in die winter ryp, maar Durban nie?","en":"Why does Johannesburg get frost in winter, but Durban does not?"},"options":[{"af":"Johannesburg lê hoog in die binneland; Durban lê laag by die see","en":"Johannesburg lies high in the interior; Durban lies low by the sea"},{"af":"Johannesburg kry in die winter baie meer reën as Durban","en":"Johannesburg gets much more rain in winter than Durban"},{"af":"Durban lê hoër bo seespieël as Johannesburg","en":"Durban lies higher above sea level than Johannesburg"},{"af":"Johannesburg lê langs die koue Benguelastroom","en":"Johannesburg lies next to the cold Benguela Current"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Hoë grond in die binneland word op winternagte baie koud. Die see hou Durban se temperatuur matig. Johannesburg is in die winter juis droog.","en":"High land in the interior gets very cold on winter nights. The sea keeps Durban’s temperature mild. Johannesburg is actually dry in winter."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter huis pas die beste by ’n warm klimaat?","en":"Which house suits a hot climate best?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Huis met klein venstertjies en ’n groot kaggel","en":"A house with tiny windows and a big fireplace"},{"af":"’n Huis met ’n stoep, breë dakrande en groot vensters","en":"A house with a veranda, wide roof overhangs and big windows"},{"af":"’n Huis met dik mure en ’n verwarmer in elke kamer","en":"A house with thick walls and a heater in every room"},{"af":"’n Huis met ’n donker dak en geen skaduwee nie","en":"A house with a dark roof and no shade"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In ’n warm klimaat wil jy skaduwee en koel lug hê: ’n stoep en breë dakrande gee skaduwee, en groot vensters laat die wind deurwaai. Kaggels en verwarmers pas by koue plekke.","en":"In a hot climate you want shade and cool air: a veranda and wide roof overhangs give shade, and big windows let the breeze through. Fireplaces and heaters suit cold places."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Minerale in Suid-Afrika","en":"Minerals in South Africa"},"topics":[{"id":"sw5-t4-geo-minerale","title":{"af":"Suid-Afrika se minerale","en":"South Africa’s minerals"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik wat ’n mineraal en ’n erts is, Suid-Afrika se belangrike minerale kan noem en sê waar hulle gevind word en waarvoor ons hulle gebruik, en minerale op ’n kaart met simbole kan lees.","en":"You will be able to explain what a mineral and an ore are, name South Africa’s important minerals and say where they are found and what we use them for, and read minerals on a map with symbols."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is minerale en erts?\n\n’n **Mineraal** is ’n natuurlike, nie-lewende stof wat in die rotse van die aarde gevorm het, soos goud, platinum en diamante. Mense maak nie minerale nie – ons moet dit uit die grond **myn**.\n\n’n **Erts** is rots wat genoeg van ’n mineraal of metaal bevat dat dit die moeite werd is om dit te myn. **Ystererts** is byvoorbeeld rots met baie yster daarin. Die erts word fyngemaak en verhit om die metaal daaruit te kry.\n\n**Steenkool** is eintlik nie ’n mineraal nie – dit het baie lank gelede uit plante gevorm – maar ons tel dit saam met die minerale wat ons myn.\n\nSuid-Afrika is baie **ryk aan minerale**. Ons het byvoorbeeld meer platinum as enige ander land in die wêreld.\n\n## Belangrike minerale\n\n| Mineraal | Waar in Suid-Afrika | Gebruike |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Goud** | Gauteng (die Witwatersrand) en die Vrystaat (rondom Welkom) | Juweliersware, elektronika soos selfone en rekenaars, munte |\n| **Platinum** | Noordwes (rondom Rustenburg) en Limpopo | **Katalitiese omsetters** in motors, wat uitlaatgasse skoner maak; juweliersware |\n| **Steenkool** | Mpumalanga (rondom eMalahleni, wat *plek van steenkool* beteken) | Word in **kragstasies** verbrand om **elektrisiteit** op te wek; ook om staal te maak |\n| **Diamante** | Noord-Kaap (Kimberley), langs die weskus en in die see | Juweliersware; omdat diamant so hard is, ook om mee te sny, te boor en te slyp |\n| **Ystererts** | Noord-Kaap (rondom Kathu) | Om **yster** en **staal** te maak vir motors, geboue, brûe en gereedskap |\n| **Mangaan** | Noord-Kaap (in die Kalahari, naby Hotazel) | Maak staal harder en sterker |\n| **Chroom** | Noordwes, Limpopo en Mpumalanga | **Vlekvrye staal** (vir wasbakke, potte en messe) en blink chroomlae |\n\n> **Onthou:** Die meeste van Suid-Afrika se **elektrisiteit** kom van **steenkool** wat in kragstasies verbrand word.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie **goud** en **platinum** se provinsies omruil nie. **Goud** kry ons in Gauteng en die Vrystaat; **platinum** in Noordwes en Limpopo.\n\n## Minerale op ’n kaart\n\nOp ’n kaart word minerale met **simbole** gewys, en die **sleutel** verduidelik wat elke simbool beteken. Dit kan ’n vorm, ’n prentjie of ’n letter wees. Hier is ’n voorbeeld van so ’n sleutel:\n\n| Simbool | Mineraal |\n|---|---|\n| ▲ (driehoek) | steenkool |\n| ● (kol) | goud |\n| ◆ (ruit) | diamante |\n| ■ (vierkant) | ystererts |\n| ★ (ster) | platinum |\n\nOp ’n mineraalkaart van Suid-Afrika met hierdie sleutel sal jy baie ▲ in Mpumalanga sien, ● in Gauteng en die Vrystaat, ★ in Noordwes en Limpopo, en ◆ en ■ in die Noord-Kaap. Hoe meer simbole in ’n gebied, hoe meer myne is daar.\n\nOnthou: elke kaart kan sy eie simbole kies. Lees dus altyd eers die sleutel.\n\n## Waarom is minerale belangrik?\n\n- Mynbou gee **werk** aan baie mense, en dorpe groei rondom myne.\n- Baie minerale word aan ander lande verkoop (**uitvoer**). Dit bring geld na Suid-Afrika.\n- Ons gebruik minerale elke dag: die **staal** in ’n motor of brug, die **elektrisiteit** in jou huis en die goud in ’n selfoon.\n- Minerale is **nie-hernubaar**: wanneer hulle uitgemyn is, groei hulle nie weer aan nie. Daarom moet ons hulle verstandig gebruik en metaal **herwin** waar ons kan.","en":"## What are minerals and ores?\n\nA **mineral** is a natural, non-living substance that formed in the rocks of the Earth, such as gold, platinum and diamonds. People do not make minerals – we have to **mine** them from the ground.\n\nAn **ore** is rock that contains enough of a mineral or metal to make it worth mining. **Iron ore**, for example, is rock with a lot of iron in it. The ore is crushed and heated to get the metal out of it.\n\n**Coal** is actually not a mineral – it formed from plants a very long time ago – but we count it with the minerals that we mine.\n\nSouth Africa is very **rich in minerals**. For example, we have more platinum than any other country in the world.\n\n## Important minerals\n\n| Mineral | Where in South Africa | Uses |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Gold** | Gauteng (the Witwatersrand) and the Free State (around Welkom) | Jewellery, electronics such as cellphones and computers, coins |\n| **Platinum** | North West (around Rustenburg) and Limpopo | **Catalytic converters** in cars, which make exhaust gases cleaner; jewellery |\n| **Coal** | Mpumalanga (around eMalahleni, which means *place of coal*) | Burned in **power stations** to make **electricity**; also used to make steel |\n| **Diamonds** | Northern Cape (Kimberley), along the west coast and in the sea | Jewellery; because diamond is so hard, also for cutting, drilling and grinding |\n| **Iron ore** | Northern Cape (around Kathu) | To make **iron** and **steel** for cars, buildings, bridges and tools |\n| **Manganese** | Northern Cape (in the Kalahari, near Hotazel) | Makes steel harder and stronger |\n| **Chrome** | North West, Limpopo and Mpumalanga | **Stainless steel** (for sinks, pots and knives) and shiny chrome layers |\n\n> **Remember:** Most of South Africa’s **electricity** comes from **coal** that is burned in power stations.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not swap the provinces for **gold** and **platinum**. We find **gold** in Gauteng and the Free State; **platinum** in North West and Limpopo.\n\n## Minerals on a map\n\nOn a map, minerals are shown with **symbols**, and the **key** explains what each symbol means. It can be a shape, a picture or a letter. Here is an example of such a key:\n\n| Symbol | Mineral |\n|---|---|\n| ▲ (triangle) | coal |\n| ● (dot) | gold |\n| ◆ (diamond shape) | diamonds |\n| ■ (square) | iron ore |\n| ★ (star) | platinum |\n\nOn a mineral map of South Africa with this key you would see many ▲ in Mpumalanga, ● in Gauteng and the Free State, ★ in North West and Limpopo, and ◆ and ■ in the Northern Cape. The more symbols in an area, the more mines there are.\n\nRemember: every map can choose its own symbols. So always read the key first.\n\n## Why are minerals important?\n\n- Mining gives **jobs** to many people, and towns grow around mines.\n- Many minerals are sold to other countries (**export**). This brings money into South Africa.\n- We use minerals every day: the **steel** in a car or bridge, the **electricity** in your home and the gold in a cellphone.\n- Minerals are **non-renewable**: once they have been mined, they do not grow back. That is why we must use them wisely and **recycle** metal where we can."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Mineraal","en":"Mineral"},"def":{"af":"’n Natuurlike, nie-lewende stof wat in die rotse van die aarde gevorm het, soos goud of diamant.","en":"A natural, non-living substance that formed in the rocks of the Earth, such as gold or diamond."}},{"term":{"af":"Erts","en":"Ore"},"def":{"af":"Rots wat genoeg van ’n mineraal of metaal bevat om die myn werd te wees, soos ystererts.","en":"Rock that contains enough of a mineral or metal to be worth mining, such as iron ore."}},{"term":{"af":"Mynbou","en":"Mining"},"def":{"af":"Om minerale uit die grond te haal.","en":"Taking minerals out of the ground."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitvoer","en":"Export"},"def":{"af":"Om goedere, soos minerale, aan ander lande te verkoop.","en":"Selling goods, such as minerals, to other countries."}},{"term":{"af":"Nie-hernubaar","en":"Non-renewable"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat nie weer aangroei of vervang word nie as dit opgebruik is, soos minerale en steenkool.","en":"Something that does not grow back or get replaced once it is used up, like minerals and coal."}},{"term":{"af":"Katalitiese omsetter","en":"Catalytic converter"},"def":{"af":"’n Deel in ’n motor se uitlaatpyp, met platinum daarin, wat die uitlaatgasse skoner maak.","en":"A part in a car’s exhaust pipe, with platinum in it, that makes the exhaust gases cleaner."}},{"term":{"af":"Staal","en":"Steel"},"def":{"af":"’n Sterk metaal wat van yster gemaak word, dikwels met mangaan of chroom bygevoeg.","en":"A strong metal made from iron, often with manganese or chrome added."}},{"term":{"af":"Kragstasie","en":"Power station"},"def":{"af":"’n Groot aanleg waar elektrisiteit opgewek word, in Suid-Afrika meestal deur steenkool te verbrand.","en":"A large plant where electricity is made, in South Africa mostly by burning coal."}},{"term":{"af":"Herwinning","en":"Recycling"},"def":{"af":"Om ou materiaal, soos metaal, weer te gebruik om nuwe dinge te maak.","en":"Using old material, such as metal, again to make new things."}},{"term":{"af":"Mineraalkaart","en":"Mineral map"},"def":{"af":"’n Kaart wat met simbole wys waar minerale gevind en gemyn word.","en":"A map that uses symbols to show where minerals are found and mined."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n mineraalkaart","en":"Read a mineral map"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato se kaart het hierdie sleutel: ▲ = steenkool, ● = goud, ★ = platinum, ◆ = diamante, ■ = ystererts. Sy sien baie ▲ in Mpumalanga en baie ★ rondom Rustenburg in Noordwes. (a) Wat word in Mpumalanga gemyn, en waarvoor word dit gebruik? (b) Watter mineraal word rondom Rustenburg gemyn, en waarvoor word dit in motors gebruik?","en":"Lerato’s map has this key: ▲ = coal, ● = gold, ★ = platinum, ◆ = diamonds, ■ = iron ore. She sees many ▲ in Mpumalanga and many ★ around Rustenburg in North West. (a) What is mined in Mpumalanga, and what is it used for? (b) Which mineral is mined around Rustenburg, and what is it used for in cars?"},"steps":[{"af":"Kyk in die sleutel: ▲ = **steenkool**. Steenkool word in kragstasies verbrand om **elektrisiteit** op te wek.","en":"Look in the key: ▲ = **coal**. Coal is burned in power stations to make **electricity**."},{"af":"Kyk weer in die sleutel: ★ = **platinum**.","en":"Look in the key again: ★ = **platinum**."},{"af":"Platinum word in motors se **katalitiese omsetters** gebruik om die uitlaatgasse skoner te maak.","en":"Platinum is used in cars’ **catalytic converters** to make the exhaust gases cleaner."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Steenkool – vir elektrisiteit (b) Platinum – in katalitiese omsetters","en":"(a) Coal – for electricity (b) Platinum – in catalytic converters"}},{"title":{"af":"Van ystererts tot ’n motor","en":"From iron ore to a car"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik die verskil tussen ystererts en yster, en beskryf kortliks hoe ystererts uit die Noord-Kaap deel van ’n motor word.","en":"Explain the difference between iron ore and iron, and briefly describe how iron ore from the Northern Cape becomes part of a car."},"steps":[{"af":"**Ystererts** is rots wat baie yster bevat, maar ook ander stowwe. **Yster** is die suiwer metaal.","en":"**Iron ore** is rock that contains a lot of iron, but also other substances. **Iron** is the pure metal."},{"af":"Die erts word naby Kathu gemyn, fyngemaak en baie warm verhit sodat die yster uitsmelt.","en":"The ore is mined near Kathu, crushed and heated until very hot so that the iron melts out."},{"af":"Van die yster word **staal** gemaak; mangaan maak dit sterker en chroom maak dit vlekvry.","en":"The iron is made into **steel**; manganese makes it stronger and chrome makes it stainless."},{"af":"Die staal word in plate gerol en in ’n fabriek gebruik vir die bakwerk en onderdele van ’n motor.","en":"The steel is rolled into sheets and used in a factory for the body and parts of a car."}],"answer":{"af":"Erts is rots met yster daarin; yster is die metaal. Erts → yster → staal → motor.","en":"Ore is rock with iron in it; iron is the metal. Ore → iron → steel → car."}},{"title":{"af":"Van steenkool tot lig","en":"From coal to light"},"problem":{"af":"Beskryf hoe steenkool wat in Mpumalanga gemyn word, die lig in Sipho se huis laat brand.","en":"Describe how coal that is mined in Mpumalanga makes the light in Sipho’s house shine."},"steps":[{"af":"Die steenkool word uit die grond gemyn en na ’n **kragstasie** vervoer.","en":"The coal is mined from the ground and transported to a **power station**."},{"af":"In die kragstasie word die steenkool **verbrand**. Die hitte kook water, en die stoom draai groot **turbines**.","en":"In the power station the coal is **burned**. The heat boils water, and the steam turns big **turbines**."},{"af":"Die turbines dryf **kragopwekkers** aan wat elektrisiteit maak.","en":"The turbines drive **generators** that make electricity."},{"af":"Kraglyne vervoer die elektrisiteit na dorpe en huise, waar dit die lig laat brand.","en":"Power lines carry the electricity to towns and houses, where it makes the light shine."}],"answer":{"af":"Myn → kragstasie (steenkool verbrand, stoom draai turbines) → kraglyne → huis","en":"Mine → power station (coal burned, steam turns turbines) → power lines → house"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is ’n erts?","en":"What is an ore?"},"options":[{"af":"Rots wat genoeg van ’n mineraal bevat om die myn werd te wees","en":"Rock that contains enough of a mineral to be worth mining"},{"af":"’n Soort plant wat minerale in die grond maak","en":"A kind of plant that makes minerals in the ground"},{"af":"Die groot gat wat ’n myn in die grond maak","en":"The big hole that a mine makes in the ground"},{"af":"’n Masjien wat goud en diamante skoonmaak","en":"A machine that cleans gold and diamonds"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Erts is rots met genoeg van ’n mineraal of metaal daarin, soos ystererts. Dit word gemyn en verwerk om die metaal te kry.","en":"An ore is rock with enough of a mineral or metal in it, like iron ore. It is mined and processed to get the metal."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Platinum word in motors se katalitiese ___ gebruik.","en":"Platinum is used in cars’ catalytic ___."},"answers":{"af":["omsetters","omsetter"],"en":["converters","converter"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["enjins","bande","batterye"],"en":["engines","tyres","batteries"]}},"explain":{"af":"Katalitiese omsetters in die uitlaatpyp gebruik platinum om skadelike uitlaatgasse skoner te maak.","en":"Catalytic converters in the exhaust pipe use platinum to make harmful exhaust gases cleaner."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter provinsie word die meeste steenkool gemyn?","en":"In which province is the most coal mined?"},"options":[{"af":"Wes-Kaap","en":"Western Cape"},{"af":"Noord-Kaap","en":"Northern Cape"},{"af":"Mpumalanga","en":"Mpumalanga"},{"af":"Oos-Kaap","en":"Eastern Cape"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Mpumalanga het die grootste steenkoolvelde, bv. rondom eMalahleni (‘plek van steenkool’). Die Noord-Kaap is bekend vir diamante, ystererts en mangaan.","en":"Mpumalanga has the biggest coalfields, e.g. around eMalahleni (‘place of coal’). The Northern Cape is known for diamonds, iron ore and manganese."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Steenkool word in kragstasies verbrand om elektrisiteit op te wek.","en":"Coal is burned in power stations to make electricity."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die meeste van Suid-Afrika se elektrisiteit kom van steenkool wat in kragstasies verbrand word.","en":"True. Most of South Africa’s electricity comes from coal that is burned in power stations."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar in Suid-Afrika word diamante gemyn?","en":"Where in South Africa are diamonds mined?"},"options":[{"af":"Rondom eMalahleni in Mpumalanga","en":"Around eMalahleni in Mpumalanga"},{"af":"By Kimberley en langs die weskus","en":"At Kimberley and along the west coast"},{"af":"In die Karoo by die Sneeuberge","en":"In the Karoo at the Sneeuberg"},{"af":"In die suikerrietlande van KwaZulu-Natal","en":"In the sugar cane fields of KwaZulu-Natal"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Diamante word in die Noord-Kaap gemyn, by Kimberley, en ook langs die weskus en in die see. eMalahleni is bekend vir steenkool.","en":"Diamonds are mined in the Northern Cape, at Kimberley, and also along the west coast and in the sea. eMalahleni is known for coal."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke mineraal by een van sy gebruike.","en":"Match each mineral to one of its uses."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Goud","en":"Gold"},"r":{"af":"Elektronika in selfone en rekenaars","en":"Electronics in cellphones and computers"}},{"l":{"af":"Platinum","en":"Platinum"},"r":{"af":"Katalitiese omsetters in motors","en":"Catalytic converters in cars"}},{"l":{"af":"Steenkool","en":"Coal"},"r":{"af":"Elektrisiteit in kragstasies","en":"Electricity in power stations"}},{"l":{"af":"Ystererts","en":"Iron ore"},"r":{"af":"Staal vir brûe en geboue","en":"Steel for bridges and buildings"}},{"l":{"af":"Diamante","en":"Diamonds"},"r":{"af":"Gereedskap om mee te sny en te boor","en":"Tools for cutting and drilling"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke mineraal het sy eie gebruike. Diamant is so hard dat dit ander harde stowwe kan sny, en goud gelei elektrisiteit goed en roes nie.","en":"Each mineral has its own uses. Diamond is so hard that it can cut other hard materials, and gold conducts electricity well and does not rust."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarvoor word ystererts hoofsaaklik gebruik?","en":"What is iron ore mainly used for?"},"options":[{"af":"Om juweliersware soos ringe te maak","en":"To make jewellery such as rings"},{"af":"Om elektrisiteit in kragstasies op te wek","en":"To make electricity in power stations"},{"af":"Om motors se uitlaatgasse skoner te maak","en":"To make cars’ exhaust gases cleaner"},{"af":"Om staal te maak vir motors, geboue en brûe","en":"To make steel for cars, buildings and bridges"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Uit ystererts kry ons yster, en van yster maak ons staal. Elektrisiteit kom van steenkool, en platinum maak uitlaatgasse skoner.","en":"From iron ore we get iron, and from iron we make steel. Electricity comes from coal, and platinum makes exhaust gases cleaner."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op ’n mineraalkaart is die sleutel: ▲ = steenkool, ◆ = diamante, ★ = platinum, ● = goud. Rondom Rustenburg is daar baie ★. Wat word daar gemyn?","en":"On a mineral map the key is: ▲ = coal, ◆ = diamonds, ★ = platinum, ● = gold. Around Rustenburg there are many ★. What is mined there?"},"options":[{"af":"Steenkool","en":"Coal"},{"af":"Diamante","en":"Diamonds"},{"af":"Platinum","en":"Platinum"},{"af":"Goud","en":"Gold"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Volgens die sleutel staan ★ vir platinum. Dit klop: Rustenburg in Noordwes is bekend vir platinummyne.","en":"According to the key, ★ stands for platinum. This fits: Rustenburg in North West is known for platinum mines."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die mineraal wat in Gauteng en die Vrystaat gemyn word en in juweliersware en selfone gebruik word, is ___.","en":"The mineral that is mined in Gauteng and the Free State and used in jewellery and cellphones is ___."},"answers":{"af":["goud"],"en":["gold"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["platinum","steenkool","mangaan"],"en":["platinum","coal","manganese"]}},"explain":{"af":"Goud word in Gauteng (die Witwatersrand) en die Vrystaat gemyn. Platinum kom uit Noordwes en Limpopo.","en":"Gold is mined in Gauteng (the Witwatersrand) and the Free State. Platinum comes from North West and Limpopo."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom sê ons minerale is nie-hernubaar?","en":"Why do we say minerals are non-renewable?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle is te duur om uit die grond te myn","en":"They are too expensive to mine from the ground"},{"af":"Hulle groei nie weer aan wanneer hulle uitgemyn is nie","en":"They do not grow back once they have been mined"},{"af":"Hulle kan nie aan ander lande verkoop word nie","en":"They cannot be sold to other countries"},{"af":"Hulle word net in een provinsie gevind","en":"They are only found in one province"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Minerale het miljoene jare gevat om te vorm. As ons hulle uitmyn, is hulle op. Daarom moet ons hulle verstandig gebruik en herwin.","en":"Minerals took millions of years to form. Once we mine them, they are gone. That is why we must use them wisely and recycle."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Mineraal is iets wat mense in fabrieke maak.","en":"A mineral is something that people make in factories."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Minerale is natuurlike stowwe wat in die rotse van die aarde gevorm het. Mense myn hulle, maar maak hulle nie.","en":"False. Minerals are natural substances that formed in the rocks of the Earth. People mine them, but do not make them."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter mineraal word by staal gevoeg om vlekvrye staal te maak?","en":"Which mineral is added to steel to make stainless steel?"},"options":[{"af":"Steenkool","en":"Coal"},{"af":"Goud","en":"Gold"},{"af":"Diamant","en":"Diamond"},{"af":"Chroom","en":"Chrome"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Chroom maak staal vlekvry, sodat dit nie maklik roes nie – dink aan ’n blink wasbak of ’n mes.","en":"Chrome makes steel stainless, so that it does not rust easily – think of a shiny sink or a knife."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Rots wat genoeg yster bevat om dit te myn, heet ___.","en":"Rock that contains enough iron to mine it is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["ystererts"],"en":["iron ore"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["staal","steenkool","mangaan"],"en":["steel","coal","manganese"]}},"explain":{"af":"Ystererts is die rots wat gemyn word. Staal is wat later van die yster gemaak word.","en":"Iron ore is the rock that is mined. Steel is what is made from the iron later."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is mynbou belangrik vir Suid-Afrika?","en":"Why is mining important for South Africa?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit gee werk en bring geld in deur uitvoer","en":"It gives jobs and brings in money through exports"},{"af":"Dit maak die lug en riviere skoner","en":"It makes the air and rivers cleaner"},{"af":"Dit laat meer reën oor die land val","en":"It makes more rain fall over the country"},{"af":"Dit maak nuwe minerale in die grond","en":"It makes new minerals in the ground"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Myne gee werk aan baie mense, en minerale wat aan ander lande verkoop word, bring geld na Suid-Afrika. Mynbou maak die omgewing eerder vuiler, nie skoner nie.","en":"Mines give jobs to many people, and minerals sold to other countries bring money into South Africa. Mining tends to make the environment dirtier, not cleaner."}}]},{"id":"sw5-t4-geo-mynbou","title":{"af":"Mynbou, mense en die omgewing","en":"Mining, people and the environment"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die drie mynboumetodes kan beskryf, kan vertel hoe diamante en goud Kimberley en Johannesburg laat ontstaan het, en kan verduidelik hoe mynbou mense en die omgewing raak en hoe grond herstel word.","en":"You will be able to describe the three mining methods, tell how diamonds and gold made Kimberley and Johannesburg grow, and explain how mining affects people and the environment and how land is restored."},"summary":{"af":"## Hoe word minerale gemyn?\n\n| Metode | Hoe dit werk | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Oopgroefmyn** | Die erts lê **naby die oppervlak**. Die grond bo-oor word weggegrawe en ’n groot, oop gat word gemaak. Groot masjiene en trokke haal die erts uit. | Ystererts naby Kathu; baie steenkoolmyne in Mpumalanga |\n| **Ondergrondse myn (skagmyn)** | Die erts lê **diep**. ’n **Skag** (’n regaf tonnel) word gegrawe. Hysers neem werkers en masjiene af, en tonnels loop sywaarts na die erts. | Goudmyne aan die Witwatersrand; sommige is meer as 3 km diep |\n| **Alluviale mynbou** | Riviere en die see het oor baie jare minerale uit rotse gespoel en in sand en gruis neergesit. Die gruis word **gespoel** en gesif om die minerale te vind. | Diamante langs die Oranjerivier en die weskus, ook van die seebodem af |\n\n## Diamante en goud: ’n kort geskiedenis\n\n- **Diamante, 1867:** Die eerste diamant is naby die Oranjerivier, by Hopetown, gevind. ’n Paar jaar later is baie diamante op ’n koppie gevind waar **Kimberley** nou is. Duisende mense het met pikke en grawe gegrawe, en die gat het al hoe dieper geword. Vandag is dit die **Groot Gat**, vol water en ’n bekende toeristeplek. Kimberley het vinnig van ’n tentdorp tot ’n stad gegroei.\n- **Goud, 1886:** Goud is aan die **Witwatersrand** ontdek. Duisende gelukssoekers het gekom, en die tentdorp het vinnig gegroei tot **Johannesburg**, vandag Suid-Afrika se grootste stad. Dit word ook **eGoli** genoem, *plek van goud*.\n- Die goud lê diep onder die grond, so groot maatskappye, masjiene en baie werkers was nodig. Spoorlyne en paaie is gebou, en die myne het die land se ekonomie verander.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie die jaartalle omruil nie. **Diamante (1867)** kom eerste en het Kimberley laat groei; **goud (1886)** kom later en het Johannesburg laat ontstaan.\n\n## Mynbou en mense\n\n- **Werk:** Myne gee werk aan mynwerkers, ingenieurs, masjienoperateurs en trokbestuurders, en ook aan winkels en dienste in mynboudorpe.\n- **Trekarbeid:** Baie mynwerkers kom van ver af – uit ander provinsies en uit buurlande soos Lesotho en Mosambiek. Hulle woon maande lank in **hostelle** by die myn en sien hul gesinne net af en toe. Dit is moeilik vir gesinne, want kinders sien hul ouers min.\n- **Veiligheid:** Mynbou kan gevaarlik wees: **rotsstortings**, gasontploffings in steenkoolmyne, **stof** wat longsiektes veroorsaak, hitte diep onder die grond en harde geraas. Werkers word beskerm deur **helms met lampe**, veiligheidstewels, oorbeskermers, stofmaskers, **opleiding**, vars lug wat afgepomp word, en stutte wat die tonnels se dakke ondersteun.\n\n## Mynbou en die omgewing\n\n| Probleem | Wat gebeur |\n|---|---|\n| **Waterbesoedeling** | Water uit ou myne kan suur en giftig word (**suur mynwater**) en in riviere invloei. Dit benadeel plante, visse en mense. |\n| **Lugbesoedeling** | Stof waai van mynhope af, en steenkoolkragstasies stel rook en gasse vry. |\n| **Mynhope** | Die fyn sand en rots wat oorbly ná die erts verwerk is, word in groot hope gestort, soos die geel mynhope rondom Johannesburg. |\n| **Beskadigde grond** | Oopgroefmyne laat groot gate, en plante en diere verloor hul lewensruimte. |\n\n**Rehabilitasie** beteken om die grond ná mynbou weer gesond te maak. Die wet sê myne moet die grond herstel. Hulle kan:\n\n1. gate opvul en die grond gelykmaak;\n2. bogrond terugsit en gras en bome plant;\n3. besoedelde water opvang en skoonmaak;\n4. mynhope bedek en beplant sodat stof nie waai nie.\n\n> **Onthou:** Mynbou het **voordele** (werk, geld en minerale wat ons nodig het) én **nadele** (gevaar vir werkers en besoedeling). Goeie mynbou probeer die voordele groot en die nadele klein hou.","en":"## How are minerals mined?\n\n| Method | How it works | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Open-pit mine** | The ore lies **close to the surface**. The ground on top is dug away and a big, open hole is made. Huge machines and trucks take out the ore. | Iron ore near Kathu; many coal mines in Mpumalanga |\n| **Underground (shaft) mine** | The ore lies **deep down**. A **shaft** (a tunnel going straight down) is dug. Lifts take workers and machines down, and tunnels run sideways to the ore. | Gold mines on the Witwatersrand; some are more than 3 km deep |\n| **Alluvial mining** | Over many years rivers and the sea washed minerals out of rocks and left them in sand and gravel. The gravel is **washed** and sieved to find the minerals. | Diamonds along the Orange River and the west coast, also from the sea floor |\n\n## Diamonds and gold: a short history\n\n- **Diamonds, 1867:** The first diamond was found near the Orange River, at Hopetown. A few years later many diamonds were found on a koppie where **Kimberley** is now. Thousands of people dug with picks and shovels, and the hole became deeper and deeper. Today it is the **Big Hole**, filled with water and a well-known tourist spot. Kimberley quickly grew from a tent town into a city.\n- **Gold, 1886:** Gold was discovered on the **Witwatersrand**. Thousands of fortune seekers came, and the tent town quickly grew into **Johannesburg**, today South Africa’s biggest city. It is also called **eGoli**, *place of gold*.\n- The gold lies deep underground, so big companies, machines and many workers were needed. Railways and roads were built, and the mines changed the country’s economy.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not swap the dates. **Diamonds (1867)** come first and made Kimberley grow; **gold (1886)** comes later and led to Johannesburg.\n\n## Mining and people\n\n- **Jobs:** Mines give work to miners, engineers, machine operators and truck drivers, and also to shops and services in mining towns.\n- **Migrant labour:** Many mineworkers come from far away – from other provinces and from neighbouring countries such as Lesotho and Mozambique. They live for months in **hostels** at the mine and only see their families now and then. This is hard for families, because children see their parents very little.\n- **Safety:** Mining can be dangerous: **rockfalls**, gas explosions in coal mines, **dust** that causes lung diseases, heat deep underground and loud noise. Workers are protected by **helmets with lamps**, safety boots, ear protectors, dust masks, **training**, fresh air pumped down, and supports that hold up the roofs of the tunnels.\n\n## Mining and the environment\n\n| Problem | What happens |\n|---|---|\n| **Water pollution** | Water from old mines can become acidic and poisonous (**acid mine water**) and flow into rivers. It harms plants, fish and people. |\n| **Air pollution** | Dust blows off mine dumps, and coal power stations give off smoke and gases. |\n| **Mine dumps** | The fine sand and rock left over after the ore has been processed is dumped in big heaps, like the yellow mine dumps around Johannesburg. |\n| **Damaged land** | Open-pit mines leave huge holes, and plants and animals lose their habitat. |\n\n**Rehabilitation** means making the land healthy again after mining. The law says mines must restore the land. They can:\n\n1. fill in holes and level the ground;\n2. put back topsoil and plant grass and trees;\n3. collect polluted water and clean it;\n4. cover mine dumps and plant on them so that dust does not blow.\n\n> **Remember:** Mining has **advantages** (jobs, money and minerals we need) and **disadvantages** (danger to workers and pollution). Good mining tries to keep the advantages big and the disadvantages small."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Oopgroefmyn","en":"Open-pit mine"},"def":{"af":"’n Myn waar ’n groot, oop gat gegrawe word om erts naby die oppervlak uit te haal.","en":"A mine where a big, open hole is dug to take out ore close to the surface."}},{"term":{"af":"Ondergrondse myn (skagmyn)","en":"Underground (shaft) mine"},"def":{"af":"’n Myn met skagte en tonnels om erts te bereik wat diep onder die grond lê.","en":"A mine with shafts and tunnels to reach ore that lies deep underground."}},{"term":{"af":"Skag","en":"Shaft"},"def":{"af":"’n Regaf tonnel waardeur hysers werkers en masjiene na die diep dele van ’n myn neem.","en":"A tunnel going straight down, through which lifts take workers and machines to the deep parts of a mine."}},{"term":{"af":"Alluviale mynbou","en":"Alluvial mining"},"def":{"af":"Om minerale, soos diamante, uit die sand en gruis van riviere of die see te spoel en te sif.","en":"Washing and sieving minerals, such as diamonds, out of the sand and gravel of rivers or the sea."}},{"term":{"af":"Groot Gat","en":"Big Hole"},"def":{"af":"Die groot gat in Kimberley wat mense met die hand gegrawe het om diamante te soek.","en":"The huge hole in Kimberley that people dug by hand to look for diamonds."}},{"term":{"af":"Trekarbeid","en":"Migrant labour"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer werkers ver van hul huise af gaan werk en hul gesinne net af en toe sien.","en":"When workers go to work far from their homes and only see their families now and then."}},{"term":{"af":"Hostel","en":"Hostel"},"def":{"af":"’n Groot gebou by ’n myn waar baie mynwerkers saam woon.","en":"A large building at a mine where many mineworkers live together."}},{"term":{"af":"Mynhoop","en":"Mine dump"},"def":{"af":"’n Groot hoop fyn sand en rots wat oorbly nadat die erts verwerk is.","en":"A big heap of fine sand and rock left over after the ore has been processed."}},{"term":{"af":"Suur mynwater","en":"Acid mine water"},"def":{"af":"Suur, giftige water uit myne wat riviere kan besoedel.","en":"Acidic, poisonous water from mines that can pollute rivers."}},{"term":{"af":"Rehabilitasie","en":"Rehabilitation"},"def":{"af":"Om grond ná mynbou weer gesond te maak, bv. deur gate op te vul en plante te plant.","en":"Making land healthy again after mining, e.g. by filling in holes and planting plants."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Kies die regte mynboumetode","en":"Choose the right mining method"},"problem":{"af":"’n Maatskappy vind (a) steenkool net 30 m onder die oppervlak, (b) goud 3 km diep onder die grond en (c) diamante in die gruis van ’n ou rivierbedding. Watter mynboumetode moet hulle vir elkeen gebruik?","en":"A company finds (a) coal only 30 m below the surface, (b) gold 3 km deep underground and (c) diamonds in the gravel of an old riverbed. Which mining method must they use for each?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die steenkool lê **naby die oppervlak**. Dit is goedkoper om die grond bo-oor weg te grawe: ’n **oopgroefmyn**.","en":"(a) The coal lies **close to the surface**. It is cheaper to dig away the ground on top: an **open-pit mine**."},{"af":"(b) Die goud lê **baie diep**. ’n Oop gat van 3 km is onmoontlik, so hulle grawe ’n skag: ’n **ondergrondse myn**.","en":"(b) The gold lies **very deep**. An open hole of 3 km is impossible, so they dig a shaft: an **underground mine**."},{"af":"(c) Die diamante lê in **riviergruis**. Die gruis word gespoel en gesif: **alluviale mynbou**.","en":"(c) The diamonds lie in **river gravel**. The gravel is washed and sieved: **alluvial mining**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Oopgroefmyn (b) Ondergrondse myn (c) Alluviale mynbou","en":"(a) Open-pit mine (b) Underground mine (c) Alluvial mining"}},{"title":{"af":"Hoe het Johannesburg ontstaan?","en":"How did Johannesburg begin?"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik in ’n paar stappe hoe die ontdekking van goud in 1886 tot die stad Johannesburg gelei het.","en":"Explain in a few steps how the discovery of gold in 1886 led to the city of Johannesburg."},"steps":[{"af":"In 1886 is goud aan die **Witwatersrand** ontdek.","en":"In 1886 gold was discovered on the **Witwatersrand**."},{"af":"Duisende gelukssoekers het gekom en in tente gewoon – ’n **tentdorp** het ontstaan.","en":"Thousands of fortune seekers came and lived in tents – a **tent town** grew up."},{"af":"Die goud lê diep, so groot myne met baie werkers is oopgemaak. Winkels, huise, paaie en spoorlyne het gevolg.","en":"The gold lies deep, so big mines with many workers were opened. Shops, houses, roads and railways followed."},{"af":"Die tentdorp het vinnig tot ’n stad gegroei: **Johannesburg**, of **eGoli** (plek van goud).","en":"The tent town quickly grew into a city: **Johannesburg**, or **eGoli** (place of gold)."}],"answer":{"af":"Goud ontdek → gelukssoekers en ’n tentdorp → myne, werkers en dienste → die stad Johannesburg","en":"Gold discovered → fortune seekers and a tent town → mines, workers and services → the city of Johannesburg"}},{"title":{"af":"Herstel ’n ou myn","en":"Restore an old mine"},"problem":{"af":"’n Ou oopgroefmyn naby Zanele se dorp is gesluit. Daar is ’n groot gat, ’n stowwerige mynhoop en suur water wat in die rivier loop. Noem twee probleme en sê hoe die grond gerehabiliteer kan word.","en":"An old open-pit mine near Zanele’s town has closed. There is a big hole, a dusty mine dump and acidic water running into the river. Name two problems and say how the land can be rehabilitated."},"steps":[{"af":"**Probleem 1:** Stof waai van die mynhoop af – dit is **lugbesoedeling** en sleg vir mense se longe.","en":"**Problem 1:** Dust blows off the mine dump – this is **air pollution** and bad for people’s lungs."},{"af":"**Probleem 2:** Suur mynwater vloei in die rivier – dit is **waterbesoedeling** wat visse, plante en mense benadeel.","en":"**Problem 2:** Acid mine water flows into the river – this is **water pollution** that harms fish, plants and people."},{"af":"**Rehabilitasie:** vul die gat op, sit bogrond terug, bedek en beplant die mynhoop, en vang die suur water op en maak dit skoon.","en":"**Rehabilitation:** fill in the hole, put back topsoil, cover and plant the mine dump, and collect and clean the acidic water."}],"answer":{"af":"Probleme: stof (lugbesoedeling) en suur water (waterbesoedeling). Rehabilitasie: gat opvul, plant op die mynhoop, water skoonmaak.","en":"Problems: dust (air pollution) and acidic water (water pollution). Rehabilitation: fill the hole, plant on the dump, clean the water."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Mynwerker se veiligheidstoerusting","en":"A mineworker’s safety equipment"},"problem":{"af":"Johan werk in ’n ondergrondse myn. Hy dra ’n helm met ’n lamp, ’n stofmasker, oorbeskermers en veiligheidstewels. Verduidelik waarteen elkeen hom beskerm.","en":"Johan works in an underground mine. He wears a helmet with a lamp, a dust mask, ear protectors and safety boots. Explain what each one protects him against."},"steps":[{"af":"**Helm met lamp:** beskerm sy kop teen vallende klippe, en die lamp laat hom in die donker tonnels sien.","en":"**Helmet with lamp:** protects his head against falling stones, and the lamp lets him see in the dark tunnels."},{"af":"**Stofmasker:** keer dat hy stof inasem wat **longsiektes** kan veroorsaak.","en":"**Dust mask:** stops him breathing in dust that can cause **lung diseases**."},{"af":"**Oorbeskermers:** beskerm sy gehoor teen die harde geraas van masjiene en boorwerk.","en":"**Ear protectors:** protect his hearing against the loud noise of machines and drilling."},{"af":"**Veiligheidstewels:** beskerm sy voete teen swaar voorwerpe en skerp klippe.","en":"**Safety boots:** protect his feet against heavy objects and sharp stones."}],"answer":{"af":"Helm – kop en lig; masker – longe; oorbeskermers – gehoor; stewels – voete.","en":"Helmet – head and light; mask – lungs; ear protectors – hearing; boots – feet."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter mynboumetode word gebruik as die erts naby die oppervlak lê?","en":"Which mining method is used when the ore lies close to the surface?"},"options":[{"af":"Ondergrondse myn","en":"Underground mine"},{"af":"Alluviale mynbou","en":"Alluvial mining"},{"af":"Oopgroefmyn","en":"Open-pit mine"},{"af":"Skagmyn","en":"Shaft mine"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"As die erts naby die oppervlak lê, word die grond bo-oor weggegrawe en ’n oopgroefmyn gemaak. Skagmyne (ondergrondse myne) is vir erts wat diep lê.","en":"If the ore lies close to the surface, the ground on top is dug away and an open-pit mine is made. Shaft mines (underground mines) are for ore that lies deep."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Johannesburg het ontstaan ná die ontdekking van goud aan die Witwatersrand.","en":"Johannesburg began after gold was discovered on the Witwatersrand."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Ná die ontdekking van goud in 1886 het ’n tentdorp vinnig tot Johannesburg gegroei. Daarom word dit eGoli genoem.","en":"True. After gold was discovered in 1886, a tent town quickly grew into Johannesburg. That is why it is called eGoli."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter jaar is goud aan die Witwatersrand ontdek?","en":"In which year was gold discovered on the Witwatersrand?"},"options":[{"af":"1867","en":"1867"},{"af":"1886","en":"1886"},{"af":"1910","en":"1910"},{"af":"1948","en":"1948"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Goud is in 1886 ontdek. Moenie dit met 1867 verwar nie – dit is die jaar toe die eerste diamant naby die Oranjerivier gevind is.","en":"Gold was discovered in 1886. Do not confuse it with 1867 – that is the year the first diamond was found near the Orange River."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is trekarbeid?","en":"What is migrant labour?"},"options":[{"af":"Werkers wat ver van hul huise af werk en hul gesinne min sien","en":"Workers who work far from their homes and see their families very little"},{"af":"Werkers wat met trekkers en trokke in die myn werk","en":"Workers who work with tractors and trucks in the mine"},{"af":"Werk wat net in die somermaande gedoen word","en":"Work that is only done in the summer months"},{"af":"Werkers wat elke aand by hul gesinne tuis slaap","en":"Workers who sleep at home with their families every night"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Trekarbeiders kom van ver af, bv. uit ander provinsies of uit Lesotho en Mosambiek. Hulle woon in hostelle by die myn en sien hul gesinne net af en toe.","en":"Migrant workers come from far away, e.g. from other provinces or from Lesotho and Mozambique. They live in hostels at the mine and see their families only now and then."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die Groot Gat, wat met die hand gegrawe is om diamante te soek, is in die stad ___.","en":"The Big Hole, which was dug by hand to look for diamonds, is in the city of ___."},"answers":{"af":["Kimberley"],"en":["Kimberley"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Johannesburg","Bloemfontein","Welkom"],"en":["Johannesburg","Bloemfontein","Welkom"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die Groot Gat is in Kimberley in die Noord-Kaap. Johannesburg en Welkom is bekend vir goud, nie diamante nie.","en":"The Big Hole is in Kimberley in the Northern Cape. Johannesburg and Welkom are known for gold, not diamonds."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke term by sy beskrywing.","en":"Match each term to its description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Oopgroefmyn","en":"Open-pit mine"},"r":{"af":"’n Groot, oop gat vir erts naby die oppervlak","en":"A big, open hole for ore close to the surface"}},{"l":{"af":"Ondergrondse myn","en":"Underground mine"},"r":{"af":"Skagte en tonnels na erts wat diep lê","en":"Shafts and tunnels to ore that lies deep"}},{"l":{"af":"Alluviale mynbou","en":"Alluvial mining"},"r":{"af":"Gruis uit riviere of die see spoel en sif","en":"Washing and sieving gravel from rivers or the sea"}},{"l":{"af":"Mynhoop","en":"Mine dump"},"r":{"af":"’n Hoop oorblywende sand en rots","en":"A heap of leftover sand and rock"}},{"l":{"af":"Rehabilitasie","en":"Rehabilitation"},"r":{"af":"Die grond ná mynbou weer gesond maak","en":"Making the land healthy again after mining"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die drie metodes hang af van waar die minerale lê: naby die oppervlak, diep onder die grond of in riviere en die see. Mynhope en rehabilitasie gaan oor die omgewing.","en":"The three methods depend on where the minerals lie: close to the surface, deep underground or in rivers and the sea. Mine dumps and rehabilitation are about the environment."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is ’n skag?","en":"What is a shaft?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Hoop sand wat oorbly ná die erts verwerk is","en":"A heap of sand left over after the ore is processed"},{"af":"’n Groot oop gat by die oppervlak","en":"A big open hole at the surface"},{"af":"’n Masjien wat gruis in ’n rivier spoel","en":"A machine that washes gravel in a river"},{"af":"’n Regaf tonnel wat diep in die grond af na die erts gaan","en":"A tunnel going straight down deep into the ground to the ore"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Skag gaan regaf in die grond in. Hysers neem werkers en masjiene daardeur af na die tonnels by die erts.","en":"A shaft goes straight down into the ground. Lifts take workers and machines down it to the tunnels at the ore."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer ’n myn die grond ná mynbou herstel en weer plante plant, heet dit ___.","en":"When a mine restores the land after mining and plants things again, it is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["rehabilitasie","rehabilitering"],"en":["rehabilitation"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["besoedeling","trekarbeid","uitvoer"],"en":["pollution","migrant labour","export"]}},"explain":{"af":"Rehabilitasie maak die grond weer gesond: gate word opgevul, bogrond teruggesit en gras en bome geplant.","en":"Rehabilitation makes the land healthy again: holes are filled in, topsoil is put back and grass and trees are planted."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter metode word gebruik om diamante uit die gruis langs die Oranjerivier te kry?","en":"Which method is used to get diamonds out of the gravel along the Orange River?"},"options":[{"af":"Oopgroefmyn","en":"Open-pit mine"},{"af":"Ondergrondse myn","en":"Underground mine"},{"af":"Skagmyn","en":"Shaft mine"},{"af":"Alluviale mynbou","en":"Alluvial mining"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die rivier het die diamante oor baie jare in sy gruis neergesit. Die gruis word gespoel en gesif – dit is alluviale mynbou.","en":"Over many years the river left the diamonds in its gravel. The gravel is washed and sieved – this is alluvial mining."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter toerusting beskerm ’n mynwerker teen longsiektes?","en":"Which equipment protects a mineworker against lung diseases?"},"options":[{"af":"Veiligheidstewels","en":"Safety boots"},{"af":"’n Stofmasker","en":"A dust mask"},{"af":"Oorbeskermers","en":"Ear protectors"},{"af":"’n Helm met ’n lamp","en":"A helmet with a lamp"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Stof in myne kan longsiektes veroorsaak. ’n Stofmasker keer dat die werker die stof inasem.","en":"Dust in mines can cause lung diseases. A dust mask stops the worker breathing in the dust."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Mynbou het geen invloed op die omgewing nie.","en":"Mining has no effect on the environment."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Mynbou kan water en lug besoedel, mynhope en groot gate laat, en plante en diere se lewensruimte vernietig. Daarom is rehabilitasie nodig.","en":"False. Mining can pollute water and air, leave mine dumps and huge holes, and destroy the habitat of plants and animals. That is why rehabilitation is needed."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die eerste diamant is in ___ naby die Oranjerivier gevind.","en":"The first diamond was found near the Orange River in ___."},"answers":{"af":["1867"],"en":["1867"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1886","1910","1948"],"en":["1886","1910","1948"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die eerste diamant is in 1867 by Hopetown gevind. Goud aan die Witwatersrand het later gekom, in 1886.","en":"The first diamond was found in 1867 at Hopetown. Gold on the Witwatersrand came later, in 1886."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter probleem veroorsaak suur mynwater?","en":"What problem does acid mine water cause?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit laat meer reën oor die myn val","en":"It makes more rain fall over the mine"},{"af":"Dit veroorsaak rotsstortings diep in die myn","en":"It causes rockfalls deep in the mine"},{"af":"Dit besoedel riviere en benadeel plante, visse en mense","en":"It pollutes rivers and harms plants, fish and people"},{"af":"Dit maak die mynhope rondom die stad geler","en":"It makes the mine dumps around the city more yellow"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Suur, giftige water uit ou myne vloei in riviere in en besoedel dit. Plante, visse en mense wat die water gebruik, word benadeel.","en":"Acidic, poisonous water from old mines flows into rivers and pollutes them. Plants, fish and people who use the water are harmed."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is die goudmyne aan die Witwatersrand ondergrondse myne en nie oopgroefmyne nie?","en":"Why are the gold mines on the Witwatersrand underground mines and not open-pit mines?"},"options":[{"af":"Die goud lê baie diep onder die grond","en":"The gold lies very deep underground"},{"af":"Die goud lê in die sand van riviere","en":"The gold lies in the sand of rivers"},{"af":"Daar is te veel water op die oppervlak","en":"There is too much water on the surface"},{"af":"Oopgroefmyne kan net steenkool myn","en":"Open-pit mines can only mine coal"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die goud lê kilometers diep. ’n Oop gat so diep is onmoontlik, so skagte en tonnels word gegrawe. Oopgroefmyne word vir baie minerale gebruik, solank dit naby die oppervlak lê.","en":"The gold lies kilometres deep. An open hole that deep is impossible, so shafts and tunnels are dug. Open-pit mines are used for many minerals, as long as they lie close to the surface."}}]}]}]},"geskiedenis":{"id":"geskiedenis","grade":5,"name":{"af":"Geskiedenis","en":"History"},"short":{"af":"Gesk","en":"Hist"},"icon":"🏺","color":"#92400e","intro":{"af":"Geskiedenis vorm saam met Geografie die vak Sosiale Wetenskappe. In Graad 5 leer jy oor die eerste mense van Suider-Afrika – die San-jagter-versamelaars, die Khoikhoi-veewagters en die Bantoesprekende boere wat yster gesmelt en in opstalle gewoon het – oor antieke Egipte, ’n groot Afrika-beskawing, en oor ons erfenis in die nege provinsies. Die eksamen toets feite en begrippe, maar ook of jy bronne soos rotsskilderye, foto’s, tabelle en kort tekste kan lees en in volsinne kan verduidelik wat hulle ons vertel.","en":"History forms the subject Social Sciences together with Geography. In Grade 5 you learn about the first people of southern Africa – the San hunter-gatherers, the Khoikhoi herders and the Bantu-speaking farmers who smelted iron and lived in homesteads – about ancient Egypt, a great African civilisation, and about our heritage in the nine provinces. The exam tests facts and concepts, but also whether you can read sources such as rock paintings, photos, tables and short texts and explain in full sentences what they tell us."},"examTips":[{"af":"Leer die sleutelterme met hul betekenis – baie vrae vra presies dit, soos jagter-versamelaar, veewagter, besproeiing en erfenis.","en":"Learn the key terms with their meanings – many questions ask exactly that, such as hunter-gatherer, herder, irrigation and heritage."},{"af":"By ’n bronvraag: sê eers watter soort bron dit is (primêr of sekondêr), beskryf wat jy sien, en sê wat die bron ons vertel én wat dit nie vertel nie.","en":"In a source question: first say what kind of source it is (primary or secondary), describe what you see, and say what the source tells us and what it does not tell us."},{"af":"Ken die verskille tussen die San, die Khoikhoi en die eerste boere. Teken self ’n vergelykingstabel met kos, woning, groepgrootte en leiers.","en":"Know the differences between the San, the Khoikhoi and the first farmers. Draw your own comparison table with food, homes, group size and leaders."},{"af":"Leer die paar belangrike datums (soos 1652, 1922 en 24 September), maar sê ‘ongeveer’ by ou tye, soos ‘ongeveer 2 000 jaar gelede’.","en":"Learn the few important dates (such as 1652, 1922 and 24 September), but say ‘about’ for ancient times, such as ‘about 2 000 years ago’."},{"af":"Antwoord ‘verduidelik’- en ‘waarom’-vrae in volsinne en gee altyd ’n rede met ‘omdat’ of ‘want’.","en":"Answer ‘explain’ and ‘why’ questions in full sentences and always give a reason using ‘because’."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"DBE Reënboog-werkboeke","en":"DBE Rainbow Workbooks"},"url":"https://www.education.gov.za/Curriculum/Workbooks.aspx","note":{"af":"Gratis amptelike CAPS-werkboeke van die Departement van Basiese Onderwys, in Afrikaans en Engels. Kyk op die webwerf watter Graad 5-werkboeke beskikbaar is.","en":"Free official CAPS workbooks from the Department of Basic Education, in Afrikaans and English. Check the website to see which Grade 5 workbooks are available."}},{"title":{"af":"Siyavula: oop handboeke en oefening","en":"Siyavula: open textbooks and practice"},"url":"https://www.siyavula.com","note":{"af":"Gratis oop handboeke en aanlyn oefening. Dit fokus veral op Wiskunde en Wetenskap, maar help jou om goeie studiegewoontes op te bou.","en":"Free open textbooks and online practice. It focuses mainly on Maths and Science, but helps you build good study habits."}}],"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Jagter-versamelaars en veewagters","en":"Hunter-gatherers and herders"},"topics":[{"id":"sw5-t1-gesk-san","title":{"af":"Die San: jagter-versamelaars","en":"The San: hunter-gatherers"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe die San as jagter-versamelaars gelewe het, en ’n rotsskildery as ’n bron kan lees om uit te vind wat dit ons van hulle vertel.","en":"You will be able to explain how the San lived as hunter-gatherers, and read a rock painting as a source to find out what it tells us about them."},"summary":{"af":"## Wie is die San?\n\nDie **San** is die eerste mense van Suider-Afrika. Hulle voorouers woon al **duisende jare** hier. Die San was nie net een groep nie: daar was baie groepe, elk met sy eie taal. Baie San-tale het **klikklanke**.\n\nDie San was **jagter-versamelaars**. Hulle het nie gewasse geplant of vee aangehou nie. Hulle het wilde diere **gejag** en **veldkos** (wilde plantkos) **versamel**. Hulle het in **klein groepe** van ’n paar families saamgewoon en saam rondgetrek.\n\n## Werk vir mans en vroue\n\n| Wie | Werk | Gereedskap |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mans | Jag wild soos elande en springbokke, en vang klein diere en voëls | Pyl en boog met **gif**, **strikke** |\n| Vroue | Versamel wortels, bolle, bessies, neute, insekte en voëleiers | **Graafstok** met ’n swaar klip met ’n gat daarin |\n\n- Die **gif** op die pylpunte is van kewerlarwes of plante gemaak. Dit werk stadig, daarom moes jagters ’n gewonde dier soms ure of selfs dae lank **spoorsny**.\n- Die vroue se veldkos was dikwels **die grootste deel** van die groep se kos, want jag het nie altyd geslaag nie.\n- **Volstruiseierdoppe** is as waterhouers gebruik en vol water in die sand begrawe vir droë tye. Van stukkies dop is **krale** gemaak.\n\nAs ’n jagter ’n eland geskiet het, het **almal** in die groep vleis gekry. Vandag deel jy, môre deel ’n ander met jou – so het almal oorleef. Niemand was ryk of arm nie, en daar was **geen hoofman** nie. Die groep het besluite saam geneem.\n\n## Op trek met die seisoene\n\nKos en water was nie die hele jaar op een plek nie. Die San het met die **seisoene** getrek na plekke waar plante ryp was en wild gewei het. Hulle het **tydelike skuilings** van takke en gras gebou, of in **grotte** en rotsskuilings gebly. Omdat hulle gereeld getrek het, het hulle **min besittings** gehad – net wat hulle kon dra.\n\nDie San het die natuur baie goed geken. Hulle kon diere aan hul **spore** uitken en het geweet watter plante kos, medisyne of gif is.\n\n## Rotskuns: ’n venster op die verlede\n\nDie San het duisende **rotsskilderye** gelaat, veral in grotte en rotsskuilings in berge soos die Drakensberg en die Sederberg. Op die vlaktes van die binneland, soos in die Noord-Kaap, het hulle **rotsgravures** gemaak: prente wat in die klip ingekap of ingekrap is.\n\n- **Verf:** rooi en geel **oker** (ysterryke grond), swart **houtskool** en wit klei, gemeng met dierevet, bloed of plantsap.\n- **Kwaste:** vere, diere-hare of stokkies.\n- Die **eland** is die dier wat die meeste in die Drakensberg geskilder is. Dit was vir die San ’n besonder kragtige dier.\n\nBaie skilderye wys die **trance-dans**. Die vroue het hande geklap en gesing, en die **genesers** het lank gedans totdat hulle in ’n **trance** (’n droomagtige toestand) gegaan het. Die San het geglo dat ’n geneser in ’n trance siekes kon genees, reën kon bring en met die geesteswêreld kon praat.\n\n> **Onthou:** ’n Rotsskildery is ’n **primêre bron**, want die San het dit self gemaak. Dit wys ons wat hulle gesien, gedoen en geglo het.\n\n## Hoe weet ons van die San?\n\nDie San het nie geskryf nie. Historici gebruik daarom ander **bronne**:\n\n1. **Rotskuns** – wys diere, jagtogte, dans en geloof.\n2. **Argeologie** – argeoloë grawe versigtig in grotte en vind klipgereedskap, volstruiseierkrale, bene van diere en ou vuurmaakplekke.\n3. **Mondelinge oorlewering** – stories en kennis wat ouers aan kinders oorvertel. In die 1870’s het Wilhelm Bleek en Lucy Lloyd in Kaapstad baie stories van ǀXam-San opgeskryf.\n\n’n Bron vertel nie alles nie. ’n Skildery wys byvoorbeeld ’n jagtog, maar nie wanneer dit was of wat die jagters se name was nie.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie dink die San het ‘niks’ gehad nie. Hulle het min **besittings** gehad, maar ryk **kennis**, kuns, musiek en gelowe.\n\n## Die San vandag\n\nVandag woon San-gemeenskappe veral in die **Kalahari**-gebied van Botswana, Namibië en die Noord-Kaap. Baie het hul grond verloor en leef nie meer net van jag en versameling nie. Sommige werk as spoorsnyers, kunstenaars en gidse. Die San se erfenis behoort aan ons almal: die mensfigure op Suid-Afrika se **landswapen** kom van ’n San-rotsskildery, en die leuse, *!ke e: ǀxarra ǁke*, is in die ǀXam-taal. Dit beteken ‘verskillende mense verenig’.","en":"## Who are the San?\n\nThe **San** are the first people of southern Africa. Their ancestors have lived here for **thousands of years**. The San were not just one group: there were many groups, each with its own language. Many San languages have **click sounds**.\n\nThe San were **hunter-gatherers**. They did not plant crops or keep livestock. They **hunted** wild animals and **gathered** **veld food** (wild plant food). They lived together in **small groups** of a few families and moved around together.\n\n## Work for men and women\n\n| Who | Work | Tools |\n|---|---|---|\n| Men | Hunted game such as eland and springbok, and caught small animals and birds | Bow and arrows with **poison**, **snares** |\n| Women | Gathered roots, bulbs, berries, nuts, insects and birds’ eggs | **Digging stick** with a heavy stone with a hole in it |\n\n- The **poison** on the arrowheads was made from beetle larvae or plants. It works slowly, so hunters sometimes had to **track** a wounded animal for hours or even days.\n- The women’s veld food was often **the biggest part** of the group’s food, because hunting did not always succeed.\n- **Ostrich eggshells** were used as water containers and buried full of water in the sand for dry times. Pieces of shell were made into **beads**.\n\nWhen a hunter shot an eland, **everyone** in the group got meat. Today you share, tomorrow someone else shares with you – that is how everyone survived. Nobody was rich or poor, and there was **no chief**. The group made decisions together.\n\n## Moving with the seasons\n\nFood and water were not in one place all year. The San moved with the **seasons** to places where plants were ripe and game was grazing. They built **temporary shelters** of branches and grass, or stayed in **caves** and rock shelters. Because they moved often, they had **few possessions** – only what they could carry.\n\nThe San knew nature very well. They could recognise animals by their **tracks** and knew which plants were food, medicine or poison.\n\n## Rock art: a window on the past\n\nThe San left thousands of **rock paintings**, especially in caves and rock shelters in mountains such as the Drakensberg and the Cederberg. On the plains of the interior, such as in the Northern Cape, they made **rock engravings**: pictures chipped or scratched into the rock.\n\n- **Paint:** red and yellow **ochre** (iron-rich earth), black **charcoal** and white clay, mixed with animal fat, blood or plant juice.\n- **Brushes:** feathers, animal hair or small sticks.\n- The **eland** is the animal painted most often in the Drakensberg. To the San it was a specially powerful animal.\n\nMany paintings show the **trance dance**. The women clapped and sang, and the **healers** danced for a long time until they went into a **trance** (a dream-like state). The San believed that a healer in a trance could heal sick people, bring rain and speak to the spirit world.\n\n> **Remember:** A rock painting is a **primary source**, because the San made it themselves. It shows us what they saw, did and believed.\n\n## How do we know about the San?\n\nThe San did not write. So historians use other **sources**:\n\n1. **Rock art** – shows animals, hunts, dancing and beliefs.\n2. **Archaeology** – archaeologists dig carefully in caves and find stone tools, ostrich-eggshell beads, animal bones and old fireplaces.\n3. **Oral tradition** – stories and knowledge that parents retell to their children. In the 1870s Wilhelm Bleek and Lucy Lloyd wrote down many stories of ǀXam San in Cape Town.\n\nA source does not tell us everything. A painting shows a hunt, for example, but not when it happened or what the hunters’ names were.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Don’t think the San had ‘nothing’. They had few **possessions**, but rich **knowledge**, art, music and beliefs.\n\n## The San today\n\nToday San communities live mainly in the **Kalahari** area of Botswana, Namibia and the Northern Cape. Many lost their land and no longer live only by hunting and gathering. Some work as trackers, artists and guides. The heritage of the San belongs to all of us: the human figures on South Africa’s **coat of arms** come from a San rock painting, and the motto, *!ke e: ǀxarra ǁke*, is in the ǀXam language. It means ‘diverse people unite’."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Jagter-versamelaars","en":"Hunter-gatherers"},"def":{"af":"Mense wat wilde diere jag en wilde plantkos versamel, sonder om gewasse te plant of vee aan te hou.","en":"People who hunt wild animals and gather wild plant food, without planting crops or keeping livestock."}},{"term":{"af":"Veldkos","en":"Veld food"},"def":{"af":"Wilde plantkos soos wortels, bolle, bessies en neute wat in die veld versamel word.","en":"Wild plant food such as roots, bulbs, berries and nuts that is gathered in the veld."}},{"term":{"af":"Graafstok","en":"Digging stick"},"def":{"af":"’n Skerp stok, swaarder gemaak met ’n klip met ’n gat, waarmee vroue wortels en bolle uitgegrawe het.","en":"A sharp stick, made heavier with a stone with a hole in it, that women used to dig up roots and bulbs."}},{"term":{"af":"Rotsskildery","en":"Rock painting"},"def":{"af":"’n Prent wat die San met verf op die rotswand van ’n grot of rotsskuiling geskilder het.","en":"A picture that the San painted with paint on the rock wall of a cave or rock shelter."}},{"term":{"af":"Rotsgravure","en":"Rock engraving"},"def":{"af":"’n Prent wat in ’n rots ingekap of ingekrap is, meestal op die vlaktes van die binneland.","en":"A picture chipped or scratched into a rock, mostly on the plains of the interior."}},{"term":{"af":"Oker","en":"Ochre"},"def":{"af":"Ysterryke grond wat rooi of geel verf gee.","en":"Iron-rich earth that gives red or yellow paint."}},{"term":{"af":"Trance-dans","en":"Trance dance"},"def":{"af":"’n Dans waartydens San-genesers in ’n droomagtige toestand gegaan het om siekes te genees en met die geesteswêreld te praat.","en":"A dance during which San healers went into a dream-like state to heal the sick and speak to the spirit world."}},{"term":{"af":"Argeologie","en":"Archaeology"},"def":{"af":"Die studie van die verlede deur dinge te ondersoek wat mense agtergelaat het, soos gereedskap, bene en krale.","en":"The study of the past by examining things people left behind, such as tools, bones and beads."}},{"term":{"af":"Mondelinge oorlewering","en":"Oral tradition"},"def":{"af":"Stories, liedere en kennis wat mondeling van een geslag na die volgende oorvertel word.","en":"Stories, songs and knowledge that are passed on by word of mouth from one generation to the next."}},{"term":{"af":"Primêre bron","en":"Primary source"},"def":{"af":"’n Bron wat gemaak is deur mense wat self daar was, soos ’n San-rotsskildery.","en":"A source made by people who were there themselves, such as a San rock painting."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n rotsskildery as bron","en":"Read a rock painting as a source"},"problem":{"af":"’n Rotsskildery in die Drakensberg wys vyf mans met pyl en boog wat ’n trop elande bekruip. Een eland het ’n pyl in sy sy. (a) Watter soort bron is dit? (b) Noem twee dinge wat die bron ons van die San vertel. (c) Noem een ding wat die bron ons nie vertel nie.","en":"A rock painting in the Drakensberg shows five men with bows and arrows sneaking up on a herd of eland. One eland has an arrow in its side. (a) What kind of source is this? (b) Name two things the source tells us about the San. (c) Name one thing the source does not tell us."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die San het die skildery self gemaak, so dit is ’n **primêre bron**.","en":"(a) The San made the painting themselves, so it is a **primary source**."},{"af":"(b) Kyk mooi na wat jy sien: die mans jag saam in ’n groep, hulle gebruik pyl en boog, en hulle jag elande.","en":"(b) Look carefully at what you see: the men hunt together in a group, they use bows and arrows, and they hunt eland."},{"af":"(c) Dink aan wat ontbreek: die skildery sê nie wanneer dit geskilder is of wat die mans se name was nie, en ook nie of die jagtog geslaag het nie.","en":"(c) Think about what is missing: the painting does not say when it was painted or what the men’s names were, nor whether the hunt succeeded."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) ’n Primêre bron. (b) Die mans het in groepe gejag en pyl en boog gebruik; die eland was ’n belangrike prooi. (c) Byvoorbeeld wanneer dit geskilder is, of die jagters se name.","en":"(a) A primary source. (b) The men hunted in groups and used bows and arrows; the eland was important prey. (c) For example when it was painted, or the hunters’ names."}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik hoe die San gelewe het","en":"Explain how the San lived"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik in drie of vier sinne waarom die San in klein groepe gewoon en gereeld rondgetrek het.","en":"Explain in three or four sentences why the San lived in small groups and moved around often."},"steps":[{"af":"Dink aan kos: wilde diere en veldkos raak op ’n plek op, en plante word net in sekere seisoene ryp.","en":"Think about food: wild animals and veld food run out in one place, and plants only ripen in certain seasons."},{"af":"Dink aan die groepgrootte: ’n klein groep kan makliker genoeg kos en water vir almal kry as ’n groot groep.","en":"Think about group size: a small group can more easily find enough food and water for everyone than a big group."},{"af":"Dink aan besittings: wie gereeld trek, kan net min dinge saamdra.","en":"Think about possessions: people who move often can only carry a few things."}],"answer":{"af":"Die San het van wilde diere en veldkos gelewe, en dit was nie die hele jaar op een plek nie. Daarom het hulle met die seisoene getrek na plekke met kos en water. ’n Klein groep kon makliker genoeg kos vir almal kry. Hulle het min besittings gehad sodat hulle maklik kon trek.","en":"The San lived on wild animals and veld food, which were not in one place all year. So they moved with the seasons to places with food and water. A small group could more easily find enough food for everyone. They had few possessions so that they could move easily."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Skildery van ’n ruiter","en":"A painting of a rider"},"problem":{"af":"Ravi sien in ’n museum ’n foto van ’n San-rotsskildery van ’n man op ’n perd met ’n geweer. Hy sê: ‘Dit is seker een van die oudste skilderye in Suid-Afrika.’ Is hy reg? Verduidelik.","en":"In a museum Ravi sees a photo of a San rock painting of a man on a horse with a gun. He says: ‘This must be one of the oldest paintings in South Africa.’ Is he right? Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"Vra eers: wanneer het perde na Suider-Afrika gekom? Die eerste perde het eers ná 1652 saam met die Nederlanders na die Kaap gekom. Gewere het ook saam met Europeërs gekom.","en":"First ask: when did horses come to southern Africa? The first horses only came to the Cape with the Dutch after 1652. Guns also came with Europeans."},{"af":"Die San kon dus eers ’n perd en ’n geweer skilder nadat hulle dit gesien het – ná daardie tyd.","en":"So the San could only paint a horse and a gun after they had seen them – after that time."},{"af":"Die skildery is dus een van die jonger skilderye. Dit wys ook dat die San nuwe mense ontmoet het en dat hul lewe verander het.","en":"So the painting is one of the younger paintings. It also shows that the San met new people and that their lives changed."}],"answer":{"af":"Nee. Die skildery moet geskilder gewees het nadat Europeërs perde en gewere na Suider-Afrika gebring het, dus is dit een van die jonger rotsskilderye.","en":"No. The painting must have been made after Europeans brought horses and guns to southern Africa, so it is one of the younger rock paintings."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken dit as ons sê die San was jagter-versamelaars?","en":"What do we mean when we say the San were hunter-gatherers?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle het gewasse geplant en beeste aangehou","en":"They planted crops and kept cattle"},{"af":"Hulle het skape aangehou en met hulle na weiding getrek","en":"They kept sheep and moved with them to grazing"},{"af":"Hulle het wilde diere gejag en wilde plantkos versamel","en":"They hunted wild animals and gathered wild plant food"},{"af":"Hulle het kos by handelaars gekoop en in dorpe gewoon","en":"They bought food from traders and lived in towns"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Jagter-versamelaars jag wild en versamel veldkos. Hulle plant nie gewasse nie en hou nie vee aan nie. Skape aanhou is wat veewagters soos die Khoikhoi gedoen het.","en":"Hunter-gatherers hunt game and gather veld food. They do not plant crops or keep livestock. Keeping sheep is what herders such as the Khoikhoi did."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die San het in groot dorpe gewoon onder ’n magtige hoofman.","en":"The San lived in large villages under a powerful chief."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die San het in klein groepe van ’n paar families gewoon, gereeld getrek en geen hoofman gehad nie. Die groep het besluite saam geneem.","en":"False. The San lived in small groups of a few families, moved often and had no chief. The group made decisions together."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom moes San-jagters ’n gewonde dier soms ure of dae lank volg?","en":"Why did San hunters sometimes have to follow a wounded animal for hours or days?"},"options":[{"af":"Die gif op die pyl het stadig gewerk","en":"The poison on the arrow worked slowly"},{"af":"Die pyle was te klein om ’n dier seer te maak","en":"The arrows were too small to hurt an animal"},{"af":"Die jagters wou die dier lewend vang","en":"The hunters wanted to catch the animal alive"},{"af":"Die hoofman moes eers toestemming gee","en":"The chief first had to give permission"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die gif van kewerlarwes of plante het stadig gewerk. Die jagters moes die dier spoorsny totdat die gif dit verswak het. Die San het geen hoofman gehad nie.","en":"The poison from beetle larvae or plants worked slowly. The hunters had to track the animal until the poison weakened it. The San had no chief."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"San-vroue het ’n ___ gebruik om wortels en bolle uit te grawe.","en":"San women used a ___ to dig up roots and bulbs."},"answers":{"af":["graafstok"],"en":["digging stick","digging-stick"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["skoffel","spies","boog"],"en":["hoe","spear","bow"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die graafstok was ’n skerp stok met ’n swaar klip met ’n gat daarin. Die klip het die stok swaarder gemaak sodat dit makliker gegrawe het. Skoffels van yster het eers later saam met die boere gekom.","en":"The digging stick was a sharp stick with a heavy stone with a hole in it. The stone made the stick heavier so that it dug more easily. Iron hoes only came later with the farmers."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter dier is die meeste in die Drakensberg se rotsskilderye geskilder?","en":"Which animal was painted most often in the rock paintings of the Drakensberg?"},"options":[{"af":"Die leeu","en":"The lion"},{"af":"Die olifant","en":"The elephant"},{"af":"Die springbok","en":"The springbok"},{"af":"Die eland","en":"The eland"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die eland is die meeste geskilder. Dit was vir die San ’n besonder kragtige dier wat ook met hul geloof verbind was – nie net ’n dier om te jag nie.","en":"The eland was painted most often. To the San it was a specially powerful animal that was also linked to their beliefs – not just an animal to hunt."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom het die San min besittings gehad?","en":"Why did the San have few possessions?"},"options":[{"af":"Die hoofman het alles vir homself gehou","en":"The chief kept everything for himself"},{"af":"Hulle het gereeld getrek en moes alles dra","en":"They moved often and had to carry everything"},{"af":"Hulle kon nie gereedskap maak nie","en":"They could not make tools"},{"af":"Hulle het alles aan boere verkoop","en":"They sold everything to farmers"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Wie met die seisoene trek, kan net saamneem wat hy kan dra. Die San het wel slim gereedskap gemaak, soos pyl en boog, strikke en graafstokke.","en":"People who move with the seasons can only take what they can carry. The San did make clever tools, such as bows and arrows, snares and digging sticks."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke bron by wat dit ons van die San vertel.","en":"Match each source to what it tells us about the San."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Rotsskildery van ’n trance-dans","en":"Rock painting of a trance dance"},"r":{"af":"Wys hul geloof en hoe hulle siekes genees het","en":"Shows their beliefs and how they healed the sick"}},{"l":{"af":"Volstruiseierdop in ’n grot","en":"Ostrich eggshell in a cave"},"r":{"af":"Wys hoe hulle water gedra en gestoor het","en":"Shows how they carried and stored water"}},{"l":{"af":"Elandbene langs ’n ou vuurmaakplek","en":"Eland bones next to an old fireplace"},"r":{"af":"Wys wat hulle gejag en geëet het","en":"Shows what they hunted and ate"}},{"l":{"af":"ǀXam-stories wat in die 1870’s opgeskryf is","en":"ǀXam stories written down in the 1870s"},"r":{"af":"Wys die San se gedagtes in hul eie woorde","en":"Shows the thoughts of the San in their own words"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke bron vertel iets anders: rotskuns wys geloof, argeologiese vondste (eierdoppe, bene) wys die daaglikse lewe, en mondelinge oorlewering gee die San se eie woorde.","en":"Each source tells us something different: rock art shows beliefs, archaeological finds (eggshells, bones) show daily life, and oral tradition gives the San’s own words."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom noem ons ’n San-rotsskildery ’n primêre bron?","en":"Why do we call a San rock painting a primary source?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is die belangrikste bron in die museum","en":"It is the most important source in the museum"},{"af":"Die San het dit self gemaak in die tyd waaroor ons leer","en":"The San made it themselves in the time we are learning about"},{"af":"’n Historikus het dit onlangs in ’n boek beskryf","en":"A historian described it recently in a book"},{"af":"Dit is met primêre kleure geskilder","en":"It was painted in primary colours"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Primêre bron is gemaak deur mense wat self daar was. ’n Boek wat ’n historikus later oor die skildery skryf, is ’n sekondêre bron.","en":"A primary source was made by people who were there themselves. A book that a historian writes about the painting later is a secondary source."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die rooi en geel verf vir rotsskilderye is van ___ gemaak, ’n ysterryke grond.","en":"The red and yellow paint for rock paintings was made from ___, an iron-rich earth."},"answers":{"af":["oker"],"en":["ochre","ocher"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["houtskool","klei","bloed"],"en":["charcoal","clay","blood"]}},"explain":{"af":"Oker gee rooi en geel. Houtskool gee swart en klei gee wit. Bloed en dierevet is gebruik om die verf te meng, nie vir die kleur rooi en geel self nie.","en":"Ochre gives red and yellow. Charcoal gives black and clay gives white. Blood and animal fat were used to mix the paint, not for the red and yellow colour itself."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n San-skildery wys ’n man op ’n perd met ’n geweer. Wat kan ’n historikus daaruit aflei?","en":"A San painting shows a man on a horse with a gun. What can a historian work out from it?"},"options":[{"af":"Die San het al baie lank voor 1652 perde aangehou","en":"The San kept horses long before 1652"},{"af":"Dit is die oudste rotsskildery in Suider-Afrika","en":"It is the oldest rock painting in southern Africa"},{"af":"Die San het net diere geskilder wat hulle gejag het","en":"The San only painted animals that they hunted"},{"af":"Dit is geskilder nadat Europeërs perde hierheen gebring het","en":"It was painted after Europeans brought horses here"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Perde het eers ná 1652 saam met die Nederlanders na die Kaap gekom, en gewere het ook saam met Europeërs gekom. Die San kon ’n ruiter met ’n geweer eers skilder nadat hulle een gesien het, dus is die skildery een van die jonger skilderye.","en":"Horses only came to the Cape with the Dutch after 1652, and guns also came with Europeans. The San could only paint a rider with a gun after they had seen one, so the painting is one of the younger paintings."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die veldkos wat die vroue versamel het, was dikwels die grootste deel van die groep se kos.","en":"The veld food that the women gathered was often the biggest part of the group’s food."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Jag het nie altyd geslaag nie, maar veldkos was amper elke dag te kry. Die vroue se werk was dus baie belangrik vir oorlewing.","en":"True. Hunting did not always succeed, but veld food could be found almost every day. So the women’s work was very important for survival."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat het die San geglo kon ’n geneser in ’n trance doen?","en":"What did the San believe a healer in a trance could do?"},"options":[{"af":"Siekes genees en reën bring","en":"Heal the sick and bring rain"},{"af":"Wilde diere mak maak vir die boere","en":"Tame wild animals for the farmers"},{"af":"Verf maak van oker en vet","en":"Make paint from ochre and fat"},{"af":"Die groep se hoofman kies","en":"Choose the group’s chief"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die San het geglo dat ’n geneser in ’n trance siekes kon genees, reën kon bring en met die geesteswêreld kon praat. Baie rotsskilderye wys hierdie dansers.","en":"The San believed that a healer in a trance could heal the sick, bring rain and speak to the spirit world. Many rock paintings show these dancers."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vandag woon baie San in die ___-gebied van Botswana, Namibië en die Noord-Kaap.","en":"Today many San live in the ___ area of Botswana, Namibia and the Northern Cape."},"answers":{"af":["Kalahari"],"en":["Kalahari"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Sahara","Karoo","Drakensberg"],"en":["Sahara","Karoo","Drakensberg"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die Kalahari is ’n droë sanderige gebied wat oor Botswana, Namibië en die Noord-Kaap strek. Die Sahara is in Noord-Afrika.","en":"The Kalahari is a dry, sandy area that stretches across Botswana, Namibia and the Northern Cape. The Sahara is in North Africa."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom het ’n San-jagter sy vleis met die hele groep gedeel?","en":"Why did a San hunter share his meat with the whole group?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat hulle nie geweet het hoe om vleis gaar te maak nie","en":"Because they did not know how to cook meat"},{"af":"Omdat hy die vleis vir krale aan die ander wou verkoop","en":"Because he wanted to sell the meat to the others for beads"},{"af":"Omdat almal so oorleef het: môre deel ’n ander met hom","en":"Because that is how everyone survived: tomorrow someone shares with him"},{"af":"Omdat die hoofman van die groep dit so beveel het","en":"Because the chief of the group ordered it"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Jag het nie elke dag geslaag nie. Deur te deel het almal kos gekry, en wanneer hy niks geskiet het nie, het ’n ander met hom gedeel. Die San het geen hoofman gehad nie, en hulle het vleis gedeel, nie verkoop nie.","en":"Hunting did not succeed every day. By sharing, everyone got food, and when he shot nothing, someone else shared with him. The San had no chief, and they shared meat rather than selling it."}}]},{"id":"sw5-t1-gesk-khoikhoi","title":{"af":"Die Khoikhoi: veewagters","en":"The Khoikhoi: herders"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe die Khoikhoi as nomadiese veewagters gelewe het, hul lewe met dié van die San kan vergelyk en kan sê wat ons vandag nog van hulle erf.","en":"You will be able to explain how the Khoikhoi lived as nomadic herders, compare their way of life with that of the San and say what we still inherit from them today."},"summary":{"af":"## Wie was die Khoikhoi?\n\nOngeveer **2 000 jaar gelede** het sommige mense in Suider-Afrika begin om **vee** aan te hou. Eers het hulle **vetstertskape** gehad en later ook **beeste**. Die skape het uit die noorde na Suider-Afrika gekom. Hierdie **veewagters** word die **Khoikhoi** genoem. Hulle het veral in die westelike en suidelike dele van Suider-Afrika gewoon.\n\nDie Khoikhoi en die San was verwant: albei se tale het klikklanke, en historici noem hulle saam die **Khoe-San**. Die groot verskil was hoe hulle gelewe het: die Khoikhoi het **vee besit**.\n\n## ’n Lewe met vee\n\nDie Khoikhoi was **nomadies**: hulle het nie altyd op een plek gebly nie. Hul vee het **weiding** (gras) en **water** nodig gehad, en dit verander met die **seisoene**. Wanneer die gras op ’n plek op was of die water opgedroog het, het die hele groep met hul vee na nuwe weiveld getrek. Dikwels het hulle elke jaar ’n bekende roete gevolg.\n\n- **Melk** was hul belangrikste kos. Hulle het ook gejag en veldkos versamel.\n- Vee is **selde geslag** – gewoonlik net by spesiale geleenthede soos ’n troue of ’n fees.\n- Osse is as **pakosse** gebruik om goed te dra, en mense het ook op osse gery.\n- Hulle het **kleipotte** gemaak om kos in te kook.\n\n## Die matjieshuis\n\nDie Khoikhoi het in **matjieshuise** gewoon – koepelvormige hutte:\n\n1. ’n **Raam** van gebuigde pale word in ’n sirkel in die grond gesteek en bo vasgemaak.\n2. Die raam word met **matte** van biesies bedek. Die vroue het die matte gevleg en die huise gebou.\n3. Om te trek, word die huis **afgebreek**, op pakosse gelaai en op die nuwe plek weer opgebou.\n\nAs dit warm is, laat die matte lug deur. As dit reën, swel die biesies op en hou die water uit. Die hutte is in ’n **kring** gebou, en snags is die vee in die middel gehou, veilig teen roofdiere.\n\n> **Onthou:** Die matjieshuis pas by ’n **nomadiese** lewe: dit is lig en kan vinnig afgebreek, vervoer en weer opgebou word.\n\n## Vee is rykdom\n\nBy die Khoikhoi het **vee rykdom** beteken. Wie baie skape en beeste gehad het, was ryk en belangrik. Anders as by die San was sommige mense dus ryker as ander.\n\n- Die Khoikhoi het in **groter groepe** as die San gewoon, want vee kon meer mense voed.\n- ’n Groep het ’n **hoofman** gehad wat saam met ’n raad van ouer mans besluite geneem het.\n- **Handel:** Die Khoikhoi het vee geruil vir dinge wat hulle nie self gemaak het nie, soos koper, yster en krale – met boere in die ooste en, vanaf die 1500’s, met Europese seevaarders by die Kaap. Nadat die Nederlanders hulle in 1652 aan die Kaap gevestig het, het die Khoikhoi stadigaan baie van hul grond en vee verloor.\n\n## Die Khoikhoi en die San\n\n| | San | Khoikhoi |\n|---|---|---|\n| Kos | Jag en versamel | Melk en vee, ook jag en versamel |\n| Groepe | Klein groepe | Groter groepe |\n| Leiers | Geen hoofman nie | Hoofman en raad |\n| Rykdom | Niemand ryk nie | Vee is rykdom |\n| Woning | Skuilings van takke, grotte | Matjieshuise |\n\nDie verhouding was soms **vriendelik**: hulle het gehandel en met mekaar getrou, en San het soms vir Khoikhoi as veewagters of jagters gewerk. Soms was daar **konflik**, byvoorbeeld oor water en weiveld, of wanneer San die Khoikhoi se vee gejag het.\n\n## Hoe weet ons van die Khoikhoi?\n\n- **Argeologie:** skaapbene en stukke kleipotte in grotte wys dat mense ongeveer 2 000 jaar gelede al skape aangehou het.\n- **Rotskuns:** sommige skilderye wys skape of beeste.\n- **Geskrewe bronne:** dagboeke en tekeninge van Europese reisigers. Hulle is nuttig, maar die skrywers was **buitestaanders** wat dikwels nie die Khoikhoi se taal of gebruike verstaan het nie. Sulke bronne kan **eensydig** wees.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** ’n Bron wat ’n Europese besoeker geskryf het, is nie die Khoikhoi se eie stem nie. Vra altyd: *Wie het dit gemaak, en wat het hy dalk nie verstaan nie?*\n\n## Ons Khoi-erfenis\n\n- **Woorde** in Afrikaans: *gogga, kierie, abba, boegoe* en *kwagga*.\n- **Plekname:** Karoo, Tsitsikamma, Outeniqua en Gamtoos.\n- Die **Nama** in die Noord-Kaap, soos in die Richtersveld, is afstammelinge van die Khoikhoi. Party bou nog matjieshuise, trek met hul vee en praat Khoekhoegowab.","en":"## Who were the Khoikhoi?\n\nAbout **2 000 years ago** some people in southern Africa began to keep **livestock**. First they had **fat-tailed sheep** and later also **cattle**. The sheep came to southern Africa from the north. These **herders** are called the **Khoikhoi**. They lived mainly in the western and southern parts of southern Africa.\n\nThe Khoikhoi and the San were related: both their languages have click sounds, and historians call them together the **Khoe-San**. The big difference was how they lived: the Khoikhoi **owned livestock**.\n\n## A life with livestock\n\nThe Khoikhoi were **nomadic**: they did not always stay in one place. Their animals needed **grazing** (grass) and **water**, and these change with the **seasons**. When the grass in a place was finished or the water had dried up, the whole group moved with their animals to new grazing. Often they followed a familiar route every year.\n\n- **Milk** was their most important food. They also hunted and gathered veld food.\n- Animals were **seldom slaughtered** – usually only on special occasions such as a wedding or a feast.\n- Oxen were used as **pack oxen** to carry things, and people also rode on oxen.\n- They made **clay pots** to cook food in.\n\n## The mat house\n\nThe Khoikhoi lived in **mat houses** (*matjieshuise*) – dome-shaped huts:\n\n1. A **frame** of bent poles is pushed into the ground in a circle and tied together at the top.\n2. The frame is covered with **mats** made of reeds. The women wove the mats and built the houses.\n3. To move, the house is **taken apart**, loaded onto pack oxen and put up again in the new place.\n\nWhen it is hot, the mats let air through. When it rains, the reeds swell and keep the water out. The huts were built in a **circle**, and at night the animals were kept in the middle, safe from predators.\n\n> **Remember:** The mat house suits a **nomadic** life: it is light and can be quickly taken apart, transported and put up again.\n\n## Livestock is wealth\n\nFor the Khoikhoi, **livestock meant wealth**. Whoever had many sheep and cattle was rich and important. Unlike among the San, some people were therefore richer than others.\n\n- The Khoikhoi lived in **bigger groups** than the San, because livestock could feed more people.\n- A group had a **chief** who made decisions together with a council of older men.\n- **Trade:** The Khoikhoi exchanged livestock for things they did not make themselves, such as copper, iron and beads – with farmers in the east and, from the 1500s, with European sailors at the Cape. After the Dutch settled at the Cape in 1652, the Khoikhoi slowly lost much of their land and livestock.\n\n## The Khoikhoi and the San\n\n| | San | Khoikhoi |\n|---|---|---|\n| Food | Hunting and gathering | Milk and livestock, also hunting and gathering |\n| Groups | Small groups | Bigger groups |\n| Leaders | No chief | Chief and council |\n| Wealth | Nobody rich | Livestock is wealth |\n| Home | Shelters of branches, caves | Mat houses |\n\nThe relationship was sometimes **friendly**: they traded and married each other, and San sometimes worked for Khoikhoi as herders or hunters. Sometimes there was **conflict**, for example over water and grazing, or when San hunted the Khoikhoi’s animals.\n\n## How do we know about the Khoikhoi?\n\n- **Archaeology:** sheep bones and pieces of clay pots in caves show that people already kept sheep about 2 000 years ago.\n- **Rock art:** some paintings show sheep or cattle.\n- **Written sources:** diaries and drawings by European travellers. They are useful, but the writers were **outsiders** who often did not understand the Khoikhoi’s language or customs. Such sources can be **one-sided** (biased).\n\n> **Common mistake:** A source written by a European visitor is not the Khoikhoi’s own voice. Always ask: *Who made it, and what might he not have understood?*\n\n## Our Khoi heritage\n\n- **Words** in Afrikaans: *gogga* (insect), *kierie* (walking stick), *abba* (carry a baby on your back), *boegoe* (buchu) and *kwagga* (quagga).\n- **Place names:** Karoo, Tsitsikamma, Outeniqua and Gamtoos.\n- The **Nama** in the Northern Cape, such as in the Richtersveld, are descendants of the Khoikhoi. Some still build mat houses, move with their livestock and speak Khoekhoegowab."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Veewagters","en":"Herders"},"def":{"af":"Mense wat van hul vee lewe en met hul vee na weiding en water trek.","en":"People who live from their livestock and move with their animals to grazing and water."}},{"term":{"af":"Vetstertskaap","en":"Fat-tailed sheep"},"def":{"af":"’n Skaap met ’n dik stert waarin vet gestoor word; die eerste vee van die Khoikhoi.","en":"A sheep with a thick tail in which fat is stored; the first livestock of the Khoikhoi."}},{"term":{"af":"Nomadies","en":"Nomadic"},"def":{"af":"Om nie vas op een plek te woon nie, maar van plek tot plek te trek.","en":"Not living permanently in one place, but moving from place to place."}},{"term":{"af":"Weiding","en":"Grazing"},"def":{"af":"Gras en ander plante waarvan vee lewe.","en":"Grass and other plants that livestock feed on."}},{"term":{"af":"Matjieshuis","en":"Mat house"},"def":{"af":"’n Koepelvormige hut van gebuigde pale wat met biesiematte bedek is en maklik afgebreek en vervoer kan word.","en":"A dome-shaped hut of bent poles covered with reed mats that can easily be taken apart and transported."}},{"term":{"af":"Pakos","en":"Pack ox"},"def":{"af":"’n Os wat gebruik word om goed op sy rug te dra.","en":"An ox used to carry things on its back."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoofman","en":"Chief"},"def":{"af":"Die leier van ’n groep wat saam met ’n raad besluite neem.","en":"The leader of a group who makes decisions together with a council."}},{"term":{"af":"Ruilhandel","en":"Barter"},"def":{"af":"Handel waarin goedere vir ander goedere geruil word, sonder geld.","en":"Trade in which goods are exchanged for other goods, without money."}},{"term":{"af":"Khoe-San","en":"Khoe-San"},"def":{"af":"Die naam wat historici gebruik vir die San en die Khoikhoi saam.","en":"The name historians use for the San and the Khoikhoi together."}},{"term":{"af":"Eensydige bron","en":"Biased source"},"def":{"af":"’n Bron wat net een kant van die saak wys, dikwels omdat die skrywer die ander mense nie verstaan het nie.","en":"A source that shows only one side of the story, often because the writer did not understand the other people."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Waarom ’n matjieshuis?","en":"Why a mat house?"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik waarom die matjieshuis goed gepas het by die manier waarop die Khoikhoi gelewe het.","en":"Explain why the mat house suited the way the Khoikhoi lived."},"steps":[{"af":"Begin by hul lewe: die Khoikhoi was nomadies en het met hul vee na nuwe weiding en water getrek.","en":"Start with their way of life: the Khoikhoi were nomadic and moved with their animals to new grazing and water."},{"af":"Kyk na die huis: ’n raam van pale met biesiematte is lig en kan vinnig afgebreek word.","en":"Look at the house: a frame of poles with reed mats is light and can be taken apart quickly."},{"af":"Verbind die twee: die pale en matte kon op pakosse gelaai en op die nuwe plek weer opgebou word. Die matte het ook in warm en nat weer gewerk.","en":"Link the two: the poles and mats could be loaded onto pack oxen and put up again at the new place. The mats also worked in hot and wet weather."}],"answer":{"af":"Die Khoikhoi het gereeld met hul vee getrek. ’n Matjieshuis is lig, maklik om af te breek en op pakosse te vervoer, en kan vinnig weer opgebou word.","en":"The Khoikhoi moved often with their animals. A mat house is light, easy to take apart and carry on pack oxen, and can be put up again quickly."}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyk die San en die Khoikhoi","en":"Compare the San and the Khoikhoi"},"problem":{"af":"Noem drie verskille tussen die lewe van die San en die lewe van die Khoikhoi.","en":"Name three differences between the life of the San and the life of the Khoikhoi."},"steps":[{"af":"Dink aan **kos**: die San het gejag en versamel; die Khoikhoi het vee aangehou en veral van melk gelewe.","en":"Think about **food**: the San hunted and gathered; the Khoikhoi kept livestock and lived mainly on milk."},{"af":"Dink aan **leiers en rykdom**: die San het geen hoofman gehad nie en niemand was ryk nie; die Khoikhoi het ’n hoofman gehad, en vee was rykdom.","en":"Think about **leaders and wealth**: the San had no chief and nobody was rich; the Khoikhoi had a chief, and livestock was wealth."},{"af":"Dink aan **groepgrootte en woning**: San-groepe was klein en het in skuilings en grotte gebly; Khoikhoi-groepe was groter en het in matjieshuise gewoon.","en":"Think about **group size and homes**: San groups were small and stayed in shelters and caves; Khoikhoi groups were bigger and lived in mat houses."}],"answer":{"af":"Enige drie, bv.: (1) San het gejag en versamel, Khoikhoi het vee aangehou. (2) San het geen hoofman gehad nie, Khoikhoi wel. (3) San-groepe was klein, Khoikhoi-groepe groter.","en":"Any three, e.g.: (1) The San hunted and gathered, the Khoikhoi kept livestock. (2) The San had no chief, the Khoikhoi did. (3) San groups were small, Khoikhoi groups were bigger."}},{"title":{"af":"Ondersoek ’n geskrewe bron","en":"Examine a written source"},"problem":{"af":"Lees hierdie bron, soos ’n skeepskaptein dit in die 1600’s in sy dagboek kon geskryf het: ‘Die mense by die baai het honderde beeste, maar hulle wil vir al ons krale net drie maer osse gee. Hulle is suinig.’ (a) Wat vertel die bron ons van die Khoikhoi? (b) Waarom kan hierdie bron eensydig wees?","en":"Read this source, as a ship’s captain might have written it in his diary in the 1600s: ‘The people at the bay have hundreds of cattle, but for all our beads they will give only three thin oxen. They are stingy.’ (a) What does the source tell us about the Khoikhoi? (b) Why might this source be biased?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Soek feite in die bron: die Khoikhoi het baie beeste gehad, en hulle het met seevaarders gehandel.","en":"(a) Look for facts in the source: the Khoikhoi had many cattle, and they traded with sailors."},{"af":"(b) Vra wie dit geskryf het: ’n Europese buitestaander wat beeste wou kry.","en":"(b) Ask who wrote it: a European outsider who wanted to get cattle."},{"af":"Dink aan wat hy nie verstaan het nie: vir die Khoikhoi was vee rykdom wat selde weggegee is. Hulle was nie ‘suinig’ nie – hulle het hul rykdom beskerm.","en":"Think about what he did not understand: for the Khoikhoi livestock was wealth that was seldom given away. They were not ‘stingy’ – they were protecting their wealth."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Die Khoikhoi het baie beeste gehad en met seevaarders gehandel. (b) Die skrywer was ’n buitestaander wat net sy eie kant wys; hy het nie verstaan dat vee vir die Khoikhoi rykdom was nie.","en":"(a) The Khoikhoi had many cattle and traded with sailors. (b) The writer was an outsider who shows only his own side; he did not understand that livestock was wealth to the Khoikhoi."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ongeveer hoe lank gelede het die Khoikhoi begin om vee aan te hou?","en":"About how long ago did the Khoikhoi begin to keep livestock?"},"options":[{"af":"Ongeveer 200 jaar gelede","en":"About 200 years ago"},{"af":"Ongeveer 2 000 jaar gelede","en":"About 2 000 years ago"},{"af":"Ongeveer 20 000 jaar gelede","en":"About 20 000 years ago"},{"af":"Ongeveer 200 000 jaar gelede","en":"About 200 000 years ago"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Argeologiese vondste soos skaapbene en stukke kleipotte wys dat mense ongeveer 2 000 jaar gelede in Suider-Afrika skape begin aanhou het.","en":"Archaeological finds such as sheep bones and pieces of clay pots show that people began keeping sheep in southern Africa about 2 000 years ago."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die Khoikhoi het in koepelvormige ___ gewoon wat met biesiematte bedek was.","en":"The Khoikhoi lived in dome-shaped ___ that were covered with reed mats."},"answers":{"af":["matjieshuise","matjieshuis"],"en":["mat houses","mat house","matjieshuise","mat huts"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kleihutte","kliphuise","grotte"],"en":["mud huts","stone houses","caves"]}},"explain":{"af":"Matjieshuise was lig en kon vinnig afgebreek en op pakosse gelaai word. Kliphuise en kleihutte kan nie saam getrek word nie.","en":"Mat houses were light and could be taken apart quickly and loaded onto pack oxen. Stone houses and mud huts cannot move with you."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom het die Khoikhoi gereeld van plek tot plek getrek?","en":"Why did the Khoikhoi move from place to place so often?"},"options":[{"af":"Om nuwe grond te vind om mielies te plant","en":"To find new land to plant maize"},{"af":"Omdat die hoofman elke maand ’n nuwe huis wou hê","en":"Because the chief wanted a new home every month"},{"af":"Om weg te kom van die koue in die somer","en":"To get away from the cold in summer"},{"af":"Om weiding en water vir hul vee te vind","en":"To find grazing and water for their livestock"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Hul vee het gras en water nodig gehad, en dit verander met die seisoene. Die Khoikhoi het nie gewasse geplant nie – en mielies het eers baie later uit Amerika na Afrika gekom.","en":"Their animals needed grass and water, and these change with the seasons. The Khoikhoi did not plant crops – and maize only came to Africa from America much later."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"By die Khoikhoi was iemand met baie beeste en skape ryk en belangrik.","en":"Among the Khoikhoi, someone with many cattle and sheep was rich and important."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Vee was rykdom. Daarom was sommige Khoikhoi ryker as ander – anders as by die San, waar niemand ryk was nie.","en":"True. Livestock was wealth. That is why some Khoikhoi were richer than others – unlike among the San, where nobody was rich."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat maak ’n matjieshuis die beste soort huis vir nomadiese veewagters?","en":"What makes a mat house the best kind of home for nomadic herders?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is van klip gebou en hou honderde jare","en":"It is built of stone and lasts hundreds of years"},{"af":"Dit het baie kamers vir die hele groep","en":"It has many rooms for the whole group"},{"af":"Dit is lig en kan maklik afgebreek en vervoer word","en":"It is light and can easily be taken apart and moved"},{"af":"Dit is in ’n grot gebou, ver van die vee","en":"It is built in a cave, far from the animals"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Nomades trek gereeld. ’n Matjieshuis se pale en matte kon op pakosse gelaai en op die nuwe plek weer opgebou word. ’n Kliphuis kan nie saamtrek nie.","en":"Nomads move often. A mat house’s poles and mats could be loaded onto pack oxen and put up again in the new place. A stone house cannot move with you."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Hierdie Afrikaanse woorde kom uit die Khoikhoi se taal. Pas elke woord by sy betekenis.","en":"These Afrikaans words come from the Khoikhoi language. Match each word to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"gogga","en":"gogga"},"r":{"af":"’n insek","en":"an insect"}},{"l":{"af":"kierie","en":"kierie"},"r":{"af":"’n kort stok om mee te loop","en":"a short walking stick"}},{"l":{"af":"abba","en":"abba"},"r":{"af":"om ’n baba op jou rug te dra","en":"to carry a baby on your back"}},{"l":{"af":"boegoe","en":"boegoe"},"r":{"af":"’n geurige plant wat as medisyne gebruik word","en":"a fragrant plant used as medicine"}},{"l":{"af":"Karoo","en":"Karoo"},"r":{"af":"’n pleknaam vir ’n droë gebied","en":"a place name for a dry area"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hierdie woorde en plekname wys dat die Khoikhoi se erfenis vandag nog in ons taal en ons landkaart voortleef.","en":"These words and place names show that the heritage of the Khoikhoi still lives on today in our language and on our map."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat was die Khoikhoi se belangrikste kos?","en":"What was the most important food of the Khoikhoi?"},"options":[{"af":"Melk van hul vee","en":"Milk from their animals"},{"af":"Mieliepap","en":"Maize porridge"},{"af":"Vleis van vee wat elke dag geslag is","en":"Meat from animals slaughtered every day"},{"af":"Brood van koring","en":"Bread made from wheat"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die Khoikhoi het veral van melk gelewe. Hulle het hul vee selde geslag, want vee was hul rykdom. Hulle het nie mielies of koring geplant nie.","en":"The Khoikhoi lived mainly on milk. They seldom slaughtered their animals, because livestock was their wealth. They did not plant maize or wheat."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die Khoikhoi het osse as ___ gebruik om hul pale en matte te dra.","en":"The Khoikhoi used oxen as ___ to carry their poles and mats."},"answers":{"af":["pakosse","pakos"],"en":["pack oxen","pack ox","pack animals"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["perde","kamele","donkies"],"en":["horses","camels","donkeys"]}},"explain":{"af":"Osse het die swaar pale en matte gedra wanneer die groep getrek het, en mense het ook op osse gery. Perde het eers later saam met Europeërs gekom.","en":"Oxen carried the heavy poles and mats when the group moved, and people also rode on oxen. Horses only came later with Europeans."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling wys ’n verskil tussen die Khoikhoi en die San?","en":"Which statement shows a difference between the Khoikhoi and the San?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Khoikhoi het vee besit en ’n hoofman gehad; die San nie","en":"The Khoikhoi owned livestock and had a chief; the San did not"},{"af":"Die San het in matjieshuise gewoon; die Khoikhoi in grotte","en":"The San lived in mat houses; the Khoikhoi in caves"},{"af":"Die San het skape aangehou; die Khoikhoi het net gejag","en":"The San kept sheep; the Khoikhoi only hunted"},{"af":"Die Khoikhoi se tale het klikklanke gehad; die San s’n nie","en":"The Khoikhoi languages had clicks; the San languages did not"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die Khoikhoi was veewagters met hoofmanne; die San was jagter-versamelaars sonder hoofmanne. Albei se tale het klikklanke, en die Khoikhoi het in matjieshuise gewoon.","en":"The Khoikhoi were herders with chiefs; the San were hunter-gatherers without chiefs. Both groups’ languages have clicks, and the Khoikhoi lived in mat houses."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die Khoikhoi het elke dag van hul beeste geslag om vleis te eet.","en":"The Khoikhoi slaughtered some of their cattle every day to eat meat."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Vee was rykdom en is selde geslag – gewoonlik net by spesiale geleenthede. Melk was die belangrikste kos.","en":"False. Livestock was wealth and was seldom slaughtered – usually only on special occasions. Milk was the most important food."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Europese seevaarder skryf dat die Khoikhoi ‘suinig’ is omdat hulle min beeste wil ruil. Waarom is hierdie bron eensydig?","en":"A European sailor writes that the Khoikhoi are ‘stingy’ because they will trade only a few cattle. Why is this source biased?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat seevaarders in hul dagboeke nooit die waarheid geskryf het nie","en":"Because sailors never wrote the truth in their diaries"},{"af":"Omdat die Khoikhoi in werklikheid geen beeste gehad het nie","en":"Because the Khoikhoi actually had no cattle"},{"af":"Omdat hy nie verstaan het dat vee die Khoikhoi se rykdom was nie","en":"Because he did not understand that livestock was the Khoikhoi’s wealth"},{"af":"Omdat dit in ’n dagboek geskryf is en nie in ’n boek nie","en":"Because it was written in a diary and not in a book"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die skrywer was ’n buitestaander wat net sy eie kant wys. Vir die Khoikhoi was vee rykdom wat hulle nie maklik weggegee het nie. ’n Dagboek kan wel ’n nuttige bron wees – ons moet net vra wie dit geskryf het.","en":"The writer was an outsider who shows only his own side. For the Khoikhoi livestock was wealth that they did not give away easily. A diary can be a useful source – we just have to ask who wrote it."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Historici gebruik die naam ___ vir die San en die Khoikhoi saam.","en":"Historians use the name ___ for the San and the Khoikhoi together."},"answers":{"af":["Khoe-San","Khoesan","Khoisan","Khoi-San"],"en":["Khoe-San","Khoesan","Khoisan","Khoi-San"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Nama","Bantoesprekendes","Europeërs"],"en":["Nama","Bantu-speakers","Europeans"]}},"explain":{"af":"Khoe-San is die naam vir die verwante San en Khoikhoi saam. Die Nama is net een Khoikhoi-groep, en Bantoesprekende boere is ’n ander groep wat later gekom het.","en":"Khoe-San is the name for the related San and Khoikhoi together. The Nama are only one Khoikhoi group, and Bantu-speaking farmers are a different group who came later."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom kon die Khoikhoi in groter groepe as die San woon?","en":"Why could the Khoikhoi live in bigger groups than the San?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat hulle in die woestyn gewoon het","en":"Because they lived in the desert"},{"af":"Omdat hulle nie kos nodig gehad het nie","en":"Because they did not need food"},{"af":"Omdat hulle nooit getrek het nie","en":"Because they never moved"},{"af":"Omdat hul vee meer mense kon voed","en":"Because their livestock could feed more people"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Melk en vleis van vee was ’n meer seker voorraad kos as wild alleen, dus kon meer mense saam leef. Die Khoikhoi het wel getrek – met hul vee.","en":"Milk and meat from livestock were a more reliable food supply than wild animals alone, so more people could live together. The Khoikhoi did move – with their animals."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Argeoloë vind skaapbene van ongeveer 2 000 jaar gelede in ’n grot naby die kus. Wat vertel dit ons?","en":"Archaeologists find sheep bones from about 2 000 years ago in a cave near the coast. What does this tell us?"},"options":[{"af":"Dat Europeërs 2 000 jaar gelede skape gebring het","en":"That Europeans brought sheep 2 000 years ago"},{"af":"Dat mense toe al skape aangehou het","en":"That people already kept sheep at that time"},{"af":"Dat die San nooit vleis geëet het nie","en":"That the San never ate meat"},{"af":"Dat skape van nature in grotte woon","en":"That sheep naturally live in caves"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Skaapbene van daardie ouderdom is bewys dat veewagters toe al skape aangehou het. Europeërs het eers baie later, vanaf die 1500’s, by die Kaap aangekom.","en":"Sheep bones of that age are evidence that herders already kept sheep then. Europeans only arrived at the Cape much later, from the 1500s."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Die eerste boere in Suider-Afrika","en":"The first farmers in southern Africa"},"topics":[{"id":"sw5-t2-gesk-eerste-boere","title":{"af":"Die eerste boere kom aan","en":"The arrival of the first farmers"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik wie die Bantoesprekende boere was, waar en waarom hulle hulle in Suider-Afrika gevestig het, en hul lewe met dié van jagter-versamelaars en veewagters kan vergelyk.","en":"You will be able to explain who the Bantu-speaking farmers were, where and why they settled in southern Africa, and compare their way of life with that of hunter-gatherers and herders."},"summary":{"af":"## Wie was die eerste boere?\n\nDie eerste boere in Suider-Afrika was **Bantoesprekende** mense. **Bantoe** is die naam wat historici en taalkundiges gebruik vir ’n groot **taalfamilie**: honderde verwante tale wat in groot dele van Afrika gepraat word. In isiZulu en isiXhosa beteken *abantu* byvoorbeeld ‘mense’. In Suid-Afrika behoort isiZulu, isiXhosa, isiNdebele, siSwati, Sesotho, Sepedi, Setswana, Xitsonga en Tshivenda almal aan hierdie taalfamilie.\n\nTydens apartheid is die woord ‘Bantoe’ op ’n kwetsende manier vir mense gebruik. Daarom gebruik ons dit net vir die **taalfamilie**, in die woord **Bantoesprekend**.\n\n## ’n Stadige trek oor baie eeue\n\nLank gelede het die voorouers van hierdie boere in Wes-Sentraal-Afrika gewoon, naby die huidige Kameroen en Nigerië. Oor **baie eeue** het klein groepe stadig oos- en suidwaarts getrek. Dit was nie een groot trek nie: elke geslag het net ’n entjie verder gegaan, op soek na nuwe grond vir hul lande en weiding vir hul vee.\n\nHulle het **ongeveer 2 000 jaar gelede** (sowat 1 700 tot 2 000 jaar gelede) in Suider-Afrika aangekom.\n\n## Waar het hulle gaan woon?\n\nDie boere het plekke gekies met:\n\n- **somerreën** vir hul gewasse,\n- **vrugbare grond** en water naby riviere,\n- **weiding** vir hul vee, en\n- **hout** vir vuur en bouwerk.\n\nSulke plekke was veral in die **Limpopo-vallei**, die oostelike laeveld, **KwaZulu-Natal** en die **Oos-Kaap**. Hulle het nie in die Wes-Kaap gaan woon nie, want daar reën dit veral in die winter, en hul gewasse het somerreën nodig gehad. Die weste en die Karoo het ook te min reën gekry.\n\n> **Onthou:** Die boere het hulle gevestig waar daar **somerreën**, goeie grond en water was – daarom in die ooste en nie in die droë weste nie.\n\n## Boerdery: gewasse en vee\n\n| Wat | Voorbeelde | Waarvoor |\n|---|---|---|\n| Graangewasse | Sorghum, babala (pêrel-giers) | Pap en bier |\n| Ander gewasse | Bone, melone, kalbasse | Kos; kalbasse as houers |\n| Vee | Beeste, skape, bokke | Melk, vleis, velle en rykdom |\n\n- Die vroue het die lande met **skoffels** bewerk; mans en seuns het na die vee omgesien.\n- Hulle het steeds gejag en veldkos versamel.\n- Graan is in **graanputte** of in graanskure op pale gestoor vir die droë seisoen.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die eerste boere het **nie mielies** geplant nie! Mielies kom van Amerika en het eers die afgelope paar honderd jaar ’n gewone gewas in Suider-Afrika geword. Die eerste boere het **sorghum** en **babala** geplant.\n\n## Vaste nedersettings\n\nOmdat hulle hul lande moes bewerk en oes, het die boere **op een plek gebly** in **vaste nedersettings**. Hul huise was ronde hutte van **pale, takke en klei** met ’n **grasdak**. ’n Nedersetting het jare lank bestaan, totdat die grond uitgeput was en hulle nuwe lande moes soek. Die boere het ook **yster** gesmelt en **kleipotte** gemaak.\n\n## Drie maniere van lewe\n\n| | San | Khoikhoi | Eerste boere |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Kos | Jag en versamel | Vee (melk), ook jag | Gewasse en vee |\n| Woon | Trek rond | Trek met vee | Bly op een plek |\n| Huise | Skuilings, grotte | Matjieshuise | Hutte van pale en klei |\n| Groepe | Klein | Groter | Groot nedersettings |\n| Leiers | Geen hoofman | Hoofman en raad | Hoofman en raad |\n\n## Hoe weet ons dit?\n\nArgeoloë vind by ou nedersettings stukke **versierde kleipotte**, **ysterslak** (afval van ystersmelt), verkoolde **sorghumsaad**, beesbene en oorblyfsels van graanputte en hutvloere. Deur byvoorbeeld houtskool te **dateer**, kan hulle uitwerk ongeveer hoe oud ’n nedersetting is. Die tale self is ook ’n bron: verwante woorde in tale ver van mekaar wys dat hierdie tale uit dieselfde ou taal ontwikkel het.","en":"## Who were the first farmers?\n\nThe first farmers in southern Africa were **Bantu-speaking** people. **Bantu** is the name historians and language experts use for a large **language family**: hundreds of related languages spoken in large parts of Africa. In isiZulu and isiXhosa, for example, *abantu* means ‘people’. In South Africa isiZulu, isiXhosa, isiNdebele, siSwati, Sesotho, Sepedi, Setswana, Xitsonga and Tshivenda all belong to this language family.\n\nDuring apartheid the word ‘Bantu’ was used in a hurtful way for people. That is why we use it only for the **language family**, in the word **Bantu-speaking**.\n\n## A slow journey over many centuries\n\nLong ago the ancestors of these farmers lived in west-central Africa, near present-day Cameroon and Nigeria. Over **many centuries** small groups slowly moved east and south. It was not one big journey: each generation went only a little further, looking for new land for their fields and grazing for their animals.\n\nThey arrived in southern Africa **about 2 000 years ago** (roughly 1 700 to 2 000 years ago).\n\n## Where did they settle?\n\nThe farmers chose places with:\n\n- **summer rain** for their crops,\n- **fertile soil** and water near rivers,\n- **grazing** for their animals, and\n- **wood** for fires and building.\n\nSuch places were mainly in the **Limpopo valley**, the eastern lowveld, **KwaZulu-Natal** and the **Eastern Cape**. They did not settle in the Western Cape, because there it rains mainly in winter, and their crops needed summer rain. The west and the Karoo also got too little rain.\n\n> **Remember:** The farmers settled where there was **summer rain**, good soil and water – that is why they settled in the east and not in the dry west.\n\n## Farming: crops and livestock\n\n| What | Examples | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| Grain crops | Sorghum, pearl millet (babala) | Porridge and beer |\n| Other crops | Beans, melons, calabashes (gourds) | Food; calabashes as containers |\n| Livestock | Cattle, sheep, goats | Milk, meat, skins and wealth |\n\n- The women worked the fields with **hoes**; men and boys looked after the animals.\n- They still hunted and gathered veld food.\n- Grain was stored in **storage pits** or in granaries on poles for the dry season.\n\n> **Common mistake:** The first farmers did **not** plant maize! Maize comes from America and only became a common crop in southern Africa in the last few hundred years. The first farmers planted **sorghum** and **pearl millet**.\n\n## Settled villages\n\nBecause they had to work and harvest their fields, the farmers **stayed in one place** in **settled villages** (settlements). Their homes were round huts of **poles, branches and clay** with a **thatched roof**. A settlement lasted for years, until the soil was worn out and they had to look for new fields. The farmers also smelted **iron** and made **clay pots**.\n\n## Three ways of life\n\n| | San | Khoikhoi | First farmers |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Food | Hunting and gathering | Livestock (milk), also hunting | Crops and livestock |\n| Living | Move around | Move with animals | Stay in one place |\n| Homes | Shelters, caves | Mat houses | Huts of poles and clay |\n| Groups | Small | Bigger | Large settlements |\n| Leaders | No chief | Chief and council | Chief and council |\n\n## How do we know?\n\nAt old settlements archaeologists find pieces of **decorated clay pots**, **iron slag** (waste from iron smelting), burnt **sorghum seeds**, cattle bones and the remains of storage pits and hut floors. By **dating** things like charcoal, they can work out roughly how old a settlement is. The languages themselves are also a source: related words in languages far apart show that these languages developed from the same old language."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Bantoesprekend","en":"Bantu-speaking"},"def":{"af":"Iemand wat ’n taal uit die Bantoe-taalfamilie praat, soos isiZulu, Sesotho of Tshivenda.","en":"Someone who speaks a language from the Bantu language family, such as isiZulu, Sesotho or Tshivenda."}},{"term":{"af":"Taalfamilie","en":"Language family"},"def":{"af":"’n Groep tale wat verwant is omdat hulle uit dieselfde ou taal ontwikkel het.","en":"A group of languages that are related because they developed from the same old language."}},{"term":{"af":"Migrasie","en":"Migration"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer mense oor ’n lang tyd van een gebied na ’n ander trek om daar te gaan woon.","en":"When people move over a long time from one area to another to live there."}},{"term":{"af":"Nedersetting","en":"Settlement"},"def":{"af":"’n Plek waar mense hulle vir ’n lang tyd vestig en huise bou.","en":"A place where people settle for a long time and build homes."}},{"term":{"af":"Gewas","en":"Crop"},"def":{"af":"’n Plant wat boere plant en oes vir kos of ander gebruike.","en":"A plant that farmers grow and harvest for food or other uses."}},{"term":{"af":"Sorghum","en":"Sorghum"},"def":{"af":"’n Graangewas wat die eerste boere geplant het om pap en bier van te maak.","en":"A grain crop that the first farmers grew to make porridge and beer."}},{"term":{"af":"Babala (pêrel-giers)","en":"Pearl millet (babala)"},"def":{"af":"’n Graangewas met klein korrels wat goed in warm, droërige gebiede groei.","en":"A grain crop with small seeds that grows well in warm, fairly dry areas."}},{"term":{"af":"Somerreën","en":"Summer rainfall"},"def":{"af":"Reën wat meestal in die somer val; die eerste boere se gewasse het dit nodig gehad.","en":"Rain that falls mostly in summer; the first farmers’ crops needed it."}},{"term":{"af":"Graanput","en":"Storage pit"},"def":{"af":"’n Gat in die grond waarin graan vir die droë seisoen gestoor is.","en":"A hole in the ground in which grain was stored for the dry season."}},{"term":{"af":"Vrugbare grond","en":"Fertile soil"},"def":{"af":"Grond met baie voedingstowwe waarin gewasse goed groei.","en":"Soil with plenty of nutrients in which crops grow well."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik die term ‘Bantoesprekend’","en":"Explain the term ‘Bantu-speaking’"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato lees in haar handboek van ‘Bantoesprekende boere’. Sy vra: ‘Was dit een volk met een taal?’ Verduidelik die term aan haar.","en":"Lerato reads about ‘Bantu-speaking farmers’ in her textbook. She asks: ‘Was this one people with one language?’ Explain the term to her."},"steps":[{"af":"Begin by die woord: **Bantoe** is die naam van ’n **taalfamilie**, nie van een volk nie.","en":"Start with the word: **Bantu** is the name of a **language family**, not of one people."},{"af":"Verduidelik: dit is honderde verwante tale. In Suid-Afrika is isiZulu, isiXhosa, Sesotho, Setswana, Sepedi, Xitsonga, Tshivenda, siSwati en isiNdebele almal Bantoetale.","en":"Explain: it is hundreds of related languages. In South Africa isiZulu, isiXhosa, Sesotho, Setswana, Sepedi, Xitsonga, Tshivenda, siSwati and isiNdebele are all Bantu languages."},{"af":"Noem waarom ons die woord versigtig gebruik: tydens apartheid is ‘Bantoe’ kwetsend gebruik, daarom gebruik historici dit net vir die taalfamilie.","en":"Say why we use the word carefully: during apartheid ‘Bantu’ was used in a hurtful way, so historians use it only for the language family."}],"answer":{"af":"Nee. ‘Bantoesprekend’ beteken dat mense ’n taal uit die groot Bantoe-taalfamilie praat. Die eerste boere was baie groepe met verskillende, maar verwante tale.","en":"No. ‘Bantu-speaking’ means that people speak a language from the large Bantu language family. The first farmers were many groups with different but related languages."}},{"title":{"af":"Waarom in die ooste?","en":"Why in the east?"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik waarom die eerste boere hulle in die Limpopo-vallei, KwaZulu-Natal en die Oos-Kaap gevestig het, maar nie in die Wes-Kaap nie.","en":"Explain why the first farmers settled in the Limpopo valley, KwaZulu-Natal and the Eastern Cape, but not in the Western Cape."},"steps":[{"af":"Noem wat boere nodig het: reën op die regte tyd, vrugbare grond, water, weiding en hout.","en":"Name what farmers need: rain at the right time, fertile soil, water, grazing and wood."},{"af":"Dink aan hul gewasse: sorghum en babala word in die somer geplant en het **somerreën** nodig.","en":"Think about their crops: sorghum and pearl millet are planted in summer and need **summer rain**."},{"af":"Vergelyk die gebiede: die ooste kry somerreën; die Wes-Kaap kry veral winterreën, en die weste is droog.","en":"Compare the areas: the east gets summer rain; the Western Cape gets mainly winter rain, and the west is dry."}],"answer":{"af":"Die oostelike gebiede het somerreën, vrugbare grond, water en weiding gehad. Die Wes-Kaap kry veral winterreën en die weste is droog, dus sou hul somergewasse daar nie goed gegroei het nie.","en":"The eastern areas had summer rain, fertile soil, water and grazing. The Western Cape gets mainly winter rain and the west is dry, so their summer crops would not have grown well there."}},{"title":{"af":"Lees argeologiese bewyse","en":"Read archaeological evidence"},"problem":{"af":"By ’n ou terrein in KwaZulu-Natal vind argeoloë: stukke versierde kleipotte, ysterslak, verkoolde sorghumsaad, beesbene en die oorblyfsels van hutvloere. Watter soort mense het hier gewoon? Gee redes.","en":"At an old site in KwaZulu-Natal archaeologists find: pieces of decorated clay pots, iron slag, burnt sorghum seeds, cattle bones and the remains of hut floors. What kind of people lived here? Give reasons."},"steps":[{"af":"Sorghumsaad wys dat hulle **gewasse geplant** het – jagter-versamelaars en veewagters het dit nie gedoen nie.","en":"Sorghum seeds show that they **grew crops** – hunter-gatherers and herders did not do this."},{"af":"Beesbene wys dat hulle **vee** aangehou het; ysterslak wys dat hulle **yster gesmelt** het.","en":"Cattle bones show that they **kept livestock**; iron slag shows that they **smelted iron**."},{"af":"Hutvloere wys dat hulle **op een plek gebly** het in ’n vaste nedersetting.","en":"Hut floors show that they **stayed in one place** in a settled village."}],"answer":{"af":"Bantoesprekende boere: hulle het sorghum geplant, beeste aangehou, yster gesmelt en in ’n vaste nedersetting gewoon.","en":"Bantu-speaking farmers: they grew sorghum, kept cattle, smelted iron and lived in a settled village."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarna verwys die woord ‘Bantoe’ in ‘Bantoesprekende boere’?","en":"What does the word ‘Bantu’ in ‘Bantu-speaking farmers’ refer to?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Groot familie van verwante tale","en":"A large family of related languages"},{"af":"Een volk wat net een taal gepraat het","en":"One people who spoke only one language"},{"af":"’n Plek in Sentraal-Afrika","en":"A place in central Africa"},{"af":"’n Soort gewas wat die boere geplant het","en":"A kind of crop that the farmers grew"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Bantoe is die naam van ’n taalfamilie met honderde verwante tale, soos isiZulu, Sesotho en Tshivenda. Dit was nie een volk nie.","en":"Bantu is the name of a language family with hundreds of related languages, such as isiZulu, Sesotho and Tshivenda. It was not one people."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die eerste boere in Suider-Afrika het mielies as hul hoofgewas geplant.","en":"The first farmers in southern Africa grew maize as their main crop."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Mielies kom van Amerika en het eers die afgelope paar honderd jaar hier ’n gewone gewas geword. Die eerste boere het sorghum en babala geplant.","en":"False. Maize comes from America and only became a common crop here in the last few hundred years. The first farmers grew sorghum and pearl millet."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ongeveer wanneer het die eerste boere in Suider-Afrika aangekom?","en":"Roughly when did the first farmers arrive in southern Africa?"},"options":[{"af":"In 1652","en":"In 1652"},{"af":"Ongeveer 200 jaar gelede","en":"About 200 years ago"},{"af":"Ongeveer 2 000 jaar gelede","en":"About 2 000 years ago"},{"af":"Ongeveer 20 000 jaar gelede","en":"About 20 000 years ago"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die boere het sowat 1 700 tot 2 000 jaar gelede aangekom, ná ’n stadige trek oor baie eeue. 1652 is toe die Nederlanders hulle aan die Kaap gevestig het – baie later.","en":"The farmers arrived roughly 1 700 to 2 000 years ago, after a slow journey over many centuries. 1652 is when the Dutch settled at the Cape – much later."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die graangewas ___ was een van die belangrikste gewasse van die eerste boere.","en":"The grain crop ___ was one of the most important crops of the first farmers."},"answers":{"af":["sorghum","graansorghum"],"en":["sorghum"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["mielies","koring","rys"],"en":["maize","wheat","rice"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die eerste boere het sorghum en babala geplant. Mielies het eers later uit Amerika gekom, en koring en rys is nie deur die eerste boere hier geplant nie.","en":"The first farmers grew sorghum and pearl millet. Maize only came later from America, and wheat and rice were not grown here by the first farmers."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom het die eerste boere hulle nie in die Wes-Kaap gevestig nie?","en":"Why did the first farmers not settle in the Western Cape?"},"options":[{"af":"Daar was glad geen riviere of water in die Wes-Kaap nie","en":"There were no rivers or water at all in the Western Cape"},{"af":"Die Wes-Kaap kry veral winterreën, maar hul gewasse het somerreën nodig gehad","en":"The Western Cape gets mainly winter rain, but their crops needed summer rain"},{"af":"Die San en die Khoikhoi het hulle verbied om daar te woon","en":"The San and the Khoikhoi forbade them to live there"},{"af":"Dit was in die Wes-Kaap te koud vir beeste en bokke","en":"It was too cold for cattle and goats in the Western Cape"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Sorghum en babala het somerreën nodig. Die Wes-Kaap kry veral in die winter reën, dus sou hul gewasse daar nie goed gegroei het nie.","en":"Sorghum and pearl millet need summer rain. The Western Cape gets its rain mainly in winter, so their crops would not have grown well there."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke ding by waarvoor die eerste boere dit gebruik het.","en":"Match each thing to what the first farmers used it for."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Sorghum","en":"Sorghum"},"r":{"af":"Pap en bier","en":"Porridge and beer"}},{"l":{"af":"Kalbas","en":"Calabash"},"r":{"af":"Houer vir water of melk","en":"Container for water or milk"}},{"l":{"af":"Beeste","en":"Cattle"},"r":{"af":"Melk, vleis en rykdom","en":"Milk, meat and wealth"}},{"l":{"af":"Graanput","en":"Storage pit"},"r":{"af":"Graan stoor vir die droë seisoen","en":"Storing grain for the dry season"}},{"l":{"af":"Skoffel","en":"Hoe"},"r":{"af":"Die lande bewerk","en":"Working the fields"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die boere het gewasse geplant en geoes, vee aangehou en graan gestoor sodat hulle deur die droë seisoen kos gehad het.","en":"The farmers grew and harvested crops, kept livestock and stored grain so that they had food through the dry season."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom het die eerste boere in vaste nedersettings gewoon en nie rondgetrek nie?","en":"Why did the first farmers live in settled villages and not move around?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat hulle geen vee gehad het om mee te trek nie","en":"Because they had no livestock to move with"},{"af":"Omdat hulle in die woestyn gewoon het","en":"Because they lived in the desert"},{"af":"Omdat hulle hul lande moes bewerk en oes","en":"Because they had to work and harvest their fields"},{"af":"Omdat die hoofman verbied het dat hulle trek","en":"Because the chief forbade them to move"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Wie gewasse plant, moet naby die lande bly om te skoffel, die oes te beskerm en te oes. Die boere het wel vee gehad.","en":"People who grow crops must stay near their fields to weed, protect the harvest and reap it. The farmers did have livestock."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Plek waar mense vir ’n lang tyd bly en huise bou, is ’n ___.","en":"A place where people stay for a long time and build homes is a ___."},"answers":{"af":["nedersetting","vaste nedersetting"],"en":["settlement","settled village"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["skuiling","matjieshuis","grot"],"en":["shelter","mat house","cave"]}},"explain":{"af":"In ’n nedersetting woon mense jare lank op een plek. Skuilings en matjieshuise pas by mense wat gereeld trek.","en":"In a settlement people live in one place for years. Shelters and mat houses suit people who move often."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van hierdie tale is NIE ’n Bantoetaal nie?","en":"Which one of these languages is NOT a Bantu language?"},"options":[{"af":"isiZulu","en":"isiZulu"},{"af":"Setswana","en":"Setswana"},{"af":"Tshivenda","en":"Tshivenda"},{"af":"Afrikaans","en":"Afrikaans"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"isiZulu, Setswana en Tshivenda behoort aan die Bantoe-taalfamilie. Afrikaans het uit Nederlands ontwikkel en behoort aan ’n ander taalfamilie.","en":"isiZulu, Setswana and Tshivenda belong to the Bantu language family. Afrikaans developed from Dutch and belongs to a different language family."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die eerste boere het plekke met vrugbare grond en water naby riviere gekies.","en":"The first farmers chose places with fertile soil and water near rivers."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Gewasse groei goed in vrugbare grond, en mense en vee het water nodig. Daarom het hulle naby riviere gaan woon.","en":"True. Crops grow well in fertile soil, and people and animals need water. That is why they settled near rivers."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"By ’n ou terrein vind argeoloë verkoolde sorghumsaad, ysterslak en beesbene. Wie het waarskynlik daar gewoon?","en":"At an old site archaeologists find burnt sorghum seeds, iron slag and cattle bones. Who probably lived there?"},"options":[{"af":"Jagter-versamelaars soos die San","en":"Hunter-gatherers such as the San"},{"af":"Bantoesprekende boere","en":"Bantu-speaking farmers"},{"af":"Veewagters soos die Khoikhoi","en":"Herders such as the Khoikhoi"},{"af":"Europese seevaarders","en":"European sailors"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Sorghum wys dat gewasse geplant is, en slak wys dat yster gesmelt is. Net die boere het albei gedoen. Veewagters het wel vee gehad, maar het nie sorghum geplant nie.","en":"Sorghum shows that crops were grown, and slag shows that iron was smelted. Only the farmers did both. Herders did have livestock, but did not grow sorghum."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die boere het oor baie ___ stadig suidwaarts getrek – dit was nie een groot trek nie.","en":"The farmers slowly moved south over many ___ – it was not one big journey."},"answers":{"af":["eeue"],"en":["centuries"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["dae","weke","maande"],"en":["days","weeks","months"]}},"explain":{"af":"Elke geslag het net ’n entjie verder getrek. Die hele beweging van Wes-Sentraal-Afrika na Suider-Afrika het baie eeue geduur.","en":"Each generation moved only a little further. The whole movement from west-central Africa to southern Africa took many centuries."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat was die grootste verskil tussen die Khoikhoi en die eerste boere?","en":"What was the biggest difference between the Khoikhoi and the first farmers?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Khoikhoi het vee gehad, maar die boere nie","en":"The Khoikhoi had livestock, but the farmers did not"},{"af":"Die boere het geen leiers gehad nie","en":"The farmers had no leaders"},{"af":"Die Khoikhoi het in groot dorpe van klip gewoon","en":"The Khoikhoi lived in large towns of stone"},{"af":"Die boere het ook gewasse geplant en op een plek gebly","en":"The farmers also grew crops and stayed in one place"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Albei het vee aangehou en hoofmanne gehad. Die verskil is dat die boere ook gewasse geplant het, en daarom op een plek gebly het, terwyl die Khoikhoi met hul vee getrek het.","en":"Both kept livestock and had chiefs. The difference is that the farmers also grew crops, and therefore stayed in one place, while the Khoikhoi moved with their animals."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom het ’n nedersetting van die boere ná baie jare soms verskuif?","en":"Why did a farming settlement sometimes move after many years?"},"options":[{"af":"Die grond was uitgeput en hulle het nuwe lande nodig gehad","en":"The soil was worn out and they needed new fields"},{"af":"Die boere wou die seisoene volg soos die San","en":"The farmers wanted to follow the seasons like the San"},{"af":"Die hutte kon net een jaar hou","en":"The huts could only last one year"},{"af":"Die hoofman het elke jaar ’n nuwe plek gekies","en":"The chief chose a new place every year"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Ná baie oeste het die grond minder voedingstowwe gehad en het gewasse swakker gegroei. Dan het die boere nuwe, vrugbare grond gesoek. Hulle het nie met die seisoene getrek nie.","en":"After many harvests the soil had fewer nutrients and crops grew more poorly. Then the farmers looked for new, fertile land. They did not move with the seasons."}}]},{"id":"sw5-t2-gesk-ystertydperk","title":{"af":"Yster, pottebakkery en die opstal","en":"Iron, pottery and the homestead"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe die eerste boere yster gesmelt en potte gemaak het, hoe ’n opstal uitgelê was en watter rol beeste, leiers en lobola in hul lewe gespeel het.","en":"You will be able to explain how the first farmers smelted iron and made pots, how a homestead was laid out and what role cattle, leaders and lobola played in their lives."},"summary":{"af":"## Die Ystertydperk\n\nDie Bantoesprekende boere was die eerste mense in Suider-Afrika wat **yster** kon maak. Daarom noem historici hul tyd die **Ystertydperk**. Ystergereedskap is sterker en skerper as gereedskap van klip, been of hout.\n\n## Hoe is yster gemaak?\n\n1. **Ystererts** (rots met yster daarin) is uitgegrawe en in stukkies gebreek.\n2. Die erts is saam met **houtskool** in ’n **smeltoond** van klei gepak. Houtskool brand baie warmer as gewone hout.\n3. Met **blaasbalke** van bokvel is lug deur kleipype in die oond gepomp. Die ekstra lug het die vuur so warm gemaak dat die yster uit die rots geskei het.\n4. Die afval wat oorbly, heet **slak**.\n5. Die **smid** het die yster weer warm gemaak en op ’n klip-**aambeeld** in die regte vorm geslaan.\n\nSmede was gerespekteer, want hulle het spesiale kennis gehad.\n\n| Ystergereedskap | Waarvoor |\n|---|---|\n| **Skoffels** | Grond omwerk en skoffel, sodat hulle meer lande kon bewerk |\n| **Byle** | Bome afkap vir brandhout, hutte en nuwe lande |\n| **Messe** | Vleis sny en velle bewerk |\n| **Spiese** en pylpunte | Jag en beskerming |\n\nHulle het ook **koper** gesmelt om armbande en krale te maak.\n\n## Pottebakkery\n\nDie boere het **kleipotte** gemaak om kos te kook, graan te stoor, water te dra en sorghumbier te brou. Die potte is van **rolle klei** opgebou, met **patrone** soos lyne en driehoeke versier en in ’n vuur **gebak** sodat hulle hard word. Elke groep en tydperk het sy eie styl gehad. Argeoloë gebruik die patrone om uit te werk wie op ’n plek gewoon het en wanneer.\n\nNaby Lydenburg in Mpumalanga is sewe **koppe van gebakte klei** gevind: die **Lydenburg-koppe**. Hulle is sowat **1 500 jaar oud**. Twee is groot genoeg om soos ’n masker op te sit. Hulle is waarskynlik by **seremonies** gebruik en wys dat die boere ook **kuns** gemaak het.\n\n## Handel\n\nDie boere het onder mekaar en met ander groepe goedere geruil: **yster**, **koper**, **sout**, potte en graan, **ivoor** (olifanttande) en velle, en **krale**. Later het handelaars oor die see glaskrale na die ooskus gebring.\n\n## Die opstal\n\nDie boere het in **opstalle** gewoon – die tuiste van ’n groot familie:\n\n- In die **middel** was die **beeskraal**. Daar was die beeste snags veilig en het die mans vergader. Graan is soms in putte in die kraal gestoor.\n- Die **hutte** is in ’n **sirkel** om die kraal gebou. Die belangrikste hut was gewoonlik agter, oorkant die ingang.\n- Om alles was ’n **heining** van pale of doringtakke. Die **lande** was buite die opstal.\n\n> **Onthou:** Die beeskraal is in die **middel** omdat beeste so **waardevol** was – daar was hulle die veiligste.\n\n| Wie | Take |\n|---|---|\n| Mans | Beeste oppas, jag, lande skoonmaak, hutraamwerke bou, yster bewerk |\n| Vroue | Plant, skoffel en oes, graan maal, kook, potte maak, water en hout aandra |\n| Seuns | Kalwers en bokke oppas, later die beeste |\n| Meisies | Hul ma help, kleiner kinders oppas, voëls uit die lande verjaag |\n\n## Leiers en beeste\n\n- Verskeie opstalle was onder ’n **hoofman**, wat saam met ’n **raad** van ouer mans besluite geneem en twiste besleg het. In Setswana heet die openbare vergaderplek die **kgotla**.\n- **Beeste was rykdom.** Hoe meer beeste, hoe belangriker die familie.\n- **Lobola:** wanneer ’n paar trou, gee die bruidegom se familie beeste aan die bruid se familie. Dit bind die twee families saam. Lobola word vandag nog gegee, dikwels in geld.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Lobola beteken **nie** dat ’n vrou ‘gekoop’ word nie. Dit verbind twee families aan mekaar en wys respek vir die bruid.\n\n## Boere, San en Khoikhoi\n\nDie groepe het **gehandel**: boere het yster, potte en graan geruil vir velle, vleis, heuning en volstruiseierkrale. Party San is as **reënmakers** gerespekteer, en mense het soms met mekaar getrou. Daarom het isiXhosa en isiZulu **klikklanke** uit die Khoe-San-tale oorgeneem. Daar was ook **konflik**, byvoorbeeld wanneer lande en vee die wild verdryf het.","en":"## The Iron Age\n\nThe Bantu-speaking farmers were the first people in southern Africa who could make **iron**. That is why historians call their time the **Iron Age**. Iron tools are stronger and sharper than tools of stone, bone or wood.\n\n## How was iron made?\n\n1. **Iron ore** (rock with iron in it) was dug up and broken into small pieces.\n2. The ore was packed with **charcoal** into a clay **furnace**. Charcoal burns much hotter than ordinary wood.\n3. **Bellows** made of goatskin pumped air through clay pipes into the furnace. The extra air made the fire so hot that the iron separated from the rock.\n4. The waste that is left over is called **slag**.\n5. The **smith** heated the iron again and hammered it into the right shape on a stone **anvil**.\n\nSmiths were respected, because they had special knowledge.\n\n| Iron tool | Used for |\n|---|---|\n| **Hoes** | Turning soil and weeding, so they could work more fields |\n| **Axes** | Cutting down trees for firewood, huts and new fields |\n| **Knives** | Cutting meat and working skins |\n| **Spears** and arrowheads | Hunting and protection |\n\nThey also smelted **copper** to make bangles and beads.\n\n## Pottery\n\nThe farmers made **clay pots** to cook food, store grain, carry water and brew sorghum beer. The pots were built up from **coils of clay**, decorated with **patterns** such as lines and triangles and **fired** in a fire to make them hard. Each group and period had its own style. Archaeologists use the patterns to work out who lived at a place and when.\n\nNear Lydenburg in Mpumalanga seven **heads made of fired clay** were found: the **Lydenburg Heads**. They are about **1 500 years old**. Two are big enough to wear like a mask. They were probably used in **ceremonies** and show that the farmers also made **art**.\n\n## Trade\n\nThe farmers exchanged goods among themselves and with other groups: **iron**, **copper**, **salt**, pots and grain, **ivory** (elephant tusks) and skins, and **beads**. Later traders brought glass beads across the sea to the east coast.\n\n## The homestead\n\nThe farmers lived in **homesteads** – the home of a large family:\n\n- In the **centre** was the **cattle kraal**. There the cattle were safe at night and the men met. Grain was sometimes stored in pits in the kraal.\n- The **huts** were built in a **circle** around the kraal. The most important hut was usually at the back, opposite the entrance.\n- Around everything was a **fence** of poles or thorn branches. The **fields** were outside the homestead.\n\n> **Remember:** The cattle kraal is in the **centre** because cattle were so **valuable** – that is where they were safest.\n\n| Who | Tasks |\n|---|---|\n| Men | Looking after cattle, hunting, clearing fields, building hut frames, working iron |\n| Women | Planting, weeding and harvesting, grinding grain, cooking, making pots, fetching water and wood |\n| Boys | Looking after calves and goats, later the cattle |\n| Girls | Helping their mothers, looking after younger children, chasing birds from the fields |\n\n## Leaders and cattle\n\n- Several homesteads were under a **chief**, who made decisions and settled disputes together with a **council** of older men. In Setswana the public meeting place is called the **kgotla**.\n- **Cattle were wealth.** The more cattle, the more important the family.\n- **Lobola:** when a couple marries, the groom’s family gives cattle to the bride’s family. This binds the two families together. Lobola is still given today, often as money.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Lobola does **not** mean that a woman is ‘bought’. It joins two families to each other and shows respect for the bride.\n\n## Farmers, San and Khoikhoi\n\nThe groups **traded**: farmers exchanged iron, pots and grain for skins, meat, honey and ostrich-eggshell beads. Some San were respected as **rainmakers**, and people sometimes married each other. That is why isiXhosa and isiZulu took over **click sounds** from the Khoe-San languages. There was also **conflict**, for example when fields and cattle drove away the game."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Ystererts","en":"Iron ore"},"def":{"af":"Rots wat yster bevat en waaruit yster gesmelt word.","en":"Rock that contains iron and from which iron is smelted."}},{"term":{"af":"Smeltoond","en":"Furnace"},"def":{"af":"’n Oond van klei waarin erts en houtskool baie warm gemaak word om yster te smelt.","en":"A clay oven in which ore and charcoal are made very hot to smelt iron."}},{"term":{"af":"Blaasbalk","en":"Bellows"},"def":{"af":"’n Toestel van dierevel waarmee lug in ’n vuur gepomp word om dit warmer te maak.","en":"A tool made of animal skin that pumps air into a fire to make it hotter."}},{"term":{"af":"Slak","en":"Slag"},"def":{"af":"Die afval wat oorbly wanneer yster uit erts gesmelt word.","en":"The waste that is left when iron is smelted from ore."}},{"term":{"af":"Smid","en":"Smith"},"def":{"af":"Iemand wat metaal warm maak en dit in gereedskap of ander voorwerpe slaan.","en":"Someone who heats metal and hammers it into tools or other objects."}},{"term":{"af":"Pottebakkery","en":"Pottery"},"def":{"af":"Die maak van potte en ander voorwerpe van klei wat gebak word sodat dit hard word.","en":"Making pots and other objects from clay that is fired to make it hard."}},{"term":{"af":"Lydenburg-koppe","en":"Lydenburg Heads"},"def":{"af":"Sewe koppe van gebakte klei, sowat 1 500 jaar oud, wat naby Lydenburg in Mpumalanga gevind is.","en":"Seven heads of fired clay, about 1 500 years old, found near Lydenburg in Mpumalanga."}},{"term":{"af":"Opstal","en":"Homestead"},"def":{"af":"Die tuiste van ’n familie: hutte in ’n kring om ’n beeskraal, met die lande daarbuite.","en":"The home of a family: huts in a circle around a cattle kraal, with the fields outside."}},{"term":{"af":"Beeskraal","en":"Cattle kraal"},"def":{"af":"’n Omheinde plek in die middel van die opstal waar die beeste snags gehou is.","en":"A fenced place in the centre of the homestead where the cattle were kept at night."}},{"term":{"af":"Lobola","en":"Lobola"},"def":{"af":"Beeste (vandag dikwels geld) wat die bruidegom se familie aan die bruid se familie gee om die twee families saam te bind.","en":"Cattle (today often money) that the groom’s family gives to the bride’s family to bind the two families together."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Beskryf hoe yster gesmelt is","en":"Describe how iron was smelted"},"problem":{"af":"Beskryf in die regte volgorde hoe die eerste boere ’n ysterskoffel gemaak het.","en":"Describe in the correct order how the first farmers made an iron hoe."},"steps":[{"af":"Grawe **ystererts** uit en breek dit in stukkies.","en":"Dig up **iron ore** and break it into small pieces."},{"af":"Pak die erts saam met **houtskool** in ’n **smeltoond** van klei en steek dit aan.","en":"Pack the ore with **charcoal** into a clay **furnace** and light it."},{"af":"Pomp lug met **blaasbalke** deur kleipype in die oond sodat die vuur baie warm word. Die yster skei van die rots; die afval is **slak**.","en":"Pump air with **bellows** through clay pipes into the furnace so that the fire becomes very hot. The iron separates from the rock; the waste is **slag**."},{"af":"Die **smid** maak die yster weer warm en slaan dit op ’n **aambeeld** in die vorm van ’n skoffel.","en":"The **smith** heats the iron again and hammers it into the shape of a hoe on an **anvil**."}],"answer":{"af":"Erts uitgrawe → met houtskool in ’n smeltoond pak → lug met blaasbalke inpomp → slak skei af → smid slaan die yster in ’n skoffel.","en":"Dig up ore → pack with charcoal in a furnace → pump in air with bellows → slag separates → smith hammers the iron into a hoe."}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik die uitleg van ’n opstal","en":"Explain the layout of a homestead"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho moet vir ’n projek ’n opstal teken. Beskryf wat in die middel, rondom en buite die opstal moet wees, en verduidelik waarom die beeskraal in die middel is.","en":"Sipho has to draw a homestead for a project. Describe what should be in the centre, around and outside the homestead, and explain why the cattle kraal is in the centre."},"steps":[{"af":"**Middel:** die beeskraal, met graanputte soms daarin.","en":"**Centre:** the cattle kraal, sometimes with storage pits in it."},{"af":"**Rondom:** die hutte in ’n kring, met die belangrikste hut agter, oorkant die ingang, en ’n heining om alles.","en":"**Around it:** the huts in a circle, with the most important hut at the back, opposite the entrance, and a fence around everything."},{"af":"**Buite:** die lande waar die gewasse groei.","en":"**Outside:** the fields where the crops grow."},{"af":"**Waarom:** beeste was die familie se rykdom. In die middel, omring deur hutte, was hulle die veiligste teen diewe en roofdiere.","en":"**Why:** cattle were the family’s wealth. In the centre, surrounded by huts, they were safest from thieves and predators."}],"answer":{"af":"Beeskraal in die middel, hutte in ’n kring daarom, heining om alles en lande buite. Die kraal is in die middel omdat die waardevolle beeste daar die veiligste was.","en":"Cattle kraal in the centre, huts in a circle around it, a fence around everything and fields outside. The kraal is in the centre because the valuable cattle were safest there."}},{"title":{"af":"Wat vertel die Lydenburg-koppe ons?","en":"What do the Lydenburg Heads tell us?"},"problem":{"af":"Fatima sien die Lydenburg-koppe op ’n foto: sewe koppe van gebakte klei, sowat 1 500 jaar oud, versier met lyne en klein stukkies klei. (a) Watter soort bron is dit? (b) Noem twee dinge wat dit ons van die eerste boere vertel. (c) Wat kan dit ons nie met sekerheid vertel nie?","en":"Fatima sees the Lydenburg Heads in a photo: seven heads of fired clay, about 1 500 years old, decorated with lines and small pieces of clay. (a) What kind of source is this? (b) Name two things it tells us about the first farmers. (c) What can it not tell us for certain?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die koppe is deur die boere self gemaak, so dit is ’n **primêre bron** – ’n argeologiese vonds.","en":"(a) The heads were made by the farmers themselves, so they are a **primary source** – an archaeological find."},{"af":"(b) Hulle wys dat die boere **vaardig met klei** gewerk het en **kuns** gemaak het. Omdat twee soos maskers gedra kon word, was hulle waarskynlik vir **seremonies**.","en":"(b) They show that the farmers **worked skilfully with clay** and made **art**. Because two could be worn like masks, they were probably for **ceremonies**."},{"af":"(c) Niemand het neergeskryf hoe die koppe gebruik is nie. Ons kan dus nie seker weet wat die seremonies was of wat die koppe vir die mense beteken het nie.","en":"(c) Nobody wrote down how the heads were used. So we cannot know for sure what the ceremonies were or what the heads meant to the people."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) ’n Primêre bron. (b) Die boere was vaardige pottebakkers en het kuns gemaak, waarskynlik vir seremonies. (c) Presies hoe en waarom hulle gebruik is.","en":"(a) A primary source. (b) The farmers were skilled potters and made art, probably for ceremonies. (c) Exactly how and why they were used."}},{"title":{"af":"Waarom was yster so belangrik?","en":"Why was iron so important?"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik hoe ystergereedskap die lewe van die eerste boere verbeter het. Gee drie voorbeelde.","en":"Explain how iron tools improved the lives of the first farmers. Give three examples."},"steps":[{"af":"Dink aan **boerdery**: ’n ysterskoffel is sterker as ’n houtstok, dus kon hulle meer grond bewerk en meer kos plant.","en":"Think about **farming**: an iron hoe is stronger than a wooden stick, so they could work more soil and grow more food."},{"af":"Dink aan **bou**: ’n ysterbyl kap vinniger bome af vir pale, brandhout en nuwe lande.","en":"Think about **building**: an iron axe cuts down trees faster for poles, firewood and new fields."},{"af":"Dink aan **jag en handel**: spiese en pylpunte van yster is skerp en hou lank, en yster kon vir ander goedere geruil word.","en":"Think about **hunting and trade**: iron spears and arrowheads are sharp and last long, and iron could be traded for other goods."}],"answer":{"af":"Ysterskoffels het gehelp om meer lande te bewerk, ysterbyle het bome vinniger afgekap en ysterspiese het jag en beskerming makliker gemaak. Yster was ook waardevol vir handel.","en":"Iron hoes helped them work more fields, iron axes cut trees faster and iron spears made hunting and protection easier. Iron was also valuable for trade."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter twee dinge is saam in ’n smeltoond gepak om yster te maak?","en":"Which two things were packed together in a furnace to make iron?"},"options":[{"af":"Klei en water","en":"Clay and water"},{"af":"Sout en ivoor","en":"Salt and ivory"},{"af":"Koper en krale","en":"Copper and beads"},{"af":"Ystererts en houtskool","en":"Iron ore and charcoal"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ystererts bevat die yster, en houtskool brand warm genoeg om die yster uit die rots te skei. Klei is gebruik om die oond self te bou.","en":"Iron ore contains the iron, and charcoal burns hot enough to separate the iron from the rock. Clay was used to build the furnace itself."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Met ___ van bokvel is lug in die smeltoond gepomp om die vuur warmer te maak.","en":"___ made of goatskin pumped air into the furnace to make the fire hotter."},"answers":{"af":["blaasbalke","blaasbalk"],"en":["Bellows","bellows"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kleipype","aambeelde","hamers"],"en":["Clay pipes","Anvils","Hammers"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die blaasbalke het die lug gepomp. Die kleipype het die lug net na die vuur gelei, en die aambeeld is later deur die smid gebruik.","en":"The bellows pumped the air. The clay pipes only led the air to the fire, and the anvil was used later by the smith."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom was die beeskraal in die middel van die opstal?","en":"Why was the cattle kraal in the centre of the homestead?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat beeste waardevol was en daar die veiligste was","en":"Because cattle were valuable and safest there"},{"af":"Omdat die beeste die hutte warm moes hou","en":"Because the cattle had to keep the huts warm"},{"af":"Omdat daar nie plek buite die opstal was nie","en":"Because there was no space outside the homestead"},{"af":"Omdat die vroue die beeste moes melk","en":"Because the women had to milk the cattle"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Beeste was die familie se rykdom. Omring deur hutte en ’n heining was hulle die veiligste teen diewe en roofdiere. Die mans het ook by die kraal vergader.","en":"Cattle were the family’s wealth. Surrounded by huts and a fence, they were safest from thieves and predators. The men also met at the kraal."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Lobola beteken dat die bruidegom se familie die bruid koop.","en":"Lobola means that the groom’s family buys the bride."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Lobola is ’n gebruik wat twee families aan mekaar verbind en respek vir die bruid wys. Dit is nie ’n koop nie.","en":"False. Lobola is a custom that joins two families to each other and shows respect for the bride. It is not a purchase."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Met watter ystergereedskap kon die boere die meeste grond vir gewasse bewerk?","en":"Which iron tool helped the farmers work the most land for crops?"},"options":[{"af":"Die spies","en":"The spear"},{"af":"Die skoffel","en":"The hoe"},{"af":"Die mes","en":"The knife"},{"af":"Die pylpunt","en":"The arrowhead"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Met ’n ysterskoffel kon die boere die grond omwerk en skoffel, sodat hulle meer gewasse kon plant. Spiese en pylpunte was vir jag.","en":"With an iron hoe the farmers could turn the soil and weed, so they could grow more crops. Spears and arrowheads were for hunting."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke persoon in die opstal by ’n taak wat hy of sy gehad het.","en":"Match each person in the homestead to a task he or she had."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Smid","en":"Smith"},"r":{"af":"Slaan yster in die vorm van gereedskap","en":"Hammers iron into the shape of tools"}},{"l":{"af":"Vroue","en":"Women"},"r":{"af":"Plant en oes gewasse en maak potte","en":"Plant and harvest crops and make pots"}},{"l":{"af":"Seuns","en":"Boys"},"r":{"af":"Pas die kalwers en bokke op","en":"Look after the calves and goats"}},{"l":{"af":"Hoofman","en":"Chief"},"r":{"af":"Neem besluite saam met die raad","en":"Makes decisions together with the council"}},{"l":{"af":"Meisies","en":"Girls"},"r":{"af":"Pas kleiner kinders op en help hul ma","en":"Look after younger children and help their mother"}}],"explain":{"af":"In die opstal het elkeen ’n taak gehad. Die mans het ook na die beeste omgesien en gejag, en kinders het van klein af geleer deur te help.","en":"In the homestead everyone had a task. The men also looked after the cattle and hunted, and children learnt from a young age by helping."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe help die versierings op ou kleipotte argeoloë?","en":"How do the decorations on old clay pots help archaeologists?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit wys presies hoeveel beeste die familie in die kraal gehad het","en":"They show exactly how many cattle the family had in the kraal"},{"af":"Dit gee die name van die pottebakkers wat die potte gemaak het","en":"They give the names of the potters who made the pots"},{"af":"Elke groep en tydperk het sy eie styl, dus wys dit wie daar gewoon het en wanneer","en":"Each group and period had its own style, so they show who lived there and when"},{"af":"Dit wys watter weer daar was op die dag toe die pot gemaak is","en":"They show what the weather was like on the day the pot was made"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Pottebakkers het patrone gebruik wat by hul groep en tyd gepas het. Deur die style te vergelyk, kan argeoloë sê watter groep op ’n plek gewoon het en ongeveer wanneer. Die potte het geen name op nie.","en":"Potters used patterns that belonged to their group and time. By comparing styles, archaeologists can say which group lived at a place and roughly when. The pots have no names on them."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die afval wat oorbly wanneer yster gesmelt word, heet ___.","en":"The waste that is left when iron is smelted is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["slak","ysterslak"],"en":["slag","iron slag"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["houtskool","erts","as"],"en":["charcoal","ore","ash"]}},"explain":{"af":"Slak is die afval van die rots ná die smelt. Argeoloë wat slak by ’n terrein vind, weet dat mense daar yster gesmelt het.","en":"Slag is the waste from the rock after smelting. Archaeologists who find slag at a site know that people smelted iron there."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat wys die Lydenburg-koppe ons oor die eerste boere?","en":"What do the Lydenburg Heads show us about the first farmers?"},"options":[{"af":"Dat hulle met Europese seevaarders gehandel het","en":"That they traded with European sailors"},{"af":"Dat hulle vaardige kunstenaars was wat waarskynlik seremonies gehou het","en":"That they were skilled artists who probably held ceremonies"},{"af":"Dat hulle nie met klei kon werk nie","en":"That they could not work with clay"},{"af":"Dat hulle jagter-versamelaars sonder vee was","en":"That they were hunter-gatherers without livestock"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die koppe is van gebakte klei gemaak en sowat 1 500 jaar oud. Hulle wys kuns en vaardigheid, en omdat twee soos maskers gedra kon word, is hulle waarskynlik by seremonies gebruik. Europeërs het eers baie later gekom.","en":"The heads are made of fired clay and are about 1 500 years old. They show art and skill, and because two could be worn like masks, they were probably used in ceremonies. Europeans only came much later."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die eerste boere het ook koper gesmelt om armbande en krale te maak.","en":"The first farmers also smelted copper to make bangles and beads."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Behalwe yster vir gereedskap het hulle ook koper gesmelt, veral vir versierings soos armbande en krale. Koper was ook waardevol vir handel.","en":"True. Besides iron for tools, they also smelted copper, especially for ornaments such as bangles and beads. Copper was also valuable for trade."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter goedere het die boere met die San en Khoikhoi geruil?","en":"Which goods did the farmers exchange with the San and Khoikhoi?"},"options":[{"af":"Mielies en koring vir perde en waens","en":"Maize and wheat for horses and wagons"},{"af":"Gewere en buskruit vir ivoor en goud","en":"Guns and gunpowder for ivory and gold"},{"af":"Papier en boeke vir vleis en melk","en":"Paper and books for meat and milk"},{"af":"Yster, potte en graan vir velle, heuning en krale","en":"Iron, pots and grain for skins, honey and beads"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die boere het hul yster, potte en graan geruil vir dinge wat die San en Khoikhoi gehad het, soos velle, heuning en volstruiseierkrale. Mielies, perde en gewere het eers baie later in Suider-Afrika gekom.","en":"The farmers exchanged their iron, pots and grain for things the San and Khoikhoi had, such as skins, honey and ostrich-eggshell beads. Maize, horses and guns only came to southern Africa much later."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In Setswana heet die openbare plek waar mense met die hoofman vergader die ___.","en":"In Setswana the public place where people meet with the chief is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["kgotla"],"en":["kgotla"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kraal","opstal","smeltoond"],"en":["kraal","homestead","furnace"]}},"explain":{"af":"By die kgotla het die hoofman en sy raad sake bespreek en twiste besleg. Die kraal is waar die beeste gehou is.","en":"At the kgotla the chief and his council discussed matters and settled disputes. The kraal is where the cattle were kept."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom het isiXhosa en isiZulu klikklanke?","en":"Why do isiXhosa and isiZulu have click sounds?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat die boere en die Khoe-San met mekaar gemeng en getrou het","en":"Because the farmers and the Khoe-San mixed and married each other"},{"af":"Omdat Europeërs dit vir hulle geleer het","en":"Because Europeans taught them"},{"af":"Omdat alle Bantoetale klikklanke het","en":"Because all Bantu languages have clicks"},{"af":"Omdat die smede dit gebruik het om met mekaar te praat","en":"Because the smiths used them to talk to each other"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die klikklanke kom uit die Khoe-San-tale. Deur handel, saamwoon en trou het isiXhosa en isiZulu hulle oorgeneem. Die meeste Bantoetale het nie klikklanke nie.","en":"The click sounds come from the Khoe-San languages. Through trade, living together and marriage, isiXhosa and isiZulu took them over. Most Bantu languages do not have clicks."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom moes die boere houtskool en blaasbalke gebruik om yster te smelt?","en":"Why did the farmers have to use charcoal and bellows to smelt iron?"},"options":[{"af":"Om die gesmelte yster vinnig af te koel en hard te maak","en":"To cool the melted iron quickly and make it hard"},{"af":"Om die erts nat en koel te hou sodat dit nie breek nie","en":"To keep the ore wet and cool so that it does not break"},{"af":"Om die vuur warm genoeg te maak om yster uit die rots te skei","en":"To make the fire hot enough to separate iron from the rock"},{"af":"Om rook te maak wat roofdiere van die oond af weghou","en":"To make smoke that keeps predators away from the furnace"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Yster skei net by ’n baie hoë temperatuur van die rots. Houtskool brand warmer as hout, en die lug van die blaasbalke maak die vuur nog warmer.","en":"Iron only separates from the rock at a very high temperature. Charcoal burns hotter than wood, and the air from the bellows makes the fire even hotter."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"’n Antieke Afrika-samelewing: Egipte","en":"An ancient African society: Egypt"},"topics":[{"id":"sw5-t3-gesk-egipte-nyl","title":{"af":"Die Nyl en die lewe in antieke Egipte","en":"The Nile and life in ancient Egypt"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik waarom die Nyl die lewensaar van antieke Egipte was, hoe boere besproeiing gebruik het en hoe die samelewing soos ’n piramide georganiseer was.","en":"You will be able to explain why the Nile was the lifeline of ancient Egypt, how farmers used irrigation and how society was organised like a pyramid."},"summary":{"af":"## Egipte en die Nyl\n\n**Egipte** lê in die noordooste van Afrika. Byna die hele land is **woestyn** – deel van die Sahara. Tog het een van die eerste groot **beskawings** ter wêreld ongeveer **5 000 jaar gelede** hier ontstaan, en dit het byna 3 000 jaar lank bestaan. Die rede is die **Nylrivier**.\n\nDie Nyl is die **langste rivier in Afrika**. Dit vloei van suid na **noord** en mond in die **Middellandse See** uit, waar dit ’n groot **delta** vorm. Die Nyl word die **lewensaar** van Egipte genoem: sonder sy water sou daar net woestyn wees. Die Griekse skrywer Herodotus het Egipte ‘die geskenk van die Nyl’ genoem. Byna alle Egiptenare het op die smal strook vrugbare grond langs die rivier en in die delta gewoon.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** **Bo-Egipte** is in die **suide** en **Benede-Egipte** in die **noorde**. Die name volg die rivier: die Nyl vloei van die hoër suide (bo) na die laer noorde (onder) – nie volgens die kaart nie.\n\n## Die oorstroming en swart slik\n\nElke somer het swaar reën in die hooglande van Ethiopië die Nyl laat **oorstroom**. Die water het oor die lande versprei en ’n laag **swart slik** (vrugbare modder) agtergelaat. Die Egiptenare het hul land *Kemet* genoem – ‘die swart land’ – na hierdie donker grond.\n\n| Seisoen | Wat het gebeur? |\n|---|---|\n| **Oorstroming** | Die lande was onder water. Baie boere het aan die farao se bouprojekte gewerk. |\n| **Groei** | Die water het teruggetrek. Boere het geploeg en gesaai. |\n| **Oes** | Boere het die gewasse ingesamel voordat die volgende vloed gekom het. |\n\n’n Baie hoë vloed kon dorpe wegspoel, en ’n baie lae vloed het swak oeste en **hongersnood** gebring.\n\n## Boerdery en besproeiing\n\n- **Koring** en **gars** – vir brood en bier.\n- **Vlas** – om **linne** vir klere te maak.\n- Uie, lensies, dadels en druiwe.\n- **Papirus** – ’n riet langs die rivier – vir papier, mandjies, bootjies en sandale.\n\nOm water na die lande te kry, het hulle **kanale** gegrawe en die **shadoef** gebruik: ’n lang paal op ’n staander, met ’n emmer aan die een kant en ’n swaar **teengewig** aan die ander kant. Die teengewig help die boer om die swaar emmer water maklik op te lig en in ’n kanaal te gooi. Om water só na die lande te lei, heet **besproeiing**.\n\n> **Onthou:** Die Nyl het Egipte drie dinge gegee: **water**, **vrugbare slik** en ’n **pad** vir bote.\n\n## ’n Samelewing soos ’n piramide\n\nDie samelewing kan as ’n **piramide** geteken word: min mense met baie mag bo, baie mense met min mag onder.\n\n1. **Farao** – die koning. Mense het geglo hy is ’n god op aarde.\n2. **Priesters en amptenare** – het die tempels en die land bestuur en belasting ingevorder.\n3. **Skrywers** – kon lees en skryf en het rekords gehou.\n4. **Ambagsmanne** – bouers, beeldhouers, pottebakkers en juweliers.\n5. **Boere** – die grootste groep; hulle het die kos vir almal verbou.\n6. **Slawe** – meestal krygsgevangenes.\n\n## Daaglikse lewe\n\n- **Huise** is van songedroogde **modderstene** gebou, met plat dakke waarop mense in die hitte geslaap het.\n- **Kos:** brood, groente, vis en dik bier. Ryk mense het meer vleis geëet.\n- **Klere:** ligte wit **linne** teen die hitte. Mans én vroue het swart oogverf gedra.\n- **Kinders** het met poppe, balle en bordspeletjies gespeel. Seuns het gewoonlik hul pa se werk geleer.\n- **Vervoer:** bote op die Nyl. Die stroom dra bote noordwaarts, en omdat die wind meestal uit die noorde waai, kon bote met ’n seil suidwaarts vaar.\n\n## Godsdiens\n\nDie Egiptenare het in **baie gode** geglo, byvoorbeeld **Ra** (die son), **Osiris** (die lewe na die dood), **Isis** (beskerming en towerkrag), **Anubis** (met ’n jakkalskop; die god van mummies en grafte) en **Hapi** (die Nyl se oorstroming). Tempels was die huise van die gode, en priesters het daar elke dag vir die gode gesorg.","en":"## Egypt and the Nile\n\n**Egypt** lies in the north-east of Africa. Almost the whole country is **desert** – part of the Sahara. Yet one of the first great **civilisations** in the world began here about **5 000 years ago**, and it lasted for almost 3 000 years. The reason is the **Nile River**.\n\nThe Nile is the **longest river in Africa**. It flows from south to **north** and enters the **Mediterranean Sea**, where it forms a large **delta**. The Nile is called the **lifeline** of Egypt: without its water there would only be desert. The Greek writer Herodotus called Egypt ‘the gift of the Nile’. Almost all Egyptians lived on the narrow strip of fertile land along the river and in the delta.\n\n> **Common mistake:** **Upper Egypt** is in the **south** and **Lower Egypt** is in the **north**. The names follow the river: the Nile flows from the higher south (up) to the lower north (down) – not according to the map.\n\n## The flood and black silt\n\nEvery summer heavy rain in the highlands of Ethiopia made the Nile **flood**. The water spread over the fields and left a layer of **black silt** (fertile mud). The Egyptians called their country *Kemet* – ‘the black land’ – after this dark soil.\n\n| Season | What happened? |\n|---|---|\n| **Flood** | The fields were under water. Many farmers worked on the pharaoh’s building projects. |\n| **Growing** | The water went back. Farmers ploughed and sowed. |\n| **Harvest** | Farmers gathered the crops before the next flood came. |\n\nA very high flood could wash villages away, and a very low flood brought poor harvests and **famine**.\n\n## Farming and irrigation\n\n- **Wheat** and **barley** – for bread and beer.\n- **Flax** – to make **linen** for clothes.\n- Onions, lentils, dates and grapes.\n- **Papyrus** – a reed along the river – for paper, baskets, small boats and sandals.\n\nTo get water to the fields, they dug **canals** and used the **shadoof**: a long pole on a stand, with a bucket on one end and a heavy **counterweight** on the other. The counterweight helps the farmer to lift the heavy bucket of water easily and empty it into a canal. Leading water to the fields like this is called **irrigation**.\n\n> **Remember:** The Nile gave Egypt three things: **water**, **fertile silt** and a **road** for boats.\n\n## A society like a pyramid\n\nThe society can be drawn as a **pyramid**: a few people with a lot of power at the top, many people with little power at the bottom.\n\n1. **Pharaoh** – the king. People believed he was a god on earth.\n2. **Priests and officials** – ran the temples and the country and collected taxes.\n3. **Scribes** – could read and write and kept records.\n4. **Craftsmen** – builders, sculptors, potters and jewellers.\n5. **Farmers** – the biggest group; they grew the food for everyone.\n6. **Slaves** – mostly prisoners of war.\n\n## Daily life\n\n- **Houses** were built of sun-dried **mud bricks**, with flat roofs on which people slept in the heat.\n- **Food:** bread, vegetables, fish and thick beer. Rich people ate more meat.\n- **Clothes:** light white **linen** against the heat. Men and women both wore black eye make-up.\n- **Children** played with dolls, balls and board games. Boys usually learnt their father’s work.\n- **Transport:** boats on the Nile. The current carries boats north, and because the wind mostly blows from the north, boats could sail south with a sail.\n\n## Religion\n\nThe Egyptians believed in **many gods**, for example **Ra** (the sun), **Osiris** (life after death), **Isis** (protection and magic), **Anubis** (with a jackal’s head; the god of mummies and tombs) and **Hapi** (the Nile flood). Temples were the homes of the gods, and priests cared for the gods there every day."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Beskawing","en":"Civilisation"},"def":{"af":"’n Groot, georganiseerde samelewing met dorpe, leiers, wette, skrif en kuns.","en":"A large, organised society with towns, leaders, laws, writing and art."}},{"term":{"af":"Delta","en":"Delta"},"def":{"af":"’n Driehoekige gebied van vrugbare grond waar ’n rivier in baie strome verdeel voordat dit in die see uitmond.","en":"A triangle-shaped area of fertile land where a river splits into many streams before it flows into the sea."}},{"term":{"af":"Oorstroming","en":"Flood"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n rivier oor sy walle loop en die land rondom bedek.","en":"When a river flows over its banks and covers the land around it."}},{"term":{"af":"Slik","en":"Silt"},"def":{"af":"Fyn, vrugbare modder wat ’n rivier agterlaat wanneer die vloedwater terugtrek.","en":"Fine, fertile mud that a river leaves behind when the floodwater goes back."}},{"term":{"af":"Besproeiing","en":"Irrigation"},"def":{"af":"Om water deur kanale of ander middele na lande te lei sodat gewasse kan groei.","en":"Leading water to fields through canals or other means so that crops can grow."}},{"term":{"af":"Shadoef","en":"Shadoof"},"def":{"af":"’n Paal met ’n emmer aan die een kant en ’n teengewig aan die ander kant, waarmee water uit die rivier gelig word.","en":"A pole with a bucket on one end and a counterweight on the other, used to lift water from the river."}},{"term":{"af":"Farao","en":"Pharaoh"},"def":{"af":"Die koning van antieke Egipte, wat mense as ’n god op aarde beskou het.","en":"The king of ancient Egypt, whom people saw as a god on earth."}},{"term":{"af":"Skrywer","en":"Scribe"},"def":{"af":"Iemand in antieke Egipte wat kon lees en skryf en rekords vir die farao en die tempels gehou het.","en":"Someone in ancient Egypt who could read and write and kept records for the pharaoh and the temples."}},{"term":{"af":"Papirus","en":"Papyrus"},"def":{"af":"’n Riet wat langs die Nyl groei en waarvan die Egiptenare papier, mandjies en sandale gemaak het.","en":"A reed that grows along the Nile and from which the Egyptians made paper, baskets and sandals."}},{"term":{"af":"Vlas","en":"Flax"},"def":{"af":"’n Plant waarvan die vesels gebruik is om linne vir klere te maak.","en":"A plant whose fibres were used to make linen for clothes."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Die geskenk van die Nyl","en":"The gift of the Nile"},"problem":{"af":"Herodotus het gesê Egipte is ‘die geskenk van die Nyl’. Verduidelik wat hy bedoel het.","en":"Herodotus said Egypt is ‘the gift of the Nile’. Explain what he meant."},"steps":[{"af":"Dink aan die landskap: Egipte is byna heeltemal woestyn met baie min reën.","en":"Think about the landscape: Egypt is almost completely desert with very little rain."},{"af":"Dink aan wat die rivier gee: **water** vir mense, diere en lande, en elke jaar nuwe **swart slik** wat die grond vrugbaar maak.","en":"Think about what the river gives: **water** for people, animals and fields, and new **black silt** every year that makes the soil fertile."},{"af":"Dink aan vervoer: die Nyl was ’n **pad** waarlangs bote mense en goedere vervoer het.","en":"Think about transport: the Nile was a **road** along which boats carried people and goods."}],"answer":{"af":"Sonder die Nyl sou Egipte net woestyn wees. Die rivier het water, vrugbare slik en vervoer gegee, sodat mense kon boer en ’n groot beskawing kon bou.","en":"Without the Nile Egypt would be only desert. The river gave water, fertile silt and transport, so that people could farm and build a great civilisation."}},{"title":{"af":"Hoe werk ’n shadoef?","en":"How does a shadoof work?"},"problem":{"af":"Nomsa moet in die eksamen verduidelik hoe ’n shadoef werk en waarom dit die boer se werk makliker maak.","en":"In the exam Nomsa has to explain how a shadoof works and why it makes the farmer’s work easier."},"steps":[{"af":"Noem die dele: ’n lang paal wat op ’n staander balanseer, ’n **emmer** aan die een kant en ’n swaar **teengewig** aan die ander kant.","en":"Name the parts: a long pole that balances on a stand, a **bucket** on one end and a heavy **counterweight** on the other end."},{"af":"Beskryf die beweging: die boer trek die emmer af in die rivier sodat dit volloop.","en":"Describe the movement: the farmer pulls the bucket down into the river so that it fills up."},{"af":"Die teengewig help om die vol emmer op te lig. Die boer swaai die paal om en gooi die water in ’n kanaal wat na die lande loop.","en":"The counterweight helps to lift the full bucket. The farmer swings the pole round and empties the water into a canal that runs to the fields."}],"answer":{"af":"Die teengewig doen die meeste van die swaar werk, sodat die boer maklik baie emmers water uit die rivier in die kanale kan lig om sy lande te besproei.","en":"The counterweight does most of the heavy work, so the farmer can easily lift many buckets of water from the river into the canals to irrigate his fields."}},{"title":{"af":"Lees die sosiale piramide","en":"Read the social pyramid"},"problem":{"af":"Kyk na die Egiptiese sosiale piramide. (a) Wie was bo en wie was onder? (b) Watter groep was die grootste, en waarom was hulle belangrik? (c) Waarom was skrywers hoog op die piramide?","en":"Look at the Egyptian social pyramid. (a) Who was at the top and who was at the bottom? (b) Which group was the biggest, and why were they important? (c) Why were scribes high up on the pyramid?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Bo is die **farao** – een persoon met die meeste mag. Onder is die **slawe**.","en":"(a) At the top is the **pharaoh** – one person with the most power. At the bottom are the **slaves**."},{"af":"(b) Die breë deel naby die onderkant is die **boere**. Hulle het die kos vir die hele land verbou.","en":"(b) The wide part near the bottom is the **farmers**. They grew the food for the whole country."},{"af":"(c) Min mense kon lees en skryf. **Skrywers** het belasting, oeste en wette aangeteken, so die farao en die amptenare het hulle nodig gehad.","en":"(c) Few people could read and write. **Scribes** recorded taxes, harvests and laws, so the pharaoh and the officials needed them."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Die farao bo, slawe onder. (b) Die boere; hulle het die kos vir almal verbou. (c) Hulle kon lees en skryf, wat min mense kon, en het belangrike rekords gehou.","en":"(a) The pharaoh at the top, slaves at the bottom. (b) The farmers; they grew the food for everyone. (c) They could read and write, which few people could, and kept important records."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter rigting vloei die Nyl?","en":"In which direction does the Nile flow?"},"options":[{"af":"Van noord na suid","en":"From north to south"},{"af":"Van wes na oos","en":"From west to east"},{"af":"Van suid na noord","en":"From south to north"},{"af":"Van oos na wes","en":"From east to west"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die Nyl vloei van die hooglande in die suide na die Middellandse See in die noorde. Daarom is Bo-Egipte in die suide.","en":"The Nile flows from the highlands in the south to the Mediterranean Sea in the north. That is why Upper Egypt is in the south."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die oorstromings het ’n laag vrugbare swart ___ op die lande agtergelaat.","en":"The floods left a layer of fertile black ___ on the fields."},"answers":{"af":["slik","modder"],"en":["silt","mud"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["sand","klip","sout"],"en":["sand","rock","salt"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die slik is fyn, vrugbare modder wat die vloedwater uit die hooglande saambring. Sand kom uit die woestyn en is nie vrugbaar nie.","en":"The silt is fine, fertile mud that the floodwater brings from the highlands. Sand comes from the desert and is not fertile."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarvoor het Egiptiese boere die shadoef gebruik?","en":"What did Egyptian farmers use the shadoof for?"},"options":[{"af":"Om die grond te ploeg","en":"To plough the soil"},{"af":"Om water uit die rivier in kanale te lig","en":"To lift water from the river into canals"},{"af":"Om graan fyn te maal","en":"To grind grain into flour"},{"af":"Om klipblokke te vervoer","en":"To move stone blocks"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die shadoef is ’n paal met ’n emmer en ’n teengewig. Dit lig water uit die rivier sodat dit deur kanale na die lande kan loop – dit is besproeiing.","en":"The shadoof is a pole with a bucket and a counterweight. It lifts water from the river so that it can flow through canals to the fields – this is irrigation."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Bo-Egipte lê in die noorde van Egipte, naby die Middellandse See.","en":"Upper Egypt is in the north of Egypt, near the Mediterranean Sea."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Bo-Egipte is in die suide, stroomop. Benede-Egipte is in die noorde by die delta. Die name volg die rivier, nie die kaart nie.","en":"False. Upper Egypt is in the south, upstream. Lower Egypt is in the north at the delta. The names follow the river, not the map."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wie was heel bo in die Egiptiese sosiale piramide?","en":"Who was at the very top of the Egyptian social pyramid?"},"options":[{"af":"Die priesters","en":"The priests"},{"af":"Die skrywers","en":"The scribes"},{"af":"Die boere","en":"The farmers"},{"af":"Die farao","en":"The pharaoh"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die farao was die koning en mense het geglo hy is ’n god op aarde. Priesters en amptenare was net onder hom.","en":"The pharaoh was the king and people believed he was a god on earth. Priests and officials were just below him."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter groep was die grootste in antieke Egipte?","en":"Which group was the biggest in ancient Egypt?"},"options":[{"af":"Die boere","en":"The farmers"},{"af":"Die priesters","en":"The priests"},{"af":"Die skrywers","en":"The scribes"},{"af":"Die amptenare","en":"The officials"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die boere was die breë onderste deel van die piramide. Hulle het die kos vir die hele land verbou. Daar was baie minder priesters, skrywers en amptenare.","en":"The farmers were the wide lower part of the pyramid. They grew the food for the whole country. There were far fewer priests, scribes and officials."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke Egiptiese god by waarmee hy of sy verbind was.","en":"Match each Egyptian god to what he or she was linked with."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Ra","en":"Ra"},"r":{"af":"Die son","en":"The sun"}},{"l":{"af":"Osiris","en":"Osiris"},"r":{"af":"Die lewe na die dood","en":"Life after death"}},{"l":{"af":"Anubis","en":"Anubis"},"r":{"af":"Mummies en grafte","en":"Mummies and tombs"}},{"l":{"af":"Hapi","en":"Hapi"},"r":{"af":"Die Nyl se oorstroming","en":"The Nile flood"}},{"l":{"af":"Isis","en":"Isis"},"r":{"af":"Beskerming en towerkrag","en":"Protection and magic"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die Egiptenare het in baie gode geglo. Elke god het ’n deel van die natuur of die lewe beheer, soos die son, die vloed of die lewe na die dood.","en":"The Egyptians believed in many gods. Each god controlled a part of nature or life, such as the sun, the flood or life after death."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Van vlas het die Egiptenare ___ gemaak vir hul ligte klere.","en":"From flax the Egyptians made ___ for their light clothes."},"answers":{"af":["linne"],"en":["linen"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["wol","leer","papirus"],"en":["wool","leather","papyrus"]}},"explain":{"af":"Vlas se vesels is tot linne geweef. Linne is lig en koel, goed vir die warm klimaat. Papirus is vir papier, mandjies en sandale gebruik.","en":"The fibres of flax were woven into linen. Linen is light and cool, good for the hot climate. Papyrus was used for paper, baskets and sandals."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom het byna alle Egiptenare naby die Nyl gewoon?","en":"Why did almost all Egyptians live near the Nile?"},"options":[{"af":"Net langs die rivier was daar water en vrugbare grond; die res was woestyn","en":"Only along the river was there water and fertile soil; the rest was desert"},{"af":"Die farao het verbied dat mense ver van die rivier af woon","en":"The pharaoh forbade people to live far from the river"},{"af":"Die rivier het hulle teen vyande uit die see beskerm","en":"The river protected them from enemies from the sea"},{"af":"Hulle wou naby die piramides en tempels woon om die gode te dien","en":"They wanted to live near the pyramids and temples to serve the gods"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"In die woestyn reën dit amper nooit. Net langs die Nyl en in die delta was daar water en vrugbare slik om te boer.","en":"In the desert it almost never rains. Only along the Nile and in the delta was there water and fertile silt to farm."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die Nyl is die langste rivier in Afrika.","en":"The Nile is the longest river in Africa."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die Nyl is die langste rivier in Afrika. Dit vloei deur verskeie lande voordat dit in Egipte die Middellandse See bereik.","en":"True. The Nile is the longest river in Africa. It flows through several countries before it reaches the Mediterranean Sea in Egypt."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe kon Egiptiese bote stroomop na die suide vaar?","en":"How could Egyptian boats travel upstream to the south?"},"options":[{"af":"Die stroom het hulle suidwaarts gedra","en":"The current carried them south"},{"af":"Diere het hulle met toue langs die oewer getrek","en":"Animals pulled them with ropes along the bank"},{"af":"Hulle het op die vloedwater oor die woestyn gevaar","en":"They sailed on the floodwater across the desert"},{"af":"Die wind waai meestal uit die noorde, dus kon hulle met ’n seil suid vaar","en":"The wind mostly blows from the north, so they could sail south with a sail"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die stroom vloei noordwaarts, so bote dryf maklik noord. Om suid te gaan, het hulle die seil opgesit, want die wind waai meestal uit die noorde.","en":"The current flows north, so boats drift north easily. To go south they put up the sail, because the wind mostly blows from the north."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die Egiptenare het hul land *Kemet* genoem, wat ‘die ___ land’ beteken.","en":"The Egyptians called their country *Kemet*, which means ‘the ___ land’."},"answers":{"af":["swart"],"en":["black"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["rooi","groen","goue"],"en":["red","green","golden"]}},"explain":{"af":"Kemet beteken ‘die swart land’, na die donker, vrugbare slik langs die Nyl. Die woestyn was vir hulle ‘die rooi land’.","en":"Kemet means ‘the black land’, after the dark, fertile silt along the Nile. To them the desert was ‘the red land’."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat het gebeur in ’n jaar wanneer die Nyl baie min oorstroom het?","en":"What happened in a year when the Nile flooded very little?"},"options":[{"af":"Dorpe is weggespoel","en":"Villages were washed away"},{"af":"Die oeste was swak en daar was hongersnood","en":"The harvests were poor and there was famine"},{"af":"Die boere het meer koring as ooit geoes","en":"The farmers harvested more wheat than ever"},{"af":"Die woestyn het groen geword","en":"The desert turned green"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Min water beteken min slik en droë lande, dus het gewasse swak gegroei en mense honger gely. ’n Te hoë vloed kon weer dorpe wegspoel.","en":"Little water meant little silt and dry fields, so crops grew poorly and people went hungry. A flood that was too high could wash villages away instead."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom was skrywers so belangrik in antieke Egipte?","en":"Why were scribes so important in ancient Egypt?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle het die piramides alleen en sonder hulp gebou","en":"They built the pyramids on their own without help"},{"af":"Hulle was die farao se soldate wat Egipte beskerm het","en":"They were the pharaoh’s soldiers who protected Egypt"},{"af":"Hulle kon lees en skryf en het rekords van belasting en oeste gehou","en":"They could read and write and kept records of taxes and harvests"},{"af":"Hulle het al die kos vir die hele land verbou","en":"They grew all the food for the whole country"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Min mense kon lees en skryf. Skrywers het belasting, oeste en wette aangeteken, sodat die farao en die amptenare die land kon bestuur. Die boere het die kos verbou.","en":"Few people could read and write. Scribes recorded taxes, harvests and laws, so that the pharaoh and the officials could run the country. The farmers grew the food."}}]},{"id":"sw5-t3-gesk-egipte-prestasies","title":{"af":"Piramides, mummies en hiërogliewe","en":"Pyramids, mummies and hieroglyphs"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik waarom die Egiptenare piramides gebou en hul dooies gemummifiseer het, hoe hiërogliewe ontsyfer is en waarom Egipte ’n belangrike Afrika-beskawing is.","en":"You will be able to explain why the Egyptians built pyramids and mummified their dead, how hieroglyphs were deciphered and why Egypt is an important African civilisation."},"summary":{"af":"## Piramides: grafte vir farao’s\n\nDie Egiptenare het in ’n **lewe na die dood** geglo. ’n Farao moes ’n veilige, indrukwekkende **graf** hê, daarom het hulle **piramides** gebou.\n\n- Die eerste piramide was die **trappiramide** van farao Djoser, met groot ‘trappe’ aan die kante.\n- Die **Groot Piramide van Giza** is sowat **4 500 jaar gelede** vir farao **Khufu** gebou. Dit bestaan uit meer as 2 miljoen klipblokke en was duisende jare lank die hoogste gebou op aarde. Dit is die enigste van die **Sewe Wonders van die Antieke Wêreld** wat nog staan.\n- Naby die piramides by Giza lê die **Sfinks**: ’n reuse-beeld met ’n leeu se lyf en ’n mens se kop.\n\nDuisende **werkers** het die piramides gebou – baie van hulle boere wat gewerk het terwyl hul lande onder water was. Hulle het met **koperwerktuie**, houtslee en **opritte** gewerk, en klipblokke is per boot op die Nyl vervoer. Hulle is met kos betaal en het in werkersdorpe naby die piramides gewoon.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Baie mense dink slawe het die piramides gebou. Argeoloë het egter die werkers se huise en grafte gevind, en dit wys dat dit meestal **betaalde werkers** was.\n\nLater is farao’s in grafte in die rotse van die **Vallei van die Konings** begrawe, want **grafrowers** het die piramides beroof.\n\n## Mummies\n\nDie Egiptenare het geglo die **liggaam** moet bewaar word sodat die siel dit ná die dood kan herken. Daarom is die dooies **gemummifiseer**. Dit het sowat **70 dae** geduur:\n\n1. Die **brein** is deur die neus uitgehaal.\n2. Die **organe** (longe, lewer, maag en derms) is in **kanopiese kruike** gesit. Die **hart** is in die liggaam gelos, want hulle het geglo dit is die plek van denke en gevoelens.\n3. Die liggaam is met **natron** (’n soort sout) bedek om dit uit te droog.\n4. Dit is met olies ingevryf en in **linnestroke** toegedraai, met **amulette** tussen die lae.\n5. Die mummie is in ’n **sarkofaag** (klipkis) gesit, saam met kos, meubels en skatte vir die lewe na die dood.\n\nRyk mense en selfs diere soos katte is ook gemummifiseer.\n\n## Toetankamen\n\n**Toetankamen** het sowat **3 300 jaar gelede** as ’n jong seun farao geword en is as ’n jong man oorlede. In **1922** het die Britse argeoloog **Howard Carter** sy graf in die Vallei van die Konings ontdek. Dit was amper **onaangeraak** deur grafrowers en vol skatte, soos sy **goue doodsmasker**. Die graf wys ons hoe ’n farao vir die lewe na die dood voorberei is.\n\n## Hiërogliewe\n\nDie Egiptenare het een van die eerste **skrifstelsels** ontwikkel: **hiërogliewe** – honderde prenttekens. Sommige tekens staan vir **klanke**, ander vir hele **woorde** of idees. Hiërogliewe is op tempel- en grafmure ingekap en op **papirus** geskryf. ’n Farao se naam is in ’n ovaal raam geskryf, ’n *cartouche*.\n\n### Die Rosetta-steen\n\nMettertyd het mense vergeet hoe om hiërogliewe te lees. In **1799** het Franse soldate die **Rosetta-steen** in die Nyldelta gevind. Dieselfde teks staan drie keer daarop: in **hiërogliewe**, in ’n ander Egiptiese skrif en in **antieke Grieks**. Geleerdes kon Grieks lees, en kon dus die tekste vergelyk. In **1822** het die Fransman **Jean-François Champollion** die hiërogliewe **ontsyfer**.\n\n## Ander prestasies\n\n| Prestasie | Waarom belangrik? |\n|---|---|\n| **Kalender van 365 dae** | 12 maande van 30 dae plus 5 ekstra dae; het boere gehelp om vir die vloed te beplan |\n| **Medisyne** | Dokters het gebreekte bene gespalk en heuning op wonde gesit |\n| **Wiskunde** | Om lande ná die vloed weer af te meet en groot geboue te beplan |\n| **Bouwerk** | Piramides, tempels en standbeelde wat duisende jare hou |\n\n> **Onthou:** Piramides, mummies en grafskatte hang almal saam met die geloof in ’n **lewe na die dood**.\n\n## Waarom is Egipte belangrik?\n\nAntieke Egipte is een van die oudste en belangrikste beskawings ter wêreld – en dit is ’n **Afrika**-beskawing. Dit het ander volke, soos die Grieke, beïnvloed. Egipte het ook noue bande gehad met **Nubië** (Kush) in die suide, ’n ander Afrika-koninkryk waarvan die konings ’n tyd lank ook farao’s van Egipte was.","en":"## Pyramids: tombs for pharaohs\n\nThe Egyptians believed in a **life after death**. A pharaoh had to have a safe, impressive **tomb**, so they built **pyramids**.\n\n- The first pyramid was the **step pyramid** of pharaoh Djoser, with big ‘steps’ on the sides.\n- The **Great Pyramid of Giza** was built about **4 500 years ago** for pharaoh **Khufu**. It is made of more than 2 million stone blocks and for thousands of years it was the tallest building on Earth. It is the only one of the **Seven Wonders of the Ancient World** still standing.\n- Near the pyramids at Giza lies the **Sphinx**: a giant statue with a lion’s body and a human head.\n\nThousands of **workers** built the pyramids – many of them farmers who worked while their fields were under water. They worked with **copper tools**, wooden sledges and **ramps**, and stone blocks were carried by boat on the Nile. They were paid with food and lived in workers’ villages near the pyramids.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Many people think slaves built the pyramids. But archaeologists have found the workers’ houses and graves, and these show that they were mostly **paid workers**.\n\nLater pharaohs were buried in tombs cut into the rocks of the **Valley of the Kings**, because **tomb robbers** had robbed the pyramids.\n\n## Mummies\n\nThe Egyptians believed the **body** had to be preserved so that the soul could recognise it after death. That is why the dead were **mummified**. It took about **70 days**:\n\n1. The **brain** was taken out through the nose.\n2. The **organs** (lungs, liver, stomach and intestines) were put into **canopic jars**. The **heart** was left in the body, because they believed it was the place of thoughts and feelings.\n3. The body was covered with **natron** (a kind of salt) to dry it out.\n4. It was rubbed with oils and wrapped in **linen strips**, with **amulets** (lucky charms) between the layers.\n5. The mummy was placed in a **sarcophagus** (stone coffin), together with food, furniture and treasures for the life after death.\n\nRich people and even animals such as cats were also mummified.\n\n## Tutankhamun\n\n**Tutankhamun** became pharaoh as a young boy about **3 300 years ago** and died as a young man. In **1922** the British archaeologist **Howard Carter** discovered his tomb in the Valley of the Kings. It had hardly been **touched** by tomb robbers and was full of treasures, such as his **golden death mask**. The tomb shows us how a pharaoh was prepared for the life after death.\n\n## Hieroglyphs\n\nThe Egyptians developed one of the first **writing systems**: **hieroglyphs** – hundreds of picture signs. Some signs stand for **sounds**, others for whole **words** or ideas. Hieroglyphs were carved on temple and tomb walls and written on **papyrus**. A pharaoh’s name was written inside an oval frame, a *cartouche*.\n\n### The Rosetta Stone\n\nOver time people forgot how to read hieroglyphs. In **1799** French soldiers found the **Rosetta Stone** in the Nile Delta. The same text appears on it three times: in **hieroglyphs**, in another Egyptian script and in **ancient Greek**. Scholars could read Greek, so they could compare the texts. In **1822** the Frenchman **Jean-François Champollion** **deciphered** the hieroglyphs.\n\n## Other achievements\n\n| Achievement | Why important? |\n|---|---|\n| **Calendar of 365 days** | 12 months of 30 days plus 5 extra days; helped farmers to plan for the flood |\n| **Medicine** | Doctors set broken bones in splints and put honey on wounds |\n| **Mathematics** | To measure fields again after the flood and to plan big buildings |\n| **Building** | Pyramids, temples and statues that last thousands of years |\n\n> **Remember:** Pyramids, mummies and tomb treasures are all linked to the belief in a **life after death**.\n\n## Why is Egypt important?\n\nAncient Egypt is one of the oldest and most important civilisations in the world – and it is an **African** civilisation. It influenced other peoples, such as the Greeks. Egypt also had close ties with **Nubia** (Kush) to the south, another African kingdom whose kings were, for a time, also pharaohs of Egypt."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Piramide","en":"Pyramid"},"def":{"af":"’n Groot klipgebou met ’n vierkantige onderkant en driehoekige kante wat as graf vir ’n farao gebou is.","en":"A large stone building with a square base and triangular sides that was built as a tomb for a pharaoh."}},{"term":{"af":"Lewe na die dood","en":"Life after death"},"def":{"af":"Die geloof dat ’n mens se siel ná die dood in ’n ander wêreld verder lewe.","en":"The belief that a person’s soul lives on in another world after death."}},{"term":{"af":"Mummifisering","en":"Mummification"},"def":{"af":"Die proses om ’n dooie liggaam uit te droog en toe te draai sodat dit nie vergaan nie.","en":"The process of drying out and wrapping a dead body so that it does not decay."}},{"term":{"af":"Natron","en":"Natron"},"def":{"af":"’n Soort sout wat gebruik is om liggame tydens mummifisering uit te droog.","en":"A kind of salt that was used to dry out bodies during mummification."}},{"term":{"af":"Kanopiese kruike","en":"Canopic jars"},"def":{"af":"Kruike waarin die organe van ’n gemummifiseerde mens bewaar is.","en":"Jars in which the organs of a mummified person were kept."}},{"term":{"af":"Sarkofaag","en":"Sarcophagus"},"def":{"af":"’n Groot kis, dikwels van klip, waarin ’n mummie geplaas is.","en":"A large coffin, often made of stone, in which a mummy was placed."}},{"term":{"af":"Hiërogliewe","en":"Hieroglyphs"},"def":{"af":"Die antieke Egiptiese skrif van prenttekens wat vir klanke, woorde of idees staan.","en":"The ancient Egyptian writing made of picture signs that stand for sounds, words or ideas."}},{"term":{"af":"Rosetta-steen","en":"Rosetta Stone"},"def":{"af":"’n Klip met dieselfde teks in hiërogliewe, ’n ander Egiptiese skrif en Grieks, wat gehelp het om hiërogliewe te ontsyfer.","en":"A stone with the same text in hieroglyphs, another Egyptian script and Greek, which helped to decipher hieroglyphs."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontsyfer","en":"Decipher"},"def":{"af":"Om uit te werk wat ’n onbekende skrif of kode beteken.","en":"To work out what an unknown script or code means."}},{"term":{"af":"Grafrower","en":"Tomb robber"},"def":{"af":"Iemand wat by ’n graf inbreek om die skatte daarin te steel.","en":"Someone who breaks into a tomb to steal the treasures inside it."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Beskryf mummifisering","en":"Describe mummification"},"problem":{"af":"Beskryf die vernaamste stappe van mummifisering en verduidelik waarom die Egiptenare dit gedoen het.","en":"Describe the main steps of mummification and explain why the Egyptians did it."},"steps":[{"af":"**Waarom:** hulle het geglo die siel het die liggaam ná die dood nodig, so die liggaam moes bewaar word.","en":"**Why:** they believed the soul needed the body after death, so the body had to be preserved."},{"af":"**Organe uit:** die brein deur die neus; die longe, lewer, maag en derms in kanopiese kruike. Die hart bly in die liggaam.","en":"**Organs out:** the brain through the nose; the lungs, liver, stomach and intestines into canopic jars. The heart stays in the body."},{"af":"**Uitdroog:** die liggaam word met natron bedek totdat dit heeltemal droog is.","en":"**Drying:** the body is covered with natron until it is completely dry."},{"af":"**Toedraai en begrawe:** met olies invryf, in linnestroke met amulette toedraai en in ’n sarkofaag sit, saam met dinge vir die lewe na die dood.","en":"**Wrapping and burial:** rub with oils, wrap in linen strips with amulets and place in a sarcophagus, together with things for the life after death."}],"answer":{"af":"Organe word verwyder (die hart bly), die liggaam word met natron uitgedroog en in linne toegedraai. Dit is gedoen omdat hulle geglo het die siel het die liggaam in die lewe na die dood nodig.","en":"The organs are removed (the heart stays), the body is dried with natron and wrapped in linen. This was done because they believed the soul needed the body in the life after death."}},{"title":{"af":"Hoe het die Rosetta-steen gehelp?","en":"How did the Rosetta Stone help?"},"problem":{"af":"Liam vra: ‘Hoe kan ons vandag hiërogliewe lees as niemand dit vir eeue kon lees nie?’ Verduidelik die rol van die Rosetta-steen.","en":"Liam asks: ‘How can we read hieroglyphs today if nobody could read them for centuries?’ Explain the role of the Rosetta Stone."},"steps":[{"af":"Die Rosetta-steen is in 1799 in die Nyldelta gevind.","en":"The Rosetta Stone was found in the Nile Delta in 1799."},{"af":"Dit het **dieselfde teks in drie skrifte**: hiërogliewe, ’n ander Egiptiese skrif en antieke Grieks.","en":"It has **the same text in three scripts**: hieroglyphs, another Egyptian script and ancient Greek."},{"af":"Geleerdes kon die Grieks lees. Deur die tekste te vergelyk, veral die name van konings, kon hulle uitwerk wat die hiërogliewe beteken.","en":"Scholars could read the Greek. By comparing the texts, especially the names of kings, they could work out what the hieroglyphs meant."},{"af":"Champollion het die hiërogliewe in 1822 ontsyfer.","en":"Champollion deciphered the hieroglyphs in 1822."}],"answer":{"af":"Die Rosetta-steen het dieselfde teks in hiërogliewe en in Grieks gehad. Omdat Grieks bekend was, kon Champollion die skrifte vergelyk en in 1822 die hiërogliewe ontsyfer.","en":"The Rosetta Stone had the same text in hieroglyphs and in Greek. Because Greek was known, Champollion could compare the scripts and decipher the hieroglyphs in 1822."}},{"title":{"af":"Wat vertel Toetankamen se graf ons?","en":"What does Tutankhamun’s tomb tell us?"},"problem":{"af":"In Toetankamen se graf is onder meer gevind: sy mummie in ’n goue kis, ’n goue doodsmasker, kos, meubels, klere, speletjies en strydwaens. Wat vertel hierdie bron ons oor die Egiptenare se geloof?","en":"Among other things, Tutankhamun’s tomb contained: his mummy in a golden coffin, a golden death mask, food, furniture, clothes, games and chariots. What does this source tell us about the Egyptians’ beliefs?"},"steps":[{"af":"Vra eers watter soort bron dit is: die voorwerpe is destyds gemaak en in die graf gesit, dus is dit ’n **primêre bron**.","en":"First ask what kind of source it is: the objects were made at the time and placed in the tomb, so it is a **primary source**."},{"af":"Dink na oor die kos, meubels, klere en speletjies: dit is alledaagse dinge. Hulle het geglo die farao sal dit in die **lewe na die dood** nodig hê.","en":"Think about the food, furniture, clothes and games: these are everyday things. They believed the pharaoh would need them in the **life after death**."},{"af":"Dink na oor die goud en die mummie: die farao was baie belangrik, en sy liggaam moes bewaar word.","en":"Think about the gold and the mummy: the pharaoh was very important, and his body had to be preserved."}],"answer":{"af":"Die Egiptenare het geglo die lewe gaan ná die dood voort en dat die farao sy liggaam en sy besittings daar nodig sou hê. Die skatte wys ook hoe belangrik en ryk die farao was.","en":"The Egyptians believed that life continues after death and that the pharaoh would need his body and his belongings there. The treasures also show how important and rich the pharaoh was."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom het die Egiptenare piramides gebou?","en":"Why did the Egyptians build pyramids?"},"options":[{"af":"As grafte vir farao’s","en":"As tombs for pharaohs"},{"af":"As paleise waarin farao’s gewoon het","en":"As palaces for pharaohs to live in"},{"af":"As pakhuise vir koring","en":"As storehouses for wheat"},{"af":"As tempels vir die son","en":"As temples for the sun"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Piramides was grafte. Die Egiptenare het in ’n lewe na die dood geglo, en die farao moes ’n veilige, indrukwekkende graf hê. Farao’s het in paleise gewoon, nie in piramides nie.","en":"Pyramids were tombs. The Egyptians believed in a life after death, and the pharaoh had to have a safe, impressive tomb. Pharaohs lived in palaces, not in pyramids."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Howard Carter het Toetankamen se graf in 1922 in die Vallei van die Konings ontdek.","en":"Howard Carter discovered Tutankhamun’s tomb in the Valley of the Kings in 1922."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die graf was amper onaangeraak deur grafrowers en vol skatte, soos die goue doodsmasker.","en":"True. The tomb had hardly been touched by tomb robbers and was full of treasures, such as the golden death mask."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Om die liggaam uit te droog, het die balsemers dit met ___ bedek, ’n soort sout.","en":"To dry out the body, the embalmers covered it with ___, a kind of salt."},"answers":{"af":["natron"],"en":["natron"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["suiker","sand","heuning"],"en":["sugar","sand","honey"]}},"explain":{"af":"Natron trek die vog uit die liggaam sodat dit nie vergaan nie. Heuning is deur dokters op wonde gesit, nie vir mummies gebruik nie.","en":"Natron draws the moisture out of the body so that it does not decay. Honey was put on wounds by doctors, not used for mummies."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter orgaan is tydens mummifisering in die liggaam gelos?","en":"Which organ was left in the body during mummification?"},"options":[{"af":"Die brein","en":"The brain"},{"af":"Die lewer","en":"The liver"},{"af":"Die longe","en":"The lungs"},{"af":"Die hart","en":"The heart"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die hart is gelos, want die Egiptenare het geglo dit is die plek van denke en gevoelens. Die brein is weggegooi, en die lewer en longe is in kanopiese kruike gesit.","en":"The heart was left, because the Egyptians believed it was the place of thoughts and feelings. The brain was thrown away, and the liver and lungs were put in canopic jars."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom was die Rosetta-steen so nuttig?","en":"Why was the Rosetta Stone so useful?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit het ’n kaart gehad wat die pad na Toetankamen se graf wys","en":"It had a map showing the way to Tutankhamun’s tomb"},{"af":"Dit was die eerste klip waarop iemand ooit in Egipte geskryf het","en":"It was the first stone anyone in Egypt ever wrote on"},{"af":"Dit het dieselfde teks in hiërogliewe en in Grieks gehad, wat geleerdes kon lees","en":"It had the same text in hieroglyphs and in Greek, which scholars could read"},{"af":"Dit het stap vir stap verduidelik hoe om ’n piramide te bou","en":"It explained step by step how to build a pyramid"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Omdat dieselfde teks ook in Grieks was, kon geleerdes die bekende Grieks met die onbekende hiërogliewe vergelyk. So het Champollion die skrif in 1822 ontsyfer.","en":"Because the same text was also in Greek, scholars could compare the known Greek with the unknown hieroglyphs. That is how Champollion deciphered the script in 1822."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke Egiptiese prestasie by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each Egyptian achievement to the right description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Hiërogliewe","en":"Hieroglyphs"},"r":{"af":"Skrif van prenttekens","en":"Writing made of picture signs"}},{"l":{"af":"Papirus","en":"Papyrus"},"r":{"af":"Skryfmateriaal van ’n riet","en":"Writing material made from a reed"}},{"l":{"af":"Kalender","en":"Calendar"},"r":{"af":"Jaar van 365 dae","en":"Year of 365 days"}},{"l":{"af":"Medisyne","en":"Medicine"},"r":{"af":"Gebreekte bene gespalk en heuning op wonde","en":"Broken bones splinted and honey on wounds"}},{"l":{"af":"Kanopiese kruike","en":"Canopic jars"},"r":{"af":"Het die organe van ’n mummie bewaar","en":"Kept the organs of a mummy"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die Egiptenare het op baie gebiede uitgeblink: skrif, skryfmateriaal, tydmeting, medisyne en die bewaring van liggame.","en":"The Egyptians excelled in many areas: writing, writing materials, measuring time, medicine and preserving bodies."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wie het volgens argeoloë die meeste van die werk aan die piramides gedoen?","en":"According to archaeologists, who did most of the work on the pyramids?"},"options":[{"af":"Slawe uit Europa","en":"Slaves from Europe"},{"af":"Betaalde werkers, baie van hulle boere tydens die vloedseisoen","en":"Paid workers, many of them farmers during the flood season"},{"af":"Die farao en sy priesters self","en":"The pharaoh and his priests themselves"},{"af":"Skrywers wat nie kon skryf nie","en":"Scribes who could not write"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Argeoloë het werkersdorpe en grafte naby die piramides gevind. Dit wys dat dit meestal betaalde werkers was – baie was boere wat gewerk het terwyl hul lande onder water was.","en":"Archaeologists found workers’ villages and graves near the pyramids. This shows that they were mostly paid workers – many were farmers who worked while their fields were under water."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die Groot Piramide van ___ is vir farao Khufu gebou.","en":"The Great Pyramid of ___ was built for pharaoh Khufu."},"answers":{"af":["Giza","Gizeh"],"en":["Giza"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Rosetta","Kaïro","Luxor"],"en":["Rosetta","Cairo","Luxor"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die Groot Piramide staan by Giza, sowat 4 500 jaar oud. Rosetta is waar die beroemde steen gevind is, en die Vallei van die Konings is naby Luxor.","en":"The Great Pyramid stands at Giza and is about 4 500 years old. Rosetta is where the famous stone was found, and the Valley of the Kings is near Luxor."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is latere farao’s in die Vallei van die Konings begrawe in plaas van in piramides?","en":"Why were later pharaohs buried in the Valley of the Kings instead of in pyramids?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat daar nie meer klip in Egipte was nie","en":"Because there was no more stone in Egypt"},{"af":"Omdat die Nyl die piramides weggespoel het","en":"Because the Nile washed the pyramids away"},{"af":"Omdat hulle nie meer in ’n lewe na die dood geglo het nie","en":"Because they no longer believed in a life after death"},{"af":"Omdat grafrowers die piramides beroof het","en":"Because tomb robbers had robbed the pyramids"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Piramides was maklik om te sien, en grafrowers het hulle beroof. Grafte wat in die rotse van ’n afgeleë vallei uitgekap is, was beter versteek. Die geloof in ’n lewe na die dood het gebly.","en":"Pyramids were easy to see, and tomb robbers robbed them. Tombs cut into the rocks of a remote valley were better hidden. The belief in a life after death remained."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Hiërogliewe staan net vir hele woorde en nooit vir klanke nie.","en":"Hieroglyphs stand only for whole words and never for sounds."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Sommige hiërogliewe staan vir klanke en ander vir hele woorde of idees. Dit is een rede waarom dit so moeilik was om te ontsyfer.","en":"False. Some hieroglyphs stand for sounds and others for whole words or ideas. This is one reason why they were so hard to decipher."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is Toetankamen se graf vir historici so belangrik?","en":"Why is Tutankhamun’s tomb so important to historians?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit was amper onaangeraak, so die skatte wys hoe ’n farao begrawe is","en":"It was hardly touched, so the treasures show how a pharaoh was buried"},{"af":"Toetankamen was die farao wat die Groot Piramide laat bou het","en":"Tutankhamun was the pharaoh who had the Great Pyramid built"},{"af":"Die Rosetta-steen is saam met sy mummie in die graf gevind","en":"The Rosetta Stone was found in the tomb with his mummy"},{"af":"Hy was die oudste farao wat ooit in Egipte geregeer het","en":"He was the oldest pharaoh who ever ruled Egypt"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die meeste grafte is deur grafrowers leeggemaak, maar Toetankamen s’n was amper vol. Dit gee historici ’n seldsame kyk na ’n farao se begrafnis. Khufu het die Groot Piramide laat bou, en Toetankamen is jonk oorlede.","en":"Most tombs were emptied by tomb robbers, but Tutankhamun’s was almost full. This gives historians a rare look at a pharaoh’s burial. Khufu had the Great Pyramid built, and Tutankhamun died young."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In 1822 het Champollion die hiërogliewe ___.","en":"In 1822 Champollion ___ the hieroglyphs."},"answers":{"af":["ontsyfer"],"en":["deciphered","decoded"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["uitgevind","gekopieer","verbrand"],"en":["invented","copied","burnt"]}},"explain":{"af":"Ontsyfer beteken om uit te werk wat ’n onbekende skrif beteken. Champollion het nie hiërogliewe uitgevind nie – die Egiptenare het dit duisende jare tevore gebruik.","en":"To decipher means to work out what an unknown script means. Champollion did not invent hieroglyphs – the Egyptians had used them thousands of years before."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel dae het die Egiptiese kalender gehad?","en":"How many days did the Egyptian calendar have?"},"options":[{"af":"360","en":"360"},{"af":"365","en":"365"},{"af":"300","en":"300"},{"af":"366","en":"366"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die kalender het 12 maande van 30 dae gehad (360 dae) plus 5 ekstra dae, dus 365 dae. Dit het boere gehelp om vir die vloed te beplan.","en":"The calendar had 12 months of 30 days (360 days) plus 5 extra days, so 365 days. It helped farmers to plan for the flood."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom noem ons antieke Egipte ’n belangrike Afrika-beskawing?","en":"Why do we call ancient Egypt an important African civilisation?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat dit die enigste land in Afrika met ’n groot rivier was","en":"Because it was the only country in Africa with a big river"},{"af":"Omdat Europese bouers die piramides vir die farao’s gebou het","en":"Because European builders built the pyramids for the pharaohs"},{"af":"Omdat dit een van die oudste beskawings ter wêreld is en ander volke beïnvloed het","en":"Because it is one of the oldest civilisations in the world and influenced other peoples"},{"af":"Omdat dit nooit met ander lande of volke kontak gehad het nie","en":"Because it never had contact with other countries or peoples"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Egipte is ’n Afrika-beskawing wat skrif, ’n kalender, medisyne en groot bouwerke ontwikkel het en die Grieke beïnvloed het. Dit het ook noue kontak met Nubië gehad.","en":"Egypt is an African civilisation that developed writing, a calendar, medicine and great buildings and influenced the Greeks. It also had close contact with Nubia."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Erfenisroete deur die provinsies","en":"A heritage trail through the provinces"},"topics":[{"id":"sw5-t4-gesk-erfenis","title":{"af":"Wat is erfenis?","en":"What is heritage?"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik wat erfenis is, tussen natuurlike en kulturele, en tasbare en ontasbare erfenis kan onderskei, en sê hoe ons ons erfenis kan bewaar en respekteer.","en":"You will be able to explain what heritage is, tell the difference between natural and cultural, and tangible and intangible heritage, and say how we can preserve and respect our heritage."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is erfenis?\n\n**Erfenis** is alles wat ons van **vorige geslagte** – ons ouers, grootouers en voorouers – **erf** en wat ons wil **bewaar** en aan die volgende geslag wil oordra. Dit kan plekke, dinge, gewoontes of kennis wees. Ons erfenis help ons om te weet **wie ons is** en waar ons vandaan kom.\n\n## Natuurlike en kulturele erfenis\n\n| Soort | Wat is dit? | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Natuurlike erfenis** | Dinge in die natuur wat mense nie gemaak het nie | Berge, riviere, woude, diere en plante, soos die Drakensberg, die Oranjerivier en fynbos |\n| **Kulturele erfenis** | Dinge wat mense geskep het en hul manier van lewe | Geboue, kuns, tale, liedjies, danse, resepte, klere, gebruike en feeste |\n\nSommige plekke is **albei**: die Maloti-Drakensbergpark het asemrowende berge (natuurlik) en duisende San-rotsskilderye (kultureel).\n\n## Tasbaar en ontasbaar\n\n- **Tasbare erfenis** kan jy **aanraak**: ’n gebou, ’n monument, ’n rotsskildery, ’n kleipot of ’n ou familiefoto.\n- **Ontasbare erfenis** kan jy **nie aanraak nie**: ’n taal, ’n liedjie, ’n storie, ’n dans, ’n geloof of kennis wat oorgedra word, soos hoe om ’n mandjie te vleg.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Erfenis is nie net ou geboue en monumente nie. Die liedjie wat jou ouma jou leer en die taal wat jy by die huis praat, is ook erfenis – **ontasbare** erfenis.\n\n## Van persoonlik tot wêreldwyd\n\n- **Persoonlike erfenis:** jou naam, jou taal, ’n spesiale geskenk wat iemand vir jou gegee het.\n- **Familie-erfenis:** familiefoto’s, ’n familieresep, stories oor jou voorouers, ’n erfstuk soos oupa se horlosie.\n- **Gemeenskapserfenis:** ’n plaaslike gebou soos ’n ou kerk, moskee of tempel, of ’n jaarlikse fees.\n- **Nasionale erfenis:** die landsvlag, die volkslied, die landswapen en ons amptelike tale.\n- **Wêrelderfenis:** plekke wat so belangrik is dat hulle aan die hele mensdom behoort.\n\n## Erfenisdag\n\n**24 September** is **Erfenisdag**, ’n openbare vakansiedag. September is ook **Erfenismaand**. Op Erfenisdag vier ons die **verskeidenheid** van kulture, tale en gebruike in Suid-Afrika: mense dra tradisionele klere, maak tradisionele kos, sing en dans, en baie braai saam. In KwaZulu-Natal was 24 September vroeër bekend as Shaka-dag, ter ere van koning Shaka.\n\n## Monumente, museums en erfenisterreine\n\n- ’n **Monument** is ’n gebou, beeld of gedenkteken wat ons aan ’n belangrike persoon of gebeurtenis herinner.\n- ’n **Museum** bewaar en vertoon voorwerpe uit die verlede sodat mense daaroor kan leer.\n- ’n **Erfenisterrein** is ’n plek wat bewaar word weens sy geskiedenis, kultuur of natuur. In Suid-Afrika help ’n regeringsliggaam, **SAHRA**, om sulke plekke te beskerm.\n\n**UNESCO** is ’n organisasie van die Verenigde Nasies. Dit kies plekke van **uitsonderlike waarde vir die hele wêreld** as **Wêrelderfenisterreine**. Suid-Afrika het meer as tien, soos Robbeneiland, die Wieg van die Mensdom, Mapungubwe en die Vredefort-koepel.\n\n## Hoe bewaar en respekteer ons erfenis?\n\n1. Moenie **rotskuns** aanraak, natmaak of daarop skryf nie. Die olie van jou hande en water beskadig die ou verf vir altyd.\n2. Moenie **graffiti** op monumente en geboue skryf nie, en los geen rommel nie.\n3. Moenie voorwerpe, fossiele of klipwerktuie van ’n erfenisterrein **wegneem** nie.\n4. **Besoek** museums en erfenisterreine en leer daaroor.\n5. Vra jou grootouers oor vroeër en **teken hul stories op**.\n6. Praat jou **taal**, leer tradisionele liedjies en danse, en **respekteer** ander mense se erfenis.\n\n> **Onthou:** Erfenis wat beskadig of vergeet word, kan **nooit vervang** word nie. Ons bewaar dit vir die kinders wat ná ons kom.","en":"## What is heritage?\n\n**Heritage** is everything we **inherit** from **previous generations** – our parents, grandparents and ancestors – and want to **preserve** and pass on to the next generation. It can be places, things, customs or knowledge. Our heritage helps us to know **who we are** and where we come from.\n\n## Natural and cultural heritage\n\n| Kind | What is it? | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Natural heritage** | Things in nature that people did not make | Mountains, rivers, forests, animals and plants, such as the Drakensberg, the Orange River and fynbos |\n| **Cultural heritage** | Things people created and their way of life | Buildings, art, languages, songs, dances, recipes, clothes, customs and festivals |\n\nSome places are **both**: the Maloti-Drakensberg Park has breathtaking mountains (natural) and thousands of San rock paintings (cultural).\n\n## Tangible and intangible\n\n- **Tangible heritage** is something you can **touch**: a building, a monument, a rock painting, a clay pot or an old family photo.\n- **Intangible heritage** is something you **cannot touch**: a language, a song, a story, a dance, a belief or knowledge that is passed on, such as how to weave a basket.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Heritage is not only old buildings and monuments. The song your grandmother teaches you and the language you speak at home are also heritage – **intangible** heritage.\n\n## From personal to worldwide\n\n- **Personal heritage:** your name, your language, a special gift someone gave you.\n- **Family heritage:** family photos, a family recipe, stories about your ancestors, an heirloom such as grandpa’s watch.\n- **Community heritage:** a local building such as an old church, mosque or temple, or a yearly festival.\n- **National heritage:** the national flag, the national anthem, the coat of arms and our official languages.\n- **World heritage:** places so important that they belong to all of humankind.\n\n## Heritage Day\n\n**24 September** is **Heritage Day**, a public holiday. September is also **Heritage Month**. On Heritage Day we celebrate the **diversity** of cultures, languages and customs in South Africa: people wear traditional clothes, make traditional food, sing and dance, and many have a braai together. In KwaZulu-Natal 24 September used to be known as Shaka Day, in honour of King Shaka.\n\n## Monuments, museums and heritage sites\n\n- A **monument** is a building, statue or memorial that reminds us of an important person or event.\n- A **museum** keeps and displays objects from the past so that people can learn about them.\n- A **heritage site** is a place that is preserved because of its history, culture or nature. In South Africa a government body, **SAHRA**, helps to protect such places.\n\n**UNESCO** is an organisation of the United Nations. It chooses places of **outstanding value to the whole world** as **World Heritage Sites**. South Africa has more than ten, such as Robben Island, the Cradle of Humankind, Mapungubwe and the Vredefort Dome.\n\n## How do we preserve and respect heritage?\n\n1. Don’t touch, wet or write on **rock art**. The oil from your hands and water damage the old paint forever.\n2. Don’t write **graffiti** on monuments and buildings, and don’t leave litter.\n3. Don’t **take away** objects, fossils or stone tools from a heritage site.\n4. **Visit** museums and heritage sites and learn about them.\n5. Ask your grandparents about the old days and **write down their stories**.\n6. Speak your **language**, learn traditional songs and dances, and **respect** other people’s heritage.\n\n> **Remember:** Heritage that is damaged or forgotten can **never be replaced**. We preserve it for the children who come after us."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Erfenis","en":"Heritage"},"def":{"af":"Alles wat ons van vorige geslagte erf en wil bewaar en aan die volgende geslag wil oordra.","en":"Everything we inherit from previous generations and want to preserve and pass on to the next generation."}},{"term":{"af":"Natuurlike erfenis","en":"Natural heritage"},"def":{"af":"Waardevolle dinge in die natuur wat mense nie gemaak het nie, soos berge, riviere, diere en plante.","en":"Valuable things in nature that people did not make, such as mountains, rivers, animals and plants."}},{"term":{"af":"Kulturele erfenis","en":"Cultural heritage"},"def":{"af":"Dinge wat mense geskep het en hul manier van lewe, soos geboue, kuns, tale en gebruike.","en":"Things people created and their way of life, such as buildings, art, languages and customs."}},{"term":{"af":"Tasbare erfenis","en":"Tangible heritage"},"def":{"af":"Erfenis wat jy kan aanraak, soos ’n gebou, ’n monument of ’n kleipot.","en":"Heritage you can touch, such as a building, a monument or a clay pot."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontasbare erfenis","en":"Intangible heritage"},"def":{"af":"Erfenis wat jy nie kan aanraak nie, soos ’n taal, ’n liedjie, ’n storie of ’n dans.","en":"Heritage you cannot touch, such as a language, a song, a story or a dance."}},{"term":{"af":"Monument","en":"Monument"},"def":{"af":"’n Gebou, beeld of gedenkteken wat ons aan ’n belangrike persoon of gebeurtenis herinner.","en":"A building, statue or memorial that reminds us of an important person or event."}},{"term":{"af":"Museum","en":"Museum"},"def":{"af":"’n Plek wat voorwerpe uit die verlede bewaar en vertoon sodat mense daaroor kan leer.","en":"A place that keeps and displays objects from the past so that people can learn about them."}},{"term":{"af":"Erfenisterrein","en":"Heritage site"},"def":{"af":"’n Plek wat bewaar en beskerm word weens sy geskiedenis, kultuur of natuur.","en":"A place that is preserved and protected because of its history, culture or nature."}},{"term":{"af":"Wêrelderfenisterrein","en":"World Heritage Site"},"def":{"af":"’n Plek wat UNESCO gekies het omdat dit van uitsonderlike waarde vir die hele wêreld is.","en":"A place chosen by UNESCO because it is of outstanding value to the whole world."}},{"term":{"af":"Erfenisdag","en":"Heritage Day"},"def":{"af":"’n Openbare vakansiedag op 24 September waarop Suid-Afrikaners hul verskillende kulture en erfenis vier.","en":"A public holiday on 24 September on which South Africans celebrate their different cultures and heritage."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer erfenis","en":"Classify heritage"},"problem":{"af":"Sê of elkeen natuurlike of kulturele erfenis is, en of dit tasbaar of ontasbaar is: (a) die Oranjerivier, (b) ’n San-rotsskildery, (c) ’n tradisionele liedjie, (d) ’n kleipot wat ouma gemaak het.","en":"Say whether each one is natural or cultural heritage, and whether it is tangible or intangible: (a) the Orange River, (b) a San rock painting, (c) a traditional song, (d) a clay pot that grandmother made."},"steps":[{"af":"Vra eers: **het mense dit gemaak?** Nee = natuurlik; ja = kultureel. Net die rivier is nie deur mense gemaak nie.","en":"First ask: **did people make it?** No = natural; yes = cultural. Only the river was not made by people."},{"af":"Vra dan: **kan ek dit aanraak?** Die rivier, die rotsskildery en die pot kan jy aanraak. ’n Liedjie kan jy hoor en sing, maar nie aanraak nie.","en":"Then ask: **can I touch it?** You can touch the river, the rock painting and the pot. You can hear and sing a song, but not touch it."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) natuurlik, tasbaar; (b) kultureel, tasbaar; (c) kultureel, ontasbaar; (d) kultureel, tasbaar.","en":"(a) natural, tangible; (b) cultural, tangible; (c) cultural, intangible; (d) cultural, tangible."}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik Erfenisdag","en":"Explain Heritage Day"},"problem":{"af":"Johan se maat van ’n ander land vra: ‘Wat is Erfenisdag, en waarom vier julle dit?’ Skryf ’n kort antwoord.","en":"Johan’s friend from another country asks: ‘What is Heritage Day, and why do you celebrate it?’ Write a short answer."},"steps":[{"af":"Gee die **datum**: 24 September, ’n openbare vakansiedag in Erfenismaand (September).","en":"Give the **date**: 24 September, a public holiday in Heritage Month (September)."},{"af":"Sê **waarom**: Suid-Afrika het baie kulture, tale en gebruike, en op dié dag vier ons daardie verskeidenheid.","en":"Say **why**: South Africa has many cultures, languages and customs, and on this day we celebrate that diversity."},{"af":"Gee **voorbeelde**: mense dra tradisionele klere, maak tradisionele kos, sing en dans.","en":"Give **examples**: people wear traditional clothes, make traditional food, sing and dance."}],"answer":{"af":"Erfenisdag is op 24 September. Dit is ’n vakansiedag waarop Suid-Afrikaners hul verskillende kulture, tale en gebruike vier, byvoorbeeld deur tradisionele klere te dra en tradisionele kos te maak.","en":"Heritage Day is on 24 September. It is a holiday on which South Africans celebrate their different cultures, languages and customs, for example by wearing traditional clothes and making traditional food."}},{"title":{"af":"Beskerm rotskuns","en":"Protect rock art"},"problem":{"af":"Op ’n skooluitstappie na ’n rotsskuiling wil Pieter die rotsskildery natspuit sodat die kleure helderder lyk vir sy foto. Wat sê jy vir hom, en waarom?","en":"On a school outing to a rock shelter Pieter wants to spray the rock painting with water so that the colours look brighter for his photo. What do you tell him, and why?"},"steps":[{"af":"Herken die probleem: water en die olie van hande beskadig die ou verf.","en":"Recognise the problem: water and the oil from hands damage the old paint."},{"af":"Dink aan die waarde: die skildery is honderde of selfs duisende jare oud en is ’n primêre bron oor die San.","en":"Think about the value: the painting is hundreds or even thousands of years old and is a primary source about the San."},{"af":"Dink aan die gevolg: as dit beskadig word, kan dit nooit vervang word nie, en toekomstige geslagte sal dit nie kan sien nie.","en":"Think about the result: if it is damaged, it can never be replaced, and future generations will not be able to see it."}],"answer":{"af":"Hy moet dit nie doen nie. Water en aanraking beskadig die ou verf vir altyd. Die skildery is deel van ons erfenis en moet vir toekomstige geslagte bewaar word.","en":"He must not do it. Water and touching damage the old paint forever. The painting is part of our heritage and must be preserved for future generations."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is erfenis?","en":"What is heritage?"},"options":[{"af":"Die geskenke wat jy op jou verjaarsdag kry","en":"The presents you get on your birthday"},{"af":"Wat ons van vorige geslagte erf en wil bewaar en oordra","en":"What we inherit from previous generations and want to preserve and pass on"},{"af":"Net ou geboue en monumente wat die regering besit","en":"Only old buildings and monuments that the government owns"},{"af":"Nuwe dinge wat ons vandag in die winkels koop","en":"New things we buy in the shops today"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Erfenis is wat ons van ons ouers, grootouers en voorouers erf – plekke, dinge, gewoontes en kennis – en wil bewaar vir die geslagte ná ons. Dit is nie net ou geboue nie.","en":"Heritage is what we inherit from our parents, grandparents and ancestors – places, things, customs and knowledge – and want to preserve for the generations after us. It is not only old buildings."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Taal is ’n voorbeeld van ontasbare erfenis.","en":"A language is an example of intangible heritage."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Jy kan ’n taal praat, hoor en leer, maar nie aanraak nie. Daarom is dit ontasbare erfenis.","en":"True. You can speak, hear and learn a language, but you cannot touch it. That is why it is intangible heritage."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n voorbeeld van natuurlike erfenis?","en":"Which one is an example of natural heritage?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Drakensberg se berge","en":"The mountains of the Drakensberg"},{"af":"’n Museum in Kaapstad","en":"A museum in Cape Town"},{"af":"’n Tradisionele dans","en":"A traditional dance"},{"af":"’n Ou kerkgebou","en":"An old church building"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Natuurlike erfenis is deur die natuur gevorm, nie deur mense nie. ’n Museum, ’n dans en ’n kerk is deur mense geskep, dus is dit kulturele erfenis.","en":"Natural heritage was formed by nature, not by people. A museum, a dance and a church were created by people, so they are cultural heritage."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Erfenisdag word elke jaar op ___ September gevier.","en":"Heritage Day is celebrated every year on ___ September."},"answers":{"af":["24","24ste","vier-en-twintig"],"en":["24","24th","twenty-fourth"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["16","21","27"],"en":["16","21","27"]}},"explain":{"af":"Erfenisdag is op 24 September, in Erfenismaand. Dit is ’n openbare vakansiedag waarop ons ons verskillende kulture vier.","en":"Heritage Day is on 24 September, in Heritage Month. It is a public holiday on which we celebrate our different cultures."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n voorbeeld van tasbare erfenis?","en":"Which one is an example of tangible heritage?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Volksliedjie wat ouma sing","en":"A folk song that grandma sings"},{"af":"’n Storie wat oupa vertel","en":"A story that grandpa tells"},{"af":"Die taal wat jy by die huis praat","en":"The language you speak at home"},{"af":"’n Kleipot wat ouma gemaak het","en":"A clay pot that grandma made"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Kleipot kan jy aanraak, dus is dit tasbaar. ’n Liedjie, ’n storie en ’n taal is ook erfenis, maar jy kan hulle nie aanraak nie – hulle is ontasbaar.","en":"You can touch a clay pot, so it is tangible. A song, a story and a language are also heritage, but you cannot touch them – they are intangible."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke voorbeeld by die soort erfenis.","en":"Match each example to the kind of heritage."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Die Oranjerivier","en":"The Orange River"},"r":{"af":"Natuurlike erfenis","en":"Natural heritage"}},{"l":{"af":"Ouma se resep vir pampoenkoekies","en":"Grandma’s recipe for pumpkin fritters"},"r":{"af":"Familie-erfenis","en":"Family heritage"}},{"l":{"af":"Die landsvlag","en":"The national flag"},"r":{"af":"Nasionale simbool","en":"National symbol"}},{"l":{"af":"Robbeneiland","en":"Robben Island"},"r":{"af":"UNESCO-wêrelderfenisterrein","en":"UNESCO World Heritage Site"}},{"l":{"af":"Die naam wat jou ouers vir jou gegee het","en":"The name your parents gave you"},"r":{"af":"Persoonlike erfenis","en":"Personal heritage"}}],"explain":{"af":"Erfenis kan van persoonlik (jou naam) tot familie (’n resep), nasionaal (die vlag) en wêreldwyd (Robbeneiland) strek. ’n Rivier is natuurlike erfenis.","en":"Heritage can range from personal (your name) to family (a recipe), national (the flag) and worldwide (Robben Island). A river is natural heritage."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom moet jy nooit ’n rotsskildery aanraak of natmaak nie?","en":"Why should you never touch or wet a rock painting?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat die verf giftig is","en":"Because the paint is poisonous"},{"af":"Omdat dit die skildery vir altyd beskadig en dit nie vervang kan word nie","en":"Because it damages the painting forever and it cannot be replaced"},{"af":"Omdat jy dan ’n boete by die museum moet betaal","en":"Because you then have to pay a fine at the museum"},{"af":"Omdat die skildery dan ’n ander kleur word en mooier lyk","en":"Because the painting then turns a different colour and looks nicer"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die olie van jou hande en water beskadig die ou verf. Rotskuns is honderde of duisende jare oud, en as dit beskadig word, is dit vir altyd verlore.","en":"The oil from your hands and water damage the old paint. Rock art is hundreds or thousands of years old, and if it is damaged, it is lost forever."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Plekke van uitsonderlike waarde vir die hele wêreld word deur ___ as Wêrelderfenisterreine gekies.","en":"Places of outstanding value to the whole world are chosen by ___ as World Heritage Sites."},"answers":{"af":["UNESCO"],"en":["UNESCO"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["SAHRA","FIFA","die Parlement"],"en":["SAHRA","FIFA","Parliament"]}},"explain":{"af":"UNESCO is ’n organisasie van die Verenigde Nasies wat Wêrelderfenisterreine kies. SAHRA beskerm erfenisterreine in Suid-Afrika, maar kies nie Wêrelderfenisterreine nie.","en":"UNESCO is an organisation of the United Nations that chooses World Heritage Sites. SAHRA protects heritage sites in South Africa, but does not choose World Heritage Sites."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo se oupa leer hom ’n tradisionele liedjie. Watter soort erfenis is dit?","en":"Thabo’s grandfather teaches him a traditional song. What kind of heritage is this?"},"options":[{"af":"Tasbare natuurlike erfenis","en":"Tangible natural heritage"},{"af":"Tasbare kulturele erfenis","en":"Tangible cultural heritage"},{"af":"Ontasbare kulturele erfenis","en":"Intangible cultural heritage"},{"af":"Ontasbare natuurlike erfenis","en":"Intangible natural heritage"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Mense het die liedjie geskep, dus is dit kultureel. Jy kan dit sing en hoor, maar nie aanraak nie, dus is dit ontasbaar.","en":"People created the song, so it is cultural. You can sing and hear it, but not touch it, so it is intangible."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Erfenis is net ou geboue en monumente.","en":"Heritage is only old buildings and monuments."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Erfenis sluit ook natuurlike plekke in, en ontasbare dinge soos tale, liedjies, stories, danse en gebruike.","en":"False. Heritage also includes natural places, and intangible things such as languages, songs, stories, dances and customs."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die hoofdoel van ’n museum?","en":"What is the main purpose of a museum?"},"options":[{"af":"Om ou voorwerpe aan versamelaars en toeriste te verkoop","en":"To sell old objects to collectors and tourists"},{"af":"Om nuwe geboue vir die stad te ontwerp en te bou","en":"To design and build new buildings for the city"},{"af":"Om toeriste se paspoorte en kaartjies na te gaan","en":"To check tourists’ passports and tickets"},{"af":"Om voorwerpe uit die verlede te bewaar en te vertoon sodat mense kan leer","en":"To keep and display objects from the past so that people can learn"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Museum bewaar voorwerpe uit die verlede en vertoon hulle, sodat mense van alle ouderdomme oor die geskiedenis en erfenis kan leer.","en":"A museum keeps objects from the past and displays them, so that people of all ages can learn about history and heritage."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Erfenis wat jy nie kan aanraak nie, soos ’n liedjie of ’n taal, is ___ erfenis.","en":"Heritage that you cannot touch, such as a song or a language, is ___ heritage."},"answers":{"af":["ontasbare","ontasbaar"],"en":["intangible"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["tasbare","natuurlike","nasionale"],"en":["tangible","natural","national"]}},"explain":{"af":"Ontasbaar beteken dat jy dit nie kan aanraak nie. Tasbare erfenis, soos ’n gebou of ’n pot, kan jy wel aanraak.","en":"Intangible means that you cannot touch it. Tangible heritage, such as a building or a pot, you can touch."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die beste manier om jou familie se erfenis te bewaar?","en":"What is the best way to preserve your family’s heritage?"},"options":[{"af":"Om jou grootouers se stories op te teken en ou foto’s te bewaar","en":"To write down your grandparents’ stories and keep old photos"},{"af":"Om ou familiefoto’s weg te gooi sodat die huis netjies is","en":"To throw away old family photos so that the house is tidy"},{"af":"Om net nuwe dinge in die huis te hou en ou goed te verkoop","en":"To keep only new things in the house and sell old things"},{"af":"Om nooit vir jou grootouers vrae oor die verlede te vra nie","en":"To never ask your grandparents questions about the past"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"As jy jou grootouers se stories opteken en foto’s bewaar, gaan die familie se erfenis nie verlore nie en kan jy dit aan jou eie kinders oordra.","en":"If you write down your grandparents’ stories and keep photos, the family’s heritage is not lost and you can pass it on to your own children."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter erfenisterrein is ’n goeie voorbeeld van natuurlike én kulturele erfenis saam?","en":"Which heritage site is a good example of natural and cultural heritage together?"},"options":[{"af":"Die landsvlag","en":"The national flag"},{"af":"Die Vredefort-koepel","en":"The Vredefort Dome"},{"af":"Die Maloti-Drakensbergpark","en":"The Maloti-Drakensberg Park"},{"af":"’n Familieresep","en":"A family recipe"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die Maloti-Drakensbergpark het asemrowende berge (natuurlik) en duisende San-rotsskilderye (kultureel). Die Vredefort-koepel is net natuurlike erfenis, en ’n vlag en ’n resep is nie terreine nie.","en":"The Maloti-Drakensberg Park has breathtaking mountains (natural) and thousands of San rock paintings (cultural). The Vredefort Dome is natural heritage only, and a flag and a recipe are not sites."}}]},{"id":"sw5-t4-gesk-erfenisroete","title":{"af":"’n Erfenisroete deur die nege provinsies","en":"A heritage trail through the nine provinces"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal ’n belangrike erfenisterrein in elkeen van die nege provinsies kan noem, sê waar dit is en verduidelik waarom dit deel van ons erfenis is.","en":"You will be able to name an important heritage site in each of the nine provinces, say where it is and explain why it is part of our heritage."},"summary":{"af":"## ’n Reis deur ons erfenis\n\nSuid-Afrika het **nege provinsies**, en elkeen het erfenisterreine wat ’n deel van ons storie vertel: van die oudste rotse op aarde, tot ons vroeë voorouers, ou koninkryke en die stryd vir vryheid. Kom ons volg ’n **erfenisroete** deur al nege.\n\n| Provinsie | Erfenisterrein | Waarom belangrik? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Limpopo | Mapungubwe | Ryk koninkryk van sowat 1 000 jaar gelede |\n| Gauteng | Wieg van die Mensdom; Konstitusieheuwel | Fossiele van vroeë voorouers; ou tronk, nou ons Konstitusionele Hof |\n| Noordwes | Taung-skedelterrein | Die Taung-kind, ’n fossiel van ’n vroeë voorouer |\n| Mpumalanga | Barberton Makhonjwa-berge | Van die oudste rotse op aarde |\n| KwaZulu-Natal | iSimangaliso-vleilandpark; Maloti-Drakensbergpark | Vleilande, mere en strande; berge met San-rotskuns |\n| Vrystaat | Vredefort-koepel | Grootste bekende meteoriet-impakkrater op aarde |\n| Noord-Kaap | Die Groot Gat; Richtersveld | Diamantmyn met die hand gegrawe; Nama-veewagters |\n| Oos-Kaap | Nelson Mandela-museum | Mandela se lewe en nalatenskap |\n| Wes-Kaap | Robbeneiland | Tronk vir politieke gevangenes, nou ’n museum |\n\n## Mense en koninkryke van lank gelede\n\n- **Mapungubwe:** Waar die Limpopo- en Shashe-rivier ontmoet, by die grense van Suid-Afrika, Botswana en Zimbabwe, was sowat 1 000 jaar gelede ’n ryk **koninkryk**. Die koning het bo-op ’n heuwel gewoon en die gewone mense onder. Hulle het **goud** en **ivoor** verhandel vir glaskrale en lap van handelaars van oorsee. In ’n koninklike graf is ’n klein **goue renoster** gevind.\n- **Wieg van die Mensdom:** In grotte soos die **Sterkfontein-grotte** is fossiele van ons vroeë voorouers gevind wat miljoene jare oud is, soos ‘Mrs Ples’.\n- **Taung:** In **1924** is die skedel van ’n jong kind in ’n kalksteengroef naby Taung gevind. Professor Raymond Dart het gewys dat dit ’n baie vroeë voorouer van die mens was. Dié ontdekking het gehelp om te wys dat die storie van die mens in Afrika begin het.\n\n## Ons natuurwonders\n\n- **Barberton Makhonjwa-berge:** rotse van meer as 3 000 miljoen jaar oud. Wetenskaplikes bestudeer hulle om te leer hoe die jong aarde was.\n- **Vredefort-koepel:** sowat 2 000 miljoen jaar gelede het ’n reuse-meteoriet die aarde hier getref, naby die dorp Parys.\n- **iSimangaliso-vleilandpark:** *iSimangaliso* beteken ‘wonder’ in isiZulu. Daar is mere, moerasse, strande en koraalriwwe, met seekoeie, krokodille en seeskilpaaie wat eiers op die strande lê.\n- **Maloti-Drakensbergpark:** hoë berge en duisende San-rotsskilderye – natuurlike én kulturele erfenis.\n- **Richtersveld:** ’n bergagtige woestyn waar die **Nama**, afstammelinge van die Khoikhoi, nog met hul vee trek en in **matjieshuise** woon.\n\n## Rykdom uit die grond\n\nBy **Kimberley** het duisende mense van 1871 tot 1914 met grawe en pikke na diamante gegrawe. So het **die Groot Gat** ontstaan – een van die grootste gate wat ooit met die hand gegrawe is. Die diamante het Kimberley laat groei en was die begin van groot mynbou in Suid-Afrika.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Kimberley is bekend vir **diamante**, nie goud nie. Goud is in **1886** aan die Witwatersrand in Gauteng ontdek.\n\n## Die pad na vryheid\n\n- **Robbeneiland** lê in Tafelbaai. Tydens **apartheid** was dit ’n tronk vir **politieke gevangenes** – mense wat teen apartheid geveg het. **Nelson Mandela** was 18 van sy 27 jaar in die tronk daar. Vandag is dit ’n museum.\n- **Konstitusieheuwel** in Johannesburg was ’n tronk waar onder andere Mandela en Mahatma Gandhi aangehou is. Nou staan die **Konstitusionele Hof** daar, wat ons **Grondwet** en almal se regte beskerm.\n- Die **Nelson Mandela-museum** het dele in Mthatha, Qunu en Mvezo. Mandela is in 1918 in Mvezo gebore en het in Qunu grootgeword. In 1994 het hy die eerste president van ’n **demokratiese** Suid-Afrika geword.\n\n> **Onthou:** ’n Terrein kan belangrik wees weens die **natuur** (Vredefort), **mense van lank gelede** (Mapungubwe) of **onlangse geskiedenis** (Robbeneiland).","en":"## A journey through our heritage\n\nSouth Africa has **nine provinces**, and each one has heritage sites that tell part of our story: from the oldest rocks on Earth, to our early ancestors, old kingdoms and the struggle for freedom. Let’s follow a **heritage trail** through all nine.\n\n| Province | Heritage site | Why important? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Limpopo | Mapungubwe | Rich kingdom of about 1 000 years ago |\n| Gauteng | Cradle of Humankind; Constitution Hill | Fossils of early ancestors; old prison, now our Constitutional Court |\n| North West | Taung Skull site | The Taung Child, a fossil of an early ancestor |\n| Mpumalanga | Barberton Makhonjwa Mountains | Some of the oldest rocks on Earth |\n| KwaZulu-Natal | iSimangaliso Wetland Park; Maloti-Drakensberg Park | Wetlands, lakes and beaches; mountains with San rock art |\n| Free State | Vredefort Dome | Largest known meteorite impact crater on Earth |\n| Northern Cape | The Big Hole; Richtersveld | Diamond mine dug by hand; Nama herders |\n| Eastern Cape | Nelson Mandela Museum | Mandela’s life and legacy |\n| Western Cape | Robben Island | Prison for political prisoners, now a museum |\n\n## People and kingdoms of long ago\n\n- **Mapungubwe:** Where the Limpopo and Shashe rivers meet, at the borders of South Africa, Botswana and Zimbabwe, there was a rich **kingdom** about 1 000 years ago. The king lived on top of a hill and the ordinary people below. They traded **gold** and **ivory** for glass beads and cloth from traders from overseas. A small **golden rhinoceros** was found in a royal grave.\n- **Cradle of Humankind:** In caves such as the **Sterkfontein Caves**, fossils of our early ancestors that are millions of years old have been found, such as ‘Mrs Ples’.\n- **Taung:** In **1924** the skull of a young child was found in a limestone quarry near Taung. Professor Raymond Dart showed that it was a very early ancestor of humans. This discovery helped to show that the human story began in Africa.\n\n## Our natural wonders\n\n- **Barberton Makhonjwa Mountains:** rocks more than 3 000 million years old. Scientists study them to learn what the young Earth was like.\n- **Vredefort Dome:** about 2 000 million years ago a giant meteorite struck the Earth here, near the town of Parys.\n- **iSimangaliso Wetland Park:** *iSimangaliso* means ‘wonder’ in isiZulu. There are lakes, swamps, beaches and coral reefs, with hippos, crocodiles and sea turtles that lay eggs on the beaches.\n- **Maloti-Drakensberg Park:** high mountains and thousands of San rock paintings – natural and cultural heritage.\n- **Richtersveld:** a mountainous desert where the **Nama**, descendants of the Khoikhoi, still move with their livestock and live in **mat houses**.\n\n## Wealth from the ground\n\nAt **Kimberley** thousands of people dug for diamonds with spades and picks from 1871 to 1914. That is how **the Big Hole** came about – one of the largest holes ever dug by hand. The diamonds made Kimberley grow and were the start of large-scale mining in South Africa.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Kimberley is known for **diamonds**, not gold. Gold was discovered on the Witwatersrand in Gauteng in **1886**.\n\n## The road to freedom\n\n- **Robben Island** lies in Table Bay. During **apartheid** it was a prison for **political prisoners** – people who fought against apartheid. **Nelson Mandela** spent 18 of his 27 years in prison there. Today it is a museum.\n- **Constitution Hill** in Johannesburg was a prison where Mandela and Mahatma Gandhi, among others, were held. Now the **Constitutional Court** stands there, which protects our **Constitution** and everyone’s rights.\n- The **Nelson Mandela Museum** has parts in Mthatha, Qunu and Mvezo. Mandela was born in Mvezo in 1918 and grew up in Qunu. In 1994 he became the first president of a **democratic** South Africa.\n\n> **Remember:** A site can be important because of **nature** (Vredefort), **people of long ago** (Mapungubwe) or **recent history** (Robben Island)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Erfenisroete","en":"Heritage trail"},"def":{"af":"’n Roete wat ’n reeks erfenisterreine verbind sodat mense hulle kan besoek en daaroor kan leer.","en":"A route that links a series of heritage sites so that people can visit them and learn about them."}},{"term":{"af":"Fossiel","en":"Fossil"},"def":{"af":"Die oorblyfsels of spore van ’n plant of dier van baie lank gelede wat in rots bewaar gebly het.","en":"The remains or traces of a plant or animal from very long ago that have been preserved in rock."}},{"term":{"af":"Vroeë voorouers","en":"Early ancestors"},"def":{"af":"Mensagtige wesens wat miljoene jare gelede in Afrika geleef het; hul fossiele help wetenskaplikes om te leer hoe mense ontwikkel het.","en":"Human-like beings that lived in Africa millions of years ago; their fossils help scientists learn how humans developed."}},{"term":{"af":"Impakkrater","en":"Impact crater"},"def":{"af":"’n Groot holte wat ontstaan wanneer ’n meteoriet die aarde tref.","en":"A large hollow that forms when a meteorite strikes the Earth."}},{"term":{"af":"Vleiland","en":"Wetland"},"def":{"af":"’n Gebied waar die grond die hele jaar of ’n deel van die jaar met water bedek of deurweek is.","en":"An area where the ground is covered with or soaked in water for all or part of the year."}},{"term":{"af":"Koninkryk","en":"Kingdom"},"def":{"af":"’n Gebied en sy mense wat deur ’n koning of koningin regeer word.","en":"An area and its people ruled by a king or queen."}},{"term":{"af":"Apartheid","en":"Apartheid"},"def":{"af":"’n Stelsel van wette van 1948 tot 1994 wat mense volgens hul ras geskei het en die meeste Suid-Afrikaners hul regte ontneem het.","en":"A system of laws from 1948 to 1994 that separated people by race and took away the rights of most South Africans."}},{"term":{"af":"Politieke gevangene","en":"Political prisoner"},"def":{"af":"Iemand wat in die tronk gesit word omdat hy of sy teen die regering se wette of beleid veg.","en":"Someone who is put in prison because he or she fights against the government’s laws or policies."}},{"term":{"af":"Grondwet","en":"Constitution"},"def":{"af":"Die hoogste wet van ’n land, wat sê hoe die land regeer word en watter regte almal het.","en":"The highest law of a country, which says how the country is governed and what rights everyone has."}},{"term":{"af":"Demokrasie","en":"Democracy"},"def":{"af":"’n Stelsel waarin alle volwasse burgers hul leiers kan kies deur te stem.","en":"A system in which all adult citizens can choose their leaders by voting."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Gebruik die roete-tabel","en":"Use the route table"},"problem":{"af":"Gebruik die roete-tabel. In watter provinsie moet jy wees om (a) van die oudste rotse op aarde te sien, (b) ’n reuse-meteorietkrater te besoek, en (c) die tronk te sien waar Mandela 18 jaar lank was?","en":"Use the route table. In which province must you be to (a) see some of the oldest rocks on Earth, (b) visit a giant meteorite crater, and (c) see the prison where Mandela spent 18 years?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Soek ‘oudste rotse’ in die laaste kolom: die Barberton Makhonjwa-berge – **Mpumalanga**.","en":"(a) Look for ‘oldest rocks’ in the last column: the Barberton Makhonjwa Mountains – **Mpumalanga**."},{"af":"(b) Soek ‘meteoriet’: die Vredefort-koepel – **Vrystaat**.","en":"(b) Look for ‘meteorite’: the Vredefort Dome – **Free State**."},{"af":"(c) Mandela was 18 jaar op Robbeneiland – **Wes-Kaap**.","en":"(c) Mandela spent 18 years on Robben Island – **Western Cape**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Mpumalanga, (b) Vrystaat, (c) Wes-Kaap.","en":"(a) Mpumalanga, (b) Free State, (c) Western Cape."}},{"title":{"af":"Wat vertel die goue renoster ons?","en":"What does the golden rhinoceros tell us?"},"problem":{"af":"By Mapungubwe is ’n klein goue renoster in ’n koninklike graf bo-op die heuwel gevind. Wat vertel hierdie bron ons oor die mense van Mapungubwe?","en":"At Mapungubwe a small golden rhinoceros was found in a royal grave on top of the hill. What does this source tell us about the people of Mapungubwe?"},"steps":[{"af":"**Goud:** die mense kon goud bewerk – hulle het vaardige ambagsmanne gehad.","en":"**Gold:** the people could work gold – they had skilled craftsmen."},{"af":"**Koninklike graf bo-op die heuwel:** die koning en sy familie het bo gewoon en is daar begrawe. Hulle was belangriker en ryker as die gewone mense onder.","en":"**Royal grave on top of the hill:** the king and his family lived at the top and were buried there. They were more important and richer than the ordinary people below."},{"af":"**Rykdom en handel:** goud was waardevol. Saam met glaskrale van oorsee wys dit dat Mapungubwe ’n ryk handelsryk was.","en":"**Wealth and trade:** gold was valuable. Together with glass beads from overseas, it shows that Mapungubwe was a rich trading kingdom."}],"answer":{"af":"Mapungubwe het vaardige goudsmede gehad, ’n koning wat bo die gewone mense gestaan het, en baie rykdom uit handel.","en":"Mapungubwe had skilled goldsmiths, a king who stood above the ordinary people, and great wealth from trade."}},{"title":{"af":"Beplan ’n gesinsroete","en":"Plan a family route"},"problem":{"af":"Zanele se gesin ry van Kimberley na Johannesburg, en ry by Parys verby. Noem een erfenisterrein by elke plek en sê waarom dit belangrik is.","en":"Zanele’s family drives from Kimberley to Johannesburg, and passes Parys. Name one heritage site at each place and say why it is important."},"steps":[{"af":"**Kimberley (Noord-Kaap):** die Groot Gat – met die hand gegrawe vir diamante tussen 1871 en 1914; die begin van groot mynbou.","en":"**Kimberley (Northern Cape):** the Big Hole – dug by hand for diamonds between 1871 and 1914; the start of large-scale mining."},{"af":"**Parys (Vrystaat):** die Vredefort-koepel – die grootste bekende meteoriet-impakkrater op aarde.","en":"**Parys (Free State):** the Vredefort Dome – the largest known meteorite impact crater on Earth."},{"af":"**Johannesburg (Gauteng):** Konstitusieheuwel – ’n ou tronk wat nou die Konstitusionele Hof is, wat ons regte beskerm. (Of die Wieg van die Mensdom, met fossiele van vroeë voorouers.)","en":"**Johannesburg (Gauteng):** Constitution Hill – an old prison that is now the Constitutional Court, which protects our rights. (Or the Cradle of Humankind, with fossils of early ancestors.)"}],"answer":{"af":"Die Groot Gat (diamante), die Vredefort-koepel (meteoriet) en Konstitusieheuwel (vryheid en regte) of die Wieg van die Mensdom (fossiele).","en":"The Big Hole (diamonds), the Vredefort Dome (meteorite) and Constitution Hill (freedom and rights) or the Cradle of Humankind (fossils)."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter provinsie is Mapungubwe?","en":"In which province is Mapungubwe?"},"options":[{"af":"Mpumalanga","en":"Mpumalanga"},{"af":"Noordwes","en":"North West"},{"af":"Gauteng","en":"Gauteng"},{"af":"Limpopo","en":"Limpopo"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Mapungubwe lê in Limpopo, waar die Limpopo- en Shashe-rivier ontmoet, by die grense met Botswana en Zimbabwe.","en":"Mapungubwe lies in Limpopo, where the Limpopo and Shashe rivers meet, at the borders with Botswana and Zimbabwe."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Nelson Mandela was 18 jaar lank in die tronk op ___.","en":"Nelson Mandela spent 18 years in prison on ___."},"answers":{"af":["Robbeneiland"],"en":["Robben Island"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Konstitusieheuwel","Mapungubwe","Qunu"],"en":["Constitution Hill","Mapungubwe","Qunu"]}},"explain":{"af":"Mandela was 18 van sy 27 jaar in die tronk op Robbeneiland in Tafelbaai. Qunu is waar hy grootgeword het.","en":"Mandela spent 18 of his 27 years in prison on Robben Island in Table Bay. Qunu is where he grew up."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die Vredefort-koepel?","en":"What is the Vredefort Dome?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Ou tronk in Johannesburg","en":"An old prison in Johannesburg"},{"af":"’n Grot vol fossiele van vroeë voorouers","en":"A cave full of fossils of early ancestors"},{"af":"Die grootste bekende meteoriet-impakkrater op aarde","en":"The largest known meteorite impact crater on Earth"},{"af":"’n Diamantmyn wat met die hand gegrawe is","en":"A diamond mine that was dug by hand"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Sowat 2 000 miljoen jaar gelede het ’n reuse-meteoriet die aarde naby die huidige Parys in die Vrystaat getref. Die diamantmyn is die Groot Gat in Kimberley.","en":"About 2 000 million years ago a giant meteorite struck the Earth near present-day Parys in the Free State. The diamond mine is the Big Hole in Kimberley."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die Taung-skedel, wat in 1924 gevind is, het aan ’n jong kind behoort.","en":"The Taung Skull, found in 1924, belonged to a young child."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Daarom word dit die Taung-kind genoem. Professor Raymond Dart het gewys dat dit ’n baie vroeë voorouer van die mens was.","en":"True. That is why it is called the Taung Child. Professor Raymond Dart showed that it was a very early ancestor of humans."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is die Groot Gat in Kimberley ’n erfenisterrein?","en":"Why is the Big Hole in Kimberley a heritage site?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is met die hand vir diamante gegrawe en was die begin van groot mynbou","en":"It was dug by hand for diamonds and was the start of large-scale mining"},{"af":"Dit is die plek waar goud in 1886 vir die eerste keer ontdek is","en":"It is the place where gold was first discovered in 1886"},{"af":"Dit is ’n reuse-krater wat ’n meteoriet lank gelede gemaak het","en":"It is a giant crater that a meteorite made long ago"},{"af":"Dit is ’n ou koninklike graf waarin ’n goue renoster gevind is","en":"It is an old royal grave in which a golden rhino was found"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Duisende mense het van 1871 tot 1914 met grawe en pikke na diamante gegrawe. Goud is in 1886 aan die Witwatersrand ontdek, en die meteorietkrater is by Vredefort.","en":"Thousands of people dug for diamonds with spades and picks from 1871 to 1914. Gold was discovered on the Witwatersrand in 1886, and the meteorite crater is at Vredefort."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke erfenisterrein by sy provinsie.","en":"Match each heritage site to its province."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Robbeneiland","en":"Robben Island"},"r":{"af":"Wes-Kaap","en":"Western Cape"}},{"l":{"af":"Vredefort-koepel","en":"Vredefort Dome"},"r":{"af":"Vrystaat","en":"Free State"}},{"l":{"af":"Mapungubwe","en":"Mapungubwe"},"r":{"af":"Limpopo","en":"Limpopo"}},{"l":{"af":"Barberton Makhonjwa-berge","en":"Barberton Makhonjwa Mountains"},"r":{"af":"Mpumalanga","en":"Mpumalanga"}},{"l":{"af":"iSimangaliso-vleilandpark","en":"iSimangaliso Wetland Park"},"r":{"af":"KwaZulu-Natal","en":"KwaZulu-Natal"}}],"explain":{"af":"Gebruik die roete-tabel om terreine en provinsies te onthou. ’n Kaart van Suid-Afrika met die nege provinsies help ook.","en":"Use the route table to remember sites and provinces. A map of South Africa with the nine provinces also helps."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat vertel die goue renoster van Mapungubwe ons?","en":"What does the golden rhinoceros of Mapungubwe tell us?"},"options":[{"af":"Dat die mense van Mapungubwe renosters as vee aangehou het","en":"That the people of Mapungubwe kept rhinos as livestock"},{"af":"Dat die mense vaardige goudsmede was en die koning baie ryk was","en":"That the people were skilled goldsmiths and the king was very rich"},{"af":"Dat Europese handelaars Mapungubwe gebou en regeer het","en":"That European traders built and ruled Mapungubwe"},{"af":"Dat Mapungubwe ’n tronk vir politieke gevangenes was","en":"That Mapungubwe was a prison for political prisoners"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die renoster is van goud gemaak en in ’n koninklike graf gevind. Dit wys vaardigheid met goud en dat die koning en sy familie ryk en belangrik was.","en":"The rhino is made of gold and was found in a royal grave. It shows skill with gold and that the king and his family were rich and important."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die Wieg van die Mensdom, met die Sterkfontein-grotte, is in die provinsie ___.","en":"The Cradle of Humankind, with the Sterkfontein Caves, is in the province of ___."},"answers":{"af":["Gauteng"],"en":["Gauteng"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Limpopo","Vrystaat","Wes-Kaap"],"en":["Limpopo","Free State","Western Cape"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die Wieg van die Mensdom is in Gauteng, noordwes van Johannesburg. Daar is fossiele van vroeë voorouers gevind wat miljoene jare oud is.","en":"The Cradle of Humankind is in Gauteng, north-west of Johannesburg. Fossils of early ancestors that are millions of years old have been found there."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter erfenisterrein in die Noord-Kaap wys die erfenis van die Nama, wat nog met hul vee trek?","en":"Which heritage site in the Northern Cape shows the heritage of the Nama, who still move with their livestock?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Groot Gat","en":"The Big Hole"},{"af":"Die Richtersveld","en":"The Richtersveld"},{"af":"Robbeneiland","en":"Robben Island"},{"af":"Konstitusieheuwel","en":"Constitution Hill"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In die Richtersveld trek Nama-veewagters, afstammelinge van die Khoikhoi, nog met hul vee en woon in matjieshuise. Die Groot Gat is ook in die Noord-Kaap, maar dit gaan oor diamante.","en":"In the Richtersveld Nama herders, descendants of the Khoikhoi, still move with their livestock and live in mat houses. The Big Hole is also in the Northern Cape, but it is about diamonds."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die rotse van die Barberton Makhonjwa-berge is van die jongste rotse op aarde.","en":"The rocks of the Barberton Makhonjwa Mountains are among the youngest rocks on Earth."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Hulle is van die oudste rotse op aarde, meer as 3 000 miljoen jaar oud. Daarom is hulle ’n Wêrelderfenisterrein.","en":"False. They are among the oldest rocks on Earth, more than 3 000 million years old. That is why they are a World Heritage Site."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat staan vandag op Konstitusieheuwel in Johannesburg?","en":"What stands on Constitution Hill in Johannesburg today?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Konstitusionele Hof","en":"The Constitutional Court"},{"af":"Die Uniegebou","en":"The Union Buildings"},{"af":"Die Groot Gat","en":"The Big Hole"},{"af":"Die Sterkfontein-grotte","en":"The Sterkfontein Caves"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die ou tronk op Konstitusieheuwel is nou die tuiste van die Konstitusionele Hof, wat ons Grondwet en regte beskerm. Die Uniegebou is in Pretoria.","en":"The old prison on Constitution Hill is now home to the Constitutional Court, which protects our Constitution and rights. The Union Buildings are in Pretoria."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die isiZulu-woord *iSimangaliso* beteken ‘___’.","en":"The isiZulu word *iSimangaliso* means ‘___’."},"answers":{"af":["wonder","wonderwerk"],"en":["wonder","miracle"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["berg","rivier","see"],"en":["mountain","river","sea"]}},"explain":{"af":"iSimangaliso beteken ‘wonder’. Die park in KwaZulu-Natal het mere, moerasse, strande en koraalriwwe vol diere.","en":"iSimangaliso means ‘wonder’. The park in KwaZulu-Natal has lakes, swamps, beaches and coral reefs full of animals."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar is Nelson Mandela gebore?","en":"Where was Nelson Mandela born?"},"options":[{"af":"Op Robbeneiland","en":"On Robben Island"},{"af":"In Kimberley","en":"In Kimberley"},{"af":"In Mvezo in die Oos-Kaap","en":"In Mvezo in the Eastern Cape"},{"af":"In Johannesburg","en":"In Johannesburg"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Mandela is in 1918 in Mvezo gebore en het in Qunu grootgeword. Albei is in die Oos-Kaap, waar die Nelson Mandela-museum dele het. Hy was later op Robbeneiland in die tronk.","en":"Mandela was born in Mvezo in 1918 and grew up in Qunu. Both are in the Eastern Cape, where the Nelson Mandela Museum has parts. He was later imprisoned on Robben Island."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe het die samelewing by Mapungubwe van dié van die vroeë boere verskil?","en":"How was the society at Mapungubwe different from that of the early farmers?"},"options":[{"af":"Daar was geen leier nie, en almal in die nedersetting was ewe ryk","en":"There was no leader, and everyone in the settlement was equally rich"},{"af":"Die mense het net gejag en versamel en geen vee aangehou nie","en":"The people only hunted and gathered and kept no livestock"},{"af":"Die mense het in matjieshuise gewoon en met die seisoene getrek","en":"The people lived in mat houses and moved with the seasons"},{"af":"Die koning het bo-op die heuwel gewoon, apart van die gewone mense onder","en":"The king lived on top of the hill, apart from the ordinary people below"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"By Mapungubwe was daar ’n duidelike verskil tussen ryk en arm: die koning en sy familie het bo gewoon en is daar begrawe, terwyl die gewone mense onder gewoon het.","en":"At Mapungubwe there was a clear difference between rich and poor: the king and his family lived at the top and were buried there, while the ordinary people lived below."}}]}]}]},"lewensvaardighede":{"id":"lewensvaardighede","grade":5,"name":{"af":"Lewensvaardighede","en":"Life Skills"},"short":{"af":"LV","en":"LS"},"icon":"🌱","color":"#db2777","intro":{"af":"Lewensvaardighede (Persoonlike en Sosiale Welsyn) in Graad 5 help jou om jouself en ander beter te verstaan: selfbeeld, emosies en vriendskappe, veiligheid, kinderregte, respek tussen kulture en gelowe, en gesonde keuses vir jou liggaam. In die Novembereksamen kry jy gewoonlik kort vrae oor sleutelterme, en scenario’s (kort situasies) waarin jy moet sê wat iemand behoort te doen en waarom.","en":"Life Skills (Personal and Social Well-being) in Grade 5 helps you to understand yourself and others better: self-concept, emotions and friendships, safety, children’s rights, respect between cultures and religions, and healthy choices for your body. In the November exam you usually get short questions on key terms, and scenarios (short situations) in which you must say what someone should do and why."},"examTips":[{"af":"Leer die sleutelterme met hul betekenis – baie vrae begin met “Wat beteken …?” of “Noem ’n voorbeeld van …”.","en":"Learn the key terms with their meanings – many questions start with “What does … mean?” or “Give an example of …”."},{"af":"By ’n scenario-vraag: lees die situasie twee keer, sê wat die probleem is en gee dan ’n veilige, verantwoordelike oplossing.","en":"For a scenario question: read the situation twice, say what the problem is and then give a safe, responsible solution."},{"af":"Gee altyd ’n rede as die vraag “verduidelik” of “waarom” sê – skryf “… omdat …” in ’n volsin.","en":"Always give a reason when the question says “explain” or “why” – write “… because …” in a full sentence."},{"af":"Ken die belangrike hulpnommers: Childline 116 (gratis), polisie 10111, ambulans en brandweer 10177, en 112 van ’n selfoon.","en":"Know the important help numbers: Childline 116 (free), police 10111, ambulance and fire brigade 10177, and 112 from a cellphone."},{"af":"Kyk na die punte langs die vraag: 2 punte beteken gewoonlik twee feite, twee voorbeelde of ’n feit en ’n rede.","en":"Look at the marks next to the question: 2 marks usually means two facts, two examples, or a fact and a reason."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"DBE Reënboog-werkboeke","en":"DBE Rainbow Workbooks"},"url":"https://www.education.gov.za/Curriculum/Workbooks.aspx","note":{"af":"Die amptelike webblad van die Departement van Basiese Onderwys met gratis CAPS-werkboeke in Afrikaans en Engels. Kyk watter werkboeke vir Graad 5 beskikbaar is.","en":"The official Department of Basic Education page with free CAPS workbooks in Afrikaans and English. Check which workbooks are available for Grade 5."}},{"title":{"af":"Siyavula: oop handboeke en oefening","en":"Siyavula: open textbooks and practice"},"url":"https://www.siyavula.com","note":{"af":"Gratis oop handboeke en oefenvrae volgens CAPS. Kyk watter vakke en grade beskikbaar is.","en":"Free open textbooks and practice questions following CAPS. Check which subjects and grades are available."}}],"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Ontwikkeling van die self","en":"Development of the self"},"topics":[{"id":"lv5-t1-selfbeeld-higiene","title":{"af":"Positiewe selfbeeld en higiëne","en":"Positive self-concept and hygiene"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik wat ’n positiewe selfbeeld is, jou sterk punte en suksesse kan raaksien, ’n eenvoudige aksieplan vir ’n doelwit kan maak en kan sê hoe goeie higiëne jou gesond hou.","en":"You will be able to explain what a positive self-concept is, recognise your strengths and successes, make a simple action plan for a goal and say how good hygiene keeps you healthy."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is selfbeeld?\n\nJou **selfbeeld** is hoe jy oor jouself dink en voel – die prentjie van jouself wat jy in jou kop dra. Iemand met ’n **positiewe selfbeeld** weet: “Ek is nie perfek nie, maar ek is waardevol en ek kan leer.” Iemand met ’n **negatiewe selfbeeld** dink gou: “Ek kan niks reg doen nie.”\n\nJou selfbeeld is belangrik, want dit beïnvloed hoe jy optree. As jy in jouself glo, is jy meer bereid om iets nuuts te probeer, hulp te vra en weer te probeer as iets nie uitwerk nie.\n\nJou selfbeeld word gevorm deur:\n\n- wat jy oor jouself dink en sê\n- hoe jou gesin, vriende en onderwysers jou behandel\n- jou ervarings van sukses en mislukking\n\n## Jou sterk punte en suksesse\n\nElke mens het **sterk punte** (dinge waarin jy goed is) en dinge waarmee jy nog sukkel. Sterk punte is nie net punte op ’n rapport nie. Om goed te luister, mooi te teken, goed na diere om te sien of ander te help, is ook sterk punte.\n\n’n **Persoonlike sukses** is iets wat jy bereik het en waarop jy trots kan wees, groot of klein. Lerato het byvoorbeeld leer fietsry, en Pieter ken nou sy tafel van 7. As jy aan jou suksesse dink, onthou jy dat jy kan leer en groei.\n\nAktiwiteite wat jou selfbeeld bou:\n\n- iets nuuts leer, soos ’n sport of ’n musiekinstrument\n- iemand anders help\n- ’n stokperdjie beoefen waarvan jy hou\n- by ’n span, koor of klub aansluit\n- tyd saam met mense deurbring wat jou ondersteun\n\n## Positiewe selfpraatjies\n\n**Selfpraatjies** is die dinge wat jy in jou kop vir jouself sê. Negatiewe selfpraatjies maak jou moedeloos; positiewe selfpraatjies gee jou moed om aan te hou.\n\n| Negatiewe selfpraatjie | Positiewe selfpraatjie |\n|---|---|\n| “Ek is dom.” | “Ek verstaan dit nog nie, maar ek kan leer.” |\n| “Ek gaan sekerlik misluk.” | “Ek het voorberei en ek gaan my bes doen.” |\n| “Niemand hou van my nie.” | “Ek is ’n goeie vriend en ek kan nuwe vriende maak.” |\n\n> **Onthou:** ’n Fout maak jou nie ’n mislukking nie. Elke fout leer jou iets nuuts.\n\n## ’n Aksieplan vir ’n doelwit\n\n’n **Doelwit** is iets wat jy wil bereik. ’n **Aksieplan** is die stappe wat jy sal volg om dit te bereik. Wanneer jy jou doelwit bereik, voel jy trots – en dit bou jou selfbeeld.\n\n1. Skryf jou doelwit duidelik neer, bv. “Ek wil my tafels van 6 tot 9 teen die einde van die kwartaal ken.”\n2. Breek dit op in klein stappe, bv. een tafel per week.\n3. Besluit wanneer jy elke stap sal doen.\n4. Besluit wie jou kan help.\n5. Kyk gereeld hoe dit gaan en vier jou vordering.\n\n## Higiëne: sorg vir jou liggaam\n\n**Higiëne** beteken om jou liggaam en jou goed skoon te hou sodat jy gesond bly. **Kieme** is so klein dat jy hulle nie kan sien nie, maar hulle kan siektes soos verkoue, griep en diarree versprei. As jy skoon en vars is, voel jy ook gemakliker tussen ander mense – en dit help jou selfbeeld.\n\n- **Hande was:** met seep en skoon water, ten minste 20 sekondes lank, voor jy eet en ná die toilet.\n- **Tande:** borsel twee keer per dag, soggens en voor jy gaan slaap. Dit help keer dat jy gaatjies en slegte asem kry.\n- **Bad of stort:** elke dag, veral ná sport. Soos jy ouer word, sweet jy meer.\n- **Skoon klere:** trek elke dag skoon onderklere en sokkies aan.\n- **Hare:** was en kam jou hare gereeld. As jy luise kry, sê vir ’n volwassene.\n- **Naels:** hou hulle kort en skoon, want kieme skuil onder vuil naels.\n\nMoenie jou tandeborsel, kam of handdoek met ander deel nie, want so versprei kieme en luise.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om jou hande net vinnig met water af te spoel, is nie genoeg nie. Jy het **seep** nodig om die kieme los te maak, en jy moet ook tussen jou vingers en onder jou naels skrop.","en":"## What is self-concept?\n\nYour **self-concept** is how you think and feel about yourself – the picture of yourself that you carry in your head. Someone with a **positive self-concept** knows: “I am not perfect, but I am valuable and I can learn.” Someone with a **negative self-concept** quickly thinks: “I can’t do anything right.”\n\nYour self-concept is important because it affects how you behave. If you believe in yourself, you are more willing to try something new, to ask for help and to try again when something does not work out.\n\nYour self-concept is shaped by:\n\n- what you think and say about yourself\n- how your family, friends and teachers treat you\n- your experiences of success and failure\n\n## Your strengths and successes\n\nEvery person has **strengths** (things you are good at) and things they still struggle with. Strengths are not only marks on a report card. Listening well, drawing beautifully, caring well for animals or helping others are also strengths.\n\nA **personal success** is something you have achieved and can be proud of, big or small. For example, Lerato learnt to ride a bicycle, and Pieter now knows his 7 times table. When you think about your successes, you remember that you can learn and grow.\n\nActivities that build your self-concept:\n\n- learning something new, like a sport or a musical instrument\n- helping someone else\n- doing a hobby you enjoy\n- joining a team, choir or club\n- spending time with people who support you\n\n## Positive self-talk\n\n**Self-talk** is the things you say to yourself in your head. Negative self-talk makes you lose heart; positive self-talk gives you the courage to keep going.\n\n| Negative self-talk | Positive self-talk |\n|---|---|\n| “I am stupid.” | “I don’t understand it yet, but I can learn.” |\n| “I am definitely going to fail.” | “I have prepared and I am going to do my best.” |\n| “Nobody likes me.” | “I am a good friend and I can make new friends.” |\n\n> **Remember:** A mistake does not make you a failure. Every mistake teaches you something new.\n\n## An action plan for a goal\n\nA **goal** is something you want to achieve. An **action plan** is the steps you will follow to achieve it. When you reach your goal, you feel proud – and that builds your self-concept.\n\n1. Write your goal down clearly, e.g. “I want to know my 6 to 9 times tables by the end of the term.”\n2. Break it up into small steps, e.g. one times table per week.\n3. Decide when you will do each step.\n4. Decide who can help you.\n5. Check regularly how it is going and celebrate your progress.\n\n## Hygiene: caring for your body\n\n**Hygiene** means keeping your body and your things clean so that you stay healthy. **Germs** are so small that you cannot see them, but they can spread illnesses like colds, flu and diarrhoea. When you are clean and fresh, you also feel more comfortable around other people – and that helps your self-concept.\n\n- **Washing hands:** with soap and clean water, for at least 20 seconds, before you eat and after using the toilet.\n- **Teeth:** brush twice a day, in the morning and before you go to sleep. This helps to stop holes in your teeth and bad breath.\n- **Bath or shower:** every day, especially after sport. As you get older, you sweat more.\n- **Clean clothes:** put on clean underwear and socks every day.\n- **Hair:** wash and comb your hair regularly. If you get lice, tell an adult.\n- **Nails:** keep them short and clean, because germs hide under dirty nails.\n\nDon’t share your toothbrush, comb or towel with others, because that is how germs and lice spread.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Quickly rinsing your hands with water only is not enough. You need **soap** to loosen the germs, and you must also scrub between your fingers and under your nails."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Selfbeeld","en":"Self-concept"},"def":{"af":"Hoe jy oor jouself dink en voel; die prentjie van jouself wat jy in jou kop dra.","en":"How you think and feel about yourself; the picture of yourself that you carry in your head."}},{"term":{"af":"Positiewe selfbeeld","en":"Positive self-concept"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer jy weet dat jy waardevol is en kan leer, al is jy nie perfek nie.","en":"When you know that you are valuable and can learn, even though you are not perfect."}},{"term":{"af":"Sterk punt","en":"Strength"},"def":{"af":"Iets waarin jy goed is, soos sport, teken, luister of ander help.","en":"Something you are good at, such as sport, drawing, listening or helping others."}},{"term":{"af":"Persoonlike sukses","en":"Personal success"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat jy bereik het en waarop jy trots kan wees, of dit groot of klein is.","en":"Something you have achieved and can be proud of, whether it is big or small."}},{"term":{"af":"Selfpraatjies","en":"Self-talk"},"def":{"af":"Die dinge wat jy in jou kop vir jouself sê; dit kan positief of negatief wees.","en":"The things you say to yourself in your head; it can be positive or negative."}},{"term":{"af":"Doelwit","en":"Goal"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat jy wil bereik, soos ’n nuwe vaardigheid of ’n beter punt.","en":"Something you want to achieve, such as a new skill or a better mark."}},{"term":{"af":"Aksieplan","en":"Action plan"},"def":{"af":"’n Lys klein stappe, met tye en helpers, wat jy volg om ’n doelwit te bereik.","en":"A list of small steps, with times and helpers, that you follow to reach a goal."}},{"term":{"af":"Higiëne","en":"Hygiene"},"def":{"af":"Om jou liggaam en jou goed skoon te hou sodat jy gesond bly.","en":"Keeping your body and your things clean so that you stay healthy."}},{"term":{"af":"Kieme","en":"Germs"},"def":{"af":"Baie klein dingetjies, soos bakterieë en virusse, wat jy nie kan sien nie en wat siektes kan versprei.","en":"Very tiny things, such as bacteria and viruses, that you cannot see and that can spread illness."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Verander negatiewe selfpraatjies","en":"Change negative self-talk"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho kry 9 uit 20 vir sy speltoets. Hy sê vir homself: “Ek is dom. Ek sal nooit kan spel nie.” Herskryf dit as positiewe selfpraatjies en noem twee dinge wat hy kan doen.","en":"Sipho gets 9 out of 20 for his spelling test. He tells himself: “I am stupid. I will never be able to spell.” Rewrite this as positive self-talk and name two things he can do."},"steps":[{"af":"Herken die negatiewe selfpraatjie: “Ek is dom” is ’n etiket wat nie waar is nie. Een swak toets wys net dat hy nog nie al die woorde ken nie.","en":"Recognise the negative self-talk: “I am stupid” is a label that is not true. One poor test only shows that he does not know all the words yet."},{"af":"Vervang dit met iets wat waar is én moed gee, bv. “Ek ken nog nie al die woorde nie, maar as ek oefen, sal ek beter doen.”","en":"Replace it with something that is true and gives courage, e.g. “I don’t know all the words yet, but if I practise, I will do better.”"},{"af":"Dink aan aksie: hy kan elke dag 10 minute lank sy woorde oefen, en hy kan sy onderwyser of ’n ouer vra om hom te toets.","en":"Think of action: he can practise his words for 10 minutes every day, and he can ask his teacher or a parent to test him."}],"answer":{"af":"“Ek ken dit nog nie, maar ek kan leer as ek oefen.” Hy kan elke dag oefen en iemand vra om hom te toets.","en":"“I don’t know it yet, but I can learn if I practise.” He can practise every day and ask someone to test him."}},{"title":{"af":"Maak ’n aksieplan","en":"Make an action plan"},"problem":{"af":"Aisha wil teen die einde van die kwartaal 25 m in die swembad kan swem sonder om te stop. Op die oomblik kan sy net 5 m swem. Maak ’n eenvoudige aksieplan vir haar.","en":"Aisha wants to be able to swim 25 m in the swimming pool without stopping by the end of the term. At the moment she can swim only 5 m. Make a simple action plan for her."},"steps":[{"af":"Skryf die doelwit duidelik neer: “Ek wil teen die einde van die kwartaal 25 m sonder stop kan swem.”","en":"Write the goal down clearly: “I want to be able to swim 25 m without stopping by the end of the term.”"},{"af":"Breek dit op in klein stappe: eers 10 m, dan 15 m, dan 20 m en laastens 25 m.","en":"Break it up into small steps: first 10 m, then 15 m, then 20 m and finally 25 m."},{"af":"Besluit wanneer: twee keer per week ná skool by swemoefening.","en":"Decide when: twice a week after school at swimming practice."},{"af":"Besluit wie kan help: die swemafrigter of ’n ouer by die swembad.","en":"Decide who can help: the swimming coach or a parent at the pool."},{"af":"Kyk elke week hoe ver sy kan swem en vier elke nuwe afstand wat sy haal.","en":"Check every week how far she can swim and celebrate each new distance she reaches."}],"answer":{"af":"Duidelike doelwit → klein stappe (10 m; 15 m; 20 m; 25 m) → twee keer per week oefen → afrigter of ouer help → elke week vordering nagaan en vier.","en":"Clear goal → small steps (10 m, 15 m, 20 m, 25 m) → practise twice a week → coach or parent helps → check and celebrate progress every week."}},{"title":{"af":"Higiënefoute raaksien","en":"Spot the hygiene mistakes"},"problem":{"af":"Liam kom van sokkeroefening af. Hy eet dadelik ’n toebroodjie sonder om sy hande te was. Hy stort nie en trek nie skoon klere aan nie, en hy gaan slaap sonder om sy tande te borsel. Noem drie higiënefoute en verduidelik waarom elkeen saak maak.","en":"Liam comes home from soccer practice. He immediately eats a sandwich without washing his hands. He does not shower or put on clean clothes, and he goes to sleep without brushing his teeth. Name three hygiene mistakes and explain why each one matters."},"steps":[{"af":"Fout 1: Hy was nie sy hande voor hy eet nie. Kieme van die bal en die grond kan saam met die kos in sy mond beland en hom siek maak.","en":"Mistake 1: He does not wash his hands before he eats. Germs from the ball and the ground can end up in his mouth with the food and make him sick."},{"af":"Fout 2: Hy stort nie en trek nie skoon klere aan ná sport nie. Sweet en vuil klere begin sleg ruik en kan sy vel laat jeuk.","en":"Mistake 2: He does not shower or put on clean clothes after sport. Sweat and dirty clothes start to smell bad and can make his skin itch."},{"af":"Fout 3: Hy borsel nie sy tande voor hy gaan slaap nie. Kos wat die hele nag aan sy tande bly sit, help om gaatjies en slegte asem te veroorsaak.","en":"Mistake 3: He does not brush his teeth before he goes to sleep. Food that stays on his teeth all night helps to cause holes in his teeth and bad breath."}],"answer":{"af":"Hy moet sy hande met seep was voor hy eet, ná sport stort en skoon klere aantrek, en voor slaaptyd sy tande borsel.","en":"He must wash his hands with soap before eating, shower and put on clean clothes after sport, and brush his teeth before bedtime."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken selfbeeld?","en":"What does self-concept mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Hoe jy oor jouself dink en voel","en":"How you think and feel about yourself"},{"af":"Hoe jy in ’n spieël lyk","en":"How you look in a mirror"},{"af":"Die punte op jou rapport","en":"The marks on your report card"},{"af":"Hoeveel vriende jy het","en":"How many friends you have"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Selfbeeld is die prentjie van jouself in jou kop – hoe jy oor jouself dink en voel. Jou voorkoms, punte en vriende kan dit beïnvloed, maar hulle is nie self jou selfbeeld nie.","en":"Self-concept is the picture of yourself in your head – how you think and feel about yourself. Your looks, marks and friends can affect it, but they are not your self-concept itself."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n voorbeeld van positiewe selfpraatjies?","en":"Which one is an example of positive self-talk?"},"options":[{"af":"“Ek is te dom vir wiskunde.”","en":"“I am too stupid for maths.”"},{"af":"“Ek probeer nie, want ek sal tog misluk.”","en":"“I won’t try, because I will fail anyway.”"},{"af":"“Dis moeilik, maar as ek oefen, sal ek beter word.”","en":"“It’s hard, but if I practise, I will get better.”"},{"af":"“Die ander is almal baie beter as ek.”","en":"“The others are all much better than me.”"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Positiewe selfpraatjies is eerlik én gee moed: dit erken dat iets moeilik is, maar sê dat jy kan verbeter. Die ander drie sinne maak jou moedeloos.","en":"Positive self-talk is honest and gives courage: it admits that something is hard, but says that you can improve. The other three sentences make you lose heart."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Jy het net sterk punte as jy goeie punte op skool kry.","en":"You only have strengths if you get good marks at school."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Sterk punte is dinge waarin jy goed is, soos luister, teken, sport, sing of ander help. Goeie punte op ’n rapport is net een soort sterk punt.","en":"False. Strengths are things you are good at, such as listening, drawing, sport, singing or helping others. Good marks on a report card are only one kind of strength."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die klein stappe wat jy beplan om ’n doelwit te bereik, vorm saam jou ___.","en":"The small steps you plan in order to reach a goal together make up your ___."},"answers":{"af":["aksieplan"],"en":["action plan"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["selfbeeld","selfpraatjies","sterk punt"],"en":["self-concept","self-talk","strength"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Aksieplan sê presies wat jy gaan doen, wanneer en wie jou kan help. Die doelwit is wat jy wil bereik; die aksieplan is die pad daarheen.","en":"An action plan says exactly what you are going to do, when, and who can help you. The goal is what you want to achieve; the action plan is the road to get there."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom moet jy ná die toilet jou hande met seep was?","en":"Why must you wash your hands with soap after using the toilet?"},"options":[{"af":"Sodat jou hande nie droog word nie","en":"So that your hands don’t get dry"},{"af":"Om kieme te verwyder wat siektes kan versprei","en":"To remove germs that can spread illness"},{"af":"Want water alleen maak al die kieme dood","en":"Because water on its own kills all the germs"},{"af":"Sodat jou hande lekker ruik vir ander","en":"So that your hands smell nice to others"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Kieme van die toilet kan diarree en ander siektes versprei. Seep maak die kieme los sodat die water hulle kan wegspoel. Water alleen is nie genoeg nie.","en":"Germs from the toilet can spread diarrhoea and other illnesses. Soap loosens the germs so that the water can wash them away. Water on its own is not enough."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke higiënegewoonte by die rede daarvoor.","en":"Match each hygiene habit to the reason for it."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Tande borsel","en":"Brushing your teeth"},"r":{"af":"Help keer dat jy gaatjies en slegte asem kry","en":"Helps to stop holes in your teeth and bad breath"}},{"l":{"af":"Hande was voor ete","en":"Washing hands before meals"},"r":{"af":"Hou kieme uit jou mond uit","en":"Keeps germs out of your mouth"}},{"l":{"af":"Elke dag skoon onderklere","en":"Clean underwear every day"},"r":{"af":"Keer dat sweet en vuil klere sleg ruik","en":"Stops sweat and dirty clothes from smelling bad"}},{"l":{"af":"Naels kort en skoon hou","en":"Keeping nails short and clean"},"r":{"af":"Kieme kan nie onder vuil naels wegkruip nie","en":"Germs cannot hide under dirty nails"}},{"l":{"af":"Net jou eie kam gebruik","en":"Using only your own comb"},"r":{"af":"Keer dat luise van kop tot kop versprei","en":"Stops lice from spreading from head to head"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke gewoonte keer ’n spesifieke probleem: borsel teen gaatjies, handewas teen kieme in jou mond, skoon klere teen ’n slegte reuk, kort naels sodat kieme nie kan wegkruip nie en jou eie kam teen luise.","en":"Each habit prevents a specific problem: brushing against holes in your teeth, handwashing against germs in your mouth, clean clothes against a bad smell, short nails so germs cannot hide and your own comb against lice."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Johan sê hy het geen sterk punte nie, want hy is nie goed in sport nie. Watter stelling is waar?","en":"Johan says he has no strengths because he is not good at sport. Which statement is true?"},"options":[{"af":"Net sportmense het sterk punte","en":"Only sportspeople have strengths"},{"af":"Sterk punte is net punte op ’n rapport","en":"Strengths are only marks on a report card"},{"af":"Jy word met al jou sterk punte gebore","en":"You are born with all your strengths"},{"af":"Vriendelikheid, teken en luister is ook sterk punte","en":"Kindness, drawing and listening are also strengths"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Elke mens het sterk punte, en hulle lyk nie almal dieselfde nie. Johan is dalk ’n goeie vriend, ’n kunstenaar of ’n goeie luisteraar. Jy kan ook nuwe sterk punte ontwikkel deur te oefen – jy word nie met almal gebore nie.","en":"Every person has strengths, and they don’t all look the same. Johan may be a good friend, an artist or a good listener. You can also develop new strengths by practising – you are not born with all of them."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Jy moet jou tande ___ keer per dag borsel.","en":"You should brush your teeth ___ times a day."},"answers":{"af":["twee","2"],"en":["two","2"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["een","vier","ses"],"en":["one","four","six"]}},"explain":{"af":"Borsel soggens en voor jy gaan slaap – dit is twee keer per dag. Die borsel voor slaaptyd is baie belangrik, want kos wat die hele nag aan jou tande sit, help om gaatjies te veroorsaak.","en":"Brush in the morning and before you go to sleep – that is twice a day. Brushing before bedtime is very important, because food that stays on your teeth all night helps to cause holes."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Positiewe selfpraatjies kan jou help om weer te probeer nadat jy ’n fout gemaak het.","en":"Positive self-talk can help you to try again after you have made a mistake."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. As jy vir jouself sê “Elke fout leer my iets”, gee dit jou moed om aan te hou in plaas daarvan om op te gee.","en":"True. If you tell yourself “Every mistake teaches me something”, it gives you the courage to keep going instead of giving up."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter aktiwiteit sal die meeste help om jou selfbeeld te bou?","en":"Which activity will help most to build your self-concept?"},"options":[{"af":"Jouself heeltyd met ander vergelyk","en":"Comparing yourself with others all the time"},{"af":"Wegbly van enigiets wat nuut is","en":"Staying away from anything that is new"},{"af":"’n Nuwe vaardigheid leer en oefen","en":"Learning and practising a new skill"},{"af":"Vir jouself sê dat jy nutteloos is","en":"Telling yourself that you are useless"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"As jy iets nuuts leer en sien hoe jy verbeter, voel jy trots en bekwaam. Om jouself heeltyd met ander te vergelyk, nuwe dinge te vermy of jouself af te kraak, laat jou slegter oor jouself voel.","en":"When you learn something new and see yourself improve, you feel proud and capable. Constantly comparing yourself with others, avoiding new things or putting yourself down makes you feel worse about yourself."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Zanele kry 4 uit 10 vir ’n toets. Watter reaksie wys ’n positiewe selfbeeld?","en":"Zanele gets 4 out of 10 for a test. Which reaction shows a positive self-concept?"},"options":[{"af":"“Ek gaan kyk wat ek verkeerd gedoen het en my onderwyser vra om te help.”","en":"“I’m going to look at what I got wrong and ask my teacher to help.”"},{"af":"“Ek is net nie slim genoeg vir skool nie.”","en":"“I’m just not clever enough for school.”"},{"af":"“Die toets was onregverdig, so dit maak nie saak nie.”","en":"“The test was unfair, so it doesn’t matter.”"},{"af":"“Ek sê vir niemand nie en vergeet sommer daarvan.”","en":"“I won’t tell anyone and I’ll just forget about it.”"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Iemand met ’n positiewe selfbeeld sien ’n swak punt as ’n kans om te leer. Zanele neem verantwoordelikheid en vra hulp. Om jouself af te kraak, ander te blameer of dit weg te steek, help haar nie om te verbeter nie.","en":"Someone with a positive self-concept sees a poor mark as a chance to learn. Zanele takes responsibility and asks for help. Putting yourself down, blaming others or hiding it does not help her to improve."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Baie klein dingetjies wat jy nie kan sien nie en wat siektes versprei, heet ___.","en":"Very tiny things that you cannot see and that spread illness are called ___."},"answers":{"af":["kieme"],"en":["germs"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["selle","vitamiene","minerale"],"en":["cells","vitamins","minerals"]}},"explain":{"af":"Kieme, soos bakterieë en virusse, versprei siektes soos verkoue en diarree. Daarom is handewas met seep so belangrik. Vitamiene en minerale is goeie stowwe in kos wat jou gesond hou.","en":"Germs, such as bacteria and viruses, spread illnesses like colds and diarrhoea. That is why washing your hands with soap is so important. Vitamins and minerals are good substances in food that keep you healthy."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ravi wil hierdie kwartaal vyf biblioteekboeke lees. Wat moet die eerste stap in sy aksieplan wees?","en":"Ravi wants to read five library books this term. What should the first step in his action plan be?"},"options":[{"af":"Wag tot die laaste week van die kwartaal","en":"Wait until the last week of the term"},{"af":"Vir almal sê hy is klaar voor hy begin","en":"Tell everyone he has finished before he starts"},{"af":"’n Makliker doelwit kies sodat hy nie hoef te probeer nie","en":"Choose an easier goal so that he doesn’t have to try"},{"af":"Sy doelwit duidelik neerskryf en in klein stappe opbreek","en":"Write his goal down clearly and break it into small steps"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Aksieplan begin met ’n duidelike doelwit en klein stappe, bv. een boek elke twee weke. As hy tot die einde wag, sal hy nie genoeg tyd hê nie.","en":"An action plan starts with a clear goal and small steps, e.g. one book every two weeks. If he waits until the end, he will not have enough time."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe kan goeie higiëne ook jou selfbeeld help?","en":"How can good hygiene also help your self-concept?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit maak jou slimmer as ander kinders","en":"It makes you cleverer than other children"},{"af":"Jy voel vars en gemaklik tussen ander mense","en":"You feel fresh and comfortable around other people"},{"af":"Dit beteken jy sal nooit weer siek word nie","en":"It means you will never get sick again"},{"af":"Dan moet almal outomaties van jou hou","en":"Then everyone has to like you automatically"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"As jy skoon en vars is, voel jy goed oor jouself en is jy meer selfversekerd. Higiëne verminder die kans op siekte, maar dit beteken nie dat jy nooit siek sal word nie.","en":"When you are clean and fresh, you feel good about yourself and you are more confident. Hygiene lowers the chance of illness, but it does not mean you will never get sick."}}]},{"id":"lv5-t1-terugvoering-emosies","title":{"af":"Terugvoering gee en emosies hanteer","en":"Giving feedback and managing emotions"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal op ’n positiewe, respekvolle manier terugvoering kan gee en ontvang, verskillende emosies kan herken en gesonde maniere kan kies om dit te hanteer.","en":"You will be able to give and receive feedback in a positive, respectful way, recognise different emotions and choose healthy ways to manage them."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is terugvoering?\n\n**Terugvoering** is wanneer iemand vir jou sê wat hulle van jou werk of jou optrede dink, sodat jy kan sien wat goed gaan en wat jy kan verbeter. Jy gee ook terugvoering vir ander, byvoorbeeld wanneer julle in ’n groep werk of mekaar se stories lees.\n\nGoeie terugvoering is:\n\n- **positief** – dit begin by wat goed is en wys hoe om te groei\n- **respekvol** – dit kraak nie die persoon af nie\n- **spesifiek** – dit sê presies wat jy bedoel\n\n“Dis sleg” help niemand nie. “Jou plakkaat sal beter uitstaan as jy die agtergrond inkleur” help wel.\n\n## Die terugvoeringtoebroodjie\n\n’n Maklike manier om terugvoering te gee, is die **toebroodjiemetode**. Net soos ’n toebroodjie twee snye brood met vulsel in die middel het, sit jy jou voorstel tussen twee positiewe dinge.\n\n| Deel van die toebroodjie | Wat jy sê | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Boonste sny brood | Prys iets wat goed is | “Jou storie het ’n baie spannende begin.” |\n| Vulsel | Gee ’n voorstel | “Jy kan dalk meer vertel van hoe die hond lyk.” |\n| Onderste sny brood | Bemoedig | “Ek wil graag weet wat volgende gebeur!” |\n\nWanneer jy terugvoering **ontvang**:\n\n- luister tot die einde sonder om te onderbreek\n- moenie dadelik kwaad word of jouself verdedig nie\n- vra ’n vraag as jy iets nie verstaan nie\n- sê dankie en dink na oor wat jy kan gebruik\n\n> **Onthou:** Terugvoering gaan oor die **werk** of die **gedrag**, nie oor die persoon nie. Sê “Hierdie sin is te lank” en nie “Jy is ’n swak skrywer” nie.\n\n## Ons emosies\n\n**Emosies** (gevoelens) is natuurlik. Almal voel soms bly, hartseer, kwaad, bang, jaloers of skaam. Geen emosie is “verkeerd” nie, maar wat jy **doen** met jou emosie, kan goed of sleg wees. Jou liggaam wys jou dikwels hoe jy voel: as jy kwaad is, klop jou hart vinniger en word jou gesig warm; as jy bang is, kry jy dalk ’n knop op die maag.\n\n| Emosie | Wanneer jy dit kan voel |\n|---|---|\n| Bly | Jy word vir die span gekies. |\n| Hartseer | Jou troeteldier is dood. |\n| Kwaad | Iemand het jou boek geskeur. |\n| Bang | Jy moet alleen deur ’n donker gang loop. |\n| Jaloers | Jou vriendin speel net met die nuwe meisie. |\n| Skaam | Jy val voor die hele klas. |\n\n## Gesonde maniere om emosies te hanteer\n\nWanneer ’n sterk gevoel jou oorval, kan jy die volgende probeer:\n\n1. **Haal diep asem:** asem stadig deur jou neus in en blaas stadig deur jou mond uit. Doen dit ’n paar keer.\n2. **Tel tot tien** voordat jy praat of iets doen.\n3. **Praat** met ’n vertroude volwassene of ’n goeie vriend.\n4. **Skryf of teken** hoe jy voel, byvoorbeeld in ’n dagboek.\n5. **Beweeg:** gaan stap, hardloop of speel buite. Oefening help jou liggaam om te kalmeer.\n6. **Gebruik ’n ek-boodskap:** “Ek voel kwaad wanneer jy my goed vat sonder om te vra.”\n\nDinge wat **nie help nie**:\n\n- slaan, skop of goed stukkend maak\n- skree of iemand uitskel\n- jou gevoelens altyd wegsteek en alleen sit en tob\n- iemand seermaak omdat jy jaloers is\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Baie kinders dink ’n mens mag nooit kwaad of hartseer voel nie. Dit is nie waar nie. Die gevoel is in orde – dit is net belangrik dat jy dit op ’n veilige manier wys, sonder om jouself of ander seer te maak.","en":"## What is feedback?\n\n**Feedback** is when someone tells you what they think of your work or your behaviour, so that you can see what is going well and what you can improve. You also give feedback to others, for example when you work in a group or read each other’s stories.\n\nGood feedback is:\n\n- **positive** – it starts with what is good and shows how to grow\n- **respectful** – it does not put the person down\n- **specific** – it says exactly what you mean\n\n“It’s bad” helps nobody. “Your poster will stand out more if you colour in the background” does help.\n\n## The feedback sandwich\n\nAn easy way to give feedback is the **sandwich method**. Just as a sandwich has two slices of bread with a filling in the middle, you put your suggestion between two positive things.\n\n| Part of the sandwich | What you say | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Top slice of bread | Praise something that is good | “Your story has a very exciting beginning.” |\n| Filling | Give a suggestion | “Maybe you can tell more about what the dog looks like.” |\n| Bottom slice of bread | Encourage | “I really want to know what happens next!” |\n\nWhen you **receive** feedback:\n\n- listen to the end without interrupting\n- don’t get angry straight away or defend yourself\n- ask a question if you don’t understand something\n- say thank you and think about what you can use\n\n> **Remember:** Feedback is about the **work** or the **behaviour**, not about the person. Say “This sentence is too long” and not “You are a bad writer”.\n\n## Our emotions\n\n**Emotions** (feelings) are natural. Everybody sometimes feels happy, sad, angry, scared, jealous or embarrassed. No emotion is “wrong”, but what you **do** with your emotion can be good or bad. Your body often shows you how you feel: when you are angry, your heart beats faster and your face gets hot; when you are scared, you may get a knot in your stomach.\n\n| Emotion | When you might feel it |\n|---|---|\n| Happy | You are chosen for the team. |\n| Sad | Your pet has died. |\n| Angry | Someone has torn your book. |\n| Scared | You have to walk alone down a dark passage. |\n| Jealous | Your friend only plays with the new girl. |\n| Embarrassed | You fall in front of the whole class. |\n\n## Healthy ways to manage emotions\n\nWhen a strong feeling washes over you, you can try the following:\n\n1. **Take deep breaths:** breathe in slowly through your nose and blow out slowly through your mouth. Do this a few times.\n2. **Count to ten** before you speak or do something.\n3. **Talk** to a trusted adult or a good friend.\n4. **Write or draw** how you feel, for example in a diary.\n5. **Move:** go for a walk, run or play outside. Exercise helps your body to calm down.\n6. **Use an I-message:** “I feel angry when you take my things without asking.”\n\nThings that **do not help**:\n\n- hitting, kicking or breaking things\n- shouting or calling someone names\n- always hiding your feelings and sitting alone and brooding\n- hurting someone because you are jealous\n\n> **Common mistake:** Many children think you are never allowed to feel angry or sad. That is not true. The feeling is fine – it is just important to show it in a safe way, without hurting yourself or others."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Terugvoering","en":"Feedback"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer iemand vir jou sê wat goed gaan en wat jy kan verbeter in jou werk of gedrag.","en":"When someone tells you what is going well and what you can improve in your work or behaviour."}},{"term":{"af":"Toebroodjiemetode","en":"Sandwich method"},"def":{"af":"’n Manier om terugvoering te gee: eers prys, dan ’n voorstel, en dan bemoediging.","en":"A way of giving feedback: first praise, then a suggestion, and then encouragement."}},{"term":{"af":"Respekvol","en":"Respectful"},"def":{"af":"Om iemand vriendelik en regverdig te behandel, sonder om hulle af te kraak.","en":"Treating someone kindly and fairly, without putting them down."}},{"term":{"af":"Emosie","en":"Emotion"},"def":{"af":"’n Gevoel binne-in jou, soos blydskap, hartseer, woede of vrees.","en":"A feeling inside you, such as happiness, sadness, anger or fear."}},{"term":{"af":"Jaloers","en":"Jealous"},"def":{"af":"Die gevoel wanneer jy iets wil hê wat ’n ander het, of bang is om iemand se aandag te verloor.","en":"The feeling when you want something that someone else has, or are afraid of losing someone’s attention."}},{"term":{"af":"Skaam","en":"Embarrassed"},"def":{"af":"Die ongemaklike gevoel wanneer jy dink ander lag vir jou of kyk na jou ná ’n fout.","en":"The uncomfortable feeling when you think others are laughing at you or looking at you after a mistake."}},{"term":{"af":"Ek-boodskap","en":"I-message"},"def":{"af":"’n Sin wat sê hoe jy voel en waarom, sonder om die ander persoon te beskuldig, bv. “Ek voel hartseer wanneer …”","en":"A sentence that says how you feel and why, without blaming the other person, e.g. “I feel sad when …”"}},{"term":{"af":"Selfbeheersing","en":"Self-control"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer jy jou gevoelens voel, maar self besluit hoe jy optree, sonder om ander seer te maak.","en":"When you feel your feelings but decide for yourself how to act, without hurting others."}},{"term":{"af":"Vertroude volwassene","en":"Trusted adult"},"def":{"af":"’n Grootmens wat jou veilig laat voel, na jou luister en jou sal help.","en":"A grown-up who makes you feel safe, listens to you and will help you."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Gee toebroodjie-terugvoering","en":"Give sandwich feedback"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo het ’n plakkaat oor waterbesparing gemaak. Die tekening van ’n kraan is pragtig, maar die woorde is so klein dat ’n mens hulle van agter in die klas nie kan lees nie. Skryf vir Anika ’n terugvoeringtoebroodjie wat sy vir Thabo kan gee.","en":"Thabo made a poster about saving water. The drawing of a tap is beautiful, but the words are so small that you cannot read them from the back of the class. Write a feedback sandwich that Anika can give to Thabo."},"steps":[{"af":"**Boonste sny – prys:** Begin met iets wat regtig goed is en wees spesifiek: “Jou tekening van die kraan is pragtig en baie duidelik.”","en":"**Top slice – praise:** Start with something that is really good and be specific: “Your drawing of the tap is beautiful and very clear.”"},{"af":"**Vulsel – voorstel:** Sê wat kan verbeter, oor die werk en nie oor Thabo nie: “As jy die woorde groter skryf, sal almal dit van ver af kan lees.”","en":"**Filling – suggestion:** Say what can improve, about the work and not about Thabo: “If you write the words bigger, everyone will be able to read them from far away.”"},{"af":"**Onderste sny – bemoediging:** Eindig positief: “Jou plakkaat gaan mense regtig laat dink oor water spaar!”","en":"**Bottom slice – encouragement:** End positively: “Your poster is really going to make people think about saving water!”"}],"answer":{"af":"“Jou tekening van die kraan is pragtig. As jy die woorde groter skryf, sal almal dit kan lees. Jou plakkaat gaan mense regtig laat dink oor water spaar!”","en":"“Your drawing of the tap is beautiful. If you write the words bigger, everyone will be able to read them. Your poster is really going to make people think about saving water!”"}},{"title":{"af":"Ontvang terugvoering goed","en":"Receive feedback well"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter se onderwyser sê: “Jou opstel het goeie idees, maar dit het geen paragrawe nie, so dit is moeilik om te lees.” Pieter wil uitroep: “Dis nie regverdig nie!” Wat behoort hy eerder te doen?","en":"Pieter’s teacher says: “Your essay has good ideas, but it has no paragraphs, so it is hard to read.” Pieter wants to shout: “That’s not fair!” What should he rather do?"},"steps":[{"af":"**Luister tot die einde** en haal diep asem voordat hy antwoord. Die onderwyser het eers iets goeds gesê – sy idees is goed.","en":"**Listen to the end** and take a deep breath before he answers. The teacher first said something good – his ideas are good."},{"af":"**Onthou dat dit oor die werk gaan**, nie oor hom as persoon nie. Die opstel kan verbeter word.","en":"**Remember that it is about the work**, not about him as a person. The essay can be improved."},{"af":"**Vra ’n vraag** as hy nie seker is nie: “Waar moet ek ’n nuwe paragraaf begin?”","en":"**Ask a question** if he is not sure: “Where should I start a new paragraph?”"},{"af":"**Sê dankie en gebruik dit:** hy verdeel sy opstel in paragrawe en sien dat dit beter lees.","en":"**Say thank you and use it:** he divides his essay into paragraphs and sees that it reads better."}],"answer":{"af":"Hy moet kalm luister, onthou dit gaan oor die werk, ’n vraag vra as hy nie verstaan nie, dankie sê en die raad gebruik.","en":"He should listen calmly, remember it is about the work, ask a question if he doesn’t understand, say thank you and use the advice."}},{"title":{"af":"Hanteer woede op ’n gesonde manier","en":"Handle anger in a healthy way"},"problem":{"af":"Nomsa se klein boetie het in haar huiswerkboek gekrabbel. Haar hart klop vinnig, haar gesig word warm en sy wil die boek na hom gooi. Watter emosie voel sy? Noem twee gesonde maniere om dit te hanteer en skryf ’n ek-boodskap vir haar.","en":"Nomsa’s little brother has scribbled in her homework book. Her heart beats fast, her face gets hot and she wants to throw the book at him. Which emotion is she feeling? Name two healthy ways to handle it and write an I-message for her."},"steps":[{"af":"**Benoem die emosie:** ’n vinnige hartklop en ’n warm gesig is tekens van **woede** – sy is kwaad.","en":"**Name the emotion:** a fast heartbeat and a hot face are signs of **anger** – she is angry."},{"af":"**Kalmeer eers:** sy kan ’n paar keer diep asemhaal of stadig tot tien tel voordat sy iets doen.","en":"**Calm down first:** she can take a few deep breaths or count slowly to ten before she does anything."},{"af":"**Praat eerder as om te gooi:** sy kan ’n ek-boodskap gebruik en dit dan vir ’n ouer vertel sodat hulle kan help.","en":"**Talk instead of throwing:** she can use an I-message and then tell a parent so that they can help."}],"answer":{"af":"Sy is kwaad. Sy kan diep asemhaal en tot tien tel. Ek-boodskap: “Ek voel kwaad wanneer jy in my boek krabbel, want dis my huiswerk.”","en":"She is angry. She can take deep breaths and count to ten. I-message: “I feel angry when you scribble in my book, because it is my homework.”"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is terugvoering?","en":"What is feedback?"},"options":[{"af":"Wanneer iemand jou werk oorskryf","en":"When someone copies your work"},{"af":"Wanneer iemand sê wat goed gaan en wat jy kan verbeter","en":"When someone says what is going well and what you can improve"},{"af":"Wanneer jy jou werk vir niemand wys nie","en":"When you don’t show your work to anybody"},{"af":"Wanneer iemand net foute in jou werk uitwys","en":"When someone only points out mistakes in your work"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Terugvoering wys jou wat goed is én wat jy kan verbeter, sodat jy kan groei. As iemand net foute uitwys, is dit nie goeie, positiewe terugvoering nie.","en":"Feedback shows you what is good and what you can improve, so that you can grow. If someone only points out mistakes, it is not good, positive feedback."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Dit is altyd verkeerd om kwaad te voel.","en":"It is always wrong to feel angry."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Woede is ’n natuurlike gevoel wat almal soms het. Wat saak maak, is hoe jy dit hanteer: praat of asemhaal is goed, slaan of skree is nie.","en":"False. Anger is a natural feeling that everyone has sometimes. What matters is how you handle it: talking or breathing is good, hitting or shouting is not."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat kom in die middel van ’n terugvoeringtoebroodjie?","en":"What goes in the middle of a feedback sandwich?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Grap om die persoon te laat lag","en":"A joke to make the person laugh"},{"af":"Lof vir wat goed is","en":"Praise for what is good"},{"af":"’n Lys van al die persoon se foute","en":"A list of all the person’s mistakes"},{"af":"’n Voorstel om die werk te verbeter","en":"A suggestion to improve the work"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die “vulsel” is die voorstel. Dit sit tussen twee positiewe dinge – eers lof en laastens bemoediging – sodat die persoon die raad makliker aanvaar. ’n Lys van al die foute sal die persoon net ontmoedig.","en":"The “filling” is the suggestion. It sits between two positive things – praise first and encouragement last – so that the person accepts the advice more easily. A list of all the mistakes will only discourage the person."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As jy baie kwaad is, kan jy stadig tot ___ tel voordat jy praat.","en":"When you are very angry, you can count slowly to ___ before you speak."},"answers":{"af":["tien","10"],"en":["ten","10"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["twee","drie","vyftig"],"en":["two","three","fifty"]}},"explain":{"af":"Om tot tien te tel, gee jou net genoeg tyd om te kalmeer en te dink voordat jy iets sê of doen waaroor jy later spyt kan wees.","en":"Counting to ten gives you just enough time to calm down and think before you say or do something you might be sorry about later."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter terugvoering is positief en respekvol?","en":"Which feedback is positive and respectful?"},"options":[{"af":"“Jou kleure is mooi. As jy die prent groter teken, sal dit nog beter wees.”","en":"“Your colours are lovely. If you draw the picture bigger, it will be even better.”"},{"af":"“Dit lyk soos ’n kleuterskool-tekening.”","en":"“It looks like a nursery-school drawing.”"},{"af":"“Myne is baie beter as joune.”","en":"“Mine is much better than yours.”"},{"af":"“Dis goed.” (sonder om enigiets anders te sê)","en":"“It’s fine.” (without saying anything else)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die eerste sin prys iets spesifieks en gee ’n duidelike voorstel. Die ander kraak die persoon af, vergelyk of is so vaag dat dit niemand help om te verbeter nie.","en":"The first sentence praises something specific and gives a clear suggestion. The others put the person down, compare, or are so vague that they don’t help anyone improve."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato se beste vriendin speel die hele week net met die nuwe meisie. Lerato voel ’n knop op die maag en wil nie meer met haar praat nie. Watter emosie voel Lerato waarskynlik?","en":"Lerato’s best friend plays only with the new girl all week. Lerato feels a knot in her stomach and doesn’t want to talk to her any more. Which emotion is Lerato most likely feeling?"},"options":[{"af":"Bly","en":"Happy"},{"af":"Skaam","en":"Embarrassed"},{"af":"Jaloers","en":"Jealous"},{"af":"Trots","en":"Proud"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Jaloesie is die gevoel wanneer jy bang is om iemand se aandag of vriendskap te verloor. Dit is ’n normale gevoel; Lerato kan dit hanteer deur met haar vriendin te praat of saam met die nuwe meisie te speel.","en":"Jealousy is the feeling when you are afraid of losing someone’s attention or friendship. It is a normal feeling; Lerato can handle it by talking to her friend or playing with the new girl too."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke situasie by die emosie wat ’n mens waarskynlik sal voel.","en":"Match each situation to the emotion a person will probably feel."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Jy word vir die span gekies","en":"You are chosen for the team"},"r":{"af":"Bly","en":"Happy"}},{"l":{"af":"Jou troeteldier is dood","en":"Your pet has died"},"r":{"af":"Hartseer","en":"Sad"}},{"l":{"af":"Iemand skeur jou boek doelbewus","en":"Someone tears your book on purpose"},"r":{"af":"Kwaad","en":"Angry"}},{"l":{"af":"Jy hoor ’n vreemde geluid in die donker","en":"You hear a strange noise in the dark"},"r":{"af":"Bang","en":"Scared"}},{"l":{"af":"Jy val voor die hele klas","en":"You fall in front of the whole class"},"r":{"af":"Skaam","en":"Embarrassed"}}],"explain":{"af":"Om jou emosie te benoem, is die eerste stap om dit te hanteer. As jy weet jy is kwaad of bang, kan jy kies wat sal help, soos asemhaal of met iemand praat.","en":"Naming your emotion is the first step to handling it. When you know you are angry or scared, you can choose what will help, like breathing or talking to someone."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Sin soos “Ek voel hartseer wanneer jy my nie laat saamspeel nie” is ’n ___.","en":"A sentence like “I feel sad when you don’t let me play” is an ___."},"answers":{"af":["ek-boodskap","ekboodskap"],"en":["I-message","I message"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["belediging","bevel","verskoning"],"en":["insult","order","excuse"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Ek-boodskap sê hoe jy voel en waarom, sonder om die ander persoon uit te skel. Die ander persoon luister makliker, want hulle voel nie aangeval nie.","en":"An I-message says how you feel and why, without calling the other person names. The other person listens more easily, because they don’t feel attacked."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n gesonde manier om woede te hanteer?","en":"Which one is a healthy way to handle anger?"},"options":[{"af":"Die deur so hard as moontlik toeklap","en":"Slamming the door as hard as possible"},{"af":"Gaan stap of hardloop om te kalmeer","en":"Going for a walk or a run to calm down"},{"af":"Die persoon later terugkry","en":"Getting back at the person later"},{"af":"Alles vir altyd binne-in hou","en":"Keeping everything inside forever"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Oefening help jou liggaam om die spanning van woede kwyt te raak sonder om iemand seer te maak. Om dinge te breek, wraak te neem of alles weg te steek, maak die probleem net groter.","en":"Exercise helps your body get rid of the tension of anger without hurting anyone. Breaking things, taking revenge or hiding everything only makes the problem bigger."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat behoort jy te doen wanneer iemand vir jou terugvoering gee?","en":"What should you do when someone gives you feedback?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle dadelik onderbreek en verduidelik hoekom hulle verkeerd is","en":"Interrupt them straight away and explain why they are wrong"},{"af":"Wegloop voordat hulle klaar gepraat het","en":"Walk away before they have finished speaking"},{"af":"Terugkap en hulle werk ook kritiseer","en":"Hit back and criticise their work too"},{"af":"Tot die einde luister en ’n vraag vra as jy nie verstaan nie","en":"Listen to the end and ask a question if you don’t understand"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Goeie terugvoering help jou om te groei. As jy kalm luister en vrae vra, verstaan jy presies wat jy kan verbeter. Om te stry of terug te kap, help jou nie.","en":"Good feedback helps you grow. When you listen calmly and ask questions, you understand exactly what you can improve. Arguing or hitting back does not help you."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Oefening soos stap of hardloop kan jou liggaam help om te kalmeer as jy ontsteld is.","en":"Exercise such as walking or running can help your body to calm down when you are upset."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Beweging help jou liggaam om spanning kwyt te raak, en jy kan daarna helderder dink oor die probleem.","en":"True. Movement helps your body to release tension, and afterwards you can think more clearly about the problem."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ravi se hart klop vinnig, sy gesig is warm en hy bal sy vuiste. Watter emosie voel hy waarskynlik?","en":"Ravi’s heart is beating fast, his face is hot and he clenches his fists. Which emotion is he probably feeling?"},"options":[{"af":"Kwaad","en":"Angry"},{"af":"Bly","en":"Happy"},{"af":"Hartseer","en":"Sad"},{"af":"Moeg","en":"Tired"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Vinnige hartklop, ’n warm gesig en gebalde vuiste is liggaamstekens van woede. As Ravi dit raaksien, kan hy stop en diep asemhaal voordat hy iets doen.","en":"A fast heartbeat, a hot face and clenched fists are body signs of anger. If Ravi notices them, he can stop and take deep breaths before he does anything."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Grootmens wat jou veilig laat voel, na jou luister en jou sal help, is ’n ___ volwassene.","en":"A grown-up who makes you feel safe, listens to you and will help you is a ___ adult."},"answers":{"af":["vertroude"],"en":["trusted"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vreemde","kwaai","onbekende"],"en":["strange","strict","unknown"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Vertroude volwassene kan ’n ouer, grootouer, onderwyser of skoolberader wees. Om met so iemand te praat, is een van die beste maniere om sterk gevoelens te hanteer.","en":"A trusted adult can be a parent, grandparent, teacher or school counsellor. Talking to such a person is one of the best ways to handle strong feelings."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Liam is baie hartseer omdat sy ouma ver weg getrek het. Wat sal hom die beste help?","en":"Liam is very sad because his grandmother has moved far away. What will help him most?"},"options":[{"af":"Om vir almal te sê hy gee nie om nie","en":"Telling everybody that he doesn’t care"},{"af":"Om sy maats te boelie sodat hy beter voel","en":"Bullying his friends so that he feels better"},{"af":"Om met sy ma te praat en vir sy ouma ’n brief te skryf","en":"Talking to his mom and writing a letter to his grandmother"},{"af":"Om weke lank alleen in sy kamer te sit","en":"Sitting alone in his room for weeks"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Om oor jou hartseer te praat en dit uit te druk, byvoorbeeld in ’n brief, help jou om dit te verwerk. Om te maak of jy nie omgee nie, ander seer te maak of jou af te sonder, maak dit nie beter nie.","en":"Talking about your sadness and expressing it, for example in a letter, helps you to work through it. Pretending you don’t care, hurting others or shutting yourself away does not make it better."}}]},{"id":"lv5-t1-vriendskappe","title":{"af":"Vriendskappe","en":"Friendships"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die eienskappe van ’n goeie vriend kan beskryf, kan verduidelik hoe om ’n sorgsame vriend te wees en weet hoe om ’n vriend in tye van hartseer, verlies en verandering te ondersteun.","en":"You will be able to describe the qualities of a good friend, explain how to be a caring friend and know how to support a friend in times of sadness, loss and change."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat maak ’n goeie vriend?\n\n’n **Vriend** is iemand met wie jy graag tyd deurbring, wat jou respekteer en vir jou omgee. Vriende maak die lewe lekkerder: julle speel saam, lag saam en help mekaar.\n\nEienskappe van ’n goeie vriend:\n\n- **betroubaar** – hou beloftes en vertel nie jou geheime oor nie (behalwe as iemand in gevaar is)\n- **eerlik** – sê die waarheid, ook wanneer dit moeilik is\n- **lojaal** – staan by jou en skinder nie agter jou rug oor jou nie\n- **vriendelik en hulpvaardig** – help jou as jy sukkel\n- **respekvol** – aanvaar dat jy anders kan dink of van ander dinge kan hou\n- **’n goeie luisteraar**\n\n’n Ware vriend sal jou nooit dwing om iets te doen wat verkeerd of gevaarlik is nie. Iemand wat jou boelie of jou heeltyd sleg laat voel oor jouself, is nie ’n ware vriend nie.\n\n## Hoe om ’n sorgsame vriend te wees\n\nJy kan nie net verwag dat ander goeie vriende moet wees nie – jy moet self ook een wees.\n\n- Deel en neem beurte.\n- Vra hoe dit met jou vriend gaan, en luister regtig na die antwoord.\n- Sê jammer as jy iets verkeerd gedoen het, en vergewe ook.\n- Nooi iemand wat alleen staan om saam te speel.\n- Staan op vir jou vriend as iemand hom of haar boelie.\n\n## Luister en empatie\n\n**Empatie** beteken dat jy probeer verstaan hoe iemand anders voel, asof jy in hulle skoene staan. Dit begin met **goeie luister**.\n\n| ’n Goeie luisteraar … | ’n Swak luisteraar … |\n|---|---|\n| kyk na die persoon wat praat | kyk rond of speel met ’n foon |\n| laat die ander klaar praat | val die ander in die rede |\n| vra: “Hoe voel jy daaroor?” | begin dadelik oor homself praat |\n| sê: “Dit klink regtig moeilik.” | sê: “Moenie so ’n ophef maak nie.” |\n\n## Ondersteuning in moeilike tye\n\nSoms gaan vriende deur moeilike tye. ’n **Verlies** is wanneer iemand iets of iemand belangriks verloor, byvoorbeeld wanneer ’n ouma of ’n troeteldier doodgaan. ’n **Tragedie** is iets baie hartseers wat skielik gebeur, soos ’n ongeluk of ’n huis wat afbrand. **Veranderinge** soos om na ’n ander dorp te trek, na ’n nuwe skool te gaan of ouers wat **skei**, kan ook baie seer wees.\n\nHoe jy kan help:\n\n1. **Wees daar:** sit by jou vriend, al sê julle nie veel nie.\n2. **Luister** sonder om te oordeel.\n3. **Wys dat jy omgee:** maak ’n kaartjie, deel jou kos, nooi jou vriend om saam te speel.\n4. **Moenie** skinder oor wat gebeur het nie, en moenie sê “Kom oor dit” nie.\n5. **Hou kontak:** as ’n vriend wegtrek, kan julle briewe skryf of, met jou ouers se toestemming, mekaar bel.\n6. Help ’n **nuwe leerder** om die skool en die ander kinders te leer ken.\n\n> **Onthou:** Mense **rou** op verskillende maniere. Een vriend huil baie, ’n ander word stil of gou kwaad. Wees geduldig – hartseer gaan nie in een dag weg nie.\n\n## Wanneer om ’n volwassene te betrek\n\nParty probleme is te groot vir ’n kind om alleen te hanteer. Sê vir ’n **vertroude volwassene** (’n ouer, onderwyser of skoolberader) as jou vriend:\n\n- deur iemand seergemaak word, by die huis of elders\n- baie lank hartseer is en nie meer eet of wil speel nie\n- sê dat hy of sy niks meer werd is nie of nie meer wil lewe nie\n- in enige gevaar is\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om ’n volwassene te vertel wanneer jou vriend in gevaar is, is **nie** verraad nie. ’n Goeie vriend hou nie ’n geheim wat iemand se veiligheid in gevaar stel nie. Jy kan ook **Childline** by **116** bel – die oproep is gratis.","en":"## What makes a good friend?\n\nA **friend** is someone you like spending time with, who respects you and cares about you. Friends make life more fun: you play together, laugh together and help each other.\n\nQualities of a good friend:\n\n- **trustworthy** – keeps promises and does not pass on your secrets (unless someone is in danger)\n- **honest** – tells the truth, even when it is difficult\n- **loyal** – stands by you and does not gossip about you behind your back\n- **friendly and helpful** – helps you when you struggle\n- **respectful** – accepts that you may think differently or like different things\n- **a good listener**\n\nA true friend will never force you to do something that is wrong or dangerous. Someone who bullies you or always makes you feel bad about yourself is not a true friend.\n\n## How to be a caring friend\n\nYou can’t just expect others to be good friends – you must be one yourself too.\n\n- Share and take turns.\n- Ask how your friend is doing, and really listen to the answer.\n- Say sorry if you have done something wrong, and forgive too.\n- Invite someone who is standing alone to play with you.\n- Stand up for your friend if someone bullies him or her.\n\n## Listening and empathy\n\n**Empathy** means trying to understand how someone else feels, as if you are standing in their shoes. It starts with **good listening**.\n\n| A good listener … | A poor listener … |\n|---|---|\n| looks at the person who is talking | looks around or plays with a phone |\n| lets the other person finish speaking | interrupts the other person |\n| asks: “How do you feel about it?” | starts talking about himself straight away |\n| says: “That sounds really hard.” | says: “Don’t make such a fuss.” |\n\n## Support in difficult times\n\nSometimes friends go through difficult times. A **loss** is when someone loses something or someone important, for example when a grandmother or a pet dies. A **tragedy** is something very sad that happens suddenly, such as an accident or a house that burns down. **Changes** like moving to another town, going to a new school or parents who **divorce** can also hurt a lot.\n\nHow you can help:\n\n1. **Be there:** sit with your friend, even if you don’t say much.\n2. **Listen** without judging.\n3. **Show that you care:** make a card, share your food, invite your friend to play.\n4. **Don’t** gossip about what happened, and don’t say “Get over it”.\n5. **Keep in touch:** if a friend moves away, you can write letters or, with your parents’ permission, phone each other.\n6. Help a **new learner** to get to know the school and the other children.\n\n> **Remember:** People **grieve** in different ways. One friend cries a lot, another becomes quiet or quickly angry. Be patient – sadness does not go away in one day.\n\n## When to involve an adult\n\nSome problems are too big for a child to handle alone. Tell a **trusted adult** (a parent, teacher or school counsellor) if your friend:\n\n- is being hurt by someone, at home or anywhere else\n- has been sad for a long time and no longer eats or wants to play\n- says that he or she is worth nothing or doesn’t want to live any more\n- is in any danger\n\n> **Common mistake:** Telling an adult when your friend is in danger is **not** betrayal. A good friend does not keep a secret that puts someone’s safety at risk. You can also call **Childline** on **116** – the call is free."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Vriendskap","en":"Friendship"},"def":{"af":"’n Verhouding tussen mense wat graag saam tyd deurbring, mekaar respekteer en vir mekaar omgee.","en":"A relationship between people who like spending time together, respect each other and care about each other."}},{"term":{"af":"Betroubaar","en":"Trustworthy"},"def":{"af":"Iemand op wie jy kan staatmaak, wat beloftes hou en nie jou geheime oorvertel nie.","en":"Someone you can rely on, who keeps promises and does not pass on your secrets."}},{"term":{"af":"Lojaal","en":"Loyal"},"def":{"af":"Iemand wat by jou staan, ook in moeilike tye, en nie agter jou rug oor jou skinder nie.","en":"Someone who stands by you, even in difficult times, and does not gossip about you behind your back."}},{"term":{"af":"Empatie","en":"Empathy"},"def":{"af":"Om te probeer verstaan hoe iemand anders voel, asof jy in hulle skoene staan.","en":"Trying to understand how someone else feels, as if you are standing in their shoes."}},{"term":{"af":"Goeie luisteraar","en":"Good listener"},"def":{"af":"Iemand wat na die spreker kyk, nie onderbreek nie en vrae vra om beter te verstaan.","en":"Someone who looks at the speaker, does not interrupt and asks questions to understand better."}},{"term":{"af":"Verlies","en":"Loss"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer jy iets of iemand belangriks verloor, byvoorbeeld wanneer ’n familielid of troeteldier doodgaan.","en":"When you lose something or someone important, for example when a family member or a pet dies."}},{"term":{"af":"Tragedie","en":"Tragedy"},"def":{"af":"Iets baie hartseers wat skielik gebeur, soos ’n ernstige ongeluk of ’n brand.","en":"Something very sad that happens suddenly, such as a serious accident or a fire."}},{"term":{"af":"Egskeiding","en":"Divorce"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer getroude ouers besluit om amptelik uitmekaar te gaan en nie meer saam te woon nie.","en":"When married parents decide to officially separate and no longer live together."}},{"term":{"af":"Rou","en":"Grieve"},"def":{"af":"Om diep hartseer te voel en dit te verwerk nadat jy iemand of iets belangriks verloor het.","en":"To feel deep sadness and work through it after you have lost someone or something important."}},{"term":{"af":"Vertroude volwassene","en":"Trusted adult"},"def":{"af":"’n Grootmens wat jou veilig laat voel, na jou luister en jou sal help.","en":"A grown-up who makes you feel safe, listens to you and will help you."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Ondersteun ’n vriend ná ’n verlies","en":"Support a friend after a loss"},"problem":{"af":"Fatima se ouma is verlede week oorlede. Toe sy terugkom skool toe, sit sy alleen en praat nie veel nie. Hoe kan haar vriendin Lerato haar ondersteun? Noem drie dinge en een ding wat Lerato nie moet doen nie.","en":"Fatima’s grandmother died last week. When she comes back to school, she sits alone and does not talk much. How can her friend Lerato support her? Name three things and one thing Lerato should not do."},"steps":[{"af":"**Wees daar:** Lerato kan by Fatima gaan sit, al sê sy net: “Ek is jammer oor jou ouma.”","en":"**Be there:** Lerato can go and sit with Fatima, even if she only says: “I’m sorry about your grandmother.”"},{"af":"**Luister:** as Fatima wil praat, moet Lerato luister sonder om te onderbreek, en vra: “Hoe voel jy vandag?”","en":"**Listen:** if Fatima wants to talk, Lerato should listen without interrupting, and ask: “How are you feeling today?”"},{"af":"**Wys dat sy omgee:** sy kan ’n kaartjie maak of Fatima nooi om saam met pouse te speel.","en":"**Show that she cares:** she can make a card or invite Fatima to play together at break."},{"af":"**Wat sy nie moet doen nie:** sy moet nie sê “Kom oor dit” nie, en nie vir ander kinders skinder oor wat gebeur het nie.","en":"**What she should not do:** she should not say “Get over it”, and not gossip to other children about what happened."}],"answer":{"af":"Lerato kan by haar sit, luister en ’n kaartjie maak of haar nooi om te speel. Sy moet nie sê “Kom oor dit” of skinder nie.","en":"Lerato can sit with her, listen and make a card or invite her to play. She should not say “Get over it” or gossip."}},{"title":{"af":"Help ’n nuwe leerder","en":"Help a new learner"},"problem":{"af":"Johan se gesin het van Kimberley na Durban getrek. Dis sy eerste dag in Sipho se klas, en hy staan alleen by die venster. Hoe kan Sipho ’n sorgsame vriend wees?","en":"Johan’s family moved from Kimberley to Durban. It is his first day in Sipho’s class, and he is standing alone by the window. How can Sipho be a caring friend?"},"steps":[{"af":"**Dink met empatie:** hoe sal dit voel om niemand te ken nie? Johan voel waarskynlik eensaam, skaam of bang.","en":"**Think with empathy:** how would it feel to know nobody? Johan probably feels lonely, shy or scared."},{"af":"**Maak kontak:** Sipho kan homself voorstel, Johan se naam vra en hom nooi om saam pouse te hou.","en":"**Make contact:** Sipho can introduce himself, ask Johan’s name and invite him to spend break together."},{"af":"**Help hom die skool leer ken:** wys hom waar die biblioteek, die toilette en die sportveld is, en stel hom aan ander kinders voor.","en":"**Help him get to know the school:** show him where the library, the toilets and the sports field are, and introduce him to other children."}],"answer":{"af":"Sipho kan homself voorstel, Johan nooi om saam te speel, hom die skool wys en hom aan ander kinders voorstel.","en":"Sipho can introduce himself, invite Johan to play, show him around the school and introduce him to other children."}},{"title":{"af":"Wanneer moet jy ’n volwassene vertel?","en":"When should you tell an adult?"},"problem":{"af":"Liam se vriend Ravi se ouers is besig om te skei. Ravi is al weke lank baie stil, eet nie sy kos by die skool nie en sê: “Niemand gee om vir my nie.” Hy vra Liam om vir niemand iets te sê nie. Wat moet Liam doen?","en":"Liam’s friend Ravi’s parents are getting divorced. For weeks Ravi has been very quiet, does not eat his food at school and says: “Nobody cares about me.” He asks Liam not to tell anyone. What should Liam do?"},"steps":[{"af":"**Luister en wys dat hy omgee:** Liam kan sê: “Ek gee om vir jou, en ek is jammer dit gaan so moeilik.”","en":"**Listen and show that he cares:** Liam can say: “I care about you, and I’m sorry things are so hard.”"},{"af":"**Herken die waarskuwingstekens:** Ravi is al lank baie hartseer, eet nie en voel niemand gee om nie. Dit is te groot vir ’n kind om alleen te hanteer.","en":"**Recognise the warning signs:** Ravi has been very sad for a long time, is not eating and feels that nobody cares. This is too big for a child to handle alone."},{"af":"**Vertel ’n vertroude volwassene:** Liam moet sy onderwyser, die skoolberader of sy eie ouers vertel. Dit is nie verraad nie – hy help sy vriend.","en":"**Tell a trusted adult:** Liam should tell his teacher, the school counsellor or his own parents. This is not betrayal – he is helping his friend."}],"answer":{"af":"Liam moet luister en wys dat hy omgee, maar hy moet dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene vertel, want Ravi het meer hulp nodig as wat ’n vriend alleen kan gee.","en":"Liam should listen and show that he cares, but he must tell a trusted adult, because Ravi needs more help than a friend alone can give."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter gedrag wys dat ’n vriend betroubaar is?","en":"Which behaviour shows that a friend is trustworthy?"},"options":[{"af":"Sy vertel jou geheime vir die hele klas","en":"She tells your secrets to the whole class"},{"af":"Sy speel net met jou as niemand anders daar is nie","en":"She only plays with you when nobody else is there"},{"af":"Sy hou haar beloftes en vertel nie jou geheime oor nie","en":"She keeps her promises and does not pass on your secrets"},{"af":"Sy belowe baie goed, maar doen dit nooit nie","en":"She promises many things but never does them"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Betroubaar beteken jy kan op iemand staatmaak: hulle hou beloftes en hou jou geheime. Die enigste uitsondering is ’n geheim wat iemand in gevaar stel – dit moet vir ’n volwassene vertel word.","en":"Trustworthy means you can rely on someone: they keep promises and keep your secrets. The only exception is a secret that puts someone in danger – that must be told to an adult."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken empatie?","en":"What does empathy mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Om te probeer verstaan hoe iemand anders voel","en":"Trying to understand how someone else feels"},{"af":"Om jammer te voel vir jouself","en":"Feeling sorry for yourself"},{"af":"Om altyd met jou vriende saam te stem","en":"Always agreeing with your friends"},{"af":"Om ander se probleme vir hulle op te los","en":"Solving other people’s problems for them"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Empatie is om in iemand anders se skoene te staan en te probeer voel wat hulle voel. Jy hoef nie altyd saam te stem of hulle probleme op te los nie – om te verstaan en te luister, help al baie.","en":"Empathy is standing in someone else’s shoes and trying to feel what they feel. You don’t always have to agree or solve their problems – understanding and listening already help a lot."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer iemand iets of iemand belangriks verloor, soos ’n troeteldier wat doodgaan, noem ons dit ’n ___.","en":"When someone loses something or someone important, like a pet that dies, we call it a ___."},"answers":{"af":["verlies"],"en":["loss"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["oorwinning","verrassing","uitdaging"],"en":["victory","surprise","challenge"]}},"explain":{"af":"’n Verlies laat ’n mens hartseer en dikwels eensaam voel. Vriende kan help deur daar te wees en te luister.","en":"A loss makes a person feel sad and often lonely. Friends can help by being there and listening."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Ware vriend sal jou nooit dwing om iets gevaarliks te doen nie.","en":"A true friend will never force you to do something dangerous."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Ware vriend gee om vir jou veiligheid en respekteer dit as jy “nee” sê. Iemand wat jou dwing of dreig, tree nie soos ’n vriend op nie.","en":"True. A true friend cares about your safety and respects it when you say “no”. Someone who forces or threatens you is not acting like a friend."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat doen ’n goeie luisteraar?","en":"What does a good listener do?"},"options":[{"af":"Speel met sy foon terwyl die ander praat","en":"Plays with his phone while the other person talks"},{"af":"Val die ander in die rede om sy eie storie te vertel","en":"Interrupts the other person to tell his own story"},{"af":"Sê: “Moenie so ’n ophef maak nie.”","en":"Says: “Don’t make such a fuss.”"},{"af":"Kyk na die spreker en laat hom klaar praat","en":"Looks at the speaker and lets him finish speaking"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Goeie luisteraar gee sy volle aandag: hy kyk na die persoon, onderbreek nie en wys dat hy omgee. Die ander drie maak die spreker voel dat hy nie belangrik is nie.","en":"A good listener gives his full attention: he looks at the person, does not interrupt and shows that he cares. The other three make the speaker feel unimportant."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho se vriend vertel hom dat sy ouers gaan skei. Wat is die beste ding wat Sipho kan sê?","en":"Sipho’s friend tells him that his parents are getting divorced. What is the best thing Sipho can say?"},"options":[{"af":"“Dis seker jou skuld.”","en":"“It’s probably your fault.”"},{"af":"“Dit klink baie moeilik. Wil jy daaroor praat?”","en":"“That sounds very hard. Do you want to talk about it?”"},{"af":"“Baie mense skei, so dis nie ’n groot ding nie.”","en":"“Lots of people divorce, so it’s not a big deal.”"},{"af":"“Ek gaan dit vir die hele klas vertel.”","en":"“I’m going to tell the whole class.”"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Hierdie antwoord wys empatie en gee die vriend ’n kans om te praat. ’n Egskeiding is nooit die kind se skuld nie, dit is vir die kind wél ’n groot ding, en dit is privaat.","en":"This answer shows empathy and gives the friend a chance to talk. A divorce is never the child’s fault, it is a big deal for the child, and it is private."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke situasie by die beste manier om te help.","en":"Match each situation to the best way to help."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"’n Nuwe leerder ken niemand nie","en":"A new learner knows nobody"},"r":{"af":"Stel jouself voor en wys hom die skool","en":"Introduce yourself and show him the school"}},{"l":{"af":"Jou vriend se hond is dood","en":"Your friend’s dog has died"},"r":{"af":"Sê jy is jammer en luister as sy wil praat","en":"Say you are sorry and listen if she wants to talk"}},{"l":{"af":"Jou beste vriend trek na ’n ander dorp","en":"Your best friend is moving to another town"},"r":{"af":"Maak ’n plan om kontak te hou","en":"Make a plan to keep in touch"}},{"l":{"af":"’n Vriend word by die huis seergemaak","en":"A friend is being hurt at home"},"r":{"af":"Vertel dadelik ’n vertroude volwassene","en":"Tell a trusted adult straight away"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke situasie vra ’n ander soort hulp. Vriende kan baie doen deur te luister en om te gee, maar as iemand seergemaak word, moet ’n volwassene help.","en":"Each situation needs a different kind of help. Friends can do a lot by listening and caring, but when someone is being hurt, an adult must help."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jou vriend vertel jou ’n geheim: iemand by die huis maak hom seer. Hy vra jou om niks te sê nie. Wat moet jy doen?","en":"Your friend tells you a secret: someone at home is hurting him. He asks you not to say anything. What should you do?"},"options":[{"af":"Die geheim hou, want jy het belowe","en":"Keep the secret, because you promised"},{"af":"Vir die ander kinders in die klas vertel","en":"Tell the other children in the class"},{"af":"Dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene vertel sodat hy hulp kry","en":"Tell a trusted adult so that he gets help"},{"af":"Self na sy huis gaan en die persoon konfronteer","en":"Go to his house yourself and confront the person"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Geheim wat iemand se veiligheid in gevaar stel, moet vir ’n vertroude volwassene vertel word. Dit is nie verraad nie – dit is die beste manier om jou vriend te beskerm. Moenie self probeer om dit op te los nie; jy kan ook Childline by 116 bel.","en":"A secret that puts someone’s safety at risk must be told to a trusted adult. This is not betrayal – it is the best way to protect your friend. Don’t try to sort it out yourself; you can also call Childline on 116."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Om in iemand anders se skoene te staan en te probeer verstaan hoe hulle voel, heet ___.","en":"Standing in someone else’s shoes and trying to understand how they feel is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["empatie"],"en":["empathy"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["jaloesie","lojaliteit","eerlikheid"],"en":["jealousy","loyalty","honesty"]}},"explain":{"af":"Empatie help jou om ’n sorgsame vriend te wees, veral wanneer jou vriend deur ’n moeilike tyd gaan. Lojaliteit en eerlikheid is ook goeie eienskappe, maar hulle beteken iets anders.","en":"Empathy helps you to be a caring friend, especially when your friend is going through a difficult time. Loyalty and honesty are also good qualities, but they mean something else."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy ’n volwassene vertel dat jou vriend in gevaar is, verraai jy jou vriend.","en":"If you tell an adult that your friend is in danger, you are betraying your friend."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Om hulp te kry vir ’n vriend wat in gevaar is, is een van die beste dinge wat ’n goeie vriend kan doen. Sommige probleme is te groot vir kinders om alleen te hanteer.","en":"False. Getting help for a friend who is in danger is one of the best things a good friend can do. Some problems are too big for children to handle alone."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Nuwe meisie het pas by jou skool begin. Wat is die beste manier om haar te help?","en":"A new girl has just started at your school. What is the best way to help her?"},"options":[{"af":"Wag dat sy eers vir jou kom hallo sê","en":"Wait for her to come and say hello to you first"},{"af":"Vir haar sê watter kinders sy moet vermy","en":"Tell her which children she should avoid"},{"af":"Haar uitvra oor hoekom haar gesin getrek het","en":"Question her about why her family moved"},{"af":"Haar nooi om saam met jou en jou maats te speel","en":"Invite her to play with you and your friends"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Nuwe leerder voel dikwels eensaam en skaam. As jy haar nooi om saam te speel, voel sy welkom en maak sy gouer vriende. Om te skinder of haar uit te vra oor private dinge, help nie.","en":"A new learner often feels lonely and shy. If you invite her to play, she feels welcome and makes friends sooner. Gossiping or questioning her about private things does not help."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Anika se oupa is oorlede. Een dag huil sy, die volgende dag is sy gou kwaad. Wat moet haar vriende onthou?","en":"Anika’s grandfather has died. One day she cries, the next day she gets angry quickly. What should her friends remember?"},"options":[{"af":"Sy maak net of sy hartseer is","en":"She is only pretending to be sad"},{"af":"Mense rou op verskillende maniere, so hulle moet geduldig wees","en":"People grieve in different ways, so they should be patient"},{"af":"Sy moet na ’n week oor die hartseer wees","en":"She should be over her sadness after a week"},{"af":"Hulle moet haar uitlos totdat sy weer vrolik is","en":"They should leave her alone until she is cheerful again"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Rou lyk nie by almal dieselfde nie: hartseer kan as trane, stilte of selfs woede uitkom, en dit neem tyd. Goeie vriende bly geduldig en ondersteun haar.","en":"Grieving doesn’t look the same for everyone: sadness can come out as tears, silence or even anger, and it takes time. Good friends stay patient and support her."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Vriend wat by jou staan en nie agter jou rug oor jou skinder nie, is ___.","en":"A friend who stands by you and does not gossip about you behind your back is ___."},"answers":{"af":["lojaal"],"en":["loyal"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["jaloers","oneerlik","selfsugtig"],"en":["jealous","dishonest","selfish"]}},"explain":{"af":"Lojaliteit beteken jy staan by iemand, ook wanneer dinge moeilik is. ’n Jaloerse, oneerlike of selfsugtige vriend sal eerder agter jou rug praat.","en":"Loyalty means you stand by someone, even when things are difficult. A jealous, dishonest or selfish friend is more likely to talk behind your back."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter persoon tree NIE soos ’n ware vriend op nie?","en":"Which person is NOT acting like a true friend?"},"options":[{"af":"Pieter wat sê: “Gee my jou geld, anders is ek nie meer jou vriend nie.”","en":"Pieter, who says: “Give me your money, or I won’t be your friend any more.”"},{"af":"Zanele wat sê jammer nadat sy haar vriendin se potlood gebreek het","en":"Zanele, who says sorry after she broke her friend’s pencil"},{"af":"Thabo wat sy toebroodjie deel met ’n maat wat nie kos het nie","en":"Thabo, who shares his sandwich with a classmate who has no food"},{"af":"Aisha wat haar vriend help om vir ’n toets te leer","en":"Aisha, who helps her friend study for a test"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Ware vriend dreig jou nie en gebruik die vriendskap nie om iets van jou te kry nie. Pieter probeer sy maat dwing – dit is boelie, nie vriendskap nie.","en":"A true friend does not threaten you or use the friendship to get something from you. Pieter is trying to force his classmate – that is bullying, not friendship."}}]},{"id":"lv5-t1-veilige-verhoudings","title":{"af":"Veilige en onveilige verhoudings","en":"Safe and unsafe relationships"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die verskil tussen veilige en onveilige verhoudings kan herken, veiligheidsreëls met vreemdelinge en aanlyn kan toepas en weet hoe om ‘Nee – Gaan weg – Vertel’ te gebruik.","en":"You will be able to recognise the difference between safe and unsafe relationships, apply safety rules with strangers and online, and know how to use ‘No – Go – Tell’."},"summary":{"af":"## Verskillende soorte verhoudings\n\n’n **Verhouding** is die band tussen jou en ’n ander persoon. Jy het verhoudings met:\n\n- **maats** – kinders van jou eie ouderdom, soos klasmaats en vriende\n- **ouer mense** – soos jou ouers, grootouers, onderwysers, afrigters en bure\n- **vreemdelinge** – mense wat jy nie ken nie\n\nDie meeste mense in jou lewe is goed en wil jou help. Tog is dit belangrik om te weet hoe ’n **veilige** en ’n **onveilige** verhouding lyk.\n\n## Veilig of onveilig?\n\n| ’n Veilige verhouding | ’n Onveilige verhouding |\n|---|---|\n| Die persoon respekteer jou en jou liggaam. | Die persoon raak jou aan op ’n manier wat jou ongemaklik laat voel. |\n| Jy voel gemaklik en kan “nee” sê. | Jy voel bang, skuldig of deurmekaar. |\n| Die persoon vra nooit dat jy geheime vir jou ouers hou nie. | Die persoon sê: “Dis ons geheim. Moenie vir iemand sê nie.” |\n| Die persoon dwing of dreig jou nie. | Jy word gedreig, afgekraak of met geskenke omgekoop. |\n| Jou ouers weet van die verhouding. | Die persoon wil jou alleen hê, weg van ander mense. |\n\n**Voordele van veilige verhoudings:** jy voel geliefd en beskerm, jy het iemand om mee te praat, jy kry raad en hulp, jy leer om ander te vertrou en jou selfbeeld groei.\n\nLuister na jou **gevoel van binne**. As iets vir jou verkeerd voel, is dit dikwels ’n waarskuwing.\n\n## Veiligheidsreëls met vreemdelinge\n\n’n **Vreemdeling** is enigiemand wat jy nie goed ken nie – ook iemand wat vriendelik lyk. Die meeste vreemdelinge is nie gevaarlik nie, maar jy kan nie aan iemand se voorkoms sien of hulle veilig is nie.\n\n- Moenie saam met ’n vreemdeling loop of in ’n motor klim nie, al sê hy jou ma het hom gestuur.\n- Moenie lekkers, geld of geskenke van ’n vreemdeling aanvaar nie.\n- Moenie vir ’n vreemdeling sê waar jy woon of dat jy alleen tuis is nie.\n- Maak ’n **gesinswagwoord**: net iemand wat die wagwoord ken, mag jou kom haal.\n- As jy verdwaal, vra hulp by ’n polisiebeampte, ’n winkelassistent agter die toonbank of ’n ma met kinders.\n\n## Veilig aanlyn\n\nOp die internet weet jy nooit regtig met wie jy praat nie. Iemand wat sê hy is 11 jaar oud, kan ’n volwassene wees.\n\n- Moenie **persoonlike inligting** deel nie: jou volle naam, adres, skool, foonnommer of wagwoorde.\n- Moenie foto’s van jouself stuur aan iemand wat jy net aanlyn ken nie.\n- Moet nooit iemand wat jy aanlyn leer ken het, sonder ’n ouer ontmoet nie.\n- As iemand aanlyn iets sê of stuur wat jou ongemaklik laat voel, **moenie antwoord nie**. Wys dit vir ’n volwassene.\n\n## Nee – Gaan weg – Vertel\n\nAs iemand jou onveilig laat voel, onthou hierdie drie stappe:\n\n1. **Nee!** Sê hard en duidelik “Nee!” Jy het die reg om nee te sê, selfs vir ’n volwassene.\n2. **Gaan weg!** Gaan so vinnig moontlik na ’n veilige plek waar daar mense is.\n3. **Vertel!** Vertel dadelik vir ’n **vertroude volwassene** wat gebeur het. As die eerste volwassene nie luister nie, vertel iemand anders.\n\n> **Onthou:** ’n **Vertroude volwassene** is ’n grootmens wat jou veilig laat voel, na jou luister en jou sal help – byvoorbeeld ’n ouer, ’n ouma, ’n onderwyser of die skoolberader. Jy kan ook **Childline** by **116** bel. Die oproep is **gratis**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Baie kinders dink ’n gevaarlike persoon lyk eng of onvriendelik. Dit is nie so nie. Iemand wat kinders wil seermaak, is dikwels baie vriendelik en gee geskenke. Let op wat iemand **doen**, nie hoe hy of sy lyk nie.","en":"## Different kinds of relationships\n\nA **relationship** is the bond between you and another person. You have relationships with:\n\n- **peers** – children of your own age, like classmates and friends\n- **older people** – like your parents, grandparents, teachers, coaches and neighbours\n- **strangers** – people you don’t know\n\nMost people in your life are good and want to help you. Still, it is important to know what a **safe** and an **unsafe** relationship looks like.\n\n## Safe or unsafe?\n\n| A safe relationship | An unsafe relationship |\n|---|---|\n| The person respects you and your body. | The person touches you in a way that makes you feel uncomfortable. |\n| You feel comfortable and can say “no”. | You feel scared, guilty or confused. |\n| The person never asks you to keep secrets from your parents. | The person says: “It’s our secret. Don’t tell anyone.” |\n| The person does not force or threaten you. | You are threatened, put down or bribed with gifts. |\n| Your parents know about the relationship. | The person wants you alone, away from other people. |\n\n**Benefits of safe relationships:** you feel loved and protected, you have someone to talk to, you get advice and help, you learn to trust others and your self-concept grows.\n\nListen to your **feeling inside**. If something feels wrong to you, it is often a warning.\n\n## Safety rules with strangers\n\nA **stranger** is anyone you don’t know well – also someone who looks friendly. Most strangers are not dangerous, but you cannot tell from someone’s appearance whether they are safe.\n\n- Don’t walk with a stranger or get into a car, even if he says your mom sent him.\n- Don’t accept sweets, money or gifts from a stranger.\n- Don’t tell a stranger where you live or that you are home alone.\n- Make a **family password**: only someone who knows the password may fetch you.\n- If you get lost, ask for help from a police officer, a shop assistant behind the counter or a mother with children.\n\n## Safe online\n\nOn the internet you never really know who you are talking to. Someone who says he is 11 years old could be an adult.\n\n- Don’t share **personal information**: your full name, address, school, phone number or passwords.\n- Don’t send photos of yourself to someone you only know online.\n- Never meet someone you got to know online without a parent.\n- If someone online says or sends something that makes you uncomfortable, **don’t reply**. Show it to an adult.\n\n## No – Go – Tell\n\nIf someone makes you feel unsafe, remember these three steps:\n\n1. **No!** Say “No!” loudly and clearly. You have the right to say no, even to an adult.\n2. **Go!** Go as quickly as possible to a safe place where there are people.\n3. **Tell!** Immediately tell a **trusted adult** what happened. If the first adult does not listen, tell someone else.\n\n> **Remember:** A **trusted adult** is a grown-up who makes you feel safe, listens to you and will help you – for example a parent, a grandmother, a teacher or the school counsellor. You can also call **Childline** on **116**. The call is **free**.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Many children think a dangerous person looks scary or unfriendly. That is not so. Someone who wants to hurt children is often very friendly and gives gifts. Pay attention to what someone **does**, not to what he or she looks like."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Verhouding","en":"Relationship"},"def":{"af":"Die band of verbinding tussen jou en ’n ander persoon, soos ’n vriend, ’n familielid of ’n onderwyser.","en":"The bond or connection between you and another person, such as a friend, a family member or a teacher."}},{"term":{"af":"Maat","en":"Peer"},"def":{"af":"’n Kind van omtrent jou eie ouderdom, soos ’n klasmaat of vriend.","en":"A child of about your own age, such as a classmate or friend."}},{"term":{"af":"Vreemdeling","en":"Stranger"},"def":{"af":"Iemand wat jy nie goed ken nie, al lyk hy of sy vriendelik.","en":"Someone you don’t know well, even if he or she looks friendly."}},{"term":{"af":"Veilige verhouding","en":"Safe relationship"},"def":{"af":"’n Verhouding waarin jy gerespekteer word, gemaklik voel en “nee” kan sê.","en":"A relationship in which you are respected, feel comfortable and can say “no”."}},{"term":{"af":"Onveilige verhouding","en":"Unsafe relationship"},"def":{"af":"’n Verhouding waarin jy bang, ongemaklik of gedwing voel, of waarin jy geheime moet hou.","en":"A relationship in which you feel scared, uncomfortable or forced, or in which you have to keep secrets."}},{"term":{"af":"Persoonlike inligting","en":"Personal information"},"def":{"af":"Inligting wat wys wie jy is of waar jy is, soos jou volle naam, adres, skool en foonnommer.","en":"Information that shows who you are or where you are, such as your full name, address, school and phone number."}},{"term":{"af":"Gesinswagwoord","en":"Family password"},"def":{"af":"’n Geheime woord wat net jou gesin ken, sodat jy weet of iemand regtig gestuur is om jou te kom haal.","en":"A secret word that only your family knows, so that you know whether someone was really sent to fetch you."}},{"term":{"af":"Nee – Gaan weg – Vertel","en":"No – Go – Tell"},"def":{"af":"Drie veiligheidstappe: sê hard nee, gaan weg na ’n veilige plek en vertel ’n vertroude volwassene.","en":"Three safety steps: say no loudly, go away to a safe place and tell a trusted adult."}},{"term":{"af":"Vertroude volwassene","en":"Trusted adult"},"def":{"af":"’n Grootmens wat jou veilig laat voel, na jou luister en jou sal help.","en":"A grown-up who makes you feel safe, listens to you and will help you."}},{"term":{"af":"Childline","en":"Childline"},"def":{"af":"’n Gratis hulplyn vir kinders by die nommer 116, waar iemand na jou sal luister en jou sal help.","en":"A free helpline for children on the number 116, where someone will listen to you and help you."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"’n Vreemdeling by die skoolhek","en":"A stranger at the school gate"},"problem":{"af":"Ná skool sê ’n man wat Ravi nie ken nie: “Jou ma is in die hospitaal. Sy het my gevra om jou te kom haal. Klim gou in die kar.” Wat moet Ravi doen?","en":"After school a man Ravi doesn’t know says: “Your mom is in hospital. She asked me to fetch you. Quickly get into the car.” What should Ravi do?"},"steps":[{"af":"**Herken die gevaar:** die man is ’n vreemdeling, hy jaag Ravi aan en hy gebruik ’n storie om hom bang te maak. Ravi weet nie of die storie waar is nie.","en":"**Recognise the danger:** the man is a stranger, he is rushing Ravi and he uses a story to frighten him. Ravi does not know whether the story is true."},{"af":"**Toets met die gesinswagwoord:** Ravi kan vra: “Wat is ons wagwoord?” As die man dit nie weet nie, gaan Ravi nie saam nie.","en":"**Test with the family password:** Ravi can ask: “What is our password?” If the man doesn’t know it, Ravi does not go with him."},{"af":"**Nee – Gaan weg – Vertel:** hy sê hard “Nee!”, hardloop terug die skoolterrein in en vertel dadelik ’n onderwyser of die wag, wat sy ouers kan bel.","en":"**No – Go – Tell:** he says “No!” loudly, runs back onto the school grounds and immediately tells a teacher or the guard, who can phone his parents."}],"answer":{"af":"Ravi moet nie saamgaan nie. Hy sê “Nee!”, gaan terug skool toe en vertel ’n onderwyser, wat sy ouers kan bel om te hoor of die storie waar is.","en":"Ravi must not go with him. He says “No!”, goes back to school and tells a teacher, who can phone his parents to find out whether the story is true."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Gesprek in ’n aanlyn speletjie","en":"A chat in an online game"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato speel ’n aanlyn speletjie. ’n Speler wat sê hy heet Sam en is 11 jaar oud, vra watter skool sy bywoon en of sy vir hom ’n foto van haarself kan stuur. Hy sê: “Moenie vir jou ouers sê nie, hulle sal nie verstaan nie.” Is dit veilig? Wat moet sy doen?","en":"Lerato is playing an online game. A player who says his name is Sam and that he is 11 years old asks which school she goes to and whether she can send him a photo of herself. He says: “Don’t tell your parents, they won’t understand.” Is this safe? What should she do?"},"steps":[{"af":"**Dink aan wat jy weet:** Lerato kan nie seker wees wie Sam regtig is nie. Iemand wat sê hy is 11, kan ’n volwassene wees.","en":"**Think about what you know:** Lerato cannot be sure who Sam really is. Someone who says he is 11 could be an adult."},{"af":"**Soek die waarskuwingstekens:** hy vra persoonlike inligting (haar skool), hy vra ’n foto en hy wil hê sy moet dit geheim hou vir haar ouers. Dit is drie tekens van ’n onveilige verhouding.","en":"**Look for the warning signs:** he asks for personal information (her school), he asks for a photo and he wants her to keep it secret from her parents. These are three signs of an unsafe relationship."},{"af":"**Tree op:** sy antwoord nie, stuur niks nie en wys die boodskappe dadelik vir haar ouers of ’n ander vertroude volwassene.","en":"**Take action:** she does not reply, sends nothing and shows the messages to her parents or another trusted adult immediately."}],"answer":{"af":"Nee, dit is nie veilig nie. Sy moet nie antwoord of ’n foto stuur nie, en die boodskappe vir ’n vertroude volwassene wys.","en":"No, it is not safe. She must not reply or send a photo, and she should show the messages to a trusted adult."}},{"title":{"af":"Veilige of onveilige verhouding?","en":"Safe or unsafe relationship?"},"problem":{"af":"Aisha se netbalafrigter oefen die span op die skoolveld terwyl ouers kyk, en sê altyd vir die meisies om hul ouers te vertel van die oefening. ’n Ouer buurman gee vir Aisha elke dag lekkers en sê: “Kom kuier by my, maar moenie vir jou ma sê nie.” Watter verhouding is veilig en watter een is onveilig? Verduidelik.","en":"Aisha’s netball coach trains the team on the school field while parents watch, and always tells the girls to tell their parents about practice. An older neighbour gives Aisha sweets every day and says: “Come and visit me, but don’t tell your mom.” Which relationship is safe and which one is unsafe? Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"**Kyk na die afrigter:** alles gebeur oop en bloot, ander volwassenes is daar en die ouers word ingelig. Dit is tekens van ’n veilige verhouding.","en":"**Look at the coach:** everything happens in the open, other adults are there and the parents are kept informed. These are signs of a safe relationship."},{"af":"**Kyk na die buurman:** hy gee gereeld geskenke, wil hê sy moet alleen kom kuier en vra dat sy dit geheim hou vir haar ma. Dit is waarskuwingstekens van ’n onveilige verhouding.","en":"**Look at the neighbour:** he gives gifts regularly, wants her to visit alone and asks her to keep it secret from her mom. These are warning signs of an unsafe relationship."},{"af":"**Wat Aisha moet doen:** sy moenie gaan kuier nie en moet dit dadelik vir haar ma of ’n ander vertroude volwassene vertel.","en":"**What Aisha should do:** she should not go to visit and must tell her mom or another trusted adult immediately."}],"answer":{"af":"Die afrigter is ’n veilige verhouding (oop, ouers weet). Die buurman is onveilig (geskenke, alleen, geheim). Aisha moet dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene vertel.","en":"The coach is a safe relationship (open, parents know). The neighbour is unsafe (gifts, alone, secret). Aisha must tell a trusted adult."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wie is ’n vreemdeling?","en":"Who is a stranger?"},"options":[{"af":"Net iemand wat eng of gevaarlik lyk","en":"Only someone who looks scary or dangerous"},{"af":"Enigiemand wat jy nie goed ken nie, al lyk hulle vriendelik","en":"Anyone you don’t know well, even if they look friendly"},{"af":"Enige volwassene in jou familie","en":"Any adult in your family"},{"af":"Jou beste vriend se ma, wat jy goed ken","en":"Your best friend’s mom, whom you know well"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Vreemdeling is enigiemand wat jy nie goed ken nie. Jy kan nie aan iemand se voorkoms sien of hulle veilig is nie – daarom is die reëls vir alle vreemdelinge dieselfde.","en":"A stranger is anyone you don’t know well. You can’t tell from someone’s appearance whether they are safe – that is why the rules are the same for all strangers."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n waarskuwingsteken van ’n onveilige verhouding?","en":"Which one is a warning sign of an unsafe relationship?"},"options":[{"af":"Die persoon respekteer dit as jy “nee” sê","en":"The person respects it when you say “no”"},{"af":"Jou ouers ken die persoon goed","en":"Your parents know the person well"},{"af":"Julle doen aktiwiteite saam met ander mense","en":"You do activities together with other people"},{"af":"Die persoon vra jou om ’n geheim vir jou ouers te hou","en":"The person asks you to keep a secret from your parents"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Veilige volwassene sal nooit vra dat jy geheime vir jou ouers hou nie. As iemand dit vra, is dit ’n waarskuwing en moet jy dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene vertel.","en":"A safe adult will never ask you to keep secrets from your parents. If someone asks this, it is a warning and you should tell a trusted adult."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Jy mag “nee” sê vir ’n volwassene wat jou onveilig laat voel.","en":"You may say “no” to an adult who makes you feel unsafe."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Jy het die reg om veilig te wees. As iemand – selfs ’n volwassene – jou onveilig laat voel, mag jy hard “Nee!” sê, weggaan en dit vertel.","en":"True. You have the right to be safe. If someone – even an adult – makes you feel unsafe, you may say “No!” loudly, go away and tell someone."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die drie stappe as jy onveilig voel, is: Nee – Gaan weg – ___.","en":"The three steps when you feel unsafe are: No – Go – ___."},"answers":{"af":["Vertel"],"en":["Tell"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Wag","Vergeet","Wegkruip"],"en":["Wait","Forget","Hide"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die laaste stap is om dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene te vertel. Om dit te vergeet of weg te steek, beteken dat niemand jou kan help of ander kinders kan beskerm nie.","en":"The last step is to tell a trusted adult. Forgetting or hiding it means that nobody can help you or protect other children."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter inligting moet jy NIE aanlyn deel met iemand wat jy net aanlyn ken nie?","en":"Which information should you NOT share online with someone you only know online?"},"options":[{"af":"Jou huisadres","en":"Your home address"},{"af":"Jou gunstelingkleur","en":"Your favourite colour"},{"af":"Jou gunstelingdier","en":"Your favourite animal"},{"af":"Jou gunstelingsport","en":"Your favourite sport"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Jou adres is persoonlike inligting – dit wys iemand waar om jou te kry. Jou gunstelingkleur, -dier of -sport sê niks oor waar jy is nie.","en":"Your address is personal information – it shows someone where to find you. Your favourite colour, animal or sport says nothing about where you are."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke situasie by die veilige ding om te doen.","en":"Match each situation to the safe thing to do."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"’n Vreemdeling bied jou ’n saamrygeleentheid aan","en":"A stranger offers you a lift"},"r":{"af":"Sê “Nee!” en gaan weg na mense wat jy ken","en":"Say “No!” and go to people you know"}},{"l":{"af":"Jy verdwaal in ’n winkelsentrum","en":"You get lost in a shopping centre"},"r":{"af":"Vra ’n winkelassistent agter die toonbank om hulp","en":"Ask a shop assistant behind the counter for help"}},{"l":{"af":"Iemand aanlyn vra vir jou foto","en":"Someone online asks for your photo"},"r":{"af":"Moenie antwoord nie en wys dit vir ’n volwassene","en":"Don’t reply and show it to an adult"}},{"l":{"af":"’n Man sê jou pa het hom gestuur","en":"A man says your dad sent him"},"r":{"af":"Vra die gesinswagwoord","en":"Ask for the family password"}}],"explain":{"af":"In elke situasie beskerm jy jouself deur nie saam te gaan of te antwoord nie, en deur hulp te soek by ’n veilige persoon of ’n vertroude volwassene.","en":"In each situation you protect yourself by not going along or replying, and by looking for help from a safe person or a trusted adult."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Iemand stuur vir jou aanlyn ’n boodskap wat jou ongemaklik laat voel. Wat moet jy doen?","en":"Someone sends you a message online that makes you feel uncomfortable. What should you do?"},"options":[{"af":"Antwoord en vra wat hy bedoel","en":"Reply and ask what he means"},{"af":"Die boodskap uitvee en vir niemand sê nie","en":"Delete the message and tell nobody"},{"af":"Nie antwoord nie en dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene wys","en":"Not reply and show it to a trusted adult"},{"af":"Dit vir al jou vriende aanstuur","en":"Forward it to all your friends"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Moenie antwoord nie, want dan bly die gesprek aan die gang. Wys dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene sodat hulle kan help. As jy dit uitvee en stilbly, kan niemand jou beskerm nie.","en":"Don’t reply, because then the conversation keeps going. Show it to a trusted adult so that they can help. If you delete it and stay quiet, nobody can protect you."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Jou adres, skool en foonnommer is ___ inligting wat jy nie aanlyn moet deel nie.","en":"Your address, school and phone number are ___ information that you should not share online."},"answers":{"af":["persoonlike"],"en":["personal"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["openbare","snaakse","onbelangrike"],"en":["public","funny","unimportant"]}},"explain":{"af":"Persoonlike inligting wys wie jy is en waar iemand jou kan kry. Daarom hou jy dit privaat en deel dit net met mense wat jy en jou ouers vertrou.","en":"Personal information shows who you are and where someone can find you. That is why you keep it private and only share it with people you and your parents trust."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"By die winkel sê ’n man vir Nomsa haar pa het hom gestuur om haar te kom haal, maar hy ken nie die gesinswagwoord nie. Wat moet sy doen?","en":"At the shop a man tells Nomsa that her dad sent him to fetch her, but he doesn’t know the family password. What should she do?"},"options":[{"af":"Saamgaan, want hy ken haar pa se naam","en":"Go with him, because he knows her dad’s name"},{"af":"Hom die wagwoord vertel sodat hy dit volgende keer weet","en":"Tell him the password so that he knows it next time"},{"af":"Saamgaan as hy vir haar ’n geskenk gee","en":"Go with him if he gives her a present"},{"af":"Weier, in die winkel bly en ’n winkelassistent vra om haar pa te bel","en":"Refuse, stay in the shop and ask a shop assistant to phone her dad"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"As iemand nie die wagwoord ken nie, gaan jy nie saam nie – al ken hy name. Nomsa bly waar daar mense is en vra hulp om haar pa te kontak. Sy moet nooit die wagwoord vir ’n vreemdeling sê nie.","en":"If someone does not know the password, you don’t go along – even if he knows names. Nomsa stays where there are people and asks for help to contact her dad. She must never tell a stranger the password."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Gevaarlike persoon lyk altyd eng of onvriendelik.","en":"A dangerous person always looks scary or unfriendly."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Iemand wat kinders wil seermaak, is dikwels vriendelik en gee geskenke om die kind se vertroue te wen. Let op wat iemand doen, nie hoe hy of sy lyk nie.","en":"False. Someone who wants to hurt children is often friendly and gives gifts to win the child’s trust. Pay attention to what someone does, not what he or she looks like."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is ’n voordeel van ’n veilige verhouding?","en":"What is a benefit of a safe relationship?"},"options":[{"af":"Jy kry altyd jou eie sin","en":"You always get your own way"},{"af":"Jy het iemand met wie jy oor jou probleme kan praat","en":"You have someone you can talk to about your problems"},{"af":"Jy hoef nooit meer reëls te volg nie","en":"You never have to follow rules again"},{"af":"Jy kry elke dag geskenke","en":"You get presents every day"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In ’n veilige verhouding voel jy geliefd en beskerm, en jy kan oor probleme praat en raad kry. Om elke dag geskenke te kry, kan juis ’n waarskuwingsteken wees.","en":"In a safe relationship you feel loved and protected, and you can talk about problems and get advice. Getting presents every day can actually be a warning sign."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Jy kan Childline gratis bel by die nommer ___.","en":"You can call Childline for free on the number ___."},"answers":{"af":["116"],"en":["116"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["10111","10177","112"],"en":["10111","10177","112"]}},"explain":{"af":"Childline se nommer is 116 en die oproep is gratis. 10111 is die polisie, 10177 is die nommer vir ’n ambulans of die brandweer, en 112 is die noodnommer van ’n selfoon.","en":"Childline’s number is 116 and the call is free. 10111 is the police, 10177 is the number for an ambulance or the fire brigade, and 112 is the emergency number from a cellphone."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is dit ’n waarskuwingsteken as ’n volwassene vir ’n kind geskenke gee en sê: “Dis ons geheim”?","en":"Why is it a warning sign if an adult gives a child gifts and says: “It’s our secret”?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy probeer die kind se vertroue wen sodat ander mense niks agterkom nie","en":"He is trying to win the child’s trust so that other people don’t find out anything"},{"af":"Geskenke is altyd duur en kinders mag dit nie hê nie","en":"Gifts are always expensive and children may not have them"},{"af":"Volwassenes mag nooit vir kinders iets gee nie","en":"Adults may never give children anything"},{"af":"Die kind sal te veel lekkers eet","en":"The child will eat too many sweets"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Ouers, grootouers en ander veilige volwassenes gee ook geskenke, maar hulle vra nie dat jy dit geheim hou nie. Geskenke saam met ’n geheim is ’n manier om ’n kind stil te hou – vertel dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene.","en":"Parents, grandparents and other safe adults also give gifts, but they don’t ask you to keep them secret. Gifts together with a secret are a way to keep a child quiet – tell a trusted adult."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter het in ’n groot winkelsentrum verdwaal. By wie kan hy die veiligste hulp vra?","en":"Pieter is lost in a big shopping centre. From whom can he most safely ask for help?"},"options":[{"af":"Iemand wat alleen in ’n motor op die parkeerterrein sit","en":"Someone sitting alone in a car in the parking lot"},{"af":"’n Tiener wat aanbied om hom huis toe te neem","en":"A teenager who offers to take him home"},{"af":"’n Winkelassistent agter die toonbank van ’n winkel","en":"A shop assistant behind the counter of a shop"},{"af":"Enigiemand wat sy naam roep","en":"Anyone who calls his name"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Winkelassistent werk daar, is tussen ander mense en kan oor die luidspreker of foon jou ouers help soek. Moenie wegloop met iemand of in ’n motor klim nie.","en":"A shop assistant works there, is among other people and can help find your parents over the loudspeaker or phone. Don’t walk off with someone or get into a car."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Sosiale verantwoordelikheid","en":"Social responsibility"},"topics":[{"id":"lv5-t2-diskriminasie-regte","title":{"af":"Diskriminasie, stereotipering en kinderregte","en":"Discrimination, stereotyping and children’s rights"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal diskriminasie, stereotipering en vooroordeel kan herken, kinders se regte en verantwoordelikhede kan noem en kan verduidelik wat gedoen kan word as kinderregte geskend word.","en":"You will be able to recognise discrimination, stereotyping and bias, name children’s rights and responsibilities, and explain what can be done when children’s rights are violated."},"summary":{"af":"## Stereotipering, vooroordeel en diskriminasie\n\nHierdie drie woorde klink moeilik, maar hulle gaan almal oor **onregverdige** maniere om oor mense te dink of hulle te behandel.\n\n| Woord | Wat dit beteken | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Stereotipering** | Om te dink dat almal in ’n groep dieselfde is. | “Alle seuns is goed in sport.” |\n| **Vooroordeel** | ’n Mening oor iemand wat jy vorm voordat jy hulle ken, sonder ’n goeie rede. | Pieter wil nie langs die nuwe seun sit nie, want hy praat ’n ander taal. |\n| **Diskriminasie** | Om iemand onregverdig te behandel omdat hulle anders is. | Kinders laat ’n meisie nie saamspeel nie, want sy is in ’n rolstoel. |\n\nDit begin dikwels in jou kop: eers **dink** jy iets onregverdigs (stereotipe), dan **voel** jy iets teenoor die persoon (vooroordeel), en dan **doen** jy iets onregverdigs (diskriminasie).\n\nDaar word soms teen mense gediskrimineer weens hulle ras, geslag, taal, geloof, ’n gestremdheid, hoe arm hulle is of hoe hulle lyk. Diskriminasie maak seer en gaan teen die **Grondwet** van Suid-Afrika, wat sê dat almal gelyk is.\n\nHoe jy dit kan teëwerk:\n\n- Leer mense ken voordat jy oor hulle besluit.\n- Moenie grappe maak wat ’n groep mense afkraak nie.\n- Sluit ander in en nooi die nuwe kind om saam te speel.\n- Staan op vir iemand wat onregverdig behandel word, en vertel ’n volwassene.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** “Meisies is goed met kinders” klink dalk na ’n kompliment, maar dit is steeds ’n **stereotipe**, want dit sê dat almal in ’n groep dieselfde is. Elke mens is uniek.\n\n## Kinders se regte\n\n’n **Reg** is iets waarop elke mens geregtig is, net omdat hy of sy ’n mens is. **Artikel 28** van die Grondwet beskerm spesiaal die regte van **kinders** (almal onder 18 jaar). Elke kind het die reg op:\n\n- ’n **naam en nasionaliteit** van geboorte af\n- **gesinsorg** of ouerlike sorg, of ander goeie sorg as hy of sy nie by die gesin kan woon nie\n- **basiese voeding**, **skuiling** en **basiese gesondheidsorg**\n- **beskerming** teen mishandeling, verwaarlosing en **uitbuiting** (soos kinderarbeid)\n\n’n Ander deel van die Grondwet (artikel 29) gee elkeen ook die reg op **basiese onderwys**.\n\n## Regte en verantwoordelikhede\n\n’n **Verantwoordelikheid** is iets wat jy behoort te doen. Saam met elke reg kom ’n verantwoordelikheid teenoor ander.\n\n| Reg | Verantwoordelikheid |\n|---|---|\n| Ek het die reg op onderwys. | Ek gaan skool toe, luister en doen my huiswerk. |\n| Ek het die reg om veilig te wees. | Ek boelie of slaan nie ander nie. |\n| Ek het die reg op gesondheidsorg. | Ek sorg vir my liggaam en neem medisyne soos die dokter sê. |\n| Ek het die reg op respek. | Ek behandel ander met respek. |\n\n> **Onthou:** Elke kind het hierdie regte – ongeag wie hulle is of waar hulle woon.\n\n## Wanneer kinderregte geskend word\n\nAs iemand ’n kind se regte verbreek, noem ons dit ’n **skending** van kinderregte. Voorbeelde:\n\n- **Kinderarbeid:** ’n kind moet werk doen wat te swaar of gevaarlik is, of wat hom of haar uit die skool hou. In Suid-Afrika mag niemand ’n kind onder 15 jaar in diens neem nie. (Om tuis met take soos skottelgoed te help, is nie kinderarbeid nie.)\n- **Verwaarlosing:** ’n kind kry nie genoeg kos, klere, skuiling, sorg of mediese hulp nie.\n- **Mishandeling:** iemand maak ’n kind seer.\n\nWat kan gedoen word? Die kind, of ’n bekommerde vriend, kan dit vir ’n **vertroude volwassene** of ’n onderwyser vertel, of **Childline** by **116** bel (gratis). Die **polisie (10111)** en **maatskaplike werkers** help om kinders te beskerm.","en":"## Stereotyping, bias and discrimination\n\nThese three words sound difficult, but they are all about **unfair** ways of thinking about people or treating them.\n\n| Word | What it means | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Stereotyping** | Thinking that everyone in a group is the same. | “All boys are good at sport.” |\n| **Bias** | An opinion about someone that you form before you know them, without a good reason. | Pieter doesn’t want to sit next to the new boy, because he speaks a different language. |\n| **Discrimination** | Treating someone unfairly because they are different. | Children don’t let a girl join in the game, because she is in a wheelchair. |\n\nIt often starts in your head: first you **think** something unfair (stereotype), then you **feel** something towards the person (bias), and then you **do** something unfair (discrimination).\n\nPeople are sometimes discriminated against because of their race, gender, language, religion, a disability, how poor they are or what they look like. Discrimination hurts and goes against the **Constitution** of South Africa, which says that everyone is equal.\n\nHow you can work against it:\n\n- Get to know people before you make up your mind about them.\n- Don’t make jokes that put a group of people down.\n- Include others and invite the new child to play.\n- Stand up for someone who is treated unfairly, and tell an adult.\n\n> **Common mistake:** “Girls are good with children” may sound like a compliment, but it is still a **stereotype**, because it says that everyone in a group is the same. Every person is unique.\n\n## Children’s rights\n\nA **right** is something that every person is entitled to, just because he or she is a human being. **Section 28** of the Constitution specially protects the rights of **children** (everyone under 18 years). Every child has the right to:\n\n- a **name and nationality** from birth\n- **family care** or parental care, or other proper care if he or she cannot live with the family\n- **basic nutrition**, **shelter** and **basic health care**\n- **protection** from abuse, neglect and **exploitation** (such as child labour)\n\nAnother part of the Constitution (section 29) also gives everyone the right to a **basic education**.\n\n## Rights and responsibilities\n\nA **responsibility** is something you ought to do. With every right comes a responsibility towards others.\n\n| Right | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| I have the right to education. | I go to school, listen and do my homework. |\n| I have the right to be safe. | I don’t bully or hit others. |\n| I have the right to health care. | I look after my body and take medicine as the doctor says. |\n| I have the right to respect. | I treat others with respect. |\n\n> **Remember:** Every child has these rights – no matter who they are or where they live.\n\n## When children’s rights are violated\n\nWhen someone breaks a child’s rights, we call it a **violation** of children’s rights. Examples:\n\n- **Child labour:** a child has to do work that is too heavy or dangerous, or that keeps him or her out of school. In South Africa nobody may employ a child under 15 years. (Helping at home with chores like washing dishes is not child labour.)\n- **Neglect:** a child does not get enough food, clothes, shelter, care or medical help.\n- **Abuse:** someone hurts a child.\n\nWhat can be done? The child, or a worried friend, can tell a **trusted adult** or a teacher, or call **Childline** on **116** (free). The **police (10111)** and **social workers** help to protect children."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Stereotipering","en":"Stereotyping"},"def":{"af":"Om te dink dat almal in ’n groep mense dieselfde is of op dieselfde manier optree.","en":"Thinking that everyone in a group of people is the same or behaves in the same way."}},{"term":{"af":"Vooroordeel","en":"Bias"},"def":{"af":"’n Mening of gevoel oor iemand wat jy vorm voordat jy hulle ken, sonder ’n goeie rede.","en":"An opinion or feeling about someone that you form before you know them, without a good reason."}},{"term":{"af":"Diskriminasie","en":"Discrimination"},"def":{"af":"Om iemand onregverdig te behandel omdat hulle anders is, byvoorbeeld weens hulle taal, geslag of ’n gestremdheid.","en":"Treating someone unfairly because they are different, for example because of their language, gender or a disability."}},{"term":{"af":"Reg","en":"Right"},"def":{"af":"Iets waarop elke mens geregtig is, net omdat hy of sy ’n mens is, soos die reg om veilig te wees.","en":"Something that every person is entitled to, just because he or she is a human being, like the right to be safe."}},{"term":{"af":"Verantwoordelikheid","en":"Responsibility"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat jy behoort te doen; dit gaan saam met ’n reg, soos om skool toe te gaan omdat jy die reg op onderwys het.","en":"Something you ought to do; it goes with a right, such as going to school because you have the right to education."}},{"term":{"af":"Grondwet","en":"Constitution"},"def":{"af":"Die hoogste wet van Suid-Afrika, wat die regte van alle mense, ook kinders, beskerm.","en":"The highest law of South Africa, which protects the rights of all people, including children."}},{"term":{"af":"Kinderarbeid","en":"Child labour"},"def":{"af":"Werk wat ’n kind moet doen wat te swaar of gevaarlik is, of wat hom of haar uit die skool hou.","en":"Work a child has to do that is too heavy or dangerous, or that keeps him or her out of school."}},{"term":{"af":"Verwaarlosing","en":"Neglect"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n kind nie die kos, klere, skuiling, sorg of mediese hulp kry wat hy of sy nodig het nie.","en":"When a child does not get the food, clothes, shelter, care or medical help he or she needs."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitbuiting","en":"Exploitation"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer iemand ’n kind onregverdig gebruik om self voordeel te trek, byvoorbeeld deur die kind te laat werk.","en":"When someone unfairly uses a child to benefit themselves, for example by making the child work."}},{"term":{"af":"Skending","en":"Violation"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer iemand ’n reg verbreek of ignoreer.","en":"When someone breaks or ignores a right."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Stereotipe, vooroordeel of diskriminasie?","en":"Stereotype, bias or discrimination?"},"problem":{"af":"Sê of elke situasie ’n voorbeeld is van stereotipering, vooroordeel of diskriminasie: (a) Johan sê: “Meisies kan nie sokker speel nie.” (b) Aisha besluit sy sal nie van die nuwe meisie hou nie, nog voordat sy met haar gepraat het. (c) Die span weier om Sipho te laat speel omdat hy ’n gehoorapparaat dra.","en":"Say whether each situation is an example of stereotyping, bias or discrimination: (a) Johan says: “Girls can’t play soccer.” (b) Aisha decides she won’t like the new girl, even before she has spoken to her. (c) The team refuses to let Sipho play because he wears a hearing aid."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Johan sê iets oor **alle** meisies asof hulle almal dieselfde is. Dit is ’n **stereotipe**.","en":"(a) Johan says something about **all** girls as if they are all the same. That is a **stereotype**."},{"af":"(b) Aisha vorm ’n mening oor die meisie **voordat** sy haar ken. Dit is ’n **vooroordeel**.","en":"(b) Aisha forms an opinion about the girl **before** she knows her. That is **bias**."},{"af":"(c) Die span **doen** iets onregverdigs aan Sipho omdat hy anders is – hulle sluit hom uit. Dit is **diskriminasie**.","en":"(c) The team **does** something unfair to Sipho because he is different – they exclude him. That is **discrimination**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) stereotipering; (b) vooroordeel; (c) diskriminasie","en":"(a) stereotyping, (b) bias, (c) discrimination"}},{"title":{"af":"Regte gaan saam met verantwoordelikhede","en":"Rights go with responsibilities"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo sê: “Ek het die reg op onderwys, so ek kan in die klas doen wat ek wil.” Is hy reg? Verduidelik.","en":"Thabo says: “I have the right to education, so I can do whatever I like in class.” Is he right? Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"Thabo het wel die reg op onderwys – dit beteken hy mag skool toe gaan en leer.","en":"Thabo does have the right to education – it means he may go to school and learn."},{"af":"Saam met hierdie reg kom ’n **verantwoordelikheid**: om te luister, sy werk te doen en die ander nie te steur nie.","en":"With this right comes a **responsibility**: to listen, do his work and not disturb the others."},{"af":"As Thabo doen wat hy wil, steur hy die ander leerders, en dan skend hy húlle reg op onderwys.","en":"If Thabo does whatever he likes, he disturbs the other learners, and then he violates their right to education."}],"answer":{"af":"Nee. Sy reg op onderwys gaan saam met die verantwoordelikheid om te leer en ander nie te steur nie, want hulle het dieselfde reg.","en":"No. His right to education goes with the responsibility to learn and not to disturb others, because they have the same right."}},{"title":{"af":"Herken kinderarbeid","en":"Recognise child labour"},"problem":{"af":"Zanele is 10 jaar oud. Sy moet elke dag van vroeg tot laat by ’n taxistaanplek vrugte verkoop vir ’n man wat haar min betaal, en sy gaan nie meer skool toe nie. Watter regte word geskend, en wat kan gedoen word?","en":"Zanele is 10 years old. Every day she has to sell fruit at a taxi rank from early until late for a man who pays her very little, and she no longer goes to school. Which rights are being violated, and what can be done?"},"steps":[{"af":"**Herken die probleem:** sy werk lang ure vir iemand anders en kan nie skool toe gaan nie. Dit is **kinderarbeid** en **uitbuiting**.","en":"**Recognise the problem:** she works long hours for someone else and cannot go to school. This is **child labour** and **exploitation**."},{"af":"**Noem die regte:** haar reg op beskerming teen uitbuiting (artikel 28) en haar reg op basiese onderwys word geskend. Sy is ook onder 15, so niemand mag haar in diens neem nie.","en":"**Name the rights:** her right to protection from exploitation (section 28) and her right to a basic education are being violated. She is also under 15, so nobody may employ her."},{"af":"**Kry hulp:** ’n bekommerde persoon kan Childline (116) of die polisie (10111) bel, of ’n maatskaplike werker kontak, sodat Zanele beskerm word en terug skool toe kan gaan.","en":"**Get help:** a worried person can call Childline (116) or the police (10111), or contact a social worker, so that Zanele is protected and can go back to school."}],"answer":{"af":"Haar reg op beskerming teen uitbuiting en haar reg op onderwys word geskend. Iemand moet Childline (116), die polisie (10111) of ’n maatskaplike werker kontak.","en":"Her right to protection from exploitation and her right to education are being violated. Someone should contact Childline (116), the police (10111) or a social worker."}},{"title":{"af":"Huistake of kinderarbeid?","en":"Chores or child labour?"},"problem":{"af":"Nomsa was ná aandete die skottelgoed en gee soggens die hoenders kos voordat sy skool toe gaan. Haar maat sê dit is kinderarbeid. Is dit? Verduidelik.","en":"Nomsa washes the dishes after supper and feeds the chickens in the morning before she goes to school. Her friend says this is child labour. Is it? Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"Kyk na die soort werk: dit is ligte take wat by haar ouderdom pas en nie gevaarlik is nie.","en":"Look at the kind of work: these are light chores that suit her age and are not dangerous."},{"af":"Kyk of dit haar uit die skool hou: nee, sy gaan elke dag skool toe en het tyd vir huiswerk en speel.","en":"Check whether it keeps her out of school: no, she goes to school every day and has time for homework and play."},{"af":"Om tuis te help, is ’n **verantwoordelikheid** as deel van die gesin – dit is nie uitbuiting nie.","en":"Helping at home is a **responsibility** as part of the family – it is not exploitation."}],"answer":{"af":"Nee. Ligte huistake wat by haar ouderdom pas en haar nie uit die skool hou nie, is ’n verantwoordelikheid, nie kinderarbeid nie.","en":"No. Light chores that suit her age and do not keep her out of school are a responsibility, not child labour."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is ’n stereotipe?","en":"What is a stereotype?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Reël wat almal by die skool moet volg","en":"A rule that everyone at school must follow"},{"af":"’n Reg wat in die Grondwet staan","en":"A right that is written in the Constitution"},{"af":"’n Idee dat almal in ’n groep dieselfde is","en":"An idea that everyone in a group is the same"},{"af":"’n Mening wat jy vorm nadat jy iemand goed leer ken het","en":"An opinion you form after getting to know someone well"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"’n Stereotipe is ’n vaste idee dat almal in ’n groep dieselfde is, soos “Alle seuns hou van sokker.” Om ’n mening te vorm nadat jy iemand goed ken, is regverdig – dit is nie ’n stereotipe nie.","en":"A stereotype is a fixed idea that everyone in a group is the same, like “All boys like soccer.” Forming an opinion after you know someone well is fair – that is not a stereotype."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Om iemand onregverdig te behandel omdat hulle anders is, heet ___.","en":"Treating someone unfairly because they are different is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["diskriminasie"],"en":["discrimination"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["stereotipering","verantwoordelikheid","gelykheid"],"en":["stereotyping","responsibility","equality"]}},"explain":{"af":"Diskriminasie is ’n **aksie** – jy doen iets onregverdigs aan iemand. Stereotipering is net ’n **idee** in jou kop, al lei dit dikwels tot diskriminasie.","en":"Discrimination is an **action** – you do something unfair to someone. Stereotyping is only an **idea** in your head, although it often leads to discrimination."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter situasie is ’n voorbeeld van diskriminasie?","en":"Which situation is an example of discrimination?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Leerder word uit ’n groep gesluit omdat hy ’n ander taal praat","en":"A learner is left out of a group because he speaks a different language"},{"af":"’n Leerder word gekies vir die koor omdat sy mooi sing","en":"A learner is chosen for the choir because she sings well"},{"af":"’n Leerder kry ’n prys omdat hy hard gewerk het","en":"A learner gets a prize because he worked hard"},{"af":"’n Leerder moet wag vir sy beurt om te praat","en":"A learner has to wait for his turn to speak"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Om iemand uit te sluit oor iets soos taal, is onregverdig – dit is diskriminasie. Om gekies te word omdat jy mooi sing of hard gewerk het, is regverdig, want dit gaan oor wat jy gedoen het.","en":"Excluding someone because of something like language is unfair – that is discrimination. Being chosen because you sing well or worked hard is fair, because it is about what you did."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Om tuis die skottelgoed te was, is kinderarbeid.","en":"Washing the dishes at home is child labour."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Ligte huistake wat by jou ouderdom pas en jou nie uit die skool hou nie, is ’n verantwoordelikheid. Kinderarbeid is werk wat te swaar of gevaarlik is, of wat ’n kind uit die skool hou.","en":"False. Light chores that suit your age and don’t keep you out of school are a responsibility. Child labour is work that is too heavy or dangerous, or that keeps a child out of school."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n kinderreg wat in artikel 28 van die Grondwet staan?","en":"Which one is a children’s right that is in section 28 of the Constitution?"},"options":[{"af":"Die reg om ’n selfoon te hê","en":"The right to have a cellphone"},{"af":"Die reg om so laat op te bly as wat jy wil","en":"The right to stay up as late as you like"},{"af":"Die reg om te kies om nie skool toe te gaan nie","en":"The right to choose not to go to school"},{"af":"Die reg op basiese voeding en skuiling","en":"The right to basic nutrition and shelter"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Artikel 28 beskerm kinders se basiese behoeftes, soos kos, skuiling, gesondheidsorg en gesinsorg. ’n Selfoon of laat opbly is ’n wens, nie ’n reg nie. Kinders het die reg op onderwys – dit is nie iets wat hulle kan kies om oor te slaan nie.","en":"Section 28 protects children’s basic needs, such as food, shelter, health care and family care. A cellphone or staying up late is a wish, not a right. Children have the right to education – it is not something they can choose to skip."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke reg by die verantwoordelikheid wat daarby hoort.","en":"Match each right to the responsibility that goes with it."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Die reg op onderwys","en":"The right to education"},"r":{"af":"Gaan skool toe en doen jou huiswerk","en":"Go to school and do your homework"}},{"l":{"af":"Die reg om veilig te wees","en":"The right to be safe"},"r":{"af":"Moenie ander boelie of slaan nie","en":"Don’t bully or hit others"}},{"l":{"af":"Die reg op gesondheidsorg","en":"The right to health care"},"r":{"af":"Sorg vir jou liggaam en volg die dokter se raad","en":"Look after your body and follow the doctor’s advice"}},{"l":{"af":"Die reg op respek","en":"The right to respect"},"r":{"af":"Behandel ander met respek","en":"Treat others with respect"}}],"explain":{"af":"Regte en verantwoordelikhede gaan saam: as jy ’n reg het, het ander mense dieselfde reg, en jy moet help om dit te beskerm.","en":"Rights and responsibilities go together: if you have a right, other people have the same right, and you must help to protect it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter verantwoordelikheid hoort by die reg om veilig te wees?","en":"Which responsibility goes with the right to be safe?"},"options":[{"af":"Om net met jou eie vriende te speel","en":"To play only with your own friends"},{"af":"Om ander nie te boelie of seer te maak nie","en":"Not to bully or hurt others"},{"af":"Om altyd die eerste in die ry te wees","en":"To always be first in the line"},{"af":"Om jou huiswerk betyds in te gee","en":"To hand in your homework on time"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"As jy die reg het om veilig te wees, het ander dit ook. Jou verantwoordelikheid is om hulle nie te boelie of seer te maak nie. Huiswerk betyds ingee is ’n goeie verantwoordelikheid, maar dit hoort by die reg op onderwys.","en":"If you have the right to be safe, so do others. Your responsibility is not to bully or hurt them. Handing in homework on time is a good responsibility, but it goes with the right to education."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer ’n kind nie genoeg kos, klere of sorg kry nie, noem ons dit ___.","en":"When a child does not get enough food, clothes or care, we call it ___."},"answers":{"af":["verwaarlosing"],"en":["neglect"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kinderarbeid","stereotipering","uitbuiting"],"en":["child labour","stereotyping","exploitation"]}},"explain":{"af":"Verwaarlosing beteken ’n kind se basiese behoeftes word nie versorg nie. Dit is ’n skending van die kind se reg op basiese voeding, skuiling en sorg.","en":"Neglect means a child’s basic needs are not looked after. It is a violation of the child’s right to basic nutrition, shelter and care."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter wil nie langs die nuwe seun sit nie, want hy het gehoor die seun is van ’n ander land – al het hulle nog nooit gepraat nie. Wat wys Pieter?","en":"Pieter doesn’t want to sit next to the new boy, because he heard the boy is from another country – even though they have never spoken. What is Pieter showing?"},"options":[{"af":"Respek","en":"Respect"},{"af":"Vooroordeel","en":"Bias"},{"af":"Empatie","en":"Empathy"},{"af":"Verantwoordelikheid","en":"Responsibility"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Pieter het ’n mening oor die seun gevorm voordat hy hom ken – dit is vooroordeel. As hy eers met die seun gesels, kan hy hom as ’n persoon leer ken.","en":"Pieter formed an opinion about the boy before knowing him – that is bias. If he first talks to the boy, he can get to know him as a person."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Artikel 28 van die Grondwet beskerm spesiaal die regte van kinders, dit is mense onder 18 jaar.","en":"Section 28 of the Constitution specially protects the rights of children, that is people under 18 years."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Artikel 28 gaan oor kinders, en die Grondwet sê ’n kind is iemand onder 18 jaar.","en":"True. Section 28 is about children, and the Constitution says a child is someone under 18 years."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Zanele (10) moet elke dag vrugte verkoop in plaas daarvan om skool toe te gaan. Watter reg word duidelik geskend?","en":"Zanele (10) has to sell fruit every day instead of going to school. Which right is clearly being violated?"},"options":[{"af":"Die reg op ’n naam en nasionaliteit","en":"The right to a name and nationality"},{"af":"Die reg om te stem","en":"The right to vote"},{"af":"Die reg op vryheid van geloof","en":"The right to freedom of religion"},{"af":"Die reg op basiese onderwys","en":"The right to a basic education"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Zanele kan nie skool toe gaan nie, so haar reg op basiese onderwys word geskend. Dit is ook kinderarbeid, en sy het die reg om teen uitbuiting beskerm te word.","en":"Zanele cannot go to school, so her right to a basic education is being violated. It is also child labour, and she has the right to be protected from exploitation."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In Suid-Afrika mag niemand ’n kind onder ___ jaar in diens neem nie.","en":"In South Africa nobody may employ a child under ___ years."},"answers":{"af":["15","vyftien"],"en":["15","fifteen"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["10","12","21"],"en":["10","12","21"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die wet verbied dat kinders onder 15 jaar in diens geneem word. Kinders moet eerder skool toe gaan, leer en speel.","en":"The law forbids employing children under 15 years. Children should rather go to school, learn and play."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die beste manier om diskriminasie in jou klas teë te werk?","en":"What is the best way to work against discrimination in your class?"},"options":[{"af":"Ander insluit en opstaan vir iemand wat uitgesluit word","en":"Including others and standing up for someone who is left out"},{"af":"Net met kinders speel wat soos jy is","en":"Only playing with children who are like you"},{"af":"Grappies oor ander groepe vertel, solank hulle nie hoor nie","en":"Telling jokes about other groups, as long as they don’t hear"},{"af":"Wegkyk as iemand onregverdig behandel word","en":"Looking away when someone is treated unfairly"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Diskriminasie word kleiner as mense ander insluit en opstaan vir wat reg is. Grappe wat ’n groep afkraak, is ook diskriminasie, al hoor die groep dit nie.","en":"Discrimination gets less when people include others and stand up for what is right. Jokes that put a group down are also discrimination, even if the group doesn’t hear them."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Kind se regte word geskend. Wie kan help om die kind te beskerm?","en":"A child’s rights are being violated. Who can help to protect the child?"},"options":[{"af":"Net die kind self","en":"Only the child himself or herself"},{"af":"Niemand, want dit is die gesin se privaat saak","en":"Nobody, because it is the family’s private business"},{"af":"’n Onderwyser, Childline (116), die polisie of ’n maatskaplike werker","en":"A teacher, Childline (116), the police or a social worker"},{"af":"Net ander kinders in die klas","en":"Only other children in the class"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Kinders hoef nie alleen ’n skending van hulle regte te hanteer nie. Onderwysers, Childline, die polisie (10111) en maatskaplike werkers het die taak om kinders te beskerm.","en":"Children don’t have to deal with a violation of their rights alone. Teachers, Childline, the police (10111) and social workers have the task of protecting children."}}]},{"id":"lv5-t2-mishandeling-geweld","title":{"af":"Kindermishandeling en gewelddadige situasies","en":"Child abuse and violent situations"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal weet dat elke kind die reg het om veilig te wees, dat mishandeling nooit die kind se skuld is nie, hoe om ’n gevaarlike situasie te herken en te verlaat, en by wie jy hulp kan kry.","en":"You will know that every child has the right to be safe, that abuse is never the child’s fault, how to recognise and leave a dangerous situation, and who you can go to for help."},"summary":{"af":"## Elke kind het die reg om veilig te wees\n\nElke kind het die reg om **veilig**, **geliefd** en **versorg** te wees. Die meeste grootmense wil kinders beskerm. Tog gebeur dit soms dat iemand ’n kind seermaak of nie na ’n kind omsien nie. Dit heet **kindermishandeling**. Dit is **altyd verkeerd** en dit is teen die wet.\n\nHierdie les is nie daar om jou bang te maak nie. Dit is daar om jou te help weet wat reg en verkeerd is, en waar jy hulp kan kry – vir jouself of vir ’n vriend.\n\n## Soorte mishandeling\n\n| Soort | Wat dit beteken |\n|---|---|\n| **Fisiese mishandeling** | Iemand maak ’n kind se liggaam doelbewus seer, byvoorbeeld deur te slaan of te skop. |\n| **Emosionele mishandeling** | Iemand maak ’n kind se gevoelens heeltyd seer, byvoorbeeld deur te dreig, uit te skel of te sê die kind is niks werd nie. |\n| **Verwaarlosing** | ’n Kind kry nie die kos, klere, skuiling, sorg of mediese hulp wat hy of sy nodig het nie. |\n| **Onveilige aanraking** | Iemand raak ’n kind se **privaat dele** aan, of wil hê die kind moet hulle privaat dele aanraak. |\n\nJou **privaat dele** is die dele van jou liggaam wat jou swemklere bedek. Hulle behoort aan jou. Net ’n dokter of verpleegster mag daarna kyk om jou gesond te hou, en dan moet jou ouer of ’n ander vertroude volwassene by wees.\n\n> **Onthou:** As iemand jou seermaak of onveilig aanraak, is dit **nooit jou skuld nie** – al sê die persoon dit is, en al is dit iemand wat jy ken en liefhet. Die grootmens is altyd verantwoordelik, nie die kind nie.\n\n## Goeie geheime en slegte geheime\n\nIemand wat ’n kind seermaak, sê soms: “Dis ons geheim” of “Niemand sal jou glo nie.” Dit is nie waar nie. Daar is altyd iemand wat sal luister.\n\n| ’n Goeie geheim (’n verrassing) | ’n Slegte geheim |\n|---|---|\n| Laat jou opgewonde en bly voel | Laat jou bang, ongemaklik of deurmekaar voel |\n| Word gou vertel, bv. ’n verjaardagpartytjie | Jy moet dit “vir altyd” hou |\n| Niemand word seergemaak nie | Iemand word seergemaak of is in gevaar |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Baie kinders dink hulle sal in die moeilikheid kom as hulle ’n slegte geheim vertel. Dit is nie so nie. ’n Geheim wat jou ongemaklik laat voel, **moet** jy vertel. Dit is nie skinder nie – dit beskerm jou en ander.\n\n## Wie kan help?\n\nPraat met iemand as jy of ’n vriend nie veilig voel nie. As die eerste persoon nie luister nie, vertel iemand anders – totdat iemand help.\n\n- ’n **vertroude volwassene**: ’n ouer, ouma of oupa, tannie of oom\n- jou **onderwyser** of die **skoolberader**\n- **Childline: 116** – die oproep is gratis\n- die **polisie (SAPD): 10111**, of **112** van ’n selfoon in ’n noodgeval\n- ’n **maatskaplike werker** – iemand wie se werk dit is om kinders en gesinne te beskerm en te help\n\n## Gewelddadige situasies\n\n**Geweld** is wanneer mense mekaar seermaak of dreig om mekaar seer te maak. Tekens dat ’n situasie gevaarlik raak:\n\n- mense skree baie hard vir mekaar of dreig mekaar\n- mense begin stoot en slaan\n- iemand het ’n wapen\n- ’n groep mense word kwaad en onrustig\n\nWat om te doen:\n\n1. **Moenie betrokke raak nie** en moenie probeer om ’n bakleiery te stop nie.\n2. **Gaan weg** – so vinnig en stil as moontlik.\n3. Gaan na ’n **veilige plek**: jou huis of ’n vertroude buurman se huis, die skool, ’n polisiekantoor, ’n kliniek of ’n winkel met mense.\n4. **Vertel** ’n vertroude volwassene, of vra ’n volwassene om **10111** te bel.","en":"## Every child has the right to be safe\n\nEvery child has the right to be **safe**, **loved** and **cared for**. Most grown-ups want to protect children. Still, it sometimes happens that someone hurts a child or does not look after a child. This is called **child abuse**. It is **always wrong** and it is against the law.\n\nThis lesson is not here to scare you. It is here to help you know what is right and wrong, and where you can get help – for yourself or for a friend.\n\n## Kinds of abuse\n\n| Kind | What it means |\n|---|---|\n| **Physical abuse** | Someone hurts a child’s body on purpose, for example by hitting or kicking. |\n| **Emotional abuse** | Someone hurts a child’s feelings all the time, for example by threatening, calling names or saying the child is worth nothing. |\n| **Neglect** | A child does not get the food, clothes, shelter, care or medical help he or she needs. |\n| **Unsafe touch** | Someone touches a child’s **private parts**, or wants the child to touch their private parts. |\n\nYour **private parts** are the parts of your body that your swimming costume covers. They belong to you. Only a doctor or nurse may look at them to keep you healthy, and then your parent or another trusted adult must be there.\n\n> **Remember:** If someone hurts you or touches you in an unsafe way, it is **never your fault** – even if the person says it is, and even if it is someone you know and love. The grown-up is always responsible, not the child.\n\n## Good secrets and bad secrets\n\nSomeone who hurts a child sometimes says: “It’s our secret” or “Nobody will believe you.” That is not true. There is always someone who will listen.\n\n| A good secret (a surprise) | A bad secret |\n|---|---|\n| Makes you feel excited and happy | Makes you feel scared, uncomfortable or confused |\n| Is told soon, e.g. a birthday party | You have to keep it “forever” |\n| Nobody gets hurt | Someone is being hurt or is in danger |\n\n> **Common mistake:** Many children think they will get into trouble if they tell a bad secret. That is not so. A secret that makes you feel uncomfortable is one you **must** tell. It is not telling tales – it protects you and others.\n\n## Who can help?\n\nTalk to someone if you or a friend does not feel safe. If the first person does not listen, tell someone else – until someone helps.\n\n- a **trusted adult**: a parent, grandmother or grandfather, aunt or uncle\n- your **teacher** or the **school counsellor**\n- **Childline: 116** – the call is free\n- the **police (SAPS): 10111**, or **112** from a cellphone in an emergency\n- a **social worker** – someone whose job it is to protect and help children and families\n\n## Violent situations\n\n**Violence** is when people hurt each other or threaten to hurt each other. Signs that a situation is becoming dangerous:\n\n- people shout very loudly at each other or threaten each other\n- people start pushing and hitting\n- someone has a weapon\n- a group of people gets angry and restless\n\nWhat to do:\n\n1. **Don’t get involved** and don’t try to stop a fight.\n2. **Go away** – as quickly and quietly as possible.\n3. Go to a **safe place**: your home or a trusted neighbour’s home, the school, a police station, a clinic or a shop with people in it.\n4. **Tell** a trusted adult, or ask an adult to call **10111**."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Kindermishandeling","en":"Child abuse"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer iemand ’n kind seermaak of nie na ’n kind omsien nie; dit is altyd verkeerd en teen die wet.","en":"When someone hurts a child or does not look after a child; it is always wrong and against the law."}},{"term":{"af":"Fisiese mishandeling","en":"Physical abuse"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer iemand ’n kind se liggaam doelbewus seermaak.","en":"When someone hurts a child’s body on purpose."}},{"term":{"af":"Emosionele mishandeling","en":"Emotional abuse"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer iemand ’n kind se gevoelens heeltyd seermaak deur te dreig, uit te skel of af te kraak.","en":"When someone hurts a child’s feelings all the time by threatening, calling names or putting the child down."}},{"term":{"af":"Verwaarlosing","en":"Neglect"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n kind nie die kos, klere, skuiling, sorg of mediese hulp kry wat hy of sy nodig het nie.","en":"When a child does not get the food, clothes, shelter, care or medical help he or she needs."}},{"term":{"af":"Privaat dele","en":"Private parts"},"def":{"af":"Die dele van jou liggaam wat jou swemklere bedek; hulle behoort aan jou.","en":"The parts of your body that your swimming costume covers; they belong to you."}},{"term":{"af":"Slegte geheim","en":"Bad secret"},"def":{"af":"’n Geheim wat jou bang of ongemaklik laat voel, of waar iemand seergemaak word; dit moet jy vertel.","en":"A secret that makes you feel scared or uncomfortable, or where someone is being hurt; you must tell it."}},{"term":{"af":"Vertroude volwassene","en":"Trusted adult"},"def":{"af":"’n Grootmens wat jou veilig laat voel, na jou luister en jou sal help.","en":"A grown-up who makes you feel safe, listens to you and will help you."}},{"term":{"af":"Maatskaplike werker","en":"Social worker"},"def":{"af":"Iemand wie se werk dit is om kinders en gesinne te beskerm en te help.","en":"Someone whose job it is to protect and help children and families."}},{"term":{"af":"Geweld","en":"Violence"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer mense mekaar seermaak of dreig om mekaar seer te maak.","en":"When people hurt each other or threaten to hurt each other."}},{"term":{"af":"Veilige plek","en":"Safe place"},"def":{"af":"’n Plek waar daar vertroude mense is wat jou kan help, soos jou huis, die skool, ’n kliniek of ’n polisiekantoor.","en":"A place where there are trusted people who can help you, such as your home, the school, a clinic or a police station."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Goeie of slegte geheim?","en":"Good or bad secret?"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Lerato se pa vra haar om tot Saterdag stil te bly oor die verrassingspartytjie vir haar ma. (b) ’n Ouer seun sê vir Sipho: “As jy vir iemand vertel wat ek gedoen het, sal jy in groot moeilikheid wees.” Sipho voel bang. Watter geheim is goed en watter een is sleg? Wat moet Sipho doen?","en":"(a) Lerato’s dad asks her to keep quiet until Saturday about the surprise party for her mom. (b) An older boy tells Sipho: “If you tell anyone what I did, you’ll be in big trouble.” Sipho feels scared. Which secret is good and which one is bad? What should Sipho do?"},"steps":[{"af":"**Kyk na (a):** dit laat Lerato opgewonde voel, dit word Saterdag vertel en niemand word seergemaak nie. Dit is ’n **goeie geheim** – ’n verrassing.","en":"**Look at (a):** it makes Lerato feel excited, it will be told on Saturday and nobody gets hurt. It is a **good secret** – a surprise."},{"af":"**Kyk na (b):** Sipho voel bang, hy word gedreig en hy moet dit vir altyd hou. Dit is ’n **slegte geheim**.","en":"**Look at (b):** Sipho feels scared, he is being threatened and he has to keep it forever. It is a **bad secret**."},{"af":"**Wat Sipho moet doen:** hy moet dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene vertel, soos sy ma of sy onderwyser. Hy sal nie in die moeilikheid kom nie – dit is nie sy skuld nie.","en":"**What Sipho should do:** he must tell a trusted adult, like his mom or his teacher. He will not get into trouble – it is not his fault."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) is ’n goeie geheim (verrassing); (b) is ’n slegte geheim. Sipho moet dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene vertel.","en":"(a) is a good secret (a surprise); (b) is a bad secret. Sipho must tell a trusted adult."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Bakleiery op pad huis toe","en":"A fight on the way home"},"problem":{"af":"Anika stap ná skool huis toe. Voor die winkel op die hoek begin ’n groep mans hard skree en mekaar stoot. Wat moet sy doen?","en":"Anika is walking home after school. In front of the shop on the corner a group of men starts shouting loudly and pushing each other. What should she do?"},"steps":[{"af":"**Herken die gevaar:** hard skree en stoot is tekens dat die situasie gewelddadig kan raak.","en":"**Recognise the danger:** loud shouting and pushing are signs that the situation could become violent."},{"af":"**Moenie betrokke raak nie:** sy moet nie bly staan om te kyk of probeer om die mans te keer nie.","en":"**Don’t get involved:** she should not stand and watch or try to stop the men."},{"af":"**Gaan weg na ’n veilige plek:** sy loop vinnig en stil ’n ander pad, terug skool toe of na ’n vertroude buurman se huis.","en":"**Go to a safe place:** she walks quickly and quietly another way, back to school or to a trusted neighbour’s house."},{"af":"**Vertel:** sy vertel ’n vertroude volwassene wat gebeur het, wat die polisie by 10111 kan bel as dit nodig is.","en":"**Tell:** she tells a trusted adult what happened, who can call the police on 10111 if needed."}],"answer":{"af":"Sy moet nie betrokke raak nie, vinnig weggaan na ’n veilige plek en ’n vertroude volwassene vertel, wat 10111 kan bel.","en":"She must not get involved, should quickly go to a safe place and tell a trusted adult, who can call 10111."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Vriendin het hulp nodig","en":"A friend needs help"},"problem":{"af":"Nomsa vertel vir Aisha dat sy by die huis dikwels nie aandete kry nie en dat niemand saans na haar omsien nie. Sy vra Aisha om vir niemand te sê nie. Wat moet Aisha doen?","en":"Nomsa tells Aisha that at home she often gets no supper and that nobody looks after her in the evenings. She asks Aisha not to tell anyone. What should Aisha do?"},"steps":[{"af":"**Luister en glo haar:** Aisha kan sê: “Dankie dat jy my vertel het. Dit is nie jou skuld nie.”","en":"**Listen and believe her:** Aisha can say: “Thank you for telling me. It is not your fault.”"},{"af":"**Herken die probleem:** om nie genoeg kos en sorg te kry nie, is **verwaarlosing**. Dit is te groot vir twee kinders om alleen op te los.","en":"**Recognise the problem:** not getting enough food and care is **neglect**. It is too big for two children to solve alone."},{"af":"**Kry hulp:** Aisha moet dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene vertel, soos haar onderwyser of die skoolberader, of saam met Nomsa vir Childline by 116 bel.","en":"**Get help:** Aisha must tell a trusted adult, like her teacher or the school counsellor, or call Childline on 116 together with Nomsa."}],"answer":{"af":"Aisha moet luister, vir Nomsa sê dit is nie haar skuld nie, en dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene of Childline (116) vertel sodat Nomsa hulp kry.","en":"Aisha should listen, tell Nomsa it is not her fault, and tell a trusted adult or Childline (116) so that Nomsa gets help."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"As ’n grootmens ’n kind seermaak, wie se skuld is dit?","en":"If a grown-up hurts a child, whose fault is it?"},"options":[{"af":"Die kind s’n, as die kind stout was","en":"The child’s, if the child was naughty"},{"af":"Die grootmens s’n – nooit die kind s’n nie","en":"The grown-up’s – never the child’s"},{"af":"Albei s’n ewe veel","en":"Both of them equally"},{"af":"Niemand s’n nie, dis net slegte geluk","en":"Nobody’s, it is just bad luck"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Dit is nooit die kind se skuld nie, wat ook al gebeur het. Die grootmens is altyd verantwoordelik vir sy of haar eie dade. Die kind verdien hulp en beskerming.","en":"It is never the child’s fault, whatever happened. The grown-up is always responsible for his or her own actions. The child deserves help and protection."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As ’n geheim jou bang of ongemaklik laat voel, moet jy dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene vertel.","en":"If a secret makes you feel scared or uncomfortable, you should tell a trusted adult."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Slegte geheim moet vertel word. Jy sal nie in die moeilikheid kom nie – jy beskerm jouself en dalk ook ander kinders.","en":"True. A bad secret must be told. You will not get into trouble – you are protecting yourself and maybe other children too."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter nommer kan ’n kind gratis bel om met Childline te praat?","en":"Which number can a child call for free to talk to Childline?"},"options":[{"af":"10177","en":"10177"},{"af":"10111","en":"10111"},{"af":"112","en":"112"},{"af":"116","en":"116"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Childline se nommer is 116 en die oproep is gratis. 10111 is die polisie, 10177 is vir ’n ambulans of die brandweer en 112 is die noodnommer van ’n selfoon.","en":"Childline’s number is 116 and the call is free. 10111 is the police, 10177 is for an ambulance or the fire brigade and 112 is the emergency number from a cellphone."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die nommer van die polisie (SAPD) is ___.","en":"The number of the police (SAPS) is ___."},"answers":{"af":["10111","10 111"],"en":["10111","10 111"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["10177","116","911"],"en":["10177","116","911"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die polisie se nommer is 10111. Pasop vir 911 – dit is die noodnommer in Amerika wat jy dalk in flieks hoor, nie in Suid-Afrika nie.","en":"The police number is 10111. Watch out for 911 – that is the emergency number in America that you may hear in movies, not in South Africa."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n goeie geheim?","en":"Which one is a good secret?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Verrassingsgeskenk vir jou boetie se verjaardag volgende week","en":"A surprise present for your brother’s birthday next week"},{"af":"’n Ouer kind wat sê jy moet stilbly oor iets wat jou bang maak","en":"An older child who says you must keep quiet about something that scares you"},{"af":"Iemand wat jou geskenke gee en sê jou ouers mag nie weet nie","en":"Someone who gives you gifts and says your parents may not know"},{"af":"’n Vriend wat seergemaak word en vra dat jy niks sê nie","en":"A friend who is being hurt and asks you to say nothing"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Verrassing is ’n goeie geheim: dit maak mense bly, word gou vertel en niemand word seergemaak nie. Die ander drie laat jou ongemaklik voel of iemand is in gevaar – hulle moet vertel word.","en":"A surprise is a good secret: it makes people happy, it is told soon and nobody gets hurt. The other three make you feel uncomfortable or someone is in danger – they must be told."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Mense begin buite die snoepie baklei en skree. Wat is die veiligste ding om te doen?","en":"People start fighting and shouting outside the tuck shop. What is the safest thing to do?"},"options":[{"af":"Nader gaan om beter te sien wat gebeur","en":"Go closer to see better what is happening"},{"af":"Tussenin gaan staan om hulle te keer","en":"Go and stand between them to stop them"},{"af":"Vinnig weggaan en ’n vertroude volwassene vertel","en":"Quickly go away and tell a trusted adult"},{"af":"Dit met jou foon afneem en aanstuur","en":"Film it on your phone and send it on"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"In ’n gewelddadige situasie moet jy nie betrokke raak nie. Gaan vinnig weg na ’n veilige plek en vertel ’n volwassene, wat die polisie kan bel. Om nader te gaan of af te neem, kan jou in gevaar stel.","en":"In a violent situation you should not get involved. Quickly go to a safe place and tell an adult, who can call the police. Going closer or filming can put you in danger."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke helper by die regte nommer of beskrywing.","en":"Match each helper to the correct number or description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Childline","en":"Childline"},"r":{"af":"116 – gratis hulplyn vir kinders","en":"116 – free helpline for children"}},{"l":{"af":"Polisie (SAPD)","en":"Police (SAPS)"},"r":{"af":"10111","en":"10111"}},{"l":{"af":"Ambulans of brandweer","en":"Ambulance or fire brigade"},"r":{"af":"10177","en":"10177"}},{"l":{"af":"Noodnommer van ’n selfoon","en":"Emergency number from a cellphone"},"r":{"af":"112","en":"112"}},{"l":{"af":"Maatskaplike werker","en":"Social worker"},"r":{"af":"Beskerm en help kinders en gesinne","en":"Protects and helps children and families"}}],"explain":{"af":"Leer hierdie nommers uit jou kop of skryf hulle by die huis neer. Childline (116) is spesiaal vir kinders, en die oproep is gratis.","en":"Learn these numbers by heart or write them down at home. Childline (116) is specially for children, and the call is free."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter plek is ’n veilige plek om na toe te gaan as jy in gevaar is?","en":"Which place is a safe place to go to if you are in danger?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Leë veld waar niemand jou kan sien nie","en":"An empty field where nobody can see you"},{"af":"’n Donker steeg as kortpad","en":"A dark alley as a shortcut"},{"af":"’n Vreemdeling se motor","en":"A stranger’s car"},{"af":"’n Polisiekantoor of kliniek","en":"A police station or clinic"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Veilige plek is waar daar vertroude mense is wat jou kan help, soos ’n polisiekantoor, kliniek, die skool of ’n vertroude buurman se huis. Leë of donker plekke en vreemdelinge se motors is nie veilig nie.","en":"A safe place is where there are trusted people who can help you, such as a police station, clinic, the school or a trusted neighbour’s house. Empty or dark places and strangers’ cars are not safe."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die dele van jou liggaam wat jou swemklere bedek, is jou ___ dele.","en":"The parts of your body that your swimming costume covers are your ___ parts."},"answers":{"af":["privaat"],"en":["private"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["sterk","gesonde","groot"],"en":["strong","healthy","big"]}},"explain":{"af":"Jou privaat dele behoort aan jou. As iemand dit op ’n onveilige manier aanraak, is dit nie jou skuld nie, en jy moet dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene vertel.","en":"Your private parts belong to you. If someone touches them in an unsafe way, it is not your fault, and you must tell a trusted adult."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Iemand wat ’n kind seermaak, is altyd ’n vreemdeling.","en":"Someone who hurts a child is always a stranger."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Dikwels is dit iemand wat die kind ken. Daarom is dit belangrik om te onthou: as énigiemand jou seermaak of onveilig laat voel, mag jy nee sê en dit vertel.","en":"False. Often it is someone the child knows. That is why it is important to remember: if anyone hurts you or makes you feel unsafe, you may say no and tell someone."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jou vriend sê dat sy by die huis dikwels nie kos kry nie en vra dat jy niks sê nie. Wat moet jy doen?","en":"Your friend says that she often gets no food at home and asks you not to say anything. What should you do?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene vertel sodat sy hulp kry","en":"Tell a trusted adult so that she gets help"},{"af":"Stilbly, want jy het belowe","en":"Keep quiet, because you promised"},{"af":"Dit vir die hele klas vertel","en":"Tell the whole class"},{"af":"Vir haar sê dit is seker haar eie skuld","en":"Tell her it is probably her own fault"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Om nie genoeg kos en sorg te kry nie, is verwaarlosing. ’n Goeie vriend help haar om hulp te kry deur dit vir ’n vertroude volwassene of Childline (116) te vertel. Dit is nie haar skuld nie, en dit is privaat – nie iets vir die hele klas nie.","en":"Not getting enough food and care is neglect. A good friend helps her get help by telling a trusted adult or Childline (116). It is not her fault, and it is private – not something for the whole class."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer iemand ’n kind se gevoelens heeltyd seermaak deur te dreig en uit te skel, is dit ___ mishandeling.","en":"When someone hurts a child’s feelings all the time by threatening and calling names, it is ___ abuse."},"answers":{"af":["emosionele"],"en":["emotional"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["fisiese","finansiële","mediese"],"en":["physical","financial","medical"]}},"explain":{"af":"Emosionele mishandeling maak nie die liggaam seer nie, maar dit maak ’n kind se gevoelens en selfbeeld seer. Dit is ook verkeerd, en die kind kan hulp kry. Fisiese mishandeling maak die liggaam seer.","en":"Emotional abuse does not hurt the body, but it hurts a child’s feelings and self-concept. It is also wrong, and the child can get help. Physical abuse hurts the body."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo het ’n volwassene vertel dat iemand hom seermaak, maar die volwassene het hom nie geglo nie. Wat moet hy nou doen?","en":"Thabo told an adult that someone is hurting him, but the adult did not believe him. What should he do now?"},"options":[{"af":"Ophou praat daaroor, want niemand sal hom glo nie","en":"Stop talking about it, because nobody will believe him"},{"af":"Aanhou vertel vir ander vertroude volwassenes of Childline bel totdat iemand help","en":"Keep telling other trusted adults or call Childline until someone helps"},{"af":"Self die persoon terug seermaak","en":"Hurt the person back himself"},{"af":"Wegloop van die huis af sonder om iemand te sê","en":"Run away from home without telling anyone"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"As die eerste persoon nie luister nie, moet Thabo iemand anders vertel – ’n onderwyser, die skoolberader of Childline by 116. Daar is altyd iemand wat sal luister en help.","en":"If the first person does not listen, Thabo must tell someone else – a teacher, the school counsellor or Childline on 116. There is always someone who will listen and help."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is verwaarlosing?","en":"What is neglect?"},"options":[{"af":"Wanneer ’n kind vir ’n toets moet leer","en":"When a child has to study for a test"},{"af":"Wanneer ’n kind tuis help met die skottelgoed","en":"When a child helps with the dishes at home"},{"af":"Wanneer ’n kind nie die kos, klere of sorg kry wat hy nodig het nie","en":"When a child does not get the food, clothes or care he needs"},{"af":"Wanneer ’n kind se ouers sê hy moet vroeg gaan slaap","en":"When a child’s parents say he must go to bed early"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Verwaarlosing beteken ’n kind se basiese behoeftes – kos, klere, skuiling, sorg en mediese hulp – word nie versorg nie. Om tuis te help of vroeg te gaan slaap, is gewone deel van ’n gesin se lewe.","en":"Neglect means a child’s basic needs – food, clothes, shelter, care and medical help – are not looked after. Helping at home or going to bed early is a normal part of family life."}}]},{"id":"lv5-t2-ouderdom-gender","title":{"af":"Ouderdom en gender in Suid-Afrikaanse kulture","en":"Age and gender in South African cultures"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe ouer mense en kinders in verskillende kulture respek vir mekaar wys, hoe take tuis verander en waarom enige werk deur enige geslag gedoen kan word.","en":"You will be able to explain how older people and children in different cultures show respect for each other, how tasks at home are changing and why any job can be done by any gender."},"summary":{"af":"## Respek tussen ouer mense en kinders\n\nSuid-Afrika het baie **kulture**. ’n **Kultuur** is die manier van lewe van ’n groep mense: hulle taal, gebruike, kos, musiek, klere en waardes. Hoewel kulture van mekaar verskil, het baie van hulle iets in gemeen: kinders wys **respek** vir ouer mense, en ouer mense beskerm en leer kinders.\n\nKinders wys op verskillende maniere respek, byvoorbeeld:\n\n- hulle groet ouer mense vriendelik\n- hulle gebruik ’n titel soos *Oom* en *Tannie*, *Meneer* en *Mevrou*, of in Sesotho *Ntate* en *Mme*\n- hulle luister wanneer ouer mense praat en val hulle nie in die rede nie\n- in party gesinne gee of ontvang kinders iets met albei hande; in ander gesinne leer kinders om iemand in die oë te kyk wanneer hulle praat\n\nDie maniere verskil, maar die doel is dieselfde: om te wys dat jy die persoon waardeer.\n\nRespek werk in **albei rigtings**. Ouer mense moet ook kinders met respek behandel, na hulle luister en hulle beskerm. Ouer mense deel hulle **kennis en ervaring**, soos stories, tradisies en vaardighede. Kinders kan weer help met take, of hulle grootouers wys hoe om ’n selfoon te gebruik.\n\n## Verantwoordelikhede tuis\n\nVroeër het baie mense gedink dat sekere take net vir seuns en ander net vir meisies is. Vandag verander dit. Baie gesinne deel die take regverdig uit, ongeag of jy ’n seun of ’n meisie is.\n\n| Vroeër het baie mense gedink … | Vandag weet ons … |\n|---|---|\n| net meisies kook en was skottelgoed | seuns kan ook kook en skottelgoed was |\n| net seuns sny die gras en dra swaar goed | meisies kan ook in die tuin werk |\n| net ma’s sorg vir babas | pa’s kan babas ook bad, voed en troos |\n| net mans verdien die gesin se geld | mans en vroue werk albei om vir die gesin te sorg |\n\nVerantwoordelikhede verander ook soos jy **ouer** word. ’n Vyfjarige pak sy speelgoed weg, maar ’n tienjarige kan help om kos voor te berei of na ’n jonger kind te kyk. Take word dus volgens **ouderdom en vermoë** uitgedeel, nie volgens geslag nie.\n\n## Bydraes van mans en vroue in die gemeenskap\n\nMans en vroue lewer albei belangrike **bydraes** in die **gemeenskap**. Mans én vroue is dokters, verpleërs, onderwysers, boere, ingenieurs, polisiebeamptes, sakelui en leiers. Baie mense doen ook **vrywillige werk** sonder betaling, soos om by ’n sopkombuis te help, ’n sokkerspan af te rig of na bejaardes om te sien.\n\n## Genderstereotipes uitdaag\n\n**Gender** gaan oor die idees wat mense het oor hoe seuns en meisies, en mans en vroue, “moet” wees of optree. ’n **Genderstereotipe** is ’n vaste idee dat alle seuns of alle meisies op ’n sekere manier is, byvoorbeeld “Seuns huil nie” of “Meisies kan nie motors regmaak nie.”\n\nSulke stereotipes is onregverdig, want hulle beperk mense. ’n Seun wat graag wil dans of kook, of ’n meisie wat ’n vlieënier of ’n skrynwerker wil word, kan dit doen. **Enige werk kan deur enige geslag gedoen word**, solank die persoon die nodige vaardighede leer.\n\nDie **Grondwet** sê dat almal gelyk is en dat niemand onregverdig behandel mag word weens hulle geslag nie. **Gelykheid** beteken nie dat almal presies dieselfde is nie, maar dat almal dieselfde **kanse** en **respek** verdien.\n\n> **Onthou:** Respek werk in albei rigtings – tussen jonk en oud, en tussen seuns en meisies.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om te sê “In daardie kultuur doen al die vroue …” is ook ’n stereotipe. Binne elke kultuur verskil gesinne en mense van mekaar. Leer mense ken as **individue**.","en":"## Respect between older people and children\n\nSouth Africa has many **cultures**. A **culture** is the way of life of a group of people: their language, customs, food, music, clothing and values. Although cultures differ from each other, many of them have something in common: children show **respect** for older people, and older people protect and teach children.\n\nChildren show respect in different ways, for example:\n\n- they greet older people in a friendly way\n- they use a title like *Oom* and *Tannie* (Uncle and Auntie), *Mr* and *Mrs*, or in Sesotho *Ntate* and *Mme*\n- they listen when older people speak and do not interrupt them\n- in some families children give or receive something with both hands; in other families children learn to look someone in the eye when they speak\n\nThe ways differ, but the purpose is the same: to show that you value the person.\n\nRespect works in **both directions**. Older people must also treat children with respect, listen to them and protect them. Older people share their **knowledge and experience**, such as stories, traditions and skills. Children in turn can help with tasks, or show their grandparents how to use a cellphone.\n\n## Responsibilities at home\n\nIn the past many people thought that certain tasks were only for boys and others only for girls. Today this is changing. Many families share out the tasks fairly, no matter whether you are a boy or a girl.\n\n| In the past many people thought … | Today we know … |\n|---|---|\n| only girls cook and wash dishes | boys can also cook and wash dishes |\n| only boys cut the grass and carry heavy things | girls can also work in the garden |\n| only moms care for babies | dads can also bath, feed and comfort babies |\n| only men earn the family’s money | men and women both work to provide for the family |\n\nResponsibilities also change as you get **older**. A five-year-old packs away his toys, but a ten-year-old can help to prepare food or look after a younger child. So tasks are shared out according to **age and ability**, not according to gender.\n\n## Contributions of men and women in the community\n\nMen and women both make important **contributions** in the **community**. Men and women are doctors, nurses, teachers, farmers, engineers, police officers, business people and leaders. Many people also do **volunteer work** without pay, such as helping at a soup kitchen, coaching a soccer team or looking after elderly people.\n\n## Challenging gender stereotypes\n\n**Gender** is about the ideas people have about how boys and girls, and men and women, “should” be or behave. A **gender stereotype** is a fixed idea that all boys or all girls are a certain way, for example “Boys don’t cry” or “Girls can’t fix cars.”\n\nSuch stereotypes are unfair, because they limit people. A boy who would love to dance or cook, or a girl who wants to become a pilot or a carpenter, can do it. **Any job can be done by any gender**, as long as the person learns the necessary skills.\n\nThe **Constitution** says that everyone is equal and that nobody may be treated unfairly because of their gender. **Equality** does not mean that everyone is exactly the same, but that everyone deserves the same **chances** and **respect**.\n\n> **Remember:** Respect works in both directions – between young and old, and between boys and girls.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Saying “In that culture all the women …” is also a stereotype. Within every culture, families and people differ from each other. Get to know people as **individuals**."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Kultuur","en":"Culture"},"def":{"af":"Die manier van lewe van ’n groep mense, soos hulle taal, gebruike, kos, musiek en waardes.","en":"The way of life of a group of people, such as their language, customs, food, music and values."}},{"term":{"af":"Respek","en":"Respect"},"def":{"af":"Om iemand te waardeer en hulle gevoelens, mening en regte in ag te neem.","en":"Valuing someone and taking their feelings, opinions and rights into account."}},{"term":{"af":"Gender","en":"Gender"},"def":{"af":"Die idees wat ’n samelewing het oor hoe seuns en meisies, en mans en vroue, moet wees of optree.","en":"The ideas a society has about how boys and girls, and men and women, should be or behave."}},{"term":{"af":"Genderstereotipe","en":"Gender stereotype"},"def":{"af":"’n Vaste idee dat alle seuns of alle meisies op ’n sekere manier is, soos “Seuns huil nie.”","en":"A fixed idea that all boys or all girls are a certain way, like “Boys don’t cry.”"}},{"term":{"af":"Gelykheid","en":"Equality"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer almal dieselfde kanse en respek kry, ongeag hulle geslag, ouderdom of kultuur.","en":"When everyone gets the same chances and respect, no matter their gender, age or culture."}},{"term":{"af":"Verantwoordelikheid","en":"Responsibility"},"def":{"af":"’n Taak of plig wat jy behoort te doen, soos om tuis met die werk te help.","en":"A task or duty that you ought to do, such as helping with the work at home."}},{"term":{"af":"Bydrae","en":"Contribution"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat jy doen of gee om ander of die gemeenskap te help.","en":"Something you do or give to help others or the community."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemeenskap","en":"Community"},"def":{"af":"Die mense wat in dieselfde area woon of saamwerk, soos jou buurt, dorp of skool.","en":"The people who live in the same area or work together, such as your neighbourhood, town or school."}},{"term":{"af":"Vrywillige werk","en":"Volunteer work"},"def":{"af":"Werk wat iemand uit eie keuse en sonder betaling doen om ander te help.","en":"Work that someone does by choice and without pay to help others."}},{"term":{"af":"Tradisie","en":"Tradition"},"def":{"af":"’n Gebruik of gewoonte wat van ouer mense na jonger mense oorgedra word.","en":"A custom or habit that is passed on from older people to younger people."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Daag ’n genderstereotipe uit","en":"Challenge a gender stereotype"},"problem":{"af":"Zanele wil by die skool se robotika-klub aansluit. Liam sê: “Robotika is vir seuns. Meisies verstaan nie masjiene nie.” Verduidelik waarom dit ’n genderstereotipe is en hoe Zanele of ’n maat op ’n respekvolle manier kan antwoord.","en":"Zanele wants to join the school’s robotics club. Liam says: “Robotics is for boys. Girls don’t understand machines.” Explain why this is a gender stereotype and how Zanele or a classmate can answer in a respectful way."},"steps":[{"af":"**Herken die stereotipe:** Liam sê iets oor **alle** meisies, asof hulle almal dieselfde is. Dit is ’n vaste idee, nie ’n feit nie.","en":"**Recognise the stereotype:** Liam says something about **all** girls, as if they are all the same. It is a fixed idea, not a fact."},{"af":"**Dink aan die feite:** of jy masjiene verstaan, hang af van belangstelling en oefening, nie van jou geslag nie. Vroue werk ook as ingenieurs en wetenskaplikes.","en":"**Think about the facts:** whether you understand machines depends on interest and practice, not on your gender. Women also work as engineers and scientists."},{"af":"**Antwoord met respek:** “Enigiemand kan robotika leer as hy of sy belangstel. Kom ons werk saam en kyk wat ons kan bou.”","en":"**Answer with respect:** “Anyone can learn robotics if he or she is interested. Let’s work together and see what we can build.”"}],"answer":{"af":"Dit is ’n genderstereotipe, want dit sê alle meisies is dieselfde. Enige geslag kan robotika leer; Zanele kan kalm en vriendelik antwoord en by die klub aansluit.","en":"It is a gender stereotype, because it says all girls are the same. Any gender can learn robotics; Zanele can answer calmly and kindly and join the club."}},{"title":{"af":"Wys respek vir ’n ouer persoon","en":"Show respect to an older person"},"problem":{"af":"Ravi gaan by sy vriend Thabo kuier, en Thabo se ouma is ook daar. Noem drie maniere waarop Ravi respek vir haar kan wys.","en":"Ravi visits his friend Thabo, and Thabo’s grandmother is also there. Name three ways in which Ravi can show respect to her."},"steps":[{"af":"**Groet eerste en vriendelik:** Ravi groet haar wanneer hy instap, voordat hy gaan speel.","en":"**Greet first and in a friendly way:** Ravi greets her when he walks in, before he goes to play."},{"af":"**Gebruik ’n respekvolle titel:** hy kan Thabo vra hoe hulle haar aanspreek, bv. *Gogo* of *Ouma*, en dit gebruik.","en":"**Use a respectful title:** he can ask Thabo what they call her, e.g. *Gogo* or *Ouma* (Granny), and use it."},{"af":"**Luister en volg die gesin se gebruike:** hy luister as sy praat, val haar nie in die rede nie, en as dit die gesin se gebruik is, ontvang hy iets met albei hande.","en":"**Listen and follow the family’s customs:** he listens when she speaks, does not interrupt her, and if it is the family’s custom, he receives something with both hands."}],"answer":{"af":"Ravi kan haar eerste en vriendelik groet, ’n respekvolle titel gebruik, en luister sonder om haar in die rede te val terwyl hy die gesin se gebruike volg.","en":"Ravi can greet her first and in a friendly way, use a respectful title, and listen without interrupting her while following the family’s customs."}},{"title":{"af":"Maak ’n regverdige taakrooster","en":"Make a fair chore roster"},"problem":{"af":"Johan is 11 en sy suster Anika is 8. Hulle ma vra hulle om ’n regverdige rooster vir vier take te maak: skottelgoed was, vullis uitvat, die tafel dek en die hond kos gee. Hoe moet hulle dit uitdeel?","en":"Johan is 11 and his sister Anika is 8. Their mom asks them to make a fair roster for four chores: washing dishes, taking out the rubbish, setting the table and feeding the dog. How should they share them out?"},"steps":[{"af":"**Deel volgens ouderdom en vermoë, nie geslag nie:** Johan is ouer, so hy kan die skottelgoed was. Die tafel dek en die hond kos gee is ook vir ’n agtjarige maklik genoeg.","en":"**Share according to age and ability, not gender:** Johan is older, so he can wash the dishes. Setting the table and feeding the dog are easy enough for an eight-year-old too."},{"af":"**Maak dit regverdig:** elkeen kry twee take, bv. Johan: skottelgoed en vullis; Anika: tafel dek en hond kos gee.","en":"**Make it fair:** each one gets two chores, e.g. Johan: dishes and rubbish; Anika: setting the table and feeding the dog."},{"af":"**Ruil gereeld om:** die take wat albei kan doen, soos die vullis en die hond, kan hulle elke week omruil, sodat albei alles leer.","en":"**Swap regularly:** the chores both can do, like the rubbish and the dog, can be swapped every week, so that both learn everything."}],"answer":{"af":"Elkeen kry twee take volgens ouderdom en vermoë (Johan: skottelgoed en vullis; Anika: tafel en hond), en hulle ruil die take wat albei kan doen, weekliks om.","en":"Each gets two chores according to age and ability (Johan: dishes and rubbish; Anika: table and dog), and they swap the chores both can do every week."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is ’n genderstereotipe?","en":"What is a gender stereotype?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Vaste idee dat alle seuns of alle meisies op ’n sekere manier is","en":"A fixed idea that all boys or all girls are a certain way"},{"af":"’n Wet wat sê dat almal gelyk is","en":"A law that says that everyone is equal"},{"af":"’n Tradisie wat deur ouer mense oorgedra word","en":"A tradition that is passed on by older people"},{"af":"’n Taak wat jy tuis moet doen","en":"A task that you have to do at home"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Genderstereotipe sê dat almal van een geslag dieselfde is, soos “Meisies kan nie motors regmaak nie.” Dit is onregverdig, want elke mens is anders.","en":"A gender stereotype says that everyone of one gender is the same, like “Girls can’t fix cars.” It is unfair, because every person is different."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n manier om respek vir ’n ouer persoon te wys?","en":"Which one is a way to show respect to an older person?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle in die rede val as jy iets belangriks wil sê","en":"Interrupting them when you want to say something important"},{"af":"Hulle op hulle voornaam noem sonder om te vra","en":"Calling them by their first name without asking"},{"af":"Verbyloop sonder om te groet","en":"Walking past without greeting"},{"af":"Hulle vriendelik groet en luister wanneer hulle praat","en":"Greeting them in a friendly way and listening when they speak"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Om vriendelik te groet en te luister, is ’n manier om respek te wys wat in die meeste kulture waardeer word. Om iemand in die rede te val of nie te groet nie, is onbeleefd.","en":"Greeting in a friendly way and listening is a way of showing respect that is valued in most cultures. Interrupting someone or not greeting is rude."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die manier van lewe van ’n groep mense – hulle taal, gebruike, kos en waardes – is hulle ___.","en":"The way of life of a group of people – their language, customs, food and values – is their ___."},"answers":{"af":["kultuur"],"en":["culture"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["gemeenskap","geslag","gesin"],"en":["community","gender","family"]}},"explain":{"af":"Kultuur sluit alles in wat ’n groep mense se manier van lewe uitmaak. ’n Gemeenskap is die mense wat in ’n area woon; dit kan uit baie kulture bestaan.","en":"Culture includes everything that makes up a group of people’s way of life. A community is the people who live in an area; it can be made up of many cultures."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Enige werk kan deur enige geslag gedoen word as die persoon die nodige vaardighede leer.","en":"Any job can be done by any gender if the person learns the necessary skills."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Vrou kan ’n vlieënier of ingenieur word en ’n man kan ’n verpleër of kok word. Wat saak maak, is belangstelling en vaardighede, nie geslag nie.","en":"True. A woman can become a pilot or engineer and a man can become a nurse or chef. What matters is interest and skills, not gender."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom verander ’n kind se verantwoordelikhede tuis soos hy of sy ouer word?","en":"Why do a child’s responsibilities at home change as he or she gets older?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat ouer kinders minder hoef te help","en":"Because older children have to help less"},{"af":"Omdat seuns en meisies ander take kry","en":"Because boys and girls get different tasks"},{"af":"Omdat ouer kinders meer kan doen en meer vaardighede het","en":"Because older children can do more and have more skills"},{"af":"Omdat ouers nie meer self wil werk nie","en":"Because parents don’t want to work themselves any more"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Soos jy groei, leer jy meer vaardighede en kan jy veiliger moeiliker take doen. Take word dus volgens ouderdom en vermoë uitgedeel, nie volgens geslag nie.","en":"As you grow, you learn more skills and can safely do harder tasks. So tasks are shared out according to age and ability, not according to gender."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke genderstereotipe by ’n antwoord wat dit uitdaag.","en":"Match each gender stereotype to an answer that challenges it."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"“Seuns huil nie.”","en":"“Boys don’t cry.”"},"r":{"af":"Almal het gevoelens, en seuns mag ook huil.","en":"Everyone has feelings, and boys may cry too."}},{"l":{"af":"“Meisies kan nie motors regmaak nie.”","en":"“Girls can’t fix cars.”"},"r":{"af":"Enigiemand wat dit leer, kan ’n motorwerktuigkundige word.","en":"Anyone who learns it can become a car mechanic."}},{"l":{"af":"“Net ma’s kan na babas kyk.”","en":"“Only moms can look after babies.”"},"r":{"af":"Pa’s kan babas ook voed, bad en troos.","en":"Dads can also feed, bath and comfort babies."}},{"l":{"af":"“Kook is nie vir seuns nie.”","en":"“Cooking is not for boys.”"},"r":{"af":"Baie bekende sjefs is mans, en almal moet kan kook.","en":"Many well-known chefs are men, and everyone should be able to cook."}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke stereotipe beperk mense. Om dit uit te daag, wys jy dat vaardighede en gevoelens nie van jou geslag afhang nie.","en":"Every stereotype limits people. By challenging it, you show that skills and feelings don’t depend on your gender."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato wil eendag ’n ingenieur word. Pieter sê: “Dis ’n man se werk.” Wat is die beste antwoord?","en":"Lerato wants to become an engineer one day. Pieter says: “That’s a man’s job.” What is the best answer?"},"options":[{"af":"“Jy is reg, ek sal eerder iets anders kies.”","en":"“You’re right, I’ll rather choose something else.”"},{"af":"“Enige werk kan deur enige geslag gedoen word – vroue is ook ingenieurs.”","en":"“Any job can be done by any gender – women are engineers too.”"},{"af":"“Seuns is in elk geval nie slim genoeg daarvoor nie.”","en":"“Boys aren’t clever enough for it anyway.”"},{"af":"“Ek gaan nooit weer met jou praat nie.”","en":"“I’m never going to talk to you again.”"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die beste antwoord daag die stereotipe kalm en met ’n feit uit. Om terug te kap met ’n ander stereotipe oor seuns, is net so onregverdig.","en":"The best answer challenges the stereotype calmly and with a fact. Hitting back with another stereotype about boys is just as unfair."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer almal dieselfde kanse en respek kry, ongeag hulle geslag, noem ons dit ___.","en":"When everyone gets the same chances and respect, no matter their gender, we call it ___."},"answers":{"af":["gelykheid"],"en":["equality"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["diskriminasie","stereotipering","ongelykheid"],"en":["discrimination","stereotyping","inequality"]}},"explain":{"af":"Gelykheid beteken nie dat almal dieselfde is nie, maar dat almal dieselfde kanse en respek verdien. Die Grondwet beskerm hierdie gelykheid.","en":"Equality doesn’t mean that everyone is the same, but that everyone deserves the same chances and respect. The Constitution protects this equality."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In Fatima se vriendin se gesin ontvang kinders iets van ’n ouer persoon met albei hande. In Fatima se gesin kyk kinders iemand in die oë as hulle praat. Wat is waar?","en":"In Fatima’s friend’s family, children receive something from an older person with both hands. In Fatima’s family, children look someone in the eye when they speak. What is true?"},"options":[{"af":"Net een van die gesinne wys respek","en":"Only one of the families shows respect"},{"af":"Albei gesinne wys respek, net op verskillende maniere","en":"Both families show respect, just in different ways"},{"af":"Albei gesinne is onbeleefd teenoor ouer mense","en":"Both families are rude to older people"},{"af":"Fatima moet haar vriendin vertel dat sy dit verkeerd doen","en":"Fatima should tell her friend that she is doing it wrong"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Kulture en gesinne wys respek op verskillende maniere, maar die doel is dieselfde: om te wys dat jy die persoon waardeer. Geen manier is beter as ’n ander nie.","en":"Cultures and families show respect in different ways, but the purpose is the same: to show that you value the person. No way is better than another."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Net kinders hoef respek te wys; ouer mense hoef kinders nie met respek te behandel nie.","en":"Only children need to show respect; older people don’t need to treat children with respect."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Respek werk in albei rigtings. Ouer mense moet ook na kinders luister, hulle beskerm en hulle met respek behandel.","en":"False. Respect works in both directions. Older people must also listen to children, protect them and treat them with respect."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat sê die Suid-Afrikaanse Grondwet oor geslag?","en":"What does the South African Constitution say about gender?"},"options":[{"af":"Mans moet meer verdien as vroue","en":"Men must earn more than women"},{"af":"Net seuns mag sekere sportsoorte speel","en":"Only boys may play certain sports"},{"af":"Elke gesin moet self besluit wie gelyk is","en":"Every family must decide for itself who is equal"},{"af":"Almal is gelyk en niemand mag weens hulle geslag onregverdig behandel word nie","en":"Everyone is equal and nobody may be treated unfairly because of their gender"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die Grondwet is die hoogste wet van die land en sê almal is gelyk. Om iemand onregverdig te behandel weens hulle geslag, is diskriminasie.","en":"The Constitution is the highest law of the country and says everyone is equal. Treating someone unfairly because of their gender is discrimination."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Om ’n ouer persoon ‘Oom’ of ‘Tannie’, of ‘Ntate’ of ‘Mme’, te noem, is ’n manier om ___ te wys.","en":"Calling an older person ‘Oom’ or ‘Tannie’, or ‘Ntate’ or ‘Mme’, is a way of showing ___."},"answers":{"af":["respek"],"en":["respect"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["jaloesie","vrees","woede"],"en":["jealousy","fear","anger"]}},"explain":{"af":"Titels soos Oom, Tannie, Ntate en Mme wys dat jy die ouer persoon waardeer. Verskillende tale en kulture het verskillende titels, maar die doel is dieselfde.","en":"Titles like Oom, Tannie, Ntate and Mme show that you value the older person. Different languages and cultures have different titles, but the purpose is the same."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ravi sê: “In daardie kultuur kook al die mans nooit nie.” Wat is fout met hierdie stelling?","en":"Ravi says: “In that culture all the men never cook.” What is wrong with this statement?"},"options":[{"af":"Niks nie, dit is ’n feit oor die kultuur","en":"Nothing, it is a fact about the culture"},{"af":"Hy moes “vroue” in plaas van “mans” gesê het","en":"He should have said “women” instead of “men”"},{"af":"Dit is ’n stereotipe, want mense binne ’n kultuur verskil van mekaar","en":"It is a stereotype, because people within a culture differ from each other"},{"af":"Mans mag nie volgens die wet kook nie","en":"Men are not allowed to cook by law"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Ravi sê iets oor álle mans in ’n kultuur, asof hulle almal dieselfde is. Binne elke kultuur verskil gesinne en mense, daarom moet ons mense as individue leer ken.","en":"Ravi says something about all men in a culture, as if they are all the same. Within every culture families and people differ, so we should get to know people as individuals."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n voorbeeld van vrywillige werk in die gemeenskap?","en":"Which one is an example of volunteer work in the community?"},"options":[{"af":"Sonder betaling by ’n sopkombuis help om kos uit te deel","en":"Helping to hand out food at a soup kitchen without pay"},{"af":"Elke maand ’n salaris by ’n bank verdien","en":"Earning a salary at a bank every month"},{"af":"Jou eie kamer opruim","en":"Tidying your own room"},{"af":"Vir ’n toets by die skool leer","en":"Studying for a test at school"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Vrywillige werk doen jy uit eie keuse en sonder betaling om ander te help. Werk vir ’n salaris is ’n betaalde werk, en om jou kamer op te ruim of te leer, help net jouself.","en":"Volunteer work is done by choice and without pay to help others. Work for a salary is a paid job, and tidying your room or studying only helps yourself."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Godsdiens, veiligheid en gesondheid","en":"Religion, safety and health"},"topics":[{"id":"lv5-t3-feeste-gelowe","title":{"af":"Feeste en gebruike van gelowe in Suid-Afrika","en":"Festivals and customs of religions in South Africa"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die belangrikste feeste en gebruike van vyf gelowe in Suid-Afrika kan beskryf, kan sê wat elke fees vier en kan wys hoe om respek vir ander se geloof te toon.","en":"You will be able to describe the main festivals and customs of five religions in South Africa, say what each festival celebrates and show how to respect other people’s beliefs."},"summary":{"af":"## Baie gelowe, een land\n\nSuid-Afrika is ’n land met mense van baie verskillende **gelowe** (godsdienste). In jou klas kan daar Christene, Moslems, Hindoes en Jode wees, kinders wie se gesinne die **Afrika-tradisionele godsdiens** volg, en ook kinders wie se gesinne nie godsdienstig is nie. Die **Grondwet** gee elke mens **vryheid van godsdiens**: jy mag glo wat jy wil, en jy moet ander se reg om hul geloof te beoefen **respekteer**.\n\nElke geloof het **feeste** (spesiale dae wat gevier word) en **gebruike** (dinge wat mense gereeld op ’n sekere manier doen). As jy van ander se feeste leer, verstaan jy jou maats en bure beter.\n\n| Geloof | Heilige boek | Plek van aanbidding | Feeste |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Christendom | Bybel | Kerk | Kersfees, Paasfees |\n| Islam | Koran | Moskee | Ramadan, Eid-ul-Fitr |\n| Hindoeïsme | Vedas, Bhagavad Gita | Tempel | Diwali |\n| Judaïsme | Tora | Sinagoge | Pasga (Pesach), Chanoeka |\n| Afrika-tradisionele godsdiens | Geen geskrewe boek – kennis word mondelings oorgedra | Tuis of op spesiale plekke | Seremonies om die voorvaders te eer |\n\n## Feeste en wat hulle vier\n\n### Christendom\n- **Kersfees** (25 Desember) vier die **geboorte van Jesus**. Christene gaan kerk toe, sing Kersliedere, gee geskenke en eet saam as gesin.\n- **Paasfees** (Maart of April) herdenk Jesus se **dood** op **Goeie Vrydag** en sy **opstanding** op **Paassondag**.\n\n### Islam\n- **Ramadan** is ’n heilige maand waarin Moslems **vas**: van dagbreek tot sononder eet en drink hulle niks nie. Klein kinders, siek mense en bejaardes hoef nie te vas nie. Ná sononder breek gesinne saam die vas, dikwels met dadels en water. Dit is ’n tyd van gebed en om ander te help.\n- **Eid-ul-Fitr** is die blye fees aan die **einde van Ramadan**. Moslems bid saam in die moskee, trek nuwe klere aan, besoek familie en gee vir mense in nood.\n\n### Hindoeïsme\n- **Diwali** is die Hindoe-**ligfees** (Oktober of November). Dit vier dat **lig oor duisternis** en goed oor kwaad wen. Hindoes steek klein olielampies (**diyas**) aan, maak kleurvolle **rangoli**-patrone op die vloer, bid, deel soetgoed en kuier by mekaar.\n\n### Judaïsme\n- **Pasga (Pesach)** herdenk hoe die Israeliete uit **slawerny in Egipte** bevry is. Gesinne eet die **Sedermaal** en vertel die verhaal. Hulle eet **matzah** (ongesuurde brood), want die Israeliete moes so haastig vertrek dat hul brood nie tyd gehad het om te rys nie.\n- **Chanoeka** is ’n Joodse **ligfees van agt aande** (gewoonlik in Desember). Elke aand word een kers meer op die **menora** aangesteek. Dit herinner aan olie wat agt dae lank gebrand het.\n\n### Afrika-tradisionele godsdiens\n- Volgelinge glo in ’n **Skepper** (in isiZulu *uMvelinqangi*, in Sesotho *Modimo*) en **eer die voorvaders**, wat volgens hul geloof oor die familie waak.\n- **Seremonies** word gehou by ’n baba se geboorte, grootword, ’n troue, ’n begrafnis of om dankie te sê vir die oes. Die familie kom bymekaar; daar is sang, dans en gedeelde kos. Gebruike verskil van kultuur tot kultuur.\n\n> **Onthou:** Baie feeste val nie elke jaar op dieselfde datum nie, want hulle word met die **maan** bereken. Die Islamitiese kalender is ’n maankalender, daarom skuif Ramadan elke jaar omtrent 11 dae vroeër.\n\n## Hoe om respek te toon\n\n- **Vra** vriendelik en belangstellend oor ’n maat se fees – moenie spot nie.\n- Wens jou maat ’n gelukkige fees toe, byvoorbeeld *Eid Mubarak* of *Gelukkige Diwali*.\n- Wees **bedagsaam**: moenie tydens Ramadan voor ’n vastende maat met jou kos spog nie.\n- Dink aan **kosreëls** as jy ’n partytjie hou: Moslems en baie Jode eet nie varkvleis nie, en baie Hindoes eet nie beesvleis nie.\n- Volg die reëls as jy ’n ander geloof se plek van aanbidding besoek.\n- **Geen geloof is beter as ’n ander nie.** Mense kan verskil en steeds goeie vriende wees.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om Diwali en Chanoeka te verwar omdat albei ligfeeste is. **Diwali** is ’n **Hindoe**-fees met olielampies en rangoli; **Chanoeka** is ’n **Joodse** fees met ’n menora.\n\n## Wat feeste gemeen het\n\nAl verskil die feeste, het hulle baie in gemeen: gesinne kom **saam**, mense **bid** of dink na, hulle eet **spesiale kos**, hulle **gee vir ander** en hulle onthou belangrike **verhale** uit hul geloof.","en":"## Many religions, one country\n\nSouth Africa is a country with people of many different **religions** (faiths). In your class there may be Christians, Muslims, Hindus and Jews, children whose families follow **African Traditional Religion**, and also children whose families are not religious. The **Constitution** gives every person **freedom of religion**: you may believe what you choose, and you must **respect** other people’s right to practise their religion.\n\nEvery religion has **festivals** (special days that are celebrated) and **customs** (things people regularly do in a certain way). When you learn about other people’s festivals, you understand your friends and neighbours better.\n\n| Religion | Holy book | Place of worship | Festivals |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Christianity | Bible | Church | Christmas, Easter |\n| Islam | Qur’an | Mosque | Ramadan, Eid-ul-Fitr |\n| Hinduism | Vedas, Bhagavad Gita | Temple | Diwali |\n| Judaism | Torah | Synagogue | Passover (Pesach), Hanukkah |\n| African Traditional Religion | No written book – knowledge is passed on by word of mouth | At home or at special places | Ceremonies to honour the ancestors |\n\n## Festivals and what they celebrate\n\n### Christianity\n- **Christmas** (25 December) celebrates the **birth of Jesus**. Christians go to church, sing Christmas carols, give presents and eat together as a family.\n- **Easter** (March or April) remembers Jesus’ **death** on **Good Friday** and his **resurrection** (rising from the dead) on **Easter Sunday**.\n\n### Islam\n- **Ramadan** is a holy month in which Muslims **fast**: from dawn to sunset they do not eat or drink anything. Young children, sick people and the elderly do not have to fast. After sunset families break the fast together, often with dates and water. It is a time of prayer and of helping others.\n- **Eid-ul-Fitr** is the happy festival at the **end of Ramadan**. Muslims pray together at the mosque, wear new clothes, visit family and give to people in need.\n\n### Hinduism\n- **Diwali** is the Hindu **festival of lights** (October or November). It celebrates **light winning over darkness** and good over evil. Hindus light small oil lamps (**diyas**), make colourful **rangoli** patterns on the floor, pray, share sweets and visit each other.\n\n### Judaism\n- **Passover (Pesach)** remembers how the Israelites were freed from **slavery in Egypt**. Families eat the **Seder meal** and tell the story. They eat **matzah** (unleavened bread), because the Israelites had to leave in such a hurry that their bread had no time to rise.\n- **Hanukkah** is a Jewish **festival of lights lasting eight nights** (usually in December). Each night one more candle is lit on the **menorah**. It is a reminder of oil that burned for eight days.\n\n### African Traditional Religion\n- Followers believe in a **Creator** (in isiZulu *uMvelinqangi*, in Sesotho *Modimo*) and **honour the ancestors**, who, according to their belief, watch over the family.\n- **Ceremonies** are held at a baby’s birth, growing up, a wedding, a funeral or to give thanks for the harvest. The family gathers; there is singing, dancing and shared food. Customs differ from culture to culture.\n\n> **Remember:** Many festivals do not fall on the same date every year, because they are worked out by the **moon**. The Islamic calendar is a moon calendar, so Ramadan moves about 11 days earlier every year.\n\n## How to show respect\n\n- **Ask** in a friendly, interested way about a friend’s festival – do not make fun of it.\n- Wish your friend a happy festival, for example *Eid Mubarak* or *Happy Diwali*.\n- Be **considerate**: during Ramadan, do not show off your food in front of a friend who is fasting.\n- Think about **food rules** when you have a party: Muslims and many Jews do not eat pork, and many Hindus do not eat beef.\n- Follow the rules when you visit another religion’s place of worship.\n- **No religion is better than another.** People can differ and still be good friends.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Mixing up Diwali and Hanukkah because both are festivals of lights. **Diwali** is a **Hindu** festival with oil lamps and rangoli; **Hanukkah** is a **Jewish** festival with a menorah.\n\n## What festivals have in common\n\nEven though the festivals differ, they have a lot in common: families come **together**, people **pray** or reflect, they eat **special food**, they **give to others** and they remember important **stories** from their religion."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Geloof (godsdiens)","en":"Religion (faith)"},"def":{"af":"Wat ’n groep mense glo oor God of ’n hoër mag, en hoe hulle dit beoefen.","en":"What a group of people believe about God or a higher power, and how they practise it."}},{"term":{"af":"Fees","en":"Festival"},"def":{"af":"’n Spesiale dag of tyd wat ’n geloof vier, dikwels met gebed, kos en familie.","en":"A special day or time that a religion celebrates, often with prayer, food and family."}},{"term":{"af":"Gebruik","en":"Custom"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat mense van ’n geloof of kultuur gereeld op ’n sekere manier doen, soos om saam te bid of spesiale kos te eet.","en":"Something people of a religion or culture regularly do in a certain way, such as praying together or eating special food."}},{"term":{"af":"Vryheid van godsdiens","en":"Freedom of religion"},"def":{"af":"Die reg in die Grondwet wat sê elke mens mag self kies wat hy of sy glo en dit beoefen.","en":"The right in the Constitution that says every person may choose what they believe and practise it."}},{"term":{"af":"Plek van aanbidding","en":"Place of worship"},"def":{"af":"’n Gebou of plek waar mense bymekaarkom om te bid, soos ’n kerk, moskee, tempel of sinagoge.","en":"A building or place where people gather to pray, such as a church, mosque, temple or synagogue."}},{"term":{"af":"Vas","en":"Fast"},"def":{"af":"Om vir ’n tyd lank niks te eet of te drink nie, soos Moslems van dagbreek tot sononder tydens Ramadan doen.","en":"To eat or drink nothing for a time, as Muslims do from dawn to sunset during Ramadan."}},{"term":{"af":"Voorvaders","en":"Ancestors"},"def":{"af":"Familielede wat lank gelede gelewe het; in die Afrika-tradisionele godsdiens word hulle geëer en glo mense dat hulle oor die familie waak.","en":"Family members who lived long ago; in African Traditional Religion they are honoured and people believe they watch over the family."}},{"term":{"af":"Menora","en":"Menorah"},"def":{"af":"’n Kandelaar waarop Jode tydens Chanoeka elke aand een kers meer aansteek.","en":"A candle holder on which Jewish people light one more candle each night during Hanukkah."}},{"term":{"af":"Matzah","en":"Matzah"},"def":{"af":"Plat, ongesuurde brood wat Jode tydens Pasga eet om die haastige vertrek uit Egipte te onthou.","en":"Flat, unleavened bread that Jewish people eat at Passover to remember the hurried escape from Egypt."}},{"term":{"af":"Rangoli","en":"Rangoli"},"def":{"af":"Kleurvolle patrone wat Hindoes tydens Diwali op die vloer of by die deur maak.","en":"Colourful patterns that Hindus make on the floor or at the door during Diwali."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Maak ’n feeskalender","en":"Make a festival calendar"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato se klas maak ’n feeskalender. Skryf by elke fees die geloof en wat dit vier: Kersfees, Eid-ul-Fitr, Diwali en Pasga.","en":"Lerato’s class is making a festival calendar. For each festival, write the religion and what it celebrates: Christmas, Eid-ul-Fitr, Diwali and Passover."},"steps":[{"af":"**Kersfees** is ’n Christelike fees. Dit vier die geboorte van Jesus.","en":"**Christmas** is a Christian festival. It celebrates the birth of Jesus."},{"af":"**Eid-ul-Fitr** is ’n Islamitiese fees. Dit vier die einde van die vasmaand Ramadan.","en":"**Eid-ul-Fitr** is an Islamic festival. It celebrates the end of the month of fasting, Ramadan."},{"af":"**Diwali** is ’n Hindoe-fees. Dit vier dat lig oor duisternis en goed oor kwaad wen.","en":"**Diwali** is a Hindu festival. It celebrates light winning over darkness and good over evil."},{"af":"**Pasga** is ’n Joodse fees. Dit herdenk die Israeliete se bevryding uit slawerny in Egipte.","en":"**Passover** is a Jewish festival. It remembers the Israelites being freed from slavery in Egypt."}],"answer":{"af":"Kersfees – Christendom, geboorte van Jesus; Eid-ul-Fitr – Islam, einde van Ramadan; Diwali – Hindoeïsme, lig wen oor duisternis; Pasga – Judaïsme, bevryding uit Egipte.","en":"Christmas – Christianity, birth of Jesus; Eid-ul-Fitr – Islam, end of Ramadan; Diwali – Hinduism, light wins over darkness; Passover – Judaism, freedom from Egypt."}},{"title":{"af":"Respek tydens Ramadan","en":"Respect during Ramadan"},"problem":{"af":"Dit is Ramadan en Aisha vas. Pouse sit die ander kinders langs haar en eet. Een seun sê: ‘Jy mis uit, kyk hoe lekker is my koek!’ Hoe kan die klas eerder respek toon?","en":"It is Ramadan and Aisha is fasting. At break the other children sit next to her and eat. One boy says: ‘You’re missing out, look how nice my cake is!’ How can the class rather show respect?"},"steps":[{"af":"Verstaan eers wat gebeur: Aisha vas omdat dit deel van haar geloof is. Sy het self gekies om dit te doen.","en":"First understand what is happening: Aisha is fasting because it is part of her religion. She chose to do it."},{"af":"Die seun se woorde spot met haar geloof. Dit is nie respekvol nie, al bedoel hy dit as ’n grap.","en":"The boy’s words make fun of her religion. That is not respectful, even if he means it as a joke."},{"af":"Wys respek: moenie met kos spog nie, vra haar vriendelik oor Ramadan en nooi haar om saam te speel of te gesels.","en":"Show respect: do not show off food, ask her kindly about Ramadan and invite her to play or chat."}],"answer":{"af":"Die klas kan bedagsaam wees deur nie met kos te spog nie, nie te spot nie en Aisha by ander aktiwiteite in te sluit.","en":"The class can be considerate by not showing off food, not making fun of her and including Aisha in other activities."}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyk twee ligfeeste","en":"Compare two festivals of lights"},"problem":{"af":"Noem twee ooreenkomste en twee verskille tussen Diwali en Chanoeka.","en":"Give two similarities and two differences between Diwali and Hanukkah."},"steps":[{"af":"**Ooreenkoms 1:** Albei is ligfeeste – by albei word ligte aangesteek.","en":"**Similarity 1:** Both are festivals of lights – lights are lit at both."},{"af":"**Ooreenkoms 2:** By albei kom gesinne saam, bid hulle en eet hulle spesiale kos.","en":"**Similarity 2:** At both, families come together, pray and eat special food."},{"af":"**Verskil 1:** Diwali is ’n **Hindoe**-fees; Chanoeka is ’n **Joodse** fees.","en":"**Difference 1:** Diwali is a **Hindu** festival; Hanukkah is a **Jewish** festival."},{"af":"**Verskil 2:** By Diwali steek mense olielampies (diyas) aan en maak hulle rangoli; by Chanoeka word agt aande lank kerse op ’n menora aangesteek.","en":"**Difference 2:** At Diwali people light oil lamps (diyas) and make rangoli; at Hanukkah candles are lit on a menorah for eight nights."}],"answer":{"af":"Ooreenkomste: albei is ligfeeste; gesinne kom saam, bid en eet spesiale kos. Verskille: verskillende gelowe (Hindoe teenoor Joods); diyas en rangoli teenoor ’n menora vir agt aande.","en":"Similarities: both are festivals of lights; families come together, pray and eat special food. Differences: different religions (Hindu versus Jewish); diyas and rangoli versus a menorah for eight nights."}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik ’n seremonie vir die voorvaders","en":"Explain a ceremony for the ancestors"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho se familie volg die Afrika-tradisionele godsdiens. Nadat sy niggie gebore is, hou die familie ’n seremonie. Verduidelik wat voorvaders is en waarom so ’n seremonie gehou word.","en":"Sipho’s family follows African Traditional Religion. After his cousin is born, the family holds a ceremony. Explain what ancestors are and why such a ceremony is held."},"steps":[{"af":"**Voorvaders** is familielede wat lank gelede gelewe het. Volgelinge glo dat hulle steeds oor die familie waak.","en":"**Ancestors** are family members who lived long ago. Followers believe that they still watch over the family."},{"af":"By belangrike oomblikke, soos ’n geboorte, word die voorvaders **geëer** en word die nuwe baba in die familie verwelkom.","en":"At important moments, such as a birth, the ancestors are **honoured** and the new baby is welcomed into the family."},{"af":"Die familie kom bymekaar met sang, dans en gedeelde kos. Die besonderhede verskil van kultuur tot kultuur.","en":"The family gathers with singing, dancing and shared food. The details differ from culture to culture."}],"answer":{"af":"Voorvaders is oorlede familielede wat volgens die geloof oor die familie waak. Die seremonie eer hulle by ’n belangrike oomblik en bring die familie saam.","en":"Ancestors are family members who have died and who, according to the belief, watch over the family. The ceremony honours them at an important moment and brings the family together."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat vier Christene met Kersfees?","en":"What do Christians celebrate at Christmas?"},"options":[{"af":"Die opstanding van Jesus","en":"The resurrection of Jesus"},{"af":"Die geboorte van Jesus","en":"The birth of Jesus"},{"af":"Die einde van die vasmaand","en":"The end of the month of fasting"},{"af":"Die bevryding uit Egipte","en":"The freedom from Egypt"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Kersfees (25 Desember) vier die geboorte van Jesus. Die opstanding van Jesus word met Paasfees herdenk – moenie die twee Christelike feeste verwar nie.","en":"Christmas (25 December) celebrates the birth of Jesus. The resurrection of Jesus is remembered at Easter – do not mix up the two Christian festivals."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die heilige boek van Moslems is die ___.","en":"The holy book of Muslims is the ___."},"answers":{"af":["Koran","Quran","Qur’an"],"en":["Qur’an","Quran","Koran"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Bybel","Tora","Vedas"],"en":["Bible","Torah","Vedas"]}},"explain":{"af":"Moslems lees die Koran. Die Bybel is die Christene se heilige boek, die Tora die Jode s’n en die Vedas is heilige boeke van die Hindoes.","en":"Muslims read the Qur’an. The Bible is the Christians’ holy book, the Torah is the Jews’ and the Vedas are holy books of the Hindus."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wanneer vier Moslems Eid-ul-Fitr?","en":"When do Muslims celebrate Eid-ul-Fitr?"},"options":[{"af":"Aan die begin van Ramadan","en":"At the start of Ramadan"},{"af":"Op 25 Desember elke jaar","en":"On 25 December every year"},{"af":"Tydens die ligfees in November","en":"During the festival of lights in November"},{"af":"Aan die einde van Ramadan","en":"At the end of Ramadan"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Eid-ul-Fitr is die blye fees wat die vasmaand Ramadan afsluit. Die datum skuif elke jaar, want die Islamitiese kalender volg die maan.","en":"Eid-ul-Fitr is the happy festival that ends the month of fasting, Ramadan. The date moves every year, because the Islamic calendar follows the moon."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Diwali is ’n Joodse fees waartydens kerse op ’n menora aangesteek word.","en":"Diwali is a Jewish festival during which candles are lit on a menorah."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Diwali is ’n Hindoe-ligfees met olielampies (diyas) en rangoli. Die Joodse ligfees met ’n menora is Chanoeka.","en":"False. Diwali is a Hindu festival of lights with oil lamps (diyas) and rangoli. The Jewish festival of lights with a menorah is Hanukkah."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom eet Jode matzah (ongesuurde brood) tydens Pasga?","en":"Why do Jewish people eat matzah (unleavened bread) at Passover?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Israeliete het so haastig uit Egipte vertrek dat hul brood nie kon rys nie","en":"The Israelites left Egypt in such a hurry that their bread could not rise"},{"af":"Hulle vas die hele week en mag net droë brood eet","en":"They fast the whole week and may only eat dry bread"},{"af":"Plat brood herinner hulle aan die geboorte van ’n profeet","en":"Flat bread reminds them of the birth of a prophet"},{"af":"Dit is die enigste kos wat op ’n menora gebak kan word","en":"It is the only food that can be baked on a menorah"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Pasga herdenk die bevryding uit slawerny in Egipte. Die Israeliete moes vinnig vertrek, en hul brood het nie tyd gehad om te rys nie. Matzah help hulle om dit te onthou.","en":"Passover remembers being freed from slavery in Egypt. The Israelites had to leave quickly, and their bread had no time to rise. Matzah helps them to remember this."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ravi nooi jou na sy gesin se Diwali-viering. Wat is die mees respekvolle ding om te doen?","en":"Ravi invites you to his family’s Diwali celebration. What is the most respectful thing to do?"},"options":[{"af":"Sê vir hom jou eie fees is beter, maar jy sal kom","en":"Tell him your own festival is better, but you will come"},{"af":"Gaan, maar lag oor die rangoli-patrone op die vloer","en":"Go, but laugh at the rangoli patterns on the floor"},{"af":"Gaan, wees vriendelik en vra belangstellend oor die gebruike","en":"Go, be friendly and ask with interest about the customs"},{"af":"Bly weg, want ’n ander geloof se fees is nie vir jou nie","en":"Stay away, because another religion’s festival is not for you"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Respek beteken jy is vriendelik, wil leer en spot nie. Geen geloof is beter as ’n ander nie, so dit is nie respekvol om te sê jou fees is beter of om te lag nie.","en":"Respect means you are friendly, want to learn and do not make fun. No religion is better than another, so it is not respectful to say your festival is better or to laugh."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke fees of gebruik by die geloof waaraan dit behoort.","en":"Match each festival or custom to the religion it belongs to."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Paasfees","en":"Easter"},"r":{"af":"Christendom","en":"Christianity"}},{"l":{"af":"Eid-ul-Fitr","en":"Eid-ul-Fitr"},"r":{"af":"Islam","en":"Islam"}},{"l":{"af":"Diwali","en":"Diwali"},"r":{"af":"Hindoeïsme","en":"Hinduism"}},{"l":{"af":"Chanoeka","en":"Hanukkah"},"r":{"af":"Judaïsme","en":"Judaism"}},{"l":{"af":"Seremonie om die voorvaders te eer","en":"Ceremony to honour the ancestors"},"r":{"af":"Afrika-tradisionele godsdiens","en":"African Traditional Religion"}}],"explain":{"af":"Paasfees is Christelik, Eid-ul-Fitr is Islamities, Diwali is ’n Hindoe-fees, Chanoeka is Joods, en seremonies om die voorvaders te eer hoort by die Afrika-tradisionele godsdiens.","en":"Easter is Christian, Eid-ul-Fitr is Islamic, Diwali is a Hindu festival, Hanukkah is Jewish, and ceremonies to honour the ancestors belong to African Traditional Religion."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat herdenk Christene met Paasfees?","en":"What do Christians remember at Easter?"},"options":[{"af":"Die geboorte van Jesus in ’n stal","en":"The birth of Jesus in a stable"},{"af":"Jesus se dood en sy opstanding","en":"Jesus’ death and his resurrection"},{"af":"Die olie wat agt dae lank gebrand het","en":"The oil that burned for eight days"},{"af":"Die oes wat aan die voorvaders gewy is","en":"The harvest given to the ancestors"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Met Paasfees onthou Christene Jesus se dood op Goeie Vrydag en sy opstanding op Paassondag. Sy geboorte word met Kersfees gevier.","en":"At Easter Christians remember Jesus’ death on Good Friday and his resurrection on Easter Sunday. His birth is celebrated at Christmas."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Tydens Chanoeka word elke aand een kers meer op die ___ aangesteek.","en":"During Hanukkah one more candle is lit on the ___ each night."},"answers":{"af":["menora","menorah"],"en":["menorah","menora"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["diya","kersboom","Sederbord"],"en":["diya","Christmas tree","Seder plate"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die menora is die Joodse kandelaar vir Chanoeka. ’n Diya is ’n Hindoe-olielampie vir Diwali, en die Sederbord hoort by die Pasgamaal.","en":"The menorah is the Jewish candle holder for Hanukkah. A diya is a Hindu oil lamp for Diwali, and the Seder plate belongs to the Passover meal."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling oor die Afrika-tradisionele godsdiens is korrek?","en":"Which statement about African Traditional Religion is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Volgelinge eer die voorvaders en hou seremonies by belangrike oomblikke","en":"Followers honour the ancestors and hold ceremonies at important moments"},{"af":"Volgelinge lees elke week uit een geskrewe heilige boek","en":"Followers read from one written holy book every week"},{"af":"Volgelinge vas ’n hele maand van dagbreek tot sononder","en":"Followers fast for a whole month from dawn to sunset"},{"af":"Volgelinge vier net een fees per jaar, op dieselfde datum","en":"Followers celebrate only one festival a year, on the same date"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"In die Afrika-tradisionele godsdiens word die voorvaders geëer met seremonies by geboortes, troues, begrafnisse en oeste. Daar is geen geskrewe boek nie – kennis word mondelings oorgedra. Om ’n maand te vas is ’n Islamitiese gebruik.","en":"In African Traditional Religion the ancestors are honoured with ceremonies at births, weddings, funerals and harvests. There is no written book – knowledge is passed on by word of mouth. Fasting for a month is an Islamic custom."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Ramadan val nie elke jaar op dieselfde tyd nie, want die Islamitiese kalender volg die maan.","en":"Ramadan does not fall at the same time every year, because the Islamic calendar follows the moon."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die Islamitiese kalender is ’n maankalender wat korter as ons gewone jaar is. Daarom skuif Ramadan elke jaar omtrent 11 dae vroeër.","en":"True. The Islamic calendar is a moon calendar that is shorter than our normal year. That is why Ramadan moves about 11 days earlier every year."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Dit is middag. Fatima eet en drink niks nie, maar sy is gesond en vrolik. Watter tyd van die jaar is dit waarskynlik vir haar gesin?","en":"It is midday. Fatima is not eating or drinking anything, but she is healthy and cheerful. Which time of year is it most likely for her family?"},"options":[{"af":"Chanoeka","en":"Hanukkah"},{"af":"Diwali","en":"Diwali"},{"af":"Kersfees","en":"Christmas"},{"af":"Ramadan","en":"Ramadan"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Tydens Ramadan vas Moslems van dagbreek tot sononder. Die ander feeste is vreugdevolle feeste met spesiale kos – nie vastye nie.","en":"During Ramadan Muslims fast from dawn to sunset. The other festivals are joyful festivals with special food – not times of fasting."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Tydens Diwali maak Hindoes kleurvolle patrone op die vloer, wat ___ genoem word.","en":"During Diwali, Hindus make colourful patterns on the floor, which are called ___."},"answers":{"af":["rangoli"],"en":["rangoli"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["menora","matzah","diyas"],"en":["menorah","matzah","diyas"]}},"explain":{"af":"Rangoli is kleurvolle patrone, dikwels van gekleurde poeier of blomblare. Diyas is die olielampies wat Hindoes aansteek – dit is nie die patrone nie.","en":"Rangoli are colourful patterns, often made with coloured powder or flower petals. Diyas are the oil lamps that Hindus light – they are not the patterns."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Tydens ’n klasbespreking sê Johan: ‘My geloof is die enigste regte een, so ander mense se feeste is dom.’ Wat is die beste antwoord?","en":"During a class discussion Johan says: ‘My religion is the only right one, so other people’s festivals are silly.’ What is the best reply?"},"options":[{"af":"‘Jy is reg, ons moet net jou fees in die klas vier.’","en":"‘You are right, we should only celebrate your festival in class.’"},{"af":"‘Dan is jou fees ook dom, so daar!’","en":"‘Then your festival is silly too, so there!’"},{"af":"‘Jy mag in jou geloof glo, maar ander het dieselfde reg – ons respekteer almal se feeste.’","en":"‘You may believe in your religion, but others have the same right – we respect everyone’s festivals.’"},{"af":"‘Ons moet eerder glad nie oor gelowe praat nie.’","en":"‘We should rather not talk about religions at all.’"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die Grondwet gee elke mens vryheid van godsdiens. Johan mag sy eie geloof hê, maar hy moet ander se reg respekteer. Om terug te skel of alle gesprekke te verbied help nie.","en":"The Constitution gives every person freedom of religion. Johan may have his own religion, but he must respect other people’s right. Insulting him back or banning all discussion does not help."}}]},{"id":"lv5-t3-veiligheid-huis","title":{"af":"Veiligheid tuis en in die omgewing","en":"Safety at home and in the environment"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal gevare tuis en in jou omgewing kan herken, gevaarsimbole op etikette kan lees, weet wat om by ’n brand te doen en die regte noodnommer kan bel.","en":"You will be able to recognise dangers at home and in your surroundings, read hazard symbols on labels, know what to do in a fire and call the right emergency number."},"summary":{"af":"## Gevare in die huis\n\nBaie ongelukke met kinders gebeur **tuis**. As jy weet waar die gevare is, kan jy jouself en jou kleiner boeties en sussies beskerm.\n\n### Skadelike huishoudelike produkte\nProdukte soos **bleikmiddel**, **paraffien**, afvoerskoonmaker, insekgif en rottegif is **giftig**. As iemand dit drink of in die oë kry, kan dit ernstige skade doen.\n\n- Bêre dit **hoog** of in ’n **toegesluite kas**, weg van kos.\n- Hou dit in die **oorspronklike houer** met die etiket.\n- Gooi dit **nooit** in ’n koeldrankbottel of koppie nie. ’n Klein kindjie kan paraffien vir water of koeldrank aansien en dit drink.\n\n| Gevaarsimbool | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| Doodskop met gekruiste bene | **Giftig** – kan jou baie siek maak of doodmaak |\n| Vlam | **Brandbaar** – vat maklik vlam |\n| Druppels wat op ’n hand val | **Bytend** – brand vel en oë |\n| Uitroepteken | **Skadelik** – kan vel, oë of longe irriteer |\n\n### Medisyne\n- Neem medisyne **net as ’n ouer of vertroude volwassene** dit vir jou gee, en net soveel as wat voorgeskryf is.\n- Neem **nooit** iemand anders se medisyne nie, al voel jy dieselfde siek.\n- Pille is nie lekkers nie. Hou medisyne buite klein kinders se bereik.\n\n### Elektrisiteit en warm water\n- Raak nooit aan proppe of skakelaars met **nat hande** nie, en steek niks in ’n kragsok nie.\n- Gebruik nie toestelle met **beskadigde koorde** nie.\n- Draai pothandvatsels na binne en hou die ketelkoord weg van klein kinders.\n- Brand jy jou? Hou die brandwond onder **koel lopende water** (omtrent 20 minute) en vertel ’n volwassene. Moenie botter of tandepasta daarop smeer nie.\n\n## Vuurveiligheid\n\n- **Kerse:** in ’n stewige houer, weg van gordyne; blaas dit dood voor jy gaan slaap.\n- **Paraffienstofies:** op ’n plat, stewige oppervlak; moet dit nooit volmaak terwyl dit brand nie.\n- Vuurhoutjies en aanstekers is nie speelgoed nie.\n\n**As jou klere vlam vat: Stop, val en rol!**\n1. **Stop** – moenie hardloop nie; hardloop blaas die vlamme groter.\n2. **Val** op die grond en bedek jou gesig met jou hande.\n3. **Rol** heen en weer totdat die vlamme dood is.\n\n**As die huis brand:** **bly laag** en kruip uit, want rook styg op en die lug naby die vloer is skoner. Gaan uit, **bly uit** en gaan nooit terug vir iets nie.\n\n> **Onthou:** Rook is baie gevaarlik – dit kan jou laat flou word voordat jy die vlamme sien.\n\n## Veiligheid in die omgewing\n\n- **Strate:** steek oor by ’n voetoorgang of verkeerslig. Kyk **regs, links en weer regs**, want in Suid-Afrika ry motors aan die linkerkant van die pad.\n- **Water:** swem net waar ’n volwassene toesig hou. Moenie in damme of riviere swem nie – jy weet nie hoe diep dit is of hoe sterk die stroom is nie. Moenie deur vloedwater loop nie.\n- **Kragdrade:** bly **ver weg** van kragdrade wat op die grond lê, al lyk hulle ‘dood’. Moenie in kragpale klim of vlieërs naby kragdrade vlieg nie. Onwettige aansluitings is lewensgevaarlik.\n\n## Noodnommers\n\n| Nommer | Wanneer |\n|---|---|\n| **10177** | Ambulans en brandweer |\n| **112** | Enige noodgeval, van ’n selfoon af |\n| **10111** | Polisie |\n\nAs jy bel, sê **wie** jy is, **wat** gebeur het, **waar** jy is en **hoeveel** mense beseer is. Bly aan die lyn totdat hulle sê jy kan afsit.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om iemand wat gif of paraffien ingesluk het, te laat opgooi. Dit kan meer skade doen. Kry dadelik ’n volwassene, bel 10177 of 112 en neem die houer saam kliniek of hospitaal toe.","en":"## Dangers in the home\n\nMany accidents involving children happen **at home**. If you know where the dangers are, you can protect yourself and your younger brothers and sisters.\n\n### Harmful household products\nProducts such as **bleach**, **paraffin**, drain cleaner, insect spray and rat poison are **poisonous**. If someone drinks them or gets them in their eyes, they can do serious harm.\n\n- Store them **high up** or in a **locked cupboard**, away from food.\n- Keep them in the **original container** with the label.\n- **Never** pour them into a cooldrink bottle or a cup. A small child may think paraffin is water or cooldrink and drink it.\n\n| Hazard symbol | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Skull and crossbones | **Poisonous** – can make you very ill or kill you |\n| Flame | **Flammable** – catches fire easily |\n| Drops falling on a hand | **Corrosive** – burns skin and eyes |\n| Exclamation mark | **Harmful** – can irritate skin, eyes or lungs |\n\n### Medicine\n- Take medicine **only when a parent or trusted adult** gives it to you, and only as much as was prescribed.\n- **Never** take someone else’s medicine, even if you feel sick in the same way.\n- Pills are not sweets. Keep medicine out of small children’s reach.\n\n### Electricity and hot water\n- Never touch plugs or switches with **wet hands**, and never push anything into a plug socket.\n- Do not use appliances with **damaged cords**.\n- Turn pot handles inwards and keep the kettle cord away from small children.\n- Have you burnt yourself? Hold the burn under **cool running water** (about 20 minutes) and tell an adult. Do not put butter or toothpaste on it.\n\n## Fire safety\n\n- **Candles:** in a sturdy holder, away from curtains; blow them out before you go to sleep.\n- **Paraffin stoves:** on a flat, steady surface; never fill one while it is burning.\n- Matches and lighters are not toys.\n\n**If your clothes catch fire: Stop, drop and roll!**\n1. **Stop** – do not run; running fans the flames.\n2. **Drop** to the ground and cover your face with your hands.\n3. **Roll** back and forth until the flames are out.\n\n**If the house is on fire:** **stay low** and crawl out, because smoke rises and the air near the floor is cleaner. Get out, **stay out** and never go back in for anything.\n\n> **Remember:** Smoke is very dangerous – it can make you pass out before you even see the flames.\n\n## Safety in the environment\n\n- **Streets:** cross at a pedestrian crossing or traffic light. Look **right, left and right again**, because in South Africa cars drive on the left side of the road.\n- **Water:** only swim where an adult is watching. Do not swim in dams or rivers – you do not know how deep the water is or how strong the current is. Do not walk through floodwater.\n- **Power lines:** stay **far away** from power lines lying on the ground, even if they look ‘dead’. Do not climb electricity poles or fly kites near power lines. Illegal connections are deadly.\n\n## Emergency numbers\n\n| Number | When |\n|---|---|\n| **10177** | Ambulance and fire brigade |\n| **112** | Any emergency, from a cellphone |\n| **10111** | Police |\n\nWhen you call, say **who** you are, **what** happened, **where** you are and **how many** people are hurt. Stay on the line until they tell you that you can hang up.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Making someone who has swallowed poison or paraffin vomit. This can cause more harm. Get an adult immediately, call 10177 or 112 and take the container along to the clinic or hospital."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Giftig","en":"Poisonous"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat jou baie siek kan maak of kan doodmaak as jy dit insluk, inasem of op jou vel kry.","en":"Something that can make you very ill or kill you if you swallow it, breathe it in or get it on your skin."}},{"term":{"af":"Gevaarsimbool","en":"Hazard symbol"},"def":{"af":"’n Prentjie op ’n etiket wat wys watter soort gevaar ’n produk inhou, soos ’n doodskop of ’n vlam.","en":"A picture on a label that shows what kind of danger a product has, such as a skull or a flame."}},{"term":{"af":"Brandbaar","en":"Flammable"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat maklik vlam vat, soos paraffien en petrol.","en":"Something that catches fire easily, such as paraffin and petrol."}},{"term":{"af":"Bytend","en":"Corrosive"},"def":{"af":"’n Stof wat vel, oë en ander oppervlakke kan verbrand, soos sterk afvoerskoonmaker.","en":"A substance that can burn skin, eyes and other surfaces, such as strong drain cleaner."}},{"term":{"af":"Voorgeskrewe medisyne","en":"Prescribed medicine"},"def":{"af":"Medisyne wat ’n dokter of kliniek vir een spesifieke persoon gegee het, met die regte hoeveelheid om te neem.","en":"Medicine that a doctor or clinic gave to one specific person, with the right amount to take."}},{"term":{"af":"Stop, val en rol","en":"Stop, drop and roll"},"def":{"af":"Wat jy doen as jou klere vlam vat: stop, val op die grond, bedek jou gesig en rol tot die vlamme dood is.","en":"What you do if your clothes catch fire: stop, drop to the ground, cover your face and roll until the flames are out."}},{"term":{"af":"Noodnommer","en":"Emergency number"},"def":{"af":"’n Telefoonnommer wat jy in ’n noodgeval gratis kan bel, soos 10177, 112 en 10111.","en":"A telephone number you can call free of charge in an emergency, such as 10177, 112 and 10111."}},{"term":{"af":"Voetoorgang","en":"Pedestrian crossing"},"def":{"af":"’n Gemerkte plek in die pad waar voetgangers veilig kan oorsteek.","en":"A marked place in the road where people on foot can cross safely."}},{"term":{"af":"Toesig","en":"Supervision"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n volwassene na kinders kyk om seker te maak dat hulle veilig is, byvoorbeeld by ’n swembad.","en":"When an adult watches children to make sure they are safe, for example at a swimming pool."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Paraffien in ’n koeldrankbottel","en":"Paraffin in a cooldrink bottle"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho se oom hou paraffien in ’n leë koeldrankbottel onder die wasbak. Sipho se boetie is drie jaar oud. Verduidelik die gevaar en sê hoe die paraffien veilig gebêre moet word.","en":"Sipho’s uncle keeps paraffin in an empty cooldrink bottle under the sink. Sipho’s little brother is three years old. Explain the danger and say how the paraffin should be stored safely."},"steps":[{"af":"**Herken die gevaar:** ’n Klein kind ken nie die verskil nie. Hy kan dink die paraffien is water of koeldrank en dit drink.","en":"**Recognise the danger:** A small child does not know the difference. He may think the paraffin is water or cooldrink and drink it."},{"af":"**Waarom dit gevaarlik is:** Paraffien is giftig as dit ingesluk word, en dit is ook brandbaar.","en":"**Why it is dangerous:** Paraffin is poisonous if swallowed, and it is also flammable."},{"af":"**Bêre dit reg:** in ’n houer wat net vir paraffien gebruik word en duidelik gemerk is, hoog of toegesluit, weg van kos en van vuur.","en":"**Store it correctly:** in a container used only for paraffin and clearly labelled, high up or locked away, away from food and from fire."},{"af":"**As iemand dit drink:** moenie hom laat opgooi nie; kry ’n volwassene, bel 10177 of 112 en neem die bottel saam.","en":"**If someone drinks it:** do not make him vomit; get an adult, call 10177 or 112 and take the bottle along."}],"answer":{"af":"Die kind kan die paraffien vir koeldrank aansien en dit drink. Dit moet in ’n gemerkte paraffienhouer, hoog of toegesluit, weg van kos en vuur gebêre word.","en":"The child may mistake the paraffin for cooldrink and drink it. It must be stored in a labelled paraffin container, high up or locked away, away from food and fire."}},{"title":{"af":"Lees ’n etiket","en":"Read a label"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato sien twee simbole op ’n bottel ovenskoonmaker: druppels wat op ’n hand val, en ’n uitroepteken. Wat beteken die simbole, en hoe moet die bottel hanteer word?","en":"Lerato sees two symbols on a bottle of oven cleaner: drops falling on a hand, and an exclamation mark. What do the symbols mean, and how should the bottle be handled?"},"steps":[{"af":"Druppels wat op ’n hand val beteken **bytend**: die stof kan vel en oë verbrand.","en":"Drops falling on a hand mean **corrosive**: the substance can burn skin and eyes."},{"af":"’n Uitroepteken beteken **skadelik**: dit kan vel, oë of longe irriteer.","en":"An exclamation mark means **harmful**: it can irritate skin, eyes or lungs."},{"af":"Dus moet net ’n volwassene dit gebruik, liefs met handskoene, en dit moet in die oorspronklike bottel, hoog of toegesluit, gebêre word.","en":"So only an adult should use it, preferably with gloves, and it must be stored in the original bottle, high up or locked away."}],"answer":{"af":"Die produk is bytend en skadelik. ’n Volwassene moet dit versigtig gebruik en dit buite kinders se bereik in die oorspronklike bottel bêre.","en":"The product is corrosive and harmful. An adult must use it carefully and store it out of children’s reach in the original bottle."}},{"title":{"af":"Brand in die kombuis","en":"Fire in the kitchen"},"problem":{"af":"Nomsa se mou vat vlam by die paraffienstofie. Kort daarna is die kamer vol rook. Skryf in die regte volgorde neer wat sy moet doen.","en":"Nomsa’s sleeve catches fire at the paraffin stove. Soon afterwards the room is full of smoke. Write down in the correct order what she must do."},"steps":[{"af":"**Stop, val en rol:** sy moet nie hardloop nie, op die grond val, haar gesig bedek en rol tot die vlamme dood is.","en":"**Stop, drop and roll:** she must not run, drop to the ground, cover her face and roll until the flames are out."},{"af":"**Bly laag:** rook styg op, so sy moet onder die rook uitkruip.","en":"**Stay low:** smoke rises, so she must crawl out under the smoke."},{"af":"**Gaan uit en bly uit:** sy moet nie teruggaan nie. Van buite moet sy of ’n volwassene 10177 of 112 bel.","en":"**Get out and stay out:** she must not go back in. From outside she or an adult must call 10177 or 112."},{"af":"**Versorg die brandwond:** hou dit onder koel lopende water vir omtrent 20 minute en gaan kliniek toe.","en":"**Treat the burn:** hold it under cool running water for about 20 minutes and go to the clinic."}],"answer":{"af":"Stop, val en rol → bly laag en kruip uit → bly buite en bel 10177 of 112 → koel die brandwond met lopende water en gaan kliniek toe.","en":"Stop, drop and roll → stay low and crawl out → stay outside and call 10177 or 112 → cool the burn with running water and go to the clinic."}},{"title":{"af":"’n Kragdraad op die sypaadjie","en":"A power line on the pavement"},"problem":{"af":"Ná ’n storm sien Pieter ’n kragdraad op die sypaadjie lê. Sy maat sê: ‘Kom ons skuif dit met ’n stok weg.’ Wat moet hulle doen?","en":"After a storm Pieter sees a power line lying on the pavement. His friend says: ‘Let’s move it out of the way with a stick.’ What should they do?"},"steps":[{"af":"’n Draad op die grond kan nog elektrisiteit dra, al lyk dit ‘dood’. ’n Skok kan dodelik wees.","en":"A line on the ground can still carry electricity, even if it looks ‘dead’. A shock can be deadly."},{"af":"Hulle moet nie daaraan raak nie, ook nie met ’n stok nie, en ver weg bly.","en":"They must not touch it, not even with a stick, and must stay far away."},{"af":"Hulle moet ander mense waarsku en dadelik ’n volwassene vertel, wat die munisipaliteit of die kragverskaffer bel, of 112 as iemand in gevaar is.","en":"They must warn other people and tell an adult immediately, who will call the municipality or the electricity supplier, or 112 if someone is in danger."}],"answer":{"af":"Bly ver weg, raak glad nie daaraan nie, waarsku ander en laat ’n volwassene dit dadelik aanmeld.","en":"Stay far away, do not touch it at all, warn others and let an adult report it immediately."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar is die veiligste plek om paraffien te bêre?","en":"Where is the safest place to store paraffin?"},"options":[{"af":"In ’n leë koeldrankbottel in die yskas","en":"In an empty cooldrink bottle in the fridge"},{"af":"In ’n koppie langs die stofie","en":"In a cup next to the stove"},{"af":"In ’n gemerkte houer, hoog of toegesluit, weg van vuur","en":"In a labelled container, high up or locked away, away from fire"},{"af":"Onder die bed, waar niemand dit sien nie","en":"Under the bed, where nobody can see it"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Paraffien is giftig en brandbaar. Dit moet gemerk wees, buite kinders se bereik en weg van vuur. In ’n koeldrankbottel of koppie kan ’n kind dit vir iets om te drink aansien, en onder die bed kan ’n klein kind dit maklik kry.","en":"Paraffin is poisonous and flammable. It must be labelled, out of children’s reach and away from fire. In a cooldrink bottle or cup a child may think it is something to drink, and a small child can easily reach it under the bed."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Dit is veilig om jou maat se medisyne te drink as julle dieselfde siek voel.","en":"It is safe to take your friend’s medicine if you feel sick in the same way."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Medisyne word vir een spesifieke persoon en siekte voorgeskryf. Dit kan jou skade aandoen. Neem net medisyne wat ’n ouer of vertroude volwassene vir jou gee.","en":"False. Medicine is prescribed for one specific person and illness. It can harm you. Only take medicine that a parent or trusted adult gives you."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken ’n doodskop met gekruiste bene op ’n etiket?","en":"What does a skull and crossbones on a label mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Die produk is giftig","en":"The product is poisonous"},{"af":"Die produk vat maklik vlam","en":"The product catches fire easily"},{"af":"Die produk is net vir volwassenes se klere","en":"The product is only for adults’ clothes"},{"af":"Die produk se datum het verval","en":"The product’s date has expired"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die doodskop met gekruiste bene is die simbool vir gif. ’n Vlam beteken brandbaar. As jy hierdie simbool sien, moet jy nie aan die produk raak nie.","en":"The skull and crossbones is the symbol for poison. A flame means flammable. If you see this symbol, do not touch the product."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As jou klere vlam vat, moet jy stop, ___ en rol.","en":"If your clothes catch fire, you must stop, ___ and roll."},"answers":{"af":["val"],"en":["drop"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["hardloop","skree","spring"],"en":["run","shout","jump"]}},"explain":{"af":"Stop, val en rol. As jy hardloop, kry die vlamme meer lug en brand hulle groter. Deur te val en te rol, smoor jy die vlamme.","en":"Stop, drop and roll. If you run, the flames get more air and grow bigger. By dropping and rolling you smother the flames."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom moet jy laag bly en uitkruip as ’n huis brand?","en":"Why should you stay low and crawl out when a house is on fire?"},"options":[{"af":"Sodat die brandweer jou van buite kan sien","en":"So that the fire brigade can see you from outside"},{"af":"Omdat die vloer die koelste plek is om te slaap","en":"Because the floor is the coolest place to sleep"},{"af":"Sodat jy jou speelgoed op die vloer kan optel","en":"So that you can pick up your toys from the floor"},{"af":"Omdat rook opstyg en die lug naby die vloer skoner is","en":"Because smoke rises and the air near the floor is cleaner"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Warm rook styg op. Naby die vloer is daar minder rook, so jy kan makliker asemhaal. Rook kan jou laat flou word, daarom is dit so belangrik.","en":"Hot smoke rises. Near the floor there is less smoke, so you can breathe more easily. Smoke can make you pass out, so this is very important."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Julle bal rol tot naby ’n kragdraad wat ná ’n storm op die grond lê. Wat doen jy?","en":"Your ball rolls close to a power line lying on the ground after a storm. What do you do?"},"options":[{"af":"Haal die bal vinnig uit, solank jy nie aan die draad raak nie","en":"Fetch the ball quickly, as long as you do not touch the line"},{"af":"Los die bal, bly ver weg en vertel dadelik ’n volwassene","en":"Leave the ball, stay far away and tell an adult immediately"},{"af":"Skuif die draad met ’n droë stok weg en haal dan die bal","en":"Move the line with a dry stick and then fetch the ball"},{"af":"Gooi water op die draad sodat dit afkoel","en":"Throw water on the line so that it cools down"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"’n Draad op die grond kan nog elektrisiteit dra, al lyk dit dood. Selfs naby die draad is jy in gevaar. Geen bal is jou lewe werd nie – bly weg en kry ’n volwassene.","en":"A line on the ground can still carry electricity, even if it looks dead. Even near the line you are in danger. No ball is worth your life – stay away and get an adult."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke gevaarsimbool by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each hazard symbol to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Doodskop met gekruiste bene","en":"Skull and crossbones"},"r":{"af":"Giftig","en":"Poisonous"}},{"l":{"af":"Vlam","en":"Flame"},"r":{"af":"Brandbaar","en":"Flammable"}},{"l":{"af":"Druppels wat op ’n hand val","en":"Drops falling on a hand"},"r":{"af":"Bytend – brand vel en oë","en":"Corrosive – burns skin and eyes"}},{"l":{"af":"Uitroepteken","en":"Exclamation mark"},"r":{"af":"Skadelik – kan irriteer","en":"Harmful – can irritate"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die simbole wys vinnig watter gevaar ’n produk inhou, selfs as jy nie die woorde op die etiket kan lees nie.","en":"The symbols quickly show what danger a product holds, even if you cannot read the words on the label."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Anika brand haar hand aan ’n warm ketel. Wat is die beste eerste hulp?","en":"Anika burns her hand on a hot kettle. What is the best first aid?"},"options":[{"af":"Smeer dadelik botter op die brandwond","en":"Put butter on the burn immediately"},{"af":"Sit tandepasta op en draai dit styf toe","en":"Put toothpaste on it and wrap it tightly"},{"af":"Hou dit omtrent 20 minute onder koel lopende water","en":"Hold it under cool running water for about 20 minutes"},{"af":"Blaas ’n paar sekondes daarop en speel verder","en":"Blow on it for a few seconds and carry on playing"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Koel lopende water haal die hitte uit die vel en keer dat die brandwond erger word. Botter en tandepasta hou die hitte in en kan kieme inbring. Sy moet ook ’n volwassene vertel.","en":"Cool running water takes the heat out of the skin and stops the burn from getting worse. Butter and toothpaste keep the heat in and can bring in germs. She must also tell an adult."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Rook styg op, daarom moet jy by ’n brand ___ bly en uitkruip.","en":"Smoke rises, so in a fire you must stay ___ and crawl out."},"answers":{"af":["laag"],"en":["low"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["hoog","binne","stil"],"en":["high","inside","still"]}},"explain":{"af":"Naby die vloer is daar minder rook en skoner lug. Moet nooit binne bly of wegkruip nie – gaan uit en bly uit.","en":"Near the floor there is less smoke and cleaner air. Never stay inside or hide – get out and stay out."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy bel 10177 omdat jou oupa geval het en nie wakker word nie. Wat moet jy vir hulle sê?","en":"You call 10177 because your grandpa has fallen and is not waking up. What must you tell them?"},"options":[{"af":"Jou naam, wat gebeur het, waar jy is en hoeveel mense beseer is","en":"Your name, what happened, where you are and how many people are hurt"},{"af":"Net ‘Help asseblief!’, en dan sit jy vinnig af","en":"Just ‘Please help!’, and then you hang up quickly"},{"af":"Jou oupa se ouderdom en sy gunsteling-kos","en":"Your grandpa’s age and his favourite food"},{"af":"Net jou naam, want hulle sal die res self uitvind","en":"Only your name, because they will find out the rest themselves"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die nooddiens moet weet wie bel, wat gebeur het, waar om heen te kom en hoeveel mense hulp nodig het. Sit eers af wanneer hulle sê jy kan.","en":"The emergency service must know who is calling, what happened, where to come and how many people need help. Only hang up when they tell you that you can."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In Suid-Afrika kyk jy eers regs voordat jy die straat oorsteek, want motors ry aan die linkerkant van die pad.","en":"In South Africa you look right first before you cross the street, because cars drive on the left side of the road."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die motors naaste aan jou kom van regs af, daarom kyk jy regs, links en weer regs.","en":"True. The cars closest to you come from the right, so you look right, left and right again."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Zanele se klein sussie het bleikmiddel gedrink. Wat moet Zanele eerste doen?","en":"Zanele’s little sister has drunk bleach. What should Zanele do first?"},"options":[{"af":"Laat haar sussie dadelik opgooi sodat die gif uitkom","en":"Make her sister vomit straight away so the poison comes out"},{"af":"Wag ’n uur om te sien of haar sussie siek word","en":"Wait an hour to see if her sister gets sick"},{"af":"Gee haar sussie ’n ander medisyne uit die kas","en":"Give her sister some other medicine from the cupboard"},{"af":"Kry dadelik ’n volwassene en bel 10177 of 112","en":"Get an adult immediately and call 10177 or 112"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Gif is ’n noodgeval – moenie wag nie. Moenie iemand laat opgooi nie, want bleikmiddel kan op pad terug weer brand. Neem die bottel saam sodat die dokter weet wat gedrink is.","en":"Poisoning is an emergency – do not wait. Do not make someone vomit, because bleach can burn again on the way back up. Take the bottle along so the doctor knows what was swallowed."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hou skoonmaakmiddels altyd in hul ___ houer met die etiket.","en":"Always keep cleaning products in their ___ container with the label."},"answers":{"af":["oorspronklike","eie"],"en":["original","own"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["mooiste","oop","kleinste"],"en":["prettiest","open","smallest"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die oorspronklike houer het die etiket met die gevaarsimbole en aanwysings. As jy dit in ’n ander houer gooi, weet niemand wat daarin is nie.","en":"The original container has the label with the hazard symbols and instructions. If you pour it into another container, nobody knows what is inside."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op ’n warm dag wil Thabo se maats sonder ’n volwassene in die plaasdam gaan swem. Wat is die veiligste keuse?","en":"On a hot day Thabo’s friends want to go swimming in the farm dam without an adult. What is the safest choice?"},"options":[{"af":"Swem net in die vlak deel, want dan kan niks gebeur nie","en":"Swim only in the shallow part, because then nothing can happen"},{"af":"Sê nee en swem net waar ’n volwassene toesig hou","en":"Say no and only swim where an adult is watching"},{"af":"Swem, maar bly naby die maat wat die beste kan swem","en":"Swim, but stay close to the friend who swims best"},{"af":"Spring eers in om te toets hoe diep die water is","en":"Jump in first to test how deep the water is"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In ’n dam weet jy nie hoe diep die water is of wat onder die water is nie, en die bodem kan skielik wegsak. Swem net met ’n volwassene wat toesig hou. ’n Maat kan jou nie veilig red nie.","en":"In a dam you do not know how deep the water is or what is under the water, and the bottom can drop away suddenly. Only swim with an adult watching. A friend cannot rescue you safely."}}]},{"id":"lv5-t3-water","title":{"af":"Water: ’n basiese behoefte","en":"Water: a basic need"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik waarom water ’n basiese behoefte en ’n reg is, maniere kan noem om water te bespaar en te beskerm, en weet hoe om water veilig te maak om te drink.","en":"You will be able to explain why water is a basic need and a right, name ways to save and protect water, and know how to make water safe to drink."},"summary":{"af":"## Waarom water ’n basiese behoefte is\n\n’n **Basiese behoefte** is iets wat jy **moet** hê om te lewe. Meer as die helfte van jou liggaam bestaan uit water. Jy het water nodig om:\n\n- te **drink** – jou liggaam kan net ’n paar dae sonder water oorleef;\n- kos te **kook** en kos te **verbou** – plante en diere het ook water nodig;\n- jou **hande, liggaam en klere** te was sodat jy nie siek word nie;\n- toilette te spoel en jou omgewing skoon te hou.\n\nOmdat water so belangrik is, sê die **Grondwet** dat elke mens die **reg** het op toegang tot genoeg kos en water. Met ’n reg kom ’n **verantwoordelikheid**: ons moet water oppas sodat daar genoeg vir almal is.\n\n## Suid-Afrika is ’n droë land\n\nSuid-Afrika kry gemiddeld net omtrent die **helfte** van die wêreld se gemiddelde reënval. Die reën val ook nie eweredig nie: die ooste is natter, terwyl die weste, soos die Noord-Kaap, baie droog is. **Droogtes** (lang tye sonder genoeg reën) kom gereeld voor.\n\nOns water kom uit **riviere**, **damme**, **boorgate** (water onder die grond) en **reënwatertenks**. Water uit damme en riviere word by ’n **waterreinigingsaanleg** skoongemaak voordat dit deur pype na ons krane gaan.\n\n## Maniere om water te bespaar\n\n| Tuis | By die skool |\n|---|---|\n| Stort kort in plaas van om te bad | Draai krane styf toe ná gebruik |\n| Draai die kraan toe terwyl jy tande borsel | Meld lekkende krane en toilette aan |\n| Laat lekkende krane herstel | Plant inheemse plante wat min water nodig het |\n| Gee die tuin vroegoggend of saans water | Vang reënwater in ’n tenk op |\n| Gebruik grys water vir die tuin | Begin ’n span wat lekke soek |\n\n**Grys water** is water wat al gebruik is om te bad, klere te was of skottelgoed te was. Dit is nie veilig om te drink nie, maar jy kan dit gebruik om die tuin nat te maak of die toilet te spoel. Water uit die toilet is **nie** grys water nie.\n\nWaarom saans of vroegoggend natmaak? Dan is dit koeler, en minder water **verdamp** voordat die plante dit kan opneem.\n\n> **Onthou:** Elke druppel tel. ’n Kraan wat drup, mors dag en nag water, al lyk dit min.\n\n## Waterbesoedeling\n\n**Waterbesoedeling** is wanneer skadelike stowwe of kieme in water kom sodat dit onveilig word. Oorsake is:\n\n- **rommel** en plastiek wat in riviere beland;\n- **riool** wat uit gebreekte pype lek;\n- **chemikalieë** van fabrieke, en kunsmis en gif van plase;\n- olie en verf in **stormwaterdreine** – hierdie dreine loop reguit na riviere en die see.\n\nBesoedelde water kan mense **siek** maak, byvoorbeeld met diarree, en visse en plante kan doodgaan. **Beskerm water** deur rommel in die asblik te gooi, nooit olie of chemikalieë in dreine te gooi nie, riool-lekke by die munisipaliteit aan te meld en met skoonmaakdae te help.\n\n## Veilige drinkwater\n\nWater uit ’n rivier, dam of tenk kan **kieme** bevat, al lyk dit skoon. As jy nie seker is nie:\n\n1. Laat vuil water eers staan sodat die modder afsak, en gooi dit deur ’n skoon lap. Dit haal vuilgoed uit, maar **maak nie kieme dood nie**.\n2. **Kook** die water: laat dit minstens een minuut lank borrelend kook, en laat dit dan afkoel.\n3. ’n Volwassene kan ook watersuiweringstablette of ’n klein hoeveelheid bleikmiddel byvoeg, presies soos die kliniek of munisipaliteit aanbeveel.\n4. Bêre die water in ’n **skoon houer met ’n deksel** en skep dit met ’n skoon beker uit.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om te dink helder water is altyd veilig. Kieme is te klein om te sien – helder water kan jou steeds siek maak.","en":"## Why water is a basic need\n\nA **basic need** is something you **must** have to live. More than half of your body is made of water. You need water to:\n\n- **drink** – your body can survive only a few days without water;\n- **cook** food and **grow** food – plants and animals need water too;\n- wash your **hands, body and clothes** so that you do not get sick;\n- flush toilets and keep your surroundings clean.\n\nBecause water is so important, the **Constitution** says that every person has the **right** to have access to enough food and water. With a right comes a **responsibility**: we must look after water so that there is enough for everyone.\n\n## South Africa is a dry country\n\nOn average, South Africa gets only about **half** of the world’s average rainfall. The rain also does not fall evenly: the east is wetter, while the west, like the Northern Cape, is very dry. **Droughts** (long periods without enough rain) happen often.\n\nOur water comes from **rivers**, **dams**, **boreholes** (water under the ground) and **rainwater tanks**. Water from dams and rivers is cleaned at a **water treatment works** before it goes through pipes to our taps.\n\n## Ways to save water\n\n| At home | At school |\n|---|---|\n| Take a short shower instead of a bath | Close taps tightly after use |\n| Turn off the tap while you brush your teeth | Report leaking taps and toilets |\n| Have leaking taps fixed | Plant indigenous plants that need little water |\n| Water the garden early in the morning or in the evening | Catch rainwater in a tank |\n| Use grey water for the garden | Start a team that looks for leaks |\n\n**Grey water** is water that has already been used for bathing, washing clothes or washing dishes. It is not safe to drink, but you can use it to water the garden or flush the toilet. Water from the toilet is **not** grey water.\n\nWhy water in the evening or early morning? Then it is cooler, and less water **evaporates** before the plants can take it in.\n\n> **Remember:** Every drop counts. A dripping tap wastes water day and night, even if it looks like very little.\n\n## Water pollution\n\n**Water pollution** is when harmful substances or germs get into water so that it becomes unsafe. Causes are:\n\n- **litter** and plastic that end up in rivers;\n- **sewage** leaking from broken pipes;\n- **chemicals** from factories, and fertiliser and poison from farms;\n- oil and paint in **stormwater drains** – these drains run straight to rivers and the sea.\n\nPolluted water can make people **sick**, for example with diarrhoea, and fish and plants can die. **Protect water** by putting litter in the bin, never pouring oil or chemicals into drains, reporting sewage leaks to the municipality and helping with clean-up days.\n\n## Safe drinking water\n\nWater from a river, dam or tank can contain **germs**, even if it looks clean. If you are not sure:\n\n1. First let dirty water stand so that the mud settles, and pour it through a clean cloth. This removes dirt, but **does not kill germs**.\n2. **Boil** the water: let it bubble and boil for at least one minute, then let it cool down.\n3. An adult can also add water purification tablets or a small amount of bleach, exactly as the clinic or municipality recommends.\n4. Store the water in a **clean container with a lid** and scoop it out with a clean cup.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Thinking that clear water is always safe. Germs are too small to see – clear water can still make you sick."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Basiese behoefte","en":"Basic need"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat ’n mens moet hê om te lewe, soos water, kos en skuiling.","en":"Something a person must have to live, such as water, food and shelter."}},{"term":{"af":"Reg","en":"Right"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat elke mens volgens die Grondwet mag hê of mag doen, soos toegang tot genoeg water.","en":"Something every person may have or do according to the Constitution, such as access to enough water."}},{"term":{"af":"Droogte","en":"Drought"},"def":{"af":"’n Lang tyd sonder genoeg reën, sodat damme leeg raak en plante doodgaan.","en":"A long time without enough rain, so that dams run low and plants die."}},{"term":{"af":"Grys water","en":"Grey water"},"def":{"af":"Water wat al gebruik is om te bad of te was, en wat jy weer vir die tuin of die toilet kan gebruik.","en":"Water that has already been used for bathing or washing, and that you can use again for the garden or the toilet."}},{"term":{"af":"Waterbesoedeling","en":"Water pollution"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer skadelike stowwe of kieme in water kom sodat dit onveilig word vir mense, diere en plante.","en":"When harmful substances or germs get into water so that it becomes unsafe for people, animals and plants."}},{"term":{"af":"Riool","en":"Sewage"},"def":{"af":"Vuil water van toilette en wasbakke wat deur pype weggevoer word.","en":"Dirty water from toilets and basins that is carried away through pipes."}},{"term":{"af":"Stormwaterdrein","en":"Stormwater drain"},"def":{"af":"’n Drein langs die straat wat reënwater reguit na riviere en die see lei.","en":"A drain next to the street that carries rainwater straight to rivers and the sea."}},{"term":{"af":"Boorgat","en":"Borehole"},"def":{"af":"’n Diep, smal gat wat in die grond geboor word om water onder die grond uit te pomp.","en":"A deep, narrow hole drilled into the ground to pump up water from under the ground."}},{"term":{"af":"Waterreinigingsaanleg","en":"Water treatment works"},"def":{"af":"’n Plek waar water uit damme en riviere skoongemaak word sodat dit veilig is om te drink.","en":"A place where water from dams and rivers is cleaned so that it is safe to drink."}},{"term":{"af":"Inheemse plante","en":"Indigenous plants"},"def":{"af":"Plante wat natuurlik in Suid-Afrika groei; baie het min water nodig.","en":"Plants that grow naturally in South Africa; many need little water."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Bereken hoeveel water jy spaar","en":"Work out how much water you save"},"problem":{"af":"Liam bad elke dag. ’n Bad gebruik omtrent 80 liter water en ’n kort stort omtrent 50 liter. Hoeveel water spaar hy in een week as hy elke dag kort stort in plaas van bad?","en":"Liam takes a bath every day. A bath uses about 80 litres of water and a short shower about 50 litres. How much water does he save in one week if he takes a short shower every day instead of a bath?"},"steps":[{"af":"Bereken die besparing per dag: 80 ℓ − 50 ℓ = 30 ℓ.","en":"Work out the saving per day: 80 ℓ − 50 ℓ = 30 ℓ."},{"af":"’n Week het 7 dae: 30 ℓ × 7 = 210 ℓ.","en":"A week has 7 days: 30 ℓ × 7 = 210 ℓ."},{"af":"Dink na: as die hele gesin dit doen, word die besparing nog groter.","en":"Think about it: if the whole family does this, the saving becomes even bigger."}],"answer":{"af":"Hy spaar omtrent 210 liter water per week.","en":"He saves about 210 litres of water per week."}},{"title":{"af":"Vind die besoedeling","en":"Find the pollution"},"problem":{"af":"’n Rivier vloei verby ’n fabriek, ’n mielieplaas en ’n woonbuurt waar ’n rioolpyp gebreek het. Kinders gooi ook papiere in die rivier. Noem drie oorsake van besoedeling en een oplossing vir elkeen.","en":"A river flows past a factory, a maize farm and a neighbourhood where a sewage pipe has broken. Children also throw papers into the river. Name three causes of pollution and one solution for each."},"steps":[{"af":"**Fabriek:** chemikalieë kan in die rivier beland. Oplossing: die fabriek moet sy afval veilig hanteer, en mense kan dit by die munisipaliteit aanmeld.","en":"**Factory:** chemicals can end up in the river. Solution: the factory must deal with its waste safely, and people can report it to the municipality."},{"af":"**Gebreekte rioolpyp:** riool bring kieme in die water. Oplossing: meld die lek dadelik by die munisipaliteit aan.","en":"**Broken sewage pipe:** sewage brings germs into the water. Solution: report the leak to the municipality immediately."},{"af":"**Papiere en rommel:** dit maak die water vuil en kan diere skaad. Oplossing: gooi rommel in ’n asblik en reël ’n skoonmaakdag.","en":"**Papers and litter:** these make the water dirty and can harm animals. Solution: put litter in a bin and organise a clean-up day."},{"af":"Die plaas kan ook kunsmis of gif in die rivier laat spoel – dit is ’n vierde oorsaak.","en":"The farm can also let fertiliser or poison wash into the river – that is a fourth cause."}],"answer":{"af":"Chemikalieë van die fabriek (afval veilig hanteer), riool uit die gebreekte pyp (lek aanmeld), rommel (in die asblik gooi en skoonmaak).","en":"Chemicals from the factory (handle waste safely), sewage from the broken pipe (report the leak), litter (put it in the bin and clean up)."}},{"title":{"af":"Maak water veilig om te drink","en":"Make water safe to drink"},"problem":{"af":"Daar is vir ’n paar dae nie water in die krane nie. Nomsa se gesin skep water uit ’n rivier. Die water lyk effens troebel. Hoe kan hulle dit veilig maak om te drink?","en":"For a few days there is no water in the taps. Nomsa’s family fetches water from a river. The water looks slightly cloudy. How can they make it safe to drink?"},"steps":[{"af":"Laat die water staan sodat die modder afsak, en gooi dit dan deur ’n skoon lap.","en":"Let the water stand so that the mud settles, then pour it through a clean cloth."},{"af":"Die lap haal net vuilgoed uit. Om **kieme dood te maak**, moet hulle die water minstens een minuut lank laat kook (of ’n volwassene gebruik watersuiweringstablette volgens die aanwysings).","en":"The cloth only removes dirt. To **kill germs**, they must boil the water for at least one minute (or an adult uses water purification tablets according to the instructions)."},{"af":"Laat dit afkoel en bêre dit in ’n skoon houer met ’n deksel, sodat dit nie weer vuil word nie.","en":"Let it cool and store it in a clean container with a lid, so that it does not get dirty again."}],"answer":{"af":"Laat dit afsak, filtreer dit deur ’n lap, kook dit minstens een minuut, laat dit afkoel en bêre dit toegemaak in ’n skoon houer.","en":"Let it settle, filter it through a cloth, boil it for at least one minute, let it cool and store it covered in a clean container."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken dit dat water ’n basiese behoefte is?","en":"What does it mean that water is a basic need?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is iets wat net ryk mense kan bekostig","en":"It is something only rich people can afford"},{"af":"Dit is iets wat ’n mens net in die somer nodig het","en":"It is something a person needs only in summer"},{"af":"Dit is iets wat lekker is, maar nie noodsaaklik nie","en":"It is something nice to have, but not essential"},{"af":"Dit is iets wat ’n mens moet hê om te lewe","en":"It is something a person must have to live"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Basiese behoefte is iets waarsonder jy nie kan lewe nie. Jou liggaam kan net ’n paar dae sonder water oorleef, en jy het water nodig vir kos en higiëne.","en":"A basic need is something you cannot live without. Your body can survive only a few days without water, and you need water for food and hygiene."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Water wat al gebruik is om te bad of klere te was, word ___ water genoem.","en":"Water that has already been used for bathing or washing clothes is called ___ water."},"answers":{"af":["grys"],"en":["grey","gray"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vars","skoon","reën"],"en":["fresh","clean","rain"]}},"explain":{"af":"Grys water is gebruikte water van bad, wasgoed of skottelgoed. Jy kan dit vir die tuin of die toilet gebruik, maar nie drink nie.","en":"Grey water is used water from bathing, laundry or dishes. You can use it for the garden or the toilet, but you must not drink it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom word Suid-Afrika ’n droë land genoem?","en":"Why is South Africa called a dry country?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat dit nooit in Suid-Afrika reën nie","en":"Because it never rains in South Africa"},{"af":"Omdat dit gemiddeld net omtrent die helfte van die wêreld se gemiddelde reënval kry","en":"Because it gets only about half of the world’s average rainfall"},{"af":"Omdat al sy riviere in die see uitloop","en":"Because all its rivers flow into the sea"},{"af":"Omdat dit net in die winter reën in die hele land","en":"Because it rains only in winter in the whole country"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Suid-Afrika kry wel reën, maar minder as die meeste lande – omtrent die helfte van die wêreldgemiddeld – en dit val ongelyk: die weste is baie droog.","en":"South Africa does get rain, but less than most countries – about half of the world average – and it falls unevenly: the west is very dry."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As water helder lyk, is dit altyd veilig om te drink.","en":"If water looks clear, it is always safe to drink."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Kieme is te klein om te sien. Helder water uit ’n rivier of dam kan jou steeds siek maak, daarom kook jy dit as jy nie seker is nie.","en":"False. Germs are too small to see. Clear water from a river or dam can still make you sick, so you boil it if you are not sure."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die beste manier om water te spaar wanneer jy jou tande borsel?","en":"What is the best way to save water when you brush your teeth?"},"options":[{"af":"Draai die kraan toe terwyl jy borsel en gebruik ’n beker water om te spoel","en":"Turn off the tap while you brush and use a cup of water to rinse"},{"af":"Laat die kraan stadig loop sodat jy minder water mors","en":"Let the tap run slowly so that you waste less water"},{"af":"Borsel jou tande net een keer per week","en":"Brush your teeth only once a week"},{"af":"Borsel jou tande onder die stort","en":"Brush your teeth in the shower"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Kraan wat loop terwyl jy borsel, mors water selfs as dit stadig loop. Met die kraan toe en ’n beker water spaar jy die meeste. Jy moet steeds jou tande gereeld borsel.","en":"A tap that runs while you brush wastes water even if it runs slowly. With the tap closed and a cup of water you save the most. You must still brush your teeth regularly."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke waterprobleem by die beste oplossing.","en":"Match each water problem to the best solution."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"’n Kraan wat drup","en":"A dripping tap"},"r":{"af":"Laat dit herstel of meld dit aan","en":"Have it fixed or report it"}},{"l":{"af":"’n Lang, vol bad elke dag","en":"A long, full bath every day"},"r":{"af":"Stort eerder kort","en":"Take a short shower instead"}},{"l":{"af":"Die tuin word in die middag natgemaak","en":"The garden is watered at midday"},"r":{"af":"Maak vroegoggend of saans nat","en":"Water early in the morning or in the evening"}},{"l":{"af":"Ou kookolie wat weggegooi moet word","en":"Old cooking oil that must be thrown away"},"r":{"af":"Gooi dit in ’n toe houer vir die asblik, nie in die drein nie","en":"Put it in a closed container for the bin, not down the drain"}},{"l":{"af":"Rommel langs die rivier","en":"Litter next to the river"},"r":{"af":"Hou ’n skoonmaakdag","en":"Hold a clean-up day"}}],"explain":{"af":"Lekke herstel en kort stort spaar water; saans natmaak keer verdamping; olie hoort nie in dreine nie, want dit besoedel water; en skoonmaakdae haal rommel uit die rivier.","en":"Fixing leaks and short showers save water; watering in the evening prevents evaporation; oil does not belong in drains because it pollutes water; and clean-up days remove litter from the river."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n oorsaak van waterbesoedeling?","en":"Which one is a cause of water pollution?"},"options":[{"af":"Reënwater wat in ’n tenk opgevang word","en":"Rainwater caught in a tank"},{"af":"Inheemse plante langs ’n rivier","en":"Indigenous plants next to a river"},{"af":"Riool wat uit ’n gebreekte pyp lek","en":"Sewage leaking from a broken pipe"},{"af":"Water wat by ’n reinigingsaanleg skoongemaak word","en":"Water being cleaned at a treatment works"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Riool bevat kieme wat mense siek kan maak. Die ander opsies help eerder om water te bespaar of skoon te hou.","en":"Sewage contains germs that can make people sick. The other options rather help to save water or keep it clean."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Om kieme in water dood te maak, moet jy die water minstens een minuut lank ___.","en":"To kill germs in water, you must ___ the water for at least one minute."},"answers":{"af":["kook","laat kook"],"en":["boil"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["filtreer","afkoel","roer"],"en":["filter","cool","stir"]}},"explain":{"af":"Kook maak kieme dood. Om water deur ’n lap te filtreer haal net vuilgoed uit – die kieme bly in die water.","en":"Boiling kills germs. Filtering water through a cloth only removes dirt – the germs stay in the water."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom moet jy nooit verf of olie in ’n stormwaterdrein gooi nie?","en":"Why must you never pour paint or oil into a stormwater drain?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat stormwaterdreine reguit na riviere en die see loop","en":"Because stormwater drains run straight to rivers and the sea"},{"af":"Omdat die verf die drein se kleur sal verander","en":"Because the paint will change the colour of the drain"},{"af":"Omdat stormwaterdreine net vir drinkwater gebruik word","en":"Because stormwater drains are used only for drinking water"},{"af":"Omdat olie die reën sal keer om te val","en":"Because oil will stop the rain from falling"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Water in stormwaterdreine word nie skoongemaak nie. Wat jy daarin gooi, beland in riviere en die see en besoedel die water vir mense, visse en plante.","en":"Water in stormwater drains is not cleaned. What you pour into them ends up in rivers and the sea and pollutes the water for people, fish and plants."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die Grondwet sê elke mens het die reg op toegang tot genoeg water.","en":"The Constitution says every person has the right to have access to enough water."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Omdat water ’n basiese behoefte is, is toegang tot genoeg water ’n reg. Ons het ook die verantwoordelikheid om water op te pas.","en":"True. Because water is a basic need, access to enough water is a right. We also have the responsibility to look after water."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"’n Bad gebruik omtrent 80 liter water en ’n kort stort omtrent 50 liter. Hoeveel water spaar Fatima in 5 dae as sy elke dag stort in plaas van bad?","en":"A bath uses about 80 litres of water and a short shower about 50 litres. How much water does Fatima save in 5 days if she showers every day instead of bathing?"},"options":[{"af":"30 liter","en":"30 litres"},{"af":"250 liter","en":"250 litres"},{"af":"400 liter","en":"400 litres"},{"af":"150 liter","en":"150 litres"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Sy spaar 80 − 50 = 30 liter per dag. In 5 dae is dit 30 × 5 = 150 liter. 30 liter is net een dag se besparing, en 250 liter is wat die storte self gebruik.","en":"She saves 80 − 50 = 30 litres per day. In 5 days that is 30 × 5 = 150 litres. 30 litres is only one day’s saving, and 250 litres is what the showers themselves use."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Lang tyd sonder genoeg reën heet ’n ___.","en":"A long time without enough rain is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["droogte"],"en":["drought"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vloed","storm","oes"],"en":["flood","storm","harvest"]}},"explain":{"af":"Tydens ’n droogte raak damme leeg en sterf plante en diere. Omdat droogtes in Suid-Afrika gereeld voorkom, moet ons altyd water spaar.","en":"During a drought dams run low and plants and animals die. Because droughts happen often in South Africa, we must always save water."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarvoor kan jy grys water veilig gebruik?","en":"What can you safely use grey water for?"},"options":[{"af":"Om koffie of tee mee te maak","en":"To make coffee or tea with"},{"af":"Om die tuin nat te maak","en":"To water the garden"},{"af":"Om groente in te kook","en":"To cook vegetables in"},{"af":"Om vir die baba se bottel te gebruik","en":"To use for the baby’s bottle"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Grys water het seep en vuilgoed in en is nie veilig om te drink of mee te kook nie. Dit is wel goed genoeg vir die tuin of om die toilet te spoel.","en":"Grey water contains soap and dirt and is not safe for drinking or cooking. It is good enough for the garden or for flushing the toilet."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jou skool wil minder water gebruik. Watter plan sal die meeste help?","en":"Your school wants to use less water. Which plan will help the most?"},"options":[{"af":"Spuit die speelgrond elke middag met ’n tuinslang af","en":"Hose down the playground every afternoon"},{"af":"Plant net grasperke wat elke dag water nodig het","en":"Plant only lawns that need water every day"},{"af":"Herstel lekkende krane en vang reënwater vir die tuin op","en":"Fix leaking taps and catch rainwater for the garden"},{"af":"Laat die krane oop sodat die pype skoon bly","en":"Leave the taps open so that the pipes stay clean"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Lekke herstel keer dat water dag en nag gemors word, en opgevangde reënwater vervang kraanwater in die tuin. Die ander planne mors water.","en":"Fixing leaks stops water being wasted day and night, and caught rainwater replaces tap water in the garden. The other plans waste water."}}]},{"id":"lv5-t3-gesonde-eetgewoontes","title":{"af":"Gesonde eetgewoontes vir kinders","en":"Healthy eating for children"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die voedselgroepe kan noem, kan verduidelik waarom ontbyt en water belangrik is, kan sê wat ons voedselkeuses beïnvloed en ’n gesonde kosblik kan beplan.","en":"You will be able to name the food groups, explain why breakfast and water are important, say what influences our food choices and plan a healthy lunchbox."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat jou liggaam nodig het\n\nJy groei elke dag, en jy speel, leer en dink baie. Daarom het jou liggaam **goeie kos** nodig wat:\n\n- vir jou **energie** gee om te speel en te konsentreer;\n- jou help om te **groei** en sterk spiere te bou;\n- jou **bene en tande** sterk maak;\n- jou help om **siektes te beveg**.\n\nGeen enkele kos gee jou alles nie. Daarom eet jy ’n **verskeidenheid** kos uit al die voedselgroepe. Dit noem ons ’n **gebalanseerde dieet**. *Dieet* beteken hier net al die kos wat jy gewoonlik eet.\n\n## Die voedselgroepe\n\n| Voedselgroep | Voorbeelde | Wat dit vir jou doen |\n|---|---|---|\n| Styselkos | mieliepap, bruinbrood, rys, aartappels, hawermout | Gee energie |\n| Groente en vrugte | spinasie, wortels, pampoen, appels, piesangs | Gee vitamiene en minerale wat jou gesond hou |\n| Proteïen | bone, lensies, eiers, hoender, vis, vleis, grondboontjiebotter | Help jou om te groei en spiere te bou |\n| Suiwel | melk, maas, jogurt, kaas | Gee kalsium vir sterk bene en tande |\n| Vette en olies | olie, botter, margarien | ’n Bietjie is nodig, maar **gebruik min** |\n\nDrink ook elke dag genoeg skoon **water** – dit is die beste drankie as jy dors is. Eet **baie groente en vrugte** in verskillende kleure, want elke kleur bring ander goeie stowwe.\n\n## Begin die dag met ontbyt\n\nNá ’n hele nag sonder kos het jou liggaam en brein **brandstof** nodig. Kinders wat ontbyt eet, kan beter **konsentreer** en het meer energie in die klas. Ontbyt hoef nie duur te wees nie: mieliepap of hawermout met melk, bruinbrood met grondboontjiebotter, of ’n gekookte eier en ’n piesang.\n\n> **Onthou:** Ontbyt is soos brandstof vir ’n motor – sonder dit sukkel jou brein om deur die oggend te kom.\n\n## Gemorskos en suiker\n\n**Gemorskos**, soos skyfies, lekkers, koeldrank en baie gebraaide kitskos, bevat baie **suiker, sout of vet**, maar min van die goeie stowwe wat jou liggaam nodig het om te groei. Dit maak jou gou vol, maar die energie hou nie lank nie.\n\n- Te veel suiker veroorsaak **gaatjies** in jou tande.\n- Koeldrank bevat baie suiker; **water** of melk is ’n beter keuse.\n- Gemorskos is ’n **soms-kos**, nie ’n elke-dag-kos nie. Jy hoef nie skuldig te voel as jy op ’n partytjie koek eet nie.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om te dink vrugtesap of ’n energiedrankie is net so goed soos water. Baie sappe en drankies bevat baie suiker, en energiedrankies is nie vir kinders bedoel nie.\n\n## Wat beïnvloed wat ons eet?\n\n| Faktor | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|\n| Kultuur en geloof | Gesinne eet tradisionele geregte; party gelowe het kosreëls |\n| Geld | Gesinne koop wat hulle kan bekostig; bone en eiers is goedkoper proteïen |\n| Advertensies | Helder verpakking en spotprentkarakters laat lekkers aantreklik lyk |\n| Maats | Jy wil dalk eet wat jou maats eet |\n| Beskikbaarheid | Wat in die winkel naby is of in die tuin groei |\n| Gewoonte | Wat jou gesin nog altyd eet |\n\nAs jy weet wat jou keuses beïnvloed, kan jy self **slim kies**. Vra by ’n advertensie: *Wat probeer hulle my laat koop, en is dit regtig goed vir my?*\n\n## Beplan ’n gesonde kosblik\n\n’n Goeie kosblik het iets uit verskillende groepe:\n\n1. **Styselkos** – bruinbrood, ’n toebroodjie of oorskietrys\n2. **Proteïen** – ’n eier, grondboontjiebotter, hoender of bone\n3. **Groente of vrugte** – ’n appel, piesang, wortelstokkies of tamatie\n4. **Suiwel** – jogurt, kaas of maas\n5. **Water** in ’n bottel\n\nWas jou hande voor jy eet, en was vrugte en groente eers. Eet stadig, geniet jou kos en luister na jou liggaam: eet as jy honger is en hou op as jy vol is.","en":"## What your body needs\n\nYou grow every day, and you play, learn and think a lot. That is why your body needs **good food** that:\n\n- gives you **energy** to play and concentrate;\n- helps you to **grow** and build strong muscles;\n- makes your **bones and teeth** strong;\n- helps you **fight illness**.\n\nNo single food gives you everything. That is why you eat a **variety** of food from all the food groups. We call this a **balanced diet**. Here *diet* simply means all the food you usually eat.\n\n## The food groups\n\n| Food group | Examples | What it does for you |\n|---|---|---|\n| Starchy food | maize porridge, brown bread, rice, potatoes, oats | Gives energy |\n| Vegetables and fruit | spinach, carrots, pumpkin, apples, bananas | Gives vitamins and minerals that keep you healthy |\n| Protein | beans, lentils, eggs, chicken, fish, meat, peanut butter | Helps you grow and build muscles |\n| Dairy | milk, maas, yoghurt, cheese | Gives calcium for strong bones and teeth |\n| Fats and oils | oil, butter, margarine | A little is needed, but **use little** |\n\nAlso drink enough clean **water** every day – it is the best drink when you are thirsty. Eat **plenty of vegetables and fruit** in different colours, because each colour brings different good substances.\n\n## Start the day with breakfast\n\nAfter a whole night without food, your body and brain need **fuel**. Children who eat breakfast can **concentrate** better and have more energy in class. Breakfast does not have to be expensive: maize porridge or oats with milk, brown bread with peanut butter, or a boiled egg and a banana.\n\n> **Remember:** Breakfast is like fuel for a car – without it your brain struggles to get through the morning.\n\n## Junk food and sugar\n\n**Junk food**, such as chips, sweets, fizzy drinks and a lot of fried fast food, contains a lot of **sugar, salt or fat**, but little of the good substances your body needs to grow. It fills you up quickly, but the energy does not last long.\n\n- Too much sugar causes **cavities** (holes) in your teeth.\n- Fizzy drinks contain a lot of sugar; **water** or milk is a better choice.\n- Junk food is a **sometimes food**, not an every-day food. You do not have to feel guilty for eating cake at a party.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Thinking that fruit juice or an energy drink is just as good as water. Many juices and drinks contain a lot of sugar, and energy drinks are not meant for children.\n\n## What influences what we eat?\n\n| Factor | Example |\n|---|---|\n| Culture and religion | Families eat traditional dishes; some religions have food rules |\n| Money | Families buy what they can afford; beans and eggs are cheaper protein |\n| Advertisements | Bright packaging and cartoon characters make sweets look attractive |\n| Friends | You may want to eat what your friends eat |\n| Availability | What is in the shop nearby or grows in the garden |\n| Habit | What your family has always eaten |\n\nWhen you know what influences your choices, you can **choose wisely** yourself. Ask when you see an advert: *What are they trying to make me buy, and is it really good for me?*\n\n## Plan a healthy lunchbox\n\nA good lunchbox has something from different groups:\n\n1. **Starchy food** – brown bread, a sandwich or leftover rice\n2. **Protein** – an egg, peanut butter, chicken or beans\n3. **Vegetables or fruit** – an apple, banana, carrot sticks or a tomato\n4. **Dairy** – yoghurt, cheese or maas\n5. **Water** in a bottle\n\nWash your hands before you eat, and wash fruit and vegetables first. Eat slowly, enjoy your food and listen to your body: eat when you are hungry and stop when you are full."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Gebalanseerde dieet","en":"Balanced diet"},"def":{"af":"Om elke dag ’n verskeidenheid kos uit al die voedselgroepe te eet, sodat jou liggaam alles kry wat dit nodig het.","en":"Eating a variety of food from all the food groups every day, so that your body gets everything it needs."}},{"term":{"af":"Voedselgroep","en":"Food group"},"def":{"af":"’n Groep kosse wat dieselfde soort goeie stowwe aan jou liggaam gee, soos styselkos of suiwel.","en":"A group of foods that give your body the same kind of good substances, such as starchy food or dairy."}},{"term":{"af":"Styselkos","en":"Starchy food"},"def":{"af":"Kos soos pap, brood, rys en aartappels wat jou liggaam energie gee.","en":"Food such as porridge, bread, rice and potatoes that gives your body energy."}},{"term":{"af":"Proteïen","en":"Protein"},"def":{"af":"’n Voedingstof in kos soos bone, eiers, vis en vleis wat jou help om te groei en spiere te bou.","en":"A nutrient in food such as beans, eggs, fish and meat that helps you grow and build muscles."}},{"term":{"af":"Suiwel","en":"Dairy"},"def":{"af":"Melk en kos wat van melk gemaak word, soos maas, jogurt en kaas.","en":"Milk and food made from milk, such as maas, yoghurt and cheese."}},{"term":{"af":"Kalsium","en":"Calcium"},"def":{"af":"’n Mineraal in suiwel wat jou bene en tande sterk maak.","en":"A mineral in dairy that makes your bones and teeth strong."}},{"term":{"af":"Vitamiene en minerale","en":"Vitamins and minerals"},"def":{"af":"Klein hoeveelhede goeie stowwe, veral in groente en vrugte, wat jou liggaam gesond hou en help om siektes te beveg.","en":"Small amounts of good substances, especially in vegetables and fruit, that keep your body healthy and help it fight illness."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemorskos","en":"Junk food"},"def":{"af":"Kos met baie suiker, sout of vet maar min goeie stowwe, soos skyfies, lekkers en koeldrank.","en":"Food with a lot of sugar, salt or fat but few good substances, such as chips, sweets and fizzy drinks."}},{"term":{"af":"Advertensie","en":"Advertisement"},"def":{"af":"’n Boodskap op TV, die internet of ’n verpakking wat jou probeer oorhaal om iets te koop.","en":"A message on TV, the internet or packaging that tries to persuade you to buy something."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Verbeter ’n kosblik","en":"Improve a lunchbox"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo se kosblik bevat ’n pakkie skyfies, ’n stafie sjokolade en ’n blikkie koeldrank. Watter voedselgroepe ontbreek, en hoe kan hy sy kosblik verbeter?","en":"Thabo’s lunchbox contains a packet of chips, a chocolate bar and a can of fizzy drink. Which food groups are missing, and how can he improve his lunchbox?"},"steps":[{"af":"Kyk na elke item: skyfies, sjokolade en koeldrank is almal **gemorskos** met baie suiker, sout of vet.","en":"Look at each item: chips, chocolate and fizzy drink are all **junk food** with a lot of sugar, salt or fat."},{"af":"Kontroleer die groepe: daar is geen gesonde styselkos, proteïen, groente of vrugte, of suiwel nie – en geen water nie.","en":"Check the groups: there is no healthy starchy food, protein, vegetables or fruit, or dairy – and no water."},{"af":"Vervang: ’n bruinbroodtoebroodjie met eier (stysel en proteïen), ’n piesang (vrugte), ’n jogurt (suiwel) en ’n bottel water.","en":"Replace: a brown bread sandwich with egg (starch and protein), a banana (fruit), a yoghurt (dairy) and a bottle of water."}],"answer":{"af":"Styselkos, proteïen, groente/vrugte en suiwel ontbreek. ’n Beter kosblik: eiertoebroodjie op bruinbrood, ’n piesang, jogurt en water.","en":"Starchy food, protein, vegetables/fruit and dairy are missing. A better lunchbox: egg sandwich on brown bread, a banana, yoghurt and water."}},{"title":{"af":"Sorteer kos in groepe","en":"Sort food into groups"},"problem":{"af":"Sorteer hierdie kosse in hul voedselgroepe: maas, lensies, pampoen, mieliepap, botter.","en":"Sort these foods into their food groups: maas, lentils, pumpkin, maize porridge, butter."},"steps":[{"af":"**Maas** word van melk gemaak – dit is **suiwel**.","en":"**Maas** is made from milk – it is **dairy**."},{"af":"**Lensies** is ’n peulgewas soos bone – dit is **proteïen**.","en":"**Lentils** are a legume like beans – they are **protein**."},{"af":"**Pampoen** is ’n groente – **groente en vrugte**. **Mieliepap** is **styselkos**.","en":"**Pumpkin** is a vegetable – **vegetables and fruit**. **Maize porridge** is **starchy food**."},{"af":"**Botter** is ’n vet – **vette en olies**, dus gebruik min.","en":"**Butter** is a fat – **fats and oils**, so use little."}],"answer":{"af":"Maas – suiwel; lensies – proteïen; pampoen – groente en vrugte; mieliepap – styselkos; botter – vette en olies.","en":"Maas – dairy; lentils – protein; pumpkin – vegetables and fruit; maize porridge – starchy food; butter – fats and oils."}},{"title":{"af":"Ontleed ’n advertensie","en":"Analyse an advertisement"},"problem":{"af":"’n Advertensie wys ’n spotprentleeu wat ’n soet ontbytgraan eet en sê: ‘Vol energie vir die hele dag!’ Lerato wil dadelik die graan hê. Hoe probeer die advertensie haar beïnvloed, en wat moet sy oorweeg?","en":"An advert shows a cartoon lion eating a sweet breakfast cereal and saying: ‘Full of energy for the whole day!’ Lerato immediately wants the cereal. How is the advert trying to influence her, and what should she think about?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die **spotprentkarakter** en helder kleure is spesiaal gekies om kinders se aandag te trek.","en":"The **cartoon character** and bright colours were chosen specially to catch children’s attention."},{"af":"Die slagspreuk belowe energie, maar baie soet graan bevat veel suiker – die energie hou nie lank nie.","en":"The slogan promises energy, but a lot of sweet cereal contains much sugar – the energy does not last long."},{"af":"Lerato kan vra: *Is dit regtig goed vir my?* Hawermout of pap met melk gee energie wat langer hou.","en":"Lerato can ask: *Is it really good for me?* Oats or porridge with milk give energy that lasts longer."}],"answer":{"af":"Die advertensie gebruik ’n spotprentkarakter, helder kleure en ’n belofte van energie. Lerato moet nadink oor die suiker en eerder ’n gesonder ontbyt kies.","en":"The advert uses a cartoon character, bright colours and a promise of energy. Lerato should think about the sugar and rather choose a healthier breakfast."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voedselgroep gee jou hoofsaaklik energie?","en":"Which food group mainly gives you energy?"},"options":[{"af":"Styselkos, soos pap en brood","en":"Starchy food, such as porridge and bread"},{"af":"Suiwel, soos melk en kaas","en":"Dairy, such as milk and cheese"},{"af":"Vette, soos botter en olie","en":"Fats, such as butter and oil"},{"af":"Water, soos kraanwater","en":"Water, such as tap water"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Styselkos soos pap, brood, rys en aartappels is jou liggaam se hoofbron van energie. Suiwel gee veral kalsium, en vette moet jy min gebruik.","en":"Starchy food such as porridge, bread, rice and potatoes is your body’s main source of energy. Dairy gives mostly calcium, and you should use little fat."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Kinders wat ontbyt eet, kan gewoonlik beter in die klas konsentreer.","en":"Children who eat breakfast can usually concentrate better in class."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Ná ’n nag sonder kos het jou brein brandstof nodig. Ontbyt gee jou energie om te konsentreer en te leer.","en":"True. After a night without food your brain needs fuel. Breakfast gives you energy to concentrate and learn."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter kos help die meeste om jou bene en tande sterk te maak?","en":"Which food helps most to make your bones and teeth strong?"},"options":[{"af":"Skyfies","en":"Chips"},{"af":"Rys","en":"Rice"},{"af":"Maas","en":"Maas"},{"af":"Koeldrank","en":"Fizzy drink"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Maas is ’n suiwelproduk vol kalsium, wat bene en tande sterk maak. Rys gee energie, en skyfies en koeldrank is gemorskos.","en":"Maas is a dairy product full of calcium, which makes bones and teeth strong. Rice gives energy, and chips and fizzy drinks are junk food."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"’n Gebalanseerde dieet bevat kos uit al die ___.","en":"A balanced diet contains food from all the ___."},"answers":{"af":["voedselgroepe","kosgroepe"],"en":["food groups","foodgroups"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["winkels","advertensies","kitskosplekke"],"en":["shops","adverts","fast-food places"]}},"explain":{"af":"Geen enkele kos gee jou alles nie. Deur uit al die voedselgroepe te eet, kry jou liggaam energie, proteïen, kalsium, vitamiene en minerale.","en":"No single food gives you everything. By eating from all the food groups, your body gets energy, protein, calcium, vitamins and minerals."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy het pas sokker gespeel en is baie dors. Wat is die beste drankie?","en":"You have just played soccer and are very thirsty. What is the best drink?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Energiedrankie","en":"An energy drink"},{"af":"Skoon water","en":"Clean water"},{"af":"’n Groot koeldrank","en":"A big fizzy drink"},{"af":"’n Soet vrugtesap","en":"A sweet fruit juice"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Water les jou dors sonder ekstra suiker. Koeldrank en baie sappe bevat baie suiker, en energiedrankies is nie vir kinders bedoel nie.","en":"Water quenches your thirst without extra sugar. Fizzy drinks and many juices contain a lot of sugar, and energy drinks are not meant for children."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke kos by sy voedselgroep.","en":"Match each food to its food group."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Lensies","en":"Lentils"},"r":{"af":"Proteïen","en":"Protein"}},{"l":{"af":"Jogurt","en":"Yoghurt"},"r":{"af":"Suiwel","en":"Dairy"}},{"l":{"af":"Spinasie","en":"Spinach"},"r":{"af":"Groente en vrugte","en":"Vegetables and fruit"}},{"l":{"af":"Mieliepap","en":"Maize porridge"},"r":{"af":"Styselkos","en":"Starchy food"}},{"l":{"af":"Margarien","en":"Margarine"},"r":{"af":"Vette en olies","en":"Fats and oils"}}],"explain":{"af":"Lensies is ’n peulgewas vol proteïen, jogurt word van melk gemaak, spinasie is ’n groente, mieliepap is styselkos en margarien is ’n vet.","en":"Lentils are a legume full of protein, yoghurt is made from milk, spinach is a vegetable, maize porridge is starchy food and margarine is a fat."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho wil ’n sekere ontbytgraan hê omdat sy gunsteling-spotprentkarakter op die boks is. Watter faktor beïnvloed sy keuse?","en":"Sipho wants a certain breakfast cereal because his favourite cartoon character is on the box. Which factor influences his choice?"},"options":[{"af":"Kultuur","en":"Culture"},{"af":"Beskikbaarheid","en":"Availability"},{"af":"Gewoonte","en":"Habit"},{"af":"Advertensies","en":"Advertisements"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Spotprentkarakters en helder verpakking is ’n vorm van advertering wat spesiaal kinders teiken. Dit sê niks oor hoe gesond die kos is nie.","en":"Cartoon characters and bright packaging are a form of advertising aimed especially at children. They say nothing about how healthy the food is."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Te veel suiker kan ___ in jou tande veroorsaak.","en":"Too much sugar can cause ___ in your teeth."},"answers":{"af":["gaatjies","gate"],"en":["cavities","holes"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kalsium","vitamiene","spiere"],"en":["calcium","vitamins","muscles"]}},"explain":{"af":"Kieme in jou mond leef van suiker en maak ’n suur wat gaatjies in jou tande maak. Kalsium help juis om tande sterk te hou.","en":"Germs in your mouth feed on sugar and make an acid that causes cavities in your teeth. Calcium actually helps to keep teeth strong."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter kosblik is die beste gebalanseer?","en":"Which lunchbox is the best balanced?"},"options":[{"af":"Twee pakkies skyfies en ’n koeldrank","en":"Two packets of chips and a fizzy drink"},{"af":"Drie snye witbrood met konfyt","en":"Three slices of white bread with jam"},{"af":"’n Appel, ’n piesang en ’n lemoen","en":"An apple, a banana and an orange"},{"af":"’n Eiertoebroodjie, wortelstokkies, jogurt en water","en":"An egg sandwich, carrot sticks, yoghurt and water"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die eiertoebroodjie gee stysel en proteïen, die wortels is groente, die jogurt is suiwel en water is die beste drankie. Die vrugte-kosblik is gesond, maar het net een voedselgroep.","en":"The egg sandwich gives starch and protein, the carrots are vegetables, the yoghurt is dairy and water is the best drink. The fruit lunchbox is healthy, but has only one food group."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Gemorskos gee jou liggaam baie van die goeie stowwe wat dit nodig het om te groei.","en":"Junk food gives your body many of the good substances it needs to grow."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Gemorskos bevat baie suiker, sout of vet, maar min proteïen, vitamiene en minerale. Dit is ’n soms-kos, nie ’n elke-dag-kos nie.","en":"False. Junk food contains a lot of sugar, salt or fat, but little protein, vitamins and minerals. It is a sometimes food, not an every-day food."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is dit goed om groente en vrugte in verskillende kleure te eet?","en":"Why is it good to eat vegetables and fruit in different colours?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat dit die bord mooier laat lyk, maar dit maak nie saak nie","en":"Because it makes the plate look nicer, but it does not matter"},{"af":"Omdat elke kleur ander vitamiene en minerale bring","en":"Because each colour brings different vitamins and minerals"},{"af":"Omdat net groen groente enigsins goed vir jou is","en":"Because only green vegetables are good for you at all"},{"af":"Omdat gekleurde kos meer energie as styselkos gee","en":"Because coloured food gives more energy than starchy food"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Verskillende groente en vrugte bevat verskillende goeie stowwe. As jy ’n verskeidenheid kleure eet, kry jou liggaam ’n groter verskeidenheid vitamiene en minerale.","en":"Different vegetables and fruit contain different good substances. If you eat a variety of colours, your body gets a bigger variety of vitamins and minerals."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Bone, eiers en vis is goeie bronne van ___.","en":"Beans, eggs and fish are good sources of ___."},"answers":{"af":["proteïen","proteien"],"en":["protein"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["stysel","suiker","vet"],"en":["starch","sugar","fat"]}},"explain":{"af":"Proteïen help jou om te groei en spiere te bou. Bone en eiers is ook ’n goedkoper bron van proteïen as vleis.","en":"Protein helps you grow and build muscles. Beans and eggs are also a cheaper source of protein than meat."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato se maats koop elke dag skyfies by die snoepie, en sy voel sy moet ook. Watter faktor beïnvloed haar?","en":"Lerato’s friends buy chips at the tuck shop every day, and she feels she must too. Which factor is influencing her?"},"options":[{"af":"Maats","en":"Friends"},{"af":"Geloof","en":"Religion"},{"af":"Beskikbaarheid","en":"Availability"},{"af":"Kultuur","en":"Culture"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Sy wil eet wat haar maats eet – dit is die invloed van maats. Sy kan self kies en dalk ’n vrug of ’n toebroodjie saambring.","en":"She wants to eat what her friends eat – that is the influence of friends. She can make her own choice and perhaps bring a fruit or a sandwich."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ravi sê: ‘Ek eet nie ontbyt nie, want ek eet pouse lekkers en dit gee ook energie.’ Wat is die beste antwoord?","en":"Ravi says: ‘I don’t eat breakfast, because I eat sweets at break and they give energy too.’ What is the best reply?"},"options":[{"af":"‘Reg so, lekkers en ontbyt is presies dieselfde.’","en":"‘That’s fine, sweets and breakfast are exactly the same.’"},{"af":"‘Eet net ’n groter koeldrank, dan sal jy reg wees.’","en":"‘Just drink a bigger fizzy drink, then you will be fine.’"},{"af":"‘Lekkers se energie hou nie lank nie; ’n ontbyt soos pap met melk help jou die hele oggend konsentreer.’","en":"‘The energy from sweets doesn’t last long; a breakfast like porridge with milk helps you concentrate all morning.’"},{"af":"‘Moet glad nie eet voor ná skool nie, dan is jy meer wakker.’","en":"‘Don’t eat at all until after school, then you’ll be more awake.’"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Suiker gee net vinnige energie wat gou opraak, en dit gee min goeie stowwe. Ontbyt van styselkos en suiwel gee brandstof wat die hele oggend hou.","en":"Sugar gives only quick energy that runs out fast, and it gives few good substances. A breakfast of starchy food and dairy gives fuel that lasts all morning."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Gesondheid en welstand","en":"Health and well-being"},"topics":[{"id":"lv5-t4-plaaslike-siektes","title":{"af":"Plaaslike gesondheidsprobleme","en":"Local health problems"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die oorsaak, simptome, voorkoming en behandeling van TB, diarree, malaria en masels kan beskryf en weet wanneer om kliniek toe te gaan.","en":"You will be able to describe the cause, symptoms, prevention and treatment of TB, diarrhoea, malaria and measles, and know when to go to the clinic."},"summary":{"af":"## Kieme en siektes in ons gemeenskap\n\nSommige siektes kom baie in Suid-Afrika voor. Hulle word deur **kieme** veroorsaak: **bakterieë**, **virusse** of **parasiete** wat te klein is om te sien. Die goeie nuus is dat ’n mens hierdie siektes kan **voorkom** en **behandel**. Toetse en behandeling by staatsklinieke is gratis.\n\n## Tuberkulose (TB)\n\n- **Oorsaak:** ’n **bakterie** wat meestal die **longe** aantas. Dit versprei deur die **lug** wanneer iemand met TB hoes of nies.\n- **Simptome:** ’n **hoes wat langer as twee weke** duur, koors, nagsweet, moegheid en ’n swak eetlus.\n- **Voorkoming:** babas kry die **BCG-inenting** by geboorte. Hou vensters oop vir vars lug en bedek jou mond as jy hoes.\n- **Behandeling:** TB is **geneesbaar**. Die pille moet elke dag geneem word vir die **volle kursus** (gewoonlik ses maande), al voel jy gou beter.\n\n## Diarree\n\n- **Oorsaak:** kieme in **vuil water**, op **vuil hande** of in kos wat nie skoon gehou is nie.\n- **Simptome:** los, waterige stoelgang drie keer of meer per dag, soms met maagkrampe.\n- **Gevaar:** die liggaam verloor water en soute. Dit heet **ontwatering**. Tekens: dors, ’n droë mond, min urine, moegheid en ingesonke oë.\n- **Behandeling:** drink baie, veral **ORS** (orale rehidrasie-oplossing) uit ’n pakkie van die kliniek. ’n Volwassene kan ook ’n **suiker-soutoplossing** maak: 1 liter gekookte, afgekoelde water, 8 afgestrykte teelepels suiker en ’n halwe gelyk teelepel sout.\n- **Voorkoming:** **was hande met seep** ná die toilet en voor jy eet, drink veilige water en hou kos toegemaak.\n\n## Malaria\n\n- **Oorsaak:** ’n klein **parasiet** wat deur die byt van ’n besmette **muskiet** oorgedra word. Hierdie muskiete byt veral **snags**.\n- **Waar:** in warm, laagliggende dele van **Limpopo, Mpumalanga en die noorde van KwaZulu-Natal**, en in buurlande soos Mosambiek.\n- **Simptome:** soos griep – hoë **koors**, koue rillings, hoofpyn, sweet en lyfseer. Malaria kan baie vinnig ernstig word.\n- **Voorkoming:** slaap onder ’n **muskietnet**, gebruik insekweerder, dra saans lang moue en sit gaas voor vensters.\n- **Behandeling:** gaan **dadelik** kliniek toe vir ’n bloedtoets en malariamedisyne.\n\n## Masels\n\n- **Oorsaak:** ’n **virus** wat baie **aansteeklik** is en deur die lug versprei wanneer iemand hoes of nies.\n- **Simptome:** hoë koors, loopneus, hoes en rooi, waterige oë. ’n Paar dae later kom ’n rooi **uitslag** wat by die gesig begin en oor die lyf versprei.\n- **Gevaar:** masels kan longontsteking en oor- en oogprobleme veroorsaak, veral by babas.\n- **Voorkoming:** **inenting** by die kliniek is die beste beskerming.\n- **Behandeling:** antibiotika werk nie teen virusse nie. Die siek kind moet rus, baie drink, kliniek toe gaan en tuis bly sodat ander nie siek word nie.\n\n| Siekte | Oorsaak | Belangrikste voorkoming |\n|---|---|---|\n| TB | Bakterie | BCG-inenting, vars lug, bedek jou hoes |\n| Diarree | Kieme in water, op hande of kos | Was hande, veilige water |\n| Malaria | Parasiet deur ’n muskiet | Muskietnet, insekweerder |\n| Masels | Virus | Inenting |\n\n> **Onthou:** Gaan kliniek toe as iemand langer as twee weke hoes, koors kry ná ’n besoek aan ’n malaria-gebied, tekens van ontwatering het of koors met ’n uitslag kry. Vertel altyd ’n volwassene as jy siek voel.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om op te hou om TB-pille te neem sodra jy beter voel. Nie al die kieme is dan dood nie. Die TB kan terugkom en moeiliker word om te behandel.","en":"## Germs and illnesses in our community\n\nSome illnesses are common in South Africa. They are caused by **germs**: **bacteria**, **viruses** or **parasites** that are too small to see. The good news is that these illnesses can be **prevented** and **treated**. Tests and treatment at government clinics are free.\n\n## Tuberculosis (TB)\n\n- **Cause:** a **bacterium** that mostly affects the **lungs**. It spreads through the **air** when someone with TB coughs or sneezes.\n- **Symptoms:** a **cough lasting longer than two weeks**, fever, night sweats, tiredness and a poor appetite.\n- **Prevention:** babies get the **BCG vaccination** at birth. Keep windows open for fresh air and cover your mouth when you cough.\n- **Treatment:** TB is **curable**. The pills must be taken every day for the **full course** (usually six months), even if you soon feel better.\n\n## Diarrhoea\n\n- **Cause:** germs in **dirty water**, on **dirty hands** or in food that has not been kept clean.\n- **Symptoms:** loose, watery stools three or more times a day, sometimes with stomach cramps.\n- **Danger:** the body loses water and salts. This is called **dehydration**. Signs: thirst, a dry mouth, little urine, tiredness and sunken eyes.\n- **Treatment:** drink a lot, especially **ORS** (oral rehydration solution) from a sachet from the clinic. An adult can also make a **sugar-salt solution**: 1 litre of boiled, cooled water, 8 level teaspoons of sugar and half a level teaspoon of salt.\n- **Prevention:** **wash hands with soap** after the toilet and before you eat, drink safe water and keep food covered.\n\n## Malaria\n\n- **Cause:** a tiny **parasite** passed on by the bite of an infected **mosquito**. These mosquitoes bite mainly **at night**.\n- **Where:** in warm, low-lying parts of **Limpopo, Mpumalanga and northern KwaZulu-Natal**, and in neighbouring countries such as Mozambique.\n- **Symptoms:** like flu – high **fever**, shivering, headache, sweating and body aches. Malaria can become very serious very quickly.\n- **Prevention:** sleep under a **mosquito net**, use insect repellent, wear long sleeves in the evening and put gauze in front of windows.\n- **Treatment:** go to the clinic **immediately** for a blood test and malaria medicine.\n\n## Measles\n\n- **Cause:** a **virus** that is very **contagious** and spreads through the air when someone coughs or sneezes.\n- **Symptoms:** high fever, runny nose, cough and red, watery eyes. A few days later a red **rash** appears that starts on the face and spreads over the body.\n- **Danger:** measles can cause pneumonia and ear and eye problems, especially in babies.\n- **Prevention:** **vaccination** at the clinic is the best protection.\n- **Treatment:** antibiotics do not work against viruses. The sick child must rest, drink a lot, go to the clinic and stay at home so that others do not get sick.\n\n| Illness | Cause | Main prevention |\n|---|---|---|\n| TB | Bacterium | BCG vaccination, fresh air, cover your cough |\n| Diarrhoea | Germs in water, on hands or food | Wash hands, safe water |\n| Malaria | Parasite passed on by a mosquito | Mosquito net, insect repellent |\n| Measles | Virus | Vaccination |\n\n> **Remember:** Go to the clinic if someone has coughed for longer than two weeks, gets a fever after visiting a malaria area, shows signs of dehydration or has a fever with a rash. Always tell an adult if you feel sick.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Stopping TB pills as soon as you feel better. Not all the germs are dead yet. The TB can come back and become harder to treat."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Kiem","en":"Germ"},"def":{"af":"’n Baie klein lewende ding, soos ’n bakterie, virus of parasiet, wat siekte kan veroorsaak.","en":"A very small living thing, such as a bacterium, virus or parasite, that can cause illness."}},{"term":{"af":"Bakterie","en":"Bacterium"},"def":{"af":"’n Kiem wat net onder ’n mikroskoop gesien kan word; sommige bakterieë veroorsaak siektes soos TB.","en":"A germ that can only be seen under a microscope; some bacteria cause illnesses such as TB."}},{"term":{"af":"Virus","en":"Virus"},"def":{"af":"’n Baie klein kiem wat siektes soos masels en griep veroorsaak; antibiotika werk nie daarteen nie.","en":"A very tiny germ that causes illnesses such as measles and flu; antibiotics do not work against it."}},{"term":{"af":"Parasiet","en":"Parasite"},"def":{"af":"’n Organisme wat in of op ’n ander lewende ding leef en dit skade aandoen, soos die malariaparasiet.","en":"An organism that lives in or on another living thing and harms it, such as the malaria parasite."}},{"term":{"af":"Aansteeklik","en":"Contagious"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n siekte maklik van een persoon na ’n ander versprei.","en":"When an illness spreads easily from one person to another."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontwatering","en":"Dehydration"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer die liggaam te veel water en soute verloor, byvoorbeeld deur diarree.","en":"When the body loses too much water and salts, for example through diarrhoea."}},{"term":{"af":"ORS (orale rehidrasie-oplossing)","en":"ORS (oral rehydration solution)"},"def":{"af":"’n Drankie met die regte hoeveelheid suiker en sout wat die water en soute vervang wat by diarree verlore gaan.","en":"A drink with the right amount of sugar and salt that replaces the water and salts lost through diarrhoea."}},{"term":{"af":"Inenting","en":"Vaccination"},"def":{"af":"’n Druppel of inspuiting wat jou liggaam leer om ’n sekere siekte te beveg voordat jy dit kry.","en":"Drops or an injection that teach your body to fight a certain illness before you get it."}},{"term":{"af":"Volle kursus","en":"Full course"},"def":{"af":"Om al die medisyne te neem, elke dag, vir so lank as wat die kliniek sê – selfs as jy al beter voel.","en":"Taking all the medicine, every day, for as long as the clinic says – even if you already feel better."}},{"term":{"af":"Muskietnet","en":"Mosquito net"},"def":{"af":"’n Fyn net wat oor ’n bed hang sodat muskiete jou nie snags kan byt nie.","en":"A fine net that hangs over a bed so that mosquitoes cannot bite you at night."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Herken die siekte","en":"Recognise the illness"},"problem":{"af":"Johan se oom hoes al drie weke lank. Hy sweet snags, is altyd moeg en wil nie eet nie. Watter siekte kan hy hê, en wat moet hy doen?","en":"Johan’s uncle has been coughing for three weeks. He sweats at night, is always tired and does not want to eat. Which illness could he have, and what should he do?"},"steps":[{"af":"Kyk na die simptome: ’n hoes langer as twee weke, nagsweet, moegheid en ’n swak eetlus is tipiese tekens van **TB**.","en":"Look at the symptoms: a cough lasting longer than two weeks, night sweats, tiredness and a poor appetite are typical signs of **TB**."},{"af":"Hy moet so gou moontlik kliniek toe gaan vir ’n gratis TB-toets.","en":"He must go to the clinic as soon as possible for a free TB test."},{"af":"As hy TB het, moet hy die pille elke dag vir die volle kursus neem. Intussen bedek hy sy hoes en hou die vensters oop sodat die gesin nie besmet word nie.","en":"If he has TB, he must take the pills every day for the full course. Meanwhile he covers his cough and keeps the windows open so that the family does not get infected."}],"answer":{"af":"Hy kan TB hê. Hy moet dadelik kliniek toe gaan vir ’n toets en, as hy TB het, die volle kursus pille neem.","en":"He could have TB. He must go to the clinic straight away for a test and, if he has TB, take the full course of pills."}},{"title":{"af":"Diarree by ’n klein kind","en":"Diarrhoea in a small child"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato se boetie (4 jaar) het sedert die oggend vyf keer diarree gehad. Sy mond is droog en hy is baie moeg. Wat moet die gesin doen?","en":"Lerato’s little brother (4 years old) has had diarrhoea five times since the morning. His mouth is dry and he is very tired. What should the family do?"},"steps":[{"af":"Herken die gevaar: ’n droë mond en moegheid is tekens van **ontwatering** – sy liggaam verloor te veel water en soute.","en":"Recognise the danger: a dry mouth and tiredness are signs of **dehydration** – his body is losing too much water and salts."},{"af":"Gee hom gereeld klein slukkies **ORS** of ’n suiker-soutoplossing wat ’n volwassene gemaak het (1 liter gekookte, afgekoelde water, 8 afgestrykte teelepels suiker, ½ afgestrykte teelepel sout).","en":"Give him small sips of **ORS** often, or a sugar-salt solution made by an adult (1 litre of boiled, cooled water, 8 level teaspoons of sugar, ½ level teaspoon of salt)."},{"af":"Neem hom **kliniek toe**, want hy het reeds tekens van ontwatering. Klein kinders kan baie vinnig ernstig siek word.","en":"Take him to the **clinic**, because he already shows signs of dehydration. Small children can become seriously ill very quickly."},{"af":"Voorkom verspreiding: almal was hul hande met seep ná die toilet en voor hulle eet.","en":"Prevent spreading: everyone washes their hands with soap after the toilet and before eating."}],"answer":{"af":"Gee hom gereeld ORS of suiker-soutoplossing, neem hom kliniek toe weens die tekens van ontwatering, en laat almal hul hande gereeld met seep was.","en":"Give him ORS or sugar-salt solution often, take him to the clinic because of the signs of dehydration, and have everyone wash their hands with soap often."}},{"title":{"af":"Vakansie in ’n malaria-gebied","en":"Holiday in a malaria area"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter se gesin gaan in die somer met vakansie naby die Krugerwildtuin in Mpumalanga. Hoe kan hulle hulself teen malaria beskerm, en wat as Pieter ná die vakansie koors kry?","en":"Pieter’s family is going on holiday near the Kruger National Park in Mpumalanga in summer. How can they protect themselves against malaria, and what if Pieter gets a fever after the holiday?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die gebied is warm en laagliggend – ’n **malaria-gebied**. Malaria word deur muskiete oorgedra wat veral snags byt.","en":"The area is warm and low-lying – a **malaria area**. Malaria is passed on by mosquitoes that bite mainly at night."},{"af":"Voor die tyd kan die gesin by die kliniek of dokter vra oor malariapille vir die reis.","en":"Beforehand the family can ask at the clinic or doctor about malaria pills for the trip."},{"af":"Daar: slaap onder muskietnette, smeer insekweerder aan en dra saans lang moue en langbroeke.","en":"While there: sleep under mosquito nets, put on insect repellent and wear long sleeves and long trousers in the evening."},{"af":"As Pieter ná die vakansie koors, hoofpyn of koue rillings kry, moet hy **dadelik** kliniek toe gaan en sê waar hy was.","en":"If Pieter gets a fever, headache or shivering after the holiday, he must go to the clinic **immediately** and say where he has been."}],"answer":{"af":"Muskietnette, insekweerder en lang klere saans (en vra oor malariapille). Koors ná die reis beteken dadelik kliniek toe, en vertel waar hy was.","en":"Mosquito nets, insect repellent and long clothes in the evening (and ask about malaria pills). A fever after the trip means going to the clinic immediately and saying where he has been."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat veroorsaak malaria?","en":"What causes malaria?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Virus wat deur hoes versprei","en":"A virus that spreads through coughing"},{"af":"’n Parasiet wat deur ’n muskietbyt oorgedra word","en":"A parasite passed on by a mosquito bite"},{"af":"Kieme in vuil drinkwater","en":"Germs in dirty drinking water"},{"af":"’n Bakterie in die longe","en":"A bacterium in the lungs"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Malaria word deur ’n klein parasiet veroorsaak wat ’n besmette muskiet deur sy byt oordra. Jy kry dit nie deur hoes of vuil water nie – dit is masels en diarree.","en":"Malaria is caused by a tiny parasite that an infected mosquito passes on through its bite. You do not get it from coughing or dirty water – that is measles and diarrhoea."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die grootste gevaar van diarree is ___, wanneer die liggaam te veel water en soute verloor.","en":"The biggest danger of diarrhoea is ___, when the body loses too much water and salts."},"answers":{"af":["ontwatering","uitdroging"],"en":["dehydration"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["koors","uitslag","hoes"],"en":["fever","rash","coughing"]}},"explain":{"af":"Ontwatering kan baie gevaarlik wees, veral vir klein kinders. Daarom drink jy baie, veral ORS, en gaan jy kliniek toe as jy tekens soos ’n droë mond sien.","en":"Dehydration can be very dangerous, especially for small children. That is why you drink a lot, especially ORS, and go to the clinic if you see signs such as a dry mouth."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter simptoom is ’n belangrike waarskuwingsteken van TB?","en":"Which symptom is an important warning sign of TB?"},"options":[{"af":"’n Rooi uitslag wat by die gesig begin","en":"A red rash that starts on the face"},{"af":"Los, waterige stoelgang","en":"Loose, watery stools"},{"af":"’n Jeukerige muskietbyt","en":"An itchy mosquito bite"},{"af":"’n Hoes wat langer as twee weke duur","en":"A cough that lasts longer than two weeks"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"TB tas meestal die longe aan, daarom is ’n hoes langer as twee weke ’n belangrike teken. Die uitslag pas by masels en waterige stoelgang by diarree.","en":"TB mostly affects the lungs, so a cough lasting longer than two weeks is an important sign. The rash goes with measles and watery stools with diarrhoea."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Antibiotika maak die masel-virus dood.","en":"Antibiotics kill the measles virus."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Antibiotika werk teen sommige bakterieë, nie teen virusse nie. Masels word voorkom deur inenting, en ’n siek kind moet rus, baie drink en kliniek toe gaan.","en":"False. Antibiotics work against some bacteria, not against viruses. Measles is prevented by vaccination, and a sick child must rest, drink a lot and go to the clinic."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom moet iemand met TB die pille vir die volle kursus neem, selfs as hy beter voel?","en":"Why must someone with TB take the pills for the full course, even if he feels better?"},"options":[{"af":"Sodat hy nie meer na die kliniek hoef te gaan nie","en":"So that he does not have to go to the clinic anymore"},{"af":"Omdat die pille ook teen malaria beskerm","en":"Because the pills also protect against malaria"},{"af":"Omdat nie al die kieme dood is nie en die TB kan terugkom","en":"Because not all the germs are dead and the TB can come back"},{"af":"Omdat die pille sy longe groter maak","en":"Because the pills make his lungs bigger"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Jy voel beter lank voordat al die TB-kieme dood is. As jy te vroeg ophou, kan die TB terugkom en moeiliker word om te behandel.","en":"You feel better long before all the TB germs are dead. If you stop too early, the TB can come back and become harder to treat."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke siekte by sy oorsaak.","en":"Match each illness to its cause."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"TB","en":"TB"},"r":{"af":"’n Bakterie wat deur die lug versprei","en":"A bacterium that spreads through the air"}},{"l":{"af":"Masels","en":"Measles"},"r":{"af":"’n Baie aansteeklike virus","en":"A very contagious virus"}},{"l":{"af":"Malaria","en":"Malaria"},"r":{"af":"’n Parasiet wat ’n muskiet oordra","en":"A parasite passed on by a mosquito"}},{"l":{"af":"Diarree","en":"Diarrhoea"},"r":{"af":"Kieme in vuil water of op vuil hande","en":"Germs in dirty water or on dirty hands"}}],"explain":{"af":"As jy die oorsaak ken, weet jy hoe om die siekte te voorkom: vars lug vir TB, inenting vir masels, muskietnette vir malaria en handewas en veilige water vir diarree.","en":"If you know the cause, you know how to prevent the illness: fresh air for TB, vaccination for measles, mosquito nets for malaria and handwashing and safe water for diarrhoea."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die beste beskerming teen masels?","en":"What is the best protection against measles?"},"options":[{"af":"Inenting by die kliniek","en":"Vaccination at the clinic"},{"af":"Om onder ’n muskietnet te slaap","en":"Sleeping under a mosquito net"},{"af":"Om net gekookte water te drink","en":"Drinking only boiled water"},{"af":"Om elke dag antibiotika te drink","en":"Taking antibiotics every day"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Inenting leer jou liggaam om die masel-virus te beveg voordat jy siek word. Muskietnette help teen malaria en gekookte water teen diarree, maar nie teen masels nie.","en":"Vaccination teaches your body to fight the measles virus before you get sick. Mosquito nets help against malaria and boiled water against diarrhoea, but not against measles."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In ’n malaria-gebied slaap jy onder ’n ___ sodat muskiete jou nie snags kan byt nie.","en":"In a malaria area you sleep under a ___ so that mosquitoes cannot bite you at night."},"answers":{"af":["muskietnet","muskietnetjie"],"en":["mosquito net","net"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kombers","laken","sambreel"],"en":["blanket","sheet","umbrella"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die muskiete wat malaria oordra, byt veral snags. ’n Muskietnet oor die bed hou hulle weg. ’n Kombers of laken beskerm nie jou gesig en arms nie.","en":"The mosquitoes that carry malaria bite mainly at night. A mosquito net over the bed keeps them away. A blanket or sheet does not protect your face and arms."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die beste eerste behandeling tuis vir iemand met diarree?","en":"What is the best first treatment at home for someone with diarrhoea?"},"options":[{"af":"Laat hom gereeld ORS of ’n suiker-soutoplossing drink","en":"Let him drink ORS or a sugar-salt solution often"},{"af":"Laat hom ophou drink sodat die diarree stop","en":"Let him stop drinking so that the diarrhoea stops"},{"af":"Gee hom net koeldrank vir energie","en":"Give him only fizzy drinks for energy"},{"af":"Gee hom iemand anders se pille","en":"Give him someone else’s pills"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"ORS vervang die water en soute wat verlore gaan en keer ontwatering. Om op te hou drink maak ontwatering erger, en iemand anders se pille kan skade doen.","en":"ORS replaces the water and salts that are lost and prevents dehydration. Stopping drinking makes dehydration worse, and someone else’s pills can cause harm."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Jy kan nie malaria kry deur ’n persoon met malaria te druk nie.","en":"You cannot get malaria by hugging a person who has malaria."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Malaria word net deur die byt van ’n besmette muskiet oorgedra, nie deur aanraking, drukkies of saam eet nie.","en":"True. Malaria is passed on only by the bite of an infected mosquito, not by touching, hugging or eating together."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter dele van Suid-Afrika kom malaria voor?","en":"In which parts of South Africa does malaria occur?"},"options":[{"af":"In die koue berge van die Oos-Kaap","en":"In the cold mountains of the Eastern Cape"},{"af":"In die droë Karoo en die Noord-Kaap","en":"In the dry Karoo and the Northern Cape"},{"af":"In warm, laagliggende dele van Limpopo, Mpumalanga en noordelike KwaZulu-Natal","en":"In warm, low-lying parts of Limpopo, Mpumalanga and northern KwaZulu-Natal"},{"af":"Net in die groot stede soos Kaapstad en Johannesburg","en":"Only in big cities like Cape Town and Johannesburg"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die muskiete wat malaria dra, hou van warm, vogtige, laagliggende gebiede. Daarom kom malaria in die noordooste van die land voor, naby Mosambiek en Zimbabwe.","en":"The mosquitoes that carry malaria like warm, humid, low-lying areas. That is why malaria occurs in the north-east of the country, near Mozambique and Zimbabwe."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Babas kry die BCG-inenting by geboorte om hulle teen ___ te beskerm.","en":"Babies get the BCG vaccination at birth to protect them against ___."},"answers":{"af":["TB","tuberkulose"],"en":["TB","tuberculosis"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["masels","malaria","diarree"],"en":["measles","malaria","diarrhoea"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die BCG-inenting beskerm babas teen TB. Masels het ’n eie inenting, en daar is geen BCG-inenting teen malaria of diarree nie.","en":"The BCG vaccination protects babies against TB. Measles has its own vaccination, and there is no BCG vaccination against malaria or diarrhoea."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wanneer is dit die belangrikste om jou hande met seep te was om diarree te voorkom?","en":"When is it most important to wash your hands with soap to prevent diarrhoea?"},"options":[{"af":"Net wanneer jou hande vuil lyk","en":"Only when your hands look dirty"},{"af":"Net een keer in die oggend","en":"Only once in the morning"},{"af":"Net nadat jy met ’n hond gespeel het","en":"Only after you have played with a dog"},{"af":"Ná die toilet en voor jy eet of kos maak","en":"After the toilet and before you eat or make food"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Kieme wat diarree veroorsaak, kom van die toilet af op jou hande en dan in jou mond of kos. Hande kan skoon lyk en steeds kieme dra.","en":"Germs that cause diarrhoea get from the toilet onto your hands and then into your mouth or food. Hands can look clean and still carry germs."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Tien dae ná ’n vakansie in Mosambiek kry Fatima hoë koors, koue rillings en hoofpyn. Wat moet haar gesin doen?","en":"Ten days after a holiday in Mozambique, Fatima gets a high fever, shivering and a headache. What should her family do?"},"options":[{"af":"Wag ’n week, want dit is seker net griep","en":"Wait a week, because it is probably just flu"},{"af":"Neem haar dadelik kliniek toe en sê waar sy was","en":"Take her to the clinic straight away and say where she has been"},{"af":"Gee haar ORS en laat haar by die skool rus","en":"Give her ORS and let her rest at school"},{"af":"Sit ’n muskietnet oor haar bed, dan sal sy gesond word","en":"Put a mosquito net over her bed, then she will get better"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Koors ná ’n besoek aan ’n malaria-gebied kan malaria wees, en malaria kan vinnig ernstig word. Sy het ’n bloedtoets en medisyne nodig. ’n Muskietnet voorkom malaria, maar genees dit nie.","en":"A fever after visiting a malaria area can be malaria, and malaria can become serious quickly. She needs a blood test and medicine. A mosquito net prevents malaria, but does not cure it."}}]},{"id":"lv5-t4-miv-vigs","title":{"af":"MIV en vigs","en":"HIV and AIDS"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik wat MIV en vigs is, weet hoe jy MIV nie kry nie, universele voorsorgmaatreëls by bloed kan toepas en mense met MIV met empatie en respek behandel.","en":"You will be able to explain what HIV and AIDS are, know how you do not get HIV, apply universal precautions with blood and treat people with HIV with empathy and respect."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is MIV en vigs?\n\nJou liggaam het ’n **immuunstelsel** – soos ’n span soldate wat jou teen kieme beskerm. Spesiale **witbloedselle** veg teen kieme wat jou siek wil maak.\n\n**MIV** (menslike immuniteitsgebrekvirus) is ’n **virus** wat hierdie witbloedselle aanval. Sonder behandeling word die immuunstelsel oor ’n aantal jare al hoe swakker, en dan kry die persoon maklik ander siektes, soos TB of longontsteking. Hierdie latere stadium heet **vigs**.\n\n- **MIV** = die virus.\n- **Vigs** = die siekte wat later kan ontwikkel as MIV nie behandel word nie.\n\nJy kan nie aan iemand sien of hy of sy MIV het nie. Die enigste manier om seker te weet, is ’n **MIV-toets** by die kliniek.\n\n## Lewe met MIV\n\nDaar is nog nie ’n kuur vir MIV nie, maar daar is goeie medisyne: **ARV’s** (antiretrovirale middels). As iemand elke dag sy of haar ARV’s neem, kan die virus nie die immuunstelsel verswak nie. Mense met MIV kan dan ’n **lang, gesonde lewe** lei: skoolgaan, werk, sport doen en ’n gesin hê. ARV’s is gratis by staatsklinieke.\n\n## Hoe MIV oorgedra word – en hoe nie\n\nMIV word net oorgedra wanneer sekere **liggaamsvloeistowwe**, soos **bloed**, van ’n persoon met MIV in ’n ander persoon se liggaam kom. Dit kan gebeur deur bloed-tot-bloed-kontak (soos om naalde of skeerlemmetjies te deel), tydens seksuele kontak, of van ’n ma na haar baba – medisyne kan laasgenoemde grootliks voorkom. As jy vrae hieroor het, praat met ’n ouer of vertroude volwassene.\n\n| Situasie | Kan jy MIV kry? |\n|---|---|\n| Drukkies, hand skud, saam speel en sport doen | Nee |\n| Kos, borde, koppies en potlode deel | Nee |\n| Dieselfde toilet of swembad gebruik | Nee |\n| Hoes, nies, trane of sweet | Nee |\n| Muskietbyte | Nee |\n| Naalde of skeerlemmetjies deel | Ja – deel dit nooit nie |\n\n> **Onthou:** Dit is heeltemal veilig om met ’n maat wat MIV het, te speel, te leer en kos te deel.\n\n## Universele voorsorgmaatreëls\n\nAs iemand bloei, weet jy nie watter kieme in die bloed is nie – nie net MIV nie. Daarom hanteer ons **alle bloed** asof dit kieme kan bevat. Dit noem ons **universele voorsorgmaatreëls**:\n\n1. Moenie bloed met jou kaal hande aanraak nie. Trek **rubberhandskoene** aan of sit **plastieksakke** oor jou hande.\n2. Laat die beseerde persoon, as hy kan, self ’n skoon lap of verband op die wond druk.\n3. Roep ’n volwassene om te help.\n4. Bedek wonde met ’n pleister of verband.\n5. Was ná die tyd jou hande met seep en water, selfs al het jy handskoene gedra.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om net versigtig te wees met mense wat jy *dink* MIV het. Universele voorsorgmaatreëls geld vir **almal se bloed** – ook jou beste maat s’n.\n\n## Stigma, diskriminasie en ondersteuning\n\n**Stigma** is wanneer mense negatiewe, onregverdige idees oor iemand het. **Diskriminasie** is wanneer iemand daarom onregverdig behandel word, byvoorbeeld as kinders weier om met iemand te speel, skinder of name noem. Stigma maak mense eensaam en bang om hulle te laat toets of medisyne te gaan haal.\n\n- ’n Kind met MIV het dieselfde **regte** as enige ander kind, ook die reg om skool toe te gaan.\n- ’n Persoon se **MIV-status** is **privaat**. Niemand hoef dit vir ander te vertel nie, en jy moet nooit iemand se geheim versprei nie.\n- Wys **empatie**: sluit almal in, luister, wees ’n goeie vriend en help kinders wie se familielede siek is.\n- Die **rooi lint** wys ondersteuning vir mense wat met MIV leef. Wêreldvigsdag is op 1 Desember.\n\nAs jy bekommerd is of vrae het, praat met ’n ouer, onderwyser of ander vertroude volwassene, of bel **Childline 116** (gratis).","en":"## What are HIV and AIDS?\n\nYour body has an **immune system** – like a team of soldiers that protects you against germs. Special **white blood cells** fight germs that want to make you sick.\n\n**HIV** (human immunodeficiency virus) is a **virus** that attacks these white blood cells. Without treatment the immune system becomes weaker and weaker over a number of years, and then the person easily gets other illnesses, such as TB or pneumonia. This later stage is called **AIDS**.\n\n- **HIV** = the virus.\n- **AIDS** = the illness that can develop later if HIV is not treated.\n\nYou cannot see by looking at someone whether he or she has HIV. The only way to know for sure is an **HIV test** at the clinic.\n\n## Living with HIV\n\nThere is no cure for HIV yet, but there is good medicine: **ARVs** (antiretroviral medicines). If someone takes his or her ARVs every day, the virus cannot weaken the immune system. People with HIV can then live a **long, healthy life**: go to school, work, play sport and have a family. ARVs are free at government clinics.\n\n## How HIV is passed on – and how not\n\nHIV is passed on only when certain **body fluids**, such as **blood**, from a person with HIV get into another person’s body. This can happen through blood-to-blood contact (such as sharing needles or razor blades), during sexual contact, or from a mother to her baby – medicine can mostly prevent the last one. If you have questions about this, talk to a parent or trusted adult.\n\n| Situation | Can you get HIV? |\n|---|---|\n| Hugging, shaking hands, playing and doing sport together | No |\n| Sharing food, plates, cups and pencils | No |\n| Using the same toilet or swimming pool | No |\n| Coughing, sneezing, tears or sweat | No |\n| Mosquito bites | No |\n| Sharing needles or razor blades | Yes – never share them |\n\n> **Remember:** It is completely safe to play, learn and share food with a friend who has HIV.\n\n## Universal precautions\n\nWhen someone is bleeding, you do not know which germs are in the blood – not only HIV. That is why we treat **all blood** as if it could contain germs. We call this **universal precautions**:\n\n1. Do not touch blood with your bare hands. Put on **rubber gloves** or put **plastic bags** over your hands.\n2. Let the injured person, if he can, press a clean cloth or bandage on the wound himself.\n3. Call an adult to help.\n4. Cover wounds with a plaster or bandage.\n5. Afterwards wash your hands with soap and water, even if you wore gloves.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Only being careful with people you *think* have HIV. Universal precautions apply to **everyone’s blood** – including your best friend’s.\n\n## Stigma, discrimination and support\n\n**Stigma** is when people have negative, unfair ideas about someone. **Discrimination** is when someone is treated unfairly because of this, for example when children refuse to play with someone, gossip or call names. Stigma makes people lonely and afraid to get tested or to fetch medicine.\n\n- A child with HIV has the same **rights** as any other child, including the right to go to school.\n- A person’s **HIV status** is **private**. Nobody has to tell others, and you must never spread someone’s secret.\n- Show **empathy**: include everyone, listen, be a good friend and help children whose family members are ill.\n- The **red ribbon** shows support for people living with HIV. World AIDS Day is on 1 December.\n\nIf you are worried or have questions, talk to a parent, teacher or other trusted adult, or call **Childline 116** (free)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"MIV","en":"HIV"},"def":{"af":"Menslike immuniteitsgebrekvirus: ’n virus wat die witbloedselle van die immuunstelsel aanval.","en":"Human immunodeficiency virus: a virus that attacks the white blood cells of the immune system."}},{"term":{"af":"Vigs","en":"AIDS"},"def":{"af":"Die latere stadium wanneer MIV, sonder behandeling, die immuunstelsel so verswak het dat die persoon maklik ander siektes kry.","en":"The later stage when HIV, without treatment, has weakened the immune system so much that the person easily gets other illnesses."}},{"term":{"af":"Immuunstelsel","en":"Immune system"},"def":{"af":"Die liggaam se verdedigingstelsel wat teen kieme veg.","en":"The body’s defence system that fights germs."}},{"term":{"af":"Witbloedselle","en":"White blood cells"},"def":{"af":"Selle in die bloed wat kieme aanval en jou help om gesond te bly.","en":"Cells in the blood that attack germs and help you stay healthy."}},{"term":{"af":"ARV’s","en":"ARVs"},"def":{"af":"Antiretrovirale medisyne wat mense met MIV elke dag neem sodat die virus hulle nie siek maak nie.","en":"Antiretroviral medicines that people with HIV take every day so that the virus does not make them sick."}},{"term":{"af":"Universele voorsorgmaatreëls","en":"Universal precautions"},"def":{"af":"Reëls om almal se bloed te hanteer asof dit kieme kan bevat, byvoorbeeld deur handskoene of plastieksakke te gebruik.","en":"Rules for treating everyone’s blood as if it could contain germs, for example by using gloves or plastic bags."}},{"term":{"af":"Stigma","en":"Stigma"},"def":{"af":"Negatiewe, onregverdige idees wat mense oor ’n persoon of groep het.","en":"Negative, unfair ideas that people have about a person or group."}},{"term":{"af":"Diskriminasie","en":"Discrimination"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer iemand onregverdig behandel word omdat hy of sy anders is of iets het, soos MIV.","en":"When someone is treated unfairly because he or she is different or has something, such as HIV."}},{"term":{"af":"Empatie","en":"Empathy"},"def":{"af":"Om te probeer verstaan hoe iemand anders voel en hulle met omgee te behandel.","en":"Trying to understand how someone else feels and treating them with care."}},{"term":{"af":"MIV-status","en":"HIV status"},"def":{"af":"Of iemand MIV het of nie; dit is privaat inligting.","en":"Whether someone has HIV or not; it is private information."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik MIV en vigs","en":"Explain HIV and AIDS"},"problem":{"af":"Anika se kleiner neef vra: ‘Is MIV en vigs dieselfde ding?’ Hoe kan sy dit eenvoudig verduidelik?","en":"Anika’s younger cousin asks: ‘Are HIV and AIDS the same thing?’ How can she explain it simply?"},"steps":[{"af":"Begin by die immuunstelsel: dit is soos soldate in die liggaam wat teen kieme veg.","en":"Start with the immune system: it is like soldiers in the body that fight germs."},{"af":"**MIV** is ’n virus wat die soldate (witbloedselle) aanval.","en":"**HIV** is a virus that attacks the soldiers (white blood cells)."},{"af":"As MIV nie behandel word nie, is daar ná ’n aantal jare te min soldate oor om die liggaam te beskerm. Dan kry die persoon maklik ander siektes – dit is **vigs**.","en":"If HIV is not treated, after a number of years there are too few soldiers left to protect the body. Then the person easily gets other illnesses – that is **AIDS**."},{"af":"Met ARV’s elke dag word die soldate beskerm, en die persoon kan gesond bly.","en":"With ARVs every day the soldiers are protected, and the person can stay healthy."}],"answer":{"af":"Nee. MIV is die virus; vigs is die latere siekte wat kan ontwikkel as MIV nie behandel word nie.","en":"No. HIV is the virus; AIDS is the later illness that can develop if HIV is not treated."}},{"title":{"af":"Help ’n maat wat bloei","en":"Help a friend who is bleeding"},"problem":{"af":"Liam val op die speelgrond en sy knie bloei erg. Jy wil help. Watter stappe volg jy?","en":"Liam falls on the playground and his knee is bleeding badly. You want to help. Which steps do you follow?"},"steps":[{"af":"Moenie die bloed met kaal hande aanraak nie. Sit handskoene aan, of plastieksakke oor jou hande as daar nie handskoene is nie.","en":"Do not touch the blood with bare hands. Put on gloves, or plastic bags over your hands if there are no gloves."},{"af":"Gee vir Liam ’n skoon lap sodat hy self druk op die wond kan sit.","en":"Give Liam a clean cloth so that he can press on the wound himself."},{"af":"Roep ’n onderwyser of ander volwassene om die wond te versorg en te verbind.","en":"Call a teacher or another adult to clean and bandage the wound."},{"af":"Was ná die tyd jou hande goed met seep en water.","en":"Afterwards wash your hands well with soap and water."}],"answer":{"af":"Handskoene of plastieksakke aan, laat Liam self druk op die wond sit, roep ’n volwassene, en was daarna jou hande.","en":"Gloves or plastic bags on, let Liam press on the wound himself, call an adult, and wash your hands afterwards."}},{"title":{"af":"Stop die stigma","en":"Stop the stigma"},"problem":{"af":"Daar is ’n gerug in die klas dat Zanele se ma MIV het. Party kinders wil nie meer langs Zanele sit of haar koeldrank deel nie. Wat is fout hiermee, en wat kan jy doen?","en":"There is a rumour in class that Zanele’s mom has HIV. Some children no longer want to sit next to Zanele or share her cooldrink. What is wrong with this, and what can you do?"},"steps":[{"af":"**Feite:** jy kan nie MIV kry deur langs iemand te sit of ’n koeldrank te deel nie.","en":"**Facts:** you cannot get HIV by sitting next to someone or sharing a cooldrink."},{"af":"**Privaatheid:** ’n persoon se MIV-status is privaat. Om gerugte te versprei, is onregverdig en kan baie seermaak.","en":"**Privacy:** a person’s HIV status is private. Spreading rumours is unfair and can hurt a lot."},{"af":"**Diskriminasie:** om Zanele uit te sluit, is diskriminasie. Sy het dieselfde regte as almal.","en":"**Discrimination:** leaving Zanele out is discrimination. She has the same rights as everyone."},{"af":"**Optrede:** wees vriendelik met Zanele, sit by haar, moenie die gerug versprei nie en vertel die onderwyser van die gerug.","en":"**Action:** be friendly to Zanele, sit with her, do not spread the rumour and tell the teacher about the rumour."}],"answer":{"af":"Die kinders diskrimineer op grond van ’n gerug en ’n mite. Jy kan Zanele insluit, die gerug stop en ’n vertroude volwassene vertel.","en":"The children are discriminating because of a rumour and a myth. You can include Zanele, stop the rumour and tell a trusted adult."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat doen MIV in die liggaam?","en":"What does HIV do in the body?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit maak die bene swak en bros","en":"It makes the bones weak and brittle"},{"af":"Dit veroorsaak ’n rooi uitslag op die vel","en":"It causes a red rash on the skin"},{"af":"Dit val die witbloedselle van die immuunstelsel aan","en":"It attacks the white blood cells of the immune system"},{"af":"Dit maak die longe vol water","en":"It fills the lungs with water"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"MIV is ’n virus wat die witbloedselle aanval. Sonder behandeling word die immuunstelsel swak, en dan kry die persoon maklik ander siektes.","en":"HIV is a virus that attacks the white blood cells. Without treatment the immune system becomes weak, and then the person easily gets other illnesses."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Jy kan MIV kry as jy ’n maat wat MIV het, ’n drukkie gee.","en":"You can get HIV if you give a friend who has HIV a hug."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. MIV word nie deur gewone kontak soos drukkies, hand skud of saam speel oorgedra nie. Drukkies is veilig – en ’n maat met MIV het dit net so nodig soos enigiemand.","en":"False. HIV is not passed on through ordinary contact such as hugs, shaking hands or playing together. Hugs are safe – and a friend with HIV needs them just as much as anyone."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende kan MIV oordra?","en":"Which one of the following can pass on HIV?"},"options":[{"af":"Om skeerlemmetjies of naalde te deel","en":"Sharing razor blades or needles"},{"af":"Om ’n toebroodjie te deel","en":"Sharing a sandwich"},{"af":"Om saam in ’n swembad te swem","en":"Swimming together in a pool"},{"af":"Om deur ’n muskiet gebyt te word","en":"Being bitten by a mosquito"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Skeerlemmetjies en naalde kan bloed van een persoon na ’n ander oordra. Kos deel, swem en muskietbyte dra nie MIV oor nie.","en":"Razor blades and needles can carry blood from one person to another. Sharing food, swimming and mosquito bites do not pass on HIV."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die medisyne wat mense met MIV elke dag neem om gesond te bly, word ___ genoem.","en":"The medicine that people with HIV take every day to stay healthy is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["ARV’s","ARVs","antiretrovirale middels"],"en":["ARVs","ARV’s","antiretrovirals"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["antibiotika","vitamiene","inentings"],"en":["antibiotics","vitamins","vaccines"]}},"explain":{"af":"ARV’s (antiretrovirale middels) keer dat die virus die immuunstelsel verswak. Antibiotika werk teen bakterieë, nie teen MIV nie.","en":"ARVs (antiretroviral medicines) stop the virus from weakening the immune system. Antibiotics work against bacteria, not against HIV."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ravi se maat se neus begin bloei op die speelgrond. Wat moet Ravi eerste doen?","en":"Ravi’s friend’s nose starts bleeding on the playground. What should Ravi do first?"},"options":[{"af":"Die bloed vinnig met sy hemp afvee","en":"Quickly wipe the blood with his shirt"},{"af":"Wegloop en niks sê nie","en":"Walk away and say nothing"},{"af":"Die bloed met sy kaal hande stop","en":"Stop the blood with his bare hands"},{"af":"Sy hande beskerm en ’n volwassene roep","en":"Protect his hands and call an adult"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Universele voorsorgmaatreëls: moenie bloed met kaal hande of klere aanraak nie. Gebruik handskoene of plastieksakke, laat jou maat self druk en roep ’n volwassene.","en":"Universal precautions: do not touch blood with bare hands or clothes. Use gloves or plastic bags, let your friend press himself and call an adult."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke woord by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each word to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"MIV","en":"HIV"},"r":{"af":"Die virus wat die immuunstelsel aanval","en":"The virus that attacks the immune system"}},{"l":{"af":"Vigs","en":"AIDS"},"r":{"af":"Die latere siekte as MIV nie behandel word nie","en":"The later illness if HIV is not treated"}},{"l":{"af":"ARV’s","en":"ARVs"},"r":{"af":"Medisyne wat die virus onder beheer hou","en":"Medicine that keeps the virus under control"}},{"l":{"af":"Immuunstelsel","en":"Immune system"},"r":{"af":"Die liggaam se verdediging teen kieme","en":"The body’s defence against germs"}},{"l":{"af":"Stigma","en":"Stigma"},"r":{"af":"Negatiewe, onregverdige idees oor mense","en":"Negative, unfair ideas about people"}}],"explain":{"af":"MIV is die virus en vigs die latere siekte. ARV’s beskerm die immuunstelsel, en stigma is die onregverdige idees wat ons moet help uitroei.","en":"HIV is the virus and AIDS the later illness. ARVs protect the immune system, and stigma is the unfair ideas we must help to wipe out."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom moet ons universele voorsorgmaatreëls by almal se bloed toepas, nie net by mense wat ons dink MIV het nie?","en":"Why must we use universal precautions with everyone’s blood, not only with people we think have HIV?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat almal se bloed MIV bevat","en":"Because everyone’s blood contains HIV"},{"af":"Omdat jy nie aan iemand kan sien watter kieme in sy bloed is nie","en":"Because you cannot see by looking at someone which germs are in his blood"},{"af":"Omdat die skoolreëls sê jy mag nooit iemand help nie","en":"Because the school rules say you may never help anyone"},{"af":"Omdat handskoene die wond vinniger laat gesond word","en":"Because gloves make the wound heal faster"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Jy kan nie aan iemand sien of hy MIV of ander kieme het nie. Daarom hanteer ons alle bloed versigtig – so is almal veilig en word niemand uitgesonder nie.","en":"You cannot see by looking at someone whether he has HIV or other germs. That is why we handle all blood carefully – this keeps everyone safe and nobody is singled out."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As daar geen handskoene is nie, kan jy ___ oor jou hande sit voordat jy iemand help wat bloei.","en":"If there are no gloves, you can put ___ over your hands before you help someone who is bleeding."},"answers":{"af":["plastieksakke","plastieksakkies","plastieksak"],"en":["plastic bags","plastic bag"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["papierhanddoeke","sokkies","lappies"],"en":["paper towels","socks","cloths"]}},"explain":{"af":"Plastiek laat nie bloed deur nie. Papier, sokkies en lappe suig bloed op, sodat dit tog aan jou vel raak.","en":"Plastic does not let blood through. Paper, socks and cloths soak up blood, so it still touches your skin."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe kan ’n mens seker weet of iemand MIV het?","en":"How can a person know for sure whether someone has HIV?"},"options":[{"af":"Deur te kyk of die persoon maer of siek lyk","en":"By looking at whether the person looks thin or sick"},{"af":"Net deur ’n MIV-toets by die kliniek","en":"Only through an HIV test at the clinic"},{"af":"Deur te kyk of die persoon baie hoes","en":"By looking at whether the person coughs a lot"},{"af":"Deur die persoon se maats uit te vra","en":"By asking the person’s friends"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Jy kan nie aan iemand sien of hy MIV het nie – baie mense met MIV lyk en voel gesond. Net ’n toets wys dit, en die uitslag is privaat.","en":"You cannot see by looking at someone whether he has HIV – many people with HIV look and feel healthy. Only a test shows it, and the result is private."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Mense met MIV wat elke dag hul ARV’s neem, kan ’n lang, gesonde lewe lei.","en":"People with HIV who take their ARVs every day can live a long, healthy life."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ARV’s hou die virus onder beheer, sodat die immuunstelsel sterk bly. Mense met MIV kan skoolgaan, werk, sport doen en gesinne hê.","en":"True. ARVs keep the virus under control, so the immune system stays strong. People with HIV can go to school, work, play sport and have families."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho se pa is siek, en party kinders lag Sipho uit. Watter optrede wys die meeste empatie?","en":"Sipho’s dad is ill, and some children laugh at Sipho. Which action shows the most empathy?"},"options":[{"af":"Lag saam sodat die ander jou nie ook uitlag nie","en":"Laugh along so that the others don’t laugh at you too"},{"af":"Vertel almal wat jy oor sy pa gehoor het","en":"Tell everyone what you have heard about his dad"},{"af":"Bly ver weg van Sipho totdat sy pa gesond is","en":"Stay far away from Sipho until his dad is well"},{"af":"Sit by Sipho, luister na hom en nooi hom om saam te speel","en":"Sit with Sipho, listen to him and invite him to play"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Empatie beteken jy probeer verstaan hoe Sipho voel en jy behandel hom met omgee. Om saam te lag, te skinder of weg te bly, is stigma en diskriminasie.","en":"Empathy means you try to understand how Sipho feels and you treat him with care. Laughing along, gossiping or staying away is stigma and discrimination."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die ___ is ’n simbool van ondersteuning vir mense wat met MIV leef.","en":"The ___ is a symbol of support for people living with HIV."},"answers":{"af":["rooi lint","rooilint"],"en":["red ribbon"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["pienk lint","geel lint","groen lint"],"en":["pink ribbon","yellow ribbon","green ribbon"]}},"explain":{"af":"Mense dra die rooi lint, veral op Wêreldvigsdag (1 Desember), om te wys dat hulle omgee vir mense met MIV en teen stigma staan.","en":"People wear the red ribbon, especially on World AIDS Day (1 December), to show that they care about people with HIV and stand against stigma."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jou maat vertel jou in vertroue dat haar boetie MIV het. Wat is die regte ding om te doen?","en":"Your friend tells you in confidence that her little brother has HIV. What is the right thing to do?"},"options":[{"af":"Hou dit privaat en bly ’n goeie vriend vir haar en haar boetie","en":"Keep it private and stay a good friend to her and her brother"},{"af":"Waarsku die ander kinders om weg te bly van haar boetie","en":"Warn the other children to stay away from her brother"},{"af":"Sê vir haar julle kan nie meer saam kos eet nie","en":"Tell her you can no longer eat together"},{"af":"Plaas dit op ’n groepsklets sodat almal kan help","en":"Post it on a group chat so that everyone can help"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Persoon se MIV-status is privaat. Om dit te versprei, kan stigma en diskriminasie veroorsaak. Kos saam eet is heeltemal veilig. As jy bekommerd is, kan jy met ’n vertroude volwassene praat.","en":"A person’s HIV status is private. Spreading it can cause stigma and discrimination. Eating together is completely safe. If you are worried, you can talk to a trusted adult."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die verskil tussen MIV en vigs?","en":"What is the difference between HIV and AIDS?"},"options":[{"af":"MIV is ’n bakterie en vigs is ’n parasiet","en":"HIV is a bacterium and AIDS is a parasite"},{"af":"Daar is geen verskil nie – dit is twee name vir dieselfde ding","en":"There is no difference – they are two names for the same thing"},{"af":"MIV is die virus; vigs is die latere siekte as MIV nie behandel word nie","en":"HIV is the virus; AIDS is the later illness if HIV is not treated"},{"af":"Vigs kom eerste, en MIV ontwikkel later daaruit","en":"AIDS comes first, and HIV develops from it later"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"MIV is die virus wat die immuunstelsel aanval. Vigs is die latere stadium as die immuunstelsel baie swak geword het. Met ARV’s ontwikkel vigs gewoonlik nie.","en":"HIV is the virus that attacks the immune system. AIDS is the later stage when the immune system has become very weak. With ARVs, AIDS usually does not develop."}}]},{"id":"lv5-t4-dwelmmisbruik","title":{"af":"Middelmisbruik","en":"Substance abuse"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik wat middels en middelmisbruik is, hoe middels jou liggaam, skoolwerk en verhoudings skaad, hoe om ‘nee’ te sê vir groepsdruk en waar om hulp te kry.","en":"You will be able to explain what substances and substance abuse are, how substances harm your body, schoolwork and relationships, how to say ‘no’ to peer pressure and where to get help."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is middels?\n\n’n **Middel** is ’n stof wat verander hoe jou liggaam of brein werk wanneer dit in jou liggaam kom. In hierdie les praat ons oor:\n\n- **sigarette** (tabak) en **vapes** (e-sigarette), wat gewoonlik albei **nikotien** bevat;\n- **alkohol**, soos bier, wyn en sterk drank;\n- **dagga** en **ander dwelms** wat onwettig verkoop word;\n- **medisyne** wat verkeerd gebruik word.\n\n**Middelmisbruik** is wanneer iemand ’n middel gebruik op ’n manier wat hulself of ander skade aandoen. Vir kinders is enige gebruik van alkohol, sigarette, vapes, dagga of ander dwelms skadelik, want hul **brein en liggaam groei nog**. Dit is teen die wet om alkohol of sigarette aan kinders onder 18 te verkoop.\n\n**Medisyne** help as dit reg gebruik word. Dit word **misbruik** as iemand dit neem sonder dat dit vir hom voorgeskryf is, meer neem as wat voorgeskryf is, of iemand anders se medisyne neem.\n\n## Hoe middels skade doen\n\n| Middel | Moontlike skade |\n|---|---|\n| Sigarette en vapes | Nikotien is **verslawend**; skade aan longe en hart; hoes en kortasem by sport |\n| Alkohol | Vertraag die brein; swak besluite en ongelukke; skade aan die lewer en brein |\n| Dagga | Swakker geheue, konsentrasie en leer; kan die longe en geestesgesondheid skaad |\n| Ander dwelms | Baie verslawend; kan die brein en hart ernstig beskadig en selfs dodelik wees |\n\n**Verslawing** beteken jou liggaam en brein voel dat hulle die middel **moet** hê. Dan is dit baie moeilik om op te hou, al wil jy.\n\nMiddels skaad nie net die liggaam nie:\n\n- **Skoolwerk:** jy sukkel om te konsentreer, jou punte daal en jy bly dalk weg van die skool.\n- **Verhoudings:** mense begin lieg, baklei met hul gesin en verloor hul vriende se vertroue.\n- **Geld:** geld word aan middels spandeer in plaas van aan kos of skoolklere.\n- **Veiligheid:** iemand **onder die invloed** maak gevaarlike keuses.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om te dink vapes is onskadelik omdat hulle soos lekkers of vrugte ruik. Die meeste vapes bevat nikotien, wat verslawend is en ’n jong brein en longe kan skaad.\n\n## Groepsdruk en hoe om ‘nee’ te sê\n\nMense begin dikwels met middels uit **nuuskierigheid**, om **in te pas**, omdat hulle **verveeld** is of omdat hulle met probleme sukkel. Middels los nie probleme op nie – hulle skep nuwes.\n\n**Groepsdruk** is wanneer jou maats jou probeer oorhaal om iets te doen. Dit kan positief wees (‘Kom ons oefen saam!’) of negatief (‘Almal doen dit, moenie ’n baba wees nie!’). So sê jy **nee**:\n\n1. **Sê duidelik nee:** ‘Nee, dankie.’ Kyk die persoon in die oë en praat met ’n ferm stem.\n2. **Gee ’n rede** as jy wil: ‘Ek wil fiks bly vir netbal.’\n3. **Stel iets anders voor:** ‘Kom ons speel eerder sokker.’\n4. **Herhaal** jou nee so dikwels as nodig.\n5. **Loop weg** na ’n veilige plek of ’n volwassene.\n6. Hou by **maats wat goeie keuses maak**.\n\n> **Onthou:** ’n Ware vriend sal jou ‘nee’ respekteer. Jy hoef niks te doen wat jy nie wil doen nie.\n\n## Waar om hulp te kry\n\n- Praat met ’n **vertroude volwassene**: ’n ouer, onderwyser, skoolberader of geestelike leier.\n- Bel **Childline 116** (gratis), ook as iemand in jou huis middels misbruik. Dit is **nooit jou skuld nie**.\n- ’n **Kliniek** kan ook help.\n- As iemand flou word of nie wakker word nie, roep dadelik ’n volwassene en bel **10177** of **112**.\n- As jy pille, naalde of iets verdags kry, moenie daaraan raak nie – vertel ’n volwassene.\n\n## Gesonde keuses\n\nJy kan op gesonde maniere pret hê en stres hanteer: doen **sport**, speel buite, leer ’n nuwe **stokperdjie**, slaap genoeg en **praat oor jou gevoelens** met iemand wat jy vertrou.","en":"## What are substances?\n\nA **substance** is something that changes how your body or brain works when it gets into your body. In this lesson we talk about:\n\n- **cigarettes** (tobacco) and **vapes** (e-cigarettes), which usually both contain **nicotine**;\n- **alcohol**, such as beer, wine and spirits;\n- **dagga** and **other drugs** that are sold illegally;\n- **medicine** that is used wrongly.\n\n**Substance abuse** is when someone uses a substance in a way that harms themselves or others. For children, any use of alcohol, cigarettes, vapes, dagga or other drugs is harmful, because their **brain and body are still growing**. It is against the law to sell alcohol or cigarettes to children under 18.\n\n**Medicine** helps when it is used correctly. It is **misused** when someone takes it without it being prescribed for them, takes more than was prescribed, or takes someone else’s medicine.\n\n## How substances cause harm\n\n| Substance | Possible harm |\n|---|---|\n| Cigarettes and vapes | Nicotine is **addictive**; damage to lungs and heart; coughing and shortness of breath during sport |\n| Alcohol | Slows down the brain; poor decisions and accidents; damage to the liver and brain |\n| Dagga | Weaker memory, concentration and learning; can harm the lungs and mental health |\n| Other drugs | Very addictive; can seriously damage the brain and heart and can even be deadly |\n\n**Addiction** means your body and brain feel that they **must** have the substance. Then it is very hard to stop, even if you want to.\n\nSubstances do not only harm the body:\n\n- **Schoolwork:** you struggle to concentrate, your marks drop and you may stay away from school.\n- **Relationships:** people start lying, fight with their family and lose their friends’ trust.\n- **Money:** money is spent on substances instead of on food or school clothes.\n- **Safety:** someone **under the influence** makes dangerous choices.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Thinking that vapes are harmless because they smell like sweets or fruit. Most vapes contain nicotine, which is addictive and can harm a young brain and lungs.\n\n## Peer pressure and how to say ‘no’\n\nPeople often start using substances out of **curiosity**, to **fit in**, because they are **bored** or because they are struggling with problems. Substances do not solve problems – they create new ones.\n\n**Peer pressure** is when your friends try to persuade you to do something. It can be positive (‘Let’s practise together!’) or negative (‘Everyone does it, don’t be a baby!’). This is how you say **no**:\n\n1. **Say no clearly:** ‘No, thanks.’ Look the person in the eyes and speak in a firm voice.\n2. **Give a reason** if you want to: ‘I want to stay fit for netball.’\n3. **Suggest something else:** ‘Let’s rather play soccer.’\n4. **Repeat** your no as often as needed.\n5. **Walk away** to a safe place or an adult.\n6. Stick with **friends who make good choices**.\n\n> **Remember:** A true friend will respect your ‘no’. You do not have to do anything you do not want to do.\n\n## Where to get help\n\n- Talk to a **trusted adult**: a parent, teacher, school counsellor or religious leader.\n- Call **Childline 116** (free), also if someone in your home abuses substances. It is **never your fault**.\n- A **clinic** can also help.\n- If someone faints or does not wake up, call an adult immediately and phone **10177** or **112**.\n- If you find pills, needles or anything suspicious, do not touch it – tell an adult.\n\n## Healthy choices\n\nYou can have fun and handle stress in healthy ways: play **sport**, play outside, learn a new **hobby**, get enough sleep and **talk about your feelings** with someone you trust."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Middel","en":"Substance"},"def":{"af":"’n Stof, soos alkohol, nikotien of ’n dwelm, wat verander hoe jou liggaam of brein werk.","en":"Something, such as alcohol, nicotine or a drug, that changes how your body or brain works."}},{"term":{"af":"Middelmisbruik","en":"Substance abuse"},"def":{"af":"Om ’n middel te gebruik op ’n manier wat jouself of ander skade aandoen.","en":"Using a substance in a way that harms yourself or others."}},{"term":{"af":"Verslawing","en":"Addiction"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer jou liggaam en brein voel dat hulle ’n middel moet hê, sodat dit baie moeilik is om op te hou.","en":"When your body and brain feel that they must have a substance, so that it is very hard to stop."}},{"term":{"af":"Nikotien","en":"Nicotine"},"def":{"af":"Die verslawende stof in sigarette en die meeste vapes.","en":"The addictive substance in cigarettes and most vapes."}},{"term":{"af":"Vape (e-sigaret)","en":"Vape (e-cigarette)"},"def":{"af":"’n Elektroniese toestel wat ’n damp met chemikalieë, gewoonlik ook nikotien, vrystel; dit is nie veilig vir kinders nie.","en":"An electronic device that gives off a vapour with chemicals, usually including nicotine; it is not safe for children."}},{"term":{"af":"Groepsdruk","en":"Peer pressure"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer maats of mense van jou ouderdom jou probeer oorhaal om iets te doen.","en":"When friends or people your age try to persuade you to do something."}},{"term":{"af":"Selfgeldend","en":"Assertive"},"def":{"af":"Om jou mening en besluit duidelik, kalm en met respek te stel, soos wanneer jy ferm ‘nee’ sê.","en":"Stating your opinion and decision clearly, calmly and respectfully, such as when you firmly say ‘no’."}},{"term":{"af":"Onder die invloed","en":"Under the influence"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer ’n middel op die oomblik verander hoe iemand dink, voel of optree.","en":"When a substance is, at that moment, changing how someone thinks, feels or acts."}},{"term":{"af":"Vertroude volwassene","en":"Trusted adult"},"def":{"af":"’n Grootmens wat jy ken en vertrou, soos ’n ouer, onderwyser of skoolberader, met wie jy oor probleme kan praat.","en":"A grown-up you know and trust, such as a parent, teacher or school counsellor, with whom you can talk about problems."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Sê nee vir ’n vape","en":"Say no to a vape"},"problem":{"af":"Ná skool by die park bied ’n paar ouer kinders vir Thabo ’n vape aan. ‘Toemaar, dis net aarbeigeur,’ sê een. Hoe kan Thabo nee sê?","en":"After school at the park some older children offer Thabo a vape. ‘Don’t worry, it’s just strawberry flavour,’ one says. How can Thabo say no?"},"steps":[{"af":"**Herken die groepsdruk:** die geur moet dit onskadelik laat klink, maar die meeste vapes bevat nikotien, wat verslawend is.","en":"**Recognise the peer pressure:** the flavour is meant to make it sound harmless, but most vapes contain nicotine, which is addictive."},{"af":"**Sê duidelik nee**, met oogkontak en ’n ferm stem: ‘Nee, dankie.’","en":"**Say no clearly**, with eye contact and a firm voice: ‘No, thanks.’"},{"af":"**Gee ’n rede of stel iets anders voor:** ‘Ek wil fiks bly vir sokker. Kom ons skop eerder bal.’","en":"**Give a reason or suggest something else:** ‘I want to stay fit for soccer. Let’s rather kick a ball.’"},{"af":"As hulle aanhou: **herhaal** jou nee, **loop weg** en vertel ’n vertroude volwassene.","en":"If they keep on: **repeat** your no, **walk away** and tell a trusted adult."}],"answer":{"af":"Thabo sê ferm ‘Nee, dankie’, gee ’n rede of stel ’n ander aktiwiteit voor, en loop weg en vertel ’n volwassene as hulle aanhou.","en":"Thabo firmly says ‘No, thanks’, gives a reason or suggests another activity, and walks away and tells an adult if they keep on."}},{"title":{"af":"Hoe ’n middel ’n lewe raak","en":"How a substance affects a life"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato se neef (16) gebruik dagga. Sy punte het gedaal, hy baklei gedurig met sy ma en hy het geld uit haar beursie gevat. Noem drie maniere waarop die middel sy lewe raak, en waar hy hulp kan kry.","en":"Lerato’s cousin (16) uses dagga. His marks have dropped, he keeps fighting with his mom and he took money from her purse. Name three ways in which the substance affects his life, and where he can get help."},"steps":[{"af":"**Skoolwerk:** dagga verswak geheue en konsentrasie, daarom daal sy punte.","en":"**Schoolwork:** dagga weakens memory and concentration, so his marks drop."},{"af":"**Verhoudings:** hy baklei met sy ma en verloor haar vertroue.","en":"**Relationships:** he fights with his mom and loses her trust."},{"af":"**Geld en eerlikheid:** hy het geld gevat om die middel te koop – middels kan mense laat lieg en steel.","en":"**Money and honesty:** he took money to buy the substance – substances can make people lie and steal."},{"af":"**Hulp:** hy kan met ’n vertroude volwassene of skoolberader praat of na ’n kliniek gaan. Lerato kan Childline 116 bel as sy bekommerd is.","en":"**Help:** he can talk to a trusted adult or school counsellor or go to a clinic. Lerato can call Childline 116 if she is worried."}],"answer":{"af":"Dit raak sy skoolwerk (punte daal), sy verhoudings (baklei, vertroue weg) en sy eerlikheid en geld (steel). Hulp: vertroude volwassene, skoolberader, kliniek of Childline 116.","en":"It affects his schoolwork (marks drop), his relationships (fighting, trust lost) and his honesty and money (stealing). Help: trusted adult, school counsellor, clinic or Childline 116."}},{"title":{"af":"Medisyne reg of verkeerd gebruik","en":"Using medicine correctly or wrongly"},"problem":{"af":"Ravi hoes erg. Hy dink: ‘As ek dubbel soveel hoesstroop drink, sal ek vinniger gesond word.’ Sy sussie stel ook voor hy drink van haar pille. Is dit veilig? Verduidelik.","en":"Ravi has a bad cough. He thinks: ‘If I drink double the amount of cough syrup, I will get better faster.’ His sister also suggests that he takes some of her pills. Is this safe? Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"Medisyne help net as dit **reg** gebruik word: die regte medisyne, vir die regte persoon, in die regte hoeveelheid.","en":"Medicine only helps when it is used **correctly**: the right medicine, for the right person, in the right amount."},{"af":"Om meer te neem as wat op die etiket of deur die dokter voorgeskryf is, is **misbruik** en kan jou vergiftig.","en":"Taking more than the label or the doctor prescribes is **misuse** and can poison you."},{"af":"Sy sussie se pille is vir haar en haar siekte voorgeskryf. Dit kan Ravi skade aandoen.","en":"His sister’s pills were prescribed for her and her illness. They can harm Ravi."},{"af":"Ravi moet vir ’n ouer sê hy hoes, en net medisyne neem wat die volwassene vir hom gee.","en":"Ravi must tell a parent that he is coughing, and only take medicine that the adult gives him."}],"answer":{"af":"Nee. Albei is medisynemisbruik. Ravi moet net sy eie medisyne neem, in die voorgeskrewe hoeveelheid, soos ’n volwassene dit vir hom gee.","en":"No. Both are medicine misuse. Ravi must only take his own medicine, in the prescribed amount, as an adult gives it to him."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is ’n middel?","en":"What is a substance?"},"options":[{"af":"Enige kos wat baie suiker bevat","en":"Any food that contains a lot of sugar"},{"af":"’n Oefening wat jou brein sterk maak","en":"An exercise that makes your brain strong"},{"af":"’n Reël wat sê wat kinders mag doen","en":"A rule that says what children may do"},{"af":"’n Stof wat verander hoe jou liggaam of brein werk","en":"Something that changes how your body or brain works"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Middel, soos alkohol, nikotien of ’n dwelm, verander hoe jou liggaam of brein werk wanneer dit in jou liggaam kom.","en":"A substance, such as alcohol, nicotine or a drug, changes how your body or brain works when it gets into your body."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die verslawende stof in sigarette en die meeste vapes heet ___.","en":"The addictive substance in cigarettes and most vapes is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["nikotien"],"en":["nicotine"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kafeïen","suurstof","kalsium"],"en":["caffeine","oxygen","calcium"]}},"explain":{"af":"Nikotien is baie verslawend. Daarom vind mense dit so moeilik om op te hou rook of vape sodra hulle begin het.","en":"Nicotine is very addictive. That is why people find it so hard to stop smoking or vaping once they have started."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is ’n voorbeeld van medisynemisbruik?","en":"Which one is an example of medicine misuse?"},"options":[{"af":"Om jou eie hoesstroop te drink soos die dokter gesê het","en":"Taking your own cough syrup as the doctor said"},{"af":"Om jou broer se pille te drink omdat jy ook kopseer het","en":"Taking your brother’s pills because you also have a headache"},{"af":"Om ’n ouer te vra voordat jy medisyne neem","en":"Asking a parent before you take medicine"},{"af":"Om medisyne buite klein kinders se bereik te bêre","en":"Storing medicine out of small children’s reach"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Medisyne word vir een persoon en een siekte voorgeskryf. Om iemand anders se medisyne te neem, is misbruik en kan jou skade aandoen.","en":"Medicine is prescribed for one person and one illness. Taking someone else’s medicine is misuse and can harm you."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Vapes is veilig vir kinders omdat hulle soos vrugte ruik.","en":"Vapes are safe for children because they smell like fruit."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die lekker geur is daar om mense, ook kinders, te lok. Die meeste vapes bevat nikotien, wat verslawend is en ’n jong brein en longe kan skaad.","en":"False. The nice flavour is there to attract people, including children. Most vapes contain nicotine, which is addictive and can harm a young brain and lungs."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken verslawing?","en":"What does addiction mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Om ’n middel net een keer te probeer","en":"Trying a substance only once"},{"af":"Om iets graag te doen, soos sokker speel","en":"Liking to do something, such as playing soccer"},{"af":"Om te voel jy moet ’n middel hê en nie maklik te kan ophou nie","en":"Feeling you must have a substance and not being able to stop easily"},{"af":"Om iemand anders te help om op te hou","en":"Helping someone else to stop"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"By verslawing voel jou liggaam en brein dat hulle die middel moet hê, en dan is dit baie moeilik om op te hou – al wil jy. Daarom is dit die beste om nooit te begin nie.","en":"With addiction your body and brain feel that they must have the substance, and then it is very hard to stop – even if you want to. That is why it is best never to start."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke manier om ‘nee’ te sê by ’n voorbeeld.","en":"Match each way of saying ‘no’ to an example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Sê duidelik nee","en":"Say no clearly"},"r":{"af":"‘Nee, dankie.’","en":"‘No, thanks.’"}},{"l":{"af":"Gee ’n rede","en":"Give a reason"},"r":{"af":"‘Ek wil fiks bly vir netbal.’","en":"‘I want to stay fit for netball.’"}},{"l":{"af":"Stel iets anders voor","en":"Suggest something else"},"r":{"af":"‘Kom ons speel eerder krieket.’","en":"‘Let’s rather play cricket.’"}},{"l":{"af":"Herhaal jou nee","en":"Repeat your no"},"r":{"af":"‘Nee. Ek het gesê nee.’","en":"‘No. I said no.’"}},{"l":{"af":"Loop weg","en":"Walk away"},"r":{"af":"Jy draai om en gaan na die onderwyser.","en":"You turn around and go to the teacher."}}],"explain":{"af":"Jy kan hierdie maniere saam gebruik. Begin met ’n duidelike nee; as die druk aanhou, herhaal dit en loop weg na ’n veilige plek of ’n volwassene.","en":"You can use these ways together. Start with a clear no; if the pressure keeps on, repeat it and walk away to a safe place or an adult."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe beïnvloed alkohol die brein?","en":"How does alcohol affect the brain?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit vertraag die brein, sodat iemand swak besluite neem","en":"It slows down the brain, so that someone makes poor decisions"},{"af":"Dit maak die brein vinniger en slimmer","en":"It makes the brain faster and cleverer"},{"af":"Dit het geen uitwerking op die brein nie, net op die maag","en":"It has no effect on the brain, only on the stomach"},{"af":"Dit help kinders se brein om vinniger te groei","en":"It helps children’s brains grow faster"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Alkohol vertraag die brein. Iemand onder die invloed reageer stadiger, neem swak besluite en kan in ongelukke betrokke raak. Vir kinders se groeiende brein is dit veral skadelik.","en":"Alcohol slows down the brain. Someone under the influence reacts more slowly, makes poor decisions and can be involved in accidents. It is especially harmful to children’s growing brains."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As jou maats jou probeer oorhaal om iets te doen, noem ons dit ___.","en":"When your friends try to persuade you to do something, we call it ___."},"answers":{"af":["groepsdruk","portuurdruk"],"en":["peer pressure"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["selfbeeld","verslawing","empatie"],"en":["self-esteem","addiction","empathy"]}},"explain":{"af":"Groepsdruk kan positief of negatief wees. As dit jou na iets skadeliks druk, soos ’n middel, sê jy duidelik nee en loop weg.","en":"Peer pressure can be positive or negative. If it pushes you towards something harmful, like a substance, you say no clearly and walk away."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe kan middelmisbruik ’n leerder se skoolwerk raak?","en":"How can substance abuse affect a learner’s schoolwork?"},"options":[{"af":"Die leerder kry beter punte omdat hy meer ontspanne is","en":"The learner gets better marks because he is more relaxed"},{"af":"Die leerder sukkel om te konsentreer en sy punte daal","en":"The learner struggles to concentrate and his marks drop"},{"af":"Dit raak net sy sport, nie sy skoolwerk nie","en":"It only affects his sport, not his schoolwork"},{"af":"Die leerder hoef minder te leer omdat hy alles onthou","en":"The learner has to study less because he remembers everything"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Middels verswak konsentrasie en geheue. Leerders wat middels gebruik, se punte daal dikwels en hulle bly dalk weg van die skool.","en":"Substances weaken concentration and memory. The marks of learners who use substances often drop and they may stay away from school."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"’n Ware vriend sal jou ‘nee’ respekteer.","en":"A true friend will respect your ‘no’."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. ’n Ware vriend wil hê jy moet veilig en gesond wees. As iemand jou aanhoudend druk om iets skadeliks te doen, is dit nie ware vriendskap nie.","en":"True. A true friend wants you to be safe and healthy. If someone keeps pressuring you to do something harmful, that is not true friendship."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Zanele se oom drink elke aand te veel en skree dan op die gesin. Zanele voel dit is haar skuld. Wat is die beste raad vir haar?","en":"Zanele’s uncle drinks too much every evening and then shouts at the family. Zanele feels it is her fault. What is the best advice for her?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is nie haar skuld nie; sy kan met ’n vertroude volwassene praat of Childline 116 bel","en":"It is not her fault; she can talk to a trusted adult or call Childline 116"},{"af":"Sy moet stilbly, want dit is ’n familiegeheim","en":"She must keep quiet, because it is a family secret"},{"af":"Sy moet harder probeer om haar oom gelukkig te hou","en":"She must try harder to keep her uncle happy"},{"af":"Sy moet sy drank wegsteek sonder om iemand te vertel","en":"She must hide his alcohol without telling anyone"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"’n Kind is nooit verantwoordelik vir ’n volwassene se middelmisbruik nie. Geheime wat jou bang of ongelukkig maak, moet vertel word. ’n Vertroude volwassene of Childline 116 (gratis) kan help.","en":"A child is never responsible for an adult’s substance abuse. Secrets that make you scared or unhappy must be told. A trusted adult or Childline 116 (free) can help."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Childline se gratis nommer vir kinders wat hulp nodig het, is ___.","en":"Childline’s free number for children who need help is ___."},"answers":{"af":["116"],"en":["116"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["10111","10177","112"],"en":["10111","10177","112"]}},"explain":{"af":"Childline 116 is gratis en jy kan oor enige probleem praat. 10111 is die polisie, 10177 die ambulans en 112 die noodnommer van ’n selfoon af.","en":"Childline 116 is free and you can talk about any problem. 10111 is the police, 10177 the ambulance and 112 the emergency number from a cellphone."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is middels soos alkohol en dagga veral skadelik vir kinders?","en":"Why are substances like alcohol and dagga especially harmful to children?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat kinders nie van die smaak hou nie","en":"Because children do not like the taste"},{"af":"Omdat dit vir kinders duurder is as vir volwassenes","en":"Because it is more expensive for children than for adults"},{"af":"Omdat kinders dit net in die vakansie gebruik","en":"Because children only use it in the holidays"},{"af":"Omdat kinders se brein en liggaam nog groei","en":"Because children’s brains and bodies are still growing"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"’n Brein wat nog groei, word makliker beskadig, en dit kan geheue, leer en gesondheid lank raak. Daarom is enige gebruik vir kinders skadelik.","en":"A brain that is still growing is damaged more easily, and this can affect memory, learning and health for a long time. That is why any use is harmful for children."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Nomsa voel gestres oor die eksamen. Watter keuse is die gesondste manier om haar stres te hanteer?","en":"Nomsa feels stressed about the exam. Which choice is the healthiest way to handle her stress?"},"options":[{"af":"Om ’n maat se vape te probeer om te ontspan","en":"Trying a friend’s vape to relax"},{"af":"Om haar ma se slaappille te drink sodat sy kan slaap","en":"Taking her mom’s sleeping pills so that she can sleep"},{"af":"Om te gaan stap, genoeg te slaap en met iemand wat sy vertrou te praat","en":"Going for a walk, getting enough sleep and talking to someone she trusts"},{"af":"Om al haar gevoelens vir haarself te hou","en":"Keeping all her feelings to herself"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Oefening, slaap en praat help om stres op ’n gesonde manier te hanteer. ’n Vape of iemand anders se pille is middelmisbruik en skep nuwe probleme, en om alles in te hou, maak dit dikwels erger.","en":"Exercise, sleep and talking help to handle stress in a healthy way. A vape or someone else’s pills is substance abuse and creates new problems, and keeping everything inside often makes it worse."}}]}]}]}}};